                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider integrable boundary conditions for both \
discrete and continuum\\nclassical integrable models. Local integrals of \
motion generated by the\\ncorresponding transfer matrices give rise to time \
evolution equations for the\\ninitial Lax operator. We systematically \
identify the modified Lax pairs for\\nboth discrete and continuum boundary \
integrable models, depending on the\\nclassical r-matrix and the boundary \
matrix.\\n\""}]}, {
