               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alessandro Nigro\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the Integrable Structure of the Ising Model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"18 pages, no figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Stat.Mech.0801:P01017,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1742-5468/2008/01/P01017\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Starting from the lattice $A_3$ realization of the \
Ising model defined on a\\nstrip with integrable boundary conditions, the \
exact spectrum (including\\nexcited states) of all the local integrals of \
motion is derived in the\\ncontinuum limit by means of TBA techniques. It is \
also possible to follow the\\nmassive flow of this spectrum between the UV \
$c=1/2$ conformal fixed point and\\nthe massive IR theory. The UV expression \
of the eigenstates of such integrals\\nof motion in terms of Virasoro modes \
is found to have only rational\\ncoefficients and their fermionic \
representation turns out to be simply related\\nto the quantum numbers \
describing the spectrum.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
