            "10.1088/1742-5468/2008/01/P01017", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  Starting from the lattice $A_3$ realization of the Ising model \
defined on a\nstrip with integrable boundary conditions, the exact spectrum \
(including\nexcited states) of all the local integrals of motion is derived \
in the\ncontinuum limit by means of TBA techniques. It is also possible to \
follow the\nmassive flow of this spectrum between the UV $c=1/2$ conformal \
fixed point and\nthe massive IR theory. The UV expression of the eigenstates \
of such integrals\nof motion in terms of Virasoro modes is found to have only \
rational\ncoefficients and their fermionic representation turns out to be \
simply related\nto the quantum numbers describing the spectrum.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
