Frappat\\n  (LAPTH), Eric Ragoucy (LAPTH)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Generalised integrable Hubbard models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Talk given by G. Feverati at the workshop \\\"RAQIS'07 \
Recent Advances\\n  in Quantum Integrable Systems\\\", 11-14 Sept. 2007, \
LAPTH, Annecy-le-Vieux,\\n  France\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"LAPTH-Conf-1222/07\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the XX and Hubbard-like models based on \
unitary superalgebras\\ngl(N|M) generalizing Shastry's and Maassarani's \
approach. We introduce the\\nR-matrix of the gl(N|M) XX-type model; the one \
of the Hubbard-like model is\\ndefined by \\\"coupling\\\" two independent XX \
models. In both cases, we show that\\nthe R-matrices satisfy the Yang-Baxter \
equation. We derive the corresponding\\nlocal Hamiltonian in the transfer \
matrix formalism and we determine its\\nsymmetries. A perturbative \
calculation \\\"\\\\`a la Klein and Seitz\\\" is performed.\\nSome explicit \
examples are worked out. We give a description of the\\ntwo-particle \
scattering.\\n\""}]}, {
