           "id" -> "0712.1940", "submitter" -> "Giovanni Feverati", "authors" -> 
            "James Drummond (LAPTH), Giovanni Feverati (LAPTH), Luc Frappat\n \
 (LAPTH), Eric Ragoucy (LAPTH)", "title" -> 
            "Generalised integrable Hubbard models", "comments" -> 
            "Talk given by G. Feverati at the workshop \"RAQIS'07 Recent \
Advances\n  in Quantum Integrable Systems\", 11-14 Sept. 2007, LAPTH, \
Annecy-le-Vieux,\n  France", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> "LAPTH-Conf-1222/07", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct the XX and Hubbard-like models based on unitary \
superalgebras\ngl(N|M) generalizing Shastry's and Maassarani's approach. We \
introduce the\nR-matrix of the gl(N|M) XX-type model; the one of the \
Hubbard-like model is\ndefined by \"coupling\" two independent XX models. In \
both cases, we show that\nthe R-matrices satisfy the Yang-Baxter equation. We \
derive the corresponding\nlocal Hamiltonian in the transfer matrix formalism \
and we determine its\nsymmetries. A perturbative calculation \"\\`a la Klein \
and Seitz\" is performed.\nSome explicit examples are worked out. We give a \
description of the\ntwo-particle scattering.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 12 Dec 2007 14:11:29 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
