                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Anomalous dimension and higher conserved charges in \
the $sl(2)$ sector of\\n${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM for generic spin $s$ and twist \
$L$ are described by using a\\nnovel kind of non-linear integral equation \
(NLIE). The latter can be derived\\nunder typical situations of the SYM \
sectors, i.e. when the scattering need not\\ndepend on the difference of the \
rapidities and these, in their turn, may also\\nlie on a bounded range. Here \
the non-linear (finite range) integral terms,\\nappearing in the NLIE and in \
the dimension formula, go to zero as $s\\\\to\\n\\\\infty$. Therefore they \
can be neglected at least up to the $O(s^0)$ order,\\nthus implying a linear \
integral equation (LIE) and a linear dimension/charge\\nformula respectively, \
likewise the 'thermodynamic' (i.e. infinite spin) case.\\nImportantly, these \
non-linear terms go faster than any inverse logarithm power\\n$(\\\\ln \
s)^{-n}$, $n>0$, thus extending the linearity validity.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
