            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Generic classically integrable boundary conditions for the \
$A_{n}^{(1)}$\naffine Toda field theories (ATFT) are investigated. The \
present analysis rests\nprimarily on the underlying algebra, defined by the \
classical version of the\nreflection equation. We use as a prototype example \
the first non-trivial model\nof the hierarchy i.e. the $A_2^{(1)}$ ATFT, \
however our results may be\ngeneralized for any $A_{n}^{(1)}$ ($n>1$). We \
assume here two distinct types of\nboundary conditions called some times \
soliton preserving (SP), and soliton\nnon-preserving (SNP) associated to two \
distinct algebras, i.e. the reflection\nalgebra and the ($q$) twisted Yangian \
respectively. The boundary local\nintegrals of motion are then systematically \
extracted from the asymptotic\nexpansion of the associated transfer matrix. \
In the case of SNP boundary\nconditions we recover previously known results. \
The other type of boundary\nconditions (SP), associated to the reflection \
algebra, are novel in this\ncontext and lead to a different set of conserved \
quantities that depend on free\nboundary parameters. It also turns out that \
the number of local integrals of\nmotion for SP boundary conditions is \
`double' compared to those of the SNP\ncase.\n", 
