                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In integrable field theories the S-matrix is usually a \
product of a\\nrelatively simple matrix and a complicated scalar factor. We \
make an\\nobservation that in many relativistic integrable field theories the \
scalar\\nfactor can be expressed as a convolution of simple kernels appearing \
in the\\nnested levels of the nested Bethe ansatz. We formulate a proposal, \
up to some\\ndiscrete ambiguities, how to reconstruct the scalar factor from \
the nested\\nBethe equations and check it for several relativistic integrable \
field\\ntheories. We then apply this proposal to the AdS asymptotic Bethe \
ansatz and\\nrecover the dressing factor in the integral representation of \
Dorey, Hofman and\\nMaldacena.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
