            "  In integrable field theories the S-matrix is usually a product \
of a\nrelatively simple matrix and a complicated scalar factor. We make an\n\
observation that in many relativistic integrable field theories the scalar\n\
factor can be expressed as a convolution of simple kernels appearing in the\n\
nested levels of the nested Bethe ansatz. We formulate a proposal, up to some\
\ndiscrete ambiguities, how to reconstruct the scalar factor from the nested\n\
Bethe equations and check it for several relativistic integrable field\n\
theories. We then apply this proposal to the AdS asymptotic Bethe ansatz and\n\
recover the dressing factor in the integral representation of Dorey, Hofman \
and\nMaldacena.\n", 
