                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Anomalous dimensions of high-twist Wilson operators \
have a nontrivial scaling\\nbehavior in the limit when their Lorentz spin \
grows exponentially with the\\ntwist. To describe the corresponding scaling \
function in planar N=4 SYM theory,\\nwe analyze an integral equation recently \
proposed by Freyhult, Rej and\\nStaudacher and argue that at strong coupling \
it can be casted into a form\\nidentical to the thermodynamical Bethe Ansatz \
equations for the nonlinear O(6)\\nsigma model. This result is in a perfect \
agreement with the proposal put\\nforward by Alday and Maldacena within the \
dual string description, that the\\nscaling function should coincide with the \
energy density of the nonlinear O(6)\\nsigma model embedded into \
AdS_5xS^5.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 27 May 2008 19:50:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
