, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  A method for determining the generalised scaling \
function(s) arising in the\\nhigh spin behaviour of long operator anomalous \
dimensions in the planar $sl(2)$\\nsector of ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM is proposed. \
The all-order perturbative expansion\\naround the strong coupling is detailed \
for the prototypical third and fourth\\nscaling functions, showing the \
emergence of the O(6) Non-Linear Sigma Model\\nmass-gap from different SYM \
'mass' functions. Remarkably, only the fourth one\\ngains contribution from \
the non-BES reducible densities and also shows up, as\\nfirst, NLSM \
interaction and specific model dependence. Finally, the computation\\nof the \
$n$-th generalised function is sketched and might be easily finalised\\nfor \
checks versus the computations in the sigma model or the complete \
string\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
