               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop algebraic methods for finding loop \
corrections to the N=4 SYM\\ndilatation generator, within the noncompact \
psu(1,1|2) sector. This sector\\ngives a 't Hooft coupling lambda-dependent \
representation of psu(1,1|2) times\\npsu(1|1)^2. At first working \
independently of the representation, we present an\\nall-order algebraic \
ansatz for the lambda-dependence of this Lie algebra's\\ngenerators. The \
ansatz solves the symmetry constraints if an auxiliary\\ngenerator, h, \
satisfies certain simple commutation relations with the Lie\\nalgebra \
generators. Applying this to the psu(1,1|2) sector leads to an\\niterative \
solution for the planar three-loop dilatation generator in terms of\\nleading \
order symmetry generators and h, which passes a thorough set of\\nspectral \
tests. We argue also that this algebraic ansatz may be applicable to\\nthe \
nonplanar theory as well.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
