               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, Freyhult, Rej and Staudacher (FRS) proposed \
an integral equation\\ndetermining the leading logarithmic term of the \
anomalous dimension of sl(2)\\ntwist-operators in N=4 SYM for large Lorentz \
spin M and twist L at fixed j =\\nL/log(M). We discuss the large j limit of \
the FRS equation. This limit can be\\nmatched with the {\\\\em fast long \
string} limit of AdS_5 X S^5 superstring\\nperturbation theory at all \
couplings. In particular, a certain part of the\\nclassical and one-loop \
string result is known to be protected and can be\\ncomputed in the weakly \
coupled large-j limit of the FRS equation. We present\\nvarious analytical \
and numerical results supporting agreement at one and two\\nloops in the \
gauge theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
