             "abstract" -> 
             "  We describe a procedure for determining the generalised \
scaling functions\n$f_n(g)$ at all the values of the coupling constant. These \
functions describe\nthe high spin contribution to the anomalous dimension of \
large twist operators\n(in the $sl(2)$ sector) of ${\\cal N}=4$ SYM. At fixed \
$n$, $f_n(g)$ can be\nobtained by solving a linear integral equation (or, \
equivalently, a linear\nsystem with an infinite number of equations), whose \
inhomogeneous term only\ndepends on the solutions at smaller $n$. In other \
