 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Asymptotic behavior of the anomalous dimensions of \
Wilson operators with high\\nspin and twist is governed in planar N=4 SYM \
theory by the scaling function\\nwhich coincides at strong coupling with the \
energy density of a two-dimensional\\nbosonic O(6) sigma model. We calculate \
this function by combining the two-loop\\ncorrection to the energy density \
for the O(n) model with two-loop correction to\\nthe mass gap determined by \
the all-loop Bethe ansatz in N=4 SYM theory. The\\nresult is in agreement \
with the prediction coming from the thermodynamical\\nlimit of the quantum \
string Bethe ansatz equations, but disagrees with the\\ntwo-loop stringy \
corrections to the folded spinning string solution.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
