 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, O. Aharony, O. Bergman, D. L. Jafferis and J. \
Maldacena (ABJM)\\nproposed three-dimensional super Chern-Simons-matter \
theory, which at level k\\nis supposed to describe the low energy limit of N \
M2-branes. For large N and k,\\nbut fixed 't Hooft coupling \\\\lambda=N/k, \
it is dual to type IIA string theory\\non AdS_4 x CP^3. For large N but \
finite k, it is dual to M theory on AdS_4 x\\nS^7/Z_k. In this paper, relying \
on the second duality, we find exact giant\\nmagnon and single spike \
solutions of membrane configurations on AdS_4 x S^7/Z_k\\nby reducing the \
system to the Neumann-Rosochatius integrable model. We derive\\nthe \
dispersion relations and their finite-size corrections with \
explicit\\ndependence on the level k.\\n\""}]}, {
