Kim\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Universal entanglement entropy in 2D conformal quantum \
critical points\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"14 pages, 3 figures, v2 references updated, minor changes\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. B 79, 115421 (2009)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevB.79.115421\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th quant-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the scaling behavior of the entanglement \
entropy of two dimensional\\nconformal quantum critical systems, i.e. systems \
with scale invariant wave\\nfunctions. They include two-dimensional \
generalized quantum dimer models on\\nbipartite lattices and quantum loop \
models, as well as the quantum Lifshitz\\nmodel and related gauge theories. \
We show that, under quite general conditions,\\nthe entanglement entropy of a \
large and simply connected sub-system of an\\ninfinite system with a smooth \
boundary has a universal finite contribution, as\\nwell as scale-invariant \
terms for special geometries. The universal finite\\ncontribution to the \
entanglement entropy is computable in terms of the\\nproperties of the \
conformal structure of the wave function of these quantum\\ncritical systems. \
The calculation of the universal term reduces to a problem in\\nboundary \
conformal field theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
