                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We study the first sub-leading correction $O((\\\\ln \
s)^0)$ to the cusp\\nanomalous dimension in the high spin expansion of finite \
twist operators in\\n${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM theory. Since this approximation is \
still governed by a linear\\nintegral equation (derived already from the \
Bethe Ansatz equations in a\\nprevious paper), we finalise it better in order \
to study the weak and strong\\ncoupling regimes. In fact, we emphasise how \
easily the weak coupling expansion\\ncan be obtained, confirms the known four \
loop result and predicts the higher\\norders. Eventually, we pay particular \
attention to the strong coupling regime\\nshowing agreement and predictions \
in comparison with string expansion;\\nspeculations on the 'universal' part \
(upon subtracting the collinear anomalous\\ndimension) are brought \
forward.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
