               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Changrim Ahn, Rafael I. Nepomechie\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Two-loop test of the N=6 Chern-Simons theory \
S-matrix\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, no figure; references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0903:144,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2009/03/144\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UMTG-262\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Starting from the integrable two-loop spin-chain \
Hamiltonian describing the\\nanomalous dimensions of scalar operators in the \
planar N=6 superconformal\\nChern-Simons theory of ABJM, we perform a direct \
coordinate Bethe ansatz\\ncomputation of the corresponding two-loop S-matrix. \
The result matches with the\\nweak-coupling limit of the scalar sector of the \
all-loop S-matrix which we have\\nrecently proposed. In particular, we \
confirm that the scattering of A and B\\nparticles is reflectionless. As a \
warm up, we first review the analogous\\ncomputation of the one-loop S-matrix \
from the one-loop dilatation operator for\\nthe scalar sector of planar N=4 \
superconformal Yang-Mills theory, and compare\\nthe result with the all-loop \
SU(2|2)^{2} S-matrix.\\n\""}]}, {
