 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a formula for the five-loop anomalous \
dimension of N=4 SYM\\ntwist-three operators in the sl(2) sector. We obtain \
its asymptotic part from\\nthe Bethe Ansatz and finite volume corrections \
from the generalized Luescher\\nformalism, considering scattering processes \
of spin chain magnons with virtual\\nparticles that travel along the \
cylinder. The complete result respects the\\nexpected large spin scaling \
properties and passes non-trivial tests including\\nreciprocity constraints. \
We analyze the pole structure and find agreement with\\na conjectured \
resummation formula. In analogy with the twist-two anomalous\\ndimension at \
four-loops, wrapping effects are of order log^2 M/M^2 for large\\nvalues of \
the spin.\\n\""}]}, {
