                 "\"L. Freyhult, M. Kruczenski, A. Tirziu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spiky strings in the SL(2) Bethe Ansatz\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages, 6 figures; v2: minor corrections, references \
added; v3:\\n  minor corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2009/07/038\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study spiky strings in the context of the SL(2) \
Bethe ansatz equations. We\\nfind an asymmetric distribution of Bethe roots \
along one cut that determines\\nthe all loop anomalous dimension at leading \
and subleading orders in a large S\\nexpansion. At leading order in strong \
coupling (large lambda) we obtain that\\nthe energy of such states is given, \
in terms of the spin S and the number of\\nspikes n by E-S=n sqrt{lambda}/(2 \
pi) (ln 16 pi S/(n sqrt{lambda})+ ln sin\\n(pi/n) - 1)+ O(ln S/S). This \
result matches perfectly the same expansion\\nobtained from the known spiky \
string classical solution.\\n  We then discuss a two cut spiky string Bethe \
root distribution at one-loop in\\nthe SL(2) Bethe ansatz. In this case we \
find a limit where n goes to infinity,\\nkeeping (E+S)/n^2, (E-S)/n, J/n \
fixed. This is the one loop version of a limit\\npreviously considered in the \
context of the string classical solutions in AdS5\\nx S5. In that case it was \
related to a string solution in the AdS pp-wave\\nbackground.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
