           "id" -> "0907.4118", "submitter" -> "Martin Kruczenski", "authors" -> 
            "M. Kruczenski and A. Tirziu", "title" -> 
            "On the dressing phase in the SL(2) Bethe Ansatz", "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, 1 figure, LaTeX. V2: References added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rev.D80:086002,2009", "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.80.086002",
             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we study the function chi(x1,x2,g) that \
determines the dressing\nphase that appears in the all-loop Bethe Ansatz \
equations for the SL(2) sector\nof N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. First, we \
consider the coefficients c_{r,s}(g)\nof the expansion of chi(x1,x2,g) in \
inverse powers of x1, x2. We obtain an\nexpression in terms of a single \
integral valid for all values of the coupling\ng. The expression is such that \
the small and large coupling expansion can be\nsimply computed in agreement \
with the expected results. This proves the, up to\nnow conjectured, \
equivalence of both expansions of the phase. The strong\ncoupling expansion \
is only asymptotic but we find an exact expression for the\nvalue of the \
residue which can be seen to decrease exponentially with g.\n  After that, we \
consider the function chi(x1,x2,g) itself and, using the same\nmethod, expand \
it for small and large coupling. All small and large coupling\ncoefficients \
chi^(n)(x1,x2), for even and odd n, are explicitly given in terms\nof finite \
sums or, alternatively, in terms of the residues of generating\nfunctions at \
certain poles.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
