             "abstract" -> 
             "  In the high spin limit the minimal anomalous dimension of \
(fixed) twist\noperators in the $sl(2)$ sector of planar ${\\cal N}=4$ Super \
Yang-Mills theory\nexpands as $\\gamma(g,s,L)=f(g) \\ln s + f_{sl}(g,L) + \
\\sum \\limits_{n=1}^\\infty\n\\gamma^{(n)}(g,L) (\\ln s)^{-n} + ... $. We \
find that the sub-logarithmic\ncontribution $\\gamma^{(n)}(g,L) $ is governed \
by a linear integral equation,\ndepending on the solution of the linear \
integral equations appearing at the\nsteps $n'\\leq n-3$. We work out this \
recursive procedure and determine\nexplicitly $\\gamma^{(n)}(g,L) $ (in \
particular $\\gamma^{(1)}(g,L)=0$ and\n\
$\\gamma^{(n)}(g,2)=\\gamma^{(n)}(g,3)=0$). Furthermore, we connect the\n\
$\\gamma^{(n)}(g,L) $ (for finite $L$) to the generalised scaling functions,\n\
$f^{(r)}_n(g)$, appearing in the limit of large twist $L\\sim\\ln s$. \
Finally, we\nprovide the first orders of weak and strong coupling for the \
first\n$\\gamma^{(n)}(g,L)$ (and hence $f^{(r)}_n(g)$).\n", 
