 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We identify the gauge theory dual of a spinning string \
of minimal energy with\\nspins S_1, S_2 on AdS_5 and charge J on S^5. For \
this purpose we focus on a\\ncertain set of local operators with two \
different types of covariant\\nderivatives acting on complex scalar fields. \
We analyse the corresponding\\nnested Bethe equations for the ground states \
in the limit of large spins. The\\nauxiliary Bethe roots form certain string \
configurations in the complex plane,\\nwhich enable us to derive integral \
equations for the leading and sub-leading\\ncontribution to the anomalous \
dimension. The results can be expressed through\\nthe observables of the \
sl(2) sub-sector, i.e. the cusp anomaly f(g) and the\\nvirtual scaling \
function B_L(g), rendering the strong-coupling analysis\\nstraightforward. \
Furthermore, we also study a particular sub-class of these\\noperators \
specialising to a scaling limit with finite values of the second spin\\nat \
weak and strong coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
