            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1002:050,2010", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP02(2010)050", "report-no" -> 
            "AEI-2009-111, Imperial-TP-AR-2009-3, UUITP-24/09", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We identify the gauge theory dual of a spinning string of \
minimal energy with\nspins S_1, S_2 on AdS_5 and charge J on S^5. For this \
purpose we focus on a\ncertain set of local operators with two different \
types of covariant\nderivatives acting on complex scalar fields. We analyse \
the corresponding\nnested Bethe equations for the ground states in the limit \
of large spins. The\nauxiliary Bethe roots form certain string configurations \
in the complex plane,\nwhich enable us to derive integral equations for the \
leading and sub-leading\ncontribution to the anomalous dimension. The results \
can be expressed through\nthe observables of the sl(2) sub-sector, i.e. the \
cusp anomaly f(g) and the\nvirtual scaling function B_L(g), rendering the \
strong-coupling analysis\nstraightforward. Furthermore, we also study a \
particular sub-class of these\noperators specialising to a scaling limit with \
finite values of the second spin\nat weak and strong coupling.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 12 Nov 2009 20:44:31 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 4 Jan 2010 20:06:38 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-02-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Freyhult", "Lisa", ""}, {
              "Rej", "Adam", ""}, {"Zieme", "Stefan", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
