 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In [1], the spectrum (eigenvalues and eigenstates) of a \
lattice\\nregularizations of the Sine-Gordon model has been completely \
characterized in\\nterms of polynomial solutions with certain properties of \
the Baxter equation.\\nThis characterization for cyclic representations has \
been derived by the use of\\nthe Separation of Variables (SOV) method of \
Sklyanin and by the direct\\nconstruction of the Baxter Q-operator family. \
Here, we reconstruct the Baxter\\nQ-operator and the same characterization of \
the spectrum by only using the SOV\\nmethod. This analysis allows us to \
deduce the main features required for the\\nextension to cyclic \
representations of other integrable quantum models of this\\nkind of spectrum \
characterization.\\n\""}]}, {
