               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the computation of the 2-loop correction to \
the energy of a folded\\nspinning string in AdS_5 with an angular momentum J \
in S^5 in the scaling limit\\nlog S, J >>1 with J / log S fixed. This \
correction gives the third term in the\\nstrong-coupling expansion of the \
generalized scaling function. The computation,\\nusing the AdS light-cone \
gauge approach developed in our previous paper, is\\ndone by expanding the \
AdS_5 x S^5 superstring partition function near the\\ngeneralized null cusp \
world surface associated to the spinning string solution.\\nThe result \
corrects and extends the previous conformal gauge result of\\narXiv:0712.2479 \
and is found to be in complete agreement with the corresponding\\nterms in \
the generalized scaling function as obtained from the asymptotic \
Bethe\\nansatz in arXiv:0805.4615 (and also partially from the quantum O(6) \
model and\\nthe Bethe ansatz data in arXiv:0809.4952). This provides a highly \
nontrivial\\nstrong coupling comparison of the Bethe ansatz proposal with the \
quantum AdS_5\\nx S^5 superstring theory, which goes beyond the leading \
semiclassical term\\neffectively controlled by the underlying algebraic \
curve. The 2-loop\\ncomputation we perform involves all the structures in the \
AdS light-cone gauge\\nsuperstring action of hep-th/0009171 and thus tests \
its ultraviolet finiteness\\nand, through the agreement with the Bethe \
ansatz, its quantum integrability. We\\ndo most of the computations for a \
generalized spinning string solution or the\\ncorresponding null cusp surface \
that involves both the orbital momentum and the\\nwinding in a large circle \
of S^5.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
