          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1002.0018", "submitter" -> "Radu Roiban", "authors" -> 
            "S. Giombi, R. Ricci, R. Roiban, A.A. Tseytlin, C. Vergu", 
            "title" -> 
            "Generalized scaling function from light-cone gauge AdS_5 x S^5\n \
 superstring", "comments" -> "50 pages, latex", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 1006:060,2010", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP06(2010)060", 
            "report-no" -> "Imperial-TP-RR-01-2010, Brown-HET-1596", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We revisit the computation of the 2-loop correction to the \
energy of a folded\nspinning string in AdS_5 with an angular momentum J in \
S^5 in the scaling limit\nlog S, J >>1 with J / log S fixed. This correction \
gives the third term in the\nstrong-coupling expansion of the generalized \
scaling function. The computation,\nusing the AdS light-cone gauge approach \
developed in our previous paper, is\ndone by expanding the AdS_5 x S^5 \
superstring partition function near the\ngeneralized null cusp world surface \
associated to the spinning string solution.\nThe result corrects and extends \
the previous conformal gauge result of\narXiv:0712.2479 and is found to be in \
complete agreement with the corresponding\nterms in the generalized scaling \
function as obtained from the asymptotic Bethe\nansatz in arXiv:0805.4615 \
(and also partially from the quantum O(6) model and\nthe Bethe ansatz data in \
arXiv:0809.4952). This provides a highly nontrivial\nstrong coupling \
comparison of the Bethe ansatz proposal with the quantum AdS_5\nx S^5 \
superstring theory, which goes beyond the leading semiclassical term\n\
effectively controlled by the underlying algebraic curve. The 2-loop\n\
computation we perform involves all the structures in the AdS light-cone \
gauge\nsuperstring action of hep-th/0009171 and thus tests its ultraviolet \
finiteness\nand, through the agreement with the Bethe ansatz, its quantum \
integrability. We\ndo most of the computations for a generalized spinning \
string solution or the\ncorresponding null cusp surface that involves both \
the orbital momentum and the\nwinding in a large circle of S^5.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 1 Feb 2010 20:50:17 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-11-20", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Giombi", "S.", ""}, {"Ricci", "R.", ""}, {
              "Roiban", "R.", ""}, {"Tseytlin", "A. A.", ""}, {
              "Vergu", "C.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
