 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the expectation value of a local operator \
on a strip with\\nnon-trivial boundaries in 1+1 dimensional massive \
integrable QFT. Using finite\\nvolume regularisation in the crossed channel \
and extending the boundary state\\nformalism to the finite volume case we \
give a series expansion for the\\none-point function in terms of the exact \
form factors of the theory. The\\ntruncated series is compared with the \
numerical results of the truncated\\nconformal space approach in the scaling \
Lee-Yang model. We discuss the\\nrelevance of our results to quantum quench \
problems.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
