          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1003.3118\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Francesco Fiamberti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Francesco Fiamberti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wrapping effects in supersymmetric gauge theories\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ph.D. thesis\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1002/prop.201000065\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Several perturbative computations of finite-size \
effects, performed on the\\ngauge side of the AdS/CFT correspondence by means \
of superspace techniques, are\\npresented. First, wrapping effects are \
analyzed in the standard N = 4 theory,\\nby means of the calculation of the \
four-loop anomalous dimension of the Konishi\\noperator. Then, a similar \
computation at five loops is described. Afterwards,\\nfinite-size effects are \
studied in the beta-deformed case, where thanks to the\\nreduced number of \
supersymmetries the simpler class of single-impurity\\noperators can be \
considered, so that the leading corrections to the anomalous\\ndimensions at \
generic order can be reduced to the computation of a class of\\nintegrals. \
Explicit results are given up to eleven loops. A further chapter \
is\\ndedicated to the computation of the leading finite-size effects on \
operators\\ndual to open strings. In the end, some comments are made and \
proposals for\\nfuture developments are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 16 Mar 2010 10:10:39 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-05-18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Fiamberti\"", ",", "\"Francesco\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1003.3118", "submitter" -> "Francesco Fiamberti", 
            "authors" -> "Francesco Fiamberti", "title" -> 
            "Wrapping effects in supersymmetric gauge theories", "comments" -> 
            "Ph.D. thesis", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1002/prop.201000065", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Several perturbative computations of finite-size effects, \
performed on the\ngauge side of the AdS/CFT correspondence by means of \
superspace techniques, are\npresented. First, wrapping effects are analyzed \
in the standard N = 4 theory,\nby means of the calculation of the four-loop \
anomalous dimension of the Konishi\noperator. Then, a similar computation at \
five loops is described. Afterwards,\nfinite-size effects are studied in the \
beta-deformed case, where thanks to the\nreduced number of supersymmetries \
the simpler class of single-impurity\noperators can be considered, so that \
the leading corrections to the anomalous\ndimensions at generic order can be \
reduced to the computation of a class of\nintegrals. Explicit results are \
given up to eleven loops. A further chapter is\ndedicated to the computation \
of the leading finite-size effects on operators\ndual to open strings. In the \
end, some comments are made and proposals for\nfuture developments are \
discussed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 16 Mar 2010 10:10:39 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-05-18", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fiamberti", "Francesco", ""}}}], 
