           "id" -> "1003.4214", "submitter" -> "Didina Serban", "authors" -> 
            "Didina Serban", "title" -> 
            "Integrability and the AdS/CFT correspondence", "comments" -> 
            "106 pages, 9 figures, habilitation thesis; minor corrections,\n  \
published version", "journal-ref" -> "J.Phys.A44:124001,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/44/12/124001", "report-no" -> "IPhT-T10-042", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The description of gauge theories at strong coupling is one of \
the\nlong-standing problems in theoretical physics. The idea of a relation \
between\nstrongly coupled gauge theories and string theory was pioneered by \
't Hooft,\nWilson and Polyakov. A decade ago, Maldacena made this relation \
explicit by\nconjecturing the exact equivalence of a conformally invariant \
theory in four\ndimensions, the maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory, \
with string theory\nin the AdS5 x S5 background. Other examples of \
correspondence between a\nconformally invariant theory and string theory in \
an AdS background were\ndiscovered recently. The comparison of the two sides \
of the correspondence\nrequires the use of non-perturbative methods. The \
discovery of integrable\nstructures in gauge theory and string theory led to \
the conjecture that the two\ntheories are integrable for any value of the \
coupling constant and that they\nshare the same integrable structure defined \
non-perturbatively. The last eight\nyears brought remarkable progress in \
identifying this solvable model and in\nexplicitly solving the problem of \
computing the spectrum of conformal\ndimensions of the theory. The progress \
came from the identification of the\ndilatation operator with an integrable \
spin chain and from the study of the\nstring sigma model. In this thesis, I \
present the evolution of the concept of\nintegrability in the framework of \
the AdS/CFT correspondence and the the main\nresults obtained using this \
approach.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
