, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  This review is devoted to collecting some results on \
the high spin expansion\\nof (minimal) anomalous dimension. Thanks to the \
recent rationale on\\nintegrability, planar ${\\\\cal N}=4$ super Yang-Mills \
theory (or its\\n$\\\\text{AdS}_5\\\\times\\\\text{S}^5$ string counterpart) \
represents a very\\npracticable field. Here the attention will be restricted \
to its sector of twist\\noperators, although the analysis tools are quite \
general (in integrable\\ntheories). Some structures and ideas turn out to be \
general also for other\\nsectors or gauge theories.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
