            "  Using recently proposed method of discrete Hirota dynamics for \
integrable\n(1+1)D quantum field theories on a finite space circle of length \
L, we derive\nand test numerically a finite system of nonlinear integral \
equations for the\nexact spectrum of energies of SU(N)xSU(N) principal chiral \
field model as\nfunctions of m L, where m is the mass scale. We propose a \
determinant solution\nof the underlying Y-system, or Hirota equation, in \
terms of determinants\n(Wronskians) of NxN matrices parameterized by N-1 \
functions of the spectral\nparameter, with the known analytical properties at \
finite L. Although the\nmethod works in principle for any state, the explicit \
equations are written for\nstates in the U(1) sector only. For N>2, we \
encounter and clarify a few\nsubtleties in these equations related to the \
presence of bound states, absent\nin the previously considered N=2 case. In \
particular, we solve these equations\nnumerically for a few low-lying states \
for N=3 in a wide range of m L.\n", 
