 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study finite-size corrections to the magnon \
dispersion relation in three\\nmodels which differ from string theory on AdS5 \
x S5 in their boundary\\nconditions. Asymptotically, this is accomplished by \
twisting the transfer\\nmatrix in a way which manifestly preserves \
integrability. In model I all\\nworld-sheet fields are periodic, whereas \
model II represents a particular\\norbifold of AdS5 x S5 and model III is a \
beta-deformed theory. For models I and\\nII we construct the one-particle TBA \
equations and use them to determine the\\nleading finite-size correction to \
the asymptotic Bethe equation. We also make\\nsome interesting observations \
concerning the quantization conditions for the\\nmomentum. For the same \
models we compute the leading and for model II the\\nnext-to-leading order \
finite-size corrections to the asymptotic magnon\\ndispersion relation. \
Furthermore, we apply L\\\\\\\"uscher's formulae to compute the\\nleading \
finite-size corrections in beta-deformed theory. In addition to\\nreproducing \
known results, we provide new predictions for two-particle states\\nfrom the \
sl(2) sector, to be confronted with explicit field-theoretic\\ncalculations \
in the dual gauge theory. Finally, we prove that the leading\\nfinite-size \
correction to the energy of an sl(2) magnon in orbifold theory is\\nthe same \
as the one for an su(2) magnon in beta-deformed theory for special\\nvalues \
of beta. We also speculate that for these values of beta our result for\\nthe \
next-to-leading order correction in the orbifold model might coincide \
with\\nthe corresponding correction to the energy of su(2) magnon in \
beta-deformed\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
