            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1012.3454\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dmytro Volin\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dmytro Volin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"String hypothesis for gl(n|m) spin chains: a \
particle/hole democracy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"38 pages; v2: references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s11005-012-0570-9\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.other math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper is devoted to integrable gl(n|m) spin chains \
which allow for\\nformulation of the string hypothesis. Considering the \
thermodynamic limit of\\nsuch spin chains, we derive linear functional \
equations that symmetricaly treat\\nholes and particles. The functional \
equations naturally organize different\\ntypes of excitations into a pattern \
equivalent to the one of Y-system, and, not\\nsurprisingly, the Y-system can \
be easily derived from the functional equations.\\nThe Y-system is known to \
contain most of the information about the symmetry of\\nthe model, therefore \
we map the symmetry knowledge directly to the description\\nof string \
excitations. Our analysis is applicable for highest weight\\nrepresentations \
which for some choice of the Kac-Dynkin diagram have only one\\nnonzero \
Dynkin label. This generalizes known results for the AdS/CFT \
spectral\\nproblem and for the Hubbard model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
