           "id" -> "1012.3994", "submitter" -> "Romuald A. Janik", "authors" -> 
            "Romuald A. Janik", "title" -> 
            "Review of AdS/CFT Integrability, Chapter III.5: Luscher \
corrections", "comments" -> 
            "18 pages, see also overview article arXiv:1012.3982, v2: \
references\n  to other chapters updated, v3: references added; v4: various \
comments added,\n  journal version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/s11005-011-0511-z", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In integrable quantum field theories the large volume spectrum \
is given by\nthe Bethe Ansatz. The leading corrections, due to virtual \
particles circulating\naround the cylinder, are encoded in so-called Luscher \
corrections. In order to\napply these techniques to the AdS/CFT \
correspondence one has to generalize\nthese corrections to the case of \
generic dispersion relations and to\nmultiparticle states. We review these \
various generalizations and the\napplications of Luscher's corrections to the \
study of the worldsheet QFT of the\nsuperstring in AdS5xS5 and, consequently, \
to anomalous dimensions of operators\nin N=4 SYM theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 17 Dec 2010 20:58:13 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
