            "Davide Astolfi, Valentina Giangreco M. Puletti, Gianluca \
Grignani,\n  Troels Harmark, Marta Orselli", "title" -> 
            "Finite-size corrections for quantum strings on AdS_4 x CP^3", 
            "comments" -> 
            "Published version, references added. A discussion on single\n  \
oscillator states included", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP05(2011)128", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We revisit the calculation of curvature corrections to the \
pp-wave energy of\ntype IIA string states on AdS_4 x CP^3 initiated in \
arXiv:0807.1527. Using the\nnear pp-wave Hamiltonian found in \
arXiv:0912.2257, we compute the first\nnon-vanishing correction to the energy \
of a set of bosonic string states at\norder 1/R^2, where R is the curvature \
radius of the background. The leading\ncurvature corrections give rise to \
cubic, order 1/R, and quartic, order 1/R^2,\nterms in the Hamiltonian, for \
which we implement the appropriate normal\nordering prescription. Including \
the contributions from all possible fermionic\nand bosonic string states, we \
find that there exist logarithmic divergences in\nthe sums over mode numbers \
which cancel between the cubic and quartic\nHamiltonian. We show that the \
cubic Hamiltonian naturally requires that the\ncutoff for summing over heavy \
modes must be twice the one for light modes. With\nthis prescription the \
strong-weak coupling interpolating function h(\\lambda),\nentering the magnon \
dispersion relation, does not receive a one-loop\ncorrection, in agreement \
with the algebraic curve spectrum. However, the single\nmagnon dispersion \
relation exhibits finite-size exponential corrections.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 29 Dec 2010 21:00:03 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 21 May 2011 09:07:01 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
