                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In [1] an integrable quantum model was introduced and a \
class of its cyclic\\nrepresentations was proven to define lattice \
regularizations of the Sine-Gordon\\nmodel. Here, we analyze general cyclic \
representations of this integrable\\nquantum model by extending the spectrum \
construction introduced in [2] in the\\nframework of the Separation of \
Variables (SOV) of Sklyanin. We show that as in\\n[1] also for general \
representations, the transfer matrix spectrum (eigenvalues\\nand eigenstates) \
is completely characterized in terms of polynomial solutions\\nof an \
associated functional Baxter equation. Moreover, we prove that the \
method\\nhere developed has two fundamental built-in features: i) the \
completeness of\\nthe set of the transfer matrix eigenstates constructed from \
the solutions of\\nthe associated Bethe ansatz equations, ii) the existence \
and complete\\ncharacterization of the Baxter Q-operator.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
