            "authors" -> "G. Niccoli", "title" -> 
            "Completeness of Bethe Ansatz by Sklyanin SOV for Cyclic \
Representations\n  of Integrable Quantum Models", "comments" -> 
            "38 pages, two references added, minor modifications", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1103:123,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP03(2011)123", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "math-ph hep-th math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In [1] an integrable quantum model was introduced and a class \
of its cyclic\nrepresentations was proven to define lattice regularizations \
of the Sine-Gordon\nmodel. Here, we analyze general cyclic representations of \
this integrable\nquantum model by extending the spectrum construction \
introduced in [2] in the\nframework of the Separation of Variables (SOV) of \
Sklyanin. We show that as in\n[1] also for general representations, the \
transfer matrix spectrum (eigenvalues\nand eigenstates) is completely \
characterized in terms of polynomial solutions\nof an associated functional \
Baxter equation. Moreover, we prove that the method\nhere developed has two \
fundamental built-in features: i) the completeness of\nthe set of the \
transfer matrix eigenstates constructed from the solutions of\nthe associated \
Bethe ansatz equations, ii) the existence and complete\ncharacterization of \
the Baxter Q-operator.\n", 
