            "  We study gluon scattering amplitudes/Wilson loops in N=4 super \
Yang-Mills\ntheory at strong coupling by calculating the area of the minimal \
surfaces in\nAdS_3 based on the associated thermodynamic Bethe ansatz system. \
The remainder\nfunction of the amplitudes is computed by evaluating the free \
energy, the T-\nand Y-functions of the homogeneous sine-Gordon model. Using \
conformal field\ntheory (CFT) perturbation, we examine the mass corrections \
to the free energy\naround the CFT point corresponding to the regular \
polygonal Wilson loop. Based\non the equivalence between the T-functions and \
the g-functions, which measure\nthe boundary entropy, we calculate \
corrections to the T- and Y-functions as\nwell as express them at the CFT \
point by the modular S-matrix. We evaluate the\nremainder function around the \
CFT point for 8 and 10-point amplitudes\nexplicitly and compare these \
analytic expressions with the 2-loop formulas. The\ntwo rescaled remainder \
functions show very similar power series structures.\n", 
