                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz equations arising in \
the context of the\\n$AdS_5/CFT_4$ correspondence exhibit an important \
difference with respect to\\ntheir analogues in relativistic integrable \
quantum field theories: their\\nsolutions (the Y functions) are not \
meromorphic functions of the rapidity, but\\nlive on a complicated Riemann \
surface with an infinite number of branch points\\nand therefore enjoy a new \
kind of extended Y-system. In this paper we review\\nthe analytic properties \
of the TBA solutions, and present new information\\ncoming from their \
numerical study. An identity allowing to simplify the\\nequations and the \
numerical implementation is presented, together with various\\nplots which \
highlight the analytic structure of the Y functions.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 2 Mar 2011 17:45:37 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-03-03\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
