             "  The thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz equations arising in the \
context of the\n$AdS_5/CFT_4$ correspondence exhibit an important difference \
with respect to\ntheir analogues in relativistic integrable quantum field \
theories: their\nsolutions (the Y functions) are not meromorphic functions of \
the rapidity, but\nlive on a complicated Riemann surface with an infinite \
number of branch points\nand therefore enjoy a new kind of extended Y-system. \
