Functions\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"4 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.Lett.106:241601,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1103/PhysRevLett.106.241601\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using AdS/CFT we derive from the folded spinning string \
ordinary differential\\nequations for the anomalous dimension of the dual N=4 \
SYM twist-two operators\\nat strong coupling. We show that for large spin the \
asymptotic solutions have\\nthe Gribov-Lipatov recirocity property. To obtain \
this result we use a hidden\\nmodular invariance of the energy-spin relation \
of the folded spinning string.\\nFurther we identify the Moch-Vermaseren-Vogt \
(MVV) relations, which were first\\nrecognized in plain QCD calculations, as \
the recurrence relations of the\\nasymptotic series ansatz.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
