            "authors" -> "Alessandro Torrielli", "title" -> 
            "Yangians, S-matrices and AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "95 pages, pdfLaTeX, 1 figure. This is an author-created,\n  \
un-copyedited version of an invited topical review accepted for publication\n \
 in Journal of Physics A: Mathematical and Theoretical. IOP Publishing Ltd is\
\n  not responsible for any errors or omissions in this version of the \
manuscript\n  or any version derived from it. v2: fixed sign in (15), added \
comment about\n  Jacobi identity in footnote 50", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J.Phys.A44:263001,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/44/26/263001", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This review is meant to be an account of the properties of the\
\ninfinite-dimensional quantum group (specifically, Yangian) symmetry lying\n\
behind the integrability of the AdS/CFT spectral problem. In passing, the\n\
chance is taken to give a concise anthology of basic facts concerning \
Yangians\nand integrable systems, and to store a series of remarks, \
observations and\nproofs the author has collected in a five-year span of \
research on the subject.\nWe hope this exercise will be useful for future \
attempts to study Yangians in\nfield and string theories, with or without \
supersymmetry.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 13 Apr 2011 12:54:32 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 6 Jul 2011 16:12:54 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-07-07", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Torrielli", "Alessandro", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
