            "  We consider N=4 SYM and a class of spin N, length-3, twist \
operators beyond\nthe well studied sl(2) subsector. They can be identified at \
one-loop with three\ngluon operators. At strong coupling, they are associated \
with spinning strings\nwith two spins in AdS5. We exploit the Y-system to \
compute the leading\nweak-coupling four loop wrapping correction to their \
anomalous dimension. The\nresult is written in closed form as a function of \
the spin N. We combine the\nwrapping correction with the known four-loop \
asymptotic Bethe Ansatz\ncontribution and analyze special limits in the spin \
N. In particular, at large\nN, we prove that a generalized Gribov-Lipatov \
reciprocity holds. At negative\nunphysical spin, we present a simple \
BFKL-like equation predicting the\nrightmost leading poles.\n", 
