                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8113/45/2/025201\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A procedure to construct $K$-matrices from the \
generalized $q$-Onsager\\nalgebra $\\\\cO_{q}(\\\\hat{g})$ is proposed. This \
procedure extends the intertwiner\\ntechniques used to obtain scalar \
(c-number) solutions of the reflection\\nequation to dynamical (non-c-number) \
solutions. It shows the relation between\\nsoliton non-preserving reflection \
equations or twisted reflection equations and\\nthe generalized $q$-Onsager \
algebras. These dynamical $K$-matrices are\\nimportant to quantum integrable \
models with extra degrees of freedom located at\\nthe boundaries: for \
instance, in the quantum affine Toda field theories on the\\nhalf-line they \
yield the boundary amplitudes. As examples, the cases \
of\\n$\\\\cO_{q}(a^{(2)}_{2})$ and $\\\\cO_{q}(a^{(1)}_{2})$ are treated in \
details.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
