            "  A procedure to construct $K$-matrices from the generalized \
$q$-Onsager\nalgebra $\\cO_{q}(\\hat{g})$ is proposed. This procedure extends \
the intertwiner\ntechniques used to obtain scalar (c-number) solutions of the \
reflection\nequation to dynamical (non-c-number) solutions. It shows the \
relation between\nsoliton non-preserving reflection equations or twisted \
reflection equations and\nthe generalized $q$-Onsager algebras. These \
dynamical $K$-matrices are\nimportant to quantum integrable models with extra \
degrees of freedom located at\nthe boundaries: for instance, in the quantum \
affine Toda field theories on the\nhalf-line they yield the boundary \
amplitudes. As examples, the cases of\n$\\cO_{q}(a^{(2)}_{2})$ and \
$\\cO_{q}(a^{(1)}_{2})$ are treated in details.\n", 
