            "  We consider the space of boundary conditions of Virasoro \
minimal models\nformed from the composition of a collection of flows \
generated by \\phi_{1,3}.\nThese have recently been shown to fall naturally \
into a sequence, each term\nhaving a coordinate on it in terms of a boundary \
parameter, but no global\nparameter has been proposed. Here we investigate \
the idea that the overlaps of\nparticular bulk states with the boundary \
states give natural coordinates on the\nmoduli space of boundary conditions. \
We find formulae for these overlaps using\nthe known thermodynamic Bethe \
Ansatz descriptions of the ground and first\nexcited state on the cylinder \
and show that they give a global coordinate on\nthe space of boundary \
conditions, showing it is smooth and compact as expected.\n", 
