               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study gluon scattering amplitudes/Wilson loops in \
N=4 super Yang-Mills\\ntheory at strong coupling which correspond to minimal \
surfaces with a\\nlight-like polygonal boundary in AdS_3. We find a concise \
expression of the\\nremainder function in terms of the T-function of the \
associated thermodynamic\\nBethe ansatz (TBA) system. Continuing our previous \
work on the analytic\\nexpansion around the CFT/regular-polygonal limit, we \
derive a formula of the\\nleading-order expansion for the general 2n-point \
remainder function. The\\nT-system allows us to encode its momentum \
dependence in only one function of\\nthe TBA mass parameters, which is \
obtained by conformal perturbation theory. We\\ncompute its explicit form in \
the single mass cases. We also find that the\\nrescaled remainder functions \
at strong coupling and at two loops are close to\\neach other, and their \
ratio at the leading order approaches a constant near 0.9\\nfor large \
n.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
