 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Basic notions regarding classical integrable systems \
are reviewed. An\\nalgebraic description of the classical integrable models \
together with the zero\\ncurvature condition description is presented. The \
classical r-matrix approach\\nfor discrete and continuum classical integrable \
models is introduced. Using\\nthis framework the associated classical \
integrals of motion and the\\ncorresponding Lax pair are extracted based on \
algebraic considerations. Our\\nattention is restricted to classical discrete \
and continuum integrable systems\\nwith periodic boundary conditions. Typical \
examples of discrete (Toda chain,\\ndiscrete NLS model) and continuum \
integrable models (NLS, sine-Gordon models\\nand affine Toda field theories) \
are also discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
