                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A systematic approach to Liouville integrable defects \
is proposed, based on\\nan underlying Poisson algebraic structure. The \
non-linear Schrodinger model in\\nthe presence of a single particle-like \
defect is investigated through this\\nalgebraic approach. Local integrals of \
motions are constructed as well as the\\ntime components of the corresponding \
Lax pairs. Continuity conditions imposed\\nupon the time components of the \
Lax pair to all orders give rise to sewing\\nconditions, which turn out to be \
compatible with the hierarchy of charges in\\ninvolution. Coincidence of our \
results with the continuum limit of the discrete\\nexpressions obtained in \
earlier works further confirms our approach.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
