 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the anomalous dimension for a short \
single-trace operator in\\nplanar ABJM theory at intermediate coupling. This \
is done by solving\\nnumerically the set of Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz \
equations which are expected\\nto describe the exact spectrum of the theory. \
We implement a truncation method\\nwhich significantly reduces the number of \
integral equations to be solved and\\nimproves numerical efficiency. Results \
are obtained for a range of 't Hooft\\ncoupling lambda corresponding to $0 \\\
\\leq h(\\\\lambda) \\\\leq 1$, where h(lambda) is\\nthe interpolating \
function of the AdS4/CFT3 Bethe equations.\\n\""}]}, {
