            "  We compute the first curvature corrections to the spectrum of \
light-cone\ngauge type IIA string theory that arise in the expansion of \
$AdS_4\\times\n\\mathbb{CP}^3$ about a plane-wave limit. The resulting \
spectrum is shown to\nmatch precisely, both in magnitude and degeneration \
that of the corresponding\nsolutions of the all-loop Gromov--Vieira Bethe \
Ansatz. The one-loop dispersion\nrelation correction is calculated for all \
the single oscillator states of the\ntheory, with the level matching \
condition lifted. It is shown to have all\nlogarithmic divergences cancelled \
and to leave only a finite exponentially\nsuppressed contribution, as shown \
earlier for light bosons. We argue that there\nis no ambiguity in the choice \
of the regularization for the self-energy sum,\nsince the regularization \
applied is the only one preserving unitarity.\nInteraction matrices in the \
full degenerate two-oscillator sector are\ncalculated and the spectrum of all \
two light magnon oscillators is completely\ndetermined. The same finite-size \
corrections, at the order 1/J, where $J$ is\nthe length of the chain, in the \
two-magnon sector are calculated from the all\nloop Bethe Ansatz. The \
corrections obtained by the two completely different\nmethods coincide up to \
the fourth order in $\\lambda' =\\lambda/J^2$. We\nconjecture that the \
equivalence extends to all orders in $\\lambda$ and to\nhigher orders in 1/J.\
\n", "versions" -> {{
