            "  We study the boundary free energy of the XXZ spin-$\\tf{1}{2}$ \
chain subject\nto diagonal boundary fields. We first show that the \
representation for its\nfinite Trotter number approximant obtained by Bortz, \
Frahm and G\\\"{o}hmann is\nrelated to the partition function of the \
six-vertex model with reflecting ends.\nBuilding on the Tsuchiya determinant \
representation for the latter quantity we\nare able to take the infinite \
Trotter number limit. This yields a\nrepresentation for the surface free \
energy which involves the solution of the\nnon-linear integral equation that \
governs the thermodynamics of the XXZ\nspin-1/2 chain subject to periodic \
boundary conditions. We show that this\nintegral representation allows one to \
extract the low-$T$ asymptotic behavior\nof the boundary magnetization at \
finite external magnetic field on the one hand\nand numerically plot this \
function on the other hand.\n", 
