           "id" -> "1204.3302", "submitter" -> "Valentina Forini", "authors" -> 
            "V. Forini, V. Giangreco M. Puletti, O. Ohlsson Sax", "title" -> 
            "Generalized cusp in AdS_4 x CP^3 and more one-loop results from\n\
  semiclassical strings", "comments" -> 
            "48 pages, 2 figures, version 3, corrected misprints in formulas \
2.12,\n  B.86, C.33, added comment on verification of the light-like limit", 
            "journal-ref" -> "J.Phys. A46 (2013) 115402", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/46/11/115402", "report-no" -> 
            "ICCUB-12-127; HU-EP-12/11; NORDITA-2012-22; \
ITP-UU-12/11;SPIN-12/10", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We evaluate the exact one-loop partition function for \
fundamental strings\nwhose world-surface ends on a cusp at the boundary of \
AdS_4 and has a \"jump\" in\nCP^3. This allows us to extract the stringy \
prediction for the ABJM generalized\ncusp anomalous dimension \
Gamma_{cusp}^{ABJM} (phi,theta) up to NLO in\nsigma-model perturbation \
theory. With a similar analysis, we present the exact\npartition functions \
for folded closed string solutions moving in the AdS_3\nparts of AdS_4 x CP^3 \
and AdS_3 x S^3 x S^3 x S^1 backgrounds. Results are\nobtained applying to \
the string solutions relevant for the AdS_4/CFT_3 and\nAdS_3/CFT_2 \
correspondence the tools previously developed for their AdS_5 x S^5\n\
counterparts.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
