               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The tau_2-model and the chiral Potts model revisited: \
completeness of\\n  Bethe equations from Sklyanin's SOV method\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages. Minor modifications in the text and some \
notations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Stat. Mech. (2012) P11005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1742-5468/2012/11/P11005\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The most general cyclic representations of the quantum \
integrable tau_2-model\\nare analyzed. The complete characterization of the \
tau_2-spectrum (eigenvalues\\nand eigenstates) is achieved in the framework \
of Sklyanin's Separation of\\nVariables (SOV) method by extending and \
adapting the ideas first introduced in\\n[1, 2]: i) The determination of the \
tau_2-spectrum is reduced to the\\nclassification of the solutions of a given \
functional equation in a class of\\npolynomials. ii) The determination of the \
tau_2-eigenstates is reduced to the\\nclassification of the solutions of an \
associated Baxter equation. These last\\nsolutions are proven to be \
polynomials for a quite general class of\\ntau_2-self-adjoint representations \
and the completeness of the associated Bethe\\nansatz type equations is \
derived. Finally, the following results are derived\\nfor the inhomogeneous \
chiral Potts model: i) Simplicity of the spectrum, for\\ngeneral \
representations. ii) Complete characterization of the chiral Potts\\nspectrum \
(eigenvalues and eigenstates) and completeness of Bethe ansatz \
type\\nequations, for the self-adjoint representations of tau_2-model on the \
chiral\\nPotts algebraic curves.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 21 May 2012 14:35:32 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 11 Jun 2012 15:59:48 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
