            "authors" -> "N. Grosjean and G. Niccoli", "title" -> 
            "The tau_2-model and the chiral Potts model revisited: \
completeness of\n  Bethe equations from Sklyanin's SOV method", "comments" -> 
            "40 pages. Minor modifications in the text and some notations", 
            "journal-ref" -> "J. Stat. Mech. (2012) P11005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/2012/11/P11005", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "math-ph cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th math.MP", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The most general cyclic representations of the quantum \
integrable tau_2-model\nare analyzed. The complete characterization of the \
tau_2-spectrum (eigenvalues\nand eigenstates) is achieved in the framework of \
Sklyanin's Separation of\nVariables (SOV) method by extending and adapting \
the ideas first introduced in\n[1, 2]: i) The determination of the \
tau_2-spectrum is reduced to the\nclassification of the solutions of a given \
functional equation in a class of\npolynomials. ii) The determination of the \
tau_2-eigenstates is reduced to the\nclassification of the solutions of an \
associated Baxter equation. These last\nsolutions are proven to be \
polynomials for a quite general class of\ntau_2-self-adjoint representations \
and the completeness of the associated Bethe\nansatz type equations is \
derived. Finally, the following results are derived\nfor the inhomogeneous \
chiral Potts model: i) Simplicity of the spectrum, for\ngeneral \
representations. ii) Complete characterization of the chiral Potts\nspectrum \
(eigenvalues and eigenstates) and completeness of Bethe ansatz type\n\
equations, for the self-adjoint representations of tau_2-model on the chiral\n\
Potts algebraic curves.\n", 
