            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP09(2012)006", 
            "report-no" -> 
            "ITP-UU-12-22, SPIN-12-20, TCD-MATH-12-05, HMI-12-02", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider one particularly interesting class of composite \
gauge-invariant\noperators in N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. An exceptional \
feature of these\noperators is that in the Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz \
approach the one-loop\nrapidities of the constituent magnons are shown to be \
exact in the 't Hooft\ncoupling constant. This is used to propose the mirror \
TBA description for these\noperators. The proposal is shown to pass several \
non-trivial checks.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 30 May 2012 13:10:27 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-05", 
