                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2012)075\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the quark--anti-quark potential on the \
three sphere or the\\ngeneralized cusp anomalous dimension in planar N=4 SYM. \
We concentrate on the\\nvacuum potential in the near BPS limit with $L$ units \
of R-charge.\\nEquivalently, we study the anomalous dimension of a \
super-Wilson loop with L\\nlocal fields inserted at a cusp. The system is \
described by a recently proposed\\ninfinite set of non-linear integral \
equations of the Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz\\n(TBA) type. That system of TBA \
equations is very similar to the one of the\\nspectral problem but simplifies \
a bit in the near BPS limit. Using techniques\\nbased on the Y-system of \
functional equations we first reduced the infinite\\nsystem of TBA equations \
to a Finite set of Nonlinear Integral Equations\\n(FiNLIE). Then we solve the \
FiNLIE system analytically, obtaining a simple\\nanalytic result for the \
potential! Surprisingly, we find that the system has\\nequivalent \
descriptions in terms of an effective Baxter equation and in terms\\nof a \
matrix model. At L=0, our result matches the one obtained before \
using\\nlocalization techniques. At all other L's, the result is new. Having \
a new\\nparameter, L, allows us to take the large L classical limit. We use \
the matrix\\nmodel description to solve the classical limit and match the \
result with a\\nstring theory computation. Moreover, we find that the \
classical string\\nalgebraic curve matches the algebraic curve arising from \
the matrix model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
