 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the null-polygonal minimal surfaces in AdS_4, \
which correspond to\\nthe gluon scattering amplitudes/Wilson loops in N=4 \
super Yang-Mills theory at\\nstrong coupling. The area of the minimal \
surfaces with n cusps is characterized\\nby the thermodynamic Bethe ansatz \
(TBA) integral equations or the Y-system of\\nthe homogeneous sine-Gordon \
model, which is regarded as the\\nSU(n-4)_4/U(1)^{n-5} generalized \
parafermion theory perturbed by the\\nweight-zero adjoint operators. Based on \
the relation to the TBA systems of the\\nperturbed W minimal models, we solve \
the TBA equations by using the conformal\\nperturbation theory, and obtain \
the analytic expansion of the remainder\\nfunction around the \
UV/regular-polygonal limit for n=6 and 7. We compare the\\nrescaled remainder \
function for n=6 with the two-loop one, to observe that they\\nare close to \
each other similarly to the AdS_3 case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
