               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Multiple zeta functions and double wrapping in planar N=4 \
SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"49 pages. Available online Mathematica packages contain \
routines for\\n  working with multiple Hurwitz zeta functions and weak \
coupling expansion of\\n  the FiNLIE, they are an important part of the \
article. The article has\\n  interactive symbols \\\"#\\\" (they work in \
pdf-viewers that support JavaScript);\\n  v2: terminology is made more \
precise, references added; v3: published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nuclear Physics B (2013), Volume 875, Isuue 3, Pages \
757-789\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2013.07.020\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the FiNLIE solution of the AdS/CFT Y-system, we \
compute the anomalous\\ndimension of the Konishi operator in planar N=4 SYM \
up to eight loops, i.e. up\\nto the leading double wrapping order. At this \
order a non reducible\\nEuler-Zagier sum, zeta(1,2,8), appears for the first \
time. We find that at all\\norders in perturbation, every spectral-dependent \
quantity of the Y-system is\\nexpressed through multiple Hurwitz zeta \
functions, hence we provide a\\nMathematica package to manipulate these \
functions, including the particular\\ncase of Euler-Zagier sums. Furthermore, \
we conjecture that only Euler-Zagier\\nsums can appear in the answer for the \
anomalous dimension at any order in\\nperturbation theory.\\n  We also resum \
the leading transcendentality terms of the anomalous dimension\\nat all \
orders, obtaining a simple result in terms of Bessel functions. Finally,\\nwe \
demonstrate that exact Bethe equations should be related to an absence \
of\\npoles condition that becomes especially nontrivial at double \
wrapping.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
