           "id" -> "1302.1135", "submitter" -> "S\\'ebastien Leurent", 
            "authors" -> "S\\'ebastien Leurent, Dmytro Volin", "title" -> 
            "Multiple zeta functions and double wrapping in planar N=4 SYM", 
            "comments" -> 
            "49 pages. Available online Mathematica packages contain routines \
for\n  working with multiple Hurwitz zeta functions and weak coupling \
expansion of\n  the FiNLIE, they are an important part of the article. The \
article has\n  interactive symbols \"#\" (they work in pdf-viewers that \
support JavaScript);\n  v2: terminology is made more precise, references \
added; v3: published version", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nuclear Physics B (2013), Volume 875, Isuue 3, Pages 757-789", 
            "doi" -> "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2013.07.020", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Using the FiNLIE solution of the AdS/CFT Y-system, we compute \
the anomalous\ndimension of the Konishi operator in planar N=4 SYM up to \
eight loops, i.e. up\nto the leading double wrapping order. At this order a \
non reducible\nEuler-Zagier sum, zeta(1,2,8), appears for the first time. We \
find that at all\norders in perturbation, every spectral-dependent quantity \
of the Y-system is\nexpressed through multiple Hurwitz zeta functions, hence \
we provide a\nMathematica package to manipulate these functions, including \
the particular\ncase of Euler-Zagier sums. Furthermore, we conjecture that \
only Euler-Zagier\nsums can appear in the answer for the anomalous dimension \
at any order in\nperturbation theory.\n  We also resum the leading \
transcendentality terms of the anomalous dimension\nat all orders, obtaining \
a simple result in terms of Bessel functions. Finally,\nwe demonstrate that \
exact Bethe equations should be related to an absence of\npoles condition \
that becomes especially nontrivial at double wrapping.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 5 Feb 2013 18:00:17 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 12 Feb 2013 14:43:35 GMT"}, {
