           "id" -> "1302.2208", "submitter" -> "Jun-Bao Wu", "authors" -> 
            "Song He, Jun-Bao Wu", "title" -> 
            "Note on Integrability of Marginally Deformed ABJ(M) Theories", 
            "comments" -> 
            "22 pages, 7 figures. An term in eq. (3.12) was deleted. After \
the\n  paper was published in JHEP, We corrected some errors especially the \
ones in\n  the action of $\\beta$-deformed ABJM theory in the e-print on \
arXiv. Main\n  conclusion and results are unchanged", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 1304 (2013) 012; Erratum 1604 (2016) 139", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP04(2013)012 10.1007/JHEP04(2016)139", "report-no" -> 
            "CAS-KITPC/ITP-360", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the anomalous dimensions of operators in the scalar \
sector of\n\\beta-deformed ABJ(M) theories. We show that the anomalous \
dimension matrix at\ntwo-loop order gives an integrable Hamiltonian acting on \
an alternating SU(4)\nspin chain with the spins at odd lattice sides in the \
fundamental\nrepresentation and the spins at even lattices in the \
anti-fundamental\nrepresentation. We get a set of $\\beta$-deformed Bethe \
ansatz equations which\ngive the eigenvalues of Hamiltonian of this deformed \
spin chain system. Based\non our computations, we also extend our study to \
non-supersymmetric\nthree-parameter $\\gamma$-deformation of ABJ(M) theories \
and find that the\ncorresponding Hamiltonian is the same as the one in \
\\beta-deformed case at\ntwo-loop level in the scalar sector.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
