            "  The cosmological constant problem and the absence of new \
natural physics at\nthe electroweak scale, if confirmed by the LHC, may \
either indicate that the\nnature is fine-tuned or that a refined notion of \
naturalness is required. We\nconstruct a family of toy UV complete quantum \
theories providing a proof of\nconcept for the second possibility. Low energy \
physics is described by a tuned\neffective field theory, which exhibits \
relevant interactions not protected by\nany symmetries and separated by an \
arbitrary large mass gap from the new\n\"gravitational\" physics, represented \
by a set of irrelevant operators.\nNevertheless, the only available language \
to describe dynamics at all energy\nscales does not require any fine-tuning. \
The interesting novel feature of this\nconstruction is that UV physics is not \
described by a fixed point, but rather\nexhibits asymptotic fragility. \
Observation of additional unprotected scalars at\nthe LHC would be a smoking \
gun for this scenario. Natural tuning also favors\nTeV scale unification.\n", 
