            "  Studying the scattering of excitations around a dynamical \
background has a\nlong history in the context of integrable models. The \
Gubser-Klebanov-Polyakov\nstring solution provides such a background for the \
string/gauge correspondence.\nTaking the conjectured all-loop asymptotic \
equations for the AdS_4/CFT_3\ncorrespondence as the starting point, we \
derive the S-matrix and a set of\nspectral equations for the lowest-lying \
excitations. We find that these\nequations resemble closely the analogous \
equations for AdS_5/CFT_4, which are\nalso discussed in this paper. At large \
values of the coupling constant we show\nthat they reproduce the Bethe \
equations proposed to describe the spectrum of\nthe low-energy limit of the \
AdS_4xCP^3 sigma model.\n", 
