, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We derive the Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz equations for \
the relativistic sigma\\nmodel describing the AdS(4)XCP(3) string II A theory \
at strong coupling (i.e.\\nin the Alday-Maldacena decoupling limit). The \
corresponding Y-system involves\\nan infinite number of Y functions and is of \
a new type, although it shares a\\npeculiar feature with the Y-system for \
AdS(4)XCP(3). A truncation of the\\nequations at level p and a further \
generalisation to generic rank N allow us an\\nalternative description of the \
theory as the N=4, p= \\\\infty representative in\\nan infinite family of \
models corresponding to the conformal cosets CP(N-1)_p X\\nU(1), perturbed by \
a relevant composite field \\\\phi(N,p) =\\\\phi_[CP(N-1)_p] \
X\\n\\\\phi[U(1)] that couples the two independent conformal field theories. \
The\\ncalculation of the ultraviolet central charge confirms the conjecture \
by Basso\\nand Rej and the conformal dimension of the perturbing operator, at \
every N and\\np, is obtained using the Y-system periodicity. The conformal \
dimension of\\n\\\\phi[CP(N-1)_p] matches that of the field identified by \
Fendley while\\ndiscussing integrability issues for the purely bosonic \
CP(N-1) sigma model.\\n\""}]}, {
