               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable structure of Quantum Field Theory: Classical \
flat connections\\n  versus quantum stationary states\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"63 pages, 8 figures; v2:typos corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2014)147\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"RUNHETC-2013-18\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We establish a correspondence between an infinite set \
of special solutions of\\nthe (classical) modified sinh-Gordon equation and a \
set of stationary states in\\nthe finite-volume Hilbert space of the \
integrable 2D QFT invented by V.A.\\nFateev. The modified sinh-Gordon \
equation arise in this case as a\\nzero-curvature condition for a class of \
multivalued connections of the\\npunctured Riemann sphere, similarly to \
Hitchin's self-duality equations. The\\nproposed correspondence between the \
classical and quantum integrable systems\\nprovides a powerful tool for \
deriving functional and integral equations which\\ndetermine the full \
spectrum of local integrals of motion for massive QFT in a\\nfinite volume. \
Potential applications of our results to the problem of\\nnon-perturbative \
quantization of classically integrable non-linear sigma models\\nare briefly \
discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
