          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1310.4854", "submitter" -> "Stijn van Tongeren", 
            "authors" -> "Stijn J. van Tongeren", "title" -> 
            "Integrability of the AdS_5 x S^5 superstring and its \
deformations", "comments" -> 
            "v3, published version, introduction slightly broadened, typos\n  \
corrected, updates to outlook and references. Review based on author's PhD\n  \
thesis, 214 pages, many figures. Partly based on arXiv:1009.4118,\n  \
arXiv:1103.5853, arXiv:1111.0564, arXiv:1201.1451, arXiv:1208.3478, and\n  \
arXiv:1210.8185", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 47 (2014) 433001", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/47/43/433001", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This article reviews the application of integrability to the \
spectral problem\nof strings on AdS_5 x S^5 and its deformations. We begin \
with a pedagogical\nintroduction to integrable field theories culminating in \
the description of\ntheir finite-volume spectra through the thermodynamic \
Bethe ansatz. Next, we\napply these ideas to the AdS_5 x S^5 string and in \
later chapters discuss how\nto account for particular integrable \
deformations. Through the AdS/CFT\ncorrespondence this gives an exact \
description of anomalous scaling dimensions\nof single trace operators in \
planar N=4 supersymmetry Yang-Mills theory, its\n`orbifolds', and beta and \
gamma-deformed supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory. We\nalso touch upon some \
subtleties arising in these deformed theories.\nFurthermore, we consider \
complex excited states (bound states) in the su(2)\nsector and give their \
thermodynamic Bethe ansatz description. Finally we\ndiscuss the thermodynamic \
Bethe ansatz for a quantum deformation of the AdS_5 x\nS^5 superstring \
S-matrix, with close relations to among others Pohlmeyer\nreduced string \
theory, and briefly indicate more recent developments in this\narea.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 17 Oct 2013 20:56:26 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 5 Nov 2013 15:36:57 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 10 Oct 2014 14:19:33 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-01-13", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"van Tongeren", "Stijn J.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{7.101714451163087, -6.40098730427714}, 0.10102143756118451],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1310.5735\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Georgios Papathanasiou\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Georgios Papathanasiou\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hexagon Wilson Loop OPE and Harmonic \
Polylogarithms\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"34 pages, 4 figures, 7 ancillary files; v2: typos \
corrected,\\n  references updated\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1311 (2013) 150\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2013)150\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A recent, integrability-based conjecture in the \
framework of the Wilson loop\\nOPE for N=4 SYM theory, predicts the leading \
OPE contribution for the hexagon\\nMHV remainder function and NMHV ratio \
function to all loops, in integral form.\\nWe prove that these integrals \
evaluate to a particular basis of harmonic\\npolylogarithms, at any order in \
the weak coupling expansion. The proof\\nconstitutes an algorithm for the \
direct computation of the integrals, which we\\nemploy in order to obtain the \
full (N)MHV OPE contribution in question up to 6\\nloops, and certain parts \
of it up to 12 loops. We attach computer-readable\\nfiles with our results, \
as well as an algorithm implementation which may be\\nreadily used to \
generate higher-loop corrections. The feasibility of obtaining\\nthe explicit \
kinematical dependence of the first term in the OPE in principle\\nat \
arbitrary loop order, offers promise for the suitability of this approach \
as\\na non-perturbative description of Wilson loops/scattering amplitudes.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 21 Oct 2013 21:51:06 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 17 Feb 2014 10:22:56 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
