                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze the spectrum of open strings stretched \
between a D-brane and an\\nanti-D-brane in planar AdS/CFT using various \
tools. We focus on open strings\\nending on two giant gravitons with \
different orientation in $AdS_5 \\\\times S^5$\\nand study the spectrum of \
string excitations using the following approaches:\\nopen spin-chain, \
boundary asymptotic Bethe ansatz and boundary thermodynamic\\nBethe ansatz \
(BTBA). We find agreement between a perturbative high order\\ndiagrammatic \
calculation in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM and the leading finite-size\\nboundary \
Luscher correction. We study the ground state energy of the system \
at\\nfinite coupling by deriving and numerically solving a set of BTBA \
equations.\\nWhile the numerics give reasonable results at small coupling, \
they break down\\nat finite coupling when the total energy of the string gets \
close to zero,\\npossibly indicating that the state turns tachyonic. The \
location of the\\nbreakdown is also predicted analytically.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
