 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The boundary thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (BTBA) \
equations introduced in\\narXiv:1203.1913 and arXiv:1203.1617 to describe the \
cusp anomalous dimension\\ncontain imaginary chemical potentials and singular \
boundary fugacities, which\\nmake its systematic expansion problematic. We \
propose an alternative\\nformulation based on real chemical potentials and \
additional source terms. We\\nexpand our equations to double wrapping order \
and find complete agreement with\\nthe direct two-loop gauge theory \
computation of the cusp anomalous dimension.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
