Saulius\\n  Valatka\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum Spectral Curve at Work: From Small Spin to Strong \
Coupling in\\n  N=4 SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages, references added; v3: due to a typo in the \
coefficients C_2\\n  and D_2 on page 29 we corrected the rational part of the \
strong coupling\\n  predictions in equations (1.5-6), (6.22-24), (6.27-30) \
and in Table 1\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2014)156\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We apply the recently proposed quantum spectral curve \
technique to the study\\nof twist operators in planar N=4 SYM theory. We \
focus on the small spin\\nexpansion of anomalous dimensions in the sl(2) \
sector and compute its first two\\norders exactly for any value of the 't \
Hooft coupling. At leading order in the\\nspin S we reproduced Basso's slope \
function. The next term of order S^2\\nstructurally resembles the \
Beisert-Eden-Staudacher dressing phase and takes\\ninto account wrapping \
contributions. This expansion contains rich information\\nabout the spectrum \
of local operators at strong coupling. In particular, we\\nfound a new \
coefficient in the strong coupling expansion of the Konishi\\noperator \
dimension and confirmed several previously known terms. We also\\nobtained \
several new orders of the strong coupling expansion of the BFKL\\npomeron \
intercept. As a by-product we formulated a prescription for the \
correct\\nanalytical continuation in S which opens a way for deriving the \
BFKL regime of\\ntwist two anomalous dimensions from AdS/CFT \
integrability.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
