 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In these notes, we study a class of grand-canonical \
partition functions with\\na kernel depending on a small parameter \
$\\\\epsilon$. This class is directly\\nrelevant to Nekrasov partition \
functions of $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SUSY gauge theories\\non the 4d \
$\\\\Omega$-background, for which $\\\\epsilon$ is identified with one \
of\\nthe equivariant deformation parameter. In the Nekrasov-Shatashvili limit\
\\n$\\\\epsilon\\\\to0$, we show that the free energy is given by an on-shell \
effective\\naction. The equations of motion take the form of a TBA equation. \
The free\\nenergy is identified with the Yang-Yang functional of the \
corresponding system\\nof Bethe roots. We further study the associated \
canonical model that takes the\\nform of a generalized matrix model. \
Confinement of the eigenvalues by the\\nshort-range potential is observed. In \
the limit where this confining potential\\nbecomes weak, the collective field \
theory formulation is recovered. Finally, we\\ndiscuss the connection with \
the alternative expression of instanton partition\\nfunctions as sums over \
Young tableaux.\\n\""}]}, {
