         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1402.1626", "submitter" -> "Jean-Emile Bourgine", 
            "authors" -> "Jean-Emile Bourgine", "title" -> 
            "Confinement and Mayer cluster expansions", "comments" -> 
            "24 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1142/S0217751X14500778", "report-no" -> "APCTP Pre2014-001", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In these notes, we study a class of grand-canonical partition \
functions with\na kernel depending on a small parameter $\\epsilon$. This \
class is directly\nrelevant to Nekrasov partition functions of \
$\\mathcal{N}=2$ SUSY gauge theories\non the 4d $\\Omega$-background, for \
which $\\epsilon$ is identified with one of\nthe equivariant deformation \
parameter. In the Nekrasov-Shatashvili limit\n$\\epsilon\\to0$, we show that \
the free energy is given by an on-shell effective\naction. The equations of \
motion take the form of a TBA equation. The free\nenergy is identified with \
the Yang-Yang functional of the corresponding system\nof Bethe roots. We \
further study the associated canonical model that takes the\nform of a \
generalized matrix model. Confinement of the eigenvalues by the\nshort-range \
potential is observed. In the limit where this confining potential\nbecomes \
weak, the collective field theory formulation is recovered. Finally, we\n\
discuss the connection with the alternative expression of instanton partition\
\nfunctions as sums over Young tableaux.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
