                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the QCD string as an effective string, \
whose action describes\\nlong-range stringy fluctuations. The leading \
infrared contribution to the\\nground state energy is given by the \
Alvarez-Arvis formula, usually derived\\nusing the Nambu-Goto action. Here we \
rederive it by a saddle point calculation\\nusing the Polyakov formulation of \
the free string, where the world sheet metric\\nand the target space \
coordinates are treated as independent variables. The next\\norder relevant \
in the infrared term in the effective action is the extrinsic\\ncurvature \
term. We show that the spectrum does not change order by order in \
the\\ninverse string length, but may change at intermediate \
distances.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
