            "  We consider the QCD string as an effective string, whose \
action describes\nlong-range stringy fluctuations. The leading infrared \
contribution to the\nground state energy is given by the Alvarez-Arvis \
formula, usually derived\nusing the Nambu-Goto action. Here we rederive it by \
a saddle point calculation\nusing the Polyakov formulation of the free \
string, where the world sheet metric\nand the target space coordinates are \
treated as independent variables. The next\norder relevant in the infrared \
term in the effective action is the extrinsic\ncurvature term. We show that \
the spectrum does not change order by order in the\ninverse string length, \
but may change at intermediate distances.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 4 Mar 2014 18:38:22 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
