                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the spectrum of a string propagating on \
eta-deformed AdS_5 x S^5\\nby treating its world-sheet theory as an \
integrable quantum field theory. The\\nexact S-matrix of this field theory is \
given by a q-deformation of the AdS_5 x\\nS^5 world-sheet S-matrix with real \
deformation parameter. By considering mirror\\n(double Wick-rotated) versions \
of these world-sheet theories we give the\\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz \
description of their exact finite size spectra.\\nInterestingly, this class \
of models maps onto itself under the mirror\\ntransformation. At the level of \
the string this appears to say that the\\nlight-cone worldsheet theories of \
strings on particular pairs of backgrounds\\nare related by a double Wick \
rotation, a feature we call 'mirror duality'. We\\nprovide a partial check of \
these statements at the level of the sigma model by\\nconsidering reduced \
actions and their corresponding (mirror) giant magnon\\nsolutions.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
