                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider twist $J$ operators with spin $S$ in the \
$sl(2)$ sector of\\n$\\\\mathcal N=4$ SYM. The small spin expansion of their \
anomalous dimension\\ndefines the so-called slope functions. Much is known \
about the linear term, but\\nthe study of the quadratic correction, the \
curvature function, started only\\nvery recently. At any fixed $J$, the \
curvature function can be extracted at all\\nloops from the \
$\\\\mathbf{P}\\\\mu$-system formulation of the Thermodynamical \
Bethe\\nAnsatz. Here, we work at the one-loop level and follow a different \
approach. We\\npresent a systematic double expansion of the Bethe Ansatz \
equations at large\\n$J$ and small winding number. We succeed in fully \
resumming this expansion and\\nobtain a closed explicit simple formula for \
the one-loop curvature function.\\nThe formula is parametric in $J$ and can \
be evaluated with minor effort for any\\nfixed $J$. The result is an explicit \
series in odd-index $\\\\zeta$ values. Our\\napproach provides a complete \
reconciliation between the $\\\\mathbf{P}\\\\mu$-system\\npredictions and the \
large $J$ approach.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 3 Apr 2014 13:10:58 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
