 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore a direct connection between the collinear \
limit and the\\nmulti-Regge limit for scattering amplitudes in the N=4 super \
Yang-Mills theory.\\nStarting with the collinear expansion for the six-gluon \
amplitude in the\\nEuclidean kinematic region, we perform an analytic \
continuation term by term to\\nthe so-called Mandelstam region. We find that \
the result coincides with the\\ncollinear expansion of the analytically \
continued amplitude. We then take the\\nmulti-Regge limit, and conjecture \
that the final result precisely reproduces\\nthe one from the BFKL approach. \
Combining this procedure with the OPE for null\\npolygonal Wilson loops, we \
explicitly compute the leading contribution in the\\n\\\"collinear-Regge\\\" \
limit up to five loops. Our results agree with all the known\\nresults up to \
four loops. At five-loop, our results up to the\\nnext-to-next-to-leading \
logarithmic approximation (NNLLA) also reproduce the\\nknown results, and for \
the N^3LLA and the N^4LLA give non-trivial predictions.\\nWe further present \
an all-loop prediction for the imaginary part of the\\nnext-to-double-leading \
logarithmic approximation. Our procedure has a\\npossibility of an \
interpolation from weak to strong coupling in the multi-Regge\\nlimit with \
the help of the OPE.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
