            "Wilson loop OPE, analytic continuation and multi-Regge limit", 
            "comments" -> 
            "37 pages, 5 figures, v2: references added, v3: published \
version, a\n  computational error in eq.(5.32) corrected", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP10(2014)038", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We explore a direct connection between the collinear limit and \
the\nmulti-Regge limit for scattering amplitudes in the N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory.\nStarting with the collinear expansion for the six-gluon amplitude in \
the\nEuclidean kinematic region, we perform an analytic continuation term by \
term to\nthe so-called Mandelstam region. We find that the result coincides \
with the\ncollinear expansion of the analytically continued amplitude. We \
then take the\nmulti-Regge limit, and conjecture that the final result \
precisely reproduces\nthe one from the BFKL approach. Combining this \
procedure with the OPE for null\npolygonal Wilson loops, we explicitly \
compute the leading contribution in the\n\"collinear-Regge\" limit up to five \
loops. Our results agree with all the known\nresults up to four loops. At \
five-loop, our results up to the\nnext-to-next-to-leading logarithmic \
approximation (NNLLA) also reproduce the\nknown results, and for the N^3LLA \
and the N^4LLA give non-trivial predictions.\nWe further present an all-loop \
prediction for the imaginary part of the\nnext-to-double-leading logarithmic \
approximation. Our procedure has a\npossibility of an interpolation from weak \
to strong coupling in the multi-Regge\nlimit with the help of the OPE.\n", 
