                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A new integrable boundary for the classical nonlinear \
Schr\\\\\\\"odinger model is\\nderived by dressing a boundary with a defect. \
A complete investigation of the\\nintegrability of the new boundary is \
carried out in the sense that the boundary\\n${\\\\cal K}$ matrix is derived \
and the integrability is proved via the classical\\n$r$-matrix. The issue of \
conserved charges is also discussed. The key point in\\nproving the \
integrability of the new boundary is the use of suitable modified\\nPoisson \
brackets. Finally, concerning the kind of defect used in the \
present\\ncontext, this investigation offers the opportunity to prove - \
beyond any doubts\\n- their integrability.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
