                 "\"  Chiral-antichiral pairs of non-Abelian Hall states, \
like the Pfaffian,\\nRead-Rezayi and NASS states, can be used to model \
two-dimensional time-reversal\\ninvariant topological insulators. Their \
stability was shown to be associated to\\nthe presence of a Z_2 anomaly and \
characterized by the same Z_2 index\\nintroduced for free fermion and Abelian \
systems. In this work, we continue the\\nstability analysis by providing the \
form of time-reversal invariant\\ninteractions that gap the non-Abelian edge \
excitations. Our approach is based\\non the description of non-Abelian states \
as projections of corresponding\\n\\\"parent\\\" Abelian states.\\n\""}]}, {
