                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Scattering amplitudes in maximally supersymmetric gauge \
theory receive a dual\\ndescription in terms of the expectation value of the \
super Wilson loop\\nstretched on a null polygonal contour. This makes the \
analysis amenable to\\nnonperturbative techniques. Presently, we elaborate on \
a refined form of the\\noperator product expansion in terms of pentagon \
transitions to compute\\ntwist-two contributions to NMHV amplitudes. To start \
with, we provide a novel\\nderivation of scattering matrices starting from \
Baxter equations for flux-tube\\nexcitations propagating on magnon \
background. We propose bootstrap equations\\nobeyed by pentagon form factors \
with nonsinglet quantum numbers with respected\\nto the R-symmetry group and \
provide solutions to them to all orders in 't Hooft\\ncoupling. These are \
then successfully confronted against available perturbative\\ncalculations \
for NMHV amplitudes to three-loop order.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
