            "  We compute the null cusp anomalous dimension of ABJM theory at \
strong\ncoupling up to two-loop order. This is done by evaluating corrections \
to the\ncorresponding superstring partition function, weighted by the \
$AdS_4\\times\n\\mathbb{CP}^3$ action in AdS light-cone gauge. We compare our \
result, where we\nuse an anomalous shift in the $AdS_4$ radius, with the cusp \
anomaly of\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM, and extract the two-loop contribution to \
the non-trivial\nintegrable coupling $h(\\lambda)$ of ABJM theory. It \
coincides with the strong\ncoupling expansion of the exact expression for $ \
h(\\lambda)$ recently\nconjectured by Gromov and Sizov. Our work provides \
thus a non-trivial\nperturbative check for the latter, as well as evidence \
for two-loop\nUV-finiteness and quantum integrability of the Type IIA \
$AdS_4\\times\n\\mathbb{CP}^3$ superstring in this gauge.\n", 
