 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the methods of the recently proposed Quantum \
Spectral Curve (QSC)\\noriginating from integrability of ${\\\\cal N}=4$ \
Super--Yang-Mills theory we\\nanalytically continue the scaling dimensions of \
twist-2 operators and reproduce\\nthe so-called pomeron eigenvalue of the \
Balitsky-Fadin-Kuraev-Lipatov (BFKL)\\nequation. Furthermore, we recovered \
the Faddeev-Korchemsky Baxter equation for\\nLipatov's spin chain and also \
found its generalization for the next-to-leading\\norder in the BFKL scaling. \
Our results provide a non-trivial test of QSC\\ndescribing the exact spectrum \
in planar ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM at infinitely many\\nloops for a highly \
nontrivial non-BPS quantity and also opens a way for a\\nsystematic expansion \
in the BFKL regime.\\n\""}]}, {
