                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Describing the bosonic AdS_3 x S^3 particle and string \
in SU(1,1) x SU(2)\\ngroup variables, we provide a Hamiltonian treatment of \
the isometry group\\norbits of solutions via analysis of the pre-symplectic \
form. For the particle\\nwe obtain a one-parameter family of orbits \
parameterized by\\ncreation-annihilation variables, which leads to the \
Holstein-Primakoff\\nrealization of the isometry group generators. The scheme \
is then applied to\\nspinning string solutions characterized by one winding \
number in AdS_3 and two\\nwinding numbers in S^3. We find a two-parameter \
family of orbits, where\\nquantization again provides the Holstein-Primakoff \
realization of the symmetry\\ngenerators with an oscillator type energy \
spectrum. Analyzing the minimal\\nenergy at strong coupling we verify the \
spectrum of short strings at special\\nvalues of winding numbers.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
