 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Inspired by recent results in the context of AdS/CFT \
integrability, we\\nreconsider the Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz equations \
describing the 1D fermionic\\nHubbard model at finite temperature. We prove \
that the infinite set of TBA\\nequations are equivalent to a simple nonlinear \
Riemann-Hilbert problem for a\\nfinite number of unknown functions. The \
latter can be transformed into a set of\\nthree coupled nonlinear integral \
equations defined over a finite support, which\\ncan be easily solved \
numerically. We discuss the emergence of an exact Bethe\\nAnsatz and the link \
between the TBA approach and the results by \
J\\\\\\\"uttner,\\nKl\\\\\\\"umper and Suzuki based on the Quantum Transfer \
Matrix method. We also\\ncomment on the analytic continuation mechanism \
leading to excited states and on\\nthe mirror equations describing the \
finite-size Hubbard model with twisted\\nboundary conditions.\\n\""}]}, {
