               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1502.03976\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Omar El Deeb\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Omar El Deeb\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lee-Yang Model in Presence of Defects\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PhD Thesis 122 pages, 42 figure, 6 tables Note: ABF \
Lattice model\\n  based on arXiv:hep-th/0012223 by Paul A. Pearce, Leung \
Chim, Changrim Ahn\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  I choose the Lee-Yang model and go through different \
approaches to analyze it\\nusing the form factor approach and the bootstrap \
program, the lattice\\ndescription and the lattice TBA equations for a full \
understanding of the\\nmodel.\\n  The bootstrap program aims to explicitly \
solve 1+1 dimensional integrable\\nquantum field theories. In the first step, \
called the S-matrix bootstrap, the\\nscattering matrix, is determined from \
its properties. In developing a defect\\nform factor program the first step \
is the T-matrix bootstrap. Interacting\\nintegrable defect theories are \
purely transmitting and topological. We analyze\\nboth operators localized in \
the bulk and also on the defect. By finding their\\nsolutions, the spectral \
representation of any correlator can be determined.\\n  Next we consider the \
model on the lattice. The lattice approach allows to\\nobtain both massive \
and massless excited TBA equations by studying the\\ncontinuum scaling limit \
of the associated integrable lattice models. The most\\nimportant input from \
the lattice approach is an insight into the analytic\\nstructure of the \
excited state solutions of the TBA equations. Previously this\\nstructure had \
to be guessed. In this thesis we turn our attention to the\\nsimplest example \
of a non-unitary minimal theory, namely, the Lee-Yang minimal\\nmodel M(2,5). \
We study the Lee-Yang model on the lattice. We analyze the\\nperiodic, \
boundary and the seam cases in both massive and massless regimes. We\\nderive \
their ground state TBA equations and analyze the flows between \
different\\nboundary and defect conditions.\\n  Finally, in the large volume \
limit, we calculate the L\\\\\\\"uscher correction\\nterms of the TBA energy \
of a one-particle state. We display those ideas in the\\nend of the thesis as \
this is an important direction of work in string theory,\\nparticularly in \
the AdS/CFT correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 13 Feb 2015 13:07:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 16 Feb 2015 16:28:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-02-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Deeb\"", ",", "\"Omar El\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
