 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study integrable models in the context of the \
recently discovered\\nGauge/YBE correspondence, where the Yang-Baxter \
equation is promoted to a\\nduality between two supersymmetric gauge \
theories. We study flavored elliptic\\ngenus of 2d $\\\\mathcal{N}=(2,2)$ \
quiver gauge theories, which theories are\\ndefined from statistical lattices \
regarded as quiver diagrams. Our R-matrices\\nare written in terms of theta \
functions, and simplifies considerably when the\\ngauge groups at the quiver \
nodes are Abelian. We also discuss the modularity\\nproperties of the \
R-matrix, reduction of 2d index to 1d Witten index, and\\nstring theory \
realizations of our theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
