 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We developed an efficient numerical algorithm for \
computing the spectrum of\\nanomalous dimensions of the planar ${\\\\cal \
N}=4$ Super-Yang--Mills at finite\\ncoupling. The method is based on the \
Quantum Spectral Curve formalism. In\\ncontrast to Thermodynamic Bethe \
Ansatz, worked out only for some very special\\noperators, this method is \
applicable for generic states/operators and is much\\nfaster and precise due \
to its Q-quadratic convergence rate.\\n  To demonstrate the method we \
evaluate the dimensions $\\\\Delta$ of twist\\noperators in $sl(2)$ sector \
directly for any value of the spin $S$ including\\nnon-integer values. In \
particular, we compute the BFKL pomeron intercept in a\\nwide range of the 't \
Hooft coupling constant with up to $20$ significant\\nfigures precision, \
confirming two previously known from the perturbation theory\\norders and \
giving prediction for several new coefficients. Furthermore, we\\nexplore \
numerically a rich branch cut structure for complexified spin $S$.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
