                  "\"  We derive the first $\\\\epsilon_2$-correction to the \
instanton partition\\nfunctions of $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ Super Yang-Mills (SYM) \
in four dimensions in the\\nNekrasov-Shatashvili limit \
$\\\\epsilon_2\\\\rightarrow 0$. In the latter we recall\\nthe emergence of \
the famous Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz-like equation which has\\nbeen found by \
Mayer expansion techniques. Here we combine efficiently these to\\nfield \
theory arguments. In a nutshell, we find natural and resolutive \
the\\nintroduction of a new operator $\\\\nabla$ that distinguishes the \
singularities\\nwithin and outside the integration contour of the partition \
function.\\n\""}]}, {
