            "  We revisit the strong coupling limit of the cusp anomalous \
dimension in\nplanar N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. It is known that the strong \
coupling\nexpansion is asymptotic and non-Borel summable. As a consequence, \
the cusp\nanomalous dimension receives non-perturbative corrections, and the \
complete\nstrong coupling expansion should be a resurgent transseries. We \
reveal that the\nperturbative and non-perturbative parts in the transseries \
are closely\ninterrelated. Solving the Beisert-Eden-Staudacher equation \
systematically, we\nanalyze in detail the large order behavior in the strong \
coupling perturbative\nexpansion and show that the non-perturbative \
information is indeed encoded\nthere. An ambiguity of (lateral) Borel \
resummations of the perturbative\nexpansion is precisely canceled by the \
contributions from the non-perturbative\nsectors,\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
