, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We consider scalar Wilson operators of ${\\\\cal N}=4$ \
SYM at high spin, $s$,\\nand generic twist in the multi-color limit. We show \
that the corresponding\\n(non)linear integral equations (originating from the \
asymptotic Bethe Ansatz\\nequations) respect certain 'reciprocity' and \
functional 'self-tuning' relations\\nup to all terms $\\\\frac{1}{s(\\\\ln \
s)^n}$ (inclusive) at any fixed 't Hooft\\ncoupling $\\\\lambda$. Of course, \
this relation entails straightforwardly the\\nwell-known (homonymous) \
relations for the anomalous dimension at the same order\\nin $s$. On this \
basis we give some evidence that wrapping corrections should\\nenter the \
non-linear integral equation and anomalous dimension expansions at\\nthe next \
order $\\\\frac{(\\\\ln s)^{2}}{s^2}$, at fixed 't Hooft coupling, in such \
a\\nway to re-establish the aforementioned relation (which fails \
otherwise).\\n\""}]}, {
