 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We address the near-collinear expansion of NMHV \
six-particle scattering\\namplitudes at strong value of 't Hooft coupling in \
planar maximally\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory. We complement recent \
studies of this\\nobservable within the context of the Pentagon Operator \
Product Expansion, via\\nthe dual superWilson loop description, by studying \
effects of multiple scalar\\nexchanges that accompany (or not) massive \
flux-tube excitations. Due to the\\nfact that holes have a very small, \
nonperturbatively generated mass which is\\nexponentially suppressed in 't \
Hooft coupling, their exchanges must be resummed\\nin the ultraviolet limit. \
This procedure yields a contribution to the\\nexpectation value of the \
superloop which enters on equal footing with the\\nclassical area, --- a \
phenomenon which was earlier observed for MHV amplitudes.\\nIn all \
components, the near-massless scalar exchanges factorize from the ones\\nof \
massive particles, at leading order in strong coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
