            "  In the context of 4D/2D dualities, SH$^c$ algebra, introduced \
by Schiffmann\nand Vasserot, provides a systematic method to analyse the \
instanton partition\nfunctions of $\\mathcal{N}=2$ supersymmetric gauge \
theories. In this paper, we\nrewrite the SH$^c$ algebra in terms of three \
holomorphic fields $D_0(z)$,\n$D_{\\pm1}(z)$ with which the algebra and its \
epresentations are simplified. The\ninstanton partition functions for \
arbitrary $\\mathcal{N}=2$ super Yang-Mills\ntheories with $A_n$ and \
$A^{(1)}_n$ type quiver diagrams are compactly\nexpressed as a product of \
four building blocks: Gaiotto state, dilatation,\nflavor vertex operator and \
intertwiner which are written in terms of SH$^c$ and\nthe orthogonal basis \
introduced by Alba, Fateev, Litvinov and Tarnopolskiy.\nThese building blocks \
are characterized by new conditions which generalize the\nknown ones on the \
Gaiotto state and the Carlsson-Okounkov vertex. Consistency\nconditions of \
the inner product give algebraic relations for the chiral ring\ngenerating \
functions defined by Nekrasov, Pestun and Shatashvili. In particular\nwe show \
the polynomiality of the qq-characters which have been introduced as a\n\
deformation of the Yangian characters. These relations define a second\n\
quantization of the Seiberg-Witten geometry, and, accordingly, reduce to a\n\
Baxter TQ-equation in the Nekrasov-Shatashvili limit of the Omega-background.\
\n", "versions" -> {{
