               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1604.01676\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Lorenzo Bianchi\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Lorenzo Bianchi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Perturbation theory for string sigma models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"198 pages. Based on the author's PhD thesis and on the \
publications\\n  arXiv:1304.1798, arXiv:1401.0448, arXiv:1405.7947, \
arXiv:1407.4788,\\n  arXiv:1505.00783\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this thesis we investigate quantum aspects of the \
Green-Schwarz\\nsuperstring in various AdS backgrounds relevant for the \
AdS/CFT correspondence,\\nproviding several examples of perturbative \
computations in the corresponding\\nintegrable sigma-models. We start by \
reviewing in details the supercoset\\nconstruction of the superstring action \
in $AdS_5 \\\\times S^5$, pointing out the\\nlimits of this procedure for \
$AdS_4$ and $AdS_3$ backgrounds. For the $AdS_4\\n\\\\times CP^3$ case we \
give a thorough derivation of an alternative action, based\\non the \
double-dimensional reduction of eleven-dimensional super-membranes. We\\nthen \
consider the expansion about the BMN vacuum and the S-matrix for \
the\\nscattering of worldsheet excitations in the decompactification limit. \
To\\nevaluate its elements efficiently we describe a unitarity-based \
method\\nresulting in a very compact formula yielding the cut-constructible \
part of any\\none-loop two-dimensional S-matrix. In the second part of this \
review we analyze\\nthe superstring action on $AdS_4 \\\\times CP^3$ expanded \
around the null cusp\\nvacuum. The free energy of this model, whose \
computation we reproduce up to\\ntwo-loops at strong coupling, is related to \
the cusp anomalous dimension of the\\nABJM theory and, indirectly, to a \
non-trivial effective coupling $h(\\\\lambda)$\\nfeaturing all \
integrability-based calculations in $AdS_4/CFT_3$. Finally, we\\nextensively \
discuss the comparison of the perturbative results and the\\nintegrability \
predictions for the one-loop dispersion relation of GKP\\nexcitations. Our \
results provide valuable data in support of the quantum\\nconsistency of the \
string actions - often debated due to possible issues with\\ncancellation of \
UV divergences and the lack of manifest power-counting\\nrenormalizability - \
and furnish non-trivial stringent tests for the quantum\\nintegrability of \
the analyzed models.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
