                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper, we solved numerically the Quantum \
Spectral Curve (QSC)\\nequations corresponding to some twist-2 single trace \
operators with even spin\\nfrom the $sl(2)$ sector of $AdS_5/CFT_4$ \
correspondence. We describe all\\ntechnical details of the numerical method \
which are necessary to implement it\\nin C++ language.\\n  In the $S=2,4,6,8$ \
cases, our numerical results confirm the analytical\\nresults, known in the \
literature for the first 4 coefficients of the strong\\ncoupling expansion \
for the anomalous dimensions of twist-2 operators. In the\\ncase of the \
Konishi operator, due to the high precision of the numerical data\\nwe could \
give numerical predictions to the values of two further coefficients,\\nas \
well.\\n  The strong coupling behaviour of the coefficients $c_{a,n}$ in the \
power\\nseries representation of the ${\\\\bf P}_{\\\\!a}$-functions is also \
investigated.\\nBased on our numerical data, in the regime, where the index \
of the coefficients\\nis much smaller than $\\\\lambda^{1/4}$, we conjecture \
that the coefficients have\\npolynomial index dependence at strong coupling. \
This allows one to propose a\\nstrong coupling series representation for the \
${\\\\bf P}$-functions being valid\\nfar enough from the real short cut. In \
the paper the qualitative strong\\ncoupling behaviour of the ${\\\\bf \
P}$-functions at the branch points is also\\ndiscussed.\\n\""}]}, {
