           "id" -> "1604.02346", "submitter" -> "Arpad Hegedus", "authors" -> 
            "Arpad Hegedus, Jozsef Konczer", "title" -> 
            "Strong coupling results from the numerical solution of the \
quantum\n  spectral curve", "comments" -> 
            "72 pages, 9 figures, 5 ancillary files", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2016)061", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper, we solved numerically the Quantum Spectral \
Curve (QSC)\nequations corresponding to some twist-2 single trace operators \
with even spin\nfrom the $sl(2)$ sector of $AdS_5/CFT_4$ correspondence. We \
describe all\ntechnical details of the numerical method which are necessary \
to implement it\nin C++ language.\n  In the $S=2,4,6,8$ cases, our numerical \
results confirm the analytical\nresults, known in the literature for the \
first 4 coefficients of the strong\ncoupling expansion for the anomalous \
dimensions of twist-2 operators. In the\ncase of the Konishi operator, due to \
the high precision of the numerical data\nwe could give numerical predictions \
to the values of two further coefficients,\nas well.\n  The strong coupling \
behaviour of the coefficients $c_{a,n}$ in the power\nseries representation \
of the ${\\bf P}_{\\!a}$-functions is also investigated.\nBased on our \
numerical data, in the regime, where the index of the coefficients\nis much \
smaller than $\\lambda^{1/4}$, we conjecture that the coefficients have\n\
polynomial index dependence at strong coupling. This allows one to propose a\n\
strong coupling series representation for the ${\\bf P}$-functions being \
valid\nfar enough from the real short cut. In the paper the qualitative \
strong\ncoupling behaviour of the ${\\bf P}$-functions at the branch points \
is also\ndiscussed.\n", 
