            "  We develop analytical methods for computing the structure \
constant for three\nheavy operators, starting from the recently proposed \
hexagon approach. Such a\nstructure constant is a semiclassical object, with \
the scale set by the inverse\nlength of the operators playing the role of the \
Planck constant. We reformulate\nthe hexagon expansion in terms of multiple \
contour integrals and recast it as a\nsum over clusters generated by the \
residues of the measure of integration. We\ntest the method on two examples. \
First, we compute the asymptotic three-point\nfunction of heavy fields at any \
coupling and show the result in the\nsemiclassical limit matches both the \
string theory computation at strong\ncoupling and the tree-level results \
obtained before. Second, in the case of one\nnon-BPS and two BPS operators at \
strong coupling we sum up all wrapping\ncorrections associated with the \
opposite bridge to the non-trivial operator, or\nthe \"bottom\" mirror \
channel. We also give an alternative interpretation of the\nresults in terms \
of a gas of fermions and show that they can be expressed\ncompactly as an \
operator-valued super-determinant.\n", 
