            "  We consider possible discretizations for a gauge-fixed \
Green-Schwarz action\nof Type IIB superstring. We use them for measuring the \
action, from which we\nextract the cusp anomalous dimension of planar \
$\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM as derived\nfrom AdS/CFT, as well as the mass of the two \
$AdS$ excitations transverse to\nthe relevant null cusp classical string \
solution. We perform lattice\nsimulations employing a Rational Hybrid Monte \
Carlo (RHMC) algorithm and two\nWilson-like fermion discretizations, one of \
which preserves the global $SO(6)$\nsymmetry of the model. We compare our \
results with the expected behavior at\nvarious values of \
$g=\\frac{\\sqrt{\\lambda}}{4\\pi}$. For both the observables, we\nfind a \
good agreement for large $g$, which is the perturbative regime of the\n\
sigma-model. For smaller values of $g$, the expectation value of the action\n\
exhibits a deviation compatible with the presence of quadratic divergences.\n\
After their non-perturbative subtraction the continuum limit can be taken, \
and\nsuggests a qualitative agreement with the non-perturbative expectation \
from\nAdS/CFT. Furthermore, we detect a phase in the fermion determinant, \
whose\norigin we explain, that for very small $g$ leads to a sign problem not\
\ntreatable via standard reweigthing. The continuum extrapolations of the\n\
observables in the two different discretizations agree within errors, which \
is\nstrongly suggesting that they lead to the same continuum limit. Part of \
the\nresults discussed here were presented earlier in arXiv:1601.04670.\n", 
