                 "\"Andrea Cavagli\\\\`a, Nikolay Gromov, Fedor \
Levkovich-Maslyuk\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the Exact Interpolating Function in ABJ Theory\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"13 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP12(2016)086\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Based on the recent indications of integrability in the \
planar ABJ model, we\\nconjecture an exact expression for the interpolating \
function\\nh(\\\\lambda_1,\\\\lambda_2) in this theory. Our conjecture is \
based on the\\nobservation that the integrability structure of the ABJM \
theory given by its\\nQuantum Spectral Curve is very rigid and does not allow \
for a simple consistent\\nmodification. Under this assumption, we revised the \
previous comparison of\\nlocalization results and exact all loop \
integrability calculations done for the\\nABJM theory by one of the authors \
and Grigory Sizov, fixing\\nh(\\\\lambda_1,\\\\lambda_2). We checked our \
conjecture against various weak coupling\\nexpansions, at strong coupling and \
also demonstrated its invariance under the\\nSeiberg-like duality. This match \
also gives further support to the\\nintegrability of the model. If our \
conjecture is correct, it extends all the\\navailable integrability results \
in the ABJM model to the ABJ model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
