         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1605.04888", "submitter" -> "Fedor Levkovich-Maslyuk", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Andrea Cavagli\\`a, Nikolay Gromov, Fedor Levkovich-Maslyuk", 
            "title" -> "On the Exact Interpolating Function in ABJ Theory", 
            "comments" -> "13 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP12(2016)086", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Based on the recent indications of integrability in the planar \
ABJ model, we\nconjecture an exact expression for the interpolating function\n\
h(\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2) in this theory. Our conjecture is based on the\n\
observation that the integrability structure of the ABJM theory given by its\n\
Quantum Spectral Curve is very rigid and does not allow for a simple \
consistent\nmodification. Under this assumption, we revised the previous \
comparison of\nlocalization results and exact all loop integrability \
calculations done for the\nABJM theory by one of the authors and Grigory \
Sizov, fixing\nh(\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2). We checked our conjecture against \
various weak coupling\nexpansions, at strong coupling and also demonstrated \
its invariance under the\nSeiberg-like duality. This match also gives further \
support to the\nintegrability of the model. If our conjecture is correct, it \
extends all the\navailable integrability results in the ABJM model to the ABJ \
model.\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 16 May 2016 19:50:22 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-02-01", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Cavagli\[AGrave]", "Andrea", ""}, {
              "Gromov", "Nikolay", ""}, {"Levkovich-Maslyuk", "Fedor", ""}}}],
