                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Operator Product Expansion for null polygonal \
Wilson loop in planar\\nmaximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory runs \
systematically in terms of\\nmultiparticle pentagon transitions which encode \
the physics of excitations\\npropagating on the color flux tube ending on the \
sides of the four-dimensional\\ncontour. Their dynamics was unravelled in the \
past several years and culminated\\nin a complete description of pentagons as \
an exact function of the 't Hooft\\ncoupling. In this paper we provide a \
solution for the last building block in\\nthis program, the SU(4) matrix \
structure arising from internal symmetry indices\\nof scalars and fermions. \
This is achieved by a recursive solution of the Mirror\\nand Watson equations \
obeyed by the so-called singlet pentagons and fixing the\\nform of the \
twisted component in their tensor decomposition. The non-singlet,\\nor \
charged, pentagons are deduced from these by a limiting procedure.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
