                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 94, 066008 (2016)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.94.066008\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DMUS-MP-16/17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the recently discovered q-deformed Poincare' \
supersymmetry of the\\nAdS_3/CFT_2 integrable massless scattering, and \
demonstrate how the S-matrix is\\ninvariant under boosts. The boost generator \
has a non-local coproduct, which\\nacts on the scattering matrix as a \
differential operator, annihilating it. We\\npropose to reinterpret the boost \
action in terms of covariant derivatives on\\nbundles, and derive an \
expression for the S-matrix as the path-ordered\\nexponential of a flat \
connection. We provide a list of possible alternative\\ninterpretations of \
this emergent geometric picture, including a one-dimensional\\nauxiliary \
Schroedinger problem. We support our claims by performing a\\nsimplified \
algebraic Bethe ansatz, which bears some resemblance \
to\\nantiferromagnets.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
