                 "\"Gleb Arutyunov, Daniele Dorigoni and Sergei Savin\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Resurgence of the dressing phase for ${\\\\rm \
AdS}_5\\\\times {\\\\rm S}^5$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"53 pages, 5 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2017)055\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the resummation of the strong coupling \
asymptotic expansion of the\\ndressing phase of the ${\\\\rm AdS}_5\\\\times \
{\\\\rm S}^5$ superstring. The dressing\\nphase proposed by Beisert, Eden and \
Staudacher can be recovered from a modified\\nBorel-Ecalle resummation of \
this asymptotic expansion only by completing it\\nwith new, non-perturbative \
and exponentially suppressed terms that can be\\norganized into different \
sectors labelled by an instanton-like number. We\\ncompute the contribution \
to the dressing phase coming from the sum over all the\\ninstanton sectors \
and show that it satisfies the homogeneous crossing symmetry\\nequation. We \
comment on the semiclassical origin of the non-perturbative terms\\nfrom the \
world-sheet theory point of view even though their precise \
explanation\\nremains still quite mysterious.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
