           "id" -> "1608.03797", "submitter" -> "Daniele Dorigoni Dr", 
            "authors" -> "Gleb Arutyunov, Daniele Dorigoni and Sergei Savin", 
            "title" -> 
            "Resurgence of the dressing phase for ${\\rm AdS}_5\\times {\\rm \
S}^5$", "comments" -> "53 pages, 5 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP01(2017)055", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss the resummation of the strong coupling asymptotic \
expansion of the\ndressing phase of the ${\\rm AdS}_5\\times {\\rm S}^5$ \
superstring. The dressing\nphase proposed by Beisert, Eden and Staudacher can \
be recovered from a modified\nBorel-Ecalle resummation of this asymptotic \
expansion only by completing it\nwith new, non-perturbative and exponentially \
suppressed terms that can be\norganized into different sectors labelled by an \
instanton-like number. We\ncompute the contribution to the dressing phase \
coming from the sum over all the\ninstanton sectors and show that it \
satisfies the homogeneous crossing symmetry\nequation. We comment on the \
semiclassical origin of the non-perturbative terms\nfrom the world-sheet \
theory point of view even though their precise explanation\nremains still \
quite mysterious.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 12 Aug 2016 14:07:30 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-02-01", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Arutyunov", "Gleb", ""}, {
              "Dorigoni", "Daniele", ""}, {"Savin", "Sergei", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
