            "authors" -> "F.A. Smirnov, A.B. Zamolodchikov", "title" -> 
            "On space of integrable quantum field theories", "comments" -> 
            "25 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2016.12.014", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study deformations of 2D Integrable Quantum Field Theories \
(IQFT) which\npreserve integrability (the existence of infinitely many local \
integrals of\nmotion). The IQFT are understood as \"effective field \
theories\", with finite\nultraviolet cutoff. We show that for any such IQFT \
there are infinitely many\nintegrable deformations generated by scalar local \
fields $X_s$, which are in\none-to-one correspondence with the local \
integrals of motion; moreover, the\nscalars $X_s$ are built from the \
components of the associated conserved\ncurrents in a universal way. The \
first of these scalars, $X_1$, coincides with\nthe composite field $(T{\\bar \
T})$ built from the components of the\nenergy-momentum tensor. The \
deformations of quantum field theories generated by\n$X_1$ are \"solvable\" \
in a certain sense, even if the original theory is not\nintegrable. In a \
massive IQFT the deformations $X_s$ are identified with the\ndeformations of \
the corresponding factorizable S-matrix via the CDD factor. The\nsituation is \
illustrated by explicit construction of the form factors of the\noperators \
$X_s$ in sine-Gordon theory. We also make some remarks on the problem\nof UV \
completeness of such integrable deformations.\n", 
