               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marco Baggio, Olof Ohlsson Sax, Alessandro Sfondrini, \
Bogdan Stefanski\\n  and Alessandro Torrielli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Protected string spectrum in AdS3/CFT2 from worldsheet \
integrability\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"37 pages; v2: 40 pages, discussion of wrapping effects \
added (section\\n  8), as accepted by JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2017)091\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"NORDITA-2017-5, DMUS-MP-17/01\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the protected closed-string spectra of \
AdS3/CFT2 dual pairs with 16\\nsupercharges at arbitrary values of the string \
tension and of the three-form\\nfluxes. These follow immediately from the \
all-loop Bethe equations for the\\nspectra of the integrable worldsheet \
theories. Further, representing the\\nunderlying integrable systems as spin \
chains, we find that their dynamics\\ninvolves length-changing interactions \
and that protected states correspond to\\ngapless excitations above the \
Berenstein-Maldacena-Nastase vacuum. In the case\\nof AdS3 x S3 x T4 the \
degeneracies of such operators precisely match those of\\nthe dual CFT2 and \
the supergravity spectrum. On the other hand, we find that\\nfor AdS3 x S3 x \
S3 x S1 there are fewer protected states than previous\\nsupergravity \
calculations had suggested. In particular, protected states have\\nthe same \
su(2) charge with respect to the two three-spheres.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
