            "  We derive the protected closed-string spectra of AdS3/CFT2 \
dual pairs with 16\nsupercharges at arbitrary values of the string tension \
and of the three-form\nfluxes. These follow immediately from the all-loop \
Bethe equations for the\nspectra of the integrable worldsheet theories. \
Further, representing the\nunderlying integrable systems as spin chains, we \
find that their dynamics\ninvolves length-changing interactions and that \
protected states correspond to\ngapless excitations above the \
Berenstein-Maldacena-Nastase vacuum. In the case\nof AdS3 x S3 x T4 the \
degeneracies of such operators precisely match those of\nthe dual CFT2 and \
the supergravity spectrum. On the other hand, we find that\nfor AdS3 x S3 x \
S3 x S1 there are fewer protected states than previous\nsupergravity \
calculations had suggested. In particular, protected states have\nthe same \
su(2) charge with respect to the two three-spheres.\n", 
