            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1701.08914\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Belitsky\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A.V. Belitsky\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Twisting perturbed parafermions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"16 pages, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2017.04.038\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The near-collinear expansion of scattering amplitudes \
in maximally\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory at strong coupling is \
governed by the dynamics\\nof stings propagating on the five sphere. The \
pentagon transitions in the\\noperator product expansion which systematize \
the series get reformulated in\\nterms of matrix elements of branch-point \
twist operators in the two-dimensional\\nO(6) nonlinear sigma model. The \
facts that the latter is an asymptotically free\\nfield theory and that there \
exists no local realization of twist fields\\nprevents one from explicit \
calculation of their scaling dimensions and operator\\nproduct expansion \
coefficients. This complication is bypassed making use of the\\nequivalence \
of the sigma model to the infinite-level limit of WZNW models\\nperturbed by \
current-current interactions, such that one can use conformal\\nsymmetry and \
conformal perturbation theory for systematic calculations.\\nPresently, to \
set up the formalism, we consider the O(3) sigma model which \
is\\nreformulated as perturbed parafermions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 31 Jan 2017 04:44:43 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2017-04-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Belitsky\"", ",", "\"A. V.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
