           "id" -> "1701.08914", "submitter" -> "Andrei Belitsky", "authors" -> 
            "A.V. Belitsky", "title" -> "Twisting perturbed parafermions", 
            "comments" -> "16 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physletb.2017.04.038", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The near-collinear expansion of scattering amplitudes in \
maximally\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory at strong coupling is governed by \
the dynamics\nof stings propagating on the five sphere. The pentagon \
transitions in the\noperator product expansion which systematize the series \
get reformulated in\nterms of matrix elements of branch-point twist operators \
in the two-dimensional\nO(6) nonlinear sigma model. The facts that the latter \
is an asymptotically free\nfield theory and that there exists no local \
realization of twist fields\nprevents one from explicit calculation of their \
scaling dimensions and operator\nproduct expansion coefficients. This \
complication is bypassed making use of the\nequivalence of the sigma model to \
the infinite-level limit of WZNW models\nperturbed by current-current \
interactions, such that one can use conformal\nsymmetry and conformal \
perturbation theory for systematic calculations.\nPresently, to set up the \
formalism, we consider the O(3) sigma model which is\nreformulated as \
perturbed parafermions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
