                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Continuous symmetries of the Hirota difference \
equation, commuting with\\nshifts of independent variables, are derived by \
means of the dressing\\nprocedure. Action of these symmetries on the \
dependent variables of the\\nequation is presented. Commutativity of these \
symmetries enables interpretation\\nof their parameters as \\\"times\\\" of \
the nonlinear integrable partial\\ndifferential-difference and differential \
equations. Examples of equations\\nresulting in such procedure and their Lax \
pairs are given. Besides these,\\nordinary, symmetries the additional ones \
are introduced and their action on the\\nScattering data is \
presented.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
