                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Twist fields emerge in a number of physical \
applications ranging from\\nentanglement entropy to scattering amplitudes in \
four-dimensional gauge\\ntheories. In this work, their vacuum expectation \
values are studied in the path\\nintegral framework. By performing a gauge \
transformation, their correlation\\nfunctions are reduced to field theory of \
matter fields in external\\nAharonov-Bohm vortices. The resulting functional \
determinants are then analyzed\\nwithin the zeta function regularization for \
the spectrum of Bessel zeros and\\nconcise formulas are derived.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
