           "id" -> "1705.00319", "submitter" -> "Arpad Hegedus", "authors" -> 
            "Arpad Hegedus", "title" -> 
            "Lattice approach to finite volume form-factors of the Massive\n  \
Thirring/Sine-Gordon model", "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP08(2017)059", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we demonstrate, that the light-cone lattice \
approach for the\nMassive-Thirring (sine-Gordon) model, through the quantum \
inverse scattering\nmethod, admits an appropriate framework for computing the \
finite volume\nform-factors of local operators of the model. In this work we \
compute the\nfinite volume diagonal matrix elements of the $U(1)$ conserved \
current in the\npure soliton sector of the theory. Based on the systematic \
large volume\nexpansion of our results, we conjecture an exact expression for \
the finite\nvolume expectation values of local operators in pure soliton \
states. At large\nvolume in leading order these expectation values have the \
same form as in\npurely elastic scattering theories, but exponentially small \
corrections differ\nfrom previous Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz conjectures of \
purely elastic\nscattering theories.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 30 Apr 2017 14:25:43 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-09-13", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Hegedus", "Arpad", ""}}}], 
