          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1705.03898\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marius de Leeuw\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marius de Leeuw, Asger C. Ipsen, Charlotte Kristjansen, \
Kasper E.\\n  Vardinghus and Matthias Wilhelm\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Two-point functions in AdS/dCFT and the boundary \
conformal bootstrap\\n  equations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"34 pages, 2 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 08 (2017) 020\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2017)020\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate the leading contributions to the connected \
two-point functions\\nof protected scalar operators in the defect version of \
N=4 SYM theory which is\\ndual to the D5-D3 probe-brane system with k units \
of background gauge field\\nflux. This involves several types of two-point \
functions which are vanishing in\\nthe theory without the defect, such as \
two-point functions of operators of\\nunequal conformal dimension. We \
furthermore exploit the operator product\\nexpansion (OPE) and the boundary \
operator expansion (BOE), which form the basis\\nof the boundary conformal \
bootstrap equations, to extract conformal data both\\nabout the defect CFT \
and about N=4 SYM theory without the defect. From the\\nknowledge of the one- \
and two-point functions of the defect theory, we extract\\ncertain structure \
constants of N=4 SYM theory using the (bulk) OPE and\\nconstrain certain \
bulk-bulk-to-boundary couplings using the BOE. The extraction\\nof the former \
relies on a non-trivial, polynomial k dependence of the \
one-point\\nfunctions, which we explicitly demonstrate. In addition, it \
requires the\\nknowledge of the one-point functions of SU$(2)$ descendant \
operators, which we\\nlikewise explicitly determine.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 10 May 2017 18:00:30 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2022-08-24\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"de Leeuw\"", ",", "\"Marius\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Ipsen\"", ",", "\"Asger C.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Kristjansen\"", ",", "\"Charlotte\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Vardinghus\"", ",", "\"Kasper E.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Wilhelm\"", ",", "\"Matthias\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
