E.\n  Vardinghus and Matthias Wilhelm", "title" -> 
            "Two-point functions in AdS/dCFT and the boundary conformal \
bootstrap\n  equations", "comments" -> "34 pages, 2 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 08 (2017) 020", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2017)020", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate the leading contributions to the connected \
two-point functions\nof protected scalar operators in the defect version of \
N=4 SYM theory which is\ndual to the D5-D3 probe-brane system with k units of \
background gauge field\nflux. This involves several types of two-point \
functions which are vanishing in\nthe theory without the defect, such as \
two-point functions of operators of\nunequal conformal dimension. We \
furthermore exploit the operator product\nexpansion (OPE) and the boundary \
operator expansion (BOE), which form the basis\nof the boundary conformal \
bootstrap equations, to extract conformal data both\nabout the defect CFT and \
about N=4 SYM theory without the defect. From the\nknowledge of the one- and \
two-point functions of the defect theory, we extract\ncertain structure \
constants of N=4 SYM theory using the (bulk) OPE and\nconstrain certain \
bulk-bulk-to-boundary couplings using the BOE. The extraction\nof the former \
relies on a non-trivial, polynomial k dependence of the one-point\nfunctions, \
which we explicitly demonstrate. In addition, it requires the\nknowledge of \
the one-point functions of SU$(2)$ descendant operators, which we\nlikewise \
explicitly determine.\n", 
