                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present the three-loop calculation of the \
Bremsstrahlung function\\nassociated to the 1/2-BPS cusp in ABJM theory, \
including color subleading\\ncorrections. Using the BPS condition we reduce \
the computation to that of a\\ncusp with vanishing angle. We work within the \
framework of heavy quark\\neffective theory (HQET) that further simplifies \
the analytic evaluation of the\\nrelevant cusp anomalous dimension in the \
near-BPS limit. The result passes\\nnontrivial tests, such as exponentiation, \
and is in agreement with the\\nconjecture made in [1] for the exact \
expression of the Bremsstrahlung function,\\nbased on the relation with \
fermionic latitude Wilson loops.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
