 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Twist fields were introduced a few decades ago as a \
quantum counterpart to\\nclassical kink configurations and disorder variables \
in low dimensional field\\ntheories. In recent years they received a new \
incarnation within the framework\\nof geometric entropy and strong coupling \
limit of four-dimensional scattering\\namplitudes. In this paper, we study \
their two-point correlation functions in a\\nfree massless scalar theory, \
namely, twist--twist and twist--anti-twist\\ncorrelators. In spite of the \
simplicity of the model in question, the\\nproperties of the latter are far \
from being trivial. The problem is reduced,\\nwithin the formalism of the \
path integral, to the study of spectral\\ndeterminants on surfaces with \
conical points, which are then computed exactly\\nmaking use of the zeta \
function regularization. We also provide an insight into\\ntwist correlators \
for a massive complex scalar by means of the Lifshitz-Krein\\ntrace \
formula.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
