            "Spectral determinants for twist field correlators", "comments" -> 
            "21 pages, 2 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys. Rev. D 97, 086008 (2018)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.97.086008", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Twist fields were introduced a few decades ago as a quantum \
counterpart to\nclassical kink configurations and disorder variables in low \
dimensional field\ntheories. In recent years they received a new incarnation \
within the framework\nof geometric entropy and strong coupling limit of \
four-dimensional scattering\namplitudes. In this paper, we study their \
two-point correlation functions in a\nfree massless scalar theory, namely, \
twist--twist and twist--anti-twist\ncorrelators. In spite of the simplicity \
of the model in question, the\nproperties of the latter are far from being \
trivial. The problem is reduced,\nwithin the formalism of the path integral, \
to the study of spectral\ndeterminants on surfaces with conical points, which \
are then computed exactly\nmaking use of the zeta function regularization. We \
also provide an insight into\ntwist correlators for a massive complex scalar \
by means of the Lifshitz-Krein\ntrace formula.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
