 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explicitly calculate the $AdS_2 \\\\times S^2 \
\\\\times T^6$ transfer-matrix\\neigenvalues in the massless sector using the \
exact integrable S-matrix, for up\\nto 5 particles. This enables us to \
conjecture the general pattern. We use the\\nconjectured form of the \
eigenvalues to write down a set of massless Bethe\\nansatz equations. The \
same procedure applies to the relativistic as well as to\\nthe \
non-relativistic situation. In the relativistic case, the right and \
left\\nmodes decouple. We speculate that the relativistic massless Bethe \
ansatz we\\nobtain in that case might capture the integrable structure of an \
underlying 2D\\ncritical theory. We finally take advantage of some remarkable \
simplifications\\nto make progress in the massive case as well.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
