            "  We construct new families of 1/4 BPS Wilson loops in circular \
quiver\n$\\mathcal N=4$ superconformal Chern-Simons-matter (SCSM) theories in \
three\ndimensions. They are defined as the holonomy of superconnections that \
contain\nnon-trivial couplings to scalar and fermions, and cannot be reduced \
to\nblock-diagonal matrices. Consequently, the new operators cannot be \
written in\nterms of double-node Wilson loops, as the ones considered so far \
in the\nliterature. For particular values of the couplings the \
superconnection becomes\nblock-diagonal and we recover the known fermionic \
1/4 and 1/2 BPS Wilson loops.\nThe new operators are cohomologically \
equivalent to bosonic 1/4 BPS Wilson\nloops and are then amenable of exact \
evaluation via localization techniques.\nMoreover, in the case of orbifold \
ABJM theory we identify the corresponding\ngravity duals for some of the 1/4 \
and 1/2 BPS Wilson loops.\n", 
