                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Using an extension of the concept of twist field in \
QFT to space-time\\n(external) symmetries, we study conical twist fields in \
two-dimensional\\nintegrable QFT. These create conical singularities of \
arbitrary excess angle.\\nWe show that, upon appropriate identification \
between the excess angle and the\\nnumber of sheets, they have the same \
conformal dimension as branch-point twist\\nfields commonly used to represent \
partition functions on Riemann surfaces, and\\nthat both fields have closely \
related form factors. However, we show that\\nconical twist fields are truly \
different from branch-point twist fields. They\\ngenerate different operator \
product expansions (short distance expansions) and\\nform factor expansions \
(large distance expansions). In fact, we verify in free\\nfield theories, by \
re-summing form factors, that the conical twist fields\\noperator product \
expansions are correctly reproduced. We propose that conical\\ntwist fields \
are the correct fields in order to understand null polygonal\\nWilson \
loops/gluon scattering amplitudes of planar maximally \
supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills theory.\\n\""}]}, {
