            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1710.06567\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Belitsky\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A.V. Belitsky\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Resummed tree heptagon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"23 pages, 3 figures; typos fixed\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2018.01.031\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The form factor program for the regularized space-time \
S-matrix in planar\\nmaximally supersymmetric gauge theory, known as the \
pentagon operator product\\nexpansion, is formulated in terms of flux-tube \
excitations propagating on a\\ndual two-dimensional world-sheet, whose \
dynamics is known exactly as a function\\nof 't Hooft coupling. Both MHV and \
non-MHV amplitudes are described in a\\nuniform, systematic fashion within \
this framework, with the difference between\\nthe two encoded in \
coupling-dependent helicity form factors expressed via\\nZhukowski variables. \
The nontrivial SU(4) tensor structure of flux-tube\\ntransitions is coupling \
independent and is known for any number of charged\\nexcitations from \
solutions of a system of Watson and Mirror equations. This\\ndescription \
allows one to resum the infinite series of form factors and recover\\nthe \
space-time S-matrix exactly in kinematical variables at a given order \
of\\nperturbation series. Recently, this was done for the hexagon. Presently, \
we\\nsuccessfully perform resummation for the seven-leg tree NMHV amplitude. \
To this\\nend, we construct the flux-tube integrands of the fifteen \
independent Grassmann\\ncomponent of the heptagon with an infinite number of \
small fermion-antifermion\\npairs accounted for in NMHV two-channel conformal \
blocks.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
