Runov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bukhvostov-Lipatov model and quantum-classical \
duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"49 pages, 8 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2017.12.022\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Bukhvostov-Lipatov model is an exactly soluble \
model of two interacting\\nDirac fermions in 1+1 dimensions. The model \
describes weakly interacting\\ninstantons and anti-instantons in the $O(3)$ \
non-linear sigma model. In our\\nprevious work [arXiv:1607.04839] we have \
proposed an exact formula for the\\nvacuum energy of the Bukhvostov-Lipatov \
model in terms of special solutions of\\nthe classical sinh-Gordon equation, \
which can be viewed as an example of a\\nremarkable duality between \
integrable quantum field theories and integrable\\nclassical field theories \
in two dimensions. Here we present a complete\\nderivation of this duality \
based on the classical inverse scattering transform\\nmethod, traditional \
Bethe ansatz techniques and analytic theory of ordinary\\ndifferential \
equations. In particular, we show that the Bethe ansatz equations\\ndefining \
the vacuum state of the quantum theory also define connection\\ncoefficients \
of an auxiliary linear problem for the classical sinh-Gordon\\nequation. \
Moreover, we also present details of the derivation of the \
non-linear\\nintegral equations determining the vacuum energy and other \
spectral\\ncharacteristics of the model in the case when the vacuum state is \
filled by\\n2-string solutions of the Bethe ansatz equations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
