           "id" -> "1712.00412", "submitter" -> "Andrei Onishchenko", 
            "authors" -> "R.N. Lee and A.I. Onishchenko", "title" -> 
            "ABJM quantum spectral curve and Mellin transform", "comments" -> 
            "33 pages, typos corrected and clarifications added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2018)179", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The present techniques for the perturbative solution of \
quantum spectral\ncurve problems in N=4 SYM and ABJM models are limited to \
the situation when the\nstates quantum numbers are given explicitly as some \
integer numbers. These\ntechniques are sufficient to recover full analytical \
structure of the conserved\ncharges provided that we know a finite basis of \
functions in terms of which\nthey could be written explicitly. It is known \
that in the case of N=4 SYM both\nthe contributions of asymptotic Bethe \
ansatz and wrapping or finite size\ncorrections are expressed in terms of the \
harmonic sums. However, in the case\nof ABJM model only the asymptotic \
contribution can still be written in the\nharmonic sums basis, while the \
wrapping corrections part can not. Moreover, the\ngeneralization of harmonic \
sums basis for this problem is not known. In this\npaper we present a Mellin \
space technique for the solution of multiloop Baxter\nequations, which is the \
main ingredient for the solution of corresponding\nquantum spectral problems, \
and provide explicit results for the solution of\nABJM quantum spectral curve \
in the case of twist 1 operators in sl(2) sector\nfor arbitrary spin values \
up to four loop order with explicit account for\nwrapping corrections. It is \
shown that the result for anomalous dimensions\ncould be expressed in terms \
of harmonic sums decorated by the fourth root of\nunity factors, so that \
maximum transcendentality principle holds.\n", 
