            "  We derive an operator based factorization theorem for the \
energy-energy\ncorrelation (EEC) observable in the back-to-back region, \
allowing the cross\nsection to be written as a convolution of hard, jet and \
soft functions. We\nprove the equivalence of the soft functions for the EEC \
and color singlet\ntransverse-momentum resummation to all-loop order, and \
give their analytic\nresult to three-loops. Large logarithms appearing in the \
perturbative expansion\nof the EEC can be resummed to all orders using \
renormalization group evolution.\nWe give analytic results for all required \
anomalous dimensions to three-loop\norder, providing the first example of a \
transverse-momentum (recoil) sensitive\n$e^+e^-$ event shape whose anomalous \
dimensions are known at this order. The\nEEC can now be computed to \
next-to-next-to-next-to-leading logarithm matched to\nnext-to-next-to-leading \
order, making it a prime candidate for precision QCD\nstudies and extractions \
of the strong coupling constant. We anticipate that our\nfactorization \
theorem will also be crucial for understanding non-perturbative\npower \
corrections for the EEC, and their relationship to those appearing in\nother \
observables.\n", 
