                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the UV dynamics of $\\\\mu T \\\\bar T$ \
deformed conformal field theories\\nformulated as a deformation of generating \
functions. We explore the issue of\\nnon-perturbative completion of the \
$\\\\mu$ expansion by deriving an integral\\nexpression using the \
Fourier/Legendre transform technique, and show that it is\\nmore natural to \
impose Neumann, as opposed to the Dirichlet, boundary\\ncondition, for the \
metric at the cut-off surface recently proposed by McGough,\\nMezei, and \
Verlinde. We also comment on interesting connection to boundary\\nconformal \
field theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
