            "Lorenzo Bianchi, Michelangelo Preti and Edoardo Vescovi", 
            "title" -> "Exact Bremsstrahlung functions in ABJM theory", 
            "comments" -> 
            "43 pages, 3 figures. Minor changes. Published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP07(2018)060", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we study the Bremsstrahlung functions for the \
1/6 BPS and the\n1/2 BPS Wilson lines in ABJM theory. First we use a \
superconformal defect\napproach to prove a conjectured relation between the \
Bremsstrahlung functions\nassociated to the geometric ($B^{\\varphi}_{1/6}$) \
and R-symmetry\n($B^{\\theta}_{1/6}$) deformations of the 1/6 BPS Wilson \
line. This result,\nnon-trivially following from a defect supersymmetric Ward \
identity, provides an\nexact expression for $B^{\\theta}_{1/6}$ based on a \
known result for\n$B^{\\varphi}_{1/6}$. Subsequently, we explore the \
consequences of this relation\nfor the 1/2 BPS Wilson line and, using the \
localization result for the multiply\nwound Wilson loop, we provide an exact \
closed form for the corresponding\nBremsstrahlung function. Interestingly, \
for the comparison with integrability,\nthis expression appears particularly \
natural in terms of the conjectured\ninterpolating function $h(\\lambda)$. \
During the derivation of these results we\nanalyze the protected defect \
supermultiplets associated to the broken\nsymmetries, including their two- \
and three-point correlators.\n", 
