          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1803.00577", "submitter" -> "Sergei Dubovsky", "authors" -> 
            "Sergei Dubovsky", "title" -> "A Simple Worldsheet Black Hole", 
            "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, 8 figures; v2: refs updated, typos corrected, several\n\
  comments added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP07(2018)011", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc hep-lat hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study worldsheet theory of confining strings in \
two-dimensional massive\nadjoint QCD. Similarly to confining strings in \
higher dimensions this theory\nexhibits a non-trivial $S$-matrix surviving \
even in the strict planar limit. In\nthe process of two-particle scattering a \
zigzag is formed on the worldsheet. It\nleads to an interesting non-locality \
and exhibits some properties of a quantum\nblack hole. Ordinarily, identical \
quantum particles do not carry identity. On\nthe worldsheet they acquire \
off-shell identity due to strings attached.\nIdentity implies \
complementarity. We discuss similarities and differences of\nthe worldsheet \
scattering with the $T\\bar{T}$ deformation. We also propose a\npromising \
candidate for a supersymmetric model with integrable confining\nstrings.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 1 Mar 2018 19:00:04 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 21 May 2018 19:24:29 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2018-08-01", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Dubovsky", "Sergei", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{10.05642201632476, -2.8860661191490564`}, 
           0.10102143756118451],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
