                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Building on the recently established connection between \
the Hagedorn\\ntemperature and integrability [Phys.Rev.Lett. 120 (2018) no.7, \
071605], we show\\nhow the Quantum Spectral Curve formalism can be used to \
calculate the Hagedorn\\ntemperature of AdS5/CFT4 for any value of the 't \
Hooft coupling. We solve this\\nfinite system of finite-difference equations \
perturbatively at weak coupling\\nand numerically at finite coupling. We \
confirm previous results at weak\\ncoupling and obtain the previously unknown \
three-loop Hagedorn temperature. Our\\nfinite-coupling results interpolate \
between weak and strong coupling and allow\\nus to extract the first \
perturbative order at strong coupling. Our results\\nindicate that the \
Hagedorn temperature for large 't Hooft coupling approaches\\nthat of type \
IIB string theory in ten-dimensional Minkowski space.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
