            "  The Quantum Spectral Curve (QSC) equations for planar \
$\\mathcal{N}=6$\nsuper-conformal Chern-Simons (SCS) are solved numerically \
at finite values of\nthe coupling constant for states in the \
$\\mathfrak{sl}(2|1)$ sector. New weak\ncoupling results for conformal \
dimensions of operators outside the\n$\\mathfrak{sl}(2)$-like sector are \
obtained by adapting a recently proposed\nalgorithm for the QSC perturbative \
solution. Besides being interesting in their\nown right, these perturbative \
results are necessary initial inputs for the\nnumerical algorithm to converge \
on the correct solution. The non-perturbative\nnumerical outcomes nicely \
interpolate between the weak coupling and the known\nsemiclassical \
expansions, and novel strong coupling exact results are deduced\nfrom the \
numerics. Finally, the existence of contour crossing singularities in\nthe \
TBA equations for the operator $\\textbf{20}$ is ruled out by our analysis.\n\
The results of this paper are an important test of the QSC formalism for this\
\nmodel, open the way to new quantitative studies and provide further \
evidence in\nfavour of the conjectured weak/strong coupling duality between $\
\\mathcal{N}=6$\nSCS and type IIA superstring theory on $AdS_4 \\times CP^3$. \
Attached to the\narXiv submission, a Mathematica implementation of the \
numerical method and\nancillary files containing the numerical results are \
provided.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
