 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose an alternative, statistical, derivation of \
the Thermodynamic Bethe\\nAnsatz based on the tree expansion of the Gaudin \
determinant. We illustrate the\\nmethod on the simplest example of a theory \
with diagonal scattering and no\\nbound states. We reproduce the expression \
for the free energy density and the\\nfinite size corrections to the energy \
of an excited state as well as the\\nLeClair-Mussardo series for the \
one-point function for local operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
