                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The problem of separation of variables (SoV) in \
supersymmetric spin chains is\\nclosely related to the calculation of \
correlation functions in N=4 SYM theory\\nwhich is integrable in the planar \
limit. To address this question we find a\\ncompact formula for the spin \
chain eigenstates, which does not have any sums\\nover auxiliary roots one \
usually gets in the widely adopted nested Bethe\\nansatz. Our construction \
only involves one application of a simple Bg(u_k)\\noperator to the reference \
state for each of the magnons, in complete analogy\\nwith the su(2) algebraic \
Bethe ansatz. This generalizes our SoV based\\nconstruction for su(n) to the \
supersymmetric su(1|2) case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
