            "  The $T{\\bar T}$ deformation of a relativistic two-dimensional \
theory results\nin a solvable gravitational theory. Deformed scattering \
amplitudes can be\nobtained from coupling the undeformed theory to the flat \
space\nJackiw--Teitelboim (JT) gravity. We show that the JT description is \
applicable\nand useful also in finite volume. Namely, we calculate the torus \
partition\nfunction of an arbitrary matter theory coupled to the JT gravity, \
formulated in\nthe first order (vierbein) formalism. The first order \
description provides a\nnatural set of dynamical clocks and rods for this \
theory, analogous to the\ntarget space coordinates in string theory. These \
dynamical coordinates play the\nrole of relational observables allowing to \
define a torus path integral for the\nJT gravity. The resulting partition \
function is one-loop exact and reproduces\nthe $T\\bar{T}$ deformed finite \
volume spectrum.\n", 
