                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"MHV amplitudes at strong coupling and linearized TBA \
equations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"41 pages, 9 figures; (v2) a reference added, typos \
corrected, minor\\n  revisions\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2018)002\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"TIT/HEP-668, UTHEP-718\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The maximally helicity violating (MHV) amplitudes of ${\
\\\\cal N} =4$ super\\nYang-Mills theory at strong coupling are obtained by \
solving auxiliary\\nthermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA) integral equations. We \
consider a limit where\\nthe TBA equations are linearized for large chemical \
potentials and masses\\ntherein. By solving the linearized equations, we \
derive analytic expansions of\\nthe 6-point MHV amplitudes in terms of the \
ratio of the chemical potential $A$\\nand the mass $M$. The expansions are \
valid up to corrections exponentially\\nsmall in $A$ or inversely \
proportional to powers of $A$. The analytic\\nexpansions describe the \
amplitudes for small conformal cross-ratios of the\\nparticle momenta in a \
standard basis, and interpolate the amplitudes with equal\\ncross-ratios and \
those in soft/collinear limits. The leading power corrections\\nare also \
obtained analytically. We compare the 6-point rescaled remainder\\nfunctions \
at strong coupling and at 2 loops for the above kinematics. They are\\nrather \
different, in contrast to other kinematic regions discussed in \
the\\nliterature where they are found to be similar to each other.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
