            "  The maximally helicity violating (MHV) amplitudes of ${\\cal \
N} =4$ super\nYang-Mills theory at strong coupling are obtained by solving \
auxiliary\nthermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA) integral equations. We consider a \
limit where\nthe TBA equations are linearized for large chemical potentials \
and masses\ntherein. By solving the linearized equations, we derive analytic \
expansions of\nthe 6-point MHV amplitudes in terms of the ratio of the \
chemical potential $A$\nand the mass $M$. The expansions are valid up to \
corrections exponentially\nsmall in $A$ or inversely proportional to powers \
of $A$. The analytic\nexpansions describe the amplitudes for small conformal \
cross-ratios of the\nparticle momenta in a standard basis, and interpolate \
the amplitudes with equal\ncross-ratios and those in soft/collinear limits. \
The leading power corrections\nare also obtained analytically. We compare the \
6-point rescaled remainder\nfunctions at strong coupling and at 2 loops for \
the above kinematics. They are\nrather different, in contrast to other \
kinematic regions discussed in the\nliterature where they are found to be \
similar to each other.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
