               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Surprising links between the deformation of 2D quantum \
field theories induced\\nby the composite $\\\\textrm{T} \
\\\\bar{\\\\textrm{T}}$ operator, effective string\\nmodels and the $AdS/$CFT \
correspondence, have recently emerged. The purpose of\\nthis article is to \
discuss various classical aspects related to the deformation\\nof 2D \
interacting field theories. Special attention is given to the\\nsin(h)-Gordon \
model, for which we were able to construct the \
$\\\\textrm{T}\\n\\\\bar{\\\\textrm{T}}$-deformed Lax pair. We consider the \
Lax pair formulation to be\\nthe first essential step toward a more \
satisfactory geometrical interpretation\\nof this deformation within the \
integrable model framework.\\n  Furthermore, it is shown that the 4D \
Maxwell-Born-Infeld theory, possibly\\nwith the addition of a mass term or a \
derivative-independent potential,\\ncorresponds to a natural extension of the \
2D examples. Finally, we briefly\\ncomment on 2D Yang-Mills theory and \
propose a modification of the heat kernel,\\nfor a generic surface with genus \
$p$ and $n$ boundaries, which fully accounts\\nfor the $\\\\textrm{T} \
\\\\bar{\\\\textrm{T}}$ contribution.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
