           "id" -> "1806.11515", "submitter" -> "Stefano Negro", "authors" -> 
            "Riccardo Conti, Leonardo Iannella, Stefano Negro, Roberto Tateo",
             "title" -> 
            "Generalised Born-Infeld models, Lax operators and the \
$\\textrm{T}\n  \\bar{\\textrm{T}}$ perturbation", "comments" -> 
            "22 pages, 2 figures, v2: new comments, hyperlinks and minor \
typos\n  corrected", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP11(2018)007", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Surprising links between the deformation of 2D quantum field \
theories induced\nby the composite $\\textrm{T} \\bar{\\textrm{T}}$ operator, \
effective string\nmodels and the $AdS/$CFT correspondence, have recently \
emerged. The purpose of\nthis article is to discuss various classical aspects \
related to the deformation\nof 2D interacting field theories. Special \
attention is given to the\nsin(h)-Gordon model, for which we were able to \
construct the $\\textrm{T}\n\\bar{\\textrm{T}}$-deformed Lax pair. We \
consider the Lax pair formulation to be\nthe first essential step toward a \
more satisfactory geometrical interpretation\nof this deformation within the \
integrable model framework.\n  Furthermore, it is shown that the 4D \
Maxwell-Born-Infeld theory, possibly\nwith the addition of a mass term or a \
derivative-independent potential,\ncorresponds to a natural extension of the \
2D examples. Finally, we briefly\ncomment on 2D Yang-Mills theory and propose \
a modification of the heat kernel,\nfor a generic surface with genus $p$ and \
$n$ boundaries, which fully accounts\nfor the $\\textrm{T} \
\\bar{\\textrm{T}}$ contribution.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
