, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The contributions of scalars and fermions to the null \
polygonal bosonic\\nWilson loops/gluon MHV scattering amplitudes in \
$\\\\mathcal{N} = 4$ SYM are\\nconsidered. We first examine the re-summation \
of scalars at strong coupling.\\nThen, we disentangle the form of the fermion \
contribution and show its strong\\ncoupling expansion. In particular, we \
derive the leading order with the\\nappearance of a fermion-anti-fermion \
bound state first and then effective\\nmultiple bound states thereof. This \
reproduces the string minimal area result\\nand also applies to the Nekrasov \
instanton partition function $\\\\mathcal{Z}$ of\\nthe $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
theories. Especially, in the latter case the method appears\\nto be suitable \
for a systematic expansion.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
