        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{7.447596239588568, -6.732594898373}, 0.10102143756118451],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1807.09695\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alfredo Bonini\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alfredo Bonini\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Supersymmetric 4d gauge theories and Integrability\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"181 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This thesis is devoted to some particular aspects of \
integrability in $4d$\\nSUSY gauge theories. Taking advantage of the \
integrable structures emergent in\\nthe theory, non-local observables such as \
null polygonal Wilson loops are\\nstudied in $4d$ planar $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
Super Yang-Mills. Their duality with the\\n$4d$ gluon scattering amplitudes \
makes the analysis even more interesting. The\\nso-called \\\\emph{Pentagon \
approach}, an application of the Operator Product\\nExpansion (OPE) method to \
the null polygonal Wilsol loops, makes possible a\\nnon-perturbative \
evaluation of these objects. They are recast as an OPE series\\nover the $2d$ \
GKP flux-tube excitations, a description reminescent of the QCD\\nflux-tube \
stretching between quarks. The integrability of the flux-tube allows\\nus to \
evaluate the series, in principle, for any value of the coupling\\nconstant. \
From this analysis, several results have been obtained. In the \
strong\\ncoupling regime we reproduced the TBA-like equations expected from \
the minimal\\narea problem in string theory, finding agreement with the \
$AdS/CFT$ prediction.\\nIn this respect, of fundamental importance is the \
emergence of effective bound\\nstates between elementary fermionic \
excitations. Along the way, we encountered\\nsome intriguing analogies \
between these null polygonal Wilson loops and the\\nNekrasov instanton \
partition function $\\\\mathcal{Z}$ for $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$\\ntheories. \
Furthermore, a new non-perturbative enhancement of the classical\\nstring \
argument has been confirmed, stemming from the dynamics of the string \
on\\nthe five sphere $S^5$ and described by the non-linear $\\\\sigma$-model \
$O(6)$.\\nSome properties of a fundamental building block of the OPE series, \
the $SU(4)$\\nstructure of the form factors for a specific twist operator $\\\
\\hat{P}$, have\\nbeen analysed. This $SU(4)$ matrix part is given a \
representation in terms of\\nrational functions, organized in a Young \
diagrams pattern.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 25 Jul 2018 16:14:58 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
