         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1807.09695", "submitter" -> "Alfredo Bonini", "authors" -> 
            "Alfredo Bonini", "title" -> 
            "Supersymmetric 4d gauge theories and Integrability", "comments" -> 
            "181 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This thesis is devoted to some particular aspects of \
integrability in $4d$\nSUSY gauge theories. Taking advantage of the \
integrable structures emergent in\nthe theory, non-local observables such as \
null polygonal Wilson loops are\nstudied in $4d$ planar $\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
Super Yang-Mills. Their duality with the\n$4d$ gluon scattering amplitudes \
makes the analysis even more interesting. The\nso-called \\emph{Pentagon \
approach}, an application of the Operator Product\nExpansion (OPE) method to \
the null polygonal Wilsol loops, makes possible a\nnon-perturbative \
evaluation of these objects. They are recast as an OPE series\nover the $2d$ \
GKP flux-tube excitations, a description reminescent of the QCD\nflux-tube \
stretching between quarks. The integrability of the flux-tube allows\nus to \
evaluate the series, in principle, for any value of the coupling\nconstant. \
From this analysis, several results have been obtained. In the strong\n\
coupling regime we reproduced the TBA-like equations expected from the \
minimal\narea problem in string theory, finding agreement with the $AdS/CFT$ \
prediction.\nIn this respect, of fundamental importance is the emergence of \
effective bound\nstates between elementary fermionic excitations. Along the \
way, we encountered\nsome intriguing analogies between these null polygonal \
Wilson loops and the\nNekrasov instanton partition function $\\mathcal{Z}$ \
for $\\mathcal{N}=2$\ntheories. Furthermore, a new non-perturbative \
enhancement of the classical\nstring argument has been confirmed, stemming \
from the dynamics of the string on\nthe five sphere $S^5$ and described by \
the non-linear $\\sigma$-model $O(6)$.\nSome properties of a fundamental \
building block of the OPE series, the $SU(4)$\nstructure of the form factors \
for a specific twist operator $\\hat{P}$, have\nbeen analysed. This $SU(4)$ \
matrix part is given a representation in terms of\nrational functions, \
organized in a Young diagrams pattern.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 25 Jul 2018 16:14:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2018-07-26", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Bonini", "Alfredo", ""}}}], 
