 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We generalize the $T\\\\overline{T}$ deformation of \
CFT$_2$ to\\nhigher-dimensional large-$N$ CFTs, and show that in holographic \
theories, the\\nresulting effective field theory matches semiclassical \
gravity in AdS with a\\nfinite radial cutoff. We also derive the deformation \
dual to arbitrary bulk\\nmatter theories. Generally, the deformations involve \
background fields as well\\nas CFT operators. By keeping track of these \
background fields along the flow,\\nwe demonstrate how to match correlation \
functions on the two sides in some\\nsimple examples, as well as other \
observables.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
