Hernandez-Chifflet", "title" -> 
            "Undressing Confining Flux Tubes with $T\\bar T$", "comments" -> 
            "added some comments in the introduction, matches published \
version", "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. D 98, 114024 (2018)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.98.114024", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th hep-lat hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Lattice QCD simulations provide crucial information about the \
worldsheet\ndynamics of confining strings (flux tubes). An accurate \
extraction of the\nworldsheet $S$-matrix from lattice spectra requires \
accounting for polarization\neffects. Approximate integrability of the low \
energy worldsheet theory makes it\npossible to apply the Thermodynamic Bethe \
Ansatz to incorporate polarization\neffects at all orders in the number of \
windings and at the leading order in the\nderivative expansion. However, a \
systematic application of this technique in\nthe presence of non-integrable \
effects and for multiparticle states becomes\nincreasingly challenging. We \
point out that a recently understood equivalence\nbetween gravitational \
dressing and $T\\bar{T}$ deformation provides a fully\nsystematic and \
straightforward recipe to incorporate the leading polarization\neffects in \
the presence of an arbitrary inelasticity and for any number of\nparticles. \
We illustrate this technique with several examples.\n", 
