               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riccardo Conti, Stefano Negro and Roberto Tateo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The $\\\\textrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\textrm{T}}$ perturbation \
and its geometric\\n  interpretation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2 : Expanded version with new comments, numerical \
results and 16\\n  figures added. Minor typos corrected. Extra references \
added. 25 pages. 4\\n  figures v3 : JHEP version. Section 6 added. Minor \
typos corrected. Extra\\n  reference added. 30 pages. 5 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2019)085\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Starting from the recently-discovered \
$\\\\textrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\textrm{T}}$-perturbed\\nLagrangians, we prove that \
the deformed solutions to the classical EoMs for\\nbosonic field theories are \
equivalent to the unperturbed ones but for a\\nspecific field-dependent local \
change of coordinates. This surprising geometric\\noutcome is fully \
consistent with the identification \
of\\n$\\\\textrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\textrm{T}}$-deformed 2D quantum field theories \
as topological\\nJT gravity coupled to generic matter fields. Although our \
conclusion is valid\\nfor generic interacting potentials, it first emerged \
from a detailed study of\\nthe sine-Gordon model and in particular from the \
fact that solitonic\\npseudo-spherical surfaces embedded in $\\\\mathbb R^3$ \
are left invariant by the\\ndeformation. Analytic and numerical results \
concerning the perturbation of\\nspecific sine-Gordon soliton solutions are \
presented.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
