        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{5.0768058964871985`, -5.74779276356135}, 
           0.10102143756118451],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1810.05434\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrea Fontanella\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrea Fontanella\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Black Horizons and Integrability in String Theory\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"223 pages, 13 figures, PhD Thesis\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This thesis is devoted to the study of geometric \
aspects of black holes and\\nintegrable structures in string theory. In the \
first part, symmetries of the\\nhorizon and its bulk extension will be \
investigated. We investigate the horizon\\nconjecture beyond the supergravity \
approximation, by considering \\\\alpha'\\ncorrections of heterotic \
supergravity in perturbation theory, and show that\\nstandard global \
techniques can no longer be applied. A sufficient condition to\\nestablish \
the horizon conjecture will be identified. As a consequence of \
our\\nanalysis, we find a no-go theorem for AdS2 backgrounds in heterotic \
theory. The\\nbulk extension of a prescribed near-horizon geometry will then \
be considered in\\nvarious theories. The horizon fields will be expanded at \
first order in the\\nradial coordinate. The moduli space of radial \
deformations will be proved to be\\nfinite dimensional, by showing that the \
moduli must satisfy elliptic PDEs.\\n  In the second part, geometric aspects \
and spectral properties of integrable\\nanti-de Sitter backgrounds will be \
discussed. We formulate a Bethe ansatz in\\nAdS2 x S2 x T6 type IIB \
superstring, overcoming the problem of the lack of\\npseudo-vacuum state \
affecting this background. In AdS3 x S3 x T4 type IIB\\nsuperstring, we show \
that the S-matrix is annihilated by the boost generator of\\nthe q-deformed \
Poincar\\\\'e superalgebra, and interpret this condition as a\\nparallel \
equation for the S-matrix with respect to a connection on a fibre\\nbundle. \
This hints that the algebraic problem associated with the \
scattering\\nprocess can be geometrically rewritten. This allows us to \
propose a Universal\\nS-matrix.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 12 Oct 2018 09:54:18 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2018-10-15\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Fontanella\"", ",", "\"Andrea\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                    "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> Left, 
             ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1810.05434", "submitter" -> "Andrea Fontanella", 
            "authors" -> "Andrea Fontanella", "title" -> 
            "Black Horizons and Integrability in String Theory", "comments" -> 
            "223 pages, 13 figures, PhD Thesis", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  This thesis is devoted to the study of geometric aspects of \
black holes and\nintegrable structures in string theory. In the first part, \
symmetries of the\nhorizon and its bulk extension will be investigated. We \
investigate the horizon\nconjecture beyond the supergravity approximation, by \
considering \\alpha'\ncorrections of heterotic supergravity in perturbation \
theory, and show that\nstandard global techniques can no longer be applied. A \
sufficient condition to\nestablish the horizon conjecture will be identified. \
As a consequence of our\nanalysis, we find a no-go theorem for AdS2 \
backgrounds in heterotic theory. The\nbulk extension of a prescribed \
near-horizon geometry will then be considered in\nvarious theories. The \
horizon fields will be expanded at first order in the\nradial coordinate. The \
moduli space of radial deformations will be proved to be\nfinite dimensional, \
by showing that the moduli must satisfy elliptic PDEs.\n  In the second part, \
geometric aspects and spectral properties of integrable\nanti-de Sitter \
backgrounds will be discussed. We formulate a Bethe ansatz in\nAdS2 x S2 x T6 \
type IIB superstring, overcoming the problem of the lack of\npseudo-vacuum \
state affecting this background. In AdS3 x S3 x T4 type IIB\nsuperstring, we \
show that the S-matrix is annihilated by the boost generator of\nthe \
q-deformed Poincar\\'e superalgebra, and interpret this condition as a\n\
parallel equation for the S-matrix with respect to a connection on a fibre\n\
bundle. This hints that the algebraic problem associated with the scattering\n\
process can be geometrically rewritten. This allows us to propose a Universal\
\nS-matrix.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 12 Oct 2018 09:54:18 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2018-10-15", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fontanella", "Andrea", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
