                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Anastasia Doikou, Iain Findlay, Spyridoula \
Sklaveniti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-commutative NLS-type hierarchies: dressing & \
solutions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"29 pages, LaTex. Minor modifications\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl. Phys. B941 (2019) 376\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2019.02.019\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph hep-th math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the generalized matrix non-linear \
Schrodinger (NLS) hierarchy. By\\nemploying the universal Darboux-dressing \
scheme we derive solutions for the\\nhierarchy of integrable PDEs via \
solutions of the matrix\\nGelfand-Levitan-Marchenko equation, and we also \
identify recursion relations\\nthat yield the Lax pairs for the whole matrix \
NLS-type hierarchy. These results\\nare obtained considering either \
matrix-integral or general $n^{th}$ order\\nmatrix-differential operators as \
Darboux-dressing transformations. In this\\nframework special links with the \
Airy and Burgers equations are also discussed.\\nThe matrix version of the \
Darboux transform is also examined leading to the\\nnon-commutative version \
of the Riccati equation. The non-commutative Riccati\\nequation is solved and \
hence suitable conserved quantities are derived. In this\\ncontext we also \
discuss the infinite dimensional case of the NLS matrix model\\nas it \
provides a suitable candidate for a quantum version of the usual NLS\\nmodel. \
Similarly, the non-commutitave Riccati equation for the general \
dressing\\ntransform is derived and it is naturally equivalent to the one \
emerging from\\nthe solution of the auxiliary linear problem.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
