           "id" -> "1810.10937", "submitter" -> "Anastasia Doikou", "authors" -> 
            "Anastasia Doikou, Iain Findlay, Spyridoula Sklaveniti", "title" -> 
            "Non-commutative NLS-type hierarchies: dressing & solutions", 
            "comments" -> "29 pages, LaTex. Minor modifications", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl. Phys. B941 (2019) 376", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2019.02.019", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "math-ph hep-th math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the generalized matrix non-linear Schrodinger \
(NLS) hierarchy. By\nemploying the universal Darboux-dressing scheme we \
derive solutions for the\nhierarchy of integrable PDEs via solutions of the \
matrix\nGelfand-Levitan-Marchenko equation, and we also identify recursion \
relations\nthat yield the Lax pairs for the whole matrix NLS-type hierarchy. \
These results\nare obtained considering either matrix-integral or general \
$n^{th}$ order\nmatrix-differential operators as Darboux-dressing \
transformations. In this\nframework special links with the Airy and Burgers \
equations are also discussed.\nThe matrix version of the Darboux transform is \
also examined leading to the\nnon-commutative version of the Riccati \
equation. The non-commutative Riccati\nequation is solved and hence suitable \
conserved quantities are derived. In this\ncontext we also discuss the \
infinite dimensional case of the NLS matrix model\nas it provides a suitable \
candidate for a quantum version of the usual NLS\nmodel. Similarly, the \
non-commutitave Riccati equation for the general dressing\ntransform is \
derived and it is naturally equivalent to the one emerging from\nthe solution \
of the auxiliary linear problem.\n", 
