               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In previous works, we have developed an approach to fix \
the leading behaviors\\nof the pure AdS$_3$ and BTZ black hole from the \
entanglement entropies of the\\nfree CFT$_2$ and finite temperature CFT$_2$, \
respectively. We exclusively use\\nholographic principle only and make no \
restriction about the bulk geometry, not\\nonly the kinematics but also the \
dynamics. In order to verify the universality\\nand correctness of our \
method, in this paper, we apply it to the $T\\\\bar{T}$\\ndeformed CFT$_2$, \
which breaks the conformal symmetry. In terms of the physical\\narguments of \
the $T\\\\bar{T}$ deformed CFT$_2$, the derived metric is a deformed\\nBTZ \
black hole. The requirement that the CFT$_2$ lives on a conformally \
flat\\nboundary leads to $r_{c}^{2}=\\\\ 6R_{AdS}^{4}/(\\\\pi c\\\\mu)$ \
naturally, in perfect\\nagreement with previous conjectures in literature. \
The energy spectum and\\npropagation speed calculated with this deformed BTZ \
metric are the same as\\nthese derived from $T\\\\bar{T}$ deformed CFT$_2$. \
We furthermore fix the dual\\ngeometry of highly excited states with our \
approach. The result contains the\\ndescriptions for the conical defect and \
BTZ black hole.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
