                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  There is a number of indications that scattering \
amplitudes in the\\nAharony-Bergman-Jafferis-Maldacena theory might have a \
dual description in\\nterms of a holonomy of a supergauge connection on a \
null polygonal contour in a\\nway analogous to the four-dimensional maximally \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills\\ntheory. However, so far its explicit \
implementations evaded a successful\\ncompletion. The difficulty is \
intimately tied to the lack of the T-self-duality\\nof the sigma model on the \
string side of the gauge/string correspondence.\\nUnscathed by the last \
misfortune, we initiate with this study an application of\\nthe pentagon \
paradigm to scattering amplitudes of the theory. With the language\\nbeing \
democratic and nondiscriminatory to whether one considers a Wilson \
loop\\nexpectation value or an amplitude, the success in the application of \
the\\nprogram points towards a possible unified observable on the field \
theory side.\\nOur present consideration is focused on two-loop perturbation \
theory in the\\nplanar limit, begging for higher loop data in order to \
bootstrap current\\nanalysis to all orders in the 't Hooft \
coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
