            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1811.09839", "submitter" -> "Benjamin Basso", "authors" -> 
            "Benjamin Basso, Andrei V. Belitsky", "title" -> 
            "ABJM flux-tube and scattering amplitudes", "comments" -> 
            "46 pages, 9 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP09(2019)116", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  There is a number of indications that scattering amplitudes in \
the\nAharony-Bergman-Jafferis-Maldacena theory might have a dual description \
in\nterms of a holonomy of a supergauge connection on a null polygonal \
contour in a\nway analogous to the four-dimensional maximally supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills\ntheory. However, so far its explicit implementations evaded a \
successful\ncompletion. The difficulty is intimately tied to the lack of the \
T-self-duality\nof the sigma model on the string side of the gauge/string \
correspondence.\nUnscathed by the last misfortune, we initiate with this \
study an application of\nthe pentagon paradigm to scattering amplitudes of \
the theory. With the language\nbeing democratic and nondiscriminatory to \
whether one considers a Wilson loop\nexpectation value or an amplitude, the \
success in the application of the\nprogram points towards a possible unified \
observable on the field theory side.\nOur present consideration is focused on \
two-loop perturbation theory in the\nplanar limit, begging for higher loop \
data in order to bootstrap current\nanalysis to all orders in the 't Hooft \
coupling.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
