 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the ODE/IM correspondence for all states of \
the quantum\\n$\\\\widehat{\\\\mathfrak{g}}$-KdV model, where $\\\\widehat{\\\
\\mathfrak{g}}$ is the\\naffinization of a simply-laced simple Lie algebra \
$\\\\mathfrak{g}$. We construct\\nquantum $\\\\widehat{\\\\mathfrak{g}}$-KdV \
opers as an explicit realization of the\\nclass of opers introduced by Feigin \
and Frenkel, which are defined by fixing\\nthe singularity structure at $0$ \
and $\\\\infty$, and by allowing a finite number\\nof additional singular \
terms with trivial monodromy. We prove that the\\ngeneralized monodromy data \
of the quantum $\\\\widehat{\\\\mathfrak{g}}$-KdV opers\\nsatisfy the Bethe \
Ansatz equations of the quantum $\\\\widehat{\\\\mathfrak{g}}$-KdV\\nmodel. \
The trivial monodromy conditions are equivalent to a complete system \
of\\nalgebraic equations for the additional singularities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
