 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We continue the effort to optimise and generalise the \
solution of the\\nspectral problem of AdS$_5$/CFT$_4$ in the planar limit via \
integrability. We\\npresent a simple strategy to solve the quantum spectral \
curve perturbatively\\nfor general states by focusing on the $\\\\mathbf{P}\\\
\\mu$-system. A Mathematica\\nnotebook with an implementation of this \
algorithm is provided, as well as an\\nextensive database with a \
user-friendly interface containing more than 8.000\\nsolutions of the QSC. \
When investigating the solution space, we observe a\\ncurious phenomenon: \
existence of solutions for which the Q-system degenerates\\nin the limit $g\\\
\\to 0$. These degeneracies are lifted at higher orders in\\nperturbation \
theory. The degenerating solutions have auxiliary Bethe roots\\nmerging with \
branch points at weak coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
