 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Two-dimensional conformal field theories with just \
Virasoro symmetry are\\nendowed with integrable structure. We review how to \
construct the integrable\\ncharges in a two-dimensional conformal field \
theory and how to relate them to\\nthe charges of quantum Sinh-Gordon theory \
when c>25. We then explicitly\\ncalculate the single charge characters in the \
large c limit for all charges and\\nthereby reveal how their degeneracies \
grow within one module. This, in\\nparticular, allows us to approximate the \
characters in the limit of small\\nchemical potential, which source the \
respective charges. The latter give us\\ninsights into possible \
transformation properties of the characters. We also\\ncomment on the full \
generalized Gibbs ensemble and approximations to pure\\nstates.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
