            "Two Mathematica notebooks attached, v3: Corrected a sign error, \
which\n  allowed us to extend the large c analysis odd KdV charges, too. \
Additionally\n  we have corrected a few typos, and added a few references", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. D 101, 086025 (2020)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.101.086025", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            
            "  Two-dimensional conformal field theories with just Virasoro \
symmetry are\nendowed with integrable structure. We review how to construct \
the integrable\ncharges in a two-dimensional conformal field theory and how \
to relate them to\nthe charges of quantum Sinh-Gordon theory when c>25. We \
then explicitly\ncalculate the single charge characters in the large c limit \
for all charges and\nthereby reveal how their degeneracies grow within one \
module. This, in\nparticular, allows us to approximate the characters in the \
limit of small\nchemical potential, which source the respective charges. The \
latter give us\ninsights into possible transformation properties of the \
characters. We also\ncomment on the full generalized Gibbs ensemble and \
approximations to pure\nstates.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 29 Jan 2019 16:01:12 GMT"}, {
