            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1902.00320\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Benjamin Doyon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Benjamin Doyon and Jason Myers\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Fluctuations in ballistic transport from Euler \
hydrodynamics\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"27+22 pages, one figure\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Ann. Henri Poincar\\\\'e 21, 255-302 (2020)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s00023-019-00860-w\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a general formalism, within large deviation \
theory, giving access\\nto the exact statistics of fluctuations of \
ballistically transported conserved\\nquantities in homogeneous, stationary \
states. The formalism is expected to\\napply to any system with an Euler \
hydrodynamic description, classical or\\nquantum, integrable or not, in or \
out of equilibrium. We express the exact\\nscaled cumulant generating \
function (or full counting statistics) for any\\n(quasi-)local conserved \
quantity in terms of the flux Jacobian. We show that\\nthe \\\"extended \
fluctuation relations\\\" of Bernard and Doyon follow from the\\nlinearity of \
the hydrodynamic equations, forming a marker of \\\"freeness\\\" much\\nlike \
the absence of hydrodynamic diffusion does. We show how an extension of\\nthe \
formalism gives exact exponential behaviours of spatio-temporal \
two-point\\nfunctions of twist fields, with applications to order-parameter \
dynamical\\ncorrelations in arbitrary homogeneous, stationary state. We \
explain in what\\nsituations the large deviation principle at the basis of \
the results fail, and\\ndiscuss how this connects with nonlinear fluctuating \
hydrodynamics. Applying\\nthe formalism to conformal hydrodynamics, we \
evaluate the exact cumulants of\\nenergy transport in quantum critical \
systems of arbitrary dimension at low but\\nnonzero temperatures, observing a \
phase transition for Lorentz boosts at the\\nsound velocity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 1 Feb 2019 13:37:37 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-12-09\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
