               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We focus on the non-linear Schrodinger model and we \
extend the notion of\\nspace-time dualities in the presence of integrable \
time-like boundary\\nconditions. We identify the associated time-like \
`conserved' quantities and Lax\\npairs as well as the corresponding boundary \
conditions. In particular, we\\nderive the generating function of the space \
components of the Lax pairs in the\\ncase of time-like boundaries defined by \
solutions of the reflection equation.\\nAnalytical conditions on the boundary \
Lax pair lead to the time like-boundary\\nconditions. The time-like dressing \
is also performed for the first time, as an\\neffective means to produce the \
space components of the Lax pair of the\\nassociated hierarchy. This is \
particularly relevant in the absence of a\\nclassical r-matrix, or when \
considering complicated underlying algebraic\\nstructures. The associated \
time Riccati equations and hence the time-like\\nconserved quantities are \
also derived. We use as the main paradigm for this\\npurpose the matrix \
NLS-type hierarchy.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
