               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Vincent Caudrelier\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Vincent Caudrelier, Nicolas Crampe\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"New integrable boundary conditions for the Ablowitz-Ladik \
model: from\\n  Hamiltonian formalism to nonlinear mirror image method\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages. References added. Accepted authors \
version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl. Phys. B946 (2019) 114720\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2019.114720\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using Sklyanin's classical theory of integrable \
boundary conditions, we use\\nthe Hamiltonian approach to derive new \
integrable boundary conditions for the\\nAblowitz-Ladik model on the finite \
and half infinite lattice. In the case of\\nhalf infinite lattice, the \
special and new emphasis of this paper is to connect\\ndirectly the \
Hamiltonian approach, based on the classical $r$-matrix, with the\\nzero \
curvature representation and B\\\\\\\"acklund transformation approach \
that\\nallows one to implement a nonlinear mirror image method and construct \
explicit\\nsolutions. It is shown that for our boundary conditions, which \
generalise\\n(discrete) Robin boundary conditions, a nontrivial extension of \
the known\\nmirror image method to what we call {\\\\it time-dependent \
boundary conditions} is\\nneeded. A careful discussion of this extension is \
given and is facilitated by\\nintroducing the notion of intrinsic and \
extrinsic picture for describing\\nboundary conditions. This gives the \
specific link between Sklyanin's reflection\\nmatrices and B\\\\\\\"acklund \
transformations combined with folding, {\\\\it in the case\\nof non-diagonal \
reflection matrices}. All our results reproduce the known Robin\\nboundary \
conditions setup as a special case: the diagonal case. Explicit\\nformulas \
for constructing multisoliton solutions on the half-lattice with \
our\\ntime-dependent boundary conditions are given and some examples are \
plotted.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 19 Mar 2019 18:00:11 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 19 Aug 2019 17:27:56 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2019-08-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Caudrelier\"", ",", "\"Vincent\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Crampe\"", ",", "\"Nicolas\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
