         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1903.10759", "submitter" -> "Andrea Fontanella", 
            "authors" -> "Andrea Fontanella and Alessandro Torrielli", 
            "title" -> 
            "Geometry of Massless Scattering in Integrable Superstring", 
            "comments" -> "Matching with the published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP06(2019)116", 
            "report-no" -> "DMUS--MP--19--05 , IFT-UAM/CSIC-19-33", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the action of the $q$-deformed Poincar\\'e \
superalgebra on the\nmassless non-relativistic R-matrix in ordinary \
(undeformed) integrable $AdS_2\n\\times S^2 \\times T^6$ type IIB superstring \
theory. The boost generator acts\nnon-trivially on the R-matrix, confirming \
the existence of a non-relativistic\nrapidity $\\gamma$ with respect to which \
the R-matrix must be of difference\nform. We conjecture that from a massless \
AdS/CFT integrable relativistic\nR-matrix one can obtain the parental \
massless non-relativistic R-matrix simply\nby replacing the relativistic \
rapidity with $\\gamma$. We check our conjecture\nin ordinary (undeformed) \
$AdS_n \\times S^n \\times T^{10 - 2n}$, $n = 2, 3$. In\nthe case $n=3$, we \
check that the matrix part and the dressing factor - up to\nnumerical \
accuracy for real momenta - obey our prescription. In the $n=2$ case,\nwe \
check the matrix part and propose the non-relativistic dressing factor. We\n\
then start a programme of classifying R-matrices in terms of connections on\n\
fibre bundles. The conditions obtained for the connection are tested on a set\
\nof known integrable R-matrices.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
