 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the behaviour of two-dimensional quantum \
field theories with\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=(0,2)$ supersymmetry under a \
deformation induced by the\\n`$T\\\\bar{T}$' composite operator. We show that \
the deforming operator can be\\ndefined by a point-splitting regularisation \
in such a way as to preserve\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=(0,2)$ supersymmetry. As an \
example of this construction, we work\\nout the deformation of a free \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=(0,2)$ theory and compare to that\\ninduced by the Noether \
stress-energy tensor. Finally, we show that the\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=(0,2)$ \
supersymmetric deformed action actually possesses\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=(2,2)$ \
symmetry, half of which is non-linearly realised.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
