           "id" -> "1904.12827", "submitter" -> "Jun-Ichi Sakamoto", 
            "authors" -> "Jun-ichi Sakamoto", "title" -> 
            "Integrable deformations of string sigma models and generalized\n \
 supergravity", "comments" -> "Ph.D. Thesis, 227 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This thesis is mainly devoted to studying integrable \
deformations of the\n${\\rm AdS}_5 \\times {\\rm S}^5$ superstring and \
generalized supergravity. We\nstart to give a brief review of the ${\\rm \
AdS}_5 \\times {\\rm S}^5$ superstring\nformulated in the Green-Schwartz \
formalism, and then introduce homogeneous\nYang-Baxter (YB) deformation of \
the ${\\rm AdS}_5 \\times {\\rm S}^5$ superstring\nbased on $r$-matrices \
which are solutions to the homogeneous classical YB\nequation. By performing \
a supercoset construction, we derive the general\nformula for homogeneous YB \
deformed backgrounds associated with bosonic\n$r$-matrices. The deformed \
backgrounds are shown to be solutions of the\nstandard type IIB supergravity \
or generalized supergravity. Next, we explain\nthat homogeneous YB \
deformation can be regarded as a kind of the $O(d,d)$\nduality \
transformations. Once YB deformations are realized as duality\n\
transformations, the corresponding $O(d,d)$ transformations are applied to\n\
almost all backgrounds. Moreover, we discuss spacetime structures of\n\
homogeneous YB deformed backgrounds and clarify a T-fold structure of them by\
\nshowing the associated $O(d,d; \\mathbb{Z})$ $T$-duality monodromy. \
Finally, we\nconsider the Weyl invariance of string theories in generalized \
supergravity\nbackgrounds. We show that generalized supergravity can be \
reproduced from\ndouble field theory with the dilaton depending on a linear \
dual coordinate.\nFrom this result, we construct a possible counterterm to \
cancel out the Weyl\nanomaly of bosonic string theories on generalized \
supergravity backgrounds. In\nparticular, we show that the counterterm is \
definitely local. In this sense,\nstring theories can be consistently defined \
in generalized supergravity\nbackgrounds.\n", 
