               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1905.01444\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gregory Korchemsky\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"G. P. Korchemsky\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Energy correlations in the end-point region\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2020)008\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"IPhT-T19/041\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The energy-energy correlation (EEC) measures the \
angular distribution of the\\nenergy that flows through two calorimeters \
separated by some relative angle in\\nthe final state created by a source. We \
study this observable in the limit of\\nsmall and large angles when it \
describes the correlation between particles\\nbelonging, respectively, to the \
same jet and to two almost back-to-back jets.\\nWe present a new approach to \
resumming large logarithmically enhanced\\ncorrections in both limits that \
exploits the relation between the energy\\ncorrelations and four-point \
correlation functions of conserved currents. At\\nlarge angle, we derive the \
EEC from the behaviour of the correlation function\\nin the limit when four \
operators are light-like separated in a sequential\\nmanner. At small angle, \
in a conformal theory, we obtain the EEC from\\nresummation of the conformal \
partial wave expansion of the correlation function\\nat short-distance \
separation between the calorimeters. In both cases, we obtain\\na concise \
representation of the EEC in terms of the conformal data of \
twist-two\\noperators and verify it by comparing with the results of explicit \
calculation\\nat next-to-next-to-leading order in maximally supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory.\\nAs a byproduct of our analysis, we predict the maximal \
weight part of the\\nanalogous QCD expression in the back-to-back \
limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
