         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1905.01444", "submitter" -> "Gregory Korchemsky", 
            "authors" -> "G. P. Korchemsky", "title" -> 
            "Energy correlations in the end-point region", "comments" -> 
            "31 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP01(2020)008", "report-no" -> "IPhT-T19/041", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The energy-energy correlation (EEC) measures the angular \
distribution of the\nenergy that flows through two calorimeters separated by \
some relative angle in\nthe final state created by a source. We study this \
observable in the limit of\nsmall and large angles when it describes the \
correlation between particles\nbelonging, respectively, to the same jet and \
to two almost back-to-back jets.\nWe present a new approach to resumming \
large logarithmically enhanced\ncorrections in both limits that exploits the \
relation between the energy\ncorrelations and four-point correlation \
functions of conserved currents. At\nlarge angle, we derive the EEC from the \
behaviour of the correlation function\nin the limit when four operators are \
light-like separated in a sequential\nmanner. At small angle, in a conformal \
theory, we obtain the EEC from\nresummation of the conformal partial wave \
expansion of the correlation function\nat short-distance separation between \
the calorimeters. In both cases, we obtain\na concise representation of the \
EEC in terms of the conformal data of twist-two\noperators and verify it by \
comparing with the results of explicit calculation\nat \
next-to-next-to-leading order in maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory.\n\
As a byproduct of our analysis, we predict the maximal weight part of the\n\
analogous QCD expression in the back-to-back limit.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 4 May 2019 06:49:00 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-01-29", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Korchemsky", "G. P.", ""}}}],
           "Tooltip"]& ], 
