 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present an algorithmic perturbative solution of ABJM \
quantum spectral\\ncurve at twist 1 in sl(2) sector for arbitrary spin \
values, which can be\\napplied to, in principle, arbitrary order of \
perturbation theory. We determined\\nthe class of functions -- products of \
rational functions in spectral parameter\\nwith sums of Baxter polynomials \
and Hurwitz functions -- closed under\\nelementary operations, such as shifts \
and partial fractions, as well as\\ndifferentiation. It turns out, that this \
class of functions is also sufficient\\nfor finding solutions of \
inhomogeneous Baxter equations involved. For the\\nlatter purpose we present \
recursive construction of the dictionary for the\\nsolutions of Baxter \
equations for given inhomogeneous parts. As an application\\nof the proposed \
method we present the computation of anomalous dimensions of\\ntwist 1 \
operators at six loop order. There is still a room for improvements of\\nthe \
proposed algorithm related to the simplifications of arising sums. \
The\\nadvanced techniques for their reduction to the basis of generalized \
harmonic\\nsums will be the subject of subsequent paper. We expect this \
method to be\\ngeneralizable to higher twists as well as to other theories, \
such as N=4 SYM.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
