           "id" -> "1905.03116", "submitter" -> "Andrei Onishchenko", 
            "authors" -> "R.N. Lee and A.I. Onishchenko", "title" -> 
            "ABJM quantum spectral curve at twist 1: algorithmic perturbative\
\n  solution", "comments" -> "38 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP11(2019)018", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th hep-ph math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present an algorithmic perturbative solution of ABJM \
quantum spectral\ncurve at twist 1 in sl(2) sector for arbitrary spin values, \
which can be\napplied to, in principle, arbitrary order of perturbation \
theory. We determined\nthe class of functions -- products of rational \
functions in spectral parameter\nwith sums of Baxter polynomials and Hurwitz \
functions -- closed under\nelementary operations, such as shifts and partial \
fractions, as well as\ndifferentiation. It turns out, that this class of \
functions is also sufficient\nfor finding solutions of inhomogeneous Baxter \
equations involved. For the\nlatter purpose we present recursive construction \
of the dictionary for the\nsolutions of Baxter equations for given \
inhomogeneous parts. As an application\nof the proposed method we present the \
computation of anomalous dimensions of\ntwist 1 operators at six loop order. \
There is still a room for improvements of\nthe proposed algorithm related to \
the simplifications of arising sums. The\nadvanced techniques for their \
reduction to the basis of generalized harmonic\nsums will be the subject of \
subsequent paper. We expect this method to be\ngeneralizable to higher twists \
as well as to other theories, such as N=4 SYM.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
