                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.KT math.MP math.QA\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Quantum toroidal algebras are obtained from quantum \
affine algebras by a\\nfurther affinization, and, like the latter, can be \
used to construct integrable\\nsystems. These algebras also describe the \
symmetries of instanton partition\\nfunctions for 5D $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ \
supersymmetric quiver gauge theories. We\\nconsider here the gauge theories \
defined on an orbifold\\n$S^1\\\\times\\\\mathbb{C}^2/\\\\mathbb{Z}_p$ where \
the action of $\\\\mathbb{Z}_p$ is\\ndetermined by two integer parameters \
$(\\\\nu_1,\\\\nu_2)$. The corresponding quantum\\ntoroidal algebra is \
introduced as a deformation of the quantum toroidal algebra\\nof \
$\\\\mathfrak{gl}(p)$. We show that it has the structure of a Hopf algebra, \
and\\npresent two representations, called vertical and horizontal, obtained \
by\\ndeforming respectively the Fock representation and Saito's \
vertex\\nrepresentations of the quantum toroidal algebra of \
$\\\\mathfrak{gl}(p)$. We\\nconstruct the vertex operator intertwining \
between these two types of\\nrepresentations. This object is identified with \
a $(\\\\nu_1,\\\\nu_2)$-deformation\\nof the refined topological vertex, \
allowing us to reconstruct the Nekrasov\\npartition function and the \
$qq$-characters of the quiver gauge theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
