 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We apply the recently developped analytical methods for \
computing the\\nboundary entropy, or the g-function, in integrable theories \
with non-diagonal\\nscattering. We consider the particular case of the \
current-perturbed $SU(2)_k$\\nWZNW model with boundary and compute the \
boundary entropy for a specific\\nboundary condition. The main problem we \
encounter is that in case of\\nnon-diagonal scattering the boundary entropy \
is infinite. We show that this\\ninfinity can be cured by a subtraction. The \
difference of the boundary\\nentropies in the UV and in the IR limits is \
finite, and matches the known\\ng-functions for the unperturbed $SU(2)_k$ \
WZNW model for even values of the\\nlevel.\\n\""}]}, {
