            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We develop a novel nonperturbative approach to a class of \
three-point\nfunctions in planar $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM based on Thermodynamic \
Bethe Ansatz\n(TBA). More specifically, we study three-point functions of a \
non-BPS\nsingle-trace operator and two determinant operators dual to maximal \
Giant\nGraviton D-branes in AdS$_5\\times$S$^{5}$. They correspond to disk \
one-point\nfunctions on the worldsheet and admit a simpler and more powerful \
integrability\ndescription than the standard single-trace three-point \
functions. We first\nintroduce two new methods to efficiently compute such \
correlators at weak\ncoupling; one based on large $N$ collective fields, \
which provides an example\nof open-closed-open duality discussed by \
Gopakumar, and the other based on\ncombinatorics. The results so obtained \
exhibit a simple determinant structure\nand indicate that the correlator can \
be interpreted as a generalization of\n$g$-functions in 2d QFT; an overlap \
between an integrable boundary state and a\nstate corresponding to the \
single-trace operator. We then determine the\nboundary state at finite \
coupling using the symmetry, the crossing equation and\nthe boundary \
Yang-Baxter equation. With the resulting boundary state, we derive\nthe \
ground-state $g$-function based on TBA and conjecture its generalization to\n\
other states. This is the first fully nonperturbative proposal for the\n\
structure constants of operators of finite length. The results are tested\n\
extensively at weak and strong couplings. Finally, we point out that\n\
determinant operators can provide better probes of sub-AdS locality than\n\
single-trace operators and discuss possible applications.\n", 
