 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper, we regard the \
$T\\\\bar{T}$/$J\\\\bar{T}$-deformed CFTs as\\nperturbation theories and \
calculate the first order correction of the\\ncorrelation functions due to \
the $T\\\\bar{T}$/$J\\\\bar{T}$-deformation. As\\napplications, we study the \
R\\\\'enyi entanglement entropy of excited state in \
the\\n$T\\\\bar{T}$/$J\\\\bar{T}$-deformed two-dimensional CFTs. We find, up \
to the\\nperturbation first order of the deformation, the R\\\\'enyi \
entanglement entropy\\nof locally excited states will acquire a non-trivial \
time dependence. The\\nexcess of the R\\\\'enyi entanglement entropy of \
locally excited state will also\\nbe dramatically changed up to order \
${\\\\cal O}(c)$. Furthermore, the out of time\\nordered correlation function \
is investigated to confirm that \
the\\n$T\\\\bar{T}$/$J\\\\bar{T}$-deformations do not change the maximal \
chaotic behavior\\nof holographic CFTs up to the first order of the \
deformations.\\n\""}]}, {
