            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1908.09299", "submitter" -> "Alessandro Sfondrini", 
            "authors" -> "Alessandro Sfondrini, Stijn J. van Tongeren", 
            "title" -> "$T\\bar{T}$ deformations as TsT transformations", 
            "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, 1 figure; v2: further examples (section 5) and \
discussion\n  of JTbar deformations (appendix B) added, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. D 101, 066022 (2020)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.101.066022", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The relationship between $T\\bar{T}$ deformations and the \
uniform light-cone\ngauge, first noted in arXiv:1804.01998, provides a \
powerful generating\ntechnique for deformed models. We recall this \
construction, distinguishing\nbetween changes of the gauge frame, which do \
not affect the theory, and genuine\ndeformations. We investigate the \
geometric interpretation of the latter and\nargue that they affect the global \
features of the geometry before gauge fixing.\nExploiting a formal relation \
between uniform light-cone gauge and static gauge\nin a T-dual frame, we \
interpret such a change as a TsT transformation involving\nthe two light-cone \
coordinates. In the static-gauge picture, the $T\\bar{T}$ CDD\nfactor then \
has a natural interpretation as a Drinfel'd-Reshetikhin twist of\nthe \
worldsheet S matrix. To illustrate these ideas, we find the geometries\n\
yielding a $T\\bar{T}$ deformation of the worldsheet S matrix of pp-wave and\n\
Lin-Lunin-Maldacena backgrounds.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 25 Aug 2019 10:49:11 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 30 Sep 2019 18:00:16 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-04-01", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Sfondrini", "Alessandro", ""}, {
              "van Tongeren", "Stijn J.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{10.25325801545149, -5.207564287166954}, 
           0.10102143756118451],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1908.10379\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sever Amit\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nikolay Gromov, Amit Sever\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Holographic Dual of Strongly \\\\gamma-deformed N=4 \
SYM Theory:\\n  Derivation, Generalization, Integrability and Discrete \
Reparametrization\\n  Symmetry\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages, 11 figures. v2: references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2020)035\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CERN-TH-2019-144\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP quant-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, we constructed the first-principle derivation \
of the holographic\\ndual of N=4 SYM in the double-scaled \
$\\\\gamma$-deformed limit directly from the\\nCFT side. The dual fishchain \
model is a novel integrable chain of particles in\\nAdS5. It can be viewed as \
a discretized string and revives earlier string-bit\\napproaches. The \
original derivation was restricted to the operators built out\\nof one of two \
types of scalar fields. In this paper, we extend our results to\\nthe general \
operators having any number of scalars of both types, except for a\\nvery \
special case when their numbers are equal. Interestingly, the \
extended\\nmodel reveals a new discrete reparametrization symmetry of the \
\\\"world-sheet\\\",\\npreserving all integrals of motion. We use \
integrability to formulate a closed\\nsystem of equations, which allows us to \
solve for the spectrum of the model in\\nfull generality, and present \
non-perturbative numerical results. We show that\\nour results are in \
agreement with the Asymptotic Bethe Ansatz of the fishnet\\nmodel up to the \
wrapping order at weak coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 27 Aug 2019 18:00:07 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 29 Aug 2019 15:24:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-03-18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Gromov\"", ",", "\"Nikolay\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sever\"", ",", "\"Amit\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
