         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1908.10379", "submitter" -> "Sever Amit", "authors" -> 
            "Nikolay Gromov, Amit Sever", "title" -> 
            "The Holographic Dual of Strongly \\gamma-deformed N=4 SYM \
Theory:\n  Derivation, Generalization, Integrability and Discrete \
Reparametrization\n  Symmetry", "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, 11 figures. v2: references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP02(2020)035", "report-no" -> 
            "CERN-TH-2019-144", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP quant-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently, we constructed the first-principle derivation of the \
holographic\ndual of N=4 SYM in the double-scaled $\\gamma$-deformed limit \
directly from the\nCFT side. The dual fishchain model is a novel integrable \
chain of particles in\nAdS5. It can be viewed as a discretized string and \
revives earlier string-bit\napproaches. The original derivation was \
restricted to the operators built out\nof one of two types of scalar fields. \
In this paper, we extend our results to\nthe general operators having any \
number of scalars of both types, except for a\nvery special case when their \
numbers are equal. Interestingly, the extended\nmodel reveals a new discrete \
reparametrization symmetry of the \"world-sheet\",\npreserving all integrals \
of motion. We use integrability to formulate a closed\nsystem of equations, \
which allows us to solve for the spectrum of the model in\nfull generality, \
and present non-perturbative numerical results. We show that\nour results are \
in agreement with the Asymptotic Bethe Ansatz of the fishnet\nmodel up to the \
wrapping order at weak coupling.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 27 Aug 2019 18:00:07 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 29 Aug 2019 15:24:10 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-03-18", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Gromov", "Nikolay", ""}, {
              "Sever", "Amit", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{7.859253334430025, -8.086137473019631}, 
           0.10102143756118451],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1909.00697\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Calum Milloy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Giulio Falcioni, Einan Gardi and Calum Milloy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Relating amplitude and PDF factorisation through \
Wilson-line geometries\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages, 5 figures; references added, typos fixed, \
journal version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP11(2019)100\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2019)100\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study long-distance singularities governing \
different physical quantities\\ninvolving massless partons in perturbative \
QCD by using factorisation in terms\\nof Wilson-line correlators. By \
isolating the process-independent hard-collinear\\nsingularities from quark \
and gluon form factors, and identifying these with the\\nones governing the \
elastic limit of the perturbative Parton Distribution\\nFunctions (PDFs) -- $\
\\\\delta(1-x)$ in the large-$x$ limit of DGLAP splitting\\nfunctions -- we \
extract the anomalous dimension controlling soft singularities\\nof the PDFs, \
verifying that it admits Casimir scaling. We then perform an\\nindependent \
diagrammatic computation of the latter using its definition in\\nterms of \
Wilson lines, confirming explicitly the above result through two\\nloops. By \
comparing our eikonal PDF calculation to that of the eikonal form\\nfactor by \
Erdogan and Sterman and the classical computation of the \
closed\\nparallelogram by Korchemsky and Korchemskaya, a consistent picture \
emerges\\nwhereby all singularities emerge in diagrammatic configurations \
localised at\\nthe cusps or along lightlike lines, but where distinct \
contributions to the\\nanomalous dimensions are associated with finite \
(closed) lightlike segments as\\ncompared to infinite (open) ones. Both are \
relevant for resumming large\\nlogarithms in physical quantities, notably the \
anomalous dimension controlling\\nDrell-Yan or Higgs production near \
threshold on the one hand, and the gluon\\nRegge trajectory controlling the \
high-energy limit of partonic scattering on\\nthe other.\\n\""}]}, {
