               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Efficient and powerful approaches to the computation of \
correlation functions\\ninvolving determinant, sub-determinant and permanent \
operators, as well as\\ntraces, have recently been developed in the setting \
of ${\\\\cal N}=4$ super\\nYang-Mills theory. In this article we show that \
they can be extended to ABJM\\nand ABJ theory. After making use of a novel \
identity which follows from\\ncharacter orthogonality, an integral \
representation of certain projection\\noperators used to define Schur \
polynomials is given. This integral\\nrepresentation provides an effective \
description of the correlation functions\\nof interest. The resulting \
effective descriptions have ${1\\\\over N}$ as the loop\\ncounting parameter, \
strongly suggesting their relevance for holography.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
