correlation functions\ninvolving determinant, sub-determinant and permanent \
operators, as well as\ntraces, have recently been developed in the setting of \
${\\cal N}=4$ super\nYang-Mills theory. In this article we show that they can \
be extended to ABJM\nand ABJ theory. After making use of a novel identity \
which follows from\ncharacter orthogonality, an integral representation of \
