                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider space discretizations of the matrix \
Zakharov-Shabat AKNS scheme,\\nin particular the discrete matrix non-linear \
Scrhr\\\\\\\"odinger (DNLS) model, and\\nthe matrix generalization of the \
Ablowitz-Ladik (AL) model, which is the more\\nwidely acknowledged \
discretization. We focus on the derivation of solutions via\\nlocal Darboux \
transforms for both discretizations, and we derive novel\\nsolutions via \
generic solutions of the associated discrete linear equations.\\nThe \
continuum analogue is also discussed, and as an example we \
identify\\nsolutions of the matrix NLS equation in terms of the heat kernel. \
In this frame\\nwe also derive a discretization of the Burgers equation via \
the analogue of the\\nCole-Hopf transform. Using the basic Darboux transforms \
for each scheme we\\nidentify both matrix DNLS-like and AL hierarchies, i.e. \
we extract the\\nassociated Lax pairs, via the dressing process. We also \
discuss the global\\nDarboux transform, which is the discrete analogue of the \
integral transform,\\nthrough the discrete Gelfand-Levitan-Marchenko (GLM) \
equation. The derivation\\nof the discrete matrix GLM equation and associated \
solutions are also presented\\ntogether with explicit linearizations. \
Particular emphasis is given in the\\ndiscretization schemes, i.e. \
forward/backward in the discrete matrix DNLS\\nscheme versus symmetric in the \
discrete matrix AL model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
