Cole-Hopf transform. Using the basic Darboux transforms for each scheme we\n\
identify both matrix DNLS-like and AL hierarchies, i.e. we extract the\n\
associated Lax pairs, via the dressing process. We also discuss the global\n\
Darboux transform, which is the discrete analogue of the integral transform,\n\
through the discrete Gelfand-Levitan-Marchenko (GLM) equation. The derivation\
\nof the discrete matrix GLM equation and associated solutions are also \
presented\ntogether with explicit linearizations. Particular emphasis is \
given in the\ndiscretization schemes, i.e. forward/backward in the discrete \
matrix DNLS\nscheme versus symmetric in the discrete matrix AL model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 2 Oct 2019 13:55:10 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 18 Oct 2019 16:56:39 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 10 May 2020 11:59:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-07-16", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Doikou", "Anastasia", ""}, {
              "Sklaveniti", "Spyridoula", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
