 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The $T\\\\bar{T}$ deformation of a supersymmetric \
two-dimensional theory\\npreserves the original supersymmetry. Moreover, in \
several interesting cases\\nthe deformed theory possesses additional \
non-linearly realized supersymmetries.\\nWe show this for certain \
$\\\\mathcal N =(2,2)$ models in two dimensions, where we\\nobserve an \
intriguing similarity with known $\\\\mathcal N=1 $ models in \
four\\ndimensions. This suggests that higher-dimensional models with \
non-linearly\\nrealized supersymmetries might also be obtained from \
$T\\\\bar{T}$-like flow\\nequations. We show that in four dimensions this is \
indeed the case for\\n$\\\\mathcal N=1 $ Born-Infeld theory, as well as for \
the Goldstino action for\\nspontaneously broken $\\\\mathcal N=1 $ \
supersymmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
