           "id" -> "1910.05741", "submitter" -> "Jung Hun Lee", "authors" -> 
            "Chanyong Park, Jung Hun Lee", "title" -> 
            "Exotic RG Flow of Entanglement Entropy", "comments" -> 
            "20 pages, 9 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys. Rev. D 101, 086008 (2020)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.101.086008", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper, we holographically study the renormalization \
group (RG) flow\nin a three-dimensional Einstein-dilaton gravity with a \
potential permitting\nseveral types of the RG flow with nontrivial \
beta-functions. By using the\nintrinsic parameter of the potential, we \
classify possible holographic RG flows\nand examine their physical features. \
Using the Ryu-Takayanagi formulation,\nfurthermore, we investigate how the \
$c$-function of the entanglement entropy\nbehaves along the RG flow \
numerically. We show that the entanglement\n$c$-function monotonically \
decreases even in the cases with a nontrivial\nbeta-function. For checking \
the consistency, we also compare the result of the\nentanglement entropy with \
the $c$-function derived from the holographic\nrenormalization procedure.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 13 Oct 2019 12:39:43 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-04-15", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Park", "Chanyong", ""}, {
              "Lee", "Jung Hun", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
