                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lorenzo Bianchi, Valentina Forini, Bj\\\\\\\"orn Leder, \
Philipp T\\\\\\\"opfer,\\n  Edoardo Vescovi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"New linearization and reweighting for simulations of \
string sigma-model\\n  on the lattice\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v1: 9 figures, 27 pages of which the first 9 overlap with \
Proceedings\\n  in arxiv:1702.02005; v2: cosmetic modification of one plot; \
v3: it matches\\n  the version published in JHEP (modified introduction and \
abstract)\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2020)174\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"HU-EP-19/29, Imperial-TP-EV-2019-04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-lat\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the discretized worldsheet of Type IIB strings \
in the\\nGubser-Klebanov-Polyakov background in a new setup, which eliminates \
a complex\\nphase previously detected in the fermionic determinant. A sign \
ambiguity\\nremains, which a study of the fermionic spectrum shows to be \
related to\\nYukawa-like terms, including those present in the original \
Lagrangian before\\nthe linearization standard in a lattice QFT approach. \
Monte Carlo simulations\\nare performed in a large region of the parameter \
space, where the sign problem\\nstarts becoming severe and instabilities \
appear due to the zero eigenvalues of\\nthe fermionic operator. To face these \
problems, simulations are conducted using\\nthe absolute value of a fermionic \
Pfaffian obtained introducing a small\\ntwisted-mass term, acting as an \
infrared regulator, into the action. The sign\\nof the Pfaffian and the low \
modes of the quadratic fermionic operator are then\\ntaken into account by a \
reweighting procedure of which we discuss the impact on\\nthe measurement of \
the observables. In this setup we study bosonic and\\nfermionic correlators \
and observe a divergence in the latter, which we argue -\\nalso via a \
one-loop analysis in lattice perturbation theory - to originate from\\nthe \
U(1)-breaking of our Wilson-like discretization for the fermionic \
sector.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
