            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider current-current deformations that generalise \
$T\\bar{T}$ ones, and\nshow that they may be also introduced for integrable \
spin chains. In analogy\nwith the integrable QFT setup, we define the \
deformation as a modification of\nthe S matrix in the Bethe equations. Using \
results by Bargheer, Beisert and\nLoebbert we show that the deforming \
operator is composite and constructed out\nof two currents on the lattice; \
its expectation value factorises like for\n$T\\bar{T}$. Such a deformation \
may be considered for any combination of charges\nthat preserve the model's \
integrable structure.\n", 
