            "  This review describes a link between Lax operators, embedded \
surfaces and\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz equations for integrable quantum \
field theories.\nThis surprising connection between classical and quantum \
models is undoubtedly\none of the most striking discoveries that emerged from \
the off-critical\ngeneralisation of the ODE/IM correspondence, which \
initially involved only\nconformal invariant quantum field theories. We will \
mainly focus of the KdV and\nsinh-Gordon models. However, various aspects of \
other interesting systems, such\nas affine Toda field theories and non-linear \
sigma models, will be mentioned.\nWe also discuss the implications of these \
ideas in the AdS/CFT context,\ninvolving minimal surfaces and Wilson loops. \
This work is a follow-up of the\nODE/IM review published more than ten years \
ago by JPA, before the discovery of\nits off-critical generalisation and the \
corresponding geometrical\ninterpretation. (Partially based on lectures given \
at the Young Researchers\nIntegrability School 2017, in Dublin.)\n", 
