               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ian Moult, Gherardo Vita and Kai Yan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Subleading Power Resummation of Rapidity Logarithms: The \
Energy-Energy\\n  Correlator in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages, a small number of figures. v2: fixed minor \
typos, journal\\n  version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2020)005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"MIT-CTP 5162, MPP-2019-243\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive and solve renormalization group equations \
that allow for the\\nresummation of subleading power rapidity logarithms. Our \
equations involve\\noperator mixing into a new class of operators, which we \
term the \\\"rapidity\\nidentity operators\\\", that will generically appear \
at subleading power in\\nproblems involving both rapidity and virtuality \
scales. To illustrate our\\nformalism, we analytically solve these equations \
to resum the power suppressed\\nlogarithms appearing in the back-to-back \
(double light cone) limit of the\\nEnergy-Energy Correlator (EEC) in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}$=4 super-Yang-Mills. These\\nlogarithms can also be extracted \
to $\\\\mathcal{O}(\\\\alpha_s^3)$ from a recent\\nperturbative calculation, \
and we find perfect agreement to this order. Instead\\nof the standard \
Sudakov exponential, our resummed result for the subleading\\npower \
logarithms is expressed in terms of Dawson's integral, with an \
argument\\nrelated to the cusp anomalous dimension. We call this functional \
form \\\"Dawson's\\nSudakov\\\". Our formalism is widely applicable for the \
resummation of subleading\\npower rapidity logarithms in other more \
phenomenologically relevant\\nobservables, such as the EEC in QCD, the $p_T$ \
spectrum for color singlet boson\\nproduction at hadron colliders, and the \
resummation of power suppressed\\nlogarithms in the Regge limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
