            "Ian Moult, Gherardo Vita and Kai Yan", "title" -> 
            "Subleading Power Resummation of Rapidity Logarithms: The \
Energy-Energy\n  Correlator in $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM", "comments" -> 
            "32 pages, a small number of figures. v2: fixed minor typos, \
journal\n  version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP07(2020)005", "report-no" -> 
            "MIT-CTP 5162, MPP-2019-243", "categories" -> "hep-ph hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We derive and solve renormalization group equations that allow \
for the\nresummation of subleading power rapidity logarithms. Our equations \
involve\noperator mixing into a new class of operators, which we term the \
\"rapidity\nidentity operators\", that will generically appear at subleading \
power in\nproblems involving both rapidity and virtuality scales. To \
illustrate our\nformalism, we analytically solve these equations to resum the \
power suppressed\nlogarithms appearing in the back-to-back (double light \
cone) limit of the\nEnergy-Energy Correlator (EEC) in $\\mathcal{N}$=4 \
super-Yang-Mills. These\nlogarithms can also be extracted to \
$\\mathcal{O}(\\alpha_s^3)$ from a recent\nperturbative calculation, and we \
find perfect agreement to this order. Instead\nof the standard Sudakov \
exponential, our resummed result for the subleading\npower logarithms is \
expressed in terms of Dawson's integral, with an argument\nrelated to the \
cusp anomalous dimension. We call this functional form \"Dawson's\nSudakov\". \
Our formalism is widely applicable for the resummation of subleading\npower \
rapidity logarithms in other more phenomenologically relevant\nobservables, \
such as the EEC in QCD, the $p_T$ spectrum for color singlet boson\n\
production at hadron colliders, and the resummation of power suppressed\n\
logarithms in the Regge limit.\n", 
