               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marco Bill\\\\'o\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Emanuele Beratto, Marco Billo', Michele Caselle\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the $T\\\\bar T$ deformation of the compactified boson \
and its\\n  interpretation in Lattice Gauge Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, 2 figures. V2: expanded comments in sections \
2.2, 2.3 and 4\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 102, 014504 (2020)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.102.014504\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-lat\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the effective string description of space-like \
Polyakov loop\\ncorrelators at finite temperature with the goal of describing \
the behaviour of\\nthe space--like string tension in the vicinity of the \
deconfinement transition.\\nTo this end we construct the partition function \
of the Nambu-Goto effective\\nstring theory in presence of a compact \
transverse direction of length $L$ equal\\nto the inverse temperature. We \
then show that, under particular conditions, our\\nresult can be interpreted \
as the partition function of the $T\\\\bar T$\\ndeformation of the 2d quantum \
field theory describing a compactified bosonic\\nfield and that this mapping \
allows a deeper insight on the behaviour of the\\nspace-like observables of \
the theory. In particular we show, by imposing that\\nthe spectrum of the \
model obeys the inviscid Burgers equation, that the $T\\\\bar\\nT$ \
deformations follow well defined trajectories in the parameter \
space\\n$(\\\\sigma,L)$ of the model, where $\\\\sigma$ is the string \
tension, which are\\ncharacterized by a constant value of the dimensionless \
compactification radius\\n$\\\\rho=L\\\\sqrt{\\\\sigma/2\\\\pi}$. We discuss \
the potential usefulness of these\\nresults for studying the space--like \
string tension of the underlying Lattice\\nGauge Theory and its behaviour \
across the deconfinement transition.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
