           "id" -> "1912.08654", "submitter" -> "Marco Bill\\'o", "authors" -> 
            "Emanuele Beratto, Marco Billo', Michele Caselle", "title" -> 
            "On the $T\\bar T$ deformation of the compactified boson and its\n\
  interpretation in Lattice Gauge Theory", "comments" -> 
            "28 pages, 2 figures. V2: expanded comments in sections 2.2, 2.3 \
and 4", "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. D 102, 014504 (2020)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.102.014504", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th hep-lat", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the effective string description of space-like \
Polyakov loop\ncorrelators at finite temperature with the goal of describing \
the behaviour of\nthe space--like string tension in the vicinity of the \
deconfinement transition.\nTo this end we construct the partition function of \
the Nambu-Goto effective\nstring theory in presence of a compact transverse \
direction of length $L$ equal\nto the inverse temperature. We then show that, \
under particular conditions, our\nresult can be interpreted as the partition \
function of the $T\\bar T$\ndeformation of the 2d quantum field theory \
describing a compactified bosonic\nfield and that this mapping allows a \
deeper insight on the behaviour of the\nspace-like observables of the theory. \
In particular we show, by imposing that\nthe spectrum of the model obeys the \
inviscid Burgers equation, that the $T\\bar\nT$ deformations follow well \
defined trajectories in the parameter space\n$(\\sigma,L)$ of the model, \
where $\\sigma$ is the string tension, which are\ncharacterized by a constant \
value of the dimensionless compactification radius\n\
$\\rho=L\\sqrt{\\sigma/2\\pi}$. We discuss the potential usefulness of these\n\
results for studying the space--like string tension of the underlying Lattice\
\nGauge Theory and its behaviour across the deconfinement transition.\n", 
