                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study numerically the ODE/IM correspondence for \
untwisted affine Lie\\nalgebras associated with simple Lie algebras including \
exceptional type. We\\nconsider the linear problem obtained from the massless \
limit of that of the\\nmodified affine Toda field equation. We found that the \
Q-functions in\\nintegrable models are expressed as the inner product of the \
solution of the\\ndual linear problem and the subdominant solution of the \
linear problem. Using\\nCheng's algorithm to obtain the solution of the \
linear problem, we can\\ndetermine efficiently the zeros of the Q-function, \
which is known to provide\\nthe solutions of the Bethe ansatz equations. We \
calculate the zeros\\nnumerically, which are shown to agree with the results \
from the Non-Linear\\nIntegral Equations for simply-laced affine Lie algebras \
including the\\nexceptional type. By the folding procedure of the Dynkin \
diagrams of\\nsimply-laced Lie algebras, we also find the correspondence for \
the linear\\nproblem of the non-simply-laced affine Lie algebras.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
