            "  We study numerically the ODE/IM correspondence for untwisted \
affine Lie\nalgebras associated with simple Lie algebras including \
exceptional type. We\nconsider the linear problem obtained from the massless \
limit of that of the\nmodified affine Toda field equation. We found that the \
Q-functions in\nintegrable models are expressed as the inner product of the \
solution of the\ndual linear problem and the subdominant solution of the \
linear problem. Using\nCheng's algorithm to obtain the solution of the linear \
problem, we can\ndetermine efficiently the zeros of the Q-function, which is \
known to provide\nthe solutions of the Bethe ansatz equations. We calculate \
