 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The 1/2-BPS Wilson loop in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory\\nis an important and well-studied example \
of conformal defect. In particular,\\nmuch work has been done for the \
correlation functions of operator insertions on\\nthe Wilson loop in the \
fundamental representation. In this paper, we extend\\nsuch analyses to \
Wilson loops in the large-rank symmetric and antisymmetric\\nrepresentations, \
which correspond to probe D3 and D5 branes with $AdS_2 \\\\times\\nS^2$ and \
$AdS_2 \\\\times S^4$ worldvolume geometries, ending at the \
$AdS_5$\\nboundary along a one-dimensional contour. We first compute the \
correlation\\nfunctions of protected scalar insertions from supersymmetric \
localization, and\\nobtain a representation in terms of multiple integrals \
that are similar to the\\neigenvalue integrals of the random matrix, but with \
important differences.\\nUsing ideas from the Fermi Gas formalism and the \
Clustering method, we evaluate\\ntheir large $N$ limit exactly as a function \
of the 't Hooft coupling. The\\nresults are given by simple integrals of \
polynomials that resemble the\\n$Q$-functions of the Quantum Spectral Curve, \
with integration measures\\ndepending on the number of insertions. Next, we \
study the correlation functions\\nof fluctuations on the probe D3 and D5 \
branes in AdS. We compute a selection of\\nthree- and four-point functions \
from perturbation theory on the D-branes, and\\nshow that they agree with the \
results of localization when restricted to\\nsupersymmetric kinematics. We \
also explain how the difference of the internal\\ngeometries of the D3 and D5 \
branes manifests itself in the localization\\ncomputation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
