 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Casimir scaling function characterising the \
ground-state energy of the\\nsine-Gordon model in a finite circle has been \
studied analytically and\\nnumerically both in the repulsive and attractive \
regimes. The numerical\\ncalculations of the scaling function at several \
values of the coupling constant\\nwere performed by the iterative solution of \
the Destri-de Vega nonlinear\\nintegral equations. The ultraviolet \
asymptotics of the Casimir scaling\\nfunctions was calculated by perturbative \
solution of these equations, and by\\nmeans of the perturbed conformal \
field-theory technique, and compared with\\nnumerical results.\\n\""}]}, {
