           "id" -> "2008.04336", "submitter" -> "Rouven Frassek", "authors" -> 
            "Gwena\\\"el Ferrando, Rouven Frassek, Vladimir Kazakov", "title" -> 
            "QQ-system and Weyl-type transfer matrices in integrable SO(2r) \
spin\n  chains", "comments" -> 
            "42 pages, 9 Figures; v2: typos fixed, references added; v3:\n  \
references added, section 9 improved", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP02(2021)193", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We propose the full system of Baxter Q-functions (QQ-system) \
for the\nintegrable spin chains with the symmetry of the $D_r$ Lie algebra. \
We use this\nQQ-system to derive new Weyl-type formulas expressing transfer \
matrices in all\nsymmetric and antisymmetric (fundamental) representations \
through $r+1$ basic\nQ-functions. Our functional relations are consistent \
with the Q-operators\nproposed recently by one of the authors and verified \
explicitly on the level of\noperators at small finite length.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 10 Aug 2020 18:02:12 GMT"}, {
