               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008.10597\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Hongfei Shu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Simon Ekhammar, Hongfei Shu, Dmytro Volin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Extended systems of Baxter Q-functions and fused flags I: \
simply-laced\\n  case\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Typos and mistakes corrected, references added, improved \
clarity of\\n  text and simplified sign conventions\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph hep-th math.MP math.QA nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The spectrum of integrable models is often encoded in \
terms of commuting\\nfunctions of a spectral parameter that satisfy \
functional relations. We propose\\nto describe this commutative algebra in a \
covariant way by means of the\\nextended Q-system that comprise Q-vectors in \
each of the fundamental\\nrepresentations of the (Langlands dual of) the \
underlying symmetry algebra.\\nThese Q-vectors turn out to parameterise a \
collection of complete flags which\\nare fused with one another in a \
particular way. We show that the fused flag is\\na finite-difference oper in \
a particular gauge, explicit identification depends\\non a choice of a \
Coxeter element.\\n  The paper considers the case of simple Lie algebras with \
a simply-laced\\nDynkin diagram. For the $A_r$ series, the construction \
coincides with already\\nknown results in the literature. We apply the \
proposed formalism to the case of\\nthe $D_r$ series and the exceptional \
algebras $E_r$, $r=6,7,8$. In particular,\\nwe solve Hirota bilinear \
equations in terms of Q-functions and give the\\nexplicit character solution \
of the extended Q-system in the $D_r$ case. We also\\nshow how to build up \
the extended Q-system of $D_r$ type starting either from\\nvectors, by a \
procedure similar to the $A_r$ scenario which however constructs\\na fused \
flag of isotropic spaces, or from pure spinors, \\\\via fused \
Fierz\\nrelations.\\n  Finally, for the case of rational, trigonometric, and \
elliptic spin chains,\\nwe propose an explicit ansatz for the analytic \
structure of Q-functions of the\\nextended Q-system. We conjecture that the \
extended Q-system constrained in such\\na way is always in bijection with the \
Bethe algebra of commuting transfer\\nmatrices of these models and moreover \
can be used to show that the Bethe\\nalgebra has a simple joint \
spectrum.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 24 Aug 2020 17:59:23 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 6 Jan 2021 19:47:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2021-01-11\""}]}, {
