           "id" -> "2008.10597", "submitter" -> "Hongfei Shu", "authors" -> 
            "Simon Ekhammar, Hongfei Shu, Dmytro Volin", "title" -> 
            "Extended systems of Baxter Q-functions and fused flags I: \
simply-laced\n  case", "comments" -> 
            "Typos and mistakes corrected, references added, improved clarity \
of\n  text and simplified sign conventions", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "math-ph hep-th math.MP math.QA nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The spectrum of integrable models is often encoded in terms of \
commuting\nfunctions of a spectral parameter that satisfy functional \
relations. We propose\nto describe this commutative algebra in a covariant \
way by means of the\nextended Q-system that comprise Q-vectors in each of the \
fundamental\nrepresentations of the (Langlands dual of) the underlying \
symmetry algebra.\nThese Q-vectors turn out to parameterise a collection of \
complete flags which\nare fused with one another in a particular way. We show \
that the fused flag is\na finite-difference oper in a particular gauge, \
explicit identification depends\non a choice of a Coxeter element.\n  The \
paper considers the case of simple Lie algebras with a simply-laced\nDynkin \
diagram. For the $A_r$ series, the construction coincides with already\nknown \
results in the literature. We apply the proposed formalism to the case of\n\
the $D_r$ series and the exceptional algebras $E_r$, $r=6,7,8$. In \
particular,\nwe solve Hirota bilinear equations in terms of Q-functions and \
give the\nexplicit character solution of the extended Q-system in the $D_r$ \
case. We also\nshow how to build up the extended Q-system of $D_r$ type \
starting either from\nvectors, by a procedure similar to the $A_r$ scenario \
which however constructs\na fused flag of isotropic spaces, or from pure \
spinors, \\via fused Fierz\nrelations.\n  Finally, for the case of rational, \
trigonometric, and elliptic spin chains,\nwe propose an explicit ansatz for \
the analytic structure of Q-functions of the\nextended Q-system. We \
conjecture that the extended Q-system constrained in such\na way is always in \
bijection with the Bethe algebra of commuting transfer\nmatrices of these \
models and moreover can be used to show that the Bethe\nalgebra has a simple \
joint spectrum.\n", 
