                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The relation between supersymmetric gauge theories in \
four dimensions and\\nquantum spin systems is exploited to find an explicit \
formula for the Jost\\nfunction of the $N$ site $\\\\mathfrak{sl}_{2}$ $XXX$ \
spin chain (for infinite\\ndimensional complex spin representations), as well \
as the $SL_N$ Gaudin system,\\nwhich reduces, in a limiting case, to that of \
the $N$-particle periodic Toda\\nchain. Using the non-perturbative \
Dyson-Schwinger equations of the\\nsupersymmetric gauge theory we establish \
relations between the spin chain\\ncommuting Hamiltonians with the twisted \
chiral ring of gauge theory. Along the\\nway we explore the chamber \
dependence of the supersymmetric partition function,\\nalso the expectation \
value of the surface defects, giving new evidence for the\\nAGT \
conjecture.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
