                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the large momentum limit of the monster \
potentials of\\nBazhanov-Lukyanov-Zamolodchikov, which -- according to the \
ODE/IM\\ncorrespondence -- should correspond to excited states of the Quantum \
KdV model.\\n  We prove that the poles of these potentials asymptotically \
condensate about\\nthe complex equilibria of the ground state potential, and \
we express the\\nleading correction to such asymptotics in terms of the roots \
of Wronskians of\\nHermite polynomials.\\n  This allows us to associate to \
each partition of $N$ a unique monster\\npotential with $N$ roots, of which \
we compute the spectrum. As a consequence,\\nwe prove -- up to a few \
mathematical technicalities -- that, fixed an integer\\n$N$, the number of \
monster potentials with $N$ roots coincides with the number\\nof integer \
partitions of $N$, which is the dimension of the level $N$ subspace\\nof the \
quantum KdV model. In striking accordance with the \
ODE/IM\\ncorrespondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
