         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2009.14638", "submitter" -> "Davide Masoero", "authors" -> 
            "Riccardo Conti and Davide Masoero", "title" -> 
            "Counting monster potentials", "comments" -> 
            "39 pages + Appendix, 8 figures. Minor modifications", 
            "journal-ref" -> 
            "Journal of High Energy Physics 2021.2 (2021): 1-60", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP02(2021)059", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "math-ph hep-th math.CA math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the large momentum limit of the monster potentials of\
\nBazhanov-Lukyanov-Zamolodchikov, which -- according to the ODE/IM\n\
correspondence -- should correspond to excited states of the Quantum KdV \
model.\n  We prove that the poles of these potentials asymptotically \
condensate about\nthe complex equilibria of the ground state potential, and \
we express the\nleading correction to such asymptotics in terms of the roots \
of Wronskians of\nHermite polynomials.\n  This allows us to associate to each \
partition of $N$ a unique monster\npotential with $N$ roots, of which we \
compute the spectrum. As a consequence,\nwe prove -- up to a few mathematical \
technicalities -- that, fixed an integer\n$N$, the number of monster \
potentials with $N$ roots coincides with the number\nof integer partitions of \
$N$, which is the dimension of the level $N$ subspace\nof the quantum KdV \
model. In striking accordance with the ODE/IM\ncorrespondence.\n", 
