            "  We show that $T \\bar T, J \\bar T$ and $J T_a$ - deformed \
classical CFTs\npossess an infinite set of symmetries that take the form of a \
field-dependent\ngeneralization of two-dimensional conformal transformations. \
If, in addition,\nthe seed CFTs possess an affine $U(1)$ symmetry, we show \
that it also survives\nin the deformed theories, again in a field-dependent \
form. These symmetries can\nbe understood as the infinitely-extended \
conformal and $U(1)$ symmetries of the\nunderlying two-dimensional CFT, seen \
through the prism of the \"dynamical\ncoordinates\" that characterise each of \
these deformations. We also compute the\nPoisson bracket algebra of the \
associated conserved charges, using the\nHamiltonian formalism. In the case \
of the $J \\bar T$ and $J T_a$ deformations,\nwe find two copies of a \
functional Witt - Kac-Moody algebra. In the case of the\n$T \\bar T$ \
deformation, we show that it is also possible to obtain two\ncommuting copies \
of the Witt algebra.\n", 
