               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we first demonstrate explicitly that the \
new models of\\nintegrable nearest-neighbour Hamiltonians recently introduced \
in PRL 125 (2020)\\n031604 satisfy the so-called free fermion condition. This \
both implies that all\\nthese models are amenable to reformulations as free \
fermion theories, and\\nestablishes the universality of this condition. We \
explicitly recast the\\ntransfer matrix in free fermion form for arbitrary \
number of sites in the\\n6-vertex sector, and on two sites in the 8-vertex \
sector, using a Bogoliubov\\ntransformation. We then put this observation to \
use in lower-dimensional\\ninstances of AdS/CFT integrable R-matrices, \
specifically pure Ramond-Ramond\\nmassless and massive AdS_3, mixed-flux \
relativistic AdS_3 and massless AdS_2.\\nWe also attack the class of models \
akin to AdS_5 with our free fermion\\nmachinery. In all cases we use the free \
fermion realisation to greatly simplify\\nand reinterpret a wealth of known \
results, and to provide a very suggestive\\nreformulation of the spectral \
problem in all these situations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
