                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fedor Levkovich-Maslyuk\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nikolay Gromov, Fedor Levkovich-Maslyuk, Paul Ryan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Determinant Form of Correlators in High Rank Integrable \
Spin Chains via\\n  Separation of Variables\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"85 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2021)169\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we take further steps towards developing \
the separation of\\nvariables program for integrable spin chains with gl(N) \
symmetry. By finding,\\nfor the first time, the matrix elements of the SoV \
measure explicitly we were\\nable to compute correlation functions and wave \
function overlaps in a simple\\ndeterminant form. In particular, we show how \
an overlap between on-shell and\\noff-shell algebraic Bethe states can be \
written as a determinant. Another\\nresult, particularly useful for AdS/CFT \
applications, is an overlap between two\\nBethe states with different twists, \
which also takes a determinant form in our\\napproach. Our results also \
extend our previous works in collaboration with A.\\nCavaglia and D. Volin to \
general values of the spin, including the SoV\\nconstruction in the \
higher-rank non-compact case for the first time.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
