            "  We study stress-tensor correlators in the $T\\bar{T}$-deformed \
conformal field\ntheories in two dimensions. Using the random geometry \
approach to the\n$T\\bar{T}$ deformation, we develop a geometrical method to \
compute\nstress-tensor correlators. More specifically, we derive the \
$T\\bar{T}$\ndeformation to the Polyakov-Liouville conformal anomaly action \
and calculate\nthree and four-point correlators to the first-order in the \
$T\\bar{T}$\ndeformation from the deformed Polyakov-Liouville action. The \
results are\nchecked against the standard conformal perturbation theory \
computation and we\nfurther check consistency with the $T\\bar{T}$-deformed \
operator product\nexpansions of the stress tensor. A salient feature of the \
$T\\bar{T}$-deformed\nstress-tensor correlators is a logarithmic correction \
that is absent in two and\nthree-point functions but starts appearing in a \
four-point function.\n", 
