 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study perturbative renormalization of the composite \
operators in the\\n$T\\\\bar T$-deformed two-dimensional free field theories. \
The pattern of\\nrenormalization for the stress-energy tensor is different in \
the massive and\\nmassless cases. While in the latter case the canonical \
stress tensor is not\\nrenormalized up to high order in the perturbative \
expansion, in the massive\\ntheory there are induced counterterms at linear \
order. For a massless theory\\nour results match the general formula derived \
recently in [1].\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
