                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the six-particle amplitude in planar \
$\\\\mathcal{N} = 4$ super\\nYang-Mills theory in the double scaling (DS) \
limit, the only nontrivial\\ncodimension-one boundary of its positive \
kinematic region. We construct the\\nrelevant function space, which is \
significantly constrained due to the extended\\nSteinmann relations, up to \
weight 13 in coproduct form, and up to weight 12 as\\nan explicit \
polylogarithmic representation. Expanding the latter in the\\ncollinear \
boundary of the DS limit, and using the Pentagon Operator \
Product\\nExpansion, we compute the non-divergent coefficient of a certain \
component of\\nthe Next-to-Maximally-Helicity-Violating amplitude through \
weight 12 and eight\\nloops. We also specialize our results to the \
overlapping origin limit,\\nobserving a general pattern for its leading \
divergences.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
