construct the\nrelevant function space, which is significantly constrained \
due to the extended\nSteinmann relations, up to weight 13 in coproduct form, \
and up to weight 12 as\nan explicit polylogarithmic representation. Expanding \
the latter in the\ncollinear boundary of the DS limit, and using the Pentagon \
Operator Product\nExpansion, we compute the non-divergent coefficient of a \
certain component of\nthe Next-to-Maximally-Helicity-Violating amplitude \
through weight 12 and eight\nloops. We also specialize our results to the \
overlapping origin limit,\nobserving a general pattern for its leading \
divergences.\n", 
