physics.optics\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The light-cone gauge approach to $T\\\\overline{T}$ \
deformed models is used to\\nderive the $T\\\\overline{T}$ deformed matrix \
nonlinear Schr\\\\\\\"odinger equation,\\nthe Landau--Lifshitz equation, and \
the Gardner equation. Properties of\\none-soliton solutions of the \
$T\\\\overline{T}$ deformed nonlinear Schr\\\\\\\"odinger\\nand Korteweg--de \
Vries equations are discussed in detail. The NLS soliton\\nexhibits the \
recently discussed phenomenon of widening/narrowing width of\\nparticles \
under the $T\\\\overline{T}$ deformation. However, whether the \
soliton's\\nsize is increasing or decreasing depends not only on the sign of \
the\\ndeformation parameter but also on soliton and potential parameters. The\
\\n$T\\\\overline{T}$ deformed KdV equation admits a one-parameter family \
of\\none-soliton solutions in addition to the usual velocity parameter. The \
extra\\nparameter modifies the properties of the soliton, in particular, it \
appears in\\nthe dispersion relation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
