            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2103.15800\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrea Cavagli\\\\`a\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Andrea Cavagli\\\\`a, Nikolay Gromov, Fedor \
Levkovich-Maslyuk\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Separation of Variables in AdS/CFT: Functional Approach \
for the Fishnet\\n  CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages + appendices, 5 figures. v2: references added, \
small changes\\n  to the text. Accepted for publication in JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2021)131\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The major simplification in a number of quantum \
integrable systems is the\\nexistence of special coordinates in which the \
eigenstates take a factorised\\nform. Despite many years of studies, the \
basis realising the separation of\\nvariables (SoV) remains unknown in N=4 \
SYM and similar models, even though it\\nis widely believed they are \
integrable. In this paper we initiate the SoV\\napproach for observables with \
nontrivial coupling dependence in a close cousin\\nof N=4 SYM - the fishnet \
4D CFT. We develop the functional SoV formalism in\\nthis theory, which \
allows us to compute non-perturbatively some nontrivial\\nobservables in a \
form suitable for numerical evaluation. We present some\\napplications of \
these methods. In particular, we discuss the possible SoV\\nstructure of the \
one-point correlators in presence of a defect, and write down\\na SoV-type \
expression for diagonal OPE coefficients involving an arbitrary\\nstate and \
the Lagrangian density operator. We believe that many of the findings\\nof \
this paper can be applied in the N=4 SYM case, as we speculate in the \
last\\npart of the article.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 29 Mar 2021 17:51:35 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 10 Jun 2021 12:55:02 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
