 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop an integrability-based framework to compute \
structure constants of\\ntwo sub-determinant operators and a single-trace \
non-BPS operator in ABJM\\ntheory in the planar limit. In this first paper, \
we study them at weak coupling\\nusing a relation to an integrable spin \
chain. We first develop a nested Bethe\\nansatz for an alternating SU(4) spin \
chain that describes single-trace\\noperators made out of scalar fields. We \
then apply it to the computation of the\\nstructure constants and show that \
they are given by overlaps between a Bethe\\neigenstate and a matrix product \
state. We conjecture that the determinant\\noperator corresponds to an \
integrable matrix product state and present a\\nclosed-form expression for \
the overlap, which resembles the so-called Gaudin\\ndeterminant. We also \
provide evidence for the integrability of general\\nsub-determinant \
operators. The techniques developed in this paper can be\\napplied to other \
quantities in ABJM theory including three-point functions of\\nsingle-trace \
operators.\\n\""}]}, {
