                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a model to implement and simulate different \
traffic-flow\\nconditions in terms of quantum graphs hosting an ($N$+1)-level \
dot at each\\nsite, which allows us to keep track of the type and of the \
destination of each\\nvehicle. By implementing proper Lindbladian local \
dissipators, we derive the\\nmaster equations that describe the traffic flow \
in our system. To show the\\nversatility and the reliability of our \
technique, we employ it to model\\ndifferent types of traffic flow (the \
symmetric three-way roundabout and the\\nthree-road intersection). \
Eventually, we successfully compare our predictions\\nwith results from \
classical models.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
