               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we derive from field theory a \
L\\\\\\\"uscher-formula, which gives\\nthe leading exponentially small in \
volume corrections to the 1-particle\\nform-factors in non-diagonally \
scattering integrable quantum field theories.\\nOur final formula is \
expressed in terms of appropriate expressions of 1- and\\n3-particle \
form-factors, and can be considered as the generalization of\\nprevious \
results obtained for diagonally scattering bosonic integrable quantum\\nfield \
theories. Since our formulas are also valid for fermions and operators\\nwith \
non-zero Lorentz-spin, we demonstrated our results in the Massive \
Thirring\\nModel, and checked our formula against 1-loop perturbation theory \
finding\\nperfect agreement.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
