            "\\'Arp\\'ad Heged\\H{u}s", "title" -> 
            "L\\\"uscher-corrections for 1-particle form-factors in \
non-diagonally\n  scattering integrable quantum field theories", "comments" -> 
            "28 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we derive from field theory a \
L\\\"uscher-formula, which gives\nthe leading exponentially small in volume \
corrections to the 1-particle\nform-factors in non-diagonally scattering \
integrable quantum field theories.\nOur final formula is expressed in terms \
of appropriate expressions of 1- and\n3-particle form-factors, and can be \
considered as the generalization of\nprevious results obtained for diagonally \
scattering bosonic integrable quantum\nfield theories. Since our formulas are \
also valid for fermions and operators\nwith non-zero Lorentz-spin, we \
demonstrated our results in the Massive Thirring\nModel, and checked our \
formula against 1-loop perturbation theory finding\nperfect agreement.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
