               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The encoding of all possible sets of Bethe equations \
for a spin chain with\\nSU(N|M) symmetry into a QQ-system calls for an \
expression of spin chain\\noverlaps entirely in terms of Q-functions. We take \
a significant step towards\\nderiving such a universal formula in the case of \
overlaps between Bethe\\neigenstates and integrable boundary states, of \
relevance for AdS/dCFT, by\\ndetermining the transformation properties of the \
overlaps under fermionic as\\nwell as bosonic dualities which allows us to \
move between any two descriptions\\nof the spin chain encoded in the \
QQ-system. An important part of our analysis\\ninvolves introducing a \
suitable regularization for singular Bethe root\\nconfigurations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
