                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph math.MP math.QA\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A unified framework for the Chevalley and equitable \
presentation of\\n$U_q(sl_2)$ is introduced. It is given in terms of a system \
of Freidel-Maillet\\ntype equations satisfied by a pair of quantum \
K-operators ${\\\\mathcal K}^\\\\pm$,\\nwhose entries are expressed in terms \
of either Chevalley or equitable\\ngenerators. The Hopf algebra structure is \
reconsidered in light of this unified\\nframework, and interwining relations \
for each pair of ${\\\\mathcal K}^\\\\pm$ are\\nobtained. A K-operator \
solving a spectral parameter dependent Freidel-Maillet\\ntype equation is \
also considered. Different specializations of this K-operator\\nare shown to \
admit a decomposition in terms of ${\\\\mathcal K}^\\\\pm$ of Chevalley\\nor \
equitable type. Explicit examples of K-matrices without/with \
spectral\\nparameter are derived by specializing the K-operators previously \
obtained.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
