of Freidel-Maillet\ntype equations satisfied by a pair of quantum K-operators \
${\\mathcal K}^\\pm$,\nwhose entries are expressed in terms of either \
Chevalley or equitable\ngenerators. The Hopf algebra structure is \
reconsidered in light of this unified\nframework, and interwining relations \
for each pair of ${\\mathcal K}^\\pm$ are\nobtained. A K-operator solving a \
spectral parameter dependent Freidel-Maillet\ntype equation is also \
