, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We shall interpret the null hexagonal Wilson loop (or, \
equivalently, six\\ngluon scattering amplitude) in 4D ${\\\\cal N}=4$ Super \
Yang-Mills, or, precisely,\\nan integral representation of its matrix part, \
via an ADHM-like instanton\\nconstruction. In this way, we can apply \
localisation techniques to obtain\\ncombinatorial expressions in terms of \
Young diagrams. Then, we use our general\\nformula to obtain explicit \
expressions in several explicit cases. In\\nparticular, we discuss those \
already available in the literature and find exact\\nagreement. Moreover, we \
are capable to determine explicitly the denominator\\n(poles) of the matrix \
part, and find some interesting recursion properties for\\nthe residues, as \
well.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
