                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study two integrable systems associated with the \
coupled NLS equation: the\\nintegrable defect system and the integrable \
boundary systems. Regarding the\\nfirst one, we present a type I defect \
condition, which is described by a\\nB\\\\\\\"{a}cklund transformation frozen \
at the defect location. For the resulting\\ndefect system, we prove its \
integrability both by showing the existence of an\\ninfinite set of conserved \
quantities and by implementing the classical\\n$r$-matrix method. Regarding \
the second one, we present some new integrable\\nboundary conditions for the \
coupled NLS equation by imposing suitable\\nreductions on the defect \
conditions. Our new boundary conditions, unlike the\\nusual boundary \
conditions (such as the Robin boundary), involve time\\nderivatives of the \
coupled NLS fields and are characterised by non constant\\n$K(\\\\lambda)$ \
matrices. We prove the integrability of our new boundary\\nconditions by \
using Sklyanin's approach.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
