               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Theresa Abl, Martin Sprenger\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exploring Reggeon bound states in strongly-coupled \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super\\n  Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages, 9 figures. v2: Added arguments regarding the \
uniqueness of\\n  crossing patterns, typos corrected. Matches version \
published in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. High Energ. Phys. 2022, 21 (2022)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2022)021\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The multi-Regge limit of scattering amplitudes in \
strongly-coupled\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills is described by the \
large mass limit of a set\\nof thermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA) equations. A \
non-trivial remainder function\\narises in this setup in certain kinematical \
regions due to excitations of the\\nTBA equations which appear during the \
analytic continuation into these\\nkinematical regions. So far, these \
analytic continuations were carried out on a\\ncase-by-case basis for the \
six- and seven-gluon remainder function. In this\\nnote, we show that the set \
of possible excitations appearing in any analytic\\ncontinuation in the \
multi-Regge limit for any number of particles is rather\\nconstrained. In \
particular, we show that the BFKL eigenvalue of any possible\\nReggeon bound \
state is a multiple of the two-Reggeon BFKL eigenvalue appearing\\nin the \
six-gluon case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
