                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present new integrable models of interacting \
spin-1/2 chains, which can be\\ninterpreted as hard rod deformations of the \
XXZ Heisenberg chains. The models\\nsupport multiple particle types: \
dynamical hard rods of length $\\\\ell$ and\\nparticles with lengths \
$\\\\ell'<\\\\ell$ that are immobile except for the\\ninteraction with the \
hard rods. We encounter a remarkable phenomenon in these\\ninteracting \
models: exact spectral degeneracies across different deformations\\nand \
volumes. The algebraic integrability of these systems is also treated \
using\\na recently developed formalism for medium range integrable spin \
chains. We\\npresent the detailed Bethe Ansatz solution for the case \
$\\\\ell=2$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
