            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2109.06164\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dmytro Volin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Simon Ekhammar, Dmytro Volin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Monodromy Bootstrap for SU(2|2) Quantum Spectral Curves: \
From Hubbard\\n  model to AdS3/CFT2\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages; substantial revision\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2022)192\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"UUITP-44/21, NORDITA 2021-090\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"math-ph hep-th math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a procedure to derive quantum spectral \
curves of AdS/CFT type by\\nrequiring that a specially designed analytic \
continuation around the branch\\npoint results in an automorphism of the \
underlying algebraic structure. In this\\nway we derive four new curves. Two \
are based on SU(2|2) symmetry, and we show\\nthat one of them, under the \
assumption of square root branch points, describes\\nHubbard model. Two more \
are based on SU(2|2) x SU(2|2). In the special subcase\\nof zero central \
charge, they both reduce to the unique nontrivial curve which\\nfurthermore \
has analytic properties compatible with PSU(1,1|2) x PSU(1,1|2)\\nreal form. \
A natural conjecture follows that this is the quantum spectral curve\\nof \
AdS/CFT integrable system with AdS3 x S3 x T4 background supported \
by\\nRR-flux. We support the conjecture by verifying its consistency with the\
\\nmassive sector of asymptotic Bethe equations in the large volume regime. \
For\\nthis spectral curve, it is compulsory that branch points are not of the \
square\\nroot type which qualitatively distinguishes it from the previously \
known cases.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 13 Sep 2021 17:58:44 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
