            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a study of the effective string that describes the \
infrared\ndynamics of SU(2) Yang-Mills theory in three dimensions. By \
combining\nhigh-precision lattice simulation results for Polyakov-loop \
correlators at\nfinite temperatures close to (and less than) the \
deconfinement one with the\nanalytical constraints from renormalization-group \
arguments, from the exact\nintegrability of the two-dimensional Ising model \
that describes the\nuniversality class of the critical point of the theory, \
from conformal\nperturbation theory, and from Lorentz invariance, we derive \
tight quantitative\nbounds on the corrections to the effective string action \
beyond the Nambu-Goto\napproximation. We show that these corrections are \
compatible with the\npredictions derived from a bootstrap analysis of the \
effective string theory,\nand have a value which does not allow to prove the \
Axionic String Ansatz for\nthis model\n", 
