            "  We exploit the recently proposed correspondence between \
gravitational\nperturbations and quantum Seiberg-Witten curves to compute the \
spectrum of\nquasi-normal modes of asymptotically flat Kerr Newman black \
holes and establish\ndetailed gauge/gravity dictionaries for a large class of \
black holes, D-branes\nand fuzzballs in diverse dimensions. QNM frequencies \
obtained from the quantum\nperiods of $SU(2)$ ${\\cal N}=2$ SYM with $N_f=3$ \
flavours are compared against\nnumerical results, WKB (eikonal) approximation \
and geodetic motion showing\nremarkable agreement. Starting from the master \
example relating quasi-normal\nmodes of Kerr-Newman black holes in AdS$_4$ to \
$SU(2)$ gauge theory with\n$N_f=4$, we illustrate the procedure for some \
simple toy-models that allow\nanalytic solutions. We also argue that the AGT \
version of the gauge/gravity\ncorrespondence may give precious hints as to \
the physical/geometric origin of\nthe quasi-normal modes/Seiberg-Witten \
connection and further elucidate\ninteresting properties (such as tidal Love \
numbers and grey-body factors) that\ncan help discriminating black holes from \
fuzzballs.\n", 
