               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2109.14280\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ana Lucia Retore Ph.D\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ana L. Retore\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Introduction to classical and quantum \
integrability\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v1: These notes were written for the lectures delivered \
at the school\\n  \\\"Integrability, Dualities and Deformations\\\", that ran \
from 23 to 27 August\\n  2021 in Santiago de Compostela and virtually. 61 \
pages, 10 figures, v2: I\\n  corrected typos, added a few comments and added \
several references\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/ac5a8e\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In these lecture notes we aim for a pedagogical \
introduction to both\\nclassical and quantum integrability. Starting from \
Liouville integrability and\\npassing through Lax pair and r-matrix we \
discuss the construction of the\\nconserved charges for classical integrable \
models taking as example the\\nharmonic oscillator. The construction of these \
charges for 2D integrable field\\ntheories is also discussed using a Lax \
connection and the Sine-Gordon model as\\nexample. On the quantum side, the \
XXZ spin chain is used to explain the\\nsystematic construction of the \
conserved charges starting from a quantum\\nR-matrix, solution of the quantum \
Yang-Baxter equation. The diagonalization of\\nthese charges is performed \
using the algebraic Bethe ansatz. At the end, the\\ninterpretation of the \
R-matrix as an S-matrix in a scattering process is also\\npresented. These \
notes were written for the lectures delivered at the \
school\\n\\\"Integrability, Dualities and Deformations\\\", that ran from 23 \
to 27 August 2021\\nin Santiago de Compostela and virtually.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
