           "id" -> "2109.14280", "submitter" -> "Ana Lucia Retore Ph.D", 
            "authors" -> "Ana L. Retore", "title" -> 
            "Introduction to classical and quantum integrability", "comments" -> 
            "v1: These notes were written for the lectures delivered at the \
school\n  \"Integrability, Dualities and Deformations\", that ran from 23 to \
27 August\n  2021 in Santiago de Compostela and virtually. 61 pages, 10 \
figures, v2: I\n  corrected typos, added a few comments and added several \
references", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8121/ac5a8e", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In these lecture notes we aim for a pedagogical introduction \
to both\nclassical and quantum integrability. Starting from Liouville \
integrability and\npassing through Lax pair and r-matrix we discuss the \
construction of the\nconserved charges for classical integrable models taking \
as example the\nharmonic oscillator. The construction of these charges for 2D \
integrable field\ntheories is also discussed using a Lax connection and the \
Sine-Gordon model as\nexample. On the quantum side, the XXZ spin chain is \
used to explain the\nsystematic construction of the conserved charges \
starting from a quantum\nR-matrix, solution of the quantum Yang-Baxter \
equation. The diagonalization of\nthese charges is performed using the \
algebraic Bethe ansatz. At the end, the\ninterpretation of the R-matrix as an \
S-matrix in a scattering process is also\npresented. These notes were written \
for the lectures delivered at the school\n\"Integrability, Dualities and \
Deformations\", that ran from 23 to 27 August 2021\nin Santiago de Compostela \
and virtually.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 29 Sep 2021 09:01:34 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 2 Mar 2022 18:41:59 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2022-04-12", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Retore", "Ana L.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
