               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Luc\\\\'ia C\\\\'ordova\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Luc\\\\'ia C\\\\'ordova, Stefano Negro, Fidel I. \
Schaposnik Massolo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz past turning points: the \
(elliptic)\\n  sinh-Gordon model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"37 pages, 11 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2022)035\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze the Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (TBA) for \
various integrable\\nS-matrices in the context of generalized $T\\\\bar T$ \
deformations. We focus on\\nthe sinh-Gordon model and its elliptic \
deformation in both its fermionic and\\nbosonic realizations. We confirm that \
the determining factor for a turning\\npoint in the TBA, interpreted as a \
finite Hagedorn temperature, is the\\ndifference between the number of bound \
states and resonances in the theory.\\nImplementing the numerical \
pseudo-arclength continuation method, we are able to\\nfollow the solutions \
to the TBA equations past the turning point all the way to\\nthe ultraviolet \
regime. We find that for any number $k$ of resonances the pair\\nof complex \
conjugate solutions below the turning point is such that the\\neffective \
central charge is minimized. As $k\\\\to\\\\infty$ the UV effective \
central\\ncharge goes to zero as in the elliptic sinh-Gordon model. Finally \
we uncover a\\nnew family of UV complete integrable theories defined by the \
bosonic\\ncounterparts of the S-matrices describing the $\\\\Phi_{1,3}$ \
integrable\\ndeformation of non-unitary minimal models $\\\\mathcal \
M_{2,2n+3}$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
