           "id" -> "2110.14666", "submitter" -> "Luc\\'ia C\\'ordova", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Luc\\'ia C\\'ordova, Stefano Negro, Fidel I. Schaposnik Massolo",
             "title" -> 
            "Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz past turning points: the (elliptic)\n \
 sinh-Gordon model", "comments" -> "37 pages, 11 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP01(2022)035", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We analyze the Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (TBA) for various \
integrable\nS-matrices in the context of generalized $T\\bar T$ deformations. \
We focus on\nthe sinh-Gordon model and its elliptic deformation in both its \
fermionic and\nbosonic realizations. We confirm that the determining factor \
for a turning\npoint in the TBA, interpreted as a finite Hagedorn \
temperature, is the\ndifference between the number of bound states and \
resonances in the theory.\nImplementing the numerical pseudo-arclength \
continuation method, we are able to\nfollow the solutions to the TBA \
equations past the turning point all the way to\nthe ultraviolet regime. We \
find that for any number $k$ of resonances the pair\nof complex conjugate \
solutions below the turning point is such that the\neffective central charge \
is minimized. As $k\\to\\infty$ the UV effective central\ncharge goes to zero \
as in the elliptic sinh-Gordon model. Finally we uncover a\nnew family of UV \
complete integrable theories defined by the bosonic\ncounterparts of the \
S-matrices describing the $\\Phi_{1,3}$ integrable\ndeformation of \
non-unitary minimal models $\\mathcal M_{2,2n+3}$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
