               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riccardo Conti and Davide Masoero\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On solutions of the Bethe Ansatz for the Quantum KdV \
model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"49 pages, 3 figures. Minor revision. Accepted version. To \
appear on\\n  Communications in Mathematical Physics (2023)\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s00220-023-04728-3\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph hep-th math.CA math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the Bethe Ansatz Equations for the Quantum KdV \
model, which are also\\nknown to be solved by the spectral determinants of a \
specific family of\\nanharmonic oscillators called monster potentials (ODE/IM \
correspondence). These\\nBethe Ansatz Equations depend on two parameters, \
identified with the momentum\\nand the degree at infinity of the anharmonic \
oscillators. We provide a complete\\nclassification of the solutions with \
only real and positive roots -- when the\\ndegree is greater than 2 -- in \
terms of admissible sequences of holes. In\\nparticular, we prove that \
admissible sequences of holes are naturally\\nparameterised by integer \
partitions, and we prove that they are in one-to-one\\ncorrespondence with \
solutions of the Bethe Ansatz Equations if the momentum is\\nlarge enough. \
Consequently, we deduce that the monster potentials are complete,\\nin the \
sense that every solution of the Bethe Ansatz Equations coincides with\\nthe \
spectrum of a unique monster potential. This essentially (i.e. up to \
gaps\\nin the previous literature) proves the ODE/IM correspondence for the \
Quantum\\nKdV model/monster potentials -- which was conjectured by \
Dorey-Tateo and\\nBazhanov-Lukyanov-Zamolodchikov -- when the degree is \
greater than 2. Our\\napproach is based on the transformation of the Bethe \
Ansatz Equations into a\\nfree-boundary nonlinear integral equation -- akin \
to the equations known in the\\nphysics literature as DDV or KBP or NLIE -- \
of which we develop the\\nmathematical theory from the beginning.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
