            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the Bethe Ansatz Equations for the Quantum KdV model, \
which are also\nknown to be solved by the spectral determinants of a specific \
family of\nanharmonic oscillators called monster potentials (ODE/IM \
correspondence). These\nBethe Ansatz Equations depend on two parameters, \
identified with the momentum\nand the degree at infinity of the anharmonic \
oscillators. We provide a complete\nclassification of the solutions with only \
real and positive roots -- when the\ndegree is greater than 2 -- in terms of \
admissible sequences of holes. In\nparticular, we prove that admissible \
sequences of holes are naturally\nparameterised by integer partitions, and we \
prove that they are in one-to-one\ncorrespondence with solutions of the Bethe \
Ansatz Equations if the momentum is\nlarge enough. Consequently, we deduce \
that the monster potentials are complete,\nin the sense that every solution \
of the Bethe Ansatz Equations coincides with\nthe spectrum of a unique \
monster potential. This essentially (i.e. up to gaps\nin the previous \
literature) proves the ODE/IM correspondence for the Quantum\nKdV \
model/monster potentials -- which was conjectured by Dorey-Tateo and\n\
Bazhanov-Lukyanov-Zamolodchikov -- when the degree is greater than 2. Our\n\
approach is based on the transformation of the Bethe Ansatz Equations into a\n\
free-boundary nonlinear integral equation -- akin to the equations known in \
the\nphysics literature as DDV or KBP or NLIE -- of which we develop the\n\
mathematical theory from the beginning.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
