         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2201.00438", "submitter" -> "Julio Oliva", "authors" -> 
            "Monserrat Aguayo, Ankai Hern\\'andez, Jos\\'e Mena, Julio Oliva, \
Marcelo\n  Oyarzo", "title" -> 
            "Exact scalar (quasi-)normal modes of black holes and solitons in \
gauged\n  SUGRA", "comments" -> "18 pages, 3 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP07(2022)021", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we identify a new family of black holes and \
solitons that lead\nto the exact integration of scalar probes, even in the \
presence of a\nnon-minimal coupling with the Ricci scalar which has a \
non-trivial profile. The\nbackgrounds are planar and spherical black holes as \
well as solitons of\n$SU\\left( 2\\right) \\times SU\\left( 2\\right) $ \
$\\mathcal{N}=4$ gauged\nsupergravity in four dimensions. On these \
geometries, we compute the spectrum\nof (quasi-)normal modes for the \
non-minimally coupled scalar field. We find\nthat the equation for the radial \
dependence can be integrated in terms of\nhypergeometric functions leading to \
an exact expression for the frequencies.\nThe solutions do not asymptote to a \
constant curvature spacetime, nevertheless\nthe asymptotic region acquires an \
extra conformal Killing vector. For the black\nhole, the scalar probe is \
purely ingoing at the horizon, and requiring that the\nsolutions lead to an \
extremum of the action principle we impose a Dirichlet\nboundary condition at \
infinity. Surprisingly, the quasinormal modes do not\ndepend on the radius of \
the black hole, therefore this family of geometries can\nbe interpreted as \
isospectral in what regards to the wave operator\nnon-minimally coupled to \
the Ricci scalar. We find both purely damped modes, as\nwell as exponentially \
growing unstable modes depending on the values of the\nnon-minimal coupling \
parameter. For the solitons we show that the same\nintegrability property is \
achieved separately in a non-supersymmetric solutions\nas well as for the \
supersymmetric one. Imposing regularity at the origin and a\nwell defined \
extremum for the action principle we obtain the spectra that can\nalso lead \
to purely oscillatory modes as well as to unstable scalar probes,\ndepending \
on the values of the non-minimal coupling.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 3 Jan 2022 00:01:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2022-07-13", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Aguayo", "Monserrat", ""}, {
              "Hern\[AAcute]ndez", "Ankai", ""}, {
              "Mena", "Jos\[EAcute]", ""}, {"Oliva", "Julio", ""}, {
              "Oyarzo", "Marcelo", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
