                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The time and band limiting operator is introduced to \
optimize the\\nreconstruction of a signal from only a partial part of its \
spectrum. In the\\ndiscrete case, this operator commutes with the so-called \
algebraic Heun\\noperator which appears in the context of the quantum \
integrable systems. The\\nconstruction of both operators and the proof of \
their commutativity is\\nrecalled. A direct connection between their spectra \
is obtained. Then, the\\nBethe ansatz, a well-known method to diagonalize \
integrable quantum\\nHamiltonians, is used to diagonalize the Heun operator \
and to obtain insights\\non the spectrum of the time and band limiting \
operator.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
