            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The time and band limiting operator is introduced to optimize \
the\nreconstruction of a signal from only a partial part of its spectrum. In \
the\ndiscrete case, this operator commutes with the so-called algebraic Heun\n\
operator which appears in the context of the quantum integrable systems. The\n\
construction of both operators and the proof of their commutativity is\n\
recalled. A direct connection between their spectra is obtained. Then, the\n\
Bethe ansatz, a well-known method to diagonalize integrable quantum\n\
Hamiltonians, is used to diagonalize the Heun operator and to obtain insights\
\non the spectrum of the time and band limiting operator.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
