               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Vitaly Velizhanin\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"V.N. Velizhanin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exact result in N=4 SYM theory: Generalised \
double-logarithmic equation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"36 pages, 1 figure, 2 ancillary files, some details and \
references\\n  added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2022)176\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present the new results for the generalised \
double-logarithmic equation,\\nobtained from the analytical continuation of \
the seven-loop anomalous dimension\\nof twist-2 operators in the planar N=4 \
SYM theory. The double-logarithmic\\nequation is related to the special \
asymptotic of the scattering amplitudes,\\nwhen the large logarithms of the \
energy of scattering particles are appeared\\nand should be summed in all \
order of perturbative theory. These large\\nlogarithms correspond to the \
poles of the analytically continued anomalous\\ndimension. The generalised \
double-logarithmic equation includes the subleading\\nlogarithms. We have \
found, that the expansion of the generalised\\ndouble-logarithmic equation \
can be ressumed in the form of rational functions\\nwith simple denominator. \
The solution of the generalised double-logarithmic\\nequation provides a lot \
of information about the poles of the analytically\\ncontinued anomalous \
dimension in all orders of perturbative theory. We have\\nfound also the \
generalised double-logarithmic equation for the analytically\\ncontinued \
anomalous dimension near the value, which is related with\\nBFKL-equation.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
