 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  State-average calculations based on mixture of states \
are increasingly being\\nexploited across chemistry and physics as versatile \
procedures for addressing\\nexcitations of quantum many-body systems. If not \
too many states should need to\\nbe addressed, calculations performed on \
individual states is also a common\\noption. Here we show how the two \
approaches can be merged into one method,\\ndealing with a generalized yet \
single pure state. Implications in electronic\\nstructure calculations are \
discussed and for quantum computations are pointed\\nout.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
