         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2204.07542", "submitter" -> "Joao A. Silva", "authors" -> 
            "Luis F. Alday, Tobias Hansen and Joao A. Silva", "title" -> 
            "AdS Virasoro-Shapiro from dispersive sum rules", "comments" -> 
            "32 pages. Published version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2022)036", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the four-point correlator of the stress-energy \
tensor in ${\\cal\nN}=4$ SYM, to leading order in inverse powers of the \
central charge, but\nincluding all order corrections in $1/\\lambda$. This \
corresponds to the AdS\nversion of the Virasoro-Shapiro amplitude to all \
orders in the small\n$\\alpha'$/low energy expansion. Using dispersion \
relations in Mellin space, we\nderive an infinite set of sum rules. These sum \
rules strongly constrain the\nform of the amplitude, and determine all \
coefficients in the low energy\nexpansion in terms of the CFT data for heavy \
string operators, in principle\navailable from integrability. For the first \
set of corrections to the flat\nspace amplitude we find a unique solution \
consistent with the results from\nintegrability and localisation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 15 Apr 2022 16:57:30 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 14 Sep 2022 11:31:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2022-10-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Alday", "Luis F.", ""}, {
              "Hansen", "Tobias", ""}, {"Silva", "Joao A.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
