 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The rapidity anomalous dimension controls the scaling \
of transverse momentum\\ndependent observables in the Sudakov region. In a \
conformal theory it is\\nequivalent to the soft anomalous dimension, but in \
QCD this relation is broken\\nby anomalous terms proportional to the \
$\\\\beta$-function. In this paper we first\\ngive a simple proof of this \
relation using two different representations of the\\nenergy-energy \
correlator observable. We then calculate the anomalous terms to\\nthree loops \
by computing the three-loop fully differential soft function \
to\\n$\\\\mathcal{O}(\\\\epsilon)$. Combined with recent perturbative data \
from the study\\nof on-shell form factors and splitting functions, this \
allows us to derive the\\nfour loop rapidity anomalous dimension in \
QCD.\\n\""}]}, {
