            "authors" -> 
            "Per Kraus, Ruben Monten and Konstantinos Roumpedakis", "title" -> 
            "Refining the Cutoff 3d Gravity / $T\\bar{T}$ Correspondence", 
            "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, minor typos fixed, new subsection added to make \
contact\n  with previous literature, version accepted for publication in \
JHEP", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Pure gravity in AdS$_3$ is a theory of boundary excitations, \
most simply\nexpressed as a constrained free scalar with an improved stress \
tensor that is\nneeded to match the Brown--Henneaux central charge. Excising \
a finite part of\nAdS gives rise to a static gauge Nambu--Goto action for the \
boundary graviton.\nWe show that this is the $T\\bar{T}$ deformation of the \
infinite volume theory,\nas the effect of the improvement term on the \
deformed action can be absorbed\ninto a field redefinition. The classical \
gravitational stress tensor is\nreproduced order by order by the $T\\bar{T}$ \
trace equation. We calculate the\nfinite volume energy spectrum in static \
gauge and find that the trace equation\nimposes sufficient constraints on the \
ordering ambiguities to guarantee\nagreement with the light-cone gauge \
prediction. The correlation functions,\nhowever, are not completely fixed by \
the trace equation. We show how both the\ngravitational action and the \
$T\\bar{T}$ deformation allow for finite\nimprovement terms, and we match \
these to the undetermined total derivative\nterms in Zamolodchikov's point \
splitting definition of the $T\\bar{T}$ operator.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
