            "  We explore the phenomena of absorption/emission of solitons by \
an integrable\nboundary for the nonlinear Schr\\\"odinger equation on the \
half-line. This is\nbased on the investigation of time-dependent reflection \
matrices which satisfy\nthe boundary zero curvature equation. In particular, \
this leads to\nabsorption/emission processes at the boundary that can take \
place for solitons\nand higher-order solitons. As a consequence, the usual \
charges on the half-line\nare no longer conserved but we show explicitly how \
to restore an infinite set\nof conserved quantities by taking the boundary \
into account. The Hamiltonian\ndescription and Poisson structure of the model \
are presented, which allows us\nto derive for the first time a classical \
version of the boundary algebra used\noriginally in the context of the \
quantum nonlinear Schr\\\"odinger equation.\n", 
