 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present an integrability-based conjecture for the \
three-point functions of\\nsingle-trace operators in planar \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super-Yang-Mills theory at\\nfinite coupling, in the case \
where two operators are protected. Our proposal is\\nbased on the hexagon \
representation for structure constants of long operators,\\nwhich we complete \
to incorporate operators of any length using data from the\\nTBA/QSC \
formalism. We perform various tests of our conjecture, at weak and\\nstrong \
coupling, finding agreement with the gauge theory through 5 loops for\\nthe \
shortest three-point function and with string theory in the \
classical\\nlimit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
