Paul Ryan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exploring the Quantum Spectral Curve for \
AdS${}_3$/CFT${}_2$\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Despite the rich and fruitful history of the \
integrability approach to string\\ntheory on the $AdS_3\\\\times S^3\\\\times \
T^4$ background, it has not been possible\\nto extract many concrete \
predictions from integrability, except in a strict\\nasymptotic regime of \
large quantum numbers, due to the severity of wrapping\\neffects. The \
situation changed radically with two independent and identical\\nproposals \
for the Quantum Spectral Curve (QSC) for this system in a background\\nof \
pure Ramond-Ramond flux. This formulation is expected to capture \
all\\nwrapping effects exactly and describe the full planar spectrum. \
Massless modes\\nconjecturally manifest themselves in a new property of this \
QSC: the\\nnon-quadratic nature of the branch-cut singularities of the QSC \
Q-functions.\\nThis feature implies new technical challenges in solving the \
QSC equations as\\ncompared to the well-studied case of N=4 SYM. In this \
paper we resolve these\\ndifficulties and obtain the first ever predictions \
for generic unprotected\\nstring excitations. We explain how to extract a \
systematic expansion around the\\nanalogue of the weak 't Hooft coupling \
limit in N=4 SYM and also obtain\\nhigh-precision numerical results. This \
concrete data and others obtainable from\\nthe QSC could help to identify the \
so-far mysterious dual CFT.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
