               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The ODE/IM correspondence is an exact link between \
classical and quantum\\nintegrable models. The primary purpose of this work \
is to show that it remains\\nvalid after \
$\\\\mathrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\mathrm{T}}$ perturbation on both sides of \
the\\ncorrespondence. In particular, we prove that the deformed Lax pair of \
the\\nsinh-Gordon model, obtained from the unperturbed one through a \
dynamical change\\nof coordinates, leads to the same Burgers-type equation \
governing the quantum\\nspectral flow induced by \
$\\\\mathrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\mathrm{T}}$. Our main conclusions\\nhave general \
validity, as the analysis may be easily adapted to all the known\\nODE/IM \
examples involving integrable quantum field theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
