Tateo", "title" -> 
            "Deforming the ODE/IM correspondence with \
$\\mathrm{T}\\bar{\\mathrm{T}}$", "comments" -> "27 pages, 4 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP03(2023)084", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  The ODE/IM correspondence is an exact link between classical \
and quantum\nintegrable models. The primary purpose of this work is to show \
that it remains\nvalid after $\\mathrm{T}\\bar{\\mathrm{T}}$ perturbation on \
both sides of the\ncorrespondence. In particular, we prove that the deformed \
Lax pair of the\nsinh-Gordon model, obtained from the unperturbed one through \
a dynamical change\nof coordinates, leads to the same Burgers-type equation \
governing the quantum\nspectral flow induced by \
$\\mathrm{T}\\bar{\\mathrm{T}}$. Our main conclusions\nhave general validity, \
as the analysis may be easily adapted to all the known\nODE/IM examples \
involving integrable quantum field theories.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
