               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Daniele Bielli, Vaibhav Gautam, Alessandro \
Torrielli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A study of integrable form factors in massless \
relativistic $AdS_2$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25 pages, 12 figures. V2: comments and references added, \
matches\\n  published version. V3: error corrected and comments added\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 06 (2023) 005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2023)005\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DMUS-MP-23/02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we initiate the study of form factors for \
the massless\\nscattering of integrable $AdS_2$ superstrings, where the \
difference-form of the\\n$S$-matrix can be exploited to implement the \
relativistic form factor\\nbootstrap. The non-standard nature of the \
$S$-matrix implies that traditional\\nmethods do not apply. We use the fact \
that the massless $AdS_2$ $S$-matrix is a\\nlimit of a better-behaved \
$S$-matrix found by Fendley. We show that the\\npreviously conjectured \
massless $AdS_2$ dressing factor coincides with the\\nlimit of the De Martino \
- Moriconi improved dressing factor for the Fendley\\n$S$-matrix. After \
finding a method to construct integral representations of\\nrelativistic \
dressing factors satisfying specific assumptions, we obtain\\nanalytic proofs \
of crossing and unitarity relations and propose a solution to\\nthe form \
factors constraints in the two-particle case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
