               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Diego H. Correa, Victor I. Giraldo-Rivera and Mart\\\\'in \
Lagares\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable Wilson loops in ABJM: a $Y$-system computation \
of the cusp\\n  anomalous dimension\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"44 pages, 2 figures; v2: clarifications added and typos \
corrected.\\n  Version to appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2023)179\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the integrability properties of Wilson loops \
in the ${\\\\cal N}=6$\\nthree-dimensional Chern-Simons-matter (ABJM) theory. \
We begin with the\\nconstruction of an open spin chain that describes the \
anomalous dimensions of\\noperators inserted along the contour of a 1/2 BPS \
Wilson loop. Moreover, we\\ncompute the all-loop reflection matrices that \
govern the interaction of\\nspin-chain excitations with the boundary, \
including their dressing factors, and\\nwe check them against weak- and \
strong-coupling results. Furthermore, we\\npropose a $Y$-system of equations \
for the cusped Wilson line of ABJM, and we\\nuse it to reproduce the one-loop \
cusp anomalous dimension of ABJM from a\\nleading-order finite-size \
correction. Finally, we write a set of BTBA equations\\nconsistent with the \
$Y$-system proposal.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
