            "Integrable Wilson loops in ABJM: a $Y$-system computation of the \
cusp\n  anomalous dimension", "comments" -> 
            "44 pages, 2 figures; v2: clarifications added and typos \
corrected.\n  Version to appear in JHEP", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP06(2023)179", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the integrability properties of Wilson loops in the \
${\\cal N}=6$\nthree-dimensional Chern-Simons-matter (ABJM) theory. We begin \
with the\nconstruction of an open spin chain that describes the anomalous \
dimensions of\noperators inserted along the contour of a 1/2 BPS Wilson loop. \
Moreover, we\ncompute the all-loop reflection matrices that govern the \
interaction of\nspin-chain excitations with the boundary, including their \
dressing factors, and\nwe check them against weak- and strong-coupling \
results. Furthermore, we\npropose a $Y$-system of equations for the cusped \
Wilson line of ABJM, and we\nuse it to reproduce the one-loop cusp anomalous \
dimension of ABJM from a\nleading-order finite-size correction. Finally, we \
write a set of BTBA equations\nconsistent with the $Y$-system proposal.\n", 
