               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find the connection between relativistic and \
non-relativistic string vacua\\nin AdS$_5 \\\\times$S$^5$ in terms of a free \
parameter $c$ flow. First, we show\\nthat the famous relativistic BMN vacuum \
flows in the large $c$ parameter to an\\nunphysical solution of the \
non-relativistic theory. Then, we consider the\\nsimplest non-relativistic \
vacuum, found in arXiv:2109.13240 (called BMN-like),\\nand we identify its \
relativistic origin, namely a non-compact version of the\\nfolded string with \
zero spin, ignored in the past due to its infinite energy.\\nWe show that, \
once the critical closed B-field required by the non-relativistic\\nlimit is \
included, the total energy of such relativistic solution is finite,\\nand in \
the large $c$ parameter it precisely matches the one of the \
BMN-like\\nstring. We also analyse the case with spin in the transverse AdS \
directions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
