               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The study of \
$\\\\mathrm{T}\\\\overline{\\\\mathrm{T}}$-perturbed quantum field\\ntheories \
is an active area of research with deep connections to fundamental\\naspects \
of the scattering theory of integrable quantum field theories,\\ngeneralised \
Gibbs ensembles, and string theory. Many features of these\\ntheories, such \
as the peculiar behaviour of their ground state energy and the\\nform of \
their scattering matrices, have been studied in the literature.\\nHowever, so \
far, very few studies have approached these theories from the\\nviewpoint of \
the form factor program. From the perspective of scattering\\ntheory, the \
effects of a $\\\\mathrm{T}\\\\overline{\\\\mathrm{T}}$ perturbation \
(and\\nhigher spin versions thereof) is encoded in a universal deformation of \
the\\ntwo-body scattering matrix by a CDD factor. It is then natural to ask \
how these\\nperturbations influence the form factor equations and, more \
generally, the form\\nfactor program. In this paper, we address this question \
for free theories,\\nalthough some of our results extend more generally. We \
show that the form\\nfactor equations admit general solutions and how these \
can help us study the\\ndistinct behaviour of correlation functions at short \
distances in theories\\nperturbed by irrelevant operators.\\n\""}]}, {
