           "id" -> "2306.01640", "submitter" -> "Olalla Castro Alvaredo", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Olalla A. Castro-Alvaredo, Stefano Negro and Fabio Sailis", 
            "title" -> 
            "Form Factors and Correlation Functions of\n  \
$\\mathrm{T}\\overline{\\mathrm{T}}$-Deformed Integrable Quantum Field \
Theories", "comments" -> 
            "29 Pages and 4 Figures. Version 2 contains a minor correction to\
\n  Section 3. Version 3 contain various additional minor corrections", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The study of $\\mathrm{T}\\overline{\\mathrm{T}}$-perturbed \
quantum field\ntheories is an active area of research with deep connections \
to fundamental\naspects of the scattering theory of integrable quantum field \
theories,\ngeneralised Gibbs ensembles, and string theory. Many features of \
these\ntheories, such as the peculiar behaviour of their ground state energy \
and the\nform of their scattering matrices, have been studied in the \
literature.\nHowever, so far, very few studies have approached these theories \
from the\nviewpoint of the form factor program. From the perspective of \
scattering\ntheory, the effects of a $\\mathrm{T}\\overline{\\mathrm{T}}$ \
perturbation (and\nhigher spin versions thereof) is encoded in a universal \
deformation of the\ntwo-body scattering matrix by a CDD factor. It is then \
natural to ask how these\nperturbations influence the form factor equations \
and, more generally, the form\nfactor program. In this paper, we address this \
question for free theories,\nalthough some of our results extend more \
generally. We show that the form\nfactor equations admit general solutions \
and how these can help us study the\ndistinct behaviour of correlation \
functions at short distances in theories\nperturbed by irrelevant operators.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 2 Jun 2023 16:01:37 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
