                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Olalla A. Castro-Alvaredo, Stefano Negro and Fabio Sailis\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Entanglement Entropy from Form Factors in\\n  \
$\\\\mathrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\mathrm{T}}$-Deformed Integrable Quantum Field \
Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"23 pages and 6 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In two recent papers we have proposed a program of \
study which allows us to\\ncompute the correlation functions of local and \
semi-local fields in \
generalised\\n$\\\\mathrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\mathrm{T}}$-deformed integrable \
quantum field theories. This\\nnew program, based on the construction of form \
factors, opens many avenues for\\nfuture study, one of which we address in \
this paper: computing entanglement\\nmeasures employing branch point twist \
fields. Indeed, over the past 15 years,\\nthis has become one the leading \
methods for the computation of entanglement\\nmeasures, both in conformal \
field theory and integrable quantum field theory.\\nThus the generalisation \
of this program to\\n$\\\\mathrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\mathrm{T}}$-perturbed theories \
offers a promising new tool for\\nthe study of entanglement measures in the \
presence of irrelevant perturbations.\\nIn this paper, we show that the \
natural two-particle form factor solution for\\nbranch point twist fields in \
replica theories with diagonal scattering admits a\\nsimple generalisation to \
a solution for $\\\\mathrm{T}\\\\bar{\\\\mathrm{T}}$-perturbed\\ntheories. \
Starting with this solution, some of the known properties of\\nentanglement \
measures in massive integrable quantum field theories can be\\ngeneralised to \
the perturbed models. We show this by focusing on the Ising\\nfield theory. \
During the completion of this paper, we became aware of a \
recent\\npublication where the same problem has been addressed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 19 Jun 2023 16:58:14 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
