           "id" -> "2306.11064", "submitter" -> "Olalla Castro Alvaredo", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Olalla A. Castro-Alvaredo, Stefano Negro and Fabio Sailis", 
            "title" -> 
            "Entanglement Entropy from Form Factors in\n  \
$\\mathrm{T}\\bar{\\mathrm{T}}$-Deformed Integrable Quantum Field Theories", 
            "comments" -> "23 pages and 6 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In two recent papers we have proposed a program of study which \
allows us to\ncompute the correlation functions of local and semi-local \
fields in generalised\n$\\mathrm{T}\\bar{\\mathrm{T}}$-deformed integrable \
quantum field theories. This\nnew program, based on the construction of form \
factors, opens many avenues for\nfuture study, one of which we address in \
this paper: computing entanglement\nmeasures employing branch point twist \
fields. Indeed, over the past 15 years,\nthis has become one the leading \
methods for the computation of entanglement\nmeasures, both in conformal \
field theory and integrable quantum field theory.\nThus the generalisation of \
this program to\n$\\mathrm{T}\\bar{\\mathrm{T}}$-perturbed theories offers a \
promising new tool for\nthe study of entanglement measures in the presence of \
irrelevant perturbations.\nIn this paper, we show that the natural \
two-particle form factor solution for\nbranch point twist fields in replica \
theories with diagonal scattering admits a\nsimple generalisation to a \
solution for $\\mathrm{T}\\bar{\\mathrm{T}}$-perturbed\ntheories. Starting \
with this solution, some of the known properties of\nentanglement measures in \
massive integrable quantum field theories can be\ngeneralised to the \
perturbed models. We show this by focusing on the Ising\nfield theory. During \
the completion of this paper, we became aware of a recent\npublication where \
the same problem has been addressed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 19 Jun 2023 16:58:14 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
