non-perturbative approach\nto describe confinement in Yang-Mills theory that \
models the confining flux\ntube as a thin vibrating string. EST calculations \
are usually performed using\nthe zeta-function regularization: however there \
are situations (for instance\nthe study of the shape of the flux tube or of \
the higher order corrections\nbeyond the Nambu-Goto EST) which involve \
