            "The ABJM Hagedorn Temperature from Integrability", "comments" -> 
            "19 pages, 5 figures, 2 ancillary files. V2: references added, \
typos\n  corrected, updated numerical data", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> "UUITP-16/23, MIT-CTP/5574", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We use the quantum spectral curve to compute the Hagedorn \
temperature for\nABJM theory in terms of the interpolating function \
$h(\\lambda)$. At weak\ncoupling we compute this temperature up to eight-loop \
order, showing that it\nmatches the known tree-level and two-loop results. At \
strong coupling we\ncompute the dependence numerically, showing that it is \
consistent with\nexpectations from supergravity and the plane-wave limit for \
the four leading\nterms in the strong coupling expansion, up to an overall \
shift of the\nzero-point energy for type IIA string theory on AdS$_4\\times\n\
\\mathbb{C}\\textrm{P}^3$. We conjecture an analytic form for this shift to\n\
leading order that is consistent with our numerical results.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
