                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper represents the completion of our work on the \
ODE/IM correspondence\\nfor the generalised quantum Drinfeld-Sokolov models. \
We present a unified and\\ngeneral mathematical theory, encompassing all \
particular cases that we had\\nalready addressed, and we fill important \
analytic and algebraic gaps in the\\nliterature on the ODE/IM correspondence. \
For every affine Lie algebra\\n$\\\\mathfrak{g}$ -- whose Langlands dual \
$\\\\mathfrak{g}'$ is the untwisted\\naffinisation of a simple Lie algebra -- \
we study a class of affine twisted\\nparabolic Miura $\\\\mathfrak{g}$-opers, \
introduced by Feigin, Frenkel and\\nHernandez. The Feigin-Frenkel-Hernandez \
opers are defined by fixing the\\nsingularity structure at $0$ and \
$\\\\infty$, and by allowing a finite number of\\nadditional singular terms \
with trivial monodromy. We define the central\\nconnection matrix and Stokes \
matrix for these opers, and prove that the\\ncoefficients of the former \
satisfy the the $QQ$ system of the \
quantum\\n$\\\\mathfrak{g}'$-Drinfeld-Sokolov (or quantum \
$\\\\mathfrak{g}'$-KdV) model. If\\n$\\\\mathfrak{g}$ is untwisted, it is \
known that the trivial monodromy conditions\\nare equivalent to a complete \
system of algebraic equations for the additional\\nsingularities. We prove a \
suprising negative result in the case $\\\\mathfrak{g}$\\nis twisted: in this \
case, the trivial monodromy conditions have no \
non-trivial\\nsolutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 4 Dec 2023 15:14:38 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
