            "Feigin-Frenkel-Hernandez Opers and the QQ-system", "comments" -> 
            "55 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Commun. Math. Phys. 405, 193 (2024)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/s00220-024-05064-w", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "math-ph hep-th math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This paper represents the completion of our work on the ODE/IM \
correspondence\nfor the generalised quantum Drinfeld-Sokolov models. We \
present a unified and\ngeneral mathematical theory, encompassing all \
particular cases that we had\nalready addressed, and we fill important \
analytic and algebraic gaps in the\nliterature on the ODE/IM correspondence. \
For every affine Lie algebra\n$\\mathfrak{g}$ -- whose Langlands dual \
$\\mathfrak{g}'$ is the untwisted\naffinisation of a simple Lie algebra -- we \
study a class of affine twisted\nparabolic Miura $\\mathfrak{g}$-opers, \
introduced by Feigin, Frenkel and\nHernandez. The Feigin-Frenkel-Hernandez \
opers are defined by fixing the\nsingularity structure at $0$ and $\\infty$, \
and by allowing a finite number of\nadditional singular terms with trivial \
monodromy. We define the central\nconnection matrix and Stokes matrix for \
these opers, and prove that the\ncoefficients of the former satisfy the the \
$QQ$ system of the quantum\n$\\mathfrak{g}'$-Drinfeld-Sokolov (or quantum \
$\\mathfrak{g}'$-KdV) model. If\n$\\mathfrak{g}$ is untwisted, it is known \
that the trivial monodromy conditions\nare equivalent to a complete system of \
algebraic equations for the additional\nsingularities. We prove a suprising \
negative result in the case $\\mathfrak{g}$\nis twisted: in this case, the \
trivial monodromy conditions have no non-trivial\nsolutions.\n", 
