Alessandro\n  Tanzini, Zihan Zhou", "title" -> 
            "Black Hole Perturbation Theory Meets CFT$_2$: Kerr Compton \
Amplitudes\n  from Nekrasov-Shatashvili Functions", "comments" -> 
            "18 pages, 3 figs; the helicity reversing amplitude is considered \
in\n  the new version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a novel study of Kerr Compton amplitudes in a \
partial wave basis\nin terms of the Nekrasov-Shatashvili (NS) function of the \
confluent Heun\nequation (CHE). Remarkably, NS-functions enjoy analytic \
properties and\nsymmetries that are naturally inherited by the Compton \
amplitudes. Based on\nthis, we characterize the analytic dependence of the \
Compton phase-shift in the\nKerr spin parameter and provide a direct \
comparison to the standard\npost-Minkowskian (PM) perturbative approach \
within General Relativity (GR). We\nalso analyze the universal large \
frequency behavior of the relevant\ncharacteristic exponent of the CHE -- \
also known as the renormalized angular\nmomentum -- and find agreement with \
numerical computations. Moreover, we\ndiscuss the analytic continuation in \
the harmonics quantum number $\\ell$ of the\npartial wave, and show that the \
limit to the physical integer values commutes\nwith the PM expansion of the \
observables. Finally, we obtain the contributions\nto the tree level, \
point-particle, gravitational Compton amplitude in a\ncovariant basis through \
$O(a_{\\text{BH}}^8)$, without the need to take the\nsuper-extremal limit for \
Kerr spin.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
