            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2405.12005\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Siwei Zhong\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Zohar Komargodski, Siwei Zhong\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Baryon Junction and String Interactions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"reference added and typo corrected in v2\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study junctions between confining strings. We show \
that the effective\\ntheory of such junctions is very predictive with only \
one new parameter, the\\njunction's mass, controlling the first couple of \
terms in the expansion in the\\nsystem size. By open-closed duality these \
considerations about the baryon\\njunction map to interaction vertices of \
closed strings. Therefore, we calculate\\nthe interaction vertices of closed \
strings in theories such as Yang-Mills\\ntheory. We find some surprising \
selection rules for string interactions in 3+1\\ndimensions. Requiring \
perturbative stability and that the string coupling is\\nweak, we suggest \
constraints on the junction's mass.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
