            "  We study junctions between confining strings. We show that the \
effective\ntheory of such junctions is very predictive with only one new \
parameter, the\njunction's mass, controlling the first couple of terms in the \
expansion in the\nsystem size. By open-closed duality these considerations \
about the baryon\njunction map to interaction vertices of closed strings. \
Therefore, we calculate\nthe interaction vertices of closed strings in \
theories such as Yang-Mills\ntheory. We find some surprising selection rules \
for string interactions in 3+1\ndimensions. Requiring perturbative stability \
and that the string coupling is\nweak, we suggest constraints on the \
junction's mass.\n", 
