               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2405.12636\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sujay Ashok\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sujay K. Ashok, Sanhita Parihar, Tanmoy Sengupta, Adarsh \
Sudhakar,\\n  Roberto Tateo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable Structure of Higher Spin CFT and the ODE/IM \
Correspondence\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"47 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study two dimensional systems with extended \
conformal symmetry generated\\nby the ${\\\\mathcal W}_3$ algebra. These are \
expected to have an infinite number\\nof commuting conserved charges, which \
we refer to as the quantum Boussinesq\\ncharges. We compute the eigenvalues \
of the quantum Boussinesq charges in both\\nthe vacuum and first excited \
states of the higher spin module through the\\nODE/IM correspondence. By \
studying the higher spin conformal field theory on\\nthe torus, we also \
calculate thermal correlators involving the energy-momentum\\ntensor and the \
spin-3 current by making use of the Zhu recursion relations. By\\ncombining \
these results, we show that it is possible to derive the current\\ndensities, \
whose integrals are the quantum Boussinesq charges. We also evaluate\\nthe \
thermal expectation values of the conserved charges, and show that \
these\\nare quasi-modular differential operators acting on the character of \
the higher\\nspin module.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
