Sudhakar,\n  Roberto Tateo", "title" -> 
            "Integrable Structure of Higher Spin CFT and the ODE/IM \
Correspondence", "comments" -> "47 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study two dimensional systems with extended conformal \
symmetry generated\nby the ${\\mathcal W}_3$ algebra. These are expected to \
have an infinite number\nof commuting conserved charges, which we refer to as \
the quantum Boussinesq\ncharges. We compute the eigenvalues of the quantum \
Boussinesq charges in both\nthe vacuum and first excited states of the higher \
spin module through the\nODE/IM correspondence. By studying the higher spin \
conformal field theory on\nthe torus, we also calculate thermal correlators \
involving the energy-momentum\ntensor and the spin-3 current by making use of \
the Zhu recursion relations. By\ncombining these results, we show that it is \
possible to derive the current\ndensities, whose integrals are the quantum \
Boussinesq charges. We also evaluate\nthe thermal expectation values of the \
conserved charges, and show that these\nare quasi-modular differential \
operators acting on the character of the higher\nspin module.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 21 May 2024 09:40:52 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-05-22", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ashok", "Sujay K.", ""}, {
