               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Michele Caselle, Nicodemo Magnoli, Alessandro Nada, Marco \
Panero,\\n  Dario Panfalone and Lorenzo Verzichelli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Confining strings in three-dimensional gauge theories \
beyond the\\n  Nambu--Got\\\\=o approximation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages, 14 figures, 17 tables\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2024)198\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-lat hep-th\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We carry out a systematic study of the effective \
bosonic string describing\\nconfining flux tubes in $\\\\mathrm{SU}(N)$ \
Yang--Mills theories in three\\nspacetime dimensions. While their low-energy \
properties are known to be\\nuniversal and are described well by the \
Nambu--Got\\\\=o action, a non-trivial\\ndependence on the gauge group is \
encoded in a series of undetermined subleading\\ncorrections in an expansion \
around the limit of an arbitrarily long string. We\\nquantify the first two \
of these corrections by means of high-precision Monte\\nCarlo simulations of \
Polyakov-loop correlators in the lattice regularization.\\nWe compare the \
results of novel lattice simulations for theories with $N=3$ and\\n$6$ color \
charges, and report an improved estimate for the $N=2$ case,\\ndiscussing the \
approach to the large-$N$ limit. Our results are compatible with\\nanalytical \
bounds derived from the S-matrix bootstrap approach. In addition, we\\nalso \
present a new test of the Svetitsky--Yaffe conjecture for \
the\\n$\\\\mathrm{SU}(3)$ theory in three dimensions, finding that the \
lattice results\\nfor the Polyakov-loop correlation function are in excellent \
agreement with the\\npredictions of the Svetitsky--Yaffe mapping, which are \
worked out\\nquantitatively applying conformal perturbation theory to the \
three-state Potts\\nmodel in two dimensions. The implications of these \
results are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
