            "Katsushi Ito, Jingjing Yang", "title" -> 
            "TBA equations and quantum periods for D-type Argyres-Douglas \
theories", "comments" -> "41 pages, 39 figures, 3 tables", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> "TIT/HEP-704", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct TBA equations for D-type Argyres-Douglas theories \
with an SU(2)\nflavor symmetry based on their spectral networks. We show that \
the solutions of\nthese TBA equations agree with the quantum periods of the \
corresponding quantum\nSeiberg-Witten curves defined in the \
Nekrosov-Shatashvili limit of the Omega\nbackground, including a centrifugal \
correction. We study the variety of TBA\nsystems across the Coulomb branch \
moduli space and find that they correspond to\nthe Dynkin diagrams of $D_n$ \
Lie algebras in the minimal chamber, and reproduce\nthe TBA equations for \
reflectionless D scattering theories at the maximally\nsymmetric point. \
Numerical computations demonstrate that the quantum periods\nobtained from \
the Borel-Pad\\'e resummation and their WKB expansions are in\nagreement with \
the solutions of the TBA equations.\n", 
