               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2408.06031\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Tommaso Morone\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nicol\\\\`o Brizio, Tommaso Morone, Roberto Tateo\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Stress-energy tensor deformations, Ricci flows and black \
holes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"48 pages, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper reviews and extends the recently discovered \
connections between\\nmarginal and irrelevant stress-energy tensor \
deformations and gravity theories\\nin arbitrary space-time dimensions. We \
start by discussing how $T\\\\bar{T}$ and\\nRoot-$T\\\\bar{T}$ deformations \
of two-dimensional field theories can be\\nequivalently interpreted as the \
coupling of the undeformed matter sector to a\\ngravity theory. We then \
extend this duality to higher-dimensional scenarios by\\nusing an approach \
that relies on the non-trivial eigenvalue degeneracy\\ncharacterising the \
energy-momentum tensor of specific physical theories. We\\nalso explore \
incorporating dynamical degrees of freedom in the gravity sector,\\nand show \
that the deformed space-time geometry induced by the \
$T\\\\bar{T}$-like\\ndeformations defines a Ricci-Bourguignon flow of the \
metric tensor, which\\nreduces to a Ricci flow in four dimensions. Finally, \
exploiting a dressing-type\\nmechanism for the action functional \
characterizing a broad class of\\n$T\\\\bar{T}$-like deformations we study \
explicit examples, such as Einstein-Ricci\\nsolitons, $(d-1)$-form field \
theories, and spherically symmetric electrovacuum\\nsolutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 12 Aug 2024 09:48:18 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-08-13\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Brizio\"", ",", "\"Nicol\[OGrave]\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Morone\"", ",", "\"Tommaso\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Tateo\"", ",", "\"Roberto\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
