           "id" -> "2408.06031", "submitter" -> "Tommaso Morone", "authors" -> 
            "Nicol\\`o Brizio, Tommaso Morone, Roberto Tateo", "title" -> 
            "Stress-energy tensor deformations, Ricci flows and black holes", 
            "comments" -> "48 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This paper reviews and extends the recently discovered \
connections between\nmarginal and irrelevant stress-energy tensor \
deformations and gravity theories\nin arbitrary space-time dimensions. We \
start by discussing how $T\\bar{T}$ and\nRoot-$T\\bar{T}$ deformations of \
two-dimensional field theories can be\nequivalently interpreted as the \
coupling of the undeformed matter sector to a\ngravity theory. We then extend \
this duality to higher-dimensional scenarios by\nusing an approach that \
relies on the non-trivial eigenvalue degeneracy\ncharacterising the \
energy-momentum tensor of specific physical theories. We\nalso explore \
incorporating dynamical degrees of freedom in the gravity sector,\nand show \
that the deformed space-time geometry induced by the $T\\bar{T}$-like\n\
deformations defines a Ricci-Bourguignon flow of the metric tensor, which\n\
reduces to a Ricci flow in four dimensions. Finally, exploiting a \
dressing-type\nmechanism for the action functional characterizing a broad \
class of\n$T\\bar{T}$-like deformations we study explicit examples, such as \
Einstein-Ricci\nsolitons, $(d-1)$-form field theories, and spherically \
symmetric electrovacuum\nsolutions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 12 Aug 2024 09:48:18 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-08-13", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Brizio", "Nicol\[OGrave]", ""}, {
