             "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  The knowledge of {\\it non usual} and sometimes {\\it hidden} \
symmetries of\n(classical) integrable systems provides a very powerful \
setting-out of\nsolutions of these models. Primarily, the understanding and \
possibly the\nquantisation of intriguing symmetries could give rise to deeper \
insight into\nthe nature of field spectrum and correlation functions in \
quantum integrable\nmodels. With this perspective in mind we will propose a \
general framework for\ndiscovery and investigation of local, quasi-local and \
non-local symmetries in\nclassical integrable systems. We will pay particular \
attention to the structure\nof symmetry algebra and to the r\\^ole of \
conserved quantities. We will also\nstress a nice unifying point of view \
about KdV hierarchies and Toda field\ntheories with the result of obtaining a \
Virasoro algebra as exact symmetry of\nSine-Gordon Model.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
