                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In the framework of the Sine-Gordon (SG) theory we \
will present the\\nconstruction of a dynamical Virasoro symmetry which has \
nothing to do with the\\nspace-time Virasoro symmetry of 2D CFT. Although, it \
is non-local in the SG\\nfield theory, nevertheless it gives rise to a local \
action on specific\\nN-soliton solution variables. These {\\\\it analytic} \
variables possess a\\nbeautiful geometrical meaning and enter the Form Factor \
expressions. At the\\nend, we will also give some preliminary hints about the \
quantisation.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
