         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0105177", "submitter" -> "Vladimir Bazhanov", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Vladimir V. Bazhanov, Anthony N. Hibberd and Sergey M. \
Khoroshkin", "title" -> 
            "Integrable structure of W_3 Conformal Field Theory, Quantum \
Boussinesq\n  Theory and Boundary Affine Toda Theory", "comments" -> 
            "LaTeX, 87 pages, 1 figure. Misprints corrected", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B622:475-547,2002", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0550-3213(01)00595-8", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we study the Yang-Baxter integrable structure of \
Conformal\nField Theories with extended conformal symmetry generated by the \
W_3 algebra.\nWe explicitly construct various T- and Q-operators which act in \
the irreducible\nhighest weight modules of the W_3 algebra. These operators \
can be viewed as\ncontinuous field theory analogues of the commuting transfer \
matrices and\nQ-matrices of the integrable lattice systems associated with \
the quantum\nalgebra U_q(\\hat{sl}(3)). We formulate several conjectures \
detailing certain\nanalytic characteristics of the Q-operators and propose \
exact asymptotic\nexpansions of the T- and Q-operators at large values of the \
spectral parameter.\nWe show, in particular, that the asymptotic expansion of \
the T-operators\ngenerates an infinite set of local integrals of motion of \
the W_3 CFT which in\nthe classical limit reproduces an infinite set of \
conserved Hamiltonians\nassociated with the classical Boussinesq equation. We \
further study the vacuum\neigenvalues of the Q-operators (corresponding to \
the highest weight vector of\nthe W_3 module) and show that they are simply \
related to the expectation values\nof the boundary exponential fields in the \
non-equilibrium boundary affine Toda\nfield theory with zero bulk mass.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 18 May 2001 09:08:45 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 21 May 2001 01:26:31 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 20 Dec 2001 04:48:23 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-02-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Bazhanov", "Vladimir V.", ""}, {
              "Hibberd", "Anthony N.", ""}, {
              "Khoroshkin", "Sergey M.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{3.6490980482079176`, -7.645012003286106}, 
           0.10102143756118451],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0107015\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andreas Fring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Olalla Castro-Alvaredo and Andreas Fring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Form factors from free fermionic Fock fields, the \
Federbush model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages Latex, one section added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B618 (2001) 437-464\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(01)00462-X\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  By representing the field content as well as the \
particle creation operators\\nin terms of fermionic Fock operators, we \
compute the corresponding matrix\\nelements of the Federbush model. Only when \
these matrix elements satisfy the\\nform factor consistency equations \
involving anyonic factors of local\\ncommutativity, the corresponding \
operators are local. We carry out the\\nultraviolet limit, analyze the \
momentum space cluster properties and\\ndemonstrate how the Federbush model \
can be obtained from the\\n$SU(3)_3$-homogeneous sine-Gordon model. We \
propose a new Lagrangian which on\\none hand constitutes a generalization of \
the Federbush model in a Lie algebraic\\nfashion and on the other a certain \
limit of the homogeneous sine-Gordon models.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 3 Jul 2001 13:20:29 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 9 Jul 2001 16:38:14 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-07\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
