            "  By representing the field content as well as the particle \
creation operators\nin terms of fermionic Fock operators, we compute the \
corresponding matrix\nelements of the Federbush model. Only when these matrix \
elements satisfy the\nform factor consistency equations involving anyonic \
factors of local\ncommutativity, the corresponding operators are local. We \
carry out the\nultraviolet limit, analyze the momentum space cluster \
properties and\ndemonstrate how the Federbush model can be obtained from the\n\
$SU(3)_3$-homogeneous sine-Gordon model. We propose a new Lagrangian which on\
\none hand constitutes a generalization of the Federbush model in a Lie \
algebraic\nfashion and on the other a certain limit of the homogeneous \
sine-Gordon models.\n", 
