            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We examine some excited state energies in the non-unitary \
integrable quantum\nfield theory obtained from the perturbation of the \
minimal conformal field\ntheory model $M_{3,5}$ by its operator \
$\\phi_{2,1}$. Using the correspondence\nof this IQFT to the scaling limit of \
the dilute $A_2$ lattice model (in a\nparticular regime) we derive the \
functional equations for the QFT commuting\ntransfer matrices. These \
functional equations can be transformed to a closed\nset of TBA-like integral \
equations which determine the excited state energies\nin the finite-size \
system. In particular, we explicitly construct these\nequations for the \
ground state and two lowest excited states. Numerical results\nfor the \
associated energy gaps are compared with those obtained by the\ntruncated \
conformal space approach (TCSA).\n", 
