technical\\n  details) to be published in Phys. Lett. B\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett.B550:128-134,2002\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0370-2693(02)02970-2\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"SINP/TNP/24 -02\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A challenge in the theory of integrable systems is to \
show for every\\nnonultralocal quantum integrable model, a possible \
connection to an ultralocal\\nmodel. Some of such gauge connections were \
discovered earlier. We complete the\\ntask by identifying the same for the \
remaining ones along with two new models.\\nWe also unveil the underlying \
algebraic structure for these nonultralocal\\nmodels.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
