 details) to be published in Phys. Lett. B", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Lett.B550:128-134,2002", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0370-2693(02)02970-2", "report-no" -> "SINP/TNP/24 -02",
             "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat nlin.SI", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  A challenge in the theory of integrable systems is to show for \
every\nnonultralocal quantum integrable model, a possible connection to an \
ultralocal\nmodel. Some of such gauge connections were discovered earlier. We \
complete the\ntask by identifying the same for the remaining ones along with \
two new models.\nWe also unveil the underlying algebraic structure for these \
nonultralocal\nmodels.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 20 Aug 2002 15:36:35 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 8 Oct 2002 07:46:59 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 5 Nov 2002 13:30:22 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-07-19", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kundu", "Anjan", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{2.7302707674895585`, -6.904507026099661}, 
           0.10102143756118451],
