               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The integrals of motion of the tricritical Ising model \
are obtained by\\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (TBA) equations derived from the \
A_4 integrable\\nlattice model. They are compared with those given by the \
conformal field theory\\nleading to a unique one-to-one lattice-conformal \
correspondence. They can also\\nbe followed along the renormalization group \
flows generated by the action of\\nthe boundary field \\\\phi_{1,3} on \
conformal boundary conditions in close analogy\\nto the usual TBA description \
of energies.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
