               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0405139\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Giuseppe Mussardo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"G. Mussardo, V. Riva, G. Sotkov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Semiclassical Scaling Functions of Sine--Gordon \
Model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"33 pages, 6 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B699 (2004) 545-574\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.08.004\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ISAS/32/2004/FM\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present an analytic study of the finite size effects \
in Sine--Gordon\\nmodel, based on the semiclassical quantization of an \
appropriate kink\\nbackground defined on a cylindrical geometry. The \
quasi--periodic kink is\\nrealized as an elliptic function with its real \
period related to the size of\\nthe system. The stability equation for the \
small quantum fluctuations around\\nthis classical background is of Lame' \
type and the corresponding energy\\neigenvalues are selected inside the \
allowed bands by imposing periodic boundary\\nconditions. We derive \
analytical expressions for the ground state and excited\\nstates scaling \
functions, which provide an explicit description of the flow\\nbetween the IR \
and UV regimes of the model. Finally, the semiclassical form\\nfactors and \
two-point functions of the basic field and of the energy operator\\nare \
obtained, completing the semiclassical quantization of the \
Sine--Gordon\\nmodel on the cylinder.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 16 May 2004 15:45:48 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-10\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Mussardo\"", ",", "\"G.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Riva\"", ",", "\"V.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sotkov\"", ",", "\"G.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
