           "id" -> "hep-th/0405139", "submitter" -> "Giuseppe Mussardo", 
            "authors" -> "G. Mussardo, V. Riva, G. Sotkov", "title" -> 
            "Semiclassical Scaling Functions of Sine--Gordon Model", 
            "comments" -> "33 pages, 6 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys. B699 (2004) 545-574", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.08.004", "report-no" -> 
            "ISAS/32/2004/FM", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We present an analytic study of the finite size effects in \
Sine--Gordon\nmodel, based on the semiclassical quantization of an \
appropriate kink\nbackground defined on a cylindrical geometry. The \
quasi--periodic kink is\nrealized as an elliptic function with its real \
period related to the size of\nthe system. The stability equation for the \
small quantum fluctuations around\nthis classical background is of Lame' type \
and the corresponding energy\neigenvalues are selected inside the allowed \
bands by imposing periodic boundary\nconditions. We derive analytical \
expressions for the ground state and excited\nstates scaling functions, which \
provide an explicit description of the flow\nbetween the IR and UV regimes of \
the model. Finally, the semiclassical form\nfactors and two-point functions \
of the basic field and of the energy operator\nare obtained, completing the \
semiclassical quantization of the Sine--Gordon\nmodel on the cylinder.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 16 May 2004 15:45:48 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-10", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Mussardo", "G.", ""}, {"Riva", "V.", ""}, {
              "Sotkov", "G.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
