            "  In this paper we consider the possibility of application of \
the quantum\ninverse scattering method for studying the superconformal field \
theory and it's\nintegrable perturbations. The classical limit of the \
considered constructions\nis based on $\\hat{osp}(1|2)$ super-KdV hierarchy. \
The quantum counterpart of\nthe monodromy matrix corresponding to the linear \
problem associated with the\nL-operator is introduced. Using the explicit \
form of the irreducible\nrepresentations of $\\hat{osp}_q(1|2)$, the ``fusion \
relations'' for the\ntransfer-matrices (i.e. the traces of the monodromy \
matrices in different\nrepresentations) are obtained.\n", 
