           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0504122\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Davide Fioravanti\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Davide Fioravanti and Marco Rossi\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"From finite geometry exact quantities to (elliptic) \
scattering\\n  amplitudes for spin chains: the 1/2-XYZ\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Article, 41 pages, Latex\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0508:010,2005\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/08/010\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"YITP-04-58\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Initially, we derive a nonlinear integral equation for \
the vacuum counting\\nfunction of the spin 1/2-XYZ chain in the {\\\\it \
disordered regime}, thus\\nparalleling similar results by Kl\\\\\\\"umper \
\\\\cite{KLU}, achieved through a\\ndifferent technique in the {\\\\it \
antiferroelectric regime}. In terms of the\\ncounting function we obtain the \
usual physical quantities, like the energy and\\nthe transfer matrix \
(eigenvalues). Then, we introduce a double scaling limit\\nwhich appears to \
describe the sine-Gordon theory on cylindrical geometry, so\\ngeneralising \
famous results in the plane by Luther \\\\cite{LUT} and Johnson et\\nal. \
\\\\cite{JKM}. Furthermore, after extending the nonlinear integral equation \
to\\nexcitations, we derive scattering amplitudes involving \
solitons/antisolitons\\nfirst, and bound states later. The latter case comes \
out as manifestly related\\nto the Deformed Virasoro Algebra of Shiraishi et \
al. \\\\cite{SKAO}. Although this\\nnonlinear integral equations framework \
was contrived to deal with finite\\ngeometries, we prove it to be effective \
for discovering or rediscovering\\nS-matrices. As a particular example, we \
prove that this unique model furnishes\\nexplicitly two S-matrices, proposed \
respectively by Zamolodchikov \\\\cite{ZAMe}\\nand Lukyanov-Mussardo-Penati \
\\\\cite{LUK, MP} as plausible scattering description\\nof unknown integrable \
field theories.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 13 Apr 2005 18:36:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Fioravanti\"", ",", "\"Davide\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Rossi\"", ",", "\"Marco\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
              Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
            Function[BoxForm`e$, 
             TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "hep-th/0504122", "submitter" -> "Davide Fioravanti", 
             "authors" -> "Davide Fioravanti and Marco Rossi", "title" -> 
             "From finite geometry exact quantities to (elliptic) scattering\n\
  amplitudes for spin chains: the 1/2-XYZ", "comments" -> 
             "Article, 41 pages, Latex", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0508:010,2005",
              "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2005/08/010", "report-no" -> 
             "YITP-04-58", "categories" -> 
             "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
             Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  Initially, we derive a nonlinear integral equation for the \
vacuum counting\nfunction of the spin 1/2-XYZ chain in the {\\it disordered \
regime}, thus\nparalleling similar results by Kl\\\"umper \\cite{KLU}, \
achieved through a\ndifferent technique in the {\\it antiferroelectric \
regime}. In terms of the\ncounting function we obtain the usual physical \
quantities, like the energy and\nthe transfer matrix (eigenvalues). Then, we \
introduce a double scaling limit\nwhich appears to describe the sine-Gordon \
theory on cylindrical geometry, so\ngeneralising famous results in the plane \
by Luther \\cite{LUT} and Johnson et\nal. \\cite{JKM}. Furthermore, after \
extending the nonlinear integral equation to\nexcitations, we derive \
scattering amplitudes involving solitons/antisolitons\nfirst, and bound \
states later. The latter case comes out as manifestly related\nto the \
Deformed Virasoro Algebra of Shiraishi et al. \\cite{SKAO}. Although this\n\
nonlinear integral equations framework was contrived to deal with finite\n\
geometries, we prove it to be effective for discovering or rediscovering\n\
S-matrices. As a particular example, we prove that this unique model \
furnishes\nexplicitly two S-matrices, proposed respectively by Zamolodchikov \
\\cite{ZAMe}\nand Lukyanov-Mussardo-Penati \\cite{LUK, MP} as plausible \
scattering description\nof unknown integrable field theories.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Wed, 13 Apr 2005 18:36:55 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2009-11-11", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fioravanti", "Davide", ""}, {
               "Rossi", "Marco", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
        TagBox[
