           "id" -> "hep-th/0512337", "submitter" -> "Roberto Tateo", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Patrick Dorey, Anna Lishman, Chaiho Rim, Roberto Tateo", "title" -> 
            "Reflection factors and exact g-functions for purely elastic \
scattering\n  theories", "comments" -> 
            "45 pages, 7 figures. v2: minor typos corrected, 3 new references \
and\n  some further discussion of the massless boundary flows included", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B744:239-276,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.02.043", "report-no" -> "DCPT-05/63", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss reflection factors for purely elastic scattering \
theories and\nrelate them to perturbations of specific conformal boundary \
conditions, using\nrecent results on exact off-critical g-functions. For the \
non-unitary cases, we\nsupport our conjectures using a relationship with \
quantum group reductions of\nthe sine-Gordon model. Our results imply the \
existence of a variety of new\nflows between conformal boundary conditions, \
some of them driven by\nboundary-changing operators.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
