                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Non-linear integral equations derived from Bethe \
Ansatz are used to evaluate\\nfinite size corrections to the highest (i.e. \
{\\\\it anti-ferromagnetic}) and\\nimmediately lower anomalous dimensions of \
scalar operators in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM.\\nIn specific, multi-loop \
corrections are computed in the SU(2) operator\\nsubspace, whereas in the \
general SO(6) case only one loop calculations have\\nbeen finalised. In these \
cases, the leading finite size corrections are given\\nby means of explicit \
formul\\\\ae and compared with the exact numerical\\nevaluation. In addition, \
the method here proposed is quite general and\\nespecially suitable for \
numerical evaluations.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
