               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0603112\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Anastasia Doikou\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Anastasia Doikou\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The open XXZ and associated models at q root of \
unity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"31 pages, LATEX, minor typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Stat.Mech.0609:P05010,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1742-5468/2006/09/P09010\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The generalized open XXZ model at $q$ root of unity is \
considered. We review\\nhow associated models, such as the $q$ harmonic \
oscillator, and the lattice\\nsine-Gordon and Liouville models are obtained. \
Explicit expressions of the\\nlocal Hamiltonian of the spin ${1 \\\\over 2}$ \
XXZ spin chain coupled to dynamical\\ndegrees of freedom at the one end of \
the chain are provided. Furthermore, the\\nboundary non-local charges are \
given for the lattice sine Gordon model and the\\n$q$ harmonic oscillator \
with open boundaries. We then identify the spectrum and\\nthe corresponding \
Bethe states, of the XXZ and the q harmonic oscillator in the\\ncyclic \
representation with special non diagonal boundary conditions. Moreover,\\nthe \
spectrum and Bethe states of the lattice versions of the sine-Gordon \
and\\nLiouville models with open diagonal boundaries is examined. The role of \
the\\nconserved quantities (boundary non-local charges) in the derivation of \
the\\nspectrum is also discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
