                 "\"Bulk induced boundary perturbations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages, 1 figure, minor corrections, references \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"J.Phys.A40:F17,2007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The influence of closed string moduli on the D-brane \
moduli space is studied\\nfrom a worldsheet point of view. Whenever a D-brane \
cannot be adjusted to an\\ninfinitesimal change of the closed string \
background, the corresponding exactly\\nmarginal bulk operator ceases to be \
exactly marginal in the presence of the\\nbrane. The bulk perturbation then \
induces a renormalisation group flow on the\\nboundary whose end-point \
describes a conformal D-brane of the perturbed theory.\\nWe derive the \
relevant RG equations in general and illustrate the phenomenon\\nwith a \
number of examples, in particular the radius deformation of a free boson\\non \
a circle. At the self-dual radius we can give closed formulae for \
the\\ninduced boundary flows which are exact in the boundary coupling \
constants.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
