            "abstract" -> 
            "  The influence of closed string moduli on the D-brane moduli \
space is studied\nfrom a worldsheet point of view. Whenever a D-brane cannot \
be adjusted to an\ninfinitesimal change of the closed string background, the \
corresponding exactly\nmarginal bulk operator ceases to be exactly marginal \
in the presence of the\nbrane. The bulk perturbation then induces a \
renormalisation group flow on the\nboundary whose end-point describes a \
conformal D-brane of the perturbed theory.\nWe derive the relevant RG \
equations in general and illustrate the phenomenon\nwith a number of \
examples, in particular the radius deformation of a free boson\non a circle. \
At the self-dual radius we can give closed formulae for the\ninduced boundary \
flows which are exact in the boundary coupling constants.\n", 
