               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the strong coupling limit of AdS/CFT \
correspondence in the framework\\nof a recently proposed fermionic \
formulation of the Bethe Ansatz equations\\ngoverning the gauge theory \
anomalous dimensions. We provide examples of states\\nthat do not follow the \
Gubser-Klebanov-Polyakov law at large 't Hooft coupling\\n$\\\\lambda$, in \
contrast with recent results on the quantum string Bethe\\nequations valid in \
that regime. This result indicates that the fermionic\\nconstruction cannot \
be trusted at large $\\\\lambda$, although it remains an\\nefficient tool to \
compute the weak coupling expansion of anomalous dimensions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
