           "id" -> "hep-th/0702036", "submitter" -> "Albion Lawrence", 
            "authors" -> "Matthias R. Gaberdiel and Albion Lawrence", "title" -> 
            "Bulk perturbations of N=2 branes", "comments" -> 
            "35 pages (30 pages plus title and references), 8 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0705:087,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/05/087", "report-no" -> 
            "BRX-TH-581, NSF-KITP-06-125", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The evolution of supersymmetric A-type D-branes under the bulk\
\nrenormalization group flow between two different N=2 minimal models is \
studied.\nUsing the Landau-Ginzburg description we show that a specific set \
of branes\ndecouples from the infrared theory, and we make detailed \
predictions for the\nbehavior of the remaining branes. The Landau-Ginzburg \
picture is then checked\nagainst a direct conformal field theory analysis. In \
particular we construct a\nnatural index pairing which is preserved by the RG \
flow, and show that the\nbranes that decouple have vanishing index with the \
surviving branes.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 6 Feb 2007 16:02:34 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
