            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0703031\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ivan K. Kostov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ivan Kostov, Didina Serban, Dmytro Volin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Strong coupling limit of Bethe Ansatz equations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Typos corrected, references added, discrepancy with \
Beccaria at al.\\n  eliminated\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B789:413-451,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2007.06.017\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"SPhT-T07/029\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop a method to analyze the strong coupling \
limit of the Bethe ansatz\\nequations supposed to give the spectrum of \
anomalous dimensions of the planar\\n${\\\\cal N}=4$ gauge theory. This \
method is particularly adapted for the three\\nrank-one sectors, $su(2)$, \
$su(1|1)$ and $sl(2)$. We use the elliptic\\nparametrization of the Bethe \
ansatz variables, which degenerates to a\\nhyperbolic one in the strong \
coupling limit. We analyze the equations for the\\nhighest excited states in \
the su(2) and $su(1|1)$ sectors and for the state\\ncorresponding to the \
twist-two operator in the $sl(2)$ sector, both without and\\nwith the \
dressing kernel. In some cases we were able to give analytic\\nexpressions \
for the leading order magnon densities. Our method reproduces all\\nexisting \
analytical and numerical results for these states at the \
leading\\norder.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
