                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9510047\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Francesco Ravanini\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Davide Fioravanti, Francesco Ravanini and Marian \
Stanishkov\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Generalized KdV and Quantum Inverse Scattering \
Description of Conformal\\n  Minimal Models\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"12 pages, latex. 1 reference added\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Lett. B367 (1996) 113-120\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/0370-2693(95)01463-2\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DFUB-95-08\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We propose an alternative description of 2 dimensional \
Conformal Field Theory\\nin terms of Quantum Inverse Scattering. It is based \
on the generalized KdV\\nsystems attached to $A_2^{(2)}$, yielding the \
classical limit of Virasoro as\\nPoisson bracket structure. The corresponding \
T-system is shown to coincide with\\nthe one recently proposed by Kuniba and \
Suzuki. We classify the primary\\noperators of the minimal models that \
commute with all the Integrals of Motion,\\nand that are therefore candidates \
to perturb the model by keeping the\\nconservation laws. For our $A_2^{(2)}$ \
structure these happen to be\\n$\\\\phi_{1,2},\\\\phi_{2,1},\\\\phi_{1,5}$, \
in contrast to the $A_1^{(1)}$ case,\\nstudied by Bazhanov, Lukyanov and \
Zamolodchikov~\\\\cite{BLZ}, related to\\n$\\\\phi_{1,3}$.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
