             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  We propose an alternative description of 2 dimensional \
Conformal Field Theory\nin terms of Quantum Inverse Scattering. It is based \
on the generalized KdV\nsystems attached to $A_2^{(2)}$, yielding the \
classical limit of Virasoro as\nPoisson bracket structure. The corresponding \
T-system is shown to coincide with\nthe one recently proposed by Kuniba and \
Suzuki. We classify the primary\noperators of the minimal models that commute \
with all the Integrals of Motion,\nand that are therefore candidates to \
perturb the model by keeping the\nconservation laws. For our $A_2^{(2)}$ \
structure these happen to be\n$\\phi_{1,2},\\phi_{2,1},\\phi_{1,5}$, in \
contrast to the $A_1^{(1)}$ case,\nstudied by Bazhanov, Lukyanov and \
Zamolodchikov~\\cite{BLZ}, related to\n$\\phi_{1,3}$.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Mon, 9 Oct 1995 17:40:10 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
                "Thu, 19 Oct 1995 19:56:39 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2009-10-28", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fioravanti", "Davide", ""}, {
               "Ravanini", "Francesco", ""}, {"Stanishkov", "Marian", ""}}}], 
           "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[
          DiskBox[{2.080959039268521, -8.298200921109505}, 
           0.10102143756118451],
          TagBox[
