            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9607168\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Leung Hok Chim\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Leung Chim\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Central Charge and the Andrews-Bailey Construction\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex2e, requires cite.sty package, 13 pages. Additional \
footnote,\\n  citation and references\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Math.Phys. 40 (1999) 3761-3772\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1063/1.532925\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Research Report No.7, 1996\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  From the equivalence of the bosonic and fermionic \
representations of\\nfinitized characters in conformal field theory, one can \
extract mathematical\\nobjects known as Bailey pairs. Recently Berkovich, \
McCoy and Schilling have\\nconstructed a `generalized' character formula \
depending on two parameters $\\\\ra$\\nand $\\\\r2$, using the Bailey pairs \
of the unitary model $M(p-1,p)$. By taking\\nappropriate limits of these \
parameters, they were able to obtain the characters\\nof model $M(p,p+1)$, \
$N=1$ model $SM(p,p+2)$, and the unitary $N=2$ model with\\ncentral charge \
$c=3(1-{\\\\frac{2}{p}})$. In this letter we computed the effective\\ncentral \
charge associated with this `generalized' character formula using a\\nsaddle \
point method. The result is a simple expression in dilogarithms \
which\\ninterpolates between the central charges of these unitary \
models.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 22 Jul 1996 02:16:18 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 24 Jul 1996 07:15:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-10-30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Chim\"", ",", "\"Leung\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
