            "Central Charge and the Andrews-Bailey Construction", "comments" -> 
            "Latex2e, requires cite.sty package, 13 pages. Additional \
footnote,\n  citation and references", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J.Math.Phys. 40 (1999) 3761-3772", "doi" -> "10.1063/1.532925", 
            "report-no" -> "Research Report No.7, 1996", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  From the equivalence of the bosonic and fermionic \
representations of\nfinitized characters in conformal field theory, one can \
extract mathematical\nobjects known as Bailey pairs. Recently Berkovich, \
McCoy and Schilling have\nconstructed a `generalized' character formula \
depending on two parameters $\\ra$\nand $\\r2$, using the Bailey pairs of the \
unitary model $M(p-1,p)$. By taking\nappropriate limits of these parameters, \
they were able to obtain the characters\nof model $M(p,p+1)$, $N=1$ model \
$SM(p,p+2)$, and the unitary $N=2$ model with\ncentral charge \
$c=3(1-{\\frac{2}{p}})$. In this letter we computed the effective\ncentral \
charge associated with this `generalized' character formula using a\nsaddle \
point method. The result is a simple expression in dilogarithms which\n\
interpolates between the central charges of these unitary models.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
