               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9703026\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Vladimir Bazhanov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"R.M. Ellem, V.V. Bazhanov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz for the subleading magnetic \
perturbation of\\n  the tricritical Ising model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages, minor changes, references added. LaTeX file and \
postscript\\n  figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B512:563-580,1998\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00748-7\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give further support to Smirnov's conjecture on the \
exact kink S-matrix\\nfor the massive Quantum Field Theory describing the \
integrable perturbation of\\nthe c=0.7 minimal Conformal Field theory (known \
to describe the tri-critical\\nIsing model) by the operator $\\\\phi_{2,1}$. \
This operator has conformal\\ndimensions $(7/16,7/16)$ and is identified with \
the subleading magnetic\\noperator of the tri-critical Ising model. In this \
paper we apply the\\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (TBA) approach to the kink \
scattering theory by\\nexplicitly utilising its relationship with the \
solvable lattice hard hexagon\\nmodel. Analytically examining the ultraviolet \
scaling limit we recover the\\nexpected central charge c=0.7 of the \
tri-critical Ising model. We also compare\\nnumerical values for the ground \
state energy of the finite size system obtained\\nfrom the TBA equations with \
the results obtained by the Truncated Conformal\\nSpace Approach and \
Conformal Perturbation Theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
