          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9712220\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Barry McCoy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A. Berkovich, B.M. McCoy and P.A. Pearce\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The perturbations $\\\\phi_{2,1}$ and $\\\\phi_{1,5}$ of \
the minimal models\\n  $M(p,p')$ and the trinomial analogue of Bailey's lemma\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"34 pages, 15 figures, harvmac. References added and the \
TBA\\n  conjecture refined\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B519 (1998) 597-625\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(98)00167-9\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ITPSB 97-70\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th q-alg\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the fermionic polynomial generalizations of \
the characters of the\\nintegrable perturbations $\\\\phi_{2,1}$ and \
$\\\\phi_{1,5}$ of the general minimal\\n$M(p,p')$ conformal field theory by \
use of the recently discovered trinomial\\nanalogue of Bailey's lemma. For \
$\\\\phi_{2,1}$ perturbations results are given\\nfor all models with $2p>p'$ \
and for $\\\\phi_{1,5}$ perturbations results for all\\nmodels with \
${p'\\\\over 3}<p< {p'\\\\over 2}$ are obtained. For the \
$\\\\phi_{2,1}$\\nperturbation of the unitary case $M(p,p+1)$ we use the \
incidence matrix\\nobtained from these character polynomials to conjecture a \
set of TBA equations.\\nWe also find that for $\\\\phi_{1,5}$ with $2<p'/p < \
5/2$ and for $\\\\phi_{2,1}$\\nsatisfying $3p<2p'$ there are usually several \
different fermionic polynomials\\nwhich lead to the identical bosonic \
polynomial. We interpret this to mean that\\nin these cases the specification \
of the perturbing field is not sufficient to\\ndefine the theory and that an \
independent statement of the choice of the proper\\nvacuum must be \
made.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
