            "categories" -> "hep-th q-alg", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We derive the fermionic polynomial generalizations of the \
characters of the\nintegrable perturbations $\\phi_{2,1}$ and $\\phi_{1,5}$ \
of the general minimal\n$M(p,p')$ conformal field theory by use of the \
recently discovered trinomial\nanalogue of Bailey's lemma. For $\\phi_{2,1}$ \
perturbations results are given\nfor all models with $2p>p'$ and for \
$\\phi_{1,5}$ perturbations results for all\nmodels with ${p'\\over 3}<p< {p'\
\\over 2}$ are obtained. For the $\\phi_{2,1}$\nperturbation of the unitary \
case $M(p,p+1)$ we use the incidence matrix\nobtained from these character \
polynomials to conjecture a set of TBA equations.\nWe also find that for \
$\\phi_{1,5}$ with $2<p'/p < 5/2$ and for $\\phi_{2,1}$\nsatisfying $3p<2p'$ \
there are usually several different fermionic polynomials\nwhich lead to the \
identical bosonic polynomial. We interpret this to mean that\nin these cases \
the specification of the perturbing field is not sufficient to\ndefine the \
theory and that an independent statement of the choice of the proper\nvacuum \
must be made.\n", 
