               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"B. Stefanski Jr\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Landau-Lifshitz sigma-models, fermions and the AdS/CFT \
correspondence\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"42 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0707:009,2007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/07/009\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We define Landau-Lifshitz sigma models on general coset \
space $G/H$, with $H$\\na maximal stability sub-group of $G$. These are \
non-relativistic models that\\nhave $G$-valued N\\\\\\\"other charges, local \
$H$ invariance and are classically\\nintegrable. Using this definition, we \
construct the $PSU(2,2|4)/PS(U(2|2)^2)$\\nLandau-Lifshitz sigma-model. This \
sigma model describes the thermodynamic limit\\nof the spin-chain Hamiltonian \
obtained from the complete one-loop dilatation\\noperator of the N=4 super \
Yang-Mills (SYM) theory. In the second part of the\\npaper, we identify a \
number of consistent truncations of the Type IIB\\nGreen-Schwarz action on \
$AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ whose field content consists of two\\nreal bosons and \
4,8 or 16 real fermions. We show that $\\\\kappa$-symmetry acts\\ntrivially \
in these sub-sectors. In the context of the large spin limit of the\\nAdS/CFT \
correspondence, we map the Lagrangians of these sub-sectors \
to\\ncorresponding truncations of the $PSU(2,2|4)/PS(U(2|2)^2)$ \
Landau-Lifshitz\\nsigma-model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 11 Apr 2007 17:18:59 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
