            "  We define Landau-Lifshitz sigma models on general coset space \
$G/H$, with $H$\na maximal stability sub-group of $G$. These are \
non-relativistic models that\nhave $G$-valued N\\\"other charges, local $H$ \
invariance and are classically\nintegrable. Using this definition, we \
construct the $PSU(2,2|4)/PS(U(2|2)^2)$\nLandau-Lifshitz sigma-model. This \
sigma model describes the thermodynamic limit\nof the spin-chain Hamiltonian \
obtained from the complete one-loop dilatation\noperator of the N=4 super \
