Trancanelli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"More supersymmetric Wilson loops\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"9 pages, LaTeX\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D76:107703,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.76.107703\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"HU-EP-07/13, YITP-SB-07-12, Imperial/TP/07/RR/02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a large new family of Wilson loop operators \
in N=4 supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills theory. For an arbitrary curve on the \
three dimensional sphere one\\ncan add certain scalar couplings to the Wilson \
loop so it preserves at least\\ntwo supercharges. Some previously known \
loops, notably the 1/2 BPS circle,\\nbelong to this class, but we point out \
many more special cases which were not\\nknown before and could provide \
further tests of the AdS/CFT correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
