            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Solitons in field theory provide a window into regimes not \
directly\naccessible by the fundamental perturbative degrees of freedom. \
Motivated by\ninterest in the worldsheet S-matrix of string theory in AdS_5 x \
S^5 in the\nlimit of infinite worldsheet volume we consider the semiclassical \
quantization\nof a particular soliton of this theory: the Hofman-Maldacena \
`giant magnon'\nspinning string. We obtain explicit formulas for the complete \
spectrum of\nbosonic and fermionic fluctuations around the giant magnon. As \
an application\nof these results we confirm that the one-loop correction to \
the classical\nenergy vanishes as expected.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
