            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0705.0890\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Charlotte Kristjansen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"P. Y. Casteill (NBI) and C. Kristjansen (NBI and NORDITA)\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Strong Coupling Limit of the Scaling Function from \
the Quantum\\n  String Bethe Ansatz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages, one figure, v2: footnote changed, v3: reference \
added, typo\\n  corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B785:1-18,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2007.06.011\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NORDITA-2007-14\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the quantum string Bethe ansatz we derive the \
one-loop energy of a\\nfolded string rotating with angular momenta (S,J) in \
AdS_3 x S^1 inside AdS_5 x\\nS^5 in the limit 1 << J << S, z=\\\\lambda^(1/2) \
log(S/J) /(\\\\pi J) fixed. The\\none-loop energy is a sum of two \
contributions, one originating from the\\nHernandez-Lopez phase and another \
one being due to spin chain finite size\\neffects. We find a result which at \
the functional level exactly matches the\\nresult of a string theory \
computation. Expanding the result for large z we\\nobtain the strong coupling \
limit of the scaling function for low twist, high\\nspin operators of the \
SL(2) sector of N=4 SYM. In particular we recover the\\nfamous -3 \
log(2)/\\\\pi. Its appearance is a result of non-trivial \
cancellations\\nbetween the finite size effects and the Hernandez-Lopez \
correction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 7 May 2007 11:46:14 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 25 May 2007 13:38:35 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 7 Sep 2007 12:52:53 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
