           "id" -> "0705.0890", "submitter" -> "Charlotte Kristjansen", 
            "authors" -> 
            "P. Y. Casteill (NBI) and C. Kristjansen (NBI and NORDITA)", 
            "title" -> 
            "The Strong Coupling Limit of the Scaling Function from the \
Quantum\n  String Bethe Ansatz", "comments" -> 
            "18 pages, one figure, v2: footnote changed, v3: reference added, \
typo\n  corrected", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B785:1-18,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2007.06.011", "report-no" -> 
            "NORDITA-2007-14", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  Using the quantum string Bethe ansatz we derive the one-loop \
energy of a\nfolded string rotating with angular momenta (S,J) in AdS_3 x S^1 \
inside AdS_5 x\nS^5 in the limit 1 << J << S, z=\\lambda^(1/2) log(S/J) \
/(\\pi J) fixed. The\none-loop energy is a sum of two contributions, one \
originating from the\nHernandez-Lopez phase and another one being due to spin \
chain finite size\neffects. We find a result which at the functional level \
exactly matches the\nresult of a string theory computation. Expanding the \
result for large z we\nobtain the strong coupling limit of the scaling \
function for low twist, high\nspin operators of the SL(2) sector of N=4 SYM. \
In particular we recover the\nfamous -3 log(2)/\\pi. Its appearance is a \
result of non-trivial cancellations\nbetween the finite size effects and the \
Hernandez-Lopez correction.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 7 May 2007 11:46:14 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 25 May 2007 13:38:35 GMT"}, {
