        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.167765734591462`, -2.261948416892708}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0705.2429\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Kruczenski\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riei Ishizeki, Martin Kruczenski\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Single spike solutions for strings on S2 and S3\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX, 20 pages, 3 figures. v2: Refs added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D76:126006,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.76.126006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study solutions for rigidly rotating strings on a \
two sphere. Among them\\nwe find two limiting cases that have a particular \
interest, one is the already\\nknown giant magnon and the other we call the \
single spike solution. The\\nlimiting behavior of this last solution is a \
string infinitely wrapped around\\nthe equator. It differs from that solution \
by the existence of a single spike\\nof height theta that points toward the \
north pole.\\n  We study its properties and compute its energy E and angular \
momentum J as a\\nfunction of theta. We further generalize the solution by \
adding one angular\\nmomentum to obtain a solution on S3. We find a spin \
chain interpretations of\\nthese results in terms of free fermions and the \
Hubbard model but the exact\\nrelation with the same models derived from the \
field theory is not clear.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 17 May 2007 16:47:50 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 11 Oct 2007 22:01:58 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
