            "LaTeX, 20 pages, 3 figures. v2: Refs added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rev.D76:126006,2007", "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.76.126006",
             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null,
             "abstract" -> 
            "  We study solutions for rigidly rotating strings on a two \
sphere. Among them\nwe find two limiting cases that have a particular \
interest, one is the already\nknown giant magnon and the other we call the \
single spike solution. The\nlimiting behavior of this last solution is a \
string infinitely wrapped around\nthe equator. It differs from that solution \
by the existence of a single spike\nof height theta that points toward the \
north pole.\n  We study its properties and compute its energy E and angular \
momentum J as a\nfunction of theta. We further generalize the solution by \
adding one angular\nmomentum to obtain a solution on S3. We find a spin chain \
interpretations of\nthese results in terms of free fermions and the Hubbard \
model but the exact\nrelation with the same models derived from the field \
theory is not clear.\n", 
