         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0705.3131", "submitter" -> "Amir Esmaeil Mosaffa", 
            "authors" -> "A. E. Mosaffa, B. Safarzadeh", "title" -> 
            "Dual Spikes; New Spiky String Solutions", "comments" -> 
            "Added references", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0708:017,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/08/017", "report-no" -> "IPM/P-2007/033", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We find a new class of spiky solutions for closed strings in \
flat,\n$AdS_3\\subset AdS_5$ and $R\\times S^2(\\subset S^5)$ backgrounds. In \
the flat\ncase the new solutions turn out to be T-dual configurations of \
spiky strings\nfound by Kruczenski hep-th/0410226. In the case of solutions \
living in $AdS$,\nwe make a semi classical analysis by taking the large \
angular momentum limit.\nThe anomalous dimension for these dual spikes is \
similar to that for rotating\nand pulsating circular strings in AdS with \
angular momentum playing the role of\nthe level number. This replaces the \
well known logarithmic dependence for\nspinning strings. For the dual spikes \
living on sphere we find that no large\nangular momentum limit exists.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 22 May 2007 10:31:19 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 28 Jun 2007 13:18:51 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-04-30", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Mosaffa", "A. E.", ""}, {
              "Safarzadeh", "B.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{8.504466258286676, -11.213211285500858`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0705.3909\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Cristina Manuel\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Cristina Manuel and Felipe Llanes-Estrada\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bulk viscosity in a cold CFL superfluid\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"19 pages, 2 figures; one reference added, version to be \
published in\\n  JCAP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JCAP0708:001,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2007/08/001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute one of the bulk viscosity coefficients of \
cold CFL quark matter in\\nthe temperature regime where the contribution of \
mesons, quarks and gluons to\\ntransport phenomena is Boltzmann suppressed. \
In that regime dissipation occurs\\ndue to collisions of superfluid phonons, \
the Goldstone modes associated to the\\nspontaneous breaking of baryon \
symmetry. We first review the hydrodynamics of\\nrelativistic superfluids, \
and remind that there are at least three bulk\\nviscosity coefficients in \
these systems. We then compute the bulk viscosity\\ncoefficient associated to \
the normal fluid component of the superfluid. In our\\nanalysis we use Son's \
effective field theory for the superfluid phonon, amended\\nto include scale \
breaking effects proportional to the square of the strange\\nquark mass m_s. \
We compute the bulk viscosity at leading order in the scale\\nbreaking \
parameter, and find that it is dominated by collinear splitting and\\njoining \
processes. The resulting transport coefficient is zeta=0.011 \
m_s^4/T,\\ngrowing at low temperature T until the phonon fluid description \
stops making\\nsense. Our results are relevant to study the rotational \
properties of a compact\\nstar formed by CFL quark matter.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
