                 "\"A Yangian Double for the AdS/CFT Classical \
r-matrix\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages, no figures, LaTeX. v2: references added and \
minor changes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0706:083,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/06/083\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"MIT-CTP-3843\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We express the classical r-matrix of AdS/CFT in terms \
of tensor products\\ninvolving an infinite family of generators, which takes \
a form suggestive of\\nthe universal expression obtained from a Yangian \
double. This should provide an\\ninsight into the structure of the infinite \
dimensional symmetry algebra\\nunderlying the integrability of the model, and \
give a clue to the construction\\nof its universal R-matrix. We derive the \
commutation relations under which the\\nalgebra of these new generators \
close.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
