               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Finite size effects and 2-string deviations in the spin-1 \
XXZ chains\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A40:12007-12032,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8113/40/40/001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In an earlier work [1] J. Suzuki proposed a set of \
nonlinear integral\\nequations (NLIE) to describe the excited state spectrum \
of the integrable\\nspin-1 XXZ chain in its repulsive regime. In this paper \
we extend his equations\\nfor the attractive regime of the model, and \
calculate analytically the\\nconformal spectrum of the spin chain. We also \
discuss the typical root\\nconfigurations of the thermodynamic limit as well \
as the 2-string deviations of\\ncertain excited states of the model. Special \
objects appearing in the NLIE are\\nalso treated with special care.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
