            "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8113/40/40/001", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In an earlier work [1] J. Suzuki proposed a set of nonlinear \
integral\nequations (NLIE) to describe the excited state spectrum of the \
integrable\nspin-1 XXZ chain in its repulsive regime. In this paper we extend \
his equations\nfor the attractive regime of the model, and calculate \
analytically the\nconformal spectrum of the spin chain. We also discuss the \
typical root\nconfigurations of the thermodynamic limit as well as the \
2-string deviations of\ncertain excited states of the model. Special objects \
appearing in the NLIE are\nalso treated with special care.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
