               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0706.3751\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Donovan Young\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Donovan Young\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The AdS/CFT Correspondence: Classical, Quantum, and \
Thermodynamical\\n  Aspects\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PhD Thesis (supervisor: Gordon W. Semenoff), University \
of British\\n  Columbia, 190 pages, numerous figures. Section 2.5 contains \
some previously\\n  unpublished results for DLCQ plane-wave strings. Updated \
references in v2\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Certain aspects of the AdS/CFT correspondence are \
studied in detail. We\\ninvestigate the one-loop mass shift to certain \
two-impurity string states in\\nlight-cone string field theory on a plane \
wave background. We find that there\\nexist logarithmic divergences in the \
sums over intermediate mode numbers which\\ncancel between the cubic \
Hamiltonian and quartic \\\"contact term\\\". We argue that\\ngenerically, \
every order in intermediate state impurities contributes to the\\nmass shift \
at leading perturbative order. The same mass shift is also computed\\nusing \
an improved 3-string vertex proposed by Dobashi and Yoneya. The result \
is\\nfound to agree with gauge theory at leading order and is close but not \
quite in\\nagreement at subleading order. We extend the analysis to include \
discrete\\nlight-cone quantization, considering states with up to three units \
of p+. We\\nstudy the (apparently) first-order phase transition in the weakly \
coupled\\nplane-wave matrix model at finite temperature. We analyze the \
effect of\\ninteractions by computing the relevant parts of the effective \
potential for the\\nPolyakov loop operator to three loop order. We show that \
the phase transition\\nis indeed of first order. We also compute the 2-loop \
correction to the Hagedorn\\ntemperature. Finally, correlation functions of \
1/4 BPS Wilson loops with the\\ninfinite family of 1/2 BPS chiral primary \
operators are computed in N=4 super\\nYang-Mills theory by summing planar \
ladder diagrams. The correlation functions\\nare also computed in the \
strong-coupling limit using string theory; the result\\nis found to agree \
with the extrapolation of the planar ladders. The result is\\nrelated to \
similar correlators of 1/2 BPS loops by a simple re-scaling of the\\ncoupling \
constant, discovered by Drukker for the case of the 1/4 BPS loop \
VEV.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 26 Jun 2007 04:01:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 9 Jul 2007 20:46:19 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2007-07-09\""}]}, {
