            "PhD Thesis (supervisor: Gordon W. Semenoff), University of \
British\n  Columbia, 190 pages, numerous figures. Section 2.5 contains some \
previously\n  unpublished results for DLCQ plane-wave strings. Updated \
references in v2", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Certain aspects of the AdS/CFT correspondence are studied in \
detail. We\ninvestigate the one-loop mass shift to certain two-impurity \
string states in\nlight-cone string field theory on a plane wave background. \
We find that there\nexist logarithmic divergences in the sums over \
intermediate mode numbers which\ncancel between the cubic Hamiltonian and \
quartic \"contact term\". We argue that\ngenerically, every order in \
intermediate state impurities contributes to the\nmass shift at leading \
perturbative order. The same mass shift is also computed\nusing an improved \
3-string vertex proposed by Dobashi and Yoneya. The result is\nfound to agree \
with gauge theory at leading order and is close but not quite in\nagreement \
at subleading order. We extend the analysis to include discrete\nlight-cone \
quantization, considering states with up to three units of p+. We\nstudy the \
(apparently) first-order phase transition in the weakly coupled\nplane-wave \
matrix model at finite temperature. We analyze the effect of\ninteractions by \
computing the relevant parts of the effective potential for the\nPolyakov \
loop operator to three loop order. We show that the phase transition\nis \
indeed of first order. We also compute the 2-loop correction to the Hagedorn\n\
temperature. Finally, correlation functions of 1/4 BPS Wilson loops with the\n\
infinite family of 1/2 BPS chiral primary operators are computed in N=4 super\
\nYang-Mills theory by summing planar ladder diagrams. The correlation \
functions\nare also computed in the strong-coupling limit using string \
theory; the result\nis found to agree with the extrapolation of the planar \
ladders. The result is\nrelated to similar correlators of 1/2 BPS loops by a \
simple re-scaling of the\ncoupling constant, discovered by Drukker for the \
case of the 1/4 BPS loop VEV.\n", 
