               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0706.3936\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Davide Fioravanti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Davide Fioravanti and Marco Rossi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the commuting charges for the highest dimension SU(2) \
operators in\\n  planar ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex file, 20 pages, some typos corrected, some \
technical details\\n  expanded and explained\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0708:089,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/08/089\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the highest anomalous dimension operator in \
the SU(2) sector of\\nplanar ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM at all-loop, though \
neglecting wrapping contributions.\\nIn any case, the latter enter the loop \
expansion only after a precise\\nlength-depending order. In the thermodynamic \
limit we write both a linear\\nintegral equation for the Bethe root density \
and a linear system obeyed by the\\ncommuting charges. Consequently, we \
determine the leading strong coupling\\ncontribution to the density and from \
this an approximation to the leading and\\nsub-leading terms of any charge \
$Q_r$: it scales as $\\\\lambda ^{1/4-r/2}$, which\\ngeneralises the \
Gubser-Klebanov-Polyakov energy law. In the end, we briefly\\nextend these \
considerations to finite lengths and 'excited' operators by using\\nthe idea \
of a non-linear integral equation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
