               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0706.4121\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Belitsky\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A.V. Belitsky\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Analytic Bethe Ansatz and Baxter equations for long-range \
psl(2|2) spin\\n  chain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"32 pages, 2 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B793:363-395,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2007.09.009\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the largest particle-number-preserving sector \
of the dilatation\\noperator in maximally supersymmetric gauge theory. After \
exploring one-loop\\nBethe Ansatze for the underlying spin chain with \
psl(2|2) symmetry for simple\\nroot systems related to several Kac-Dynkin \
diagrams, we use the analytic Bethe\\nAnzats to construct eigenvalues of \
transfer matrices with finite-dimensional\\natypical representations in the \
auxiliary space. We derive closed Baxter\\nequations for eigenvalues of \
nested Baxter operators. We extend these\\nconsiderations for a \
non-distinguished root system with FBBF grading to all\\norders of \
perturbation theory in 't Hooft coupling. We construct generating\\nfunctions \
for all transfer matrices with auxiliary space determined by \
Young\\nsupertableaux (1^a) and (s) and find determinant formulas for \
transfer matrices\\nwith auxiliary spaces corresponding to skew Young \
supertableaux. The latter\\nyields fusion relations for transfer matrices \
with auxiliary space\\ncorresponding to representations labelled by square \
Young supertableaux. We\\nderive asymptotic Baxter equations which determine \
spectra of anomalous\\ndimensions of composite Wilson operators in noncompact \
psl(2|2) subsector of\\nN=4 super-Yang-Mills theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
