            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0707.1621\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Troels Harmark\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Troels Harmark, Kristjan R. Kristjansson and Marta \
Orselli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Decoupling limits of N=4 super Yang-Mills on R x \
S^3\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"48 pages, 1 figure; added references, published \
version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0709:115,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/09/115\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find new decoupling limits of N=4 super Yang-Mills \
(SYM) on R x S^3 with\\ngauge group SU(N). These decoupling limits lead to \
decoupled theories that are\\nmuch simpler than the full N=4 SYM but still \
contain many of its interesting\\nfeatures. The decoupling limits correspond \
to being in a near-critical region,\\nnear a point with zero temperature and \
critical chemical potentials. The new\\ndecoupling limits are found by \
generalizing the limits of hep-th/0605234 to\\ninclude not only the chemical \
potentials for the SU(4) R-symmetry of N=4 SYM\\nbut also the chemical \
potentials corresponding to the SO(4) symmetry. In the\\ndecoupled theories \
it is possible to take a strong coupling limit in a\\ncontrollable manner \
since the full effective Hamiltonian is known. For planar\\nN=4 SYM on R x \
S^3 all the decoupled theories correspond to fully integrable\\nspin chains. \
We study the thermodynamics of the decoupled theories and find the\\nHagedorn \
temperature for small and large values of the effective coupling. We\\nfind \
an alternative formulation of the decoupling limits in the \
microcanonical\\nensemble. This leads to a characterization of certain \
regimes of weakly coupled\\nN=4 SYM in which there are string-like states. \
Finally, we find a similar\\ndecoupling limit for pure Yang-Mills theory, \
which for the planar limit leads\\nto a fully integrable decoupled theory.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 11 Jul 2007 13:53:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 28 Sep 2007 09:20:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-04-30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Harmark\"", ",", "\"Troels\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Kristjansson\"", ",", "\"Kristjan R.\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Orselli\"", ",", "\"Marta\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
