            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0707.1676\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Erik Tonni\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sergio Benvenuti, Erik Tonni\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Near-flat space limit and Einstein manifolds\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"30 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0802:022,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/02/022\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the near-flat space limit for strings on \
AdS(5)xM(5), where the\\ninternal manifold M(5) is equipped with a generic \
metric with U(1)xU(1)xU(1)\\nisometry. In the bosonic sector, the limiting \
sigma model is similar to the one\\nfound for AdS(5)xS(5), as the global \
symmetries are reduced in the most general\\ncase. When M(5) is a \
Sasaki-Einstein space like T(1,1), Y(p,q) and L(p,q,r),\\nwhose dual CFT's \
have N=1 supersymmetry, the near-flat space limit gives the\\nsame bosonic \
sector of the sigma model found for AdS(5)xS(5). This indicates\\nthe generic \
presence of integrable subsectors in AdS/CFT.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 11 Jul 2007 18:13:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-04-30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Benvenuti\"", ",", "\"Sergio\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Tonni\"", ",", "\"Erik\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0707.1676", "submitter" -> "Erik Tonni", "authors" -> 
            "Sergio Benvenuti, Erik Tonni", "title" -> 
            "Near-flat space limit and Einstein manifolds", "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0802:022,2008", 
            "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/02/022", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the near-flat space limit for strings on AdS(5)xM(5), \
where the\ninternal manifold M(5) is equipped with a generic metric with \
U(1)xU(1)xU(1)\nisometry. In the bosonic sector, the limiting sigma model is \
similar to the one\nfound for AdS(5)xS(5), as the global symmetries are \
reduced in the most general\ncase. When M(5) is a Sasaki-Einstein space like \
T(1,1), Y(p,q) and L(p,q,r),\nwhose dual CFT's have N=1 supersymmetry, the \
near-flat space limit gives the\nsame bosonic sector of the sigma model found \
for AdS(5)xS(5). This indicates\nthe generic presence of integrable \
subsectors in AdS/CFT.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 11 Jul 2007 18:13:55 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-04-30", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Benvenuti", "Sergio", ""}, {
              "Tonni", "Erik", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.125474648251295`, -4.467434855642976}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0707.2082\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Thomas Klose\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Valentina Giangreco Marotta Puletti, Thomas Klose and \
Olof Ohlsson Sax\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Factorized world-sheet scattering in near-flat AdS_5 x \
S^5\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages, 5 figures, v2: reference added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B792:228-256,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2007.09.018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UUITP-14/07\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show the factorization of the three-particle \
world-sheet S-matrix of AdS_5\\nx S^5 superstring theory in the \
near-flat-space limit at one loop order. This\\nis done by computing various \
scattering amplitudes from Feynman diagrams in the\\nworld-sheet theory. The \
knowledge of certain highest weight amplitudes allows\\nus to fix all the \
freedom in the three-particle S-matrix, which we argue to be\\nconstrained up \
to four scalar functions due to the symmetries of the model. We\\ndemonstrate \
that these amplitudes are given by corresponding products of the\\nknown \
two-particle S-matrix elements, from which it follows that the \
scattering\\nof any three world-sheet excitations factorizes. This provides \
an explicit and\\ndirect check of the quantum integrability of string theory \
in near-flat AdS_5 x\\nS^5 as it renders evidence for the existence of higher \
conserved charges. By\\ncomputing further amplitudes we also obtain an \
indirect confirmation of the\\nsupersymmetries of the near-flat-space \
model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 16 Jul 2007 18:12:52 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 24 Jul 2007 09:55:19 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
