         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0707.2082", "submitter" -> "Thomas Klose", "authors" -> 
            "Valentina Giangreco Marotta Puletti, Thomas Klose and Olof \
Ohlsson Sax", "title" -> 
            "Factorized world-sheet scattering in near-flat AdS_5 x S^5", 
            "comments" -> "33 pages, 5 figures, v2: reference added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B792:228-256,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2007.09.018", "report-no" -> "UUITP-14/07", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We show the factorization of the three-particle world-sheet \
S-matrix of AdS_5\nx S^5 superstring theory in the near-flat-space limit at \
one loop order. This\nis done by computing various scattering amplitudes from \
Feynman diagrams in the\nworld-sheet theory. The knowledge of certain highest \
weight amplitudes allows\nus to fix all the freedom in the three-particle \
S-matrix, which we argue to be\nconstrained up to four scalar functions due \
to the symmetries of the model. We\ndemonstrate that these amplitudes are \
given by corresponding products of the\nknown two-particle S-matrix elements, \
from which it follows that the scattering\nof any three world-sheet \
excitations factorizes. This provides an explicit and\ndirect check of the \
quantum integrability of string theory in near-flat AdS_5 x\nS^5 as it \
renders evidence for the existence of higher conserved charges. By\ncomputing \
further amplitudes we also obtain an indirect confirmation of the\n\
supersymmetries of the near-flat-space model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 16 Jul 2007 18:12:52 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 24 Jul 2007 09:55:19 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{
              "Puletti", "Valentina Giangreco Marotta", ""}, {
              "Klose", "Thomas", ""}, {"Sax", "Olof Ohlsson", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
