                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"HU-EP-07/23, YITP-SB-07-23, Imperial/TP/07/RR/03\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this note we study supersymmetric Wilson loops \
restricted to an S^2\\nsubmanifold of four-dimensional space in N=4 super \
Yang-Mills. We provide\\nevidence from both perturbation theory and the AdS \
dual that those loops are\\nequal to the analogous observables in \
two-dimensional Yang-Mills on S^2\\n(excluding non-perturbative \
contributions). This relates a subsector of N=4 SYM\\nto a low-dimensional \
soluble model and also suggests that this subsector of N\\n=4 SYM is \
invariant under area preserving diffeomorphisms.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
