            "  We consider high spin operators. We give a general argument \
for the\nlogarithmic scaling of their anomalous dimensions which is based on \
the\nsymmetries of the problem. By an analytic continuation we can also see \
the\norigin of the double logarithmic divergence in the Sudakov factor. We \
show that\nthe cusp anomalous dimension is the energy density for a flux \
configuration of\nthe gauge theory on $AdS_3 \\times S^1$. We then focus on \
operators in ${\\cal\nN}=4$ super Yang Mills which carry large spin and SO(6) \
charge and show that in\na particular limit their properties are described in \
