               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Chong-Sun Chu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Chong-Sun Chu, Dimitrios Giataganas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Near BPS Wilson Loop in beta-deformed Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX. v2: corrections and comments added (22 pages). v3: \
proof of\\n  the finitness of the vev of the Wilson loop is extended to the \
next to\\n  leading order. appendices C and D added. version to appear in \
JHEP (23 pages)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0710:108,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/10/108\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a definition of the Wilson loop operator in \
the N=1 beta-deformed\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory. Although the \
operator is not BPS, it has a\\nfinite expectation value at least up to order \
(g^2 N)^2. This does not happen\\ngenerally for a generic non-BPS Wilson loop \
whose expectation value is UV\\ndivergent. For this reason we call this a \
near-BPS Wilson loop and conjecture\\nthat its exact expectation value is \
finite. We derive the general form of the\\nboundary condition satisfied by \
the dual string worldsheet and find that it is\\ndeformed. Finiteness of the \
expectation value of the Wilson loop, together with\\nsome rather remarkable \
properties of the Lunin-Maldacena metric and the\\nB-field, fixes the \
boundary condition to be one which is characterized by the\\nvielbein of the \
deformed supergravity metric. The Wilson loop operators provide\\nnatural \
candidates as dual descriptions to some of the existing \
D-brane\\nconfigurations in the Lunin-Maldacena background. We also construct \
the string\\ndual configuration for a near-1/4 BPS circular Wilson loop \
operator. The string\\nlies on a deformed three-sphere instead of a \
two-sphere as in the undeformed\\ncase. The expectation value of the Wilson \
loop operator is computed using the\\nAdS/CFT correspondence and is found to \
be independent of the deformation. We\\nconjecture that the exact expectation \
value of the Wilson loop is given by the\\nsame matrix model as in the \
undeformed case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 6 Aug 2007 17:13:52 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
