            "LaTeX. v2: corrections and comments added (22 pages). v3: proof \
of\n  the finitness of the vev of the Wilson loop is extended to the next to\n\
  leading order. appendices C and D added. version to appear in JHEP (23 \
pages)", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0710:108,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/10/108", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We propose a definition of the Wilson loop operator in the N=1 \
beta-deformed\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory. Although the operator is not \
BPS, it has a\nfinite expectation value at least up to order (g^2 N)^2. This \
does not happen\ngenerally for a generic non-BPS Wilson loop whose \
expectation value is UV\ndivergent. For this reason we call this a near-BPS \
Wilson loop and conjecture\nthat its exact expectation value is finite. We \
derive the general form of the\nboundary condition satisfied by the dual \
string worldsheet and find that it is\ndeformed. Finiteness of the \
expectation value of the Wilson loop, together with\nsome rather remarkable \
properties of the Lunin-Maldacena metric and the\nB-field, fixes the boundary \
condition to be one which is characterized by the\nvielbein of the deformed \
supergravity metric. The Wilson loop operators provide\nnatural candidates as \
dual descriptions to some of the existing D-brane\nconfigurations in the \
Lunin-Maldacena background. We also construct the string\ndual configuration \
for a near-1/4 BPS circular Wilson loop operator. The string\nlies on a \
deformed three-sphere instead of a two-sphere as in the undeformed\ncase. The \
expectation value of the Wilson loop operator is computed using the\nAdS/CFT \
correspondence and is found to be independent of the deformation. We\n\
conjecture that the exact expectation value of the Wilson loop is given by \
the\nsame matrix model as in the undeformed case.\n", 
