            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0708.1625\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Mironov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A. Mironov, A. Morozov and T. N. Tomaras\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On n-point Amplitudes in N=4 SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"minor cosmetic changes, references added in the \
introduction\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0711:021,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/11/021\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The computation of n-point planar amplitudes in N=4 SYM \
at strong coupling is\\nknown to be reduced to the search for solutions of \
the integrable 2d SO(4,2)\\nsigma-model with growing asymptotics on the \
world-sheet and to the study of\\ntheir Whitham deformations induced by an \
epsilon-regularization, which breaks\\nboth integrability and SO(4,2) \
symmetry. A multi-parameter (moduli) family of\\nsuch solutions is \
constructed for n=4. They all correspond to the same s and t\\nand some are \
related by SO(4,2) transformations. Nevertheless, they lead to\\ndifferent \
regularized areas, whose minimum is the Alday-Maldacena solution. A\\nbrief \
review of results on n-point amplitudes is also provided, with \
special\\nemphasis on the underlying equivalence of the above regularized \
minimal area in\\nAdS and a double contour integral along the same boundary, \
two purely geometric\\nquantities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
