            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The computation of n-point planar amplitudes in N=4 SYM at \
strong coupling is\nknown to be reduced to the search for solutions of the \
integrable 2d SO(4,2)\nsigma-model with growing asymptotics on the \
world-sheet and to the study of\ntheir Whitham deformations induced by an \
epsilon-regularization, which breaks\nboth integrability and SO(4,2) \
symmetry. A multi-parameter (moduli) family of\nsuch solutions is constructed \
for n=4. They all correspond to the same s and t\nand some are related by \
SO(4,2) transformations. Nevertheless, they lead to\ndifferent regularized \
areas, whose minimum is the Alday-Maldacena solution. A\nbrief review of \
results on n-point amplitudes is also provided, with special\nemphasis on the \
underlying equivalence of the above regularized minimal area in\nAdS and a \
double contour integral along the same boundary, two purely geometric\n\
quantities.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
