          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0708.2568\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Oisin A. P. Mac Conamhna\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Oisin A. P. Mac Conamhna\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spacetime singularity resolution by M-theory fivebranes: \
calibrated\\n  geometry, Anti-de Sitter solutions and special holonomy \
metrics\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1+52 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Commun.Math.Phys.284:345-389,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s00220-008-0570-x\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial/TP/2007/OC/03\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The supergravity description of various configurations \
of supersymmetric\\nM-fivebranes wrapped on calibrated cycles of special \
holonomy manifolds is\\nstudied. The description is provided by solutions of \
eleven-dimensional\\nsupergravity which interpolate smoothly between a \
special holonomy manifold and\\nan event horizon with Anti-de Sitter \
geometry. For known examples of Anti-de\\nSitter solutions, the associated \
special holonomy metric is derived. One\\nexplicit Anti-de Sitter solution of \
M-theory is so treated for fivebranes\\nwrapping each of the following \
cycles: K\\\\\\\"{a}hler cycles in Calabi-Yau two-,\\nthree- and four-folds; \
special lagrangian cycles in three- and four-folds;\\nassociative three- and \
co-associative four-cycles in $G_2$ manifolds; complex\\nlagrangian \
four-cycles in $Sp(2)$ manifolds; and Cayley four-cycles in\\n$Spin(7)$ \
manifolds. In each case, the associated special holonomy metric \
is\\nsingular, and is a hyperbolic analogue of a known metric. The analogous \
known\\nmetrics are respectively: Eguchi-Hanson, the resolved conifold and \
the\\nfour-fold resolved conifold; the deformed conifold, and the Stenzel \
four-fold\\nmetric; the Bryant-Salamon-Gibbons-Page-Pope $G_2$ metrics on an \
$\\\\mathbb{R}^4$\\nbundle over $S^3$, and an $\\\\mathbb{R}^3$ bundle over \
$S^4$ or $\\\\mathbb{CP}^2$;\\nthe Calabi hyper-K\\\\\\\"{a}hler metric on \
$T^*\\\\mathbb{CP}^2$; and the\\nBryant-Salamon-Gibbons-Page-Pope $Spin(7)$ \
metric on an $\\\\mathbb{R}^4$ bundle\\nover $S^4$. By the AdS/CFT \
correspondence, a conformal field theory is\\nassociated to each of the new \
singular special holonomy metrics, and defines\\nthe quantum gravitational \
physics of the resolution of their singularities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 20 Aug 2007 15:34:50 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Mac Conamhna\"", ",", "\"Oisin A. P.\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
