          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0708.2568", "submitter" -> "Oisin A. P. Mac Conamhna", 
            "authors" -> "Oisin A. P. Mac Conamhna", "title" -> 
            "Spacetime singularity resolution by M-theory fivebranes: \
calibrated\n  geometry, Anti-de Sitter solutions and special holonomy \
metrics", "comments" -> "1+52 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Commun.Math.Phys.284:345-389,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/s00220-008-0570-x", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial/TP/2007/OC/03", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The supergravity description of various configurations of \
supersymmetric\nM-fivebranes wrapped on calibrated cycles of special holonomy \
manifolds is\nstudied. The description is provided by solutions of \
eleven-dimensional\nsupergravity which interpolate smoothly between a special \
holonomy manifold and\nan event horizon with Anti-de Sitter geometry. For \
known examples of Anti-de\nSitter solutions, the associated special holonomy \
metric is derived. One\nexplicit Anti-de Sitter solution of M-theory is so \
treated for fivebranes\nwrapping each of the following cycles: K\\\"{a}hler \
cycles in Calabi-Yau two-,\nthree- and four-folds; special lagrangian cycles \
in three- and four-folds;\nassociative three- and co-associative four-cycles \
in $G_2$ manifolds; complex\nlagrangian four-cycles in $Sp(2)$ manifolds; and \
Cayley four-cycles in\n$Spin(7)$ manifolds. In each case, the associated \
special holonomy metric is\nsingular, and is a hyperbolic analogue of a known \
metric. The analogous known\nmetrics are respectively: Eguchi-Hanson, the \
resolved conifold and the\nfour-fold resolved conifold; the deformed \
conifold, and the Stenzel four-fold\nmetric; the \
Bryant-Salamon-Gibbons-Page-Pope $G_2$ metrics on an $\\mathbb{R}^4$\nbundle \
over $S^3$, and an $\\mathbb{R}^3$ bundle over $S^4$ or $\\mathbb{CP}^2$;\n\
the Calabi hyper-K\\\"{a}hler metric on $T^*\\mathbb{CP}^2$; and the\n\
Bryant-Salamon-Gibbons-Page-Pope $Spin(7)$ metric on an $\\mathbb{R}^4$ \
bundle\nover $S^4$. By the AdS/CFT correspondence, a conformal field theory \
is\nassociated to each of the new singular special holonomy metrics, and \
defines\nthe quantum gravitational physics of the resolution of their \
singularities.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 20 Aug 2007 15:34:50 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Mac Conamhna", "Oisin A. P.", ""}}}], 
