                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Observing that the Hamiltonian of the renormalisable \
scalar field theory on\\n4-dimensional Moyal space A is the square of a Dirac \
operator D of spectral\\ndimension 8, we complete (A,D) to a compact \
8-dimensional spectral triple. We\\nadd another Connes-Lott copy and compute \
the spectral action of the\\ncorresponding U(1)-Yang-Mills-Higgs model. We \
find that in the Higgs potential\\nthe square \\\\phi^2 of the Higgs field is \
shifted to \\\\phi * \\\\phi + const X_\\\\mu *\\nX^\\\\mu, where X_\\\\mu is \
the covariant coordinate. The classical field equations\\nof our model imply \
that the vacuum is no longer given by a constant Higgs\\nfield, but both the \
Higgs and gauge fields receive non-constant vacuum\\nexpectation \
values.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
