        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.996964404976666`, -4.294413631945356}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0709.3487\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pedro Vieira G.\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nikolay Gromov, Pedro Vieira\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Complete 1-loop test of AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"12 figures. References added. Couple of words added to \
abstract\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0804:046,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/04/046\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze nested Bethe ansatz (NBA) and the \
corresponding finite size\\ncorrections. We find an integral equation which \
describes these corrections in\\na closed form. As an application we \
considered the conjectured\\nBeisert-Staudacher (BS) equations with the \
Hernandez-Lopez dressing factor\\nwhere the finite size corrections should \
reproduce generic one (worldsheet)\\nloop computations around any classical \
superstring motion in the AdS_5 x S^5\\nbackground with exponential precision \
in the large angular momentum of the\\nstring states. Indeed, we show that \
our integral equation can be interpreted as\\na sum over all physical \
fluctuations and thus prove the complete 1-loop\\nconsistency of the BS \
equations. In other words we demonstrate that any local\\nconserved charge \
(including the AdS Energy) computed from the BS equations is\\nindeed given \
at 1-loop by the sum of charges of fluctuations up to\\nexponentially \
suppressed contributions. Contrary to all previous studies of\\nfinite size \
corrections, which were limited to simple configurations inside\\nrank one \
subsectors, our treatment is completely general.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 21 Sep 2007 17:59:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 30 Oct 2007 21:27:50 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-06-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Gromov\"", ",", "\"Nikolay\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Vieira\"", ",", "\"Pedro\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0709.3487", "submitter" -> "Pedro Vieira G.", "authors" -> 
            "Nikolay Gromov, Pedro Vieira", "title" -> 
            "Complete 1-loop test of AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "12 figures. References added. Couple of words added to abstract",
             "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0804:046,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/04/046", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We analyze nested Bethe ansatz (NBA) and the corresponding \
finite size\ncorrections. We find an integral equation which describes these \
corrections in\na closed form. As an application we considered the \
conjectured\nBeisert-Staudacher (BS) equations with the Hernandez-Lopez \
dressing factor\nwhere the finite size corrections should reproduce generic \
one (worldsheet)\nloop computations around any classical superstring motion \
in the AdS_5 x S^5\nbackground with exponential precision in the large \
angular momentum of the\nstring states. Indeed, we show that our integral \
equation can be interpreted as\na sum over all physical fluctuations and thus \
prove the complete 1-loop\nconsistency of the BS equations. In other words we \
demonstrate that any local\nconserved charge (including the AdS Energy) \
computed from the BS equations is\nindeed given at 1-loop by the sum of \
charges of fluctuations up to\nexponentially suppressed contributions. \
Contrary to all previous studies of\nfinite size corrections, which were \
limited to simple configurations inside\nrank one subsectors, our treatment \
is completely general.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 21 Sep 2007 17:59:00 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 30 Oct 2007 21:27:50 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-06-19", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Gromov", "Nikolay", ""}, {
              "Vieira", "Pedro", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
