          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0709.4033", "submitter" -> "Keisuke Okamura", "authors" -> 
            "Hirotaka Hayashi, Keisuke Okamura, Ryo Suzuki, Benoit Vicedo", 
            "title" -> "Large Winding Sector of AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "1+52 pages, 10 figures, v2: references and comments added, v3: \
minor\n  changes and a reference added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0711:033,2007", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/11/033", 
            "report-no" -> "UT-07-26, DAMTP-2007-83", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study a family of classical strings on R x S^3 subspace of \
the AdS_5 x S^5\nbackground that interpolates between pulsating strings and \
single-spike\nstrings. They are obtained from the helical strings of \
hep-th/0609026 by\ninterchanging worldsheet time and space coordinates, which \
maps\nrotating/spinning string states with large spins to oscillating states \
with\nlarge winding numbers. From a finite-gap perspective, this \
transformation is\nrealised as an interchange of quasi-momentum and \
quasi-energy defined for the\nalgebraic curve. The gauge theory duals are \
also discussed, and are identified\nwith operators in the non-holomorphic \
sector of N=4 super Yang-Mills. They can\nbe viewed as excited states above \
the ``antiferromagnetic'' state, which is\n``the farthest from BPS'' in the \
spin-chain spectrum. Furthermore, we\ninvestigate helical strings on AdS_3 x \
S^1 in an appendix.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 26 Sep 2007 10:28:33 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 2 Oct 2007 14:22:38 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 19 Nov 2007 17:05:28 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-06-19", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Hayashi", "Hirotaka", ""}, {
              "Okamura", "Keisuke", ""}, {"Suzuki", "Ryo", ""}, {
              "Vicedo", "Benoit", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.557673440994776`, -3.5143201152279975`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0710.0217\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matteo Beccaria\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Beccaria and Valentina Forini\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Anomalous dimensions of finite size field strength \
operators in N=4 SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages, 3 eps figures. v2: published version, minor \
changes,\\n  references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0711:031,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/11/031\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-EP-07/29\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the N=4 super Yang-Mills theory, we consider the \
higher order anomalous\\ndimensions gamma_L(g) of purely gluonic operators \
Tr(F^L) where F is a\\ncomponent of the self-dual field strength. We propose \
compact closed\\nexpressions depending parametrically on L that reproduce the \
prediction of\\nBethe Ansatz equations up to five loop order, including \
transcendental dressing\\ncorrections. The size dependence follows a simple \
pattern as the perturbative\\norder is increased and suggests hidden \
relations for these special operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
