           "id" -> "0710.0217", "submitter" -> "Matteo Beccaria", "authors" -> 
            "Matteo Beccaria and Valentina Forini", "title" -> 
            "Anomalous dimensions of finite size field strength operators in \
N=4 SYM", "comments" -> 
            "26 pages, 3 eps figures. v2: published version, minor changes,\n \
 references added", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0711:031,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/11/031", "report-no" -> "HU-EP-07/29", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In the N=4 super Yang-Mills theory, we consider the higher \
order anomalous\ndimensions gamma_L(g) of purely gluonic operators Tr(F^L) \
where F is a\ncomponent of the self-dual field strength. We propose compact \
closed\nexpressions depending parametrically on L that reproduce the \
prediction of\nBethe Ansatz equations up to five loop order, including \
transcendental dressing\ncorrections. The size dependence follows a simple \
pattern as the perturbative\norder is increased and suggests hidden relations \
for these special operators.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 1 Oct 2007 07:20:09 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 14 Nov 2007 12:05:40 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
