               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arutyunov Gleb E\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gleb Arutyunov and Sergey Frolov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On String S-matrix, Bound States and TBA\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"77 pages, 6 figures, v2: the statement about the \
periodicity\\n  condition for mirror fermions corrected; typos corrected; \
references added,\\n  v3: misprints corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0712:024,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/12/024\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"ITP-UU-07-50, SPIN-07-37, TCDMATH 07-15\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The study of finite J effects for the light-cone AdS \
superstring by means of\\nthe Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz requires an \
understanding of a companion 2d\\ntheory which we call the mirror model. It \
is obtained from the original string\\nmodel by the double Wick rotation. The \
S-matrices describing the scattering of\\nphysical excitations in the string \
and mirror models are related to each other\\nby an analytic continuation. We \
show that the unitarity requirement for the\\nmirror S-matrix fixes the \
S-matrices of both theories essentially uniquely. The\\nresulting string \
S-matrix S(z_1,z_2) satisfies the generalized unitarity\\ncondition and, up \
to a scalar factor, is a meromorphic function on the elliptic\\ncurve \
associated to each variable z. The double Wick rotation is \
then\\naccomplished by shifting the variables z by quarter of the imaginary \
period of\\nthe torus. We discuss the apparent bound states of the string and \
mirror\\nmodels, and show that depending on a choice of the physical region \
there are\\none, two or 2^{M-1} solutions of the M-particle bound state \
equations sharing\\nthe same conserved charges. For very large but finite \
values of J, most of\\nthese solutions, however, exhibit various signs of \
pathological behavior. In\\nparticular, they might receive a finite J \
correction to their energy which is\\ncomplex, or the energy correction might \
exceed corrections arising due to\\nfinite J modifications of the Bethe \
equations thus making the asymptotic Bethe\\nansatz inapplicable.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 8 Oct 2007 14:53:59 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 22 Oct 2007 13:09:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 3 Dec 2007 14:33:39 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-06-10\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
