            "authors" -> "C. D. Fosco and G. A. Silva", "title" -> 
            "Noncommutative real scalar field theory in 2+1 dimensions at \
finite\n  temperature", "comments" -> 
            "22 pages. v2: reference added, JHEP accepted", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP0801:011,2008", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/01/011", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study thermal effects for a noncommutative real scalar \
field in 2+1\ndimensions including a Grosse-Wulkenhaar term. Using a \
perturbative expansion\nfor the free energy, we deduce some general \
properties of the corresponding\ncontributions, in the thermodynamic limit. \
We show that the model can be\nconsistently interpreted as defined on a \
finite volume, which is naturally\ndetermined by the noncommutativity scale.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 20 Oct 2007 12:16:13 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 3 Jan 2008 19:13:30 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fosco", "C. D.", ""}, {
              "Silva", "G. A.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
