               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Contribution to the \\\"International Conference on \
Noncommutative\\n  Geometry and Physics\\\", April 2007, Orsay \
(France)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.Conf.Ser.103:012015,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1742-6596/103/1/012015\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  I present the exact energy eigenstates and eigenvalues \
of a quantum many-body\\nsystem of bosons on non-commutative space and in a \
harmonic oszillator\\nconfining potential at the selfdual point. I also argue \
that this exactly\\nsolvable system is a prototype model which provides a \
generalization of mean\\nfield theory taking into account non-trivial \
correlations which are peculiar to\\nboson systems in two space dimensions \
and relevant in condensed matter physics.\\nThe prologue and epilogue contain \
a few remarks to relate my main story to\\nrecent developments in \
non-commutative quantum field theory and an addendum to\\nour previous work \
together with Szabo and Zarembo on this latter subject.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
