          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0711.0155", "submitter" -> "Arkady Tseytlin", "authors" -> 
            "M. Grigoriev and A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Pohlmeyer reduction of AdS_5 x S^5 superstring sigma model", 
            "comments" -> 
            "56 pages. v2: section 6.4 expanded with comments on mass \
spectrum and\n  the corresponding S-matrix; v3,v4: minor corrections and \
clarifications added", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B800:450-501,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2008.01.006", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AT-2007-4, NI07093", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Motivated by a desire to find a useful 2d Lorentz-invariant \
reformulation of\nthe AdS_5 x S^5 superstring world-sheet theory in terms of \
physical degrees of\nfreedom we construct the Pohlmeyer-reduced version of \
the corresponding sigma\nmodel. The Pohlmeyer reduction procedure involves \
several steps. Starting with\na coset space string sigma model in the \
conformal gauge and writing the\nclassical equations in terms of currents one \
can fix the residual conformal\ndiffeomorphism symmetry and kappa-symmetry \
and introduce a new set of variables\n(related locally to currents but \
non-locally to the original string coordinate\nfields) so that the Virasoro \
constraints are automatically satisfied. The\nresulting gauge-fixed equations \
can be obtained from a Lagrangian of a\nnon-abelian Toda type: a gauged WZW \
model with an integrable potential coupled\nalso to a set of 2d fermionic \
fields. A gauge-fixed form of the\nPohlmeyer-reduced theory can be found by \
integrating out the 2d gauge field of\nthe gauged WZW model. Its \
small-fluctuation spectrum contains 8 bosonic and 8\nfermionic degrees of \
freedom with equal masses. We conjecture that the reduced\nmodel has \
world-sheet supersymmetry and is ultraviolet-finite. We show that in\nthe \
special case of the AdS_2 x S^2 superstring model the reduced theory is\n\
indeed supersymmetric: it is equivalent to the N=2 supersymmetric extension \
of\nthe sine-Gordon model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 1 Nov 2007 19:57:01 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 6 Nov 2007 19:52:08 GMT"}, {
