        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{19.45436840472266, -4.6783502573180025`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0711.0707\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Wolf\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riccardo Ricci, Arkady A. Tseytlin, Martin Wolf\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On T-Duality and Integrability for Strings on AdS \
Backgrounds\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"20 pages; v2: misprints corrected, references and \
minor\\n  clarifications added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0712:082,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/12/082\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-RR-04/2007\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss an interplay between T-duality and \
integrability for certain\\nclassical non-linear sigma models. In particular, \
we consider strings on the\\nAdS_5 x S^5 background and perform T-duality \
along the four isometry directions\\nof AdS_5 in the Poincare patch. The \
T-dual of the AdS_5 sigma model is again a\\nsigma model on an AdS_5 space. \
This classical T-duality relation was used in\\nthe recently uncovered \
connection between light-like Wilson loops and MHV gluon\\nscattering \
amplitudes in the strong coupling limit of the AdS/CFT duality. We\\nshow \
that the explicit coordinate dependence along the T-duality directions \
of\\nthe associated Lax connection (flat current) can be eliminated by means \
of a\\nfield dependent gauge transformation. As a result, the gauge \
equivalent Lax\\nconnection can easily be T-dualized, i.e. written in terms \
of the dual set of\\nisometric coordinates. The T-dual Lax connection can be \
used for the derivation\\nof infinitely many conserved charges in the T-dual \
model. Our construction\\nimplies that local (Noether) charges of the \
original model are mapped to\\nnon-local charges of the T-dual model and vice \
versa.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 5 Nov 2007 18:29:58 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 8 Nov 2007 17:03:42 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-09-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Ricci\"", ",", "\"Riccardo\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Tseytlin\"", ",", "\"Arkady A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Wolf\"", ",", "\"Martin\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0711.0707", "submitter" -> "Martin Wolf", "authors" -> 
            "Riccardo Ricci, Arkady A. Tseytlin, Martin Wolf", "title" -> 
            "On T-Duality and Integrability for Strings on AdS Backgrounds", 
            "comments" -> 
            "20 pages; v2: misprints corrected, references and minor\n  \
clarifications added", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0712:082,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/12/082", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-RR-04/2007", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss an interplay between T-duality and integrability \
for certain\nclassical non-linear sigma models. In particular, we consider \
strings on the\nAdS_5 x S^5 background and perform T-duality along the four \
isometry directions\nof AdS_5 in the Poincare patch. The T-dual of the AdS_5 \
sigma model is again a\nsigma model on an AdS_5 space. This classical \
T-duality relation was used in\nthe recently uncovered connection between \
light-like Wilson loops and MHV gluon\nscattering amplitudes in the strong \
coupling limit of the AdS/CFT duality. We\nshow that the explicit coordinate \
dependence along the T-duality directions of\nthe associated Lax connection \
(flat current) can be eliminated by means of a\nfield dependent gauge \
transformation. As a result, the gauge equivalent Lax\nconnection can easily \
be T-dualized, i.e. written in terms of the dual set of\nisometric \
coordinates. The T-dual Lax connection can be used for the derivation\nof \
infinitely many conserved charges in the T-dual model. Our construction\n\
implies that local (Noether) charges of the original model are mapped to\n\
non-local charges of the T-dual model and vice versa.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 5 Nov 2007 18:29:58 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 8 Nov 2007 17:03:42 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-09-17", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ricci", "Riccardo", ""}, {
              "Tseytlin", "Arkady A.", ""}, {"Wolf", "Martin", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{0.4766335072798764, -4.429516306496723}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0711.1525\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Richard Szabo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mauro Riccardi and Richard J. Szabo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Duality and Braiding in Twisted Quantum Field \
Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages; v2: Typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0801:016,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/01/016\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HWM-07-42, EMPG-07-22\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We re-examine various issues surrounding the definition \
of twisted quantum\\nfield theories on flat noncommutative spaces. We propose \
an interpretation\\nbased on nonlocal commutative field redefinitions which \
clarifies previously\\nobserved properties such as the formal equivalence of \
Green's functions in the\\nnoncommutative and commutative theories, \
causality, and the absence of UV/IR\\nmixing. We use these fields to define \
the functional integral formulation of\\ntwisted quantum field theory. We \
exploit techniques from braided tensor algebra\\nto argue that the twisted \
Fock space states of these free fields obey\\nconventional statistics. We \
support our claims with a detailed analysis of the\\nmodifications induced in \
the presence of background magnetic fields, which\\ninduces additional twists \
by magnetic translation operators and alters the\\neffective noncommutative \
geometry seen by the twisted quantum fields. When two\\nsuch field theories \
are dual to one another, we demonstrate that only our\\nbraided physical \
states are covariant under the duality.\\n\""}]}, {
