         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0711.1525", "submitter" -> "Richard Szabo", "authors" -> 
            "Mauro Riccardi and Richard J. Szabo", "title" -> 
            "Duality and Braiding in Twisted Quantum Field Theory", 
            "comments" -> "35 pages; v2: Typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP0801:016,2008", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/01/016", 
            "report-no" -> "HWM-07-42, EMPG-07-22", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We re-examine various issues surrounding the definition of \
twisted quantum\nfield theories on flat noncommutative spaces. We propose an \
interpretation\nbased on nonlocal commutative field redefinitions which \
clarifies previously\nobserved properties such as the formal equivalence of \
Green's functions in the\nnoncommutative and commutative theories, causality, \
and the absence of UV/IR\nmixing. We use these fields to define the \
functional integral formulation of\ntwisted quantum field theory. We exploit \
techniques from braided tensor algebra\nto argue that the twisted Fock space \
states of these free fields obey\nconventional statistics. We support our \
claims with a detailed analysis of the\nmodifications induced in the presence \
of background magnetic fields, which\ninduces additional twists by magnetic \
translation operators and alters the\neffective noncommutative geometry seen \
by the twisted quantum fields. When two\nsuch field theories are dual to one \
another, we demonstrate that only our\nbraided physical states are covariant \
under the duality.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 9 Nov 2007 19:09:24 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 10 Dec 2007 15:46:53 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Riccardi", "Mauro", ""}, {
              "Szabo", "Richard J.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
