            "  This paper studies in great detail a family of supersymmetric \
Wilson loop\noperators in N=4 supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory we have \
recently found. For a\ngeneric curve on an S^3 in space-time the loops \
preserve two supercharges but\nwe will also study special cases which \
preserve 4, 8 and 16 supercharges. For\ncertain loops we find the string \
theory dual explicitly and for the general\ncase we show that string \
solutions satisfy a first order differential equation.\nThis equation \
expresses the fact that the strings are pseudo-holomorphic with\nrespect to a \
novel almost complex structure we construct on AdS_4 x S^2. We\nthen discuss \
loops restricted to S^2 and provide evidence that they can be\ncalculated in \
terms of similar observables in purely bosonic YM in two\ndimensions on the \
sphere.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
