           "id" -> "0711.3404", "submitter" -> "Rafael Hernandez", "authors" -> 
            "Cesar Gomez, Johan Gunnesson, Rafael Hernandez", "title" -> 
            "The Ising model and planar N=4 Yang-Mills", "comments" -> 
            "24 pages. v2: References added and minor typos corrected", 
            "journal-ref" -> "J.Phys.A41:275205,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/41/27/275205", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The scattering-matrix for planar Yang-Mills with N=4 \
supersymmetry relies on\nthe assumption that integrability holds to all \
orders in perturbation theory.\nIn this note we define a map from the \
spectral variables x^{\\pm},\nparameterizing the long-range magnon momenta, \
to couplings in a two-dimensional\nIsing model. Under this map integrability \
of planar N=4 Yang-Mills becomes\nequivalent to the Yang-Baxter equation for \
the two-dimensional Ising model, and\nthe long-range variables x^{\\pm} \
translate into the entries of the Ising\ntransfer matrices. We explore the \
Ising correlation length which equals the\ninverse magnon momentum in the \
small momentum limit. The critical regime is\nthus reached for vanishing \
magnon momentum. We also discuss the meaning of the\nKramers-Wannier duality \
transformation on the gauge theory, together with that\nof the Ising model \
critical points.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
