               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0711.3895\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mannque Rho\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mannque Rho\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hidden Local Symmetry and Dense Half-Skyrmion \
Matter\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"6 pages, 1 figure, 1 reference corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"nucl-th hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Transition from baryonic matter to color-flavor-locked \
quark matter is\\ndescribed in terms of skyrmion matter changing into \
half-skyrmion matter. The\\nintermediate phase between the density $n_p$ at \
which a skyrmion turns into two\\nhalf skyrmions and the chiral transition \
density $n_c^{\\\\chi SR}$ at which\\nhadronic matter changes over to quark \
matter corresponds to a chiral symmetry\\nrestored phase characterized by a \
vanishing quark condensate and a {\\\\em\\nnon-vanishing} pion decay \
constant. When hidden local fields are incorporated,\\nthe vector \
manifestation of Harada-Yamawaki HLS theory implies that as \
density\\napproaches $n_c^{\\\\chi SR}$, the gauge coupling $g$ goes to zero \
(in the chiral\\nlimit) and the symmetry \\\"swells\\\" to $SU(N_f)^4$ as \
proposed by Georgi for the\\n\\\"vector limit.\\\" This enhanced symmetry, \
not present in QCD, can be interpreted\\nas \\\"emergent\\\" in medium due to \
collective excitations. The fractionization of\\nskyrmions into \
half-skyrmions resembles closely the magnetic N\\\\'eel--to-valence\\nbond \
solid (VBS) paramagnet transition where \\\"baby\\\" half-skyrmions enter \
as\\nrelevant degrees of freedom in the intermediate phase. It is suggested \
that the\\nhalf-skyrmion phase in dense matter corresponds to the \
\\\"hadronic freedom\\\"\\nregime that plays a singularly important role in \
inducing kaon condensation\\nthat leads to the collapse of massive compact \
stars into black holes..\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 25 Nov 2007 12:52:16 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 28 Nov 2007 07:22:35 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2007-11-28\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Rho\"", ",", "\"Mannque\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
