            "10.1142/S0217751X08042304", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss tachyon-free examples of (Type IIB on) non-compact\n\
non-supersymmetric orbifolds. Tachyons are projected out by discrete torsion\n\
between orbifold twists, while supersymmetry is broken by a Scherk-Schwarz\n\
phase (+1/-1 when acting on space-time bosons/fermions) accompanying some \
even\norder twists. The absence of tachyons is encouraging for constructing\n\
non-supersymmetric D3-brane gauge theories with stable infrared fixed points.\
\nThe D3-brane gauge theories in our orbifold backgrounds have chiral N = 1\n\
supersymmetric spectra, but non-supersymmetric interactions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
