               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DESY 07-216\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"nlin.SI hep-th\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Bethe equations, arising in description of the \
spectrum of the dilatation\\noperator for the su(2) sector of the N=4 \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory, are\\nconsidered in the anti-ferromagnetic \
regime. These equations are deformation of\\nthose for the Heisenberg XXX \
magnet. It is proven that in the thermodynamic\\nlimit roots of the deformed \
equations group into strings. It is proven that the\\ncorresponding Yang's \
action is convex, which implies uniqueness of solution for\\ncenters of the \
strings. The state formed of strings of length (2n+1) is\\nconsidered and the \
density of their distribution is found. It is shown that the\\nenergy of such \
a state decreases as n grows. It is observed that\\nnon-analyticity of the \
left hand side of the Bethe equations leads to an\\nadditional contribution \
to the density and energy of strings of even length.\\nWhence it is concluded \
that the structure of the anti-ferromagnetic vacuum is\\ndetermined by the \
behaviour of exponential corrections to string solutions in\\nthe \
thermodynamic limit and possibly involves strings of length 2.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 6 Dec 2007 14:43:49 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Bytsko\"", ",", "\"A. G.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Shenderovich\"", ",", "\"I. E.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
