            "  The Bethe equations, arising in description of the spectrum of \
the dilatation\noperator for the su(2) sector of the N=4 supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory, are\nconsidered in the anti-ferromagnetic regime. These \
equations are deformation of\nthose for the Heisenberg XXX magnet. It is \
proven that in the thermodynamic\nlimit roots of the deformed equations group \
into strings. It is proven that the\ncorresponding Yang's action is convex, \
which implies uniqueness of solution for\ncenters of the strings. The state \
formed of strings of length (2n+1) is\nconsidered and the density of their \
distribution is found. It is shown that the\nenergy of such a state decreases \
as n grows. It is observed that\nnon-analyticity of the left hand side of the \
Bethe equations leads to an\nadditional contribution to the density and \
energy of strings of even length.\nWhence it is concluded that the structure \
of the anti-ferromagnetic vacuum is\ndetermined by the behaviour of \
exponential corrections to string solutions in\nthe thermodynamic limit and \
possibly involves strings of length 2.\n", 
