A.Vladikas\\n  and H.Wittig\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-perturbative renormalisation of Delta F=2 \
four-fermion operators in\\n  two-flavour QCD\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"26 pages, 8 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0805:065,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/05/065\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-lat\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using Schroedinger Functional methods, we compute the \
non-perturbative\\nrenormalisation and renormalisation group running of \
several four-fermion\\noperators, in the framework of lattice simulations \
with two dynamical Wilson\\nquarks. Two classes of operators have been \
targeted: (i) those with left-left\\ncurrent structure and four propagating \
quark fields; (ii) all operators\\ncontaining two static quarks. In both \
cases, only the parity-odd contributions\\nhave been considered, being the \
ones that renormalise multiplicatively. Our\\nresults, once combined with \
future simulations of the corresponding lattice\\nhadronic matrix elements, \
may be used for the computation of phenomenological\\nquantities of interest, \
such as B_K and B_B (the latter also in the static\\nlimit).\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
