                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute finite-size corrections to dyonic giant \
magnons in two ways. One\\nis by examining the asymptotic behavior of helical \
strings of hep-th/0609026 as\\nelliptic modulus k goes to unity, and the \
other is by applying the generalized\\nLuscher formula for mu-term of \
arXiv:0708.2208 to the situation in which\\nincoming particles are \
boundstates. By careful choice of poles in the\\nsu(2|2)^2-invariant \
S-matrix, we find agreement of the two results, which makes\\npossible to \
predict the (leading) finite-size correction for dyonic giant\\nmagnons to \
all orders in the 't Hooft coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
