            "  We compute finite-size corrections to dyonic giant magnons in \
two ways. One\nis by examining the asymptotic behavior of helical strings of \
hep-th/0609026 as\nelliptic modulus k goes to unity, and the other is by \
applying the generalized\nLuscher formula for mu-term of arXiv:0708.2208 to \
the situation in which\nincoming particles are boundstates. By careful choice \
of poles in the\nsu(2|2)^2-invariant S-matrix, we find agreement of the two \
results, which makes\npossible to predict the (leading) finite-size \
correction for dyonic giant\nmagnons to all orders in the 't Hooft coupling.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 6 Jan 2008 12:58:17 GMT"}, {
