Niarchos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-Supersymmetric Seiberg Duality, Orientifold QCD and \
Non-Critical\\n  Strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"45 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D77:105009,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.77.105009\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose an electric-magnetic duality and conjecture \
an exact conformal\\nwindow for a class of non-supersymmetric U(N_c) gauge \
theories with fermions in\\nthe (anti)symmetric representation of the gauge \
group and N_f additional scalar\\nand fermion flavors. The duality exchanges \
N_c with N_f -N_c \\\\mp 4 leaving N_f\\ninvariant, and has common features \
with Seiberg duality in N=1 SQCD with SU or\\nSO/Sp gauge group. At large N \
the duality holds due to planar equivalence with\\nN=1 SQCD. At finite N we \
embed these gauge theories in a setup with D-branes\\nand orientifolds in a \
non-supersymmetric, but tachyon-free, non-critical type\\n0B string theory \
and argue in favor of the duality in terms of boundary and\\ncrosscap state \
monodromies as in analogous supersymmetric situations. One can\\nverify \
explicitly that the resulting duals have matching global \
anomalies.\\nFinally, we comment on the moduli space of these gauge theories \
and discuss\\nother potential non-supersymmetric examples that could exhibit \
similar\\ndualities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
