           "id" -> "0801.2064", "submitter" -> "Joseph A. Minahan", "authors" -> 
            "J. A. Minahan, O. Ohlsson Sax", "title" -> 
            "Finite size effects for giant magnons on physical strings", 
            "comments" -> "24 pages, 7 figures; v2 typos fixed", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B801:97-117,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2008.04.018", "report-no" -> "UUITP-20/07", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Using finite gap methods, we find the leading order finite \
size corrections\nfor an arbitrary number of giant magnons on physical \
strings, where the sum of\nthe momenta is a multiple of 2\\pi. Our results \
are valid for the\nHofman-Maldacena fundamental giant magnons as well as \
their dyonic\ngeneralizations. The energy corrections turn out to be \
surprisingly simple,\nespecially if all the magnons are fundamental, and at \
leading order are\nindependent of the magnon flavors. We also show how to use \
the Bethe ansatz to\nfind finite size corrections for dyonic giant magnons \
with large R-charges.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
