            "  Understanding the finite-size corrections to the fundamental \
excitations of a\ntheory is the first step towards completely solving for the \
spectrum in finite\nvolume. We compute the leading exponential correction to \
the quantum energy of\nthe fundamental excitation of the light-cone gauged \
string in AdS(5) x S(5),\nwhich is the giant magnon solution. We present two \
independent ways to obtain\nthis correction: the first approach makes use of \
the algebraic curve\ndescription of the giant magnon. The second relies on \
the purely\nfield-theoretical Luscher formulas, which depend on the \
world-sheet S-matrix.\nWe demonstrate the agreement to all orders in g/Delta \
of these approaches,\nwhich in particular presents a further test of the \
S-matrix. We comment on\ngeneralizations of this method of computation to \
other string configurations.\n", 
