               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Diego Bombardelli, Davide Fioravanti and Marco \
Rossi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Large spin corrections in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM sl(2): \
still a linear\\n  integral equation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex file, typos corrected, 2 figures, appendix, \
references and\\n  clarifications added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B810:460-490,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2008.09.030\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Anomalous dimension and higher conserved charges in the \
$sl(2)$ sector of\\n${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM for generic spin $s$ and twist $L$ \
are described by using a\\nnovel kind of non-linear integral equation (NLIE). \
The latter can be derived\\nunder typical situations of the SYM sectors, i.e. \
when the scattering need not\\ndepend on the difference of the rapidities and \
these, in their turn, may also\\nlie on a bounded range. Here the non-linear \
(finite range) integral terms,\\nappearing in the NLIE and in the dimension \
formula, go to zero as $s\\\\to\\n\\\\infty$. Therefore they can be neglected \
at least up to the $O(s^0)$ order,\\nthus implying a linear integral equation \
(LIE) and a linear dimension/charge\\nformula respectively, likewise the \
'thermodynamic' (i.e. infinite spin) case.\\nImportantly, these non-linear \
terms go faster than any inverse logarithm power\\n$(\\\\ln s)^{-n}$, $n>0$, \
thus extending the linearity validity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
