               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0803.0315\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alin Tirziu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M. Kruczenski and A. Tirziu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matching the circular Wilson loop with dual open string \
solution at\\n  1-loop in strong coupling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages; v2: typos corrected, acknowledgments added; v3: \
minor\\n  corrections, references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0805:064,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/05/064\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the 1-loop correction to the effective \
action for the string\\nsolution in AdS_5 x S^5 dual to the circular Wilson \
loop. More generically, the\\nmethod we use can be applied whenever the two \
dimensional spectral problem\\nfactorizes, to regularize and define the \
fluctuation determinants in terms of\\nsolutions of one-dimensional \
differential equations. A such it can be applied\\nto non-homogeneous \
solutions both for open and closed strings and to various\\nboundary \
conditions. In the case of the circular Wilson loop, we obtain, for\\nthe \
1-loop partition function a result which up to a factor of two matches \
the\\nexpectation from the exact gauge theory computation. The discrepancy \
can be\\nattributed to an overall constant in the string partition function \
coming from\\nthe normalization of zero modes, which we have not \
fixed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
