 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We employ the analytic Bethe Anzats to construct \
eigenvalues of transfer\\nmatrices with finite-dimensional atypical \
representations in the auxiliary\\nspace for the putative long-range spin \
chain encoding anomalous dimensions of\\nall composite single-trace gauge \
invariant operators of the maximally\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory. They \
obey an infinite fusion hierarchy which\\ncan be reduced to a finite set of \
integral relations for a minimal set of\\ntransfer matrices. This set is used \
to derive a finite systems of functional\\nequations for eigenvalues of \
nested Baxter polynomials.\\n\""}]}, {
