               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explicitly construct a large class of finite-volume \
two-magnon string\\nsolutions moving on R x S^2. In particular, by making use \
of the relationship\\nbetween the O(3) sigma model and sine-Gordon theory we \
are able to find\\nsolutions corresponding to the periodic analogues of \
magnon scattering and\\nbreather-like solutions. After semi-classically \
quantizing these solutions we\\ninvert the implicit expressions for the \
excitation energies in certain limits\\nand find the corrections for the \
multi-magnon states. For the breather-like\\nsolutions we express the \
energies directly in terms of the action variable\\nwhereas for the \
scattering solution we express the result as a combination of\\ncorrections \
to the dispersion relation and to the scattering phase.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
