         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0803.4222", "submitter" -> "Michael Abbott", "authors" -> 
            "Michael C. Abbott, In\\^es Aniceto", "title" -> 
            "Vibrating giant spikes and the large-winding sector", "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, 5 figures. v2 has extra references and thanks", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0806:088,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/06/088", "report-no" -> "BROWN-HET 1497", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The single spike is a rigidly rotating classical string \
configuration closely\nrelated to the giant magnon. We calculate bosonic and \
fermionic modes of this\nsolution, from which we see that it is not \
supersymmetric. It can be viewed as\nan excitation above a hoop of string \
wound around the equator, in the same\nsense that the magnon is an excitation \
above an orbiting point particle. We\nfind the operator which plays the role \
of the Hamiltonian for this sector,\nwhich compared to the magnon's E-J has \
the angular momentum replaced by a\nwinding charge. The single spike solution \
is unstable, and we use the modes to\nattempt a semi-classical computation of \
its lifetime.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 31 Mar 2008 18:16:04 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 5 May 2008 03:30:45 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Abbott", "Michael C.", ""}, {
              "Aniceto", "In\[EHat]s", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
