                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review recent developments in the theory of brane \
tilings and\\nfour-dimensional N=1 supersymmetric quiver gauge theories. This \
review consists\\nof two parts. In part I, we describe foundations of brane \
tilings, emphasizing\\nthe physical interpretation of brane tilings as \
fivebrane systems. In part II,\\nwe discuss application of brane tilings to \
AdS/CFT correspondence and\\nhomological mirror symmetry. More topics, such \
as orientifold of brane tilings,\\nphenomenological model building, \
similarities with BPS solitons in\\nsupersymmetric gauge theories, are also \
briefly discussed.\\n  This paper is a revised version of the author's \
master's thesis submitted to\\nDepartment of Physics, Faculty of Science, the \
University of Tokyo on January\\n2008, and is based on his several papers: \
math.AG/0605780, math.AG/0606548,\\nhep-th/0702049, math.AG/0703267, \
arXiv:0801.3528 and some works in progress.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
