            "Brane Tilings and Their Applications", "comments" -> 
            "208 pages, 92 figures, based on master's thesis; v2: minor\n  \
corrections, to appear in Fortschr. Phys", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Fortsch.Phys.56:555-686,2008", "doi" -> "10.1002/prop.200810536",
             "report-no" -> "UT-08-05", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We review recent developments in the theory of brane tilings \
and\nfour-dimensional N=1 supersymmetric quiver gauge theories. This review \
consists\nof two parts. In part I, we describe foundations of brane tilings, \
emphasizing\nthe physical interpretation of brane tilings as fivebrane \
systems. In part II,\nwe discuss application of brane tilings to AdS/CFT \
correspondence and\nhomological mirror symmetry. More topics, such as \
orientifold of brane tilings,\nphenomenological model building, similarities \
with BPS solitons in\nsupersymmetric gauge theories, are also briefly \
discussed.\n  This paper is a revised version of the author's master's thesis \
submitted to\nDepartment of Physics, Faculty of Science, the University of \
Tokyo on January\n2008, and is based on his several papers: math.AG/0605780, \
math.AG/0606548,\nhep-th/0702049, math.AG/0703267, arXiv:0801.3528 and some \
works in progress.\n", 
