               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0804.0324\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Till Bargheer\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Till Bargheer, Niklas Beisert, Nikolay Gromov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum Stability for the Heisenberg Ferromagnet\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"82 pages, a figure a page or so\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"New J. Phys. 10 (2008) 103023\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1367-2630/10/10/103023\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"AEI-2008-010, LPTENS 08/19, SPhT-t08/051\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Highly spinning classical strings on RxS^3 are \
described by the\\nLandau-Lifshitz model or equivalently by the Heisenberg \
ferromagnet in the\\nthermodynamic limit. The spectrum of this model can be \
given in terms of\\nspectral curves. However, it is a priori not clear \
whether any given admissible\\nspectral curve can actually be realised as a \
solution to the discrete Bethe\\nequations, a property which can be referred \
to as stability. In order to study\\nthe issue of stability, we find and \
explore the general two-cut solution or\\nelliptic curve. It turns out that \
the moduli space of this elliptic curve shows\\na surprisingly rich \
structure. We present the various cases with illustrations\\nand thus gain \
some insight into the features of multi-cut solutions. It appears\\nthat all \
admissible spectral curves are indeed stable if the branch cuts \
are\\npositioned in a suitable, non-trivial fashion.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 2 Apr 2008 10:33:15 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-10-31\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Bargheer\"", ",", "\"Till\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Beisert\"", ",", "\"Niklas\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Gromov\"", ",", "\"Nikolay\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
