            "Quantum Stability for the Heisenberg Ferromagnet", "comments" -> 
            "82 pages, a figure a page or so", "journal-ref" -> 
            "New J. Phys. 10 (2008) 103023", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1367-2630/10/10/103023", "report-no" -> 
            "AEI-2008-010, LPTENS 08/19, SPhT-t08/051", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Highly spinning classical strings on RxS^3 are described by \
the\nLandau-Lifshitz model or equivalently by the Heisenberg ferromagnet in \
the\nthermodynamic limit. The spectrum of this model can be given in terms of\
\nspectral curves. However, it is a priori not clear whether any given \
admissible\nspectral curve can actually be realised as a solution to the \
discrete Bethe\nequations, a property which can be referred to as stability. \
In order to study\nthe issue of stability, we find and explore the general \
two-cut solution or\nelliptic curve. It turns out that the moduli space of \
this elliptic curve shows\na surprisingly rich structure. We present the \
various cases with illustrations\nand thus gain some insight into the \
features of multi-cut solutions. It appears\nthat all admissible spectral \
curves are indeed stable if the branch cuts are\npositioned in a suitable, \
non-trivial fashion.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
