               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study solutions for the rotating strings on the \
sphere with a background\\nNS-NS field and on the Anti-de-Sitter spacetime. \
We show the existence of\\nmagnon and single spike solutions on \
R$\\\\times$S$^2$ in the presence of constant\\nmagnetic field as two \
limiting cases. We also study the solution for strings on\\nAdS$_3\\\\times$ \
S$^3$ with Melvin deformation. The dispersion relations among\\nvarious \
conserved charges are shown to receive finite corrections due to \
the\\ndeformation parameter. We further study the rotating string on AdS$_3 \
\\\\times$\\nS$^3$ geometry with two conserved angular momenta on S$^3$ and \
one spin along\\nthe AdS$_3$. We show that there exists two kinds of \
solutions: a circular\\nstring solution and a helical string. We find out the \
dispersion relation among\\nvarious charges and give physical interpretation \
of these solutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
