Orselli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Finite-size corrections to the rotating string and the \
winding state\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2: 33 pages, misprints corrected, references added, \
version accepted\\n  for publication in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0808:099,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/08/099\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute higher order finite size corrections to the \
energies of the\\ncircular rotating string on AdS_5 x S^5, of its orbifolded \
generalization on\\nAdS_5 x S^5/Z_M and of the winding state which is \
obtained as the limit of the\\norbifolded circular string solution when J -> \
infinity and J/M^2 is kept fixed.\\nWe solve, at the first order in \
lambda'=lambda/J^2, where lambda is the 't\\nHooft coupling, the Bethe \
equations that describe the anomalous dimensions of\\nthe corresponding gauge \
dual operators in an expansion in m/K, where m is the\\nwinding number and K \
is the \\\"magnon number\\\", and to all orders in the angular\\nmomentum J. \
The solution for the circular rotating string and for the winding\\nstate can \
be matched to the energy computed from an effective quantum\\nLandau-Lifshitz \
model beyond the first order correction in 1/J. For the leading\\n1/J \
corrections to the circular rotating string in m^2 and m^4 and for \
the\\nsubleading 1/J^2 corrections to the m^2 term, we find agreement. For \
the\\nwinding state we match the energy completely up to, and including, the \
order\\n1/J^2 finite-size corrections. The solution of the Bethe \
equations\\ncorresponding to the spinning closed string is also provided in \
an expansion in\\nm/K and to all orders in J.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
