generalization on\nAdS_5 x S^5/Z_M and of the winding state which is obtained \
as the limit of the\norbifolded circular string solution when J -> infinity \
and J/M^2 is kept fixed.\nWe solve, at the first order in lambda'=lambda/J^2, \
where lambda is the 't\nHooft coupling, the Bethe equations that describe the \
anomalous dimensions of\nthe corresponding gauge dual operators in an \
expansion in m/K, where m is the\nwinding number and K is the \"magnon number\
\", and to all orders in the angular\nmomentum J. The solution for the \
circular rotating string and for the winding\nstate can be matched to the \
energy computed from an effective quantum\nLandau-Lifshitz model beyond the \
first order correction in 1/J. For the leading\n1/J corrections to the \
circular rotating string in m^2 and m^4 and for the\nsubleading 1/J^2 \
corrections to the m^2 term, we find agreement. For the\nwinding state we \
