               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sum rules for higher twist sl(2)operators in N=4 \
SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages, 2 eps figures\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0806:103,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/06/103\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The spectrum of anomalous dimensions of twist sl(2) \
operators in N=4 SYM has\\nan intriguing feature in low twist 2 or 3. The \
anomalous dimension of the\\nlowest state, dual a folded string on AdS_5 X \
S^5, can be computed by Bethe\\nAnsatz at 3, 4 loops respectively as a simple \
closed function of the Lorentz\\nspin. This feature is apparently lost at \
higher twist. We propose sum rules for\\nthe excited anomalous dimensions \
where closed expressions can still be\\nprovided, even at higher twist. We \
present several explicit three loop\\nexamples. Many structural regularities \
can be observed leading to closed\\nexpressions which depend parametrically \
both on the spin and the twist. They\\nallow to compute the subleading term \
in the logarithmic large spin expansion of\\nthe sum rules as a compact \
simple function of the twist, in analogy with the\\nrecent results by \
Freyhult, Rej and Staudacher in arXiv:0712.2743 [hep-th].\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 23 Apr 2008 13:16:21 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
