            "comments" -> "31 pages, 2 eps figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP0806:103,2008", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/06/103", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The spectrum of anomalous dimensions of twist sl(2) operators \
in N=4 SYM has\nan intriguing feature in low twist 2 or 3. The anomalous \
dimension of the\nlowest state, dual a folded string on AdS_5 X S^5, can be \
computed by Bethe\nAnsatz at 3, 4 loops respectively as a simple closed \
function of the Lorentz\nspin. This feature is apparently lost at higher \
twist. We propose sum rules for\nthe excited anomalous dimensions where \
closed expressions can still be\nprovided, even at higher twist. We present \
several explicit three loop\nexamples. Many structural regularities can be \
observed leading to closed\nexpressions which depend parametrically both on \
the spin and the twist. They\nallow to compute the subleading term in the \
logarithmic large spin expansion of\nthe sum rules as a compact simple \
function of the twist, in analogy with the\nrecent results by Freyhult, Rej \
and Staudacher in arXiv:0712.2743 [hep-th].\n", 
