          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0804.3973", "submitter" -> "Domenico Seminara", "authors" -> 
            "Antonio Bassetto (Padua U., INFN), Luca Griguolo (Parma U., \
INFN),\n  Fabrizio Pucci (Florence U., INFN) and Domenico Seminara (Florence \
U., INFN)", "title" -> "Supersymmetric Wilson loops at two loops", "comments" -> 
            "35 pages, 14 figures, typos corrected, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0806:083,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/06/083", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the quantum properties of certain BPS Wilson loops in \
${\\cal N}=4$\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory. They belong to a general \
family, introduced\nrecently, in which the addition of particular scalar \
couplings endows generic\nloops on $S^3$ with a fraction of supersymmetry. \
When restricted to $S^2$,\ntheir quantum average has been further conjectured \
to be exactly computed by\nthe matrix model governing the zero-instanton \
sector of YM$_2$ on the sphere.\nWe perform a complete two-loop analysis on a \
class of cusped Wilson loops lying\non a two-dimensional sphere, finding \
perfect agreement with the conjecture. The\nperturbative computation \
reproduces the matrix-model expectation through a\nhighly non-trivial \
interplay between ladder diagrams and self-energies/vertex\ncontributions, \
suggesting the existence of a localization procedure.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 24 Apr 2008 19:52:32 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 5 May 2008 18:39:13 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-11-18", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{
