               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Donovan Young\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Donovan Young\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"BPS Wilson Loops on S^2 at Higher Loops\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"39 pages, 15 figures. v2 references added, minor cosmetic \
changes. v3\\n  minor error in eq. (40) corrected. v4 error in coincident \
limit of correlator\\n  corrected; claims of disagreement with 2-d Yang-Mills \
retracted\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0805:077,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/05/077\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-EP-08/13\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider supersymmetric Wilson loops of the variety \
constructed by\\nDrukker, Giombi, Ricci, and Trancanelli, whose spatial \
contours lie on a\\ntwo-sphere. Working to second order in the 't Hooft \
coupling in planar N=4\\nSupersymmetric Yang-Mills Theory (SYM), we compute \
the vacuum expectation value\\nof a wavy-latitude and of a loop composed of \
two longitudes. We evaluate the\\nresulting integrals numerically and find \
that the results are consistent with\\nthe zero-instanton sector calculation \
of Wilson loops in 2-d Yang-Mills on S^2\\nperformed by Bassetto and \
Griguolo. We also consider the connected correlator\\nof two distinct \
latitudes to third order in the 't Hooft coupling in planar N=4\\nSYM. We \
compare the result in the limit where the latitudes become coincident\\nto a \
perturbative calculation in 2-d Yang-Mills on S^2 using a \
light-cone\\nWu-Mandelstam-Leibbrandt prescription. We are not able to \
calculate the SYM\\nresult at the required order in the separation between \
the latitudes necessary\\nfor a match with 2-d Yang-Mills; the result, \
however, does not preclude such a\\nmatch.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 25 Apr 2008 12:22:15 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 21 May 2008 13:04:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 15 Jun 2009 15:44:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
