            "Donovan Young", "title" -> 
            "BPS Wilson Loops on S^2 at Higher Loops", "comments" -> 
            "39 pages, 15 figures. v2 references added, minor cosmetic \
changes. v3\n  minor error in eq. (40) corrected. v4 error in coincident \
limit of correlator\n  corrected; claims of disagreement with 2-d Yang-Mills \
retracted", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0805:077,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/05/077", "report-no" -> "HU-EP-08/13", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider supersymmetric Wilson loops of the variety \
constructed by\nDrukker, Giombi, Ricci, and Trancanelli, whose spatial \
contours lie on a\ntwo-sphere. Working to second order in the 't Hooft \
coupling in planar N=4\nSupersymmetric Yang-Mills Theory (SYM), we compute \
the vacuum expectation value\nof a wavy-latitude and of a loop composed of \
two longitudes. We evaluate the\nresulting integrals numerically and find \
that the results are consistent with\nthe zero-instanton sector calculation \
of Wilson loops in 2-d Yang-Mills on S^2\nperformed by Bassetto and Griguolo. \
We also consider the connected correlator\nof two distinct latitudes to third \
order in the 't Hooft coupling in planar N=4\nSYM. We compare the result in \
the limit where the latitudes become coincident\nto a perturbative \
calculation in 2-d Yang-Mills on S^2 using a light-cone\n\
Wu-Mandelstam-Leibbrandt prescription. We are not able to calculate the SYM\n\
result at the required order in the separation between the latitudes \
necessary\nfor a match with 2-d Yang-Mills; the result, however, does not \
preclude such a\nmatch.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 25 Apr 2008 12:22:15 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 21 May 2008 13:04:04 GMT"}, {
