         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0804.4507", "submitter" -> "Brenno Carlini Vallilo", 
            "authors" -> "William D. Linch III, Brenno Carlini Vallilo", 
            "title" -> 
            "Integrability of the Gauged Linear Sigma Model for AdS_5xS^5", 
            "comments" -> "20 pages, refs added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0911:007,2009", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2009/11/007", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently, a gauged linear sigma model was proposed by \
Berkovits and Vafa\nwhich can be used to describe the AdS_5xS^5 superstring \
at finite and zero\nradius. In this paper we show that the model is \
classically integrable by\nconstructing its first non-local conserved charge \
and a superspace Lax\n\"quartet\". Quantum conservation of the non-local \
charge follows easily from\nsuperspace rules.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
