          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0805.0636\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gorsky Alexander\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A.S.Gorsky and V.I.Zakharov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Flux-Tube Formation and Holographic Tunneling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"15 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett.B669:186-192,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2008.09.043\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider correlator of two concentric Wilson loops, \
a small and large ones\\nrelated to the problem of flux-tube formation. There \
are three mechanisms which\\ncan contribute to the connected correlator and \
yield different dependences on\\nthe radius of the small loop. The first one \
is quite standard and concerns\\nexchange by supergravity modes. We also \
consider a novel mechanism when the\\nflux-tube formation is described by a \
barrier transition in the string\\nlanguage, dual to the field-theoretic \
formulation of Yang-Mills theories. The\\nmost interesting possibility within \
this approach is resonant tunneling which\\nwould enhance the correlator of \
the Wilson loops for particular geometries. The\\nthird possibility involves \
exchange by a dyonic string supplied with the string\\njunction. We introduce \
also t'Hooft and composite dyonic loops as probes of the\\nflux tube. \
Implications for lattice measurements are briefly discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 6 May 2008 02:52:19 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Gorsky\"", ",", "\"A. S.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Zakharov\"", ",", "\"V. I.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
