 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In non-supersymmetric orbifolds of N =4 super \
Yang-Mills, conformal\\ninvariance is broken by the logarithmic running of \
double-trace operators -- a\\nleading effect at large N. A tachyonic \
instability in AdS_5 has been proposed\\nas the bulk dual of double-trace \
running. In this paper we make this\\ncorrespondence more precise. By \
standard field theory methods, we show that the\\ndouble-trace beta function \
is quadratic in the coupling, to all orders in\\nplanar perturbation theory. \
Tuning the double-trace coupling to its (complex)\\nfixed point, we find \
conformal dimensions of the form 2 + i b, as formally\\nexpected for \
operators dual to bulk scalars that violate the stability bound.\\nWe also \
show that conformal invariance is broken in perturbation theory if and\\nonly \
if dynamical symmetry breaking occurs. Our analysis is applicable to \
a\\ngeneral large N field theory with vanishing single-trace beta \
functions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 15 May 2008 11:53:47 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
