                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop Yang-Baxter integrability structures \
connected with the quantum\\naffine superalgebra Uq(\\\\hat sl(2|1)). \
Baxter's Q-operators are explicitly\\nconstructed as supertraces of certain \
monodromy matrices associated with\\n(q-deformed) bosonic and fermionic \
oscillator algebras. There are six different\\nQ-operators in this case, \
obeying a few fundamental fusion relations, which\\nimply all functional \
relations between various commuting transfer matrices. The\\nresults are \
universal in the sense that they do not depend on the quantum space\\nof \
states and apply both to lattice models and to continuous quantum \
field\\ntheory models as well.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
