            "report-no" -> "DAMTP-2008-52", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We develop algebraic methods for finding loop corrections to \
the N=4 SYM\ndilatation generator, within the noncompact psu(1,1|2) sector. \
This sector\ngives a 't Hooft coupling lambda-dependent representation of \
psu(1,1|2) times\npsu(1|1)^2. At first working independently of the \
representation, we present an\nall-order algebraic ansatz for the \
lambda-dependence of this Lie algebra's\ngenerators. The ansatz solves the \
symmetry constraints if an auxiliary\ngenerator, h, satisfies certain simple \
commutation relations with the Lie\nalgebra generators. Applying this to the \
psu(1,1|2) sector leads to an\niterative solution for the planar three-loop \
dilatation generator in terms of\nleading order symmetry generators and h, \
which passes a thorough set of\nspectral tests. We argue also that this \
algebraic ansatz may be applicable to\nthe nonplanar theory as well.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
