               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0806.2032\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold Steinacker\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold Steinacker\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Emergent Gravity and Noncommutative Branes from \
Yang-Mills Matrix Models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages. V2: typos corrected, reference added. V3: \
discussion and\\n  references added. V4: derivation of Ward identity \
fixed\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B810:1-39,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2008.10.014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The framework of emergent gravity arising from \
Yang-Mills matrix models is\\ndeveloped further, for general noncommutative \
branes embedded in R^D. The\\neffective metric on the brane turns out to have \
a universal form reminiscent of\\nthe open string metric, depending on the \
dynamical Poisson structure and the\\nembedding metric in R^D. A covariant \
form of the tree-level equations of motion\\nis derived, and the Newtonian \
limit is discussed. This points to the necessity\\nof branes in higher \
dimensions. The quantization is discussed qualitatively,\\nwhich singles out \
the IKKT model as a prime candidate for a quantum theory of\\ngravity coupled \
to matter. The Planck scale is then identified with the scale\\nof N=4 SUSY \
breaking. A mechanism for avoiding the cosmological constant\\nproblem is \
exhibited.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
