            "  Recently, Freyhult, Rej and Staudacher (FRS) proposed an \
integral equation\ndetermining the leading logarithmic term of the anomalous \
dimension of sl(2)\ntwist-operators in N=4 SYM for large Lorentz spin M and \
twist L at fixed j =\nL/log(M). We discuss the large j limit of the FRS \
equation. This limit can be\nmatched with the {\\em fast long string} limit \
of AdS_5 X S^5 superstring\nperturbation theory at all couplings. In \
particular, a certain part of the\nclassical and one-loop string result is \
known to be protected and can be\ncomputed in the weakly coupled large-j \
limit of the FRS equation. We present\nvarious analytical and numerical \
results supporting agreement at one and two\nloops in the gauge theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 23 Jun 2008 15:16:55 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-06-02", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Beccaria", "Matteo", ""}}}], 
