 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Motivated by desire to shed light on the strong \
coupling behaviour of\\nanomalous dimensions of \\\"short\\\" gauge theory \
operators we consider the famous\\nexample of folded spinning string in AdS_5 \
in the limit of small semiclassical\\nspin parameter \\\\S = S/sqrt[lambda]. \
In this limit the string becomes short and\\nis moving in a near-flat central \
region of AdS_5. Its energy scales with spin\\nas E = sqrt[2 S] [ a_0 + a_1 S \
+ a_2 S^2 + ...]. We explicitly compute the\\nleading 1-loop quantum AdS_5 x \
S^5 superstring corrections to the short-string\\nlimit coefficients a_0 and \
a_1 and show, in particular, that a_1 receives a\\ncontribution containing \\\
\\zeta(3).\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
