         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0807.0643", "submitter" -> "Yasuyuki Hatsuda", "authors" -> 
            "Yasuyuki Hatsuda and Ryo Suzuki", "title" -> 
            "Finite-Size Effects for Multi-Magnon States", "comments" -> 
            "1+35 pages, v3: further clarification provided in Section 4, \
Section\n  5 moved to an appendix, v4: improved arguments for the case of \
multi dyonic\n  giant magnons, based on the published version", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0809:025,2008", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/09/025", 
            "report-no" -> "TCDMATH 08-09, UT-08-22", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We propose the generalized Luscher formula for multi-magnon \
states by which\none can compute the finite-size correction to the energy of \
multi giant magnons\nat classical and one-loop levels. It is shown that the \
F-term of our formula is\nconsistent with the exact finite-size spectrum of \
the sinh-Gordon model, and\nthe mu-term agrees with the finite-size energy of \
magnon boundstate of the\nasymptotic Bethe Ansatz in the su(2) sector at \
strong coupling. In an appendix,\nwe evaluate our formula at weak coupling \
under some approximations, and find\nthat the transcendental terms arise from \
a sum over an infinite tower of BPS\nboundstates.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
