 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study giant magnon solutions in AdS4 \\\\times CP3. \
We compute quantum\\ncorrections to their dispersion relation. We find out \
that the one--loop\\ncorrection vanishes in infinite volume. This implies \
that the interpolating\\nfunction h(\\\\lambda) between strong and weak \
coupling regimes does not have a\\nconstant term \\\\lambda^0 at strong \
coupling. We also compute first nonvanishing\\nfinite volume correction to \
the one--loop expression. When compared to the\\nL\\\\\\\"{u}sher formula, \
our results could provide a nontrivial check of the AdS4\\n\\\\times CP3 \
S--matrix proposed recently in arXiv:0807.1924.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
