               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This review cover our current understanding of strongly \
coupled Quark-Gluon\\nPlasma (sQGP), especially theoretical progress in (i) \
explaining the RHIC data\\nby hydrodynamics, (ii) describing lattice data \
using electric-magnetic duality;\\n(iii) understanding of gauge-string \
duality known as AdS/CFT and its\\napplication for \\\"conformal\\\" plasma. \
In view of interdisciplinary nature of the\\nsubject, we include brief \
introduction into several topics \\\"for pedestrians\\\".\\nSome fundamental \
questions addressed are: Why is sQGP such a good liquid? What\\nis the nature \
of (de)confinement and what do we know about ''magnetic'' objects\\ncreating \
it? Do they play any important role in sQGP physics? Can we understand\\nthe \
AdS/CFT predictions, from the gauge theory side? Can they be \
tested\\nexperimentally? Can AdS/CFT duality help us understand \
rapid\\nequilibration/entropy production? Can we work out a complete \
dynamical \\\"gravity\\ndual\\\" to heavy ion collisions?\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
