               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0807.3330\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Diego Trancanelli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"Jaume Gomis, Shunji Matsuura, Takuya Okuda, Diego \
Trancanelli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wilson loop correlators at strong coupling: from matrices \
to bubbling\\n  geometries\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"51 pages, 2 figures; v2: minor changes; v3: minor \
corrections\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0808:068,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2008/08/068\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NSF-KITP-08-96\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute at strong coupling the large N correlation \
functions of\\nsupersymmetric Wilson loops in large representations of the \
gauge group with\\nlocal operators of N=4 super Yang-Mills. The gauge theory \
computation of these\\ncorrelators is performed using matrix model \
techniques. We show that the strong\\ncoupling correlator of the Wilson loop \
with the stress tensor computed using\\nthe matrix model exactly matches the \
semiclassical computation of the\\ncorrelator of the 't Hooft loop with the \
stress tensor, providing a non-trivial\\nquantitative test of \
electric-magnetic duality of N=4 super Yang-Mills. We then\\nperform these \
calculations using the dual bulk gravitational picture, where the\\nWilson \
loop is described by a \\\"bubbling\\\" geometry. By applying \
holographic\\nmethods to these backgrounds we calculate the Wilson loop \
correlation\\nfunctions, finding perfect agreement with our gauge theory \
results.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
