            "Jaume Gomis, Shunji Matsuura, Takuya Okuda, Diego Trancanelli", 
            "title" -> 
            "Wilson loop correlators at strong coupling: from matrices to \
bubbling\n  geometries", "comments" -> 
            "51 pages, 2 figures; v2: minor changes; v3: minor corrections", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0808:068,2008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2008/08/068", "report-no" -> "NSF-KITP-08-96", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute at strong coupling the large N correlation \
functions of\nsupersymmetric Wilson loops in large representations of the \
gauge group with\nlocal operators of N=4 super Yang-Mills. The gauge theory \
computation of these\ncorrelators is performed using matrix model techniques. \
We show that the strong\ncoupling correlator of the Wilson loop with the \
stress tensor computed using\nthe matrix model exactly matches the \
semiclassical computation of the\ncorrelator of the 't Hooft loop with the \
stress tensor, providing a non-trivial\nquantitative test of \
electric-magnetic duality of N=4 super Yang-Mills. We then\nperform these \
calculations using the dual bulk gravitational picture, where the\nWilson \
loop is described by a \"bubbling\" geometry. By applying holographic\n\
methods to these backgrounds we calculate the Wilson loop correlation\n\
functions, finding perfect agreement with our gauge theory results.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
