                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that there are two supersymmetric completions \
of the\\nthree-dimensional Chern-Simons theory of level k with gauge group \
U(N)xU(N)\\ncoupled to four sets of massless scalars and spinors in the \
bi-fundamental\\nrepresentation, if we require Sp(2) global symmetry with the \
matter fields in\\nthe fundamental representation of SU(4). One is the N=6 \
superconformal theory\\nrecently studied in arXiv:0806.1218 [hep-th] and \
another is a new theory with\\nN=1 superconformal symmetry. We conjecture \
that the N=1 theory is dual to M\\ntheory on AdS_4 x Squashed \
S^7/Z_k.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
