                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop an approach for constructing the Baxter \
Q-operators for generic\\nsl(N) spin chains. The key element of our approach \
is the possibility to\\nrepresent a solution of the the Yang Baxter equation \
in the factorized form. We\\nprove that such a representation holds for a \
generic sl(N) invariant R-operator\\nand find the explicit expression for the \
factorizing operators. Taking trace of\\nmonodromy matrices constructed of \
the factorizing operators one defines a\\nfamily of commuting (Baxter) \
operators on the quantum space of the model. We\\nshow that a generic \
transfer matrix factorizes into the product of N Baxter\\nQ-operators and \
discuss an application of this representation for a derivation\\nof \
functional relations for transfer matrices.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
