                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study Wilson loop operators in three-dimensional, \
N=6 superconformal\\nChern-Simons theory dual to IIA superstring theory on \
AdS4 x CP3. Novelty of\\nWilson loop operators in this theory is that, for a \
given contour, there are\\ntwo linear combinations of Wilson loop \
transforming oppositely under\\ntime-reversal transformation. We show that \
one combination is holographically\\ndual to IIA fundamental string, while \
orthogonal combination is set to zero. We\\ngather supporting evidences from \
detailed comparative study of generalized\\ntime-reversal transformations in \
both D2-brane worldvolume and ABJM theories.\\nWe then classify \
supersymmetric Wilson loops and find at most\\n1/6-supersymmetry. We next \
study Wilson loop expectation value in planar\\nperturbation theory. For \
circular Wilson loop, we find features remarkably\\nparallel to circular \
Wilson loop in N=4 super Yang-Mills theory in four\\ndimensions. First, all \
odd loop diagrams vanish identically and even loops\\ncontribute nontrivial \
contributions. Second, quantum corrected gauge and scalar\\npropagators take \
the same form as those of N=4 super Yang-Mills theory.\\nCombining these \
results, we propose that expectation value of circular Wilson\\nloop is given \
by Wilson loop expectation value in pure Chern-Simons theory\\ntimes \
zero-dimensional Gaussian matrix model whose variance is specified by \
an\\ninterpolating function of `t Hooft coupling. We suggest the \
function\\ninterpolates smoothly between weak and strong coupling regime, \
offering new\\ntest ground of the AdS/CFT correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
