           "id" -> "0809.3786", "submitter" -> "Soo-Jong Rey", "authors" -> 
            "Soo-Jong Rey, Takao Suyama, Satoshi Yamaguchi", "title" -> 
            "Wilson Loops in Superconformal Chern-Simons Theory and \
Fundamental\n  Strings in Anti-de Sitter Supergravity Dual", "comments" -> 
            
            "v1. 34 pages, 11 figures: v2. major revision, all loop proof \
added 42\n  pages, 11 figures", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0903:127,2009", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2009/03/127", "report-no" -> "SNUST 080903", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study Wilson loop operators in three-dimensional, N=6 \
superconformal\nChern-Simons theory dual to IIA superstring theory on AdS4 x \
CP3. Novelty of\nWilson loop operators in this theory is that, for a given \
contour, there are\ntwo linear combinations of Wilson loop transforming \
oppositely under\ntime-reversal transformation. We show that one combination \
is holographically\ndual to IIA fundamental string, while orthogonal \
combination is set to zero. We\ngather supporting evidences from detailed \
comparative study of generalized\ntime-reversal transformations in both \
D2-brane worldvolume and ABJM theories.\nWe then classify supersymmetric \
Wilson loops and find at most\n1/6-supersymmetry. We next study Wilson loop \
expectation value in planar\nperturbation theory. For circular Wilson loop, \
we find features remarkably\nparallel to circular Wilson loop in N=4 super \
Yang-Mills theory in four\ndimensions. First, all odd loop diagrams vanish \
identically and even loops\ncontribute nontrivial contributions. Second, \
quantum corrected gauge and scalar\npropagators take the same form as those \
of N=4 super Yang-Mills theory.\nCombining these results, we propose that \
expectation value of circular Wilson\nloop is given by Wilson loop \
expectation value in pure Chern-Simons theory\ntimes zero-dimensional \
Gaussian matrix model whose variance is specified by an\ninterpolating \
function of `t Hooft coupling. We suggest the function\ninterpolates smoothly \
between weak and strong coupling regime, offering new\ntest ground of the \
AdS/CFT correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
