            "  In the string theory in AdS_4 \\times CP^3 we construct the \
giant magnon and\nspike solutions with two spins in two kinds of subspaces of \
R_t \\times CP^3 and\nderive the dispersion relations for them. For the \
single giant magnon solution\nin one subspace we show that its dispersion \
relation is associated with that of\nthe big one-spin giant magnon solution \
in the RP^2 subspace. For the single\ngiant magnon solution in the other \
complementary subspace its dispersion\nrelation is similar to that of the \
one-spin giant magnon solution living in the\nS^2 subspace but has one \
additional spin dependence.\n", 
