                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"ITP-UH-15/08, HWM-08-6, EMPG-08-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We prove that a scalar quantum field theory defined on \
noncommutative\\nMinkowski spacetime with noncommuting momentum coordinates \
is covariant with\\nrespect to the UV/IR duality which exchanges coordinates \
and momenta. The proof\\nis based on suitable resonance expansions of charged \
noncommutative scalar\\nfields in a background electric field, which yields \
an effective description of\\nthe field theory in terms of a coupled complex \
two-matrix model. The two\\nindependent matrix degrees of freedom ensure \
unitarity and manifest\\nCT-invariance of the field theory. The formalism \
describes an analytic\\ncontinuation of the renormalizable Grosse-Wulkenhaar \
models to Minkowski\\nsignature.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
