               RowBox[{"\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Finite-g Strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PhD thesis, 339 pages, 69 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 44 (2011) 124002\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In view of one day proving the AdS/CFT correspondence, \
a deeper understanding\\nof string theory on certain curved backgrounds such \
as AdS_5xS^5 is required.\\nIn this dissertation we make a step in this \
direction by focusing on RxS^3. It\\nwas discovered in recent years that \
string theory on AdS_5xS^5 admits a Lax\\nformulation. However, the complete \
statement of integrability requires not only\\nthe existence of a Lax \
formulation, but also that the resulting integrals of\\nmotion are in \
pairwise involution. This idea is central to the first part of\\nthis thesis. \
Exploiting this integrability we apply algebro-geometric methods\\nto string \
theory on RxS^3 and obtain the general finite-gap solution. \
The\\nconstruction is based on an invariant algebraic curve previously found \
in the\\nAdS_5xS^5 case. However, encoding the dynamics of the solution \
requires\\nspecification of additional marked points. By restricting the \
symplectic\\nstructure of the string to this algebro-geometric data we derive \
the\\naction-angle variables of the system. We then perform a first-principle\
\\nsemiclassical quantisation of string theory on RxS^3 as a toy model for \
strings\\non AdS_5xS^5. The result is exactly what one expects from the dual \
gauge theory\\nperspective, namely the underlying algebraic curve discretises \
in a natural\\nway. We also derive a general formula for the fluctuation \
energies around the\\ngeneric finite-gap solution. The ideas used can be \
generalised to AdS_5xS^5.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 19 Oct 2008 14:39:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-02-23\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Vicedo\"", ",", "\"Benoit\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0810.3402", "submitter" -> "Benoit Vicedo", "authors" -> 
            "Benoit Vicedo", "title" -> "Finite-g Strings", "comments" -> 
            "PhD thesis, 339 pages, 69 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 44 (2011) 124002", "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In view of one day proving the AdS/CFT correspondence, a \
deeper understanding\nof string theory on certain curved backgrounds such as \
AdS_5xS^5 is required.\nIn this dissertation we make a step in this direction \
by focusing on RxS^3. It\nwas discovered in recent years that string theory \
on AdS_5xS^5 admits a Lax\nformulation. However, the complete statement of \
integrability requires not only\nthe existence of a Lax formulation, but also \
that the resulting integrals of\nmotion are in pairwise involution. This idea \
is central to the first part of\nthis thesis. Exploiting this integrability \
we apply algebro-geometric methods\nto string theory on RxS^3 and obtain the \
general finite-gap solution. The\nconstruction is based on an invariant \
algebraic curve previously found in the\nAdS_5xS^5 case. However, encoding \
the dynamics of the solution requires\nspecification of additional marked \
points. By restricting the symplectic\nstructure of the string to this \
algebro-geometric data we derive the\naction-angle variables of the system. \
We then perform a first-principle\nsemiclassical quantisation of string \
theory on RxS^3 as a toy model for strings\non AdS_5xS^5. The result is \
exactly what one expects from the dual gauge theory\nperspective, namely the \
underlying algebraic curve discretises in a natural\nway. We also derive a \
general formula for the fluctuation energies around the\ngeneric finite-gap \
solution. The ideas used can be generalised to AdS_5xS^5.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 19 Oct 2008 14:39:55 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-02-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Vicedo", "Benoit", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
