               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"HU-EP-08/46, LAPTH-CONF-1284/08\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We summarise the status of an intriguing new duality \
between planar maximally\\nhelicity violating scattering amplitudes and \
light-like Wilson loops in N=4\\nsuper Yang-Mills. In particular, we focus on \
the role played by (dual)\\nconformal symmetry, which is made predictive by \
deriving anomalous conformal\\nWard identities for the Wilson loops. Assuming \
the duality, the conformal\\nsymmetry of the dual Wilson loops becomes an \
unexpected new symmetry of\\nscattering amplitudes in N=4 SYM.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
