            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We summarise the status of an intriguing new duality between \
planar maximally\nhelicity violating scattering amplitudes and light-like \
Wilson loops in N=4\nsuper Yang-Mills. In particular, we focus on the role \
played by (dual)\nconformal symmetry, which is made predictive by deriving \
anomalous conformal\nWard identities for the Wilson loops. Assuming the \
duality, the conformal\nsymmetry of the dual Wilson loops becomes an \
unexpected new symmetry of\nscattering amplitudes in N=4 SYM.\n", 
