matrix of AdS5 x S5\nstring theory in the Green-Schwarz formulation is \
determined by using a\nfirst-order Hamiltonian formulation and by adding to \
the Bena-Polchinski-Roiban\nLax connection terms proportional to constraints. \
This enables in particular to\nshow that the conserved charges of this theory \
are in involution. This result\nis obtained for a general world-sheet metric. \
The same exchange algebra is\nobtained within the pure spinor description of \
AdS5 x S5 string theory. These\nresults are compared to the one obtained by \
A. Mikhailov and S. Schaefer-Nameki\nfor the pure spinor formulation.\n", 
