               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We pursue the question of multi-magnon dynamics, \
focusing on the simplest\\ncase of magnons moving on RxS2 and working at the \
semiclassical level. Through\\na Pohlmeyer reduction, the problem reduces to \
another well known integrable\\nfield theory, the sine-Gordon model, which \
can be exactly described through an\\nN-body model of Calogero type. The two \
theories coincide at the level of\\nequations of motion, but physical \
quantities like the energies (of magnons and\\nsolitons) and the associated \
phase shifts are different. We start from the\\nequivalence of the two \
systems at the level of equations of motion and require\\nthat the new \
(string theory) model reproduces the correct magnon energies and\\nthe phase \
shift, both of which differ from the soliton case. From the\\ncomparison of \
energies we suggest a Hamiltonian, and from requiring the correct\\nphase \
shift we are led to a nontrivial Poisson structure representing \
the\\nmagnons.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 27 Oct 2008 18:37:50 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
