            "19 pages, no figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> "BROWN-HET 1567", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We pursue the question of multi-magnon dynamics, focusing on \
the simplest\ncase of magnons moving on RxS2 and working at the semiclassical \
level. Through\na Pohlmeyer reduction, the problem reduces to another well \
known integrable\nfield theory, the sine-Gordon model, which can be exactly \
described through an\nN-body model of Calogero type. The two theories \
coincide at the level of\nequations of motion, but physical quantities like \
the energies (of magnons and\nsolitons) and the associated phase shifts are \
different. We start from the\nequivalence of the two systems at the level of \
equations of motion and require\nthat the new (string theory) model \
reproduces the correct magnon energies and\nthe phase shift, both of which \
differ from the soliton case. From the\ncomparison of energies we suggest a \
Hamiltonian, and from requiring the correct\nphase shift we are led to a \
nontrivial Poisson structure representing the\nmagnons.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 27 Oct 2008 18:37:50 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-10-28", 
