                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper studies giant magnons in CP3, which in all \
known cases are old\\nsolutions from S5 placed into two- and \
three-dimensional subspaces of CP3,\\nnamely CP1, RP2 and RP3. We clarify \
some points about these subspaces, and\\nother potentially interesting three- \
and four-dimensional subspaces. After\\nconfirming that E-(J1-J4)/2 is a \
Hamiltonian for small fluctuations of the\\nrelevant 'vacuum' point particle \
solution, we use it to calculate the\\ndispersion relation of each of the \
inequivalent giant magnons. We comment on\\nthe embedding of finite-J \
solutions, and use these to compare string solutions\\nto giant magnons in \
the algebraic curve.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
