                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The differential calculus based on the derivations of \
an associative algebra\\nunderlies most of the noncommutative field theories \
considered so far. We\\nreview the essential properties of this framework and \
the main features of\\nnoncommutative connections in the case of non graded \
associative unital\\nalgebras with involution. We extend this framework to \
the case of\\n${\\\\mathbb{Z}}_2$-graded unital involutive algebras. We show, \
in the case of the\\nMoyal algebra or some related ${\\\\mathbb{Z}}_2$-graded \
version of it, that the\\nderivation based differential calculus is a \
suitable framework to construct\\nYang-Mills-Higgs type models on Moyal (or \
related) algebras, the covariant\\ncoordinates having in particular a natural \
interpretation as Higgs fields. We\\nalso exhibit, in one situation, a link \
between the renormalisable NC\\n$\\\\phi^4$-model with harmonic term and a \
gauge theory model. Some possible\\nconsequences of this are briefly \
discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 24 Nov 2008 12:03:21 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
