               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Remarks on the entanglement entropy for disconnected \
regions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"14 pages, 4 figures, some additions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0903:048,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2009/03/048\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Few facts are known about the entanglement entropy for \
disconnected regions\\nin quantum field theory. We study here the property of \
extensivity of the\\nmutual information, which holds for free massless \
fermions in two dimensions.\\nWe uncover the structure of the entropy \
function in the extensive case, and\\nfind an interesting connection with the \
renormalization group irreversibility.\\nThe solution is a function on \
space-time regions which complies with all the\\nknown requirements a \
relativistic entropy function has to satisfy. We show that\\nthe holographic \
ansatz of Ryu and Takayanagi, the free scalar and Dirac fields\\nin \
dimensions greater than two, and the massive free fields in two \
dimensions\\nall fail to be exactly extensive, disproving recent conjectures.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
