(1) ((1)\\n  Theoretical Department SPb State University, (2) SPb Department \
of Steklov\\n  Institute of Mathematics)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On a property of branching coefficients for affine Lie \
algebras\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"17 pages, 3 figures, to be published in Algebra i \
Analiz\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"SPbU-IP-08-03\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math.RT math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It is demonstrated that decompositions of integrable \
highest weight modules\\nof a simple Lie algebra with respect to its \
reductive subalgebra obey the set\\nof algebraic relations leading to the \
recursive properties for the\\ncorresponding branching coefficients. These \
properties are encoded in the\\nspecial element (of the formal algebra E(g)) \
Gamma_(a ->g) that describes the\\ninjection and is called the fan. In the \
simplest case, when \\\"a\\\" is a Cartan\\nsubalgebra of g, the recursion \
procedure generates the weight diagram of the\\nmodule L(g). When applied to \
a reduction of highest weight modules the\\nrecursion described by the fan \
provides a highly effective tool to obtain the\\nexplicit values of branching \
coefficients.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
