            "  It is demonstrated that decompositions of integrable highest \
weight modules\nof a simple Lie algebra with respect to its reductive \
subalgebra obey the set\nof algebraic relations leading to the recursive \
properties for the\ncorresponding branching coefficients. These properties \
are encoded in the\nspecial element (of the formal algebra E(g)) Gamma_(a \
->g) that describes the\ninjection and is called the fan. In the simplest \
case, when \"a\" is a Cartan\nsubalgebra of g, the recursion procedure \
generates the weight diagram of the\nmodule L(g). When applied to a reduction \
of highest weight modules the\nrecursion described by the fan provides a \
highly effective tool to obtain the\nexplicit values of branching \
coefficients.\n", 
