         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0812.2431", "submitter" -> "Alin Tirziu", "authors" -> 
            "R. Ishizeki, M. Kruczenski, A. Tirziu and A.A. Tseytlin", 
            "title" -> 
            "Spiky strings in AdS_3 x S^1 and their AdS-pp-wave limits", 
            "comments" -> 
            "34 pages, 4 figures; v2: references added; v3: typos corrected", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D79:026006,2009", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.79.026006", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study a class of classical solutions for closed strings \
moving in AdS_3 x\nS^1 part of AdS_5 x S^5 with energy E and spin S in AdS_3 \
and angular momentum\nJ and winding m in S^1. They have rigid shape with n \
spikes in AdS_3. We find\nthat when J or m are non-zero, the spikes do not \
end in cusps. We consider in\ndetail a special large n limit in which S ~ \
n^2, J ~ n, i.e. S >> J >> 1, with\n(E+S)/ n^2, (E-S)/ n, J/n, m/n staying \
finite. In that limit the spiky spinning\nstring approaches the boundary of \
AdS_5. We show that the corresponding\nsolution can be interpreted as \
describing a periodic-spike string moving in\nAdS_3 --pp-wave x S^1 \
background. The resulting expression for the string\nenergy should represent \
a strong-coupling prediction for anomalous dimension of\na class of dual \
gauge theory states in a particular thermodynamic limit of the\nSL(2) spin \
chain.\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 12 Dec 2008 17:15:29 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 21 Jan 2009 19:13:56 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 25 Feb 2010 19:58:25 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-02-25", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ishizeki", "R.", ""}, {
