Yang-Mills theory in terms\nof tree-level disk correlation functions and the \
scalar one-loop box integral.\nAs a check, known results for all four-point \
functions and for n-point extremal\nand near-extremal correlators are \
rederived. The result is then used to\nevaluate explicitly a selection of \
five and six-point functions. Our findings\nsuggest that a general one-loop \
five-point function may be represented through\nthe minimal four-point and \
five-point functions of weight two operators.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 17 Dec 2008 17:10:37 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 3 Mar 2009 09:18:39 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-06-24", 
