                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The effective geometry and the gravitational coupling \
of nonabelian gauge and\\nscalar fields on generic NC branes in Yang-Mills \
matrix models is determined.\\nCovariant field equations are derived from the \
basic matrix equations of\\nmotions, known as Yang-Mills algebra. Remarkably, \
the equations of motion for\\nthe Poisson structure and for the nonabelian \
gauge fields follow from a matrix\\nNoether theorem, and are therefore \
protected from quantum corrections. This\\nprovides a transparent derivation \
and generalization of the effective action\\ngoverning the SU(n) gauge fields \
obtained in [1], including the would-be\\ntopological term. In particular, \
the IKKT matrix model is capable of describing\\n4-dimensional NC space-times \
with a general effective metric. Metric\\ndeformations of flat Moyal-Weyl \
space are briefly discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
