                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Deviation from Alday-Maldacena Duality For Wavy \
Circle\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"23 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B823:289-319,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2009.06.009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"OCU-PHYS-308, FIAN/TD-27/08, ITEP/TH-69/08\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Alday-Maldacena conjecture is that the area A_P of the \
minimal surface in\\nAdS_5 space with a boundary P, located in Euclidean \
space at infinity of AdS_5,\\ncoincides with a double integral D_P along P, \
the Abelian Wilson average in an\\nauxiliary dual model. The boundary P is a \
polygon formed by momenta of n\\nexternal light-like particles in N=4 SYM \
theory, and in a certain n=infty limit\\nit can be substituted by an \
arbitrary smooth curve (wavy circle). The\\nAlday-Maldacena conjecture is \
known to be violated for n>5, when it fails to be\\nsupported by the peculiar \
global conformal invariance, however, the structure\\nof deviations remains \
obscure. The case of wavy lines can appear more\\nconvenient for analysis of \
these deviations due to the systematic method\\ndeveloped in arXiv:0803.1547 \
for (perturbative) evaluation of minimal areas,\\nwhich is not yet available \
in the presence of angles at finite n. We correct a\\nmistake in that paper \
and explicitly evaluate the h^2\\\\bar h^2 terms, where the\\nfirst deviation \
from the Alday-Maldacena duality arises for the wavy circle.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
