formed by momenta of n\nexternal light-like particles in N=4 SYM theory, and \
in a certain n=infty limit\nit can be substituted by an arbitrary smooth \
curve (wavy circle). The\nAlday-Maldacena conjecture is known to be violated \
for n>5, when it fails to be\nsupported by the peculiar global conformal \
invariance, however, the structure\nof deviations remains obscure. The case \
of wavy lines can appear more\nconvenient for analysis of these deviations \
due to the systematic method\ndeveloped in arXiv:0803.1547 for (perturbative) \
evaluation of minimal areas,\nwhich is not yet available in the presence of \
angles at finite n. We correct a\nmistake in that paper and explicitly \
evaluate the h^2\\bar h^2 terms, where the\nfirst deviation from the \
Alday-Maldacena duality arises for the wavy circle.\n", 
