, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We consider two-loop anomalous dimensions for \
fermionic operators in the ABJM\\nmodel and the ABJ model. We find the \
appropriate Hamiltonian and show that it\\nis consistent with a previously \
predicted Bethe ansatz for the ABJM model. The\\ndifference between the ABJ \
and ABJM models is invisible at the two-loop level\\nby cancelation of parity \
violating diagrams. We then construct a Hamiltonian\\nfor the full two-loop \
OSp(6|4) spin chain by first constructing the Hamiltonian\\nfor an SL(2|1) \
subgroup, and then lifting to OSp(6|4). We show that this\\nHamiltonian is \
consistent with the Hamiltonian found for the \
fermionic\\noperators.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
