 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate Poisson-Lie symmetry for T-dual sigma \
models on supermanifolds\\nin general and on Lie supergroups in particular. \
We show that the integrability\\ncondition on this super Poisson-Lie symmetry \
is equivalent to the super Jacobi\\nidentities of the Lie super-bialgebras. \
As examples we consider models related\\nto four dimensional Lie \
super-bialgebras $((2A1,1 + 2A)^1, D10_p=1/2)$ and\\n$((2A1,1 + 2A)^1, I)$. \
Then generally it is shown that for Abelian case (g, I)\\nthe super \
Poisson-Lie T-duality transforms the role of fermionic (bosonic)\\nfields in \
the model to bosonic (fermionic) fields on the dual model and \
vice\\nversa.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
