         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0901.3334", "submitter" -> "Changrim Ahn", "authors" -> 
            "Changrim Ahn, Rafael I. Nepomechie", "title" -> 
            "Two-loop test of the N=6 Chern-Simons theory S-matrix", 
            "comments" -> "21 pages, no figure; references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0903:144,2009", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2009/03/144", "report-no" -> "UMTG-262", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            
            "  Starting from the integrable two-loop spin-chain Hamiltonian \
describing the\nanomalous dimensions of scalar operators in the planar N=6 \
superconformal\nChern-Simons theory of ABJM, we perform a direct coordinate \
Bethe ansatz\ncomputation of the corresponding two-loop S-matrix. The result \
matches with the\nweak-coupling limit of the scalar sector of the all-loop \
S-matrix which we have\nrecently proposed. In particular, we confirm that the \
scattering of A and B\nparticles is reflectionless. As a warm up, we first \
review the analogous\ncomputation of the one-loop S-matrix from the one-loop \
dilatation operator for\nthe scalar sector of planar N=4 superconformal \
Yang-Mills theory, and compare\nthe result with the all-loop SU(2|2)^{2} \
S-matrix.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 21 Jan 2009 18:43:06 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 28 Jan 2009 09:30:17 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-05-27", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ahn", "Changrim", ""}, {
              "Nepomechie", "Rafael I.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
