               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we study the n-point correlation \
functions of two different\\nfamilies of local gauge invariant operators in \
N=4 supersymmetric Yang-Mills\\ntheory. The main idea is to consider the \
correlation functions of operators\\nwhich all share a number of \
supersymmetries irrespective of their relative\\nlocations. We achieve this \
by equipping the operators with explicit space-time\\ndependence. We provide \
evidence by different methods that these n-point\\ncorrelators do not receive \
quantum corrections in perturbation theory and are\\nhence given exactly by \
their tree-level result. The arguments rely on explicit\\nchecks for general \
four-point correlators, some five-point and six-point\\ncorrelators and a \
more abstract calculation based on a novel topological\\ntwisting of N=4 \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
