               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Till Bargheer, Niklas Beisert, Florian Loebbert\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Long-Range Deformations for Integrable Spin Chains\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"63 pages, v2: references added, v3: typos corrected in \
eqs (8.20) and\\n  (8.24)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A42:285205,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/42/28/285205\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2009-009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a recursion relation for the explicit \
construction of integrable\\nspin chain Hamiltonians with long-range \
interactions. Based on arbitrary\\nshort-range (e.g. nearest-neighbor) \
integrable spin chains, it allows to\\nconstruct an infinite set of conserved \
long-range charges. We explain the\\nmoduli space of deformation parameters \
by different classes of generating\\noperators. The rapidity map and dressing \
phase in the long-range Bethe\\nequations are a result of these deformations. \
The closed chain asymptotic Bethe\\nequations for long-range spin chains \
transforming under a generic symmetry\\nalgebra are derived. Notably, our \
construction applies to generalizations of\\nstandard nearest-neighbor chains \
such as alternating spin chains. We also\\ndiscuss relevant properties for \
its application to planar D=4, N=4 and D=3, N=6\\nsupersymmetric gauge \
theories. Finally, we present a map between long-range and\\ninhomogeneous \
spin chains delivering more insight into the structures of these\\nmodels as \
well as their limitations at wrapping order.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
