arbitrary\nshort-range (e.g. nearest-neighbor) integrable spin chains, it \
allows to\nconstruct an infinite set of conserved long-range charges. We \
explain the\nmoduli space of deformation parameters by different classes of \
generating\noperators. The rapidity map and dressing phase in the long-range \
Bethe\nequations are a result of these deformations. The closed chain \
