                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the solitons of the symmetric space \
sine-Gordon theories that arise\\nonce the Pohlmeyer reduction has been \
imposed on a sigma model with the\\nsymmetric space as target. Under this map \
the solitons arise as giant magnons\\nthat are relevant to string theory in \
the context of the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence. In particular, we consider the \
cases S^n, CP^n and SU(n) in\\nsome detail. We clarify the construction of \
the charges carried by the solitons\\nand also address the possible \
Lagrangian formulations of the symmetric space\\nsine-Gordon theories. We \
show that the dressing, or Backlund, transformation\\nnaturally produces \
solitons directly in both the sigma model and the symmetric\\nspace \
sine-Gordon equations without the need to explicitly map from one to \
the\\nother. In particular, we obtain a new magnon solution in CP^3. We show \
that the\\ndressing method does not produce the more general \\\"dyonic\\\" \
solutions which\\ninvolve non-trivial motion of the collective coordinates \
carried by the\\nsolitons.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
