               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0902.2489\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Radu Roiban\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"R. Roiban, A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"UV finiteness of Pohlmeyer-reduced form of the AdS_5xS^5 \
superstring\\n  theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages, Latex; v2: typos corrected, minor clarifying \
remarks added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0904:078,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2009/04/078\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the Pohlmeyer-type reduced theory found by \
explicitly solving the\\nVirasoro constraints in the formulation of AdS_5xS^5 \
superstring in terms of\\nsupercoset currents. The resulting set of \
classically equivalent, integrable\\nLagrangian equations of motion has the \
advantage of involving only a physical\\nnumber of degrees of freedom and yet \
being 2d Lorentz invariant. The\\ncorresponding reduced theory action may be \
written as a gauged WZW model\\ncoupled to fermions with further bosonic and \
fermionic potential terms. Since\\nthe AdS_5xS^5 superstring sigma model is \
conformally invariant, its classical\\nrelation to the reduced theory may \
extend to the quantum level only if the\\nlatter is, in fact, UV finite. This \
theory is power counting renormalizable\\nwith the only possible divergences \
being of potential type. We explicitly\\nverify its 1-loop finiteness and \
show that the 2-loop divergences are, in\\ngeneral, scheme dependent and \
vanish in dimensional reduction scheme. We expect\\nthat the reduced theory \
is finite to all orders in the loop expansion.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
