conformally invariant, its classical\nrelation to the reduced theory may \
extend to the quantum level only if the\nlatter is, in fact, UV finite. This \
theory is power counting renormalizable\nwith the only possible divergences \
being of potential type. We explicitly\nverify its 1-loop finiteness and show \
that the 2-loop divergences are, in\ngeneral, scheme dependent and vanish in \
dimensional reduction scheme. We expect\nthat the reduced theory is finite to \
all orders in the loop expansion.\n", 
