               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"BPS Wilson loops in N=4 SYM: Examples on hyperbolic \
submanifolds of\\n  space-time\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, 7 figues, pdftex\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D79:106006,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.79.106006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-EP-09/05\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we present a family of supersymmetric \
Wilson loops of N=4\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory in Minkowski space. \
Our examples focus on\\ncurves restricted to hyperbolic submanifolds, H_3 and \
H_2, of space-time.\\nGenerically they preserve two supercharges, but in \
special cases more,\\nincluding a case which has not been discussed before, \
of the hyperbolic line,\\nconformal to the straight line and circle, which is \
half-BPS. We discuss some\\ngeneral properties of these Wilson loops and \
their string duals and study\\nspecial examples in more detail. Generically \
the string duals propagate on a\\ncomplexification of AdS_5 x S^5 and in some \
specific examples the compact\\nsphere is effectively replaced by a de-Sitter \
space.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 26 Feb 2009 13:47:32 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-07-30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
