            "Phys.Rev.D79:106006,2009", "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.79.106006",
             "report-no" -> "HU-EP-09/05", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we present a family of supersymmetric Wilson \
loops of N=4\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory in Minkowski space. Our \
examples focus on\ncurves restricted to hyperbolic submanifolds, H_3 and H_2, \
of space-time.\nGenerically they preserve two supercharges, but in special \
cases more,\nincluding a case which has not been discussed before, of the \
hyperbolic line,\nconformal to the straight line and circle, which is \
half-BPS. We discuss some\ngeneral properties of these Wilson loops and their \
string duals and study\nspecial examples in more detail. Generically the \
string duals propagate on a\ncomplexification of AdS_5 x S^5 and in some \
specific examples the compact\nsphere is effectively replaced by a de-Sitter \
space.\n", "versions" -> {{
