               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0903.0609\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Niklas Beisert\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Niklas Beisert\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"T-Duality, Dual Conformal Symmetry and Integrability for \
Strings on\\n  AdS_5 x S^5\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"11 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Fortschr.Phys.57:329-337,2009\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1002/prop.200900060\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2009-027\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In recent years two intriguing observations have been \
made for N=4 super\\nYang-Mills theory and for superstrings on AdS5xS5: In \
the planar limit the\\ncomputation of the spectrum is vastly simplified by \
the apparent integrability\\nof the models. Furthermore, planar scattering \
amplitudes of the gauge theory\\ndisplay remarkable features which have been \
attributed to the appearance of a\\ndual superconformal symmetry. Here we \
review the connection of these two\\ndevelopments from the point of view of \
the classical symmetry by means of a\\nsuper-T-self-duality. In particular, \
we show explicitly how the charges of\\nconformal symmetry and of the \
integrable structure are related to the dual\\nones.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
