         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0903.0609", "submitter" -> "Niklas Beisert", "authors" -> 
            "Niklas Beisert", "title" -> 
            "T-Duality, Dual Conformal Symmetry and Integrability for Strings \
on\n  AdS_5 x S^5", "comments" -> "11 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Fortschr.Phys.57:329-337,2009", "doi" -> 
            "10.1002/prop.200900060", "report-no" -> "AEI-2009-027", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In recent years two intriguing observations have been made for \
N=4 super\nYang-Mills theory and for superstrings on AdS5xS5: In the planar \
limit the\ncomputation of the spectrum is vastly simplified by the apparent \
integrability\nof the models. Furthermore, planar scattering amplitudes of \
the gauge theory\ndisplay remarkable features which have been attributed to \
the appearance of a\ndual superconformal symmetry. Here we review the \
connection of these two\ndevelopments from the point of view of the classical \
symmetry by means of a\nsuper-T-self-duality. In particular, we show \
explicitly how the charges of\nconformal symmetry and of the integrable \
structure are related to the dual\nones.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 3 Mar 2009 20:45:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-06-22", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Beisert", "Niklas", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
