                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The AdS(4)/CFT(3) duality is a new example of an \
integrable and exactly\\nsolvable AdS/CFT system. There is, however, a \
puzzling mismatch between the\\nnumber of degrees of freedom used in the \
exact solution (4B+4F scattering\\nstates) and 8B+8F transverse oscillation \
modes of critical superstring theory.\\nWe offer a resolution of this puzzle \
by arguing that half of the string modes\\ndissolve in the continuum of \
two-particle states once alpha' corrections are\\ntaken into account. We also \
check that the conjectured exact S-matrix of\\nAdS(4)/CFT(3) agrees with the \
tree-level worldsheet calculation.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
