               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pawe{\\\\l}  Caputa\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Pawel Caputa, Charlotte Kristjansen and Konstantinos \
Zoubos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-planar ABJ Theory and Parity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"11 pages, 1 figure. v2: Typos fixed, minor clarifications\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett.B677:197-202,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2009.05.021\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  While the ABJ Chern-Simons-matter theory and its string \
theory dual\\nmanifestly lack parity invariance, no sign of parity violation \
has so far been\\nobserved on the weak coupling spin chain side. In \
particular, the planar\\ntwo-loop dilatation generator of ABJ theory is \
parity invariant. In this letter\\nwe derive the non-planar part of the \
two-loop dilatation generator of ABJ\\ntheory in its SU(2)xSU(2) sub-sector. \
Applying the dilatation generator to\\nshort operators, we explicitly \
demonstrate that, for operators carrying\\nexcitations on both spin chains, \
the non-planar part breaks parity invariance.\\nFor operators with only one \
type of excitation, however, parity remains\\nconserved at the non-planar \
level. We furthermore observe that, as for ABJM\\ntheory, the degeneracy \
between planar parity pairs is lifted when non-planar\\ncorrections are taken \
into account.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 19 Mar 2009 18:11:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
