         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0903.3354", "submitter" -> "Pawe{\\l}  Caputa", "authors" -> 
            "Pawel Caputa, Charlotte Kristjansen and Konstantinos Zoubos", 
            "title" -> "Non-planar ABJ Theory and Parity", "comments" -> 
            "11 pages, 1 figure. v2: Typos fixed, minor clarifications", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Lett.B677:197-202,2009", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physletb.2009.05.021", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  While the ABJ Chern-Simons-matter theory and its string theory \
dual\nmanifestly lack parity invariance, no sign of parity violation has so \
far been\nobserved on the weak coupling spin chain side. In particular, the \
planar\ntwo-loop dilatation generator of ABJ theory is parity invariant. In \
this letter\nwe derive the non-planar part of the two-loop dilatation \
generator of ABJ\ntheory in its SU(2)xSU(2) sub-sector. Applying the \
dilatation generator to\nshort operators, we explicitly demonstrate that, for \
operators carrying\nexcitations on both spin chains, the non-planar part \
breaks parity invariance.\nFor operators with only one type of excitation, \
however, parity remains\nconserved at the non-planar level. We furthermore \
observe that, as for ABJM\ntheory, the degeneracy between planar parity pairs \
is lifted when non-planar\ncorrections are taken into account.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 19 Mar 2009 18:11:27 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 14 Apr 2009 14:54:43 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
