               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper studies giant magnons in AdS_4 x CP^3 using \
both the string\\nsigma-model and the algebraic curve. We complete the \
dictionary of solutions by\\nfinding the dyonic generalisation of the CP^1 \
string solution, which matches\\nthe `small' giant magnon in the algebraic \
curve, and by pointing out that the\\nsolution recently constructed by the \
dressing method is the `big' giant magnon.\\nWe then use the curve to compute \
finite-J corrections to all cases, which for\\nthe non-dyonic cases always \
match the AFZ result. For the dyonic RP^3 magnon we\\nrecover the S^5 answer, \
but for the `small' and `big' giant magnons we obtain\\nnew \
corrections.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
