             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We use S-duality and planarity to propose an argument for the\n\
non-renormalization of the dispersion relation of giant magnon solutions in\n\
type IIB string theory on AdS_5 x S^5. We compute the spectrum of giant \
magnons\nfor (p,q)-strings from field theory at strong coupling by using the \
central\ncharge properties of electrically and magnetically charged \
supersymmetric\nstates in the Coulomb branch of N=4 super Yang-Mills. We \
argue that the\ncoupling dependence of the giant magnon dispersion relation \
conjectured in the\nliterature using integrability assumptions is in fact the \
only functional\ndependence compatible with S-duality.\n", 
