            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0904.3665\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrey Zayakin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A. Gorsky, A. Monin, A. V. Zayakin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Correlator of Wilson and t'Hooft Loops at Strong Coupling \
in\\n  $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"17 pages, 9 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett.B679:529-534,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2009.08.017\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"ITEP-TH-10/09, FTPI-MINN-09/12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate the correlator of a 't Hooft and a Wilson \
coplanar circular\\nconcentric loops at strong coupling in N=4 SYM theory \
when it reduces to the\\ncalculation of the composite minimal surface in the \
curved space with the\\nproper boundary conditions. The minimal admissible \
ratio of the radii of 't\\nHooft and Wilson loops for such a configuration is \
found to be\\n$\\\\mathrm{e}^{-1/2}\\\\approx 0.606$ at zero temperature and \
the dependence of the\\nminimal admissible radii ratio on temperature is \
derived. At low temperatures\\nthe minimal admissible ratio for 't Hooft and \
Wilson loops remains close to\\n0.6, whereas at high temperatures $T$ it \
becomes equal to $\\\\frac{1}{\\\\pi T}$. We\\nfind that at any temperature \
there exists a phase transition point: beneath\\nsome specific value of 't \
Hooft loop radius the dual counterpart of Wilson-'t\\nHooft correlator is \
organized as two disconnected surfaces in AdS, whereas for\\n't Hooft loop \
radius above it, there exists a connected configuration with a\\njunction of \
monopole, charge and dyon surfaces. We suggest a generalization of\\nthe \
entanglement entropy for charged boundaries and make some comments on \
its\\ncalculation at strong coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 Apr 2009 17:10:43 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-09-28\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Gorsky\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Monin\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Zayakin\"", ",", "\"A. V.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
