           "id" -> "0904.3665", "submitter" -> "Andrey Zayakin", "authors" -> 
            "A. Gorsky, A. Monin, A. V. Zayakin", "title" -> 
            "Correlator of Wilson and t'Hooft Loops at Strong Coupling in\n  \
$\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM Theory", "comments" -> "17 pages, 9 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Lett.B679:529-534,2009", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physletb.2009.08.017", "report-no" -> 
            "ITEP-TH-10/09, FTPI-MINN-09/12", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate the correlator of a 't Hooft and a Wilson \
coplanar circular\nconcentric loops at strong coupling in N=4 SYM theory when \
it reduces to the\ncalculation of the composite minimal surface in the curved \
space with the\nproper boundary conditions. The minimal admissible ratio of \
the radii of 't\nHooft and Wilson loops for such a configuration is found to \
be\n$\\mathrm{e}^{-1/2}\\approx 0.606$ at zero temperature and the dependence \
of the\nminimal admissible radii ratio on temperature is derived. At low \
temperatures\nthe minimal admissible ratio for 't Hooft and Wilson loops \
remains close to\n0.6, whereas at high temperatures $T$ it becomes equal to $\
\\frac{1}{\\pi T}$. We\nfind that at any temperature there exists a phase \
transition point: beneath\nsome specific value of 't Hooft loop radius the \
dual counterpart of Wilson-'t\nHooft correlator is organized as two \
disconnected surfaces in AdS, whereas for\n't Hooft loop radius above it, \
there exists a connected configuration with a\njunction of monopole, charge \
and dyon surfaces. We suggest a generalization of\nthe entanglement entropy \
for charged boundaries and make some comments on its\ncalculation at strong \
coupling.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
