                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Generalized Dynamical Spin Chain and 4-Loop Integrability \
in N=6\\n  Superconformal Chern-Simons Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages, 13 figures, v2. references added and conclusion \
changed;\\n  v3. references updated, v4. final published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B827:381-405,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2009.10.011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SNUST 090401, UOSTP 09031\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit unitary representation of centrally extended \
(2 | 2) excitation\\nsuperalgebra. We find most generally that \
`pseudo-momentum', not lattice\\nmomentum, diagonalizes spin chain \
Hamiltonian and leads to generalized dynamic\\nspin chain. All known results \
point to lattice momentum diagonalization for N=4\\nsuper Yang-Mills theory. \
Having different interacting structure, we ask if N=6\\nsuperconformal \
Chern-Simons theory provides an example of pseudo-momentum\\ndiagonalization. \
For SO(6) sector, we study maximal shuffling and\\nnext-to-maximal shuffling \
terms in the dilatation operator and compare them\\nwith results expected \
from psu(2|2) superalgebbra and integrability. At two\\nloops, we rederive \
maximal shuffling term (3-site) and find perfect agreement\\nwith known \
results. At four loops, we first find absence of next-to-maximal\\nshuffling \
term (4-site), in agreement with prediction based on integrability.\\nWe next \
extract maximal shuffling term (5-site), the most relevant term \
for\\nchecking the possibility of pseudo-momentum diagonalization. Curiously, \
we find\\nthat result agrees with integraility prediction based on lattice \
momentum, as\\nin N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. Consistency of our results is \
fully ensured by\\nchecks of renormalizability up to six loops.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
