two-sphere\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"52 pages, Minor typos fixed and some comments added in \
Sec. 8\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1007:088,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2010)088\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a recently discovered family of 1/8-BPS \
supersymmetric Wilson loops\\nin N=4 super Yang-Mills theory and their string \
theory duals. The operators are\\ndefined for arbitrary contours on a \
two-sphere in space-time, and they were\\nconjectured to be captured \
perturbatively by 2d bosonic Yang-Mills theory. In\\nthe AdS dual, they are \
described by pseudo-holomorphic string surfaces living\\non a certain \
submanifold of AdS_5 x S^5. We show that the regularized area of\\nthese \
string surfaces is invariant under area preserving diffeomorphisms of \
the\\nboundary loop, in agreement with the conjecture. Further, we find a \
connection\\nbetween the pseudo-holomorphicity equations and an auxiliary \
sigma-model on\\nS^3, which may help to construct new 1/8-BPS string \
solutions. We also show\\nthat the conjectured relation to 2d Yang-Mills \
implies that a connected\\ncorrelator of two Wilson loops is computed by a \
Hermitian Gaussian two-matrix\\nmodel. On the AdS dual side, we argue that \
the connected correlator is\\ndescribed by two disconnected disks interacting \
through the exchange of\\nsupergravity modes, and we show that this agrees \
with the strong coupling\\nplanar limit of the two-matrix model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
