               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold Blas\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"L. F. dos Santos, H. Blas and M. J. B. F. da Silva\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonvanishing boundary conditions and dark solitons in the \
NLS model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTex, 7 pages, 2 figures. Poster contribution to the \
Fifth\\n  International School on Field Theory and Gravitation, Cuiaba', Mato \
Grosso,\\n  MT, Brasil, April 20-24 2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PoS ISFTG:043,2009\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider non-vanishing boundary conditions (NVBC) \
for the NLS model\\n[6,7,27] in the context of the hybrid dressing \
transformation and\\n$\\\\tau$-function approach. In order to write the NLS \
model in a suitable form to\\ndeal with non-vanishing boundary conditions it \
is introduced a new spectral\\nparameter in such a way that the usual NLS \
parameter will depend on the affine\\nparameter through the so-called \
Zukowsky function. In the context of the\\ndressing transformation the \
introduction of the affine parameter avoids the\\nconstruction of certain \
Riemann sheets for the usual NLS spectral parameter. In\\nthis way one \
introduces a Lax pair defined for the new spectral parameter and\\nthe \
relevant NVBC NLS $\\\\tau$ functions are obtained by the \
dressing\\ntransformation method. We construct the one and two dark-soliton \
solutions\\nexplicitly.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
