         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0906.0131", "submitter" -> "Harold Blas", "authors" -> 
            "L. F. dos Santos, H. Blas and M. J. B. F. da Silva", "title" -> 
            "Nonvanishing boundary conditions and dark solitons in the NLS \
model", "comments" -> 
            "LaTex, 7 pages, 2 figures. Poster contribution to the Fifth\n  \
International School on Field Theory and Gravitation, Cuiaba', Mato Grosso,\n \
 MT, Brasil, April 20-24 2009", "journal-ref" -> "PoS ISFTG:043,2009", "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider non-vanishing boundary conditions (NVBC) for the \
NLS model\n[6,7,27] in the context of the hybrid dressing transformation and\n\
$\\tau$-function approach. In order to write the NLS model in a suitable form \
to\ndeal with non-vanishing boundary conditions it is introduced a new \
spectral\nparameter in such a way that the usual NLS parameter will depend on \
the affine\nparameter through the so-called Zukowsky function. In the context \
of the\ndressing transformation the introduction of the affine parameter \
avoids the\nconstruction of certain Riemann sheets for the usual NLS spectral \
parameter. In\nthis way one introduces a Lax pair defined for the new \
spectral parameter and\nthe relevant NVBC NLS $\\tau$ functions are obtained \
by the dressing\ntransformation method. We construct the one and two \
dark-soliton solutions\nexplicitly.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 31 May 2009 03:20:33 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-06-09", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Santos", "L. F. dos", ""}, {
              "Blas", "H.", ""}, {"da Silva", "M. J. B. F.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
