 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We localize the four-dimensional N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory on a four-sphere\\nto the two-dimensional constrained \
Hitchin/Higgs-Yang-Mills (cHYM) theory on a\\ntwo-sphere S^2. We show that \
expectation values of certain 1/8 BPS\\nsupersymmetric Wilson loops on S^2 in \
the 4d N=4 SYM is captured by the 2d cHYM\\ntheory. We further argue that \
expectation values of Wilson loops in the cHYM\\ntheory agree with the \
prescription \\\"two-dimensional bosonic Yang-Mills\\nexcluding instanton \
contributions\\\". Hence, we support the recent conjecture by\\nDrukker, \
Giombi, Ricci and Trancanelli on the 1/8 BPS Wilson loops on S^2 in\\nthe 4d \
N=4 SYM.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
