            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We propose that, in N=4 Super Yang-Mills theory, correlation \
functions of\ncertain 1/8 BPS Wilson loops and local operators inserted on a \
S^2 in\nspace-time may be computed in terms of analogous observables in the\n\
\"zero-instanton\" sector of 2d Yang-Mills theory. The Wilson loops are \
mapped to\nthe standard Wilson loops of the 2d theory, as recently \
conjectured, while the\nlocal operators are mapped to powers of the 2d field \
strength. We give several\nperturbative checks of the correspondence, and \
derive from 2d Yang-Mills a\ntwo-matrix model for the correlator of a local \
operator and a Wilson loop of\narbitrary shape. We show that the strong \
coupling planar limit of the\ntwo-matrix model precisely agrees with a string \
theory calculation in AdS_5 x\nS^5.\n", 
