            "  Recently a set of functional equations defining the anomalous \
dimensions of\narbitrary local single trace operators in planar N=4 \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills\ntheory has been conjectured. These functional \
equations take the form of a\nY-system defined on a special shaped domain. \
This Y-system can be equivalently\nreformulated as a T-system defined on a \
\"T-shaped fat hook\". The elements of\nthe T-system satisfy discrete Hirota \
equations. In the present paper the\ndiscrete Hirota equations for AdS/CFT \
are solved by means of a chain of\nBacklund transformations and as a result \
TT-, TQ-, and QQ-relations are\nobtained for AdS/CFT.\n", 
