               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Takuya Okuda\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Jaume Gomis and Takuya Okuda\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"S-duality, 't Hooft operators and the operator product \
expansion\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages; v2: references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0909:072,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2009/09/072\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study S-duality in N=4 super Yang-Mills with an \
arbitrary gauge group by\\ndetermining the operator product expansion of the \
circular BPS Wilson and 't\\nHooft loop operators. The coefficients in the \
expansion of an 't Hooft loop\\noperator for chiral primary operators and the \
stress-energy tensor are\\ncalculated in perturbation theory using the \
quantum path-integral definition of\\nthe 't Hooft operator recently \
proposed. The corresponding operator product\\ncoefficients for the dual \
Wilson loop operator are determined in the strong\\ncoupling expansion. The \
results for the 't Hooft operator in the weak coupling\\nexpansion exactly \
reproduce those for the dual Wilson loop operator in the\\nstrong coupling \
expansion, thereby demonstrating the quantitative prediction of\\nS-duality \
for these observables.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
