               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0906.3568\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Soo-Jong Rey\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Andreas Gustavsson, Soo-Jong Rey\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Enhanced N=8 Supersymmetry of ABJM Theory on R(8) and \
R(8)/Z(2)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v1. 1+43 pages; v2. 1+47 pages, further comments and \
rewritings at\\n  various places\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The ABJM theory refers to superconformal \
Chern-Simons-matter theory with\\nproduct gauge group U(L)xU(R) and level +k, \
-k, respectively. The theory is a\\ncandidate for worldvolume dynamics of \
M2-branes sitting at C(4)/Z(k)k. By\\nutilizing monopole operators, we prove \
that ABJM theory gets enhanced N=8\\nsupersymmetry and SO(8) R-symmetry at \
Chern-Simons levels k=1,2. We first show\\nthat the ABJM Lagrangian can be \
written in a manifestly SO(8) invariant form up\\nto certain extra terms. We \
then show that upon integrating out Chern-Simons\\ngauge fields these extra \
terms vanish precisely at levels k=1,2. Utilizing\\nmonopole operators at \
these levels, we identify new N=2 supersymmetry. We\\ndemonstrate that they \
combine with the manifest N=6 supersymmetry to close\\non-shell on N=8 \
supersymmetry. We finally show that the ABJM scalar potential\\nis SO(8) \
invariant.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
