            "  The ABJM theory refers to superconformal Chern-Simons-matter \
theory with\nproduct gauge group U(L)xU(R) and level +k, -k, respectively. \
The theory is a\ncandidate for worldvolume dynamics of M2-branes sitting at \
C(4)/Z(k)k. By\nutilizing monopole operators, we prove that ABJM theory gets \
enhanced N=8\nsupersymmetry and SO(8) R-symmetry at Chern-Simons levels \
k=1,2. We first show\nthat the ABJM Lagrangian can be written in a manifestly \
SO(8) invariant form up\nto certain extra terms. We then show that upon \
integrating out Chern-Simons\ngauge fields these extra terms vanish precisely \
at levels k=1,2. Utilizing\nmonopole operators at these levels, we identify \
new N=2 supersymmetry. We\ndemonstrate that they combine with the manifest \
N=6 supersymmetry to close\non-shell on N=8 supersymmetry. We finally show \
that the ABJM scalar potential\nis SO(8) invariant.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
