 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the perturbative five loop anomalous \
dimension of the Konishi\\noperator in N = 4 SYM theory from the integrable \
string sigma model by\\nevaluating finite size effects using Luscher formulas \
adapted to multimagnon\\nstates at weak coupling. In addition, we derive the \
five loop wrapping\\ncontribution for the L=2 single impurity state in the \
beta deformed theory,\\nwhich may be within reach of a direct perturbative \
computation. The Konishi\\nexpression exhibits two new features - a \
modification of Asymptotic Bethe\\nAnsatz quantization and sensitiveness to \
an infinite set of coefficients of the\\nBES/BHL dressing phase. The result \
satisfies nontrivial self-consistency\\nconditions - simple transcendentality \
structure and cancellation of mu-term\\npoles. It may be a testing ground for \
the proposed AdS/CFT TBA systems.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
