               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Radu Roiban\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"R. Roiban, A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum strings in AdS_5 x S^5: strong-coupling \
corrections to dimension\\n  of Konishi operator\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages, Latex v2: minor comments added, misprints \
corrected v3:\\n  misprint corrected v4: misprints corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0911:013,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2009/11/013\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"IMPERIAL-TP-AT-2009-3\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider leading strong coupling corrections to the \
energy of the lightest\\nmassive string modes in AdS_5 x S^5, which should be \
dual to members of the\\nKonishi operator multiplet in N=4 SYM theory. This \
determines the general\\nstructure of the strong-coupling expansion of the \
anomalous dimension of the\\nKonishi operator. We use 1-loop results for \
several semiclassical string states\\nto extract information about the \
leading coefficients in this expansion. Our\\nprediction is\\n  Delta= 2 \
lambda^{1/4} + b_0 + b_1 lambda^{-1/4} + b_3 lambda^{-3/4} +...,\\nwhere b_0 \
and b_1 are rational while b_3 is transcendental containing \
zeta(3).\\nExplicitly, we argue that b_0= Delta_0 - 4 (where Delta_0 is the \
canonical\\ndimension of the corresponding gauge-theory operator in the \
Konishi multiplet)\\nand b_1=1. Our conclusions are sensitive to few \
assumptions, implied by a\\ncorrespondence with flat-space expressions, on \
how to translate semiclassical\\nquantization results into predictions for \
the exact quantum string spectrum.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
