            "  We consider leading strong coupling corrections to the energy \
of the lightest\nmassive string modes in AdS_5 x S^5, which should be dual to \
members of the\nKonishi operator multiplet in N=4 SYM theory. This determines \
the general\nstructure of the strong-coupling expansion of the anomalous \
dimension of the\nKonishi operator. We use 1-loop results for several \
semiclassical string states\nto extract information about the leading \
coefficients in this expansion. Our\nprediction is\n  Delta= 2 lambda^{1/4} + \
b_0 + b_1 lambda^{-1/4} + b_3 lambda^{-3/4} +...,\nwhere b_0 and b_1 are \
rational while b_3 is transcendental containing zeta(3).\nExplicitly, we \
argue that b_0= Delta_0 - 4 (where Delta_0 is the canonical\ndimension of the \
corresponding gauge-theory operator in the Konishi multiplet)\nand b_1=1. Our \
conclusions are sensitive to few assumptions, implied by a\ncorrespondence \
with flat-space expressions, on how to translate semiclassical\nquantization \
results into predictions for the exact quantum string spectrum.\n", 
