                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Type IIA superstring action on the AdS_4 x CP^3 \
background, obtainable by\\nthe double dimensional reduction of the AdS_4 x \
S^7 supermembrane, is\\nconsidered in the kappa-symmetry light-cone gauge, in \
which the light-like\\ndirections are chosen on the D=3 Minkowski boundary of \
AdS_4. Such choice of\\nthe gauge condition relies on representing the AdS_4 \
x S^7 background isometry\\nsuperalgebra osp(4|8) (and correspondingly the \
osp(4|6) isometry superalgebra\\nof the AdS_4 x CP^3 background) as D=3 \
extended superconformal algebra. The\\ngauge-fixed action includes \
contributions up to the 4th power in the fermions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
