Sully\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holography from Conformal Field Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"49 pages. Minor corrections. Figure and references \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0910:079,2009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2009/10/079\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NSF-KITP-09-110\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The locality of bulk physics at distances below the AdS \
length is one of the\\nremarkable aspects of AdS/CFT duality, and one of the \
least tested. It requires\\nthat the AdS radius be large compared to the \
Planck length and the string\\nlength. In the CFT this implies a large-N \
expansion and a gap in the spectum of\\nanomalous dimensions. We conjecture \
that the implication also runs in the other\\ndirection, so that any CFT with \
a planar expansion and a large gap has a local\\nbulk dual. For an abstract \
CFT we formulate the consistency conditions, most\\nnotably crossing \
symmetry, and show that the conjecture is true in a broad\\nrange of CFT's, \
to first nontrivial order in 1/N^2: any CFT with a gap and a\\nplanar \
expansion is generated via the AdS/CFT dictionary from a local \
bulk\\ninteraction. We establish this result by a counting argument on each \
side, and\\nalso investigate various properties of some explicit \
solutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 1 Jul 2009 19:57:13 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 11 Aug 2009 21:07:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 5 Oct 2009 17:00:50 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-13\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Heemskerk\"", ",", "\"Idse\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Penedones\"", ",", "\"Joao\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Polchinski\"", ",", "\"Joseph\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sully\"", ",", "\"James\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
