         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0907.0151", "submitter" -> "Joao Penedones", "authors" -> 
            "Idse Heemskerk, Joao Penedones, Joseph Polchinski, James Sully", 
            "title" -> "Holography from Conformal Field Theory", "comments" -> 
            "49 pages. Minor corrections. Figure and references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0910:079,2009", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2009/10/079", "report-no" -> "NSF-KITP-09-110",
             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The locality of bulk physics at distances below the AdS length \
is one of the\nremarkable aspects of AdS/CFT duality, and one of the least \
tested. It requires\nthat the AdS radius be large compared to the Planck \
length and the string\nlength. In the CFT this implies a large-N expansion \
and a gap in the spectum of\nanomalous dimensions. We conjecture that the \
implication also runs in the other\ndirection, so that any CFT with a planar \
expansion and a large gap has a local\nbulk dual. For an abstract CFT we \
formulate the consistency conditions, most\nnotably crossing symmetry, and \
show that the conjecture is true in a broad\nrange of CFT's, to first \
nontrivial order in 1/N^2: any CFT with a gap and a\nplanar expansion is \
generated via the AdS/CFT dictionary from a local bulk\ninteraction. We \
establish this result by a counting argument on each side, and\nalso \
investigate various properties of some explicit solutions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 1 Jul 2009 19:57:13 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 11 Aug 2009 21:07:00 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 5 Oct 2009 17:00:50 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-13", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Heemskerk", "Idse", ""}, {
              "Penedones", "Joao", ""}, {"Polchinski", "Joseph", ""}, {
              "Sully", "James", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
