            "Renormalization of Twist-Four Operators in QCD", "comments" -> 
            "64 pages", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B826:235-293,2010", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2009.10.005", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-ph hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Extending the work by Bukhvostov, Frolov, Lipatov and Kuraev \
(BFLK) on the\nrenormalization of quasipartonic operators we derive a \
complete set of\ntwo-particle renormalization group kernels that enter QCD \
evolution equations\nto twist-four accuracy. It is shown that the 2->2 \
evolution kernels which\ninvolve ``non-partonic'' components of field \
operators, and, most remarkably,\nalso 2->3 kernels do not require \
independent calculation and can be restored\nfrom the known results for \
quasipartonic operators using conformal symmetry and\nLorentz \
transformations. The kernels are presented for the renormalization of\n\
light-ray operators built of chiral fields in a particular basis such that \
the\nconformal symmetry is manifest. The results can easily be recast in \
momentum\nspace, in the form of evolution equations for generalized parton \
distributions.\n", 
