               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Christoph Sieg\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.A. Minahan, O. Ohlsson Sax, C. Sieg\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Magnon dispersion to four loops in the ABJM and ABJ \
models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX, feynmp, 17 pages; v2: coupling factor in one \
Feynman diagram\\n  corrected: modified result in the ABJ case only, \
formulations improved, typos\\n  fixed, references added; v3: signs of three \
diagrams corrected, modifying the\\n  final result\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A43:275402,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/43/27/275402\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UUITP-20/09\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The ABJM model is a superconformal Chern-Simons theory \
with N=6 supersymmetry\\nwhich is believed to be integrable in the planar \
limit. However, there is a\\ncoupling dependent function that appears in the \
magnon dispersion relation and\\nthe asymptotic Bethe ansatz that is only \
known to leading order at strong and\\nweak coupling. We compute this \
function to four loops in perturbation theory by\\nan explicit Feynman \
diagram calculation for both the ABJM model and the ABJ\\nextension. We find \
that all coefficients have maximal transcendentality. We\\nthen compute the \
four-loop wrapping correction for a scalar operator in the 20\\nof SU(4) and \
find that it agrees with a recent prediction from the ABJM\\nY-system of \
Gromov, Kazakov and Vieira. We also propose a limit of the ABJ\\nmodel that \
might be perturbatively integrable at all loop orders but has a\\nshort range \
Hamiltonian.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
