            "  The ABJM model is a superconformal Chern-Simons theory with \
N=6 supersymmetry\nwhich is believed to be integrable in the planar limit. \
However, there is a\ncoupling dependent function that appears in the magnon \
dispersion relation and\nthe asymptotic Bethe ansatz that is only known to \
leading order at strong and\nweak coupling. We compute this function to four \
loops in perturbation theory by\nan explicit Feynman diagram calculation for \
both the ABJM model and the ABJ\nextension. We find that all coefficients \
have maximal transcendentality. We\nthen compute the four-loop wrapping \
correction for a scalar operator in the 20\nof SU(4) and find that it agrees \
with a recent prediction from the ABJM\nY-system of Gromov, Kazakov and \
Vieira. We also propose a limit of the ABJ\nmodel that might be \
perturbatively integrable at all loop orders but has a\nshort range \
Hamiltonian.\n", 
