               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Per Sundin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the worldsheet theory of the type IIA AdS(4) x CP(3) \
superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages, 2 figures. v3: Minor clarifications made and \
reference list\\n  updated. Published version.\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1004:014,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2010)014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-EP-09/41\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We perform a detailed study of the type IIA superstring \
in AdS(4) x CP(3).\\nAfter introducing suitable bosonic light-cone and \
fermionic kappa worldsheet\\ngauges we derive the pure boson and fermion \
SU(2|2) x U(1) covariant light-cone\\nHamiltonian up to quartic order in \
fields.\\n  As a first application of our derivation we calculate energy \
shifts for\\nstring configurations in a closed fermionic subsector and \
successfully match\\nthese with a set of light-cone Bethe equations. We then \
turn to investigate the\\nmismatch between the degrees of freedom of \
scattering states and oscillatory\\nstring modes. Since only light string \
modes appear as fundamental Bethe roots\\nin the scattering theory, the \
physical role of the remaining $4_F+4_B$ massive\\noscillators is rather \
unclear. By continuing a line of research initiated by\\nZarembo, we shed \
light on this question by calculating quantum corrections for\\nthe \
propagators of the bosonic massive fields. We show that, once \
loop\\ncorrections are incorporated, the massive coordinates dissolve in a \
continuum\\nstate of two light particles.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 3 Sep 2009 16:08:15 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 4 Sep 2009 16:44:31 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 19 Mar 2010 11:49:40 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2014-11-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sundin\"", ",", "\"Per\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
