           "id" -> "0909.0697", "submitter" -> "Per Sundin", "authors" -> 
            "Per Sundin", "title" -> 
            "On the worldsheet theory of the type IIA AdS(4) x CP(3) \
superstring", "comments" -> 
            "40 pages, 2 figures. v3: Minor clarifications made and reference \
list\n  updated. Published version.", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1004:014,2010", 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP04(2010)014", "report-no" -> "HU-EP-09/41", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We perform a detailed study of the type IIA superstring in \
AdS(4) x CP(3).\nAfter introducing suitable bosonic light-cone and fermionic \
kappa worldsheet\ngauges we derive the pure boson and fermion SU(2|2) x U(1) \
covariant light-cone\nHamiltonian up to quartic order in fields.\n  As a \
first application of our derivation we calculate energy shifts for\nstring \
configurations in a closed fermionic subsector and successfully match\nthese \
with a set of light-cone Bethe equations. We then turn to investigate the\n\
mismatch between the degrees of freedom of scattering states and oscillatory\n\
string modes. Since only light string modes appear as fundamental Bethe roots\
\nin the scattering theory, the physical role of the remaining $4_F+4_B$ \
massive\noscillators is rather unclear. By continuing a line of research \
initiated by\nZarembo, we shed light on this question by calculating quantum \
corrections for\nthe propagators of the bosonic massive fields. We show that, \
once loop\ncorrections are incorporated, the massive coordinates dissolve in \
a continuum\nstate of two light particles.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 3 Sep 2009 16:08:15 GMT"}, {
