               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bulk viscosities of a cold relativistic superfluid: \
color-flavor locked\\n  quark matter\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"13 pages, 1 figure, minor changes, references \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D81:043002,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.81.043002\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-ph astro-ph.SR hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the phonon contribution to the bulk \
viscosities $\\\\zeta_1,\\n\\\\zeta_2$ and $\\\\zeta_3$ of a cold \
relativistic superfluid. We assume the low\\ntemperature $T$ regime and that \
the transport properties of the system are\\ndominated by the phonons. We use \
kinetic theory in the relaxation time\\napproximation and the low energy \
effective field theory of the corresponding\\nsystem. The parametric \
dependence of the bulk viscosity coefficients is fixed\\nonce the equation of \
state is specified, and the phonon dispersion law to cubic\\norder in \
momentum is known. We first present a general discussion, valid for\\nany \
superfluid, then we focus on the color-flavor locked superfluid because \
all\\nthe parameters needed in the analysis can be computed in the high \
density limit\\nof QCD, and also because of the possible astrophysical \
applications. For the\\nthree independent bulk viscosity coefficients we find \
that they scale with the\\ntemperature as $\\\\zeta_i \\\\sim 1/T$, and that \
in the conformal limit only the\\nthird coefficient $\\\\zeta_3$ is non-zero.\
\\n\""}]}, {
