         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0909.4486", "submitter" -> "Massimo Mannarelli", 
            "authors" -> "Massimo Mannarelli, Cristina Manuel", "title" -> 
            "Bulk viscosities of a cold relativistic superfluid: color-flavor \
locked\n  quark matter", "comments" -> 
            "13 pages, 1 figure, minor changes, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D81:043002,2010", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.81.043002", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-ph astro-ph.SR hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the phonon contribution to the bulk viscosities \
$\\zeta_1,\n\\zeta_2$ and $\\zeta_3$ of a cold relativistic superfluid. We \
assume the low\ntemperature $T$ regime and that the transport properties of \
the system are\ndominated by the phonons. We use kinetic theory in the \
relaxation time\napproximation and the low energy effective field theory of \
the corresponding\nsystem. The parametric dependence of the bulk viscosity \
coefficients is fixed\nonce the equation of state is specified, and the \
phonon dispersion law to cubic\norder in momentum is known. We first present \
a general discussion, valid for\nany superfluid, then we focus on the \
color-flavor locked superfluid because all\nthe parameters needed in the \
analysis can be computed in the high density limit\nof QCD, and also because \
of the possible astrophysical applications. For the\nthree independent bulk \
viscosity coefficients we find that they scale with the\ntemperature as \
$\\zeta_i \\sim 1/T$, and that in the conformal limit only the\nthird \
coefficient $\\zeta_3$ is non-zero.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 24 Sep 2009 16:09:10 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 15 Jan 2010 13:49:59 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-04-06", 
