            "  We show how Newtonian gravity emerges on 4-dimensional \
non-commutative\nspacetime branes in Yang-Mills matrix models. Large matter \
clusters such as\ngalaxies are embedded in large-scale harmonic deformations \
of the space-time\nbrane, which screen gravity for long distances. On shorter \
scales, the local\nmatter distribution reproduces Newtonian gravity via local \
deformations of the\nbrane and its metric. The harmonic ``gravity bag'' acts \
as a halo with\neffective positive energy density. This leads in particular \
to a significant\nenhancement of the orbital velocities around galaxies at \
large distances\ncompared with the Newtonian case, before dropping to zero as \
the geometry\nmerges with a Milne-like cosmology. Besides these ``harmonic'' \
solutions, there\nis another class of solutions which is more similar to \
Einstein gravity. Thus\nthe IKKT model provides an accessible candidate for a \
quantum theory of\ngravity.\n", 
