            "nucl-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate the kaonic contribution to the shear viscosity of \
quark matter\nin the kaon-condensed color-flavor locked phase (CFL-K0). This \
contribution\ncomes from a light pseudo-Goldstone boson which arises from the \
spontaneous\nbreaking of the flavor symmetry by the kaon condensate. The \
other contribution,\nfrom the exactly massless superfluid 'phonon\", has been \
calculated previously.\nWe specialize to a particular form of the interaction \
lagrangian, parameterized\nby a single coupling. We find that if we make \
reasonable guesses for the values\nof the parameters of the effective theory, \
the kaons have a much smaller shear\nviscosity than the superfluid phonons, \
but also a much shorter mean free path,\nso they could easily provide the \
dominant contribution to the shear viscosity\nof CFL-K0 quark matter in a \
neutron star in the temperature range 0.01 to 1 MeV\n(10^8 to 10^10 K).\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
