                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently Kazakov, Vieira and the author conjectured the \
Y-system set of\\nequations describing the planar spectrum of AdS/CFT. In \
this paper we solve the\\nY-system equations in the strong coupling scaling \
limit. We show that the\\nquasi-classical spectrum of string moving inside \
AdS3 x S1 matches precisely\\nwith the prediction of the Y-system. Thus the \
Y-system, unlike the asymptotic\\nBethe ansatz, describes correctly the \
spectrum of one-loop string energies\\nincluding all exponential finite size \
corrections. This gives a very\\nnon-trivial further support in favor of the \
conjecture.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
