               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0910.5158\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Axel de Goursac\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Axel de Goursac\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Noncommutative geometry, gauge theory and renormalization\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"159 pages, 14 figures, PhD thesis, v2: revised \
version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Verlag Dr Muller (2010)\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph hep-th math.MP math.OA math.QA math.RA\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Nowadays, noncommutative geometry is a growing domain \
of mathematics, which\\ncan appear as a promising framework for modern \
physics. Quantum field theories\\non \\\"noncommutative spaces\\\" are indeed \
much investigated, and suffer from a new\\ntype of divergence called the \
ultraviolet-infrared mixing. However, this\\nproblem has recently been solved \
by H. Grosse and R. Wulkenhaar by adding to\\nthe action of a noncommutative \
scalar model a harmonic term, which renders it\\nrenormalizable.\\n  One aim \
of this thesis is the extension of this procedure to gauge theories\\non the \
Moyal space. Indeed, we have introduced a new noncommutative gauge\\ntheory, \
strongly related to the Grosse-Wulkenhaar model, and candidate \
to\\nrenormalizability. We have then studied the most important properties of \
this\\naction, and in particular its vacuum configurations. Finally, we give \
a\\nmathematical interpretation of this new action in terms of a \
derivation-based\\ndifferential calculus associated to a superalgebra.\\n  \
This work contains among the results of this PhD, an introduction \
to\\nnoncommutative geometry, an introduction to epsilon-graded algebras, and \
an\\nintroduction to renormalization of scalar (wilsonian and BPHZ point of \
view)\\nand gauge quantum field theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 27 Oct 2009 16:19:16 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 8 Jul 2010 10:41:01 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-08-22\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"de Goursac\"", ",", "\"Axel\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
