               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Dongsu Bak, Hyunsoo Min, Soo-Jong Rey\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrability of N=6 Chern-Simons Theory at Six Loops and \
Beyond\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+39 pages, 12 figures, references added, minor \
structural changes,\\n  typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D81:126004,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.81.126004\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study issues concerning perturbative integrability \
of N=6 Chern-Simons\\ntheory at planar and weak `t Hooft coupling regime. By \
Feynman diagrammatics,\\nwe derive so called maximal-ranged interactions in \
the quantum dilatation\\ngenerator, originating from homogeneous and \
inhomogeneous diagrams. These\\ndiagrams require proper regularization of not \
only ultraviolet but also\\ninfrared divergences. We first consider standard \
operator mixing method. We\\nshow that homogeneous diagrams are obtainable by \
recursive method to all\\norders. The method, however, is not easily \
extendable to inhomogeneous\\ndiagrams. We thus consider two-point function \
method and study both operator\\ncontents and spectrum of the quantum \
dilatation generator up to six loop\\norders. We show that, of two possible \
classes of operators, only one linear\\ncombination actually contributes. \
Curiously, this is exactly the same\\ncombination as in N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory. We then study spectrum of\\nanomalous dimension up to six loops. We \
find that the spectrum agrees perfectly\\nwith the prediction based on \
quantum integrability. In evaluating the six loop\\ndiagrams, we utilized \
remarkable integer-relation algorithm (PSLQ) developed by\\nFerguson, Baily \
and Arno.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
