            "1+39 pages, 12 figures, references added, minor structural \
changes,\n  typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D81:126004,2010", 
            "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.81.126004", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study issues concerning perturbative integrability of N=6 \
Chern-Simons\ntheory at planar and weak `t Hooft coupling regime. By Feynman \
diagrammatics,\nwe derive so called maximal-ranged interactions in the \
quantum dilatation\ngenerator, originating from homogeneous and inhomogeneous \
diagrams. These\ndiagrams require proper regularization of not only \
ultraviolet but also\ninfrared divergences. We first consider standard \
operator mixing method. We\nshow that homogeneous diagrams are obtainable by \
recursive method to all\norders. The method, however, is not easily \
extendable to inhomogeneous\ndiagrams. We thus consider two-point function \
method and study both operator\ncontents and spectrum of the quantum \
dilatation generator up to six loop\norders. We show that, of two possible \
classes of operators, only one linear\ncombination actually contributes. \
Curiously, this is exactly the same\ncombination as in N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory. We then study spectrum of\nanomalous dimension up to six loops. We \
find that the spectrum agrees perfectly\nwith the prediction based on quantum \
integrability. In evaluating the six loop\ndiagrams, we utilized remarkable \
integer-relation algorithm (PSLQ) developed by\nFerguson, Baily and Arno.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
