 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the spectrum around the \
\\\"antiferromagnetic\\\" states of the planar\\nAdS_5/CFT_4 duality. In \
contrast to the familiar large-spin limit J \\\\to \\\\infty\\nwhere each \
magnon momentum scales as p \\\\sim 1/J << 1, we consider a \
novel\\n\\\"large-winding\\\" limit in which the total momentum becomes \
infinitely large,\\n\\\\sum_j p_j \\\\to \\\\infty. Upon taking the limit we \
identify \\\"spinon\\\" excitations\\nof both gauge and string theories. In \
particular, a (classical) string spinon\\nturns out to be an infinite set of \
spiky strings, which are closely related to\\nwell-known infinite-spin \
strings: giant magnons. Furthermore, we show that the\\ncurious agreement of \
scattering phase-shifts of two spikes and that of two\\ngiant magnons can be \
accounted for by regarding the spinon scattering as\\nfactorised scatterings \
of infinitely many magnons.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
