                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the spectrum of anomalous dimensions of short \
operators in planar\\nABJM theory at two loops. Specifically we develop a \
method for solving the\\nOSp(6|4) Bethe ansatz equations for a certain class \
of unpaired length-4 states\\nwith arbitrarily high number of excitations, \
and apply it to identify three new\\nsequences of rational eigenvalues. \
Results for low-lying paired states in the\\nOSp(4|2) sector are obtained by \
direct diagonalization of the spin chain\\nHamiltonian. We also study the \
SL(2|1) sector and identify the set of states\\nthat corresponds to the \
SL(2)-like Bethe ansatz of Gromov and Vieira. Finally\\nwe extend part of our \
analysis to length-6 operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
