                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study various methods for computing the one-loop \
correction to the energy\\nof classical solutions to type IIA string theory \
in AdS4 x CP3. This involves\\ncomputing the spectrum of fluctuations and \
then adding up the fluctuation\\nfrequencies. We focus on two classical \
solutions with support in CP3: a\\nrotating point-particle and a circular \
spinning string with two angular momenta\\nequal to J. For each of these \
solutions, we compute the spectrum of\\nfluctuations using two techniques, \
known as the algebraic curve approach and\\nthe world-sheet approach. If we \
use the same prescription for adding\\nfluctuation frequencies that was used \
for type IIB string theory in AdS5 x S5,\\nthen we find that the world-sheet \
spectrum gives convergent one-loop\\ncorrections but the algebraic curve \
spectrum gives divergent ones. On the other\\nhand, we find a new summation \
prescription which gives finite results when\\napplied to both the algebraic \
curve and world-sheet spectra. Naively, this\\ngives three predictions for \
the one-loop correction to the spinning string\\nenergy (one from the \
algebraic curve and two from the world-sheet), however we\\nfind that in the \
large-j limit (where j=J/sqrt(2pi^2 lambda)), the j^(-2n)\\nterms in all \
three cases agree. We therefore obtain a unique prediction for the\\none-loop \
correction to the spinning string energy.\\n\""}]}, {
