               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nested algebraic Bethe ansatz for open GL(N) spin chains \
with projected\\n  K-matrices\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"27 pages; v2: minor change; v3: references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2010.01.006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UMTG-265\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider an open spin chain model with GL(N) bulk \
symmetry that is broken\\nto GL(M) x GL(N-M) by the boundary, which is a \
generalization of a model\\narising in string/gauge theory. We prove the \
integrability of this model by\\nconstructing the corresponding commuting \
transfer matrix. This construction\\nuses operator-valued \\\"projected\\\" \
K-matrices. We solve this model for general\\nvalues of N and M using the \
nested algebraic Bethe ansatz approach, despite the\\nfact that the \
K-matrices are not diagonal. The key to obtaining this solution\\nis an \
identity based on a certain factorization property of the \
reduced\\nK-matrices into products of R-matrices. Numerical evidence suggests \
that the\\nsolution is complete.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
