            "  We consider an open spin chain model with GL(N) bulk symmetry \
that is broken\nto GL(M) x GL(N-M) by the boundary, which is a generalization \
of a model\narising in string/gauge theory. We prove the integrability of \
this model by\nconstructing the corresponding commuting transfer matrix. This \
construction\nuses operator-valued \"projected\" K-matrices. We solve this \
model for general\nvalues of N and M using the nested algebraic Bethe ansatz \
approach, despite the\nfact that the K-matrices are not diagonal. The key to \
obtaining this solution\nis an identity based on a certain factorization \
property of the reduced\nK-matrices into products of R-matrices. Numerical \
evidence suggests that the\nsolution is complete.\n", 
