             "hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We investigate the AdS(3)/CFT(2) correspondence for theories \
with 16\nsupercharges using the integrability approach. We construct \
Green-Schwarz\nactions for Type IIB strings on AdS(3)xS(3)xM(4) where \
M(4)=T(4) or S(3)xS(1)\nusing the coset approach. These actions are based on \
a Z(4) automorphism of the\nsuper-coset \
D(2,1;alpha)xD(2,1;alpha)/SO(1,2)xSO(3)xSO(3). The equations of\nmotion admit \
a representation in terms of a Lax connection, showing that the\nsystem is \
classically integrable. We present the finite gap equations for these\n\
actions. When alpha=0,1/2,1 we propose a set of quantum Bethe equations valid\
\nat all values of the coupling. The AdS(3)/CFT(2) duals contain novel \
massless\nmodes whose role remains to be explored.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
