 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the Wilson loop operator of N=6 super \
Chern-Simons-matter which\\nis invariant under half of the supercharges of \
the theory and is dual to the\\nsimplest macroscopic open string in AdS_4 x \
CP^3. The Wilson loop couples, in\\naddition to the gauge and scalar fields \
of the theory, also to the fermions in\\nthe bi-fundamental representation of \
the U(N) x U(M) gauge group. These\\ningredients are naturally combined into \
a superconnection whose holonomy gives\\nthe Wilson loop, which can be \
defined for any representation of the supergroup\\nU(N|M). Explicit \
expressions for loops supported along an infinite straight\\nline and along a \
circle are presented. Using the localization calculation of\\nKapustin et al. \
we show that the circular loop is computed by a supermatrix\\nmodel and \
discuss the connection to pure Chern-Simons theory with \
supergroup\\nU(N|M).\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
