               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exact Results in ABJM Theory from Topological \
Strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages, two figures, small misprints corrected and \
references\\n  added, final version to appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1006:011,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2010)011\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, Kapustin, Willett and Yaakov have found, by \
using localization\\ntechniques, that vacuum expectation values of Wilson \
loops in ABJM theory can\\nbe calculated with a matrix model. We show that \
this matrix model is closely\\nrelated to Chern-Simons theory on a lens space \
with a gauge supergroup. This\\ntheory has a topological string large N dual, \
and this makes possible to solve\\nthe matrix model exactly in the large N \
expansion. In particular, we find the\\nexact expression for the vacuum \
expectation value of a 1/6 BPS Wilson loop in\\nthe ABJM theory, as a \
function of the 't Hooft parameters, and in the planar\\nlimit. This \
expression gives an exact interpolating function between the weak\\nand the \
strong coupling regimes. The behavior at strong coupling is in \
precise\\nagreement with the prediction of the AdS string dual. We also give \
explicit\\nresults for the 1/2 BPS Wilson loop recently constructed by \
Drukker and\\nTrancanelli\\n\""}]}, {
