            "  Recently, Kapustin, Willett and Yaakov have found, by using \
localization\ntechniques, that vacuum expectation values of Wilson loops in \
ABJM theory can\nbe calculated with a matrix model. We show that this matrix \
model is closely\nrelated to Chern-Simons theory on a lens space with a gauge \
supergroup. This\ntheory has a topological string large N dual, and this \
makes possible to solve\nthe matrix model exactly in the large N expansion. \
In particular, we find the\nexact expression for the vacuum expectation value \
of a 1/6 BPS Wilson loop in\nthe ABJM theory, as a function of the 't Hooft \
parameters, and in the planar\nlimit. This expression gives an exact \
interpolating function between the weak\nand the strong coupling regimes. The \
behavior at strong coupling is in precise\nagreement with the prediction of \
the AdS string dual. We also give explicit\nresults for the 1/2 BPS Wilson \
loop recently constructed by Drukker and\nTrancanelli\n", 
