 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a four parameter family of classical string \
solutions in AdS_3 x\\nS^3, which end along a light-like tetragon at the \
boundary of AdS_3 and carry\\nangular momentum along two cycles on the \
sphere. The string surfaces are\\nspace-like and their projections on AdS_3 \
and on S^3 have constant mean\\ncurvature. The construction is based on the \
Pohlmeyer reduction of the related\\nsigma model. After embedding in AdS_5 x \
S^5, we calculate the regularized area\\nand analyze conserved charges. \
Comments on possible relations to scattering\\namplitudes are presented. We \
also sketch time-like versions of our solutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
