               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0912.4282\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Massimo Siani\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marco S. Bianchi, Silvia Penati, Massimo Siani\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Infrared Stability of N=2 Chern-Simons Matter \
Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+30 pages, 8 figures; v2: references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1005:106,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2010)106\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  According to the AdS4/CFT3 correspondence, N=2 \
supersymmetric Chern-Simons\\nmatter theories should have a stable fixed \
point in the infrared. In order to\\nsupport this prediction we study RG \
flows of two-level Chern-Simons matter\\ntheories with/without flavors \
induced by the most general marginal\\nsuperpotential compatible with N=2 \
supersymmetry. At two loops we determine the\\ncomplete spectrum of fixed \
points and study their IR stability. Our analysis\\ncovers a large class of \
models including perturbations of the ABJM/ABJ theories\\nwith and without \
flavors, N=2,3 theories with different CS levels corresponding\\nto turning \
on a Romans mass and beta-deformations. In all cases we find curves\\n(or \
surfaces) of fixed points which are globally IR stable but locally \
unstable\\nin the following sense: The system has only one direction of \
stability which in\\nthe ABJM case coincides with the maximal global symmetry \
preserving\\nperturbation, whereas along any other direction it flows to a \
different fixed\\npoint on the surface. The question of conformal invariance \
vs. finiteness is\\nalso addressed: While in general vanishing beta-functions \
imply two-loop\\nfiniteness, we find a particular set of flavored theories \
where this is no\\nlonger true.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 22 Dec 2009 13:48:31 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 4 Feb 2010 10:01:56 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2014-11-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Bianchi\"", ",", "\"Marco S.\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Penati\"", ",", "\"Silvia\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Siani\"", ",", "\"Massimo\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0912.4282", "submitter" -> "Massimo Siani", "authors" -> 
            "Marco S. Bianchi, Silvia Penati, Massimo Siani", "title" -> 
            "Infrared Stability of N=2 Chern-Simons Matter Theories", 
            "comments" -> "1+30 pages, 8 figures; v2: references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1005:106,2010", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP05(2010)106", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  According to the AdS4/CFT3 correspondence, N=2 supersymmetric \
Chern-Simons\nmatter theories should have a stable fixed point in the \
infrared. In order to\nsupport this prediction we study RG flows of two-level \
Chern-Simons matter\ntheories with/without flavors induced by the most \
general marginal\nsuperpotential compatible with N=2 supersymmetry. At two \
loops we determine the\ncomplete spectrum of fixed points and study their IR \
stability. Our analysis\ncovers a large class of models including \
perturbations of the ABJM/ABJ theories\nwith and without flavors, N=2,3 \
theories with different CS levels corresponding\nto turning on a Romans mass \
and beta-deformations. In all cases we find curves\n(or surfaces) of fixed \
points which are globally IR stable but locally unstable\nin the following \
sense: The system has only one direction of stability which in\nthe ABJM case \
coincides with the maximal global symmetry preserving\nperturbation, whereas \
along any other direction it flows to a different fixed\npoint on the \
surface. The question of conformal invariance vs. finiteness is\nalso \
addressed: While in general vanishing beta-functions imply two-loop\n\
finiteness, we find a particular set of flavored theories where this is no\n\
longer true.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 22 Dec 2009 13:48:31 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 4 Feb 2010 10:01:56 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-11-20", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Bianchi", "Marco S.", ""}, {
              "Penati", "Silvia", ""}, {"Siani", "Massimo", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
