         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "0912.4911", "submitter" -> "Fedor Levkovich-Maslyuk", 
            "authors" -> "Nikolay Gromov, Fedor Levkovich-Maslyuk", "title" -> 
            "Y-system, TBA and Quasi-Classical Strings in AdS4 x CP3", 
            "comments" -> 
            "references added + minor changes; published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1006:088,2010", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP06(2010)088", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the exact spectrum of the AdS4/CFT3 duality put \
forward by Aharony,\nBergman, Jafferis and Maldacena (ABJM). We derive \
thermodynamic Bethe ansatz\n(TBA) equations for the planar ABJM theory, \
starting from \"mirror\" asymptotic\nBethe equations which we conjecture. We \
also propose generalization of the TBA\nequations for excited states. The \
recently proposed Y-system is completely\nconsistent with the TBA equations \
for a large subsector of the theory, but\nshould be modified in general. We \
find the general asymptotic infinite length\nsolution of the Y-system, and \
also several solutions to all wrapping orders in\nthe strong coupling scaling \
limit. To make a comparison with results obtained\nfrom string theory, we \
assume that the all-loop Bethe ansatz of N.G. and P.\nVieira is the valid \
worldsheet theory description in the asymptotic regime. In\nthis case we find \
complete agreement, to all orders in wrappings, between the\nsolution of our \
Y-system and generic quasi-classical string spectrum in AdS3 x\nS.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
