         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1002.1097", "submitter" -> "Niklas Beisert", "authors" -> 
            "Niklas Beisert", "title" -> 
            "The Classical Trigonometric r-Matrix for the Quantum-Deformed \
Hubbard\n  Chain", "comments" -> 
            "41 pages, v2: minor textual improvements, references added, v3: \
minor\n  improvements, references added, change of convention \
x(v2)=h'x(v3)-ih", "journal-ref" -> "J.Phys.A44:265202,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/44/26/265202", "report-no" -> "AEI-2010-016", 
            "categories" -> "math-ph hep-th math.MP math.QA", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The one-dimensional Hubbard model is an exceptional integrable \
spin chain\nwhich is apparently based on a deformation of the Yangian for the \
superalgebra\ngl(2|2). Here we investigate the quantum-deformation of the \
Hubbard model in\nthe classical limit. This leads to a novel classical \
r-matrix of trigonometric\nkind. We derive the corresponding one-parameter \
family of Lie bialgebras as a\ndeformation of the affine gl(2|2) Kac-Moody \
superalgebra. In particular, we\ndiscuss the affine extension as well as \
discrete symmetries, and we scan for\nsimpler limiting cases, such as the \
rational r-matrix for the undeformed\nHubbard model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 5 Feb 2010 09:58:32 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 24 Feb 2010 13:11:41 GMT"}, {
