           "id" -> "1002.1831", "submitter" -> "Victor Mikhaylov", "authors" -> 
            "Victor Mikhaylov", "title" -> 
            "On the Fermionic Frequencies of Circular Strings", "comments" -> 
            "13 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> "J.Phys.A43:335401,2010", 
            "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8113/43/33/335401", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We revisit the semiclassical computation of the fluctuation \
spectrum around\ndifferent circular string solutions in AdS_5xS^5 and \
AdS_4xCP^3, starting from\nthe Green-Schwarz action. It has been known that \
the results for these\nfrequencies obtained from the algebraic curve and from \
the worldsheet\ncomputations sometimes do not agree. In particular, different \
methods give\ndifferent results for the half-integer shifts in the mode \
numbers of the\nfrequencies. We find that these discrepancies can be removed \
if one carefully\ntakes into account the transition matrices in the spin \
bundle over the target\nspace.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 9 Feb 2010 11:59:32 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-11-20", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Mikhaylov", "Victor", ""}}}],
