                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore how to compute, classically at strong \
coupling, correlation\\nfunctions of local operators corresponding to \
classical spinning string states.\\nThe picture we obtain is of `fattened' \
Witten diagrams, the evaluation of which\\nturns out to be surprisingly \
subtle and requires a modification of the naive\\nclassical action due to a \
necessary projection onto appropriate wave functions.\\nWe examine string \
solutions which compute the simplest case of a two-point\\nfunction and \
reproduce the right scaling with the anomalous dimensions\\ncorresponding to \
the energies of the associated spinning string solutions. We\\nalso describe, \
under some simplifying assumptions, how the spacetime dependence\\nof a \
conformal three-point correlation function arises in this setup.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
