                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study spiky string solutions in AdS3 x S1 that are \
characterized by two\\nspins S,J as well as winding m in S1 and spike number \
n. We construct\\nexplicitly two-cut solutions by using the SL(2) asymptotic \
Bethe Ansatz\\nequations at leading order in strong coupling. Unlike the \
folded spinning\\nstring, these solutions have asymmetric distributions of \
Bethe roots. The\\nsolutions match the known spiky string classical results \
obtained directly from\\nstring theory for arbitrary semiclassical \
parameters, including J=0 and any\\nvalue of S, namely short and long \
strings. At large spins and winding number\\nthe string touches the boundary, \
and we find a new scaling limit with the\\nenergy given as E-S = n /2/ pi \
sqrt[1+ 4 pi^2/n^2 (J^2/ln^2 S + m^2/ln^2 S)] ln\\nS. This is a \
generalization of the known scaling for the folded \
spinning\\nstring.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
