         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1002.4843", "submitter" -> "Alin Tirziu", "authors" -> 
            "M. Kruczenski, A. Tirziu", "title" -> 
            "Spiky strings in Bethe Ansatz at strong coupling", "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, 2 figures; v2: minor changes", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rev.D81:106004,2010", "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.81.106004",
             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study spiky string solutions in AdS3 x S1 that are \
characterized by two\nspins S,J as well as winding m in S1 and spike number \
n. We construct\nexplicitly two-cut solutions by using the SL(2) asymptotic \
Bethe Ansatz\nequations at leading order in strong coupling. Unlike the \
folded spinning\nstring, these solutions have asymmetric distributions of \
Bethe roots. The\nsolutions match the known spiky string classical results \
obtained directly from\nstring theory for arbitrary semiclassical parameters, \
including J=0 and any\nvalue of S, namely short and long strings. At large \
spins and winding number\nthe string touches the boundary, and we find a new \
scaling limit with the\nenergy given as E-S = n /2/ pi sqrt[1+ 4 pi^2/n^2 \
(J^2/ln^2 S + m^2/ln^2 S)] ln\nS. This is a generalization of the known \
scaling for the folded spinning\nstring.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 25 Feb 2010 18:27:38 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
