            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The classical integrable structure of Z_4-graded supercoset \
sigma-models,\narising in the AdS/CFT correspondence, is formulated within \
the R-matrix\napproach. The central object in this construction is the \
standard R-matrix of\nthe Z_4-twisted loop algebra. However, in order to \
correctly describe the Lax\nmatrix within this formalism, the standard inner \
product on this twisted loop\nalgebra requires a further twist induced by the \
Zhukovsky map, which also plays\na key role in the AdS/CFT correspondence. \
The non-ultralocality of the\nsigma-model can be understood as stemming from \
this latter twist since it leads\nto a non skew-symmetric R-matrix.\n", 
