               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"High Energy Bounds on Soft N=4 SYM Amplitudes from \
AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"25 pages, 3 eps figures\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1005:037,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2010)037\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the AdS/CFT correspondence, we study the \
high-energy behavior of\\ncolorless dipole elastic scattering amplitudes in \
N=4 SYM gauge theory through\\nthe Wilson loop correlator formalism and \
Euclidean to Minkowskian analytic\\ncontinuation. The purely elastic behavior \
obtained at large impact-parameter L,\\nthrough duality from disconnected \
AdS_5 minimal surfaces beyond the\\nGross-Ooguri transition point, is \
combined with unitarity and analyticity\\nconstraints in the central region. \
In this way we obtain an absolute bound on\\nthe high-energy behavior of the \
forward scattering amplitude due to the\\ngraviton interaction between \
minimal surfaces in the bulk. The dominant\\n\\\"Pomeron\\\" intercept is \
bounded by alpha less than or equal to 11/7 using the\\nAdS/CFT constraint of \
a weak gravitational field in the bulk. Assuming the\\nelastic eikonal \
approximation in a larger impact-parameter range gives alpha\\nbetween 4/3 \
and 11/7. The actual intercept becomes 4/3 if one assumes the\\nelastic \
eikonal approximation within its maximally allowed range L larger \
than\\nexp{Y/3}, where Y is the total rapidity. Subleading AdS/CFT \
contributions at\\nlarge impact-parameter due to the other d=10 supergravity \
fields are obtained.\\nA divergence in the real part of the tachyonic KK \
scalar is cured by\\nanalyticity but signals the need for a theoretical \
completion of the AdS/CFT\\nscheme.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
