            "  Using the AdS/CFT correspondence, we study the high-energy \
behavior of\ncolorless dipole elastic scattering amplitudes in N=4 SYM gauge \
theory through\nthe Wilson loop correlator formalism and Euclidean to \
Minkowskian analytic\ncontinuation. The purely elastic behavior obtained at \
large impact-parameter L,\nthrough duality from disconnected AdS_5 minimal \
surfaces beyond the\nGross-Ooguri transition point, is combined with \
unitarity and analyticity\nconstraints in the central region. In this way we \
obtain an absolute bound on\nthe high-energy behavior of the forward \
scattering amplitude due to the\ngraviton interaction between minimal \
surfaces in the bulk. The dominant\n\"Pomeron\" intercept is bounded by alpha \
less than or equal to 11/7 using the\nAdS/CFT constraint of a weak \
gravitational field in the bulk. Assuming the\nelastic eikonal approximation \
in a larger impact-parameter range gives alpha\nbetween 4/3 and 11/7. The \
actual intercept becomes 4/3 if one assumes the\nelastic eikonal \
approximation within its maximally allowed range L larger than\nexp{Y/3}, \
where Y is the total rapidity. Subleading AdS/CFT contributions at\nlarge \
impact-parameter due to the other d=10 supergravity fields are obtained.\nA \
divergence in the real part of the tachyonic KK scalar is cured by\n\
analyticity but signals the need for a theoretical completion of the AdS/CFT\n\
scheme.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 11 Mar 2010 11:35:16 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 15 Sep 2010 16:39:16 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-09-16", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Giordano", "Matteo", ""}, {
              "Peschanski", "Robi", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.768094787750833`, -4.746418521644594}, 0.],
