            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1003.3964\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sergei Alexandrov\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sergei Alexandrov and Philippe Roche\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"TBA for non-perturbative moduli spaces\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"25 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1006 (2010) 066\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2010)066\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"LPTA/10-020\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, an exact description of instanton corrections \
to the moduli spaces\\nof 4d N=2 supersymmetric gauge theories compactified \
on a circle and Calabi-Yau\\ncompactifications of Type II superstring \
theories was found. The equations\\ndetermining the instanton contributions \
turn out to have the form of\\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz. We explore further \
this relation and, in\\nparticular, we identify the contact potential of \
quaternionic string moduli\\nspace with the free energy of the integrable \
system and the Kahler potential of\\nthe gauge theory moduli space with the \
Yang-Yang functional. We also show that\\nthe corresponding S-matrix \
satisfies all usual constraints of 2d integrable\\nmodels, including crossing \
and bootstrap, and derive the associated Y-system.\\nSurprisingly, in the \
simplest case the Y-system is described by the MacMahon\\nfunction relevant \
for crystal melting and topological strings.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 21 Mar 2010 02:20:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2012-10-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Alexandrov\"", ",", "\"Sergei\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Roche\"", ",", "\"Philippe\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
