          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1003.3964", "submitter" -> "Sergei Alexandrov", "authors" -> 
            "Sergei Alexandrov and Philippe Roche", "title" -> 
            "TBA for non-perturbative moduli spaces", "comments" -> 
            "25 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1006 (2010) 066", 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP06(2010)066", "report-no" -> "LPTA/10-020", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently, an exact description of instanton corrections to the \
moduli spaces\nof 4d N=2 supersymmetric gauge theories compactified on a \
circle and Calabi-Yau\ncompactifications of Type II superstring theories was \
found. The equations\ndetermining the instanton contributions turn out to \
have the form of\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz. We explore further this \
relation and, in\nparticular, we identify the contact potential of \
quaternionic string moduli\nspace with the free energy of the integrable \
system and the Kahler potential of\nthe gauge theory moduli space with the \
Yang-Yang functional. We also show that\nthe corresponding S-matrix satisfies \
all usual constraints of 2d integrable\nmodels, including crossing and \
bootstrap, and derive the associated Y-system.\nSurprisingly, in the simplest \
case the Y-system is described by the MacMahon\nfunction relevant for crystal \
melting and topological strings.\n", 
