         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1003.4214", "submitter" -> "Didina Serban", "authors" -> 
            "Didina Serban", "title" -> 
            "Integrability and the AdS/CFT correspondence", "comments" -> 
            "106 pages, 9 figures, habilitation thesis; minor corrections,\n  \
published version", "journal-ref" -> "J.Phys.A44:124001,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/44/12/124001", "report-no" -> "IPhT-T10-042", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The description of gauge theories at strong coupling is one of \
the\nlong-standing problems in theoretical physics. The idea of a relation \
between\nstrongly coupled gauge theories and string theory was pioneered by \
't Hooft,\nWilson and Polyakov. A decade ago, Maldacena made this relation \
explicit by\nconjecturing the exact equivalence of a conformally invariant \
theory in four\ndimensions, the maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory, \
with string theory\nin the AdS5 x S5 background. Other examples of \
correspondence between a\nconformally invariant theory and string theory in \
an AdS background were\ndiscovered recently. The comparison of the two sides \
of the correspondence\nrequires the use of non-perturbative methods. The \
discovery of integrable\nstructures in gauge theory and string theory led to \
the conjecture that the two\ntheories are integrable for any value of the \
coupling constant and that they\nshare the same integrable structure defined \
non-perturbatively. The last eight\nyears brought remarkable progress in \
identifying this solvable model and in\nexplicitly solving the problem of \
computing the spectrum of conformal\ndimensions of the theory. The progress \
came from the identification of the\ndilatation operator with an integrable \
spin chain and from the study of the\nstring sigma model. In this thesis, I \
present the evolution of the concept of\nintegrability in the framework of \
the AdS/CFT correspondence and the the main\nresults obtained using this \
approach.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 22 Mar 2010 17:01:34 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 23 Apr 2010 09:39:23 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 13 Mar 2011 22:13:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-03-18", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Serban", "Didina", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.938518898392527`, -3.4414884812227076`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1003.4725\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dmytro Volin\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dmytro Volin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum integrability and functional equations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PhD thesis. Contains also unpublished previously results \
and\\n  introduction to the subject of integrability in terms of \
functional\\n  equations. 210 pages+references; v2: references added, typos \
corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 44 (2011) 124003\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/44/12/124003\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this thesis a general procedure to represent the \
integral Bethe Ansatz\\nequations in the form of the Reimann-Hilbert problem \
is given. This allows us\\nto study in simple way integrable spin chains in \
the thermodynamic limit. Based\\non the functional equations we give the \
procedure that allows finding the\\nsubleading orders in the solution of \
various integral equations solved to the\\nleading order by the Wiener-Hopf \
technics. The integral equations are studied\\nin the context of the AdS/CFT \
correspondence, where their solution allows\\nverification of the \
integrability conjecture up to two loops of the strong\\ncoupling expansion. \
In the context of the two-dimensional sigma models we\\nanalyze the \
large-order behavior of the asymptotic perturbative expansion.\\nObtained \
experience with the functional representation of the integral\\nequations \
allowed us also to solve explicitly the crossing equations that\\nappear in \
the AdS/CFT spectral problem.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 24 Mar 2010 19:53:58 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 28 Apr 2010 02:38:39 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-03-13\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Volin\"", ",", "\"Dmytro\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
