               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The harmonic term in the scalar field theory on the \
Moyal space removes the\\nUV-IR mixing, so that the theory is renormalizable \
to all orders. In this\\npaper, we review the three principal interpretations \
of this harmonic term: the\\nLangmann-Szabo duality, the superalgebraic \
approach and the noncommutative\\nscalar curvature interpretation. Then, we \
show some deep relationship between\\nthese interpretations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
