two-dimensional Minkowski space\\nwith Grosse-Wulkenhaar potential is \
discussed in two ways: In terms of a\\ncontinuous set of generalised \
eigenfunctions of the wave operator, and directly\\nin position space. In \
both settings, we find a new type of divergence in planar\\ngraphs. It is \
present at and above the self-dual point. This new kind of\\ndivergence might \
make the construction of a Minkowski space version of the\\nGrosse-Wulkenhaar \
model impossible.\\n\""}]}, {
