               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A limit on the ABJ model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"5 pages; Proceedings of Quantum Theory and Symmetries 6, \
(Lexington,\\n  KY, USA, July 2009); v2 Fixed one expression\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UUITP-18/10\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  There is a large amount of evidence that the ABJM model \
is integrable in the\\nplanar limit. Less clear is whether or not the ABJ \
model is integrable. Here we\\ninvestigate a limit of the ABJ model in the \
weak coupling limit where one 't\\nHooft parameter is much greater than the \
other. At the 4 loop level in the\\nSU(2) x SU(2) sector the anomalous \
dimensions of single trace operators map to\\ntwo Heisenberg spin chains with \
nearest neighbor interactions with an overall\\ncoefficient that is a \
function of one of the 't Hooft parameters. We conjecture\\nthe form of this \
function and show that is consistent with observations about\\nthe ABJ model \
concerning unitarity and parity, including strong \
coupling\\nstatements.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
