               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On semiclassical approximation for correlators of closed \
string vertex\\n  operators in AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"19 pages, 1 figure; minor corrections, references added, \
footnote\\n  below eq. (4.5) added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1008:057,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2010)057\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-AT-2010-2\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the 2-point function of string vertex \
operators representing\\nstring state with large spin in AdS_5. We compute \
this correlator in the\\nsemiclassical approximation and show that it has the \
expected (on the basis of\\nstate-operator correspondence) form of the \
strong-coupling limit of the 2-point\\nfunction of single trace minimal twist \
operators in gauge theory. The\\nsemiclassical solution representing the \
stationary point of the path integral\\nwith two vertex operator insertions \
is found to be related to the large spin\\nlimit of the folded spinning \
string solution by a euclidean continuation,\\ntransformation to Poincare \
coordinates and conformal map from cylinder to\\ncomplex plane. The role of \
the source terms coming from the vertex operator\\ninsertions is to specify \
the parameters of the solution in terms of quantum\\nnumbers (dimension and \
spin) of the corresponding string state. Understanding\\nfurther how similar \
semiclassical methods may work for 3-point functions may\\nshed light on \
strong-coupling limit of the corresponding correlators in gauge\\ntheory as \
was recently suggested by Janik et al in arXiv:1002.4613.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
