vertex\n  operators in AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "19 pages, 1 figure; minor corrections, references added, \
footnote\n  below eq. (4.5) added", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1008:057,2010", 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2010)057", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AT-2010-2", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the 2-point function of string vertex operators \
representing\nstring state with large spin in AdS_5. We compute this \
correlator in the\nsemiclassical approximation and show that it has the \
expected (on the basis of\nstate-operator correspondence) form of the \
strong-coupling limit of the 2-point\nfunction of single trace minimal twist \
operators in gauge theory. The\nsemiclassical solution representing the \
stationary point of the path integral\nwith two vertex operator insertions is \
found to be related to the large spin\nlimit of the folded spinning string \
solution by a euclidean continuation,\ntransformation to Poincare coordinates \
and conformal map from cylinder to\ncomplex plane. The role of the source \
terms coming from the vertex operator\ninsertions is to specify the \
parameters of the solution in terms of quantum\nnumbers (dimension and spin) \
of the corresponding string state. Understanding\nfurther how similar \
semiclassical methods may work for 3-point functions may\nshed light on \
strong-coupling limit of the corresponding correlators in gauge\ntheory as \
was recently suggested by Janik et al in arXiv:1002.4613.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
