               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider polygonal Wilson loops with null edges in \
conformal gauge\\ntheories. We derive an OPE-like expansion when several \
successive lines of the\\npolygon are becoming aligned. The limit corresponds \
to a collinear, or\\nmulticollinear, limit and we explain the systematics of \
all the subleading\\ncorrections, going beyond the leading terms that were \
previously considered.\\nThese subleading corrections are governed by \
excitations of high spin\\noperators, or excitations of a flux tube that goes \
between two Wilson lines.\\nThe discussion is valid for any conformal gauge \
theory, for any coupling and in\\nany dimension. For N=4 super Yang Mills we \
check this expansion at strong\\ncoupling and at two loops at weak coupling . \
We also make predictions for the\\nremainder function at higher loops. In the \
process, we also derived a new\\nversion for the TBA integral equations that \
determine the strong coupling\\nanswer and present the area as the associated \
Yang-Yang functional.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
