            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            
            "  One of the main topics in the modern String Theory are the \
AdS/CFT dualities.\nProving such conjectures is extremely difficult since the \
gauge and string\ntheory perturbative regimes do not overlap. In this \
perspective, the discovery\nof infinitely many conserved charges, i.e. the \
integrability, in the planar\nAdS/CFT has allowed us to reach immense \
progresses in understanding and\nconfirming the duality. We review the \
fundamental concepts and properties of\nintegrability in two-dimensional \
sigma-models and in the AdS/CFT context. The\nfirst part is focused on the \
AdS_5/CFT_4 duality, especially the classical and\nquantum integrability of \
the type IIB superstring on AdS_5 x S^5 are discussed\nin both pure spinor \
and Green-Schwarz formulations. The second part is\ndedicated to the \
AdS_4/CFT_3 duality with particular attention to the type IIA\nsuperstring on \
AdS_4 x CP^3 and its integrability. This review is based on a\nshortened and \
revised version of the author's PhD thesis, discussed at Uppsala\nUniversity \
in September 2009.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
