           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1006.3667\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Timothy J. Hollowood\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Timothy J. Hollowood and J. Luis Miramontes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Relativistic Avatars of Giant Magnons and their \
S-Matrix\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages, important correction to S-matrix to ensure \
crossing\\n  symmetry\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1010:012,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2010)012\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The motion of strings on symmetric space target spaces \
underlies the\\nintegrability of the AdS/CFT correspondence. Although these \
theories, whose\\nexcitations are giant magnons, are non-relativistic they \
are classically\\nequivalent, via the Polhmeyer reduction, to a relativistic \
integrable field\\ntheory known as a symmetric space sine-Gordon theory. \
These theories can be\\nformulated as integrable deformations of gauged WZW \
models. In this work we\\nconsider the class of symmetric spaces CP^{n+1} and \
solve the corresponding\\ngeneralized sine-Gordon theories at the quantum \
level by finding the exact\\nspectrum of topological solitons, or kinks, and \
their S-matrix. The latter\\ninvolves a trignometric solution of the \
Yang-Baxer equation which exhibits a\\nquantum group symmetry with a tower of \
states that is bounded, unlike for\\nmagnons, as a result of the quantum \
group deformation parameter q being a root\\nof unity. We test the S-matrix \
by taking the semi-classical limit and comparing\\nwith the time delays for \
the scattering of classical solitons. We argue that\\nthe internal CP^{n-1} \
moduli space of collective coordinates of the solitons in\\nthe classical \
theory can be interpreted as a q-deformed fuzzy space in the\\nquantum \
theory. We analyse the n=1 case separately and provide a further test\\nof \
the S-matrix conjecture in this case by calculating the central charge \
of\\nthe UV CFT using the thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 18 Jun 2010 11:36:48 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
