            "33 pages, important correction to S-matrix to ensure crossing\n  \
symmetry", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1010:012,2010", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2010)012", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The motion of strings on symmetric space target spaces \
underlies the\nintegrability of the AdS/CFT correspondence. Although these \
theories, whose\nexcitations are giant magnons, are non-relativistic they are \
classically\nequivalent, via the Polhmeyer reduction, to a relativistic \
integrable field\ntheory known as a symmetric space sine-Gordon theory. These \
theories can be\nformulated as integrable deformations of gauged WZW models. \
In this work we\nconsider the class of symmetric spaces CP^{n+1} and solve \
the corresponding\ngeneralized sine-Gordon theories at the quantum level by \
finding the exact\nspectrum of topological solitons, or kinks, and their \
S-matrix. The latter\ninvolves a trignometric solution of the Yang-Baxer \
equation which exhibits a\nquantum group symmetry with a tower of states that \
is bounded, unlike for\nmagnons, as a result of the quantum group deformation \
parameter q being a root\nof unity. We test the S-matrix by taking the \
semi-classical limit and comparing\nwith the time delays for the scattering \
of classical solitons. We argue that\nthe internal CP^{n-1} moduli space of \
collective coordinates of the solitons in\nthe classical theory can be \
interpreted as a q-deformed fuzzy space in the\nquantum theory. We analyse \
the n=1 case separately and provide a further test\nof the S-matrix \
conjecture in this case by calculating the central charge of\nthe UV CFT \
using the thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 18 Jun 2010 11:36:48 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 8 Jul 2010 13:42:13 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-11-21", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Hollowood", "Timothy J.", ""}, {
              "Miramontes", "J. Luis", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.982181521279045`, -4.115773876928887}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1006.5419\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gokce Basar\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gokce Basar\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A semiclassical analysis of the fluctuation eigenvalues \
and the one-loop\\n  energy of the folded spinning superstring in AdS_5 x S^5\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"27 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We systematically construct a semiclassical expansion \
for the eigenvalues of\\nthe 2nd order quantum fluctuations of the folded \
spinning superstring rotating\\nin the AdS_3 part of AdS_5 x S^5 with two \
alternative methods; by using the\\nexact expression of the Bloch momentum \
generated by the curvature induced\\nperiodic potentials and by using the \
large energy expansion of the dispersion\\nrelation. We then calculate the \
one-loop correction to the energy by summing\\nover the eigenvalues. Our \
results are extremely accurate for strings whose ends\\nare not too close to \
the AdS radius. Finally we derive the small spin Regge\\nexpansion in the \
context of zeta function approximation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
