            "Ki-Myeong Lee, and Sungjay Lee", "title" -> 
            "1/2-BPS Wilson Loops and Vortices in ABJM Model", "comments" -> 
            "22 pages", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1009:004,2010", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP09(2010)004", "report-no" -> "KIAS-P10018", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We explore the low-energy dynamics of 1/2-BPS heavy particles \
coupled to the\nABJM model via the Higgsing of M2-branes, with focus on \
physical understanding\nof the recently discovered 1/2-BPS Wilson loop \
operators. The low-energy theory\nof 1/2-BPS heavy particles turns out to \
have the U(N|N) supergauge symmetry,\nwhich explains the novel structure of \
the 1/2-BPS Wilson loop operator as a\nholonomy of a U(N|N) superconnection. \
We show that the supersymmetric\ntransformation of the Wilson loop operator \
can be identified as a fermionic\nsupergauge transformation, which leads to \
their invariance under half of the\nsupersymmetry. We also argue that 1/2-BPS \
Wilson loop operators appear as\n1/2-BPS vortices with vorticity 1/k. Such a \
vortex can be naturally interpreted\nas a membrane wrapping the Z_k cycle \
once, or type IIA fundamental string.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 29 Jun 2010 12:22:06 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-03-28", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Lee", "Ki-Myeong", ""}, {
              "Lee", "Sungjay", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
