                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We start from the classical action describing a single \
M2-brane on AdS_4 x\\nS^7/ Z_k and consider semiclassical fluctuaitions \
around a static, 1/2 BPS\\nconfiguration whose shape is AdS_2 x S^1. The \
internal manifold S^7/ Z_k is\\ndescribed as a U(1) fibration over CP^3 and \
the static configuration is wrapped\\non the U(1) fiber. Then the \
configuration is reduced to an AdS_2 world-sheet of\\ntype IIA string on \
AdS_4 x CP^3 through the Kaluza-Klein reduction on the S^1.\\nIt is shown \
that the fluctuations form an infinite set of N=1 supermultiplets\\non AdS_2, \
for k=1,2. The set is invariant under SO(8) which may be consistent\\nwith \
N=8 supersymmetry on AdS_2. We discuss the behavior of the \
fluctuations\\naround the boundary of AdS_2 and its relation to deformations \
of Wilson loop\\noperator.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
