               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marcos Marino\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nadav Drukker, Marcos Marino and Pavel Putrov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"From weak to strong coupling in ABJM theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"51 pages, 5 figures; v4: misprints corrected, added \
constant map\\n  contributions to the free energies, which were missing in \
the previous\\n  versions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Commun.Math.Phys.306:511-563,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s00220-011-1253-6\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-EP-10/39\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The partition function of N=6 supersymmetric \
Chern-Simons-matter theory\\n(known as ABJM theory) on S^3, as well as \
certain Wilson loop observables, are\\ncaptured by a zero dimensional \
super-matrix model. This super-matrix model is\\nclosely related to a matrix \
model describing topological Chern-Simons theory on\\na lens space. We \
explore further these recent observations and extract more\\nexact results in \
ABJM theory from the matrix model. In particular we calculate\\nthe planar \
free energy, which matches at strong coupling the classical \
IIA\\nsupergravity action on AdS_4 x CP^3 and gives the correct N^{3/2} \
scaling for\\nthe number of degrees of freedom of the M2 brane theory. \
Furthermore we find\\ncontributions coming from world-sheet instanton \
corrections in CP^3. We also\\ncalculate non-planar corrections, both to the \
free energy and to the Wilson\\nloop expectation values. This matrix model \
appears also in the study of\\ntopological strings on a toric Calabi-Yau \
manifold, and an intriguing\\nconnection arises between the space of \
couplings of the planar ABJM theory and\\nthe moduli space of this \
Calabi-Yau. In particular it suggests that, in\\naddition to the usual \
perturbative and strong coupling (AdS) expansions, a\\nthird natural \
expansion locus is the line where one of the two 't Hooft\\ncouplings \
vanishes and the other is finite. This is the conifold locus of \
the\\nCalabi-Yau, and leads to an expansion around topological Chern-Simons \
theory.\\nWe present some explicit results for the partition function and \
Wilson loop\\nobservables around this locus.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
