\n  contributions to the free energies, which were missing in the previous\n  \
versions", "journal-ref" -> "Commun.Math.Phys.306:511-563,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/s00220-011-1253-6", "report-no" -> "HU-EP-10/39", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The partition function of N=6 supersymmetric \
Chern-Simons-matter theory\n(known as ABJM theory) on S^3, as well as certain \
Wilson loop observables, are\ncaptured by a zero dimensional super-matrix \
model. This super-matrix model is\nclosely related to a matrix model \
describing topological Chern-Simons theory on\na lens space. We explore \
further these recent observations and extract more\nexact results in ABJM \
theory from the matrix model. In particular we calculate\nthe planar free \
energy, which matches at strong coupling the classical IIA\nsupergravity \
action on AdS_4 x CP^3 and gives the correct N^{3/2} scaling for\nthe number \
of degrees of freedom of the M2 brane theory. Furthermore we find\n\
contributions coming from world-sheet instanton corrections in CP^3. We also\n\
calculate non-planar corrections, both to the free energy and to the Wilson\n\
loop expectation values. This matrix model appears also in the study of\n\
topological strings on a toric Calabi-Yau manifold, and an intriguing\n\
connection arises between the space of couplings of the planar ABJM theory \
and\nthe moduli space of this Calabi-Yau. In particular it suggests that, in\n\
addition to the usual perturbative and strong coupling (AdS) expansions, a\n\
third natural expansion locus is the line where one of the two 't Hooft\n\
couplings vanishes and the other is finite. This is the conifold locus of the\
\nCalabi-Yau, and leads to an expansion around topological Chern-Simons \
theory.\nWe present some explicit results for the partition function and \
Wilson loop\nobservables around this locus.\n", 
