               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a three-loop O(g^6) calculation of the \
difference between the\\nexpectation values of Wilson loops evaluated in N=4 \
and superconformal N=2\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory with gauge group \
SU(N) using dimensional\\nreduction. We find a massive reduction of required \
Feynman diagrams, leaving\\nonly certain two-matter-loop corrections to the \
gauge field and associated\\nscalar propagator. This \\\"diagrammatic \
difference\\\" leaves a finite result\\nproportional to the bare propagators \
and allows the recovery of the zeta(3)\\nterm coming from the matrix model \
for the 1/2 BPS circular Wilson loop in the\\nN=2 theory. The result is valid \
also for closed Wilson loops of general shape.\\nComments are made concerning \
light-like polygons and supersymmetric loops in\\nthe plane and on \
S^2.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
