            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a three-loop O(g^6) calculation of the difference \
between the\nexpectation values of Wilson loops evaluated in N=4 and \
superconformal N=2\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory with gauge group SU(N) \
using dimensional\nreduction. We find a massive reduction of required Feynman \
diagrams, leaving\nonly certain two-matter-loop corrections to the gauge \
field and associated\nscalar propagator. This \"diagrammatic difference\" \
leaves a finite result\nproportional to the bare propagators and allows the \
recovery of the zeta(3)\nterm coming from the matrix model for the 1/2 BPS \
circular Wilson loop in the\nN=2 theory. The result is valid also for closed \
Wilson loops of general shape.\nComments are made concerning light-like \
polygons and supersymmetric loops in\nthe plane and on S^2.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 28 Jul 2010 10:56:27 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 24 Sep 2010 13:33:43 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 3 Nov 2010 08:45:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-11-04", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Andree", "Roman", ""}, {
              "Young", "Donovan", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.803784240477086`, -4.306497378994724}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1007.4931\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marius de Leeuw\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marius de Leeuw\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The S-matrix of the AdS5 x S5 superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Based on PhD thesis, 177 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ITP-UU-10-13,SPIN-10-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this article we review the world-sheet scattering \
theory of strings on AdS\\n5 x S5. The asymptotic spectrum of this \
world-sheet theory contains both\\nfundamental particles and bound states of \
the latter. We explicitly derive the\\nS-matrix that describes scattering of \
arbitrary bound states. The key feature\\nthat enables this derivation is the \
so-called Yangian symmetry which is related\\nto the centrally extended \
su(2|2) superalgebra. Subsequently, we study the\\nuniversal algebraic \
properties of the found S-matrix. As in many integrable\\nmodels, the \
S-matrix plays a key role in the determination of the energy\\nspectrum. In \
this context, we employ the Bethe ansatz approach to compute the\\nlarge \
volume energy spectrum of string bound states.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 28 Jul 2010 11:44:29 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2010-07-29\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"de Leeuw\"", ",", "\"Marius\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
