            "  In this article we review the world-sheet scattering theory of \
strings on AdS\n5 x S5. The asymptotic spectrum of this world-sheet theory \
contains both\nfundamental particles and bound states of the latter. We \
explicitly derive the\nS-matrix that describes scattering of arbitrary bound \
states. The key feature\nthat enables this derivation is the so-called \
Yangian symmetry which is related\nto the centrally extended su(2|2) \
superalgebra. Subsequently, we study the\nuniversal algebraic properties of \
the found S-matrix. As in many integrable\nmodels, the S-matrix plays a key \
role in the determination of the energy\nspectrum. In this context, we employ \
the Bethe ansatz approach to compute the\nlarge volume energy spectrum of \
string bound states.\n", 
