                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss a hidden symmetry of a two-dimensional sigma \
model on a squashed\\nS^3. The SU(2) current can be improved so that it can \
be regarded as a flat\\nconnection. Then we can obtain an infinite number of \
conserved non-local\\ncharges and show the Yangian algebra by directly \
checking the Serre relation.\\nThis symmetry is also deduced from the coset \
structure of the squashed sphere.\\nThe same argument is applicable to the \
warped AdS_3 spaces via double Wick\\nrotations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
