                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We solve the operator ordering problem for the quantum \
continuous integrable\\nsu(1,1) Landau-Lifshitz model, and give a \
prescription to obtain the quantum\\ntrace identities, and the spectrum for \
the higher-order local charges. We also\\nshow that this method, based on \
operator regularization and renormalization,\\nwhich guarantees quantum \
integrability, as well as the construction of\\nself-adjoint extensions, can \
be used as an alternative to the discretization\\nprocedure, and unlike the \
latter, is based only on integrable representations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
