               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On three-point correlation functions in the gauge/gravity \
duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1011:141,2010\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2010)141\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the effect of marginal and irrelevant \
deformations on the\\nrenormalization of operators near a CFT fixed point. \
New divergences in a given\\noperator are determined by its OPE with the \
operator D that generates the\\ndeformation. This provides a scheme to \
compute the couplings a_DAB between the\\noperator D and two arbitrary \
operators O_A and O_B. We exemplify for the case\\nof N=4 SYM, considering \
the simplest case of the exact Lagrangian deformation.\\nIn this case the \
deformed anomalous dimension matrix is determined by the\\nderivative of the \
anomalous dimension matrix with respect to the coupling. We\\nuse \
integrability techniques to compute the one-loop couplings a_LAB \
between\\nthe Lagrangian and two distinct large operators built with Magnons, \
in the\\nSU(2) sector of the theory. Then we consider a_DAA at strong \
coupling, and show\\nhow to compute it using the gauge/gravity duality, when \
D is a chiral operator\\ndual to any supergravity field and O_A is dual to a \
heavy string state. We\\nexemplify for the Lagrangian and operators O_A dual \
to heavy string states,\\nshowing agreement with the prediction derived from \
the renormalization group\\narguments.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
