            "  We study the effect of marginal and irrelevant deformations on \
the\nrenormalization of operators near a CFT fixed point. New divergences in \
a given\noperator are determined by its OPE with the operator D that \
generates the\ndeformation. This provides a scheme to compute the couplings \
a_DAB between the\noperator D and two arbitrary operators O_A and O_B. We \
exemplify for the case\nof N=4 SYM, considering the simplest case of the \
exact Lagrangian deformation.\nIn this case the deformed anomalous dimension \
matrix is determined by the\nderivative of the anomalous dimension matrix \
with respect to the coupling. We\nuse integrability techniques to compute the \
one-loop couplings a_LAB between\nthe Lagrangian and two distinct large \
operators built with Magnons, in the\nSU(2) sector of the theory. Then we \
consider a_DAA at strong coupling, and show\nhow to compute it using the \
gauge/gravity duality, when D is a chiral operator\ndual to any supergravity \
field and O_A is dual to a heavy string state. We\nexemplify for the \
Lagrangian and operators O_A dual to heavy string states,\nshowing agreement \
with the prediction derived from the renormalization group\narguments.\n", 
