 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The planar solution is discussed for an N=3 \
Chern-Simons-matter theory\\nconstructed recently by Gaiotto and Tomasiello. \
The planar resolvent is\\nobtained in terms of contour integrals. If the sum \
of two Chern-Simons levels\\nk_1,k_2 is small, the expectation value of a \
supersymmetric Wilson loop grows\\nexponentially with the total 't Hooft \
coupling, as is expected from AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence. If one of the \
Chern-Simons levels, say k_2, is taken to\\ninfinity, for which one of the 't \
Hooft coupling constants becomes zero, then\\nthe exponential behavior \
disappears.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
