               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider higher derivative gravity lagrangians in 3 \
and 4 dimensions,\\nwhich admit simple c-theorems, including upto six \
derivative curvature\\ninvariants. Following a suggestion by Myers, these \
lagrangians are restricted\\nsuch that the fluctuations around (anti) de \
Sitter spaces have second order\\nlinearized equations of motion. We study \
c-theorems both in the context of\\nAdS/CFT and cosmology. In the context of \
cosmology, the monotonic function is\\nthe entropy defined on the apparent \
horizon through Wald's formula. Exact black\\nhole solutions which are \
asymptotically (anti) de Sitter are presented. An\\ninteresting lower bound \
for entropy is found in de Sitter space. Some aspects\\nof cosmology in both \
D=3 and D=4 are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
