         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1008.4921", "submitter" -> "Radu Roiban", "authors" -> 
            "R. Roiban, A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "On semiclassical computation of 3-point functions of closed \
string\n  vertex operators in AdS_5 x S^5", "comments" -> 
            "24 pages, Latex v2: typos corrected, clarifying remarks and\n  \
references added v3: minor corrections, fixed normalization of dilaton vertex\
\n  operator", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D82:106011,2010", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.82.106011", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the leading large string tension correction to \
correlation\nfunctions of three vertex operators of particular massive string \
states in\nAdS_5 x S^5 string theory. We assume that two of these states are \
\"heavy\"\ncarrying large spins (of order string tension) and thus can be \
treated\nsemiclassically while the third state is \"light\" having fixed \
quantum numbers.\nWe study several examples. In the case when the \"heavy\" \
states are described by\na folded string with large spin in AdS_5 the 3-point \
function scales as a\nsemiclassical spin parameter of the \"heavy\" state in \
power of the string level\nof the \"light\" massive string state. We observe \
similar behavior in the case of\n\"heavy\" states which admit a small angular \
momentum limit which may thus\nrepresent correlators of three quantum massive \
string states.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 29 Aug 2010 13:20:35 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 24 Sep 2010 20:39:36 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 22 Dec 2010 21:22:12 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-12-24", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Roiban", "R.", ""}, {
              "Tseytlin", "A. A.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.367391708222183`, -5.316292866167677}, 0.],
