                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyse semiclassical strings in AdS in the limit of \
one large spin. In\\nthis limit, classical string dynamics is described by a \
finite number of\\ncollective coordinates corresponding to spikes or cusps of \
the string. The\\nsemiclassical spectrum consists of two branches of \
excitations corresponding to\\n\\\"large\\\" and \\\"small\\\" spikes \
respectively. We propose that these states are dual\\nto the excitations \
known as large and small holes in the spin chain description\\nof N=4 SUSY \
Yang-Mills. The dynamics of large spikes in classical string theory\\ncan be \
mapped to that of a classical spin chain of fixed length. In turn, \
small\\nspikes correspond to classical solitons propagating on the background \
formed by\\nthe large spikes. We derive the dispersion relation for these \
excitations\\ndirectly in the finite gap formalism.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
