            "36 pages, 9 figures", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1012:014,2010", 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP12(2010)014", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We analyse semiclassical strings in AdS in the limit of one \
large spin. In\nthis limit, classical string dynamics is described by a \
finite number of\ncollective coordinates corresponding to spikes or cusps of \
the string. The\nsemiclassical spectrum consists of two branches of \
excitations corresponding to\n\"large\" and \"small\" spikes respectively. We \
propose that these states are dual\nto the excitations known as large and \
small holes in the spin chain description\nof N=4 SUSY Yang-Mills. The \
dynamics of large spikes in classical string theory\ncan be mapped to that of \
a classical spin chain of fixed length. In turn, small\nspikes correspond to \
classical solitons propagating on the background formed by\nthe large spikes. \
We derive the dispersion relation for these excitations\ndirectly in the \
finite gap formalism.\n", 
