Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exact computation of one-loop correction to energy of \
pulsating strings\\n  in AdS_5 x S^5\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"49 pages; v2: appendix F and note about antiperiodic \
fermions added,\\n  typos corrected, references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A44:015404,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8113/44/1/015404\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-AT-2010-03\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the present paper, which is a sequel to \
arXiv:1001:4018, we compute the\\none-loop correction to the energy of \
pulsating string solutions in AdS_5 x S^5.\\nWe show that, as for rigid \
spinning string elliptic solutions, the fluctuation\\noperators for pulsating \
solutions can be also put into the single-gap Lame'\\nform. A novel aspect of \
pulsating solutions is that the one-loop correction to\\ntheir energy is \
expressed in terms of the stability angles of the quadratic\\nfluctuation \
operators. We explicitly study the \\\"short string\\\" limit of \
the\\ncorresponding one-loop energies, demonstrating a certain universality \
of the\\nform of the energy of \\\"small\\\" semiclassical strings. Our \
results may help to\\nshed light on the structure of strong-coupling \
expansion of anomalous\\ndimensions of dual gauge theory operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
