            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In the present paper, which is a sequel to arXiv:1001:4018, we \
compute the\none-loop correction to the energy of pulsating string solutions \
in AdS_5 x S^5.\nWe show that, as for rigid spinning string elliptic \
solutions, the fluctuation\noperators for pulsating solutions can be also put \
into the single-gap Lame'\nform. A novel aspect of pulsating solutions is \
that the one-loop correction to\ntheir energy is expressed in terms of the \
stability angles of the quadratic\nfluctuation operators. We explicitly study \
the \"short string\" limit of the\ncorresponding one-loop energies, \
demonstrating a certain universality of the\nform of the energy of \"small\" \
semiclassical strings. Our results may help to\nshed light on the structure \
of strong-coupling expansion of anomalous\ndimensions of dual gauge theory \
operators.\n", 
