                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using N=2 superspace techniques we compute the \
four-loop spectrum of single\\ntrace operators in the SU(2) x SU(2) sector of \
ABJM and ABJ supersymmetric\\nChern-Simons theories. Our computation yields a \
four-loop contribution to the\\nfunction h^2(\\\\lambda) (and its ABJ \
generalization) in the magnon dispersion\\nrelation which has fixed maximum \
transcendentality and coincides with the\\nfindings in components given in \
the revised versions of arXiv:0908.2463 and\\narXiv:0912.3460. We also \
discuss possible scenarios for an all-loop function\\nh^2(\\\\lambda) that \
interpolates between weak and strong couplings.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
