Zengo Tsuboi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wronskian Solution for AdS/CFT Y-system\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"31 pages, 4 figures, 1 attached mathematica file\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1101:155,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2011)155\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"LPT ENS-10/38\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the discrete Hirota integrability we find the \
general solution of the\\nfull quantum Y-system for the spectrum of anomalous \
dimensions of operators in\\nthe planar AdS5/CFT4 correspondence in terms of \
Wronskian-like determinants\\nparameterized by a finite number of Baxter's \
Q-functions. We consider it as a\\nuseful step towards the construction of a \
finite system of non-linear integral\\nequations (FiNLIE) for the full \
spectrum. The explicit asymptotic form of all\\nthe Q-functions for the large \
size operators is presented. We establish the\\nsymmetries and the \
analyticity properties of the asymptotic Q-functions and\\ndiscuss their \
possible generalization to any finite size operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
