I.\\n  Nepomechie\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Twisted Bethe equations from a twisted S-matrix\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"42 pages; v2: a new appendix on sl(2) grading, 2 \
additional\\n  references, and some minor changes; v3: improved Appendix D, \
additional\\n  references, and further minor changes, to appear in \
JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1102:027,2011\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2011)027\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UMTG-268\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  All-loop asymptotic Bethe equations for a 3-parameter \
deformation of\\nAdS5/CFT4 have been proposed by Beisert and Roiban. We \
propose a Drinfeld twist\\nof the AdS5/CFT4 S-matrix, together with c-number \
diagonal twists of the\\nboundary conditions, from which we derive these \
Bethe equations. Although the\\nundeformed S-matrix factorizes into a product \
of two su(2|2) factors, the\\ndeformed S-matrix cannot be so factored. \
Diagonalization of the corresponding\\ntransfer matrix requires a \
generalization of the conventional algebraic Bethe\\nansatz approach, which \
we first illustrate for the simpler case of the twisted\\nsu(2) principal \
chiral model. We also demonstrate that the same twisted Bethe\\nequations can \
alternatively be derived using instead untwisted S-matrices and\\nboundary \
conditions with operatorial twists.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
