               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We continue the investigation of two-loop string \
corrections to the energy of\\na folded string with a spin S in AdS_5 and an \
angular momentum J in S^5, in the\\nscaling limit of large J and S with \
ell=pi J/(lambda^(1/2) ln S)=fixed. We\\ncompute the generalized scaling \
function at two-loop order f_2(ell) both for\\nsmall and large values of ell \
matching the predictions based on the asymptotic\\nBethe ansatz. In \
particular, in the small ell expansion, we derive an exact\\nintegral form \
for the ell-dependent coefficient of the Catalan's constant term\\nin \
f_2(ell). Also, by resumming a certain subclass of multi-loop \
Feynman\\ndiagrams we obtain an exact expression for the leading (ln ell) \
part of\\nf(lambda^(1/2), ell) which is valid to any order in the \
alpha'~1/lambda^(1/2)\\nexpansion. At large ell the string energy has a \
BMN-like expansion and the\\nfirst few leading coefficients are expected to \
be the same at weak and at\\nstrong coupling. We provide a new example of \
this non-renormalization for the\\nterm which is generated at two loops in \
string theory and at one-loop in gauge\\ntheory (sub-sub-leading in 1/J). We \
also derive a simple algebraic formula for\\nthe term of maximal \
transcendentality in f_2(ell) expanded at large ell. In the\\nsecond part of \
the paper we initiate the study of 2-loop finite size\\ncorrections to the \
string energy by formally compactifying the spatial\\nworld-sheet direction \
in the string action expanded near long fast-spinning\\nstring. We observe \
that the leading finite-size corrections are of \\\"Casimir\\\"\\ntype coming \
from terms containing at least one massless propagator. We consider\\nin \
detail the one-loop order (reproducing the leading Landau-Lifshitz \
model\\nprediction) and then focus on the two-loop contributions to the (1/ln \
S) term\\n(for J=0). We find that in a certain regularization scheme used to \
discard\\npower divergences the two-loop coefficient of the (1/ln S) term \
appears to\\nvanish.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 21 Oct 2010 22:15:48 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 Dec 2010 17:03:36 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
