            "  We continue the investigation of two-loop string corrections \
to the energy of\na folded string with a spin S in AdS_5 and an angular \
momentum J in S^5, in the\nscaling limit of large J and S with ell=pi \
J/(lambda^(1/2) ln S)=fixed. We\ncompute the generalized scaling function at \
two-loop order f_2(ell) both for\nsmall and large values of ell matching the \
predictions based on the asymptotic\nBethe ansatz. In particular, in the \
small ell expansion, we derive an exact\nintegral form for the ell-dependent \
coefficient of the Catalan's constant term\nin f_2(ell). Also, by resumming a \
certain subclass of multi-loop Feynman\ndiagrams we obtain an exact \
expression for the leading (ln ell) part of\nf(lambda^(1/2), ell) which is \
valid to any order in the alpha'~1/lambda^(1/2)\nexpansion. At large ell the \
string energy has a BMN-like expansion and the\nfirst few leading \
coefficients are expected to be the same at weak and at\nstrong coupling. We \
provide a new example of this non-renormalization for the\nterm which is \
generated at two loops in string theory and at one-loop in gauge\ntheory \
(sub-sub-leading in 1/J). We also derive a simple algebraic formula for\nthe \
term of maximal transcendentality in f_2(ell) expanded at large ell. In the\n\
second part of the paper we initiate the study of 2-loop finite size\n\
corrections to the string energy by formally compactifying the spatial\n\
world-sheet direction in the string action expanded near long fast-spinning\n\
string. We observe that the leading finite-size corrections are of \
\"Casimir\"\ntype coming from terms containing at least one massless \
propagator. We consider\nin detail the one-loop order (reproducing the \
leading Landau-Lifshitz model\nprediction) and then focus on the two-loop \
contributions to the (1/ln S) term\n(for J=0). We find that in a certain \
regularization scheme used to discard\npower divergences the two-loop \
coefficient of the (1/ln S) term appears to\nvanish.\n", 
