 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The strong-coupling limit of three-point correlation \
functions of local\\noperators can be analyzed beyond the supergravity regime \
using vertex operators\\nrepresenting spinning string states. When two of the \
vertex operators\\ncorrespond to heavy string states having large quantum \
numbers, while the third\\noperator corresponds to a light state with fixed \
charges, the correlator can be\\ncomputed in the large string tension limit \
by means of a semiclassical\\napproximation. We study the case when the heavy \
string states are circular\\nstring solutions with one AdS_5 spin and three \
different angular momenta along\\nS^5, for several choices of the light \
string state.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
