               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We use AdS_5 x S^5 superstring sigma model perturbation \
theory to compute the\\nleading one-loop corrections to the dispersion \
relations of the excitations\\nnear a long spinning string in AdS. This \
investigation is partially motivated\\nby the OPE-based approach to the \
computation of the expectation value of null\\npolygonal Wilson loops \
suggested in arXiv:1006.2788. Our results are in partial\\nagreement with the \
recent asymptotic Bethe ansatz computation in\\narXiv:1010.5237. In \
particular, we find that the heaviest AdS mode (absent in\\nthe ABA approach) \
is stable and has a corrected one-loop dispersion relation\\nsimilar to the \
other massive modes. Its stability might hold also at the\\nnext-to-leading \
order as we suggest using a unitarity-based argument.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
