         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1011.2755", "submitter" -> "Simone Giombi", "authors" -> 
            "S. Giombi, R. Ricci, R. Roiban, A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Quantum dispersion relations for excitations of long folded \
spinning\n  superstring in AdS_5 x S^5", "comments" -> 
            "22 pages, 3 figures. v3: small corrections and a comment added \
in\n  sec. 4.1", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1101:128,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP01(2011)128", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We use AdS_5 x S^5 superstring sigma model perturbation theory \
to compute the\nleading one-loop corrections to the dispersion relations of \
the excitations\nnear a long spinning string in AdS. This investigation is \
partially motivated\nby the OPE-based approach to the computation of the \
expectation value of null\npolygonal Wilson loops suggested in \
arXiv:1006.2788. Our results are in partial\nagreement with the recent \
asymptotic Bethe ansatz computation in\narXiv:1010.5237. In particular, we \
find that the heaviest AdS mode (absent in\nthe ABA approach) is stable and \
has a corrected one-loop dispersion relation\nsimilar to the other massive \
modes. Its stability might hold also at the\nnext-to-leading order as we \
suggest using a unitarity-based argument.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 11 Nov 2010 20:41:51 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 22 Nov 2010 19:46:07 GMT"}, {
