 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study line operators in the two-dimensional \
sigma-model on PSl(n|n) using\\nthe current-current OPEs. We regularize and \
renormalize these line operators,\\nand compute their fusion up to second \
order in perturbation theory. In\\nparticular we show that the transfer \
matrix associated to a one-parameter\\nfamily of flat connections is free of \
divergences. Moreover this transfer\\nmatrix satisfies the Hirota equation \
(which can be rewritten as a Y-system, or\\nThermodynamic Bethe Ansatz \
equations) for all values of the two parameters\\ndefining the sigma-model. \
This provides a first-principles derivation of the\\nHirota equation which \
does not rely on the string hypothesis nor on the\\nassumption of quantum \
integrability.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
