            "  We study deformed WZW models on supergroups with vanishing \
Killing form. The\ndeformation is generated by the isotropic current-current \
perturbation which is\nexactly marginal under these assumptions. It breaks \
half of the global\nisometries of the original supergroup. The current \
corresponding to the\nremaining symmetry is conserved but its components are \
neither holomorphic nor\nanti-holomorphic. We obtain the exact two- and \
three-point functions of this\ncurrent and a four-point function in the first \
two leading orders of a 1/k\nexpansion but to all orders in the deformation \
parameter. We further study the\noperator product algebra of the currents, \
the equal time commutators and the\nquantum equations of motion. The form of \
the equations of motion suggests the\nexistence of non-local charges which \
generate a Yangian. Possible applications\nto string theory on Anti-de Sitter \
spaces and to condensed matter problems are\nbriefly discussed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 22 Nov 2010 13:55:17 GMT"}, {
