          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1011.5181\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"George Georgiou\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"George Georgiou\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Two and three-point correlators of operators dual to \
folded string\\n  solutions at strong coupling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages 3 figures,typos corrected,references \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1102:046,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2011)046\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A particular analytic continuation of classical string \
solutions having a\\nsingle AdS_5 spin is considered. These solutions \
describe strings tunnelling\\nfrom the boundary to the boundary of AdS_5. We \
use the Legendre transform of\\nthe dimensionally regularised action of these \
solutions to evaluate the 2-point\\nfunctions of the dual operators, \
holographically. Subsequently, we evaluate the\\nstructure coefficient of \
correlators involving two operators with spin S and a\\nBPS state, at strong \
coupling. Our expressions are valid for any value of the\\nAdS spin \
S/\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda} and can be applied both at the case of long and \
short\\nstrings. For long strings and at leading order, the structure \
coefficient is\\nindependent of the spin S for twist J operators, while it \
scales as\\n1/\\\\log^l{\\\\frac{S}{\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}}} for the case of \
operators with two equal\\nangular momenta in S^5. For short strings, the \
structure coefficient is\\nproportional to the energy E of the string. \
Finally, we comment on the\\npossibility of relating the strong coupling \
3-point function coefficient of\\nthree large spin twist 2 operators to the \
action of the 6-gluon scattering\\namplitude.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 23 Nov 2010 17:59:56 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
