         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1011.5181", "submitter" -> "George Georgiou", "authors" -> 
            "George Georgiou", "title" -> 
            "Two and three-point correlators of operators dual to folded \
string\n  solutions at strong coupling", "comments" -> 
            "22 pages 3 figures,typos corrected,references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1102:046,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP02(2011)046", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  A particular analytic continuation of classical string \
solutions having a\nsingle AdS_5 spin is considered. These solutions describe \
strings tunnelling\nfrom the boundary to the boundary of AdS_5. We use the \
Legendre transform of\nthe dimensionally regularised action of these \
solutions to evaluate the 2-point\nfunctions of the dual operators, \
holographically. Subsequently, we evaluate the\nstructure coefficient of \
correlators involving two operators with spin S and a\nBPS state, at strong \
coupling. Our expressions are valid for any value of the\nAdS spin \
S/\\sqrt{\\lambda} and can be applied both at the case of long and short\n\
strings. For long strings and at leading order, the structure coefficient is\n\
independent of the spin S for twist J operators, while it scales as\n\
1/\\log^l{\\frac{S}{\\sqrt{\\lambda}}} for the case of operators with two \
equal\nangular momenta in S^5. For short strings, the structure coefficient \
is\nproportional to the energy E of the string. Finally, we comment on the\n\
possibility of relating the strong coupling 3-point function coefficient of\n\
three large spin twist 2 operators to the action of the 6-gluon scattering\n\
amplitude.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 23 Nov 2010 17:59:56 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 7 Dec 2010 11:52:08 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 20 Sep 2015 16:25:50 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-09-22", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Georgiou", "George", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
