Putrov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Unquenched flavor and tropical geometry in strongly \
coupled\\n  Chern-Simons-matter theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages, 7 figures. v2: small corrections, added an \
Appendix on the\\n  relation with the approach of 1011.5487. v3: further \
corrections and\\n  clarifications, final version to appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2011)139\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.AG\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study various aspects of the matrix models \
calculating free energies and\\nWilson loop observables in supersymmetric \
Chern-Simons-matter theories on the\\nthree-sphere. We first develop \
techniques to extract strong coupling results\\ndirectly from the spectral \
curve describing the large N master field. We show\\nthat the strong coupling \
limit of the gauge theory corresponds to the so-called\\ntropical limit of \
the spectral curve. In this limit, the curve degenerates to a\\nplanar graph, \
and matrix model calculations reduce to elementary line integrals\\nalong the \
graph. As an important physical application of these tropical\\ntechniques, \
we study N=3 theories with fundamental matter, both in the quenched\\nand in \
the unquenched regimes. We calculate the exact spectral curve in \
the\\nVeneziano limit, and we evaluate the planar free energy and Wilson loop\
\\nobservables at strong coupling by using tropical geometry. The results are \
in\\nagreement with the predictions of the AdS duals involving \
tri-Sasakian\\nmanifolds\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
