            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study various aspects of the matrix models calculating free \
energies and\nWilson loop observables in supersymmetric Chern-Simons-matter \
theories on the\nthree-sphere. We first develop techniques to extract strong \
coupling results\ndirectly from the spectral curve describing the large N \
master field. We show\nthat the strong coupling limit of the gauge theory \
corresponds to the so-called\ntropical limit of the spectral curve. In this \
limit, the curve degenerates to a\nplanar graph, and matrix model \
calculations reduce to elementary line integrals\nalong the graph. As an \
important physical application of these tropical\ntechniques, we study N=3 \
theories with fundamental matter, both in the quenched\nand in the unquenched \
regimes. We calculate the exact spectral curve in the\nVeneziano limit, and \
we evaluate the planar free energy and Wilson loop\nobservables at strong \
coupling by using tropical geometry. The results are in\nagreement with the \
predictions of the AdS duals involving tri-Sasakian\nmanifolds\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
