               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1012.0716\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Timothy J. Hollowood\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Timothy J. Hollowood and J. Luis Miramontes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Classical and Quantum Solitons in the Symmetric Space \
Sine-Gordon\\n  Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages, additional comments and small errors corrected, \
final\\n  journal version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2011)119\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the soliton solutions in the symmetric \
space sine-Gordon\\ntheories. The latter are a series of integrable field \
theories in\\n1+1-dimensions which are associated to a symmetric space F/G, \
and are related\\nvia the Pohlmeyer reduction to theories of strings moving \
on symmetric spaces.\\nWe show that the solitons are kinks that carry an \
internal moduli space that\\ncan be identified with a particular co-adjoint \
orbit of the unbroken subgroup H\\nof G. Classically the solitons come in a \
continuous spectrum which encompasses\\nthe perturbative fluctuations of the \
theory as the kink charge becomes small.\\nWe show that the solitons can be \
quantized by allowing the collective\\ncoordinates to be time-dependent to \
yield a form of quantum mechanics on the\\nco-adjoint orbit. The quantum \
states correspond to symmetric tensor\\nrepresentations of the symmetry group \
H and have the interpretation of a fuzzy\\ngeometric version of the \
co-adjoint orbit. The quantized finite tower of\\nsoliton states includes the \
perturbative modes at the base.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
