  journal version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP04(2011)119",
             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct the soliton solutions in the symmetric space \
sine-Gordon\ntheories. The latter are a series of integrable field theories \
in\n1+1-dimensions which are associated to a symmetric space F/G, and are \
related\nvia the Pohlmeyer reduction to theories of strings moving on \
symmetric spaces.\nWe show that the solitons are kinks that carry an internal \
moduli space that\ncan be identified with a particular co-adjoint orbit of \
the unbroken subgroup H\nof G. Classically the solitons come in a continuous \
spectrum which encompasses\nthe perturbative fluctuations of the theory as \
the kink charge becomes small.\nWe show that the solitons can be quantized by \
allowing the collective\ncoordinates to be time-dependent to yield a form of \
quantum mechanics on the\nco-adjoint orbit. The quantum states correspond to \
symmetric tensor\nrepresentations of the symmetry group H and have the \
interpretation of a fuzzy\ngeometric version of the co-adjoint orbit. The \
quantized finite tower of\nsoliton states includes the perturbative modes at \
the base.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
