 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We use Integrability techniques to compute structure \
constants in N=4 SYM to\\nleading order. Three closed spin chains, which \
represent the single trace\\ngauge-invariant operators in N=4 SYM, are cut \
into six open chains which are\\nthen sewed back together into some nice \
pants, the three-point function. The\\nalgebraic and coordinate Bethe ansatz \
tools necessary for this task are\\nreviewed. Finally, we discuss the \
classical limit of our results, anticipating\\nsome predictions for \
quasi-classical string correlators in terms of algebraic\\ncurves.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
