               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jorge Russo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.G. Russo and A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Large spin expansion of semiclassical 3-point correlators \
in AdS_5 x S^5\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"17 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1102:029,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2011)029\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"ICCUB-10-199, Imperial-TP-AT-2010-04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  3-point correlators in AdS_5xS^5 string theory in which \
two states are\\n\\\"heavy\\\" (have large quantum numbers) and the third is \
\\\"light\\\" (here chosen as\\nchiral primary scalar) can be computed \
semiclassically in terms of the \\\"light\\\"\\nvertex operator evaluated on \
the classical string solution sourced by the two\\n\\\"heavy\\\" operators. \
We observe that in the case when the \\\"heavy\\\" operators\\nrepresent BPS \
states there is an ambiguity in the computation depending on\\nwhether the \
mass shell (or marginality) condition is imposed before or \
after\\nintegration over the world sheet. We show that this ambiguity is \
resolved in a\\nuniversal way by defining the BPS correlator as a limit of \
the one with non-BPS\\n\\\"heavy\\\" states. We consider several examples \
with \\\"heavy\\\" states represented by\\nfolded or circular spinning \
strings in AdS_5xS^5 that admit a point-like\\nBMN-type limit when one S^5 \
spin J is much larger than the others. Remarkably,\\nin all of these cases \
the large J expansion of the 3-point correlator has the\\nsame structure as \
expected in perturbative (tree-level and one-loop) dual gauge\\ntheory. We \
conjecture that, like the leading chiral primary correlator term,\\nthe \
coefficients of the first few subleading terms are also protected, \
i.e.\\nshould be the same at strong and weak coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
