          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1012.3989", "submitter" -> "Sakura Schafer-Nameki", 
            "authors" -> "Sakura Schafer-Nameki", "title" -> 
            "Review of AdS/CFT Integrability, Chapter II.4: The Spectral \
Curve", "comments" -> 
            "20 pages, see also overview article arXiv:1012.3982, v3: \
published\n  version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/s11005-011-0525-6", "report-no" -> "kcl-mth-10-18", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> "\
  We review the spectral curve for the classical string in AdS5xS5. Classical\
\nintegrability of the AdS5xS5 string implies the existence of a flat \
connection,\nwhose monodromies generate an infinite set of conserved charges. \
The spectral\ncurve is constructed out of the quasi-momenta, which are \
eigenvalues of the\nmonodromy matrix, and each finite-gap classical solution \
can be characterized\nin terms of such a curve. This provides a concise and \
powerful description of\nthe classical solution space. In addition, \
semi-classical quantization of the\nstring can be performed in terms of the \
quasi-momenta. We review the general\nframe-work of the semi-classical \
quantization in this context and exemplify it\nwith the circular string \
solution which is supported on RxS3 in AdS5xS5.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 17 Dec 2010 20:58:08 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 20 Dec 2010 19:14:53 GMT"}, {
