 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  There is a growing amount of evidence that QCD (and \
four-dimensional gauge\\ntheories in general) possess a hidden symmetry which \
does not exhibit itself as\\na symmetry of classical Lagrangians but is only \
revealed on the quantum level.\\nIn this review we consider the scale \
dependence of local gauge invariant\\noperators and high-energy (Regge) \
behavior of scattering amplitudes to explain\\nthat the effective QCD \
dynamics in both cases is described by completely\\nintegrable systems that \
prove to be related to the celebrated Heisenberg spin\\nchain and its \
generalizations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
