                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the calculation of curvature corrections to \
the pp-wave energy of\\ntype IIA string states on AdS_4 x CP^3 initiated in \
arXiv:0807.1527. Using the\\nnear pp-wave Hamiltonian found in \
arXiv:0912.2257, we compute the first\\nnon-vanishing correction to the \
energy of a set of bosonic string states at\\norder 1/R^2, where R is the \
curvature radius of the background. The leading\\ncurvature corrections give \
rise to cubic, order 1/R, and quartic, order 1/R^2,\\nterms in the \
Hamiltonian, for which we implement the appropriate normal\\nordering \
prescription. Including the contributions from all possible fermionic\\nand \
bosonic string states, we find that there exist logarithmic divergences \
in\\nthe sums over mode numbers which cancel between the cubic and \
quartic\\nHamiltonian. We show that the cubic Hamiltonian naturally requires \
that the\\ncutoff for summing over heavy modes must be twice the one for \
light modes. With\\nthis prescription the strong-weak coupling interpolating \
function h(\\\\lambda),\\nentering the magnon dispersion relation, does not \
receive a one-loop\\ncorrection, in agreement with the algebraic curve \
spectrum. However, the single\\nmagnon dispersion relation exhibits \
finite-size exponential corrections.\\n\""}]}, {
