            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1101.0400\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Amit Dekel\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Amit Dekel and Yaron Oz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Self-Duality of Green-Schwarz Sigma-Models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"39 pages, 1 figure. v2 references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1103:117,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2011)117\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study fermionic T-duality symmetries of integrable \
Green-Schwarz\\nsigma-models on Anti-de-Sitter backgrounds with Ramond-Ramond \
fluxes,\\nconstructed as Z_4 supercosets of superconformal algebras. We find \
three\\nalgebraic conditions that guarantee self-duality of the backgrounds \
under\\nfermionic T-duality, we classify those that satisfy them and \
construct the map\\nof the monodromy matrix. We introduce new T-duality \
directions, where some of\\nthem contain no bosonic directions, along which \
the backgrounds are self-dual.\\nWe find that the only self-dual backgrounds \
are AdS_n x S^n for n=2,3,5. In\\naddition we find that the backgrounds AdS_n \
x S^1 for n=2,3,5, AdS_4 x S^2 and\\nAdS_2 x S^4 are self-dual at the level \
of the classical action, but have a\\nnon-trivial transformation of the \
dilaton.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
