            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study fermionic T-duality symmetries of integrable \
Green-Schwarz\nsigma-models on Anti-de-Sitter backgrounds with Ramond-Ramond \
fluxes,\nconstructed as Z_4 supercosets of superconformal algebras. We find \
three\nalgebraic conditions that guarantee self-duality of the backgrounds \
under\nfermionic T-duality, we classify those that satisfy them and construct \
the map\nof the monodromy matrix. We introduce new T-duality directions, \
where some of\nthem contain no bosonic directions, along which the \
backgrounds are self-dual.\nWe find that the only self-dual backgrounds are \
AdS_n x S^n for n=2,3,5. In\naddition we find that the backgrounds AdS_n x \
S^1 for n=2,3,5, AdS_4 x S^2 and\nAdS_2 x S^4 are self-dual at the level of \
the classical action, but have a\nnon-trivial transformation of the dilaton.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
