            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1101.3216\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Edward Witten\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Edward Witten\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fivebranes and Knots\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"numerous small corrections from v. 1; 148 pp\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.GT math.RT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop an approach to Khovanov homology of knots \
via gauge theory\\n(previous physics-based approches involved other \
descriptions of the relevant\\nspaces of BPS states). The starting point is a \
system of D3-branes ending on an\\nNS5-brane with a nonzero theta-angle. On \
the one hand, this system can be\\nrelated to a Chern-Simons gauge theory on \
the boundary of the D3-brane\\nworldvolume; on the other hand, it can be \
studied by standard techniques of\\n$S$-duality and $T$-duality. Combining \
the two approaches leads to a new and\\nmanifestly invariant description of \
the Jones polynomial of knots, and its\\ngeneralizations, and to a manifestly \
invariant description of Khovanov\\nhomology, in terms of certain elliptic \
partial differential equations in four\\nand five dimensions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
