            "hep-th math.GT math.RT", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We develop an approach to Khovanov homology of knots via gauge \
theory\n(previous physics-based approches involved other descriptions of the \
relevant\nspaces of BPS states). The starting point is a system of D3-branes \
ending on an\nNS5-brane with a nonzero theta-angle. On the one hand, this \
system can be\nrelated to a Chern-Simons gauge theory on the boundary of the \
D3-brane\nworldvolume; on the other hand, it can be studied by standard \
techniques of\n$S$-duality and $T$-duality. Combining the two approaches \
leads to a new and\nmanifestly invariant description of the Jones polynomial \
of knots, and its\ngeneralizations, and to a manifestly invariant description \
of Khovanov\nhomology, in terms of certain elliptic partial differential \
equations in four\nand five dimensions.\n", 
