               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Spectrum of Excitations of Holographic Wilson \
Loops\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28+23 pages, 3 tables, no figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1105:018,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2011)018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"MCTP-11-02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the holographic framework, a half BPS Wilson loop in \
${\\\\cal N}=4$\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills in the fundamental, symmetric or \
antisymmetric\\nrepresentation of SU(N), is best described by a fundamental \
string, a D3 brane\\nor a D5 brane with fluxes in their worldvolumes, \
respectively. We derive the\\nspectrum of excitations of such D3 brane in \
$AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ explicitly,\\nconsidering its action in both the bosonic \
and the fermionic sectors, and\\ndemonstrate that it is organized according \
to short multiplets of the\\nsupergroup $OSp(4^*|4)$. We also show that the \
modes of the fundamental string\\nform an ultra-short multiplet of this \
supergroup. In the case of the D5 brane\\nthe bosonic spectrum is only \
partially known but we argue that it also fills\\nrepresentations of \
$OSp(4^*|4)$. This way we provide a step towards a unifying\\npicture for the \
description of holographic excitations of the circular and\\nstraight \
supersymmetric Wilson loops in arbitrary representations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
