            "report-no" -> "MCTP-11-02", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In the holographic framework, a half BPS Wilson loop in \
${\\cal N}=4$\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills in the fundamental, symmetric or \
antisymmetric\nrepresentation of SU(N), is best described by a fundamental \
string, a D3 brane\nor a D5 brane with fluxes in their worldvolumes, \
respectively. We derive the\nspectrum of excitations of such D3 brane in \
$AdS_5\\times S^5$ explicitly,\nconsidering its action in both the bosonic \
and the fermionic sectors, and\ndemonstrate that it is organized according to \
short multiplets of the\nsupergroup $OSp(4^*|4)$. We also show that the modes \
of the fundamental string\nform an ultra-short multiplet of this supergroup. \
In the case of the D5 brane\nthe bosonic spectrum is only partially known but \
we argue that it also fills\nrepresentations of $OSp(4^*|4)$. This way we \
provide a step towards a unifying\npicture for the description of holographic \
excitations of the circular and\nstraight supersymmetric Wilson loops in \
arbitrary representations.\n", 
