        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.74558726827934, -7.033730027189929}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1102.0153\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jan Troost\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jan Troost\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Massless particles on supergroups and AdS3 x S3 \
supergravity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"16 pages, 10 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1107:042,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2011)042\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Firstly, we study the state space of a massless \
particle on a supergroup with\\na reparameterization invariant action. After \
gauge fixing the\\nreparameterization invariance, we compute the physical \
state space through the\\nBRST cohomology and show that the quadratic Casimir \
Hamiltonian becomes\\ndiagonalizable in cohomology. We illustrate the general \
mechanism in detail in\\nthe example of a supergroup target GL(1|1). The \
space of physical states\\nremains an indecomposable infinite dimensional \
representation of the space-time\\nsupersymmetry algebra. Secondly, we show \
how the full string BRST cohomology in\\nthe particle limit of string theory \
on AdS3 x S3 renders the quadratic Casimir\\ndiagonalizable, and reduces the \
Hilbert space to finite dimensional\\nrepresentations of the space-time \
supersymmetry algebra (after analytic\\ncontinuation). Our analysis provides \
an efficient way to calculate the\\nKaluza-Klein spectrum for supergravity on \
AdS3 x S3. It may also be a step\\ntowards the identification of an \
interesting and simpler subsector of\\nlogarithmic supergroup conformal field \
theories, relevant to string theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 1 Feb 2011 13:26:33 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 27 Jun 2011 11:46:58 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-07-13\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Troost\"", ",", "\"Jan\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
