           "id" -> "1102.0153", "submitter" -> "Jan Troost", "authors" -> 
            "Jan Troost", "title" -> 
            "Massless particles on supergroups and AdS3 x S3 supergravity", 
            "comments" -> "16 pages, 10 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 1107:042,2011", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP07(2011)042", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Firstly, we study the state space of a massless particle on a \
supergroup with\na reparameterization invariant action. After gauge fixing \
the\nreparameterization invariance, we compute the physical state space \
through the\nBRST cohomology and show that the quadratic Casimir Hamiltonian \
becomes\ndiagonalizable in cohomology. We illustrate the general mechanism in \
detail in\nthe example of a supergroup target GL(1|1). The space of physical \
states\nremains an indecomposable infinite dimensional representation of the \
space-time\nsupersymmetry algebra. Secondly, we show how the full string BRST \
cohomology in\nthe particle limit of string theory on AdS3 x S3 renders the \
quadratic Casimir\ndiagonalizable, and reduces the Hilbert space to finite \
dimensional\nrepresentations of the space-time supersymmetry algebra (after \
analytic\ncontinuation). Our analysis provides an efficient way to calculate \
the\nKaluza-Klein spectrum for supergravity on AdS3 x S3. It may also be a \
step\ntowards the identification of an interesting and simpler subsector of\n\
logarithmic supergroup conformal field theories, relevant to string theory.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 1 Feb 2011 13:26:33 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 27 Jun 2011 11:46:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-07-13", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Troost", "Jan", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
