Mattelliano and Roberto\\n  Tateo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the $AdS_5/CFT_4$ TBA and its analytic \
properties\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex, 32 pages, 25 figures. Contribution to the \
Proceedings of the\\n  conference \\\"Infinite Analysis 10: Developments in \
Quantum Integrable\\n  Systems\\\", RIMS (Kyoto June 14 -- 16, 2010)\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz equations arising in the \
context of the\\n$AdS_5/CFT_4$ correspondence exhibit an important difference \
with respect to\\ntheir analogues in relativistic integrable quantum field \
theories: their\\nsolutions (the Y functions) are not meromorphic functions \
of the rapidity, but\\nlive on a complicated Riemann surface with an infinite \
number of branch points\\nand therefore enjoy a new kind of extended \
Y-system. In this paper we review\\nthe analytic properties of the TBA \
solutions, and present new information\\ncoming from their numerical study. \
An identity allowing to simplify the\\nequations and the numerical \
implementation is presented, together with various\\nplots which highlight \
the analytic structure of the Y functions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
