               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1103.0786\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Donovan Young\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Abhishek Agarwal, Donovan Young\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Manifest SO(N) invariance and S-matrices of \
three-dimensional N=2,4,8\\n  SYM\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"28 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1105:100,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2011)100\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  An on-shell formalism for the computation of S-matrices \
of SYM theories in\\nthree spacetime dimensions is presented. The framework \
is a generalization of\\nthe spinor-helicity formalism in four dimensions. \
The formalism is applied to\\nestablish the manifest SO(N) covariance of the \
on-shell superalgebra relevant\\nto N =2,4 and 8 SYM theories in d=3. The \
results are then used to argue for the\\nSO(N) invariance of the S-matrices \
of these theories: a claim which is proved\\nexplicitly for the four-particle \
scattering amplitudes. Recursion relations\\nrelating tree amplitudes of \
three-dimensional SYM theories are shown to follow\\nfrom their \
four-dimensional counterparts. The results for the four-particle\\namplitudes \
are verified by tree-level perturbative computations and a unitarity\\nbased \
construction of the integrand corresponding to the leading \
perturbative\\ncorrection is also presented for the N=8 theory. For N=8 SYM, \
the manifest\\nSO(8) symmetry is used to develop a map between the \
color-ordered amplitudes of\\nthe SYM and superconformal Chern-Simons \
theories, providing a direct connection\\nbetween on-shell observables of D2 \
and M2-brane theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 3 Mar 2011 21:10:26 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
