            "  An on-shell formalism for the computation of S-matrices of SYM \
theories in\nthree spacetime dimensions is presented. The framework is a \
generalization of\nthe spinor-helicity formalism in four dimensions. The \
formalism is applied to\nestablish the manifest SO(N) covariance of the \
on-shell superalgebra relevant\nto N =2,4 and 8 SYM theories in d=3. The \
results are then used to argue for the\nSO(N) invariance of the S-matrices of \
these theories: a claim which is proved\nexplicitly for the four-particle \
scattering amplitudes. Recursion relations\nrelating tree amplitudes of \
three-dimensional SYM theories are shown to follow\nfrom their \
four-dimensional counterparts. The results for the four-particle\namplitudes \
are verified by tree-level perturbative computations and a unitarity\nbased \
construction of the integrand corresponding to the leading perturbative\n\
correction is also presented for the N=8 theory. For N=8 SYM, the manifest\n\
SO(8) symmetry is used to develop a map between the color-ordered amplitudes \
of\nthe SYM and superconformal Chern-Simons theories, providing a direct \
connection\nbetween on-shell observables of D2 and M2-brane theories.\n", 
