               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1103.2024\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jun-Bao Wu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Dongsu Bak, Bin Chen and Jun-Bao Wu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic Correlation Functions for Open Strings and \
Branes\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"25 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1106:014,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2011)014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper, we compute holographically the two-point \
and three-point\\nfunctions of giant gravitons with open strings. We consider \
the maximal giant\\ngraviton in $S^5$ and the string configurations \
corresponding to the ground\\nstates of Z=0 and Y=0 open spin chain, and the \
spinning string in AdS$_5$\\ncorresponding to the derivative type impurities \
in Y=0 or Z=0 open spin chain\\nas well. We treat the D-brane and open string \
contribution separately and find\\nthe corresponding D3-brane and string \
configurations in bulk which connect the\\ncomposite operators at the AdS$_5$ \
boundary. We apply a new prescription to\\ntreat the string state \
contribution and find agreements for the two-point\\nfunctions. For the \
three-point functions of two giant gravitons with open\\nstrings and one \
certain half-BPS chiral primary operator, we find that the\\nD-brane \
contributions to structure constant are always vanishing and the \
open\\nstring contribution for the Y=0 ground state is in perfect match with \
the\\nprediction in the free field limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
