            "  In this paper, we compute holographically the two-point and \
three-point\nfunctions of giant gravitons with open strings. We consider the \
maximal giant\ngraviton in $S^5$ and the string configurations corresponding \
to the ground\nstates of Z=0 and Y=0 open spin chain, and the spinning string \
in AdS$_5$\ncorresponding to the derivative type impurities in Y=0 or Z=0 \
open spin chain\nas well. We treat the D-brane and open string contribution \
separately and find\nthe corresponding D3-brane and string configurations in \
bulk which connect the\ncomposite operators at the AdS$_5$ boundary. We apply \
a new prescription to\ntreat the string state contribution and find \
agreements for the two-point\nfunctions. For the three-point functions of two \
giant gravitons with open\nstrings and one certain half-BPS chiral primary \
operator, we find that the\nD-brane contributions to structure constant are \
always vanishing and the open\nstring contribution for the Y=0 ground state \
is in perfect match with the\nprediction in the free field limit.\n", 
