               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"B. Hoare and A. A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Towards the quantum S-matrix of the Pohlmeyer reduced \
version of AdS_5 x\\n  S^5 superstring theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"61 pages, 2 figures; v2: minor corrections and reference \
added; v3:\\n  minor corrections\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B851:161-237,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2011.05.016\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-BH-2011-01\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the structure of the quantum S-matrix \
for perturbative\\nexcitations of the Pohlmeyer reduced version of the AdS_5 \
x S^5 superstring\\nfollowing arXiv:0912.2958. The reduced theory is a \
fermionic extension of a\\ngauged WZW model with an integrable potential. We \
use as an input the result of\\nthe one-loop perturbative scattering \
amplitude computation and an analogy with\\nsimpler reduced AdS_n x S^n \
theories with n=2,3. The n=2 theory is equivalent\\nto the N=2 2-d \
supersymmetric sine-Gordon model for which the exact quantum\\nS-matrix is \
known. In the n=3 case the one-loop perturbative S-matrix, improved\\nby a \
contribution of a local counterterm, satisfies the group \
factorization\\nproperty and the Yang-Baxter equation, and reveals the \
existence of a novel\\nquantum-deformed 2-d supersymmetry which is not \
manifest in the action. The\\none-loop perturbative S-matrix of the reduced \
AdS_5 x S^5 theory has the group\\nfactorisation property but does not \
satisfy the Yang-Baxter equation suggesting\\nsome subtlety with the \
realisation of quantum integrability. As a possible\\nresolution, we propose \
that the S-matrix of this theory may be identified with\\nthe \
quantum-deformed [psu(2|2)]^2 x R^2 symmetric R-matrix constructed \
in\\narXiv:1002.1097. We conjecture the exact all-order form of this S-matrix \
and\\ndiscuss its possible relation to the perturbative S-matrix defined by \
the path\\nintegral. As in the AdS_3 x S^3 case the symmetry of the S-matrix \
may be\\ninterpreted as an extended quantum-deformed 2-d \
supersymmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
