           "id" -> "1104.2423", "submitter" -> "Ben Hoare", "authors" -> 
            "B. Hoare and A. A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Towards the quantum S-matrix of the Pohlmeyer reduced version of \
AdS_5 x\n  S^5 superstring theory", "comments" -> 
            "61 pages, 2 figures; v2: minor corrections and reference added; \
v3:\n  minor corrections", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B851:161-237,2011", 
            "doi" -> "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2011.05.016", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-BH-2011-01", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate the structure of the quantum S-matrix for \
perturbative\nexcitations of the Pohlmeyer reduced version of the AdS_5 x S^5 \
superstring\nfollowing arXiv:0912.2958. The reduced theory is a fermionic \
extension of a\ngauged WZW model with an integrable potential. We use as an \
input the result of\nthe one-loop perturbative scattering amplitude \
computation and an analogy with\nsimpler reduced AdS_n x S^n theories with \
n=2,3. The n=2 theory is equivalent\nto the N=2 2-d supersymmetric \
sine-Gordon model for which the exact quantum\nS-matrix is known. In the n=3 \
case the one-loop perturbative S-matrix, improved\nby a contribution of a \
local counterterm, satisfies the group factorization\nproperty and the \
Yang-Baxter equation, and reveals the existence of a novel\nquantum-deformed \
2-d supersymmetry which is not manifest in the action. The\none-loop \
perturbative S-matrix of the reduced AdS_5 x S^5 theory has the group\n\
factorisation property but does not satisfy the Yang-Baxter equation \
suggesting\nsome subtlety with the realisation of quantum integrability. As a \
possible\nresolution, we propose that the S-matrix of this theory may be \
identified with\nthe quantum-deformed [psu(2|2)]^2 x R^2 symmetric R-matrix \
constructed in\narXiv:1002.1097. We conjecture the exact all-order form of \
this S-matrix and\ndiscuss its possible relation to the perturbative S-matrix \
defined by the path\nintegral. As in the AdS_3 x S^3 case the symmetry of the \
S-matrix may be\ninterpreted as an extended quantum-deformed 2-d \
supersymmetry.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 13 Apr 2011 09:23:47 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 23 May 2011 14:55:17 GMT"}, {
