                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study analytical properties of the five-loop \
anomalous dimension of\\ntwist-2 operators at negative even values of Lorentz \
spin. Following L. N.\\nLipatov and A. I. Onishchenko, we have found two \
possible generalizations of\\ndouble-logarithmic equation, which allow to \
predict a lot of poles of anomalous\\ndimension of twist-2 operators at all \
orders of perturbative theory from the\\nknown results. Second generalization \
is related with the reciprocity-respecting\\nfunction, which is a \
single-logarithmic function in this case. We have found,\\nthat the knowledge \
of first orders of the reciprocity-respecting function gives\\nall-loop \
predictions for the highest poles. Obtained predictions can be used\\nfor the \
reconstruction of a general form of the wrapping corrections for\\ntwist-2 \
operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
