        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.784494871221277`, -5.386594715016809}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1105.0480\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Justin David R\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Justin R. David and Abhishake Sadhukhan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Classical integrability in the BTZ black hole\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages, Reference added, typos corrected, discussion on \
geodesics\\n  improved to include all geodesics\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2011)079\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the fact the BTZ black hole is a quotient of \
AdS_3 we show that\\nclassical string propagation in the BTZ background is \
integrable. We construct\\nthe flat connection and its monodromy matrix which \
generates the non-local\\ncharges. From examining the general behaviour of \
the eigen values of the\\nmonodromy matrix we determine the set of integral \
equations which constrain\\nthem. These equations imply that each classical \
solution is characterized by a\\ndensity function in the complex plane. For \
classical solutions which correspond\\nto geodesics and winding strings we \
solve for the eigen values of the monodromy\\nmatrix explicitly and show that \
geodesics correspond to zero density in the\\ncomplex plane. We solve the \
integral equations for BMN and magnon like\\nsolutions and obtain their \
dispersion relation. Finally we show that the set of\\nintegral equations \
which constrain the eigen values of the monodromy matrix can\\nbe identified \
with the continuum limit of the Bethe equations of a twisted\\nSL(2, R) spin \
chain at one loop.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 3 May 2011 06:07:37 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 27 May 2011 06:50:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-05-28\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
