          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1105.0480", "submitter" -> "Justin David R", "authors" -> 
            "Justin R. David and Abhishake Sadhukhan", "title" -> 
            "Classical integrability in the BTZ black hole", "comments" -> 
            "45 pages, Reference added, typos corrected, discussion on \
geodesics\n  improved to include all geodesics", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP08(2011)079", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Using the fact the BTZ black hole is a quotient of AdS_3 we \
show that\nclassical string propagation in the BTZ background is integrable. \
We construct\nthe flat connection and its monodromy matrix which generates \
the non-local\ncharges. From examining the general behaviour of the eigen \
values of the\nmonodromy matrix we determine the set of integral equations \
which constrain\nthem. These equations imply that each classical solution is \
characterized by a\ndensity function in the complex plane. For classical \
solutions which correspond\nto geodesics and winding strings we solve for the \
eigen values of the monodromy\nmatrix explicitly and show that geodesics \
correspond to zero density in the\ncomplex plane. We solve the integral \
equations for BMN and magnon like\nsolutions and obtain their dispersion \
relation. Finally we show that the set of\nintegral equations which constrain \
the eigen values of the monodromy matrix can\nbe identified with the \
continuum limit of the Bethe equations of a twisted\nSL(2, R) spin chain at \
one loop.\n", 
