               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On strong-coupling correlation functions of circular \
Wilson loops and\\n  local operators\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25 pages,v3:small changes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A44:395401,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/44/39/395401\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Motivated by the problem of understanding 3-point \
correlation functions of\\ngauge-invariant operators in N =4 super Yang-Mills \
theory we consider\\ncorrelators involving Wilson loops and a \\\"light\\\" \
operator with fixed quantum\\nnumbers. At leading order in the strong \
coupling expansion such correlators are\\ngiven by the \\\"light\\\" vertex \
operator evaluated on a semiclassical string world\\nsurface ending on the \
corresponding loops at the boundary of AdS_5 x S^5. We\\nstudy in detail the \
example of a correlator of two concentric circular Wilson\\nloops and a \
dilaton vertex operator. The resulting expression is given by an\\nintegral \
of combinations of elliptic functions and can be computed analytically\\nin \
some special limits. We also consider a generalization of the \
minimal\\nsurface ending on two circles to the case of non-zero angular \
momentum J in S^5\\nand discuss a special limit when one of the Wilson loops \
is effectively\\nreplaced by a \\\"heavy\\\" operator with charge \
J.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
