            "authors" -> "Luis F. Alday and Arkady A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "On strong-coupling correlation functions of circular Wilson \
loops and\n  local operators", "comments" -> "25 pages,v3:small changes", 
            "journal-ref" -> "J.Phys.A44:395401,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/44/39/395401", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Motivated by the problem of understanding 3-point correlation \
functions of\ngauge-invariant operators in N =4 super Yang-Mills theory we \
consider\ncorrelators involving Wilson loops and a \"light\" operator with \
fixed quantum\nnumbers. At leading order in the strong coupling expansion \
such correlators are\ngiven by the \"light\" vertex operator evaluated on a \
semiclassical string world\nsurface ending on the corresponding loops at the \
boundary of AdS_5 x S^5. We\nstudy in detail the example of a correlator of \
two concentric circular Wilson\nloops and a dilaton vertex operator. The \
resulting expression is given by an\nintegral of combinations of elliptic \
functions and can be computed analytically\nin some special limits. We also \
consider a generalization of the minimal\nsurface ending on two circles to \
the case of non-zero angular momentum J in S^5\nand discuss a special limit \
when one of the Wilson loops is effectively\nreplaced by a \"heavy\" operator \
with charge J.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
