               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Hovhannes Grigoryan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hovhannes R. Grigoryan and Yuri V. Kovchegov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gravity Dual Corrections to the Heavy Quark Potential \
at\\n  Finite-Temperature\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages, 14 figures; v2: refs added, typos \
corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B852:1-38,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2011.06.009\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th hep-lat hep-ph nucl-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We apply gauge/gravity duality to compute $1/N^2_c$ \
corrections to the heavy\\nquark potentials of a quark--anti-quark pair ($Q\\\
\\bar Q$) and of a quark--quark\\npair ($QQ$) immersed into the strongly \
coupled N = 4 SYM plasma. On the gravity\\nside these corrections come from \
the exchanges of supergravity modes between\\ntwo string worldsheets \
stretching from the UV boundary of AdS space to the\\nblack hole horizon in \
the bulk and smeared over $S^5$. We find that the\\ncontributions to the $Q\\\
\\bar Q$ potential coming from the exchanges of all of\\nthe relevant modes \
(such as dilaton, massive scalar, 2-form field, and\\ngraviton) are all \
attractive, leading to an attractive net $Q\\\\bar Q$ potential.\\nWe show \
that at large separations $r$ and/or high-temperature $T$ the potential\\nis \
of Yukawa-type, dominated by the graviton exchange, in agreement \
with\\nearlier findings. On the other hand, at small-$r T$ the $Q\\\\bar Q$ \
potential\\nscales as $\\\\sim (1/r) \\\\ln (1/rT)$. In the case of $QQ$ \
potential the 2-form\\ncontribution changes sign and becomes repulsive: \
however, the net $QQ$\\npotential remains attractive. At large-$r T$ it is \
dominated by the graviton\\nexchange, while at small-$r T$ the $QQ$ potential \
becomes Coulomb-like.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 11 May 2011 20:01:02 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 Jun 2011 18:46:17 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-08-05\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Grigoryan\"", ",", "\"Hovhannes R.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Kovchegov\"", ",", "\"Yuri V.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
