                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the Pohlmeyer reduced sigma model \
describing AdS$_5$ minimal\\nsurfaces. We show that, similar to the affine \
Toda models, there exists a\\nconformal extension to this model which admits \
a Lax formulation. The Lax\\nconnection is shown to be valued in a \
${\\\\mathbb Z}_4$-invariant subalgebra of\\nthe affine Lie algebra \
$\\\\widehat{su(4)}$. Using this, we perform a modified\\nversion of a \
Laznov-Savelev analysis, which allows us to write formal\\nexpressions for \
the general solutions for the Pohlmeyer reduced AdS$_5$ theory.\\nThis \
analysis relies on the a certain decomposition for the \
exponentiated\\nalgebra elements.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 16 May 2011 21:28:24 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-09-06\""}]}, {
