         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1105.3227", "submitter" -> "Benjamin Burrington", 
            "authors" -> "Benjamin A. Burrington", "title" -> 
            "General Leznov-Savelev solutions for Pohlmeyer reduced AdS$_5$ \
minimal\n  surfaces", "comments" -> "29 pages + 7 pages appendices", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1109:002,2011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP09(2011)002", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the Pohlmeyer reduced sigma model describing \
AdS$_5$ minimal\nsurfaces. We show that, similar to the affine Toda models, \
there exists a\nconformal extension to this model which admits a Lax \
formulation. The Lax\nconnection is shown to be valued in a ${\\mathbb \
Z}_4$-invariant subalgebra of\nthe affine Lie algebra $\\widehat{su(4)}$. \
Using this, we perform a modified\nversion of a Laznov-Savelev analysis, \
which allows us to write formal\nexpressions for the general solutions for \
the Pohlmeyer reduced AdS$_5$ theory.\nThis analysis relies on the a certain \
decomposition for the exponentiated\nalgebra elements.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 16 May 2011 21:28:24 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-09-06", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Burrington", "Benjamin A.", ""}}}], 
