            "Bi-harmonic superspace for N=4 d=4 super Yang-Mills", "comments" -> 
            "1+19 pages; minor corrections, references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP09(2011)056", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We develop N=4 d=4 bi-harmonic superspace and use it to derive \
a novel form\nfor the low-energy effective action in N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory. We solve\nthe N=4 supergauge constraints in this superspace in terms \
of analytic\nsuperfields. Using these superfields, we construct a simple \
functional that\nrespects N=4 supersymmetry and scale invariance. In \
components, it reproduces\nall on-shell terms in the four-derivative part of \
the N=4 SYM effective action;\nin particular, the F^4/X^4 and Wess-Zumino \
terms. The latter comes out in a\nnovel SO(3) x SO(3)-invariant form.\n", 
