                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The dilatation operator of planar N=4 super Yang-Mills \
in the pure scalar\\nSO(6) sector is derived at the two-loop order. \
Representation theory allows for\\neight free coefficients in an ansatz for \
the corresponding spin-chain\\nhamiltonian acting on three adjacent scalar \
states. While four out of these\\nfollow from the known SU(2|3) sector \
two-loop dilatation operator, the\\nremaining four coefficients are derived \
by diagrammatic techniques and a match\\nto the known dimension of a length \
three primary operator. Finally, comments\\nupon the use of this result for \
the evaluation of three-point structure\\nfunctions of scalar operators at \
the one-loop order are given.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
