               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1106.0737\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Michael Abbott\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Michael C. Abbott (TIFR) and Per Sundin (UCT)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Near-Flat-Space and BMN Limits for Strings in AdS4 x \
CP3 at One Loop\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"32 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Phys. A 45 (2012) 025401\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8113/45/2/025401\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"TIFR/TH/11-25\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper studies type IIA string theory in AdS4 x CP3 \
in both the BMN limit\\nand the Maldacena-Swanson or near-flat-space limit. \
We derive the simpler\\nLagrangian for the latter limit by taking a large \
worldsheet boost of the BMN\\ntheory. We then calculate one-loop corrections \
to the correlators of the\\nvarious fields using both theories. In all cases \
the near-flat-space results\\nagree with a limit of the BMN results, \
providing evidence for the quantum\\nconsistency of this truncation. The \
corrections can also be compared to an\\nexpansion of the exact dispersion \
relation, known from integrability apart from\\none interpolating function \
h(lambda). Here we see agreement with the results of\\nMcLoughlin, Roiban & \
Tseytlin, and we observe that it does not appear to be\\npossible to fully \
implement the cutoff suggested by Gromov & Mikhaylov,\\nalthough for some \
terms we can do so. In both the near-flat-space and BMN\\ncalculations there \
are some extra terms in the mass shifts which break\\nsupersymmetry. These \
terms are extremely sensitive to the cutoff used, and can\\nperhaps be seen \
as a consequence of using dimensional regularisation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 3 Jun 2011 19:58:46 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
