         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1106.0737", "submitter" -> "Michael Abbott", "authors" -> 
            "Michael C. Abbott (TIFR) and Per Sundin (UCT)", "title" -> 
            "The Near-Flat-Space and BMN Limits for Strings in AdS4 x CP3 at \
One Loop", "comments" -> "32 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J. Phys. A 45 (2012) 025401", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/45/2/025401", "report-no" -> "TIFR/TH/11-25", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This paper studies type IIA string theory in AdS4 x CP3 in \
both the BMN limit\nand the Maldacena-Swanson or near-flat-space limit. We \
derive the simpler\nLagrangian for the latter limit by taking a large \
worldsheet boost of the BMN\ntheory. We then calculate one-loop corrections \
to the correlators of the\nvarious fields using both theories. In all cases \
the near-flat-space results\nagree with a limit of the BMN results, providing \
evidence for the quantum\nconsistency of this truncation. The corrections can \
also be compared to an\nexpansion of the exact dispersion relation, known \
from integrability apart from\none interpolating function h(lambda). Here we \
see agreement with the results of\nMcLoughlin, Roiban & Tseytlin, and we \
observe that it does not appear to be\npossible to fully implement the cutoff \
suggested by Gromov & Mikhaylov,\nalthough for some terms we can do so. In \
both the near-flat-space and BMN\ncalculations there are some extra terms in \
the mass shifts which break\nsupersymmetry. These terms are extremely \
sensitive to the cutoff used, and can\nperhaps be seen as a consequence of \
using dimensional regularisation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 3 Jun 2011 19:58:46 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-12-12", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Abbott", "Michael C.", "", "TIFR"}, {
              "Sundin", "Per", "", "UCT"}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
