           "id" -> "1106.4298", "submitter" -> "Dimo Arnaudov", "authors" -> 
            "D. Arnaudov, R.C. Rashkov", "title" -> 
            "Three-point correlators: Examples from Lunin-Maldacena \
background", "comments" -> 
            "11 pages, no figures, incorrect subsection removed, typos fixed,\
\n  references added and updated", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys. Rev. D 84, 086009 (2011)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.84.086009", "report-no" -> "TUW-11-11", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently there has been progress on the calculation of \
three-point functions\nwith two \"heavy\" operators via semiclassical \
methods. We extend this analysis\nto the case of the Lunin-Maldacena \
background, and examine the suggested\nprocedure for several simple string \
solutions. By making use of AdS/CFT\nduality, we derive the relevant \
correlation functions of operators belonging to\nthe dual N=1 superconformal \
gauge theory, and recover an important relation\nconnecting the dimensions of \
\"heavy\" states and the structure constants.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 21 Jun 2011 19:30:28 GMT"}, {
