           "id" -> "1106.4978", "submitter" -> "Alexander Krikun", "authors" -> 
            "P. N. Kopnin, A. Krikun", "title" -> 
            "Wilson loops in holographic models with a gluon condensate", 
            "comments" -> "24 pages, 6 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.84.066002", "report-no" -> "ITEP-TH-19/11", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The aim of this work is to study the holographic dual to the \
gauge theory\nwith a nonzero gluon condensate. We check for consistency the \
holographic way\nof describing the condensate and calculate the expectation \
value of a small\nWilson loop in the presence of the gluon condensate, thus \
obtaining the\nrelevant coefficient in the operator product expansion of the \
small loop in\ndifferent holographic models. We also study the effect of the \
condensate on the\nGross-Ooguri phase transition in the correlator of two \
circular Wilson loops in\nparallel and concentric configurations. In the \
numerical study of the\nconcentric case, we find that the phase transition \
changes its order when the\nsize of the loops is of order of the gluon \
condensate. We report this change of\nthe phase transition order to be a new \
effect in Wilson loop correlators.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 24 Jun 2011 14:30:25 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2013-05-29", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kopnin", "P. N.", ""}, {
              "Krikun", "A.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
