 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We describe an analytic continuation of the Euclidean \
Grosse-Wulkenhaar and\\nLSZ models which defines a one-parameter family of \
duality covariant\\nnoncommutative field theories interpolating between \
Euclidean and Minkowski\\nspace versions of these models, and provides an \
alternative regularization to\\nthe usual Feynman prescription. This \
regularization allows for a matrix model\\nrepresentation of the field \
theories in terms of a complex generalization of\\nthe usual basis of Landau \
wavefunctions. The corresponding propagators are\\ncalculated and identified \
with the Feynman propagators of the field theories.\\nThe regulated quantum \
field theories are shown to be UV/IR-duality covariant.\\nWe study the \
asymptotics of the regularized propagators in position and matrix\\nspace \
representations, and confirm that they generically possess a \
comparably\\ngood decay behaviour as in the Euclidean case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
