                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold Steinacker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"Athanasios Chatzistavrakidis, Harold Steinacker, George \
Zoupanos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Intersecting branes and a standard model realization in \
matrix models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages. V2: discussion on SUSY added V3: improved \
discussion of the\\n  Higgs sector\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP09(2011)115\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2011)115\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UWThPh-2011-21\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider intersecting brane solutions of the type \
IIB matrix model. It is\\nshown that fermionic zero-modes arise on such \
backgrounds, localized at the\\nbrane intersections. They lead to chiral \
fermions in four dimensions under\\ncertain conditions. Such configurations \
reproduce many of the welcome features\\nin similar string-theoretic \
constructions. Therefore they can be used to\\nconstruct semi-realistic \
particle physics models in the framework of Yang-Mills\\nmatrix models. In \
particular, we present a brane configuration which realizes\\nthe correct \
chiral spectrum of the standard model in the matrix model.\\nFurthermore, the \
stability of intersecting branes is discussed by analyzing the\\n1-loop \
effective action. It is shown that intersecting branes may form a \
bound\\nstate for certain flux configurations. The four-dimensional geometry \
of the\\nbranes is generic, and determined by the (emergent) gravity sector \
of the\\nmatrix model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
