                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"More three-point correlators of giant magnons with finite \
size\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"14 pages, no figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1108:121,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2011)121\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the framework of the semiclassical approach, we \
compute the normalized\\nstructure constants in three-point correlation \
functions, when two of the\\nvertex operators correspond to heavy string \
states, while the third vertex\\ncorresponds to a light state. This is done \
for the case when the heavy string\\nstates are finite-size giant magnons \
with one or two angular momenta, and for\\ntwo different choices of the light \
state, corresponding to dilaton operator and\\nprimary scalar operator. The \
relevant operators in the dual gauge theory are\\nTr(F_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}^2 \
Z^j+...) and Tr(Z^j). We first consider the case of AdS_5 x S^5\\nand N = 4 \
super Yang-Mills. Then we extend the obtained results to the\\ngamma-deformed \
AdS_5 x S^5_\\\\gamma, dual to N = 1 super Yang-Mills theory,\\narising as an \
exactly marginal deformation of N = 4 super Yang-Mills.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 13 Jul 2011 19:54:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
