            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In the framework of the semiclassical approach, we compute the \
normalized\nstructure constants in three-point correlation functions, when \
two of the\nvertex operators correspond to heavy string states, while the \
third vertex\ncorresponds to a light state. This is done for the case when \
the heavy string\nstates are finite-size giant magnons with one or two \
angular momenta, and for\ntwo different choices of the light state, \
corresponding to dilaton operator and\nprimary scalar operator. The relevant \
operators in the dual gauge theory are\nTr(F_{\\mu\\nu}^2 Z^j+...) and \
Tr(Z^j). We first consider the case of AdS_5 x S^5\nand N = 4 super \
Yang-Mills. Then we extend the obtained results to the\ngamma-deformed AdS_5 \
x S^5_\\gamma, dual to N = 1 super Yang-Mills theory,\narising as an exactly \
marginal deformation of N = 4 super Yang-Mills.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
