               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1107.3139\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marco Stefano Bianchi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marco S. Bianchi, Matias Leoni, Andrea Mauri, Silvia \
Penati and\\n  Alberto Santambrogio\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Scattering Amplitudes/Wilson Loop Duality In ABJM \
Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+16 pages, 2 figures, minor modifications and references \
added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2012)056\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  For N=6 superconformal Chern-Simons-matter theories in \
three dimensions, by a\\ndirect superspace Feynman diagram approach, we \
compute the two-loop four-point\\nscattering amplitude with external chiral \
matter fields. We find that the\\nresult is in perfect agreement with the \
two-loop result for a light-like\\nfour-polygon Wilson loop. This is a \
nontrivial evidence of the scattering\\namplitudes/Wilson loop duality in \
three dimensions. Moreover, both the IR\\ndivergent and the finite parts of \
our two-loop result agree with a BDS-like\\nansatz for all-loop amplitudes \
where the scaling function is given in terms of\\nthe N=4 SYM one, according \
to the conjectured Bethe equations for ABJM.\\nConsequently, we are able to \
make a prediction for the four-loop correction to\\nthe amplitude. We also \
discuss the dual conformal invariance of the two-loop\\nresult.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
