            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  For N=6 superconformal Chern-Simons-matter theories in three \
dimensions, by a\ndirect superspace Feynman diagram approach, we compute the \
two-loop four-point\nscattering amplitude with external chiral matter fields. \
We find that the\nresult is in perfect agreement with the two-loop result for \
a light-like\nfour-polygon Wilson loop. This is a nontrivial evidence of the \
scattering\namplitudes/Wilson loop duality in three dimensions. Moreover, \
both the IR\ndivergent and the finite parts of our two-loop result agree with \
a BDS-like\nansatz for all-loop amplitudes where the scaling function is \
given in terms of\nthe N=4 SYM one, according to the conjectured Bethe \
equations for ABJM.\nConsequently, we are able to make a prediction for the \
four-loop correction to\nthe amplitude. We also discuss the dual conformal \
invariance of the two-loop\nresult.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
