            "  We present a systematic search for Type IIB supergravity \
solutions whose\nspacetimes include AdS5 and S2 factors, which would be \
candidate duals to N = 2\nfour-dimensional Superconformal field theories. The \
candidate solutions encode\nthe SU(2) R-symmetry geometrically on the S2 and \
an additional Killing vector\ngenerates the U(1) R-symmetry. By analysing the \
Killing spinor equations we\nshow that no such solutions exist. This suggests \
that, if Type IIB backgrounds\ndual to N = 2 SCFTs exist, the SU(2) \
R-symmetry is realised non-geometrically.\nFinally, we also show that, in the \
context of both N = 1 and N = 2 Type IIB\nbackgrounds with an AdS5 factor, \
the only candidate U(1) R-symmetry Killing\nvector directions are the ones \
that appear for generic values of the Killing\nspinors; no further Killing \
vectors exist for special values of the Killing\nspinors.\n", 
