         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1107.5795", "submitter" -> "Michal Michalcik", "authors" -> 
            "Michal Michalcik, Radoslav C. Rashkov and Maria Schimpf", 
            "title" -> 
            "On semiclassical calculation of three-point functions in AdS_5 \
\\times\n  T^(1,1)", "comments" -> "18 pages, added reference", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1142/S0217732312500915", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently there has been progress on the computation of two- \
and three-point\ncorrelation functions with two \"heavy\" states via \
semiclassical methods. We\nextend this analysis to the case of AdS_5 \\times \
T^(1,1), and examine the\nsuggested procedure for the case of several simple \
string solutions. By making\nuse of AdS/CFT duality, we derive the relevant \
correlation functions of\noperators belonging to the dual gauge theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 28 Jul 2011 19:05:24 GMT"}, {
