               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On Lie-algebraic solutions of the type IIB matrix \
model\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"22 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.84.106010\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A systematic search for Lie algebra solutions of the \
type IIB matrix model is\\nperformed. Our survey is based on the \
classification of all Lie algebras for\\ndimensions up to five and of all \
nilpotent Lie algebras of dimension six. It is\\nshown that Lie-type \
solutions of the equations of motion of the type IIB matrix\\nmodel exist and \
they correspond to certain nilpotent and solvable Lie algebras.\\nTheir \
representation in terms of Hermitian matrices is discussed in detail.\\nThese \
algebras give rise to certain non-commutative spaces for which \
the\\ncorresponding star-products are provided. Finally the issue of \
constructing\\nquantized compact nilmanifolds and solvmanifolds based on the \
above algebras is\\naddressed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
