               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Konishi superconformal multiplet is an important \
theoretical laboratory\\nwhere one can test AdS/CFT methods to compute strong \
coupling corrections to\\nthe spectrum of superstrings in AdS_5 x S^5. In \
particular, one can exploit\\nintegrability for finite charge \
states/operators. The multiplet ground state is\\na singlet operator with two \
simple descendants in the rank-1 sectors sl(2) and\\nsu(2) of N=4 super \
Yang-Mills theory. Recently, the next-to-leading quantum\\ncorrection to the \
sl(2) state has been computed. Here, we use the algebraic\\ncurve approach to \
determine the correction to the other state recovering\\nuniversality of the \
correction inside the multiplet.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
