               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Plamen Bozhilov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Three-point correlators: finite-size giant magnons and \
singlet scalar\\n  operators on higher string levels\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"15 pages, no figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2011.10.008\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the framework of the semiclassical approach, we \
compute the normalized\\nstructure constants in three-point correlation \
functions, when two of the\\nvertex operators correspond to \\\"heavy\\\" \
string states, while the third vertex\\ncorresponds to a \\\"light\\\" state. \
This is done for the case when the \\\"heavy\\\"\\nstring states are \
finite-size giant magnons, carrying one or two angular\\nmomenta. The \
\\\"light\\\" states are taken to be singlet scalar operators on \
higher\\nstring levels. We first consider the case of string theory on \
AdS_5xS^5 dual to\\nN = 4 super Yang-Mills. Then we extend the obtained \
results to the\\ngamma-deformed AdS_5x S^5, corresponding to N = 1 super \
Yang-Mills theory,\\nappearing as an exactly marginal deformation of N=4 \
super Yang-Mills.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
