            "  In the framework of the semiclassical approach, we compute the \
normalized\nstructure constants in three-point correlation functions, when \
two of the\nvertex operators correspond to \"heavy\" string states, while the \
third vertex\ncorresponds to a \"light\" state. This is done for the case \
when the \"heavy\"\nstring states are finite-size giant magnons, carrying one \
or two angular\nmomenta. The \"light\" states are taken to be singlet scalar \
operators on higher\nstring levels. We first consider the case of string \
theory on AdS_5xS^5 dual to\nN = 4 super Yang-Mills. Then we extend the \
obtained results to the\ngamma-deformed AdS_5x S^5, corresponding to N = 1 \
super Yang-Mills theory,\nappearing as an exactly marginal deformation of N=4 \
super Yang-Mills.\n", 
