               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1108.4927\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Raphael Benichou\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Raphael Benichou\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"First-principles derivation of the AdS/CFT \
Y-systems\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages, 5 figures; v2: minor additions, JHEP \
version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2011)112\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We provide a first-principles, perturbative derivation \
of the AdS5/CFT4\\nY-system that has been proposed to solve the spectrum \
problem of N=4 SYM. The\\nproof relies on the computation of quantum effects \
in the fusion of some loop\\noperators, namely the transfer matrices. More \
precisely we show that the\\nleading quantum corrections in the fusion of \
transfer matrices induce the\\ncorrect shifts of the spectral parameter in \
the T-system. As intermediate steps\\nwe study UV divergences in line \
operators up to first order and compute the\\nfusion of line operators up to \
second order for the pure spinor string in\\nAdS5xS5. We also argue that the \
derivation can be easily extended to other\\nintegrable models, some of which \
describe string theory on AdS4, AdS3 and AdS2\\nspacetimes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
