               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1109.3097\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold Steinacker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Daniel N. Blaschke, Harold Steinacker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the 1-loop effective action for the IKKT model and \
non-commutative\\n  branes\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"38 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1110:120,2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2011)120\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UWThPh-2011-29\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the one-loop effective action of the IKKT or \
IIB model on a\\n4-dimensional non-commutative brane background. The \
trace-U(1) sector is\\ngoverned by non-commutativity, and leads - assuming no \
SUSY breaking - to a\\nhigher-derivative effective action. In contrast, the \
non-Abelian sector at low\\nenergies reduces to SU(n) N=4 Super-Yang-Mills on \
the brane, with a global\\nSO(9,1) symmetry broken spontaneously by the \
background. In the Coulomb branch,\\nwe recover the leading contribution to \
the Dirac-Born-Infeld (DBI) action,\\nexhibiting a S^5 \\\\times AdS^5 bulk \
geometry around a stack of branes. SUSY may\\nbe broken by compact extra \
dimensions M^4 x K, leading to an induced\\ngravitational action on M^4 due \
to the trace-U(1) sector. The one-loop\\neffective action is UV finite on \
such backgrounds, and the UV/IR mixing is\\nnon-pathological.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
