            "  We study the one-loop effective action of the IKKT or IIB \
model on a\n4-dimensional non-commutative brane background. The trace-U(1) \
sector is\ngoverned by non-commutativity, and leads - assuming no SUSY \
breaking - to a\nhigher-derivative effective action. In contrast, the \
non-Abelian sector at low\nenergies reduces to SU(n) N=4 Super-Yang-Mills on \
the brane, with a global\nSO(9,1) symmetry broken spontaneously by the \
background. In the Coulomb branch,\nwe recover the leading contribution to \
the Dirac-Born-Infeld (DBI) action,\nexhibiting a S^5 \\times AdS^5 bulk \
geometry around a stack of branes. SUSY may\nbe broken by compact extra \
dimensions M^4 x K, leading to an induced\ngravitational action on M^4 due to \
the trace-U(1) sector. The one-loop\neffective action is UV finite on such \
backgrounds, and the UV/IR mixing is\nnon-pathological.\n", 
