                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yukinori Iwashita\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Y. Iwashita, R. Roiban, A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Two-loop corrections to partition function of \
Pohlmeyer-reduced theory\\n  for AdS_5 x S^5 superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"36 pages, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.84.126017\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-YI-2011-01\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Pohlmeyer reduction of AdS_5 x S^5 superstring leads to \
a set of equations of\\nmotion following from an action containing a bosonic \
Sp(2,2) x Sp(4)/[SU(2)]^4\\ngauged WZW term, an integrable potential and a \
fermionic part coupling bosons\\nfrom the two factors. The original \
superstring and the reduced model are in\\ndirect correspondence at the \
classical level but their relation at the quantum\\nlevel remains an open \
question. As was found earlier, the one-loop partition\\nfunctions of the two \
theories computed on the respective classical backgrounds\\nmatch; here we \
explore the fate of this relation at the two-loop level. We\\nconsider the \
example of the reduced theory solution corresponding to the long\\nfolded \
spinning string in AdS. The logarithm of the AdS_5 x S^5 \
superstring\\npartition function computed on the spinning string background \
is known to be\\nproportional to the universal scaling function which depends \
on the string\\ntension ~ \\\\l^{1/2} where \\\\l=\\\\lambda is `t Hooft \
coupling. Its \\\"quantum\\\" part is\\nf(\\\\l) = a1 + \\\\l^{-1/2} a2 + ... \
where the one-loop term is a1 = - 3 \\\\ln 2 and\\nthe two-loop term is minus \
the Catalan's constant, a2=-K. We find that the\\ncounterpart of f(\\\\l) in \
the reduced theory is f'(k) =a1' + 2 k^{-1} a2' + ...,\\nwhere k is the \
coupling of the reduced theory. Here the one-loop coefficient is\\nthe same \
as in the string theory, a1'= a1, while the two-loop one is a2' =a2 -\\n1/4 \
(a1)^2. Remarkably, the first Catalan's constant term here matches \
the\\nstring theory result if we identify the two couplings as k= \
2\\\\l^{1/2}.\\nNevertheless, the presence of the additional (a1)^2 ~ (\\\\ln \
2)^2 term implies\\nthat a relation between the two quantum partition \
functions (if any) is not a\\nsimple equality. Similar results are found in \
the case of AdS_3 x S^3\\nsuperstring theory where a1= - 2 \\\\ln 2 and a2=0, \
while in the corresponding\\nreduced theory a1'=a1, a2'= a2- 1/4 \
(a1)^2.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
