                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the correspondence between scattering \
amplitudes and Wilson loops in\\nthree-dimensional Chern-Simons matter \
theories. In particular, using N=2\\nsuperspace formalism, we compute at one \
loop the whole spectrum of four-point\\nsuperamplitudes for generic N>=2 \
supersymmetric theories and find a vanishing\\nresult for N=6 ABJ(M) and N=8 \
BLG models. This restricts the possible range of\\ntheories for which Wilson \
loops/scattering amplitudes duality might work. At\\ntwo loops, we present \
the computation of the four-point ABJ scattering\\namplitude for external \
chiral superfields. Extending the known result for the\\nABJM Wilson loop to \
the ABJ case we find perfect agreement. We also discuss the\\ndual conformal \
invariance of our results and the relationship between the\\nFeynman diagram \
computation and unitarity methods. While for the ABJM theory\\ndual \
conformally invariant integrals exactly reproduce the amplitude, for \
the\\nABJ case this happens only up to a residual constant depending on \
the\\nparity-violating parameter. Finally we propose a BDS-like \
exponentiation for\\nthe amplitude based on an analogy with the \
four-dimensional N=4 SYM case, and\\ndiscuss its strong coupling dual \
counterpart.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 4 Oct 2011 16:06:56 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
