           "id" -> "1110.0738", "submitter" -> "Andrea Mauri", "authors" -> 
            "Marco S. Bianchi, Matias Leoni, Andrea Mauri, Silvia Penati and\n\
  Alberto Santambrogio", "title" -> "Scattering in ABJ theories", "comments" -> 
            "1+54 pages, 8 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP12(2011)073", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the correspondence between scattering amplitudes and \
Wilson loops in\nthree-dimensional Chern-Simons matter theories. In \
particular, using N=2\nsuperspace formalism, we compute at one loop the whole \
spectrum of four-point\nsuperamplitudes for generic N>=2 supersymmetric \
theories and find a vanishing\nresult for N=6 ABJ(M) and N=8 BLG models. This \
restricts the possible range of\ntheories for which Wilson loops/scattering \
amplitudes duality might work. At\ntwo loops, we present the computation of \
the four-point ABJ scattering\namplitude for external chiral superfields. \
Extending the known result for the\nABJM Wilson loop to the ABJ case we find \
perfect agreement. We also discuss the\ndual conformal invariance of our \
results and the relationship between the\nFeynman diagram computation and \
unitarity methods. While for the ABJM theory\ndual conformally invariant \
integrals exactly reproduce the amplitude, for the\nABJ case this happens \
only up to a residual constant depending on the\nparity-violating parameter. \
Finally we propose a BDS-like exponentiation for\nthe amplitude based on an \
analogy with the four-dimensional N=4 SYM case, and\ndiscuss its strong \
coupling dual counterpart.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 4 Oct 2011 16:06:56 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-05-30", 
