            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1110.0861\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shan  Hu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Shan Hu, Dimitri Nanopoulos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hopf-Wess-Zumino term in the effective action of the 6d, \
(2, 0) field\\n  theory revisted\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"24 pages, accepted by JHEP; v2: references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1110:054, 2011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2011)054\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ACT-16-11; MIFPA-11-46\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the Hopf-Wess-Zumino term in the effective \
action of the 6d (2, 0)\\ntheory of the type A_{N-1} in a generic Coulomb \
branch. For such terms, the\\nsupergravity calculation could be trusted. We \
calculate the WZ term on\\nsupergravity side and show that it could \
compensate the anomaly deficit, as is\\nrequired by the anomaly matching \
condition. In contrast with the SYM theory, in\\nwhich each WZ term involves \
one root e_{i}-e_{j}, here, the typical WZ term\\ninvolves two roots \
e_{i}-e_{j} and e_{k}-e_{j}. Such kind of triple interaction\\nmay come from \
the integrating out of the massive states carrying three indices.\\nA natural \
candidate is the recently proposed 1/4 BPS objects in the Coulomb\\nphase of \
the 6d (2, 0) theories. The WZ term could be derived from the field\\ntheory \
by the integration out of massive degrees of freedom. Without the 6d (2,\\n0) \
theory at hand, we take the supersymmetric equations for the \
3-algebra\\nvalued (2, 0) tensor multiplet as the prototype to see how far we \
can go. The\\nH_{3}\\\\wedge A_{3} part of the WZ term is obtained, while the \
A_{3}\\\\wedge F_{4}\\npart, which is the term accounting for the anomaly \
matching, cannot be produced\\nby the standard fermion loop \
integration.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 4 Oct 2011 22:01:53 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 10 Oct 2011 17:07:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-11-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Hu\"", ",", "\"Shan\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Nanopoulos\"", ",", "\"Dimitri\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
