 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present in detail the implementation of the \
Blaizot-M\\\\'endez-Wschebor\\n(BMW) approximation scheme of the \
nonperturbative renormalization group, which\\nallows for the computation of \
the full momentum dependence of correlation\\nfunctions. We discuss its \
signification and its relation with other schemes, in\\nparticular the \
derivative expansion. Quantitative results are presented for the\\ntestground \
of scalar O(N) theories. Besides critical exponents which are\\nzero-momentum \
quantities, we compute in three dimensions in the whole momentum\\nrange the \
two-point function at criticality and, in the high temperature phase,\\nthe \
universal structure factor. In all cases, we find very good agreement \
with\\nthe best existing results.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
