            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1110.2687\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Chong-Sun Chu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Chong-Sun Chu and Gurdeep S. Sehmbi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"D1-Strings in Large RR 3-Form Flux, Quantum Nambu \
Geometry and M5-Branes\\n  in C-Field\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"34 pages. LaTex\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8113/45/5/055401\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DCPT-11/45\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider D1-branes in a RR flux background and show \
that there is a low\\nenergy - large flux double scaling limit where the \
D1-branes action is\\ndominated by a Chern-Simons-Myers coupling term. As a \
classical solution to the\\nmatrix model, we find a novel quantized geometry \
characterized by a quantum\\nNambu 3-bracket. Infinite dimensional \
representations of the quantum Nambu\\ngeometry are constructed which \
demonstrate that the quantum Nambu geometry is\\nintrinsically different from \
the ordinary Lie algebra type noncommutative\\ngeometry. Matrix models for \
the IIB string, IIA string and M-theory in the\\ncorresponding backgrounds \
are constructed. A classical solution of a quantum\\nNambu geometry in the \
IIA Matrix string theory gives rise to an expansion of\\nthe fundamental \
strings into a system of multiple D4-branes and the fluctuation\\nis found to \
describe an action for a non-abelian 3-form field strength which is\\na \
natural non-abelian generalization of the PST action for a single \
D4-brane.\\nIn view of the recent proposals of the M5-branes theory in terms \
of the\\nD4-branes, we suggest a natural way to include all the KK modes and \
propose an\\naction for the the multiple M5-branes in a constant C-field. The \
worldvolume of\\nthe M5-branes in a C-field is found to be described by a \
quantum Nambu geometry\\nwith self-dual parameters. It is intriguing that our \
action is naturally\\nformulated in terms of a 1-form gauge field living on a \
six dimensional quantum\\nNambu geometry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 12 Oct 2011 16:06:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-05-30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Chu\"", ",", "\"Chong-Sun\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Sehmbi\"", ",", "\"Gurdeep S.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
