            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1110.2687", "submitter" -> "Chong-Sun Chu", "authors" -> 
            "Chong-Sun Chu and Gurdeep S. Sehmbi", "title" -> 
            "D1-Strings in Large RR 3-Form Flux, Quantum Nambu Geometry and \
M5-Branes\n  in C-Field", "comments" -> "34 pages. LaTex", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8113/45/5/055401", "report-no" -> 
            "DCPT-11/45", "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider D1-branes in a RR flux background and show that \
there is a low\nenergy - large flux double scaling limit where the D1-branes \
action is\ndominated by a Chern-Simons-Myers coupling term. As a classical \
solution to the\nmatrix model, we find a novel quantized geometry \
characterized by a quantum\nNambu 3-bracket. Infinite dimensional \
representations of the quantum Nambu\ngeometry are constructed which \
demonstrate that the quantum Nambu geometry is\nintrinsically different from \
the ordinary Lie algebra type noncommutative\ngeometry. Matrix models for the \
IIB string, IIA string and M-theory in the\ncorresponding backgrounds are \
constructed. A classical solution of a quantum\nNambu geometry in the IIA \
Matrix string theory gives rise to an expansion of\nthe fundamental strings \
into a system of multiple D4-branes and the fluctuation\nis found to describe \
an action for a non-abelian 3-form field strength which is\na natural \
non-abelian generalization of the PST action for a single D4-brane.\nIn view \
of the recent proposals of the M5-branes theory in terms of the\nD4-branes, \
we suggest a natural way to include all the KK modes and propose an\naction \
for the the multiple M5-branes in a constant C-field. The worldvolume of\nthe \
M5-branes in a C-field is found to be described by a quantum Nambu geometry\n\
with self-dual parameters. It is intriguing that our action is naturally\n\
formulated in terms of a 1-form gauge field living on a six dimensional \
quantum\nNambu geometry.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 12 Oct 2011 16:06:08 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-05-30", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Chu", "Chong-Sun", ""}, {
              "Sehmbi", "Gurdeep S.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
