                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Adapting the powerful integrability-based formalism \
invented previously for\\nthe calculation of gluon scattering amplitudes at \
strong coupling, we develop a\\nmethod for computing the holographic three \
point functions for the large spin\\nlimit of Gubser-Klebanov- Polyakov (GKP) \
strings. Although many of the ideas\\nfrom the gluon scattering problem can \
be transplanted with minor modifications,\\nthe fact that the information of \
the external states is now encoded in the\\nsingularities at the vertex \
insertion points necessitates several new\\ntechniques. Notably, we develop a \
new generalized Riemann bilinear identity,\\nwhich allows one to express the \
area integral in terms of appropriate contour\\nintegrals in the presence of \
such singularities. We also give some general\\ndiscussions on how \
semiclassical vertex operators for heavy string states\\nshould be \
constructed systematically from the solutions of the \
Hamilton-Jacobi\\nequation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
