          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1110.3949", "submitter" -> "Shota Komatsu", "authors" -> 
            "Yoichi Kazama and Shota Komatsu", "title" -> 
            "On holographic three point functions for GKP strings from \
integrability", "comments" -> 
            "62 pages;v2 Typos and equation (3.7) corrected. Clarifying \
remarks\n  added in Section 4.1. Published version;v3 Minor errors found in \
version 2\n  are corrected. For explanation of the revision, see Erratum \
published in\n  http://www.springerlink.com/content/m67055235407vx67/?MUD=MP",
             "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1201 (2012) 110", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP01(2012)110", "report-no" -> "UT-Komaba 11-9", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Adapting the powerful integrability-based formalism invented \
previously for\nthe calculation of gluon scattering amplitudes at strong \
coupling, we develop a\nmethod for computing the holographic three point \
functions for the large spin\nlimit of Gubser-Klebanov- Polyakov (GKP) \
strings. Although many of the ideas\nfrom the gluon scattering problem can be \
transplanted with minor modifications,\nthe fact that the information of the \
external states is now encoded in the\nsingularities at the vertex insertion \
points necessitates several new\ntechniques. Notably, we develop a new \
generalized Riemann bilinear identity,\nwhich allows one to express the area \
integral in terms of appropriate contour\nintegrals in the presence of such \
singularities. We also give some general\ndiscussions on how semiclassical \
vertex operators for heavy string states\nshould be constructed \
systematically from the solutions of the Hamilton-Jacobi\nequation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 18 Oct 2011 12:08:48 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
