                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Semiclassical correlators of three states with large S^5 \
charges in\\n  string theory in AdS_5 x S^5\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"43 pages, 4 figures; v2: minor corrections; v3: comments \
added at the\\n  end of section 3 and in section 5; v4: minor corrections; \
v5: discussion in\\n  subsection 3.3 corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D 85: 026001, 2012\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.85.026001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider semiclassical computation of 3-point \
correlation functions of\\n(BPS or non-BPS) string states represented by \
vertex operators carrying large\\ncharges in S5. We argue that the AdS5 part \
of the construction of relevant\\nsemiclassical solution involves the two \
basic ingredients: (i) configuration of\\nthree glued geodesics in AdS2 \
suggested by Klose and McLoughlin in\\narXiv:1106.0495 and (ii) a particular \
Schwarz-Christoffel map of the 3-geodesic\\nsolution in cylindrical (tau, \
sigma) domain into the complex plane with three\\nmarked points. This map is \
constructed using the expression for the AdS2 string\\nstress tensor which is \
uniquely determined by the 3 scaling dimensions as noted\\nby Janik and \
Wereszczynski in arXiv:1109.6262 (our solution, however, is\\ndifferent from \
theirs). We also find the S5 part of the solution and thus the\\nfull \
expression for the semiclassical part of the 3-point correlator for\\nseveral \
examples: extremal and non-extremal correlators of BPS states and \
a\\nparticular correlator of \\\"small\\\" circular spinning strings in S3 \
part of S5. We\\ndemonstrate that for the BPS correlators the results agree \
with the large\\ncharge limit of the corresponding supergravity and free \
gauge theory\\nexpressions.\\n\""}]}, {
