 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose an alternative method to study the saddle \
point equation in the\\nstrong coupling limit for the Wilson loop in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ D=4 super\\nYang-Mills with an SU(N) gauge group and 2N \
hypermultiplets. This method is\\nbased on an approximation of the integral \
equation kernel which allows to solve\\nthe simplified problem exactly. To \
determine the accuracy of this\\napproximation, we compare our results to \
those obtained recently by Passerini\\nand Zarembo. Although less precise, \
this simpler approach provides an explicit\\nexpression for the density of \
eigenvalues that is used to derive the planar\\nfree energy.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
