            "  We compute three-point functions between one large classical \
operator and two\nlarge BPS operators at weak coupling. We consider operators \
made out of the\nscalars of N=4 SYM, dual to strings moving in the sphere. \
The three-point\nfunction exponentiates and can be thought of as a classical \
tunneling process\nin which the classical string-like operator decays into \
two classical BPS\nstates. From an Integrability/Condensed Matter point of \
view, we simplified\ninner products of spin chain Bethe states in a classical \
limit corresponding to\nlong wavelength excitations above the ferromagnetic \
vacuum. As a by-product we\nsolved a new long-range Ising model in the \
thermodynamic limit.\n", 
