               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Michael C. Abbott, In\\\\^es Aniceto and Diego \
Bombardelli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Real and Virtual Bound States in L\\\\\\\"uscher \
Corrections for CP3 Magnons\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages and 3 figures. v3 adds new section treating \
F-terms of all\\n  orders; version to appear in J. Phys. A\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Phys. A 45 335401, 2012\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/45/33/335401\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"TIFR/TH/11-46\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study classical and quantum finite-size corrections \
to giant magnons in\\nAdS_4 x CP^3 using generalised L\\\\\\\"uscher \
formulae. L\\\\\\\"uscher F-terms are\\norganised in powers of the \
exponential suppression factor exp(-Delta/2h)^m, and\\nwe calculate all terms \
in this series, matching one-loop algebraic curve\\nresults from our previous \
paper arXiv:1006.2174. Starting with the second term,\\nthe structure of \
these terms is different to those in AdS_5 x S^5 thanks to the\\nappearance \
of heavy modes in the loop, which can here be interpreted as\\ntwo-particle \
bound states in the mirror theory. By contrast, physical bound\\nstates can \
represent dyonic giant magnons, and we also calculate F-terms for\\nthese \
solutions. L\\\\\\\"uscher mu-terms, suppressed by exp(-Delta/E), instead \
give\\nat leading order the classical finite-size correction. For an \
elementary dyonic\\ngiant magnon, we recover the correction given by \
arXiv:0903.3365. We then\\nextend this to calculate the next term in 1/h, \
giving a one-loop prediction.\\nFinally we also calculate F-terms for the \
various composite giant magnons, RP^3\\nand `big', again finding agreement to \
all orders.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
