            "title" -> 
            "Real and Virtual Bound States in L\\\"uscher Corrections for CP3 \
Magnons", "comments" -> 
            "33 pages and 3 figures. v3 adds new section treating F-terms of \
all\n  orders; version to appear in J. Phys. A", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J. Phys. A 45 335401, 2012", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/45/33/335401", "report-no" -> "TIFR/TH/11-46", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study classical and quantum finite-size corrections to \
giant magnons in\nAdS_4 x CP^3 using generalised L\\\"uscher formulae. \
L\\\"uscher F-terms are\norganised in powers of the exponential suppression \
factor exp(-Delta/2h)^m, and\nwe calculate all terms in this series, matching \
one-loop algebraic curve\nresults from our previous paper arXiv:1006.2174. \
Starting with the second term,\nthe structure of these terms is different to \
those in AdS_5 x S^5 thanks to the\nappearance of heavy modes in the loop, \
which can here be interpreted as\ntwo-particle bound states in the mirror \
theory. By contrast, physical bound\nstates can represent dyonic giant \
magnons, and we also calculate F-terms for\nthese solutions. L\\\"uscher \
mu-terms, suppressed by exp(-Delta/E), instead give\nat leading order the \
classical finite-size correction. For an elementary dyonic\ngiant magnon, we \
recover the correction given by arXiv:0903.3365. We then\nextend this to \
calculate the next term in 1/h, giving a one-loop prediction.\nFinally we \
also calculate F-terms for the various composite giant magnons, RP^3\nand \
`big', again finding agreement to all orders.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
