               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1111.4145\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Igor Samsonov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"I. L. Buchbinder, E. A. Ivanov, I. B. Samsonov, B. M. \
Zupnik\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Superconformal N=3 SYM Low-Energy Effective Action\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+29 pages; v2: minor corrections, JHEP style\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2012)001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct a manifestly N=3 supersymmetric low-energy \
effective action of\\nN=3 super Yang-Mills theory. The effective action is \
written in the N=3\\nharmonic superspace and respects the full N=3 \
superconformal symmetry. On mass\\nshell this action is responsible for the \
four-derivative terms in the N=4 SYM\\neffective action, such as F^4/X^4 and \
its supersymmetric completions, while off\\nshell it involves also \
higher-derivative terms. For constant Maxwell and scalar\\nfields its bosonic \
part coincides, up to the F^6/X^8 order, with the bosonic\\npart of the D3 \
brane action in the AdS_5 x S^5 background. We also argue that\\nin the \
sector of scalar fields it involves the correctly normalized \
Wess-Zumino\\nterm with the implicit SU(3) symmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
