               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1111.6628\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrey Zayakin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Davide Astolfi, Gianluca Grignani, Enrico Ser-Giacomi, A. \
V. Zayakin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Strings in AdS_4 x CP^3: finite size spectrum vs. Bethe \
Ansatz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages. Published version; journal reference \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP04(2012)005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2012)005\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ITEP-TH-51/11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the first curvature corrections to the \
spectrum of light-cone\\ngauge type IIA string theory that arise in the \
expansion of $AdS_4\\\\times\\n\\\\mathbb{CP}^3$ about a plane-wave limit. \
The resulting spectrum is shown to\\nmatch precisely, both in magnitude and \
degeneration that of the corresponding\\nsolutions of the all-loop \
Gromov--Vieira Bethe Ansatz. The one-loop dispersion\\nrelation correction is \
calculated for all the single oscillator states of the\\ntheory, with the \
level matching condition lifted. It is shown to have all\\nlogarithmic \
divergences cancelled and to leave only a finite exponentially\\nsuppressed \
contribution, as shown earlier for light bosons. We argue that there\\nis no \
ambiguity in the choice of the regularization for the self-energy \
sum,\\nsince the regularization applied is the only one preserving unitarity.\
\\nInteraction matrices in the full degenerate two-oscillator sector \
are\\ncalculated and the spectrum of all two light magnon oscillators is \
completely\\ndetermined. The same finite-size corrections, at the order 1/J, \
where $J$ is\\nthe length of the chain, in the two-magnon sector are \
calculated from the all\\nloop Bethe Ansatz. The corrections obtained by the \
two completely different\\nmethods coincide up to the fourth order in \
$\\\\lambda' =\\\\lambda/J^2$. We\\nconjecture that the equivalence extends \
to all orders in $\\\\lambda$ and to\\nhigher orders in 1/J.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
