               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Geometry of open strings ending on backreacting D3-branes\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"64 pages, 20 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2012)025\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate open string theory on backreacting \
D3-branes using a spacetime\\napproach. We study in detail the half-BPS \
supergravity solutions describing\\nopen strings ending on D3-branes, in the \
near horizon of the D3-branes. We\\nrecover quantitatively several \
non-trivial features of open string physics\\nincluding the appearance of \
D3-brane spikes, the polarization of fundamental\\nstrings into D5-branes, \
and the Hanany-Witten effect. Finally we detail the\\ncomputation of the \
gravitational potential between two open strings, and\\ncontrast it with the \
holographic computation of Wilson lines. We argue that the\\nD-brane \
backreaction has a large influence on the low-energy gravity, which \
may\\nlead to experimental tests for string theory brane-world \
scenarios.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
