            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate open string theory on backreacting D3-branes \
using a spacetime\napproach. We study in detail the half-BPS supergravity \
solutions describing\nopen strings ending on D3-branes, in the near horizon \
of the D3-branes. We\nrecover quantitatively several non-trivial features of \
open string physics\nincluding the appearance of D3-brane spikes, the \
polarization of fundamental\nstrings into D5-branes, and the Hanany-Witten \
effect. Finally we detail the\ncomputation of the gravitational potential \
between two open strings, and\ncontrast it with the holographic computation \
of Wilson lines. We argue that the\nD-brane backreaction has a large \
influence on the low-energy gravity, which may\nlead to experimental tests \
for string theory brane-world scenarios.\n", 
