                 "\"Connes distance by examples: Homothetic spectral metric \
spaces\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"23 pages. Misprints corrected, references updated, one \
remark added\\n  at the end of the section 3. To appear in Review in \
Mathematical Physics\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Rev. Math. Phys. Vol.24, No 9 (2012) 1250027\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1142/S0129055X12500274\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"math-ph hep-th math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study metric properties stemming from the Connes \
spectral distance on\\nthree types of non compact noncommutative spaces which \
have received attention\\nrecently from various viewpoints in the physics \
literature. These are the\\nnoncommutative Moyal plane, a family of harmonic \
Moyal spectral triples for\\nwhich the Dirac operator squares to the harmonic \
oscillator Hamiltonian and a\\nfamily of spectral triples with Dirac operator \
related to the Landau operator.\\nWe show that these triples are homothetic \
spectral metric spaces, having an\\ninfinite number of distinct pathwise \
connected components. The homothetic\\nfactors linking the distances are \
related to determinants of effective Clifford\\nmetrics. We obtain as a by \
product new examples of explicit spectral distance\\nformulas. The results \
are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
