 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  For an arbitrary generalized quantum integrable spin \
chain we introduce a\\n\\\"master T -operator\\\" which represents a \
generating function for commuting\\nquantum transfer matrices constructed by \
means of the fusion procedure in the\\nauxiliary space.\\n  We show that the \
functional relations for the transfer matrices are\\nequivalent to an \
infinite set of model-independent bilinear equations of the\\nHirota form for \
the master T -operator, which allows one to identify it \
with\\n{\\\\tau}-function of an integrable hierarchy of classical soliton \
equations.\\n  In this paper we consider spin chains with rational \
GL(N)-invariant\\nR-matrices but the result is independent of a particular \
functional form of the\\ntransfer matrices and directly applies to quantum \
integrable models with more\\ngeneral (trigonometric and elliptic) R-matrices \
and to supersymmetric spin\\nchains.\\n\""}]}, {
