                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We systematically study the spectrum of excitations and \
the one-loop\\ndeterminant of holographic Wilson loop operators in \
antisymmetric\\nrepresentations of $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory.\\nHolographically, these operators are described by \
D5-branes carrying electric\\nflux and wrapping an $S^4 \\\\subset S^5$ in \
the $AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ bulk\\nbackground. We derive the dynamics of both \
bosonic and fermionic excitations\\nfor such D5-branes. A particularly \
important configuration in this class is the\\nD5-brane with $AdS_2\\\\times \
S^4$ worldvolume and $k$ units of electric flux,\\nwhich is dual to the \
circular Wilson loop in the totally antisymmetric\\nrepresentation of rank \
$k$. For this Wilson loop, we obtain the spectrum, show\\nexplicitly that it \
is supersymmetric and calculate the one-loop effective\\naction using heat \
kernel techniques.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
