            "  We systematically study the spectrum of excitations and the \
one-loop\ndeterminant of holographic Wilson loop operators in antisymmetric\n\
representations of $\\mathcal{N}=4$ supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory.\n\
Holographically, these operators are described by D5-branes carrying electric\
\nflux and wrapping an $S^4 \\subset S^5$ in the $AdS_5\\times S^5$ bulk\n\
background. We derive the dynamics of both bosonic and fermionic excitations\n\
for such D5-branes. A particularly important configuration in this class is \
the\nD5-brane with $AdS_2\\times S^4$ worldvolume and $k$ units of electric \
flux,\nwhich is dual to the circular Wilson loop in the totally antisymmetric\
\nrepresentation of rank $k$. For this Wilson loop, we obtain the spectrum, \
show\nexplicitly that it is supersymmetric and calculate the one-loop \
effective\naction using heat kernel techniques.\n", 
