               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic 3-point function at one loop\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"24 pages, 2 figures. v2: Typos fixed, Ref. added, figure \
improved.\\n  v3: Several typos and misprints fixed, Ref. updated, figures \
improved, new\\n  section 2.3 added on correction from spin-flipped coherent \
state,\\n  computations on string theory side improved\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2012)133\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore the recent weak/strong coupling match of \
three-point functions in\\nthe AdS/CFT correspondence for two semi-classical \
operators and one light\\nchiral primary operator found by Escobedo et al. \
This match is between the\\ntree-level three-point function with the two \
semi-classical operators described\\nby coherent states while on the string \
side the three-point function is found\\nin the Frolov-Tseytlin limit. We \
compute the one-loop correction to the\\nthree-point function on the gauge \
theory side and compare this to the\\ncorresponding correction on the string \
theory side. We find that the\\ncorrections do not match. Finally, we discuss \
the possibility of further\\ncontributions on the gauge theory side that can \
alter our results.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
