         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1112.5182", "submitter" -> "S. Prem Kumar", "authors" -> 
            "Benedict Fraser and S. Prem Kumar", "title" -> 
            "Large rank Wilson loops in N=2 superconformal QCD at strong \
coupling", "comments" -> 
            "Typos corrected, reference added, replaced with version to \
appear in\n  JHEP (25 pages, 2 figures)", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP03(2012)077", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute the expectation values of circular Wilson loops in \
large\nrepresentations at strong coupling, in the large-N limit of the N=2\n\
superconformal theory with SU(N) gauge group and 2N hypermultiplets. \
Employing\nPestun's matrix integral, we focus attention on symmetric and \
antisymmetric\nrepresentations with ranks of order N. We find that large rank \
antisymmetric\nloops are independent of the coupling at strong 't Hooft \
coupling while\nsymmetric Wilson loops grow exponentially with it. Symmetric \
loops display a\nnon-analyticity as a function of the rank, characterized by \
the splitting of a\nsingle matrix model eigenvalue from the continuum, \
bearing close resemblance to\nBose-Einstein condensation in an ideal gas. We \
discuss implications of these\nfor a putative large-N string dual. The method \
of calculation we adopt makes\nexplicit the connection to Fermi and Bose gas \
descriptions and also suggests a\ntantalizing connection of the above system \
to a multichannel Kondo model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 21 Dec 2011 21:35:40 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 28 Feb 2012 14:59:43 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-03", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fraser", "Benedict", ""}, {
              "Kumar", "S. Prem", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
