                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We report on a systematic perturbative study of \
three-point functions in\\nplanar SU(N) N=4 super Yang-Mills theory at the \
one-loop level involving scalar\\nfield operators up to length five. For this \
we have computed a sample of 40\\nstructure constants involving primary \
operators of up to and including length\\nfive which are built entirely from \
scalar fields. A combinatorial dressing\\ntechnique has been developed to \
promote tree-level correlators to one-loop\\nlevel. In addition we have \
resolved the mixing up to the order (g_YM)^2 level\\nof the operators \
involved, which amounts to mixings with bi-fermions, with\\nbi-derivative \
insertions as well as self-mixing contributions in the scalar\\nsector. This \
work supersedes a preprint by two of the authors from 2010 which\\nhad \
neglected the mixing contributions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
