            "  We report on a systematic perturbative study of three-point \
functions in\nplanar SU(N) N=4 super Yang-Mills theory at the one-loop level \
involving scalar\nfield operators up to length five. For this we have \
computed a sample of 40\nstructure constants involving primary operators of \
up to and including length\nfive which are built entirely from scalar fields. \
A combinatorial dressing\ntechnique has been developed to promote tree-level \
correlators to one-loop\nlevel. In addition we have resolved the mixing up to \
