            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1201.1884\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fabian Spill\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fabian Spill\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Yangians in Integrable Field Theories, Spin Chains and \
Gauge-String\\n  Dualities\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"133 pages, accepted for publication in Reviews in \
Mathematical\\n  Physics\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1142/S0129055X12300014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP math.QA\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the following paper, which is based on the authors \
PhD thesis submitted to\\nImperial College London, we explore the \
applicability of Yangian symmetry to\\nvarious integrable models, in \
particular, in relation with S-matrices. One of\\nthe main themes in this \
work is that, after a careful study of the mathematics\\nof the symmetry \
algebras one finds that in an integrable model, one can\\ndirectly \
reconstruct S-matrices just from the algebra. It has been known for a\\nlong \
time that S-matrices in integrable models are fixed by symmetry. \
However,\\nLie algebra symmetry, the Yang-Baxter equation, crossing and \
unitarity, which\\nare what constrains the S-matrix in integrable models, are \
often taken to be\\nseparate, independent properties of the S-matrix. Here, \
we construct scattering\\nmatrices purely from the Yangian, showing that the \
Yangian is the right\\nalgebraic object to unify all required symmetries of \
many integrable models. In\\nparticular, we reconstruct the S-matrix of the \
principal chiral field, and, up\\nto a CDD factor, of other integrable field \
theories with su(n) symmetry.\\nFurthermore, we study the AdS/CFT \
correspondence, which is also believed to be\\nintegrable in the planar \
limit. We reconstruct the S-matrices at weak and at\\nstrong coupling from \
the Yangian or its classical limit. We give a pedagogical\\nintroduction into \
the subject, presenting a unified perspective of Yangians and\\ntheir \
applications in physics. This paper should hence be accessible \
to\\nmathematicians who would like to explore the application of algebraic \
objects\\nto physics as well as to physicists interested in a deeper \
understanding of the\\nmathematical origin of physical quantities.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 9 Jan 2012 19:37:13 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-03-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Spill\"", ",", "\"Fabian\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
