            Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8113/45/15/155401", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AAT-2012-01", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider semiclassical quantization of spiky strings \
spinning in AdS_3\npart of AdS_5 X S^5 using integrability-based (algebraic \
curve) method. In the\n\"short string\" (small spin) limit the expansion of \
string energy starts with\nits flat-space expression. We compute the leading \
quantum string correction to\n\"short\" spiky string energy and find the \
explicit form of the corresponding\n1-loop coefficient a_01. It turns out to \
be rational and expressed in terms of\nthe harmonic sums as functions of the \
number n of spikes. In the special case\nof n=2 when the spiky string reduces \
to the single-folded spinning string the\ncoefficient a_01 takes the value \
(-1/4) found in arXiv:1102.1040. We also\nconsider a similar computation for \
the m-folded string and more general spiky\nstring with an extra \"winding\" \
number, finding similar expressions for a_01.\nThese results may be useful \
for a description of energies of higher excited\nstates in the quantum AdS_5 \
X S^5 string spectrum, generalizing earlier\ndiscussions of the string \
counterparts of the Konishi operator.\n", 
