                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the relation between correlation functions \
of twist-two large spin\\noperators and expectation values of Wilson loops \
along light-like trajectories.\\nAfter presenting some heuristic field \
theoretical arguments suggesting this\\nrelation, we compute the divergent \
part of the correlator in the limit of large\\n't Hooft coupling and large \
spins, using a semi-classical worldsheet which\\nasymptotically looks like a \
GKP rotating string. We show this diverges as\\nexpected from the expectation \
value of a null Wilson loop, namely, as\\n$(\\\\ln{\\\\mu^{-2}})^ 2$, \
$\\\\mu$ being a cut-off of the theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
