 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive an exact formula for the cusp anomalous \
dimension at small angles.\\nThis is done by relating the latter to the \
computation of certain 1/8 BPS\\nWilson loops which was performed by \
supersymmetric localization. This function\\nof the coupling also determines \
the power emitted by a moving quark in N=4\\nsuper Yang Mills, as well as the \
coefficient of the two point function of the\\ndisplacement operator on the \
Wilson loop. By a similar method we compute the\\nnear BPS expansion of the \
generalized cusp anomalous dimension.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
