          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1202.5271\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Darren Smyth Mr.\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Moshe Rozali, Darren Smyth and Evgeny Sorkin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Holographic Higgs Phases\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Corrected typos\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2012)118\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss phases of gauge theories in the holographic \
context, and formulate\\na criterion for the existence of a Higgs phase, \
where the gauge redundancy is\\n\\\"spontaneously broken\\\", in purely bulk \
language. This condition, the existence\\nof a finite tension solitonic \
string representing a narrow magnetic flux tube,\\nis necessary for a bulk \
theory to be interpreted as a Higgs phase of a boundary\\ngauge theory. We \
demonstrate the existence of such solitons in both top-down\\nand bottom-up \
examples of holographic theories. In particular, we numerically\\nconstruct \
new solitonic solutions in AdS black hole background, for various\\nvalues of \
the boundary gauge coupling, which are used to demonstrate that the\\nbulk \
theory models a superconductor, rather than a superfluid. The criterion \
we\\nfind is expected to be useful in finding holographic duals of \
color\\nsuperconducting phases of gauge theories at finite density.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 Feb 2012 19:43:15 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 11 Jun 2012 22:11:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 11 Dec 2015 22:14:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-12-15\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Rozali\"", ",", "\"Moshe\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Smyth\"", ",", "\"Darren\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sorkin\"", ",", "\"Evgeny\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1202.5271", "submitter" -> "Darren Smyth Mr.", "authors" -> 
            "Moshe Rozali, Darren Smyth and Evgeny Sorkin", "title" -> 
            "Holographic Higgs Phases", "comments" -> "Corrected typos", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2012)118", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss phases of gauge theories in the holographic \
context, and formulate\na criterion for the existence of a Higgs phase, where \
the gauge redundancy is\n\"spontaneously broken\", in purely bulk language. \
This condition, the existence\nof a finite tension solitonic string \
representing a narrow magnetic flux tube,\nis necessary for a bulk theory to \
be interpreted as a Higgs phase of a boundary\ngauge theory. We demonstrate \
the existence of such solitons in both top-down\nand bottom-up examples of \
holographic theories. In particular, we numerically\nconstruct new solitonic \
solutions in AdS black hole background, for various\nvalues of the boundary \
gauge coupling, which are used to demonstrate that the\nbulk theory models a \
superconductor, rather than a superfluid. The criterion we\nfind is expected \
to be useful in finding holographic duals of color\nsuperconducting phases of \
gauge theories at finite density.\n", 
