 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a general class of supersymmetric Wilson loops \
operator in N = 4\\nsuper Yang-Mills theory, obtained as orbits of conformal \
transformations. These\\nloops are the natural generalization of the familiar \
circular Wilson-Maldacena\\noperator and their supersymmetric properties are \
encoded into a Killing spinor\\nthat is not pure. We present a systematic \
analysis of their scalar couplings\\nand of the preserved supercharges, \
modulo the action of the global symmetry\\ngroup, both in the compact and in \
the non-compact case. The quantum behavior of\\ntheir expectation value is \
also addressed, in the simplest case of the\\nLissajous contours: explicit \
computations at weak-coupling, through Feynman\\ndiagrams expansion, and at \
strong-coupling, by means of AdS/CFT correspondence,\\nsuggest the \
possibility of an exact evaluation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
