unchanged", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP10(2013)135", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The generalized quark-antiquark potential of N=4 \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills\ntheory on S^3 x R calculates the potential between \
a pair of heavy charged\nparticles separated by an arbitrary angle on S^3 and \
also an angle in flavor\nspace. It can be calculated by a Wilson loop \
following a prescribed path and\ncouplings, or after a conformal \
transformation, by a cusped Wilson loop in flat\nspace, hence also \
generalizing the usual concept of the cusp anomalous\ndimension. In AdS_5 x \
S^5 this is calculated by an infinite open string. I\npresent here an open \
spin-chain model which calculates the spectrum of\nexcitations of such open \
strings. In the dual gauge theory these are cusped\nWilson loops with extra \
operator insertions at the cusp. The boundaries of the\nspin-chain introduce \
a non-trivial reflection phase and break the bulk symmetry\ndown to a single \
copy of psu(2|2). The dependence on the two angles is captured\nby the two \
embeddings of this algebra into \\psu(2|2)^2, i.e., by a global\nrotation. \
The exact answer to this problem is conjectured to be given by\nsolutions to \
a set of twisted boundary thermodynamic Bethe ansatz integral\nequations. In \
particular the generalized quark-antiquark potential or cusp\nanomalous \
dimension is recovered by calculating the ground state energy of the\nminimal \
length spin-chain, with no sites. It gets contributions only from\nvirtual \
particles reflecting off the boundaries. I reproduce from this\ncalculation \
some known weak coupling perturtbative results.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 7 Mar 2012 21:00:02 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 9 Aug 2013 14:30:20 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-04", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Drukker", "Nadav", ""}}}], 
