               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive a set of integral equations of the TBA type \
for the generalized\\ncusp anomalous dimension, or the quark antiquark \
potential on the three sphere,\\nas a function of the angles. We do this by \
considering a family of local\\noperators on a Wilson loop with charge L. In \
the large L limit the problem can\\nbe solved in terms of a certain boundary \
reflection matrix. We determine this\\nreflection matrix by using the \
symmetries and the boundary crossing equation.\\nThe cusp is introduced \
through a relative rotation between the two boundaries.\\nThen the TBA trick \
of exchanging space and time leads to an exact equation for\\nall values of \
L. The L=0 case corresponds to the cusped Wilson loop with no\\noperators \
inserted. We then derive a slightly simplified integral equation\\nwhich \
describes the small angle limit. We solve this equation up to three \
loops\\nin perturbation theory and match the results that were obtained with \
more\\ndirect approaches.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
