 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The algebraic curve (finite-gap) classification of \
rotating string solutions\\nwas very important in the development of \
integrability through comparison with\\nanalogous structures at weak \
coupling. The classification was based on the\\nanalysis of monodromy around \
the closed string cylinder. In this paper we show\\nthat certain classical \
Wilson loop minimal surfaces corresponding to the null\\ncusp and qqbar \
potential with trivial monodromy can, nevertheless, be described\\nby \
appropriate algebraic curves. We also show how a correlation function of \
a\\ncircular Wilson loop with a local operator fits into this framework. The \
latter\\nsolution has identical monodromy to the pointlike BMN string and yet \
is\\nsignificantly different.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
