               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A note on the eigenvectors of long-range spin chains and \
their scalar\\n  products\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"15 pages, some more typos corrected, published \
version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP01 (2013) 012\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2013)012\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"T12/033\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this note, we propose an expression for the \
eigenvectors and scalar\\nproducts for a class of spin chains with long-range \
interaction and su(2)\\nsymmetry. This class includes the Inozemtsev spin \
chain as well as the BDS spin\\nchain, which is a reduction of the \
one-dimensional Hubbard model at\\nhalf-filling to the spin sector. The \
proposal is valid for large spin chains\\nand is based on the construction of \
the monodromy matrix using the Dunkl\\noperators. For the Inozemtsev model \
these operators are known explicitly. This\\nconstruction gives in particular \
the eigenvectors of (an operator closely\\nrelated to) the dilatation \
operator of the N=4 gauge theory in the su(2) sector\\nup to three-loop \
order, as well as their scalar products. We suggest how this\\nwill affect \
the expression for the quasi classical limit of the three-point\\nfunctions \
obtained by I. Kostov and how to include the all-loop interaction.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
