                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We evaluate the exact one-loop partition function for \
fundamental strings\\nwhose world-surface ends on a cusp at the boundary of \
AdS_4 and has a \\\"jump\\\" in\\nCP^3. This allows us to extract the stringy \
prediction for the ABJM generalized\\ncusp anomalous dimension \
Gamma_{cusp}^{ABJM} (phi,theta) up to NLO in\\nsigma-model perturbation \
theory. With a similar analysis, we present the exact\\npartition functions \
for folded closed string solutions moving in the AdS_3\\nparts of AdS_4 x \
CP^3 and AdS_3 x S^3 x S^3 x S^1 backgrounds. Results are\\nobtained applying \
to the string solutions relevant for the AdS_4/CFT_3 and\\nAdS_3/CFT_2 \
correspondence the tools previously developed for their AdS_5 x \
S^5\\ncounterparts.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
