 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  For three dimensional N=6 superconformal field theories \
we compute one-loop\\nscattering amplitudes for any number of external \
particles. We focus on a\\nparticular subsector of N=2 invariant \
superamplitudes for which the ordinary\\nperturbative evaluation becomes very \
easy. The result we obtain is in general\\nnon-vanishing. For six external \
particles our findings are sufficient for\\ndetermining the complete \
expression of the N=6 superamplitude at this order. We\\ndiscuss the \
symmetries of the result and its anomalous variation under\\nsuperconformal \
generators.\\n\""}]}, {
