 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In these lectures I review some basic examples of how \
the concepts of\\nuniversality and scaling can be used to study aspects of \
the chiral and the\\ndeconfinement transition, if not in QCD directly but in \
QCD-like theories. As\\nan example for flavor dynamics I discuss a \
quark-hadron model to describe the\\nphase diagram of two-color QCD with the \
functional renormalization group.\\nUniversal aspects of deconfinement are \
illustrated mainly in the 2+1\\ndimensional SU(N) gauge theories with second \
order transition where many exact\\nresults from spin models can be \
exploited.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
