               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ivan K. Kostov\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ivan Kostov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Three-point function of semiclassical states at weak \
coupling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, 5 figures, cosmetic changes and more typos \
corrected in v3\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/45/49/494018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"IPhT/t12/035\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give the derivation of the previously announced \
analytic expression for\\nthe correlation function of three heavy non-BPS \
operators in N=4\\nsuper-Yang-Mills theory at weak coupling. The three \
operators belong to three\\ndifferent su(2) sectors and are dual to three \
classical strings moving on the\\nsphere. Our computation is based on the \
reformulation of the problem in terms\\nof the Bethe Ansatz for periodic XXX \
spin-1/2 chains. In these terms the three\\noperators are described by \
long-wave-length excitations over the ferromagnetic\\nvacuum, for which the \
number of the overturned spins is a finite fraction of\\nthe length of the \
chain, and the classical limit is known as the Sutherland\\nlimit. \
Technically our main result is a factorized operator expression for \
the\\nscalar product of two Bethe states. The derivation is based on a \
fermionic\\nrepresentation of Slavnov's determinant formula, and a subsequent \
bosonisation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
