 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop a general method of computing the \
contribution of the vertex\\noperators to the semi-classical correlation \
functions of heavy string states,\\nbased on the state-operator \
correspondence and the integrable structure of the\\nsystem. Our method \
requires only the knowledge of the local behavior of the\\nsaddle point \
configuration around each vertex insertion point and can be\\napplied to \
cases where the precise forms of the vertex operators are not known.\\nAs an \
important application, we compute the contributions of the vertex\\noperators \
to the three-point functions of the large spin limit of \
the\\nGubser-Klebanov-Polyakov (GKP) strings in $AdS_3$ spacetime, left \
unevaluated\\nin our previous work [arXiv:1110.3949] which initiated such a \
study. Combining\\nwith the finite part of the action already computed \
previously and with the\\nnewly evaluated divergent part of the action, we \
obtain finite three-point\\nfunctions with the expected dependence of the \
target space boundary coordinates\\non the dilatation charge and the spin.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
