            "  We develop a general method of computing the contribution of \
the vertex\noperators to the semi-classical correlation functions of heavy \
string states,\nbased on the state-operator correspondence and the integrable \
structure of the\nsystem. Our method requires only the knowledge of the local \
behavior of the\nsaddle point configuration around each vertex insertion \
point and can be\napplied to cases where the precise forms of the vertex \
operators are not known.\nAs an important application, we compute the \
contributions of the vertex\noperators to the three-point functions of the \
