 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider one particularly interesting class of \
composite gauge-invariant\\noperators in N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. An \
exceptional feature of these\\noperators is that in the Thermodynamic Bethe \
Ansatz approach the one-loop\\nrapidities of the constituent magnons are \
shown to be exact in the 't Hooft\\ncoupling constant. This is used to \
propose the mirror TBA description for these\\noperators. The proposal is \
shown to pass several non-trivial checks.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
