                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"QMUL-PH-12-10; WIS/05/12-MAY-DPPA\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We establish a connection between tree-level \
superamplitudes in ABJM theory\\nand leading singularities associated to \
special three-particle cuts of one-loop\\nsuperamplitudes where one of the \
tree amplitudes entering the cut is a\\nfour-point amplitude. Using these \
relations, we show that certain intriguing\\nsimilarities between one-loop \
and tree-level superamplitudes observed recently\\nbecome completely \
manifest. This connection is reminiscent of a similar\\nrelation in the \
maximally supersymmetric gauge theory in four dimensions, where\\nthe sum of \
two-mass hard and one-mass box coefficients of a one-loop amplitude\\nequals \
the corresponding tree-level amplitude. As an application, we present \
a\\nvery simple re-derivation of the six-point superamplitude and calculate \
the\\neight-point superamplitude at one loop in ABJM theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
