            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We establish a connection between tree-level superamplitudes \
in ABJM theory\nand leading singularities associated to special \
three-particle cuts of one-loop\nsuperamplitudes where one of the tree \
amplitudes entering the cut is a\nfour-point amplitude. Using these \
relations, we show that certain intriguing\nsimilarities between one-loop and \
tree-level superamplitudes observed recently\nbecome completely manifest. \
This connection is reminiscent of a similar\nrelation in the maximally \
supersymmetric gauge theory in four dimensions, where\nthe sum of two-mass \
hard and one-mass box coefficients of a one-loop amplitude\nequals the \
corresponding tree-level amplitude. As an application, we present a\nvery \
simple re-derivation of the six-point superamplitude and calculate the\n\
eight-point superamplitude at one loop in ABJM theory.\n", 
