            "  We consider holographic three-point functions for operators \
dual to short\nstring states at strong coupling in N=4 super Yang-Mills. We \
treat the states\nas point-like as they come in from the boundary but as \
strings in the\ninteraction region in the bulk. The interaction position is \
determined by\nsaddle point, which is equivalent to conservation of the \
canonical momentum for\nthe interacting particles, and leads to conservation \
of their conformal\ncharges. We further show that for large dimensions the \
rms size of the\ninteraction region is small compared to the radius of \
curvature of the AdS\nspace, but still large compared to the string Compton \
wave-length. Hence, one\ncan approximate the string vertex operators as \
flat-space vertex operators with\na definite momentum, which depends on the \
conformal and R-charges of the\noperator. We then argue that the string \
vertex operator dual to a primary\noperator is chosen by satisfying a twisted \
version of Q^L=Q^R, up to spurious\nterms. This leads to a unique choice for \
a scalar vertex operator with the\nappropriate charges at the first massive \
level. We then comment on some\nfeatures of the corresponding three-point \
functions, including the application\nof these results to Konishi operators.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 14 Jun 2012 15:07:10 GMT"}, {
