               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This PhD thesis explores the similarities between \
integrable spin chains and\\nquantum field theories, such as Super Yang \
Mills. We first study integrable\\nspin chains and build explicitly a \
polynomial \\\"Backlund flow\\\" and polynomial\\n\\\"Q-operators\\\", which \
allow to diagonalize the Hamiltonian. We then study\\nintegrable field \
theories et show how to obtain \\\"Q-functions\\\", analogous to \
the\\nQ-operators built for spin chains. It turns out that several \
important\\ninformations are contained in the analytic properties of these Q \
-functions.\\nThat allows to obtain, in the framework of the thermodynamic \
Bethe ansatz, a\\nfinite number of non-linear integral equations encoding the \
finite-size\\nspectrum of the theory which we study. This system of equations \
is equivalent\\nto an infinite system of equations, known as \
\\\"Y-system\\\", which had been quite\\nrecently conjectured in the case of \
the AdS/CFT duality.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
