            "PhD thesis : 275 pages, including 10 introductory pages in \
french at\n  the begining (repeated afterwards in english) v2 : typos fixed \
and five\n  references added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This PhD thesis explores the similarities between integrable \
spin chains and\nquantum field theories, such as Super Yang Mills. We first \
study integrable\nspin chains and build explicitly a polynomial \"Backlund \
flow\" and polynomial\n\"Q-operators\", which allow to diagonalize the \
Hamiltonian. We then study\nintegrable field theories et show how to obtain \
\"Q-functions\", analogous to the\nQ-operators built for spin chains. It \
turns out that several important\ninformations are contained in the analytic \
properties of these Q -functions.\nThat allows to obtain, in the framework of \
the thermodynamic Bethe ansatz, a\nfinite number of non-linear integral \
equations encoding the finite-size\nspectrum of the theory which we study. \
This system of equations is equivalent\nto an infinite system of equations, \
known as \"Y-system\", which had been quite\nrecently conjectured in the case \
of the AdS/CFT duality.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
