               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The fate of the Wilson-Fisher fixed point in \
non-commutative \\\\phi^4\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"19 pages, 7 figures, v2:one reference added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Math. Phys. 53, 102301 (2012);\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1063/1.4754816\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech hep-ph math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this article we study non-commutative vector sigma \
model with the most\\ngeneral \\\\phi^4 interaction on Moyal-Weyl spaces. We \
compute the 2- and 4-point\\nfunctions to all orders in the large N limit and \
then apply the approximate\\nWilson renormalization group recursion formula \
to study the renormalized\\ncoupling constants of the theory. The \
non-commutative Wilson-Fisher fixed point\\ninterpolates between the \
commutative Wilson-Fisher fixed point of the Ising\\nuniversality class which \
is found to lie at zero value of the critical coupling\\nconstant a_* of the \
zero dimensional reduction of the theory, and a novel\\nstrongly interacting \
fixed point which lies at infinite value of a_*\\ncorresponding to maximal \
non-commutativity beyond which the two-sheeted\\nstructure of a_* as a \
function of the dilation parameter disappears.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
