         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1206.5653", "submitter" -> "Badis Ydri", "authors" -> 
            "Badis Ydri, Adel Bouchareb", "title" -> 
            "The fate of the Wilson-Fisher fixed point in non-commutative \
\\phi^4", "comments" -> "19 pages, 7 figures, v2:one reference added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "J. Math. Phys. 53, 102301 (2012);", "doi" -> 
            "10.1063/1.4754816", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech hep-ph math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this article we study non-commutative vector sigma model \
with the most\ngeneral \\phi^4 interaction on Moyal-Weyl spaces. We compute \
the 2- and 4-point\nfunctions to all orders in the large N limit and then \
apply the approximate\nWilson renormalization group recursion formula to \
study the renormalized\ncoupling constants of the theory. The non-commutative \
Wilson-Fisher fixed point\ninterpolates between the commutative Wilson-Fisher \
fixed point of the Ising\nuniversality class which is found to lie at zero \
value of the critical coupling\nconstant a_* of the zero dimensional \
reduction of the theory, and a novel\nstrongly interacting fixed point which \
lies at infinite value of a_*\ncorresponding to maximal non-commutativity \
beyond which the two-sheeted\nstructure of a_* as a function of the dilation \
parameter disappears.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 25 Jun 2012 11:41:12 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 6 Nov 2012 19:25:53 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2012-11-07", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ydri", "Badis", ""}, {
              "Bouchareb", "Adel", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
