          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1206.6758\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gurdeep Sehmbi\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gurdeep S. Sehmbi\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Branes and Geometry in String and M-Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PhD Thesis, 143 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DCPT-12/27\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This thesis is based on two papers by the author and \
consists of two parts.\\nWe review the recent developments in the theory of \
multiple M2-branes and\\n3-algebras leading to multiple D2-brane theories. \
The inclusion of flux terms\\nfor the supersymmetric BLG and ABJM theories of \
closed M2-branes is discussed\\nand then generalised to open M2-branes. Here \
the boundary condition is derived\\nand different BPS configurations are \
examined where we find a mass deformed\\nBasu-Harvey equation for the M2-M5 \
system. The Lorentzian 3-algebra is then\\nemployed for obtaining a theory of \
D2-branes in a flux background, we then\\nobtain the new fuzzy funnel \
solution of the system of D2-D4 branes in a flux.\\nMatrix theories and their \
compactifications as well as noncommutative geometry\\nand noncommutative \
gauge theories are reviewed with a discussion of their\\ngeneralisations to \
three dimensions to be used to describe the M-theory three\\nform potential \
$C_3$. A new feature of string theory is then obtained called\\nthe quantum \
Nambu geometry (QNG). It is found by considering the action for\\nD1-strings \
in a RR flux background and we demonstrate that there is a large\\nflux \
double scaling limit where the action is dominated by a \
Chern-Simons-Myers\\ncoupling term. A classical solution to this is the \
quantised spacetime known as\\nthe quantum Nambu geometry. Various matrix \
models are obtained from this\\naction, these are the large flux dominated \
terms of the full actions for the\\ncorresponding matrix models. The QNG \
gives rise to an expansion of D1-strings\\nto D4-branes in the IIA theory, so \
we obtain an action for the large flux terms\\nfor this action which is \
verified by a dimensional reduction of the PST action\\ndescribing M5-branes. \
We make a generalisation of the D4-brane action to\\ndescribe M5-branes using \
a duality. We are describing the 3-form self-dual\\nfield strength of a \
non-abelian generalisation of the PST action.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 28 Jun 2012 16:40:17 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2012-06-29\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Sehmbi\"", ",", "\"Gurdeep S.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                    "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> Left, 
             ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
