         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1206.6758", "submitter" -> "Gurdeep Sehmbi", "authors" -> 
            "Gurdeep S. Sehmbi", "title" -> 
            "Branes and Geometry in String and M-Theory", "comments" -> 
            "PhD Thesis, 143 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> "DCPT-12/27", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This thesis is based on two papers by the author and consists \
of two parts.\nWe review the recent developments in the theory of multiple \
M2-branes and\n3-algebras leading to multiple D2-brane theories. The \
inclusion of flux terms\nfor the supersymmetric BLG and ABJM theories of \
closed M2-branes is discussed\nand then generalised to open M2-branes. Here \
the boundary condition is derived\nand different BPS configurations are \
examined where we find a mass deformed\nBasu-Harvey equation for the M2-M5 \
system. The Lorentzian 3-algebra is then\nemployed for obtaining a theory of \
D2-branes in a flux background, we then\nobtain the new fuzzy funnel solution \
of the system of D2-D4 branes in a flux.\nMatrix theories and their \
compactifications as well as noncommutative geometry\nand noncommutative \
gauge theories are reviewed with a discussion of their\ngeneralisations to \
three dimensions to be used to describe the M-theory three\nform potential \
$C_3$. A new feature of string theory is then obtained called\nthe quantum \
Nambu geometry (QNG). It is found by considering the action for\nD1-strings \
in a RR flux background and we demonstrate that there is a large\nflux double \
scaling limit where the action is dominated by a Chern-Simons-Myers\ncoupling \
term. A classical solution to this is the quantised spacetime known as\nthe \
quantum Nambu geometry. Various matrix models are obtained from this\naction, \
these are the large flux dominated terms of the full actions for the\n\
corresponding matrix models. The QNG gives rise to an expansion of D1-strings\
\nto D4-branes in the IIA theory, so we obtain an action for the large flux \
terms\nfor this action which is verified by a dimensional reduction of the \
PST action\ndescribing M5-branes. We make a generalisation of the D4-brane \
action to\ndescribe M5-branes using a duality. We are describing the 3-form \
self-dual\nfield strength of a non-abelian generalisation of the PST action.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 28 Jun 2012 16:40:17 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2012-06-29", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Sehmbi", "Gurdeep S.", ""}}}], 
