            "  The formation of a confining string (or a p-brane) in a \
Poincare' invariant\ntheory breaks spontaneously this symmetry which is \
thereby realized\nnon-linearly in the effective action of these extended \
objects. As a\nconsequence the form of the action is strongly constrained. A \
new general\nmethod is described to obtain in a systematic way higher order \
Lorentz\ninvariant contributions to this action. We find a simple recipe to \
promote a\nterm invariant under the stability subgroup to an expression \
invariant under\nthe whole Lorentz group. It is based on the following three \
steps: in the\nsaturation of worldsheet (or worldvolume) indices replace the \
Minkowski metric\nwith the inverse of the induced metric; in the saturation \
of indices of the\ntransverse coordinates describing the position of the \
extended object replace\nthe Euclidean metric with a certain new metric; \
finally replace the field\nderivatives of order higher than two with a \
certain covariant derivative.\nLorentz invariance of the expression modified \
this way immediately follows. We\nfind in particular that the leading bulk \
deviation of the Nambu Goto action in\nany space-time dimensions is \
proportional to the square of scalar curvature.\n", 
