                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Daniel N. Blaschke, Thomas Garschall, Francois Gieres, \
Franz Heindl,\\n  Manfred Schweda and Michael Wohlgenannt\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the Renormalization of Non-Commutative Field \
Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"29 pages; v2 minor corrections and references added, to \
appear in\\n  EPJC\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Eur. Phys. J. C73:2262, 2013\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1140/epjc/s10052-012-2262-0\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UWThPh-2012-25\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper addresses three topics concerning the \
quantization of\\nnon-commutative field theories (as defined in terms of the \
Moyal star product\\ninvolving a constant tensor describing the \
non-commutativity of coordinates in\\nEuclidean space). To start with, we \
discuss the Quantum Action Principle and\\nprovide evidence for its validity \
for non-commutative quantum field theories by\\nshowing that the equation of \
motion considered as insertion in the generating\\nfunctional Zc[j] of \
connected Green functions makes sense. Second, we consider\\nthe \
generalization of the BPHZ renormalization scheme to non-commutative \
field\\ntheories and apply it to the case of a self-interacting real scalar \
field.\\nFinally, we discuss the renormalizability of various models for \
a\\nself-interacting complex scalar field by using the approach of \
algebraic\\nrenormalization.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
