Heindl,\n  Manfred Schweda and Michael Wohlgenannt", "title" -> 
            "On the Renormalization of Non-Commutative Field Theories", 
            "comments" -> 
            "29 pages; v2 minor corrections and references added, to appear \
in\n  EPJC", "journal-ref" -> "Eur. Phys. J. C73:2262, 2013", "doi" -> 
            "10.1140/epjc/s10052-012-2262-0", "report-no" -> "UWThPh-2012-25",
             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This paper addresses three topics concerning the quantization \
of\nnon-commutative field theories (as defined in terms of the Moyal star \
product\ninvolving a constant tensor describing the non-commutativity of \
coordinates in\nEuclidean space). To start with, we discuss the Quantum \
Action Principle and\nprovide evidence for its validity for non-commutative \
quantum field theories by\nshowing that the equation of motion considered as \
insertion in the generating\nfunctional Zc[j] of connected Green functions \
makes sense. Second, we consider\nthe generalization of the BPHZ \
renormalization scheme to non-commutative field\ntheories and apply it to the \
case of a self-interacting real scalar field.\nFinally, we discuss the \
renormalizability of various models for a\nself-interacting complex scalar \
field by using the approach of algebraic\nrenormalization.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
