               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1207.5531\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Per Sundin and Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Classical integrability and quantum aspects of the AdS(3) \
x S(3) x S(3)\\n  x S(1) superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"29 pages; v2: updated references and \
acknowledgment\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2012)109\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"MIFPA-12-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we continue the investigation of aspects \
of integrability of\\nthe type IIA AdS(3) x S(3) x S(3) x S(1) and AdS(3) x \
S(3) x T(4) superstrings.\\nBy constructing a one parameter family of flat \
connections we prove that the\\nGreen-Schwarz string is classically \
integrable, at least to quadratic order in\\nfermions, without fixing the \
kappa-symmetry. We then compare the quantum\\ndispersion relation, fixed by \
integrability up to an unknown interpolating\\nfunction h(lambda), to \
explicit one-loop calculations on the string worldsheet.\\nFor AdS(3) x S(3) \
x S(3) x S(1) the spectrum contains heavy, as well as light\\nand massless \
modes, and we find that the one-loop contribution differs\\ndepending on how \
we treat these modes showing that similar regularization\\nambiguities as \
appeared in AdS(4)/CFT(3) occur also here.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
