           "id" -> "1207.5531", "submitter" -> "Linus Wulff", "authors" -> 
            "Per Sundin and Linus Wulff", "title" -> 
            "Classical integrability and quantum aspects of the AdS(3) x S(3) \
x S(3)\n  x S(1) superstring", "comments" -> 
            "29 pages; v2: updated references and acknowledgment", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP10(2012)109", 
            "report-no" -> "MIFPA-12-26", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we continue the investigation of aspects of \
integrability of\nthe type IIA AdS(3) x S(3) x S(3) x S(1) and AdS(3) x S(3) \
x T(4) superstrings.\nBy constructing a one parameter family of flat \
connections we prove that the\nGreen-Schwarz string is classically \
integrable, at least to quadratic order in\nfermions, without fixing the \
kappa-symmetry. We then compare the quantum\ndispersion relation, fixed by \
integrability up to an unknown interpolating\nfunction h(lambda), to explicit \
one-loop calculations on the string worldsheet.\nFor AdS(3) x S(3) x S(3) x \
S(1) the spectrum contains heavy, as well as light\nand massless modes, and \
we find that the one-loop contribution differs\ndepending on how we treat \
these modes showing that similar regularization\nambiguities as appeared in \
AdS(4)/CFT(3) occur also here.\n", 
