         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1207.6908", "submitter" -> "Congkao Wen", "authors" -> 
            "Andreas Brandhuber, Gabriele Travaglini, Congkao Wen", "title" -> 
            "All one-loop amplitudes in N=6 superconformal Chern-Simons \
theory", "comments" -> "22 pages, 7 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2012)145", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We exploit a recently found connection between special \
triple-cut diagrams\nand tree-level recursive diagrams to derive a general \
formula capturing the\nmulti-particle factorisation of arbitrary one-loop \
amplitudes in the ABJM\ntheory. This formula contains certain anomalous \
contributions which are\nreminiscent of the so-called non-factorising \
contributions appearing in the\nfactorisation of one-loop amplitudes in \
four-dimensional gauge theory. In the\nsecond part of the paper we derive a \
recursion relation for the\nsupercoefficients of one-loop amplitudes in ABJM \
theory. By applying this\nrecursion relation, any one-loop supercoefficient \
can be reduced to special\ntriple-cut diagrams involving at least one \
four-point tree amplitude. In turn,\nthis implies that any one-loop \
supercoefficient can be derived from tree-level\nrecursive diagrams.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 30 Jul 2012 12:14:08 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-05", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Brandhuber", "Andreas", ""}, {
              "Travaglini", "Gabriele", ""}, {"Wen", "Congkao", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
