                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Badr Awad Elseid Mohammed\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonplanar Integrability and Parity in ABJ Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+12 pages, Corrected typos, more clarifications, figure \
and appendix\\n  added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"IJMPA Vol. 28 (2013) 1350043\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1142/S0217751X13500437\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"WITS-CTP-101\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this article we study the action of the non-planar \
two-loop dilatation\\noperator in an SU(2)*SU(2) sub-sector of the ABJ \
Chern-Simons-matter theory.\\nThe gauge invariant operators we consider are \
the restricted Schur polynomials.\\nAs in ABJM theory, there is a limit in \
which the spectrum reduces to a set of\\ndecoupled harmonic oscillators, \
indicating integrability in the large M and N\\ndouble limit of the theory. \
We then consider parity transformations on the\\ngauge invariant operators. \
In this case the non-planar anomalous dimensions\\nbreak parity invariance. \
Our analysis shows that (M-N) is related to the\\nholonomy in the string \
theory, confirming one of the main features of the\\ntheory and its string \
dual. Furthermore, in the limit where ABJ theory reduces\\nto ABJM theory, \
parity invariance is restored.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
