                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study correlation functions of Wilson loops and \
local operators in a\\nsubsector of N=4 SYM which preserves two supercharges. \
Localization arguments\\nallow to map the problem to a calculation in bosonic \
two-dimensional Yang-Mills\\ntheory. In turn, this can be reduced to \
computing correlators in certain\\nGaussian multi-matrix models. We focus on \
the correlation function of a Wilson\\nloop and two local operators, and \
solve the corresponding three-matrix model\\nexactly in the planar limit. We \
compare the strong coupling behavior to string\\ntheory in AdS_5xS^5, finding \
precise agreement. We pay particular attention to\\nthe case in which the \
local operators have large R-charge J \\\\sim sqrt{lambda}\\nat strong \
coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
