            "comments" -> 
            "harvmac, 26 pages, 9 figures; v2: minor corrections", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1210 (2012) 098", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2012)098", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.str-el", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study holographic entanglement entropy in the background of \
charged\ndilatonic black holes which can be viewed as holographic duals of \
certain\nfinite density states of N=4 super Yang-Mills. These charged black \
holes are\ndistinguished in that they have vanishing ground state entropy. \
The\nentanglement entropy for a slab experiences a second order phase \
transition as\nthe thickness of the slab is varied, while the entanglement \
entropy for a\nsphere is a smooth function of the radius. This suggests that \
the second scale\nintroduced by the anisotropy of the slab plays an important \
role in driving the\nphase transition. In both cases we do not observe any \
logarithmic violation of\nthe area law indicative of hidden Fermi surfaces. \
We investigate how these\nresults are affected by the inclusion of the \
Gauss-Bonnet term in the bulk\ngravitational action. We also observe that \
such addition to the bulk action\ndoes not change the logarithmic violation \
of the area law in the backgrounds\nwith hyperscaling violation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 14 Aug 2012 18:21:44 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 11 Sep 2012 12:24:07 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2012-10-22", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kulaxizi", "Manuela", ""}, {
              "Parnachev", "Andrei", ""}, {"Schalm", "Koenraad", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
