                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the correlation function of a circular \
Wilson loop with two local\\nscalar operators at generic 4-positions in \
planar N=4 supersymmetric gauge\\ntheory. We show that such correlator is \
fixed by conformal invariance up to a\\nfunction of 't Hooft coupling and two \
scalar combinations of the positions\\ninvariant under the conformal \
transformations preserving the circle. We compute\\nthis function at leading \
orders at weak and strong coupling for some simple\\nchoices of local BPS \
operators. We also check that correlators of an infinite\\nline Wilson loop \
with local operators are the same as those for the circular\\nloop.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
