            "  We construct a generalized cusped Wilson loop operator in N = \
6 super\nChern-Simons-matter theories which is locally invariant under half \
of the\nsupercharges. It depends on two parameters and interpolates smoothly \
between\nthe 1/2 BPS line or circle and a pair of antiparallel lines, \
representing a\nnatural generalization of the quark-antiquark potential in \
ABJ(M) theories. For\nparticular choices of the parameters we obtain 1/6 BPS \
configurations that,\nmapped on S^2 by a conformal transformation, realize a \
three-dimensional\nanalogue of the wedge DGRT Wilson loop of N = 4. The cusp \
couples, in addition\nto the gauge and scalar fields of the theory, also to \
the fermions in the\nbifundamental representation of the U(N)xU(M) gauge \
group and its expectation\nvalue is expressed as the holonomy of a suitable \
superconnection. We discuss\nthe definition of these observables in terms of \
traces and the role of the\nboundary conditions of fermions along the loop. \
We perform a complete two-loop\nanalysis, obtaining an explicit result for \
the generalized cusp at the second\nnon-trivial order, from which we read off \
the interaction potential between\nheavy 1/2 BPS particles in the ABJ(M) \
model. Our results open the possibility\nto explore in the three-dimensional \
case the connection between localization\nproperties and integrability, \
recently advocated in D = 4.\n", 
