                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We determine the complete NLL running of the static \
potential associated with\\nthe locally 1/2 BPS Wilson loop in N=4 \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory. We\\npresent results for the SU(N_c) \
singlet as well as for the adjoint\\nconfiguration and arbitrary N_c at weak \
coupling. In order to derive the\\nrespective anomalous dimensions we perform \
a two-loop calculation in the N=4\\nsupersymmetric version of the effective \
field theory pNRQCD. In addition we\\nconfirm the recently obtained \
fixed-order result for the singlet static\\npotential generated exclusively \
by ladder diagrams to the third order in the\\nt`Hooft coupling. We also give \
an explicit expression for the logarithmic\\ncontribution of all non-ladder \
diagrams at this order.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
