                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present two new families of Wilson loop operators in \
N= 6 supersymmetric\\nChern-Simons theory. The first one is defined for an \
arbitrary contour on the\\nthree dimensional space and it resembles the \
Zarembo's construction in N=4 SYM.\\nThe second one involves arbitrary curves \
on the two dimensional sphere. In both\\ncases one can add certain scalar and \
fermionic couplings to the Wilson loop so\\nit preserves at least two \
supercharges. Some previously known loops, notably\\nthe 1/2 BPS circle, \
belong to this class, but we point out more special cases\\nwhich were not \
known before. They could provide further tests of the\\ngauge/gravity \
correspondence in the ABJ(M) case and interesting observables,\\nexactly \
computable by localization\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
