               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Jeff Murugan, Per Sundin and Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Classical and quantum integrability in \
AdS(2)/CFT(1)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages, 2 figures; v2: References added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2013)047\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"MIFPA-12-33; QGaSLAB-12-04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the type IIA string on AdS(2)xS(2)xT(6) \
supported by RR-flux\\nwhich describes the gravitational side of the \
AdS(2)/CFT(1) correspondence.\\nWhile the four-dimensional part AdS(2)xS(2) \
can be realized as a supercoset,\\nthe full superstring has both coset and \
non-coset excitations, the latter\\ngiving rise to massless worldsheet modes, \
a somewhat novel feature in AdS/CFT.\\nThe string is nevertheless known to be \
integrable at the classical level. In\\nthis paper we perform several \
computations checking aspects of both classical\\nand quantum string \
integrability. At the classical level we compute energies\\nfor the near BMN \
string and successfully match these against Bethe ansatz\\npredictions. \
Furthermore, integrability dictates a magnon dispersion relation\\nwhich we \
compare with the poles of loop corrected propagators, at both the one\\nand \
two-loop level. At one loop, where only tadpole diagrams contribute, \
we\\nfind that the bosonic and fermionic contributions sum up to zero. Under \
the\\nassumption of worldsheet supersymmetry, we then compute the two-loop \
sunset\\ndiagram in the near flat space limit. As in AdS(5)xS(5) we find that \
the result\\nfits nicely into the sine-square structure of the dispersion \
relation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 26 Sep 2012 20:02:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 18 Oct 2012 14:28:57 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-06-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Murugan\"", ",", "\"Jeff\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sundin\"", ",", "\"Per\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Wulff\"", ",", "\"Linus\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
