               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1210.1561\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Guillermo Ballesteros\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Guillermo Ballesteros and Brando Bellazzini\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Effective perfect fluids in cosmology\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matches JCAP version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JCAP04(2013)001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2013/04/001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We describe the cosmological dynamics of perfect fluids \
within the framework\\nof effective field theories. The effective action is a \
derivative expansion\\nwhose terms are selected by the symmetry requirements \
on the relevant\\nlong-distance degrees of freedom, which are identified with \
comoving\\ncoordinates. The perfect fluid is defined by requiring invariance \
of the action\\nunder internal volume-preserving diffeomorphisms and general \
covariance. At\\nlowest order in derivatives, the dynamics is encoded in a \
single function of\\nthe entropy density that characterizes the properties of \
the fluid, such as the\\nequation of state and the speed of sound. This \
framework allows a neat\\nsimultaneous description of fluid and metric \
perturbations. Longitudinal fluid\\nperturbations are closely related to the \
adiabatic modes, while the transverse\\nmodes mix with vector metric \
perturbations as a consequence of vorticity\\nconservation. This formalism \
features a large flexibility which can be of\\npractical use for higher order \
perturbation theory and cosmological parameter\\nestimation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
