                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this work we consider various correlators with Schur \
polynomials in ABJ(M)\\nmodels that on the dual gravity side should \
correspond to processes involving\\ngiant gravitons. Our analysis imposes \
several constraints on the physics of the\\nprobe branes on AdS4xCP3 as well \
as sheds more light on giant graviton\\nsolutions in this background with \
additional NS B-field. Our main tool is a\\nformula that we derive for \
extremal n-point functions of the single trace\\nchiral primary operators in \
the free field theory limit. The formula expresses\\nthe correlators in terms \
of the two-point function of Schur polynomials labeled\\nby hook diagrams and \
is valid for a large class of gauge theories. In\\nparticular, in N = 4 SYM, \
it proves the conjecture of Beisert et al.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
