               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We demonstrate the equivalence between the worldsheet \
one-loop partition\\nfunctions computed near classical string solutions in \
the Green-Schwarz and in\\nthe pure-spinor formulations of superstrings in \
AdS(5) x S(5). While their\\nbosonic sectors are the same in the conformal \
gauge, their fermionic sectors\\nsuperficially appear to be very different \
(first vs second derivative kinetic\\nterms, presence vs absence of fermionic \
gauge symmetry). Still, we show that\\nthe quadratic fluctuation spectrum of \
sixteen fermionic modes of the\\npure-spinor formulation is the same as in \
the Green-Schwarz superstring and the\\ncontribution of the extra \
\\\"massless\\\" fermionic modes cancels against that of\\nthe pure-spinor \
ghosts. We also provide evidence for a similar semiclassical\\nequivalence \
between the Green-Schwarz and the hybrid formulations of\\nsuperstrings in \
AdS(2) x S(2) x T(6) by studying several particular examples of\\nstring \
solutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
