            "  We demonstrate the equivalence between the worldsheet one-loop \
partition\nfunctions computed near classical string solutions in the \
Green-Schwarz and in\nthe pure-spinor formulations of superstrings in AdS(5) \
x S(5). While their\nbosonic sectors are the same in the conformal gauge, \
their fermionic sectors\nsuperficially appear to be very different (first vs \
second derivative kinetic\nterms, presence vs absence of fermionic gauge \
symmetry). Still, we show that\nthe quadratic fluctuation spectrum of sixteen \
fermionic modes of the\npure-spinor formulation is the same as in the \
