               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrej Stepanchuk\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A. Stepanchuk, A. A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On (non)integrability of classical strings in p-brane \
backgrounds\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"27 pages, 1 figure, v2: added references, minor \
corrections\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A46:125401,2013\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/46/12/125401\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-AS-2012-01\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the question of possible integrability \
of classical string\\nmotion in curved p-brane backgrounds. For example, the \
D3-brane metric\\ninterpolates between the flat and the AdS_5 x S^5 regions \
in which string\\npropagation is integrable. We find that while the \
point-like string (geodesic)\\nequations are integrable, the equations \
describing an extended string in the\\ncomplete D3-brane geometry are not. \
The same conclusion is reached for similar\\nbrane intersection backgrounds \
interpolating between flat space and AdS_k x\\nS^k. We consider, in \
particular, the case of the NS 5-brane-fundamental string\\nbackground. To \
demonstrate non-integrability we make a special \\\"pulsating\\nstring\\\" \
ansatz for which the string equations reduce to an \
effective\\none-dimensional system. Expanding near this simple solution leads \
to a linear\\ndifferential equation for small fluctuations that cannot be \
solved in\\nquadratures, implying non-integrability of the original set of \
string\\nequations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
