            "Non-equilibrium Wilson loops in N=4 SYM", "comments" -> 
            "24 pages, 7 figures. Parts of the text rewritten. Section 5 has \
been\n  expanded. Agrees with the published version", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys. Rev. D 88, 105022 (2013)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.88.105022", "report-no" -> 
            "Nordita-2012-92; RH-11-2012", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider rectangular Wilson loops in certain \
non-equilibrium quantum\nstates in N=4 SYM at weak coupling, prepared with a \
quantum quench. We find\nthat in the ladder approximation, the Bethe-Salpeter \
equation can be reduced to\nsolving a massive 1+1 dimensional wave-equation \
with a leaking boundary\ncondition leading to a quasinormal behavior \
analogous to what is found in\nstudying dynamics of fields in black hole \
backrounds. Furthermore, we find that\nthe Wilson loops with size L approach \
a thermal form after time T=L/2. The\nthermal form found in the current paper \
follows from the particular initial\nstate chosen.\n", 
