                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper studies semiclassical strings in AdS3 x S3 x \
S3 x S1 using the\\nalgebraic curve. Calculating one-loop corrections to the \
energy of the giant\\nmagnon fixes the constant term c in the expansion of \
the coupling h(\\\\lambda).\\nComparing these to similar corrections for long \
spinning strings gives a\\nprediction for the one-loop term f_1 in the \
expansion of the cusp anomalous\\ndimension f(h), for all \\\\alpha (where \\\
\\alpha --> 1 is the AdS3 x S3 x T4\\nlimit). For these semiclassical mode \
sums there is a similar choice of\\nregularisation prescriptions to that \
encountered in AdS4 x CP3. However at\\n\\\\alpha \\\\neq 1/2 they lead to \
different values of f_1 and are therefore not\\nrelated by a simple change of \
the coupling. The algebraic curve is also used to\\ncalculate various \
finite-size corrections for giant magnons, which are\\nwell-behaved as \
\\\\alpha --> 1, and can be compared to the recently \
published\\nS-matrices.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
