            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1211.5838\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Chanyong Park\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bum-Hoon Lee, Bogeun Gwak, and Chanyong Park\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Correlation functions of the ABJM model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"16 pages, no figure\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.87.086002\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the ABJM model, we study the three-point function of \
two heavy operators\\nand an (ir)relevant one. Following the AdS/CFT \
correspondence, the structure\\nconstant in the large 't Hooft coupling limit \
can be factorized into two parts.\\nOne is the structure constant with a \
marginal operator, which is fully\\ndetermined by the physical quantities of \
heavy operator and gives rise to the\\nconsistent result with the RG \
analysis. The other can be expressed as the\\nuniversal form depending only \
on the conformal dimension of an (ir)relevant\\noperator. We also investigate \
the new size effect of a circular string dual to\\na certain closed spin \
chain.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
