            "  We study the leading quantum string correction to the dressing \
phase in the\nasymptotic Bethe Ansatz system for superstring in AdS_3 x S^3 x \
T^4 supported\nby RR flux. We find that the phase should be different from \
the BES phase\nappearing in the AdS_5 x S^5 case. We use the simplest example \
of a rigid\ncircular string with two equal spins in S^3 and also consider the \
general\napproach based on the algebraic curve description. We also discuss \
the case of\nthe AdS_3 x S^3 x S^3 x S^1 theory and find the dependence of \
the 1-loop\ncorrection to the effective string tension function h(\\lambda) \
(expected to\nenter the magnon dispersion relation) on the parameters alpha \
related to the\nratio of the two 3-sphere radii. This correction vanishes in \
the AdS_3 x S^3 x\nT^4 case.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
