            "  Using the S-matrix for the d(2,1;alpha)^2 symmetric spin-chain \
of AdS3/CFT2,\nwe propose a new set of all-loop Bethe equations for the \
system. These\nequations differ from the ones previously found in the \
literature by the choice\nof relative grading between the two copies of the \
d(2,1;alpha) superalgebra,\nand involve four undetermined scalar factors that \
play the role of dressing\nphases. Imposing crossing symmetry and comparing \
with the near-BMN form of the\nS-matrix found in the literature, we find \
several novel features. In\nparticular, the scalar factors must differ from \
the Beisert-Eden-Staudacher\nphase, and should couple nodes of different \
masses to each other. In the\nsemiclassical limit the phases are given by a \
suitable generalization of\nArutyunov-Frolov-Staudacher phase.\n", 
