            "  This review covers a number of applications of conformal field \
theory methods\nfor perturbative calculations in N=4 Super Yang-Mills and \
ABJM theory. After\nmotivating the role of superconformal symmetry for \
elementary particle physics\nresearch, we review some basic facts about \
conformal symmetry and conformal\ntransformations of fields in a pedagogical \
manner. The implications for\nperturbative quantum field theory calculations \
are discussed in terms of Ward\nidentities. Recent developments and relations \
between amplitudes, correlators\nand Wilson loops are reviewed for N=4 Super \
Yang-Mills as well as ABJM theory.\nWe give more details on previously \
published results on light-like polygonal\nWilson loops in ABJM theory as \
well as the calculation of three-point functions\nof two BPS and one \
twist-two operator in N=4 Super Yang-Mills theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 20 Dec 2012 18:27:30 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2012-12-21", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Wiegandt", "Konstantin", ""}}}], 
