, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  N=2* gauge theory in four space-time dimensions arises \
as a deformation of\\nthe parent N=4 supersymmetric Yang-Mill theory under \
which its hypermultiplet\\nacquires a mass. This theory, on the one hand, has \
a known supergravity dual\\nand on the other hand is amenable to \
localization. We explain, using\\nlocalization, a dynamical selection of the \
supergravity Coulomb branch vacuum\\nat large N. We also demonstrate that \
large Wilson loops obey perimeter law,\\nagain finding exact match between \
direct field-theory calculations and string\\ntheory. Additionally, we \
compute free energy at large 't Hooft coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
