Theory", "comments" -> "15 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1007/JHEP03(2013)062", "report-no" -> 
             "NORDITA-2013-1; UUITP-01/13; UWO-TH-13/1", "categories" -> 
             "hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  N=2* gauge theory in four space-time dimensions arises as a \
deformation of\nthe parent N=4 supersymmetric Yang-Mill theory under which \
its hypermultiplet\nacquires a mass. This theory, on the one hand, has a \
known supergravity dual\nand on the other hand is amenable to localization. \
We explain, using\nlocalization, a dynamical selection of the supergravity \
Coulomb branch vacuum\nat large N. We also demonstrate that large Wilson \
loops obey perimeter law,\nagain finding exact match between direct \
field-theory calculations and string\ntheory. Additionally, we compute free \
energy at large 't Hooft coupling.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
