               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1301.5092\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"George Georgiou\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"George Georgiou, Bum-Hoon Lee and Chanyong Park\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Correlators of massive string states with conserved \
currents\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"17 pages,comments and reference added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2013)167\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate correlation functions of the R-current or \
the stress-energy\\ntensor T_{\\\\mu\\\\nu} with two non-protected operators \
dual to generic massive\\nstring states with rotation in S^5, in the context \
of the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence. Field theory Ward identities make \
predictions about the\\nall-loop behaviour of these correlators. In \
particular, they restrict the\\nfusion coefficient to be proportional to the \
R-charge of the operators or to\\ntheir dimension, respectively, with certain \
coefficients of proportionality. We\\nreproduce these predictions, at strong \
coupling, using string theory.\\nFurthermore, we point out that the recently \
observed strong coupling\\nfactorisation of 4-point correlators is consistent \
with conformal symmetry and\\nputs constraints on the strong coupling \
expressions of 4-point correlators\\ninvolving R-currents or the \
stress-energy tensor.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
