               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1301.6377\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kenji Fukushima\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Kenji Fukushima and Chihiro Sasaki\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The phase diagram of nuclear and quark matter at high \
baryon density\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"84 pages, 35 figures, 2 tables; submitted to \
Prog.Part.Nucl.Phys;\\n  typos removed, wording corrected, references added, \
some parts significantly\\n  elaborated\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph nucl-th\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review theoretical approaches to explore the phase \
diagram of nuclear and\\nquark matter at high baryon density. We first look \
over the basic properties of\\nquantum chromodynamics (QCD) and address how \
to describe various states of QCD\\nmatter. In our discussions on nuclear \
matter we cover the relativistic\\nmean-field model, the chiral perturbation \
theory, and the approximation based\\non the large-Nc limit where Nc is the \
number of colors. We then explain the\\nliquid-gas phase transition and the \
inhomogeneous meson condensation in nuclear\\nmatter with emphasis put on the \
relevance to quark matter. We commence the next\\npart focused on quark \
matter with the bootstrap model and the Hagedorn\\ntemperature. Then we turn \
to properties associated with chiral symmetry and\\nexposit theoretical \
descriptions of the chiral phase transition. There emerge\\nsome quark-matter \
counterparts of phenomena seen in nuclear matter such as the\\nliquid-gas \
phase transition and the inhomogeneous structure of the chiral\\ncondensate. \
The third regime that is being recognized recently is what is\\ncalled \
quarkyonic matter, which has both aspects of nuclear and quark matter.\\nWe \
closely elucidate the basic idea of quarkyonic matter in the large-Nc \
limit\\nand its physics implications. Finally, we discuss some experimental \
indications\\nfor the QCD phase diagram and close the review with \
outlooks.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 27 Jan 2013 17:21:40 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
