               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1301.7220\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rafael Hernandez\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Rafael Hernandez, Juan Miguel Nieto\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic correlation functions of hexagon Wilson loops \
with one local\\n  operator\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"12 pages. Latex. v2: Reference added. v3: Added \
clarifications,\\n  published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett.B726:417-421,2013\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2013.08.029\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the ratio of the correlation function of an \
hexagon light-like\\nWilson loop with one local operator over the expectation \
value of the Wilson\\nloop within the strong-coupling regime of the AdS/CFT \
correspondence. We choose\\nthe hexagon Wilson loop within a class of minimal \
solutions obtained by cutting\\nand gluing light-like quadrangle loops. These \
surfaces do not have an\\ninterpretation in terms of dual scattering \
amplitudes but they still exhibit\\ngeneral features of the mixed correlation \
function. In the case of a regular\\nnull hexagon conformal symmetry \
constrains the space-time dependence of the\\ncorrelator up to a function of \
three conformal cross-ratios. We obtain the\\nleading-order contribution to \
the correlation function in the semiclassical\\napproximation of large string \
tension, and express the result in terms of three\\nconformal ratios in the \
case where the local operator is taken to be the\\ndilaton. We include the \
analysis of an irregular Wilson loop obtained after a\\nboost of the regular \
hexagon.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
