                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the anomalous dimensions of operators in the \
scalar sector of\\n\\\\beta-deformed ABJ(M) theories. We show that the \
anomalous dimension matrix at\\ntwo-loop order gives an integrable \
Hamiltonian acting on an alternating SU(4)\\nspin chain with the spins at odd \
lattice sides in the fundamental\\nrepresentation and the spins at even \
lattices in the anti-fundamental\\nrepresentation. We get a set of \
$\\\\beta$-deformed Bethe ansatz equations which\\ngive the eigenvalues of \
Hamiltonian of this deformed spin chain system. Based\\non our computations, \
we also extend our study to non-supersymmetric\\nthree-parameter \
$\\\\gamma$-deformation of ABJ(M) theories and find that the\\ncorresponding \
Hamiltonian is the same as the one in \\\\beta-deformed case at\\ntwo-loop \
level in the scalar sector.\\n\""}]}, {
