               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A tree-level 3-point function in the su(3)-sector of \
planar N=4 SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages, 17 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Journal of High Energy Physics, Volume 2013, Issue \
10\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2013)138\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"IPhT/t13/034\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We classify the 3-point functions of local \
gauge-invariant single-trace\\noperators in the scalar sector of planar N=4 \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills\\ninvolving at least one su(3) operator. In the \
case of two su(3) and one su(2)\\noperators, the tree-level 3-point function \
can be expressed in terms of scalar\\nproducts of su(3) Bethe vectors. \
Moreover, if the second level Bethe roots of\\none of the su(3) operators is \
trivial (set to infinity), this 3-point function\\ncan be written in a \
determinant form. Using the determinant representation, we\\nevaluate the \
structure constant in the semi-classical limit, when the number of\\nroots \
goes to infinity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
