           "id" -> "1302.3539", "submitter" -> "Ivan K. Kostov", "authors" -> 
            "Omar Foda, Yunfeng Jiang, Ivan Kostov, Didina Serban", "title" -> 
            "A tree-level 3-point function in the su(3)-sector of planar N=4 \
SYM", "comments" -> "31 pages, 17 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Journal of High Energy Physics, Volume 2013, Issue 10", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2013)138", "report-no" -> "IPhT/t13/034", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We classify the 3-point functions of local gauge-invariant \
single-trace\noperators in the scalar sector of planar N=4 supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills\ninvolving at least one su(3) operator. In the case of two su(3) \
and one su(2)\noperators, the tree-level 3-point function can be expressed in \
terms of scalar\nproducts of su(3) Bethe vectors. Moreover, if the second \
level Bethe roots of\none of the su(3) operators is trivial (set to \
infinity), this 3-point function\ncan be written in a determinant form. Using \
the determinant representation, we\nevaluate the structure constant in the \
semi-classical limit, when the number of\nroots goes to infinity.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
