 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study in detail certain brane solutions with compact \
extra dimensions M^4\\nx K in the IKKT matrix model, with K being a \
two-dimensional rotating torus\\nembedded in R^6. We focus on the \
compactification moduli and the fluctuations\\nof K \\\\subset R^6 and their \
physical significance. Mediated by the Poisson\\ntensor, they contribute to \
the effective 4-dimensional metric on the brane, and\\nthereby become \
gravitational degrees of freedom. We show that the zero modes\\ncorresponding \
to the global symmetries of the model lead to Ricci-flat\\n4-dimensional \
metric perturbations, wherever the energy-momentum tensor\\nvanishes. Their \
coupling to the energy momentum tensor depends on the extrinsic\\ncurvature \
of the brane.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
