            "  We study in detail certain brane solutions with compact extra \
dimensions M^4\nx K in the IKKT matrix model, with K being a two-dimensional \
rotating torus\nembedded in R^6. We focus on the compactification moduli and \
the fluctuations\nof K \\subset R^6 and their physical significance. Mediated \
by the Poisson\ntensor, they contribute to the effective 4-dimensional metric \
on the brane, and\nthereby become gravitational degrees of freedom. We show \
