                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We confront the recently proposed exact S-matrices for \
AdS(3)/CFT(2) with\\ndirect worldsheet calculations. Utilizing the BMN and \
Near Flat Space (NFS)\\nexpansions for strings on AdS(3) x S(3) x S(3) x S(1) \
and AdS(3) x S(3) x T(4)\\nwe compute both tree-level and one-loop scattering \
amplitudes. Up to some minor\\nissues we find nice agreement in the \
tree-level sector. At the one-loop level\\nhowever we find that certain \
non-zero tree-level processes, which are not\\nvisible in the exact solution, \
contribute, via the optical theorem, and give an\\napparent mismatch for \
certain amplitudes. Furthermore we find that a proposed\\none-loop \
modification of the dressing phase correctly reproduces the \
worldsheet\\ncalculation while the standard Hernandez-Lopez phase does not. \
We also compute\\nseveral massless to massless processes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
