                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a class of noncommutative gauge theory models \
on 2-dimensional Moyal\\nspace from the viewpoint of matrix models and \
explore some related properties.\\nExpanding the action around symmetric \
vacua generates non local matrix models\\nwith polynomial interaction terms. \
For a particular vacuum, we can invert the\\nkinetic operator which is \
related to a Jacobi operator. The resulting\\npropagator can be expressed in \
terms of Chebyschev polynomials of second kind.\\nWe show that non vanishing \
correlations exist at large separations. General\\nconsiderations on the \
kinetic operators stemming from the other class of\\nsymmetric vacua, \
indicates that only one class of symmetric vacua should lead\\nto fast \
decaying propagators. The quantum stability of the vacuum is \
briefly\\ndiscussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
