               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Takashi Kameyama, Kentaroh Yoshida\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"String theories on warped AdS backgrounds and integrable \
deformations of\\n  spin chains\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, no figure, LaTeX, v2: typos corrected, minor \
comments and\\n  references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2013)146\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"KUNS-2445\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study integrable deformations of AdS/CFT by focusing \
upon three kinds of\\nwarped AdS_3 geometries, 1) space-like warped AdS_3, 2) \
time-like warped AdS_3\\nand 3) null warped AdS_3. These geometries are \
embedded into type IIB\\nsupergravity solutions and are regarded as \
consistent string backgrounds. By\\nrestricting the classical motion of \
strings on the warped AdS_3xS^1 subspace,\\nthe Landau-Lifshitz sigma models \
are derived by taking the fast-moving limit.\\nThe first two warped AdS_3 \
spaces correspond to anisotropic deformations of the\\nsl(2) spin chain and \
the last one to Jordanian deformations. After taking the\\ncontinuum limit of \
the deformed spin chains with coherent states, the resulting\\ntheories agree \
with the Landau-Lifshitz sigma models obtained from the\\nstring-theory side.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
