            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The type IIB supergravity AdS_3 x S^3 x T^4 background with \
mixed RR and NSNS\n3-form fluxes is a near-horizon limit of a non-threshold \
bound state of D5-D1\nand NS5-NS1 branes. The corresponding superstring \
world-sheet theory is\nexpected to be integrable, opening the possibility of \
computing its exact\nspectrum for any values of the coefficient q of the NSNS \
flux and the string\ntension. In arXiv:1303.1447 we have found the tree-level \
S-matrix for the\nmassive BMN excitations in this theory, which turned out to \
have a simple\ndependence on q. Here, by analyzing the constraints of \
symmetry and\nintegrability, we propose an exact massive-sector dispersion \
relation and the\nexact S-matrix for this world-sheet theory. The S-matrix \
generalizes its recent\nconstruction in the q=0 case in arXiv:1303.5995.\n", 
