Roiban\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Generalized unitarity and the worldsheet S matrix in \
AdS_n x S^n x\\n  M^(10-2n)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"57 pages, Latex, 6 figures v2: minor misprints and \
misprints in\\n  equations in secs 7.1 and 7.2 corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The integrability-based solution of string theories \
related to\\nAdS(n)/CFT(n-1) dualities relies on the worldsheet S matrix. \
Using generalized\\nunitarity we construct the terms with logarithmic \
dependence on external\\nmomenta at one- and two-loop order in the worldsheet \
S matrix for strings in a\\ngeneral integrable worldsheet theory. We also \
discuss aspects of calculations\\nat higher orders. The S-matrix elements are \
expressed as sums of integrals with\\ncoefficients given in terms of \
tree-level worldsheet four-point scattering\\namplitudes. One-loop rational \
functions, not determined by two-dimensional\\nunitarity cuts, are fixed by \
symmetry considerations. They play an important\\nrole in the determination \
of the two-loop logarithmic contributions. We\\nillustrate the general \
analysis by computing the logarithmic terms in the one-\\nand two-loop \
four-particle S-matrix elements in the massive worldsheet sectors\\nof string \
theory in AdS_5 x S^5, AdS_4 x CP^3, AdS_3 x S^3 x S^3 x S^1 and\\nAdS_3 x \
S^3 x T^4. We explore the structure of the S matrices and provide\\nexplicit \
evidence for the absence of higher-order logarithms and for \
the\\nexponentiation of the one-loop dressing phase.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
