                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compare exact results from Pestun's localization of \
SU(N) N=2^* gauge\\ntheory on S^4 with available holographic models. While \
localization can explain\\nthe Coulomb branch vacuum of the holographic \
Pilch-Warner flow, it disagrees\\nwith the holographic Gauntlett et.al vacuum \
of N=2 super Yang-Mills theory. We\\nfurther compute the free energy of the \
Pilch-Warner flow on S^4 and show that\\nit disagrees with the localization \
result both for a finite S^4 radius, and in\\nthe S^4 decompactification \
limit. Thus, neither model represents holographic\\ndual of supersymmetric \
S^4 localization of Pestun.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
