                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider general supersymmetric Wilson loops in ABJM \
model, i.e.\\nChern-Simons-matter theory in 2+1 dimensions with N=6 \
supersymmetry. They are\\nso-called Zarembo-type: the Wilson loops of our \
interest have generic contours\\nin spacetime, but the scalar field coupling \
is arranged accordingly so that\\nthere are unbroken supersymmetries. Based \
on the supermatrix formulation of\\nWilson loops by Drukker and Trancanelli, \
we construct explicitly 1/6-BPS Wilson\\nloops and check that their \
expectation value is protected using perturbation up\\nto two loops. We also \
study the dual string configuration in AdS4 x CP3\\nbackground and check the \
supersymmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
