            "10.1142/S0217732313501502", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider general supersymmetric Wilson loops in ABJM model, \
i.e.\nChern-Simons-matter theory in 2+1 dimensions with N=6 supersymmetry. \
They are\nso-called Zarembo-type: the Wilson loops of our interest have \
generic contours\nin spacetime, but the scalar field coupling is arranged \
accordingly so that\nthere are unbroken supersymmetries. Based on the \
supermatrix formulation of\nWilson loops by Drukker and Trancanelli, we \
construct explicitly 1/6-BPS Wilson\nloops and check that their expectation \
value is protected using perturbation up\nto two loops. We also study the \
dual string configuration in AdS4 x CP3\nbackground and check the \
supersymmetry.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 29 Apr 2013 13:41:52 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 1 May 2013 15:05:00 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-15", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kim", "Nakwoo", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
