            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study membrane configurations in AdS_{7/4}xS^{4/7}. The \
membranes are\nwrapped around the compact manifold S^{4/7} and are \
dynamically equivalent to\nbosonic strings in AdS_5. We thus conveniently \
identify them as \"Stringy\nMembranes\". For the case of AdS_7xS^4, their \
construction is carried out by\nembedding the Polyakov action for classical \
bosonic strings in AdS_5, into the\ncorresponding membrane action. Therefore, \
every string configuration in AdS_5\ncan be realized by an appropriately \
chosen stringy membrane in AdS_7xS^4. We\ndiscuss the possibility of this \
being also the case for stringy membranes in\nAdS_4xS^7/Z^k (k > 1 or k = 1). \
By performing a stability analysis to the\nconstructed solutions, we find \
that the (membrane) fluctuations along their\ntransverse directions are \
organized in multiple Lam\\'{e} stability bands and\ngaps in the space of \
parameters of the configurations. In this membrane\npicture, strings exhibit \
a single band/gap structure.\n", 
