 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the classical limit of the recently \
obtained exact result for the\\nanomalous dimension of a cusped Wilson line \
with the insertion of an operator\\nwith L units of R-charge at the cusp in \
planar N=4 SYM. The classical limit\\nrequires taking both the 't Hooft \
coupling and L to infinity. Since the formula\\nfor the cusp anomalous \
dimension involves determinants of size proportional to\\nL, the classical \
limit requires a matrix model reformulation of the result. We\\nconstruct \
such matrix model-like representation and find corresponding\\nclassical \
algebraic curve. Using this we derive the classical value of the \
cusp\\nanomalous dimension and the 1-loop correction to it. We check our \
results\\nagainst the energy of the classical solution and numerically by \
extrapolating\\nfrom the quantum regime of finite L.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
