            "  We consider the classical limit of the recently obtained exact \
result for the\nanomalous dimension of a cusped Wilson line with the \
insertion of an operator\nwith L units of R-charge at the cusp in planar N=4 \
SYM. The classical limit\nrequires taking both the 't Hooft coupling and L to \
infinity. Since the formula\nfor the cusp anomalous dimension involves \
determinants of size proportional to\nL, the classical limit requires a \
matrix model reformulation of the result. We\nconstruct such matrix \
