 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This note calculates the Hernandez-Lopez phases for \
strings in AdS3 x S3 x S3\\nx S1 by semiclassical methods using the \
d(2,1;\\\\alpha)^2 algebraic curve. By\\nworking at general \\\\alpha\\\\ we \
include modes absent from previous semiclassical\\ncalculations of this phase \
in AdS3 x S3 x T4, and in particular can study the\\nscattering of particles \
of different mass. By carefully re-deriving the\\nsemiclassical formula we \
clarify some issues of antisymmetrisation, cutoffs and\\nsurface terms which \
could safely be ignored in AdS5 x S5, and some issues about\\nthe terms c_1,s \
which were absent there. As a result we see agreement with the\\nrecently \
calculated all-loop dressing phase in the AdS3 x S3 x T4 case, and\\nexactly \
1/2 this in the general case AdS3 x S3 x S3 x S1 for any \\\\alpha\\\\ \
and\\nany (light) polarisations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
