               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1306.6620\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dimitrios Giataganas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"George Georgiou, Dimitrios Giataganas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Generalised cusp anomalous dimension in beta-deformed \
super Yang Mills\\n  theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"23 pages, 2 figures, version published in JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2013)079\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this work we study the cusp anomalous dimension of \
the marginally deformed\\nN=4 sYM theory. We find the expression of the cusp \
anomalous dimension both at\\nthe weak and strong coupling limits. On the \
gravity side we partially map the\\nsystem of equations to that of undeformed \
N=4 sYM, by defining in the internal\\nspace an effective angle \\\\Delta \
\\\\theta_{eff} which depends on the deformation\\nparameter. The cusp \
anomalous dimension then can be read from that of the N=4\\nsYM theory, by \
using this effective angle instead of the usual angle of the\\nundeformed \
5-sphere. In the weak coupling regime we find no beta dependence up\\nto two \
loops. Based on these results we conjecture that for any value of\\nlambda, \
the cusp anomalous dimension is given by the N=4 sYM result using \
the\\ncoupling dependent effective angle. As a consequence of this, we derive \
a\\nBPS-like condition between the angle of the AdS space and the \
\\\\Delta\\n\\\\theta_{eff} of the deformed sphere which when satisfied, \
nullifies the cusp\\nanomalous dimension.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
