            "authors" -> "George Georgiou, Dimitrios Giataganas", "title" -> 
            "Generalised cusp anomalous dimension in beta-deformed super Yang \
Mills\n  theory", "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, 2 figures, version published in JHEP", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP10(2013)079", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this work we study the cusp anomalous dimension of the \
marginally deformed\nN=4 sYM theory. We find the expression of the cusp \
anomalous dimension both at\nthe weak and strong coupling limits. On the \
gravity side we partially map the\nsystem of equations to that of undeformed \
N=4 sYM, by defining in the internal\nspace an effective angle \\Delta \
\\theta_{eff} which depends on the deformation\nparameter. The cusp anomalous \
dimension then can be read from that of the N=4\nsYM theory, by using this \
effective angle instead of the usual angle of the\nundeformed 5-sphere. In \
the weak coupling regime we find no beta dependence up\nto two loops. Based \
on these results we conjecture that for any value of\nlambda, the cusp \
anomalous dimension is given by the N=4 sYM result using the\ncoupling \
dependent effective angle. As a consequence of this, we derive a\nBPS-like \
condition between the angle of the AdS space and the \\Delta\n\\theta_{eff} \
of the deformed sphere which when satisfied, nullifies the cusp\nanomalous \
dimension.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 27 Jun 2013 19:43:43 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 2 Dec 2013 15:04:05 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
