               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1307.0786\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marco Stefano Bianchi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marco S. Bianchi, Gaston Giribet, Matias Leoni, Silvia \
Penati\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The 1/2 BPS Wilson loop in ABJ(M) at two loops: The \
details\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"54 pages, 2 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1310 (2013) 085\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2013)085\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the expectation value of the 1/2 BPS \
circular Wilson loop operator\\nin ABJ(M) theory at two loops in perturbation \
theory. Our result turns out to\\nbe in exact agreement with the weak \
coupling limit of the prediction coming\\nfrom localization, including finite \
N contributions associated to non-planar\\ndiagrams. It also confirms the \
identification of the correct framing factor\\nthat connects framing-zero and \
framing-one expressions, previously proposed.\\nThe evaluation of the 1/2 BPS \
operator is made technically difficult in\\ncomparison with other observables \
of ABJ(M) theory by the appearance of\\nintegrals involving the coupling \
between fermions and gauge fields, which are\\nabsent for instance in the 1/6 \
BPS case. We describe in detail how to\\nanalytically solve these integrals \
in dimensional regularization with\\ndimensional reduction (DRED). By \
suitably performing the physical limit to\\nthree dimensions we clarify the \
role played by short distance divergences on\\nthe final result and the \
mechanism of their cancellation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
