            "  We compute the expectation value of the 1/2 BPS circular \
Wilson loop operator\nin ABJ(M) theory at two loops in perturbation theory. \
Our result turns out to\nbe in exact agreement with the weak coupling limit \
of the prediction coming\nfrom localization, including finite N contributions \
associated to non-planar\ndiagrams. It also confirms the identification of \
the correct framing factor\nthat connects framing-zero and framing-one \
expressions, previously proposed.\nThe evaluation of the 1/2 BPS operator is \
made technically difficult in\ncomparison with other observables of ABJ(M) \
theory by the appearance of\nintegrals involving the coupling between \
fermions and gauge fields, which are\nabsent for instance in the 1/6 BPS \
case. We describe in detail how to\nanalytically solve these integrals in \
dimensional regularization with\ndimensional reduction (DRED). By suitably \
performing the physical limit to\nthree dimensions we clarify the role played \
by short distance divergences on\nthe final result and the mechanism of their \
cancellation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 2 Jul 2013 18:29:23 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 14 Jul 2013 20:41:05 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-03-12", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Bianchi", "Marco S.", ""}, {
              "Giribet", "Gaston", ""}, {"Leoni", "Matias", ""}, {
              "Penati", "Silvia", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
