                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a complete two-loop analysis of the quantum \
expectation value for\\ncircular BPS Wilson loops in ABJ(M) theories. We \
examine in details the 1/2 BPS\\ncase, that requires non-trivial fermionic \
couplings with the contour, finding\\nperfect agreement with the exact matrix \
model answer at zero framing. The\\nresult is obtained through a careful \
application of DRED regularization scheme,\\ncombined with a judicious \
rearrangement of the relevant perturbative\\ncontributions that reduces the \
computation to simple integrals. We carefully\\nanalyze the contribution of \
fermions that is crucial for the consistency with\\nthe localization \
procedure and point out the arising of pivotal evanescent\\nterms, discussing \
their meaning in relation to Ward identities.\\n\""}]}, {
