               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1307.2831\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arsen Melikyan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A. Melikyan, G. Weber\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable theories and generalized graded Maillet \
algebras\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"37 pages. v2: replaced with published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 47 (2014) 065401\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8113/47/6/065401\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a general formalism to investigate the \
integrable properties of a\\nlarge class of non-ultralocal models which in \
principle allows the construction\\nof the corresponding lattice versions. \
Our main motivation comes from the\\nsu(1|1) subsector of the string theory \
on AdS_5 x S^5 in the uniform gauge,\\nwhere such type of non-ultralocality \
appears in the resulting\\nAlday-Arutyunov-Frolov (AAF) model. We first show \
how to account for the second\\nderivative of the delta function in the Lax \
algebra of the AAF model by\\nmodifying Maillet's r- and s-matrices \
formalism, and derive a well-defined\\nalgebra of transition matrices, which \
allows for the lattice formulation of the\\ntheory. We illustrate our \
formalism on the examples of the bosonic\\nWadati-Konno-Ichikawa-Shimizu \
(WKIS) model and the two-dimensional free massive\\nDirac fermion model, \
which can be obtained by a consistent reduction of the\\nfull AAF model, and \
give the explicit forms of their corresponding r-matrices.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 10 Jul 2013 15:49:44 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 29 Jan 2014 16:41:37 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2014-01-30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Melikyan\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Weber\"", ",", "\"G.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
