         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1307.2831", "submitter" -> "Arsen Melikyan", "authors" -> 
            "A. Melikyan, G. Weber", "title" -> 
            "Integrable theories and generalized graded Maillet algebras", 
            "comments" -> "37 pages. v2: replaced with published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> "J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 47 (2014) 065401", 
            "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8113/47/6/065401", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a general formalism to investigate the integrable \
properties of a\nlarge class of non-ultralocal models which in principle \
allows the construction\nof the corresponding lattice versions. Our main \
motivation comes from the\nsu(1|1) subsector of the string theory on AdS_5 x \
S^5 in the uniform gauge,\nwhere such type of non-ultralocality appears in \
the resulting\nAlday-Arutyunov-Frolov (AAF) model. We first show how to \
account for the second\nderivative of the delta function in the Lax algebra \
of the AAF model by\nmodifying Maillet's r- and s-matrices formalism, and \
derive a well-defined\nalgebra of transition matrices, which allows for the \
lattice formulation of the\ntheory. We illustrate our formalism on the \
examples of the bosonic\nWadati-Konno-Ichikawa-Shimizu (WKIS) model and the \
two-dimensional free massive\nDirac fermion model, which can be obtained by a \
consistent reduction of the\nfull AAF model, and give the explicit forms of \
their corresponding r-matrices.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 10 Jul 2013 15:49:44 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 29 Jan 2014 16:41:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
