                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study form factors in the light-cone gauge \
world-sheet theory for strings\\nin AdS_5 x S^5. We perturbatively calculate \
the two-particle form factor in a\\nclosed su(2) sector to one-loop in the \
near-plane-wave limit and to two-loops\\nin the Maldacena-Swanson limit. We \
also perturbatively solve the functional\\nequation which follows from the \
form factor axioms for the world-sheet theory\\nand show that the \\\"minimal\
\\\" solution correctly reproduces the discontinuities\\nof the perturbative \
calculations. Finally we propose a prescription, valid for\\npolynomial \
orders of the inverse world-sheet length, for extracting the\\nfinite-volume \
world-sheet matrix element from the form factors and show that\\nthe \
two-excitation matrix element matches with the thermodynamic limit of \
the\\nspin-chain description of certain tree-level N=4 SYM structure \
constants.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 12 Jul 2013 16:24:15 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-06-16\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Klose\"", ",", "\"Thomas\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"McLoughlin\"", ",", "\"Tristan\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
