            "UUITP-09/13, TCDMATH 13-09", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study form factors in the light-cone gauge world-sheet \
theory for strings\nin AdS_5 x S^5. We perturbatively calculate the \
two-particle form factor in a\nclosed su(2) sector to one-loop in the \
near-plane-wave limit and to two-loops\nin the Maldacena-Swanson limit. We \
also perturbatively solve the functional\nequation which follows from the \
form factor axioms for the world-sheet theory\nand show that the \"minimal\" \
solution correctly reproduces the discontinuities\nof the perturbative \
calculations. Finally we propose a prescription, valid for\npolynomial orders \
of the inverse world-sheet length, for extracting the\nfinite-volume \
world-sheet matrix element from the form factors and show that\nthe \
two-excitation matrix element matches with the thermodynamic limit of the\n\
spin-chain description of certain tree-level N=4 SYM structure constants.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 12 Jul 2013 16:24:15 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-16", 
