        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{15.677899168134106`, -6.3211007440068485`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1307.3909\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Abhishake Sadhukhan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Justin R. David, Abhishake Sadhukhan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Structure constants of $\\\\beta$ deformed super \
Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+43 pages, 12 figures, Added two references and a note \
clarifying\\n  the issue of the double trace term in the Lagrangian\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Journal of High Energy Physics October 2013, \
2013:206\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2013)206\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the structure constants of the ${\\\\cal N}=1$ \
beta deformed theory\\nperturbatively and at strong coupling. We show that \
the planar one loop\\ncorrections to the structure constants of single trace \
gauge invariant\\noperators in the scalar sector is determined by the \
anomalous dimension\\nHamiltonian. This result implies that 3 point functions \
of the chiral primaries\\nof the theory do not receive corrections at one \
loop. We then study the\\nstructure constants at strong coupling using the \
Lunin-Maldacena geometry. We\\nexplicitly construct the supergravity mode \
dual to the chiral primary with\\nthree equal U(1) R-charges in the \
Lunin-Maldacena geometry. We show that the 3\\npoint function of this \
supergravity mode with semi-classical states\\nrepresenting two other similar \
chiral primary states but with large U(1)\\ncharges to be independent of the \
beta deformation and identical to that found\\nin the $AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ \
geometry. This together with the one-loop result\\nindicate that these \
structure constants are protected by a non-renormalization\\ntheorem. We also \
show that three point function of U(1) R-currents with\\nclassical massive \
strings is proportional to the R-charge carried by the string\\nsolution. \
This is in accordance with the prediction of the R-symmetry \
Ward\\nidentity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
