         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1307.3909", "submitter" -> "Abhishake Sadhukhan", 
            "authors" -> "Justin R. David, Abhishake Sadhukhan", "title" -> 
            "Structure constants of $\\beta$ deformed super Yang-Mills", 
            "comments" -> 
            "1+43 pages, 12 figures, Added two references and a note \
clarifying\n  the issue of the double trace term in the Lagrangian", 
            "journal-ref" -> 
            "Journal of High Energy Physics October 2013, 2013:206", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2013)206", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the structure constants of the ${\\cal N}=1$ beta \
deformed theory\nperturbatively and at strong coupling. We show that the \
planar one loop\ncorrections to the structure constants of single trace gauge \
invariant\noperators in the scalar sector is determined by the anomalous \
dimension\nHamiltonian. This result implies that 3 point functions of the \
chiral primaries\nof the theory do not receive corrections at one loop. We \
then study the\nstructure constants at strong coupling using the \
Lunin-Maldacena geometry. We\nexplicitly construct the supergravity mode dual \
to the chiral primary with\nthree equal U(1) R-charges in the Lunin-Maldacena \
geometry. We show that the 3\npoint function of this supergravity mode with \
semi-classical states\nrepresenting two other similar chiral primary states \
but with large U(1)\ncharges to be independent of the beta deformation and \
identical to that found\nin the $AdS_5\\times S^5$ geometry. This together \
with the one-loop result\nindicate that these structure constants are \
protected by a non-renormalization\ntheorem. We also show that three point \
function of U(1) R-currents with\nclassical massive strings is proportional \
to the R-charge carried by the string\nsolution. This is in accordance with \
the prediction of the R-symmetry Ward\nidentity.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 15 Jul 2013 12:23:03 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 14 Aug 2013 06:04:16 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 8 Oct 2013 12:14:50 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-05-13", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"David", "Justin R.", ""}, {
              "Sadhukhan", "Abhishake", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
