               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyse the breaking of conformal invariance for \
null polygonal Wilson\\nloops in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM beyond that induced by \
the UV divergences due to the\\ncusps. It only shows up in exceptional \
configurations, where the polygon\\nintersects the critical light cone of an \
inversion or a special conformal\\ntransformation. In comparison with the \
related study for the Euclidean version\\nby Drukker and Gross, we find \
different leading terms both for weak as well as\\nfor strong coupling. Hence \
the conformal anomaly due to intersections of a null\\npolygon with a \
critical light cone defines a new universal function of the\\ncoupling \
constant.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
