          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1307.7773", "submitter" -> "Adi Armoni", "authors" -> 
            "Adi Armoni, Maurizio Piai, Ali Teimouri", "title" -> 
            "Correlators of Circular Wilson Loops from Holography", 
            "comments" -> 
            "12 pages, RevTex. 10 eps figures. v2,v3: minor corrections,\n  \
references added. To appear in Phys.Rev.D", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.88.066008", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th hep-lat", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the correlators of two circular Wilson loops of \
different radii at\nstrong coupling. In our setup one Wilson loop is located \
inside the other. We\nuse holography to calculate the connected two-point \
function. Both an AdS\nbackground and a confining background are considered. \
As the computation for\nthe confining case cannot be carried out analytically \
we solve the problem\nnumerically. In the AdS case our results agree with \
similar holographic\ncalculations. In the case of a confining background we \
find an asymptotic area\nlaw, in agreement with the result of the lattice \
strong coupling expansion. We\nalso elaborate on the subtle issue of the \
interplay between connected and\ndisconnected string worldsheets.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
