                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study worldsheet scattering for the type IIA \
superstring in AdS(2) x S(2)\\nx T(6). Using the Green--Schwarz action to \
quartic order in fermions we take\\nthe near-BMN limit, where as in the \
AdS(3)/CFT(2) case there are both massive\\nand massless excitations. For the \
massive excitations we compute all possible\\ntree-level processes, and show \
that these agree with a truncated version of the\\nexact AdS(5) x S(5) \
S-matrix. We also compute several S-matrix elements\\ninvolving massless \
excitations. At one loop we find that the dressing phase is\\nthe same \
Hernandes-Lopez phase appearing in AdS(5)/CFT(4). We see the same\\nphase \
when calculating this by semiclassical means using the \
PSU(1,1|2)/U(1)^2\\ncoset sigma model, for which we can also study the \
scattering of fermions. This\\nsupports the conjecture that the all-loop \
dressing phase is again the BES\\nphase, rather than a new phase like that \
seen in AdS(3)/CFT(2).\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
