               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1308.2820\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Timothy Adamo\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Tim Adamo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Twistor actions for gauge theory and gravity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"178 pages, 30 figures. Review based on the author's \
D.Phil. thesis.\\n  v2: references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This is a review of recent developments in the study of \
perturbative gauge\\ntheory and gravity using action functionals on twistor \
space. It is intended to\\nprovide a user-friendly introduction to twistor \
actions, geared towards\\nresearchers or graduate students interested in \
learning something about the\\nutility, prospects, and shortcomings of this \
approach. For those already\\nfamiliar with the twistor approach, it should \
provide a condensed overview of\\nthe literature as well as several novel \
results of potential interest. This\\nwork is based primarily upon the \
author's D.Phil. thesis. We first consider\\nfour-dimensional, maximally \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory as a gauge theory\\nin twistor space. We \
focus on the perturbation theory associated to this\\naction, which in an \
axial gauge leads to the MHV formalism. This allows us to\\nefficiently \
compute scattering amplitudes at tree-level (and beyond) in twistor\\nspace. \
Other gauge theory observables such as local operators and null\\npolygonal \
Wilson loops can also be formulated twistorially, leading to proofs\\nfor \
several correspondences between correlation functions and Wilson loops, \
as\\nwell as a recursive formula for computing mixed Wilson loop / local \
operator\\ncorrelators. We then apply the twistor action approach to general \
relativity,\\nusing the on-shell equivalence between conformal and Einstein \
gravity. This can\\nbe extended to N=4 supersymmetry. The perturbation theory \
of the twistor action\\nleads to formulae for the MHV amplitude with and \
without cosmological constant,\\nyields a candidate for the Einstein twistor \
action, and induces a MHV formalism\\non twistor space. Appendices include \
discussion of super-connections and\\nCoulomb branch regularization on \
twistor space.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
