 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the Bethe equations for the isotropic \
spin-1/2 Heisenberg quantum\\nspin chain with periodic boundary conditions. \
We formulate a conjecture for the\\nnumber of solutions with pairwise \
distinct roots of these equations, in terms\\nof numbers of so-called \
singular (or exceptional) solutions. Using homotopy\\ncontinuation methods, \
we find all such solutions of the Bethe equations for\\nchains of length up \
to 14. The numbers of these solutions are in perfect\\nagreement with the \
conjecture. We also discuss an indirect method of finding\\nsolutions of the \
Bethe equations by solving the Baxter T-Q equation. We briefly\\ncomment on \
implications for thermodynamical computations based on the \
string\\nhypothesis.\\n\""}]}, {
