, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Using exact results obtained from localization on S^4, \
we explore the large N\\nlimit of N=2 super-Yang-Mills theories with massive \
matter multiplets. We focus\\non three cases: N=2* theory, describing a \
massive hypermultiplet in the adjoint\\nrepresentation, SU(N) \
super-Yang-Mills with 2N massive hypermultiplets in the\\nfundamental, and \
super-QCD with massive quarks. When the radius of the\\nfour-sphere is sent \
to infinity the theories at hand are described by solvable\\nmatrix models, \
which exhibit a number of interesting phenomena including\\nquantum phase \
transitions at finite 't Hooft coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
