                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"HU-EP-13/42, NORDITA-2013-64, UUITP-10/13\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that appropriately supersymmetrized smooth \
Maldacena-Wilson loop\\noperators in N=4 super Yang-Mills theory are \
invariant under a Yangian symmetry\\nY[psu(2,2|4)] built upon the manifest \
superconformal symmetry algebra of the\\ntheory. The existence of this hidden \
symmetry is demonstrated at the one-loop\\norder in the weak coupling limit \
as well as at leading order in the strong\\ncoupling limit employing the \
classical integrability of the dual AdS_5 x S^5\\nstring description. The \
hidden symmetry generators consist of a canonical\\nnon-local second order \
variational derivative piece acting on the superpath,\\nalong with a novel \
local path dependent contribution. We match the functional\\nform of these \
Yangian symmetry generators at weak and strong coupling and find\\nevidence \
for an interpolating function. Our findings represent the \
smooth\\ncounterpart to the Yangian invariance of scattering superamplitudes \
dual to\\nlight-like polygonal super Wilson loops in the N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
