            "  We study the correlation function of two circular Wilson loops \
at strong\ncoupling in N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. Using the AdS/CFT \
correspondence, the\nproblem maps to finding the minimal surface between two \
circles defined on the\nboundary of AdS, and the fluctuations around the \
classical solution in AdS_5 x\nS^5. At the classical level, we derive the \
string solution in H_3 x S^1\nexplicitly, and focus on properties such as \
stability and phase transition.\nFurthermore, a computation of the associated \
algebraic curve is given. At the\nquantum level, the one-loop partition \
function is constructed by introducing\nquadratic bosonic and fermionic \
fluctuations around the classical solution,\nembedded in AdS_5 x S^5. We find \
an analytic, formal expression for the\npartition function in terms of an \
infinite product by employing the\nGel'fand-Yaglom method and supersymmetric \
regularization. We regulate the\nexpression and evaluate the partition \
function numerically.\n", 
