               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Adi Armoni\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Adi Armoni\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-Supersymmetric Brane Configurations, Seiberg Duality \
and Dynamical\\n  Symmetry Breaking\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages. LaTex. 5 eps figures. v2: minor changes, \
reference and a\\n  comment about the GMOR relation added. To appear in \
Phys.Rev.D\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.89.125025\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider type IIA brane configurations, similar to \
those that realize\\nSO(2N) supersymmetric QCD, that include orientifold \
planes and anti-branes.\\nSuch brane configurations lead to Sp(2N) field \
theories that become\\nsupersymmetric in the large-N limit and break \
supersymmetry upon the inclusion\\nof 1/N corrections. We argue that this \
class of field theories admit Seiberg\\nduality and interpret the potential \
between branes and orientifolds as field\\ntheory phenomena. In particular we \
find in the magnetic theory a meson\\npotential that leads to dynamical \
symmetry breaking and a meson condensate\\nsimilar to the anticipated quark \
condensate in QCD.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
