               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrability of the AdS_5 x S^5 superstring and its \
deformations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v3, published version, introduction slightly broadened, \
typos\\n  corrected, updates to outlook and references. Review based on \
author's PhD\\n  thesis, 214 pages, many figures. Partly based on \
arXiv:1009.4118,\\n  arXiv:1103.5853, arXiv:1111.0564, arXiv:1201.1451, \
arXiv:1208.3478, and\\n  arXiv:1210.8185\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 47 (2014) 433001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/47/43/433001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This article reviews the application of integrability \
to the spectral problem\\nof strings on AdS_5 x S^5 and its deformations. We \
begin with a pedagogical\\nintroduction to integrable field theories \
culminating in the description of\\ntheir finite-volume spectra through the \
thermodynamic Bethe ansatz. Next, we\\napply these ideas to the AdS_5 x S^5 \
string and in later chapters discuss how\\nto account for particular \
integrable deformations. Through the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence this gives an \
exact description of anomalous scaling dimensions\\nof single trace operators \
in planar N=4 supersymmetry Yang-Mills theory, its\\n`orbifolds', and beta \
and gamma-deformed supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory. We\\nalso touch upon \
some subtleties arising in these deformed theories.\\nFurthermore, we \
consider complex excited states (bound states) in the su(2)\\nsector and give \
their thermodynamic Bethe ansatz description. Finally we\\ndiscuss the \
thermodynamic Bethe ansatz for a quantum deformation of the AdS_5 x\\nS^5 \
superstring S-matrix, with close relations to among others \
Pohlmeyer\\nreduced string theory, and briefly indicate more recent \
developments in this\\narea.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
