            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1310.5709\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Elli Pomoni\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Elli Pomoni\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrability in N=2 superconformal gauge theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"42 pages, 33 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2015.01.006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Any N=2 superconformal gauge theory (including N=4 SYM) \
contains a set of\\nlocal operators made only out of fields in the N=2 vector \
multiplet that is\\nclosed under renormalization to all loops, namely the \
SU(2,1|2) sector. For\\nplanar N=4 SYM the spectrum of local operators can be \
obtained by mapping the\\nproblem to an integrable model (a spin chain in \
perturbation theory), in\\nprinciple for any value of the coupling constant. \
We present a diagrammatic\\nargument that for any planar N=2 superconformal \
gauge theory the SU(2,1|2)\\nHamiltonian acting on infinite spin chains is \
identical to all loops to that of\\nN=4 SYM, up to a redefinition of the \
coupling constant. Thus, this sector is\\nintegrable and anomalous dimensions \
can be, in principle, read off from the N=4\\nones up to this \
redefinition.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
