               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1310.6026\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alessandra Silvestri\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Noemi Frusciante, Marco Raveri and Alessandra \
Silvestri\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Effective Field Theory of Dark Energy: a Dynamical \
Analysis\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"matching version accepted by JCAP; references \
added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2014/02/026\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The effective field theory (EFT) of dark energy relies \
on three functions of\\ntime to describe the background dynamics. The \
viability of these functions is\\ninvestigated here by means of a thorough \
dynamical analysis. While the system\\nis underdetermined, and one can always \
find a set of functions reproducing any\\nexpansion history, we are able to \
determine general compatibility conditions\\nfor these functions by requiring \
a viable background cosmology. In particular,\\nwe identify a set of \
variables that allows us to transform the non-autonomous\\nsystem of \
equations into an infinite-dimensional one characterized by a\\nsignificant \
recursive structure. We then analyze several autonomous\\nsub-systems, \
obtained truncating the original one at increasingly higher\\ndimension, that \
correspond to increasingly general models of dark energy and\\nmodified \
gravity. Furthermore, we exploit the recursive nature of the system to\\ndraw \
some general conclusions on the different cosmologies that can be\\nrecovered \
within the EFT formalism and the corresponding compatibility\\nrequirements \
for the EFT functions. The machinery that we set up serves\\ndifferent \
purposes. It offers a general scheme for performing dynamical\\nanalysis of \
dark energy and modified gravity models within the model\\nindependent \
framework of EFT; the general results, obtained with this\\ntechnique, can be \
projected into specific models, as we show in one example. It\\nalso can be \
used to determine appropriate ansatze for the three EFT \
background\\nfunctions when studying the dynamics of cosmological \
perturbations in the\\ncontext of large scale structure tests of \
gravity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 22 Oct 2013 19:59:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 17 Feb 2014 19:48:38 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-06-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Frusciante\"", ",", "\"Noemi\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Raveri\"", ",", "\"Marco\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
