         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1310.6026", "submitter" -> "Alessandra Silvestri", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Noemi Frusciante, Marco Raveri and Alessandra Silvestri", 
            "title" -> 
            "Effective Field Theory of Dark Energy: a Dynamical Analysis", 
            "comments" -> 
            "matching version accepted by JCAP; references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1475-7516/2014/02/026", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The effective field theory (EFT) of dark energy relies on \
three functions of\ntime to describe the background dynamics. The viability \
of these functions is\ninvestigated here by means of a thorough dynamical \
analysis. While the system\nis underdetermined, and one can always find a set \
of functions reproducing any\nexpansion history, we are able to determine \
general compatibility conditions\nfor these functions by requiring a viable \
background cosmology. In particular,\nwe identify a set of variables that \
allows us to transform the non-autonomous\nsystem of equations into an \
infinite-dimensional one characterized by a\nsignificant recursive structure. \
We then analyze several autonomous\nsub-systems, obtained truncating the \
original one at increasingly higher\ndimension, that correspond to \
increasingly general models of dark energy and\nmodified gravity. \
Furthermore, we exploit the recursive nature of the system to\ndraw some \
general conclusions on the different cosmologies that can be\nrecovered \
within the EFT formalism and the corresponding compatibility\nrequirements \
for the EFT functions. The machinery that we set up serves\ndifferent \
purposes. It offers a general scheme for performing dynamical\nanalysis of \
dark energy and modified gravity models within the model\nindependent \
framework of EFT; the general results, obtained with this\ntechnique, can be \
projected into specific models, as we show in one example. It\nalso can be \
used to determine appropriate ansatze for the three EFT background\nfunctions \
when studying the dynamics of cosmological perturbations in the\ncontext of \
large scale structure tests of gravity.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 22 Oct 2013 19:59:41 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 17 Feb 2014 19:48:38 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-17", 
