                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze the ground state of the open spin-1/2 \
isotropic quantum spin chain\\nwith a non-diagonal boundary term using a \
recently proposed Bethe ansatz\\nsolution. As the coefficient of the \
non-diagonal boundary term tends to zero,\\nthe Bethe roots split evenly into \
two sets: those that remain finite, and those\\nthat become infinite. We \
argue that the former satisfy conventional Bethe\\nequations, while the \
latter satisfy a generalization of the Richardson-Gaudin\\nequations. We \
derive an expression for the leading correction to the boundary\\nenergy in \
terms of the boundary parameters.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
