            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1311.1794\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arkady Tseytlin\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"B. Hoare, A. Stepanchuk, A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Giant magnon solution and dispersion relation in string \
theory in AdS_3\\n  x S^3 x T^4 with mixed flux\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages. v2: minor comments added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2013.12.011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Imperial-TP-AS-2013-01, HU-EP-13/56\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We address the question about the exact form of the \
dispersion relation for\\nlight-cone string excitations in string theory in \
AdS3 x S3 x T4 with mixed R-R\\nand NS-NS 3-form fluxes. The analogy with \
string theory in AdS5 x S5 suggests\\nthat in addition to the data provided \
by the perturbative near-BMN expansion\\nand the symmetry algebra \
considerations there is also another source of\\ninformation about the \
dispersion relation -- the semiclassical giant magnon\\nsolution. In earlier \
work in arXiv:1303.1037 and arXiv:1304.4099 it was found\\nthat the symmetry \
algebra constraints consistent with perturbative expansion do\\nnot \
completely determine the form of the dispersion relation. The aim of \
the\\npresent paper is to fix it by constructing a generalization of the \
known dyonic\\ngiant magnon soliton on S3 to the presence of a non-zero NS-NS \
flux described\\nby a WZ term in the string action. We find that the angular \
momentum of this\\nsoliton gets shifted by a term linear in world-sheet \
momentum. We also discuss\\nthe symmetry algebra of the string light-cone \
S-matrix and show that the exact\\ndispersion relation, which should have the \
correct perturbative BMN and\\nsemiclassical giant magnon limits, should also \
contain such a linear momentum\\nterm. The simplicity of the resulting \
bound-state picture provides a strong\\nargument in favour of this dispersion \
relation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 7 Nov 2013 19:53:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 15 Nov 2013 09:32:45 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-06-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Hoare\"", ",", "\"B.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Stepanchuk\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Tseytlin\"", ",", "\"A. A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1311.1794", "submitter" -> "Arkady Tseytlin", "authors" -> 
            "B. Hoare, A. Stepanchuk, A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Giant magnon solution and dispersion relation in string theory \
in AdS_3\n  x S^3 x T^4 with mixed flux", "comments" -> 
            "32 pages. v2: minor comments added", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2013.12.011", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AS-2013-01, HU-EP-13/56", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We address the question about the exact form of the dispersion \
relation for\nlight-cone string excitations in string theory in AdS3 x S3 x \
T4 with mixed R-R\nand NS-NS 3-form fluxes. The analogy with string theory in \
AdS5 x S5 suggests\nthat in addition to the data provided by the perturbative \
near-BMN expansion\nand the symmetry algebra considerations there is also \
another source of\ninformation about the dispersion relation -- the \
semiclassical giant magnon\nsolution. In earlier work in arXiv:1303.1037 and \
arXiv:1304.4099 it was found\nthat the symmetry algebra constraints \
consistent with perturbative expansion do\nnot completely determine the form \
of the dispersion relation. The aim of the\npresent paper is to fix it by \
constructing a generalization of the known dyonic\ngiant magnon soliton on S3 \
to the presence of a non-zero NS-NS flux described\nby a WZ term in the \
string action. We find that the angular momentum of this\nsoliton gets \
shifted by a term linear in world-sheet momentum. We also discuss\nthe \
symmetry algebra of the string light-cone S-matrix and show that the exact\n\
dispersion relation, which should have the correct perturbative BMN and\n\
semiclassical giant magnon limits, should also contain such a linear momentum\
\nterm. The simplicity of the resulting bound-state picture provides a strong\
\nargument in favour of this dispersion relation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 7 Nov 2013 19:53:54 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 15 Nov 2013 09:32:45 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-17", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Hoare", "B.", ""}, {
              "Stepanchuk", "A.", ""}, {"Tseytlin", "A. A.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
