 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We proceed to study infinite-dimensional symmetries in \
two-dimensional\\nsquashed Wess-Zumino-Novikov-Witten (WZNW) models at the \
classical level. The\\ntarget space is given by squashed S^3 and the isometry \
is SU(2)_L x U(1)_R. It\\nis known that SU(2)_L is enhanced to a couple of \
Yangians. We reveal here that\\nan infinite-dimensional extension of U(1)_R \
is a deformation of quantum affine\\nalgebra, where a new deformation \
parameter is provided with the coefficient of\\nthe Wess-Zumino term. Then we \
consider the relation between the deformed\\nquantum affine algebra and the \
pair of Yangians from the viewpoint of the\\nleft-right duality of monodromy \
matrices. The integrable structure is also\\ndiscussed by computing the \
r/s-matrices that satisfy the extended classical\\nYang-Baxter equation. \
Finally two degenerate limits are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
