               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alex Buchel\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Venkat Balasubramanian and Alex Buchel\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On consistent truncations in ${\\\\cal N}=2^*$ holography\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"13 pages, 2 figures; supplemental files attached\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2014)030\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UWO-TH-13/16\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Although Pilch-Warner (PW) gravitational \
renormalization group flow\\n[arXiv:hep-th/0004063] passes a number of \
important consistency checks to be\\nidentified as a holographic dual to a \
large-$N$ $SU(N)$ ${\\\\cal N}=2^*$\\nsupersymmetric gauge theory, it fails \
to reproduce the free energy of the\\ntheory on $S^4$, computed with the \
localization techniques. This disagreement\\npoints to the existence of a \
larger dual gravitational consistent truncation,\\nwhich in the gauge theory \
flat-space limit reduces to a PW flow. Such\\ntruncation was recently \
identified by Bobev-Elvang-Freedman-Pufu (BEFP)\\n[arXiv:1311.1508]. \
Additional bulk scalars of the BEFP gravitation truncation\\nmight lead to \
destabilization of the finite-temperature deformed PW flows, and\\nthus \
modify the low-temperature thermodynamics and hydrodynamics of ${\\\\cal \
N}\\n=2^*$ plasma. We compute the quasinormal spectrum of these bulk scalar \
fields\\nin the thermal PW flows and demonstrate that these modes do not \
condense, as\\nlong as the masses of the ${\\\\cal N}=2^*$ hypermultiplet \
components are real.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
