         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1311.5044", "submitter" -> "Alex Buchel", "authors" -> 
            "Venkat Balasubramanian and Alex Buchel", "title" -> 
            "On consistent truncations in ${\\cal N}=2^*$ holography", 
            "comments" -> "13 pages, 2 figures; supplemental files attached", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP02(2014)030", 
            "report-no" -> "UWO-TH-13/16", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            
            "  Although Pilch-Warner (PW) gravitational renormalization group \
flow\n[arXiv:hep-th/0004063] passes a number of important consistency checks \
to be\nidentified as a holographic dual to a large-$N$ $SU(N)$ ${\\cal \
N}=2^*$\nsupersymmetric gauge theory, it fails to reproduce the free energy \
of the\ntheory on $S^4$, computed with the localization techniques. This \
disagreement\npoints to the existence of a larger dual gravitational \
consistent truncation,\nwhich in the gauge theory flat-space limit reduces to \
a PW flow. Such\ntruncation was recently identified by \
Bobev-Elvang-Freedman-Pufu (BEFP)\n[arXiv:1311.1508]. Additional bulk scalars \
of the BEFP gravitation truncation\nmight lead to destabilization of the \
finite-temperature deformed PW flows, and\nthus modify the low-temperature \
thermodynamics and hydrodynamics of ${\\cal N}\n=2^*$ plasma. We compute the \
quasinormal spectrum of these bulk scalar fields\nin the thermal PW flows and \
demonstrate that these modes do not condense, as\nlong as the masses of the \
${\\cal N}=2^*$ hypermultiplet components are real.\n", 
