                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We demonstrate that the large-spin expansion of the \
energy of\\nGubser-Klebanov-Polyakov (GKP) strings that rotate in RxS2 and \
AdS3 can be\\nexpressed in terms of Lambert's W-function. We compute the \
leading, subleading\\nand next-to-subleading series of exponential \
corrections to the infinite-volume\\ndispersion relation of GKP strings that \
rotate in RxS2. These strings are dual\\nto certain long operators of N=4 SYM \
theory and provide their scaling\\ndimensions at strong coupling. We also \
show that the strings obey a short-long\\n(strings) duality. For the folded \
GKP strings that spin inside AdS3 and are\\ndual to twist-2 operators, we \
confirm the known formulas for the leading and\\nnext-to-leading coefficients \
of their anomalous dimensions and derive the\\ncorresponding expressions for \
the next-to-next-to-leading coefficients.\\n\""}]}, {
