               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Changhyun Ahn\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Higher Spin Currents in Wolf Space: Part I\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"143 pages; Simplified the OPEs using compact notations, \
manifest\\n  SU(2) x SU(2) representations are given and to appear in \
JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2014)091\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  For the N=4 superconformal coset theory described by \
SU(N+2)/SU(N) (that\\ncontains a Wolf space) with N=3, the N=2 WZW affine \
current algebra with\\nconstraints is obtained. The 16 generators of the \
large N=4 linear\\nsuperconformal algebra are described by those WZW affine \
currents explicitly.\\nBy factoring out four spin-1/2 currents and the spin-1 \
current from these 16\\ngenerators, the remaining 11 generators (spin-2 \
current, four spin-3/2\\ncurrents, and six spin-1 currents) corresponding to \
the large N=4 nonlinear\\nsuperconformal algebra are obtained.\\n  Based on \
the recent work by Gaberdiel and Gopakumar on the large N=4\\nholography, the \
extra 16 currents, with spin contents (1, 3/2, 3/2, 2), (3/2,\\n2, 2, 5/2), \
(3/2, 2, 2, 5/2), and (2, 5/2, 5/2, 3) described in terms of \
N=2\\nmultiplets, are obtained and realized by the WZW affine currents. As a \
first\\nstep towards N=4 W algebra (which is NOT known so far), the operator \
product\\nexpansions (OPEs) between the above 11 currents and these extra 16 \
higher spin\\ncurrents are found explicitly. It turns out that the composite \
fields with\\ndefinite U(1) charges, made of above (11+16) currents (which \
commute with the\\nWolf space subgroup SU(N=3) x SU(2) x U(1) currents), \
occur in the right hand\\nsides of these OPEs.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
