            "  For the N=4 superconformal coset theory described by \
SU(N+2)/SU(N) (that\ncontains a Wolf space) with N=3, the N=2 WZW affine \
current algebra with\nconstraints is obtained. The 16 generators of the large \
N=4 linear\nsuperconformal algebra are described by those WZW affine currents \
explicitly.\nBy factoring out four spin-1/2 currents and the spin-1 current \
from these 16\ngenerators, the remaining 11 generators (spin-2 current, four \
spin-3/2\ncurrents, and six spin-1 currents) corresponding to the large N=4 \
nonlinear\nsuperconformal algebra are obtained.\n  Based on the recent work \
by Gaberdiel and Gopakumar on the large N=4\nholography, the extra 16 \
currents, with spin contents (1, 3/2, 3/2, 2), (3/2,\n2, 2, 5/2), (3/2, 2, 2, \
5/2), and (2, 5/2, 5/2, 3) described in terms of N=2\nmultiplets, are \
obtained and realized by the WZW affine currents. As a first\nstep towards \
N=4 W algebra (which is NOT known so far), the operator product\nexpansions \
(OPEs) between the above 11 currents and these extra 16 higher spin\ncurrents \
are found explicitly. It turns out that the composite fields with\ndefinite \
U(1) charges, made of above (11+16) currents (which commute with the\nWolf \
space subgroup SU(N=3) x SU(2) x U(1) currents), occur in the right hand\n\
sides of these OPEs.\n", 
