 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The $\\\\gamma_i$-deformed $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
super-Yang-Mills theory is a\\nnon-supersymmetric deformation of the \
maximally-supersymmetric gauge theory in\\nfour dimensions which is \
conformally-invariant at the planar level. At the\\nnon-planar level \
non-trivial renormalization of marginal double-trace operators\\nappears to \
break conformal invariance. At non-planar level, however, the\\nbehavior of \
this theory is less well understood. We study the one loop\\nrenormalization \
of the theory and the resulting flow of Yukawa and scalar\\ncoupling at the \
order ${\\\\cal O}(\\\\frac{\\\\lambda}{N^2})$, and find \
$\\\\gamma_i$\\nparameters receive nontrivial quantum corrections. We show \
that, at low\\nenergies, the $\\\\gamma_i$ parameters flow to a common value \
and\\n$\\\\gamma_i$-deformed theory reaches an \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=1$-supersymmetric fixed\\npoint described by the \
$\\\\beta$-deformed $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
