            "Qingjun Jin", "title" -> 
            "The Emergence of Supersymmetry in $\\gamma_i$-deformed ${\\cal \
N}=4$\n  super-Yang-Mills theory", "comments" -> "24 pages, 4 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The $\\gamma_i$-deformed $\\mathcal{N}=4$ super-Yang-Mills \
theory is a\nnon-supersymmetric deformation of the maximally-supersymmetric \
gauge theory in\nfour dimensions which is conformally-invariant at the planar \
level. At the\nnon-planar level non-trivial renormalization of marginal \
double-trace operators\nappears to break conformal invariance. At non-planar \
level, however, the\nbehavior of this theory is less well understood. We \
study the one loop\nrenormalization of the theory and the resulting flow of \
Yukawa and scalar\ncoupling at the order ${\\cal O}(\\frac{\\lambda}{N^2})$, \
and find $\\gamma_i$\nparameters receive nontrivial quantum corrections. We \
show that, at low\nenergies, the $\\gamma_i$ parameters flow to a common \
value and\n$\\gamma_i$-deformed theory reaches an \
$\\mathcal{N}=1$-supersymmetric fixed\npoint described by the \
$\\beta$-deformed $\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills\ntheory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
