 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Morse-Smale-Floer homology associates the critical \
points of the action\\nfunctional of a classical field theory over a manifold \
to its homology. We\\nassociate to the intersection homology of certain \
Lagrangian submanifolds of\\nR^4 the critical points of a quantum effective \
action of large-N SU(N) YM. For\\nthis purpose we construct in YM a trivial \
Topological Field Theory defined by\\ntwistor Wilson loops whose v.e.v. is 1 \
in the large-N limit for any shape of\\nthe loops supported on certain \
punctured Lagrangian submanifolds. We derive a\\nnew holomorphic loop \
equation for the twistor Wilson loops, that involves the\\nchange of \
variables in the YM functional integral from the connection to \
the\\nanti-selfdual part of the curvature and the choice of a holomorphic \
gauge.\\nEmploying the holomorphic loop equation, and viewing Floer homology \
the other\\nway around, we associate to arcs asymptotic in both directions to \
the cusps of\\nthe Lagrangian submanifolds the critical points of an \
effective action, that\\nturn out to be surface operators of Z(N) holonomy. \
At the next-to-leading 1/N\\norder a certain correlator of surface operators \
is non-topological and\\nnon-trivial, controls the mass gap of YM theory, and \
is saturated by an\\ninfinite sum of pure poles of scalar and pseudoscalar \
glueballs with positive\\ncharge conjugation. It satisfies asymptotically for \
large momentum fundamental\\nuniversal constraints arising from the \
asymptotic freedom and the\\nrenormalization group. We predict at large-N the \
ratio of the masses of the two\\nlower-mass scalar glueballs r=\\\\sqrt \
2=1.414, to be compared with the measure in\\nlattice SU(8) YM by Meyer-Teper \
r=1.42(11), and with the value implied by\\nPDG(2014) r=1.397(008). The \
construction extends to massless Veneziano large-N\\nlimit of QCD, for which \
we determine the lower edge of the conformal window\\nN_f/N=5/2 and the \
corresponding quark-mass anomalous dimension gamma=-4/5.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
