DCPT-13/47\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose that Baxter's Z-invariant six-vertex model \
at the rational gl(2)\\npoint on a planar but in general not rectangular \
lattice provides a way to\\nstudy Yangian invariants. These are identified \
with eigenfunctions of certain\\nmonodromies of an auxiliary inhomogeneous \
spin chain. As a consequence they are\\nspecial solutions to the eigenvalue \
problem of the associated transfer matrix.\\nExcitingly, this allows to \
construct them using Bethe ansatz techniques.\\nConceptually, our \
construction generalizes to general (super) Lie algebras and\\ngeneral \
representations. Here we present the explicit form of sample invariants\\nfor \
totally symmetric, finite-dimensional representations of gl(n) in terms \
of\\noscillator algebras. In particular, we discuss invariants of three- \
and\\nfour-site monodromies that can be understood respectively as \
intertwiners of\\nthe bootstrap and Yang-Baxter equation. We state a set of \
functional relations\\nsignificant for these representations of the Yangian \
and discuss their\\nsolutions in terms of Bethe roots. They arrange \
themselves into exact strings\\nin the complex plane. In addition, it is \
shown that the sample invariants can\\nbe expressed analogously to \
Grassmannian integrals. This aspect is closely\\nrelated to a recent on-shell \
formulation of scattering amplitudes in planar N=4\\nsuper Yang-Mills theory.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
