            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1312.2972\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Daniele Marmiroli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Daniele Marmiroli (NORDITA)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Notes on BPS Wilson Loops and the Cusp Anomalous \
Dimension in ABJM\\n  theory\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"NORDITA preprint number 2013-100\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We introduce a new purely bosonic, $\\\\frac{1}{6}$ BPS \
Wilson loop for ABJM\\ntheory on $S^3$ that couples scalar fields to a \
latitude at an angle $\\\\theta$\\non $S^2\\\\in\\\\mathbb{C}P^3$. Through \
localization of this operator, we relate the\\nexpansion of the cusp \
anomalous dimension at small cusp angles to the\\nlogarithmic derivative of \
the ABJM Wilson loop. This defines,\\nnon-perturbatively in the 't Hooft \
coupling, the bremsstrahlung function\\n$B(\\\\lambda)$ describing in three \
dimensions the soft radiation of a $W$-boson\\nundergoing a sudden change in \
trajectory. We compare our results for\\n$B(\\\\lambda)$ to the known \
weak/strong coupling expansions of the function\\n$h(\\\\lambda)$ that enters \
integrability. At weak coupling we precisely match the\\npreviously known \
two-loop result. At strong coupling we find agreement at\\nleading order in $\
\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}$, but a mismatch of the constant coefficient.\\nWe \
comment on the striking similarity that we observe between these two, \
in\\nprinciple, unrelated functions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
