         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1312.2972", "submitter" -> "Daniele Marmiroli", "authors" -> 
            "Daniele Marmiroli (NORDITA)", "title" -> 
            "Notes on BPS Wilson Loops and the Cusp Anomalous Dimension in \
ABJM\n  theory", "comments" -> "31 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> "NORDITA preprint number 2013-100", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We introduce a new purely bosonic, $\\frac{1}{6}$ BPS Wilson \
loop for ABJM\ntheory on $S^3$ that couples scalar fields to a latitude at an \
angle $\\theta$\non $S^2\\in\\mathbb{C}P^3$. Through localization of this \
operator, we relate the\nexpansion of the cusp anomalous dimension at small \
cusp angles to the\nlogarithmic derivative of the ABJM Wilson loop. This \
defines,\nnon-perturbatively in the 't Hooft coupling, the bremsstrahlung \
function\n$B(\\lambda)$ describing in three dimensions the soft radiation of \
a $W$-boson\nundergoing a sudden change in trajectory. We compare our results \
for\n$B(\\lambda)$ to the known weak/strong coupling expansions of the \
function\n$h(\\lambda)$ that enters integrability. At weak coupling we \
precisely match the\npreviously known two-loop result. At strong coupling we \
find agreement at\nleading order in $\\sqrt{\\lambda}$, but a mismatch of the \
constant coefficient.\nWe comment on the striking similarity that we observe \
between these two, in\nprinciple, unrelated functions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 10 Dec 2013 21:32:17 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2013-12-12", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Marmiroli", "Daniele", "", "NORDITA"}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
