            "  We investigate the completeness of the solutions of the Bethe \
equations for\nthe integrable spin-s isotropic (XXX) spin chain with periodic \
boundary\nconditions. Solutions containing the exact string i s, i (s-1), \
..., -i(s-1),\n-is are singular. For s>1/2, there exist also \"strange\" \
solutions with repeated\nroots, which nevertheless are physical (i.e., \
correspond to eigenstates of the\nHamiltonian). We derive conditions for the \
singular solutions and the solutions\nwith repeated roots to be physical. We \
formulate a conjecture for the number of\nsolutions with pairwise distinct \
roots in terms of the numbers of singular and\nstrange solutions. Using \
homotopy continuation, we solve the Bethe equations\nnumerically for s=1 and \
s=3/2 up to 8 sites, and find some support for the\nconjecture. We also \
exhibit several examples of strange solutions.\n", 
