                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a new method for the computation of quantum \
three-point functions\\nfor operators in su(2) sectors of N=4 super \
Yang-Mills theory. The method is\\nbased on the existence of a unitary \
transformation relating inhomogeneous and\\nlong-range spin chains. This \
transformation can be traced back to a combination\\nof boost operators and \
an inhomogeneous version of Baxter's corner transfer\\nmatrix. We reproduce \
the existing results for the one-loop structure constants\\nin a simplified \
form and indicate how to use the method at higher loop orders.\\nThen we \
evaluate the one-loop structure constants in the quasiclassical limit\\nand \
compare them with the recent strong coupling computation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
