 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We provide a conjecture for the following two \
quantities related with the\\nspin-$\\\\frac{1}{2}$ isotropic Heisenberg \
model defined over rings of even\\nlengths: (i) the number of the solutions \
to the Bethe ansatz equations which\\ncorrespond to non-zero Bethe vectors; \
(ii) the number of physical singular\\nsolutions of the Bethe ansatz \
equations in the sense of Nepomechie-Wang. The\\nconjecture is based on a \
natural relationship between the solutions to the\\nBethe ansatz equations \
and the rigged configurations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
