Sefusatti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonlinear effects of dark energy clustering beyond the \
acoustic scales\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"28 pages, 12 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2014/07/013\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"astro-ph.CO\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We extend the resummation method of Anselmi & Pietroni \
(2012) to compute the\\ntotal density power spectrum in models of \
quintessence characterized by a\\nvanishing speed of sound. For standard \
$\\\\Lambda$CDM cosmologies, this\\nresummation scheme allows predictions \
with an accuracy at the few percent level\\nbeyond the range of scales where \
acoustic oscillations are present, therefore\\ncomparable to other, common \
numerical tools. In addition, our theoretical\\napproach indicates an \
approximate but valuable and simple relation between the\\npower spectra for \
standard quintessence models and models where scalar field\\nperturbations \
appear at all scales. This, in turn, provides an educated guess\\nfor the \
prediction of nonlinear growth in models with generic speed of \
sound,\\nparticularly valuable since no numerical results are yet \
available.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
