            "  We extend the resummation method of Anselmi & Pietroni (2012) \
to compute the\ntotal density power spectrum in models of quintessence \
characterized by a\nvanishing speed of sound. For standard $\\Lambda$CDM \
cosmologies, this\nresummation scheme allows predictions with an accuracy at \
the few percent level\nbeyond the range of scales where acoustic oscillations \
are present, therefore\ncomparable to other, common numerical tools. In \
addition, our theoretical\napproach indicates an approximate but valuable and \
simple relation between the\npower spectra for standard quintessence models \
and models where scalar field\nperturbations appear at all scales. This, in \
turn, provides an educated guess\nfor the prediction of nonlinear growth in \
models with generic speed of sound,\nparticularly valuable since no numerical \
results are yet available.\n", 
