         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1402.6147", "submitter" -> "Io Kawaguchi", "authors" -> 
            "Io Kawaguchi, Takuya Matsumoto and Kentaroh Yoshida", "title" -> 
            "A Jordanian deformation of AdS space in type IIB supergravity", 
            "comments" -> 
            "29 pages, no figure, LaTeX, typos corrected, references added,\n \
 further clarification added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP06(2014)146", "report-no" -> 
            "KUNS-2484, ITP-UU-14/07, SPIN-14/07", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider a Jordanian deformation of the AdS_5xS^5 \
superstring action by\ntaking a simple R-operator which satisfies the \
classical Yang-Baxter equation.\nThe metric and NS-NS two-form are explicitly \
derived with a coordinate system.\nOnly the AdS part is deformed and the \
resulting geometry contains the 3D\nSchrodinger spacetime as a subspace. Then \
we present the full solution in type\nIIB supergravity by determining the \
other field components. In particular, the\ndilaton is constant and a R-R \
three-form field strength is turned on. The\nsymmetry of the solution is \
[SL(2,R)xU(1)^2] x [SU(3)xU(1)] and contains an\nanisotropic scale symmetry.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 25 Feb 2014 12:21:13 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 10 Mar 2014 04:14:03 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
