            "B. Hoare, R. Roiban and A. A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "On deformations of AdS_n x S^n supercosets", "comments" -> 
            "31 pages; v2: 33 pages, comments on unitarity and finiteness \
added\n  and misprints corrected; v3: minor changes", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP06(2014)002", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AT-2014-02, HU-EP-14/10", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the deformed AdS_5 x S^5 supercoset model of \
arXiv:1309.5850 which\ndepends on one parameter kappa and has classical \
quantum group symmetry. We\nconfirm the conjecture that in the \"maximal\" \
deformation limit kappa ->\ninfinity this model is T-dual to \"flipped\" \
double Wick rotation of the target\nspace AdS_5 x S^5, i.e. dS_5 x H^5 space \
supported by an imaginary 5-form flux.\nIn the imaginary deformation limit, \
kappa -> i, the corresponding target space\nmetric is of a pp-wave type and \
thus the resulting light-cone gauge S-matrix\nbecomes relativistically \
invariant. Omitting non-unitary contributions of\nimaginary WZ terms, we find \
that this tree-level S-matrix is equivalent to that\nof the generalized \
sine-Gordon model representing the Pohlmeyer reduction of\nthe undeformed \
AdS_5 x S^5 superstring model. We also study in some detail\nsimilar \
deformations of the AdS_3 x S^3 and AdS_2 x S^2 supercosets. The\nbosonic \
part of the deformed AdS_3 x S^3 model happens to be equivalent to the\n\
symmetric case of the sum of the Fateev integrable deformation of the SL(2) \
and\nSU(2) principal chiral models, while in the AdS_2 x S^2 case the role of \
the\nFateev model is played by the 2d \"sausage\" model. The kappa = i limits \
are\nagain directly related to the Pohlmeyer reductions of the corresponding \
AdS_n x\nS^n supercosets: (2,2) super sine-Gordon model and its complex \
sine-Gordon\nanalog. We also discuss possible deformations of AdS_3 x S^3 \
with more than one\nparameter.\n", 
