 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Puff Field Theory (PFT) is an example of a non-local \
field theory which\\narises from a novel embedding of D-branes in Melvin \
universe. We study several\\nrotating and pulsating string solutions of the \
F-string equations of motion in\\nthe supergravity dual of the PFT. Further, \
we find a PP-wave geometry from this\\nnonlocal spacetime by applying a \
Penrose limit and comment on its similarity\\nwith the maximally \
supersymmetric PP-wave background.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
