            "Matteo Beccaria, Guido Macorini", "title" -> 
            "On the one-loop curvature function in the $sl(2)$ sector of \
$\\mathcal\n  N=4$ SYM", "comments" -> "21 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP06(2014)141", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            
            "  We consider twist $J$ operators with spin $S$ in the $sl(2)$ \
sector of\n$\\mathcal N=4$ SYM. The small spin expansion of their anomalous \
dimension\ndefines the so-called slope functions. Much is known about the \
linear term, but\nthe study of the quadratic correction, the curvature \
function, started only\nvery recently. At any fixed $J$, the curvature \
function can be extracted at all\nloops from the $\\mathbf{P}\\mu$-system \
formulation of the Thermodynamical Bethe\nAnsatz. Here, we work at the \
one-loop level and follow a different approach. We\npresent a systematic \
double expansion of the Bethe Ansatz equations at large\n$J$ and small \
winding number. We succeed in fully resumming this expansion and\nobtain a \
closed explicit simple formula for the one-loop curvature function.\nThe \
formula is parametric in $J$ and can be evaluated with minor effort for any\n\
fixed $J$. The result is an explicit series in odd-index $\\zeta$ values. Our\
\napproach provides a complete reconciliation between the \
$\\mathbf{P}\\mu$-system\npredictions and the large $J$ approach.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 3 Apr 2014 13:10:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-19", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Beccaria", "Matteo", ""}, {
              "Macorini", "Guido", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
