               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the one-loop correction to the probe \
D3-brane action in AdS5 x S5\\nexpanded around the classical Drukker-Fiol \
solution ending on a circle at the\\nboundary. It is given essentially by the \
logarithm of the one-loop partition\\nfunction of an Abelian ${\\\\cal N}=4$ \
vector multiplet in AdS2 x S2 geometry.\\nThis one-loop correction is \
expected to describe the subleading 1/N term in the\\nexpectation value of \
circular Wilson loop in the totally symmetric rank k\\nrepresentation in \
SU(N) SYM theory at strong coupling. In the limit k << N when\\nthe circular \
Wilson loop expectation values for the symmetric representation\\nand for the \
product of k fundamental representations are expected to match we\\nfind that \
this one-loop D3-brane correction agrees with the gauge theory result\\nfor \
the k-fundamental case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
