 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Motivated by the recent proposal for the S-matrix in \
$AdS_3\\\\times S^3$ with\\nmixed three form fluxes, we study classical \
folded string spinning in $AdS_3$\\nwith both Ramond and Neveu-Schwarz three \
form fluxes. We solve the equations of\\nmotion of these strings and obtain \
their dispersion relation to the leading\\norder in the Neveu-Schwarz flux \
$b$. We show that dispersion relation for the\\nspinning strings with large \
spin ${\\\\cal S}$ acquires a term given \
by\\n$-\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}}{2\\\\pi} b^2\\\\log^2 {\\\\cal S}$ in \
addition to the usual\\n$\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt\\\\lambda}{\\\\pi} \\\\log \
{\\\\cal S}$ term where $\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}$ is\\nproportional to the \
square of the radius of $AdS_3$. Using SO(2,2)\\ntransformations and \
re-parmetrizations we show that these spinning strings can\\nbe related to \
light like Wilson loops in $AdS_3$ with Neveu-Schwarz flux $b$.\\nWe observe \
that the logarithmic divergence in the area of the light like Wilson\\nloop \
is also deformed by precisely the same coefficient of the $ b^2 \\\\log^2\\n{\
\\\\cal S}$ term in the dispersion relation of the spinning string. This \
result\\nindicates that the coefficient of $ b^2 \\\\log^2 {\\\\cal S}$ has a \
property similar\\nto the coefficient of the $\\\\log {\\\\cal S}$ term, \
known as cusp-anomalous\\ndimension, and can possibly be determined to all \
orders in the coupling\\n$\\\\lambda$ using the recent proposal for the \
S-matrix.\\n\""}]}, {
