                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We study local temperature fluctuations in a 2+1 \
dimensional CFT on the\\nsphere, dual to a black hole in asymptotically AdS \
spacetime. The fluctuation\\nspectrum is governed by the lowest-lying \
hydrodynamic modes of the system whose\\nfrequency and damping rate determine \
whether temperature fluctuations are\\nthermal or quantum. We calculate \
numerically the corresponding quasinormal\\nfrequencies and match the result \
with the hydrodynamics of the dual CFT at\\nlarge temperature. As a \
by-product of our analysis we determine the appropriate\\nboundary conditions \
for calculating low-lying quasinormal modes for a\\nfour-dimensional \
Reissner-Nordstr\\\\\\\"om black hole in global AdS.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
