           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "1405.4829", "submitter" -> "Sven Bjarke Gudnason", 
             "authors" -> 
             "Alexander Balatsky, Sven Bjarke Gudnason, Yaron Kedem, \
Alexander\n  Krikun, Larus Thorlacius, Konstantin Zarembo", "title" -> 
             "Classical and quantum temperature fluctuations via holography", 
             "comments" -> 
             "LaTeX: 31 pages, 7 figures; V2: reference added; V3: \
added/updated\n  charged case", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1501:011,2015", "doi" -> 
             "10.1007/JHEP01(2015)011", "report-no" -> 
             "NORDITA-2014-61, UUITP-04/14", "categories" -> 
             "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech gr-qc", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We study local temperature fluctuations in a 2+1 dimensional \
CFT on the\nsphere, dual to a black hole in asymptotically AdS spacetime. The \
fluctuation\nspectrum is governed by the lowest-lying hydrodynamic modes of \
the system whose\nfrequency and damping rate determine whether temperature \
fluctuations are\nthermal or quantum. We calculate numerically the \
corresponding quasinormal\nfrequencies and match the result with the \
hydrodynamics of the dual CFT at\nlarge temperature. As a by-product of our \
analysis we determine the appropriate\nboundary conditions for calculating \
low-lying quasinormal modes for a\nfour-dimensional Reissner-Nordstr\\\"om \
black hole in global AdS.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Mon, 19 May 2014 18:31:16 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
                "Mon, 2 Jun 2014 19:31:23 GMT"}, {
