            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study superstrings on AdS_3 x S^3 x T^4 supported by a \
combination of\nRamond-Ramond and Neveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz three form \
fluxes, and construct\na set of finite-gap equations that describe the \
classical string spectrum.\nUsing the recently proposed all-loop S-matrix we \
write down the all-loop Bethe\nansatz equations for the massive sector. In \
the thermodynamic limit the Bethe\nansatz reproduces the finite-gap \
equations. As part of this derivation we\npropose expressions for the leading \
order dressing phases. These phases differ\nfrom the well-known \
Arutyunov-Frolov-Staudacher phase that appears in the pure\nRamond-Ramond \
case. We also consider the one-loop quantization of the algebraic\ncurve and \
determine the one-loop corrections to the dressing phases. Finally we\n\
consider some classical string solutions including finite size giant magnons\n\
and circular strings.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 23 May 2014 15:03:56 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 4 Jun 2014 16:55:33 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-19", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Babichenko", "Andrei", ""}, {
              "Dekel", "Amit", ""}, {"Sax", "Olof Ohlsson", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.837517999836173`, -5.890188246755115}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1405.7947\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Lorenzo Bianchi\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lorenzo Bianchi and Ben Hoare\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"$AdS_3 \\\\times S^3 \\\\times M^4$ string S-matrices \
from unitarity cuts\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2014)097\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Continuing the program initiated in arXiv:1304.1798 we \
investigate unitarity\\nmethods applied to two-dimensional integrable field \
theories. The one-loop\\ncomputation is generalized to encompass theories \
with different masses in the\\nasymptotic spectrum and external leg \
corrections. Additionally, the\\nprescription for working with potentially \
singular cuts is modified to cope\\nwith an ambiguity that was not \
encountered before. The resulting methods are\\nthen applied to three \
light-cone gauge string theories; i) $AdS_3 \\\\times S^3\\n\\\\times T^4$ \
supported by RR flux, ii) $AdS_3 \\\\times S^3 \\\\times S^3 \\\\times \
S^1$\\nsupported by RR flux and iii) $AdS_3 \\\\times S^3 \\\\times T^4$ \
supported by a mix\\nof RR and NSNS fluxes. In the first case we find \
agreement with the exact\\nresult following from symmetry considerations and \
in the second case with\\none-loop semiclassical computations. This agreement \
crucially includes the\\nrational terms and hence supports the conjecture \
that S-matrices of integrable\\nfield theories are cut-constructible, up to a \
possible shift in the coupling.\\nIn the final case, under the assumption \
that our methods continue to give all\\nrational terms, we give a conjecture \
for the one-loop phases.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
