            "  Continuing the program initiated in arXiv:1304.1798 we \
investigate unitarity\nmethods applied to two-dimensional integrable field \
theories. The one-loop\ncomputation is generalized to encompass theories with \
different masses in the\nasymptotic spectrum and external leg corrections. \
Additionally, the\nprescription for working with potentially singular cuts is \
modified to cope\nwith an ambiguity that was not encountered before. The \
resulting methods are\nthen applied to three light-cone gauge string \
theories; i) $AdS_3 \\times S^3\n\\times T^4$ supported by RR flux, ii) \
$AdS_3 \\times S^3 \\times S^3 \\times S^1$\nsupported by RR flux and iii) \
$AdS_3 \\times S^3 \\times T^4$ supported by a mix\nof RR and NSNS fluxes. In \
the first case we find agreement with the exact\nresult following from \
symmetry considerations and in the second case with\none-loop semiclassical \
computations. This agreement crucially includes the\nrational terms and hence \
supports the conjecture that S-matrices of integrable\nfield theories are \
cut-constructible, up to a possible shift in the coupling.\nIn the final \
case, under the assumption that our methods continue to give all\nrational \
terms, we give a conjecture for the one-loop phases.\n", 
