                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We generalize the method of our recent paper on the \
large-spin expansions of\\nGubser-Klebanov-Polyakov (GKP) strings to the \
large-spin and large-winding\\nexpansions of finite-size giant magnons and \
finite-size single spikes. By\\nexpressing the energies of long open strings \
in RxS2 in terms of Lambert's\\nW-function, we compute the leading, \
subleading and next-to-subleading series of\\nclassical exponential \
corrections to the dispersion relations of\\nHofman-Maldacena giant magnons \
and infinite-winding single spikes. We also\\ncompute the corresponding \
expansions in the doubled regions of giant magnons\\nand single spikes that \
are respectively obtained when their angular and linear\\nvelocities become \
smaller or greater than unity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
