            "Towards integrability for AdS3/CFT2", "comments" -> 
            "Review, 152 pages, 29 figures; v2: minor changes, references \
added;\n  v3: more minor changes, more references; v4: misprints corrected, \
references\n  updated, as published", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 48 (2015) 023001", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/48/2/023001", "report-no" -> 
            "HU-Mathematik-2014-14, HU-EP-14/24", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We review the recent progress towards applying worldsheet \
integrability\ntechniques to the $AdS_3/CFT_2$ correspondence to find its \
all-loop S matrix\nand Bethe-Yang equations. We study in full detail the \
massive sector of\n$AdS_3\\times S^3\\times T^4$ superstrings supported by \
pure Ramond-Ramond (RR)\nfluxes. The extension of this machinery to \
accommodate massless modes, to the\n$AdS_3\\times S^3\\times S^3\\times S^1$ \
pure-RR background and to backgrounds\nsupported by mixed background fluxes \
is also reviewed. While the results\ndiscussed here were found elsewhere, our \
presentation sometimes deviates from\nthe one found in the original \
literature in an effort to be pedagogical and\nself-contained.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
