               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1406.5129\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Bartomeu Fiol\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bartomeu Fiol, Blai Garolera and Genis Torrents\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exact probes of orientifolds\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages. v2: Added references\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2014)169\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the exact vacuum expectation value of \
circular Wilson loops for\\nEuclidean ${\\\\cal N}=4$ super Yang-Mills with \
$G=SO(N),Sp(N)$, in the\\nfundamental and spinor representations. These field \
theories are dual to type\\nIIB string theory compactified on $AdS_5\\\\times \
{\\\\mathbb R} {\\\\mathbb P}^5$ plus\\ncertain choices of discrete torsion, \
and we use our results to probe this\\nholographic duality. We first revisit \
the LLM-type geometries having\\n$AdS_5\\\\times {\\\\mathbb R} {\\\\mathbb \
P}^5$ as ground state. Our results clarify\\nand refine the identification of \
these LLM-type geometries as bubbling\\ngeometries arising from fermions on a \
half harmonic oscillator. We furthermore\\nidentify the presence of discrete \
torsion with the one-fermion Wigner\\ndistribution becoming negative at the \
origin of phase space. We then turn to\\nthe string world-sheet \
interpretation of our results and argue that for the\\nquantities considered \
they imply two features: first, the contribution coming\\nfrom world-sheets \
with a single crosscap is closely related to the contribution\\ncoming from \
orientable world-sheets, and second, world-sheets with two\\ncrosscaps don't \
contribute to these quantities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
