            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute the exact vacuum expectation value of circular \
Wilson loops for\nEuclidean ${\\cal N}=4$ super Yang-Mills with \
$G=SO(N),Sp(N)$, in the\nfundamental and spinor representations. These field \
theories are dual to type\nIIB string theory compactified on $AdS_5\\times \
{\\mathbb R} {\\mathbb P}^5$ plus\ncertain choices of discrete torsion, and \
we use our results to probe this\nholographic duality. We first revisit the \
LLM-type geometries having\n$AdS_5\\times {\\mathbb R} {\\mathbb P}^5$ as \
ground state. Our results clarify\nand refine the identification of these \
LLM-type geometries as bubbling\ngeometries arising from fermions on a half \
harmonic oscillator. We furthermore\nidentify the presence of discrete \
torsion with the one-fermion Wigner\ndistribution becoming negative at the \
origin of phase space. We then turn to\nthe string world-sheet interpretation \
of our results and argue that for the\nquantities considered they imply two \
features: first, the contribution coming\nfrom world-sheets with a single \
crosscap is closely related to the contribution\ncoming from orientable \
world-sheets, and second, world-sheets with two\ncrosscaps don't contribute \
to these quantities.\n", 
