                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute four-point scattering amplitudes in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCQCD with\\ngeneral external matter configurations using \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ superspace Feynman\\ndiagrams, at one loop in the general \
case and up to two loops in the\\nfundamental sector. In the pure adjoint \
sector at one loop we confirm exact\\nagreement with the corresponding \
amplitudes in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM theory,\\nsupporting the idea that a \
closed subsector of the SCQCD might be exactly\\nintegrable. External matter \
in the fundamental representation breaks dual\\nconformal invariance already \
at one loop and also the maximum transcendentality\\nprinciple at two \
loops.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
