               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pavel Krtous\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Pavel Krtous, Andrei Zelnikov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Minimal surfaces and entanglement entropy in anti-de \
Sitter space\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"36 pages, 21 figures, for version with high-resolution \
figures see\\n  http://utf.mff.cuni.cz/~krtous/papers/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1410:077,2014\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2014)077\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alberta Thy 11-14\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  According to Ryu and Takayanagi, the entanglement \
entropy in conformal field\\ntheory (CFT) is related through the AdS/CFT \
correspondence to the area of a\\nminimal surface in the bulk. We study this \
holographic geometrical method of\\ncalculating the entanglement entropy in \
the vacuum case of a CFT which is\\nholographically dual to empty anti-de \
Sitter (AdS) spacetime. Namely, we\\ninvestigate the minimal surfaces spanned \
on boundaries of spherical domains at\\ninfinity of hyperbolic space, which \
represents a time-slice of AdS spacetime.\\nWe consider a generic position of \
two spherical domains: two disjoint domains,\\noverlapping domains, and \
touching domains. In all these cases we find the\\nexplicit expressions for \
the minimal surfaces and the renormalized expression\\nfor the area. We study \
also the embedding of the minimal surfaces into full AdS\\nspacetime and we \
find that for a proper choice of the static Killing vector we\\ncan model a \
dynamical situation of \\\"tearing\\\" of the minimal surface when \
the\\ndomains on which it is spanned are moved away from each \
other.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 30 Jun 2014 10:37:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2018-07-18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Krtous\"", ",", "\"Pavel\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Zelnikov\"", ",", "\"Andrei\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
