               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ben Hoare, Antonio Pittelli, Alessandro Torrielli\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable S-matrices, massive and massless modes and the \
AdS_2 x S^2\\n  superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages; v2: 37 pages, clarifications, including on the \
issue of\\n  double crossing, and comments added, version to appear in \
JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2014)051\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"HU-EP-14/28, DMUS--MP--14/05\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the exact S-matrix for the scattering of \
particular representations\\nof the centrally-extended psu(1|1)^2 Lie \
superalgebra, conjectured to be\\nrelated to the massive modes of the \
light-cone gauge string theory on AdS_2 x\\nS^2 x T^6. The S-matrix consists \
of two copies of a centrally-extended psu(1|1)\\ninvariant S-matrix and is in \
agreement with the tree-level result following\\nfrom perturbation theory. \
Although the overall factor is left unfixed, the\\nconstraints following from \
crossing symmetry and unitarity are given. The\\nscattering involves long \
representations of the symmetry algebra, and the\\nrelevant representation \
theory is studied in detail. We also discuss Yangian\\nsymmetry and find it \
has a standard form for a particular limit of the\\naforementioned \
representations. This has a natural interpretation as the\\nmassless limit, \
and we investigate the corresponding limits of the massive\\nS-matrix. Under \
the assumption that the massless modes of the light-cone gauge\\nstring \
theory transform in these limiting representations, the \
resulting\\nS-matrices would provide the building blocks for the full \
S-matrix. Finally,\\nsome brief comments are given on the Bethe \
ansatz.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
