            "  We derive the exact S-matrix for the scattering of particular \
representations\nof the centrally-extended psu(1|1)^2 Lie superalgebra, \
conjectured to be\nrelated to the massive modes of the light-cone gauge \
string theory on AdS_2 x\nS^2 x T^6. The S-matrix consists of two copies of a \
centrally-extended psu(1|1)\ninvariant S-matrix and is in agreement with the \
tree-level result following\nfrom perturbation theory. Although the overall \
factor is left unfixed, the\nconstraints following from crossing symmetry and \
unitarity are given. The\nscattering involves long representations of the \
symmetry algebra, and the\nrelevant representation theory is studied in \
detail. We also discuss Yangian\nsymmetry and find it has a standard form for \
a particular limit of the\naforementioned representations. This has a natural \
interpretation as the\nmassless limit, and we investigate the corresponding \
limits of the massive\nS-matrix. Under the assumption that the massless modes \
of the light-cone gauge\nstring theory transform in these limiting \
representations, the resulting\nS-matrices would provide the building blocks \
for the full S-matrix. Finally,\nsome brief comments are given on the Bethe \
ansatz.\n", 
