           "id" -> "1407.2840", "submitter" -> "Timothy J. Hollowood", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Timothy J. Hollowood, J. Luis Miramontes and David M. Schmidtt", 
            "title" -> 
            "Integrable Deformations of Strings on Symmetric Spaces", 
            "comments" -> "41 pages, typos corrected, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP11(2014)009", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  A general class of deformations of integrable sigma-models \
with symmetric\nspace F/G target-spaces are found. These deformations involve \
defining the\nnon-abelian T dual of the sigma-model and then replacing the \
coupling of the\nLagrange multiplier imposing flatness with a gauged F/F WZW \
model. The original\nsigma-model is obtained in the limit of large level. The \
resulting deformed\ntheories are shown to preserve both integrability and the \
equations-of-motion,\nbut involve a deformation of the symplectic structure. \
It is shown that this\ndeformed symplectic structure involves a linear \
combination of the original\nPoisson bracket and a generalization of the \
Faddeev-Reshetikhin Poisson bracket\nwhich we show can be re-expressed as two \
decoupled F current algebras. It is\nthen shown that the deformation can be \
incorporated into the classical model of\nstrings on R x F/G via a \
generalization of the Pohlmeyer reduction. In this\ncase, in the limit of \
large sigma-model coupling it is shown that the theory\nbecomes the \
relativistic symmetric space sine-Gordon theory. These results\npoint to the \
existence of a deformation of this kind for the full Green-Schwarz\n\
superstring on AdS5 x S5.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
