                 "\"Partition Functions of Superconformal Chern-Simons \
Theories from Fermi\\n  Gas Approach\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"36 pages, 4 figures; v2: typos corrected and \
clarifications added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2014)164\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"YITP-14-56\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the partition function of three-dimensional ${\
\\\\mathcal N}=4$\\nsuperconformal Chern-Simons theories of the circular \
quiver type, which are\\nnatural generalizations of the ABJM theory, the \
worldvolume theory of\\nM2-branes. In the ABJM case, it was known that the \
perturbative part of the\\npartition function sums up to the Airy function as\
\\n$Z(N)=e^{A}C^{-1/3}\\\\mathrm{Ai}[C^{-1/3}(N-B)]$ with coefficients $C$, \
$B$ and\\n$A$ and that for the non-perturbative part the divergences coming \
from the\\ncoefficients of worldsheet instantons and membrane instantons \
cancel among\\nthemselves. We find that many of the interesting properties in \
the ABJM theory\\nare extended to the general superconformal Chern-Simons \
theories. Especially,\\nwe find an explicit expression of $B$ for general \
${\\\\mathcal N}=4$ theories, a\\nconjectural form of $A$ for a special class \
of theories, and cancellation in\\nthe non-perturbative coefficients for the \
simplest theory next to the ABJM\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
