            "  We study the partition function of three-dimensional \
${\\mathcal N}=4$\nsuperconformal Chern-Simons theories of the circular \
quiver type, which are\nnatural generalizations of the ABJM theory, the \
worldvolume theory of\nM2-branes. In the ABJM case, it was known that the \
perturbative part of the\npartition function sums up to the Airy function as\n\
$Z(N)=e^{A}C^{-1/3}\\mathrm{Ai}[C^{-1/3}(N-B)]$ with coefficients $C$, $B$ \
and\n$A$ and that for the non-perturbative part the divergences coming from \
the\ncoefficients of worldsheet instantons and membrane instantons cancel \
among\nthemselves. We find that many of the interesting properties in the \
ABJM theory\nare extended to the general superconformal Chern-Simons \
theories. Especially,\nwe find an explicit expression of $B$ for general \
${\\mathcal N}=4$ theories, a\nconjectural form of $A$ for a special class of \
theories, and cancellation in\nthe non-perturbative coefficients for the \
simplest theory next to the ABJM\ntheory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
