               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mehrdad Mirbabayi\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Siavosh R. Behbahani, Mehrdad Mirbabayi, Leonardo \
Senatore, and\\n  Kendrick M. Smith\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"New natural shapes of non-Gaussianity from \
high-derivative interactions\\n  and their optimal limits from WMAP 9-year \
data\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"22+14 pages,\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2014/11/035\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Given the fantastic experimental effort, it is \
important to thoroughly\\nexplore the signature space of inflationary models. \
The fact that higher\\nderivative operators do not renormalize lower \
derivative ones allows us to find\\na large class of technically natural \
single-clock inflationary models where, in\\nthe context of the Effective \
Field Theory of Inflation, the leading\\ninteractions have many derivatives. \
We systematically explore the 3-point\\nfunction induced by these models and \
their overlap with the standard\\nequilateral and orthogonal templates. We \
find that in order to satisfactorily\\ncover the signature space of these \
models, two new additional templates need to\\nbe included. We then perform \
the optimal analysis of the WMAP 9-year data for\\nthe resulting four \
templates, finding that the overall significance of a\\nnon-zero signal is \
between 2--2.5$\\\\sigma$, depending on the choice of parameter\\nspace, \
partially driven by the preference for nonzero $f_{NL}^{\\\\rm orth}$ \
in\\nWMAP9.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
