            "  Given the fantastic experimental effort, it is important to \
thoroughly\nexplore the signature space of inflationary models. The fact that \
higher\nderivative operators do not renormalize lower derivative ones allows \
us to find\na large class of technically natural single-clock inflationary \
models where, in\nthe context of the Effective Field Theory of Inflation, the \
leading\ninteractions have many derivatives. We systematically explore the \
3-point\nfunction induced by these models and their overlap with the standard\
\nequilateral and orthogonal templates. We find that in order to \
