                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the possible signatures of a recently \
introduced class of healthy\\ntheories beyond Horndeski models on \
higher-order correlators of the\\ninflationary curvature fluctuation. Despite \
the apparent large number and\\ncomplexity of the cubic interactions, we show \
that the leading-order bispectrum\\ngenerated by the Generalized Horndeski \
(also called $G^3$) interactions can be\\nreduced to a linear combination of \
two well known $k$-inflationary shapes. We\\nconjecture that said behavior is \
not an accident of the cubic order but a\\nconsequence dictated by the \
requirements on the absence of Ostrogradski\\ninstability, the general \
covariance and the linear dispersion relation in these\\ntheories.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
