Horndeski", "comments" -> 
            "17 pages. Analysis expanded and some references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1475-7516/2014/10/037", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the possible signatures of a recently introduced \
class of healthy\ntheories beyond Horndeski models on higher-order \
correlators of the\ninflationary curvature fluctuation. Despite the apparent \
large number and\ncomplexity of the cubic interactions, we show that the \
leading-order bispectrum\ngenerated by the Generalized Horndeski (also called \
$G^3$) interactions can be\nreduced to a linear combination of two well known \
$k$-inflationary shapes. We\nconjecture that said behavior is not an accident \
of the cubic order but a\nconsequence dictated by the requirements on the \
absence of Ostrogradski\ninstability, the general covariance and the linear \
dispersion relation in these\ntheories.\n", 
