               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spinning strings in AdS_3 x S^3 with NS-NS flux\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"14 pages. Latex. v2: Equations (3.19) and (3.28) \
corrected and\\n  reference added. v3: Expanded discussion on the WZW limit \
and additional\\n  references. Published version. v4: Misprints \
corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2014.10.001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The sigma model describing closed strings rotating in \
AdS_3 x S^3 is known to\\nreduce to the one-dimensional Neumann-Rosochatius \
integrable system. In this\\narticle we show that closed spinning strings in \
AdS_3 x S^3 x T^4 in the\\npresence of NS-NS three-form flux can be described \
by an extension of the\\nNeumann-Rosochatius system. We consider closed \
strings rotating with one spin\\nin AdS_3 and two different angular momenta \
in S^3. For a class of solutions\\nwith constant radii we find the dependence \
of the classical energy on the spin\\nand the angular momenta as an expansion \
in the square of the 't Hooft coupling\\nof the theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
