               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the massive-sector worldsheet S-matrix for \
superstring theories in\\nAdS(n) x S(n) x T(10-2n) (with n=2,3,5) in the near \
BMN expansion up to\\none-loop order in inverse string tension. We show that, \
after taking into\\naccount the wave function renormalization, the one-loop \
S-matrix is UV finite.\\nIn an appropriate regularization scheme the S-matrix \
is consistent with the\\nunderlying symmetries of the superstring theory, \
i.e. for the n=3,5 cases it\\ncoincides with the one implied by the \
light-cone gauge symmetries with the\\ndressing phases determined from the \
crossing equations. For the n=2,3 cases we\\nobserve that the massless modes \
decouple from the one-loop calculation of\\nmassive mode scattering, i.e. the \
2n-dimensional supercoset sigma model and the\\nfull 10-dimensional \
superstring happen to have the same massive one-loop\\nS-matrix.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
