 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The two-magnon-bound-state mass gap m_2 for the \
two-dimensional quantum Ising\\nmodel was investigated by means of the \
numerical diagonalization method; the\\nlow-lying spectrum is directly \
accessible via the numerical diagonalization\\nmethod. It has been claimed \
that the ratio m_2/m_1 (m_1: one-magnon mass gap)\\nis a universal constant \
in the vicinity of the critical point. Aiming to\\nsuppress corrections to \
scaling (lattice artifact), we consider the spin-S=1\\nIsing model with \
finely-adjusted extended interactions. The simulation result\\nfor the \
finite-size cluster with N \\\\le 20 spins indicates the mass-gap \
ratio\\nm_2/m_1=1.84(1).\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
