           "id" -> "1408.3393", "submitter" -> "Yang Zhou", "authors" -> 
            "Xing Huang, Yang Zhou", "title" -> 
            "N = 4 Super-Yang-Mills on Conic Space as Hologram of STU \
Topological\n  Black Hole", "comments" -> 
            "1+48 pages, v2:typo fixed+references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP02(2015)068", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP02(2015)068", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct four-dimensional N=4 super-Yang-Mills theories on \
a conic sphere\nwith various background R-symmetry gauge fields. We study \
free energy and\nsupersymmetric Renyi entropy using heat kernel method as \
well as localization\ntechnique. We find that the universal contribution to \
the partition function in\nthe free field limit is the same as that in the \
strong coupling limit, which\nimplies that it may be protected by \
supersymmetry. Based on the fact that, the\nconic sphere can be conformally \
mapped to $S^1\\times H^3$ and the R-symmetry\nbackground fields can be \
supported by the R-charges of black hole, we propose\nthat the holographic \
dual of these theories are five-dimensional,\nsupersymmetric STU topological \
black holes. We demonstrate perfect agreement\nbetween N=4 super-Yang-Mills \
theories in the planar limit and the STU\ntopological black holes.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
