                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the supersymmetric R\\\\'enyi entropies \
across a spherical\\nentanglement surface in N=4 SU(N) SYM theory using \
localization on the\\nfour-dimensional ellipsoid. We extract the leading \
result at large N and\\n\\\\lambda, and match its universal part to a gravity \
calculation involving a\\nhyperbolically sliced supersymmetric black hole \
solution of N=4+ SU(2) X U(1)\\ngauged supergravity in five dimensions. We \
repeat the analysis in the presence\\nof a Wilson loop insertion and find \
again a perfect match with the dual string\\ntheory. Understanding the Wilson \
loop operator requires knowledge of the full\\nten-dimensional IIB \
supergravity solution which we elaborate upon.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
