               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1409.1538\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Timothy J. Hollowood\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Timothy J. Hollowood, J. Luis Miramontes and David M. \
Schmidtt\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"An Integrable Deformation of the AdS5 x S5 \
Superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"23 pages, improved and expanded discussion of metric and \
B field\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/47/49/495402\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The S-matrix on the world-sheet theory of the string in \
AdS5 x S5 has\\npreviously been shown to admit a deformation where the \
symmetry algebra is\\nreplaced by the associated quantum group. The case \
where q is real has been\\nidentified as a particular deformation of the \
Green-Schwarz sigma model. An\\ninterpretation of the case with q a root of \
unity has, until now, been lacking.\\nWe show that the Green-Schwarz sigma \
model admits a discrete deformation which\\ncan be viewed as a rather simple \
deformation of the F/F_V gauged WZW model,\\nwhere F=PSU(2,2|4). The \
deformation parameter q is then a k-th root of unity\\nwhere k is the level. \
The deformed theory has the same equations-of-motion as\\nthe Green-Schwarz \
sigma model but has a different symplectic structure. We show\\nthat the \
resulting theory is integrable and has just the right amount \
of\\nkappa-symmetries that appear as a remnant of the fermionic part of the \
original\\ngauge symmetry. This points to the existence of a fully consistent \
deformed\\nstring background.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 4 Sep 2014 19:03:30 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 24 Sep 2014 14:41:49 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-06-22\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
