           "id" -> "1409.1538", "submitter" -> "Timothy J. Hollowood", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Timothy J. Hollowood, J. Luis Miramontes and David M. Schmidtt", 
            "title" -> 
            "An Integrable Deformation of the AdS5 x S5 Superstring", 
            "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, improved and expanded discussion of metric and B \
field", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8113/47/49/495402", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The S-matrix on the world-sheet theory of the string in AdS5 x \
S5 has\npreviously been shown to admit a deformation where the symmetry \
algebra is\nreplaced by the associated quantum group. The case where q is \
real has been\nidentified as a particular deformation of the Green-Schwarz \
sigma model. An\ninterpretation of the case with q a root of unity has, until \
now, been lacking.\nWe show that the Green-Schwarz sigma model admits a \
discrete deformation which\ncan be viewed as a rather simple deformation of \
the F/F_V gauged WZW model,\nwhere F=PSU(2,2|4). The deformation parameter q \
is then a k-th root of unity\nwhere k is the level. The deformed theory has \
the same equations-of-motion as\nthe Green-Schwarz sigma model but has a \
different symplectic structure. We show\nthat the resulting theory is \
integrable and has just the right amount of\nkappa-symmetries that appear as \
a remnant of the fermionic part of the original\ngauge symmetry. This points \
to the existence of a fully consistent deformed\nstring background.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 4 Sep 2014 19:03:30 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 24 Sep 2014 14:41:49 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-22", 
