                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JCAP 12 (2014) 002\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2014/12/002\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In models with Large Extra Dimensions the smallness of \
neutrino masses can be\\nnaturally explained by introducing gauge singlet \
fermions which propagate in\\nthe bulk. The Kaluza-Klein modes of these \
fermions appear as towers of sterile\\nneutrino states on the brane. We study \
the phenomenological consequences of\\nthis picture for the high energy \
atmospheric neutrinos. For this purpose we\\nconstruct a detailed equivalence \
between a model with large extra dimensions\\nand a (3 + n) scenario \
consisting of three active and n extra sterile neutrino\\nstates, which \
provides a clear intuitive understanding of Kaluza-Klein modes.\\nFinally, we \
analyze the collected data of high energy atmospheric neutrinos by\\nIceCube \
experiment and obtain bounds on the radius of extra dimensions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
