               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"An asymptotic solution of large-$N$ $QCD$, and of \
large-$N$\\n  $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ $SUSY$ $YM$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"56 pages, latex; more details and remarks, and some \
simplification;\\n  references added; typos fixed; talk at the conference: \
HP2: High Precision\\n  for Hard Processes, September 3-5, (2014), associated \
to the workshop:\\n  Prospects and Precision at the Large Hadron Collider at \
14 TeV, at the\\n  Galileo Galilei Institute for Theoretical Physics, \
Florence, Italy\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find an asymptotic solution for two- and three-point \
correlators of local\\ngauge-invariant operators, in a lower-spin sector of \
massless large-$N$ $QCD$,\\nin terms of glueball and meson propagators, by \
means of a new purely\\nfield-theoretical technique that we call the \
asymptotically-free bootstrap. The\\nasymptotically-free bootstrap exploits \
the lowest-order conformal invariance of\\nconnected correlators of gauge \
invariant composite operators in perturbation\\ntheory, the \
renormalization-group improvement, and a recently-proved \
asymptotic\\nstructure theorem for glueball and meson propagators, that \
involves the unknown\\nparticle spectrum and the anomalous dimension of \
operators for fixed spin. In\\nprinciple the asymptotically-free bootstrap \
extends to all the higher-spin two-\\nand three-point correlators whose \
lowest-order conformal limit is non-vanishing\\nin perturbation theory, and \
by means of the operator product expansion to the\\ncorresponding asymptotic \
multi-point correlators as well. Besides, the\\nasymptotically-free bootstrap \
provides asymptotic $S$-matrix amplitudes in\\nmassless large-$N$ $QCD$ in \
terms of glueball and meson propagators as opposed\\nto perturbation theory. \
Remarkably, the asymptotic $S$-matrix depends only on\\nthe unknown particle \
spectrum, but not on the anomalous dimensions. Moreover,\\nthe \
asymptotically-free bootstrap applies to large-$N$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ \
$SUSY$\\n$YM$ as well. Practically, as just a few examples among many more, \
it follows\\nthe structure of the light by light scattering amplitude, of the \
pion form\\nfactor, and the associated vector dominance. Theoretically, the \
asymptotic\\nsolution sets the strongest constraints on any actual solution \
of large-$N$\\n$QCD$ (and of large-$N$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ $SUSY$ $YM$), and \
in particular on any\\nstring solution.\\n\""}]}, {
