               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the D3-brane dual to a $k$-quark of \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$\\nsuper-Yang-Mills theory in the totally symmetric \
representation of $SU(N)$,\\nundergoing arbitrary motion. Our method of \
construction generalizes previous\\nwork by Mikhailov, and proceeds by \
shooting light rays inward from the anti-de\\nSitter boundary, to trace out \
the brane embedding. We expect this method to\\nhave wider relevance, and \
provide evidence for this by showing that it\\ncorrectly reproduces the known \
D5-brane embeddings dual to totally\\nantisymmetric $k$-quarks. As an \
application of our solutions, we compute the\\nenergy of the D3-brane and \
extract from it the $k$-quark's intrinsic energy and\\nrate of radiation. The \
result matches expectations based on previous\\ncalculations, and makes \
contact with the exact Bremsstrahlung function for the\\nfundamental \
representation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
