                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  As holographic description of BPS Wilson loops in \
${\\\\cal N}=3$ flavored ABJM\\ntheory with $N_f=k=1$, BPS M2-branes in \
$AdS_4\\\\times N(1, 1)$ are studied in\\ndetails. Two $1/3$-BPS membrane \
configurations are found. One of them is dual\\nto the $1/3$-BPS Wilson loop \
of Gaiotto-Yin type. The regulated membrane action\\ncaptures precisely the \
leading exponential behavior of the vacuum expectation\\nvalues of $1/3$-BPS \
Wilson loops in the strong coupling limit, which was\\ncomputed before using \
supersymmetric localization technique. Moreover, there is\\nno BPS membrane \
with more supersymmetries in the background, under quite\\nnatural assumption \
on the membrane worldvolume. This suggests that there is no\\nWilson loop \
preserving more than 1/3 supersymmetries in such flavored \
ABJM\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
