            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We analyse the phase structure of an $\\mathcal{N}=2$ massive \
deformation of\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM theory on an four-dimensional ellipsoid \
using recent\nresults on supersymmetric localisation. Besides the 't~Hooft \
coupling\n$\\lambda$, the relevant parameters appearing in the theory and \
discriminating\nbetween the different phases are the hypermultiplet mass $M$ \
and the\ndeformation (or squashing) parameter $Q$. The master field \
approximation of the\nmatrix model associated to the analytically continued \
theory in the regime\n$Q\\sim 2M$ and on the compact space, is exactly \
solvable and does not display\nany phase transition, similarly to \
$\\mathcal{N}=2$ $SU(N)$ SYM with $2N$\nmassive hypermultiplets. In the \
strong coupling limit, equivalent in our\nsettings to the decompactification \
of the four-dimensional ellipsoid, we find\nevidence that the theory \
undergoes an infinite number of phase transitions\nstarting at finite \
coupling and accumulating at $\\lambda=\\infty$. Quite\ninterestingly, the \
threshold points at which transitions occur can be pushed\ntowards the weak \
coupling region by letting $Q$ approach $2M$.\n", 
