                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"In\\\\^es Aniceto, Jorge G. Russo, Ricardo \
Schiappa\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Resurgent Analysis of Localizable Observables in \
Supersymmetric Gauge\\n  Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages, 8 figures; v2: added refs, small changes, \
improved\\n  discussion on resurgence triangle, final version for JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CERN-PH-TH-2014-118\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Localization methods have recently led to a plethora of \
new exact results in\\nsupersymmetric gauge theories, as certain observables \
may be computed in terms\\nof matrix integrals. These can then be evaluated \
by making use of standard\\nlarge N techniques, or else via perturbative \
expansions in the gauge coupling.\\nEither approximation often leads to \
observables given in terms of asymptotic\\nseries, which need to be properly \
defined in order to obtain nonperturbative\\nresults. At the same time, \
resurgent analysis has recently been successfully\\napplied to several \
problems, e.g., in quantum, field and string theories,\\nprecisely to \
overcome this issue and construct nonperturbative answers out of\\nasymptotic \
perturbative expansions. The present work uses exact results \
from\\nsupersymmetric localization to address the resurgent structure of the \
free\\nenergy and partition function of Chern-Simons and ABJM gauge theories \
in three\\ndimensions, and of N=2 supersymmetric Yang-Mills theories in four \
dimensions.\\nFor each case, the complete structure of Borel singularities is \
exactly\\ndetermined, and the relation of these singularities with the \
large-order\\nbehavior of (multi-instanton) perturbative expansions is made \
fully precise.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 21 Oct 2014 20:01:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
