         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1410.8860", "submitter" -> "Ivan K. Kostov", "authors" -> 
            "Yunfeng Jiang, Ivan Kostov, Andrei Petrovskii, Didina Serban", 
            "title" -> "String Bits and the Spin Vertex", "comments" -> 
            "34 pages, 6 figures, a sign correction in eq. (3.1) and appendix\
\n  added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2015.05.029",
             "report-no" -> "t14/231", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We initiate a novel formalism for computing correlation \
functions of trace\noperators in the planar N=4 SYM theory. The central \
object in our formalism is\nthe spin vertex, which is the weak coupling \
analogy of the string vertex in\nstring field theory. We construct the spin \
vertex explicitly for all sectors at\nthe leading order using a set of \
bosonic and fermionic oscillators. We prove\nthat the vertex has trivial \
monodromy, or put in other words, it is a Yangian\ninvariant. Since the \
monodromy of the vertex is the product of the monodromies\nof the three \
states, the Yangian invariance of the vertex implies an infinite\nexact \
symmetry for the three-point function. We conjecture that this infinite\n\
symmetry can be lifted to any loop order.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 31 Oct 2014 19:33:43 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 5 Dec 2014 08:29:13 GMT"}, {
