               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fen Zuo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fen Zuo, Yi-Hong Gao\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Thermodynamics of large-$N$ gauge theories on a sphere: \
weak versus\\n  strong coupling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Discussion on the small-$\\\\lambda$ corrections improved\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2015)003\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-lat hep-ph\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently lattice simulation in pure Yang-Mills theory \
exposes significant\\nquadratic corrections for both the thermodynamic \
quantities and the\\nrenormalized Polyakov loop in the deconfined phase. \
These terms are previously\\nfound to appear naturally for ${\\\\mathcal \
N}=4$ Super Yang-Mills~(SYM) on a\\nsphere at strong coupling, through the \
gauge/gravity duality. Here we extend\\nthe investigation to the weak \
coupling regime, and for general large-$N$ gauge\\ntheories. Employing the \
matrix model description, we find some novel behavior\\nin the deconfined \
phase, which is not noticed in the literature. Due to the\\nnon-uniform \
eigenvalue distribution of the holonomy around the time circle, \
the\\ndeviation of the Polyakov loop from one starts from $1/T^3$ instead of \
$1/T^2$.\\nSuch a power is fixed by the space dimension and do not change \
with different\\ntheories. This statement is also true when perturbative \
corrections to the\\nsingle-particle partition functions are included. The \
corrections to the\\nPolyakov loop and higher moments of the distribution \
function combine to give a\\nuniversal term, $T/4$, in the free energy. These \
differences between the weak\\nand strong coupling regime could be easily \
explained if a strong/weak coupling\\nphase transition occurs in the \
deconfined phase of large-$N$ gauge theories on\\na compact \
manifold.\\n\""}]}, {
