           "id" -> "1411.0373", "submitter" -> "Fen Zuo", "authors" -> 
            "Fen Zuo, Yi-Hong Gao", "title" -> 
            "Thermodynamics of large-$N$ gauge theories on a sphere: weak \
versus\n  strong coupling", "comments" -> 
            "Discussion on the small-$\\lambda$ corrections improved", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2015)003", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th hep-lat hep-ph", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently lattice simulation in pure Yang-Mills theory exposes \
significant\nquadratic corrections for both the thermodynamic quantities and \
the\nrenormalized Polyakov loop in the deconfined phase. These terms are \
previously\nfound to appear naturally for ${\\mathcal N}=4$ Super \
Yang-Mills~(SYM) on a\nsphere at strong coupling, through the gauge/gravity \
duality. Here we extend\nthe investigation to the weak coupling regime, and \
for general large-$N$ gauge\ntheories. Employing the matrix model \
description, we find some novel behavior\nin the deconfined phase, which is \
not noticed in the literature. Due to the\nnon-uniform eigenvalue \
distribution of the holonomy around the time circle, the\ndeviation of the \
Polyakov loop from one starts from $1/T^3$ instead of $1/T^2$.\nSuch a power \
is fixed by the space dimension and do not change with different\ntheories. \
This statement is also true when perturbative corrections to the\n\
single-particle partition functions are included. The corrections to the\n\
Polyakov loop and higher moments of the distribution function combine to give \
a\nuniversal term, $T/4$, in the free energy. These differences between the \
weak\nand strong coupling regime could be easily explained if a strong/weak \
coupling\nphase transition occurs in the deconfined phase of large-$N$ gauge \
theories on\na compact manifold.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
