               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Towards a two-parameter q-deformation of AdS_3 x S^3 x \
M^4 superstrings\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"35 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2014.12.012\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-EP-14/44\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct a two-parameter deformation of the \
Metsaev-Tseytlin action for\\nsupercosets with isometry group of the form G x \
G. The resulting action is\\nclassically integrable and is Poisson-Lie \
symmetric suggesting that the\\nsymmetry of the model is q-deformed, U_q_L(G) \
x U_q_R(G). Focusing on the cases\\nrelevant for strings moving in AdS_3 x \
S^3 x T^4 and AdS_3 x S^3 x S^3 x S^1,\\nwe analyze the corresponding \
deformations of the AdS_3 and S^3 metrics. We also\\nconstruct a \
two-parameter $q$-deformation of the u(1) + psu(1|1)^2 x u(1) \
x\\nR^3-invariant R-matrix and closure condition, which underlie the \
light-cone\\ngauge S-matrix and dispersion relation of the aforementioned \
string theories.\\nWith the appropriate identification of parameters, the \
near-BMN limit of the\\ndispersion relation is shown to agree with that found \
from the deformed\\nsupercoset sigma model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
