            "Ben Hoare", "title" -> 
            "Towards a two-parameter q-deformation of AdS_3 x S^3 x M^4 \
superstrings", "comments" -> "35 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2014.12.012", "report-no" -> "HU-EP-14/44", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct a two-parameter deformation of the \
Metsaev-Tseytlin action for\nsupercosets with isometry group of the form G x \
G. The resulting action is\nclassically integrable and is Poisson-Lie \
symmetric suggesting that the\nsymmetry of the model is q-deformed, U_q_L(G) \
x U_q_R(G). Focusing on the cases\nrelevant for strings moving in AdS_3 x S^3 \
x T^4 and AdS_3 x S^3 x S^3 x S^1,\nwe analyze the corresponding deformations \
of the AdS_3 and S^3 metrics. We also\nconstruct a two-parameter \
$q$-deformation of the u(1) + psu(1|1)^2 x u(1) x\nR^3-invariant R-matrix and \
closure condition, which underlie the light-cone\ngauge S-matrix and \
dispersion relation of the aforementioned string theories.\nWith the \
appropriate identification of parameters, the near-BMN limit of the\n\
dispersion relation is shown to agree with that found from the deformed\n\
supercoset sigma model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
