 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the holographic mutual information in AdS4 of \
disjoint spatial\\ndomains in the boundary which are delimited by smooth \
closed curves. A\\nnumerical method which approximates a local minimum of the \
area functional\\nthrough triangulated surfaces is employed. After some \
checks of the method\\nagainst existing analytic results for the holographic \
entanglement entropy, we\\ncompute the holographic mutual information of \
equal domains delimited by\\nellipses, superellipses or the boundaries of two \
dimensional spherocylinders,\\nfinding also the corresponding transition \
curves along which the holographic\\nmutual information vanishes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
