                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrability and the Conformal Field Theory of the Higgs \
branch\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"29 pages; v2: improved presentation and discussion, \
computations and\\n  results unchanged\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Imperial-TP-OOS-2014-05, HU-Mathematik-2014-33, \
HU-EP-14/49\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the context of the AdS$_3$/CFT$_2$ correspondence, \
we investigate the\\nHiggs branch CFT$_2$. Witten showed that states \
localised near the small\\ninstanton singularity can be described in terms of \
vector multiplet variables.\\nThis theory has a planar, weak-coupling limit, \
in which anomalous dimensions of\\nsingle-trace composite operators can be \
calculated. At one loop, the\\ncalculation reduces to finding the spectrum of \
a spin-chain with\\nnearest-neighbour interactions. This CFT$_2$ spin-chain \
matches precisely the\\none that was previously found as the weak-coupling \
limit of the integrable\\nsystem describing the AdS$_3$ side of the duality. \
We compute the one-loop\\ndilatation operator in a non-trivial compact \
subsector and show that it\\ncorresponds to an integrable spin-chain \
Hamiltonian. This provides the first\\ndirect evidence of integrability on \
the CFT$_2$ side of the correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
