            "  In the context of the AdS$_3$/CFT$_2$ correspondence, we \
investigate the\nHiggs branch CFT$_2$. Witten showed that states localised \
near the small\ninstanton singularity can be described in terms of vector \
multiplet variables.\nThis theory has a planar, weak-coupling limit, in which \
anomalous dimensions of\nsingle-trace composite operators can be calculated. \
At one loop, the\ncalculation reduces to finding the spectrum of a spin-chain \
with\nnearest-neighbour interactions. This CFT$_2$ spin-chain matches \
precisely the\none that was previously found as the weak-coupling limit of \
the integrable\nsystem describing the AdS$_3$ side of the duality. We compute \
the one-loop\ndilatation operator in a non-trivial compact subsector and show \
that it\ncorresponds to an integrable spin-chain Hamiltonian. This provides \
the first\ndirect evidence of integrability on the CFT$_2$ side of the \
correspondence.\n", 
