            "  We compute the one-loop worldsheet S-matrix for the \
superstring in AdS(3) x\nS(3) x T(4) supported by a combination of RR and \
NSNS flux in the massive\nsector. In the appropriate regularization scheme it \
agrees with the S-matrix\nfound from symmetry considerations including the \
proposed dressing phases. As\npreviously observed in other cases the massless \
modes decouple from the\ncalculation of one-loop massive mode scattering. We \
also calculate the\ncorrection to the dispersion relation at two loops in the \
Near-Flat-Space limit\nand find agreement with a proposal for the form of the \
exact dispersion\nrelation for the massive modes. Somewhat surprisingly the \
massless modes again\ndecouple from the calculation (in a suitable \
regularization scheme). We also\ncompute the correction to the dispersion \
relation for the massless modes and\ncompare to a suggestion for the exact \
dispersion relation, finding a small\ndiscrepancy. The corresponding \
calculations for AdS(5) x S(5) and AdS(2) x S(2)\nx T(6) are used for \
comparison.\n", 
