               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pulak Ranjan Giri\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Pulak Ranjan Giri, Tetsuo Deguchi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Singular eigenstates in the even(odd) length Heisenberg \
spin chain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages, 10 figures, accepted version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 48 175207 2015\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/48/17/175207\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the implications of the regularization for the \
singular solutions on\\nthe even(odd) length spin-1/2 XXX chains in some \
specific down-spin sectors. In\\nparticular, the analytic expressions of the \
Bethe eigenstates for three\\ndown-spin sector have been obtained along with \
their numerical forms in some\\nfixed length chains. For an even-length chain \
if the singular solutions\\n\\\\{\\\\lambda_\\\\alpha\\\\} are invariant \
under the sign changes of their \
rapidities\\n{\\\\lambda_\\\\alpha\\\\}=\\\\{-\\\\lambda_\\\\alpha\\\\} , \
then the Bethe ansatz equations are\\nreduced to a system of (M-2)/2 \
((M-3)/2) equations in an even (odd) down-spin\\nsector. For an odd N length \
chain in the three down-spin sector, it has been\\nanalytically shown that \
there exist singular solutions in any finite length of\\nthe spin chain of \
the form N= 3\\\\left(2k+1\\\\right) with k=1, 2, 3, \\\\cdots. It is\\nalso \
shown that there exist no singular solutions in the four down-spin \
sector\\nfor some odd-length spin-1/2 XXX chains.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
