         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1412.1288", "submitter" -> "Arsen Melikyan", "authors" -> 
            "A. Melikyan, E. Pereira and V. O. Rivelles", "title" -> 
            "On the equivalence theorem for integrable systems", "comments" -> 
            "27 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 48 (2015) 125204", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/48/12/125204", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate the equivalence theorem for integrable systems \
using two\nformulations of the Alday-Arutyunov-Frolov model. We show that the \
S-matrix is\ninvariant under the field transformation which reduces the \
non-linear Dirac\nbrackets of one formulation into the standard commutation \
relations in the\nsecond formulation. We also explain how to perform the \
direct diagonalization\nof the transformed Hamiltonian by constructing the \
states corresponding to\nself-adjoint extensions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
