 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the recent publication arXiv:1410.8860 the spin \
vertex was introduced as a\\nnew approach for computing three-point functions \
in N = 4 SYM. In this note we\\nconsider the BMN limit of the spin vertex for \
scalar excitations and show that\\nit reproduces the string vertex in the \
light-cone string field theory which\\ndescribes the string interactions in \
the pp-wave background at the leading\\norder of BMN expansion. This is \
achieved by introducing a polynomial\\nrepresentation for the spin vertex. We \
derive the Neumann coefficients from the\\nspin vertex at weak coupling and \
show they match with the Neumann coefficients\\nfrom the string field theory.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
