               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the first part of the paper, we discuss different \
versions of the AdS/CFT\\ndictionary out of equilibrium. We show that the \
Skenderis - van Rees\\nprescription and the \\\"extrapolate\\\" dictionary \
are equivalent at the level of\\n\\\"in-in\\\" two point functions of free \
scalar fields in arbitrary asymptotically\\nAdS spacetimes. In the second \
part of the paper, we calculate two point\\ncorrelation functions in \
dynamical spacetimes using the \\\"extrapolate\\\"\\ndictionary. These \
calculations are performed for conformally coupled scalar\\nfields in \
examples of spacetimes undergoing gravitational collapse, \
the\\nAdS$_2$-Vaidya spacetime and the AdS$_3$-Vaidya spacetime, which allow \
us to\\naddress the problem of thermalization following a quench in the \
boundary field\\ntheory. The computation of the correlators is formulated as \
an initial value\\nproblem in the bulk spacetime. Finally, we compare our \
results for\\nAdS$_3$-Vaidya to results in the previous literature obtained \
using the\\ngeodesic approximation and we find qualitative \
agreement.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
