         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1412.2806", "submitter" -> "Philipp Kleinert", "authors" -> 
            "Ville Keranen, Philipp Kleinert", "title" -> 
            "Non-equilibrium scalar two point functions in AdS/CFT", 
            "comments" -> 
            "41 pages, 13 figures; v2: added section 6.5 & references", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1504 (2015) 119", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP04(2015)119", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In the first part of the paper, we discuss different versions \
of the AdS/CFT\ndictionary out of equilibrium. We show that the Skenderis - \
van Rees\nprescription and the \"extrapolate\" dictionary are equivalent at \
the level of\n\"in-in\" two point functions of free scalar fields in \
arbitrary asymptotically\nAdS spacetimes. In the second part of the paper, we \
calculate two point\ncorrelation functions in dynamical spacetimes using the \
\"extrapolate\"\ndictionary. These calculations are performed for conformally \
coupled scalar\nfields in examples of spacetimes undergoing gravitational \
collapse, the\nAdS$_2$-Vaidya spacetime and the AdS$_3$-Vaidya spacetime, \
which allow us to\naddress the problem of thermalization following a quench \
in the boundary field\ntheory. The computation of the correlators is \
formulated as an initial value\nproblem in the bulk spacetime. Finally, we \
compare our results for\nAdS$_3$-Vaidya to results in the previous literature \
obtained using the\ngeodesic approximation and we find qualitative agreement.\
\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 8 Dec 2014 22:46:54 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 24 Feb 2015 19:36:51 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
