          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1412.3339\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rouven Frassek\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rouven Frassek\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Q-operators, Yangian invariance and the quantum inverse \
scattering\\n  method\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"212 pages, PhD thesis based on the author's \
publications\\n  arXiv:1010.3699, arXiv:1012.6021, arXiv:1112.3600, \
arXiv:1207.4513 and\\n  arXiv:1312.1693\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Inspired by the integrable structures appearing in \
weakly coupled planar N=4\\nsuper Yang-Mills theory, we study Q-operators and \
Yangian invariants of\\nrational integrable spin chains. We review the \
quantum inverse scattering\\nmethod along with the Yang-Baxter equation which \
is the key relation in this\\nsystematic approach to study integrable models. \
Our main interest concerns\\nrational integrable spin chains and lattice \
models. We recall the relation\\namong them and how they can be solved using \
Bethe ansatz methods incorporating\\nso-called Q-functions. In order to \
remind the reader how the Yangian emerges in\\nthis context, an overview of \
its so-called RTT-realization is provided. The\\nmain part is based on the \
author's original publications. Firstly, we construct\\nQ-operators whose \
eigenvalues yield the Q-functions for rational homogeneous\\nspin chains. The \
Q-operators are introduced as traces over certain monodromies\\nof \
R-operators. Our construction allows us to derive the hierarchy of \
commuting\\nQ-operators and the functional relations among them. We study how \
the\\nnearest-neighbor Hamiltonian and in principle also higher local charges \
can be\\nextracted from the Q-operators directly. Secondly, we formulate the \
Yangian\\ninvariance condition, also studied in relation to scattering \
amplitudes of N=4\\nsuper Yang-Mills theory, in the RTT-realization. We find \
that Yangian\\ninvariants can be interpreted as special eigenvectors of \
certain inhomogeneous\\nspin chains. This allows us to apply the algebraic \
Bethe ansatz and derive the\\ncorresponding Bethe equations that are relevant \
to construct the invariants. We\\nexamine the connection between the Yangian \
invariant spin chain eigenstates\\nwhose components can be understood as \
partition functions of certain 2d lattice\\nmodels and tree-level scattering \
amplitudes of the four-dimensional gauge\\ntheory. Finally, we conclude and \
discuss some future directions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 10 Dec 2014 15:27:13 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2014-12-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Frassek\"", ",", "\"Rouven\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1412.3339", "submitter" -> "Rouven Frassek", "authors" -> 
            "Rouven Frassek", "title" -> 
            "Q-operators, Yangian invariance and the quantum inverse \
scattering\n  method", "comments" -> 
            "212 pages, PhD thesis based on the author's publications\n  \
arXiv:1010.3699, arXiv:1012.6021, arXiv:1112.3600, arXiv:1207.4513 and\n  \
arXiv:1312.1693", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Inspired by the integrable structures appearing in weakly \
coupled planar N=4\nsuper Yang-Mills theory, we study Q-operators and Yangian \
invariants of\nrational integrable spin chains. We review the quantum inverse \
scattering\nmethod along with the Yang-Baxter equation which is the key \
relation in this\nsystematic approach to study integrable models. Our main \
interest concerns\nrational integrable spin chains and lattice models. We \
recall the relation\namong them and how they can be solved using Bethe ansatz \
methods incorporating\nso-called Q-functions. In order to remind the reader \
how the Yangian emerges in\nthis context, an overview of its so-called \
RTT-realization is provided. The\nmain part is based on the author's original \
publications. Firstly, we construct\nQ-operators whose eigenvalues yield the \
Q-functions for rational homogeneous\nspin chains. The Q-operators are \
introduced as traces over certain monodromies\nof R-operators. Our \
construction allows us to derive the hierarchy of commuting\nQ-operators and \
the functional relations among them. We study how the\nnearest-neighbor \
Hamiltonian and in principle also higher local charges can be\nextracted from \
the Q-operators directly. Secondly, we formulate the Yangian\ninvariance \
condition, also studied in relation to scattering amplitudes of N=4\nsuper \
Yang-Mills theory, in the RTT-realization. We find that Yangian\ninvariants \
can be interpreted as special eigenvectors of certain inhomogeneous\nspin \
chains. This allows us to apply the algebraic Bethe ansatz and derive the\n\
corresponding Bethe equations that are relevant to construct the invariants. \
We\nexamine the connection between the Yangian invariant spin chain \
eigenstates\nwhose components can be understood as partition functions of \
certain 2d lattice\nmodels and tree-level scattering amplitudes of the \
four-dimensional gauge\ntheory. Finally, we conclude and discuss some future \
directions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 10 Dec 2014 15:27:13 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-12-11", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Frassek", "Rouven", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
