 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Monte Carlo simulation results for unitary matrix \
quantum mechanics,\\ndescribing two-dimensional Yang-Mills theory coupled to \
a finite density of\\nnon-dynamical quarks (adjoint Coulomb gas), are \
presented. We characterize the\\ndeconfining transition in this model, by \
measuring the Polyakov Loop\\nSusceptibility and employing finite-size \
scaling analysis. We provide evidence\\nthat the phase transition is \
first-order. Our results are consistent with the\\noutcome of earlier \
large-$N$ studies of the model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
