               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrej Stepanchuk\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A. Stepanchuk\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"String theory in AdS_3 x S^3 x T^4 with mixed flux: \
semiclassical and\\n  1-loop phase in the S-matrix\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages. v2: references added, v3: extended introduction\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A48:195401,2015\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/48/19/195401\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-AS-2014-01\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a semiclassical derivation of the tree-level \
and 1-loop dressing\\nphases in the massive sector of string theory on AdS_3 \
x S^3 x T^4 supplemented\\nby R-R and NS-NS 3-form fluxes. In analogy with \
the AdS_5 x S^5 case, we use\\nthe dressing method to obtain scattering \
solutions for dyonic giant magnons\\nwhich allows us to determine the \
semiclassical bound-state S-matrix and its\\n1-loop correction. We also find \
that the 1-loop correction to the dyonic giant\\nmagnon energy vanishes. \
Looking at the relation between the bound-state picture\\nand elementary \
magnons in terms of the fusion procedure we deduce the\\nelementary dressing \
phases. In both the semiclassical and 1-loop cases we find\\nagreement with \
recent proposals from finite-gap equations and unitarity cut\\nmethods. \
Further, we find consistency with the finite-gap picture by\\ndetermining the \
resolvent for the dyonic giant magnon from the semiclassical\\nbosonic \
scattering data.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
