            "A. Stepanchuk", "title" -> 
            "String theory in AdS_3 x S^3 x T^4 with mixed flux: \
semiclassical and\n  1-loop phase in the S-matrix", "comments" -> 
            "28 pages. v2: references added, v3: extended introduction", 
            "journal-ref" -> "J.Phys.A48:195401,2015", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8113/48/19/195401", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AS-2014-01", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a semiclassical derivation of the tree-level and \
1-loop dressing\nphases in the massive sector of string theory on AdS_3 x S^3 \
x T^4 supplemented\nby R-R and NS-NS 3-form fluxes. In analogy with the AdS_5 \
x S^5 case, we use\nthe dressing method to obtain scattering solutions for \
dyonic giant magnons\nwhich allows us to determine the semiclassical \
bound-state S-matrix and its\n1-loop correction. We also find that the 1-loop \
correction to the dyonic giant\nmagnon energy vanishes. Looking at the \
relation between the bound-state picture\nand elementary magnons in terms of \
the fusion procedure we deduce the\nelementary dressing phases. In both the \
semiclassical and 1-loop cases we find\nagreement with recent proposals from \
finite-gap equations and unitarity cut\nmethods. Further, we find consistency \
with the finite-gap picture by\ndetermining the resolvent for the dyonic \
giant magnon from the semiclassical\nbosonic scattering data.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
