               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1412.5137\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Stijn van Tongeren\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gleb Arutyunov and Stijn J. van Tongeren\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Double Wick rotating Green-Schwarz strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2, updated discussion on target space interpretation, \
elaborated\\n  discussion on minor points, content matches published version, \
28 pages, 3\\n  figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1505 (2015) 027\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2015)027\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Via an appropriate field redefinition of the fermions, \
we find a set of\\nconditions under which light cone gauge fixed world sheet \
theories of strings\\non two different backgrounds are related by a double \
Wick rotation. These\\nconditions take the form of a set of transformation \
laws for the background\\nfields, complementing a set of transformation laws \
for the metric and B field\\nwe found previously with a set for the dilaton \
and RR fields, and are\\ncompatible with the supergravity equations of \
motion. Our results prove that at\\nleast to second order in fermions, the \
AdS_5 x S^5 mirror model which plays an\\nimportant role in the field of \
integrability in AdS/CFT, represents a string on\\n`mirror AdS_5 x S^5', the \
background that follows from our transformations. We\\ndiscuss analogous \
solutions for AdS_3 x S^3 x T^4 and AdS_2 x S^2 x T^6. The\\nmain ingredient \
in our derivation is the light cone gauge fixed action for a\\nstring on an \
(almost) completely generic background, which we explicitly derive\\nto \
second order in fermions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 16 Dec 2014 19:46:18 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 5 May 2015 13:51:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-06-19\""}]}, {
