            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Via an appropriate field redefinition of the fermions, we find \
a set of\nconditions under which light cone gauge fixed world sheet theories \
of strings\non two different backgrounds are related by a double Wick \
rotation. These\nconditions take the form of a set of transformation laws for \
the background\nfields, complementing a set of transformation laws for the \
metric and B field\nwe found previously with a set for the dilaton and RR \
fields, and are\ncompatible with the supergravity equations of motion. Our \
results prove that at\nleast to second order in fermions, the AdS_5 x S^5 \
mirror model which plays an\nimportant role in the field of integrability in \
AdS/CFT, represents a string on\n`mirror AdS_5 x S^5', the background that \
follows from our transformations. We\ndiscuss analogous solutions for AdS_3 x \
S^3 x T^4 and AdS_2 x S^2 x T^6. The\nmain ingredient in our derivation is \
the light cone gauge fixed action for a\nstring on an (almost) completely \
generic background, which we explicitly derive\nto second order in fermions.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 16 Dec 2014 19:46:18 GMT"}, {
