directions of AdS3 x S3\nx S3 x S1, the massless sector cousins of su(2) and \
sl(2) sector spinning\nstrings. We describe these, and their vibrational \
modes, using the\nD(2,1;\\alpha)^2 algebraic curve. By exploiting a discrete \
symmetry of this\nstructure which reverses the direction of motion on the \
spheres, and alters the\nmasses of the fermionic modes s \\to 1-s, we find \
out how to treat the massless\nfermions which were previously missing from \
this formalism. We show that folded\nstrings behave as a special case of \
circular strings, in a sense which includes\ntheir mode frequencies, and we \
are able to recover this fact in the worldsheet\nformalism. We use these \
frequencies to calculate one-loop corrections to the\nenergy, with a version \
of the Beisert-Tseytlin resummation.\n", 
