 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We continue the rigged configurations analysis of the \
solutions to the Bethe\\nansatz equations for the spin-1/2 isotropic \
Heisenberg model. We analyze the\\nnon self-conjugate strings of Deguchi-Giri \
and the counter example for the\\nstring hypothesis discovered by \
Essler-Korepin-Schoutens. In both cases clear\\ndiscrete structures \
appear.\\n\""}]}, {
