               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1501.04202\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Amit Dekel\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Amit Dekel\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wilson Loops and Minimal Surfaces Beyond the Wavy \
Approximation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages, many figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NORDITA-2015-008\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study Euclidean Wilson loops at strong coupling \
using the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence, where the problem is mapped to finding \
the area of minimal\\nsurfaces in Hyperbolic space. We use a formalism \
introduced recently by\\nKruczenski to perturbatively compute the area \
corresponding to boundary\\ncontours which are deformations of the circle. \
Our perturbative expansion is\\ncarried to high orders compared with the wavy \
approximation and yields new\\nanalytic results. The regularized area is \
invariant under a one parameter\\nfamily of continuous deformations of the \
boundary contour which are not related\\nto the global symmetry of the \
problem. We show that this symmetry of the Wilson\\nloops breaks at weak \
coupling at an a priori unexpected order in the\\nperturbative expansion. We \
also study the corresponding Lax operator and\\nalgebraic curve for these \
solutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 17 Jan 2015 14:57:36 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-01-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
