, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The N=2* Super-Yang-Mills theory (SYM*) undergoes an \
infinite sequence of\\nlarge-N quantum phase transitions. We compute \
expectation values of Wilson\\nloops in k-symmetric and antisymmetric \
representations of the SU(N) gauge group\\nin this theory and show that the \
same phenomenon that causes the phase\\ntransitions at finite coupling leads \
to a non-analytic dependence of Wilson\\nloops on k/N when the coupling is \
strictly infinite, thus making the\\nhigher-representation Wilson loops ideal \
holographic probes of the non-trivial\\nphase structure of SYM*.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
