            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1502.05203\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rafael Hernandez\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Rafael Hernandez, Juan Miguel Nieto\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Elliptic solutions in the Neumann-Rosochatius system with \
mixed flux\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages. Latex. v2: Extended discussions, corrected \
misprints and\\n  added reference. Published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 91, 126006 (2015)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.91.126006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"  Closed strings spinning in AdS_3 x S^3 x T^4 with mixed \
R-R and NS-NS\\nthree-form fluxes are described by a deformation of the \
one-dimensional\\nNeumann-Rosochatius integrable system. In this article we \
find general\\nsolutions to this system that can be expressed in terms of \
elliptic functions.\\nWe consider closed strings rotating either in S^3 with \
two different angular\\nmomenta or in AdS_3 with one spin. In order to find \
the solutions we will need\\nto extend the Uhlenbeck integrals of motion of \
the Neumann-Rosochatius system\\nto include the contribution from the flux. \
In the limit of pure NS-NS flux,\\nwhere the problem can be described by a \
supersymmetric WZW model, we find exact\\nexpressions for the classical \
energy in terms of the spin and the angular\\nmomenta of the spinning string.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
