            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1503.00732\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Igor Shovkovy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Vladimir A. Miransky and Igor A. Shovkovy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum field theory in a magnetic field: From quantum \
chromodynamics to\\n  graphene and Dirac semimetals\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"244 pages, 49 figures; published in Physics Reports; \
typos corrected\\n  and refernces added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Physics Reports 576 (2015) 1-209\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/j.physrep.2015.02.003\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-ph cond-mat.str-el hep-th nucl-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A range of quantum field theoretical phenomena driven \
by external magnetic\\nfields and their applications in relativistic systems \
and quasirelativistic\\ncondensed matter ones, such as graphene and \
Dirac/Weyl semimetals, are\\nreviewed. We start by introducing the underlying \
physics of the magnetic\\ncatalysis. The dimensional reduction of the \
low-energy dynamics of relativistic\\nfermions in an external magnetic field \
is explained and its role in catalyzing\\nspontaneous symmetry breaking is \
emphasized. The general theoretical\\nconsideration is supplemented by the \
analysis of the magnetic catalysis in\\nquantum electrodynamics, \
chromodynamics and quasirelativistic models relevant\\nfor condensed matter \
physics. By generalizing the ideas of the magnetic\\ncatalysis to the case of \
nonzero density and temperature, we argue that other\\ninteresting phenomena \
take place. The chiral magnetic and chiral separation\\neffects are perhaps \
the most interesting among them. In addition to the general\\ndiscussion of \
the physics underlying chiral magnetic and separation effects, we\\nalso \
review their possible phenomenological implications in heavy-ion\\ncollisions \
and compact stars. We also discuss the application of the \
magnetic\\ncatalysis ideas for the description of the quantum Hall effect in \
monolayer and\\nbilayer graphene, and conclude that the generalized magnetic \
catalysis,\\nincluding both the magnetic catalysis condensates and the \
quantum Hall\\nferromagnetic ones, lies at the basis of this phenomenon. We \
also consider how\\nan external magnetic field affects the underlying physics \
in a class of\\nthree-dimensional quasirelativistic condensed matter systems, \
Dirac semimetals.\\nWhile at sufficiently low temperatures and zero density \
of charge carriers,\\nsuch semimetals are expected to reveal the regime of \
the magnetic catalysis,\\nthe regime of Weyl semimetals with chiral asymmetry \
is realized at nonzero\\ndensity...\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
