            "Physics Reports 576 (2015) 1-209", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physrep.2015.02.003", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-ph cond-mat.str-el hep-th nucl-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  A range of quantum field theoretical phenomena driven by \
external magnetic\nfields and their applications in relativistic systems and \
quasirelativistic\ncondensed matter ones, such as graphene and Dirac/Weyl \
semimetals, are\nreviewed. We start by introducing the underlying physics of \
the magnetic\ncatalysis. The dimensional reduction of the low-energy dynamics \
of relativistic\nfermions in an external magnetic field is explained and its \
role in catalyzing\nspontaneous symmetry breaking is emphasized. The general \
theoretical\nconsideration is supplemented by the analysis of the magnetic \
catalysis in\nquantum electrodynamics, chromodynamics and quasirelativistic \
models relevant\nfor condensed matter physics. By generalizing the ideas of \
the magnetic\ncatalysis to the case of nonzero density and temperature, we \
argue that other\ninteresting phenomena take place. The chiral magnetic and \
chiral separation\neffects are perhaps the most interesting among them. In \
addition to the general\ndiscussion of the physics underlying chiral magnetic \
and separation effects, we\nalso review their possible phenomenological \
implications in heavy-ion\ncollisions and compact stars. We also discuss the \
application of the magnetic\ncatalysis ideas for the description of the \
quantum Hall effect in monolayer and\nbilayer graphene, and conclude that the \
generalized magnetic catalysis,\nincluding both the magnetic catalysis \
condensates and the quantum Hall\nferromagnetic ones, lies at the basis of \
this phenomenon. We also consider how\nan external magnetic field affects the \
underlying physics in a class of\nthree-dimensional quasirelativistic \
condensed matter systems, Dirac semimetals.\nWhile at sufficiently low \
temperatures and zero density of charge carriers,\nsuch semimetals are \
expected to reveal the regime of the magnetic catalysis,\nthe regime of Weyl \
semimetals with chiral asymmetry is realized at nonzero\ndensity...\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 2 Mar 2015 21:00:21 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 10 Apr 2015 00:03:34 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-04-13", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Miransky", "Vladimir A.", ""}, {
              "Shovkovy", "Igor A.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
