                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Based on an extension of the holographic principle to \
superspace, we provide\\na strong-coupling description of smooth super Wilson \
loops in terms of minimal\\nsurfaces of the $AdS_5 \\\\times S^5$ \
superstring. We employ the classical\\nintegrability of the Green-Schwarz \
superstring on $AdS_5 \\\\times S^5$ to derive\\nthe superconformal and \
Yangian $Y[\\\\mathfrak{psu}(2,2|4)]$ Ward identities for\\nthe super Wilson \
loop, thus extending the strong coupling results obtained for\\nthe \
Maldacena-Wilson loop. In the course of the derivation, we determine \
the\\nminimal surface solution up to third order in an expansion close to the\
\\nconformal boundary.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
