            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1503.07883\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yasuyuki Hatsuda\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yasuyuki Hatsuda\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spectral zeta function and non-perturbative effects in \
ABJM Fermi-gas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages, 4 figures, v2: published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2015)086\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The exact partition function in ABJM theory on \
three-sphere can be regarded\\nas a canonical partition function of a \
non-interacting Fermi-gas with an\\nunconventional Hamiltonian. All the \
information on the partition function is\\nencoded in the discrete spectrum \
of this Hamiltonian. We explain how (quantum\\nmechanical) non-perturbative \
corrections in the Fermi-gas system appear from a\\nspectral consideration. \
Basic tools in our analysis are a Mellin-Barnes type\\nintegral \
representation and a spectral zeta function. From a consistency with\\nknown \
results, we conjecture that the spectral zeta function in the \
ABJM\\nFermi-gas has an infinite number of \\\"non-perturbative\\\" poles, \
which are\\ninvisible in the semi-classical expansion of the Planck constant. \
We observe\\nthat these poles indeed appear after summing up perturbative \
corrections. As a\\nconsequence, the perturbative resummation of the spectral \
zeta function causes\\nnon-perturbative corrections to the grand canonical \
partition function. We also\\npresent another example associated with a \
spectral problem in topological\\nstring theory. A conjectured \
non-perturbative free energy on the resolved\\nconifold is successfully \
reproduced in this framework.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 26 Mar 2015 20:04:01 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 4 Jun 2016 10:21:36 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
