                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this work, we systematically analyze higher \
derivative terms in the\\nsupersymmetric effective actions for three \
dimensional scalar field theories\\nusing $\\\\mathcal{N} =1$ superspace \
formalism. In these effective actions, we\\nshow that auxiliary fields do not \
propagate and their effective actions can be\\nexpressed in terms of the \
physical fields. So, the theory does not change its\\nfield content upon \
addition of higher derivative terms. We use derivative\\nexpansion to \
generate four, five and six dimensional terms for an interacting\\nscalar \
field theory with $\\\\mathcal{N} =1$ supersymmetry. We show that \
along\\nwith pure fermionic and bosonic terms, there are various five and six\
\\ndimensional topological terms that mix bosonic and fermionic fields. \
Finally,\\nwe use these results to obtain higher derivative topological terms \
in the\\neffective action for two M2-branes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
