            "Higher Derivative Terms in Three Dimensional Supersymmetric \
Theories", "comments" -> 
            "18 pages, 0 figures, Accepted for publication in JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1510: 002, 2015", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2015)002", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this work, we systematically analyze higher derivative \
terms in the\nsupersymmetric effective actions for three dimensional scalar \
field theories\nusing $\\mathcal{N} =1$ superspace formalism. In these \
effective actions, we\nshow that auxiliary fields do not propagate and their \
effective actions can be\nexpressed in terms of the physical fields. So, the \
theory does not change its\nfield content upon addition of higher derivative \
terms. We use derivative\nexpansion to generate four, five and six \
dimensional terms for an interacting\nscalar field theory with $\\mathcal{N} \
=1$ supersymmetry. We show that along\nwith pure fermionic and bosonic terms, \
there are various five and six\ndimensional topological terms that mix \
bosonic and fermionic fields. Finally,\nwe use these results to obtain higher \
derivative topological terms in the\neffective action for two M2-branes.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
