               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the Hamiltonian reduction and canonical \
quantization of a massive\\nAdS$_2$ superparticle realized on the coset \
OSP(1|2)/SO(1,1). The phase space\\nof the massive superparticle is \
represented as a coadjoint orbit of a timelike\\nelement of \
$\\\\mathfrak{osp}$(1|2). This orbit has a well defined \
symplectic\\nstructure and the OSP(1|2) symmetry is realized as the Poisson \
bracket algebra\\nof the Noether charges. We then construct canonical \
coordinates given by one\\nbosonic and one fermionic oscillator, whose \
quantization leads to the\\nHolstein-Primakoff type realization of \
$\\\\mathfrak{osp}$(1|2). We also perform a\\nsimilar analysis and discuss \
new features and inconsistencies in the massless\\ncase.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
