               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1504.05703\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold Steinacker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold C. Steinacker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Chiral low-energy physics from squashed branes in \
deformed ${\\\\cal N}=4$\\n  SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages, 5 figures. V2: improved discussion, refs added, \
published\\n  version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UWThPh-2015-7\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the low-energy physics which arises on \
stacks of squashed brane\\nsolutions of $SU(N)$ ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM, deformed \
by a cubic soft SUSY breaking\\npotential. A brane configuration is found \
which leads to a low-energy physics\\nsimilar to the standard model in the \
broken phase, assuming suitable VEV's of\\nthe scalar zero modes. Due to the \
triple self-intersection of the branes, the\\nmatter content includes that of \
the MSSM with precisely 3 generations and\\nright-handed neutrinos. No exotic \
quantum numbers arise, however there are\\nextra chiral superfields with the \
quantum numbers of the Higgs doublets, the\\n$W,Z$, $e_R$ and $u_R$, whose \
fate depends on the details of the rich Higgs\\nsector. The chiral low-energy \
sector is complemented by a heavy mirror sector\\nwith the opposite \
chiralities, as well as super-massive Kaluza-Klein towers\\ncompleting the ${\
\\\\cal N}=4$ multiplets. The sectors are protected by two gauged\\nglobal \
$U(1)$ symmetries.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
