         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1504.05703", "submitter" -> "Harold Steinacker", 
            "authors" -> "Harold C. Steinacker", "title" -> 
            "Chiral low-energy physics from squashed branes in deformed \
${\\cal N}=4$\n  SYM", "comments" -> 
            "33 pages, 5 figures. V2: improved discussion, refs added, \
published\n  version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "UWThPh-2015-7", "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss the low-energy physics which arises on stacks of \
squashed brane\nsolutions of $SU(N)$ ${\\cal N}=4$ SYM, deformed by a cubic \
soft SUSY breaking\npotential. A brane configuration is found which leads to \
a low-energy physics\nsimilar to the standard model in the broken phase, \
assuming suitable VEV's of\nthe scalar zero modes. Due to the triple \
self-intersection of the branes, the\nmatter content includes that of the \
MSSM with precisely 3 generations and\nright-handed neutrinos. No exotic \
quantum numbers arise, however there are\nextra chiral superfields with the \
quantum numbers of the Higgs doublets, the\n$W,Z$, $e_R$ and $u_R$, whose \
fate depends on the details of the rich Higgs\nsector. The chiral low-energy \
sector is complemented by a heavy mirror sector\nwith the opposite \
chiralities, as well as super-massive Kaluza-Klein towers\ncompleting the \
${\\cal N}=4$ multiplets. The sectors are protected by two gauged\nglobal \
$U(1)$ symmetries.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 22 Apr 2015 09:17:28 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 30 Oct 2015 19:08:57 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-11-02", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Steinacker", "Harold C.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
