               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"BPS Wilson loops in Minkowski spacetime and Euclidean \
space\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"V1, 19 pages, no figure; V2, 25 pages, typos corrected \
and proofs for\\n  general curves added thanks to the careful reading and \
valuable suggestions\\n  of the anonymous referee, version to appear in EPJC; \
V3, 25 pages, published\\n  version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Eur. Phys. J. C75 (2015) 606\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1140/epjc/s10052-015-3834-6\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give evidence that spacelike BPS Wilson loops do not \
exist in Minkowski\\nspacetime. We show that spacelike Wilson loops in \
Minkowski spacetime cannot\\npreserve any supersymmetries, in $d = 4$ \
$\\\\mathcal N = 4$ super Yang-Mills\\ntheory, $d = 3$ $\\\\mathcal N = 2$ \
super Chern-Simons-matter theory, and $d = 3$\\n$\\\\mathcal N = 6$ \
Aharony-Bergman-Jafferis-Maldacena theory. We not only show\\nthis using \
infinite straight lines and circles as examples, but also we give\\nproofs \
for general curves. We attribute this to the conflicts of \
reality\\nconditions of the spinors. However, spacelike Wilson loops do exist \
in\\nEuclidean space. There are both BPS Wilson loops along infinite straight \
lines\\nand circular BPS Wilson loops. This is because the reality conditions \
of the\\nspinors are lost after Wick rotation. The result is reasonable in \
view of the\\nAdS/CFT correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
