proofs for\n  general curves added thanks to the careful reading and valuable \
suggestions\n  of the anonymous referee, version to appear in EPJC; V3, 25 \
pages, published\n  version", "journal-ref" -> "Eur. Phys. J. C75 (2015) 606",
             "doi" -> "10.1140/epjc/s10052-015-3834-6", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We give evidence that spacelike BPS Wilson loops do not exist \
in Minkowski\nspacetime. We show that spacelike Wilson loops in Minkowski \
spacetime cannot\npreserve any supersymmetries, in $d = 4$ $\\mathcal N = 4$ \
super Yang-Mills\ntheory, $d = 3$ $\\mathcal N = 2$ super Chern-Simons-matter \
theory, and $d = 3$\n$\\mathcal N = 6$ Aharony-Bergman-Jafferis-Maldacena \
theory. We not only show\nthis using infinite straight lines and circles as \
examples, but also we give\nproofs for general curves. We attribute this to \
the conflicts of reality\nconditions of the spinors. However, spacelike \
Wilson loops do exist in\nEuclidean space. There are both BPS Wilson loops \
along infinite straight lines\nand circular BPS Wilson loops. This is because \
the reality conditions of the\nspinors are lost after Wick rotation. The \
result is reasonable in view of the\nAdS/CFT correspondence.\n", 
