                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a detailed study of the Entanglement Entropy \
for the confining\\nKlebanov-Strassler background coupled to a large number \
of dynamical flavors in\\nthe Veneziano limit. As we vary the number of the \
massless flavors the behavior\\nof the entropy strongly depends on the way we \
fix the integration constant of\\nthe warp factor, that is related to the \
glueball scale. In the case of massive\\nflavors, the mass of the flavor \
branes introduces another scale in the\\nbackground and the entropy undergoes \
two first order phase transitions. The\\ncompetition between the glueball and \
the quark scales will lead to a critical\\npoint where one of the phase \
transitions degenerates to a second order one. We\\nhave calculated the \
critical exponents and have found that they are independent\\nof the number \
of flavors and different from the mean filed theory expectations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 6 May 2015 18:46:09 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
