dynamical flavors in\nthe Veneziano limit. As we vary the number of the \
massless flavors the behavior\nof the entropy strongly depends on the way we \
fix the integration constant of\nthe warp factor, that is related to the \
glueball scale. In the case of massive\nflavors, the mass of the flavor \
branes introduces another scale in the\nbackground and the entropy undergoes \
two first order phase transitions. The\ncompetition between the glueball and \
