 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We classify all N=2 rigid supersymmetric backgrounds in \
four dimensions with\\nboth Lorentzian and Euclidean signature that preserve \
eight real supercharges,\\nup to discrete identifications. Among the \
backgrounds we find specific warpings\\nof S^3 x R and AdS_3 x R, AdS_2 x S^2 \
and H^2 x S^2 with generic radii, and\\nsome more exotic geometries. We \
provide the generic two-derivative rigid vector\\nand hypermultiplet actions \
and analyze the conditions imposed on the special\\nKahler and hyperkahler \
target spaces.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
