               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1505.03525\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On integrability of strings on symmetric spaces\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"34 pages; v3: Minor clarifications, matches published \
version; v4:\\n  Missing local Lorentz transformation added in eqs. (2.14), \
(2.15) and (4.64)\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2015)115\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-LW-2015-01\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the absence of NSNS three-form flux the bosonic \
string on a symmetric\\nspace is described by a symmetric space coset \
sigma-model. Such models are\\nknown to be classically integrable. We show \
that the integrability extends also\\nto cases with non-zero NSNS flux \
(respecting the isometries) provided that the\\nflux satisfies a condition of \
the form H_{abc}H^{cde}~R_{ab}^{de}. We then turn\\nour attention to the type \
II Green-Schwarz superstring on a symmetric space. We\\nprove that if the \
space preserves some supersymmetry there exists a truncation\\nof the full \
superspace to a supercoset space and derive the general form of \
the\\nsuperisometry algebra. In the case of vanishing NSNS flux the \
corresponding\\nsupercoset sigma-model for the string is known to be \
integrable. We prove that\\nthe integrability extends to the full string by \
augmenting the supercoset Lax\\nconnection with terms involving the fermions \
which are not captured by the\\nsupercoset model. The construction is carried \
out to quadratic order in these\\nfermions. This proves the integrability of \
strings on symmetric spaces\\nsupported by RR flux which preserve any \
non-zero amount of supersymmetry.\\nFinally we also construct Lax connections \
for some supercoset models with\\nnon-zero NSNS flux describing strings in \
AdS(2,3) x S(2,3) x S(2,3) x T(2,3,4)\\nbackgrounds preserving eight \
supersymmetries.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 13 May 2015 20:00:46 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 21 May 2015 13:11:52 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
