           "id" -> "1505.03525", "submitter" -> "Linus Wulff", "authors" -> 
            "Linus Wulff", "title" -> 
            "On integrability of strings on symmetric spaces", "comments" -> 
            "34 pages; v3: Minor clarifications, matches published version; \
v4:\n  Missing local Lorentz transformation added in eqs. (2.14), (2.15) and \
(4.64)", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP09(2015)115", 
            "report-no" -> "Imperial-TP-LW-2015-01", "categories" -> "hep-th",
             "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In the absence of NSNS three-form flux the bosonic string on a \
symmetric\nspace is described by a symmetric space coset sigma-model. Such \
models are\nknown to be classically integrable. We show that the \
integrability extends also\nto cases with non-zero NSNS flux (respecting the \
isometries) provided that the\nflux satisfies a condition of the form \
H_{abc}H^{cde}~R_{ab}^{de}. We then turn\nour attention to the type II \
Green-Schwarz superstring on a symmetric space. We\nprove that if the space \
preserves some supersymmetry there exists a truncation\nof the full \
superspace to a supercoset space and derive the general form of the\n\
superisometry algebra. In the case of vanishing NSNS flux the corresponding\n\
supercoset sigma-model for the string is known to be integrable. We prove \
that\nthe integrability extends to the full string by augmenting the \
supercoset Lax\nconnection with terms involving the fermions which are not \
captured by the\nsupercoset model. The construction is carried out to \
quadratic order in these\nfermions. This proves the integrability of strings \
on symmetric spaces\nsupported by RR flux which preserve any non-zero amount \
of supersymmetry.\nFinally we also construct Lax connections for some \
supercoset models with\nnon-zero NSNS flux describing strings in AdS(2,3) x \
S(2,3) x S(2,3) x T(2,3,4)\nbackgrounds preserving eight supersymmetries.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 13 May 2015 20:00:46 GMT"}, {
