               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1505.03850\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Thomas T. Dumitrescu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Clay Cordova, Thomas T. Dumitrescu, Xi Yin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Higher Derivative Terms, Toroidal Compactification, and \
Weyl Anomalies\\n  in Six-Dimensional (2,0) Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"48 pages + appendix, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We systematically analyze the effective action on the \
moduli space of (2,0)\\nsuperconformal field theories in six dimensions, as \
well as their toroidal\\ncompactification to maximally supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theories in five and\\nfour dimensions. We present a streamlined \
approach to non-renormalization\\ntheorems that constrain this effective \
action. The first several orders in its\\nderivative expansion are determined \
by a one-loop calculation in\\nfive-dimensional Yang-Mills theory. This fixes \
the leading higher-derivative\\noperators that describe the renormalization \
group flow into theories residing\\nat singular points on the moduli space of \
the compactified (2,0) theories. This\\nunderstanding allows us to compute \
the a-type Weyl anomaly for all (2,0)\\nsuperconformal theories. We show that \
it decreases along every renormalization\\ngroup flow that preserves (2,0) \
supersymmetry, thereby establishing the\\na-theorem for this class of \
theories. Along the way, we encounter various\\nfield-theoretic arguments for \
the ADE classification of (2,0) theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 14 May 2015 19:44:16 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-05-15\""}]}, {
