            "  We systematically analyze the effective action on the moduli \
space of (2,0)\nsuperconformal field theories in six dimensions, as well as \
their toroidal\ncompactification to maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills \
theories in five and\nfour dimensions. We present a streamlined approach to \
non-renormalization\ntheorems that constrain this effective action. The first \
several orders in its\nderivative expansion are determined by a one-loop \
calculation in\nfive-dimensional Yang-Mills theory. This fixes the leading \
higher-derivative\noperators that describe the renormalization group flow \
into theories residing\nat singular points on the moduli space of the \
compactified (2,0) theories. This\nunderstanding allows us to compute the \
a-type Weyl anomaly for all (2,0)\nsuperconformal theories. We show that it \
decreases along every renormalization\ngroup flow that preserves (2,0) \
supersymmetry, thereby establishing the\na-theorem for this class of \
theories. Along the way, we encounter various\nfield-theoretic arguments for \
the ADE classification of (2,0) theories.\n", 
