               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Logarithmic Corrections to the Entanglement \
Entropy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, reference added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 92, 126013 (2015)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.92.126013\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In a $d$-dimensional conformal field theory, it has \
been known that a\\nrelevant deformation operator with the conformal \
dimension,\\n$\\\\Delta=\\\\frac{d+2}{2}$, generates a logarithmic correction \
to the entanglement\\nentropy. In the large 't Hooft coupling limit, we can \
investigate such a\\nlogarithmic correction holographically by deforming an \
AdS space with a massive\\nscalar field dual to the operator with $\\\\Delta=\
\\\\frac{d+2}{2}$. There are two\\nsources generating the logarithmic \
correction. One is the metric deformation\\nand the other is the minimal \
surface deformation. In this work, we investigate\\nthe change of the \
entanglement entropy caused by the minimal surface\\ndeformation and find \
that the second order minimal surface deformation leads to\\nan additional \
logarithmic correction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
