               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mattias Blennow, Juan Herrero-Garcia, Thomas Schwetz and \
Stefan Vogl\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Halo-independent tests of dark matter direct detection \
signals: local DM\\n  density, LHC, and thermal freeze-out\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"23 pages, 6 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2015/08/039\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  From an assumed signal in a Dark Matter (DM) direct \
detection experiment a\\nlower bound on the product of the DM--nucleon \
scattering cross section and the\\nlocal DM density is derived, which is \
independent of the local DM velocity\\ndistribution. This can be combined \
with astrophysical determinations of the\\nlocal DM density. Within a given \
particle physics model the bound also allows a\\nrobust comparison of a \
direct detection signal with limits from the LHC.\\nFurthermore, the bound \
can be used to formulate a condition which has to be\\nfulfilled if the \
particle responsible for the direct detection signal is a\\nthermal relic, \
regardless of whether it constitutes all DM or only part of it.\\nWe \
illustrate the arguments by adopting a simplified DM model with a \
Z'\\nmediator and assuming a signal in a future xenon direct detection \
experiment.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
