            "  We introduce a non-perturbative framework for computing \
structure constants\nof single-trace operators in the N=4 SYM theory at large \
N. Our approach\nfeatures new vertices, with hexagonal shape, that can be \
patched together into\nthree- and possibly higher-point correlators. These \
newborn hexagons are more\nelementary and easier to deal with than the \
three-point functions. Moreover,\nthey can be entirely constructed using \
integrability, by means of a suitable\nbootstrap program. In this letter, we \
present our main results and conjectures\nfor these vertices, and match their \
predictions for the three-point functions\nwith both weak and strong coupling \
data available in the literature.\n", 
