                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate type IIB strings on $\\\\mathrm{AdS}_3\\\
\\times \\\\mathrm{S}^3\\\\times\\n\\\\mathrm{S}^3\\\\times\\\\mathrm{S}^1$ \
with mixed Ramond-Ramond (R-R) and\\nNeveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz (NS-NS) \
flux. By suitably gauge-fixing the closed\\nstring Green-Schwarz (GS) action \
of this theory, we derive the off-shell\\nsymmetry algebra and its \
representations. We use these to determine the\\nnon-perturbative worldsheet \
S-matrix of fundamental excitations in the theory.\\nThe analysis involves \
both massive and massless modes in complete generality.\\nThe S-matrix we \
find involves a number of phase factors, which in turn satisfy\\ncrossing \
equations that we also determine. We comment on the nature of the\\nheaviest \
modes of the theory, but leave their identification either as\\ncomposites or \
bound-states to a future investigation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
