 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We describe a one-parameter family of new holographic \
RG flows that start\\nfrom $AdS_4 \\\\times S^7$ and go to \
$\\\\widehat{AdS_5} \\\\times {\\\\cal B}_6$, where\\n${\\\\cal B}_6$ is \
conformal to a K\\\\\\\"ahler manifold and $\\\\widehat{AdS_5}$ \
is\\nPoincar\\\\'e $AdS_5$ with one spatial direction compactified and \
fibered over\\n${\\\\cal B}_6$. The new solutions \\\"flow up dimensions,\\\" \
going from the\\n$(2+1)$-dimensional conformal field theory on M2 branes in \
the UV to a\\n$(3+1)$-dimensional field theory on intersecting M5 branes in \
the infra-red.\\nThe M2 branes completely polarize into M5 branes along the \
flow and the\\nPoincar\\\\'e sections of the $\\\\widehat{AdS_5}$ are the \
$(3+1)$-dimensional common\\nintersection of the M5 branes. The emergence of \
the extra dimension in the\\ninfra-red suggests a new strongly-coupled phase \
of the M2 brane and ABJM\\ntheories in which charged solitons are becoming \
massless. The flow solution is\\nfirst analyzed by finding a four-dimensional \
$N \\\\! = \\\\! 2$ supersymmetric flow\\nin $N \\\\! = \\\\! 8$ gauged \
supergravity. This is then generalized to a one\\nparameter family of \
non-supersymmetric flows. The infra-red limit of the\\nsolutions appears to \
be quite singular in four dimensions but the uplift to\\neleven-dimensional \
supergravity is remarkable and regular (up to orbifolding).\\nOur \
construction is a non-trivial application of the recently derived \
uplift\\nformulae for fluxes, going well beyond the earlier constructions of \
stationary\\npoints solutions. The eleven-dimensional supersymmetry is also \
analyzed and\\nshows how, for the supersymmetric flow, the M2-brane \
supersymmetry in the UV is\\npolarized entirely into M5-brane supersymmetry \
in the infra-red.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
