            "  We study the cusped Wilson line operators and Bremsstrahlung \
functions\nassociated to particles transforming in the rank-$k$ symmetric \
representation\nof the gauge group $U(N)$ for ${\\cal N} = 4$ super \
Yang-Mills. We find the\nholographic D3-brane description for Wilson loops \
with internal cusps in two\ndifferent limits: small cusp angle and \
$k\\sqrt{\\lambda}\\gg N$. This allows for\na non-trivial check of a \
conjectured relation between the Bremsstrahlung\nfunction and the expectation \
value of the 1/2 BPS circular loop in the case of\na representation other \
than the fundamental. Moreover, we observe that in the\nlimit of $k\\gg N$, \
the cusped Wilson line expectation value is simply given by\nthe exponential \
of the 1-loop diagram. Using group theory arguments, this\neikonal \
exponentiation is conjectured to take place for all Wilson loop\noperators in \
symmetric representations with large $k$, independently of the\ncontour on \
which they are supported.\n", 
