for dualities.\nWilson loops are labeled by a representation of the gauge \
group and should map\nunder duality to loop operators labeled by the same \
data, yet generically, dual\ntheories have completely different gauge groups. \
In this paper we resolve this\nconundrum for three dimensional mirror \
symmetry. We show that Wilson loops are\nexchanged under mirror symmetry with \
Vortex loop operators, whose microscopic\ndefinition in terms of a \
supersymmetric quantum mechanics coupled to the theory\nencode in a \
