 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In work arXiv:1204.2788, a surface embedded in flat \
$R^3$ is associated to\\nany three hermitian matrices. We study this emergent \
surface when the matrices\\nare large, by constructing coherent states \
corresponding to points in the\\nemergent geometry. We find the original \
matrices determine not only shape of\\nthe emergent surface, but also a \
unique Poisson structure. We prove that\\ncommutators of matrix operators \
correspond to Poisson brackets. Through our\\nconstruction, we can realize \
arbitrary noncommutative membranes: for example,\\nwe examine a round sphere \
with a non-spherically symmetric Poisson structure.\\nWe also give a natural \
construction for a noncommutative torus embedded in\\n$R^3$. Finally, we make \
remarks about area and find matrix equations for\\nminimal area \
surfaces.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
