         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1506.02035", "submitter" -> "Joanna L. Karczmarek", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Mathias Hudoba de Badyn, Joanna L. Karczmarek, Philippe\n  \
Sabella-Garnier and Ken Huai-Che Yeh", "title" -> 
            "Emergent geometry of membranes", "comments" -> 
            "34 pages, 7 figures. v2: added references", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In work arXiv:1204.2788, a surface embedded in flat $R^3$ is \
associated to\nany three hermitian matrices. We study this emergent surface \
when the matrices\nare large, by constructing coherent states corresponding \
to points in the\nemergent geometry. We find the original matrices determine \
not only shape of\nthe emergent surface, but also a unique Poisson structure. \
We prove that\ncommutators of matrix operators correspond to Poisson \
brackets. Through our\nconstruction, we can realize arbitrary noncommutative \
membranes: for example,\nwe examine a round sphere with a non-spherically \
symmetric Poisson structure.\nWe also give a natural construction for a \
noncommutative torus embedded in\n$R^3$. Finally, we make remarks about area \
and find matrix equations for\nminimal area surfaces.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 5 Jun 2015 20:00:32 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 26 Jun 2015 20:30:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
