            "  As a step toward uncovering the relation between the weak and \
the strong\ncoupling regimes of the $\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills theory \
beyond the\nspecral level, we have developed in a previous paper \
[arXiv:1410.8533] a novel\ngroup theoretic interpretation of the Wick \
contraction of the fields, which\nallowed us to compute a much more general \
class of three-point functions in the\nSU(2) sector, as in the case of strong \
coupling [arXiv:1312.3727], directly in\nterms of the determinant \
representation of the partial domain wall partition\nfunciton. Furthermore, \
we derived a non-trivial identity for the three point\nfunctions with \
monodromy operators inserted, being the discrete counterpart of\nthe global \
monodromy condition which played such a crucial role in the\ncomputation at \
strong coupling. In this companion paper, we shall extend our\nstudy to the \
entire ${\\rm psu}(2,2|4)$ sector and obtain several important\n\
generalizations. They include in particular (i) the manifestly conformally\n\
covariant construction, from the basic principle, of the singlet-projection\n\
operator for performing the Wick contraction and (ii) the derivation of the\n\
monodromy relation for the case of the so-called \"harmonic R-matrix\", as \
well\nas for the usual fundamental R-matrtix. The former case, which is new \
and has\nfeatures rather different from the latter, is expected to have \
important\napplications. We also describe how the form of the monodromy \
relation is\nmodified as ${\\rm psu}(2,2|4)$ is reduced to its subsectors.\n",
