               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Mutual information is used as a purely geometrical \
regularization of\\nentanglement entropy applicable to any QFT. A coefficient \
in the mutual\\ninformation between concentric circular entangling surfaces \
gives a precise\\nuniversal prescription for the monotonous quantity in the \
c-theorem for d=3.\\nThis is in principle computable using any regularization \
for the entropy, and\\nin particular is a definition suitable for lattice \
models. We rederive the\\nproof of the c-theorem for d=3 in terms of mutual \
information, and check our\\narguments with holographic entanglement entropy, \
a free scalar field, and an\\nextensive mutual information model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
