            "Universal Features of Four-Dimensional Superconformal Field \
Theory on\n  Conic Space", "comments" -> "1+32 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 1508:052,2015", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2015)052", 
            "report-no" -> "TAUP-2996/15", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Following the set up in arXiv:1408.3393, we study 4d N=1 \
superconformal field\ntheories in conic spaces. We show that the universal \
part of supersymmetric\nR\\'enyi entropy S_q across a spherical entangling \
surface in the limit q goes\nto 0 is proportional to a linear combination of \
central charges, 3c-2a. This is\nequivalent to a similar statement about the \
free energy of SCFTs on conic space\nor hyperbolic space S^1_q*H^3 in the \
corresponding limit. We first derive the\nasymptotic formula by the free \
field computation in the presence of a U(1)\nR-symmetry background and then \
provide an independent derivation by studying\nN=1 theories on a primary Hopf \
surface S^1_\\beta*S^3_b with a particular\nscaling \\beta~1/\\sqrt{q} and b=\
\\sqrt{q}, which thus confirms the validity of\nthe formula for general \
interacting N=1 SCFTs. Finally we revisit the\nsupersymmetric R\\'enyi \
entropy of general N=2 SCFTs and find a simple formula\nfor it in terms of \
central charges a and c.\n", 
