               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Michael Cooke\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Michael Cooke, Nadav Drukker, Diego Trancanelli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A profusion of $1/2$ BPS Wilson loops in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$\\n  Chern-Simons-matter theories\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"40 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1510 (2015) 140\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2015)140\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We initiate the study of $1/2$ BPS Wilson loops in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$\\nChern-Simons-matter theories in three dimensions. We \
consider a circular or\\nlinear quiver with Chern-Simons levels $k$, $-k$ and \
$0$, and focus on loops\\npreserving one of the two $SU(2)$ subgroups of the \
$R$-symmetry. In the cases\\nwith no vanishing Chern-Simons levels, we find a \
pair of Wilson loops for each\\npair of adjacent nodes on the quiver \
connected by a hypermultiplet (nodes\\nconnected by twisted hypermultiplets \
have Wilson loops preserving another set\\nof supercharges). We expect this \
classical pairwise degeneracy to be lifted by\\nquantum corrections. In the \
case with nodes with vanishing Chern-Simons terms\\nconnected by twisted \
hypermultiplets, we find that the usual $1/4$ BPS Wilson\\nloops are \
automatically enlarged to $1/2$ BPS, as happens also in \
3-dimensional\\nYang-Mills theory. When the nodes with vanishing Chern-Simons \
levels are\\nconnected by untwisted hypermultiplets, we do not find any \
Wilson loops\\ncoupling to those nodes which are classically invariant. \
Rather, we find\\nseveral loops whose supersymmetry variation, while non \
zero, vanishes in any\\ncorrelation function, so is weakly zero. We expect \
only one linear combination\\nof those Wilson loops to remain BPS when \
quantum corrections are included. We\\nanalyze the M-theory duals of those \
Wilson loops and comment on their\\ndegeneracy. We also show that these \
Wilson loops are cohomologically equivalent\\nto certain $1/4$ BPS Wilson \
loops whose expectation value can be evaluated by\\nthe appropriate localized \
matrix model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
