                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Yunfeng Jiang, Shota Komatsu, Ivan Kostov and Didina \
Serban\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The hexagon in the mirror: the three-point function in \
the SoV\\n  representation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"37 pages, 10 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1751-8113/49/17/174007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive an integral expression for the leading-order \
type I-I-I three-point\\nfunctions in the $\\\\mathfrak{su}(2) $-sector of \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills\\ntheory, for which no determinant \
formula is known. To this end, we first map\\nthe problem to the partition \
function of the six vertex model with a hexagonal\\nboundary. The advantage \
of the six-vertex model expression is that it reveals\\nan extra symmetry of \
the problem, which is the invariance under 90$^{\\\\circ}$\\nrotation. On the \
spin-chain side, this corresponds to the exchange of the\\nquantum space and \
the auxiliary space and is reminiscent of the mirror\\ntransformation \
employed in the worldsheet S-matrix approaches. After the\\nrotation, we then \
apply Sklyanin's separation of variables (SoV) and obtain \
a\\nmultiple-integral expression of the three-point function. The \
resulting\\nintegrand is expressed in terms of the so-called Baxter \
polynomials, which is\\nclosely related to the quantum spectral curve \
approach. Along the way, we also\\nderive several new results about the SoV, \
such as the explicit construction of\\nthe basis with twisted boundary \
conditions and the overlap between the orginal\\nSoV state and the SoV states \
on the subchains.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
