I-I-I three-point\nfunctions in the $\\mathfrak{su}(2) $-sector of \
$\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills\ntheory, for which no determinant formula \
is known. To this end, we first map\nthe problem to the partition function of \
the six vertex model with a hexagonal\nboundary. The advantage of the \
six-vertex model expression is that it reveals\nan extra symmetry of the \
problem, which is the invariance under 90$^{\\circ}$\nrotation. On the \
spin-chain side, this corresponds to the exchange of the\nquantum space and \
the auxiliary space and is reminiscent of the mirror\ntransformation employed \
in the worldsheet S-matrix approaches. After the\nrotation, we then apply \
Sklyanin's separation of variables (SoV) and obtain a\nmultiple-integral \
expression of the three-point function. The resulting\nintegrand is expressed \
in terms of the so-called Baxter polynomials, which is\nclosely related to \
