           "id" -> "1507.01595", "submitter" -> "Eric Dzienkowski", "authors" -> 
            "Eric Dzienkowski", "title" -> 
            "Excited States of Open Strings From $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM", 
            "comments" -> "33 pages. Typos fixed", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP12(2015)036", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We continue the analysis of building open strings stretched \
between giant\ngravitons from $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM by going to second order \
in perturbation\ntheory using the three-loop dilatation generator from the \
field theory. In the\nprocess we build a Fock-like space of states using \
Cuntz oscillators which can\nbe used to access the excited open string \
states. We find a remarkable\ncancellation among the excited states that \
shows the ground state energy is\nconsistent with a fully relativistic \
dispersion relation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 6 Jul 2015 20:00:48 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 1 Sep 2015 16:15:06 GMT"}, {
