               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Euclidean Wilson loops and Minimal Area Surfaces in \
Minkowski AdS3\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages, 4 figures, LaTeX\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP12(2015)083\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The AdS/CFT correspondence relates Wilson loops in N=4 \
SYM theory to minimal\\narea surfaces in AdS5xS5 space. If the Wilson loop is \
Euclidean and confined to\\na plane (t,x) then the dual surface is Euclidean \
and lives in Minkowski AdS3.\\nIn this paper we study such minimal area \
surfaces generalizing previous results\\nobtained in the Euclidean case. \
Since the surfaces we consider have the\\ntopology of a disk, the holonomy of \
the flat current vanishes which is\\nequivalent to the condition that a \
certain boundary Schroedinger equation has\\nall its solutions anti-periodic. \
If the potential for that Schroedinger\\nequation is found then \
reconstructing the surface and finding the area become\\nsimpler. In \
particular we write a formula for the Area in terms of the\\nSchwarzian \
derivative of the contour. Finally an infinite parameter family \
of\\nanalytical solutions using Riemann Theta functions is described. In this \
case,\\nboth the area and the shape of the surface are given analytically and \
used to\\ncheck the previous results.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
