            "  The AdS/CFT correspondence relates Wilson loops in N=4 SYM \
theory to minimal\narea surfaces in AdS5xS5 space. If the Wilson loop is \
Euclidean and confined to\na plane (t,x) then the dual surface is Euclidean \
and lives in Minkowski AdS3.\nIn this paper we study such minimal area \
surfaces generalizing previous results\nobtained in the Euclidean case. Since \
the surfaces we consider have the\ntopology of a disk, the holonomy of the \
flat current vanishes which is\nequivalent to the condition that a certain \
boundary Schroedinger equation has\nall its solutions anti-periodic. If the \
potential for that Schroedinger\nequation is found then reconstructing the \
surface and finding the area become\nsimpler. In particular we write a \
formula for the Area in terms of the\nSchwarzian derivative of the contour. \
Finally an infinite parameter family of\nanalytical solutions using Riemann \
Theta functions is described. In this case,\nboth the area and the shape of \
the surface are given analytically and used to\ncheck the previous results.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
