               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1507.03005\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Heinze\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Heinze\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spectrum and Quantum Symmetries of the ${\\\\rm AdS}_5 \\\
\\times {\\\\rm S}^5$\\n  Superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"168 pages, PhD thesis of the author; v2: typos corrected, \
references\\n  updated\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The the duality between ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM and the \
AdS$_5\\\\times\\\\;$S$^5$\\nsuperstring appears to enjoy quantum \
integrability in the planar limit, which\\nallowed to devise powerful methods \
ostensibly solving the spectral problem.\\nHowever, quantization of the \
AdS$_5\\\\times\\\\;$S$^5$ superstring from first\\nprinciples is still an \
open question and especially the spectrum of short\\nstring states has \
previously been derived only at leading order in large 't\\nHooft coupling. \
In this thesis we investigate possible routes to take the\\nperturbative \
quantization of short string states beyond the leading order,\\nwhere equally \
our aim is to gain better appreciation of the quantum symmetries\\nat play. A \
prominent role is played by the lowest excited string states, dual\\nto the \
Konishi supermultiplet, and we start by reviewing critically an \
asserted\\nderivation of the Konishi anomalous dimension in the setup of pure \
spinor\\nstring theory. Next, we study the bosonic AdS$_5\\\\times\\\\;$S$^5$ \
string in static\\ngauge, where we construct a so-called single-mode string \
solution, which shows\\nclassical integrability and invariance under the \
isometries\\nSO(2,4)$\\\\;\\\\times\\\\;$SO(6) at the quantum level. Arguing \
heuristically about the\\neffects of supersymmetry, we indeed recover the \
first non-trivial quantum\\ncorrection to the Konishi anomalous dimension. We \
continue by implementing\\nstatic gauge for the full \
AdS$_5\\\\times\\\\;$S$^5$ superstring and find elegant\\nexpressions for the \
Lagrangian density and the supercharges. We then constrain\\nour interest to \
the superparticle and, using two different methods, find\\ncanonical \
coordinates at quadratic order in fermions. As the single-mode string\\nis \
just the SO(2,4)$\\\\;\\\\times\\\\;$SO(6) orbit of the pulsating string, we \
conclude\\nby applying orbit method quantization to the particle and spinning \
string\\nsolutions in bosonic AdS$_3\\\\times\\\\;$S$^3$ yielding consistent \
results for the\\nspectra.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 10 Jul 2015 19:50:45 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 7 Nov 2016 10:59:23 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
