           "id" -> "1507.03005", "submitter" -> "Martin Heinze", "authors" -> 
            "Martin Heinze", "title" -> 
            "Spectrum and Quantum Symmetries of the ${\\rm AdS}_5 \\times \
{\\rm S}^5$\n  Superstring", "comments" -> 
            "168 pages, PhD thesis of the author; v2: typos corrected, \
references\n  updated", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The the duality between ${\\cal N}=4$ SYM and the \
AdS$_5\\times\\;$S$^5$\nsuperstring appears to enjoy quantum integrability in \
the planar limit, which\nallowed to devise powerful methods ostensibly \
solving the spectral problem.\nHowever, quantization of the \
AdS$_5\\times\\;$S$^5$ superstring from first\nprinciples is still an open \
question and especially the spectrum of short\nstring states has previously \
been derived only at leading order in large 't\nHooft coupling. In this \
thesis we investigate possible routes to take the\nperturbative quantization \
of short string states beyond the leading order,\nwhere equally our aim is to \
gain better appreciation of the quantum symmetries\nat play. A prominent role \
is played by the lowest excited string states, dual\nto the Konishi \
supermultiplet, and we start by reviewing critically an asserted\nderivation \
of the Konishi anomalous dimension in the setup of pure spinor\nstring \
theory. Next, we study the bosonic AdS$_5\\times\\;$S$^5$ string in static\n\
gauge, where we construct a so-called single-mode string solution, which \
shows\nclassical integrability and invariance under the isometries\n\
SO(2,4)$\\;\\times\\;$SO(6) at the quantum level. Arguing heuristically about \
the\neffects of supersymmetry, we indeed recover the first non-trivial \
quantum\ncorrection to the Konishi anomalous dimension. We continue by \
implementing\nstatic gauge for the full AdS$_5\\times\\;$S$^5$ superstring \
and find elegant\nexpressions for the Lagrangian density and the \
supercharges. We then constrain\nour interest to the superparticle and, using \
two different methods, find\ncanonical coordinates at quadratic order in \
fermions. As the single-mode string\nis just the SO(2,4)$\\;\\times\\;$SO(6) \
orbit of the pulsating string, we conclude\nby applying orbit method \
quantization to the particle and spinning string\nsolutions in bosonic AdS$_3\
\\times\\;$S$^3$ yielding consistent results for the\nspectra.\n", 
