          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1507.03965", "submitter" -> "Donovan Young", "authors" -> 
            "Charlotte Kristjansen, Stefano Mori, and Donovan Young", "title" -> 
            "On the Regularization of Extremal Three-point Functions \
Involving Giant\n  Gravitons", "comments" -> 
            "5 pages, no figures. v2 updated references", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1016/j.physletb.2015.09.056", "report-no" -> 
            "QMUL-PH-15-15", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In the AdS_5/CFT_4 set-up, extremal three-point functions \
involving two giant\n1/2 BPS gravitons and one point-like 1/2 BPS graviton, \
when calculated using\nsemi-classical string theory methods, match the \
corresponding three-point\nfunctions obtained in the tree-level gauge theory. \
The string theory\ncomputation relies on a certain regularization procedure \
whose justification is\nbased on the match between gauge and string theory. \
We revisit the\nregularization procedure and reformulate it in a way which \
allows a\ngeneralization to the ABJM set-up where three-point functions of \
1/2 BPS\noperators are not protected and where a match between tree-level \
gauge theory\nand semi-classical string theory is hence not expected.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 14 Jul 2015 18:57:23 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 20 Jul 2015 13:37:04 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-10-28", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kristjansen", "Charlotte", ""}, {
              "Mori", "Stefano", ""}, {"Young", "Donovan", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
