                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate the one loop beta function for the \
would-be marginal coupling on\\nthe world sheet of the k deformed sigma \
models associated to a quantum group\\nwith q=exp(i pi/k). This includes the \
bosonic principal chiral models and\\nsymmetric space sigma models but also \
the k deformed semi-symmetric space sigma\\nmodel describing strings in a \
deformation of AdS_5 x S^5. The world sheet sigma\\nmodel is a \
current-current deformation of the gauged WZW model for the\\nsupergroup \
PSU(2,2|4) with level k. In the string theory context the beta\\nfunction is \
shown to vanish because of the vanishing of the Killing form of\\nPSU(2,2|4) \
which is another piece of evidence that the k deformed theories\\ndefine \
consistent string theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
