 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct BPS geometries describing normalizable \
excitations of AdS_2 x\\nS^2. All regular horizon-free solutions are \
parameterized by two harmonic\\nfunctions in R^3 with sources along closed \
curves. This local structure is\\nreminiscent of the \\\"bubbling solutions\\\
\" for the other AdS cases, however, due\\nto peculiar asymptotic properties \
of AdS_2, one copy of R^3 does not cover the\\nentire space, and we discuss \
the procedure for analytic continuation, which\\nleads to a nontrivial \
topological structure of the new geometries. We also\\nstudy supersymmetric \
brane probes on the new geometries, which represent the\\nAdS_2 x S^2 \
counterparts of the giant gravitons.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
