               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"J.-C. Wallet\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Antoine G\\\\'er\\\\'e, Tajron Juri\\\\'c, \
Jean-Christophe Wallet\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Noncommutative gauge theories on \
$\\\\mathbb{R}^3_\\\\lambda$: Perturbatively\\n  finite models\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"27 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP12 (2015) 045\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP12(2015)045\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"LPT-Orsay-15-56\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that natural noncommutative gauge theory models \
on\\n$\\\\mathbb{R}^3_\\\\lambda$ can accommodate gauge invariant harmonic \
terms, thanks\\nto the existence of a relationship between the center of \
$\\\\mathbb{R}^3_\\\\lambda$\\nand the components of the gauge invariant \
1-form canonical connection. This\\nlatter object shows up naturally within \
the present noncommutative differential\\ncalculus. Restricting ourselves to \
positive actions with covariant coordinates\\nas field variables, a suitable \
gauge-fixing leads to a family of matrix models\\nwith quartic interactions \
and kinetic operators with compact resolvent. Their\\nperturbative behavior \
is then studied. We first compute the 2-point and 4-point\\nfunctions at the \
one-loop order within a subfamily of these matrix models for\\nwhich the \
interactions have a symmetric form. We find that the \
corresponding\\ncontributions are finite. We then extend this result to \
arbitrary order. We\\nfind that the amplitudes of the ribbon diagrams for the \
models of this\\nsubfamily are finite to all orders in perturbation. This \
result extends finally\\nto any of the models of the whole family of matrix \
models obtained from the\\nabove gauge-fixing. The origin of this result is \
discussed. Finally, the\\nexistence of a particular model related to \
integrable hierarchies is indicated,\\nfor which the partition function is \
expressible as a product of ratios of\\ndeterminants.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
