            "title" -> 
            "Noncommutative gauge theories on $\\mathbb{R}^3_\\lambda$: \
Perturbatively\n  finite models", "comments" -> "27 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP12 (2015) 045", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP12(2015)045", 
            "report-no" -> "LPT-Orsay-15-56", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We show that natural noncommutative gauge theory models on\n\
$\\mathbb{R}^3_\\lambda$ can accommodate gauge invariant harmonic terms, \
thanks\nto the existence of a relationship between the center of \
$\\mathbb{R}^3_\\lambda$\nand the components of the gauge invariant 1-form \
canonical connection. This\nlatter object shows up naturally within the \
present noncommutative differential\ncalculus. Restricting ourselves to \
positive actions with covariant coordinates\nas field variables, a suitable \
gauge-fixing leads to a family of matrix models\nwith quartic interactions \
and kinetic operators with compact resolvent. Their\nperturbative behavior is \
then studied. We first compute the 2-point and 4-point\nfunctions at the \
one-loop order within a subfamily of these matrix models for\nwhich the \
interactions have a symmetric form. We find that the corresponding\n\
contributions are finite. We then extend this result to arbitrary order. We\n\
find that the amplitudes of the ribbon diagrams for the models of this\n\
subfamily are finite to all orders in perturbation. This result extends \
finally\nto any of the models of the whole family of matrix models obtained \
from the\nabove gauge-fixing. The origin of this result is discussed. \
Finally, the\nexistence of a particular model related to integrable \
hierarchies is indicated,\nfor which the partition function is expressible as \
a product of ratios of\ndeterminants.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 29 Jul 2015 10:00:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-12-21", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"G\[EAcute]r\[EAcute]", "Antoine", ""}, {
              "Juri\[CAcute]", "Tajron", ""}, {
              "Wallet", "Jean-Christophe", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
