               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ben Hoare\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"B. Hoare, A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Type IIB supergravity solution for the T-dual of the \
eta-deformed AdS_5\\n  x S^5 superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"20 pages; v2: minor comments and clarifications added; \
v3: 21 pages,\\n  minor comments and references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"HU-EP-15/34, Imperial-TP-AT-2015-05\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find an exact type IIB supergravity solution that \
represents a\\none-parameter deformation of the T-dual of the AdS_5 x S^5 \
background (with\\nT-duality applied in all 6 abelian bosonic isometric \
directions). The\\nnon-trivial fields are the metric, dilaton and RR 5-form \
only. The latter has\\nremarkably simple \\\"undeformed\\\" form when written \
in terms of a\\n\\\"deformation-rotated\\\" vielbein basis. An unusual \
feature of this solution is\\nthat the dilaton contains a linear dependence \
on the isometric coordinates of\\nthe metric precluding a straightforward \
reversal of T-duality. If we still\\nformally dualize back, we find exactly \
the metric, B-field and product of\\ndilaton with RR field strengths as \
recently extracted from the eta-deformed\\nAdS_5 x S^5 superstring action in \
arXiv:1507.04239. We also discuss similar\\nsolutions for deformed AdS_n x \
S^n backgrounds with n=2,3. In the eta -> i\\nlimit we demonstrate that all \
these backgrounds can be interpreted as special\\nlimits of gauged WZW models \
and are also related to (a limit of) the\\nPohlmeyer-reduced models of the \
AdS_n x S^n superstrings.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
