            "  We find an exact type IIB supergravity solution that \
represents a\none-parameter deformation of the T-dual of the AdS_5 x S^5 \
background (with\nT-duality applied in all 6 abelian bosonic isometric \
directions). The\nnon-trivial fields are the metric, dilaton and RR 5-form \
only. The latter has\nremarkably simple \"undeformed\" form when written in \
terms of a\n\"deformation-rotated\" vielbein basis. An unusual feature of \
this solution is\nthat the dilaton contains a linear dependence on the \
isometric coordinates of\nthe metric precluding a straightforward reversal of \
T-duality. If we still\nformally dualize back, we find exactly the metric, \
B-field and product of\ndilaton with RR field strengths as recently extracted \
from the eta-deformed\nAdS_5 x S^5 superstring action in arXiv:1507.04239. We \
also discuss similar\nsolutions for deformed AdS_n x S^n backgrounds with \
n=2,3. In the eta -> i\nlimit we demonstrate that all these backgrounds can \
be interpreted as special\nlimits of gauged WZW models and are also related \
to (a limit of) the\nPohlmeyer-reduced models of the AdS_n x S^n \
superstrings.\n", 
