               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1508.04313\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Per Sundin and Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The AdS(n) x S(n) x T(10-2n) BMN string at two \
loops\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages, 6 figures; v2: References and comment on type \
IIB added,\\n  acknowledgements updated; v3: Comparison to proposed exact \
massless S-matrix\\n  in sec 5.3 corrected. Only non-trivial phase appears at \
one loop. Additional\\n  minor clarifications\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2015)154\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-LW-2015-02\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate the two-loop correction to the dispersion \
relation for\\nworldsheet modes of the BMN string in AdS(n) x S(n) x T(10-2n) \
for n=2,3,5. For\\nthe massive modes the result agrees with the exact \
dispersion relation derived\\nfrom symmetry considerations with no correction \
to the interpolating function\\nh. For the massless modes in AdS(3) x S(3) x \
T(4) however our result does not\\nmatch what one expects from the \
corresponding symmetry based analysis. We also\\nderive the S-matrix for \
massless modes up to the one-loop order. The scattering\\nphase is given by \
the massless limit of the Hernandez-Lopez phase. In addition\\nwe compute a \
certain massless S-matrix element at two loops and show that it\\nvanishes \
suggesting that the two-loop phase in the massless sector is zero.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
