            "  In this letter we put AdS/CFT dualities involving probe branes \
to a precision\ntest. On the holographic side we use a new class of \
supersymmetric D7-brane\nembeddings into AdS$_5\\times$S$^5$, which allow to \
describe N=4 SYM coupled to\nmassive N=2 supersymmetric flavors on S$^4$. \
With these embeddings we can\ncompare holographic results to a field theory \
analysis of the free energy using\nsupersymmetric localization. Localization \
allows us to get results at strong\ncoupling, and hence to compare in detail \
to AdS/CFT. We find analytically\nmatching results: a phase transition at the \
same critical mass in both\ncalculations and matching free energies up to a \
scheme-dependent constant in\nboth phases.\n", 
