 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the minimal surface in AdS, relevant for \
the strong coupling\\nbehaviour of local supersymmetric Wilson loops in N=4 \
SYM for a closed contour\\nformed out of segments of two intersecting \
circles. Its regularised area is\\ncalculated including all divergent parts \
and the finite renormalised term.\\nFurthermore we prove, that for generic \
planar curved contours with cusps the\\ncusp anomalous dimensions are \
functions of the respective cusp angles alone.\\nThey do not depend on other \
local data of the cusps.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
