            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1509.00716\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"S. Prem Kumar\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Timothy J. Hollowood and S. Prem Kumar\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Partition function of N=2* SYM on a large \
four-sphere\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Replaced with version to appear in JHEP. Typos corrected, \
added\\n  discussion on S-duality of the partition function. 47 pages, 8 \
figures, uses\\n  latex\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP12(2015)016\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We examine the partition function of N=2* \
supersymmetric SU(N) Yang-Mills\\ntheory on the four-sphere in the large \
radius limit. We point out that the\\nlarge radius partition function, at \
fixed N, is computed by saddle points lying\\non particular walls of marginal \
stability on the Coulomb branch of the theory\\non R^4. For N an even (odd) \
integer and \\\\theta_YM=0, (\\\\pi), these include a\\npoint of maximal \
degeneration of the Donagi-Witten curve to a torus where BPS\\ndyons with \
electric charge [N/2] become massless. We argue that the dyon\\nsingularity \
is the lone saddle point in the SU(2) theory, while for SU(N) with\\nN>2, we \
characterize potentially competing saddle points by obtaining the\\nrelations \
between the Seiberg-Witten periods at such points. Using \
Nekrasov's\\ninstanton partition function, we solve for the maximally \
degenerate saddle\\npoint and obtain its free energy as a function of g_YM \
and N, and show that the\\nresults are \\\"large-N exact\\\". In the large-N \
theory our results provide\\nanalytical expressions for the \
periods/eigenvalues at the maximally degenerate\\nsaddle point, precisely \
matching previously known formulae following from the\\ncorrespondence \
between N=2* theory and the elliptic Calogero-Moser integrable\\nmodel. The \
maximally singular point ceases to be a saddle point of the\\npartition \
function above a critical value of the coupling, in agreement with\\nthe \
recent findings of Russo and Zarembo.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 2 Sep 2015 14:15:07 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 20 Nov 2015 22:40:38 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2016-01-27\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Hollowood\"", ",", "\"Timothy J.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kumar\"", ",", "\"S. Prem\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
