            "Partition function of N=2* SYM on a large four-sphere", 
            "comments" -> 
            "Replaced with version to appear in JHEP. Typos corrected, added\n\
  discussion on S-duality of the partition function. 47 pages, 8 figures, \
uses\n  latex", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP12(2015)016", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We examine the partition function of N=2* supersymmetric SU(N) \
Yang-Mills\ntheory on the four-sphere in the large radius limit. We point out \
that the\nlarge radius partition function, at fixed N, is computed by saddle \
points lying\non particular walls of marginal stability on the Coulomb branch \
of the theory\non R^4. For N an even (odd) integer and \\theta_YM=0, (\\pi), \
these include a\npoint of maximal degeneration of the Donagi-Witten curve to \
a torus where BPS\ndyons with electric charge [N/2] become massless. We argue \
that the dyon\nsingularity is the lone saddle point in the SU(2) theory, \
while for SU(N) with\nN>2, we characterize potentially competing saddle \
points by obtaining the\nrelations between the Seiberg-Witten periods at such \
points. Using Nekrasov's\ninstanton partition function, we solve for the \
maximally degenerate saddle\npoint and obtain its free energy as a function \
of g_YM and N, and show that the\nresults are \"large-N exact\". In the \
large-N theory our results provide\nanalytical expressions for the \
periods/eigenvalues at the maximally degenerate\nsaddle point, precisely \
matching previously known formulae following from the\ncorrespondence between \
N=2* theory and the elliptic Calogero-Moser integrable\nmodel. The maximally \
singular point ceases to be a saddle point of the\npartition function above a \
critical value of the coupling, in agreement with\nthe recent findings of \
Russo and Zarembo.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
