                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"  We verify the self-duality of Green-Schwarz supercoset \
sigma models on AdS$_d\\n\\\\times S^d $ backgrounds (d=2,3,5) under combined \
bosonic and fermionic\\nT-dualities without gauge fixing kappa symmetry. We \
also prove this property\\nfor superstrings on AdS$_d \\\\times S^d \\\\times \
S^d$ (d=2,3) described by\\nsupercoset sigma models with the isometries \
governed by the exceptional Lie\\nsupergroups $D(2,1;\\\\alpha)$ (d=2) and \
$D(2,1;\\\\alpha)\\\\times D(2,1;\\\\alpha)$\\n(d=3), which requires an \
additional T-dualisation along one of the spheres.\\nThen, by taking into \
account the contribution of non-supercoset fermionic modes\\n(up to the \
second order), we provide evidence for the T-self-duality of the\\ncomplete \
type IIA and IIB Green-Schwarz superstring theory on AdS$_d\\\\times S^d\\n\\\
\\times T^{10-2d}$ (d=2,3) backgrounds with Ramond-Ramond fluxes. \
Finally,\\napplying the Buscher-like rules to T-dualising supergravity \
fields, we prove\\nthe T-self-duality of the whole class of the \
AdS$_d\\\\times S^d \\\\times M^{10-2d}$\\nsuperbackgrounds with \
Ramond-Ramond fluxes in the context of supergravity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
