                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that the string backgrounds AdS2 x S2 x T6 and \
AdSd x Sd x Sd x T{10\\n- 3d} (d = 2, 3) are self-dual under a series of \
bosonic and fermionic\\nT-dualities. We do this using the fermionic Buscher \
rules derived by Berkovits\\nand Maldacena, thus working at the level of the \
supergravity fields. This\\nallows us to explicitly track the behaviour of \
the RR fields, from which we see\\nthat we need T-duality along some torus \
directions. For the AdS x S x S cases,\\nwhich contain cosets of \
D(2,1;alpha), it is necessary to perform bosonic\\nT-duality along some \
complexified Killing spinors in one of the spheres.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
