                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the issue of higher-dimensional counterterms \
for the N=(1,1)\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills (SYM) theory in six dimensions \
using the off-shell\\nN=(1,0) and on-shell N=(1,1) harmonic superspace \
approaches. The second\\napproach is developed in full generality and used to \
solve, for the first time,\\nthe N=(1,1) SYM constraints in terms of N=(1,0) \
superfields. This provides a\\nconvenient tool to write explicit expressions \
for the candidate counterterms\\nand other N=(1,1) invariants and may be \
conducive to proving\\nnon-renormalization theorems needed to explain the \
absence of certain\\nlogarithmic divergences in higher-loop contributions to \
scattering amplitudes\\nin N=(1,1) SYM.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
