                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that the Quantum Spectral Curve (QSC) \
formalism, initially formulated\\nfor the spectrum of anomalous dimensions of \
all local single trace operators in\\nN=4 SYM, can be extended to the \
generalized cusp anomalous dimension for all\\nvalues of the parameters. We \
find that the large spectral parameter asymptotics\\nand some analyticity \
properties have to be modified, but the functional\\nrelations are unchanged. \
As a demonstration, we find an all-loop analytic\\nexpression for the first \
two nontrivial terms in the small |phi \\\\pm theta|\\nexpansion. We also \
present nonperturbative numerical results at generic angles\\nwhich match \
perfectly 4-loop perturbation theory and the classical \
string\\nprediction.\\n  The reformulation of the problem in terms of the QSC \
opens the possibility to\\nexplore many open questions. We attach to this \
paper several Mathematica\\nnotebooks which should facilitate future studies.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
