            "comments" -> 
            "42 pages, 4 figures; supplementary Mathematica files are \
attached", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1604 (2016) 134", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP04(2016)134", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We show that the Quantum Spectral Curve (QSC) formalism, \
initially formulated\nfor the spectrum of anomalous dimensions of all local \
single trace operators in\nN=4 SYM, can be extended to the generalized cusp \
anomalous dimension for all\nvalues of the parameters. We find that the large \
spectral parameter asymptotics\nand some analyticity properties have to be \
modified, but the functional\nrelations are unchanged. As a demonstration, we \
find an all-loop analytic\nexpression for the first two nontrivial terms in \
the small |phi \\pm theta|\nexpansion. We also present nonperturbative \
numerical results at generic angles\nwhich match perfectly 4-loop \
perturbation theory and the classical string\nprediction.\n  The \
reformulation of the problem in terms of the QSC opens the possibility to\n\
explore many open questions. We attach to this paper several Mathematica\n\
notebooks which should facilitate future studies.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
