Peter Marquard\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The three-loop cusp anomalous dimension in QCD and its \
supersymmetric\\n  extensions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"63 pages, 14 figures; v2: minor changes, references \
added; v3: minor\\n  changes, eq.(D.7) corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2016)140\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"DESY 15-186, IPhT-T15/174, MITP/15-088\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present the details of the analytic calculation of \
the three-loop\\nangle-dependent cusp anomalous dimension in QCD and its \
supersymmetric\\nextensions, including the maximally supersymmetric \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super\\nYang-Mills theory. The three-loop result in the \
latter theory is new and\\nconfirms a conjecture made in our previous paper. \
We study various physical\\nlimits of the cusp anomalous dimension and \
discuss its relation to the\\nquark-antiquark potential including the effects \
of broken conformal symmetry in\\nQCD. We find that the cusp anomalous \
dimension viewed as a function of the cusp\\nangle and the new effective \
coupling given by light-like cusp anomalous\\ndimension reveals a remarkable \
universality property -- it takes the same form\\nin QCD and its \
supersymmetric extensions, to three loops at least. We exploit\\nthis \
universality property and make use of the known result for the \
three-loop\\nquark-antiquark potential to predict the special class of \
nonplanar corrections\\nto the cusp anomalous dimensions at four loops. \
Finally, we also discuss in\\ndetail the computation of all necessary Wilson \
line integrals up to three loops\\nusing the method of leading singularities \
and differential equations.\\n\""}]}, {
