               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this work we obtain the non-abelian T-dual geometry \
of the well-known\\nPilch-Warner supergravity solution in its infrared point. \
We derive the dual\\nmetric and the NS two-form by gauging the isometry group \
of the initial theory\\nand integrating out the introduced auxiliary gauge \
fields. Then we use the\\nFourier-Mukai transform from algebraic geometry to \
find the transformation\\nrules of the R-R fields. The dual background \
preserves the $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$\\nsupersymmetry of the original one due to \
the fact that the Killing spinor does\\nnot depend on the directions on which \
the N-AT-D is performed. Finally, we\\nconsider two different pp-wave limits \
of the T-dual geometry by performing\\nPenrose limits for two light-like \
geodesics.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
