MITP/15-092\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate supersymmetric Wilson loops on the \
ellipsoid for a large class\\nof $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCFT using the \
localization formula of Hama and Hosomichi.\\nFrom them we extract the \
radiation emitted by an accelerating heavy probe quark\\nas well as the \
entanglement entropy following the recent works of\\nLewkowycz-Maldacena and \
Fiol-Gerchkovitz-Komargodski. Comparing our results\\nwith the \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM ones, we obtain interpolating functions \
$f(g^2)$\\nsuch that a given $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCFT observable is obtained \
by replacing in\\nthe corresponding $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM result the \
coupling constant by $f(g^2)$.\\nThese \\\"exact effective couplings\\\" \
encode the finite, relative renormalization\\nbetween the $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
and the $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ gluon propagator, they\\ninterpolate between the \
weak and the strong coupling. We discuss the range of\\ntheir \
applicability.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
