           "id" -> "1511.02217", "submitter" -> "Vladimir Mitev", "authors" -> 
            "Vladimir Mitev and Elli Pomoni", "title" -> 
            "Exact Bremsstrahlung and Effective Couplings", "comments" -> 
            "16 pages, 10 pages appendices, 4 figures. v2, journal version", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1606 (2016) 078", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP06(2016)078", "report-no" -> 
            "DESY 15-196, HU-Mathematik-2015-12, HU-EP-15/50, MITP/15-092", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate supersymmetric Wilson loops on the ellipsoid for \
a large class\nof $\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCFT using the localization formula of \
Hama and Hosomichi.\nFrom them we extract the radiation emitted by an \
accelerating heavy probe quark\nas well as the entanglement entropy following \
the recent works of\nLewkowycz-Maldacena and Fiol-Gerchkovitz-Komargodski. \
Comparing our results\nwith the $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM ones, we obtain \
interpolating functions $f(g^2)$\nsuch that a given $\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCFT \
observable is obtained by replacing in\nthe corresponding $\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
SYM result the coupling constant by $f(g^2)$.\nThese \"exact effective \
couplings\" encode the finite, relative renormalization\nbetween the \
$\\mathcal{N}=2$ and the $\\mathcal{N}=4$ gluon propagator, they\ninterpolate \
between the weak and the strong coupling. We discuss the range of\ntheir \
applicability.\n", 
