                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Georgios Linardopoulos\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Minos Axenides and Emmanuel Floratos and Georgios \
Linardopoulos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Omega-Infinity Limit of Single Spikes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages, 14 figures. Matches published version; Contains \
equation\\n  (4.21) that gives the first few finite-size corrections to the \
energy of\\n  omega-infinity single spikes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B907:323-359,2016\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2016.04.006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A new infinite-size limit of strings in RxS2 is \
presented. The limit is\\nobtained from single spike strings by letting by \
letting the angular velocity\\nparameter omega become infinite. We derive the \
energy-momenta relation of\\nomega-infinity single spikes as their linear \
velocity v-->1 and their angular\\nmomentum J-->1. Generally, the v-->1, \
J-->1 limit of single spikes is singular\\nand has to be excluded from the \
spectrum and be studied separately. We discover\\nthat the dispersion \
relation of omega-infinity single spikes contains\\nlogarithms in the limit \
J-->1. This result is somewhat surprising, since the\\nlogarithmic behavior \
in the string spectra is typically associated with their\\nmotion in \
non-compact spaces such as AdS. Omega-infinity single spikes seem \
to\\ncompletely cover the surface of the 2-sphere they occupy, so that they \
may\\nessentially be viewed as some sort of \\\"brany strings\\\". A proof of \
the\\nsphere-filling property of omega-infinity single spikes is given in the\
\\nappendix.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
