limit of single spikes is singular\nand has to be excluded from the spectrum \
and be studied separately. We discover\nthat the dispersion relation of \
omega-infinity single spikes contains\nlogarithms in the limit J-->1. This \
result is somewhat surprising, since the\nlogarithmic behavior in the string \
spectra is typically associated with their\nmotion in non-compact spaces such \
as AdS. Omega-infinity single spikes seem to\ncompletely cover the surface of \
the 2-sphere they occupy, so that they may\nessentially be viewed as some \
sort of \"brany strings\". A proof of the\nsphere-filling property of \
omega-infinity single spikes is given in the\nappendix.\n", 
