                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the near BPS expansion of the generalized \
cusp anomalous dimension\\nwith L units of R-charge. Integrability provides \
an exact solution, obtained by\\nsolving a general TBA equation in the \
appropriate limit: we propose here an\\nalternative method based on \
supersymmetric localization. The basic idea is to\\nrelate the computation to \
the vacuum expectation value of certain 1/8 BPS\\nWilson loops with local \
operator insertions along the contour. These\\nobservables localize on a \
two-dimensional gauge theory on S^2, opening the\\npossibility of exact \
calculations. As a test of our proposal, we reproduce the\\nleading Luscher \
correction at weak coupling to the generalized cusp anomalous\\ndimension. \
This result is also checked against a genuine Feynman diagram\\napproach in \
N=4 Super Yang-Mills theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
