 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the heavy-heavy-light (HHL) three-point \
functions in the planar N =\\n4 super-Yang- Mills theory using the recently \
proposed hexagon bootstrap\\nprogram [arXiv:1505.06745]. We prove the \
conjecture of Bajnok, Janik and\\nWereszczynski [arXiv:1404.4556] on the \
polynomial L-dependence of HHL structure\\nconstant up to the leading \
finite-size corrections, where L is the length of\\nthe heavy operators. The \
proof is presented for a specific set-up but the\\nmethod can be applied to \
more general situations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
