               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Precision calculation of 1/4-BPS Wilson loops in AdS$_5\\\
\\times S^5$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"References added, comments in introduction and \
conclusions added, it\\n  matches published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2016)105\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-EP-15/58\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the strong coupling behaviour of $1/4$-BPS \
circular Wilson loops (a\\nfamily of \\\"latitudes\\\") in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ \
Super Yang-Mills theory, computing the\\none-loop corrections to the relevant \
classical string solutions in\\nAdS$_5\\\\times$S$^5$. Supersymmetric \
localization provides an exact result that,\\nin the large 't Hooft coupling \
limit, should be reproduced by the sigma-model\\napproach. To avoid \
ambiguities due to the absolute normalization of the string\\npartition \
function, we compare the $ratio$ between the generic latitude and \
the\\nmaximal 1/2-BPS circle: Any measure-related ambiguity should simply \
cancel in\\nthis way. We use Gel'fand-Yaglom method to calculate the relevant \
functional\\ndeterminants, that present some complications with respect to \
the standard\\ncircular case. After a careful numerical evaluation of our \
final expression we\\nstill find disagreement with the localization answer: \
The difference is encoded\\ninto a precise \\\"remainder function\\\". We \
comment on the possible origin and\\nresolution of this \
discordance.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
