           "id" -> "1512.00841", "submitter" -> "Edoardo Vescovi", "authors" -> 
            "V. Forini, V. Giangreco M. Puletti, L. Griguolo, D. Seminara, E.\
\n  Vescovi", "title" -> 
            "Precision calculation of 1/4-BPS Wilson loops in AdS$_5\\times \
S^5$", "comments" -> 
            "References added, comments in introduction and conclusions \
added, it\n  matches published version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP02(2016)105", "report-no" -> "HU-EP-15/58", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the strong coupling behaviour of $1/4$-BPS circular \
Wilson loops (a\nfamily of \"latitudes\") in ${\\cal N}=4$ Super Yang-Mills \
theory, computing the\none-loop corrections to the relevant classical string \
solutions in\nAdS$_5\\times$S$^5$. Supersymmetric localization provides an \
exact result that,\nin the large 't Hooft coupling limit, should be \
reproduced by the sigma-model\napproach. To avoid ambiguities due to the \
absolute normalization of the string\npartition function, we compare the \
$ratio$ between the generic latitude and the\nmaximal 1/2-BPS circle: Any \
measure-related ambiguity should simply cancel in\nthis way. We use \
Gel'fand-Yaglom method to calculate the relevant functional\ndeterminants, \
that present some complications with respect to the standard\ncircular case. \
After a careful numerical evaluation of our final expression we\nstill find \
disagreement with the localization answer: The difference is encoded\ninto a \
precise \"remainder function\". We comment on the possible origin and\n\
resolution of this discordance.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 2 Dec 2015 20:51:34 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 8 Feb 2016 19:18:25 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
