            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The string sigma model in $AdS_3\\times S^3$ supported by \
mixed three-form\nfluxes has recently been proved to be integrable which led \
to a plethora of\nwork in this background including proposals for S matrix \
and study of\nsemiclassical string profiles. Motivated by this, in this \
paper, we present a\nstudy of `spiky' strings in this background. We analyze \
the string profiles in\ndetail and also find the dispersion relation between \
the charges in the `long'\nstring limit after solving the equations of motion \
perturbatively upto the\nleading order in the Neveu-Schwarz flux $b$. We find \
that the dispersion for 2\nspikes gets corrected by the term $-\\frac{b^2}{2}\
\\log S$. We also discuss the\nfate of the solution in the limit of pure \
NS-NS flux.\n", 
