 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore quantum mechanical theories whose \
fundamental degrees of freedom\\nare rectangular matrices with Grassmann \
valued matrix elements. We study\\nparticular models where the low energy \
sector can be described in terms of a\\nbosonic Hermitian matrix quantum \
mechanics. We describe the classical curved\\nphase space that emerges in the \
low energy sector. The phase space lives on a\\ncompact Kahler manifold \
parameterized by a complex matrix, of the type\\ndiscovered some time ago by \
Berezin. The emergence of a semiclassical bosonic\\nmatrix quantum mechanics \
at low energies requires that the original Grassmann\\nmatrices be in the \
long rectangular limit. We discuss possible holographic\\ninterpretations of \
such matrix models which, by construction, are endowed with\\na finite \
dimensional Hilbert space.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
