               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the $\\\\gamma$-deformed $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
SYM in the double scaling\\nlimit of large imaginary twists and small \
coupling, which discards the gauge\\nfields and retains only certain Yukawa \
and scalar interactions with three\\narbitrary effective couplings. In the \
't~Hooft limit, these 4D theories are\\nintegrable, with most of the \
correlators being conformal such that the whole\\narsenal of AdS/CFT \
integrability remains applicable. In particular, for one\\nnon-zero effective \
coupling, we obtain a QFT of two complex scalars with a\\nchiral, quartic \
interaction. The BMN vacuum anomalous dimension is dominated in\\neach \
non-zero loop order by a single \\\"wheel\\\" graph, in principle computable \
by\\nintegrability. Thus we also provide an explicit conjecture for the \
periods of\\ndouble-wheel graphs with an arbitrary number of \
spokes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
