            "New integrable non-gauge 4D QFTs from strongly deformed planar \
N=4 SYM", "comments" -> 
            "6 pages, 3 figures. V3: references added, improvements made in \
the\n  text, double-wrapping anomalous dimensions included as an ancillary \
file. V2:\n  references added, typos corrected, statement on the conformality \
of the\n  theory corrected, equation 9 included as an ancillary file", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. Lett. 117, 201602 (2016)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevLett.117.201602", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the $\\gamma$-deformed $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM in the \
double scaling\nlimit of large imaginary twists and small coupling, which \
discards the gauge\nfields and retains only certain Yukawa and scalar \
interactions with three\narbitrary effective couplings. In the 't~Hooft \
limit, these 4D theories are\nintegrable, with most of the correlators being \
conformal such that the whole\narsenal of AdS/CFT integrability remains \
applicable. In particular, for one\nnon-zero effective coupling, we obtain a \
QFT of two complex scalars with a\nchiral, quartic interaction. The BMN \
vacuum anomalous dimension is dominated in\neach non-zero loop order by a \
single \"wheel\" graph, in principle computable by\nintegrability. Thus we \
also provide an explicit conjecture for the periods of\ndouble-wheel graphs \
with an arbitrary number of spokes.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
