                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We conjecture the form of the one-loop determinants for \
localized gauge\\ntheories with eight supersymmetries on $d$-dimensional \
spheres. Combining this\\nwith results for the localized action, we \
investigate the strong coupling\\nbehavior in the large $N$ limit for a \
continuous range of $d$. In particular,\\nwe find the $N$ dependence of the \
free energy for supersymmetric Yang-Mills\\nwith only a vector multiplet in \
$3<d<4$ and for maximally supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills in $3< d<6$. We also \
argue that this gives an effective way to\\nregularize divergences after \
localization in $d=4$ for ${\\\\mathcal N}=2$ gauge\\ntheories and $d=6$ for \
the maximally supersymmetric case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
