                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In AdS5/CFT4 integrability the Bethe ansatz gives the \
spectrum of long\\nstrings, accurate up to exponentially small corrections. \
This is no longer true\\nin AdS3, as we demonstrate here by studying Luscher \
F-terms with a massless\\nparticle running in the loop. We apply this to the \
classic test of Hernandez &\\nLopez, in which the su(2) sector Bethe \
equations (including one-loop dressing\\nphase) should match the \
semiclassical string theory result for a circular\\nspinning string. These \
calculations did not agree in AdS3xS3xT4, and we show\\nthat the sum of all \
massless Luscher F-terms can reproduce the difference.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
