 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider certain 1/4 BPS Wilson loop operators in \
SU(N) ${\\\\cal N}=4$\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory, whose expectation \
value can be computed\\nexactly via supersymmetric localization. \
Holographically, these operators are\\nmapped to fundamental strings in AdS5 \
x S5. The string on-shell action\\nreproduces the large N and large coupling \
limit of the gauge theory expectation\\nvalue and, according to the AdS/CFT \
correspondence, there should also be a\\nprecise match between subleading \
corrections to these limits. We perform a test\\nof such match at \
next-to-leading order in string theory, by deriving the\\nspectrum of quantum \
fluctuations around the classical string solution and by\\ncomputing the \
corresponding 1-loop effective action. We discuss in detail \
the\\nsupermultiplet structure of the fluctuations. To remove a possible \
source of\\nambiguity in the ghost zero mode measure, we compare the 1/4 BPS \
configuration\\nwith the 1/2 BPS one, dual to a circular Wilson loop. We find \
a discrepancy\\nbetween the string theory result and the gauge theory \
prediction, confirming a\\nprevious result in the literature. We are able to \
track the modes from which\\nthis discrepancy originates, as well as the \
modes that by themselves would give\\nthe expected result.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
