            "  We construct a closed system of equations describing the \
quark--anti-quark\npotential at any coupling in planar N=4 supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory. It is\nbased on the Quantum Spectral Curve method \
supplemented with a novel type of\nasymptotics. We present a high precision \
numerical solution reproducing the\nclassical and one-loop string predictions \
very accurately. We also analytically\ncompute the first 7 nontrivial orders \
of the weak coupling expansion.\n  Moreover, we study analytically the \
generalized quark--anti-quark potential\nin the limit of large imaginary \
twist to all orders in perturbation theory. We\ndemonstrate how the QSC \
reduces in this case to a one-dimensional Schrodinger\nequation. In the \
process we establish a link between the Q-functions and the\nsolution of the \
Bethe-Salpeter equation.\n", 
