 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the asymptotic volume dependence of the \
heavy-heavy-light\\nthree-point functions in the $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
Super-Yang-Mills theory using the\\nhexagon bootstrap approach, where the \
volume is the length of the heavy\\noperator. We extend the analysis of our \
previous short letter 1511.06199 to the\\ngeneral case where the heavy \
operators can be in any rank one sector and the\\nlight operator being a \
generic non-BPS operator. We prove the conjecture of\\nBajnok, Janik and \
Wereszczynski 1404.4556 up to leading finite size\\ncorrections.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
