               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that an integrable four-dimensional non-unitary \
field theory that was\\nrecently proposed as a certain limit of the \
$\\\\gamma_i$-deformed $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$\\nSYM theory is incomplete and not \
conformal -- not even in the planar limit. We\\ncomplete this theory by \
double-trace couplings and find conformal one-loop\\nfix-points when \
admitting respective complex coupling constants. These\\ncouplings must not \
be neglected in the planar limit, as they can contribute to\\nplanar \
multi-point functions. Based on our results for certain two-loop \
planar\\nanomalous dimensions, we propose tests of integrability.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
