               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the cusp anomalous dimension in N=6 ABJ(M) \
theory, identifying a\\nscaling limit in which the ladder diagrams dominate. \
The resummation is encoded\\ninto a Bethe-Salpeter equation that is mapped to \
a Schroedinger problem,\\nexactly solvable due to the surprising \
supersymmetry of the effective\\nHamiltonian. In the ABJ case the solution \
implies the diagonalization of the\\nU(N) and U(M) building blocks, \
suggesting the existence of two independent cusp\\nanomalous dimensions and \
an unexpected exponentiation structure for the related\\nWilson loops. While \
consistent with previous perturbative analysis, the strong\\ncoupling limit \
of our result does not agree with the string theory \
computation,\\nemphasizing a difference with the analogous resummation in the \
N=4 case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
