           "id" -> "1603.00541", "submitter" -> "Michelangelo Preti", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Marisa Bonini, Luca Griguolo, Michelangelo Preti, Domenico \
Seminara", "title" -> 
            "Surprises from the resummation of ladders in the ABJ(M) cusp \
anomalous\n  dimension", "comments" -> 
            "26 pages, 4 figures, references added, published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2016)180", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the cusp anomalous dimension in N=6 ABJ(M) theory, \
identifying a\nscaling limit in which the ladder diagrams dominate. The \
resummation is encoded\ninto a Bethe-Salpeter equation that is mapped to a \
Schroedinger problem,\nexactly solvable due to the surprising supersymmetry \
of the effective\nHamiltonian. In the ABJ case the solution implies the \
diagonalization of the\nU(N) and U(M) building blocks, suggesting the \
existence of two independent cusp\nanomalous dimensions and an unexpected \
exponentiation structure for the related\nWilson loops. While consistent with \
previous perturbative analysis, the strong\ncoupling limit of our result does \
not agree with the string theory computation,\nemphasizing a difference with \
the analogous resummation in the N=4 case.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 2 Mar 2016 01:16:47 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 31 May 2016 10:33:22 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
