           "id" -> "1603.02586", "submitter" -> "Francesco Fucito", "authors" -> 
            "Francesco Fucito, Jose Francisco Morale, Rubik Poghossian", 
            "title" -> 
            "Wilson Loops and Chiral Correlators on Squashed Spheres", 
            "comments" -> 
            "talk delivered at the conference \"Interactions between Geometry \
and\n  Physics\", Guaraja, Sao Paulo, August 17-22, 2015", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1016/j.geomphys.2016.09.004", "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  After a very brief recollection of how my scientific \
collaboration with Ugo\nstarted, in this talk I will present some recent \
results obtained with\nlocalization: the deformed gauge theory partition \
function $Z(\\vec\\tau|q)$ and\nthe expectation value of circular Wilson \
loops $W$ on a squashed four-sphere\nwill be computed. The partition function \
is deformed by turning on $\\tau_J\n\\,{\\rm tr} \\, \\Phi^J$ interactions \
with $\\Phi$ the ${\\cal N}=2$ superfield.\n  For the ${\\cal N}=4$ theory \
SUSY gauge theory exact formulae for $Z$ and $W$\nin terms of an underlying \
$U(N)$ interacting matrix model can be derived thus\nreplacing the free \
Gaussian model describing the undeformed ${\\cal N}=4$\ntheory. These results \
will be then compared with those obtained with the dual\nCFT according to the \
AGT correspondence. The interactions introduced previously\nare in fact \
related to the insertions of commuting integrals of motion in the\nfour-point \
CFT correlator and the chiral correlators are expressed as\n\
$\\tau$-derivatives of the gauge theory partition function on a finite\n\
$\\Omega$-background.\n", 
