            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1603.02768\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Igor Samsonov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"I.L. Buchbinder, E.A. Ivanov, I.B. Samsonov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The low-energy N=4 SYM effective action in diverse \
harmonic superspaces\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"102 pages, v2: references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1134/S1063779617030042\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review various superspace approaches to the \
description of the low-energy\\neffective action in N=4 super Yang-Mills \
(SYM) theory. We consider the\\nfour-derivative part of the low-energy \
effective action in the Coulomb branch.\\nThe typical components of this \
effective action are the gauge field F^4/X^4 and\\nthe scalar field \
Wess-Zumino terms. We construct N=4 supersymmetric completions\\nof these \
terms in the framework of different harmonic superspaces supporting\\nN=2,3,4 \
supersymmetries. These approaches are complementary to each other in\\nthe \
sense that they make manifest different subgroups of the total \
SU(4)\\nR-symmetry group. We show that the effective action acquires an \
extremely\\nsimple form in those superspaces which manifest the non-anomalous \
maximal\\nsubgroups of SU(4). The common characteristic feature of our \
construction is\\nthat we restore the superfield effective actions \
exclusively by employing the\\nN=4 supersymmetry and/or superconformal \
PSU(2,2|4) symmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
