          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1603.02768", "submitter" -> "Igor Samsonov", "authors" -> 
            "I.L. Buchbinder, E.A. Ivanov, I.B. Samsonov", "title" -> 
            "The low-energy N=4 SYM effective action in diverse harmonic \
superspaces", "comments" -> "102 pages, v2: references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1134/S1063779617030042", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We review various superspace approaches to the description of \
the low-energy\neffective action in N=4 super Yang-Mills (SYM) theory. We \
consider the\nfour-derivative part of the low-energy effective action in the \
Coulomb branch.\nThe typical components of this effective action are the \
gauge field F^4/X^4 and\nthe scalar field Wess-Zumino terms. We construct N=4 \
supersymmetric completions\nof these terms in the framework of different \
harmonic superspaces supporting\nN=2,3,4 supersymmetries. These approaches \
are complementary to each other in\nthe sense that they make manifest \
different subgroups of the total SU(4)\nR-symmetry group. We show that the \
effective action acquires an extremely\nsimple form in those superspaces \
which manifest the non-anomalous maximal\nsubgroups of SU(4). The common \
characteristic feature of our construction is\nthat we restore the superfield \
effective actions exclusively by employing the\nN=4 supersymmetry and/or \
superconformal PSU(2,2|4) symmetry.\n", 
