               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1603.04826\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Xiao Fang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Joseph E. McEwen, Xiao Fang, Christopher M. Hirata, \
Jonathan A. Blazek\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"FAST-PT: a novel algorithm to calculate convolution \
integrals in\\n  cosmological perturbation theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"24 pages, 5 figures, 2 tables. fig.1 corrected. changes \
made. matched\\n  with the journal version. Code available at\\n  \
https://github.com/JoeMcEwen/FAST-PT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JCAP09(2016)015\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2016/09/015\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"astro-ph.CO\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a novel algorithm, FAST-PT, for performing \
convolution or\\nmode-coupling integrals that appear in nonlinear \
cosmological perturbation\\ntheory. The algorithm uses several properties of \
gravitational structure\\nformation -- the locality of the dark matter \
equations and the scale invariance\\nof the problem -- as well as Fast \
Fourier Transforms to describe the input\\npower spectrum as a superposition \
of power laws. This yields extremely fast\\nperformance, enabling \
mode-coupling integral computations fast enough to embed\\nin Monte Carlo \
Markov Chain parameter estimation. We describe the algorithm \
and\\ndemonstrate its application to calculating nonlinear corrections to the \
matter\\npower spectrum, including one-loop standard perturbation theory and \
the\\nrenormalization group approach. We also describe our public code (in \
Python) to\\nimplement this algorithm, including the applications described \
here.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
