 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The particles produced at a potential Future Circular \
Collider with\\n$\\\\sqrt{s}$ = 100 TeV are of unprecented energies. In this \
document we present\\nthe hadronic shower containment and resolution \
parametrizations based on Geant4\\nsimulations for the Hadronic calorimetry \
needed for conceptual detector design\\nat this energy. The Geant4 toolkit \
along with FTFP\\\\_BERT physics list are used\\nin this study. Comparisons \
are made with test-beam data from the ATLAS Tile\\nhadronic calorimeter. \
These simulations motivate a 12 $\\\\lambda$ calorimeter in\\norder to \
contain at 98% level TeV single hadron showers and multi-TeV jets and\\nkeep \
a pion energy resolution constant term of 3%.\\n\""}]}, {
