            "Perturbation theory for string sigma models", "comments" -> 
            "198 pages. Based on the author's PhD thesis and on the \
publications\n  arXiv:1304.1798, arXiv:1401.0448, arXiv:1405.7947, \
arXiv:1407.4788,\n  arXiv:1505.00783", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this thesis we investigate quantum aspects of the \
Green-Schwarz\nsuperstring in various AdS backgrounds relevant for the \
AdS/CFT correspondence,\nproviding several examples of perturbative \
computations in the corresponding\nintegrable sigma-models. We start by \
reviewing in details the supercoset\nconstruction of the superstring action \
in $AdS_5 \\times S^5$, pointing out the\nlimits of this procedure for \
$AdS_4$ and $AdS_3$ backgrounds. For the $AdS_4\n\\times CP^3$ case we give a \
thorough derivation of an alternative action, based\non the \
double-dimensional reduction of eleven-dimensional super-membranes. We\nthen \
consider the expansion about the BMN vacuum and the S-matrix for the\n\
scattering of worldsheet excitations in the decompactification limit. To\n\
evaluate its elements efficiently we describe a unitarity-based method\n\
resulting in a very compact formula yielding the cut-constructible part of \
any\none-loop two-dimensional S-matrix. In the second part of this review we \
analyze\nthe superstring action on $AdS_4 \\times CP^3$ expanded around the \
null cusp\nvacuum. The free energy of this model, whose computation we \
reproduce up to\ntwo-loops at strong coupling, is related to the cusp \
anomalous dimension of the\nABJM theory and, indirectly, to a non-trivial \
effective coupling $h(\\lambda)$\nfeaturing all integrability-based \
calculations in $AdS_4/CFT_3$. Finally, we\nextensively discuss the \
comparison of the perturbative results and the\nintegrability predictions for \
the one-loop dispersion relation of GKP\nexcitations. Our results provide \
valuable data in support of the quantum\nconsistency of the string actions - \
often debated due to possible issues with\ncancellation of UV divergences and \
the lack of manifest power-counting\nrenormalizability - and furnish \
non-trivial stringent tests for the quantum\nintegrability of the analyzed \
models.\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 6 Apr 2016 16:04:39 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 7 Apr 2016 10:35:31 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
