 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"  We study quantum quenches to the one-dimensional Bose \
gas with attractive\\ninteractions in the case when the initial state is an \
ideal one-dimensional\\nBose condensate. We focus on properties of the \
stationary state reached at late\\ntimes after the quench. This displays a \
finite density of multi-particle bound\\nstates, whose rapidity distribution \
is determined exactly by means of the\\nquench action method. We discuss the \
relevance of the multi-particle bound\\nstates for the physical properties of \
the system, computing in particular the\\nstationary value of the local pair \
correlation function $g_2$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
