                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUPT-2502, MCTP-16-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the five-dimensional supergravity dual of \
the $\\\\mathcal{N}=1^*$\\nmass deformation of the $\\\\mathcal{N} =4$ \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory on\\n$S^4$ and use it to calculate the \
universal contribution to the corresponding\\n$S^4$ free energy at large 't \
Hooft coupling in the planar limit. The\\nholographic RG flow solutions are \
smooth and preserve four supercharges. As a\\nnovel feature compared to the \
holographic duals of $\\\\mathcal{N} = 1^*$ on\\n$\\\\mathbb{R}^4$, in our \
backgrounds the five-dimensional dilaton has a\\nnon-trivial profile, and the \
gaugino condensate is fixed in terms of the\\nmass-deformation parameters. \
Important aspects of the analysis involve\\ncharacterizing the ambiguities in \
the partition function of non-conformal\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ supersymmetric \
theories on $S^4$ as well as the action of\\nS-duality on the \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=1^*$ theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
