                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We interpret Janus as an interface in a conformal field \
theory and study its\\nproperties. The Janus is created by an exactly \
marginal operator and we study\\nits effect on the interface conformal field \
theory on the Janus. We do this by\\nutilizing the AdS/CFT correspondence. We \
compute the interface free energy both\\nfrom leading correction to the \
Euclidean action in the dual gravity description\\nand from conformal \
perturbation theory in the conformal field theory. We find\\nthat the two \
results agree each other and that the interface free energy \
scales\\nprecisely as expected from the conformal invariance of the Janus \
interface.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
