          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1605.00857", "submitter" -> "Dongsu Bak", "authors" -> 
            "Dongsu Bak, Andreas Gustavsson, Soo-Jong Rey", "title" -> 
            "Conformal Janus on Euclidean Sphere", "comments" -> 
            "37 pages, 5 figures, references added, section 2 and references\n\
  added, published version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP12(2016)025", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We interpret Janus as an interface in a conformal field theory \
and study its\nproperties. The Janus is created by an exactly marginal \
operator and we study\nits effect on the interface conformal field theory on \
the Janus. We do this by\nutilizing the AdS/CFT correspondence. We compute \
the interface free energy both\nfrom leading correction to the Euclidean \
action in the dual gravity description\nand from conformal perturbation \
theory in the conformal field theory. We find\nthat the two results agree \
each other and that the interface free energy scales\nprecisely as expected \
from the conformal invariance of the Janus interface.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 3 May 2016 12:16:17 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
