               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1605.03173\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Riccardo Borsato\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Riccardo Borsato\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable strings for AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Based on the author's PhD thesis. 175 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-RB-2016-03\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this PhD thesis we review some aspects of integrable \
models related to\\nstring backgrounds or their deformations. In the first \
part we develop methods\\nto obtain exact results in the AdS3/CFT2 \
correspondence. We consider the AdS_3\\nx S^3 x T^4 background with pure \
Ramond-Ramond flux and we find the all-loop\\nworldsheet S-matrix by \
exploiting the symmetries of the model in light-cone\\ngauge. As we naturally \
include the massless modes on the worldsheet, we derive\\nthe full set of \
Bethe-Yang equations. In the massive sector we give also a\\nspin-chain \
description and we write down solutions compatible with crossing for\\nthe \
scalar factors which are not constrained by simmetries. In the second \
part\\nof the thesis we consider the so-called \\\"eta-deformation\\\" of the \
superstring on\\nAdS_5 x S^5. We first discuss the effects of the deformation \
at the level of\\nthe bosonic sigma-model, and we match the tree-level \
worldsheet scattering\\nprocesses to the expansion of the q-deformed \
S-matrix. To identify the missing\\nRamond-Ramond fields we then compute the \
action quadratic in fermions, and we\\nprovide an alternative derivation by \
looking at the kappa-symmetry variations.\\nThe resulting background fields \
do not solve the equations of motion of type\\nIIB supergravity and we \
comment on this.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 10 May 2016 19:57:47 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2016-05-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Borsato\"", ",", "\"Riccardo\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
