               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matthias Wilhelm\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Isak Buhl-Mortensen, Marius de Leeuw, Asger C. Ipsen, \
Charlotte\\n  Kristjansen, Matthias Wilhelm\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"One-loop one-point functions in gauge-gravity dualities \
with defects\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"7 pages, 3 figures, 1 table; v2: shortened, \
regularisation changed,\\n  match with string theory, v3: typo in table \
corrected, title changed to match\\n  journal version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. Lett. 117, 231603 (2016)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1103/PhysRevLett.117.231603\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We initiate the calculation of loop corrections to \
correlation functions in\\n4D defect CFTs. More precisely, we consider N=4 \
SYM with a codimension-one\\ndefect separating two regions of space, x_3>0 \
and x_3<0, where the gauge group\\nis SU(N) and SU(N-k), respectively. This \
set-up is made possible by some of the\\nreal scalar fields acquiring a \
non-vanishing and x_3-dependent vacuum\\nexpectation value for x_3>0. The \
holographic dual is the D3-D5 probe brane\\nsystem where the D5 brane \
geometry is AdS_4 x S^2 and a background gauge field\\nhas k units of flux \
through the S^2. We diagonalise the mass matrix of the\\ndefect CFT making \
use of fuzzy-sphere coordinates and we handle the\\nx_3-dependence of the \
mass terms in the 4D Minkowski space propagators by\\nreformulating these as \
standard massive AdS_4 propagators. Furthermore, we show\\nthat only two \
Feynman diagrams contribute to the one-loop correction to the\\none-point \
function of any single-trace operator and we explicitly calculate\\nthis \
correction in the planar limit for the simplest chiral primary. The \
result\\nof this calculation is compared to an earlier string-theory \
computation in a\\ncertain double-scaling limit, finding perfect agreement. \
Finally, we discuss\\nhow to generalise our calculation to any single-trace \
operator, to finite N and\\nto other types of observables such as Wilson \
loops.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
