               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discover that a certain deformation of the 1+1 \
dimensional Poincare'\\nsuperalgebra is exactly realised in the massless \
sector of the AdS3/CFT2\\nintegrable scattering problem. Deformed \
Poincar\\\\'e superalgebras were\\npreviously noticed to appear in the \
AdS5/CFT4 correspondence - which displays\\nonly massive excitations -, but \
they were there only a partial symmetry. We\\nobtain a representation of the \
boost operator and its coproduct, and show that\\nthe comultiplication \
exactly satisfies the homomorphism property. We present a\\nclassical limit, \
and finally speculate on an analogy with the physics of\\nphonons.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
