               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the large 't Hooft coupling expansion of 1/2 \
BPS Wilson loops in the\\nanti-symmetric representation in $ \\\\mathcal{N}=4 \
$ super Yang-Mills (SYM)\\ntheory at the leading order in the 1/N expansion. \
Via AdS/CFT correspondence,\\nthis expansion corresponds to the $\\\\alpha'$ \
expansion in bulk type IIB string\\ntheory. We show that this expansion can \
be systematically computed by using the\\nlow temperature expansion of Fermi \
distribution function, known as the\\nSommerfeld expansion in statistical \
mechanics. We check numerically that our\\nexpansion agrees with the exact \
result of anti-symmetric Wilson loops recently\\nfound by Fiol and \
Torrents.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
