 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show how to use on-shell unitarity methods to \
calculate renormalization\\ngroup coefficients such as beta functions and \
anomalous dimensions. The central\\nobjects are the form factors of composite \
operators. Their discontinuities can\\nbe calculated via phase-space \
integrals and are related to corresponding\\nanomalous dimensions. In \
particular, we find that the dilatation operator,\\nwhich measures the \
anomalous dimensions, is given by minus the phase of the\\nS-matrix divided \
by pi. We illustrate our method using several examples from\\nYang-Mills \
theory, perturbative QCD and Yukawa theory at one-loop level and\\nbeyond.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
