 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Integrable structure has played a very important role \
in the study of various\\nnon-perturbative aspects of planar ABJM theories. \
In this paper we showed that\\nthis remarkable structure survive after \
orbifold operation with discrete \
group\\n$\\\\Gamma(\\\\simeq\\\\mathbb{Z}_n)<SU(4)_R\\\\times U(1)_b$. For \
general $\\\\Gamma$, we\\nprove the integrability in the scalar sector at the \
planar two-loop order and\\nget the Bethe ansatz equations. The eigenvalues \
of the anomalous dimension\\nmatrix are also obtained. For $\\\\Gamma<SU(4)$, \
two-loop all-sector and all-loop\\nBAEs are proposed. Supersymmetric \
orbifolds are discussed in this framework.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
