               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Magnon-bound-state hierarchy for the two-dimensional \
transverse-field\\n  Ising model in the ordered phase\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Physica A 463, 303 (2016)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/j.physa.2016.07.045\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cond-mat.stat-mech\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the ordered phase for an Ising ferromagnet, the \
magnons are attractive to\\nform a series of bound states with the mass gaps, \
$m_2<m_3 < \\\\dots$. Each ratio\\n$m_{2,3,\\\\dots}/m_1$ ($m_1$: the \
single-magnon mass) is expected to be a\\nuniversal constant in the vicinity \
of the critical point. In this paper, we\\ndevote ourselves to the \
$(2+1)$-dimensional counterpart, for which the\\nuniversal hierarchical \
character remains unclear. We employed the exact\\ndiagonalization method, \
which enables us to calculate the dynamical\\nsusceptibility via the \
continued-fraction expansion. Thereby, we observe a\\nvariety of signals \
including $m_{2,3,4}$, and the spectrum is analyzed with \
the\\nfinite-size-scaling method to estimate the universal mass-gap \
ratios.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 30 Jul 2016 06:47:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2017-03-03\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Nishiyama\"", ",", "\"Yoshihiro\"", ",", "\"\"", ",", 
                    "\"Okayama university\""}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 
