               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This is an introductory review to localization \
techniques in supersymmetric\\ntwo-dimensional gauge theories. In particular \
we describe how to construct\\nLagrangians of N=(2,2) theories on curved \
spaces, and how to compute their\\npartition functions and certain \
correlators on the sphere, the hemisphere and\\nother curved backgrounds. We \
also describe how to evaluate the partition\\nfunction of N=(0,2) theories on \
the torus, known as the elliptic genus. Finally\\nwe summarize some of the \
applications, in particular to probe mirror symmetry\\nand other \
non-perturbative dualities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
