            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1608.02956\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"David R. Morrison\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"David R. Morrison\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gromov-Witten invariants and localization\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"This is a contribution to the review volume `Localization \
techniques\\n  in quantum field theories' (eds. V. Pestun and M. Zabzine): \
arXiv:1608.02952\\n  and at https://arxiv.org/src/1608.02952/anc/LocQFT.pdf \
or\\n  http://pestun.ihes.fr/pages/LocalizationReview/LocQFT.pdf This article\
\\n  reviews portions of hep-th/9412236, hep-th/9508107, arXiv:1208.6244,\\n  \
arXiv:1305.3278, arXiv:1308.2157, and arXiv:1509.08511\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/aa6f65\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give a pedagogical review of the computation of \
Gromov-Witten invariants\\nvia localization in 2D gauged linear sigma models. \
We explain the relationship\\nbetween the two-sphere partition function of \
the theory and the Kahler\\npotential on the conformal manifold. We show how \
the Kahler potential can be\\nassembled from classical, perturbative, and \
non-perturbative contributions, and\\nexplain how the non-perturbative \
contributions are related to the Gromov-Witten\\ninvariants of the \
corresponding Calabi-Yau manifold. We then explain how\\nlocalization enables \
efficient calculation of the two-sphere partition function\\nand, ultimately, \
the Gromov-Witten invariants themselves.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
