            "Brian Willett", "title" -> 
            "Localization on three-dimensional manifolds", "comments" -> 
            "This is a contribution to the review volume `Localization \
techniques\n  in quantum field theories' (eds. V. Pestun and M. Zabzine) \
which contains 17\n  Chapters. The complete volume is summarized in \
arXiv:1608.02952 and it can be\n  downloaded at \
https://arxiv.org/src/1608.02952/anc/LocQFT.pdf or\n  \
http://pestun.ihes.fr/pages/LocalizationReview/LocQFT.pdf", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8121/aa612f", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this review article we describe the localization of three \
dimensional N=2\nsupersymmetric theories on compact manifolds, including the \
squashed sphere,\nS^3_b, the lens space, S^3_b/Z_p, and S^2 x S^1. We \
describe how to write\nsupersymmetric actions on these spaces, and then \
compute the partition\nfunctions and other supersymmetric observables by \
employing the localization\nargument. We briefly survey some applications of \
these computations.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
