           "id" -> "1608.02960", "submitter" -> "Silviu S. Pufu", "authors" -> 
            "Silviu S. Pufu", "title" -> "The F-Theorem and F-Maximization", 
            "comments" -> 
            "This is a contribution to the review volume `Localization \
techniques\n  in quantum field theories' (eds. V. Pestun and M. Zabzine) \
which contains 17\n  Chapters. The complete volume is summarized in \
arXiv:1608.02952 and it can be\n  downloaded at \
https://arxiv.org/src/1608.02952/anc/LocQFT.pdf or\n  \
http://pestun.ihes.fr/pages/LocalizationReview/LocQFT.pdf", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8121/aa6765", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This contribution contains a review of the role of the \
three-sphere free\nenergy F in recent developments related to the F-theorem \
and F-maximization.\nThe F-theorem states that for any Lorentz-invariant RG \
trajectory connecting a\nconformal field theory CFT_UV in the ultraviolet to \
a conformal field theory\nCFT_IR, the F-coefficient decreases: F_UV > F_IR. I \
provide many examples of\nCFTs where one can compute F, approximately or \
exactly, and discuss various\nchecks of the F-theorem. F-maximization is the \
principle that in an N=2 SCFT,\nviewed as the deep IR limit of an RG \
trajectory preserving N=2 supersymmetry,\nthe superconformal R-symmetry \
maximizes F within the set of all R-symmetries\npreserved by the RG \
trajectory. I review the derivation of this result and\nprovide examples.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 9 Aug 2016 20:01:45 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 14 Aug 2016 14:22:21 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 15 Oct 2016 17:58:46 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-10-25", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Pufu", "Silviu S.", ""}}}], 
