               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present an elementary review of some aspects of \
Chern-Simons theory with\\ncomplex gauge group SL(N,C). We discuss some of \
the challenges in defining the\\ntheory as a full-fledged TQFT, as well as \
some successes inspired by the 3d-3d\\ncorrespondence. The 3d-3d \
correspondence relates partition functions (and other\\naspects) of complex \
Chern-Simons theory on a 3-manifold M to supersymmetric\\npartition functions \
(and other observables) in an associated 3d theory T[M].\\nMany of these \
observables may be computed by supersymmetric localization. We\\npresent \
several prominent applications to 3-manifold topology and number theory\\nin \
light of the 3d-3d correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
