http://pestun.ihes.fr/pages/LocalizationReview/LocQFT.pdf v4: a reference\\n  \
corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/aa5df8\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"IPMU-16-0048\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  An elementary introduction to the 2d/4d correspondences \
is given. After\\nquickly reviewing the 2d q-deformed Yang-Mills theory and \
the Liouville theory,\\nwe will introduce 4d theories obtained by coupling \
trifundamentals to SU(2)\\ngauge fields. We will then see concretely that the \
supersymmetric partition\\nfunction of these theories on S^3 x S^1 and on S^4 \
is given respectively by the\\nq-deformed Yang-Mills theory and the Liouville \
theory. After giving a short\\ndiscussion on how this correspondence may be \
understood from the viewpoint of\\nthe 6d N=(2,0) theory, we conclude the \
review by enumerating future directions.\\nMost of the technical points will \
be referred to more detailed review articles.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
