        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{12.900883554879746`, -7.660834909161286}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1608.02967\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Joseph A. Minahan\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Joseph A. Minahan\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matrix models for 5d super Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"This is a contribution to the review volume `Localization \
techniques\\n  in quantum field theories' (eds. V. Pestun and M. Zabzine) \
which contains 17\\n  Chapters. The complete volume is summarized in \
arXiv:1608.02952 and it can be\\n  downloaded at \
https://arxiv.org/src/1608.02952/anc/LocQFT.pdf or\\n  \
http://pestun.ihes.fr/pages/LocalizationReview/LocQFT.pdf\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/aa5cbe\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this contribution to the review on localization in \
gauge theories we\\ninvestigate the matrix models derived from localizing N=1 \
super Yang-Mills on\\nS^5. We consider the large-N limit and attempt to solve \
the matrix model by a\\nsaddle-point approximation. In general it is not \
possible to find an analytic\\nsolution, but at the weak and the strong \
limits of the 't Hooft coupling there\\nare dramatic simplifications that \
allows us to extract most of the interesting\\ninformation. At weak coupling \
we show that the matrix model is close to the\\nGaussian matrix model and \
that the free-energy scales as N^2. At strong\\ncoupling we show that if the \
theory contains one adjoint hypermultiplet then\\nthe free-energy scales as \
N^3. We also find the expectation value of a\\nsupersymmetric Wilson loop \
that wraps the equator. We demonstrate how to\\nextract the effective \
couplings and reproduce results of Seiberg. Finally, we\\ncompare to results \
for the six-dimensional (2,0) theory derived using the\\nAdS/CFT \
correspondence. We show that by choosing the hypermultiplet mass such\\nthat \
the supersymmetry is enhanced to N=2, the Wilson loop result matches \
the\\nanalogous calculation using AdS/CFT. The free-energies differ by a \
rational\\nfraction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 9 Aug 2016 20:01:52 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 14 Aug 2016 14:22:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
