         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1608.02967", "submitter" -> "Joseph A. Minahan", 
            "authors" -> "Joseph A. Minahan", "title" -> 
            "Matrix models for 5d super Yang-Mills", "comments" -> 
            "This is a contribution to the review volume `Localization \
techniques\n  in quantum field theories' (eds. V. Pestun and M. Zabzine) \
which contains 17\n  Chapters. The complete volume is summarized in \
arXiv:1608.02952 and it can be\n  downloaded at \
https://arxiv.org/src/1608.02952/anc/LocQFT.pdf or\n  \
http://pestun.ihes.fr/pages/LocalizationReview/LocQFT.pdf", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8121/aa5cbe", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this contribution to the review on localization in gauge \
theories we\ninvestigate the matrix models derived from localizing N=1 super \
Yang-Mills on\nS^5. We consider the large-N limit and attempt to solve the \
matrix model by a\nsaddle-point approximation. In general it is not possible \
to find an analytic\nsolution, but at the weak and the strong limits of the \
't Hooft coupling there\nare dramatic simplifications that allows us to \
extract most of the interesting\ninformation. At weak coupling we show that \
the matrix model is close to the\nGaussian matrix model and that the \
free-energy scales as N^2. At strong\ncoupling we show that if the theory \
contains one adjoint hypermultiplet then\nthe free-energy scales as N^3. We \
also find the expectation value of a\nsupersymmetric Wilson loop that wraps \
the equator. We demonstrate how to\nextract the effective couplings and \
reproduce results of Seiberg. Finally, we\ncompare to results for the \
six-dimensional (2,0) theory derived using the\nAdS/CFT correspondence. We \
show that by choosing the hypermultiplet mass such\nthat the supersymmetry is \
enhanced to N=2, the Wilson loop result matches the\nanalogous calculation \
using AdS/CFT. The free-energies differ by a rational\nfraction.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 9 Aug 2016 20:01:52 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 14 Aug 2016 14:22:54 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 15 Oct 2016 17:43:13 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-10-25", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Minahan", "Joseph A.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
