            "Flavour singlets in gauge theory as Permutations", "comments" -> 
            "50 pages, v2: typos corrected, v3: to appear in JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP12(2016)142", 
            "report-no" -> "OIQP-16-03, QMUL-PH-16-15", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math.RT", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Gauge-invariant operators can be specified by equivalence \
classes of\npermutations. We develop this idea concretely for the singlets of \
the flavour\ngroup $SO(N_f)$ in $U(N_c)$ gauge theory by using Gelfand pairs \
and Schur-Weyl\nduality. The singlet operators, when specialised at $N_f =6$, \
belong to the\nscalar sector of ${\\cal N}=4$ SYM. A simple formula is given \
for the two-point\nfunctions in the free field limit of $g_{YM}^2 =0$. The \
free two-point\nfunctions are shown to be equal to the partition function on \
a 2-complex with\nboundaries and a defect, in a topological field theory of \
permutations. The\npermutation equivalence classes are Fourier transformed to \
a representation\nbasis which is orthogonal for the two-point functions at \
finite $N_c , N_f$.\nCounting formulae for the gauge-invariant operators are \
described. The one-loop\nmixing matrix is derived as a linear operator on the \
permutation equivalence\nclasses.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 10 Aug 2016 14:31:53 GMT"}, {
