            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1608.03570\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Riccardo Borsato\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riccardo Borsato and Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Target space supergeometry of $\\\\eta$ and \
$\\\\lambda$-deformed strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages. Remarks of referee addressed: references and \
comments\\n  added. Published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2016)045\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-LW-2016-03\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the integrable $\\\\eta$ and \
$\\\\lambda$-deformations of supercoset\\nstring sigma models, the basic \
example being the deformation of the $AdS_5\\n\\\\times S^5$ superstring. We \
prove that the kappa symmetry variations for these\\nmodels are of the \
standard Green-Schwarz form, and we determine the target\\nspace \
supergeometry by computing the superspace torsion. We check that \
the\\n$\\\\lambda$-deformation gives rise to a standard (generically type \
II*)\\nsupergravity background; for the $\\\\eta$-model the requirement that \
the target\\nspace is a supergravity solution translates into a simple \
condition on the\\nR-matrix which enters the definition of the deformation. \
We further construct\\nall such non-abelian R-matrices of rank four which \
solve the homogeneous\\nclassical Yang-Baxter equation for the algebra \
so(2,4). We argue that the\\ncorresponding backgrounds are equivalent to \
sequences of non-commuting\\nTsT-transformations, and verify this explicitly \
for some of the examples.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 11 Aug 2016 19:14:21 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 1 Sep 2016 12:47:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 10 Oct 2016 14:16:47 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
