            "Riccardo Borsato and Linus Wulff", "title" -> 
            "Target space supergeometry of $\\eta$ and $\\lambda$-deformed \
strings", "comments" -> 
            "32 pages. Remarks of referee addressed: references and comments\n\
  added. Published version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2016)045", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-LW-2016-03", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the integrable $\\eta$ and $\\lambda$-deformations of \
supercoset\nstring sigma models, the basic example being the deformation of \
the $AdS_5\n\\times S^5$ superstring. We prove that the kappa symmetry \
variations for these\nmodels are of the standard Green-Schwarz form, and we \
determine the target\nspace supergeometry by computing the superspace \
torsion. We check that the\n$\\lambda$-deformation gives rise to a standard \
(generically type II*)\nsupergravity background; for the $\\eta$-model the \
requirement that the target\nspace is a supergravity solution translates into \
a simple condition on the\nR-matrix which enters the definition of the \
deformation. We further construct\nall such non-abelian R-matrices of rank \
four which solve the homogeneous\nclassical Yang-Baxter equation for the \
algebra so(2,4). We argue that the\ncorresponding backgrounds are equivalent \
to sequences of non-commuting\nTsT-transformations, and verify this \
explicitly for some of the examples.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
