           "id" -> "1608.05126", "submitter" -> "Pedro Liendo", "authors" -> 
            "Pedro Liendo, Carlo Meneghelli", "title" -> 
            "Bootstrap equations for $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM with defects", 
            "comments" -> 
            "44 pages, 2 figures, v3: typos fixed, to appear in JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP01(2017)122", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This paper focuses on the analysis of $4d$ $\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
superconformal\ntheories in the presence of a defect from the point of view \
of the conformal\nbootstrap. We will concentrate first on the case of \
codimension one, where the\ndefect is a boundary that preserves half of the \
supersymmetry. After studying\nthe constraints imposed by supersymmetry, we \
will obtain the Ward identities\nassociated to two-point functions of \
$\\tfrac{1}{2}$-BPS operators and write\ntheir solution as a superconformal \
block expansion. Due to a surprising\nconnection between spacetime and \
R-symmetry conformal blocks, our results not\nonly apply to $4d$ \
$\\mathcal{N}=4$ superconformal theories with a boundary, but\nalso to three \
more systems that have the same symmetry algebra: $4d$\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
superconformal theories with a line defect, $3d$\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
superconformal theories with no defect, and $OSP(4^*|4)$\nsuperconformal \
quantum mechanics. The superconformal algebra implies that all\nthese systems \
possess a closed subsector of operators in which the bootstrap\nequations \
become polynomial constraints on the CFT data. We derive these\ntruncated \
equations and initiate the study of their solutions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
