                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We update the ingredients of the Gaussian streaming \
model (GSM) for the\\nredshift-space clustering of biased tracers using the \
techniques of Lagrangian\\nperturbation theory, effective field theory (EFT) \
and a generalized Lagrangian\\nbias expansion. After relating the GSM to the \
cumulant expansion, we present\\nnew results for the real-space correlation \
function, mean pairwise velocity and\\npairwise velocity dispersion including \
counter terms from EFT and bias terms\\nthrough third order in the linear \
density, its leading derivatives and its\\nshear up to second order. We \
discuss the connection to the Gaussian peaks\\nformalism. We compare the \
ingredients of the GSM to a suite of large N-body\\nsimulations, and show the \
performance of the theory on the low order multipoles\\nof the redshift-space \
correlation function and power spectrum. We highlight the\\nimportance of a \
general biasing scheme, which we find to be as important as\\nhigher-order \
corrections due to non-linear evolution for the halos we consider\\non the \
scales of interest to us.\\n\""}]}, {
