performance of the theory on the low order multipoles\nof the redshift-space \
correlation function and power spectrum. We highlight the\nimportance of a \
general biasing scheme, which we find to be as important as\nhigher-order \
corrections due to non-linear evolution for the halos we consider\non the \
scales of interest to us.\n", 
