                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The purpose of this contribution is to initiate the \
study of integrable\\ndeformations for different superstring theory \
formalisms that manifest the\\nproperty of (classical) integrability. In this \
paper we choose the hybrid\\nformalism of the superstring in the background \
AdS_{2}xS^{2} and explore in\\ndetail the most immediate consequences of its \
lambda-deformation. The resulting\\naction functional corresponds to the \
lambda-model of the matter part of the\\nfairly more sophisticated pure \
spinor formalism, which is also known to be\\nclassical integrable. In \
particular, the deformation preserves the\\nintegrability and the one-loop \
conformal invariance of its parent theory, hence\\nbeing a marginal \
deformation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
