               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rajesh Gupta\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Justin R. David, Edi Gava, Rajesh Kumar Gupta, Kumar \
Narain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Localization on $AdS_2\\\\times S^1$\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"28 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2017)050\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Conformal symmetry relates the metric on $AdS_2 \
\\\\times S^{1}$ to that of\\n$S^3$. This implies that under a suitable \
choice of boundary conditions for\\nfields on $AdS_2$ the partition function \
of conformal field theories on these\\nspaces must agree which makes $AdS_2 \
\\\\times S^{1}$ a good testing ground to\\nstudy localization on non-compact \
spaces. We study supersymmetry on\\n$AdS_2\\\\times S^1$ and determine the \
localizing Lagrangian for ${\\\\cal N}=2$\\nsupersymmetric Chern-Simons \
theory on $AdS_2\\\\times S^1$. We evaluate the\\npartition function of \
${\\\\cal N}=2$ supersymmetric Chern-Simons theory on $AdS_2\\n\\\\times S^1$ \
using localization, where the radius of $S^1$ is $q$ times that of\\n$AdS_2$. \
With boundary conditions on $AdS_2\\\\times S^1$ which ensure that all\\nthe \
physical fields are normalizable and lie in the space of square \
integrable\\nwave functions in $AdS_2$, the result for the partition function \
precisely\\nagrees with that of the theory on the $q$-fold covering of $S^3$.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
