            "Justin R. David, Edi Gava, Rajesh Kumar Gupta, Kumar Narain", 
            "title" -> "Localization on $AdS_2\\times S^1$", "comments" -> 
            "28 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP03(2017)050", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Conformal symmetry relates the metric on $AdS_2 \\times S^{1}$ \
to that of\n$S^3$. This implies that under a suitable choice of boundary \
conditions for\nfields on $AdS_2$ the partition function of conformal field \
theories on these\nspaces must agree which makes $AdS_2 \\times S^{1}$ a good \
testing ground to\nstudy localization on non-compact spaces. We study \
supersymmetry on\n$AdS_2\\times S^1$ and determine the localizing Lagrangian \
for ${\\cal N}=2$\nsupersymmetric Chern-Simons theory on $AdS_2\\times S^1$. \
We evaluate the\npartition function of ${\\cal N}=2$ supersymmetric \
Chern-Simons theory on $AdS_2\n\\times S^1$ using localization, where the \
radius of $S^1$ is $q$ times that of\n$AdS_2$. With boundary conditions on \
$AdS_2\\times S^1$ which ensure that all\nthe physical fields are \
normalizable and lie in the space of square integrable\nwave functions in \
$AdS_2$, the result for the partition function precisely\nagrees with that of \
the theory on the $q$-fold covering of $S^3$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
