            "authors" -> "Mykola Dedushenko, Silviu S. Pufu, and Ran Yacoby", 
            "title" -> "A one-dimensional theory for Higgs branch operators", 
            "comments" -> 
            "108 pages; v2: typos corrected, some statements clarified", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "CALT-TH 2016-029, PUPT-2509", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We use supersymmetric localization to calculate correlation \
functions of\nhalf-BPS local operators in 3d ${\\cal N} = 4$ superconformal \
field theories\nwhose Lagrangian descriptions consist of vectormultiplets \
coupled to\nhypermultiplets. The operators we primarily study are certain \
twisted linear\ncombinations of Higgs branch operators that can be inserted \
anywhere along a\ngiven line. These operators are constructed from the \
hypermultiplet scalars.\nThey form a one-dimensional non-commutative operator \
algebra with topological\ncorrelation functions. The 2- and 3-point functions \
of Higgs branch operators\nin the full 3d ${\\cal N}=4$ theory can be simply \
inferred from the 1d\ntopological algebra. After conformally mapping the 3d \
superconformal field\ntheory from flat space to a round three-sphere, we \
preform supersymmetric\nlocalization using a supercharge that does not belong \
to any 3d ${\\cal N} = 2$\nsubalgebra of the ${\\cal N}=4$ algebra. The \
result is a simple model that can\nbe used to calculate correlation functions \
in the 1d topological algebra\nmentioned above. This model is a 1d Gaussian \
theory coupled to a matrix model,\nand it can be viewed as a gauge-fixed \
version of a topological gauged quantum\nmechanics. Our results generalize to \
non-conformal theories on $S^3$ that\ncontain real mass and Fayet-Iliopolous \
parameters. We also provide partial\nresults in the 1d topological algebra \
associated with the Coulomb branch, where\nwe calculate correlation functions \
of local operators built from the\nvectormultiplet scalars.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
