                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We test the holographic relation between the vacuum \
expectation values of\\ngauge invariant operators in ${\\\\cal N} = 6$ \
${\\\\rm U}_k(N)\\\\times {\\\\rm\\nU}_{-k}(N)$ mass-deformed ABJM theory and \
the LLM geometries with\\n$\\\\mathbb{Z}_k$ orbifold in 11-dimensional \
supergravity. To do that, we apply\\nthe Kaluza-Klein reduction to construct \
a 4-dimensional gravity theory and\\nimplement the holographic \
renormalization procedure. We obtain an exact\\nholographic relation for the \
vacuum expectation values of the chiral primary\\noperator with conformal \
dimension $\\\\Delta = 1$, which is given by $\\\\langle\\n{\\\\cal \
O}^{(\\\\Delta=1)}\\\\rangle= N^{\\\\frac32} \\\\, f_{(\\\\Delta=1)}$, for \
large $N$ and\\n$k=1$. Here factor $f_{(\\\\Delta)}$ is independent of $N$. \
Our results involve\\ninfinite number of exact dual relations for all \
possible supersymmetric Higgs\\nvacua and so provide a nontrivial test of \
gauge/gravity duality away from the\\nconformal fixed point. We also extend \
our results to the case of $k\\\\ne 1$ for\\nLLM geometries represented by \
rectangular-shaped Young-diagrams.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
