U}_k(N)\\times {\\rm\nU}_{-k}(N)$ mass-deformed ABJM theory and the LLM \
geometries with\n$\\mathbb{Z}_k$ orbifold in 11-dimensional supergravity. To \
do that, we apply\nthe Kaluza-Klein reduction to construct a 4-dimensional \
gravity theory and\nimplement the holographic renormalization procedure. We \
obtain an exact\nholographic relation for the vacuum expectation values of \
the chiral primary\noperator with conformal dimension $\\Delta = 1$, which is \
given by $\\langle\n{\\cal O}^{(\\Delta=1)}\\rangle= N^{\\frac32} \\, \
f_{(\\Delta=1)}$, for large $N$ and\n$k=1$. Here factor $f_{(\\Delta)}$ is \
independent of $N$. Our results involve\ninfinite number of exact dual \
relations for all possible supersymmetric Higgs\nvacua and so provide a \
nontrivial test of gauge/gravity duality away from the\nconformal fixed \
point. We also extend our results to the case of $k\\ne 1$ for\nLLM \
geometries represented by rectangular-shaped Young-diagrams.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 5 Oct 2016 15:56:58 GMT"}, {
