                 "\"Quantization of the ${\\\\rm AdS}_3$ Superparticle on \
${\\\\rm\\n  OSP}(1|2)^2/{\\\\rm SL}(2,\\\\mathbb{R})$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25+1 pages; v2: minor changes, references added and \
updated; v3:\\n  minor changes, one reference added, matches published \
version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B915 (2017) 44-68\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2016.11.018\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"FU-Ph 10/2016 (06), NORDITA-2016-100, ZMP-HH/16-22\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze ${\\\\rm AdS}_3$ superparticle dynamics on \
the coset ${\\\\rm OSP}(1|2)\\n\\\\times {\\\\rm OSP}(1|2)/{\\\\rm \
SL}(2,\\\\mathbb{R})$. The system is quantized in\\ncanonical coordinates \
obtained by gauge invariant Hamiltonian reduction. The\\nleft and right \
Noether charges of a massive particle are parametrized by\\ncoadjoint orbits \
of a timelike element of $\\\\frak{osp}(1|2)$. Each chiral sector\\nis \
described by two bosonic and two fermionic canonical \
coordinates\\ncorresponding to a superparticle with superpotential $W=q-m/q$, \
where $m$ is\\nthe particle mass. Canonical quantization then provides a \
quantum realization\\nof $\\\\frak{osp}(1|2)\\\\oplus\\\\frak{osp}(1|2)$. For \
the massless particle the chiral\\ncharges lie on the coadjoint orbit of a \
nilpotent element of $\\\\frak{osp}(1|2)$\\nand each of them depends only on \
one real fermion, which demonstrates the\\nunderlying $\\\\kappa$-symmetry. \
These remaining left and right fermionic\\nvariables form a canonical pair \
and the system is described by four bosonic and\\ntwo fermionic canonical \
coordinates. Due to conformal invariance of the\\nmassless particle, the \
$\\\\frak{osp}(1|2)\\\\oplus\\\\frak{osp} (1|2)$ extends to \
the\\ncorresponding superconformal algebra $\\\\frak{osp}(2|4)$. Its 19 \
charges are\\ngiven by all real quadratic combinations of the canonical \
coordinates, which\\ntrivializes their quantization.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
