            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We analyze ${\\rm AdS}_3$ superparticle dynamics on the coset \
${\\rm OSP}(1|2)\n\\times {\\rm OSP}(1|2)/{\\rm SL}(2,\\mathbb{R})$. The \
system is quantized in\ncanonical coordinates obtained by gauge invariant \
Hamiltonian reduction. The\nleft and right Noether charges of a massive \
particle are parametrized by\ncoadjoint orbits of a timelike element of \
$\\frak{osp}(1|2)$. Each chiral sector\nis described by two bosonic and two \
fermionic canonical coordinates\ncorresponding to a superparticle with \
superpotential $W=q-m/q$, where $m$ is\nthe particle mass. Canonical \
quantization then provides a quantum realization\nof $\\frak{osp}(1|2)\\oplus\
\\frak{osp}(1|2)$. For the massless particle the chiral\ncharges lie on the \
coadjoint orbit of a nilpotent element of $\\frak{osp}(1|2)$\nand each of \
them depends only on one real fermion, which demonstrates the\nunderlying \
$\\kappa$-symmetry. These remaining left and right fermionic\nvariables form \
a canonical pair and the system is described by four bosonic and\ntwo \
fermionic canonical coordinates. Due to conformal invariance of the\nmassless \
particle, the $\\frak{osp}(1|2)\\oplus\\frak{osp} (1|2)$ extends to the\n\
corresponding superconformal algebra $\\frak{osp}(2|4)$. Its 19 charges are\n\
given by all real quadratic combinations of the canonical coordinates, which\n\
trivializes their quantization.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
