         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1610.05659", "submitter" -> "Dario Rosa", "authors" -> 
            "Dario Rosa", "title" -> 
            "The coupling of Poisson sigma models to topological backgrounds",
             "comments" -> 
            "31 pages; v2: typos fixed, references added, version to appear \
in\n  JHEP", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP12(2016)043", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP math.SG", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We extend the coupling to the topological backgrounds, \
recently worked out\nfor the 2-dimensional BF-model, to the most general \
Poisson sigma models. The\ncoupling involves the choice of a Casimir function \
on the target manifold and\nmodifies the BRST transformations. This in turn \
induces a change in the BRST\ncohomology of the resulting theory. The \
observables of the coupled theory are\nanalyzed and their geometrical \
interpretation is given. We finally couple the\ntheory to 2-dimensional \
topological gravity: this is the first step to study a\ntopological string \
theory in propagation on a Poisson manifold. As an\napplication, we show that \
the gauge-fixed vectorial supersymmetry of the\nPoisson sigma models has a \
natural explanation in terms of the theory coupled\nto topological gravity.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 17 Oct 2016 02:09:21 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 13 Dec 2016 02:16:32 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-02-01", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Rosa", "Dario", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
