               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Coset construction of AdS particle dynamics\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21+1 pages; v2: typos corrected, references updated; v3: \
minor\\n  changes, matches published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Math.Phys. 58 (2017) no.1, 012301\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1063/1.4974322\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"FU-Ph 10/2016 (07), NORDITA-2016-110, ZMP-HH/16-24\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"  We analyze dynamics of the AdS$_{N+1}$ particle \
realized on the coset\\nSO$(2,N)/$SO$(1,N)$. Hamiltonian reduction provides \
the physical phase space in\\nterms of the coadjoint orbit obtained by \
boosting a timelike element of ${\\\\frak\\nso}(2,N)$. We show equivalence of \
this approach to geometric quantization and\\nto the SO$(N)$ covariant \
oscillator description, for which the boost generators\\nentail a complicated \
operator ordering. As an alternative scheme, we introduce\\ndual oscillator \
variables and derive their algebra at the classical and the\\nquantum level. \
This simplifies the calculations of the commutators for the\\nboost \
generators and leads to unitary irreducible representations of \
${\\\\frak\\nso}(2,N)$ for all admissible values of the mass parameter. We \
furthermore\\ndiscuss an SO$(N)$ covariant supersymmetric extensions of the \
oscillator\\nquantization, with its realization for superparticles in AdS$_2$ \
and AdS$_3$\\ngiven by recent works.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
