 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the scalar products between Bethe states in \
the XXZ spin chain with\\nanisotropy $|\\\\Delta|>1$ in the semi-classical \
limit where the length of the\\nspin chain and the number of magnons tend to \
infinity with their ratio kept\\nfinite and fixed. Our method is a natural \
yet non-trivial generalization of\\nsimilar methods developed for the XXX \
spin chain. The final result can be\\nwritten in a compact form as a contour \
integral in terms of Faddeev's quantum\\ndilogarithm function, which in the \
isotropic limit reduces to the classical\\ndilogarithm function.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
