               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1611.00380\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Lorenzo Di Pietro\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lorenzo Di Pietro, Masazumi Honda\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Cardy Formula for 4d SUSY Theories and \
Localization\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"43 pages, v2: references added, changed slightly \
discussion in\\n  section 5\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2017)055\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study 4d $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ supersymmetric theories \
on a compact Euclidean\\nmanifold of the form $S^1 \
\\\\times\\\\mathcal{M}_3$. Partition functions of gauge\\ntheories on this \
background can be computed using localization, and explicit\\nformulas have \
been derived for different choices of the compact \
manifold\\n$\\\\mathcal{M}_3$. Taking the limit of shrinking $S^1$, we \
present a general\\nformula for the limit of the localization integrand, \
derived by simple\\neffective theory considerations, generalizing the result \
of arXiv:1512.03376.\\nThe limit is given in terms of an effective potential \
for the holonomies around\\nthe $S^1$, whose minima determine the asymptotic \
behavior of the partition\\nfunction. If the potential is minimized in the \
origin, where it vanishes, the\\npartition function has a Cardy-like behavior \
fixed by $\\\\mathrm{Tr}(R)$, while a\\nnontrivial minimum gives a shift in \
the coefficient. In all the examples that\\nwe consider, the origin is a \
minimum if $\\\\mathrm{Tr}(R) \\\\leq 0$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
