                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study four-dimensional N=1, 2 superconformal theory \
in class S obtained by\\ncompactifying the 6d N=(2, 0) theory on a Riemann \
surface C with\\nouter-automorphism twist lines. From the pair-of-pants \
decompositions C we find\\nvarious dual descriptions for the same theory \
having distinct gauge groups. We\\nshow that the various configurations of \
the twist line give rise to dual\\ndescriptions for the identical theory. We \
compute the 't Hooft anomaly\\ncoefficients and the superconformal indices to \
test dualities. Surprisingly, we\\nfind that the class S theories with twist \
lines wrapping 1-cycles of C have the\\nidentical 't Hooft anomalies as the \
ones without the twist line, whereas the\\nsuperconformal indices differ. \
This provides a set of examples where the\\nanomaly matching is insufficient \
to test dualities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
