 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore the connection between the process of \
relaxation in the BMN matrix\\nmodel and the physics of black holes in \
AdS/CFT. Focusing on Dyson-fluid\\nsolutions of the matrix model, we perform \
numerical simulations of the real\\ntime dynamics of the system. By quenching \
the equilibrium distribution we study\\nthe quasi-normal oscillations of \
scalar single trace observables, we isolate\\nthe lowest quasi-normal mode, \
and we determine its frequencies as function of\\nthe energy. Considering the \
BMN matrix model as a truncation of $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$\\nSYM, we also compute \
the frequencies of the quasi-normal modes of the dual\\nscalar fields in the \
AdS$_5$-Schwarzschild background. We compare the results,\\nand we find a \
surprising similarity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
