            "  We discuss the quantization of non-ultralocal integrable \
models directly in\nthe continuous case, using the example of the \
Alday-Arutyunov-Frolov model. We\nshow that by treating fields as \
distributions and regularizing the operator\nproduct, it is possible to avoid \
all the singularities, and allow to obtain\nresults consistent with \
