                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct 4D $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ theories on an \
infinite family of 4D toric\\nmanifolds with the topology of connected sums \
of $S^2 \\\\times S^2$. These\\ntheories are constructed through the \
dimensional reduction along a non-trivial\\n$U(1)$-fiber of 5D theories on \
toric Sasaki-Einstein manifolds. We discuss the\\nconditions under which such \
reductions can be carried out and give a partial\\nclassification result of \
the resulting 4D manifolds. We calculate the partition\\nfunctions of these \
4D theories and they involve both instanton and\\nanti-instanton \
contributions, thus generalizing Pestun's famous result on\\n$S^4$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
