            "  We explore systems with a large number of fermionic degrees of \
freedom\nsubject to non-local interactions. We study both vector and \
matrix-like models\nwith quartic interactions. The exact thermal partition \
function is expressed in\nterms of an ordinary bosonic integral, which has an \
eigenvalue repulsion term\nin the matrix case. We calculate real time \
correlations at finite temperature\nand analyze the thermal phase structure. \
When possible, calculations are\nperformed in both the original Hilbert space \
as well as the bosonic picture,\nand the exact map between the two is \
explained. At large $N$, there is a phase\ntransition to a highly entropic \
high temperature phase from a low temperature\nlow entropy phase. Thermal \
two-point functions decay in time in the high\ntemperature phase.\n", 
