               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Intersecting Surface Defects and Instanton Partition \
Functions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"66 pages; v2: minor typos corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2017)073\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze intersecting surface defects inserted in \
interacting\\nfour-dimensional N = 2 supersymmetric quantum field theories. \
We employ the\\nrealization of a class of such systems as the infrared fixed \
points of\\nrenormalization group flows from larger theories, triggered by \
perturbed\\nSeiberg-Witten monopole-like configurations, to compute their \
partition\\nfunctions. These results are cast into the form of a partition \
function of\\n4d/2d/0d coupled systems. Our computations provide concrete \
expressions for the\\ninstanton partition function in the presence of \
intersecting defects and we\\nstudy the corresponding ADHM model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
