               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study tree level one-point functions of \
non-protected scalar operators in\\nthe defect CFT, based on N=4 SYM, which \
is dual to the SO(5) symmetric D3-D7\\nprobe brane system with non-vanishing \
instanton number. Whereas symmetries\\nprevent operators from the SU(2) and \
SU(3) sub-sectors from having\\nnon-vanishing one-point functions, more \
general scalar conformal operators,\\nwhich in particular constitute Bethe \
eigenstates of the integrable SO(6) spin\\nchain, are allowed to have \
non-trivial one-point functions. For a series of\\noperators with a small \
number of excitations we find closed expressions in\\nterms of Bethe roots \
for these one-point functions, valid for any value of the\\ninstanton number. \
In addition, we present some numerical results for operators\\nwith more \
excitations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
