            "  Utilizing an exhaustive set of simplified models, we revisit \
dark matter\nscenarios potentially capable of generating the observed \
Galactic Center\ngamma-ray excess, updating constraints from the LUX and \
PandaX-II experiments,\nas well as from the LHC and other colliders. We \
identify a variety of\npseudoscalar mediated models that remain consistent \
with all constraints. In\ncontrast, dark matter candidates which annihilate \
through a spin-1 mediator are\nruled out by direct detection constraints \
unless the mass of the mediator is\nnear an annihilation resonance, or the \
mediator has a purely vector coupling to\nthe dark matter and a purely axial \
coupling to Standard Model fermions. All\nscenarios in which the dark matter \
annihilates through $t$-channel processes\nare now ruled out by a combination \
of the constraints from LUX/PandaX-II and\nthe LHC.\n", 
