 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We extend our previous work (on $D=2$) to give an exact \
solution of the\\n$\\\\Phi^3_D$ large-$\\\\mathcal{N}$ matrix model (or \
renormalised Kontsevich model)\\nin $D=4$ and $D=6$ dimensions. Induction \
proofs and the difficult combinatorics\\nare unchanged compared with $D=2$, \
but the renormalisation - performed\\naccording to Zimmermann - is much more \
involved. As main result we prove that\\nthe Schwinger 2-point function \
resulting from the $\\\\Phi^3_D$-QFT model on Moyal\\nspace satisfies, for \
real coupling constant, reflection positivity in $D=4$ and\\n$D=6$ \
dimensions. The K\\\\\\\"all\\\\'en-Lehmann mass spectrum of the \
associated\\nWightman 2-point function describes a scattering part $|p|^2 \
\\\\geq 2\\\\mu^2$ and\\nan isolated fuzzy mass shell around \
$|p|^2=\\\\mu^2$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
