            "31 pages, 2 figures. LaTeX. Dedicated to the memory of Wolfhart\n\
  Zimmermann. v2: update of arXiv:1610.00526 permitted to suppress 3 pages", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "math-ph hep-th math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We extend our previous work (on $D=2$) to give an exact \
solution of the\n$\\Phi^3_D$ large-$\\mathcal{N}$ matrix model (or \
renormalised Kontsevich model)\nin $D=4$ and $D=6$ dimensions. Induction \
proofs and the difficult combinatorics\nare unchanged compared with $D=2$, \
but the renormalisation - performed\naccording to Zimmermann - is much more \
involved. As main result we prove that\nthe Schwinger 2-point function \
resulting from the $\\Phi^3_D$-QFT model on Moyal\nspace satisfies, for real \
coupling constant, reflection positivity in $D=4$ and\n$D=6$ dimensions. The \
K\\\"all\\'en-Lehmann mass spectrum of the associated\nWightman 2-point \
function describes a scattering part $|p|^2 \\geq 2\\mu^2$ and\nan isolated \
fuzzy mass shell around $|p|^2=\\mu^2$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 22 Dec 2016 13:01:16 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 2 Jun 2017 11:00:55 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-06-05", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Grosse", "Harald", "", "Vienna"}, {
              "Sako", "Akifumi", "", "Tokyo"}, {
              "Wulkenhaar", "Raimar", "", "M\[UDoubleDot]nster"}}}], 
