                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a D3-D5 system dual to a conformal field \
theory with a\\ncodimension-one defect that separates regions where the ranks \
of the gauge\\ngroups differ by $k$. With the help of this additional \
parameter, as observed\\nby Nagasaki, Tanida and Yamaguchi, one can define a \
double scaling limit in\\nwhich the quantum corrections are organized in \
powers of $\\\\lambda/k^2$, which\\nshould allow to extrapolate results \
between weak and strong coupling regimes.\\nIn particular we consider a \
radius $R$ circular Wilson loop placed at a\\ndistance $L$, whose internal \
space orientation is given by an angle $\\\\chi$. We\\ncompute its vacuum \
expectation value and show that, in the double scaling limit\\nand for small \
$\\\\chi$ and small $L/R$, weak coupling results can be extrapolated\\nto the \
strong coupling limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
