            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The spectrum of planar N=6 superconformal Chern-Simons theory, \
dual to type\nIIA superstring theory on $AdS_4 \\times CP^3$, is accessible \
at finite coupling\nusing integrability. Starting from the results of \
[arXiv:1403.1859], we study\nin depth the basic integrability structure \
underlying the spectral problem, the\nQuantum Spectral Curve. The new results \
presented in this paper open the way to\nthe quantitative study of the \
spectrum for arbitrary operators at finite\ncoupling. Besides, we show that \
the Quantum Spectral Curve is embedded into a\nnovel kind of Q-system, which \
reflects the OSp(4|6) symmetry of the theory and\nleads to exact Bethe Ansatz \
equations. The discovery of this algebraic\nstructure, more intricate than \
the one appearing in the $AdS_5/CFT_4$ case,\ncould be a first step towards \
the extension of the method to $AdS_3/CFT_2$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
