               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alessandro Pini\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"Alessandro Pini, Diego Rodriguez-Gomez, Jorge G. \
Russo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Large $N$ correlation functions in $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
superconformal\\n  quivers\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2017)066\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using supersymmetric localization, we consider \
four-dimensional\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal quiver gauge theories \
obtained from\\n$\\\\mathbb{Z}_n$ orbifolds of $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ Super \
Yang-Mills theory in the\\nlarge $N$ limit at weak coupling. In particular, \
we show that: 1) The partition\\nfunction for arbitrary couplings can be \
constructed in terms of universal\\nbuilding blocks. 2) It can be computed in \
perturbation series, which converges\\nuniformly for \
$|\\\\lambda_I|<\\\\pi^2$, where $\\\\lambda_I$ are the 't Hooft \
coupling\\nof the gauge groups. 3) The perturbation series for two-point \
functions can be\\nexplicitly computed to arbitrary orders. There is no \
universal effective\\ncoupling by which one can express them in terms of \
correlators of the\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ theory. 4) One can define twisted and \
untwisted sector\\noperators. At the perturbative orbifold point, when all \
the couplings are the\\nsame, the correlators of untwisted sector operators \
coincide with those of\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ Super Yang-Mills theory. In the \
twisted sector, we find\\nremarkable cancellations of a certain number of \
planar loops, determined by the\\nconformal dimension of the \
operator.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 9 Jan 2017 19:01:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
