 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we study the large $N$ solution to matrix \
models describing the\\npartition functions of 3d supersymmetric gauge \
theories on $S^3$. The model we\\nfocus on has a single $U(N)$ gauge group \
and fundamental fields, whose number\\nscales with $N$, also known as the \
Veneziano limit. The novel point in our\\nmodel is our choice of masses for \
the fundamental fields. Instead of vanishing\\nor fixed masses, we consider a \
linear distribution. We show that the model can\\nstill be solved by standard \
large $N$ techniques and explore the different\\nphases of the model. We also \
commend about other natural mass distributions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
