                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider structure constants of single trace \
operators in planar\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}$ = 4 Super-Yang-Mills theory within the \
hexagon framework. The\\nstandard procedure for forming a three point \
function out of two hexagons\\ndevelops divergences when the effects of \
virtual particles wrapping around the\\noperators are taken into account. In \
this paper, we explain how to renormalize\\nthese divergences away and obtain \
definite predictions, at the leading wrapping\\norder, for some of the \
structure constants that parameterize the OPE of two\\nchiral primaries. We \
test our method at weak coupling against the four loop\\nplanar correction to \
the BPS-BPS-Konishi OPE coefficient, derived recently in\\nthe field theory. \
At strong coupling, we compare our expressions with the\\nstructure constants \
obtained in string theory for three semiclassical strings.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
