               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Type II supergravity admits an AdS(3) x S(2) x S(2) x \
T(3) solution with\\nfluxes depending on several free parameters. We \
determine the constraints on\\nthese parameters imposed by the requirement of \
(classical) integrability of the\\nsuperstring sigma model. To do this we \
analyze the low-energy effective action\\nfor the spinning GKP string. The \
absence of particle production in the\\ntree-level S-matrix of bosonic \
excitations is shown to imply the vanishing of\\ntwo of the four parameters \
in the NSNS three-form flux. This reduces the\\nsupergravity background to \
either the one-parameter AdS(3) x S(2) x S(2) x T(3)\\nbackground preserving \
eight supersymmetries, or a non-supersymmetric branch,\\nwhich differs only \
by flipping a sign in the RR flux. We show that both these\\nbranches can be \
obtained from AdS(3) x S(3) x S(3) x S(1) by T-dualities on the\\n(Hopf) \
circle fibers of the three-spheres and therefore the integrability of\\nthe \
string in these backgrounds follows.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
