Price\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum Inverse Scattering and the Lambda Deformed \
Principal Chiral\\n  Model\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"49 Pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/aa7958\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The lambda model is a one parameter deformation of the \
principal chiral model\\nthat arises when regularizing the non-compactness of \
a non-abelian T dual in\\nstring theory. It is a current-current deformation \
of a WZW model that is known\\nto be integrable at the classical and quantum \
level. The standard techniques of\\nthe quantum inverse scattering method \
cannot be applied because the Poisson\\nbracket is non ultra-local. Inspired \
by an approach of Faddeev and Reshetikhin,\\nwe show that in this class of \
models, there is a way to deform the symplectic\\nstructure of the theory \
leading to a much simpler theory that is ultra-local\\nand can be quantized \
on the lattice whilst preserving integrability. This\\nlattice theory takes \
the form of a generalized spin chain that can be solved by\\nstandard \
algebraic Bethe Ansatz techniques. We then argue that the IR limit of\\nthe \
lattice theory lies in the universality class of the lambda model \
implying\\nthat the spin chain provides a way to apply the quantum inverse \
scattering\\nmethod to this non ultra-local theory. This points to a way of \
applying the\\nsame ideas to other lambda models and potentially the string \
world-sheet theory\\nin the gauge-gravity correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 20 Mar 2017 12:06:57 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2017-08-02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Appadu\"", ",", "\"Calan\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Hollowood\"", ",", "\"Timothy J.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Price\"", ",", "\"Dafydd\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
