           "id" -> "1703.06699", "submitter" -> "Timothy J. Hollowood", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Calan Appadu, Timothy J. Hollowood and Dafydd Price", "title" -> 
            "Quantum Inverse Scattering and the Lambda Deformed Principal \
Chiral\n  Model", "comments" -> "49 Pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8121/aa7958", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The lambda model is a one parameter deformation of the \
principal chiral model\nthat arises when regularizing the non-compactness of \
a non-abelian T dual in\nstring theory. It is a current-current deformation \
of a WZW model that is known\nto be integrable at the classical and quantum \
level. The standard techniques of\nthe quantum inverse scattering method \
cannot be applied because the Poisson\nbracket is non ultra-local. Inspired \
by an approach of Faddeev and Reshetikhin,\nwe show that in this class of \
models, there is a way to deform the symplectic\nstructure of the theory \
leading to a much simpler theory that is ultra-local\nand can be quantized on \
the lattice whilst preserving integrability. This\nlattice theory takes the \
form of a generalized spin chain that can be solved by\nstandard algebraic \
Bethe Ansatz techniques. We then argue that the IR limit of\nthe lattice \
theory lies in the universality class of the lambda model implying\nthat the \
spin chain provides a way to apply the quantum inverse scattering\nmethod to \
this non ultra-local theory. This points to a way of applying the\nsame ideas \
to other lambda models and potentially the string world-sheet theory\nin the \
gauge-gravity correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 20 Mar 2017 12:06:57 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-08-02", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Appadu", "Calan", ""}, {
              "Hollowood", "Timothy J.", ""}, {"Price", "Dafydd", ""}}}], 
