           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1703.08460\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sara Pasquetti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Francesco Benini, Sergio Benvenuti, Sara Pasquetti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SUSY monopole potentials in 2+1 dimensions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"40 pages, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1708, 086 (2017)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2017)086\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SISSA 11/2017/MATE-FISI, 19/2017/FISI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Gauge theories in 2+1 dimensions can admit monopole \
operators in the\\npotential. Starting with the theory without monopole \
potential, if the monopole\\npotential is relevant there is an RG flow to the \
monopole-deformed theory.\\nHere, focusing on U(Nc) SQCD with Nf flavors and \
N=2 supersymmetry, we show\\nthat even when the monopole potential is \
irrelevant, the monopole-modified\\ntheory Tm can exist and enjoy \
Seiberg-like dualities. We provide a\\nrenormalizable UV completion of Tm and \
an electric-magnetic dual description\\nTm'. We subject our proposal to \
various consistency checks such as mass\\ndeformations and three-sphere \
partition functions checks. We observe that Tm is\\nthe S-duality wall of 4D \
N=2 SQCD. We also consider monopole-deformed theories\\nwith Chern-Simons \
couplings and their duals.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 24 Mar 2017 15:28:17 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2019-07-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
