            "  Gauge theories in 2+1 dimensions can admit monopole operators \
in the\npotential. Starting with the theory without monopole potential, if \
the monopole\npotential is relevant there is an RG flow to the \
monopole-deformed theory.\nHere, focusing on U(Nc) SQCD with Nf flavors and \
N=2 supersymmetry, we show\nthat even when the monopole potential is \
irrelevant, the monopole-modified\ntheory Tm can exist and enjoy Seiberg-like \
dualities. We provide a\nrenormalizable UV completion of Tm and an \
electric-magnetic dual description\nTm'. We subject our proposal to various \
consistency checks such as mass\ndeformations and three-sphere partition \
functions checks. We observe that Tm is\nthe S-duality wall of 4D N=2 SQCD. \
We also consider monopole-deformed theories\nwith Chern-Simons couplings and \
their duals.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
