                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the physical properties of the persistent \
charged current in a metal\\nring on a noncommutative phase space, and \
temperature dependence of the\\nnoncommutative corrections are also analyzed. \
We find that the coordinate\\nnoncommutativity only affects the total \
magnitude of the current, and it is\\ndifficult to observe it. In contrast, \
the momentum noncommutativity can violate\\nsymmetry property of the current, \
and this violation of symmetry holds at a\\nfinite temperature. Based on this \
violation effect, we introduce an asymmetry\\nobservable to measure the \
momentum noncommutativity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
