               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Joseph Hayling, Constantinos Papageorgakis, Elli Pomoni \
and Diego\\n  Rodr\\\\'iguez-G\\\\'omez\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exact Deconstruction of the 6D (2,0) Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"49 pages; v2 typos corrected, published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2017)072\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The dimensional-deconstruction prescription of \
Arkani-Hamed, Cohen, Kaplan,\\nKarch and Motl provides a mechanism for \
recovering the $A$-type (2,0) theories\\non $T^2$, starting from a \
four-dimensional $\\\\mathcal N=2$ circular-quiver\\ntheory. We put this \
conjecture to the test using two exact-counting arguments:\\nIn the \
decompactification limit, we compare the Higgs-branch Hilbert series of\\nthe \
4D $\\\\mathcal N=2$ quiver to the \\\"half-BPS\\\" limit of the \
(2,0)\\nsuperconformal index. We also compare the full partition function for \
the 4D\\nquiver on $S^4$ to the (2,0) partition function on $S^4 \\\\times \
T^2$. In both\\ncases we find exact agreement. The partition function \
calculation sets up a\\ndictionary between exact results in 4D and \
6D.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
