 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In holographic applications one can encounter scenarios \
where a\\nlong-wavelength instability can arise. In such situations, it is \
often the case\\nthat the dynamical end point of the instability is a new \
equilibrium phase with\\na nonlinear scalar hair condensate outside the black \
hole horizon. We here\\nreview holographic setups where symmetric horizons \
suffer from long-wavelength\\ninstabilities where a suitable equilibrium \
condensate phase does not exist. We\\nstudy the dynamics of the simplest \
model in this exotic class, and show that it\\nuncovers arbitrarily large \
curvatures in the vicinity of the horizon which\\nasymptotically turn such \
region singular, at finite time with respect to the\\nboundary \
theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 18 Apr 2017 18:00:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2017-09-13\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Bosch\"", ",", "\"Pablo\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Buchel\"", ",", "\"Alex\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Lehner\"", ",", "\"Luis\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
