           "id" -> "1704.05454", "submitter" -> "Pablo Bosch", "authors" -> 
            "Pablo Bosch, Alex Buchel, Luis Lehner", "title" -> 
            "Unstable horizons and singularity development in holography", 
            "comments" -> "38 pages, 41 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP07(2017)135", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In holographic applications one can encounter scenarios where \
a\nlong-wavelength instability can arise. In such situations, it is often the \
case\nthat the dynamical end point of the instability is a new equilibrium \
phase with\na nonlinear scalar hair condensate outside the black hole \
horizon. We here\nreview holographic setups where symmetric horizons suffer \
from long-wavelength\ninstabilities where a suitable equilibrium condensate \
phase does not exist. We\nstudy the dynamics of the simplest model in this \
exotic class, and show that it\nuncovers arbitrarily large curvatures in the \
vicinity of the horizon which\nasymptotically turn such region singular, at \
finite time with respect to the\nboundary theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 18 Apr 2017 18:00:00 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-09-13", 
