               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1704.07386\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matthias Wilhelm\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Isak Buhl-Mortensen, Marius de Leeuw, Asger C. Ipsen, \
Charlotte\\n  Kristjansen, Matthias Wilhelm\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Asymptotic one-point functions in AdS/dCFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"6 pages; v2: statement about match up to wrapping order \
clarified,\\n  version accepted for publication\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. Lett. 119, 261604 (2017)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.261604\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We take the first step in extending the integrability \
approach to one-point\\nfunctions in AdS/dCFT to higher loop orders. More \
precisely, we argue that the\\nformula encoding all tree-level one-point \
functions of SU(2) operators in the\\ndefect version of N=4 SYM theory, dual \
to the D5-D3 probe-brane system with\\nflux, has a natural asymptotic \
generalization to higher loop orders. The\\nasymptotic formula correctly \
encodes the information about the one-loop\\ncorrection to the one-point \
functions of non-protected operators once dressed\\nby a simple \
flux-dependent factor, as we demonstrate by an explicit \
computation\\ninvolving a novel object denoted as an amputated matrix product \
state.\\nFurthermore, when applied to the BMN vacuum state, the asymptotic \
formula gives\\na result for the one-point function which in a certain \
double-scaling limit\\nagrees with that obtained in the dual string theory up \
to wrapping order.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
