                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sergio Ferrara, Marine Samsonyan, Magnus Tournoy and \
Antoine Van\\n  Proeyen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Supercurrent and Einstein equations in the \
Superconformal\\n  formulation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"43 pages; v2: Typos corrected. A subsection, an appendix \
and\\n  references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2017)119\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CERN-TH-2017-035\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give a new expression for the supercurrent and its \
conservation in curved\\n${\\\\cal N}=1$, $D=4$ superspace using the \
superconformal approach. The first\\ncomponent of the superfield, whose \
lowest component is the vector auxiliary\\nfield gives the (super)Einstein \
equations. Its trace and couplings to conformal\\nand non-conformal matter is \
presented. In a suitable dilatational gauge, the\\nconformal gauge, we obtain \
an update of the Callan-Coleman-Jackiw improved\\ncurrents for conformal \
matter, containing $R$-symmetry corrections for a new\\ntraceless covariantly \
conserved energy--momentum tensor. We observe that in the\\nPoincar\\\\'e \
gauge, where standard Poincar\\\\'e supergravity is usually formulated,\\nthe \
currents are not improved and then the higher conformal symmetry of \
the\\nmatter sector is obscured. The curvature multiplets are used to \
find\\nsupersymmetric curved backgrounds and some examples are exhibited in \
agreement\\nwith existing results.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
