           "id" -> "1705.02272", "submitter" -> "Antoine Van Proeyen", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Sergio Ferrara, Marine Samsonyan, Magnus Tournoy and Antoine Van\
\n  Proeyen", "title" -> 
            "The Supercurrent and Einstein equations in the Superconformal\n  \
formulation", "comments" -> 
            "43 pages; v2: Typos corrected. A subsection, an appendix and\n  \
references added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2017)119", 
            "report-no" -> "CERN-TH-2017-035", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We give a new expression for the supercurrent and its \
conservation in curved\n${\\cal N}=1$, $D=4$ superspace using the \
superconformal approach. The first\ncomponent of the superfield, whose lowest \
component is the vector auxiliary\nfield gives the (super)Einstein equations. \
Its trace and couplings to conformal\nand non-conformal matter is presented. \
In a suitable dilatational gauge, the\nconformal gauge, we obtain an update \
of the Callan-Coleman-Jackiw improved\ncurrents for conformal matter, \
containing $R$-symmetry corrections for a new\ntraceless covariantly \
conserved energy--momentum tensor. We observe that in the\nPoincar\\'e gauge, \
where standard Poincar\\'e supergravity is usually formulated,\nthe currents \
are not improved and then the higher conformal symmetry of the\nmatter sector \
is obscured. The curvature multiplets are used to find\nsupersymmetric curved \
backgrounds and some examples are exhibited in agreement\nwith existing \
results.\n", 
