                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider two-point correlators in SU(N) gauge \
theories on R4 with N=2\\nsupersymmetry and Nf massless hypermultiplets in \
the fundamental\\nrepresentation. Using localization on S4, we compute the \
leading perturbative\\ncorrections to the two-point functions of \
chiral/anti-chiral operators made of\\nscalar fields. The results are \
compared at two and three loops against direct\\nfield theory computations \
for some special operators whose correlators remain\\nfinite in perturbation \
theory at the specific loop order. In the conformal\\ncase, the match is \
shown up to two loops for a generic choice of operators and\\nfor arbitrary \
N.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
