            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Covariance is a useful property for handling supergravity \
theories. In this\npaper, we prove a covariance property of supergravity \
field equations: under\nreasonable conditions, field equations of \
supergravity are covariant modulo\nother field equations. We prove that for \
any supergravity there exist such\ncovariant equations of motion, other than \
the regular equations of motion, that\nare equivalent to the latter. The \
relations that we find between field\nequations and their covariant form can \
be used to obtain multiplets of field\nequations. In practice, the covariant \
field equations are easily found by\nsimply covariantizing the ordinary field \
equations.\n", 
