               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Two-point functions of SU(2)-subsector and length-two \
operators in dCFT\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"5 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2017.08.059\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider a particular set of two-point functions in \
the setting of N = 4\\nSYM with a defect, dual to the fuzzy-funnel solution \
for the probe D5-D3-brane\\nsystem. The two-point functions in focus involve \
a single trace operator in the\\nSU(2)-subsector of arbitrary length and a \
length-two operator built out of any\\nscalars. By interpreting the \
contractions as a spin-chain operator, simple\\nexpressions were found for \
the leading contribution to the two-point functions,\\nmapping them to \
earlier known formulas for the one-point functions in \
this\\nsetting.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
