            "  The AdS/CFT duality maps supersymmetric heavy operators with \
conformal\ndimension of the order of the central charge to asymptotically AdS \
supergravity\nsolutions. We show that by studying the quadratic fluctuations \
around such\nbackgrounds it is possible to derive the 4-point correlators of \
two light and\ntwo heavy states in the supergravity approximation. We provide \
an explicit\nexample in the AdS$_3$ setup relevant for the duality with the \
D1-D5 CFT.\nContrary to previously studied examples, the supergravity \
correlator derived in\nthis work differs from the result obtained at the CFT \
orbifold point. Our\nmethod bypasses the difficulties of applying the \
standard Witten's diagrams\napproach to correlators with operators of large \
conformal dimension and also\navoids some technical steps that have made the \
computation of dynamical 4-point\ncorrelators in the AdS$_3$/CFT$_2$ context \
unfeasible until now.\n", 
