                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PUPT-2526, Imperial-TP-AT-2017-06\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study correlation functions of local operator \
insertions on the 1/2-BPS\\nWilson line in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ super Yang-Mills \
theory. These correlation\\nfunctions are constrained by the 1d \
superconformal symmetry preserved by the\\n1/2-BPS Wilson line and define a \
defect CFT$_1$ living on the line. At strong\\ncoupling, a set of elementary \
operator insertions with protected scaling\\ndimensions correspond to \
fluctuations of the dual fundamental string in AdS$_5\\n\\\\times S^5$ ending \
on the line at the boundary and can be thought of as light\\nfields \
propagating on the AdS$_2$ worldsheet. We use AdS/CFT techniques to\\ncompute \
the tree-level AdS$_2$ Witten diagrams describing the strong coupling\\nlimit \
of the four-point functions of the dual operator insertions. Using the\\nOPE, \
we also extract the leading strong coupling corrections to the \
anomalous\\ndimensions of the \\\"two-particle\\\" operators built out of \
elementary excitations.\\nIn the case of the circular Wilson loop, we match \
our results for the 4-point\\nfunctions of a special type of scalar \
insertions to the prediction of\\nlocalization to 2d Yang-Mills \
theory.\\n\""}]}, {
