               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rouven Frassek\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Rouven Frassek, Christian Marboe, David Meidinger\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Evaluation of the operatorial Q-system for non-compact \
super spin chains\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"31 pages, v2: minor changes, version published in JHEP, \
v3: typo\\n  fixed\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2017)018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present an approach to evaluate the full operatorial \
Q-system of all\\n$\\\\mathfrak{u}(p,q|r+s)$-invariant spin chains with \
representations of\\nJordan-Schwinger type. In particular, this includes the \
super spin chain of\\nplanar $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills theory at \
one loop in the presence of a\\ndiagonal twist. Our method is based on the \
oscillator construction of\\nQ-operators. The Q-operators are built as traces \
over Lax operators which are\\ndegenerate solutions of the Yang-Baxter \
equation. For non-compact\\nrepresentations these Lax operators may contain \
multiple infinite sums that\\nconceal the form of the resulting functions. We \
determine these infinite sums\\nand calculate the matrix elements of the \
lowest level Q-operators. Transforming\\nthe Lax operators corresponding to \
the Q-operators into a representation\\ninvolving only finite sums allows us \
to take the supertrace and to obtain the\\nexplicit form of the Q-operators \
in terms of finite matrices for a given magnon\\nsector. Imposing the \
functional relations, we then bootstrap the other\\nQ-operators from those of \
the lowest level. We exemplify this approach for\\nnon-compact spin $-s$ spin \
chains and apply it to $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM at the\\none-loop level using \
the BMN vacuum as an example.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
