                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We make an attempt to map the integrable boundary \
conditions for 2\\ndimensional non-linear O(N) $\\\\sigma$-models. We do it \
at various levels:\\nclassically, by demanding the existence of infinitely \
many conserved local\\ncharges and also by constructing the double row \
transfer matrix from the Lax\\nconnection, which leads to the spectral curve \
formulation of the problem; at\\nthe quantum level, we describe the solutions \
of the boundary Yang-Baxter\\nequation and derive the Bethe-Yang equations. \
We then show how to connect the\\nthermodynamic limit of the boundary \
Bethe-Yang equations to the spectral curve.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
