                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present the exact solution for the scattering \
problem in the flat space\\nJackiw-Teitelboim (JT) gravity coupled to an \
arbitrary quantum field theory. JT\\ngravity results in a gravitational \
dressing of field theoretical scattering\\namplitudes. The exact expression \
for the dressed $S$-matrix was previously\\nknown as a solvable example of a \
novel UV asymptotic behavior, dubbed\\nasymptotic fragility. This dressing is \
equivalent to the $T\\\\bar{T}$ deformation\\nof the initial quantum field \
theory. JT gravity coupled to a single massless\\nboson provides a promising \
action formulation for an integrable approximation\\nto the worldsheet theory \
of confining strings in 3D gluodynamics. We also\\nderive the dressed \
$S$-matrix as a flat space limit of the near $AdS_2$\\nholography. We show \
that in order to preserve the flat space unitarity the\\nconventional \
Schwarzian dressing of boundary correlators needs to be slightly\\nextended. \
Finally, we propose a new simple expression for flat space amplitudes\\nof \
massive particles in terms of correlators of holographic CFT's.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
