             "abstract" -> 
             "  We study the null dipole deformation of N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory, which is\nan example of a potentially solvable \"dipole CFT\": a \
theory that is non-local\nalong a null direction, has non-relativistic \
conformal invariance along the\nremaining ones, and is holographically dual \
to a Schrodinger space-time. We\ninitiate the field-theoretical study of the \
spectrum in this model by using\nintegrability inherited from the parent \
theory. The dipole deformation\ncorresponds to a nondiagonal \
Drinfeld-Reshetikhin twist in the spin chain\npicture, which renders the \
traditional Bethe ansatz inapplicable from the very\nbeginning. We use \
instead the Baxter equation supplemented with nontrivial\nasymptotics, which \
gives the full 1-loop spectrum in the sl(2) sector. We show\nthat anomalous \
dimensions of long gauge theory operators perfectly match the\nstring theory \
prediction, providing a quantitative test of Schrodinger\nholography.\n", 
