 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the strong coupling limit of a family of \
Chern-Simons-matter\\ntheories in the planar limit. The family consists of ${\
\\\\cal N}=3$ theories with\\nthe gauge group ${\\\\rm \
U}(N_1)_{k_1}\\\\times{\\\\rm U}(N_2)_{k_2}$ coupled to $n$\\nbi-fundamental \
hypermultiplets. All observables which can be determined from\\nthe planar \
resolvent turn out to have finite limits in the large 't Hooft\\ncoupling \
limit. Possible gravity duals are briefly discussed. We observe \
that\\nKac-Moody algebras govern the structure of the planar spectral curves \
of the\\ntheories.\\n\""}]}, {
