 sigma-models", "comments" -> "25 pages. Comments added. Published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP10(2017)024", 
            "report-no" -> "NORDITA 2017-065", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We elaborate on the class of deformed T-dual (DTD) models \
obtained by first\nadding a topological term to the action of a supercoset \
sigma model and then\nperforming (non-abelian) T-duality on a subalgebra \
$\\tilde{\\mathfrak{g}}$ of\nthe superisometry algebra. These models inherit \
the classical integrability of\nthe parent one, and they include as special \
cases the so-called homogeneous\nYang-Baxter sigma models as well as their \
non-abelian T-duals. Many properties\nof DTD models have simple algebraic \
interpretations. For example we show that\ntheir (non-abelian) \
T-duals---including certain deformations---are again in the\nsame class, \
where $\\tilde{\\mathfrak{g}}$ gets enlarged or shrinks by adding or\n\
removing generators corresponding to the dualised isometries. Moreover, we \
show\nthat Weyl invariance of these models is equivalent to \
$\\tilde{\\mathfrak{g}}$\nbeing unimodular; when this property is not \
satisfied one can always remove one\ngenerator to obtain a unimodular \
$\\tilde{\\mathfrak{g}}$, which is equivalent to\n(formal) T-duality. We also \
work out the target space superfields and, as a\nby-product, we prove the \
conjectured transformation law for Ramond-Ramond (RR)\nfields under bosonic \
non-abelian T-duality of supercosets, generalising it to\ncases involving \
also fermionic T-dualities.\n", 
