         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1707.02420", "submitter" -> "Tomoki Nosaka", "authors" -> 
            "Sanefumi Moriyama, Tomoki Nosaka, Katsuya Yano", "title" -> 
            "Superconformal Chern-Simons Theories from del Pezzo Geometries", 
            "comments" -> "47 pages; v3: typos corrected, published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1711 (2017) 089", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP11(2017)089", "report-no" -> 
            "OCU-PHYS 467, KIAS-P17046", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present an explicit expression for the grand potential of \
the U(N)^3\nsuperconformal Chern-Simons theory with the Chern-Simons levels \
being (k,0,-k).\nFrom the viewpoint of the Newton polygon, it is expected \
that the grand\npotential is given by the free energy of the topological \
string theory on the\nlocal D_5 del Pezzo geometry, though the explicit \
identification was a puzzle\nfor years. We show how the expectation is \
realized explicitly. As a bonus, we\ncan also study the Z_2 orbifold of this \
theory and find the grand potential is\nnow given in terms of the local E_7 \
del Pezzo geometry.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 8 Jul 2017 09:25:32 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
