               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.CD\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study (non-)integrability and the presence of chaos \
in gravity dual\\nbackgrounds of strongly coupled gauge theories with \
unquenched flavor,\\nspecifically of the four-dimensional N=2 super \
Yang-Mills theory and the\\nthree-dimensional ABJM theory. By examining \
string motion on the geometries\\ncorresponding to backreacted D3/D7 and \
D2/D6 systems, we show that integrable\\ntheories with quenched flavor become \
non-integrable when the virtual quark\\nloops are taken into account. For the \
string solutions in the backreacted D3/D7\\nsystem, we compute the leading \
Lyapunov exponent which turns out to saturate to\\na positive value as the \
number of flavors increases. The exponent depends very\\nweakly on the number \
of flavors when they approach the number of colors. This\\nsuggests that once \
a particular flavor number in the theory is reached, a\\nfurther increase \
does not lead to more severe chaotic phenomena, implying\\ncertain saturation \
effects on chaos.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
