        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{13.905971649050727`, -9.153900834098025}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1708.01037\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shinji Hirano\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shinji Hirano\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matching Renormalisation Schemes in Holography\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"12 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"YITP-17-37\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In holography there is a one-to-one correspondence \
between physical\\nobservables in the bulk and boundary theories. To define \
physical observables,\\nhowever, regularisation needs to be implemented in \
both sides of the\\ncorrespondence. It is arguable whether the correspondence \
should extend to\\nregularisation and renormalisation scheme which are not \
physical in the\\nconventional sense. However, if we are to take the \
renormalisation group (RG)\\ninterpretation of holography seriously, its \
precise understanding appears to\\nrequire the matching of regularisations \
and renormalisation schemes in the bulk\\nand boundary theories. We address \
this question in the AdS_5/CFT_4\\ncorrespondence by considering a simplest \
physical quantity, the Casimir energy\\nof the N=4 super Yang-Mills (SYM) \
theory on R x S^3, in a {\\\\zeta}-function\\nregularisation and show that \
there are choices of scheme which match the bulk\\nAdS result including the \
radial cutoff dependent corrections when the cutoff is\\nkept finite. We \
further discuss the implication of this result to the RG\\ninterpretation of \
holography.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 3 Aug 2017 07:45:03 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2017-08-04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Hirano\"", ",", "\"Shinji\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
