           "id" -> "1708.01037", "submitter" -> "Shinji Hirano", "authors" -> 
            "Shinji Hirano", "title" -> 
            "Matching Renormalisation Schemes in Holography", "comments" -> 
            "12 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "YITP-17-37", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In holography there is a one-to-one correspondence between \
physical\nobservables in the bulk and boundary theories. To define physical \
observables,\nhowever, regularisation needs to be implemented in both sides \
of the\ncorrespondence. It is arguable whether the correspondence should \
extend to\nregularisation and renormalisation scheme which are not physical \
in the\nconventional sense. However, if we are to take the renormalisation \
group (RG)\ninterpretation of holography seriously, its precise understanding \
appears to\nrequire the matching of regularisations and renormalisation \
schemes in the bulk\nand boundary theories. We address this question in the \
AdS_5/CFT_4\ncorrespondence by considering a simplest physical quantity, the \
Casimir energy\nof the N=4 super Yang-Mills (SYM) theory on R x S^3, in a \
{\\zeta}-function\nregularisation and show that there are choices of scheme \
which match the bulk\nAdS result including the radial cutoff dependent \
corrections when the cutoff is\nkept finite. We further discuss the \
implication of this result to the RG\ninterpretation of holography.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
