               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1708.05658\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Stephen Pietromonaco\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Stephen Pietromonaco\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Emergent Geometry Through Holomorphic Matrix \
Models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Masters Thesis in Physics, University of British \
Columbia, August\\n  2017, 68 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Over the years, deep insights into string theory and \
supersymmetric gauge\\ntheories have come from studying geometry emerging \
from matrix models. In this\\nthesis, I study the N=1* and N=2* theories from \
which an elliptic curve is\\nknown to emerge, alongside an elliptic function \
called the generalized\\nresolvent into which the physics is encoded. This is \
indicative of the common\\norigin of the two theories in N=4 SYM. The N=1* \
Dijkgraaf-Vafa matrix model is\\nintrinsically holomorphic with parameter \
space corresponding to the upper-half\\nplane. The Dijkgraaf-Vafa matrix \
model 't Hooft coupling S has been previously\\nshown to be holomorphic on \
the upper-half plane and quasi-modular with respect\\nto SL(2,Z). The allowed \
N=2* coupling is constrained to a Hermitian slice\\nthrough the enlarged \
moduli space of the holomorphic N=1* model. After\\nexplicitly constructing \
the map from the elliptic curve to the eigenvalue\\nplane, I argue that the \
N=1* coupling S encodes data reminiscent of N=2*. A\\ncollection of extrema \
(saddle-points) of S behave curiously like the quantum\\ncritical points of \
N=2* theory. For the first critical point, the match is\\nexact. This \
collection of points lie on the line of degeneration which behaves\\nin a \
sense, like a boundary at infinity. I also show explicitly that \
the\\nemergent elliptic curve along with the generalized resolvent allow one \
to\\nrecover exact eigenvalue densities. At weak coupling, my method \
reproduces the\\ninverse square root of N=2* as well as the Wigner \
semi-circle in N=1*. At\\nstrong coupling in N=1*, I provide encouraging \
evidence of the parabolic\\ndensity arising in the neighborhood of the line \
of degeneration. To my\\nknowledge, the parabolic density has only been \
observed asymptotically. It is\\ninteresting to see evidence that it may be \
exactly encoded in the other form of\\nemergent geometry: the elliptic curve \
with the generalized resolvent.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 15 Aug 2017 19:23:03 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2017-08-21\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Pietromonaco\"", ",", "\"Stephen\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
