            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Over the years, deep insights into string theory and \
supersymmetric gauge\ntheories have come from studying geometry emerging from \
matrix models. In this\nthesis, I study the N=1* and N=2* theories from which \
an elliptic curve is\nknown to emerge, alongside an elliptic function called \
the generalized\nresolvent into which the physics is encoded. This is \
indicative of the common\norigin of the two theories in N=4 SYM. The N=1* \
Dijkgraaf-Vafa matrix model is\nintrinsically holomorphic with parameter \
space corresponding to the upper-half\nplane. The Dijkgraaf-Vafa matrix model \
't Hooft coupling S has been previously\nshown to be holomorphic on the \
upper-half plane and quasi-modular with respect\nto SL(2,Z). The allowed N=2* \
coupling is constrained to a Hermitian slice\nthrough the enlarged moduli \
space of the holomorphic N=1* model. After\nexplicitly constructing the map \
from the elliptic curve to the eigenvalue\nplane, I argue that the N=1* \
coupling S encodes data reminiscent of N=2*. A\ncollection of extrema \
(saddle-points) of S behave curiously like the quantum\ncritical points of \
N=2* theory. For the first critical point, the match is\nexact. This \
collection of points lie on the line of degeneration which behaves\nin a \
sense, like a boundary at infinity. I also show explicitly that the\nemergent \
elliptic curve along with the generalized resolvent allow one to\nrecover \
exact eigenvalue densities. At weak coupling, my method reproduces the\n\
inverse square root of N=2* as well as the Wigner semi-circle in N=1*. At\n\
strong coupling in N=1*, I provide encouraging evidence of the parabolic\n\
density arising in the neighborhood of the line of degeneration. To my\n\
knowledge, the parabolic density has only been observed asymptotically. It is\
\ninteresting to see evidence that it may be exactly encoded in the other \
form of\nemergent geometry: the elliptic curve with the generalized \
resolvent.\n", 
