 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the $\\\\frac{1}{2}$-BPS circular Wilson loop \
in the totally\\nantisymmetric representation of the gauge group in \
$\\\\mathcal N =4 $\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills. This observable is captured \
by a Gaussian matrix\\nmodel with appropriate insertion. We compute the first \
$1/N$ correction at\\nleading order in 't Hooft coupling by means of the \
matrix model loop equations.\\nDisagreement with the 1-loop effective action \
of the holographically dual\\n$D5$-brane suggests the need to account for \
gravitational backreaction on the\\nstring theory side.\\n\""}]}, {
