\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, 4 figures. v2: References added. v3: More \
references, JHEP\\n  version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2018)047\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"MCTP-17-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  For ${\\\\cal N}=2^*$ theory with $U(N)$ gauge group we \
evaluate expectation\\nvalues of Wilson loops in representations described by \
a rectangular Young\\ntableau with $n$ rows and $k$ columns. The evaluation \
reduces to a two-matrix\\nmodel and we explain, using a combination of \
numerical and analytical\\ntechniques, the general properties of the \
eigenvalue distributions in various\\nregimes of parameters \
$(N,\\\\lambda,n,k)$ where $\\\\lambda$ is the 't Hooft\\ncoupling. In the \
large $N$ limit we present analytic results for the leading\\nand sub-leading \
contributions. In the particular cases of only one row or one\\ncolumn we \
reproduce previously known results for the totally symmetry and\\ntotally \
antisymmetric representations. We also extensively discusss the \
${\\\\cal\\nN}=4$ limit of the ${\\\\cal N}=2^*$ theory. While establishing \
these connections\\nwe clarify aspects of various orders of limits and how to \
relax them; we also\\nfind it useful to explicitly address details of the \
genus expansion. As a\\nresult, for the totally symmetric Wilson loop we find \
new contributions that\\nimprove the comparison with the dual holographic \
computation at one loop order\\nin the appropriate regime.\\n\""}]}, {
