JHEP\n  version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP01(2018)047", 
            "report-no" -> "MCTP-17-12", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  For ${\\cal N}=2^*$ theory with $U(N)$ gauge group we evaluate \
expectation\nvalues of Wilson loops in representations described by a \
rectangular Young\ntableau with $n$ rows and $k$ columns. The evaluation \
reduces to a two-matrix\nmodel and we explain, using a combination of \
numerical and analytical\ntechniques, the general properties of the \
eigenvalue distributions in various\nregimes of parameters $(N,\\lambda,n,k)$ \
where $\\lambda$ is the 't Hooft\ncoupling. In the large $N$ limit we present \
analytic results for the leading\nand sub-leading contributions. In the \
particular cases of only one row or one\ncolumn we reproduce previously known \
results for the totally symmetry and\ntotally antisymmetric representations. \
We also extensively discusss the ${\\cal\nN}=4$ limit of the ${\\cal N}=2^*$ \
theory. While establishing these connections\nwe clarify aspects of various \
orders of limits and how to relax them; we also\nfind it useful to explicitly \
address details of the genus expansion. As a\nresult, for the totally \
symmetric Wilson loop we find new contributions that\nimprove the comparison \
with the dual holographic computation at one loop order\nin the appropriate \
regime.\n", 
