 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In ABJ(M) theory a generalized cusp can be constructed \
out of the 1/6 BPS\\nWilson line by introducing an angle $\\\\varphi$ in the \
spacial contour and/or an\\nangle $\\\\theta$ in the internal R-symmetry \
space. The small angles limits of its\\nanomalous dimension are controlled by \
corresponding Bremsstrahlung functions.\\nIn this note we compute the \
internal space $\\\\theta$-Bremsstrahlung function to\\nfour loops at weak \
coupling in the planar limit. Based on this result, we\\npropose an all order \
conjecture for the $\\\\theta$-Bremsstrahlung function.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
