            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1709.01448\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ben Hoare\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ben Hoare, Fiona K. Seibold\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Poisson-Lie duals of the eta deformed symmetric space \
sigma model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"37 pages, v2: minor changes\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2017)014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Poisson-Lie dualising the eta deformation of the G/H \
symmetric space sigma\\nmodel with respect to the simple Lie group G is \
conjectured to give an analytic\\ncontinuation of the associated lambda \
deformed model. In this paper we\\ninvestigate when the eta deformed model \
can be dualised with respect to a\\nsubgroup G_0 of G. Starting from the \
first-order action on the complexified\\ngroup and integrating out the \
degrees of freedom associated to different\\nsubalgebras, we find it is \
possible to dualise when G_0 is associated to a\\nsub-Dynkin diagram. \
Additional U_1 factors built from the remaining Cartan\\ngenerators can also \
be included. The resulting construction unifies both the\\nPoisson-Lie dual \
with respect to G and the complete abelian dual of the eta\\ndeformation in a \
single framework, with the integrated algebras unimodular in\\nboth cases. We \
speculate that extending these results to the path integral\\nformalism may \
provide an explanation for why the eta deformed AdS_5 x S^5\\nsuperstring is \
not one-loop Weyl invariant, that is the couplings do not solve\\nthe \
equations of type IIB supergravity, yet its complete abelian dual and \
the\\nlambda deformed model are.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
