            "Poisson-Lie duals of the eta deformed symmetric space sigma \
model", "comments" -> "37 pages, v2: minor changes", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP11(2017)014", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Poisson-Lie dualising the eta deformation of the G/H symmetric \
space sigma\nmodel with respect to the simple Lie group G is conjectured to \
give an analytic\ncontinuation of the associated lambda deformed model. In \
this paper we\ninvestigate when the eta deformed model can be dualised with \
respect to a\nsubgroup G_0 of G. Starting from the first-order action on the \
complexified\ngroup and integrating out the degrees of freedom associated to \
different\nsubalgebras, we find it is possible to dualise when G_0 is \
associated to a\nsub-Dynkin diagram. Additional U_1 factors built from the \
remaining Cartan\ngenerators can also be included. The resulting construction \
unifies both the\nPoisson-Lie dual with respect to G and the complete abelian \
dual of the eta\ndeformation in a single framework, with the integrated \
algebras unimodular in\nboth cases. We speculate that extending these results \
to the path integral\nformalism may provide an explanation for why the eta \
deformed AdS_5 x S^5\nsuperstring is not one-loop Weyl invariant, that is the \
couplings do not solve\nthe equations of type IIB supergravity, yet its \
complete abelian dual and the\nlambda deformed model are.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 5 Sep 2017 15:22:04 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 31 Oct 2017 10:28:03 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-12-06", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Hoare", "Ben", ""}, {
              "Seibold", "Fiona K.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{15.322239495374058`, -2.7142848763422087`}, 0.],
