                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider a fundamental string in a bubbling geometry \
of arbitrary genus\\ndual to a half-supersymmetric Wilson loop in a general \
large representation\\n$\\\\mathbf{R}$ of the $SU(N)$ gauge group in \
${\\\\cal N}=4$ Supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills. We demonstrate, under some mild \
conditions, that the minimum value\\nof the string classical action for a \
bubbling geometry of arbitrary genus\\nprecisely matches the correlator of a \
Wilson loop in the fundamental\\nrepresentation and one in a general large \
representation. We work out the case\\nin which the large representation is \
given by a rectangular Young Tableau,\\ncorresponding to a genus one bubbling \
geometry, explicitly. We also present\\nexplicit results in the field theory \
for a correlator of two Wilson loops: a\\nlarge one in an arbitrary \
representation and a \\\"small\\\" one in the fundamental,\\ntotally \
symmetric or totally antisymmetric representation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
