 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We will argue that the 1/2 BPS Wilson loops in the \
anti-symmetric\\nrepresentations in the $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills \
(SYM) theory exhibit a\\nphase transition at some critical value of the 't \
Hooft coupling of order\\n$N^2$. In the matrix model computation of Wilson \
loop expectation values, this\\nphase transition corresponds to the \
transition between the one-cut phase and\\nthe two-cut phase. It turns out \
that the one-cut phase is smoothly connected to\\nthe small 't Hooft coupling \
regime and the $1/N$ corrections of Wilson loops in\\nthis phase can be \
systematically computed from the topological recursion in the\\nGaussian \
matrix model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
