               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1709.07564\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mauricio Valenzuela\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mauricio Valenzuela\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Higher spin matrix models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"13 pages, 1 table. New references and corrections from \
referee\\n  reports are included in this version. Current form accepted in \
Universe\\n  journal for the special issue on Higher Spin Gauge \
Theories\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a hybrid class of theories for higher spin \
gravity and matrix\\nmodels, i.e. which handle simultaneously higher spin \
gravity fields and matrix\\nmodels. The construction is similar to Vasiliev's \
higher spin gravity but part\\nof the equations of motion are provided by the \
action principle of a matrix\\nmodel. In particular we construct a higher \
spin (gravity) matrix model related\\nto type IIB matrix models/string theory \
which have a well defined classical\\nlimit, and which is compatible with \
higher spin gravity in $AdS$ space. As it\\nhas been suggested that higher \
spin gravity should be related to string theory\\nin a high energy \
(tensionless) regime, and therefore to M-Theory, we expect\\nthat our \
construction will be useful to explore concrete connections.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
