 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the holographic dual for $\\\\mathcal N=4$ \
SYM on $\\\\rm S^4$ and\\n$\\\\rm AdS_4$ coupled to massive $\\\\mathcal N=2$ \
supersymmetric quenched flavor\\nfields on a codimension-1 defect, which is $\
\\\\rm S^3$ and $\\\\rm AdS_3$,\\nrespectively. The holographic description \
is in terms of a D3/probe D5 brane\\nsystem. We set up and reduce the BPS \
equations for D5-brane embeddings with\\narbitrary supersymmetric \
deformations and partly solve them at the non-linear\\nlevel. The remaining \
equations are solved explicitly in a small-mass expansion.\\nWe compute the \
contribution of the defect fields to the partition function on\\nS$^4$ and \
compare to a field theory computation using supersymmetric\\nlocalization, \
for which we set up the matrix model. Both computations agree,\\nlending \
strong support to holographic probe brane constructions using \
D3/D5\\nconfigurations in general.\\n\""}]}, {
