               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Eric Perlmutter\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Simone Giombi, Eric Perlmutter\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Double-Trace Flows and the Swampland\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25+13 pages. v2: refs added, minor clarifications\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2018)026\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PUPT-2536, CALT-TH 2017-054\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore the idea that large $N$, non-supersymmetric \
conformal field\\ntheories with a parametrically large gap to higher spin \
single-trace operators\\nmay be obtained as infrared fixed points of relevant \
double-trace deformations\\nof superconformal field theories. After recalling \
the AdS interpretation and\\nsome potential pathologies of such flows, we \
introduce a concrete example that\\nappears to avoid them: the ABJM theory at \
finite $k$, deformed by $\\\\int\\\\!{\\\\cal\\nO}^2$, where ${\\\\cal O}$ is \
the superconformal primary in the stress-tensor\\nmultiplet. We address its \
relation to recent conjectures based on weak gravity\\nbounds, and discuss \
the prospects for a wider class of similarly viable flows.\\nNext, we proceed \
to analyze the spectrum and correlation functions of the\\nputative IR CFT, \
to leading non-trivial order in $1/N$. This includes analytic\\ncomputations \
of the change under double-trace flow of connected four-point\\nfunctions of \
ABJM superconformal primaries; and of the IR anomalous dimensions\\nof \
infinite classes of double-trace composite operators. These would be \
the\\nfirst analytic results for anomalous dimensions of finite-spin \
composite\\noperators in any large $N$ CFT$_3$ with an Einstein gravity dual.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
