            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We explore the idea that large $N$, non-supersymmetric \
conformal field\ntheories with a parametrically large gap to higher spin \
single-trace operators\nmay be obtained as infrared fixed points of relevant \
double-trace deformations\nof superconformal field theories. After recalling \
the AdS interpretation and\nsome potential pathologies of such flows, we \
introduce a concrete example that\nappears to avoid them: the ABJM theory at \
finite $k$, deformed by $\\int\\!{\\cal\nO}^2$, where ${\\cal O}$ is the \
superconformal primary in the stress-tensor\nmultiplet. We address its \
relation to recent conjectures based on weak gravity\nbounds, and discuss the \
prospects for a wider class of similarly viable flows.\nNext, we proceed to \
analyze the spectrum and correlation functions of the\nputative IR CFT, to \
leading non-trivial order in $1/N$. This includes analytic\ncomputations of \
the change under double-trace flow of connected four-point\nfunctions of ABJM \
superconformal primaries; and of the IR anomalous dimensions\nof infinite \
classes of double-trace composite operators. These would be the\nfirst \
analytic results for anomalous dimensions of finite-spin composite\noperators \
in any large $N$ CFT$_3$ with an Einstein gravity dual.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
