            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the Bremsstrahlung function associated to a \
1/6-BPS Wilson loop\nin ABJM theory, with a cusp in the couplings to scalar \
fields. We non-trivially\nextend its recent four-loop computation at weak \
coupling to include non-planar\ncorrections. We have recently proposed a \
conjecture relating this object to\nsupersymmetric circular Wilson loops with \
multiple windings, which can be\ncomputed via localization. We find agreement \
between this proposal and the\nperturbative computation of the Bremsstrahlung \
function, including color\nsub-leading corrections. This supports the \
conjecture and hints at its validity\nbeyond the planar approximation.\n", 
