 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Four-dimensional N = 2 superconformal quantum field \
theories contain a\\nsubsector carrying the structure of a chiral algebra. \
Using localization\\ntechniques, we show for the free hypermultiplet that \
this structure can be\\naccessed directly from the path integral on the \
four-sphere. We extend the\\nlocalization computation to include \
supersymmetric surface defects described by\\na generic 4d/2d coupled system. \
The presence of a defect corresponds to\\nconsidering a module of the chiral \
algebra: our results provide a calculational\\nwindow into its structure \
constants.\\n\""}]}, {
