                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study three-point functions of operators on the \
$1/2$ BPS Wilson loop in\\nplanar $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills theory. \
The operators we consider are\\n\\\"defect changing operators\\\", which \
change the scalar coupled to the Wilson\\nloop. We first perform the \
computation at two loops in general set-ups, and\\nthen study a special \
scaling limit called the ladders limit, in which the\\nspectrum is known to \
be described by a quantum mechanics with the\\nSL(2,$\\\\mathbb{R}$) \
symmetry. In this limit, we resum the Feynman diagrams using\\nthe \
Schwinger-Dyson equation and determine the structure constants at all \
order\\nin the rescaled coupling constant. Besides providing an interesting \
solvable\\nexample of defect conformal field theories, our result gives \
invaluable data\\nfor the integrability-based approach to the structure \
constants.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
