 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study impact of quantum phase transitions (QPTs) on \
the distribution of\\nexceptional points (EPs) of the Hamiltonian in \
complex-extended parameter\\ndomain. Analyzing first- and second-order QPTs \
in the Lipkin model, we find an\\nexponentially and polynomially close \
approach of EPs to the respective critical\\npoint with an increasing size of \
the system. If the critical Hamiltonian is\\nsubject to random perturbations \
of various kinds, the averaged distribution of\\nEPs close to the critical \
point still carries decisive information on the QPT\\ntype. We therefore \
claim that properties of the EP distribution represent \
a\\nparametrization-independent signature of criticality in quantum \
systems.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
