                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study 7D maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory \
on curved manifolds\\nthat admit Killing spinors. If the manifold admits at \
least two Killing spinors\\n(Sasaki-Einstein manifolds) we are able to \
rewrite the supersymmetric theory in\\nterms of a cohomological complex. In \
principle this cohomological complex makes\\nsense for any K-contact \
manifold. For the case of toric Sasaki-Einstein\\nmanifolds we derive \
explicitly the perturbative part of the partition function\\nand speculate \
about the non-perturbative part. We also briefly discuss the case\\nof \
3-Sasaki manifolds and suggest a plausible form for the \
full\\nnon-perturbative answer.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
