               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give a brief overview of the string landscape and \
techniques used to\\nconstruct string compactifications. We then explain how \
this motivates the\\nnotion of the swampland and review a number of \
conjectures that attempt to\\ncharacterize theories in the swampland. We also \
compare holography in the\\ncontext of superstrings with the similar, but \
much simpler case of topological\\nstring theory. For topological strings, \
there is a direct definition of\\ntopological gravity based on a sum over a \
\\\"quantum gravitational foam.\\\" In this\\ncontext, holography is the \
statement of an identification between a gravity and\\ngauge theory, both of \
which are defined independently of one another. This\\npoints to a missing \
corner in string dualities which suggests the search for a\\ndirect \
definition of quantum theory of gravity rather than relying on its\\nstrongly \
coupled holographic dual as an adequate substitute (Based on TASI \
2017\\nlectures given by C. Vafa).\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
