            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1711.02446\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Riccardo Borsato\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riccardo Borsato, Joakim Str\\\\\\\"omwall and Alessandro \
Torrielli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"$q$-Poincar\\\\'e invariance of the $AdS_3/CFT_2$ \
$R$-matrix\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages. Minor improvements and references added. \
Published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 97, 066001 (2018)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.97.066001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"DMUS-MP-17/10, NORDITA 2017-111\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the exact $R$-matrix of $AdS_3/CFT_2$, \
which is the building\\nblock for describing the scattering of worldsheet \
excitations of the light-cone\\ngauge-fixed backgrounds $AdS_3 \\\\times S^3 \
\\\\times T^4$ and $AdS_3 \\\\times S^3\\n\\\\times S^3 \\\\times S^1$ with \
pure Ramond-Ramond fluxes. We show that $R$ is\\ninvariant under a \
\\\"deformed boost\\\" symmetry, for which we write an explicit\\nexact \
coproduct, i.e. its action on 2-particle states. When we include the\\nboost, \
the symmetries of the $R$-matrix close into a \
$q$-Poincar\\\\'e\\nsuperalgebra. Our findings suggest that the recently \
discovered boost\\ninvariance in $AdS_5/CFT_4$ may be a common feature of \
$AdS/CFT$ systems that\\nare treatable with the exact techniques of \
integrability. With the aim of going\\ntowards a universal formulation of the \
underlying Hopf algebra, we also propose\\na universal form of the \
$AdS_3/CFT_2$ classical $r$-matrix.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 7 Nov 2017 12:52:38 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 3 Apr 2018 10:27:47 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2018-04-04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Borsato\"", ",", "\"Riccardo\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Str\[ODoubleDot]mwall\"", ",", "\"Joakim\"", ",", 
                    "\"\""}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Torrielli\"", ",", "\"Alessandro\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
