         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1711.02446", "submitter" -> "Riccardo Borsato", "authors" -> 
            "Riccardo Borsato, Joakim Str\\\"omwall and Alessandro Torrielli",
             "title" -> 
            "$q$-Poincar\\'e invariance of the $AdS_3/CFT_2$ $R$-matrix", 
            "comments" -> 
            "26 pages. Minor improvements and references added. Published \
version", "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. D 97, 066001 (2018)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.97.066001", "report-no" -> 
            "DMUS-MP-17/10, NORDITA 2017-111", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the exact $R$-matrix of $AdS_3/CFT_2$, which is \
the building\nblock for describing the scattering of worldsheet excitations \
of the light-cone\ngauge-fixed backgrounds $AdS_3 \\times S^3 \\times T^4$ \
and $AdS_3 \\times S^3\n\\times S^3 \\times S^1$ with pure Ramond-Ramond \
fluxes. We show that $R$ is\ninvariant under a \"deformed boost\" symmetry, \
for which we write an explicit\nexact coproduct, i.e. its action on \
2-particle states. When we include the\nboost, the symmetries of the \
$R$-matrix close into a $q$-Poincar\\'e\nsuperalgebra. Our findings suggest \
that the recently discovered boost\ninvariance in $AdS_5/CFT_4$ may be a \
common feature of $AdS/CFT$ systems that\nare treatable with the exact \
techniques of integrability. With the aim of going\ntowards a universal \
formulation of the underlying Hopf algebra, we also propose\na universal form \
of the $AdS_3/CFT_2$ classical $r$-matrix.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 7 Nov 2017 12:52:38 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 3 Apr 2018 10:27:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2018-04-04", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Borsato", "Riccardo", ""}, {
              "Str\[ODoubleDot]mwall", "Joakim", ""}, {
              "Torrielli", "Alessandro", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
