 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We demonstrate by explicit multi-loop calculation that \
\\\\gamma-deformed planar\\nN=4 SYM, supplemented with a set of double-trace \
counter-terms, has two\\nnontrivial fixed points in the recently proposed \
double scaling limit,\\ncombining vanishing 't Hooft coupling and large \
imaginary deformation\\nparameter. We provide evidence that, at the fixed \
points, the theory is\\ndescribed by an integrable non-unitary \
four-dimensional CFT. We find a closed\\nexpression for the four-point \
correlation function of the simplest protected\\noperators and use it to \
compute the exact conformal data of operators with\\narbitrary Lorentz spin. \
We conjecture that both conformal symmetry and\\nintegrability should survive \
in \\\\gamma-deformed planar N=4 SYM for arbitrary\\nvalues of the \
deformation parameters.\\n\""}]}, {
