                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the perturbative partition functions for \
gauge theories with eight\\nsupersymmetries on spheres of dimension \
$d\\\\le5$, proving a conjecture by the\\nsecond author. We apply similar \
methods to gauge theories with four\\nsupersymmetries on spheres with \
$d\\\\le3$. The results are valid for non-integer\\n$d$ as well. We further \
propose an analytic continuation from $d=3$ to $d=4$\\nthat gives the \
perturbative partition function for an $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ gauge\\ntheory. The \
results are consistent with the free multiplets and the \
one-loop\\n$\\\\beta$-functions for general $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ gauge \
theories. We also consider\\nthe analytic continuation of an \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=1$-preserving mass deformation of\\nthe maximally \
supersymmetric gauge theory and compare to recent holographic\\nresults for $\
\\\\mathcal{N}=1^*$ super Yang-Mills. We find that the general\\nstructure \
for the real part of the free energy coming from the analytic\\ncontinuation \
is consistent with the holographic results.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
