            "  We study elliptic vortices on $\\mathbb{C}\\times T^2$ by \
considering the 2d\nquiver gauge theory describing their moduli spaces. The \
elliptic genus of these\nmoduli spaces is the elliptic version of vortex \
partition function of the 4d\ntheory. We focus on two examples: the first is \
a $\\mathcal{N}=1$,\n$\\mathrm{U}(N)$ gauge theory with fundamental and \
anti-fundamental matter; the\nsecond is a $\\mathcal{N}=2$, $\\mathrm{U}(N)$ \
gauge theory with matter in the\nfundamental representation. The results are \
instances of 4d \"holomorphic\nblocks\" into which partition functions on \
more complicated surfaces factorize.\nThey can also be interpreted as \
free-field representations of elliptic Virasoro\nalgebrae.\n", 
