 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We introduce ABJM quantum field theory in the \
noncommutative spacetime by\\nusing the component formalism and show that it \
is N=6 supersymmetric. For the\\nU(1)_{\\\\kappa} x U(1)_{-\\\\kappa} case, \
we compute all one-loop 1PI two and three\\npoint functions in the Landau \
gauge and show that they are UV finite and have\\nwell-defined commutative \
limits theta^{\\\\mu\\\\nu} -> 0, corresponding exactly to\\nthe 1PI \
functions of the ordinary ABJM field theory. This result also holds for\\nall \
one-loop functions which are UV finite by power counting. It seems that \
the\\nquantum noncommutative ABJM field theory is free from the \
noncommutative IR\\ninstabilities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
