         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1712.02698", "submitter" -> "Shai Chester", "authors" -> 
            "Marco Baggio, Nikolay Bobev, Shai M. Chester, Edoardo Lauria, \
and\n  Silviu S. Pufu", "title" -> 
            "Decoding a Three-Dimensional Conformal Manifold", "comments" -> 
            "59 pages, 13 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP02(2018)062", "report-no" -> "PUPT-2544", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.str-el", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the one-dimensional complex conformal manifold that \
controls the\ninfrared dynamics of a three-dimensional $\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
supersymmetric theory\nof three chiral superfields with a cubic \
superpotential. Two special points on\nthis conformal manifold are the \
well-known XYZ model and three decoupled copies\nof the critical Wess-Zumino \
model. The conformal manifold enjoys a discrete\nduality group isomorphic to \
$S_4$ and can be thought of as an orbifold of\n$\\mathbf{CP}^1$. We use the \
$4-\\varepsilon$ expansion and the numerical\nconformal bootstrap to \
calculate the spectrum of conformal dimensions of\nlow-lying operators and \
their OPE coefficients, and find a very good\nquantitative agreement between \
the two approaches.\n", 
