               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Hagen M\\\\\\\"unkler\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Hagen M\\\\\\\"unkler\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Symmetries of Maldacena-Wilson Loops from Integrable \
String Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PhD-Thesis based on the works arXiv:1503.07553, \
arXiv:1507.02474,\\n  arXiv:1606.04104, arXiv:1610.01161. 209 pages, 11 \
figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this thesis, we investigate hidden symmetries for \
the Maldacena-Wilson\\nloop in N=4 super Yang-Mills theory, mainly focusing \
on its strong-coupling\\ndescription as a minimal surface in $AdS_5$. In the \
discussion of the symmetry\\nstructure of the underlying string model, we \
highlight the role of the master\\nsymmetry which can be employed to \
construct all symmetries of the model. The\\nalgebra of these symmetries is \
worked out. For the concrete case of minimal\\nsurfaces in $AdS_5$, we \
discuss the deformation of the four-cusp solution,\\nwhich provides the dual \
description of the four-gluon scattering amplitude.\\nThis marks the first \
step toward transferring the master symmetry to scattering\\namplitudes. \
Moreover, we compute the master and Yangian symmetry variations of\\ngeneric, \
smooth boundary curves. The discussion clarifies why previous attempts\\nto \
transfer the deformations of minimal surfaces in $AdS_3$ to weak \
coupling\\nwere unsuccessful. We discuss several attempts to transfer the \
Yangian symmetry\\nto weak or arbitrary coupling, but ultimately conclude \
that a Yangian symmetry\\nof the Maldacena-Wilson loop seems not to be \
present. This is different for the\\nnatural supersymmetric generalizations \
of the Maldacena--Wilson loop, Wilson\\nloops in superspace. Their one-loop \
expectation value is known to be Yangian\\ninvariant. We discuss the \
strong-coupling counterpart of this finding by\\nconsidering minimal surfaces \
in the superspace of type IIB superstring theory\\nin $AdS_5 \\\\times S^5$. \
The comparison of the strong-coupling invariance derived\\nhere with the \
weak-coupling generators shows that the local term must depend on\\nthe \
coupling in a non-trivial way. Additionally, we show that the \
higher-level\\nrecurrences of the hypercharge generator, the so-called bonus \
symmetries, are\\npresent in all higher levels of the Yangian.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 13 Dec 2017 10:09:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2017-12-14\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"M\[UDoubleDot]nkler\"", ",", "\"Hagen\"", ",", 
                    "\"\""}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, 
