           "id" -> "1712.04684", "submitter" -> "Hagen M\\\"unkler", 
            "authors" -> "Hagen M\\\"unkler", "title" -> 
            "Symmetries of Maldacena-Wilson Loops from Integrable String \
Theory", "comments" -> 
            "PhD-Thesis based on the works arXiv:1503.07553, \
arXiv:1507.02474,\n  arXiv:1606.04104, arXiv:1610.01161. 209 pages, 11 \
figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this thesis, we investigate hidden symmetries for the \
Maldacena-Wilson\nloop in N=4 super Yang-Mills theory, mainly focusing on its \
strong-coupling\ndescription as a minimal surface in $AdS_5$. In the \
discussion of the symmetry\nstructure of the underlying string model, we \
highlight the role of the master\nsymmetry which can be employed to construct \
all symmetries of the model. The\nalgebra of these symmetries is worked out. \
For the concrete case of minimal\nsurfaces in $AdS_5$, we discuss the \
deformation of the four-cusp solution,\nwhich provides the dual description \
of the four-gluon scattering amplitude.\nThis marks the first step toward \
transferring the master symmetry to scattering\namplitudes. Moreover, we \
compute the master and Yangian symmetry variations of\ngeneric, smooth \
boundary curves. The discussion clarifies why previous attempts\nto transfer \
the deformations of minimal surfaces in $AdS_3$ to weak coupling\nwere \
unsuccessful. We discuss several attempts to transfer the Yangian symmetry\n\
to weak or arbitrary coupling, but ultimately conclude that a Yangian \
symmetry\nof the Maldacena-Wilson loop seems not to be present. This is \
different for the\nnatural supersymmetric generalizations of the \
Maldacena--Wilson loop, Wilson\nloops in superspace. Their one-loop \
expectation value is known to be Yangian\ninvariant. We discuss the \
strong-coupling counterpart of this finding by\nconsidering minimal surfaces \
in the superspace of type IIB superstring theory\nin $AdS_5 \\times S^5$. The \
comparison of the strong-coupling invariance derived\nhere with the \
weak-coupling generators shows that the local term must depend on\nthe \
coupling in a non-trivial way. Additionally, we show that the higher-level\n\
recurrences of the hypercharge generator, the so-called bonus symmetries, are\
\npresent in all higher levels of the Yangian.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
