               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1712.06874\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matteo Beccaria\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Beccaria, Simone Giombi, Arkady Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-supersymmetric Wilson loop in N=4 SYM and defect 1d \
CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"36 pages, 3 figures. v4: minor corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2018)131\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PUPT-2543, NSF-ITP-17-141, Imperial-TP-AAT-2017-09\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Following Polchinski and Sully (arXiv:1104.5077), we \
consider a generalized\\nWilson loop operator containing a constant parameter \
$\\\\zeta$ in front of the\\nscalar coupling term, so that $\\\\zeta=0$ \
corresponds to the standard Wilson\\nloop, while $\\\\zeta=1$ to the locally \
supersymmetric one. We compute the\\nexpectation value of this operator for \
circular loop as a function of $\\\\zeta$\\nto second order in the planar \
weak coupling expansion in N=4 SYM theory. We\\nthen explain the relation of \
the expansion near the two conformal points\\n$\\\\zeta=0$ and $\\\\zeta=1$ \
to the correlators of scalar operators inserted on the\\nloop. We also \
discuss the $AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ string 1-loop correction to \
the\\nstrong-coupling expansion of the standard circular Wilson loop, as well \
as its\\ngeneralization to the case of mixed boundary conditions on the \
five-sphere\\ncoordinates, corresponding to general $\\\\zeta$. From the \
point of view of the\\ndefect 1d CFT defined on the Wilson line, the \
$\\\\zeta$-dependent term can be\\nseen as a perturbation driving a RG flow \
from the standard Wilson loop in the\\nUV to the supersymmetric Wilson loop \
in the IR. Both at weak and strong\\ncoupling we find that the logarithm of \
the expectation value of the standard\\nWilson loop for the circular contour \
is larger than that of the supersymmetric\\none, which appears to be in \
agreement with the 1d analog of the F-theorem.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 19 Dec 2017 11:42:32 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 9 Jan 2018 08:44:03 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
