               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Martin Bojowald, Suddhasattwa Brahma, Umut Buyukcam, \
Michele Ronco\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Extending general covariance: Moyal-type noncommutative \
manifolds\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 98, 026031 (2018)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.98.026031\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the Hamiltonian formulation of general relativity, \
Einstein's equation is\\nreplaced by a set of four constraints. Classically, \
the constraints can be\\nidentified with the generators of the \
hypersurface-deformation Lie algebroid\\n(HDA) that belongs to the groupoid \
of finite evolutions in space-time. Taken\\nover to deformed general \
relativity, this connection allows one to study\\npossible Drinfeld twists of \
space-time diffeomorphisms with Hopf-algebra\\ntechniques. After a review of \
noncommutative differential structures, two cases\\n--- twisted \
diffeomorphisms with standard action and deformed (or \
$\\\\star$-)\\ndiffeomorphisms with deformed action --- are considered in \
this paper. The HDA\\nof twisted diffeomorphisms agrees with the classical \
one, while the HDA\\nobtained from deformed diffeomorphisms is modified due \
to the explicit presence\\nof $\\\\star$-products in the brackets. The \
results allow one to distinguish\\nbetween twisted and deformed symmetries, \
and they indicate that the latter\\nshould be regarded as the relevant \
symmetry transformations for noncommutative\\nmanifolds. The algebroid \
brackets maintain the same general structure\\nregardless of space-time \
noncommutativity, but they still show important\\nconsequences of \
non-locality.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 20 Dec 2017 11:02:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
