Ronco", "title" -> 
            "Extending general covariance: Moyal-type noncommutative \
manifolds", "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys. Rev. D 98, 026031 (2018)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.98.026031", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In the Hamiltonian formulation of general relativity, \
Einstein's equation is\nreplaced by a set of four constraints. Classically, \
the constraints can be\nidentified with the generators of the \
hypersurface-deformation Lie algebroid\n(HDA) that belongs to the groupoid of \
finite evolutions in space-time. Taken\nover to deformed general relativity, \
this connection allows one to study\npossible Drinfeld twists of space-time \
diffeomorphisms with Hopf-algebra\ntechniques. After a review of \
noncommutative differential structures, two cases\n--- twisted \
diffeomorphisms with standard action and deformed (or $\\star$-)\n\
diffeomorphisms with deformed action --- are considered in this paper. The \
HDA\nof twisted diffeomorphisms agrees with the classical one, while the HDA\n\
obtained from deformed diffeomorphisms is modified due to the explicit \
presence\nof $\\star$-products in the brackets. The results allow one to \
distinguish\nbetween twisted and deformed symmetries, and they indicate that \
the latter\nshould be regarded as the relevant symmetry transformations for \
noncommutative\nmanifolds. The algebroid brackets maintain the same general \
structure\nregardless of space-time noncommutativity, but they still show \
important\nconsequences of non-locality.\n", 
