Zarembo", "title" -> 
             "String corrections to circular Wilson loop and anomalies", 
             "comments" -> 
             "26 pages, 3 figures; v2: minor misprints corrected, no changes \
in the\n  equations", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1007/JHEP02(2018)120", "report-no" -> 
             "NORDITA 2017-136, UUITP-52/17", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
             "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We study string quantum corrections to the ratio of latitude \
and circular\nWilson loops in N=4 super-Yang-Mills theory at strong coupling. \
Conformal gauge\nfor the corresponding minimal surface in AdS(5)xS(5) is \
singular and we show\nthat an IR anomaly associated with the divergence in \
the conformal factor\nremoves previously reported discrepancy with the exact \
field-theory result. We\nalso carefully check conformal anomaly cancellation \
and recalculate fluctuation\ndeterminants by directly evaluating phaseshifts \
for all the fluctuation modes.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Wed, 20 Dec 2017 22:17:25 GMT"}, {
