           "id" -> "1712.08861", "submitter" -> "Brian Willett", "authors" -> 
            "Chiara Toldo and Brian Willett", "title" -> 
            "Partition functions on 3d circle bundles and their gravity \
duals", "comments" -> 
            "typos in eqs 5.51 and subsequent fixed, conclusions unaltered", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2018)116", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The partition function of a three-dimensional $\\mathcal{N} \
=2$ theory on the\nmanifold $\\mathcal{M}_{g,p}$, an $S^1$ bundle of degree \
$p$ over a closed\nRiemann surface $\\Sigma_g$, was recently computed via \
supersymmetric\nlocalization. In this paper, we compute these partition \
functions at large $N$\nin a class of quiver gauge theories with holographic \
M-theory duals. We provide\nthe supergravity bulk dual having as conformal \
boundary such three-dimensional\ncircle bundles. These configurations are \
solutions to $\\mathcal{N}=2$ minimal\ngauged supergravity and pertain to the \
class of Taub-NUT-AdS and Taub-Bolt-AdS\npreserving $1/4$ of the \
supersymmetries. We discuss the conditions for the\nuplift of these solutions \
to M-theory, and compute the on-shell action via\nholographic \
renormalization. We show that the uplift condition and on-shell\naction for \
the Bolt solutions are correctly reproduced by the large $N$ limit\nof the \
partition function of the dual superconformal field theory. In\nparticular, \
the $\\Sigma_g \\times S^1 \\cong \\mathcal{M}_{g,0}$ partition\nfunction, \
which was recently shown to match the entropy of $AdS_4$ black holes,\nand \
the $S^3 \\cong \\mathcal{M}_{0,1}$ free energy, occur as special cases of\n\
our formalism, and we comment on relations between them.\n", 
