Yacoby\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Coulomb Branch Operators and Mirror Symmetry in Three \
Dimensions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"92 pages plus appendices, two figures; v2 and v3: typos \
corrected,\\n  references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2018)037\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"CALT-TH 2017-064; PUPT-2547; WIS/05/17-Dec-DPPA\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop new techniques for computing exact \
correlation functions of a\\nclass of local operators, including certain \
monopole operators, in\\nthree-dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N} = 4$ abelian gauge \
theories that have\\nsuperconformal infrared limits. These operators are \
position-dependent linear\\ncombinations of Coulomb branch operators. They \
form a one-dimensional\\ntopological sector that encodes a deformation \
quantization of the Coulomb\\nbranch chiral ring, and their correlation \
functions completely fix the ($n\\\\leq\\n3$)-point functions of all half-BPS \
Coulomb branch operators. Using these\\nresults, we provide new derivations \
of the conformal dimension of half-BPS\\nmonopole operators as well as new \
and detailed tests of mirror symmetry. Our\\nmain approach involves \
supersymmetric localization on a hemisphere $HS^3$ with\\nhalf-BPS boundary \
conditions, where operator insertions within the hemisphere\\nare represented \
by certain shift operators acting on the $HS^3$ wavefunction.\\nBy gluing a \
pair of such wavefunctions, we obtain correlators on $S^3$ with \
an\\narbitrary number of operator insertions. Finally, we show that our \
results can\\nbe recovered by dimensionally reducing the Schur index of 4D \
$\\\\mathcal{N} = 2$\\ntheories decorated by BPS 't Hooft-Wilson \
loops.\\n\""}]}, {
