            "  We develop new techniques for computing exact correlation \
functions of a\nclass of local operators, including certain monopole \
operators, in\nthree-dimensional $\\mathcal{N} = 4$ abelian gauge theories \
that have\nsuperconformal infrared limits. These operators are \
position-dependent linear\ncombinations of Coulomb branch operators. They \
form a one-dimensional\ntopological sector that encodes a deformation \
quantization of the Coulomb\nbranch chiral ring, and their correlation \
functions completely fix the ($n\\leq\n3$)-point functions of all half-BPS \
Coulomb branch operators. Using these\nresults, we provide new derivations of \
the conformal dimension of half-BPS\nmonopole operators as well as new and \
detailed tests of mirror symmetry. Our\nmain approach involves supersymmetric \
localization on a hemisphere $HS^3$ with\nhalf-BPS boundary conditions, where \
operator insertions within the hemisphere\nare represented by certain shift \
operators acting on the $HS^3$ wavefunction.\nBy gluing a pair of such \
wavefunctions, we obtain correlators on $S^3$ with an\narbitrary number of \
operator insertions. Finally, we show that our results can\nbe recovered by \
dimensionally reducing the Schur index of 4D $\\mathcal{N} = 2$\ntheories \
decorated by BPS 't Hooft-Wilson loops.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
