            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1712.09974\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Toshiaki Fujimori\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Toshiaki Fujimori, Muneto Nitta, Keisuke Ohashi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Massive Nambu-Goldstone Fermions and Bosons for \
Non-relativistic\\n  Superconformal Symmetry: Jackiw-Pi Vortices in a \
Trap\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"24 pages, 5 figures, references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Prog Theor Exp Phys (2020)\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1093/ptep/ptaa052\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss a supersymmetric extension of a \
non-relativistic Chern-Simons\\nmatter theory, known as the SUSY Jackiw-Pi \
model, in a harmonic trap. We show\\nthat the non-relativistic version of the \
superconformal symmetry, called the\\nsuper-Schr\\\\\\\"odinger symmetry, is \
not spoiled by an external field including the\\nharmonic potential. It \
survives as a modified symmetry whose generators have\\nexplicit time \
dependences determined by the strength of the trap, the rotation\\nvelocity \
of the system and the fermion number chemical potential. We construct\\n1/3 \
BPS states of trapped Jackiw-Pi vortices preserving a part of the \
modified\\nsuperconformal symmetry and discuss fluctuations around static BPS\
\\nconfigurations. In addition to the bosonic massive Nambu-Goldstone modes, \
we\\nfind that there exist massive Nambu-Goldstone fermions associated with \
broken\\nmodified super-Schr\\\\\\\"odinger symmetry generators. Furthermore, \
we find that\\neigenmodes form supermultiplets of a modified supersymmetry \
preserved by the\\nstatic BPS backgrounds. As a consequence of the modified \
supersymmetry,\\ninfinite towers of explicit spectra can be found for \
eigenmodes correspond- ing\\nto bosonic and fermionic lowest Landau \
levels.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 28 Dec 2017 18:35:15 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 8 Mar 2018 02:00:36 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-05-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Fujimori\"", ",", "\"Toshiaki\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
