         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1712.09974", "submitter" -> "Toshiaki Fujimori", 
            "authors" -> "Toshiaki Fujimori, Muneto Nitta, Keisuke Ohashi", 
            "title" -> 
            "Massive Nambu-Goldstone Fermions and Bosons for Non-relativistic\
\n  Superconformal Symmetry: Jackiw-Pi Vortices in a Trap", "comments" -> 
            "24 pages, 5 figures, references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Prog Theor Exp Phys (2020)", "doi" -> "10.1093/ptep/ptaa052", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss a supersymmetric extension of a non-relativistic \
Chern-Simons\nmatter theory, known as the SUSY Jackiw-Pi model, in a harmonic \
trap. We show\nthat the non-relativistic version of the superconformal \
symmetry, called the\nsuper-Schr\\\"odinger symmetry, is not spoiled by an \
external field including the\nharmonic potential. It survives as a modified \
symmetry whose generators have\nexplicit time dependences determined by the \
strength of the trap, the rotation\nvelocity of the system and the fermion \
number chemical potential. We construct\n1/3 BPS states of trapped Jackiw-Pi \
vortices preserving a part of the modified\nsuperconformal symmetry and \
discuss fluctuations around static BPS\nconfigurations. In addition to the \
bosonic massive Nambu-Goldstone modes, we\nfind that there exist massive \
Nambu-Goldstone fermions associated with broken\nmodified \
super-Schr\\\"odinger symmetry generators. Furthermore, we find that\n\
eigenmodes form supermultiplets of a modified supersymmetry preserved by the\n\
static BPS backgrounds. As a consequence of the modified supersymmetry,\n\
infinite towers of explicit spectra can be found for eigenmodes correspond- \
ing\nto bosonic and fermionic lowest Landau levels.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 28 Dec 2017 18:35:15 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 8 Mar 2018 02:00:36 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-05-20", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fujimori", "Toshiaki", ""}, {
              "Nitta", "Muneto", ""}, {"Ohashi", "Keisuke", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
