Ed.\n  by Jochen Bruening and Matthias Staudacher, ISBN 978-3-11-045215-0 (to \
be\n  published in March 2018)", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> "HU-EP-17/32", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this short review (to appear as a contribution to an edited \
volume) we\ndiscuss perturbative and non-perturbative approaches to the \
quantization of the\nGreen-Schwarz string in AdS backgrounds with RR-fluxes, \
where the guiding\nthread is the use of genuine field theory methods, the \
search for a good\nregularization scheme associated to them and the \
generality of the analysis\ncarried out. We touch upon various computational \
setups, both analytical and\nnumerical, and on the role of their outcomes in \
understanding the detailed\nstructure of the AdS/CFT correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
