         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1801.03838", "submitter" -> "Balazs Pozsgay", "authors" -> 
            "B. Pozsgay", "title" -> 
            "Overlaps with arbitrary two-site states in the XXZ spin chain", 
            "comments" -> "22 pages, v2: references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1742-5468/aabbe1", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "cond-mat.stat-mech nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a conjectured exact formula for overlaps between \
the Bethe states\nof the spin-1/2 XXZ chain and generic two-site states. The \
result takes the\nsame form as in the previously known cases: it involves the \
same ratio of two\nGaudin-like determinants, and a product of single-particle \
overlap functions,\nwhich can be fixed using a combination of the Quench \
Action and Quantum\nTransfer Matrix methods. Our conjecture is confirmed by \
numerical data from\nexact diagonalization. For one-site states the formula \
is found to be correct\neven in chains with odd length, where existing \
methods can not be applied. It\nis also pointed out, that the ratio of the \
Gaudin-like determinants plays a\ncrucial role in the overlap sum rule: it \
guarantees that in the thermodynamic\nlimit there remains no \
$\\mathcal{O}(1)$ piece in the Quench Action.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 11 Jan 2018 16:00:12 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 25 Jan 2018 14:03:28 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2018-05-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Pozsgay", "B.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
