            "Justin R. David, Edi Gava, Rajesh Kumar Gupta, Kumar Narain", 
            "title" -> "Boundary Conditions and Localization on AdS: Part 1", 
            "comments" -> "34 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP09(2018)063", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the role of boundary conditions on the one loop \
partition function\nof ${\\cal N}=2$ chiral multiplet of R-charge $\\Delta$ \
on $AdS_2\\times S^1$. The\nchiral multiplet is coupled to a background \
vector multiplet which preserves\nsupersymmetry. We implement normalizable \
boundary conditions in $AdS_2$ and\ndevelop the Green's function method to \
obtain the one loop determinant. We\nevaluate the one loop determinant for \
two different actions: the standard\naction and the $Q$-exact deformed \
positive definite action used for\nlocalization. We show that if there exists \
an integer $n$ in the interval $D: (\n\\frac{\\Delta-1}{2L}, \
\\frac{\\Delta}{2L} )$, where $L$ being the ratio of radius\nof $AdS_2$ to \
that of $S^1$, then the one loop determinants obtained for the\ntwo actions \
differ. It is in this situation that fields which obey normalizable\nboundary \
conditions do not obey supersymmetric boundary conditions. However if\nthere \
are no integers in $D$, then fields which obey normalizable boundary\n\
conditions also obey supersymmetric boundary conditions and the one loop\n\
determinants of the two actions precisely agree. We also show that it is only\
\nin the latter situation that the one loop determinant obtained by \
evaluating\nthe index of the $D_{10}$ operator associated with the localizing \
action agrees\nwith the one loop determinant obtained using Green's function \
method.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
