 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using $\\\\zeta$-function regularization, we study the \
one-loop effective action\\nof fundamental strings in $AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ \
dual to the latitude\\n$\\\\frac{1}{4}$-BPS Wilson loop in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
Super-Yang-Mills theory. To\\navoid certain ambiguities inherent to string \
theory on curved backgrounds we\\nsubtract the effective action of the \
holographic $\\\\frac{1}{2}$-BPS Wilson loop.\\nWe find agreement with the \
expected field theory result at first order in the\\nsmall latitude angle \
expansion but discrepancies at higher order.\\n\""}]}, {
