Penati and\\n  Domenico Seminara\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A matrix model for the latitude Wilson loop in ABJM \
theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"73 pages; v2: several improvements, JHEP published \
version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2018)060\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In ABJ(M) theory, we propose a matrix model for the \
exact evaluation of BPS\\nWilson loops on a latitude circular contour, so \
providing a new weak-strong\\ninterpolation tool. Intriguingly, the matrix \
model turns out to be a particular\\ncase of that computing torus knot \
invariants in $U(N_1|N_2)$ Chern-Simons\\ntheory. At weak coupling we check \
our proposal against a three-loop\\ncomputation, performed for generic \
framing, winding number and representation.\\nThe matrix model is amenable of \
a Fermi gas formulation, which we use to\\nsystematically compute the strong \
coupling and genus expansions. For the\\nfermionic Wilson loop the leading \
planar behavior agrees with a previous string\\ntheory prediction. For the \
bosonic operator our result provides a clue for\\nfinding the corresponding \
string dual configuration. Our matrix model is\\nconsistent with recent \
proposals for computing Bremsstrahlung functions exactly\\nin terms of \
latitude Wilson loops. As a by-product, we extend the conjecture\\nfor the \
exact $B^{\\\\theta}_{1/6}$ Bremsstrahlung function to \
generic\\nrepresentations and test it with a four-loop perturbative \
computation. Finally,\\nwe propose an exact prediction for $B_{1/2}$ at \
unequal gauge group ranks.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
