         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1802.07742", "submitter" -> "Andrea Mauri", "authors" -> 
            "Marco S. Bianchi, Luca Griguolo, Andrea Mauri, Silvia Penati and\
\n  Domenico Seminara", "title" -> 
            "A matrix model for the latitude Wilson loop in ABJM theory", 
            "comments" -> 
            "73 pages; v2: several improvements, JHEP published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2018)060", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In ABJ(M) theory, we propose a matrix model for the exact \
evaluation of BPS\nWilson loops on a latitude circular contour, so providing \
a new weak-strong\ninterpolation tool. Intriguingly, the matrix model turns \
out to be a particular\ncase of that computing torus knot invariants in \
$U(N_1|N_2)$ Chern-Simons\ntheory. At weak coupling we check our proposal \
against a three-loop\ncomputation, performed for generic framing, winding \
number and representation.\nThe matrix model is amenable of a Fermi gas \
formulation, which we use to\nsystematically compute the strong coupling and \
genus expansions. For the\nfermionic Wilson loop the leading planar behavior \
agrees with a previous string\ntheory prediction. For the bosonic operator \
our result provides a clue for\nfinding the corresponding string dual \
configuration. Our matrix model is\nconsistent with recent proposals for \
computing Bremsstrahlung functions exactly\nin terms of latitude Wilson \
loops. As a by-product, we extend the conjecture\nfor the exact \
$B^{\\theta}_{1/6}$ Bremsstrahlung function to generic\nrepresentations and \
test it with a four-loop perturbative computation. Finally,\nwe propose an \
exact prediction for $B_{1/2}$ at unequal gauge group ranks.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
