               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider conformal N=2 super Yang-Mills theories \
with gauge group SU(N)\\nand Nf=2N fundamental hypermultiplets in presence of \
a circular 1/2-BPS Wilson\\nloop. It is natural to conjecture that the matrix \
model which describes the\\nexpectation value of this system also encodes the \
one-point functions of chiral\\nscalar operators in presence of the Wilson \
loop. We obtain evidence of this\\nconjecture by successfully comparing, at \
finite N and at the two-loop order,\\nthe one-point functions computed in \
field theory with the vacuum expectation\\nvalues of the corresponding \
normal-ordered operators in the matrix model. For\\nthe part of these \
expressions with transcendentality zeta(3), we also obtain\\nresults in the \
large-N limit that are exact in the 't Hooft coupling lambda.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
