                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study worldsheet theory of confining strings in \
two-dimensional massive\\nadjoint QCD. Similarly to confining strings in \
higher dimensions this theory\\nexhibits a non-trivial $S$-matrix surviving \
even in the strict planar limit. In\\nthe process of two-particle scattering \
a zigzag is formed on the worldsheet. It\\nleads to an interesting \
non-locality and exhibits some properties of a quantum\\nblack hole. \
Ordinarily, identical quantum particles do not carry identity. On\\nthe \
worldsheet they acquire off-shell identity due to strings \
attached.\\nIdentity implies complementarity. We discuss similarities and \
differences of\\nthe worldsheet scattering with the $T\\\\bar{T}$ \
deformation. We also propose a\\npromising candidate for a supersymmetric \
model with integrable confining\\nstrings.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
