 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study supersymmetric Wilson loops in $d=3$, \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=3$ harmonic\\nsuperspace, leading to a construction of a \
supersymmetrized generalization of\\nthe $\\\\frac{1}{3}$-BPS Wilson loop for \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=3$ gauge theories. This also\\nincludes a generalization of \
the $\\\\frac{1}{6}$-BPS loop for ABJM theory. We\\nperform a 'one-loop' \
computation of the vacuum expectation value of this\\noperator directly in \
superspace and compare with the known $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$\\nlocalization \
results at large $N$. This comparison also lets us identify\\ncertain \
fermionic contributions that do not receive any subleading \
corrections.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
