                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A formula was recently proposed for the perturbative \
partition function of\\ncertain $\\\\mathcal N=1$ gauge theories on the round \
four-sphere, using an\\nanalytic-continuation argument in the number of \
dimensions. These partition\\nfunctions are not currently accessible via the \
usual\\nsupersymmetric-localisation technique. We provide a natural \
refinement of this\\nresult to the case of the ellipsoid. We then use it to \
write down the\\nperturbative partition function of an $\\\\mathcal N=1$ \
toroidal-quiver theory (a\\ndouble orbifold of $\\\\mathcal N=4$ super \
Yang-Mills) and show that, in the\\ndeconstruction limit, it reproduces the \
zero-winding contributions to the BPS\\npartition function of (1,1) Little \
String Theory wrapping an emergent torus. We\\ntherefore successfully test \
both the expressions for the $\\\\mathcal N=1$\\npartition functions, as well \
as the relationship between the toroidal-quiver\\ntheory and Little String \
Theory through dimensional deconstruction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
