            "  A formula was recently proposed for the perturbative partition \
function of\ncertain $\\mathcal N=1$ gauge theories on the round four-sphere, \
using an\nanalytic-continuation argument in the number of dimensions. These \
partition\nfunctions are not currently accessible via the usual\n\
supersymmetric-localisation technique. We provide a natural refinement of \
this\nresult to the case of the ellipsoid. We then use it to write down the\n\
perturbative partition function of an $\\mathcal N=1$ toroidal-quiver theory \
