            "  We study meson decays using instanton methods in two string \
models. The first\nmodel is the old string model in flat space which combines \
strings and massive\nparticles and the second is the holographic, \
Sakai-Sugimoto model. Using the\nthe old string model, we reproduce the QCD \
formula for the probability of\nsplitting of the QCD flux tube derived by \
Casher-Neuberger-Nussinov (CNN). In\nthe holographic model we construct a \
string worldsheet instanton which\ninterpolates between a single and double \
string configuration, which determines\nthe decay from one to two dual \
mesonic particles. The resulting probability for\nmeson decay incorporates \
both the effects of finite meson size as well as\nback-reaction of the \
produced quarks on the QCD flux tube. In the limit of very\nlarge strings the \
probability for a split reduces to the CNN formula. A\nbyproduct of our \
analysis is the analysis of the moduli space of a generic\ndouble concentric \
Wilson loop with circles which are separated in the\nholographic direction of \
the confining background.\n", 
