                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We introduce non-trivial two-point functions of the \
super Schur polynomials\\nin the ABJM matrix model and study their exact \
values with the Fermi gas\\nformalism. We find that, although defined \
non-trivially, these two-point\\nfunctions enjoy two simple relations with \
the one-point functions. One of them\\nis associated with the \
Littlewood-Richardson rule, while the other is more\\nnovel. With plenty of \
data, we also revisit the one-point functions and study\\nhow the diagonal \
BPS indices are split asymmetrically by the degree difference.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
