                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate the Spencer cohomology of the $(1,0)$ \
Poincar\\\\'e superalgebras\\nin six dimensions: with and without R-symmetry. \
As the cases of four and eleven\\ndimensions taught us, we may read off from \
this calculation a Killing spinor\\nequation which allows the determination \
of which geometries admit rigidly\\nsupersymmetric theories in this \
dimension. We prove that the resulting Killing\\nspinors generate a Lie \
superalgebra and determine the geometries admitting the\\nmaximal number of \
such Killing spinors. They are divided in two branches. One\\nbranch consists \
of the lorentzian Lie groups with bi-invariant metrics and, as\\na special \
case, it includes the lorentzian Lie groups with a self-dual \
Cartan\\nthree-form which define the maximally supersymmetric backgrounds of \
$(1,0)$\\nPoincar\\\\'e supergravity in six dimensions. The notion of Killing \
spinor on the\\nother branch does not depend on the choice of a three-form \
but rather on a\\none-form valued in the R-symmetry algebra. In this case, we \
obtain three\\ndifferent (up to local isometry) maximally supersymmetric \
backgrounds, which\\nare distinguished by the causal type of the one-form.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
