            "Jos\\'e M. Figueroa-O'Farrill", "authors" -> 
            "Paul de Medeiros, Jos\\'e Figueroa-O'Farrill, Andrea Santi", 
            "title" -> "Killing superalgebras for Lorentzian six-manifolds", 
            "comments" -> 
            "38 pages (final version to appear in Journal of Geometry and \
Physics)", "journal-ref" -> "J. Geom. Phys. 132 (2018), 13-44", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.geomphys.2018.05.019", "report-no" -> "EMPG-17-21", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math.DG math.RT", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate the Spencer cohomology of the $(1,0)$ Poincar\\'e \
superalgebras\nin six dimensions: with and without R-symmetry. As the cases \
of four and eleven\ndimensions taught us, we may read off from this \
calculation a Killing spinor\nequation which allows the determination of \
which geometries admit rigidly\nsupersymmetric theories in this dimension. We \
prove that the resulting Killing\nspinors generate a Lie superalgebra and \
determine the geometries admitting the\nmaximal number of such Killing \
spinors. They are divided in two branches. One\nbranch consists of the \
lorentzian Lie groups with bi-invariant metrics and, as\na special case, it \
includes the lorentzian Lie groups with a self-dual Cartan\nthree-form which \
define the maximally supersymmetric backgrounds of $(1,0)$\nPoincar\\'e \
supergravity in six dimensions. The notion of Killing spinor on the\nother \
branch does not depend on the choice of a three-form but rather on a\n\
one-form valued in the R-symmetry algebra. In this case, we obtain three\n\
different (up to local isometry) maximally supersymmetric backgrounds, which\n\
are distinguished by the causal type of the one-form.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
