                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study four-dimensional quantum gravity with negative \
cosmological constant\\nin the minisuperspace approximation and compute the \
partition function for the\\n$S^3$ boundary geometry. In this approximation \
scheme the path integrals become\\ndominated by a class of asymptotically AdS \
\\\"microstate geometries.\\\" Despite the\\nfact that the theory is pure \
Einstein gravity without supersymmetry, the result\\nprecisely reproduces, up \
to higher curvature corrections, the Airy function in\\nthe $S^3$ partition \
function of the maximally supersymmetric\\nChern-Simons-matter (CSM) theory \
which sums up all perturbative $1/N$\\ncorrections. We also show that this \
can be interpreted as a concrete\\nrealization of the idea that the CFT \
partition function is a solution to the\\nWheeler-DeWitt equation as \
advocated in the holographic renormalization group.\\nFurthermore, the \
agreement persists upon the inclusion of a string probe and it\\nreproduces \
the Airy function in the vev of half-BPS Wilson loops in the CSM\\ntheory. \
These results may suggest that the supergravity path integrals localize\\nto \
the minisuperspace in certain cases and the use of the \
minisuperspace\\napproximation in AdS/CFT may be a viable approach to study \
$1/N$ corrections to\\nlarge $N$ CFTs.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 3 Apr 2018 13:05:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
