                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  String theory on $AdS_3 \\\\times S^3 \\\\times T^4$ \
has 20 moduli. We investigate\\nhow the perturbative closed string spectrum \
changes as we move around this\\nmoduli space in both the RR and NSNS flux \
backgrounds. We find that, at weak\\nstring coupling, only four of the moduli \
affect the energies. In the RR\\nbackground the only effect of these moduli \
is to change the radius of curvature\\nof the background. On the other hand, \
in the NSNS background, the moduli\\nintroduce worldsheet interactions which \
enable the use of integrability methods\\nto solve the spectral problem. Our \
results show that the worldsheet theory is\\nintegrable across the 20 \
dimensional moduli space.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
