            "  Building on our previous work arXiv:1712.06874 we consider \
one-parameter\nPolchinski-Sully generalization of the Wilson-Maldacena (WM) \
loops in planar\nN=4 SYM theory. This breaks local supersymmetry of WM loop \
and leads to running\nof the deformation parameter $\\zeta$. We compute the \
three-loop ladder diagram\ncontribution to the expectation value of the \
circular loop which gives the full\nanswer for large $\\zeta$. The limit \
$\\zeta\\gg 1$, $\\lambda \\zeta^2=$ fixed in\nwhich the expectation value is \
determined by the Gaussian adjoint scalar path\nintegral might be exactly \
solvable despite the lack of global supersymmetry. We\nstudy similar \
generalization of the 1/4-BPS \"latitude\" WM loop which depends on\ntwo \
parameters (in addition to the 't Hooft coupling $\\lambda$). One may also\n\
introduce another supersymmetry-breaking parameter -- the winding number of \
the\nscalar coupling circle. We find the two-loop expression for the \
expectation\nvalue of the associated loop by combining the ladder diagram \
contribution with\nan indirect determination of the non-ladder contribution \
using 1d defect CFT\nperturbation theory.\n", 
