                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We introduce the 3-colour noncommutative quantum field \
theory model in two\\ndimensions. For this model we prove a generalised \
Ward-Takahashi identity,\\nwhich is special to coloured noncommutative QFT \
models and has no underlying\\ncontinuous symmetry. It reduces to the usual \
Ward-Takahashi identity in a\\nparticular case. The Ward-Takahashi identity \
is used to simplify the\\nSchwinger-Dyson equations for the 2-point function \
and the N-point function.\\nThe absence of any renormalisation conditions in \
the large\\n$(\\\\mathcal{N},V)$-limit in 2D leads to a recursive integral \
equation for the\\n2-point function, which we solve perturbatively to sixth \
order in the coupling\\nconstant.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
