           "id" -> "1804.06075", "submitter" -> "Alexander Hock", "authors" -> 
            "Alexander Hock, Raimar Wulkenhaar", "title" -> 
            "Noncommutative 3-colour scalar quantum field theory model in 2D",
             "comments" -> "24 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Eur.Phys.J. C78 (2018) no.7, 580", "doi" -> 
            "10.1140/epjc/s10052-018-6042-3", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We introduce the 3-colour noncommutative quantum field theory \
model in two\ndimensions. For this model we prove a generalised \
Ward-Takahashi identity,\nwhich is special to coloured noncommutative QFT \
models and has no underlying\ncontinuous symmetry. It reduces to the usual \
Ward-Takahashi identity in a\nparticular case. The Ward-Takahashi identity is \
used to simplify the\nSchwinger-Dyson equations for the 2-point function and \
the N-point function.\nThe absence of any renormalisation conditions in the \
large\n$(\\mathcal{N},V)$-limit in 2D leads to a recursive integral equation \
for the\n2-point function, which we solve perturbatively to sixth order in \
the coupling\nconstant.\n", 
