            "id" -> "1804.08925", "submitter" -> "Konstantin Zarembo", 
             "authors" -> 
             "Daniel Medina-Rincon, Arkady A. Tseytlin and Konstantin \
Zarembo", "title" -> 
             "Precision matching of circular Wilson loops and strings in \
AdS(5)xS(5)", "comments" -> "21 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1007/JHEP05(2018)199", "report-no" -> 
             "Imperial-TP-AT-2018-03, NORDITA-2018-033, UUITP-15/18", 
             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  Previous attempts to match the exact N=4 super Yang-Mills \
expression for the\nexpectation value of the 1/2-BPS circular Wilson loop \
with the semiclassical\nAdS(5)xS(5) string theory prediction were not \
successful at the first\nsubleading order. There was a missing prefactor ~ \
lambda^(-3/4) which could be\nattributed to the unknown normalization of the \
string path integral measure.\nHere we resolve this problem by computing the \
ratio of the string partition\nfunctions corresponding to the circular Wilson \
loop and the special\n1/4-supersymmetric latitude Wilson loop. The fact that \
the latter has a trivial\nexpectation value in the gauge theory allows us to \
relate the prefactor to the\ncontribution of the three zero modes of the \
\"transverse\" fluctuation operator\nin the 5-sphere directions.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Tue, 24 Apr 2018 09:36:48 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2018-07-04", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Medina-Rincon", "Daniel", ""}, {
               "Tseytlin", "Arkady A.", ""}, {"Zarembo", "Konstantin", ""}}}],
            "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
