            "  We generalize earlier results on one-point functions in N = 4 \
SYM with a\nco-dimension one defect, dual to the D3-D5-brane setup in type \
IIB string\ntheory on AdS5xS5, to a similar setup in the $\\beta$-deformed \
version of the\ntheory. The treelevel vacuum expectation values of \
single-trace operators in\nthe two-scalar-subsector are expressed as overlaps \
between a matrix product\nstate (MPS) and Bethe states in the corresponding \
twisted spin-chain picture.\nWe comment on the properties of this MPS and \
present the simplest analytical\noverlaps and their behavior in a certain \
limit (of large k). Importantly, we\nnote that the deformation alters earlier \
interpretations of the MPS as an\nintegrable boundary state, seemingly \
obstructing simplifications of the\noverlaps analogous to the compact \
determinant formula found in the non-deformed\ntheory. The results are \
supplemented with some supporting numerical results for\noperators of length \
eight with four excitations.\n", 
