                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the one-loop correction to the classical \
dispersion relation of\\nrigid closed spinning strings with two equal angular \
momenta in the $AdS_3\\n\\\\times S^3 \\\\times T^4$ background supported \
with a mixture of R-R and NS-NS\\nthree-form fluxes. This analysis is \
extended to the case of two arbitrary\\nangular momenta in the pure NS-NS \
limit. We perform this computation by means\\nof two different methods. The \
first method relies on the Euler-Lagrange\\nequations for the quadratic \
fluctuations around the classical solution, while\\nthe second one exploits \
the underlying integrability of the problem through the\\nfinite-gap \
equations. We find that the one-loop correction vanishes in the pure\\nNS-NS \
limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
