               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wilson loops and free energies in $3d$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
SYM: exact\\n  results, exponential asymptotics and duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"17 pages, v2: Section on asymptotics revised; two typos \
corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Progress of Theoretical and Experimental Physics, Vol \
2019,\\n  (2019), 053B01\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1093/ptep/ptz036\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that $U(N)$ $3d$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
supersymmetric gauge theories on\\n$S^{3}$ with $N_{f}$ massive fundamental \
hypermultiplets and with a\\nFayet-Iliopoulos (FI) term are solvable in terms \
of generalized Selberg\\nintegrals. Finite $N$ expressions for the partition \
function and Wilson loop in\\narbitrary representations are given. We obtain \
explicit analytical expressions\\nfor Wilson loops with symmetric, \
antisymmetric, rectangular and hook\\nrepresentations, in terms of Gamma \
functions of complex argument. The free\\nenergy for orthogonal and \
symplectic gauge group is also given. The asymptotic\\nexpansion of the free \
energy is also presented, including a discussion of the\\nappearance of \
exponentially small contributions. Duality checks of the\\nanalytical \
expressions for the partition functions are also carried out\\nexplicitly.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
