 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the one-loop effective action of certain \
classical type IIA string\\nconfigurations in $AdS_4\\\\times \
\\\\mathbb{CP}^3$. These configurations are dual to\\nWilson loops in the $\\\
\\mathcal{N}= 6\\\\:$ $U(N)_k \\\\times U(N)_{-k}$ Chern-Simons\\ntheory \
coupled to matter whose expectation values are known via \
supersymmetric\\nlocalization. We compute the one-loop effective actions \
using two methods:\\nperturbative heat kernel techniques and full \
$\\\\zeta$-function regularization.\\nWe find that the result of the \
perturbative heat kernel method matches the\\nfield theory prediction at the \
appropriate order while the $\\\\zeta$-function\\napproach seems to lead to a \
disagreement. We explore various issues that might\\nbe responsible for this \
state of affairs.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
