                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the exact formula for the A-twisted correlation \
functions of the two\\ndimensional $\\\\mathcal{N}=(2,2)$ gauged linear sigma \
model, we reconsider the\\ncomputation of the B-model Yukawa couplings of the \
local toric Calabi-Yau\\nvarieties. Our analysis is based on an exact result \
that has been evaluated\\nfrom the supersymmetric localization technique and \
careful treatment of its\\napplication. We provide a detailed description of \
a procedure to investigate\\nthe local B-model Yukawa couplings and also test \
our prescription by comparing\\nthe results with known expressions evaluated \
from the local mirror symmetry\\napproach. In particular, we find that the \
ambiguities of classical intersection\\nnumbers of a certain class of local \
toric Calabi-Yau varieties discovered\\npreviously can be interpreted as \
degrees of freedom of the twisted mass\\ndeformations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
