                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The 2d principal models without boundaries have \
$G\\\\times G$ symmetry. The\\nalready known integrable boundaries have \
either $H\\\\times H$ or $G_{D}$\\nsymmetries, where $H$ is such a subgroup \
of $G$ for which $G/H$ is a symmetric\\nspace while $G_{D}$ is the diagonal \
subgroup of $G\\\\times G$. These boundary\\nconditions have a common \
feature: they do not contain free parameters. We have\\nfound new integrable \
boundary conditions for which the remaining symmetry\\ngroups are either $G\\\
\\times H$ or $H\\\\times G$ and they contain one free\\nparameter. The \
related boundary monodromy matrices are also described.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
