 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The cross or soft anomalous dimension matrix describes \
the renormalization of\\nWilson loops with a self-intersection and is an \
important object in the study\\nof infrared divergences of scattering \
amplitudes. In this paper it is studied\\nfor the Maldacena--Wilson loop in \
N=4 supersymmetric Yang--Mills theory and\\nEuclidean kinematics. We consider \
both the strong-coupling description in terms\\nof minimal surfaces in AdS5 \
as well as the weak-coupling side up to the\\ntwo-loop level. In either case, \
the coefficients of the cross anomalous\\ndimension matrix can be expressed \
in terms of the cusp anomalous dimension. The\\nstrong-coupling description \
displays a Gross--Ooguri phase transition and we\\nargue that the cross \
anomalous dimension is an interesting object to study in\\nan \
integrability-based approach.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
