               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1805.06467\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jonathan Heckman\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Jonathan J. Heckman and Tom Rudelius\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Top Down Approach to 6D SCFTs\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v4: 122 pages, 4 figures, further typos corrected\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/aafc81\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.AG math.RT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Six-dimensional superconformal field theories (6D \
SCFTs) occupy a central\\nplace in the study of quantum field theories \
encountered in high energy theory.\\nThis article reviews the top down \
construction and study of this rich class of\\nquantum field theories, in \
particular, how they are realized by suitable\\nbackgrounds in string / M- / \
F-theory. We review the recent F-theoretic\\nclassification of 6D SCFTs, \
explain how to calculate physical quantities of\\ninterest such as the \
anomaly polynomial of 6D SCFTs, and also explain recent\\nprogress in \
understanding renormalization group flows for deformations of \
such\\ntheories. Additional topics covered by this review include some \
discussion on\\nthe (weighted and signed) counting of states in these \
theories via\\nsuperconformal indices. We also include several previously \
unpublished results\\nas well as a new variant on the swampland conjecture \
for general quantum field\\ntheories decoupled from gravity. The aim of the \
article is to provide a point\\nof entry into this growing literature rather \
than an exhaustive overview.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 16 May 2018 18:00:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 30 Jul 2018 22:24:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 20 Feb 2019 15:56:47 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
