         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1805.06467", "submitter" -> "Jonathan Heckman", "authors" -> 
            "Jonathan J. Heckman and Tom Rudelius", "title" -> 
            "Top Down Approach to 6D SCFTs", "comments" -> 
            "v4: 122 pages, 4 figures, further typos corrected", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8121/aafc81", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th math.AG math.RT", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Six-dimensional superconformal field theories (6D SCFTs) \
occupy a central\nplace in the study of quantum field theories encountered in \
high energy theory.\nThis article reviews the top down construction and study \
of this rich class of\nquantum field theories, in particular, how they are \
realized by suitable\nbackgrounds in string / M- / F-theory. We review the \
recent F-theoretic\nclassification of 6D SCFTs, explain how to calculate \
physical quantities of\ninterest such as the anomaly polynomial of 6D SCFTs, \
and also explain recent\nprogress in understanding renormalization group \
flows for deformations of such\ntheories. Additional topics covered by this \
review include some discussion on\nthe (weighted and signed) counting of \
states in these theories via\nsuperconformal indices. We also include several \
previously unpublished results\nas well as a new variant on the swampland \
conjecture for general quantum field\ntheories decoupled from gravity. The \
aim of the article is to provide a point\nof entry into this growing \
literature rather than an exhaustive overview.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 16 May 2018 18:00:08 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 30 Jul 2018 22:24:10 GMT"}, {
