                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Langmann-Szabo-Zarembo (LSZ) matrix model is a \
complex matrix model with\\na quartic interaction and two external matrices. \
The model appears in the study\\nof a scalar field theory on the \
non-commutative plane. We prove that the LSZ\\nmatrix model computes the \
probability of atypically large fluctuations in the\\nStieltjes-Wigert matrix \
model, which is a $q$-ensemble describing $U(N)$\\nChern-Simons theory on the \
three-sphere. The correspondence holds in a\\ngeneralized sense: depending on \
the spectra of the two external matrices, the\\nLSZ matrix model either \
describes probabilities of large fluctuations in the\\nChern-Simons partition \
function, in the unknot invariant or in the two-unknot\\ninvariant. We extend \
the result to supermatrix models, and show that a\\ngeneralized LSZ \
supermatrix model describes the probability of atypically \
large\\nfluctuations in the ABJ(M) matrix model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 26 May 2018 21:46:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
