appears in the study\nof a scalar field theory on the non-commutative plane. \
We prove that the LSZ\nmatrix model computes the probability of atypically \
large fluctuations in the\nStieltjes-Wigert matrix model, which is a \
$q$-ensemble describing $U(N)$\nChern-Simons theory on the three-sphere. The \
correspondence holds in a\ngeneralized sense: depending on the spectra of the \
two external matrices, the\nLSZ matrix model either describes probabilities \
of large fluctuations in the\nChern-Simons partition function, in the unknot \
invariant or in the two-unknot\ninvariant. We extend the result to \
supermatrix models, and show that a\ngeneralized LSZ supermatrix model \
describes the probability of atypically large\nfluctuations in the ABJ(M) \
matrix model.\n", 
