               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It was shown in arXiv:0912.1456 that the large-$N$ \
reduction holds on group\\nmanifolds in the sense that a large-$N$ gauge \
theory on a group manifold is\\nrealized by a matrix model which is obtained \
by dimensionally reducing the\\noriginal theory to zero dimension. In this \
note, generalizing the above\\nstatement, we show that a large-$N$ gauge \
theory on a group manifold is\\nequivalent to a theory which is obtained by \
reducing the original theory to its\\ncoset space. This is analogous to the \
statement of the large-$N$ reduction on\\nflat spaces that large-$N$ gauge \
theories are independent of the volume.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
