 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit and clarify some aspects of perturbative \
renormalization in pure\\nChern-Simons theory by means of a localization \
principle associated with an\\nunderlying supersymmetry. This perspective \
allows the otherwise perturbative\\none-loop shifts to be interpreted as \
nonperturbative consequences of a\\nnon-renormalization theorem, while \
providing a unified understanding of their\\norigin (particularly in the case \
of Wilson lines). We illustrate this approach\\nexplicitly for $SU(2)$ \
Chern-Simons theory in flat space, on Seifert manifolds,\\nand on a solid \
torus.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
