               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic entanglement entropy in AdS4/BCFT3 and the \
Willmore\\n  functional\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"54 pages, 17 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1808 (2018) 164\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2018)164\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the holographic entanglement entropy of \
spatial regions having\\narbitrary shapes in the AdS4/BCFT3 correspondence \
with static gravitational\\nbackgrounds, focusing on the subleading term with \
respect to the area law term\\nin its expansion as the UV cutoff vanishes. An \
analytic expression depending on\\nthe unit vector normal to the minimal area \
surface anchored to the entangling\\ncurve is obtained. When the bulk \
spacetime is a part of AdS4, this formula\\nbecomes the Willmore functional \
with a proper boundary term evaluated on the\\nminimal surface viewed as a \
submanifold of a three dimensional flat Euclidean\\nspace with boundary. For \
some smooth domains, the analytic expressions of the\\nfinite term are \
reproduced, including the case of a disk disjoint from a\\nboundary which is \
either flat or circular. When the spatial region contains\\ncorners adjacent \
to the boundary, the subleading term is a logarithmic\\ndivergence whose \
coefficient is determined by a corner function that is known\\nanalytically, \
and this result is also recovered. A numerical approach is\\nemployed to \
construct extremal surfaces anchored to entangling curves with\\narbitrary \
shapes. This analysis is used both to check some analytic results and\\nto \
find numerically the finite term of the holographic entanglement entropy \
for\\nsome ellipses at finite distance from a flat boundary.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
