            "  We study the holographic entanglement entropy of spatial \
regions having\narbitrary shapes in the AdS4/BCFT3 correspondence with static \
gravitational\nbackgrounds, focusing on the subleading term with respect to \
the area law term\nin its expansion as the UV cutoff vanishes. An analytic \
expression depending on\nthe unit vector normal to the minimal area surface \
anchored to the entangling\ncurve is obtained. When the bulk spacetime is a \
part of AdS4, this formula\nbecomes the Willmore functional with a proper \
boundary term evaluated on the\nminimal surface viewed as a submanifold of a \
three dimensional flat Euclidean\nspace with boundary. For some smooth \
domains, the analytic expressions of the\nfinite term are reproduced, \
including the case of a disk disjoint from a\nboundary which is either flat \
or circular. When the spatial region contains\ncorners adjacent to the \
boundary, the subleading term is a logarithmic\ndivergence whose coefficient \
is determined by a corner function that is known\nanalytically, and this \
result is also recovered. A numerical approach is\nemployed to construct \
extremal surfaces anchored to entangling curves with\narbitrary shapes. This \
analysis is used both to check some analytic results and\nto find numerically \
the finite term of the holographic entanglement entropy for\nsome ellipses at \
finite distance from a flat boundary.\n", 
