            "  We study semiclassical string solutions that live on white \
regions of the LLM\nplane for a generic LLM geometry. These string \
excitations are labelled by\nconserved charges E, J and S and are thus \
holographically dual to operators in\nthe SL(2) sector of N = 4 super-Yang \
Mills made up of covariant derivatives\nacting on complex scalar fields Z. On \
the other hand, the LLM geometry itself\nis dual to an operator consisting of \
O(N^2) Z-fields so that the operators dual\nto our solutions, containing both \
the stringy excitation and background, are\nnon-planar. In an appropriate \
