            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute the topological partition function (twisted index) \
of\n$\\mathcal{N}=2$ $U(N)$ Chern-Simons theory with an adjoint chiral \
multiplet on\n$\\Sigma_g \\times S^1$. The localization technique shows that \
the underlying\nFrobenius algebra is the equivariant Verlinde algebra which \
is obtained from\nthe canonical quantization of the complex Chern-Simons \
theory regularized by\n$U(1)$ equivariant parameter $t$. Our computation \
relies on a Bethe/Gauge\ncorrespondence which allows us to represent the \
equivariant Verlinde algebra in\nterms of the Hall-Littlewood polynomials $P_\
\\lambda(x_B, t)$ with a\nspecialization by Bethe roots $x_B$ of the \
$q$-boson model. We confirm a\nproposed duality to the Coulomb branch limit \
of the lens space superconformal\nindex of four dimensional $\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
theories for $SU(2)$ and $SU(3)$ with\nlower levels. In $SU(2)$ case we also \
present more direct computation based on\nJeffrey-Kirwan residue operation.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 8 Jun 2018 09:27:20 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 11 Jun 2018 15:05:46 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2019-03-27", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kanno", "Hiroaki", ""}, {
              "Sugiyama", "Katsuyuki", ""}, {"Yoshida", "Yutaka", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
