               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Riccardo Borsato\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riccardo Borsato and Linus Wulff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-abelian T-duality and Yang-Baxter deformations of \
Green-Schwarz\\n  strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages. References added, plus other minor changes. \
Example of NATD\\n  with isotropy added in appendix. Published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2018)027\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NORDITA 2018-041\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We perform non-abelian T-duality for a generic \
Green-Schwarz string with\\nrespect to an isometry (super)group G, and we \
derive the transformation rules\\nfor the supergravity background fields. \
Specializing to G bosonic, or G\\nfermionic but abelian, our results \
reproduce those available in the literature.\\nWe discuss also continuous \
deformations of the T-dual models, obtained by\\nadding a closed B-field \
before the dualization. This idea can also be used to\\ngenerate deformations \
of the original (un-dualized) model, when the 2-cocycle\\nidentified from the \
closed B is invertible. The latter construction is the\\nnatural \
generalization of the so-called Yang-Baxter deformations, based \
on\\nsolutions of the classical Yang-Baxter equation on the Lie algebra of G \
and\\noriginally constructed for group manifolds and (super)coset sigma \
models. We\\nfind that the deformed metric and B-field are obtained through a \
generalization\\nof the Seiberg-Witten map. When applied to integrable sigma \
models these\\ndeformations preserve the integrability.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
