            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We perform non-abelian T-duality for a generic Green-Schwarz \
string with\nrespect to an isometry (super)group G, and we derive the \
transformation rules\nfor the supergravity background fields. Specializing to \
G bosonic, or G\nfermionic but abelian, our results reproduce those available \
in the literature.\nWe discuss also continuous deformations of the T-dual \
models, obtained by\nadding a closed B-field before the dualization. This \
idea can also be used to\ngenerate deformations of the original (un-dualized) \
model, when the 2-cocycle\nidentified from the closed B is invertible. The \
latter construction is the\nnatural generalization of the so-called \
Yang-Baxter deformations, based on\nsolutions of the classical Yang-Baxter \
equation on the Lie algebra of G and\noriginally constructed for group \
manifolds and (super)coset sigma models. We\nfind that the deformed metric \
and B-field are obtained through a generalization\nof the Seiberg-Witten map. \
When applied to integrable sigma models these\ndeformations preserve the \
integrability.\n", 
