             "title" -> 
             "Level crossing in random matrices. II Random perturbation of a \
random\n  matrix", "comments" -> "27 pages, many figures", "journal-ref" -> 
             Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8121/ab1733", "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "math-ph hep-th math.MP", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  In this paper we study the distribution of level crossings \
for the spectra of\nlinear families A+lambda B, where A and B are square \
matrices independently\nchosen from some given Gaussian ensemble and lambda \
is a complex-valued\nparameter. We formulate a number of theoretical and \
numerical results for the\nclassical Gaussian ensembles and some \
generalisations. Besides, we present\nintriguing numerical information about \
the distribution of monodromy in case of\nlinear families for the classical \
Gaussian ensembles of 3 * 3 matrices.\n", 
