               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The finite entropy of black holes suggests that local \
regions of spacetime\\nare described by finite-dimensional factors of Hilbert \
space, in contrast with\\nthe infinite-dimensional Hilbert spaces of quantum \
field theory. With this in\\nmind, we explore how to cast finite-dimensional \
quantum mechanics in a form\\nthat matches naturally onto the smooth case, \
especially the recovery of\\nconjugate position/momentum variables, in the \
limit of large Hilbert-space\\ndimension. A natural tool for this task are \
the Generalized Pauli operators\\n(GPO). Based on an exponential form of \
Heisenberg's canonical commutation\\nrelation, the GPO offers a \
finite-dimensional generalization of conjugate\\nvariables without relying on \
any a priori structure on Hilbert space. We\\nhighlight some features of the \
GPO, its importance in studying concepts such as\\nspread induced by \
operators, and point out departures from infinite-dimensional\\nresults \
(possibly with a cutoff) that might play a crucial role in \
our\\nunderstanding of quantum gravity. We introduce the concept of \
\\\"Operator\\nCollimation,\\\" which characterizes how the action of an \
operator spreads a\\nquantum state along conjugate directions. We illustrate \
these concepts with a\\nworked example of a finite-dimensional harmonic \
oscillator, demonstrating how\\nthe energy spectrum deviates from the \
familiar infinite-dimensional case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 26 Jun 2018 03:07:13 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 Apr 2020 22:59:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-04-27\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
