               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sibylle Driezen, Alexander Sevrin and Daniel C. \
Thompson\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"D-branes in $\\\\lambda$-deformations\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"41 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2018)015\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that the geometric interpretation of D-branes \
in WZW models as\\ntwisted conjugacy classes persists in the \
$\\\\lambda$--deformed theory. We obtain\\nsuch configurations by demanding \
that a monodromy matrix constructed from the\\nLax connection of the \
$\\\\lambda$--deformed theory continues to produce conserved\\ncharges in the \
presence of boundaries. In this way the D-brane configurations\\nobtained \
correspond to `integrable' boundary configurations. We illustrate this\\nwith \
examples based on $SU(2)$ and $SL(2,\\\\mathbb{R})$, and comment on \
the\\nrelation of these D-branes to both non-Abelian T-duality and \
Poisson-Lie\\nT-duality. We show that the D2 supported by D0 charge in \
the\\n$\\\\lambda$--deformed theory map, under analytic continuation together \
with\\nPoisson-Lie T-duality, to D3 branes in the $\\\\eta$-deformation of \
the principal\\nchiral model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 27 Jun 2018 23:33:02 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2018-09-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Driezen\"", ",", "\"Sibylle\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sevrin\"", ",", "\"Alexander\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Thompson\"", ",", "\"Daniel C.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
