          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1806.10712", "submitter" -> "Daniel Thompson", "authors" -> 
            "Sibylle Driezen, Alexander Sevrin and Daniel C. Thompson", 
            "title" -> "D-branes in $\\lambda$-deformations", "comments" -> 
            "41 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP09(2018)015", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We show that the geometric interpretation of D-branes in WZW \
models as\ntwisted conjugacy classes persists in the $\\lambda$--deformed \
theory. We obtain\nsuch configurations by demanding that a monodromy matrix \
constructed from the\nLax connection of the $\\lambda$--deformed theory \
continues to produce conserved\ncharges in the presence of boundaries. In \
this way the D-brane configurations\nobtained correspond to `integrable' \
boundary configurations. We illustrate this\nwith examples based on $SU(2)$ \
and $SL(2,\\mathbb{R})$, and comment on the\nrelation of these D-branes to \
both non-Abelian T-duality and Poisson-Lie\nT-duality. We show that the D2 \
supported by D0 charge in the\n$\\lambda$--deformed theory map, under \
analytic continuation together with\nPoisson-Lie T-duality, to D3 branes in \
the $\\eta$-deformation of the principal\nchiral model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
