 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study multi spin semiclassical strings in \
$AdS_3\\\\times S^3 \\\\times T^4$\\nbackground supported by a mixture of \
Neveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz (NS-NS) and\\nRamond-Ramond (R-R) fluxes. This \
`mixed flux' background has been recently\\nproved to be classically \
integrable. We start with a particular rigidly\\nspinning fundamental string \
in $AdS_3\\\\times S^1$ coupled to the NS-NS flux and\\nclassify the possible \
profiles. We also find out how the scaling relation among\\nthe energy and \
angular momenta of such a string changes due to presence of\\nthese fluxes. \
We emphasize on pure NS-NS flux case and discuss the fate of such\\nsolutions \
in that limit.\\n\""}]}, {
