               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1807.02409\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Mironov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A. Mironov, A. Morozov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sum rules for characters from character-preservation \
property of matrix\\n  models\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"17 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. High Energ. Phys. 2018 (2018) 163\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2018)163\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"FIAN/TD-12/18; IITP/TH-12/18; ITEP/TH-18/18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  One of the main features of eigenvalue matrix models is \
that the averages of\\ncharacters are again characters, what can be \
considered as a far-going\\ngeneralization of the Fourier transform property \
of Gaussian exponential. This\\nis true for the standard Hermitian and \
unitary (trigonometric) matrix models\\nand for their various deformations, \
classical and quantum ones. Arising\\nexplicit formulas for the partition \
functions are very efficient for practical\\ncomputer calculations. However, \
to handle them theoretically, one needs to tame\\nthe remaining finite sums \
over representations of a given size, which turns\\ninto an interesting \
conceptual problem. Already the semicircle distribution in\\nthe large-$N$ \
limit implies interesting combinatorial sum rules for characters.\\nWe \
describe also implications to $W$-representations, including a \
character\\ndecomposition of cut-and-join operators, which unexpectedly \
involves only\\nsingle-hook diagrams and also requires non-trivial summation \
identities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 6 Jul 2018 13:45:50 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2018-09-05\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Mironov\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Morozov\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
