                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wolfgang M\[CapitalATilde]\.bcck\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Anthonny F. Canazas Garay, Alberto Faraggi, Wolfgang \
M\\\\\\\"uck\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Antisymmetric Wilson loops in N = 4 SYM: from exact \
results to\\n  non-planar corrections\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages, 2 figures, v2: added references\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP08(2018)149\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2018)149\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the vacuum expectation values of 1/2-BPS \
circular Wilson loops in\\nN=4 super Yang-Mills theory in the totally \
antisymmetric representation of the\\ngauge group U(N) or SU(N). Localization \
and matrix model techniques provide\\nexact, but rather formal, expressions \
for these expectation values. In this\\npaper we show how to extract the \
leading and sub-leading behavior in a 1/N\\nexpansion with fixed 't Hooft \
coupling starting from these exact results. This\\nis done by exploiting the \
relation between the generating function of\\nantisymmetric Wilson loops and \
a finite-dimensional quantum system known as the\\ntruncated harmonic \
oscillator. Sum and integral representations for the 1/N\\nterms are \
