         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1807.04052", "submitter" -> 
            "Wolfgang M\[CapitalATilde]\.bcck", "authors" -> 
            "Anthonny F. Canazas Garay, Alberto Faraggi, Wolfgang M\\\"uck", 
            "title" -> 
            "Antisymmetric Wilson loops in N = 4 SYM: from exact results to\n \
 non-planar corrections", "comments" -> 
            "32 pages, 2 figures, v2: added references", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP08(2018)149", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2018)149", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the vacuum expectation values of 1/2-BPS circular \
Wilson loops in\nN=4 super Yang-Mills theory in the totally antisymmetric \
representation of the\ngauge group U(N) or SU(N). Localization and matrix \
model techniques provide\nexact, but rather formal, expressions for these \
expectation values. In this\npaper we show how to extract the leading and \
sub-leading behavior in a 1/N\nexpansion with fixed 't Hooft coupling \
starting from these exact results. This\nis done by exploiting the relation \
between the generating function of\nantisymmetric Wilson loops and a \
finite-dimensional quantum system known as the\ntruncated harmonic \
oscillator. Sum and integral representations for the 1/N\nterms are provided.\
\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 11 Jul 2018 10:12:03 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
