            "  We investigate Poisson-Lie duals of the $\\eta$-deformed \
$\\mathrm{AdS}_2\n\\times \\mathrm{S}^2 \\times \\mathrm{T}^6$ superstring. \
The $\\eta$-deformed\nbackground satisfies a generalisation of the type II \
supergravity equations. We\ndiscuss three Poisson-Lie duals, with respect to \
(i) the full\n$\\mathfrak{psu}(1,1|2)$ superalgebra, (ii) the full bosonic \
subalgebra and\n(iii) the Cartan subalgebra, for which the corresponding \
backgrounds are\nexpected to satisfy the standard type II supergravity \
equations. The metrics\nand B-fields for the first two cases are the same and \
given by an analytic\ncontinuation of the $\\lambda$-deformed model on \
$\\mathrm{AdS}_2 \\times\n\\mathrm{S}^2 \\times \\mathrm{T}^6$ with the torus \
undeformed. However, the RR\nfluxes and dilaton will differ. Focusing on the \
second case we explicitly\nderive the background and show agreement with an \
analytic continuation of a\nknown embedding of the $\\lambda$-deformed model \
on $\\mathrm{AdS}_2 \\times\n\\mathrm{S}^2$ in type II supergravity.\n", 
