            "  Supersymmetric partition function of $\\mathcal N=1$ \
superconformal theories\non $S^1_{\\beta} \\times S^3$ is related to the \
superconformal index receiving\ncontributions from short representations. The \
leading coefficients in the small\n$\\beta$ (high \"temperature\") expansion \
of the index were previously related to\nthe conformal anomaly coefficients \
of the theory. Assumptions underlying\nuniversality of these relations were \
tested only for simplest low-spin unitary\nmultiplets. Here we consider \
examples of higher derivative non-unitary\n$\\mathcal N=1$ multiplets that \
naturally appear in the context of extended\nconformal supergravities and \
compute their superconformal index. We compare the\ncoefficients in the small \
