               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Onishchenko\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"R.N. Lee and A.I. Onishchenko\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On analytical perturbative solution of ABJM quantum \
spectral curve\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages, contribution to CQIS-2017 proceedings, to \
appear in TMPh.\\n  arXiv admin note: text overlap with arXiv:1712.00412. \
References added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1134/S0040577919020077\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently we showed how non-homogeneous second-order \
difference equations\\nappearing within ABJM quantum spectral curve \
description could be solved using\\nMellin space technique. In particular we \
provided explicit results for\\nanomalous dimensions of twist 1 operators in \
sl(2) sector at arbitrary spin\\nvalues up to four loop order. It was shown \
that the obtained results may be\\nexpressed in terms of harmonic sums \
decorated by fourth root of unity factors,\\nso that maximum \
transcendentality principle holds. In this note we show that\\nthe same \
result could be also obtained by direct solution of the mentioned\\nequations \
in spectral parameter u-space. The solution involves new highly\\nnontrivial \
identities between hypergeometric functions, which may have various\\nother \
applications. We expect this method to be more easily generalizable \
to\\nhigher loop orders as well as to other theories, such as N=4 \
SYM.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
