 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate low-energy string excitations \
in\\nAdS$_3\\\\times$S$^3\\\\times$T$^4$. When the worldsheet is \
decompactified, the\\ntheory has gapless modes whose spectrum at low energies \
is determined by\\nmassless relativistic integrable S matrices of the type \
introduced by Al. B.\\nZamolodchikov. The S matrices are non-trivial only for \
excitations with\\nidentical worldsheet chirality, indicating that the \
low-energy theory is a\\nCFT$_2$. We construct a Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz \
(TBA) for these excitations\\nand show how the massless modes' wrapping \
effects may be incorporated into the\\nAdS$_3$ spectral problem. Using the \
TBA and its associated Y-system, we\\ndetermine the central charge of the low \
energy CFT$_2$ to be $c=6$ from\\ncalculating the vacuum energy for \
antiperiodic fermions - with the vacuum\\nenergy being zero for periodic \
fermions in agreement with a supersymmetric\\ntheory - and find the energies \
of some excited states.\\n\""}]}, {
