            "  We investigate low-energy string excitations in\n\
AdS$_3\\times$S$^3\\times$T$^4$. When the worldsheet is decompactified, the\n\
theory has gapless modes whose spectrum at low energies is determined by\n\
massless relativistic integrable S matrices of the type introduced by Al. B.\n\
Zamolodchikov. The S matrices are non-trivial only for excitations with\n\
identical worldsheet chirality, indicating that the low-energy theory is a\n\
CFT$_2$. We construct a Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (TBA) for these \
excitations\nand show how the massless modes' wrapping effects may be \
incorporated into the\nAdS$_3$ spectral problem. Using the TBA and its \
associated Y-system, we\ndetermine the central charge of the low energy \
CFT$_2$ to be $c=6$ from\ncalculating the vacuum energy for antiperiodic \
fermions - with the vacuum\nenergy being zero for periodic fermions in \
agreement with a supersymmetric\ntheory - and find the energies of some \
excited states.\n", 
