               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1807.09743\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Davide Fioravanti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Alfredo Bonini, Davide Fioravanti, Simone Piscaglia and \
Marco Rossi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Fermions and scalars in $\\\\mathcal{N} = 4$ Wilson loops \
at strong\\n  coupling and beyond\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2019.114644\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the strong coupling behaviour of null \
polygonal Wilson loops/gluon\\namplitudes in $\\\\mathcal{N} = 4$ SYM, by \
using the OPE series and its\\nintegrability features. For the hexagon we \
disentangle the $SU(4)$ matrix\\nstructure of the form factors for fermions, \
organising them in a pattern\\nsimilar to the Young diagrams used previously \
for the scalar sector\\n\\\\cite{BFPR2,BFPR3}. Then, we complete and extend \
the discussion of \\\\cite{BFPR1}\\nby showing, at strong coupling, the \
appearance of a new effective particle in\\nthe series: the \
fermion-antifermion bound state, the so-called meson. We\\ndiscuss its \
interactions in the OPE series with itself by forming (effective)\\nbound \
states and with the gluons and bound states of them. These lead the \
OPE\\nseries to the known $AdS_5$ minimal area result for the Wls, described \
in terms\\nof a set of TBA-like equations. This approach allows us to detect \
all the\\none-loop contributions and, once the meson has formed, applies \
to\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ Nekrasov partition function via the parallel \
meson/instanton\\n(in particular, they share the mechanism by which their \
bound states emerge and\\nform the TBA node). Finally, to complete the strong \
coupling analysis, we\\nconsider the scalar sector for any polygon, \
confirming the emergence of a\\nleading contribution from the \
non-perturbative theory on the sphere $S^5$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 25 Jul 2018 17:48:14 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2019-06-26\""}]}, {
