 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider real mass and FI deformations of ABJM \
theory preserving\\nsupersymmetry in the large $N$ limit, and compare with \
holographic results. On\\nthe field theory side, the problems amounts to a \
spectral problem of a\\nnon-Hermitian Hamiltonian. For certain values of the \
deformation parameters\\nthis is invariant under an antiunitary operator \
(generalised $\\\\mathcal{PT}$\\nsymmetry), which ensures the partition \
function remains real and allows us to\\ncalculate the free energy using \
tools from statistical physics. The results\\nobtained are compatible with \
previous work, the important new feature being\\nthat these are obtained \
directly from the real deformations, without \
analytic\\ncontinuation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
