               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The 2d gauged linear sigma model (GLSM) gives a UV \
model for quantum\\ncohomology on a Kahler manifold X, which is reproduced in \
the IR limit. We\\npropose and explore a 3d lift of this correspondence, \
where the UV model is the\\nN=2 supersymmetric 3d gauge theory and the IR \
limit is given by Givental's\\npermutation equivariant quantum K-theory on X. \
This gives a one-parameter\\ndeformation of the 2d GLSM/quantum cohomology \
correspondence and recovers it in\\na small radius limit. We study some \
novelties of the 3d case regarding integral\\nBPS invariants, chiral rings, \
deformation spaces and mirror symmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
