            "  We study the phase transitions of three-dimensional \
$\\mathcal{N}=2$ $U(N)$\nChern-Simons theory on $\\mathbb{S}^3$ with a varied \
number of massive\nfundamental hypermultiplets and with a Fayet-Iliopoulos \
parameter. We\ncharacterize the various phase diagrams in the \
decompactification limit,\naccording to the number of different mass scales \
in the theory. For this, we\nextend the known solution of the saddle-point \
equations to the setting where\nthe one cut solution is characterized by \
asymmetric intervals. We then study\nthe large $N$ limit of Wilson loops in \
antisymmetric representations, with the\nadditional scaling corresponding to \
the variation of the size of the\nrepresentation. We give explicit \
expressions, both with and without FI terms,\nand study $1/R$ corrections for \
the different phases. These corrections break\nthe perimeter law behavior, as \
they introduce a scaling with the size of the\nrepresentation. We show how \
the phase transitions of the Wilson loops can\neither be of first or second \
order and determine the underlying mechanism in\nterms of the eventual \
asymmetry of the support of the solution of the\nsaddle-point equation, at \
the critical points.\n", 
