               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Chiral 3d SU(3) SQCD and N=2 mirror duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, 7 figures, harvmac; v2: references added, typos \
fixed\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 11 (2018) 025\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2018)025\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently a very interesting three-dimensional \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ supersymmetric\\ntheory with $SU(3)$ global symmetry was \
discussed by several authors. We denote\\nthis model by $T_x$. This was \
conjectured to have two dual descriptions, one\\nwith explicit supersymmetry \
and emergent flavor symmetry and the other with\\nexplicit flavor symmetry \
and emergent supersymmetry. We discuss a third\\ndescription of the model \
which has both flavor symmetry and supersymmetry\\nmanifest. We then \
investigate models which can be constructed by using $T_x$ as\\na building \
block gauging the global symmetry and paying special attention to\\nthe \
global structure of the gauge group. We conjecture several cases \
of\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ mirror dualities involving such constructions with \
the dual\\nbeing either a simple $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ Wess-Zumino model or a \
discrete gauging\\nthereof.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
