            "  Recently a very interesting three-dimensional $\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
supersymmetric\ntheory with $SU(3)$ global symmetry was discussed by several \
authors. We denote\nthis model by $T_x$. This was conjectured to have two \
dual descriptions, one\nwith explicit supersymmetry and emergent flavor \
symmetry and the other with\nexplicit flavor symmetry and emergent \
supersymmetry. We discuss a third\ndescription of the model which has both \
flavor symmetry and supersymmetry\nmanifest. We then investigate models which \
can be constructed by using $T_x$ as\na building block gauging the global \
symmetry and paying special attention to\nthe global structure of the gauge \
group. We conjecture several cases of\n$\\mathcal{N}=2$ mirror dualities \
involving such constructions with the dual\nbeing either a simple \
$\\mathcal{N}=2$ Wess-Zumino model or a discrete gauging\nthereof.\n", 
