               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1809.03679\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kazuma Shimizu\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kazuma Shimizu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Aspects of Massive Gauge Theories on Three Sphere in \
Infinite Mass Limit\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"41 pages, 5 figures; v3: published version in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP01(2019)090\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2019)090\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"YITP-18-99\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the $S^3$ partition function of \
three-dimensional supersymmetric\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ U($N$) SQCD with \
massive matter multiplets in the infinite mass\\nlimit with the so-called \
Coulomb branch localization. We show that in the\\ninfinite mass limit a \
specific point of the Coulomb branch is selected and\\ncontributes dominantly \
to the partition function. Therefore, we can argue\\nwhether each multiplet \
included in the theory is effectively massless in this\\nlimit, even on \
$S^3$, and conclude that the partition function becomes that of\\nthe \
effective theory on the specific point of the Coulomb branch in \
the\\ninfinite mass limit. In order to investigate which point of the Coulomb \
branch\\nis dominant, we use the saddle point approximation in the large $N$ \
limit\\nbecause the solution of the saddle point equation can be regarded as \
a specific\\npoint of the Coulomb branch. Then, we calculate the partition \
functions for\\nsmall rank $N$ and confirm that their behaviors in the \
infinite mass limit are\\nconsistent with the conjecture from the results in \
the large $N$ limit. Our\\nresult suggests that the partition function in the \
infinite mass limit\\ncorresponds to that of an interacting superconformal \
field theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 11 Sep 2018 04:36:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 19 Sep 2018 05:51:51 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 14 Jan 2019 10:26:32 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2019-01-15\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Shimizu\"", ",", "\"Kazuma\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
