            "Kazuma Shimizu", "title" -> 
            "Aspects of Massive Gauge Theories on Three Sphere in Infinite \
Mass Limit", "comments" -> 
            "41 pages, 5 figures; v3: published version in JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP01(2019)090", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP01(2019)090", "report-no" -> "YITP-18-99", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the $S^3$ partition function of three-dimensional \
supersymmetric\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ U($N$) SQCD with massive matter multiplets \
in the infinite mass\nlimit with the so-called Coulomb branch localization. \
We show that in the\ninfinite mass limit a specific point of the Coulomb \
branch is selected and\ncontributes dominantly to the partition function. \
Therefore, we can argue\nwhether each multiplet included in the theory is \
effectively massless in this\nlimit, even on $S^3$, and conclude that the \
partition function becomes that of\nthe effective theory on the specific \
point of the Coulomb branch in the\ninfinite mass limit. In order to \
investigate which point of the Coulomb branch\nis dominant, we use the saddle \
point approximation in the large $N$ limit\nbecause the solution of the \
saddle point equation can be regarded as a specific\npoint of the Coulomb \
branch. Then, we calculate the partition functions for\nsmall rank $N$ and \
confirm that their behaviors in the infinite mass limit are\nconsistent with \
the conjecture from the results in the large $N$ limit. Our\nresult suggests \
that the partition function in the infinite mass limit\ncorresponds to that \
of an interacting superconformal field theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 11 Sep 2018 04:36:12 GMT"}, {
