 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find and propose an explanation for a large variety \
of modularity-related\\nsymmetries in problems of 3-manifold topology and \
physics of 3d $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$\\ntheories where such structures a priori \
are not manifest. These modular\\nstructures include: mock modular forms, \
$SL(2,\\\\mathbb{Z})$ Weil\\nrepresentations, quantum modular forms, \
non-semisimple modular tensor\\ncategories, and chiral algebras of \
logarithmic CFTs.\\n\""}]}, {
