 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We use the exact-deconstruction prescription to lift \
various squashed-$S^3$\\npartition functions with supersymmetric-defect \
insertions to four-dimensional\\nsuperconformal indices. Starting from \
three-dimensional circular-quiver\\ntheories with vortex-loop-operator \
insertions, we recover the index of\\nfour-dimensional theories in the \
presence of codimension-two surface defects\\nwith (2,2) supersymmetry. The \
case of deconstruction with Wilson-loop\\ninsertions is discussed separately. \
We provide evidence that a certain\\nprescription leads to the index of \
four-dimensional theories in the presence of\\nsurface defects with (4,0) \
supersymmetry. In addition, we deconstruct the index\\nof four-dimensional \
gauge theories with codimension-one 1/2-BPS defects,\\nstarting from \
three-dimensional circular-quiver theories containing \
localised\\nmatter/gauge-field insertions at specific nodes. We also clarify \
certain\\ncalculational and conceptual points related to exact \
deconstruction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
