                 "\"Priodyuti Pradhan and Sarika Jalan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"From Spectra to Localized Networks: A Reverse Engineering \
Approach\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"15 pages and 8 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1109/TNSE.2020.3008999\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"physics.soc-ph nlin.AO\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Understanding the localization properties of \
eigenvectors of complex networks\\nis important to get insight into various \
structural and dynamical properties of\\nthe corresponding systems. Here, we \
analytically develop a scheme to construct\\na highly localized network for a \
given set of networks parameters that is the\\nnumber of nodes and the number \
of interactions. We find that the localization\\nbehavior of the principal \
eigenvector (PEV) of such a network is sensitive\\nagainst a single edge \
rewiring. We find evidences for eigenvalue crossing\\nphenomena as a \
consequence of the single edge rewiring, in turn providing an\\norigin to the \
sensitive behavior of the PEV localization. These insights were\\nthen used \
to analytically construct the highly localized network for a given\\nset of \
networks parameters. The analysis provides fundamental insight \
into\\nrelationships between the structural and the spectral properties of \
networks\\nfor PEV localized networks. Further, we substantiate the existence \
of the\\neigenvalue crossing phenomenon by considering a linear-dynamical \
process,\\nnamely the ribonucleic acid (RNA) neutral network population \
dynamical model.\\nThe analysis presented here on model networks aids in \
understanding the\\nsteady-state behavior of a broad range of \
linear-dynamical processes, from\\nepidemic spreading to biochemical dynamics \
associated with the adjacency\\nmatrices.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
