         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1810.00243", "submitter" -> "Priodyuti Pradhan", 
            "authors" -> "Priodyuti Pradhan and Sarika Jalan", "title" -> 
            "From Spectra to Localized Networks: A Reverse Engineering \
Approach", "comments" -> "15 pages and 8 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1109/TNSE.2020.3008999", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "physics.soc-ph nlin.AO", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Understanding the localization properties of eigenvectors of \
complex networks\nis important to get insight into various structural and \
dynamical properties of\nthe corresponding systems. Here, we analytically \
develop a scheme to construct\na highly localized network for a given set of \
networks parameters that is the\nnumber of nodes and the number of \
interactions. We find that the localization\nbehavior of the principal \
eigenvector (PEV) of such a network is sensitive\nagainst a single edge \
rewiring. We find evidences for eigenvalue crossing\nphenomena as a \
consequence of the single edge rewiring, in turn providing an\norigin to the \
sensitive behavior of the PEV localization. These insights were\nthen used to \
analytically construct the highly localized network for a given\nset of \
networks parameters. The analysis provides fundamental insight into\n\
relationships between the structural and the spectral properties of networks\n\
for PEV localized networks. Further, we substantiate the existence of the\n\
eigenvalue crossing phenomenon by considering a linear-dynamical process,\n\
namely the ribonucleic acid (RNA) neutral network population dynamical model.\
\nThe analysis presented here on model networks aids in understanding the\n\
steady-state behavior of a broad range of linear-dynamical processes, from\n\
epidemic spreading to biochemical dynamics associated with the adjacency\n\
matrices.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
