                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show how q-Virasoro constraints can be derived for a \
large class of\\n(q,t)-deformed eigenvalue matrix models by an elementary \
trick of inserting\\ncertain q-difference operators under the integral, in \
complete analogy with\\nfull-derivative insertions for beta-ensembles. From \
free-field point of view\\nthe models considered have zero momentum of the \
highest weight, which leads to\\nan extra constraint T_{-1} Z = 0. We then \
show how to solve these q-Virasoro\\nconstraints recursively and comment on \
the possible applications for gauge\\ntheories, for instance calculation of \
(supersymmetric) Wilson loop averages in\\ngauge theories on D^2 \\\\cross \
S^1 and S^3.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
