            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1810.11463\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matthias Wilhelm\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Aleix Gimenez Grau and Charlotte Kristjansen and Matthias \
Volk and\\n  Matthias Wilhelm\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A Quantum Check of Non-Supersymmetric AdS/dCFT\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33+14 pages, 5 figures; v2: typos corrected, reference \
added, version\\n  published in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 1901 (2019) 007\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2019)007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Via a challenging field-theory computation, we confirm \
a supergravity\\nprediction for the non-supersymmetric D3-D7 probe-brane \
system with probe\\ngeometry AdS_4 x S^2 x S^2, stabilized by fluxes. \
Supergravity predicts, in a\\ncertain double-scaling limit, the value of the \
one-point functions of chiral\\nprimaries of the dual defect version of N=4 \
SYM theory, where the fluxes\\ntranslate into SO(3) x SO(3)-symmetric, \
Lie-algebra-valued vacuum expectation\\nvalues for all six scalar fields. \
Using a generalization of the technique based\\non fuzzy spherical harmonics \
developed for the related D3-D5 probe-brane\\nsystem, we diagonalize the \
resulting mass matrix of the field theory.\\nSubsequently, we calculate the \
planar one-loop correction to the vacuum\\nexpectation values of the scalars \
in dimensional reduction and find that it is\\nUV finite and non-vanishing. \
We then proceed to calculating the one-loop\\ncorrection to the planar \
one-point function of any single-trace scalar operator\\nand explicitly \
evaluate this correction for a 1/2-BPS operator of length L at\\ntwo leading \
orders in the double-scaling limit, finding exact agreement with\\nthe \
supergravity prediction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
