            "Aleix Gimenez Grau and Charlotte Kristjansen and Matthias Volk \
and\n  Matthias Wilhelm", "title" -> 
            "A Quantum Check of Non-Supersymmetric AdS/dCFT", "comments" -> 
            "33+14 pages, 5 figures; v2: typos corrected, reference added, \
version\n  published in JHEP", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1901 (2019) 007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP01(2019)007", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            
            "  Via a challenging field-theory computation, we confirm a \
supergravity\nprediction for the non-supersymmetric D3-D7 probe-brane system \
with probe\ngeometry AdS_4 x S^2 x S^2, stabilized by fluxes. Supergravity \
predicts, in a\ncertain double-scaling limit, the value of the one-point \
functions of chiral\nprimaries of the dual defect version of N=4 SYM theory, \
where the fluxes\ntranslate into SO(3) x SO(3)-symmetric, Lie-algebra-valued \
vacuum expectation\nvalues for all six scalar fields. Using a generalization \
of the technique based\non fuzzy spherical harmonics developed for the \
related D3-D5 probe-brane\nsystem, we diagonalize the resulting mass matrix \
of the field theory.\nSubsequently, we calculate the planar one-loop \
correction to the vacuum\nexpectation values of the scalars in dimensional \
reduction and find that it is\nUV finite and non-vanishing. We then proceed \
to calculating the one-loop\ncorrection to the planar one-point function of \
any single-trace scalar operator\nand explicitly evaluate this correction for \
a 1/2-BPS operator of length L at\ntwo leading orders in the double-scaling \
limit, finding exact agreement with\nthe supergravity prediction.\n", 
