Pozsgay", "title" -> 
            "Integrable quenches in nested spin chains I: the exact steady \
states", "comments" -> 
            "45 pages, 7 figures; v3: presentation improved; v4: minor \
revision", "journal-ref" -> "J. Stat. Mech. (2019) 063103", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/ab1c51", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.quant-gas quant-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider quantum quenches in the integrable \
$SU(3)$-invariant spin chain\n(Lai-Sutherland model) which admits a Bethe \
ansatz description in terms of two\ndifferent quasiparticle species, \
providing a prototypical example of a model\nsolvable by nested Bethe ansatz. \
We identify infinite families of integrable\ninitial states for which \
analytic results can be obtained. We show that they\ninclude special families \
of two-site product states which can be related to\nintegrable ``soliton \
non-preserving'' boundary conditions in an appropriate\nrotated channel. We \
present a complete analytical result for the quasiparticle\nrapidity \
distribution functions corresponding to the stationary state reached\nat \
large times after the quench from the integrable initial states. Our results\n\
are obtained within a Quantum Transfer Matrix (QTM) approach, which does not\n\
rely on the knowledge of the quasilocal conservation laws or of the overlaps\n\
between the initial states and the eigenstates of the Hamiltonian. \
Furthermore,\nbased on an analogy with previous works, we conjecture analytic \
expressions for\nsuch overlaps: this allows us to employ the Quench Action \
method to derive a\nset of integral equations characterizing the \
quasi-particle distribution\nfunctions of the post-quench steady state. We \
verify that the solution to the\nlatter coincides with our analytic result \
found using the QTM approach.\nFinally, we present a direct physical \
application of our results by providing\npredictions for the propagation of \
entanglement after the quench from such\nintegrable states.\n", 
