            "  A three-parameter integrable deformation of $\\mathbb{Z}_4$ \
permutation\nsupercosets is constructed. These supercosets are of the form $ \
{\\widehat{F}} /\n{F_0}$ where $F_0$ is the bosonic diagonal subgroup of the \
product supergroup\n$\\widehat{F}=\\widehat{G} \\times \\widehat{G}$. They \
include the AdS$_3$ $\\times$\nS$^3$ and AdS$_3$ $\\times$ S$^3$ $\\times$ \
S$^3$ supercosets. This deformation\nencompasses both the bi-Yang-Baxter \
deformation of the semi-symmetric space\n$\\sigma$-model on $\\mathbb{Z}_4$ \
permutation supercosets and the mixed flux\nmodel. Truncating the action at \
the bosonic level, we show that one recovers\nthe bi-Yang-Baxter deformation \
of the principal chiral model plus Wess-Zumino\nterm.\n", 
