            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1811.06623\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Timoth\\\\'e Poulain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Timoth\\\\'e Poulain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the quantum structure of spacetime and its relation to \
the quantum\\n  theory of fields: $\\\\kappa$-Poincar\\\\'e invariant field \
theories and other\\n  examples\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ph.D. Thesis, 151 pages\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NNT : 2018SACLS331\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The dissertation deals with noncommutative field \
theories, namely field\\ntheories compatible with the existence of a minimal \
(quantum gravity) length\\nscale. Two families of quantum spacetime are \
considered. One is characterized\\nby semisimple Lie algebras of coordinates. \
The other is characterized by\\nsolvable Lie algebras. The explicit \
construction of corresponding Weyl-like\\nstar products is given. We then \
focus on two specific examples of quantum space\\nand study the quantum \
properties of various models of scalar field theory with\\nquartic \
interactions built on them. The corresponding 2-point and 4-point\\nfunctions \
are computed at one-loop and the UV/IR mixing is discussed. The \
first\\nquantum spacetime considered is known as $\\\\mathbb{R}^3_\\\\theta$ \
which is a\\ndeformation of $\\\\mathbb{R}^3$ with $\\\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ \
noncommutativity. In this\\ncase, the one-loop 2-point function is found to \
be finite with the deformation\\nparameter playing the role of a cutoff. The \
second quantum space is known as\\n$\\\\kappa$-Minkowski. In this case, the \
action functional is required\\n$\\\\kappa$-Poincar\\\\'e invariant and \
various kinetic operators are considered. In\\none case, we find that the \
one-loop 2-point function has milder UV divergence\\nthan in the commutative \
case and that the one-loop 4-point function is finite.\\nThe renormalization \
properties are discussed. Besides, the loss of cyclicity of\\nthe Lebesgue \
integral (which results from the $\\\\kappa$-Poincar\\\\'e invariance \
of\\nthe action functional) is interpreted as reflecting the occurrence of \
KMS\\ncondition at the level of the algebra of fields modelling \
$\\\\kappa$-Minkowski.\\nThis interpretation sheds new light on \
$\\\\kappa$-deformation-based quantum\\ngravity models, and solved a 25 years \
old problem in the study of\\n$\\\\kappa$-Poincar\\\\'e invariant quantum \
field theories. Possible extensions of\\nthis work are finally \
discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 15 Nov 2018 23:14:52 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2018-11-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Poulain\"", ",", "\"Timoth\[EAcute]\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
