           "id" -> "1811.06623", "submitter" -> "Timoth\\'e Poulain", 
            "authors" -> "Timoth\\'e Poulain", "title" -> 
            "On the quantum structure of spacetime and its relation to the \
quantum\n  theory of fields: $\\kappa$-Poincar\\'e invariant field theories \
and other\n  examples", "comments" -> "Ph.D. Thesis, 151 pages", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "NNT : 2018SACLS331", "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            
            "  The dissertation deals with noncommutative field theories, \
namely field\ntheories compatible with the existence of a minimal (quantum \
gravity) length\nscale. Two families of quantum spacetime are considered. One \
is characterized\nby semisimple Lie algebras of coordinates. The other is \
characterized by\nsolvable Lie algebras. The explicit construction of \
corresponding Weyl-like\nstar products is given. We then focus on two \
specific examples of quantum space\nand study the quantum properties of \
various models of scalar field theory with\nquartic interactions built on \
them. The corresponding 2-point and 4-point\nfunctions are computed at \
one-loop and the UV/IR mixing is discussed. The first\nquantum spacetime \
considered is known as $\\mathbb{R}^3_\\theta$ which is a\ndeformation of \
$\\mathbb{R}^3$ with $\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ noncommutativity. In this\ncase, the \
one-loop 2-point function is found to be finite with the deformation\n\
parameter playing the role of a cutoff. The second quantum space is known as\n\
$\\kappa$-Minkowski. In this case, the action functional is required\n\
$\\kappa$-Poincar\\'e invariant and various kinetic operators are considered. \
In\none case, we find that the one-loop 2-point function has milder UV \
divergence\nthan in the commutative case and that the one-loop 4-point \
function is finite.\nThe renormalization properties are discussed. Besides, \
the loss of cyclicity of\nthe Lebesgue integral (which results from the \
$\\kappa$-Poincar\\'e invariance of\nthe action functional) is interpreted as \
reflecting the occurrence of KMS\ncondition at the level of the algebra of \
fields modelling $\\kappa$-Minkowski.\nThis interpretation sheds new light on \
$\\kappa$-deformation-based quantum\ngravity models, and solved a 25 years \
old problem in the study of\n$\\kappa$-Poincar\\'e invariant quantum field \
theories. Possible extensions of\nthis work are finally discussed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 15 Nov 2018 23:14:52 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2018-11-19", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Poulain", "Timoth\[EAcute]", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
