               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study minimal area world sheets ending on two \
concentric circumferences on\\nthe boundary of Euclidean $AdS_{3}$ with mixed \
R-R and NS-NS three-form fluxes.\\nWe solve the problem by reducing the \
system to a one-dimensional integrable\\nmodel. We find that the NS-NS flux \
term either brings the surface near to the\\nboundary or separates the \
circumferences. In the limit of pure NS-NS flux the\\nsolution adheres to the \
boundary in the former case and the outer radius\\ndiverges in the latter. We \
further construct the underlying elliptic spectral\\ncurve, which allows us \
to analyze the deformation of other related minimal\\nsurfaces. We show that \
in the regime of pure NS-NS flux the elliptic curve\\ndegenerates.\\n\""}]}, {
              
