 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Equivalence criteria are established for an effective \
Yukawa-type theory of\\ncomposite fields representing two-particle fermion \
bound states with the\\noriginal \\\"microscopic\\\" theory of interacting \
fermions based on the spectral\\ndecomposition of the 2-to-2 fermion \
scattering amplitude. Functional\\nrenormalisation group equations of the \
effective theory are derived exploiting\\nrelations expressing the \
equivalence. The effect of truncating the spectral\\ndecomposition is \
investigated quantitatively on the example of the\\nnon-relativistic bound \
states of two oppositely charged fermi particles.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
