           "id" -> "1811.09638", "submitter" -> "Nadav Drukker", "authors" -> 
            "Michael Cooke, Amit Dekel, Nadav Drukker, Diego Trancanelli and\n\
  Edoardo Vescovi", "title" -> 
            "Deformations of the circular Wilson loop and spectral \
(in)dependence", "comments" -> 
            "25 pages. v2: minor correction and added (with sincere \
appologies)\n  missing acknowlegments", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 1901 (2019) 076", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP01(2019)076", 
            "report-no" -> "Imperial-TP-EV-2018-01, NORDITA 2018-120", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we study the expectation value of deformations \
of the circular\nWilson loop in ${\\cal N}=4$ super Yang-Mills theory. The \
leading order\ndeformation, known as the Bremsstrahlung function, can be \
obtained exactly from\nsupersymmetric localization, so our focus is on \
deformations at higher orders.\nWe find simple expressions for the \
expectation values for generic deformations\nat the quartic order at one-loop \
at weak coupling and at leading order at\nstrong coupling. We also present a \
very simple algorithm (not requiring\nintegration) to evaluate the two-loop \
result. We find that an exact symmetry of\nthe strong coupling sigma-model, \
known as the spectral-parameter independence,\nis an approximate symmetry at \
weak coupling, modifying the expectation value\nstarting only at the sextic \
order in the deformation. Furthermore, we find very\nsimple patterns for how \
the spectral parameter can appear in the weak coupling\ncalculation, \
suggesting all-order structures.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
