                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute explicitly the two-dimensional version of \
Basso-Dixon type\\nintegrals for the planar four-point correlation functions \
given by conformal\\nfishnet Feynman graphs. These diagrams are represented \
by a fragment of a\\nregular square lattice of power-like propagators, \
arising in the recently\\nproposed integrable bi-scalar fishnet CFT. The \
formula is derived from first\\nprinciples, using the formalism of separated \
variables in integrable SL(2,C)\\nspin chain. It is generalized to \
anisotropic fishnet, with different powers for\\npropagators in two \
directions of the lattice.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
