the scalar\nfields depend on the polar angle away from the north pole. \
Assuming finite\ncoupling on the north pole, this leads to zero coupling at \
the south pole for\n$d>4$ and infinite coupling at the south pole for $d<4$. \
The underlying\nsupersymmetry algebra of these theories is shown to be \
isomorphic to the\nPoincar\\'e superalgebra in $d$-dimensions. We also give a \
localization\nprocedure which leads to nontrivial results for $d=2$.\n", 
