 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The lattice studies in QCD demonstrate the nontrivial \
localization behavior\\nof the eigenmodes of the 4D Euclidean Dirac operator \
considered as Hamiltonian\\nof $4+1$ dimensional disordered system. We use \
the holographic viewpoint to\\nprovide the conjectural explanation of these \
properties. The delocalization of\\nall modes in the confined phase is \
related to the $\\\\theta=\\\\pi$ - like phenomena\\nwhen the domain walls \
between degenerated vacua are possible. It is conjectured\\nthat the \
localized modes separated by mobility edge from the rest of the\\nspectrum in \
deconfined QCD correspond to the near-horizon region in the\\nholographic \
dual.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
