 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  For Chern-Simons-matter theories in three dimensions, \
gauge invariance may\\nrequire the Chern-Simons level k to be half-integral, \
in which case parity is\\nviolated. As noted by Pasquetti for abelian \
theories with N=2 supersymmetry,\\nthe partition function on the ellipsoid \
also admits a suitable holomorphic\\nfactorization precisely when the value \
of k is properly quantized. Using known\\nformulas for the partition \
function, we investigate analytic aspects of this\\nfactorization for \
non-abelian gauge groups and general matter representations.\\nWe verify that \
factorization occurs in accord with the parity anomaly for the\\nclassical \
matrix groups and for the exceptional group G_2. In an appendix, we\\ndiscuss \
the analytic continuation of torus knot observables in the \
SU(2)\\nChern-Simons-matter theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
