                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct novel $7d$ supersymmetric gauge theories \
which include a\\nChern-Simons-like term on curved spaces. In order to so, we \
examine the\\nsupersymmetry constraints for E7-branes in type IIA$^*$ theory, \
rather than\\nmaking use of an off-shell supergravity. We find two classes of \
solutions to\\nthe constraints, expressed in terms of a $G_2$-structure with \
non-vanishing\\nintrinsic torsion. The supersymmetric gauge theories are then \
obtained by\\ncoupling flat gauge theory to such supersymmetric backgrounds. \
Various examples\\nare given, including round and squashed $S^7$ as well as \
$S^3 \\\\times M_4$ with\\n$M_4$ hyperk\\\\\\\"{a}hler.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
