 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Starting with a very pedestrian point of view we \
compare two different at the\\nfirst glance definitions for an algebra \
associated to BPS states in\\nsupersymmetric fields theories. One proposed by \
Harvey and Moore exploits\\n$S$-matrices of BPS states as structure constants \
of a new algebra. Another one\\nproposed by Kontsevich and Soibelman gives a \
construction according to the\\nstructure of cohomological Hall algebras. We \
show these two constructions give\\nequivalent algebras.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
