 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct ${\\\\cal N}=2$ supersymmetric Yang-Mills \
theory on 4D manifolds\\nwith a Killing vector field with isolated fixed \
points. It turns out that for\\nevery fixed point one can allocate either \
instanton or anti-instanton\\ncontributions to the partition function, and \
that this is compatible with\\nsupersymmetry. The equivariant \
Donaldson-Witten theory is a special case of our\\nconstruction. We present a \
unified treatment of Pestun's calculation on $S^4$\\nand equivariant \
Donaldson-Witten theory by generalizing the notion of\\nself-duality on \
manifolds with a vector field. We conjecture the full partition\\nfunction \
for a ${\\\\cal N}=2$ theory on any 4D manifold with a Killing \
vector.\\nUsing this new notion of self-duality to localize a supersymmetric \
theory is\\nwhat we call \\\"Pestunization\\\".\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
