          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1812.06473", "submitter" -> "Maxim Zabzine", "authors" -> 
            "Guido Festuccia, Jian Qiu, Jacob Winding and Maxim Zabzine", 
            "title" -> "Twisting with a Flip (the Art of Pestunization)", 
            "comments" -> 
            "58 pages, typos corrected, the final version to appear in CMP", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Commun.Math.Phys. 377 (2020) 1, 341-385", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/s00220-020-03681-9", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math.DG", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct ${\\cal N}=2$ supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory on \
4D manifolds\nwith a Killing vector field with isolated fixed points. It \
turns out that for\nevery fixed point one can allocate either instanton or \
anti-instanton\ncontributions to the partition function, and that this is \
compatible with\nsupersymmetry. The equivariant Donaldson-Witten theory is a \
special case of our\nconstruction. We present a unified treatment of Pestun's \
calculation on $S^4$\nand equivariant Donaldson-Witten theory by generalizing \
the notion of\nself-duality on manifolds with a vector field. We conjecture \
the full partition\nfunction for a ${\\cal N}=2$ theory on any 4D manifold \
with a Killing vector.\nUsing this new notion of self-duality to localize a \
supersymmetric theory is\nwhat we call \"Pestunization\".\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
