            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  According to the Axionic String Anstaz (ASA) confining flux \
tubes in pure\ngluodynamics are in the same equivalence class as a new family \
of integrable\nnon-critical strings, called axionic strings. In addition to \
translational\nmodes, axionic strings carry a set of worldsheet axions \
transforming as an\nantisymmetric tensor under the group of transverse \
rotations. We initiate a\nstudy of integrable axionic strings at general \
number of space-time dimensions\n$D$. We show that in the infinite tension \
limit worldsheet axions should be\ndescribed by a peculiar \"pseudofree\" \
theory---their $S$-matrix is trivial, but\nthe corresponding action cannot be \
brought into a free form by a local field\nredefinition. This requirement \
fixes the axionic action to take a form of the\n$O(D-2)$ Wess--Zumino--Witten \
(WZW) model.\n", 
