                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show how so-called Yang-Baxter (YB) deformations of \
sigma models, based on\\nan R-matrix solving the classical Yang-Baxter \
equation (CYBE), give rise to\\nmarginal current-current deformations when \
applied to the Wess-Zumino-Witten\\n(WZW) model. For non-compact groups these \
marginal deformations are more\\ngeneral than the ones usually considered, \
since they can involve a non-abelian\\ncurrent subalgebra. We classify such \
deformations of the AdS(3) x S(3) string.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
