           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1812.07572\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yifan Wang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M\\\\'ark Mezei, Silviu S. Pufu, and Yifan Wang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Chern-Simons theory from M5-branes and calibrated \
M2-branes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"64 pages + appendices, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2019)165\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUPT-2576\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a sector of the 5d maximally supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory on\\n$S^5$ consisting of $1/8$-BPS Wilson loop operators \
contained within a great\\n$S^3$ inside $S^5$. We conjecture that these \
observables are described by a 3d\\nChern Simons theory on $S^3$, \
analytically continued to a pure imaginary\\nChern-Simons level. Therefore, \
the expectation values of these 5d Wilson loops\\ncompute knot invariants. We \
verify this conjecture in the weakly-coupled regime\\nfrom explicit Feynman \
diagram computations. At strong coupling, these Wilson\\nloop operators lift \
to $1/8$-BPS surface operators in the 6d $(2,0)$ theory on\\n$S^1\\\\times \
S^5$. Using AdS/CFT, we show that these surface operators are dual\\nto \
M2-branes subject to certain calibration conditions required in order \
to\\npreserve supersymmetry. We compute the renormalized action of a large \
class of\\ncalibrated M2-branes and obtain a perfect match with the field \
theory\\nprediction. Finally, we present a derivation of the 3d Chern-Simons \
theory from\\n5d super-Yang-Mills theory using supersymmetric localization, \
modulo a subtle\\nissue that we discuss.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
