         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1812.07572", "submitter" -> "Yifan Wang", "authors" -> 
            "M\\'ark Mezei, Silviu S. Pufu, and Yifan Wang", "title" -> 
            "Chern-Simons theory from M5-branes and calibrated M2-branes", 
            "comments" -> "64 pages + appendices, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2019)165", "report-no" -> 
            "PUPT-2576", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study a sector of the 5d maximally supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory on\n$S^5$ consisting of $1/8$-BPS Wilson loop operators \
contained within a great\n$S^3$ inside $S^5$. We conjecture that these \
observables are described by a 3d\nChern Simons theory on $S^3$, analytically \
continued to a pure imaginary\nChern-Simons level. Therefore, the expectation \
values of these 5d Wilson loops\ncompute knot invariants. We verify this \
conjecture in the weakly-coupled regime\nfrom explicit Feynman diagram \
computations. At strong coupling, these Wilson\nloop operators lift to \
$1/8$-BPS surface operators in the 6d $(2,0)$ theory on\n$S^1\\times S^5$. \
Using AdS/CFT, we show that these surface operators are dual\nto M2-branes \
subject to certain calibration conditions required in order to\npreserve \
supersymmetry. We compute the renormalized action of a large class of\n\
calibrated M2-branes and obtain a perfect match with the field theory\n\
prediction. Finally, we present a derivation of the 3d Chern-Simons theory \
from\n5d super-Yang-Mills theory using supersymmetric localization, modulo a \
subtle\nissue that we discuss.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 18 Dec 2018 19:00:00 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2019-10-02", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Mezei", "M\[AAcute]rk", ""}, {
              "Pufu", "Silviu S.", ""}, {"Wang", "Yifan", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
