            "Francesco Aprile, Sara Pasquetti, Yegor Zenkevich", "title" -> 
            "Flipping the head of T[SU(N)]: mirror symmetry, spectral duality \
and\n  monopoles", "comments" -> "74 pages, 15 pictures", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP04(2019)138", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider T[SU(N)] and its mirror, and we argue that there \
are two more\ndual frames, which are obtained by adding flipping fields for \
the moment maps\non the Higgs and Coulomb branch. Turning on a monopole \
deformation in T[SU(N)],\nand following its effect on each dual frame, we \
obtain four new daughter\ntheories dual to each other. We are then able to \
construct pairs of 3d spectral\ndual theories by performing simple operations \
on the four dual frames of\nT[SU(N)]. Engineering these 3d spectral pairs as \
codimension-two defect\ntheories coupled to a trivial 5d theory, via \
Higgsing, we show that our 3d\nspectral dual theories descends from the 5d \
spectral duality, or fiber base\nduality in topological string. We provide \
further consistency checks about the\nweb of dualities we constructed by \
matching partition functions on the three\nsphere, and in the case of \
spectral duality, matching exactly topological\nstring computations with \
holomorphic blocks.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
