               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1812.08195\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrea Dei\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Andrea Dei, Alessandro Sfondrini\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable S matrix, mirror TBA and spectrum for the \
stringy\\n  \
$\\\\text{AdS}_{3}\\\\times\\\\text{S}^3\\\\times\\\\text{S}^3\\\\times\\\\\
text{S}^1$ WZW model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"38 pages, Version accepted for publication in JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2019)072\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the tree-level bosonic S matrix in \
light-cone gauge for\\nsuperstrings on \
pure-NSNS\\n$\\\\text{AdS}_{3}\\\\times\\\\text{S}^3\\\\times\\\\text{S}^3\\\\\
times\\\\text{S}^1$. We show that\\nit is proportional to the identity and \
that it takes the same form as for\\n$\\\\text{AdS}_{3} \\\\times \
\\\\text{S}^3\\\\times\\\\text{T}^4$ and for flat space. Based on\\nthis, we \
make a conjecture for the exact worldsheet S matrix and derive the\\nmirror \
thermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA) equations describing the spectrum.\\nDespite \
a non-trivial vacuum energy, they can be solved in closed form and\\ncoincide \
with a simple set of Bethe ansatz equations - again much \
like\\n$\\\\text{AdS}_{3}\\\\times\\\\text{S}^3\\\\times\\\\text{T}^4$ and \
flat space. This suggests\\nthat the model may have an integrable spin-chain \
interpretation. Finally, as a\\ncheck of our proposal, we compute the \
spectrum from the worldsheet CFT in the\\ncase of highest-weight \
representations of the underlying Ka\\\\v{c}-Moody\\nalgebras, and show that \
the mirror-TBA prediction matches it on the nose.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
