            "  We compute the tree-level bosonic S matrix in light-cone gauge \
for\nsuperstrings on pure-NSNS\n\
$\\text{AdS}_{3}\\times\\text{S}^3\\times\\text{S}^3\\times\\text{S}^1$. We \
show that\nit is proportional to the identity and that it takes the same form \
as for\n$\\text{AdS}_{3} \\times \\text{S}^3\\times\\text{T}^4$ and for flat \
space. Based on\nthis, we make a conjecture for the exact worldsheet S matrix \
and derive the\nmirror thermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA) equations describing \
the spectrum.\nDespite a non-trivial vacuum energy, they can be solved in \
closed form and\ncoincide with a simple set of Bethe ansatz equations - again \
much like\n$\\text{AdS}_{3}\\times\\text{S}^3\\times\\text{T}^4$ and flat \
space. This suggests\nthat the model may have an integrable spin-chain \
interpretation. Finally, as a\ncheck of our proposal, we compute the spectrum \
from the worldsheet CFT in the\ncase of highest-weight representations of the \
underlying Ka\\v{c}-Moody\nalgebras, and show that the mirror-TBA prediction \
matches it on the nose.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
