 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the partition function of an $\\\\mathcal \
N=2$ chiral multiplet on\\ntopologically twisted $H^2\\\\times S^1$. The \
chiral multiplet is coupled to a\\nbackground vector multiplet encoding a \
real mass deformation. We consider an $\\nH^2\\\\times S^1$ metric containing \
two parameters: one is the $S^1$ radius, while\\nthe other gives a fugacity \
$q$ for the angular momentum on $H^2$. The\\ncomputation is carried out by \
means of supersymmetric localization, which\\nprovides a finite answer \
written in terms of $q$-Pochammer symbols and multiple\\nZeta functions. \
Especially, the partition function of normalizable fields\\nreproduces \
three-dimensional holomorphic blocks.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
