 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the partition functions of $\\\\mathcal{N} = \
1$ gauge theories on\\n$S^2 \\\\times \\\\mathbb{R}^2_\\\\varepsilon$ using \
supersymmetric localization. The\\npath integral reduces to a sum over \
vortices at the poles of $S^2$ and at the\\norigin of \
$\\\\mathbb{R}^2_\\\\varepsilon$. The exact partition functions allow us \
to\\ntest Seiberg duality beyond the supersymmetric index. We propose the\\n$\
\\\\mathcal{N} = 1$ partition functions on the $\\\\Omega$-background, and \
show that\\nthe Nekrasov partition functions can be recovered from these \
building blocks.\\n\""}]}, {
