 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the Feynman graph structure and compute \
certain exact four-point\\ncorrelation functions in chiral CFT$_4$ proposed \
by \\\\\\\"{O}.G\\\\\\\"{u}rdo\\\\u{g}an and\\none of the authors as a double \
scaling limit of $\\\\gamma$-deformed\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM theory. We \
give full description of bulk behavior of large\\nFeynman graphs: it shows a \
generalized \\\"dynamical fishnet\\\" structure, with a\\ndynamical exchange \
of bosonic and Yukawa couplings. We compute certain\\nfour-point correlators \
in the full chiral CFT$_4$, generalizing recent results\\nfor a particular \
one-coupling version of this theory -- the bi-scalar \\\"fishnet\\\"\\nCFT. \
We sum up exactly the corresponding Feynman diagrams, including \
both\\nbosonic and fermionic loops, by Bethe-Salpeter method. This provides \
explicit\\nOPE data for various twist-2 operators with spin, showing a rich \
analytic\\nstructure, both in coordinate and coupling spaces.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
