             "abstract" -> 
             "  We clarify the relationship between probe analysis of the \
supergravity dual\nand the large-N solution of the localization matrix model \
for the planar N = 2*\nsuper-Yang-Mills theory. A formalism inspired by \
supergravity allows us to\nsystematically solve the matrix model at strong \
coupling. Quite surprisingly,\nwe find that quantum phase transitions, known \
to occur in the N = 2* theory,\nstart to be visible at the third order of the \
strong-coupling expansion and\nthus constitute a perturbative phenomenon on \
the string worldsheet.\n", 
