               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold Steinacker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marcus Sperling, Harold C. Steinacker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Covariant cosmological quantum space-time, higher-spin \
and gravity in\\n  the IKKT matrix model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"46 + 12 pages. V2: references added, minor corrections. \
V3: improved\\n  presentation, references added, on-shell modes \
corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2019)010\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UWThPh-2019-02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss a $(3{+}1)$-dimensional covariant quantum \
space-time describing a\\nFLRW cosmology with Big Bounce, obtained by a \
projection of the fuzzy\\nhyperboloid $H^4_n$. This provides a background \
solution of the IKKT matrix\\nmodel with mass term. We characterize the \
bosonic fluctuation spectrum, which\\nconsists of a tower of higher-spin \
modes, truncated at $n$. The modes are\\norganized in terms of an underlying \
$SO(4,2)$ structure group, which is broken\\nto the $SO(3,1)$ isometry of the \
background. The resulting higher-spin gauge\\ntheory includes all degrees of \
freedom required for gravity, and should be well\\nsuited for quantization. \
All modes propagate with the same speed of light, even\\nthough local boost \
invariance is not manifest. The propagating metric\\nperturbation modes \
comprise those of a massless graviton, as well as a scalar\\nmode. Gauge \
invariance allows to obtain the analog of the linearized\\nEinstein-Hilbert \
action, which is expected to be induced upon quantization.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
