                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study supergravity BPS equations which correspond to \
mass-deformation of\\nsome representative AdS/CFT examples. The field theory \
of interest are N=4, D=4\\nsuper Yang-Mills, the ABJM model in D=3, and the \
Brandhuber-Oz fixed point in\\nD=5. For these gauge theories the free energy \
with mass terms for matter\\nmultiplets is calculable in large-N limit using \
supersymmetric localization\\ntechnique. We suggest a perturbative method to \
solve the supergravity\\nequations. For the dual of mass-deformed ABJM model \
we reproduce the known\\nexact solutions. For the mass-deformed Brandhuber-Oz \
theory our method gives\\nthe holographic free energy in analytic form. For \
N=2* theory our result is in\\ngood agreement with the localization \
result.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
