Yifan Wang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ Super-Yang-Mills Correlators at Strong \
Coupling from\\n  String Theory and Localization\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages plus appendices, v2 fixed minor typos, version \
submitted to\\n  journal\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP12(2019)119\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUPT-2582\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute $1/\\\\lambda$ corrections to the four-point \
functions of half-BPS\\noperators in $SU(N)$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
super-Yang-Mills theory at large $N$ and\\nlarge 't Hooft coupling \
$\\\\lambda=g_\\\\text{YM}^2 N$ using two methods. Firstly,\\nwe relate \
integrals of these correlators to derivatives of the mass deformed\\n$S^4$ \
free energy, which was computed at leading order in large $N$ and to \
all\\norders in $1/\\\\lambda$ using supersymmetric localization. Secondly, \
we use\\nAdS/CFT to relate these $1/\\\\lambda$ corrections to higher \
derivative\\ncorrections to supergravity for scattering amplitudes of \
Kaluza-Klein scalars\\nin IIB string theory on $AdS_5\\\\times S^5$, which in \
the flat space limit are\\nknown from worldsheet calculations. These two \
methods match at the order\\ncorresponding to the tree level $R^4$ \
interaction in string theory, which\\nprovides a precise check of AdS/CFT \
beyond supergravity, and allow us to derive\\nthe holographic correlators to \
tree level $D^4R^4$ order. Combined with\\nconstraints from arXiv:1809.10670, \
our results can be used to derive CFT data\\nto one-loop $D^4R^4$ order. \
Finally, we use AdS/CFT to fix these correlators in\\nthe limit where $N$ is \
taken to be large while $g_{\\\\rm YM}$ is kept fixed. In\\nthis limit, we \
present a conjecture for the small mass limit of the $S^4$\\npartition \
function that includes all instanton corrections and is written in\\nterms of \
the same Eisenstein series that appear in the study of string \
theory\\nscattering amplitudes.\\n\""}]}, {
