            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute $1/\\lambda$ corrections to the four-point \
functions of half-BPS\noperators in $SU(N)$ $\\mathcal{N}=4$ super-Yang-Mills \
theory at large $N$ and\nlarge 't Hooft coupling $\\lambda=g_\\text{YM}^2 N$ \
using two methods. Firstly,\nwe relate integrals of these correlators to \
derivatives of the mass deformed\n$S^4$ free energy, which was computed at \
leading order in large $N$ and to all\norders in $1/\\lambda$ using \
supersymmetric localization. Secondly, we use\nAdS/CFT to relate these \
$1/\\lambda$ corrections to higher derivative\ncorrections to supergravity \
for scattering amplitudes of Kaluza-Klein scalars\nin IIB string theory on \
$AdS_5\\times S^5$, which in the flat space limit are\nknown from worldsheet \
calculations. These two methods match at the order\ncorresponding to the tree \
level $R^4$ interaction in string theory, which\nprovides a precise check of \
AdS/CFT beyond supergravity, and allow us to derive\nthe holographic \
correlators to tree level $D^4R^4$ order. Combined with\nconstraints from \
arXiv:1809.10670, our results can be used to derive CFT data\nto one-loop \
$D^4R^4$ order. Finally, we use AdS/CFT to fix these correlators in\nthe \
limit where $N$ is taken to be large while $g_{\\rm YM}$ is kept fixed. In\n\
this limit, we present a conjecture for the small mass limit of the $S^4$\n\
partition function that includes all instanton corrections and is written in\n\
terms of the same Eisenstein series that appear in the study of string theory\
\nscattering amplitudes.\n", 
