                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We solve the Wess-Zumino consistency conditions of \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ off-shell\\nconformal supergravity in four dimensions and \
determine the general form of the\\nsuperconformal anomalies for arbitrary \
$a$ and $c$ anomaly coefficients to\\nleading non trivial order in the \
gravitino. Besides the well known Weyl and\\n$R$-symmetry anomalies, we \
compute explicitly the fermionic $\\\\mathcal{Q}$- \
and\\n$\\\\mathcal{S}$-supersymmetry anomalies. In particular, we show \
that\\n$\\\\mathcal{Q}$-supersymmetry is anomalous if and only if \
$R$-symmetry is\\nanomalous. The $\\\\mathcal{Q}$- and \
$\\\\mathcal{S}$-supersymmetry anomalies give\\nrise to an anomalous \
supersymmetry transformation for the supercurrent on\\ncurved backgrounds \
admitting Killing spinors, resulting in a deformed rigid\\nsupersymmetry \
algebra. Our results may have implications for supersymmetric\\nlocalization \
and supersymmetry phenomenology. Analogous results are expected to\\nhold in \
dimensions two and six and for other supergravity theories. The \
present\\nanalysis of the Wess-Zumino consistency conditions reproduces the \
holographic\\nresult of arxiv:1703.04299 and generalizes it to arbitrary $a$ \
and $c$ anomaly\\ncoefficients.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
