           "id" -> "1902.06717", "submitter" -> "Ioannis Papadimitriou", 
            "authors" -> "Ioannis Papadimitriou", "title" -> 
            "Supersymmetry anomalies in $\\mathcal{N}=1$ conformal \
supergravity", "comments" -> 
            "13+13 pages; v2: minor corrections and improvements; references\n\
  added; v3: further minor typos corrected; version published in JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP04(2019)040", 
            "report-no" -> "KIAS-P19007", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We solve the Wess-Zumino consistency conditions of \
$\\mathcal{N}=1$ off-shell\nconformal supergravity in four dimensions and \
determine the general form of the\nsuperconformal anomalies for arbitrary $a$ \
and $c$ anomaly coefficients to\nleading non trivial order in the gravitino. \
Besides the well known Weyl and\n$R$-symmetry anomalies, we compute \
explicitly the fermionic $\\mathcal{Q}$- and\n$\\mathcal{S}$-supersymmetry \
anomalies. In particular, we show that\n$\\mathcal{Q}$-supersymmetry is \
anomalous if and only if $R$-symmetry is\nanomalous. The $\\mathcal{Q}$- and \
$\\mathcal{S}$-supersymmetry anomalies give\nrise to an anomalous \
supersymmetry transformation for the supercurrent on\ncurved backgrounds \
admitting Killing spinors, resulting in a deformed rigid\nsupersymmetry \
algebra. Our results may have implications for supersymmetric\nlocalization \
and supersymmetry phenomenology. Analogous results are expected to\nhold in \
dimensions two and six and for other supergravity theories. The present\n\
analysis of the Wess-Zumino consistency conditions reproduces the holographic\
\nresult of arxiv:1703.04299 and generalizes it to arbitrary $a$ and $c$ \
anomaly\ncoefficients.\n", 
