 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study 3d $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ Chern-Simons (CS) quiver \
theories on $S^3$ and\\n${\\\\Sigma}_{\\\\mathfrak{g}}\\\\times S^1$. Using \
localization results, we examine\\ntheir partition functions in the large \
rank limit and requiring the resulting\\nmatrix models to be local, find a \
large class of quiver theories that include\\nquivers in one-to-one \
correspondence with the $\\\\widehat{ADE}$ Dynkin diagrams.\\nWe compute \
explicitly the partition function on $S^3$ for $\\\\widehat{D}$ quivers\\nand \
that on ${\\\\Sigma}_{\\\\mathfrak{g}}\\\\times S^1$ for $\\\\widehat{AD}$ \
quivers,\\nwhich lead to certain predictions for their holographic duals. We \
also provide\\na new and simple proof of the \\\"index theorem\\\", extending \
its applicability to a\\nlarger class of theories than considered before in \
the literature.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
