          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1903.01408", "submitter" -> "Georgios Pastras", "authors" -> 
            "Dimitrios Katsinis, Ioannis Mitsoulas and Georgios Pastras", 
            "title" -> 
            "Salient Features of Dressed Elliptic String Solutions on\n  \
$\\mathbb{R}\\times$S$^2$", "comments" -> "75 pages, 27 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Eur.Phys.J.C 79 (2019) 10, 869", "doi" -> 
            "10.1140/epjc/s10052-019-7369-0", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We analyse several physical aspects of the dressed elliptic \
strings\npropagating on $\\mathbb{R} \\times \\mathrm{S}^2$ and of their \
counterparts in\nthe Pohlmeyer reduced theory, i.e. the sine-Gordon equation. \
The solutions are\ndivided into two wide classes; kinks which propagate on \
top of elliptic\nbackgrounds and those which are non-localised periodic \
disturbances of the\nlatter. The former class of solutions obey a specific \
equation of state that is\nin principle experimentally verifiable in systems \
which realize the sine-Gordon\nequation. Among both of these classes, there \
appears to be a particular class\nof interest the closed dressed strings. \
They in turn form four distinct\nsubclasses of solutions. Unlike the closed \
elliptic strings, these four\nsubclasses, exhibit interactions among their \
spikes. These interactions\npreserve a carefully defined turning number, \
which can be associated to the\ntopological charge of the sine-Gordon \
counterpart. One particular class of\nthose closed dressed strings realizes \
instabilities of the seed elliptic\nsolutions. The existence of such \
solutions depends on whether a superluminal\nkink with a specific velocity \
can propagate on the corresponding elliptic\nsine-Gordon solution. Finally, \
the dispersion relations of the dressed strings\nare studied. A qualitative \
difference between the two wide classes of dressed\nstrings is discovered. \
This would be an interesting subject for investigation\nin the dual field \
theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 4 Mar 2019 18:05:31 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-04-20", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Katsinis", "Dimitrios", ""}, {
              "Mitsoulas", "Ioannis", ""}, {"Pastras", "Georgios", ""}}}], 
