               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct several novel examples of 3d \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ models whose free\\nenergy scales as $N^{3/2}$ at large \
$N$. This is the first step towards the\\nidentification of field theories \
with an M-theory dual. Furthermore, we match\\nthe volumes extracted from the \
free energy with the ones computed from the\\nHilbert series. We perform a \
similar analysis for the 4d parents of the 3d\\nmodels, matching the volume \
extracted from the $a$ conformal anomaly to that\\nobtained from the Hilbert \
series. For some of the 4d models, we show the\\nexistence of a \
Sasaki-Einstein metric on the internal space of the candidate\\ntype IIB \
gravity dual.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
