        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{14.401634685090336`, -9.461127676638299}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1903.03623\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wolfger Peelaers\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Yiwen Pan, Wolfger Peelaers\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Schur correlation functions on $S^3\\\\times S^1$\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"49 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2019)013\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Schur limit of the superconformal index of \
four-dimensional $\\\\mathcal\\nN=2$ superconformal field theories has been \
shown to equal the supercharacter\\nof the vacuum module of their associated \
chiral algebra. Applying localization\\ntechniques to the theory suitably put \
on $S^3\\\\times S^1$, we obtain a direct\\nderivation of this fact. We also \
show that the localization computation can be\\nextended to calculate \
correlation functions of a subset of local operators,\\nnamely of the \
so-called Schur operators. Such correlators correspond to\\ninsertions of \
chiral algebra fields in the trace-formula computing the\\nsupercharacter. As \
a by-product of our analysis, we show that the standard lore\\nin the \
localization literature stating that only off-shell \
supersymmetrically\\nclosed observables are amenable to localization, is \
incomplete, and we\\ndemonstrate how insertions of fermionic operators can be \
incorporated in the\\ncomputation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
