                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Correlators of local operators inserted on a straight \
Wilson loop in a\\nconformal gauge theory have the structure of a \
one-dimensional \\\"defect\\\" CFT. As\\nwas shown in arXiv:1706.00756, in \
the case of supersymmetric Wilson-Maldacena\\nloop in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM \
one can compute the strong-coupling contributions\\nto 4-point correlators of \
operator insertions by starting with the AdS$_5\\n\\\\times S^5$ string \
action expanded near the AdS$_2$ minimal surface and\\nevaluating the \
corresponding AdS$_2$ Witten diagrams. We perform the \
analogous\\ncomputations in the non-supersymmetric case of the standard \
Wilson loop with no\\ncoupling to the scalars. The corresponding \
non-supersymmetric \\\"defect\\\" CFT$_1$\\nhas an unbroken $SO(6)$ global \
symmetry. The elementary bosonic operators (6\\nSYM scalars and 3 components \
of the SYM field strength) are dual respectively\\nto the $S^5$ embedding \
coordinates and AdS$_5$ coordinates transverse to the\\nminimal surface \
ending on the line at the boundary. The $SO(6)$ symmetry is\\npreserved \
provided the 5-sphere coordinates satisfy Neumann boundary conditions\\n(as \
opposed to Dirichlet in the supersymmetric case); one should then \
integrate\\nover the $S^5$. The massless $S^5$ fluctuations have logarithmic \
propagator,\\ncorresponding to the boundary scalar operator having dimension \
$\\\\Delta=\\n\\\\frac{5}{\\\\sqrt\\\\lambda} + \\\\ldots$ at strong \
coupling. The resulting functions of\\n1d cross-ratio in the 4-point \
functions have a more complicated structure than\\nin the supersymmetric \
case, involving polylogs (Li$_3$ and Li$_2$). We also\\ndiscuss consistency \
with the operator product expansion which allows extracting\\nthe leading \
strong coupling corrections to the anomalous dimensions of the\\noperators \
appearing in the intermediate channels.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
