               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Panagiotis Betzios\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Panos Betzios, Elias Kiritsis, Olga Papadoulaki\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Euclidean Wormholes and Holography\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"77 pages, 21 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2019)042\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Asymptotically AdS wormhole solutions are considered in \
the context of\\nholography. Correlation functions of local operators on \
distinct boundaries are\\nstudied. It is found that such correlators are \
finite at short distances.\\nCorrelation functions of non-local operators \
(Wilson loops) on distinct\\nboundaries are also studied, with similar \
conclusions. Deformations of the\\ntheory with multi-trace operators on \
distinct boundaries are considered and\\nstudied. As a consequence of these \
results, the dual theory is expected to\\nfactorize in the UV, and the two \
sectors to be coupled by a soft non-local\\ninteraction. A simple field \
theory model with such behavior is presented.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
