            "10.1007/JHEP06(2019)042", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Asymptotically AdS wormhole solutions are considered in the \
context of\nholography. Correlation functions of local operators on distinct \
boundaries are\nstudied. It is found that such correlators are finite at \
short distances.\nCorrelation functions of non-local operators (Wilson loops) \
on distinct\nboundaries are also studied, with similar conclusions. \
Deformations of the\ntheory with multi-trace operators on distinct boundaries \
are considered and\nstudied. As a consequence of these results, the dual \
theory is expected to\nfactorize in the UV, and the two sectors to be coupled \
by a soft non-local\ninteraction. A simple field theory model with such \
behavior is presented.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
