               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"The Holographic Fishchain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"5 pages. v2: references added, v3 - acknowledgment \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. Lett. 123, 081602 (2019)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.081602\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present the first-principle derivation of a \
weak-strong duality between\\nthe fishnet theory in four dimensions and a \
discretized string-like model\\nliving in five dimensions. At strong \
coupling, the dual description becomes\\nclassical and we demonstrate \
explicitly the classical integrability of the\\nmodel. We test our results by \
reproducing the strong coupling limit of the\\n$4$-point correlator computed \
before non-perturbatively from the conformal\\npartial wave expansion. Due to \
the extreme simplicity of our model, it could\\nprovide an ideal playground \
for holography with no super-symmetry. Furthermore,\\nsince the fishnet model \
and ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM theory are continuously linked our\\nconsideration \
could shed light on the derivation of AdS/CFT for the latter.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
