 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Let $F_g(t)$ be the generating function of intersection \
numbers on the moduli\\nspaces $\\\\bar{\\\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}$ of complex \
curves of genus $g$. As by-product\\nof a complete solution of all non-planar \
correlation functions of the\\nrenormalised $\\\\Phi^3$-matrical QFT model, \
we explicitly construct a Laplacian\\n$\\\\Delta_t$ on the space of formal \
parameters $t_i$ satisfying $\\\\exp(\\\\sum_{g\\\\geq\\n2} \
N^{2-2g}F_g(t))=\\\\exp((-\\\\Delta_t+F_2(t))/N^2)1$ for any $N>0$. The \
result is\\nachieved via Dyson-Schwinger equations from noncommutative \
quantum field theory\\ncombined with residue techniques from topological \
recursion. The genus-$g$\\ncorrelation functions of the $\\\\Phi^3$-matricial \
QFT model are obtained by\\nrepeated application of another differential \
operator to $F_g(t)$ and taking\\nfor $t_i$ the renormalised moments of a \
measure constructed from the covariance\\nof the model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
