                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},
               {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We determine the general structure of quantum anomalies \
for the $R$-multiplet\\nof four dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ supersymmetric \
quantum field theories in\\nthe presence of background fields for an \
arbitrary number of Abelian flavor\\nmultiplets. By solving the Wess-Zumino \
consistency conditions for off-shell new\\nminimal supergravity in four \
dimensions with an arbitrary number of Abelian\\nvector multiplets, we \
compute the anomaly in the conservation of the\\nsupercurrent to leading non \
trivial order in the gravitino and vector multiplet\\nfermions. We find that \
both $R$-symmetry and flavor anomalies necessarily lead\\nto a supersymmetry \
anomaly, thus generalizing our earlier results to non\\nsuperconformal \
theories with Abelian flavor symmetries. The anomaly in the\\nconservation of \
the supercurrent leads to an anomalous transformation for the\\nsupercurrent \
under rigid supersymmetry on bosonic backgrounds that admit new\\nminimal \
Killing spinors. The resulting deformation of the supersymmetry algebra\\nhas \
implications for supersymmetric localization computations on \
such\\nbackgrounds.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
