           "id" -> "1904.00347", "submitter" -> "Ioannis Papadimitriou", 
            "authors" -> "Ioannis Papadimitriou", "title" -> 
            "Supersymmetry anomalies in new minimal supergravity", "comments" -> 
            "34 pages; v2: generalized analysis of flavor supersymmetry \
anomalies;\n  references added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP09(2019)039", "report-no" -> "KIAS-P19022", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We determine the general structure of quantum anomalies for \
the $R$-multiplet\nof four dimensional $\\mathcal{N}=1$ supersymmetric \
quantum field theories in\nthe presence of background fields for an arbitrary \
number of Abelian flavor\nmultiplets. By solving the Wess-Zumino consistency \
conditions for off-shell new\nminimal supergravity in four dimensions with an \
arbitrary number of Abelian\nvector multiplets, we compute the anomaly in the \
conservation of the\nsupercurrent to leading non trivial order in the \
gravitino and vector multiplet\nfermions. We find that both $R$-symmetry and \
flavor anomalies necessarily lead\nto a supersymmetry anomaly, thus \
generalizing our earlier results to non\nsuperconformal theories with Abelian \
flavor symmetries. The anomaly in the\nconservation of the supercurrent leads \
to an anomalous transformation for the\nsupercurrent under rigid \
supersymmetry on bosonic backgrounds that admit new\nminimal Killing spinors. \
The resulting deformation of the supersymmetry algebra\nhas implications for \
supersymmetric localization computations on such\nbackgrounds.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 31 Mar 2019 06:32:18 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 4 May 2019 03:55:43 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
