 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We summarize the results and the ideas in 1707.06152, \
1707.06154, 1807.07768\\nwhere new warped $\\\\mathrm{AdS}_3$ backgrounds are \
derived in massive IIA string\\ntheory by uplifting exact solutions in \
$\\\\mathcal N=1$, $d=7$ and $\\\\mathcal\\nN=(1,1)$, $d=6$ gauged \
supergravities. These solutions are respectively\\nasymptotically \
$\\\\mathrm{AdS}_7$ and $\\\\mathrm{AdS}_6$ and they are related to\\nthe \
D2-D4-NS5-D6-D8 brane intersection. We provide a particular \
supergravity\\nsolution in 10d describing this bound state and we discuss the \
relations\\nbetween its near-horizon geometry and the uplifts from 6d and 7d. \
Then we give\\nthe holographic interpretation of these $\\\\mathrm{AdS}_3$ \
warped backgrounds in\\nterms of $\\\\mathcal N=(0,4)$ defect \
$\\\\mathrm{SCFT}_2$ within the $\\\\mathcal\\nN=(1,0)$ $\\\\mathrm{SCFT}_6$ \
and the $\\\\mathcal N=2$ $\\\\mathrm{SCFT}_5$.\\n\""}]}, {
