               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1904.06259\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gabriele Perfetto\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gabriele Perfetto, Lorenzo Piroli, Andrea Gambassi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quench action and large deviations: work statistics in \
the\\n  one-dimensional Bose gas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"24 Pages, 6 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. E 100, 032114 (2019)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032114\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.quant-gas quant-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the statistics of large deviations of the \
intensive work done in an\\ninteraction quench of a one-dimensional Bose gas \
with a large number N of\\nparticles, system size L and fixed density. We \
consider the case in which the\\nsystem is initially prepared in the \
non-interacting ground state and a\\nrepulsive interaction is suddenly turned \
on. For large deviations of the work\\nbelow its mean value, we show that the \
large deviation principle holds by means\\nof the quench action approach. \
Using the latter, we compute exactly the\\nso-called rate function, and study \
its properties analytically. In particular,\\nwe find that fluctuations close \
to the mean value of the work exhibit a marked\\nnon- Gaussian behavior, even \
though their probability is always exponentially\\nsuppressed below it as L \
increases. Deviations larger than the mean value,\\ninstead, exhibit an \
algebraic decay, whose exponent can not be determined\\ndirectly by \
large-deviation theory. Exploiting the exact Bethe ansatz\\nrepresentation of \
the eigenstates of the Hamiltonian, we calculate this\\nexponent for \
vanishing particle density. Our approach can be \
straightforwardly\\ngeneralized to quantum quenches in other interacting \
integrable systems.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 12 Apr 2019 14:47:32 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2019-09-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Perfetto\"", ",", "\"Gabriele\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Piroli\"", ",", "\"Lorenzo\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Gambassi\"", ",", "\"Andrea\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
