           "id" -> "1904.07502", "submitter" -> "Erez Y. Urbach", "authors" -> 
            "Ofer Aharony, Erez Y. Urbach and Maya Weiss", "title" -> 
            "Generalized Hawking-Page transitions", "comments" -> Null, 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 1908:018,2019", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP08(2019)018", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct holographic backgrounds that are dual by the \
AdS/CFT\ncorrespondence to Euclidean conformal field theories on products of \
spheres\n$S^{d_1}\\times S^{d_2}$, for conformal field theories whose dual \
may be\napproximated by classical Einstein gravity (typically these are large \
$N$\nstrongly coupled theories). For $d_2=1$ these backgrounds correspond to \
thermal\nfield theories on $S^{d_1}$, and Hawking and Page found that there \
are several\npossible bulk solutions, with two different topologies, that \
compete with each\nother, leading to a phase transition as the relative size \
of the spheres is\nmodified. By numerically solving the Einstein equations we \
find similar results\nalso for $d_2>1$, with bulk solutions in which either \
one or the other sphere\nshrinks to zero smoothly at a minimal value of the \
radial coordinate, and with\na first order phase transition (for $d_1+d_2 < \
9$) between solutions of two\ndifferent topologies as the relative radius \
changes. For a critical ratio of\nthe radii there is a (sub-dominant) \
singular solution where both spheres\nshrink, and we analytically analyze the \
behavior near this radius. For $d_1+d_2\n< 9$ the number of solutions grows \
to infinity as the critical ratio is\napproached.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
