                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently the calculation of holographic free energy for \
mass-deformed ABJM\\nmodel (mABJM) with ${\\\\cal N}=2$ supersymmetry and \
$SU(3)\\\\times U(1)$ global\\nsymmetry was tackled by Bobev et al. in \
arXiv:1812.01026. We solve the\\nassociated BPS equations, requiring IR \
regularity, using a perturbative method\\nproposed by one of us recently in \
axXiv:1902.00418. In particular, we provide\\nan analytic proof of a crucial \
conjecture made in arXiv:1812.01026 based on\\nnumerical solutions: that the \
R-charge values of three chiral multiplets in\\nmABJM should be independent \
of the IR values of a hypermultiplet scalar, which\\nis holographically dual \
to the superpotential mass term.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
