            "  de Sitter vacuum of nonconformal gauge theories is \
non-equilibrium,\nmanifested by a nonvanishing rate of the comoving entropy \
production at\nasymptotically late times. This entropy production rate is \
related to the\nentanglement entropy of the de Sitter vacuum of the theory. \
We use holographic\ncorrespondence to compute vacuum entanglement entropy \
density $s_{ent}$ of mass\ndeformed ${\\cal N}=4$ supersymmetric Yang-Mills \
theory - the ${\\cal N}=2^*$\ngauge theory - for various values of the masses \
and the coupling constant to\nthe background space-time curvature. For a \
particular choice of the curvature\ncoupling, the Euclidean model can be \
solved exactly using the supersymmetric\nlocalization. We show that ${\\cal \
N}=2^*$ de Sitter entanglement entropy is not\nthe thermodynamic entropy of \
the localization free energy at de Sitter\ntemperature. Neither it is related \
to the thermal entropy of de Sitter vacuum\nof pair-produced particles.\n", 
