                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This thesis is mainly devoted to studying integrable \
deformations of the\\n${\\\\rm AdS}_5 \\\\times {\\\\rm S}^5$ superstring and \
generalized supergravity. We\\nstart to give a brief review of the ${\\\\rm \
AdS}_5 \\\\times {\\\\rm S}^5$ superstring\\nformulated in the Green-Schwartz \
formalism, and then introduce homogeneous\\nYang-Baxter (YB) deformation of \
the ${\\\\rm AdS}_5 \\\\times {\\\\rm S}^5$ superstring\\nbased on \
$r$-matrices which are solutions to the homogeneous classical YB\\nequation. \
By performing a supercoset construction, we derive the general\\nformula for \
homogeneous YB deformed backgrounds associated with bosonic\\n$r$-matrices. \
The deformed backgrounds are shown to be solutions of the\\nstandard type IIB \
supergravity or generalized supergravity. Next, we explain\\nthat homogeneous \
YB deformation can be regarded as a kind of the $O(d,d)$\\nduality \
transformations. Once YB deformations are realized as \
duality\\ntransformations, the corresponding $O(d,d)$ transformations are \
applied to\\nalmost all backgrounds. Moreover, we discuss spacetime \
structures of\\nhomogeneous YB deformed backgrounds and clarify a T-fold \
structure of them by\\nshowing the associated $O(d,d; \\\\mathbb{Z})$ \
$T$-duality monodromy. Finally, we\\nconsider the Weyl invariance of string \
theories in generalized supergravity\\nbackgrounds. We show that generalized \
supergravity can be reproduced from\\ndouble field theory with the dilaton \
depending on a linear dual coordinate.\\nFrom this result, we construct a \
possible counterterm to cancel out the Weyl\\nanomaly of bosonic string \
theories on generalized supergravity backgrounds. In\\nparticular, we show \
that the counterterm is definitely local. In this sense,\\nstring theories \
can be consistently defined in generalized \
supergravity\\nbackgrounds.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 29 Apr 2019 17:19:53 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2019-04-30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Sakamoto\"", ",", "\"Jun-ichi\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                    "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> Left, 
             ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
