         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1905.01101", "submitter" -> "Harald Dorn", "authors" -> 
            "Harald Dorn", "title" -> 
            "More on Wilson loops for two touching circles", "comments" -> 
            "18 pages, 8 figures, references added, text as appeared in JHEP",
             "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 07 (2019) 088", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP07(2019)088", "report-no" -> "HU-EP-19/11", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate both at leading weak and strong coupling the \
renormalised\nMaldacena-Wilson loop for contours formed by consecutive \
passage of two\ntouching circles. At the touching point both circles should \
have the same\nnormal direction but form cusps of non-zero opening angle \
$\\alpha$. Particular\nemphasis is put on the behaviour in the limit $\\alpha\
\\rightarrow 0$ and its\ncomparison with the spiky situation studied in a \
previous paper, where $\\alpha$\nwas set to zero before renormalisation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
