               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"J. G. Russo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Properties of the partition function of ${\\\\cal N}=2$ \
supersymmetric QCD\\n  with massive matter\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages. References added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2019)125\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ICCUB-19-007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the different quantum phases that occur in \
massive ${\\\\cal N}=2$\\nsupersymmetric QCD with gauge groups $SU(2)$ and \
$SU(3)$ as the coupling\\n$\\\\Lambda/M$ is gradually increased from 0 to \
infinity. The phases can be\\nidentified by computing the exact partition \
function by saddle-points,\\ncombining supersymmetric localization and the \
Seiberg-Witten formalism. In all\\ncases, we find two phases, a weak coupling \
and a strong coupling phase,\\nseparated by a critical point described by a \
superconformal field theory or\\ninvolving superconformal sectors. In \
crossing the critical point, the dominant\\nsaddle-point hops from one \
singularity of the curve to another one. The\\ntheories seem to undergo a \
second-order phase transition with divergent\\nsusceptibility.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
