            "  We study the different quantum phases that occur in massive ${\
\\cal N}=2$\nsupersymmetric QCD with gauge groups $SU(2)$ and $SU(3)$ as the \
coupling\n$\\Lambda/M$ is gradually increased from 0 to infinity. The phases \
can be\nidentified by computing the exact partition function by \
saddle-points,\ncombining supersymmetric localization and the Seiberg-Witten \
formalism. In all\ncases, we find two phases, a weak coupling and a strong \
coupling phase,\nseparated by a critical point described by a superconformal \
field theory or\ninvolving superconformal sectors. In crossing the critical \
point, the dominant\nsaddle-point hops from one singularity of the curve to \
another one. The\ntheories seem to undergo a second-order phase transition \
with divergent\nsusceptibility.\n", 
