               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1905.05533\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rafael Hernandez\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Rafael Hernandez, Juan Miguel Nieto, Roberto Ruiz\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The $SU(2)$ Wess-Zumino-Witten spin chain sigma \
model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10 pages, Latex. v2: Published version. v3: \
Acknowledgement added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2019)080\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Classical strings propagating in $AdS_{3}\\\\times \
S^{3}\\\\times T^{4}$ supported\\nwith Neveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz flux are \
described by a Wess-Zumino-Witten\\nmodel. In this note, we study the \
emergence of their semiclassical $SU(2)$\\nspectrally flowed sectors as the \
Landau-Lifshitz limit of the underlying\\nquantum spin chain. We consider the \
propagator in the coherent state picture,\\nand find that the time interval \
is discretized proportionally to the lattice\\nspacing. In the \
Landau-Lifshitz limit, where both time and space become\\ncontinuous, we \
derive a path integral representation of the propagator for each\\nspectrally \
flowed sector. We prove that the arbitrariness of the global phase\\nof \
coherent states is mapped to the gauge freedom of the $B$-field in \
the\\nclassical action. We show that higher order corrections in the \
Landau-Lifshitz\\nlimit are suppressed by inverse powers of the 't Hooft \
coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
