            "  Classical strings propagating in $AdS_{3}\\times S^{3}\\times \
T^{4}$ supported\nwith Neveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz flux are described by a \
Wess-Zumino-Witten\nmodel. In this note, we study the emergence of their \
semiclassical $SU(2)$\nspectrally flowed sectors as the Landau-Lifshitz limit \
of the underlying\nquantum spin chain. We consider the propagator in the \
coherent state picture,\nand find that the time interval is discretized \
proportionally to the lattice\nspacing. In the Landau-Lifshitz limit, where \
both time and space become\ncontinuous, we derive a path integral \
representation of the propagator for each\nspectrally flowed sector. We prove \
that the arbitrariness of the global phase\nof coherent states is mapped to \
the gauge freedom of the $B$-field in the\nclassical action. We show that \
higher order corrections in the Landau-Lifshitz\nlimit are suppressed by \
inverse powers of the 't Hooft coupling.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
