               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kristof Hodsagi\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Krist\\\\'of H\\\\'ods\\\\'agi, M\\\\'arton Kormos, \
G\\\\'abor Tak\\\\'acs\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Perturbative post-quench overlaps in Quantum Field Theory\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"H\\\\'ods\\\\'agi, K., Kormos, M. & Tak\\\\'acs, G. J. \
High Energ. Phys.\\n  (2019) 2019: 47\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2019)047\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In analytic descriptions of quantum quenches, the \
overlaps between the\\ninitial pre-quench state and the eigenstates of the \
time evolving Hamiltonian\\nare crucial ingredients. We construct \
perturbative expansions of these overlaps\\nin quantum field theories where \
either the pre-quench or the post-quench\\nHamiltonian is integrable. Using \
the $E_8$ Ising field theory for concrete\\ncomputations, we give explicit \
expressions for the overlaps up to second order\\nin the quench size, and \
verify our results against numerical results obtained\\nusing the Truncated \
Conformal Space Approach. We demonstrate that the expansion\\nusing the \
post-quench basis is very effective, but find some serious\\nlimitations for \
the alternative approach using the pre-quench basis.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
