          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1905.05623", "submitter" -> "Kristof Hodsagi", "authors" -> 
            "Krist\\'of H\\'ods\\'agi, M\\'arton Kormos, G\\'abor Tak\\'acs", 
            "title" -> 
            "Perturbative post-quench overlaps in Quantum Field Theory", 
            "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> 
            "H\\'ods\\'agi, K., Kormos, M. & Tak\\'acs, G. J. High Energ. \
Phys.\n  (2019) 2019: 47", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2019)047", "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In analytic descriptions of quantum quenches, the overlaps \
between the\ninitial pre-quench state and the eigenstates of the time \
evolving Hamiltonian\nare crucial ingredients. We construct perturbative \
expansions of these overlaps\nin quantum field theories where either the \
pre-quench or the post-quench\nHamiltonian is integrable. Using the $E_8$ \
Ising field theory for concrete\ncomputations, we give explicit expressions \
for the overlaps up to second order\nin the quench size, and verify our \
results against numerical results obtained\nusing the Truncated Conformal \
Space Approach. We demonstrate that the expansion\nusing the post-quench \
basis is very effective, but find some serious\nlimitations for the \
alternative approach using the pre-quench basis.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 14 May 2019 14:07:51 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 2 Sep 2019 09:14:13 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
