                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the dependence of supersymmetric partition \
functions on continuous\\nparameters for the flavor symmetry group, $G_F$, \
for 2d $\\\\mathcal{N} = (0,2)$\\nand 4d $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ supersymmetric \
quantum field theories. In any\\ndiffeomorphism-invariant scheme and in the \
presence of $G_F$ 't Hooft\\nanomalies, the supersymmetric Ward identities \
imply that the partition function\\nhas a non-holomorphic dependence on the \
flavor parameters. We show this\\nexplicitly for the 2d torus partition \
function, $Z_{T^2}$, and for a large\\nclass of 4d partition functions on \
half-BPS four-manifolds,\\n$Z_{\\\\mathcal{M}_4}$---in particular, for \
$\\\\mathcal{M}_4=S^3 \\\\times S^1$ and\\n$\\\\mathcal{M}_4=\\\\Sigma_g \
\\\\times T^2$. We propose a new expression for\\n$Z_{\\\\mathcal{M}_{d-1} \\\
\\times S^1}$, which differs from earlier holomorphic\\nresults by the \
introduction of a non-holomorphic `Casimir' pre-factor. The\\nlatter is fixed \
by studying the `high temperature' limit of the partition\\nfunction. Our \
proposal agrees with the supersymmetric Ward identities, and with\\nexplicit \
calculations of the absolute value of the partition function using \
a\\ngauge-invariant zeta-function regularization.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
