               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1905.05807\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matteo Sacchi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sara Pasquetti and Matteo Sacchi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"3d dualities from 2d free field correlators: \
recombination and rank\\n  stabilization\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"79 pages, 16 figures; revised version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2020)061\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose various new 3d N=2 dualities exploiting \
their recently discovered\\nconnection to the duality relations for 2d free \
field CFT correlators. Most of\\nthe dualities involve, as the main building \
block, a quiver theory with\\nmonopole superpotential which enjoys various \
interesting properties such as\\nbeing self-dual and reducing, in a suitable \
real mass deformation, to the\\nfamiliar T[SU(N)] theory. In particular we \
propose a duality for the U(N)\\ntheory with one adjoint and k+1 fundamental \
flavors. By iterating some basic\\ndualities we can bring the theory to a \
stable form which, in turns, allows us\\nto find a dual frame where the rank \
of the original theory appears as a\\nparameter.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
