                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Diogo Buarque Franzosi and Gabriele Ferretti\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Anomalous dimensions of potential top-partners\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, 4 figures, 6 tables V2: Added Table 3,4,5, \
equation (9) and\\n  various comments in reply to questions and suggestions \
raised by the two\\n  Referees of SciPost. Two references also added. V3: \
Typo in footnote 6\\n  corrected. Final version in SciPost\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SciPost Phys. 7, 027 (2019)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.21468/SciPostPhys.7.3.027\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph hep-lat\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss anomalous dimensions of top-partner \
candidates in theories of\\nPartial Compositeness. First, we revisit, confirm \
and extend the computation by\\nDeGrand and Shamir of anomalous dimensions of \
fermionic trilinears. We present\\ngeneral results applicable to all matter \
representations and to composite\\noperators of any allowed spin. We then ask \
the question of whether it is\\nreasonable to expect some models to have \
composite operators of sufficiently\\nlarge anomalous dimension to serve as \
top-partners. While this question can be\\nanswered conclusively only by \
lattice gauge theory, within perturbation theory\\nwe find that such values \
could well occur for some specific models. In the\\nAppendix we collect a \
number of practical group theory results for fourth-order\\ninvariants of \
general interest in gauge theories with many irreducible\\nrepresentations of \
fermions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
