               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1906.02722\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rajesh Gupta\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Justin R. David, Edi Gava, Rajesh Kumar Gupta, Kumar \
Narain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Boundary conditions and localization on AdS: Part 2 \
General analysis\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"38 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2020)139\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop the method of Green's function to evaluate \
the one loop\\ndeterminants that arise in localization of supersymmetric \
field theories on\\n$AdS$ spaces. The theories we study have at least \
${\\\\cal N}=2$ supersymmetry\\nand normalisable boundary conditions are \
consistent with supersymmetry. We then\\nshow that under general assumptions \
the variation of the one loop determinant\\nwith respect to the localizing \
background reduces to a total derivative.\\nTherefore it receives \
contributions only from the origin of $AdS$ and from\\nasymptotic infinity. \
From expanding both the Greens function and the quadratic\\noperators at the \
origin of $AdS$ and asymptotic infinity, we show that the\\nvariation of the \
one loop determinant is proportional to an integer.\\nFurthermore, we show \
that this integer is an index of a first order\\ndifferential operator. We \
demonstrate that these assumptions are valid for\\nChern-Simons theories \
coupled to chiral multiplets on $AdS_2\\\\times S^1$.\\nFinally we use our \
results to show that $U(N_c)$ Chern-Simons theory at level\\n$k$ coupled to \
$N_f$ chiral multiplets and $N_f$ anti-chiral multiplets in the\\nfundamental \
obeys level-rank duality on $AdS_2\\\\times S^1$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
