            "Justin R. David, Edi Gava, Rajesh Kumar Gupta, Kumar Narain", 
            "title" -> 
            "Boundary conditions and localization on AdS: Part 2 General \
analysis", "comments" -> "38 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP02(2020)139", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We develop the method of Green's function to evaluate the one \
loop\ndeterminants that arise in localization of supersymmetric field \
theories on\n$AdS$ spaces. The theories we study have at least ${\\cal N}=2$ \
supersymmetry\nand normalisable boundary conditions are consistent with \
supersymmetry. We then\nshow that under general assumptions the variation of \
the one loop determinant\nwith respect to the localizing background reduces \
to a total derivative.\nTherefore it receives contributions only from the \
origin of $AdS$ and from\nasymptotic infinity. From expanding both the Greens \
function and the quadratic\noperators at the origin of $AdS$ and asymptotic \
infinity, we show that the\nvariation of the one loop determinant is \
proportional to an integer.\nFurthermore, we show that this integer is an \
index of a first order\ndifferential operator. We demonstrate that these \
assumptions are valid for\nChern-Simons theories coupled to chiral multiplets \
on $AdS_2\\times S^1$.\nFinally we use our results to show that $U(N_c)$ \
Chern-Simons theory at level\n$k$ coupled to $N_f$ chiral multiplets and \
$N_f$ anti-chiral multiplets in the\nfundamental obeys level-rank duality on \
$AdS_2\\times S^1$.\n", 
