                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"String theory on the Schrodinger pp-wave \
background\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages; v2: Minor changes, JHEP version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP08(2019)093\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2019)093\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study string theory on the pp-wave geometry obtained \
by taking the Penrose\\nlimit around a certain null geodesic of the \
non-supersymmetric Schrodinger\\nbackground. We solve for the spectrum of \
bosonic excitations and find\\ncompelling agreement with the dispersion \
relation of the giant magnons in the\\nSchrodinger background obtained \
previously in arXiv:1712.03091. Inspired by the\\npp-wave spectrum we \
conjecture an exact in the t'Hooft coupling dispersion\\nrelation for the \
magnons in the original Schrodinger background. We show that\\nthe pp-wave \
background admits exactly 16 Killing spinors. We use the explicit\\nform of \
the latter in order to derive the supersymmetry algebra of the\\nbackground \
which explicitly depends on the deformation parameter. Its \
bosonic\\nsubalgebra is of the Newton-Hooke type.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
