               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1906.09238\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ranjan Modak\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ranjan Modak, Lorenzo Piroli, Pasquale Calabrese\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Correlation and entanglement spreading in nested spin \
chains\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"12 pages, 6 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Stat. Mech. (2019) 093106\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1742-5468/ab39d5\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.quant-gas quant-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The past few years have witnessed the development of a \
comprehensive theory\\nto describe integrable systems out of equilibrium, in \
which the Bethe ansatz\\nformalism has been tailored to address specific \
problems arising in this\\ncontext. While most of the work initially focused \
on the study of prototypical\\nmodels such as the well-known Heisenberg \
chain, many theoretical results have\\nbeen recently extended to a class of \
more complicated $\\\\it{nested}$ integrable\\nsystems, displaying different \
species of quasiparticles. Still, in the simplest\\ncontext of quantum \
quenches, the vast majority of theoretical predictions have\\nbeen \
numerically verified only in systems with an elementary Bethe \
ansatz\\ndescription. In this work, we fill this gap and present a direct \
numerical test\\nof some results presented in the recent literature for \
nested systems, focusing\\nin particular on the Lai-Sutherland model. Using \
time-dependent density matrix\\nrenormalization group and exact \
diagonalization methods, we compute the\\nspreading of both correlation \
functions and entanglement entropy after a quench\\nfrom a simple class of \
product initial states. This allows us to test the\\nvalidity of the nested \
version of a conjectured formula, based on the\\nquasiparticle picture, for \
the growth of the entanglement entropy, and the\\nBethe ansatz predictions \
for the \\\"light-cone\\\" velocity of correlation\\nfunctions.\\n\""}]}, {
