         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1906.09238", "submitter" -> "Ranjan Modak", "authors" -> 
            "Ranjan Modak, Lorenzo Piroli, Pasquale Calabrese", "title" -> 
            "Correlation and entanglement spreading in nested spin chains", 
            "comments" -> "12 pages, 6 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J. Stat. Mech. (2019) 093106", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/ab39d5", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.quant-gas quant-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The past few years have witnessed the development of a \
comprehensive theory\nto describe integrable systems out of equilibrium, in \
which the Bethe ansatz\nformalism has been tailored to address specific \
problems arising in this\ncontext. While most of the work initially focused \
on the study of prototypical\nmodels such as the well-known Heisenberg chain, \
many theoretical results have\nbeen recently extended to a class of more \
complicated $\\it{nested}$ integrable\nsystems, displaying different species \
of quasiparticles. Still, in the simplest\ncontext of quantum quenches, the \
vast majority of theoretical predictions have\nbeen numerically verified only \
in systems with an elementary Bethe ansatz\ndescription. In this work, we \
fill this gap and present a direct numerical test\nof some results presented \
in the recent literature for nested systems, focusing\nin particular on the \
Lai-Sutherland model. Using time-dependent density matrix\nrenormalization \
group and exact diagonalization methods, we compute the\nspreading of both \
correlation functions and entanglement entropy after a quench\nfrom a simple \
class of product initial states. This allows us to test the\nvalidity of the \
nested version of a conjectured formula, based on the\nquasiparticle picture, \
for the growth of the entanglement entropy, and the\nBethe ansatz predictions \
for the \"light-cone\" velocity of correlation\nfunctions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 21 Jun 2019 16:58:18 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 30 Jul 2019 12:46:54 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2019-09-30", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Modak", "Ranjan", ""}, {
              "Piroli", "Lorenzo", ""}, {"Calabrese", "Pasquale", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
