Jesse van\n  Muiden", "title" -> 
            "A Holographic Kaleidoscope for $\\mathcal{N}=1^*$", "comments" -> 
            "40 pages, six figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2019)185", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study in detail the recently-found family of asymptotically \
AdS$_5\\times\nS^5$ type IIB supergravity solutions dual to the \
$\\mathcal{N}=1^*$ SYM theory\nwith equal masses. The backgrounds exhibit a \
naked singularity and are labelled\nby a dimensionless parameter, $\\lambda$, \
which is interpreted as the ratio of\nthe gaugino condensate and the mass in \
the dual field theory. When\n$|\\lambda|<1$ we show that the naked \
singularity is due to a smeared\ndistribution of polarized $(p,q)$ \
five-branes. For this range of parameters we\nstudy the nature of the \
singularity using probe strings and show that the dual\nline operators \
exhibit screening behavior. These features are in line with the\nphysics \
anticipated in the work of Polchinski-Strassler. For $|\\lambda|=1$ the\n\
naked singularity has qualitatively different behavior which has no clear \
brane\ninterpretation. We show that when $\\lambda=1$ the singularity can be \
excised\nand replaced by a smooth Euclidean supergravity solution with an \
$S^4$\nboundary.\n", 
