 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The topological vertex formalism for 5d \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ gauge theories is not\\nonly a convenient tool to compute \
the instanton partition function of these\\ntheories, but it is also \
accompanied by a nice algebraic structure that reveals\\nvarious kinds of \
nice properties such as dualities and integrability of the\\nunderlying \
theories. The usual refined topological vertex formalism is derived\\nfor \
gauge theories with $A$-type quiver structure (and $A$-type gauge \
groups).\\nIn this article, we propose a construction with a web of vertex \
operators for\\nall $ABCDEFG$-type and affine quivers by introducing several \
new vertices into\\nthe formalism, based on the reproducing of known \
instanton partition functions\\nand qq-characters for these \
theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
