               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Toshifumi Noumi\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Toshifumi Noumi, Toshiaki Takeuchi, Siyi Zhou\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"String Regge trajectory in de Sitter space and \
implications for\\n  inflation\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"6 pages, 5 figures; v2: minor revisions, references \
added; v3:\\n  version published in PRD\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 102, 126012 (2020)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.102.126012\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"KOBE-COSMO-19-12\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the spectrum of semiclassical rotating strings \
in de Sitter space\\nand its consistency. Even though a naive extrapolation \
of the linear Regge\\ntrajectory on flat space implies a violation of the \
Higuchi bound (a unitarity\\nbound on the mass of higher-spin particles in de \
Sitter space), the curved\\nspace effects turn out to modify the trajectory \
to respect the bound.\\nInterestingly, as a consequence of accelerated \
expansion, there exists a\\nmaximum spin for each Regge trajectory, which is \
helpful to make the spectrum\\nconsistent with the Higuchi bound, but at the \
same time, it could be an\\nobstruction to stringy UV completion based on an \
infinite higher-spin tower. By\\npushing further this observation, we \
demonstrate that the vacuum energy $V$\\ninflating the universe has to be \
bounded by the string scale $M_s$ as\\n$V\\\\lesssim M_s^4$, if UV completion \
is achieved with the leading Regge\\ntrajectory of higher spin states up to \
the 4D Planck scale. Its application to\\ninflation in the early universe \
implies an upper bound on the tensor-to-scalar\\nratio, $r\\\\lesssim \
0.01\\\\times(M_s/10^{16} \\\\text{GeV})^{4}$, which is within the\\nscope of \
the near future CMB experiments. We also discuss another possibility\\nthat \
UV completion is achieved by multiple Regge trajectories.\\n\""}]}, {
