 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We introduce and study a surface defect in four \
dimensional gauge theories\\nsupporting nested instantons with respect to the \
parabolic reduction of the\\ngauge group at the defect. This is engineered \
from a D3/D7-branes system on a\\nnon compact Calabi-Yau threefold $X$. For \
$X=T^2\\\\times T^*{\\\\mathcal C}_{g,k}$,\\nthe product of a two torus $T^2$ \
times the cotangent bundle over a Riemann\\nsurface ${\\\\mathcal C}_{g,k}$ \
with marked points, we propose an effective theory\\nin the limit of small \
volume of ${\\\\mathcal C}_{g,k}$ given as a comet shaped\\nquiver gauge \
theory on $T^2$, the tail of the comet being made of a flag quiver\\nfor each \
marked point and the head describing the degrees of freedom due to \
the\\ngenus $g$. Mathematically, we obtain for a single D7-brane conjectural \
explicit\\nformulae for the virtual equivariant elliptic genus of a certain \
bundle over\\nthe moduli space of the nested Hilbert scheme of points on the \
affine plane. A\\nconnection with elliptic cohomology of character varieties \
and an elliptic\\nversion of modified Macdonald polynomials naturally arises.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
