            "  We introduce and study a surface defect in four dimensional \
gauge theories\nsupporting nested instantons with respect to the parabolic \
reduction of the\ngauge group at the defect. This is engineered from a \
D3/D7-branes system on a\nnon compact Calabi-Yau threefold $X$. For \
$X=T^2\\times T^*{\\mathcal C}_{g,k}$,\nthe product of a two torus $T^2$ \
times the cotangent bundle over a Riemann\nsurface ${\\mathcal C}_{g,k}$ with \
marked points, we propose an effective theory\nin the limit of small volume \
