               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"AdS$_7$ Black-Hole Entropy and 5D $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages; v2 field-theory discussion modified, appendix \
added and\\n  typos corrected; v3 published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2020)017\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"QMUL-PH-19-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We generalise the work of 1810.11442 for the case of \
AdS$_7$/CFT$_6$.\\nStarting from the 2-equivalent charge, 3-equivalent \
rotation non-extremal\\nblack-hole solution in 7D gauged supergravity, we \
consider the supersymmetric\\nand then the extremal limit and evaluate the \
associated thermodynamic\\nquantities. Away from extremality, the black-hole \
solution becomes complex. The\\nentropy is then given by the Legendre \
transform of the on-shell action with\\nrespect to two complex chemical \
potentials subject to a constraint. At the\\nconformal boundary we derive the \
dual background and evaluate the corresponding\\npartition function for the \
$A_{N-1}$ 6D (2,0) theory at large $N$ in a\\nCardy-like limit. This is \
carried out via a 5D $\\\\mathcal N=2$ super Yang-Mills\\ncalculation on \
$S^5$. The gravitational on-shell action is found to be exactly\\nreproduced \
by the boundary partition function at large $N$. We argue that \
this\\nagreement puts strong constraints on the form of possible \
higher-derivative\\ncorrections to the 5D gauge theory that is used in the \
$S^5$ evaluation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
