               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1907.02984\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Daniel Medina Rincon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Daniel Medina-Rincon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matching quantum string corrections and circular Wilson \
loops in $AdS_4\\n  \\\\times CP^3$\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"28 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2019)158\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recent progresses in the computation of quantum string \
corrections to\\nholographic Wilson loops are extended to the case of strings \
in $AdS_{4}\\\\times\\nCP^{3}$. For this, the ratio of 1/2-BPS circular and \
1/6-BPS latitude fermionic\\nWilson loops in ABJM is considered at strong \
coupling by studying the\\ncorresponding semiclassical string partition \
functions. Explicit evaluation of\\nfluctuation determinants using \
phaseshifts and diffeomorphism invariant\\nregulators leads to exact matching \
with the recent field theory proposal. Key\\nto this computation is the \
choice of boundary conditions for massless fermions.\\nIn the limit for which \
the latitude Wilson loop has a trivial expectation\\nvalue, the long known \
localization result for the 1/2-BPS fermionic circular\\nWilson loop in ABJM \
is recovered.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
