\\times \\hat{G}$, the\neta-deformation can be generalised to a two-parameter \
integrable deformation\nwith independent $q$-deformations of the two copies. \
We study its\nkappa-symmetry and write down a formula for the Ramond-Ramond \
fluxes. We then\nfocus on $\\hat{G}= PSU(1,1|2)$ and construct two \
supergravity backgrounds for\nthe two-parameter integrable deformation of the \
$AdS_3 \\times S^3 \\times T^4$\nsuperstring, as well as explore their \
limits. We also construct backgrounds\nthat are solutions of the weaker \
generalised supergravity equations of motion\nand compare them to the \
