               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1907.06193\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Lorenzo Bianchi\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Lorenzo Bianchi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marginal deformations and defect anomalies\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"8 pages, v2: derivation on coupling independence for \
superconformal\\n  surface defects added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 100, 126018 (2019)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.100.126018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We deform a defect conformal field theory by an exactly \
marginal bulk\\noperator and we consider the dependence on the marginal \
coupling of flat and\\nspherical defect expectation values. For even \
dimensional spherical defects we\\nfind a logarithmic divergence which can be \
related to a $a$-type defect anomaly\\ncoefficient. This coefficient, for \
defect theories, is not invariant on the\\nconformal manifold and its \
dependence on the coupling is controlled to all\\norders by the one-point \
function of the associated exactly marginal operator.\\nFor odd-dimensional \
defects, the flat and spherical case exhibit different\\nqualitative \
behaviors, generalizing to arbitrary dimensions the line-circle\\nanomaly of \
superconformal Wilson loops. Our results also imply a non-trivial\\ncoupling \
dependence for the recently proposed defect $C$-function. We finally\\napply \
our general result to a few specific examples, including \
superconformal\\nWilson loops and R\\\\'enyi entropy.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
