            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1907.07186\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shu-Heng Shao\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Shota Komatsu, Raghu Mahajan, Shu-Heng Shao\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"An Index for Quantum Integrability\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"24 pages, 2 tables\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SciPost Phys. 7, 065 (2019)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.21468/SciPostPhys.7.5.065\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The existence of higher-spin quantum conserved currents \
in two dimensions\\nguarantees quantum integrability. We revisit the question \
of whether\\nclassically-conserved local higher-spin currents in \
two-dimensional sigma\\nmodels survive quantization. We define an \
integrability index $\\\\mathcal{I}(J)$\\nfor each spin $J$, with the \
property that $\\\\mathcal{I}(J)$ is a lower bound on\\nthe number of quantum \
conserved currents of spin $J$. In particular, a positive\\nvalue for the \
index establishes the existence of quantum conserved currents.\\nFor a \
general coset model, with or without extra discrete symmetries, we \
derive\\nan explicit formula for a generating function that encodes the \
indices for all\\nspins. We apply our techniques to the \
$\\\\mathbb{CP}^{N-1}$ model, the $O(N)$\\nmodel, and the flag sigma model \
$\\\\frac{U(N)}{U(1)^{N}}$. For the $O(N)$ model,\\nwe establish the \
existence of a spin-6 quantum conserved current, in addition\\nto the \
well-known spin-4 current. The indices for the $\\\\mathbb{CP}^{N-1}$ \
model\\nfor $N>2$ are all non-positive, consistent with the fact that these \
models are\\nnot integrable. The indices for the flag sigma model \
$\\\\frac{U(N)}{U(1)^{N}}$\\nfor $N>2$ are all negative. Thus, it is unlikely \
that the flag sigma models are\\nintegrable.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 16 Jul 2019 18:00:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2019-11-27\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Komatsu\"", ",", "\"Shota\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Mahajan\"", ",", "\"Raghu\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Shao\"", ",", "\"Shu-Heng\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
