               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the one-loop effective action of string \
configurations embedded in\\n$AdS_4\\\\times\\\\mathbb{CP}^3$ which are dual \
to $\\\\frac{1}{6}$-BPS latitude Wilson\\nLoops in the ABJM theory. To avoid \
ambiguities in the string path integral we\\nsubtract the \
$\\\\frac{1}{2}$-BPS case. The one-loop determinants are computed \
by\\nFourier-decomposing the two dimensional operators and then using \
the\\nGel'fand-Yaglom method. We comment on various aspects related to \
the\\nregularization procedure, showing the cancellation of a hierarchy \
of\\ndivergences. After taking into account an IR anomaly from a change in \
topology,\\nwe find a precise agreement with the field theory result known \
from\\nsupersymmetric localization.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
