            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study half-BPS line operators in 3d N=4 gauge theories, \
focusing in\nparticular on the algebras of local operators at their \
junctions. It is known\nthat there are two basic types of such line \
operators, distinguished by the\nSUSY subalgebras that they preserve; the two \
types can roughly be called\n\"Wilson lines\" and \"vortex lines\", and are \
exchanged under 3d mirror symmetry.\nWe describe a large class of vortex \
lines that can be characterized by basic\nalgebraic data, and propose a \
mathematical scheme to compute the algebras of\nlocal operators at their \
junctions --- including monopole operators --- in\nterms of this data. The \
computation generalizes mathematical and physical\ndefinitions/analyses of \
the bulk Coulomb-branch chiral ring. We fully classify\nthe junctions of \
half-BPS Wilson lines and of half-BPS vortex lines in abelian\ngauge theories \
with sufficient matter. We also test our computational scheme in\na \
non-abelian quiver gauge theory, using a 3d-mirror-map of line operators from\
\nwork of Assel and Gomis.\n", 
