            "  We study two-dimensional integrable field theories from the \
viewpoint of the\nfour-dimensional Chern-Simons-type gauge theory introduced \
recently. The\nintegrable field theories are realized as effective theories \
for the\nfour-dimensional theory coupled with two-dimensional surface \
defects, and we\ncan systematically compute their Lagrangians and the Lax \
operators satisfying\nthe zero-curvature condition. Our construction includes \
many known integrable\nfield theories, such as Gross-Neveu models, principal \
chiral models with\nWess-Zumino terms and symmetric-space coset sigma models. \
Moreover we obtain\nvarious generalization these models in a number of \
different directions, such\nas trigonometric/elliptic deformations, \
multi-defect generalizations and models\nassociated with higher-genus \
spectral curves, many of which seem to be new.\n", 
