                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss compactifications of rank $Q$ E-string \
theory on a torus with\\nfluxes for abelian subgroups of the $E_8$ global \
symmetry of the $6d$ SCFT. We\\nargue that the theories corresponding to such \
tori are built from a simple\\nmodel we denote as $E[USp(2Q)]$. This model \
has a variety of non trivial\\nproperties. In particular the global symmetry \
is $USp(2Q)\\\\times USp(2Q)\\\\times\\nU(1)^2$ with one of the two $USp(2Q)$ \
symmetries emerging in the IR as an\\nenhancement of an $SU(2)^Q$ symmetry of \
the UV Lagrangian. The $E[USp(2Q)]$\\nmodel after dimensional reduction to \
$3d$ and a subsequent Coulomb branch flow\\nis closely related to the \
familiar $3d$ $T[SU(Q)]$ theory, the model residing\\non an S-duality domain \
wall of $4d$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ $SU(Q)$ SYM. Gluing the\\n$E[USp(2Q)]$ models \
by gauging the $USp(2Q)$ symmetries with proper admixtures\\nof chiral \
superfields gives rise to systematic constructions of many examples\\nof $4d$ \
theories with emergent IR symmetries. We support our claims by \
various\\nchecks involving computations of anomalies and supersymmetric \
partition\\nfunctions. Many of the needed identities satisfied by the \
supersymmetric\\nindices follow directly from recent mathematical results \
obtained by E. Rains.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
