                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this review we discuss recent advances in the \
computation of one-point\\nfunctions in defect conformal field theories with \
holographic duals. We briefly\\nreview the appearance of integrable spin \
chains in N=4 super Yang--Mills theory\\nand reformulate the problem of \
computing one-point functions to determining\\noverlaps between Bethe states \
and a Matrix Product State. We will then\\ndemonstrate how these overlaps can \
be computed by determinant formulas. This\\nwork is based on lectures given \
at the Young Researchers Integrability School\\nand Workshop 2018. To appear \
in a special issue of J. Phys. A.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
