               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gaoli Chen, Robert de Mello Koch, Minkyoo Kim and Hendrik \
J.R. Van Zyl\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Absorption of closed strings by giant gravitons\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"50 pages, 4 figures. v2: refs added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2019)133\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A new approach to the computation of correlation \
functions involving two\\ndeterminant operators as well as one non-protected \
single trace operator has\\nrecently been developed by Jiang, Komatsu and \
Vescovi. This correlation\\nfunction provides the holographic description of \
the absorption of a closed\\nstring by a giant graviton. The analysis has a \
natural interpretation in the\\nframework of group representation theory, \
which admits a generalization to\\ngeneral Schur polynomials and restricted \
Schur polynomials. This generalizes\\nthe holographic description to any \
giant or dual giant gravitons which carry\\nmore than one angular momentum on \
the sphere. For a restricted Schur polynomial\\nlabeled by a column with $N$ \
boxes (dual to a maximal giant graviton) we find\\nevidence in favor of \
integrability.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
