                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We systematically study the interesting relations \
between the quantum\\nelliptic Calogero-Moser system (eCM) and its \
generalization, and their\\ncorresponding supersymmetric gauge theories. In \
particular, we construct the\\nsuitable characteristic polynomial for the eCM \
system by considering certain\\norbifolded instanton partition function of \
the corresponding gauge theory. This\\nis equivalent to the introduction of \
certain co-dimension two defects. We next\\ngeneralize our construction to \
the folded instanton partition function obtained\\nthrough the so-called \
\\\"gauge origami\\\" construction and precisely obtain the\\ncorresponding \
characteristic polynomial for the doubled version, named the\\nelliptic \
double Calogero-Moser (edCM) system.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
