 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We continue the effort of defining and evaluating the \
quantum entropy\\nfunction for supersymmetric black holes in 4d ${\\\\cal N} \
= 2$ gauged\\nsupergravity, initiated in [1803.05920]. The emphasis here is \
on the missing\\nsteps in the previous localization analysis, mainly dealing \
with one-loop\\ndeterminants for abelian vector multiplets and \
hypermultiplets on the\\nnon-compact space $\\\\mathbb{H}_2 \\\\times \
\\\\Sigma_{\\\\rm g}$ with particular boundary\\nconditions. We use several \
different techniques to arrive at consistent\\nresults, which have a most \
direct bearing on the logarithmic correction terms\\nto the \
Bekenstein-Hawking entropy of said black holes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
