               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give a pedagogical introduction to the study of \
supersymmetric partition\\nfunctions of 3D $\\\\mathcal{N}{=}2$ \
supersymmetric Chern-Simons-matter theories\\n(with an $R$-symmetry) on \
half-BPS closed three-manifolds---including $S^3$,\\n$S^2 \\\\times S^1$, and \
any Seifert three-manifold. Three-dimensional gauge\\ntheories can flow to \
non-trivial fixed points in the infrared. In the presence\\nof 3D \
$\\\\mathcal{N}{=}2$ supersymmetry, many exact results are known about \
the\\nstrongly-coupled infrared, due in good part to powerful \
localization\\ntechniques. We review some of these techniques and emphasize \
some more recent\\ndevelopments, which provide a simple and comprehensive \
formalism for the exact\\ncomputation of half-BPS observables on closed \
three-manifolds (partition\\nfunctions and correlation functions of line \
operators). Along the way, we also\\nreview simple examples of 3D infrared \
dualities. The computation of\\nsupersymmetric partition functions provides \
exceedingly precise tests of these\\ndualities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
