               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1908.09299\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alessandro Sfondrini\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Alessandro Sfondrini, Stijn J. van Tongeren\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"$T\\\\bar{T}$ deformations as TsT transformations\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages, 1 figure; v2: further examples (section 5) and \
discussion\\n  of JTbar deformations (appendix B) added, references \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 101, 066022 (2020)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.101.066022\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The relationship between $T\\\\bar{T}$ deformations and \
the uniform light-cone\\ngauge, first noted in arXiv:1804.01998, provides a \
powerful generating\\ntechnique for deformed models. We recall this \
construction, distinguishing\\nbetween changes of the gauge frame, which do \
not affect the theory, and genuine\\ndeformations. We investigate the \
geometric interpretation of the latter and\\nargue that they affect the \
global features of the geometry before gauge fixing.\\nExploiting a formal \
relation between uniform light-cone gauge and static gauge\\nin a T-dual \
frame, we interpret such a change as a TsT transformation involving\\nthe two \
light-cone coordinates. In the static-gauge picture, the $T\\\\bar{T}$ \
CDD\\nfactor then has a natural interpretation as a Drinfel'd-Reshetikhin \
twist of\\nthe worldsheet S matrix. To illustrate these ideas, we find the \
geometries\\nyielding a $T\\\\bar{T}$ deformation of the worldsheet S matrix \
of pp-wave and\\nLin-Lunin-Maldacena backgrounds.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
