         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1908.09299", "submitter" -> "Alessandro Sfondrini", 
            "authors" -> "Alessandro Sfondrini, Stijn J. van Tongeren", 
            "title" -> "$T\\bar{T}$ deformations as TsT transformations", 
            "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, 1 figure; v2: further examples (section 5) and \
discussion\n  of JTbar deformations (appendix B) added, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. D 101, 066022 (2020)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.101.066022", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The relationship between $T\\bar{T}$ deformations and the \
uniform light-cone\ngauge, first noted in arXiv:1804.01998, provides a \
powerful generating\ntechnique for deformed models. We recall this \
construction, distinguishing\nbetween changes of the gauge frame, which do \
not affect the theory, and genuine\ndeformations. We investigate the \
geometric interpretation of the latter and\nargue that they affect the global \
features of the geometry before gauge fixing.\nExploiting a formal relation \
between uniform light-cone gauge and static gauge\nin a T-dual frame, we \
interpret such a change as a TsT transformation involving\nthe two light-cone \
coordinates. In the static-gauge picture, the $T\\bar{T}$ CDD\nfactor then \
has a natural interpretation as a Drinfel'd-Reshetikhin twist of\nthe \
worldsheet S matrix. To illustrate these ideas, we find the geometries\n\
yielding a $T\\bar{T}$ deformation of the worldsheet S matrix of pp-wave and\n\
Lin-Lunin-Maldacena backgrounds.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 25 Aug 2019 10:49:11 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 30 Sep 2019 18:00:16 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-04-01", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Sfondrini", "Alessandro", ""}, {
              "van Tongeren", "Stijn J.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{13.382451895220715`, -6.72859223486406}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1908.11582\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wolfgang M\\\\\\\"uck\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wolfgang M\\\\\\\"uck\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Combinatorics of Wilson loops in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM \
theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"14 pages, v.2: added references, v.3: published \
version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP11(2019)096\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2019)096\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The theory of Wilson loops for gauge theories with \
unitary gauge groups is\\nformulated in the language of symmetric functions. \
The main objects in this\\ntheory are two generating functions, which are \
related to each other by the\\ninvolution that exchanges an irreducible \
representation with its conjugate.\\nBoth of them contain all information \
about the Wilson loops in arbitrary\\nrepresentations as well as the \
correlators of multiply-wound Wilson loops. This\\ngeneral framework is \
combined with the results of the Gaussian matrix model,\\nwhich calculates \
the expectation values of $1/2$-BPS circular Wilson loops \
in\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ Super-Yang-Mills theory. General, explicit, formulas \
for the\\nconnected correlators of multiply-wound Wilson loops in terms of \
the traces of\\nsymmetrized matrix products are obtained, as well as their \
inverses. It is\\nshown that the generating functions for Wilson loops in \
mutually conjugate\\nrepresentations are related by a duality relation \
whenever they can be\\ncalculated by a Hermitian matrix model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
