            "  The theory of Wilson loops for gauge theories with unitary \
gauge groups is\nformulated in the language of symmetric functions. The main \
objects in this\ntheory are two generating functions, which are related to \
each other by the\ninvolution that exchanges an irreducible representation \
with its conjugate.\nBoth of them contain all information about the Wilson \
loops in arbitrary\nrepresentations as well as the correlators of \
multiply-wound Wilson loops. This\ngeneral framework is combined with the \
results of the Gaussian matrix model,\nwhich calculates the expectation \
values of $1/2$-BPS circular Wilson loops in\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
Super-Yang-Mills theory. General, explicit, formulas for the\nconnected \
correlators of multiply-wound Wilson loops in terms of the traces of\n\
symmetrized matrix products are obtained, as well as their inverses. It is\n\
shown that the generating functions for Wilson loops in mutually conjugate\n\
representations are related by a duality relation whenever they can be\n\
calculated by a Hermitian matrix model.\n", 
