               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1909.05271\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Guido D'Amico\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Guido D'Amico, J\\\\'er\\\\^ome Gleyzes, Nickolas Kokron, \
Dida Markovic,\\n  Leonardo Senatore, Pierre Zhang, Florian Beutler, \
H\\\\'ector Gil-Mar\\\\'in\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Cosmological Analysis of the SDSS/BOSS data from the \
Effective Field\\n  Theory of Large-Scale Structure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"78 pages, 27 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1475-7516/2020/05/005\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"astro-ph.CO gr-qc hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Effective Field Theory of Large-Scale Structure \
(EFTofLSS) is a formalism\\nthat allows us to predict the clustering of \
Cosmological Large-Scale Structure\\nin the mildly non-linear regime in an \
accurate and reliable way. After\\nvalidating our technique against several \
sets of numerical simulations, we\\nperform the analysis for the cosmological \
parameters of the DR12 BOSS data. We\\nassume $\\\\Lambda$CDM, a fixed value \
of the baryon/dark-matter ratio,\\n$\\\\Omega_b/\\\\Omega_c$, and of the tilt \
of the primordial power spectrum, $n_s$,\\nand no significant input from \
numerical simulations. By using the one-loop\\npower spectrum multipoles, we \
measure the primordial amplitude of the power\\nspectrum, $A_s$, the \
abundance of matter, $\\\\Omega_m$, and the Hubble parameter,\\n$H_0$, to \
about $13\\\\%$, $3.2\\\\%$ and $3.2\\\\%$ respectively, \
obtaining\\n$\\\\ln(10^{10}As)=2.72\\\\pm 0.13$, $\\\\Omega_m=0.309\\\\pm \
0.010$, $H_0=68.5\\\\pm 2.2$\\nkm/(s Mpc) at 68\\\\% confidence level. If we \
then add a CMB prior on the sound\\nhorizon, the error bar on $H_0$ is \
reduced to $1.6\\\\%$. These results are a\\nsubstantial qualitative and \
quantitative improvement with respect to former\\nanalyses, and suggest that \
the EFTofLSS is a powerful instrument to extract\\ncosmological information \
from Large-Scale Structure.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 11 Sep 2019 18:00:28 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
