            "  The Effective Field Theory of Large-Scale Structure (EFTofLSS) \
is a formalism\nthat allows us to predict the clustering of Cosmological \
Large-Scale Structure\nin the mildly non-linear regime in an accurate and \
reliable way. After\nvalidating our technique against several sets of \
numerical simulations, we\nperform the analysis for the cosmological \
parameters of the DR12 BOSS data. We\nassume $\\Lambda$CDM, a fixed value of \
the baryon/dark-matter ratio,\n$\\Omega_b/\\Omega_c$, and of the tilt of the \
primordial power spectrum, $n_s$,\nand no significant input from numerical \
simulations. By using the one-loop\npower spectrum multipoles, we measure the \
primordial amplitude of the power\nspectrum, $A_s$, the abundance of matter, \
$\\Omega_m$, and the Hubble parameter,\n$H_0$, to about $13\\%$, $3.2\\%$ and \
$3.2\\%$ respectively, obtaining\n$\\ln(10^{10}As)=2.72\\pm 0.13$, \
$\\Omega_m=0.309\\pm 0.010$, $H_0=68.5\\pm 2.2$\nkm/(s Mpc) at 68\\% \
confidence level. If we then add a CMB prior on the sound\nhorizon, the error \
bar on $H_0$ is reduced to $1.6\\%$. These results are a\nsubstantial \
qualitative and quantitative improvement with respect to former\nanalyses, \
and suggest that the EFTofLSS is a powerful instrument to extract\n\
cosmological information from Large-Scale Structure.\n", 
