                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the ideas from the BPS/CFT correspondence, we \
give an explicit\\nrecursive formula for computing supersymmetric Wilson loop \
averages in 3d\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ Yang-Mills-Chern-Simons $U(N)$ theory on \
the squashed sphere\\n$S^3_b$ with one adjoint chiral and two antichiral \
fundamental multiplets, for\\nspecific values of Chern-Simons level \
$\\\\kappa_2$ and Fayet-Illiopoulos\\nparameter $\\\\kappa_1$. For these \
values of $\\\\kappa_1$ and $\\\\kappa_2$ the north\\nand south pole turn out \
to be completely independent, and therefore Wilson loop\\naverages factorize \
into answers for the two constituent $D^2 \\\\times S^1$\\ntheories. In \
particular, our formula provides results for the theory on the\\nround sphere \
when the squashing is removed.\\n\""}]}, {
