 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently a detailed correspondence was established \
between, on one side, four\\nand five-dimensional large-N supersymmetric \
gauge theories with $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$\\nsupersymmetry and adjoint matter, \
and, on the other side, integrable\\n1+1-dimensional quantum hydrodynamics. \
Under this correspondence the phenomenon\\nof dimensional transmutation, \
familiar in asymptotically free QFTs, gets mapped\\nto the transition from \
the elliptic Calogero-Moser many-body system to the\\nclosed Toda chain. In \
this paper we attempt to formulate the hydrodynamical\\ncounterpart of the \
dimensional transmutation phenomenon inspired by the\\nidentification of the \
periodic Intermediate Long Wave (ILW) equation as the\\nhydrodynamical limit \
of the elliptic Calogero-Moser/Ruijsenaars-Schneider\\nsystem. We also \
conjecture that the chiral flow in the vortex fluid provides\\nthe proper \
framework for the microscopic description of such dimensional\\ntransmutation \
in the 1+1d hydrodynamics. We provide a geometric description of\\nthis \
phenomenon in terms of the ADHM moduli space.\\n\""}]}, {
