           "id" -> "1910.02606", "submitter" -> "Peter Koroteev", "authors" -> 
            "Alexander Gorsky, Olesya Koroteeva, Peter Koroteev, Arkady \
Vainshtein", "title" -> 
            "On Dimensional Transmutation in 1+1D Quantum Hydrodynamics", 
            "comments" -> "32 pages, 2 figures, typos corrected", 
            "journal-ref" -> 
            "Journal of Mathematical Physics 61, 082302 (2020)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1063/1.5131471", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.str-el math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently a detailed correspondence was established between, on \
one side, four\nand five-dimensional large-N supersymmetric gauge theories \
with $\\mathcal{N}=2$\nsupersymmetry and adjoint matter, and, on the other \
side, integrable\n1+1-dimensional quantum hydrodynamics. Under this \
correspondence the phenomenon\nof dimensional transmutation, familiar in \
asymptotically free QFTs, gets mapped\nto the transition from the elliptic \
Calogero-Moser many-body system to the\nclosed Toda chain. In this paper we \
attempt to formulate the hydrodynamical\ncounterpart of the dimensional \
transmutation phenomenon inspired by the\nidentification of the periodic \
Intermediate Long Wave (ILW) equation as the\nhydrodynamical limit of the \
elliptic Calogero-Moser/Ruijsenaars-Schneider\nsystem. We also conjecture \
that the chiral flow in the vortex fluid provides\nthe proper framework for \
the microscopic description of such dimensional\ntransmutation in the 1+1d \
hydrodynamics. We provide a geometric description of\nthis phenomenon in \
terms of the ADHM moduli space.\n", 
