Villaescusa-Navarro,\\n  Alexandre Barreira\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Baryonic effects on the matter bispectrum\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"29 pages, 24 figures. v2: MNRAS published version, with \
references\\n  and clarifications added (conclusions unchanged). See Fig. 13 \
for a summary\\n  of the main results. Simulation measurements are available \
at\\n  https://github.com/sjforeman/hydro_bispectrum , and bispectrum \
measurement\\n  code is available at \
https://github.com/sjforeman/bskit\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1093/mnras/staa2523\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"astro-ph.CO astro-ph.GA\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The large-scale clustering of matter is impacted by \
baryonic physics,\\nparticularly AGN feedback. Modelling or mitigating this \
impact will be\\nessential for making full use of upcoming measurements of \
cosmic shear and\\nother large-scale structure probes. We study baryonic \
effects on the matter\\nbispectrum, using measurements from a selection of \
state-of-the-art\\nhydrodynamical simulations: IllustrisTNG, Illustris, \
EAGLE, and BAHAMAS. We\\nidentify a low-redshift enhancement of the \
bispectrum, peaking at $k\\\\sim\\n3h\\\\,{\\\\rm Mpc}^{-1}$, that is present \
in several simulations, and discuss how it\\ncan be associated to the \
evolving nature of AGN feedback at late times. This\\nenhancement does not \
appear in the matter power spectrum, and therefore\\nrepresents a new source \
of degeneracy breaking between two- and three-point\\nstatistics. In \
addition, we provide physical interpretations for other aspects\\nof these \
measurements, and make initial comparisons to predictions from\\nperturbation \
theory, empirical fitting formulas, and the response function\\nformalism. We \
publicly release our measurements (including estimates of their\\nuncertainty \
due to sample variance) and bispectrum measurement code as\\nresources for \
the community.\\n\""}]}, {
