                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In conformal $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ Super Yang-Mills \
theory, the energy emitted by\\nan accelerated heavy particle is computed by \
the one-point function of the\\nstress tensor operator in the presence of a \
Wilson line. In this paper, we\\nconsider the theory on the ellipsoid and we \
prove a conjectured relation\\nbetween the stress tensor one-point function \
and the first order expansion of\\nthe Wilson loop expectation value in the \
squashing parameter. To do this, we\\nanalyze the behavior of the Wilson loop \
for a small deformation of the\\nbackground geometry and, at first order in \
the deformation, we fix the\\nkinematics using defect CFT constraints. In the \
final part of the paper, we\\nanalyze the consequences of our results for the \
weak coupling perturbative\\nexpansion. In particular, comparing the weakly \
coupled matrix model with the\\nordinary Feynman diagram expansion, we find a \
natural transcendentality driven\\norganization for the latter.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
