            "  In conformal $\\mathcal{N}=2$ Super Yang-Mills theory, the \
energy emitted by\nan accelerated heavy particle is computed by the one-point \
function of the\nstress tensor operator in the presence of a Wilson line. In \
this paper, we\nconsider the theory on the ellipsoid and we prove a \
conjectured relation\nbetween the stress tensor one-point function and the \
first order expansion of\nthe Wilson loop expectation value in the squashing \
parameter. To do this, we\nanalyze the behavior of the Wilson loop for a \
small deformation of the\nbackground geometry and, at first order in the \
