            "  Using supersymmetric localization we compute the free energy \
and BPS Wilson\nloop vacuum expectation values for planar maximally \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills\ntheory on $S^d$ in the strong coupling limit for \
$2\\leq d<6$. The same\ncalculation can also be performed in supergravity \
using the recently found\nspherical brane solutions. We find excellent \
agreement between the two sets of\nresults. This constitutes a non-trivial \
precision test of holography in a\nnon-conformal setting. The free energy of \
maximal SYM on $S^6$ diverges in the\nstrong coupling limit which might \
signify the onset of little string theory. We\nshow how this divergence can \
be regularized both in QFT and in supergravity. We\nalso consider $d=7$ with \
a small negative 't Hooft coupling and show that the\nfree energy and Wilson \
loop vacuum expectation value agree with the results\nfrom supergravity after \
addressing some subtleties.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
