 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate classical integrability on two recently \
discovered classes of\\nbackgrounds in massive IIA supergravity. These vacua \
are of the \
form\\nAdS$_3\\\\times\\\\,$S$^2\\\\times\\\\mathbb{R}\\\\times\\\\,$CY$_2$, \
they preserve small\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=(0,4)$ supersymmetry and are associated \
with D8$-$D6$-$D4$-$D2\\nHanany-Witten brane set-ups. We choose an \
appropriate string embedding and use\\ndifferential Galois theory on its \
associated Hamiltonian system, intending to\\nproduce the conditions under \
which Liouvillian solutions may occur. By\\nconstraining the parameters of \
the system according to the consistency of the\\nassociate brane set-ups we \
prove that no such conditions exist, yielding the\\ncomplete \
non-integrability of these vacua. That is, up to the trivial cases\\nwhere \
the background reduces to the Abelian and non-Abelian T-dual \
of\\nAdS$_3\\\\times\\\\,$S$^3\\\\times\\\\,$T$^4$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
