               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Rafael Hernandez\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Rafael Hernandez, Juan Miguel Nieto, Roberto Ruiz\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum corrections to minimal surfaces with mixed \
three-form flux\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages. Latex. v2: Published version, acknowledgement \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 101, 026019 (2020)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.101.026019\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We obtain the ratio of semiclassical partition \
functions for the extension\\nunder mixed flux of the minimal surfaces \
subtending a circumference and a line\\nin Euclidean $AdS_{3}\\\\times \
S^{3}\\\\times T^{4}$. We reduce the problem to the\\ncomputation of a set of \
functional determinants. If the Ramond-Ramond flux does\\nnot vanish, we find \
that the contribution of the $B$-field is comprised in the\\nconformal \
anomaly. In this case, we successively apply the Gel'fand-Yaglom\\nmethod and \
the Abel-Plana formula to the flat-measure determinants. To cancel\\nthe \
resultant infrared divergences, we shift the regularization of the sum \
over\\nhalf-integers depending on whether it corresponds to massive or \
massless\\nfermionic modes. We show that the result is compatible with the \
zeta-function\\nregularization approach. In the limit of pure \
Neveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz flux\\nwe argue that the computation trivializes. \
We extend the reasoning to other\\nsurfaces with the same behavior in this \
regime.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
