            "Quantum corrections to minimal surfaces with mixed three-form \
flux", "comments" -> 
            "32 pages. Latex. v2: Published version, acknowledgement added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. D 101, 026019 (2020)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.101.026019", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We obtain the ratio of semiclassical partition functions for \
the extension\nunder mixed flux of the minimal surfaces subtending a \
circumference and a line\nin Euclidean $AdS_{3}\\times S^{3}\\times T^{4}$. \
We reduce the problem to the\ncomputation of a set of functional \
determinants. If the Ramond-Ramond flux does\nnot vanish, we find that the \
contribution of the $B$-field is comprised in the\nconformal anomaly. In this \
case, we successively apply the Gel'fand-Yaglom\nmethod and the Abel-Plana \
formula to the flat-measure determinants. To cancel\nthe resultant infrared \
divergences, we shift the regularization of the sum over\nhalf-integers \
depending on whether it corresponds to massive or massless\nfermionic modes. \
We show that the result is compatible with the zeta-function\nregularization \
approach. In the limit of pure Neveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz flux\nwe argue \
that the computation trivializes. We extend the reasoning to other\nsurfaces \
with the same behavior in this regime.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
