            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1911.06590\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alessandro Torrielli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Juan Miguel Nieto and Alessandro Torrielli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Norms and scalar products for AdS_3\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"32 pages, no figures; added reference\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DMUS-MP-19-10\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute scalar products and norms of Bethe vectors \
in the massless sector\\nof AdS_3 integrable superstring theories, by \
exploiting the general difference\\nform of the S-matrix of massless \
excitations in the pure Ramond-Ramond case,\\nand the difference form valid \
only in the BMN limit in the mixed-flux case. We\\nobtain determinant-like \
formulas for the scalar products, generalising a\\nprocedure developed in \
previous literature for standard R-matrices to the\\npresent non-conventional \
situation. We verify our expressions against explicit\\ncalculations using \
Bethe vectors for chains of small length, and perform some\\ncomputer tests \
of the exact formulas as far as numerical accuracy sustains us.\\nThis should \
be the first step towards the derivation of integrable form-factors\\nand \
correlation functions for the AdS_3 S-matrix theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
