            "  We compute scalar products and norms of Bethe vectors in the \
massless sector\nof AdS_3 integrable superstring theories, by exploiting the \
general difference\nform of the S-matrix of massless excitations in the pure \
Ramond-Ramond case,\nand the difference form valid only in the BMN limit in \
the mixed-flux case. We\nobtain determinant-like formulas for the scalar \
products, generalising a\nprocedure developed in previous literature for \
standard R-matrices to the\npresent non-conventional situation. We verify our \
expressions against explicit\ncalculations using Bethe vectors for chains of \
small length, and perform some\ncomputer tests of the exact formulas as far \
as numerical accuracy sustains us.\nThis should be the first step towards the \
derivation of integrable form-factors\nand correlation functions for the \
AdS_3 S-matrix theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
