               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Evgenii Ievlev\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A. Gorsky, E. Ievlev and A. Yung\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Dynamics of non-Abelian strings in the theory \
interpolating from\\n  ${\\\\mathcal N}=2$ to ${\\\\mathcal N}=1$ \
supersymmetric QCD\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"49 pages, 25 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 101, 014013 (2020)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.101.014013\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the dynamics of non-Abelian vortex strings \
supported in ${\\\\mathcal\\nN}=2$ supersymmetric QCD with the U$(N)$ gauge \
group and $N_f=N$ quark flavors\\ndeformed by the mass $\\\\mu$ of the \
adjoint matter. In the limit of large $\\\\mu$\\nthe bulk four-dimensional \
theory flows to ${\\\\mathcal N}=1$ supersymmetric QCD.\\nThe dynamics of \
orientational zero modes of the non-Abelian string is described\\nby the \
world sheet CP$(N-1)$ model. At $\\\\mu=0$ this model has ${\\\\mathcal \
N}=\\n\\\\left(2,2\\\\right) $ supersymmetry while at large $\\\\mu$ it flows \
to the\\nnon-supersymmetric CP$(N-1)$ model. We solve the world sheet model \
in the large\\n$N$ approximation and find a rich phase structure with respect \
to the\\ndeformation parameter $\\\\mu$ and quark mass differences. The \
phases include two\\nstrong coupling phases and two Higgs phases. In \
particular, the Higgs phase at\\nsmall $\\\\mu$ supports CP$(N-1)$ model \
kinks representing confined monopoles of\\nthe bulk QCD, while in the large-$\
\\\\mu$ Higgs phase monopoles disappear.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
