           "id" -> "1911.08328", "submitter" -> "Evgenii Ievlev", "authors" -> 
            "A. Gorsky, E. Ievlev and A. Yung", "title" -> 
            "Dynamics of non-Abelian strings in the theory interpolating from\
\n  ${\\mathcal N}=2$ to ${\\mathcal N}=1$ supersymmetric QCD", "comments" -> 
            "49 pages, 25 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys. Rev. D 101, 014013 (2020)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.101.014013", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the dynamics of non-Abelian vortex strings supported \
in ${\\mathcal\nN}=2$ supersymmetric QCD with the U$(N)$ gauge group and \
$N_f=N$ quark flavors\ndeformed by the mass $\\mu$ of the adjoint matter. In \
the limit of large $\\mu$\nthe bulk four-dimensional theory flows to \
${\\mathcal N}=1$ supersymmetric QCD.\nThe dynamics of orientational zero \
modes of the non-Abelian string is described\nby the world sheet CP$(N-1)$ \
model. At $\\mu=0$ this model has ${\\mathcal N}=\n\\left(2,2\\right) $ \
supersymmetry while at large $\\mu$ it flows to the\nnon-supersymmetric \
CP$(N-1)$ model. We solve the world sheet model in the large\n$N$ \
approximation and find a rich phase structure with respect to the\n\
deformation parameter $\\mu$ and quark mass differences. The phases include \
two\nstrong coupling phases and two Higgs phases. In particular, the Higgs \
phase at\nsmall $\\mu$ supports CP$(N-1)$ model kinks representing confined \
monopoles of\nthe bulk QCD, while in the large-$\\mu$ Higgs phase monopoles \
disappear.\n", 
