               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we propose a general framework to study \
the quantum geometry of\\n$\\\\sigma$-models when they are effectively \
localized to small quantum\\nfluctuations around constant maps. Such \
effective theories have surprising\\nexact descriptions at all loops in terms \
of target geometry and can be\\nrigorously formulated. We illustrate how to \
turn the physics idea of exact\\nsemi-classical approximation into a \
geometric set-up in this framework, using\\nGauss-Manin connection. As an \
application, we carry out this program in details\\nby the example of \
topological quantum mechanics, and explain how to implement\\nthe idea of \
exact semi-classical approximation into a proof of the algebraic\\nindex \
theorem. The proof resembles much of the physics derivation \
of\\nAtiyah-Singer index theorem and clarifies the geometric face of many \
other\\nmathematical constructions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
