            "  In this paper we propose a general framework to study the \
quantum geometry of\n$\\sigma$-models when they are effectively localized to \
small quantum\nfluctuations around constant maps. Such effective theories \
have surprising\nexact descriptions at all loops in terms of target geometry \
and can be\nrigorously formulated. We illustrate how to turn the physics idea \
of exact\nsemi-classical approximation into a geometric set-up in this \
framework, using\nGauss-Manin connection. As an application, we carry out \
