, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We initiate a systematic, non-perturbative study of \
the large-$N$ expansion\\nin the two-dimensional $\\\\text{SU}(N)\\\\times \\\
\\text{SU}(N)$ Principal Chiral Model\\n(PCM). Starting with the known \
infinite-$N$ solution for the ground state at\\nfixed chemical potential \
\\\\cite{Fateev:1994dp,Fateev:1994ai}, we devise an\\niterative procedure to \
solve the Bethe ansatz equations order by order in\\n$1/N$. The first few \
orders, which we explicitly compute, reveal a systematic\\nenhancement \
pattern at strong coupling calling for the near-threshold\\nresummation of \
the large-$N$ expansion. The resulting double-scaling limit\\nbears striking \
similarities to the $c=1$ non-critical string theory and\\nsuggests that the \
double-scaled PCM is dual to a non-critical string with \
a\\n$(2+1)$-dimensional target space where an additional dimension \
emerges\\ndynamically from the $\\\\text{SU}(N)$ Dynkin diagram.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
