            "  We give an introduction to the Quantum Spectral Curve in \
AdS/CFT. This is an\nintegrability-based framework which provides the exact \
spectrum of planar N = 4\nsuper Yang-Mills theory (and of the dual string \
model) in terms of a solution\nof a Riemann-Hilbert problem for a finite set \
of functions. We review the\nunderlying QQ relations starting from simple \
spin chain examples, and describe\nthe special features arising for AdS/CFT. \
We also discuss the recently found\nlinks between the Quantum Spectral Curve \
and the computation of correlation\nfunctions. To appear in a special issue \
of J Phys A based on lectures given at\nthe Young Researchers Integrability \
School and Workshop 2018.\n", 
