                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  These notes provide an introduction toward Wilson loops \
in N=4 supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills theory with a focus toward their \
integrability properties. In\\naddition to a brief discussion of exact \
results for the circular Wilson loop\\nand the cusp anomalous dimension, the \
notes focus on non-local symmetries,\\nutilizing the integrability of the \
minimal surface problem that appears at\\nstrong coupling. This work is based \
on lectures given at the Young Researchers\\nIntegrability School and \
Workshop 2018. To appear in a special issue of J.\\nPhys. A.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
