 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Integrable deformations of type IIB superstring theory \
on\\n$\\\\mathrm{AdS}_5\\\\times S^5$ have played an important role over the \
last years.\\nThe Yang-Baxter deformation is a systematic way of generating \
such integrable\\ndeformations. Since its introduction, this topic has seen \
important conceptual\\nprogress and has among others led to the intriguing \
discovery generalized\\nsupergravity, a new low-energy effective theory. This \
review endeavors to not\\nonly introduce the historical development of the \
Yang-Baxter deformation, but\\nalso its relation to generalized supergravity, \
non-geometric backgrounds,\\nnon-abelian T-duality and preserved Killing \
spinors. We supplement the general\\ntreatment with a wealth of explicit \
examples.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
