Valentin Reys,\\n  Timm Wrase\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Dyonic black hole degeneracies in $\\\\mathcal{N} = 4$ \
string theory from\\n  Dabholkar-Harvey degeneracies\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"58 pages, 9 figures, 3 tables\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2020)184\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.NT\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The degeneracies of single-centered dyonic \
$\\\\frac14$-BPS black holes (BH) in\\nType II string theory on K3$\\\\times \
T^2$ are known to be coefficients of certain\\nmock Jacobi forms arising from \
the Igusa cusp form $\\\\Phi_{10}$. In this paper\\nwe present an exact \
analytic formula for these BH degeneracies purely in terms\\nof the \
degeneracies of the perturbative $\\\\frac12$-BPS states of the theory. \
We\\nuse the fact that the degeneracies are completely controlled by the \
polar\\ncoefficients of the mock Jacobi forms, using the \
Hardy-Ramanujan-Rademacher\\ncircle method. Here we present a simple formula \
for these polar coefficients as\\na quadratic function of the \
$\\\\frac12$-BPS degeneracies. We arrive at the\\nformula by using the \
physical interpretation of polar coefficients as negative\\ndiscriminant \
states, and then making use of previous results in the literature\\nto track \
the decay of such states into pairs of $\\\\frac12$-BPS states in \
the\\nmoduli space. Although there are an infinite number of such decays, we \
show\\nthat only a finite number of them contribute to the formula. The \
phenomenon of\\nBH bound state metamorphosis (BSM) plays a crucial role in \
our analysis. We\\nshow that the dyonic BSM orbits with $U$-duality invariant \
$\\\\Delta<0$ are in\\nexact correspondence with the solution sets of the \
Brahmagupta-Pell equation,\\nwhich implies that they are isomorphic to the \
group of units in the order\\n$\\\\mathbb{Z}[\\\\sqrt{|\\\\Delta|}]$ in the \
real quadratic field\\n$\\\\mathbb{Q}(\\\\sqrt{|\\\\Delta|})$. We check our \
formula against the known numerical\\ndata arising from the Igusa cusp form, \
for the first 1650 polar coefficients,\\nand find perfect \
agreement.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 13 Dec 2019 15:35:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-12-02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
