Reys,\n  Timm Wrase", "title" -> 
            "Dyonic black hole degeneracies in $\\mathcal{N} = 4$ string \
theory from\n  Dabholkar-Harvey degeneracies", "comments" -> 
            "58 pages, 9 figures, 3 tables", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2020)184", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math.NT", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The degeneracies of single-centered dyonic $\\frac14$-BPS \
black holes (BH) in\nType II string theory on K3$\\times T^2$ are known to be \
coefficients of certain\nmock Jacobi forms arising from the Igusa cusp form $\
\\Phi_{10}$. In this paper\nwe present an exact analytic formula for these BH \
degeneracies purely in terms\nof the degeneracies of the perturbative \
$\\frac12$-BPS states of the theory. We\nuse the fact that the degeneracies \
are completely controlled by the polar\ncoefficients of the mock Jacobi \
forms, using the Hardy-Ramanujan-Rademacher\ncircle method. Here we present a \
simple formula for these polar coefficients as\na quadratic function of the $\
\\frac12$-BPS degeneracies. We arrive at the\nformula by using the physical \
interpretation of polar coefficients as negative\ndiscriminant states, and \
then making use of previous results in the literature\nto track the decay of \
such states into pairs of $\\frac12$-BPS states in the\nmoduli space. \
Although there are an infinite number of such decays, we show\nthat only a \
finite number of them contribute to the formula. The phenomenon of\nBH bound \
state metamorphosis (BSM) plays a crucial role in our analysis. We\nshow that \
the dyonic BSM orbits with $U$-duality invariant $\\Delta<0$ are in\nexact \
correspondence with the solution sets of the Brahmagupta-Pell equation,\n\
which implies that they are isomorphic to the group of units in the order\n\
$\\mathbb{Z}[\\sqrt{|\\Delta|}]$ in the real quadratic field\n\
$\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{|\\Delta|})$. We check our formula against the known \
numerical\ndata arising from the Igusa cusp form, for the first 1650 polar \
coefficients,\nand find perfect agreement.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
