                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Pablo Antonio Cano Molina-Ni\\\\~nirola\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pablo A. Cano\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Higher-Curvature Gravity, Black Holes and \
Holography\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PhD thesis, 366 pages. Based on arXiv:1607.06463, \
arXiv:1610.08019,\\n  arXiv:1610.08519, arXiv:1703.04625, arXiv:1704.02967, \
arXiv:1802.00018,\\n  arXiv:1808.01671, arXiv:1808.02052, arXiv:1906.00987. \
Contains new results\\n  and discussions, especially in chapters 3, 5 and \
6\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, the identification of new higher-curvature \
interactions known as\\nEinsteinian cubic gravity (ECG) and Generalized \
quasi-topological gravities\\n(GQGs) has allowed for important advances in \
the study of black hole solutions\\nand holographic applications of \
higher-order gravity. These theories are\\ncharacterized by having \
second-order linearized equations on maximally\\nsymmetric background and by \
possessing static, spherically symmetric (SSS)\\nblack hole solutions \
satisfying $g_{tt}g_{rr}=-1$, and whose thermodynamic\\nproperties can be \
studied analytically in a fully non-perturbative fashion. In\\nthe first part \
of this thesis, we perform a detailed analysis of the weak-field\\nlimit of $\
\\\\mathcal{L}($Riemann$)$ theories and of the condition\\n$g_{tt}g_{rr}=-1$ \
on SSS solutions, and we review the construction of ECG and\\nGeneralized \
quasi-topological gravities. In addition, we show that GQGs could\\nserve as \
building blocks to construct the most general EFT for gravity. In \
the\\nsecond part we study the non-perturbative corrections to the \
asymptotically\\nflat Schwarzschild black hole in $D=4$. We obtain closed \
exact expressions for\\nthe thermodynamic properties of spherically symmetric \
black holes with an\\narbitrary number of higher-curvature terms. We find \
that, quite generally, the\\nhigher-curvature corrections make the specific \
heat of these black holes\\npositive below certain mass, and hence black \
holes take an infinite time to\\nevaporate and the final \\\"Hawking \
explosion\\\" is avoided. In the last part we\\nstudy asymptotically AdS \
black holes and Euclidean-AdS-Taub-NUT solutions and\\nwe establish various \
entries of the holographic dictionary of $D=4$ ECG. We\\nillustrate the power \
of holographic higher-order gravities by obtaining a\\nrelation for the free \
energy of CFTs on squashed spheres, which we conjecture\\nto be valid for \
arbitrary CFTs.\\n\""}]}, {
