         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "1912.07035", "submitter" -> 
            "Pablo Antonio Cano Molina-Ni\\~nirola", "authors" -> 
            "Pablo A. Cano", "title" -> 
            "Higher-Curvature Gravity, Black Holes and Holography", 
            "comments" -> 
            "PhD thesis, 366 pages. Based on arXiv:1607.06463, \
arXiv:1610.08019,\n  arXiv:1610.08519, arXiv:1703.04625, arXiv:1704.02967, \
arXiv:1802.00018,\n  arXiv:1808.01671, arXiv:1808.02052, arXiv:1906.00987. \
Contains new results\n  and discussions, especially in chapters 3, 5 and 6", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently, the identification of new higher-curvature \
interactions known as\nEinsteinian cubic gravity (ECG) and Generalized \
quasi-topological gravities\n(GQGs) has allowed for important advances in the \
study of black hole solutions\nand holographic applications of higher-order \
gravity. These theories are\ncharacterized by having second-order linearized \
equations on maximally\nsymmetric background and by possessing static, \
spherically symmetric (SSS)\nblack hole solutions satisfying \
$g_{tt}g_{rr}=-1$, and whose thermodynamic\nproperties can be studied \
analytically in a fully non-perturbative fashion. In\nthe first part of this \
thesis, we perform a detailed analysis of the weak-field\nlimit of \
$\\mathcal{L}($Riemann$)$ theories and of the condition\n$g_{tt}g_{rr}=-1$ on \
SSS solutions, and we review the construction of ECG and\nGeneralized \
quasi-topological gravities. In addition, we show that GQGs could\nserve as \
building blocks to construct the most general EFT for gravity. In the\nsecond \
part we study the non-perturbative corrections to the asymptotically\nflat \
Schwarzschild black hole in $D=4$. We obtain closed exact expressions for\n\
the thermodynamic properties of spherically symmetric black holes with an\n\
arbitrary number of higher-curvature terms. We find that, quite generally, \
the\nhigher-curvature corrections make the specific heat of these black holes\
\npositive below certain mass, and hence black holes take an infinite time to\
\nevaporate and the final \"Hawking explosion\" is avoided. In the last part \
we\nstudy asymptotically AdS black holes and Euclidean-AdS-Taub-NUT solutions \
and\nwe establish various entries of the holographic dictionary of $D=4$ ECG. \
We\nillustrate the power of holographic higher-order gravities by obtaining a\
\nrelation for the free energy of CFTs on squashed spheres, which we \
conjecture\nto be valid for arbitrary CFTs.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 15 Dec 2019 12:54:46 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2019-12-17", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Cano", "Pablo A.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
