                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A gravitational model of magnons in thermal equilibrium \
with a ferromagnetic\\nspin chain is developed in a phenomenological \
bottom-up approach. A large\\nSchwarzschild-AdS black hole background is used \
as the thermal reservoir and\\nthe magnon dynamics is obtained by scalar \
fields and branes in the bulk. The\\nkey feature of this model is that the \
coupling of the spin chain is related\\nwith the radial position in which the \
brane is located. We further study a\\nferromagnetic spin chain with a \
competing interaction and find that the\\ncouplings are related by the \
difference of positions of the branes. We show how\\nto obtain the model from \
a weak limit of a dynamical gravitational system. This\\nallows us to embed \
the model into a holographic system. The couplings can be\\nrelated to \
entanglement entropy at finite temperature of the CFT since the\\nturning \
point of minimal surfaces coincides with the position of the branes.\\nThe \
difference of entropy is used to define a notion of distance between \
the\\nchain couplings.\\n\""}]}, {
