               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using considerations based on the thermodynamical Bethe \
ansatz as well\\nrepresentation theory of twisted Yangians we derive an exact \
expression for the\\noverlaps between the Bethe eigenstates of the $SO(6)$ \
spin chain and matrix\\nproduct states built from matrices whose commutators \
generate an irreducible\\nrepresentation of $\\\\mathfrak{so}(5)$. The latter \
play the role of boundary\\nstates in a domain wall version of ${\\\\cal \
N}=4$ SYM theory which has\\nnon-vanishing, $SO(5)$ symmetric vacuum \
expectation values on one side of a\\nco-dimension one wall. This theory, \
which constitutes a defect CFT, is known to\\nbe dual to a D3-D7 probe brane \
system. We likewise show that the same\\nmethodology makes it possible to \
prove an overlap formula, earlier presented\\nwithout proof, which is of \
relevance for the similar D3-D5 probe brane system.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
