 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct holographic Janus solutions, which \
describe a conformal\\ninterface in the theory of M2-branes, in \
four-dimensional gauged supergravities\\nusing a perturbative method. In \
particular, we study three Einstein-scalar\\nsystems and their BPS equations, \
which are derived by Bobev, Pilch, and Warner\\n(2014). The actions of our \
interest are all consistent truncations of $D=11$\\nsupergravity chosen to be \
invariant under $SO(4)\\\\times SO(4)$, $SU(3)\\\\times\\nU(1)\\\\times \
U(1)$, and $G_2$ symmetry subgroups of $SO(8)$ respectively. The\\nutility of \
our semi-analytic result is illustrated by the calculation of\\nminimal area \
surface and the associated holographic entanglement entropy.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
