           "id" -> "2001.06789", "submitter" -> "Nakwoo Kim", "authors" -> 
            "Nakwoo Kim and Se-Jin Kim", "title" -> 
            "Re-visiting Supersymmetric Janus Solutions: A Perturbative \
Construction", "comments" -> "26 pages, 3 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Chin. Phys. C 44 (2020) 7, 073104", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1674-1137/44/7/073104", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct holographic Janus solutions, which describe a \
conformal\ninterface in the theory of M2-branes, in four-dimensional gauged \
supergravities\nusing a perturbative method. In particular, we study three \
Einstein-scalar\nsystems and their BPS equations, which are derived by Bobev, \
Pilch, and Warner\n(2014). The actions of our interest are all consistent \
truncations of $D=11$\nsupergravity chosen to be invariant under \
$SO(4)\\times SO(4)$, $SU(3)\\times\nU(1)\\times U(1)$, and $G_2$ symmetry \
subgroups of $SO(8)$ respectively. The\nutility of our semi-analytic result \
is illustrated by the calculation of\nminimal area surface and the associated \
holographic entanglement entropy.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
