               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Szabolcs Borsanyi\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Szabolcs Borsanyi, Zoltan Fodor, Jana N. Guenther, Ruben \
Kara, Sandor\\n  D. Katz, Paolo Parotto, Attila Pasztor, Claudia Ratti, \
Kalman K. Szabo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The QCD crossover at finite chemical potential from \
lattice simulations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"5 pages main text + 7 pages supplementary material\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. Lett. 125, 052001 (2020)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.052001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-lat\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We provide the most accurate results for the QCD \
transition line so far. We\\noptimize the definition of the crossover \
temperature $T_c$, allowing for its\\nvery precise determination, and \
extrapolate from imaginary chemical potential\\nup to real $\\\\mu_B \
\\\\approx 300$ MeV. The definition of $T_c$ adopted in this\\nwork is based \
on the observation that the chiral susceptibility as a function\\nof the \
condensate is an almost universal curve at zero and imaganiary \
$\\\\mu_B$.\\nWe obtain the parameters $\\\\kappa_2=0.0153(18)$ and \
$\\\\kappa_4=0.00032(67)$ as a\\ncontinuum extrapolation based on $N_t=10,12$ \
and $16$ lattices with physical\\nquark masses. We also extrapolate the peak \
value of the chiral susceptibility\\nand the width of the chiral transition \
along the crossover line. In fact, both\\nof these are consistent with a \
constant function of $\\\\mu_B$. We see no sign of\\ncriticality in the \
explored range.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 7 Feb 2020 14:48:56 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-08-05\""}]}, {
