 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A quantum integrability index was proposed in \
\\\\cite{KMS}. It systematizes the\\nGoldschmidt and Witten's operator \
counting argument \\\\cite{GW} by using the\\nconformal symmetry. In this \
work we compute the quantum integrability indexes\\nfor the symmetric coset \
models ${SU(N)}/{SO(N)}$ and $SO(2N)/{SO(N)\\\\times\\nSO(N)}$. The indexes \
of these theories are all non-positive except for the case\\nof \
${SO(4)}/{SO(2)\\\\times SO(2)}$. Moreover we extend the analysis to \
the\\ntheories with fermions and consider a concrete theory: the \
$\\\\mathbb{CP}^N$\\nmodel coupled with a massless Dirac fermion. We find \
that the indexes for this\\nclass of models are non-positive as \
well.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
