               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2002.05460\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dimitrios Zoakos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"George Georgiou, Dimitrios Zoakos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Giant Gravitons on the Schrodinger pp-wave \
geometry\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"19 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2020)185\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct a new giant graviton solution on the \
recently constructed\\npp-wave geometry of the non-supersymmetric Schrodinger \
background. That\\nsolution exhibits an intriguing behavior as the \
deformation parameter of the\\nspacetime varies. Firstly, the degeneracy \
between the giant and the point\\ngraviton is lifted for the benefit of the \
giant graviton as soon as the\\ndeformation is turned on. Secondly, when the \
deformation parameter exceeds a\\ncritical value the barrier separating the \
point from the giant graviton\\ndisappears. This suggests that the mere \
presence of a D3-brane leads to the\\nspontaneous breaking of conformal \
invariance. We perform a detailed analysis of\\nthe full bosonic spectrum, \
which reveals that the deformation induces a\\ncoupling between the scalar \
and the gauge field fluctuations. It is exactly\\nthis coupling that keeps \
the giant graviton free of tachyonic instabilities.\\nFurthermore, the giant \
graviton configuration completely breaks the\\nsupersymmetry of the pp-wave \
background, as the Kappa-symmetry analysis\\nsuggests.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 13 Feb 2020 11:56:35 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-04-22\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
