            "Giant Gravitons on the Schrodinger pp-wave geometry", "comments" -> 
            "19 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP03(2020)185", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct a new giant graviton solution on the recently \
constructed\npp-wave geometry of the non-supersymmetric Schrodinger \
background. That\nsolution exhibits an intriguing behavior as the deformation \
parameter of the\nspacetime varies. Firstly, the degeneracy between the giant \
and the point\ngraviton is lifted for the benefit of the giant graviton as \
soon as the\ndeformation is turned on. Secondly, when the deformation \
parameter exceeds a\ncritical value the barrier separating the point from the \
giant graviton\ndisappears. This suggests that the mere presence of a \
D3-brane leads to the\nspontaneous breaking of conformal invariance. We \
perform a detailed analysis of\nthe full bosonic spectrum, which reveals that \
the deformation induces a\ncoupling between the scalar and the gauge field \
fluctuations. It is exactly\nthis coupling that keeps the giant graviton free \
of tachyonic instabilities.\nFurthermore, the giant graviton configuration \
completely breaks the\nsupersymmetry of the pp-wave background, as the \
Kappa-symmetry analysis\nsuggests.\n", 
