               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 103, 045010 (2021)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.103.045010\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the gauge invariant 't Hooft operator in \
canonical formalism for\\nYang-Mills theory as well as the $\\\\mathcal{N} =4 \
$ super-Yang-Mills theory with\\nthe gauge group $ U(N) $. It is shown that \
the spectrum of the 't Hooft\\noperator labeled by the arbitrary irreducible \
representation of the gauge group\\nis the same as the spectrum of the Wilson \
operator labeled by the same\\nrepresentation. So it is possible to construct \
a unitary operator $ S $ making\\nthe two kinds of loop operators transformed \
into each other. S-duality\\ntransformation could be realized by the operator \
$ S $. We compute the\\nsupersymmetry variations of the loop operators with \
the fermionic couplings\\nturned off. The result is consistent with the \
expectation that the action of $\\nS $ should make supercharges transform \
with a $ U(1)_{Y} $ phase.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
