 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review the applications of the Quantum Spectral \
Curve (QSC) method to the\\nRegge (BFKL) limit in N=4 supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory. QSC, based on\\nquantum integrability of the \
AdS$_5$/CFT$_4$ duality, was initially developed\\nas a tool for the study of \
the spectrum of anomalous dimensions of local\\noperators in the N=4 SYM in \
the planar, $N_c\\\\to\\\\infty$ limit. We explain how to\\napply the QSC for \
the BFKL limit, which requires non-trivial analytic\\ncontinuation in spin \
$S$ and extends the initial construction to non-local\\nlight-ray operators. \
We give a brief review of high precision non-perturbative\\nnumerical \
solutions and analytic perturbative data resulting from this\\napproach. We \
also describe as a simple example of the QSC construction the\\nleading order \
in the BFKL limit. We show that the QSC substantially simplifies\\nin this \
limit and reduces to the Faddeev-Korchemsky Baxter equation \
for\\nQ-functions. Finally, we review recent results for the Fishnet CFT, \
which\\ncarries a number of similarities with the Lipatov's integrable spin \
chain for\\ninteracting reggeized gluons.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
