                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  BPS Wilson loops in supersymmetric gauge theories have \
been the subjects of\\nactive research since they are often amenable to exact \
computation. So far most\\nof the studies have focused on loops that do not \
intersect. In this paper, we\\nderive exact results for intersecting 1/8 BPS \
Wilson loops in N=4\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory, using a combination \
of supersymmetric\\nlocalization and the loop equation in 2d gauge theory. \
The result is given by a\\nnovel matrix-model-like representation which \
couples multiple contour integrals\\nand a Gaussian matrix model. We evaluate \
the integral at large N, and make\\ncontact with the string worldsheet \
description at strong coupling. As an\\napplication of our results, we \
compute exactly a small-angle limit (and more\\ngenerally near-BPS limits) of \
the cross anomalous dimension which governs the\\nUV divergence of \
intersecting Wilson lines. The same quantity describes the\\nsoft anomalous \
dimension of scattering amplitudes of W-bosons in the \
Coulomb\\nbranch.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
