 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find the holographic dual to the three classes of \
superconformal Janus\\ninterfaces in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM that preserve \
three-dimensional\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$, $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$, and \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ supersymmetry. The\\nsolutions are constructed in \
five-dimensional SO(6) maximal gauged supergravity\\nand are then uplifted to \
type IIB supergravity. Corresponding to each of the\\nthree classes of Janus \
solutions, there are also AdS$_4\\\\times S^1\\\\times S^5$\\nJ-fold \
backgrounds. These J-folds have a non-trivial \
SL$(2,\\\\mathbb{Z})$\\nmonodromy for the axio-dilaton on the $S^1$ and are \
dual to three-dimensional\\nsuperconformal field theories.\\n\""}]}, {
