               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yifan Wang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Taming Defects in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
Super-Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"91 pages, 2 figures; v3: minor corrections and more \
references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2020)021\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUPT-2608\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study correlation functions involving extended \
defect operators in the\\nfour-dimensional ${\\\\cal N}=4$ super-Yang-Mills \
(SYM). The main tool is\\nsupersymmetric localization with respect to the \
supercharge $\\\\cal Q$ introduced\\nin \\\\cite{Pestun:2009nn} which \
computes observables in the $\\\\cal Q$-cohomology.\\nWe classify general \
defects of different codimensions in the ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM\\nthat belong to \
the $\\\\cal Q$-cohomology, which form ${1\\\\over 16}$-BPS \
defect\\nnetworks. By performing the $\\\\cal Q$-localization of the \
${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM on\\nthe four-dimensional hemisphere, we discover a novel \
defect-Yang-Mills (dYM)\\ntheory on a submanifold given by the \
two-dimensional hemisphere and described\\nby (constrained) two-dimensional \
Yang-Mills coupled to topological quantum\\nmechanics on the boundary circle. \
This also generalizes to interface defects in\\n${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM by the \
folding trick. We provide explicit dictionary between\\ndefect observables in \
the SYM and those in the dYM, which enables extraction of\\ngeneral \
${1\\\\over 16}$-BPS defect network observables of the SYM \
from\\ntwo-dimensional gauge theory and matrix model techniques. Applied to \
the D5\\nbrane interface in the $SU(N)$ SYM, we explicitly determine a set of \
defect\\ncorrelation functions in the large $N$ limit and obtain precise \
matching with\\nstrong coupling results from IIB supergravity on \
$AdS_5\\\\times S^5$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 24 Mar 2020 17:59:59 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 23 May 2020 19:59:30 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
