           "id" -> "2003.11016", "submitter" -> "Yifan Wang", "authors" -> 
            "Yifan Wang", "title" -> 
            "Taming Defects in $\\mathcal{N}=4$ Super-Yang-Mills", "comments" -> 
            "91 pages, 2 figures; v3: minor corrections and more references \
added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2020)021", 
            "report-no" -> "PUPT-2608", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study correlation functions involving extended defect \
operators in the\nfour-dimensional ${\\cal N}=4$ super-Yang-Mills (SYM). The \
main tool is\nsupersymmetric localization with respect to the supercharge \
$\\cal Q$ introduced\nin \\cite{Pestun:2009nn} which computes observables in \
the $\\cal Q$-cohomology.\nWe classify general defects of different \
codimensions in the ${\\cal N}=4$ SYM\nthat belong to the $\\cal \
Q$-cohomology, which form ${1\\over 16}$-BPS defect\nnetworks. By performing \
the $\\cal Q$-localization of the ${\\cal N}=4$ SYM on\nthe four-dimensional \
hemisphere, we discover a novel defect-Yang-Mills (dYM)\ntheory on a \
submanifold given by the two-dimensional hemisphere and described\nby \
(constrained) two-dimensional Yang-Mills coupled to topological quantum\n\
mechanics on the boundary circle. This also generalizes to interface defects \
in\n${\\cal N}=4$ SYM by the folding trick. We provide explicit dictionary \
between\ndefect observables in the SYM and those in the dYM, which enables \
extraction of\ngeneral ${1\\over 16}$-BPS defect network observables of the \
SYM from\ntwo-dimensional gauge theory and matrix model techniques. Applied \
to the D5\nbrane interface in the $SU(N)$ SYM, we explicitly determine a set \
of defect\ncorrelation functions in the large $N$ limit and obtain precise \
matching with\nstrong coupling results from IIB supergravity on $AdS_5\\times \
S^5$.\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 24 Mar 2020 17:59:59 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 23 May 2020 19:59:30 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 14 Dec 2020 21:22:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-12-16", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Wang", "Yifan", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
