                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The N=4 superconformal Yang-Mills theory on flat \
four-dimensional Minkowski\\nspace is a de-confined gauge theory in the sense \
that the string tension for\\nfundamental representation coloured quarks \
vanishes. In fact, static\\nfundamental representation quarks which lie in \
certain half-BPS\\nsuper-multiplets do not interact at all. An interesting \
question asks whether\\nsuch quarks would carry a well-defined global colour \
charge which, when the\\ngauge is fixed, should have the status of an \
internal symmetry. We shall\\npresent a simple paradigmatic model which \
suggests that the answer to this\\nquestion lies in the way in which infrared \
divergences are dealt with.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
