 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The 6d $\\\\mathcal{N}=(2,0)$ theory has natural \
surface operator observables,\\nwhich are akin in many ways to Wilson loops \
in gauge theories. We propose a\\ndefinition of a \\\"locally BPS\\\" surface \
operator and study its conformal\\nanomalies, the analog of the conformal \
dimension of local operators. We study\\nthe abelian theory and the \
holographic dual of the large $N$ theory refining\\npreviously used \
techniques. Introducing non-constant couplings to the scalar\\nfields allows \
for an extra anomaly coefficient, which we find in both cases to\\nbe related \
to one of the geometrical anomaly coefficients, suggesting a \
general\\nrelation due to supersymmetry. We also comment on surfaces with \
conical\\nsingularities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
