Volk", "title" -> "Wilson lines in AdS/dCFT", "comments" -> 
            "8 pages, 2 figures; typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1016/j.physletb.2020.135520", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the expectation value of Wilson lines in two \
defect versions of N\n= 4 SYM, both with supersymmetry completely broken, \
where one is described in\nterms of an integrable boundary state, the other \
one not. For both cases,\nimposing a certain double scaling limit, we find \
agreement to two leading\norders between the expectation values calculated \
from respectively the field\ntheory and the string theory side of the \
AdS/dCFT correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
