            "  In this paper we find a host of boost operators for a very \
general choice of\ncoproducts in AdS_3-inspired scattering theories, focusing \
on the massless\nsector, with and without an added trigonometric deformation. \
We find that the\nboost coproducts are exact symmetries of the R-matrices we \
construct, besides\nfulfilling the relations of modified Poincare' - type \
superalgebras. In the\nprocess, we discover an ambiguity in determining the \
boost coproduct which\nallows us to derive differential constraints on our \
R-matrices. In one\nparticular case of the trigonometric deformation, we find \
a non-coassociative\nstructure which satisfies the axioms of a quasi-Hopf \
algebra.\n", 
