            "Nadav Drukker, Simone Giombi, Arkady A. Tseytlin, Xinan Zhou", 
            "title" -> 
            "Defect CFT in the 6d (2,0) theory from M2 brane dynamics in \
AdS$_7\n  \\times$S$^4$", "comments" -> 
            "29 pages, no figure; v2,v3: minor corrections and references \
added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP07(2020)101", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Surface operators in the 6d (2,0) theory at large $N$ have a \
holographic\ndescription in terms of M2 branes probing the AdS$_7 \\times \
S^4$ M-theory\nbackground. The most symmetric, 1/2-BPS, operator is defined \
over a planar or\nspherical surface, and it preserves a 2d superconformal \
group. This includes,\nin particular, an $SO(2,2)$ subgroup of 2d conformal \
transformations, so that\nthe surface operator may be viewed as a conformal \
defect in the 6d theory. The\ndual M2 brane has an AdS$_3$ induced geometry, \
reflecting the 2d conformal\nsymmetry. Here we use the holographic \
description to extract the defect CFT\ndata associated to the surface \
operator. The spectrum of transverse\nfluctuations of the M2 brane is found \
to be in one-to-one correspondence with a\nprotected multiplet of operator \
insertions on the surface, which includes the\ndisplacement operator. We \
compute the one-loop determinants of fluctuations of\nthe M2 brane, and \
extract the conformal anomaly coefficient of the spherical\nsurface to order \
$N^0$. We also briefly discuss the RG flow from the\nnon-supersymmetric to \
the 1/2-BPS defect operator, and its consistency with a\n\"$b$-theorem\" for \
the defect CFT. Starting with the M2 brane action, we then\nuse AdS$_3$ \
Witten diagrams to compute the 4-point functions of the elementary\nbosonic \
insertions on the surface operator, and extract some of the defect CFT\ndata \
from the OPE. The 4-point function is shown to satisfy superconformal Ward\n\
identities, and we discuss a related subsector of \"twisted\" scalar \
insertions,\nwhose correlation functions are constrained by the residual \
superconformal\nsymmetry.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
