               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2004.05071\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shota Komatsu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Joao Caetano, Shota Komatsu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Functional Equations and Separation of Variables for \
Exact g-Function\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"27 pages + appendices; v2 typos corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2020)180\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The g-function is a measure of degrees of freedom \
associated to a boundary of\\ntwo-dimensional quantum field theories. In \
integrable theories, it can be\\ncomputed exactly in a form of the Fredholm \
determinant, but it is often hard to\\nevaluate numerically. In this paper, \
we derive functional equations---or\\nequivalently integral equations of the \
thermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA)\\ntype---which directly compute the \
g-function in the simplest integrable theory;\\nthe sinh-Gordon theory at the \
self-dual point. The derivation is based on the\\nclassic result by Tracy and \
Widom on the relation between Fredholm determinants\\nand TBA, which was used \
also in the context of topological string. We\\ndemonstrate the efficiency of \
our formulation through the numerical computation\\nand compare the results \
in the UV limit with the Liouville CFT. As a side\\nresult, we present \
multiple integrals of Q-functions which we conjecture to\\ndescribe a \
universal part of the g-function, and discuss its implication to\\nintegrable \
spin chains.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 10 Apr 2020 15:24:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 19 Apr 2020 02:52:53 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
