          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2004.07592", "submitter" -> "Jia Tian", "authors" -> 
            "Jun-bao Wu, Jia Tian and Bin Chen", "title" -> 
            "Loop Operators in Three-Dimensional $\\mathcal{N}=2$ Fishnet \
Theories", "comments" -> 
            "36 pages, 13 figures, version4, match the published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP07(2020)215", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP07(2020)215", "report-no" -> "CJQS-202-023", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this work, we study the line and loop operators in \
three-dimensional\n${\\mathcal N}=2$ fishnet theories in detail. We construct \
the straight line and\ncircular loop operators which are at least classically \
half-BPS. We develop a\nnew regularization scheme at frame $-1$ which is \
suitable for the study of the\nfermionic BPS loops in general \
super-Chern-Simons-matter theories. We\ninitialize the perturbative \
computation for the vacuum expectation values of\nthe circular BPS loop \
operators based on this scheme. We construct the cusped\nline operators as \
well, and compute the vacuum expectation values of these\ncusped line \
operators up to two-loop order. We find that the universal cusp\nanomalous \
dimension vanishes, if we put aside the fact that the generalized\npotential \
has a double pole in the $1/\\epsilon$ expansion.\n", 
