               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Three Dimensional Mirror Symmetry beyond $ADE$ quivers \
and\\n  Argyres-Douglas theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"(14+82) pages + appendices, many figures.Section 1 \
provides a brief\\n  summary of the paper. V2:Minor typos fixed, and \
references added, V3: Minor\\n  edits\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2021)199\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Mirror symmetry, a three dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
IR duality, has been\\nstudied in detail for quiver gauge theories of the \
$ADE$-type (as well as their\\naffine versions) with unitary gauge groups. \
The $A$-type quivers (also known as\\nlinear quivers) and the associated \
mirror dualities have a particularly simple\\nrealization in terms of a Type \
IIB system of D3-D5-NS5-branes. In this paper,\\nwe present a systematic \
field theory prescription for constructing 3d mirror\\npairs beyond the $ADE$ \
quiver gauge theories, starting from a dual pair of\\n$A$-type quivers with \
unitary gauge groups. The construction involves a certain\\ngeneralization of \
the $S$ and the $T$ operations, which arise in the context of\\nthe \
$SL(2,\\\\mathbb{Z})$ action on a 3d CFT with a $U(1)$ 0-form global \
symmetry.\\nWe implement this construction in terms of two supersymmetric \
observables --\\nthe round sphere partition function and the superconformal \
index on $S^2 \\\\times\\nS^1$. We discuss explicit examples of various \
(non-$ADE$) infinite families of\\nmirror pairs that can be obtained in this \
fashion. In addition, we use the\\nabove construction to conjecture explicit \
3d $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ Lagrangians for 3d\\nSCFTs, which arise in the deep IR \
limit of certain Argyres-Douglas theories\\ncompactified on a \
circle.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
