Argyres-Douglas theories", "comments" -> 
            "(14+82) pages + appendices, many figures.Section 1 provides a \
brief\n  summary of the paper. V2:Minor typos fixed, and references added, \
V3: Minor\n  edits", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP07(2021)199", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Mirror symmetry, a three dimensional $\\mathcal{N}=4$ IR \
duality, has been\nstudied in detail for quiver gauge theories of the \
$ADE$-type (as well as their\naffine versions) with unitary gauge groups. The \
$A$-type quivers (also known as\nlinear quivers) and the associated mirror \
dualities have a particularly simple\nrealization in terms of a Type IIB \
system of D3-D5-NS5-branes. In this paper,\nwe present a systematic field \
theory prescription for constructing 3d mirror\npairs beyond the $ADE$ quiver \
gauge theories, starting from a dual pair of\n$A$-type quivers with unitary \
gauge groups. The construction involves a certain\ngeneralization of the $S$ \
and the $T$ operations, which arise in the context of\nthe \
$SL(2,\\mathbb{Z})$ action on a 3d CFT with a $U(1)$ 0-form global symmetry.\n\
We implement this construction in terms of two supersymmetric observables --\n\
the round sphere partition function and the superconformal index on $S^2 \
\\times\nS^1$. We discuss explicit examples of various (non-$ADE$) infinite \
families of\nmirror pairs that can be obtained in this fashion. In addition, \
we use the\nabove construction to conjecture explicit 3d $\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
Lagrangians for 3d\nSCFTs, which arise in the deep IR limit of certain \
Argyres-Douglas theories\ncompactified on a circle.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 21 Apr 2020 03:34:03 GMT"}, {
