               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2004.11329\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Tamas Gombor\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Tamas Gombor, Zoltan Bajnok\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Boundary states, overlaps, nesting and bootstrapping \
AdS/dCFT\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"minor corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2020)123\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Integrable boundary states can be built up from pair \
annihilation amplitudes\\ncalled $K$-matrices. These amplitudes are related \
to mirror reflections and\\nthey both satisfy Yang Baxter equations, which \
can be twisted or untwisted. We\\nrelate these two notions to each other and \
show how they are fixed by the\\nunbroken symmetries, which, together with \
the full symmetry, must form\\nsymmetric pairs. We show that the twisted \
nature of the $K$-matrix implies\\nspecific selection rules for the overlaps. \
If the Bethe roots of the same type\\nare paired the overlap is called \
chiral, otherwise it is achiral and they\\ncorrespond to untwisted and \
twisted $K$-matrices, respectively. We use these\\nfindings to develop a \
nesting procedure for $K$-matrices, which provides the\\nfactorizing overlaps \
for higher rank algebras automatically. We apply these\\nmethods for the \
calculation of the simplest asymptotic all-loop 1-point\\nfunctions in \
AdS/dCFT. In doing so we classify the solutions of the YBE for \
the\\n$K$-matrices with centrally extended $\\\\mathfrak{su}(2|2)_{c}$ \
symmetry and\\ncalculate the generic overlaps in terms of Bethe roots and \
ratio of Gaudin\\ndeterminants.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
