 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose some new infra-red dualities for $2d$ \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=(0,2)$\\ntheories. The first one relates a $USp(2N)$ gauge \
theory with one antisymmetric\\nchiral, four fundamental chirals and $N$ \
Fermi singlets to a Landau-Ginzburg\\nmodel of $N$ Fermi and $6N$ chiral \
fields with cubic interactions. The second\\none relates $SU(2)$ linear \
quiver gauge theories of arbitrary length $N-1$ with\\nthe addition of $N$ \
Fermi singlets for any non-negative integer $N$. They can\\nbe understood as \
a generalization of the duality between an $SU(2)$ gauge\\ntheory with four \
fundamental chirals and a Landau-Ginzburg model of one Fermi\\nand six \
chirals with a cubic interaction. We derive these dualities from\\nalready \
known $4d$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ dualities by compactifications \
on\\n$\\\\mathbb{S}^2$ with suitable topological twists and we further test \
them by\\nmatching anomalies and elliptic genera. We also show how to derive \
them by\\niterative applications of some more fundamental dualities, in \
analogy with\\nsimilar derivations for parent dualities in three and four \
dimensions.\\n\""}]}, {
