                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive a holomorphic anomaly equation for the \
Vafa-Witten partition\\nfunction for twisted four-dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N} \
=4$ super Yang-Mills theory\\non $\\\\mathbb{CP}^{2}$ for the gauge group \
$SO(3)$ from the path integral of the\\neffective theory on the Coulomb \
branch. The holomorphic kernel of this\\nequation, which receives \
contributions only from the instantons, is not modular\\nbut `mock modular'. \
The partition function has correct modular properties\\nexpected from \
$S$-duality only after including the anomalous nonholomorphic\\nboundary \
contributions from anti-instantons. Using M-theory duality, we relate\\nthis \
phenomenon to the holomorphic anomaly of the elliptic genus of \
a\\ntwo-dimensional noncompact sigma model and compute it independently in \
two\\ndimensions. The anomaly both in four and in two dimensions can be \
traced to a\\ntopological term in the effective action of six-dimensional \
(2,0) theory on the\\ntensor branch. We consider generalizations to other \
manifolds and other gauge\\ngroups to show that mock modularity is generic \
and essential for exhibiting\\nduality when the relevant field space is \
noncompact.\\n\""}]}, {
