               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the large $N$ limit of the superconformal \
index of a large class of\\n5d $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ superconformal field \
theories and show it is given by the\\nsquare of the partition function on \
the squashed five-sphere. We show this\\nsimple relation implies a Cardy \
formula in 5d, which is valid in an \\\"extended\\\"\\nregime in which \
fugacities are finite and $N$ is large. For theories with\\nweakly coupled \
gravity duals we conjecture this large $N$ Cardy formula\\nuniversally \
accounts for the microscopic entropy of spinning black holes in\\nAdS$_{6}$. \
We check this explicitly for known black hole solutions in massive\\ntype IIA \
and type IIB string theory, carrying two angular momenta and one\\nelectric \
charge, and predict the entropy of black holes carrying multiple\\nelectric \
charges, yet to be constructed. We also discuss large $N$ properties\\nof the \
$S^{3}_{b}\\\\times\\\\Sigma_{\\\\mathfrak{g}}$ partition function, extending\
\\nprevious results to theories with type IIB duals.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
