(published version); v3: Typos corrected and references updated", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 2009 (2020) 124", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP09(2020)124", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the large $N$ limit of the superconformal index of a \
large class of\n5d $\\mathcal{N}=1$ superconformal field theories and show it \
is given by the\nsquare of the partition function on the squashed \
five-sphere. We show this\nsimple relation implies a Cardy formula in 5d, \
which is valid in an \"extended\"\nregime in which fugacities are finite and \
$N$ is large. For theories with\nweakly coupled gravity duals we conjecture \
this large $N$ Cardy formula\nuniversally accounts for the microscopic \
entropy of spinning black holes in\nAdS$_{6}$. We check this explicitly for \
known black hole solutions in massive\ntype IIA and type IIB string theory, \
carrying two angular momenta and one\nelectric charge, and predict the \
entropy of black holes carrying multiple\nelectric charges, yet to be \
constructed. We also discuss large $N$ properties\nof the \
$S^{3}_{b}\\times\\Sigma_{\\mathfrak{g}}$ partition function, extending\n\
previous results to theories with type IIB duals.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 1 May 2020 18:00:14 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 20 Sep 2020 17:21:54 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 29 Jun 2021 07:23:02 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2021-06-30", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Crichigno", "P. Marcos", ""}, {
              "Jain", "Dharmesh", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
