, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  A D3-D5 intersection gives rise to a defect CFT, \
wherein the rank of the\\ngauge group jumps by k units across a domain wall. \
The one-point functions of\\nlocal operators in this set-up map to overlaps \
between on-shell Bethe states in\\nthe underlying spin chain and a boundary \
state representing the D5 brane.\\nFocussing on the k=1 case, we extend the \
construction to gluonic and fermionic\\nsectors, which was prohibitively \
difficult to achieve for k>1. As a byproduct,\\nwe test an all-loop proposal \
for the one-point functions in the su(2) sector at\\nthe half-wrapping order \
of perturbation theory.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
