               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Defect conformal field theories (dCFTs) have been \
attracting increased\\nattention recently, mainly because they enable us to \
bridge the gap between\\nidealistic, highly symmetric models of our world \
(such as the particle/string\\nduality) and real-world systems. This talk is \
about the AdS/defect CFT\\ncorrespondence, an exciting new proposal that \
joins the forces of holography,\\nintegrability, supersymmetric localization \
and the conformal bootstrap program\\nin a framework that is appropriate for \
the study of defects in real-world\\nsystems. After introducing dCFTs and \
some of their holographic realizations, we\\nwill present some recent results \
for the one-point functions of the integrable\\ndCFTs that are the \
holographic duals of the D3-probe-D5 and the D3-probe-D7\\nsystems of \
intersecting branes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
