 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the AdS${}_5\\\\times$S${}^5$ Green-Schwarz \
superstring from\\nfour-dimensional Beltrami-Chern-Simons theory reduced on a \
manifold with\\nsingular boundary conditions. In this construction, the Lax \
connection and\\nspectral parameter of the integrable superstring have a \
simple geometric origin\\nin four dimensions as gauge connection and \
reduction coordinate. Kappa symmetry\\narises as a certain class of singular \
gauge transformations, while the\\nworldsheet metric comes from \
complex-structure-changing Beltrami differentials.\\nOur approach offers the \
possibility of investigating integrable holography\\nusing traditional field \
theory methods.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
