               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this thesis we consider four dimensional N=2 \
superconformal field\\ntheories, in presence of line defects such as Wilson \
loops. In this set up,\\nusing supersymmetric localization, we compute many \
observables, such as the\\nvacuum expectation value of the Wilson loop, \
correlation functions with chiral\\noperators and the emitted radiation of \
the charged particle moving along the\\nWilson loop trajectory. These results \
are achieved by exploiting the localized\\nmatrix model on a four sphere, and \
checked against a perturbative computation\\non the flat space in N=1 \
superspace formalism, up to four loops in perturbation\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
