            "Wilson loops as defects in N=2 conformal field theories", 
            "comments" -> 
            "214 pages, several figures, PhD thesis based on \
arXiv:1802.09813,\n  arXiv:1906.07085, arXiv:1910.06332", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this thesis we consider four dimensional N=2 superconformal \
field\ntheories, in presence of line defects such as Wilson loops. In this \
set up,\nusing supersymmetric localization, we compute many observables, such \
as the\nvacuum expectation value of the Wilson loop, correlation functions \
with chiral\noperators and the emitted radiation of the charged particle \
moving along the\nWilson loop trajectory. These results are achieved by \
exploiting the localized\nmatrix model on a four sphere, and checked against \
a perturbative computation\non the flat space in N=1 superspace formalism, up \
to four loops in perturbation\ntheory.\n", 
