               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Guido Festuccia, Anastasios Gorantis, Antonio Pittelli, \
Konstantina\\n  Polydorou and Lorenzo Ruggeri\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Cohomological Localization of $\\\\mathcal N = 2$ Gauge \
Theories with\\n  Matter\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"37 pages including appendices. Partial text overlap \
with\\n  arXiv:1812.06473 in appendices. Minor typo fixes, references \
added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2020)133\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct a large class of gauge theories with \
extended supersymmetry on\\nfour-dimensional manifolds with a Killing vector \
field and isolated fixed\\npoints. We extend previous results limited to \
super Yang-Mills theory to\\ngeneral $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ gauge theories \
including hypermultiplets. We present a\\ngeneral framework encompassing \
equivariant Donaldson-Witten theory and Pestun's\\ntheory on $S^4$ as two \
particular cases. This is achieved by expressing fields\\nin cohomological \
variables, whose features are dictated by supersymmetry and\\nrequire a \
generalized notion of self-duality for two-forms and of chirality \
for\\nspinors. Finally, we implement localization techniques to compute the \
exact\\npartition function of the cohomological theories we built up and \
write the\\nexplicit result for manifolds with diverse topologies.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
