            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct a large class of gauge theories with extended \
supersymmetry on\nfour-dimensional manifolds with a Killing vector field and \
isolated fixed\npoints. We extend previous results limited to super \
Yang-Mills theory to\ngeneral $\\mathcal{N}=2$ gauge theories including \
hypermultiplets. We present a\ngeneral framework encompassing equivariant \
Donaldson-Witten theory and Pestun's\ntheory on $S^4$ as two particular \
cases. This is achieved by expressing fields\nin cohomological variables, \
whose features are dictated by supersymmetry and\nrequire a generalized \
notion of self-duality for two-forms and of chirality for\nspinors. Finally, \
we implement localization techniques to compute the exact\npartition function \
of the cohomological theories we built up and write the\nexplicit result for \
manifolds with diverse topologies.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 26 May 2020 18:08:13 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 9 Jun 2020 15:21:19 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-10-28", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Festuccia", "Guido", ""}, {
              "Gorantis", "Anastasios", ""}, {"Pittelli", "Antonio", ""}, {
              "Polydorou", "Konstantina", ""}, {"Ruggeri", "Lorenzo", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{12.017432619414807`, -5.639432193428078}, 0.],
