 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Five-dimensional $Sp(N)$ supersymmetric Yang-Mills \
admits a $\\\\mathbb{Z}_2$\\nversion of a theta angle $\\\\theta$. In this \
note, we derive a double\\nquantization of the Seiberg-Witten geometry of $\\\
\\mathcal{N}=1$ $Sp(1)$ gauge\\ntheory at $\\\\theta=\\\\pi$, on the manifold \
$S^1\\\\times\\\\mathbb{R}^4$. Crucially,\\n$\\\\mathbb{R}^4$ is placed on \
the $\\\\Omega$-background, which provides the two\\nparameters to quantize \
the geometry. Physically, we are counting instantons in\\nthe presence of a \
1/2-BPS fundamental Wilson loop, both of which are wrapping\\n$S^1$. \
Mathematically, this amounts to proving the regularity of a\\n$qq$-character \
for the spin-1/2 representation of the quantum affine \
algebra\\n$U_q(\\\\widehat{A_1})$, with a certain twist due to the \
$\\\\theta$-angle. We\\nmotivate these results from two distinct string \
theory pictures. First, in a\\n$(p,q)$-web setup in type IIB, where the loop \
is characterized by a D3 brane.\\nSecond, in a type I' string setup, where \
the loop is characterized by a D4\\nbrane subject to an orientifold \
projection. We comment on the generalizations\\nto the higher rank case \
$Sp(N)$ when $N>1$, and the $SU(N)$ theory at\\nChern-Simons level \
$\\\\kappa$ when $N>2$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
