            "  We consider non-planar one-loop anomalous dimensions in \
maximally\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory and its marginally deformed \
analogues. Using\nthe basis of Bethe states, we compute matrix elements of \
the dilatation\noperator and find compact expressions in terms of off-shell \
scalar products and\nhexagon-like functions. We then use non-degenerate \
quantum-mechanical\nperturbation theory to compute the leading $1/N^2$ \
corrections to operator\ndimensions and as an example compute the large \
