 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find new asymptotically locally AdS$_4$ Euclidean \
supersymmetric solutions\\nof the STU model in four-dimensional gauged \
supergravity. These \\\"black saddles\\\"\\nhave an $S^1\\\\times \\\\Sigma_{\
\\\\mathfrak{g}}$ boundary at asymptotic infinity and\\ncap off smoothly in \
the interior. The solutions can be uplifted to eleven\\ndimensions and are \
holographically dual to the topologically twisted ABJM\\ntheory on \
$S^1\\\\times \\\\Sigma_{\\\\mathfrak{g}}$. We show explicitly that \
the\\non-shell action of the black saddle solutions agrees exactly with \
the\\ntopologically twisted index of the ABJM theory in the planar limit for \
general\\nvalues of the magnetic fluxes, flavor fugacities, and real masses. \
This\\nagreement relies on a careful holographic renormalization analysis \
combined\\nwith a novel UV/IR holographic relation between supergravity \
parameters and\\nfield theory sources. The Euclidean black saddle solution \
space contains\\nspecial points that can be Wick-rotated to regular \
Lorentzian supergravity\\nbackgrounds that correspond to the well-known \
supersymmetric dyonic AdS$_4$\\nblack holes in the STU model.\\n\""}]}, {
