                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose that the definition of holographic subregion \
complexity (HSC)\\nneeds a slight modification for supergravity solutions \
with warped anti-de\\nSitter (AdS) factors. Such warp factors can arise due \
to the nontrivial dilaton\\nprofile, for example, in $AdS_6$ solutions of \
type IIA supergravity. This\\nmodified definition ensures that the universal \
piece of the HSC is proportional\\nto that of the holographic entanglement \
entropy, as is the case for\\nsupergravity solutions without warp factors. \
This also means that the leading\\nbehaviour at large $N$ is the same for \
both these quantities, as we show for\\nsome well-known supergravity \
solutions (with and without warp factors) in\\nvarious dimensions. We also \
show that this relation between the universal\\npieces suggests \\\"universal\
\\\" relations between field theoretical analogue of HSC\\nand the sphere \
partition function or Weyl $a$-anomaly in odd or even\\ndimensions, \
respectively.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
