Fukelman\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The planar limit of $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal \
quiver theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages, 3 figures, references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the planar limit of both the free energy and \
the expectation value\\nof the $1/2$ BPS Wilson loop for four dimensional \
${\\\\cal N}=2$ superconformal\\nquiver theories, with a product of SU($N$)s \
as gauge group and bi-fundamental\\nmatter. Supersymmetric localization \
reduces the problem to a multi-matrix\\nmodel, that we rewrite in the \
zero-instanton sector as an effective action\\ninvolving an infinite number \
of double-trace terms, determined by the relevant\\nextended Cartan matrix. \
We find that the results, as in the case of\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCFTs with a \
simple gauge group, can be written as sums over\\ntree graphs. For the \
$\\\\widehat{A_1}$ case, we find that the contribution of\\neach tree can be \
interpreted as the partition function of a generalized Ising\\nmodel defined \
on the tree; we conjecture that the partition functions of these\\nmodels \
defined on trees satisfy the Lee-Yang property, i.e. all their zeros lie\\non \
the unit circle.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
