           "id" -> "2006.06379", "submitter" -> "Alan Rios Fukelman", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Bartomeu Fiol, Jairo Mart\\'inez-Montoya and Alan Rios Fukelman",
             "title" -> 
            "The planar limit of $\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal quiver \
theories", "comments" -> "26 pages, 3 figures, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute the planar limit of both the free energy and the \
expectation value\nof the $1/2$ BPS Wilson loop for four dimensional ${\\cal \
N}=2$ superconformal\nquiver theories, with a product of SU($N$)s as gauge \
group and bi-fundamental\nmatter. Supersymmetric localization reduces the \
problem to a multi-matrix\nmodel, that we rewrite in the zero-instanton \
sector as an effective action\ninvolving an infinite number of double-trace \
terms, determined by the relevant\nextended Cartan matrix. We find that the \
results, as in the case of\n$\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCFTs with a simple gauge group, \
can be written as sums over\ntree graphs. For the $\\widehat{A_1}$ case, we \
find that the contribution of\neach tree can be interpreted as the partition \
function of a generalized Ising\nmodel defined on the tree; we conjecture \
that the partition functions of these\nmodels defined on trees satisfy the \
Lee-Yang property, i.e. all their zeros lie\non the unit circle.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
