               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2006.10852\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Simone Giombi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Simone Giombi, Bendeguz Offertaler\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wilson loops in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ $SO(N)$ SYM and \
D-Branes in $AdS_5\\\\times\\n  \\\\mathbb{RP}^5$\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"41 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUPT-2618\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the half-BPS circular Wilson loop in ${\\\\cal \
N}=4$ super Yang-Mills\\nwith orthogonal gauge group. By supersymmetric \
localization, its expectation\\nvalue can be computed exactly from a matrix \
integral over the Lie algebra of\\n$SO(N)$. We focus on the large $N$ limit \
and present some simple quantitative\\ntests of the duality with type IIB \
string theory in $AdS_5\\\\times\\n\\\\mathbb{RP}^5$. In particular, we show \
that the strong coupling limit of the\\nexpectation value of the Wilson loop \
in the spinor representation of the gauge\\ngroup precisely matches the \
classical action of the dual string theory object,\\nwhich is expected to be \
a D5-brane wrapping a $\\\\mathbb{RP}^4$ subspace of\\n$\\\\mathbb{RP}^5$. We \
also briefly discuss the large $N$, large $\\\\lambda$ limits\\nof the \
$SO(N)$ Wilson loop in the symmetric/antisymmetric representations \
and\\ntheir D3/D5-brane duals. Finally, we use the D5-brane description to \
extract\\nthe leading strong coupling behavior of the \\\"bremsstrahlung \
function\\\"\\nassociated to a spinor probe charge, or equivalently the \
normalization of the\\ntwo-point function of the displacement operator on the \
spinor Wilson loop, and\\nobtain agreement with the localization \
prediction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 18 Jun 2020 21:10:35 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-06-22\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Giombi\"", ",", "\"Simone\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Offertaler\"", ",", "\"Bendeguz\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
