           "id" -> "2006.10852", "submitter" -> "Simone Giombi", "authors" -> 
            "Simone Giombi, Bendeguz Offertaler", "title" -> 
            "Wilson loops in $\\mathcal{N}=4$ $SO(N)$ SYM and D-Branes in \
$AdS_5\\times\n  \\mathbb{RP}^5$", "comments" -> "41 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> "PUPT-2618", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the half-BPS circular Wilson loop in ${\\cal N}=4$ \
super Yang-Mills\nwith orthogonal gauge group. By supersymmetric \
localization, its expectation\nvalue can be computed exactly from a matrix \
integral over the Lie algebra of\n$SO(N)$. We focus on the large $N$ limit \
and present some simple quantitative\ntests of the duality with type IIB \
string theory in $AdS_5\\times\n\\mathbb{RP}^5$. In particular, we show that \
the strong coupling limit of the\nexpectation value of the Wilson loop in the \
spinor representation of the gauge\ngroup precisely matches the classical \
action of the dual string theory object,\nwhich is expected to be a D5-brane \
wrapping a $\\mathbb{RP}^4$ subspace of\n$\\mathbb{RP}^5$. We also briefly \
discuss the large $N$, large $\\lambda$ limits\nof the $SO(N)$ Wilson loop in \
the symmetric/antisymmetric representations and\ntheir D3/D5-brane duals. \
Finally, we use the D5-brane description to extract\nthe leading strong \
coupling behavior of the \"bremsstrahlung function\"\nassociated to a spinor \
probe charge, or equivalently the normalization of the\ntwo-point function of \
the displacement operator on the spinor Wilson loop, and\nobtain agreement \
with the localization prediction.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 18 Jun 2020 21:10:35 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-06-22", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Giombi", "Simone", ""}, {
              "Offertaler", "Bendeguz", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
