               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that flag manifold $\\\\sigma$-models \
(including $\\\\mathbb{CP}^{n-1}$,\\nGrassmannian models as special cases) \
and their deformed versions may be cast\\nin the form of gauged bosonic \
Thirring/Gross-Neveu-type systems. Quantum\\nmechanically the gauging is \
violated by chiral anomalies, which may be\\ncancelled by adding fermions. We \
conjecture that such models are integrable and\\ncheck on some examples that \
the trigonometrically deformed geometries satisfy\\nthe generalized Ricci \
flow equations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
