 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We formulate and close the boundary state bootstrap for \
factorizing\\nK-matrices in AdS/CFT. We found that there are no boundary \
degrees of freedom\\nin the boundary bound states, merely the boundary \
parameters are shifted. We\\nuse this family of boundary bound states to \
describe the D3-D5 system for\\nhigher dimensional matrix product states and \
provide their asymptotic overlap\\nformulas. In doing so we generalize the \
nesting for overlaps of matrix product\\nstates and Bethe states.\\n\""}]}, {
