               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The one-loop effects to the Dirac action of $p$-branes \
in a hyperbolic\\nbackground from the path integral and the solution of the \
Wheeler-DeWitt\\nequation are analysed. The objective of comparing the \
equivalent quantization\\nprocedures is to study in detail the validity of \
the semiclassical\\napproximation and divergences associated to one-loop \
corrections. This is in\\nline with a bottom-up approach to holographic \
Wilson loops. We employ the heat\\nkernel regularization method for both \
quantization procedures and we study in\\ngreat detail one-loop corrections \
to geodesics in a 2-dimensional hyperbolic\\nspace and semi-spheres in a \
3-dimensional hyperbolic space. We show that the\\ndivergences, given by the \
high energy expansion of the heat kernel, can be\\nclassified by their \
compatibility with the semiclassical approximation and\\ngeometric nature.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
