               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Simone Giombi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Simone Giombi, Arkady A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Strong coupling expansion of circular Wilson loops and \
string theories\\n  in AdS$_5 \\\\times {\\\\rm S}^5$ and AdS$_4 \\\\times \
{\\\\rm CP}^3$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages. v3: minor corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2020)130\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-AT-2020-05\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the problem of matching the strong coupling \
expansion of the\\n$\\\\frac{1}{2}$ BPS circular Wilson loops in ${\\\\cal \
N}=4$ SYM and ABJM gauge\\ntheories with their string theory duals in \
${\\\\rm AdS}_5 \\\\times S^5$ and ${\\\\rm\\nAdS}_4 \\\\times CP^3$, at the \
first subleading (one-loop) order of the expansion\\naround the minimal \
surface. We observe that, including the overall factor\\n$1/g_{\\\\rm s}$ of \
the inverse string coupling constant, as appropriate for the\\nopen string \
partition function with disk topology, and a universal \
prefactor\\nproportional to the square root of the string tension $T$, both \
the SYM and\\nABJM results precisely match the string theory prediction. We \
provide an\\nexplanation of the origin of the $\\\\sqrt T$ prefactor based on \
special features\\nof the combination of one-loop determinants appearing in \
the string partition\\nfunction. The latter also implies a natural \
generalization $Z_\\\\chi \\\\sim (\\\\sqrt\\nT/g_{\\\\rm s})^\\\\chi$ to \
higher genus contributions with the Euler number $\\\\chi$,\\nwhich is \
consistent with the structure of the $1/N$ corrections found on the\\ngauge \
theory side.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
