           "id" -> "2007.08512", "submitter" -> "Simone Giombi", "authors" -> 
            "Simone Giombi, Arkady A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Strong coupling expansion of circular Wilson loops and string \
theories\n  in AdS$_5 \\times {\\rm S}^5$ and AdS$_4 \\times {\\rm CP}^3$", 
            "comments" -> "28 pages. v3: minor corrections", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP10(2020)130", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AT-2020-05", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We revisit the problem of matching the strong coupling \
expansion of the\n$\\frac{1}{2}$ BPS circular Wilson loops in ${\\cal N}=4$ \
SYM and ABJM gauge\ntheories with their string theory duals in ${\\rm AdS}_5 \
\\times S^5$ and ${\\rm\nAdS}_4 \\times CP^3$, at the first subleading \
(one-loop) order of the expansion\naround the minimal surface. We observe \
that, including the overall factor\n$1/g_{\\rm s}$ of the inverse string \
coupling constant, as appropriate for the\nopen string partition function \
with disk topology, and a universal prefactor\nproportional to the square \
root of the string tension $T$, both the SYM and\nABJM results precisely \
match the string theory prediction. We provide an\nexplanation of the origin \
of the $\\sqrt T$ prefactor based on special features\nof the combination of \
one-loop determinants appearing in the string partition\nfunction. The latter \
also implies a natural generalization $Z_\\chi \\sim (\\sqrt\nT/g_{\\rm \
s})^\\chi$ to higher genus contributions with the Euler number $\\chi$,\n\
which is consistent with the structure of the $1/N$ corrections found on the\n\
gauge theory side.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
