            "  We study the worldsheet scattering theory of the $\\eta$ \
deformation of the\nAdS$_\\mathsf{5} \\times $S$^\\mathsf{5}$ superstring \
corresponding to the purely\nfermionic Dynkin diagram. This theory is a \
Weyl-invariant integrable\ndeformation of the AdS$_\\mathsf{5} \\times \
$S$^\\mathsf{5}$ superstring, with\ntrigonometric quantum-deformed symmetry. \
We compute the two-body worldsheet S\nmatrix of this string in the light-cone \
gauge at tree level to quadratic order\nin fermions. The result factorizes \
into two elementary blocks, and solves the\nclassical Yang-Baxter equation. \
We also determine the corresponding exact\nfactorized S matrix, and show that \
its perturbative expansion matches our\ntree-level results, once we correctly \
identify the deformed light-cone symmetry\nalgebra of the string. Finally, we \
briefly revisit the computation of the\ncorresponding S matrix for the \
$\\eta$ deformation based on the distinguished\nDynkin diagram, finding a \
tree-level S matrix that factorizes and solves the\nclassical Yang-Baxter \
equation, in contrast to previous results.\n", 
