               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Motivated by the BPS/CFT correspondence, we explore the \
similarities between\\nthe classical $\\\\beta$-deformed Hermitean matrix \
model and the $q$-deformed\\nmatrix models associated to 3d \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ supersymmetric gauge theories on\\n$D^2\\\\times_{q}S^1$ \
and $S_b^3$ by matching parameters of the theories. The\\nnovel results that \
we obtain are the correlators for the models, together with\\nan additional \
result in the classical case consisting of the $W$-algebra\\nrepresentation \
of the generating function. Furthermore, we also obtain\\nsurprisingly simple \
expressions for the expectation values of characters which\\ngeneralize \
previously known results.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
