            "  We perform a systematic study of S-duality for ${\\cal N}=2$ \
supersymmetric\nnon-linear abelian theories on a curved manifold. \
Localization can be used to\ncompute certain supersymmetric observables in \
these theories. We point out that\nlocalization and S-duality acting as a \
Legendre transform are not compatible.\nFor these theories S-duality should \
be interpreted as Fourier transform and we\nprovide some evidence for this. \
We also suggest the notion of a coholomological\nprepotential for an abelian \
theory that gives the same partition function as a\ngiven non-abelian \
supersymmetric theory.\n", 
