                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The string theory calculation of the 1/2-BPS circular \
Wilson loop of N=4 SYM\\nin the planar limit at next to leading order at \
strong coupling is revisited in\\nthe ratio of its semiclassical string \
partition function and the one dual to a\\nlatitude Wilson loop with trivial \
expectation value. After applying a conformal\\ntransformation from the disk \
to the cylinder, this problem can be approached by\\nmeans of the \
Gel'fand-Yaglom formalism. Using results from the literature and\\nthe \
exclusion of zero modes from a modified Gel'fand-Yaglom formula, we \
obtain\\nmatching with the known field theory result. As seen in the \
phaseshift method\\ncomputation, non-zero mode contributions cancel and the \
end result comes from\\nthe zero mode degeneracies of the latitude Wilson \
loop.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
