            "  We study $\\mathrm{AdS}_3\\times S^3/\\mathbb{Z}_k\\times \
{\\tilde\nS}^3/\\mathbb{Z}_{k'}$ solutions to M-theory preserving \
$\\mathcal{N}=(0,4)$\nsupersymmetries, arising as near-horizon limits of \
M2-M5 brane intersections\nending on M5'-branes, with both types of \
five-branes placed on A-type\nsingularities. Solutions in this class \
asymptote locally to\n$\\mathrm{AdS}_7/\\mathbb{Z}_k\\times {\\tilde \
S}^3/\\mathbb{Z}_{k'}$, and can thus\nbe interpreted as holographic duals to \
surface defect CFTs within the\n$\\mathcal{N}=(1,0)$ 6d CFT dual to this \
solution. Upon reduction to Type IIA,\nwe obtain a new class of solutions of \
the form $\\mathrm{AdS}_3\\times\nS^3/\\mathbb{Z}_k\\times S^2 \\times \
\\Sigma_2$ preserving (0,4) supersymmetries.\nWe construct explicit 2d quiver \
CFTs dual to these solutions, describing D2-D4\nsurface defects embedded \
within the 6d (1,0) quiver CFT dual to the\n$\\mathrm{AdS}_7/\\mathbb{Z}_k$ \
solution to massless IIA. Finally, in the massive\ncase, we show that the \
recently constructed $\\mathrm{AdS}_3\\times S^2\\times\n\\mathrm{CY}_2$ \
solutions with $\\mathcal{N}=(0,4)$ supersymmetries gain a defect\n\
interpretation when $\\mathrm{CY}_2=T^4$ as surface CFTs originating from\n\
D2-NS5-D6 defects embedded within the 5d CFT dual to the Brandhuber-Oz\n\
$\\mathrm{AdS}_6$ background.\n", 
