 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study several quiver Chern-Simons-matter theories on \
the three-sphere,\\ncombining the matrix model formulation with a systematic \
use of Mordell's\\nintegral, computing partition functions and checking \
dualities. We also\\nconsider Wilson loops in ABJ(M) theories, distinguishing \
between typical (long)\\nand atypical (short) representations and focusing on \
the former. Using the\\nBerele-Regev factorization of supersymmetric Schur \
polynomials, we express the\\nexpectation value of the Wilson loops in terms \
of sums of observables of two\\nfactorized copies of $U(N)$ pure Chern-Simons \
theory on the sphere. Then, we\\nuse the Cauchy identity to study the \
partition functions of a number of quiver\\nChern-Simons-matter models and \
the result is interpreted as a perturbative\\nexpansion in the parameters \
$t_j = - e^{2 \\\\pi m_j}$, where $m_j$ are the\\nmasses. Through the paper, \
we incorporate different generalizations, such as\\ndeformations by real \
masses and/or Fayet-Iliopoulos parameters, the\\nconsideration of a Romans \
mass in the gravity dual, and adjoint matter.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
