 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We develop a new way to calculate the overlap of a \
boundary state with a\\nfinite volume bulk state in the truncated conformal \
space approach. We check\\nthis method in the thermally perturbed Ising model \
analytically, while in the\\nscaling Lee-Yang model numerically by comparing \
our results to excited state\\ng-functions, which we obtained by the \
analytical continuation method. We also\\ngive a simple argument for the \
structure of the asymptotic overlap between the\\nfinite volume boundary \
state and a periodic multiparticle state, which includes\\nthe ratio of \
Gaudin type determinants.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
