Wang, and\\n  Congkao Wen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"New Modular Invariants in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
Super-Yang-Mills Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages plus appendices, v2 accepted to JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2021)212\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PUPT-2620, QMUL-PH-20-16\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study modular invariants arising in the four-point \
functions of the stress\\ntensor multiplet operators of the ${\\\\cal N} = 4$ \
$SU(N)$ super-Yang-Mills\\ntheory, in the limit where $N$ is taken to be \
large while the complexified\\nYang-Mills coupling $\\\\tau$ is held fixed. \
The specific four-point functions we\\nconsider are integrated correlators \
obtained by taking various combinations of\\nfour derivatives of the squashed \
sphere partition function of the ${\\\\cal N} =\\n2^*$ theory with respect to \
the squashing parameter $b$ and mass parameter $m$,\\nevaluated at the values \
$b=1$ and $m=0$ that correspond to the ${\\\\cal N} = 4$\\ntheory on a round \
sphere. At each order in the $1/N$ expansion, these fourth\\nderivatives are \
modular invariant functions of $(\\\\tau, \\\\bar \\\\tau)$. We \
present\\nevidence that at half-integer orders in $1/N$, these modular \
invariants are\\nlinear combinations of non-holomorphic Eisenstein series, \
while at integer\\norders in $1/N$, they are certain \\\"generalized \
Eisenstein series\\\" which satisfy\\ninhomogeneous Laplace eigenvalue \
equations on the hyperbolic plane. These\\nresults reproduce known features \
of the low-energy expansion of the\\nfour-graviton amplitude in type IIB \
superstring theory in ten-dimensional flat\\nspace and have interesting \
implications for the structure of the analogous\\nexpansion in \
$AdS_5\\\\times S^5$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 6 Aug 2020 15:30:52 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
