                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Adrita Chakraborty and Kamal L. Panigrahi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Neumann-Rosochatius system for (m,n) string in $AdS_3 \
\\\\times S^3$ with\\n  mixed flux\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25 pages, better presented, abstract modified, some typos \
corrected,\\n  added references, version to appear in EPJC\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1140/epjc/s10052-021-09067-y\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  $SL(2,\\\\mathbb{Z})$ invariant action for probe \
$(m,n)$ string in $AdS_3\\\\times\\nS^3\\\\times T^4$ with mixed three-form \
fluxes can be described by an integrable\\ndeformation of an one-dimensional \
Neumann-Rosochatius (NR) system. We present\\nthe deformed features of the \
integrable model and study general class of\\nrotating and pulsating \
solutions by solving the integrable equations of motion.\\nFor the rotating \
string, the explicit solutions can be expressed in terms of\\nelliptic \
functions. We make use of the integrals of motion to find out the\\nscaling \
relation among conserved charges for the particular case of constant\\nradii \
solutions. Then we study the closed $(m,n)$ string pulsating \
in\\n$R_t\\\\times S^3$. We find the string profile and calculate the total \
energy of\\nsuch pulsating string in terms of oscillation number \
$(\\\\cal{N})$ and angular\\nmomentum $(\\\\cal{J})$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
