           "id" -> "2008.05139", "submitter" -> "Adrita Chakraborty", 
            "authors" -> "Adrita Chakraborty and Kamal L. Panigrahi", "title" -> 
            "Neumann-Rosochatius system for (m,n) string in $AdS_3 \\times \
S^3$ with\n  mixed flux", "comments" -> 
            "25 pages, better presented, abstract modified, some typos \
corrected,\n  added references, version to appear in EPJC", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1140/epjc/s10052-021-09067-y", "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  $SL(2,\\mathbb{Z})$ invariant action for probe $(m,n)$ string \
in $AdS_3\\times\nS^3\\times T^4$ with mixed three-form fluxes can be \
described by an integrable\ndeformation of an one-dimensional \
Neumann-Rosochatius (NR) system. We present\nthe deformed features of the \
integrable model and study general class of\nrotating and pulsating solutions \
by solving the integrable equations of motion.\nFor the rotating string, the \
explicit solutions can be expressed in terms of\nelliptic functions. We make \
use of the integrals of motion to find out the\nscaling relation among \
conserved charges for the particular case of constant\nradii solutions. Then \
we study the closed $(m,n)$ string pulsating in\n$R_t\\times S^3$. We find \
the string profile and calculate the total energy of\nsuch pulsating string \
in terms of oscillation number $(\\cal{N})$ and angular\nmomentum \
$(\\cal{J})$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
