               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008.06901\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dinh-Long Vu\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dinh-Long Vu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A diagrammatic approach towards the thermodynamics of \
integrable systems\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PhD thesis, 137 pages, 40 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose an exact summation method to compute \
thermodynamic observables in\\nintegrable quantum field theories. The key \
idea is to use the matrix-tree\\ntheorem to write the Gaudin determinants \
that appear in the cluster expansion\\nas a sum over graphs. For theories \
with a diagonal S-matrix, this method is\\nmore powerful than the standard \
Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz (TBA) technique as\\nit is exact to all orders of \
powers in inverse volume. We have obtained using\\nthis method the TBA \
equation, the excited state energies in finite volume, the\\nLeclair-Mussardo \
formula for one point functions, the finite-temperature\\nboundary entropy \
and cumulants of conserved charges in Generalized Gibbs\\nEnsembles. \
Moreover, the graph expansion can also be regarded as an alternative\\nto \
algebraic manipulations involving Gaudin determinants. We have applied \
this\\nidea to derive the equations of state and other transport properties \
in\\nGeneralized Hydrodynamics. For theories with a non-diagonal S-matrix, \
the\\ndescription of a complete set of states is more involved and it is not \
known\\nhow a cluster expansion can be implemented. It is nevertheless \
possible to\\napply the direct summation method in reverse and interpret \
known TBA equations\\nwith complex strings in terms of diagrams.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 16 Aug 2020 13:04:59 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2020-08-18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Vu\"", ",", "\"Dinh-Long\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2008.06901", "submitter" -> "Dinh-Long Vu", "authors" -> 
            "Dinh-Long Vu", "title" -> 
            "A diagrammatic approach towards the thermodynamics of integrable \
systems", "comments" -> "PhD thesis, 137 pages, 40 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We propose an exact summation method to compute thermodynamic \
observables in\nintegrable quantum field theories. The key idea is to use the \
matrix-tree\ntheorem to write the Gaudin determinants that appear in the \
cluster expansion\nas a sum over graphs. For theories with a diagonal \
S-matrix, this method is\nmore powerful than the standard Thermodynamic Bethe \
Ansatz (TBA) technique as\nit is exact to all orders of powers in inverse \
volume. We have obtained using\nthis method the TBA equation, the excited \
state energies in finite volume, the\nLeclair-Mussardo formula for one point \
functions, the finite-temperature\nboundary entropy and cumulants of \
conserved charges in Generalized Gibbs\nEnsembles. Moreover, the graph \
expansion can also be regarded as an alternative\nto algebraic manipulations \
involving Gaudin determinants. We have applied this\nidea to derive the \
equations of state and other transport properties in\nGeneralized \
Hydrodynamics. For theories with a non-diagonal S-matrix, the\ndescription of \
a complete set of states is more involved and it is not known\nhow a cluster \
expansion can be implemented. It is nevertheless possible to\napply the \
direct summation method in reverse and interpret known TBA equations\nwith \
complex strings in terms of diagrams.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 16 Aug 2020 13:04:59 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-08-18", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Vu", "Dinh-Long", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
