               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonrelativistic spinning strings\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex, 19 pages, Revised version, Version accepted in \
JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 11 (2020) 044\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2020)044\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct nonrelativistic spinning string solutions \
corresponding to $\\nSU(1,2|3) $ Spin-Matrix theory (SMT) limit of strings in \
$ AdS_5 \\\\times S^5 $.\\nConsidering various nonrelativistic spinning \
string configurations both in $\\nAdS_5 $ as well as $ S^5 $ we obtain \
corresponding dispersion relations in the\\nstrong coupling regime of SMT \
where the strong coupling ($ \\\\sim\\n\\\\sqrt{\\\\mathfrak{g}} $) \
corrections near the BPS bound have been estimated in\\nthe slow spinning \
limit of strings in $ AdS_5 $. We generalize our results\\nexplicitly by \
constructing three spin folded string configurations that has two\\nof its \
spins along $ AdS_5 $ and one along $ S^5 $. Our analysis reveals that\\nthe \
correction to the spectrum depends non trivially on the length of the \
NR\\nstring in $ AdS_5 $. The rest of the paper essentially unfolds the \
underlying\\nconnection between $ SU(1,2|3) $ Spin-Matrix theory (SMT) limit \
of strings in $\\nAdS_5 \\\\times S^5 $ and the nonrelativistic \
Neumann-Rosochatius like integrable\\nmodels in 1D. Taking two specific \
examples of NR spinning strings in $ R \\\\times\\nS^3 $ as well as in \
certain sub-sector of $ AdS_5 $ we show that similar\\nreduction is indeed \
possible where one can estimate the spectrum of the theory\\nusing 1D \
model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
