 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  These are lecture notes for a short course given at the \
Les Houches Summer\\nSchool on ``Integrability in Atomic and Condensed Matter \
Physics'', in summer\\n2018. Here, I pedagogically discuss recent advances in \
the study of the\\nentanglement spreading during the non-equilibrium dynamics \
of isolated\\nintegrable quantum systems. I first introduce the idea that the \
stationary\\nthermodynamic entropy is the entanglement accumulated during the\
\\nnon-equilibrium dynamics and then join such an idea with the quasiparticle\
\\npicture for the entanglement spreading to provide quantitive predictions \
for\\nthe time evolution of the entanglement entropy in arbitrary integrable \
models,\\nregardless of the interaction strength.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
