               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Johannes Branahl (1), Alexander Hock (2), Raimar \
Wulkenhaar (1) ((1)\\n  M\\\\\\\"unster, (2) Oxford)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Blobbed topological recursion of the quartic Kontsevich \
model I: Loop\\n  equations and conjectures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages, 13 figures. v2: proofs in appendix E \
considerably\\n  simplified, typos corrected. v3: added reference \
arXiv:2103.13271, where we\\n  have proved the main conjecture for $g=0$. v4: \
rearrangements to improve\\n  readability, graphical interpretation of loop \
equations added, analogies to\\n  the 2-matrix model emphasised\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Communications in Mathematical Physics 393, 1529-1582 \
(2022)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s00220-022-04392-z\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math-ph hep-th math.AG math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We provide strong evidence for the conjecture that the \
analogue of\\nKontsevich's matrix Airy function, with the cubic potential\\n$\
\\\\mathrm{Tr}(\\\\Phi^3)$ replaced by a quartic term \
$\\\\mathrm{Tr}(\\\\Phi^4)$, obeys\\nthe blobbed topological recursion of \
Borot and Shadrin. We identify in the\\nquartic Kontsevich model three \
families of correlation functions for which we\\nestablish interwoven loop \
equations. One family consists of symmetric\\nmeromorphic differential forms \
$\\\\omega_{g,n}$ labelled by genus and number of\\nmarked points of a \
complex curve. We reduce the solution of all loop equations\\nto a \
straightforward but lengthy evaluation of residues. In all evaluated\\ncases, \
the $\\\\omega_{g,n}$ consist of a part with poles at ramification \
points\\nwhich satisfies the universal formula of topological recursion, and \
of a part\\nholomorphic at ramification points for which we provide an \
explicit residue\\nformula.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
