            "  We provide strong evidence for the conjecture that the \
analogue of\nKontsevich's matrix Airy function, with the cubic potential\n\
$\\mathrm{Tr}(\\Phi^3)$ replaced by a quartic term $\\mathrm{Tr}(\\Phi^4)$, \
obeys\nthe blobbed topological recursion of Borot and Shadrin. We identify in \
the\nquartic Kontsevich model three families of correlation functions for \
which we\nestablish interwoven loop equations. One family consists of \
symmetric\nmeromorphic differential forms $\\omega_{g,n}$ labelled by genus \
and number of\nmarked points of a complex curve. We reduce the solution of \
all loop equations\nto a straightforward but lengthy evaluation of residues. \
In all evaluated\ncases, the $\\omega_{g,n}$ consist of a part with poles at \
ramification points\nwhich satisfies the universal formula of topological \
recursion, and of a part\nholomorphic at ramification points for which we \
provide an explicit residue\nformula.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
