               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008.12600\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Johan Henriksson\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Johan Henriksson\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Analytic Bootstrap for Perturbative Conformal Field \
Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"DPhil thesis. 221 pages, 11 figures. Sections 6.3 and 6.4 \
contain\\n  some previously unpublished results. v2: typos corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Conformal field theories play a central role in \
theoretical physics with many\\napplications ranging from condensed matter to \
string theory. The conformal\\nbootstrap studies conformal field theories \
using mathematical consistency\\nconditions and has seen great progress over \
the last decade. In this thesis we\\npresent an implementation of analytic \
bootstrap methods for perturbative\\nconformal field theories in dimensions \
greater than two, which we achieve by\\ncombining large spin perturbation \
theory with the Lorentzian inversion formula.\\nIn the presence of a small \
expansion parameter, not necessarily the coupling\\nconstant, we develop this \
into a systematic framework, applicable to a wide\\nrange of theories. The \
first two chapters provide the necessary background and\\na review of the \
analytic bootstrap. This is followed by a chapter which\\ndescribes the \
method in detail, taking the form of a practical guide to large\\nspin \
perturbation theory by means of a step-by-step implementation. The \
second\\npart of the thesis presents several explicit implementations of the \
framework,\\ntaking examples from a number of well-studied conformal field \
theories. We show\\nhow many literature results can be reproduced from a \
purely bootstrap\\nperspective and how a variety of new results can be \
derived.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 28 Aug 2020 12:06:43 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 8 Apr 2021 13:37:46 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
