            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Conformal field theories play a central role in theoretical \
physics with many\napplications ranging from condensed matter to string \
theory. The conformal\nbootstrap studies conformal field theories using \
mathematical consistency\nconditions and has seen great progress over the \
last decade. In this thesis we\npresent an implementation of analytic \
bootstrap methods for perturbative\nconformal field theories in dimensions \
greater than two, which we achieve by\ncombining large spin perturbation \
theory with the Lorentzian inversion formula.\nIn the presence of a small \
expansion parameter, not necessarily the coupling\nconstant, we develop this \
into a systematic framework, applicable to a wide\nrange of theories. The \
first two chapters provide the necessary background and\na review of the \
analytic bootstrap. This is followed by a chapter which\ndescribes the method \
in detail, taking the form of a practical guide to large\nspin perturbation \
theory by means of a step-by-step implementation. The second\npart of the \
thesis presents several explicit implementations of the framework,\ntaking \
examples from a number of well-studied conformal field theories. We show\nhow \
many literature results can be reproduced from a purely bootstrap\n\
perspective and how a variety of new results can be derived.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 28 Aug 2020 12:06:43 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 8 Apr 2021 13:37:46 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
