                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A large class of integrable deformations of the \
Principal Chiral Model, known\\nas the Yang-Baxter deformations, are governed \
by skew-symmetric R-matrices\\nsolving the (modified) classical Yang-Baxter \
equation. We carry out a\\nsystematic investigation of these deformations in \
the presence of the\\nWess-Zumino term for simple Lie groups, working in a \
framework that treats both\\ninhomogeneous and homogeneous deformations on \
the same footing. After analysing\\nthe cohomological conditions under which \
such a deformation is admissible, we\\nconsider an action for the general \
Yang-Baxter deformation of the Principal\\nChiral Model plus Wess-Zumino term \
and prove its classical integrability. We\\nalso show how the model is found \
from a number of alternative formulations:\\naffine Gaudin models, E-models, \
4-dimensional Chern-Simons theory and, for\\nhomogeneous deformations, \
non-abelian T-duality.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
