                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"H. Dimov, I. N. Iliev, M. Radomirov, R. C. Rashkov, T. \
Vetsov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic Fisher Information Metric in \
Schr\\\\\\\"odinger Spacetime\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Minor corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we study the Fisher information metric on \
the space of the\\ncoupling constants on both sides of the duality between \
non-relativistic dipole\\nfield theories and string theory in \
Schr\\\\\\\"odinger spacetime. We consider the\\nfollowing setup. In the \
gauge theory side one can deform a given conformal\\nfield theory by a proper \
scalar operator and compute the quantum information\\nmetric via the \
two-point correlation function between two such operators. On\\nthe string \
side the deformation corresponds to a scalar field probing the\\nbackground. \
In the large $N$ limit of the theory the probing can be done\\nwithout \
backreaction on the original spacetime, thus one can construct \
a\\nperturbative scheme for the calculation of the dual holographic \
Fisher\\ninformation metric as shown by \\\\cite{Trivella:2016brw}. \
Considering the\\nasymptotic behaviour of the holographic Fisher information \
metric close to the\\nboundary of the Schr\\\\\\\"odinger spacetime we show \
that its divergence structure\\nexactly matches its dual quantum counterpart \
up to the leading order, thus\\nextending the holographic setup up to the \
non-relativistic case. One should\\nnote that the existence of other terms \
are not seen from the boundary theory to\\nthis level of approximation. Their \
behaviour near the boundary however, is\\npointing what kind of information \
from the boundary theory is missing to be\\nable to reconstruct the bulk. \
Obviously more work is needed to refine and\\nelucidate their meaning and \
interrelations in holographic setup.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
