            "  In this paper we study the Fisher information metric on the \
space of the\ncoupling constants on both sides of the duality between \
non-relativistic dipole\nfield theories and string theory in Schr\\\"odinger \
spacetime. We consider the\nfollowing setup. In the gauge theory side one can \
deform a given conformal\nfield theory by a proper scalar operator and \
compute the quantum information\nmetric via the two-point correlation \
function between two such operators. On\nthe string side the deformation \
corresponds to a scalar field probing the\nbackground. In the large $N$ limit \
of the theory the probing can be done\nwithout backreaction on the original \
spacetime, thus one can construct a\nperturbative scheme for the calculation \
of the dual holographic Fisher\ninformation metric as shown by \
\\cite{Trivella:2016brw}. Considering the\nasymptotic behaviour of the \
holographic Fisher information metric close to the\nboundary of the \
Schr\\\"odinger spacetime we show that its divergence structure\nexactly \
matches its dual quantum counterpart up to the leading order, thus\nextending \
the holographic setup up to the non-relativistic case. One should\nnote that \
the existence of other terms are not seen from the boundary theory to\nthis \
level of approximation. Their behaviour near the boundary however, is\n\
pointing what kind of information from the boundary theory is missing to be\n\
able to reconstruct the bulk. Obviously more work is needed to refine and\n\
elucidate their meaning and interrelations in holographic setup.\n", 
