 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze symmetries corresponding to separated \
topological sectors of 3d\\n${\\\\cal} N=4$ gauge theories with Higgs vacua, \
compactified on a circle. The\\nsymmetries are encoded in Schwinger-Dyson \
identities satisfied by correlation\\nfunctions of a certain gauge-invariant \
operator, the \\\"vortex character.\\\" Such a\\ncharacter observable is \
realized as the vortex partition function of the 3d\\ngauge theory, in the \
presence of a 1/2-BPS line defect. The character enjoys a\\ndouble \
refinement, interpreted as a deformation of the usual characters \
of\\nfinite-dimensional representations of quantum affine algebras. We derive \
and\\ninterpret the Schwinger-Dyson identities for the 3d theory from various\
\\nphysical perspectives: in the 3d gauge theory itself, in a 1d gauged \
quantum\\nmechanics, in 2d $q$-Toda theory, and in 6d little string theory. \
We establish\\nthe dictionary between all approaches. Lastly, we comment on \
the transformation\\nproperties of the vortex character under the action of \
three-dimensional\\nSeiberg duality.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
