 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We establish a correspondence between a class of \
Wilson-'t Hooft lines in\\nfour-dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N} = 2$ \
supersymmetric gauge theories described by\\ncircular quivers and transfer \
matrices constructed from dynamical L-operators\\nfor trigonometric quantum \
integrable systems. We compute the vacuum expectation\\nvalues of the \
Wilson-'t Hooft lines in a twisted product space $S^1\\n\\\\times_\\\\epsilon \
\\\\mathbb{R}^2 \\\\times \\\\mathbb{R}$ by supersymmetric localization\\nand \
show that they are equal to the Wigner transforms of the transfer \
matrices.\\nA variant of the AGT correspondence implies an identification of \
the transfer\\nmatrices with Verlinde operators in Toda theory, which we also \
verify. We\\nexplain how these field theory setups are related to \
four-dimensional\\nChern-Simons theory via embedding into string theory and \
dualities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
