 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Every six-dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N}=(2,0)$ SCFT on \
$\\\\mathbf{R}^6$ contains a\\nset of protected operators whose correlation \
functions are controlled by a\\ntwo-dimensional chiral algebra. We provide an \
alternative construction of this\\nchiral algebra by performing an \
$\\\\Omega$-deformation~of a\\ntopological-holomorphic twist of the \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=(2,0)$ theory on\\n$\\\\mathbf{R}^6$ and restricting to the \
cohomology of a specific supercharge. In\\naddition, we show that the central \
charge of the chiral algebra can be obtained\\nby performing equivariant \
integration of the anomaly polynomial of the\\nsix-dimensional theory. \
Furthermore, we generalize this construction to include\\norbifolds of the \
$\\\\mathbf{R}^4$ transverse to the chiral algebra plane.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
