         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2010.02267", "submitter" -> "Pieter Bomans", "authors" -> 
            "Nikolay Bobev, Pieter Bomans and Fridrik Freyr Gautason", 
            "title" -> 
            "Comments on chiral algebras and $\\Omega$-deformations", 
            "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP04(2021)132", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Every six-dimensional $\\mathcal{N}=(2,0)$ SCFT on \
$\\mathbf{R}^6$ contains a\nset of protected operators whose correlation \
functions are controlled by a\ntwo-dimensional chiral algebra. We provide an \
alternative construction of this\nchiral algebra by performing an \
$\\Omega$-deformation~of a\ntopological-holomorphic twist of the \
$\\mathcal{N}=(2,0)$ theory on\n$\\mathbf{R}^6$ and restricting to the \
cohomology of a specific supercharge. In\naddition, we show that the central \
charge of the chiral algebra can be obtained\nby performing equivariant \
integration of the anomaly polynomial of the\nsix-dimensional theory. \
Furthermore, we generalize this construction to include\norbifolds of the \
$\\mathbf{R}^4$ transverse to the chiral algebra plane.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 5 Oct 2020 18:25:57 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 21 May 2021 07:16:22 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2021-05-24", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Bobev", "Nikolay", ""}, {
              "Bomans", "Pieter", ""}, {"Gautason", "Fridrik Freyr", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{15.752325115703645`, -4.709198278315685}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2010.03952\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dimitrios Zoakos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"George Georgiou, Dimitrios Zoakos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Giant Gravitons in the Schrodinger holography\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"20 pages, 8 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2021)017\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct and study new giant graviton \
configurations in the framework of\\nthe non-supersymmetric Schrodinger \
holography. We confirm in the original\\nSchrodinger spacetime, the picture \
discovered previously in the pp-wave limit\\nof the geometry, namely that it \
is the giant graviton that becomes the\\nenergetically favored stable \
configuration compared to the point graviton one.\\nFurthermore, there is a \
critical value of the deformation above which the point\\ngraviton disappears \
from the spectrum. The former fact leads also to the\\npossibility of \
tunnelling from the point graviton to the giant graviton\\nconfiguration. We \
calculate, explicitly, the instanton solution and its\\ncorresponding action \
which gives a measure of the tunnelling probability.\\nFinally, we evaluate \
holographically the three-point correlation function of\\ntwo giant gravitons \
and one dilaton mode as a function of the Schrodinger\\ninvariant.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 8 Oct 2020 13:24:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
