            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct and study new giant graviton configurations in \
the framework of\nthe non-supersymmetric Schrodinger holography. We confirm \
in the original\nSchrodinger spacetime, the picture discovered previously in \
the pp-wave limit\nof the geometry, namely that it is the giant graviton that \
becomes the\nenergetically favored stable configuration compared to the point \
graviton one.\nFurthermore, there is a critical value of the deformation \
above which the point\ngraviton disappears from the spectrum. The former fact \
leads also to the\npossibility of tunnelling from the point graviton to the \
giant graviton\nconfiguration. We calculate, explicitly, the instanton \
solution and its\ncorresponding action which gives a measure of the \
tunnelling probability.\nFinally, we evaluate holographically the three-point \
correlation function of\ntwo giant gravitons and one dilaton mode as a \
function of the Schrodinger\ninvariant.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
