                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Semi-classical quantisation of magnetic solitons in the \
anisotropic\\n  Heisenberg quantum chain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"61 pages, 14 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SciPost Phys. 10, 086 (2021)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.21468/SciPostPhys.10.4.086\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.str-el hep-th math-ph math.MP \
quant-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the algebro-geometric approach, we study the \
structure of\\nsemi-classical eigenstates in a weakly-anisotropic quantum \
Heisenberg spin\\nchain. We outline how classical nonlinear spin waves \
governed by the\\nanisotropic Landau-Lifshitz equation arise as coherent \
macroscopic low-energy\\nfluctuations of the ferromagnetic ground state. \
Special emphasis is devoted to\\nthe simplest types of solutions, describing \
precessional motion and elliptic\\nmagnetisation waves. The internal magnon \
structure of classical spin waves is\\nresolved by performing the \
semi-classical quantisation using the\\nRiemann-Hilbert problem approach. We \
present an expression for the overlap of\\ntwo semi-classical eigenstates and \
discuss how correlation functions at the\\nsemi-classical level arise from \
classical phase-space averaging.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
