                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mark Van Raamsdonk and Christopher Waddell\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic and Localization Calculations of Boundary F \
for ${\\\\cal N} =\\n  4$ SUSY Yang-Mills Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Reference added; minor typos corrected in Section 2.2 and \
equations\\n  (3.13), (3.14), (3.21), (3.23); terms rearranged in equation \
(4.19)\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2021)222\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  ${\\\\cal N} = 4$ Supersymmetric Yang-Mills (SYM) \
theory can be defined on a\\nhalf-space with a variety of boundary conditions \
preserving scale invariance\\nand half of the original supersymmetry; more \
general theories with the same\\nsymmetry can be obtained by coupling to a 3D \
SCFT at the boundary. Each of\\nthese theories is characterized by a quantity \
called \\\"boundary $F$\\\",\\nconjectured to decrease under boundary \
renormalization group flows. In this\\npaper, we calculate boundary $F$ for \
$U(N)$ ${\\\\cal N} = 4$ SYM theory with the\\nmost general \
half-supersymmetric boundary conditions arising from string \
theory\\nconstructions with D3-branes ending on collections of D5-branes \
and/or\\nNS5-branes. We first perform the calculation holographically by \
evaluating the\\nentanglement entropy for a half-ball centered on the \
boundary using the\\nRyu-Takayanagi formula in the dual type IIB supergravity \
solutions. For\\nboundary conditions associated with D3-branes ending on D5 \
branes only or\\nNS5-branes only, we also calculate boundary $F$ exactly by \
evaluating the\\nhemisphere partition function using supersymmetric \
localization. The leading\\nterm at large $N$ in the supergravity and \
localization results agree exactly as\\na function of the t' Hooft coupling $\
\\\\lambda$.\\n\""}]}, {
