               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gerben Oling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Troels Harmark, Jelle Hartong, Niels A. Obers, Gerben \
Oling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spin Matrix Theory String Backgrounds and Penrose Limits \
of AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"32 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2021)129\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NORDITA-2020-100\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Spin Matrix theory (SMT) limits provide a way to \
capture the dynamics of the\\nAdS/CFT correspondence near BPS bounds. On the \
string theory side, these limits\\nresult in non-relativistic sigma models \
that can be interpreted as novel\\nnon-relativistic strings. This SMT string \
theory couples to non-relativistic\\n$U(1)$-Galilean background geometries. \
In this paper, we explore the relation\\nbetween pp-wave backgrounds obtained \
from Penrose limits of AdS${}_5 \\\\times\\nS^5$, and a new type of \
$U(1)$-Galilean backgrounds that we call flat-fluxed\\n(FF) backgrounds. \
These FF backgrounds are the simplest possible SMT string\\nbackgrounds and \
correspond to free magnons from the spin chain perspective. We\\nprovide a \
catalogue of the $U(1)$-Galilean backgrounds one obtains from SMT\\nlimits of \
string theory on AdS${}_5 \\\\times S^5$ and subsequently study \
large\\ncharge limits of these geometries from which the FF backgrounds \
emerge. We show\\nthat these limits are analogous to Penrose limits of \
AdS${}_5 \\\\times S^5$ and\\ndemonstrate that the large charge/Penrose \
limits commute with the SMT limits.\\nFinally, we point out that \
$U(1)$-Galilean backgrounds prescribe a symplectic\\nmanifold for the \
transverse SMT string embedding fields. This is illustrated\\nwith a \
Hamiltonian derivation for the SMT limit of a particle.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
