            "Troels Harmark, Jelle Hartong, Niels A. Obers, Gerben Oling", 
            "title" -> 
            "Spin Matrix Theory String Backgrounds and Penrose Limits of \
AdS/CFT", "comments" -> "32 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP03(2021)129", "report-no" -> "NORDITA-2020-100", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Spin Matrix theory (SMT) limits provide a way to capture the \
dynamics of the\nAdS/CFT correspondence near BPS bounds. On the string theory \
side, these limits\nresult in non-relativistic sigma models that can be \
interpreted as novel\nnon-relativistic strings. This SMT string theory \
couples to non-relativistic\n$U(1)$-Galilean background geometries. In this \
paper, we explore the relation\nbetween pp-wave backgrounds obtained from \
Penrose limits of AdS${}_5 \\times\nS^5$, and a new type of $U(1)$-Galilean \
backgrounds that we call flat-fluxed\n(FF) backgrounds. These FF backgrounds \
are the simplest possible SMT string\nbackgrounds and correspond to free \
magnons from the spin chain perspective. We\nprovide a catalogue of the \
$U(1)$-Galilean backgrounds one obtains from SMT\nlimits of string theory on \
AdS${}_5 \\times S^5$ and subsequently study large\ncharge limits of these \
geometries from which the FF backgrounds emerge. We show\nthat these limits \
are analogous to Penrose limits of AdS${}_5 \\times S^5$ and\ndemonstrate \
that the large charge/Penrose limits commute with the SMT limits.\nFinally, \
we point out that $U(1)$-Galilean backgrounds prescribe a symplectic\n\
manifold for the transverse SMT string embedding fields. This is illustrated\n\
with a Hamiltonian derivation for the SMT limit of a particle.\n", 
