 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Starting with some known localization (matrix model) \
representations for\\ncorrelators involving 1/2 BPS circular Wilson loop \
$\\\\cal W$ in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM\\ntheory we work out their $1/N$ \
expansions in the limit of large 't Hooft\\ncoupling $\\\\lambda$. Motivated \
by a possibility of eventual matching to higher\\ngenus corrections in dual \
string theory we follow arXiv:2007.08512 and express\\nthe result in terms of \
the string coupling $g_{\\\\rm s} \\\\sim g^2_{\\\\rm YM} \
\\\\sim\\n\\\\lambda/N$ and string tension $T\\\\sim \\\\sqrt \\\\lambda$. \
Keeping only the leading\\nin $1/T$ term at each order in $g_{\\\\rm s} $ we \
observe that while the expansion\\nof $\\\\langle {\\\\cal W} \\\\rangle$ is \
a series in $g^2_{\\\\rm s} /T$, the correlator\\nof the Wilson loop with \
chiral primary operators ${\\\\cal O}_J $ has expansion in\\npowers of $g^2_{\
\\\\rm s}/T^2$. Like in the case of $\\\\langle {\\\\cal W} \
\\\\rangle$\\nwhere these leading terms are known to resum into an \
exponential of a\\n\\\"one-handle\\\" contribution $\\\\sim g^2_{\\\\rm s} \
/T$, the leading strong coupling\\nterms in $\\\\langle {\\\\cal W}\\\\, \
{\\\\cal O}_J \\\\rangle$ sum up to a simple square root\\nfunction of $g^2_{\
\\\\rm s}/T^2$. Analogous expansions in powers of $g^2_{\\\\rm\\ns}/T$ are \
found for correlators of several coincident Wilson loops and they\\nagain \
have a simple resummed form. We also find similar expansions \
for\\ncorrelators of coincident 1/2 BPS Wilson loops in the ABJM \
theory.\\n\""}]}, {
