            "authors" -> "Tristan McLoughlin, Raul Pereira and Anne Spiering",
             "title" -> 
            "Quantum Chaos in Perturbative super-Yang-Mills Theory", 
            "comments" -> "8 pages, 12 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> "TCDMATH 20-13, SAGEX-20-25", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th nlin.CD", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We provide numerical evidence that the perturbative spectrum \
of anomalous\ndimensions in maximally supersymmetric SU(N) Yang-Mills theory \
is chaotic at\nfinite values of N. We calculate the probability distribution \
of one-loop level\nspacings for subsectors of the theory and show that for \
large N it is given by\nthe Poisson distribution of integrable models, while \
at finite values it is the\nWigner-Dyson distribution of the Gaussian \
orthogonal ensemble random matrix\ntheory. We extend these results to \
two-loop order and to a one-parameter family\nof deformations. We further \
study the spectral rigidity for these models and\nshow that it is also well \
described by random matrix theory. Finally we\ndemonstrate that the finite-N \
eigenvectors possess properties of chaotic\nstates.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
