               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Julien Barrat\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Julien Barrat, Pedro Liendo, Jan Plefka\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Two-Point Correlator of Chiral Primary Operators with a \
Wilson Line\\n  Defect in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"48 pages, 5 figures, 3 tables\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2021)195\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"HU-EP-20/33-RTG, DESY 20-191\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the two-point function of the stress-tensor \
multiplet of\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM in the presence of a line defect. To be \
more precise, we\\nfocus on the single-trace operator of conformal dimension \
two that sits in the\\n$20'$ irrep of the $\\\\mathfrak{so}(6)_\\\\text{R}$ \
R-symmetry, and add a\\nMaldacena-Wilson line to the configuration which \
makes the two-point function\\nnon-trivial. We use a combination of \
perturbation theory and defect CFT\\ntechniques to obtain results up to \
next-to-leading order in the coupling\\nconstant. Being a defect CFT \
correlator, there exist two (super)conformal block\\nexpansions which capture \
defect and bulk data respectively. We present a\\nclosed-form formula for the \
defect CFT data, which allows to write an efficient\\nTaylor series for the \
correlator in the limit when one of the operators is\\nclose to the line. The \
bulk channel is technically harder and closed-form\\nformulae are \
particularly challenging to obtain, nevertheless we use our\\nanalysis to \
check against well-known data of $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM. In\\nparticular, we \
recover the correct anomalous dimensions of a famous tower of\\ntwist-two \
operators (which includes the Konishi multiplet), and successfully\\ncompare \
the one-point function of the stress-tensor multiplet with results\\nobtained \
using matrix-model techniques.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
