         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2011.04678", "submitter" -> "Julien Barrat", "authors" -> 
            "Julien Barrat, Pedro Liendo, Jan Plefka", "title" -> 
            "Two-Point Correlator of Chiral Primary Operators with a Wilson \
Line\n  Defect in $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM", "comments" -> 
            "48 pages, 5 figures, 3 tables", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP05(2021)195", "report-no" -> 
            "HU-EP-20/33-RTG, DESY 20-191", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the two-point function of the stress-tensor multiplet \
of\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM in the presence of a line defect. To be more \
precise, we\nfocus on the single-trace operator of conformal dimension two \
that sits in the\n$20'$ irrep of the $\\mathfrak{so}(6)_\\text{R}$ \
R-symmetry, and add a\nMaldacena-Wilson line to the configuration which makes \
the two-point function\nnon-trivial. We use a combination of perturbation \
theory and defect CFT\ntechniques to obtain results up to next-to-leading \
order in the coupling\nconstant. Being a defect CFT correlator, there exist \
two (super)conformal block\nexpansions which capture defect and bulk data \
respectively. We present a\nclosed-form formula for the defect CFT data, \
which allows to write an efficient\nTaylor series for the correlator in the \
limit when one of the operators is\nclose to the line. The bulk channel is \
technically harder and closed-form\nformulae are particularly challenging to \
obtain, nevertheless we use our\nanalysis to check against well-known data of \
$\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM. In\nparticular, we recover the correct anomalous \
dimensions of a famous tower of\ntwist-two operators (which includes the \
Konishi multiplet), and successfully\ncompare the one-point function of the \
stress-tensor multiplet with results\nobtained using matrix-model techniques.\
\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 9 Nov 2020 19:00:32 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 29 Dec 2020 10:21:18 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 29 Mar 2021 17:18:54 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-01-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Barrat", "Julien", ""}, {
              "Liendo", "Pedro", ""}, {"Plefka", "Jan", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
