 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The mean values of non-homogeneously parameterized \
generating exponential are\\nobtained and investigated for the periodic \
Heisenberg XX model. The norm-trace\\ngenerating function of boxed plane \
partitions with fixed volume of their\\ndiagonal parts is obtained as \
N-particles average of the generating\\nexponential. The generating function \
of self-avoiding walks of random turns\\nvicious walkers is obtained in terms \
of the circulant matrices that leads to\\ngeneralizations of the Ramus's \
identity. Under various specifications of the\\ngenerating exponential, the \
N-particles averages arise for a set of\\ninconsecutive flipped spins and for \
powers of the first moment of flipped spins\\ndistribution at large length of \
the chain. These averages are expressed through\\nthe numbers of closed \
trajectories with constrained initial/final positions.\\nThe estimates at \
large temporal parameter are expressed through the numbers of\\ndiagonally \
restricted plane partitions characterized by fixed values of the\\nmain \
diagonal trace or by fixed heights of the diagonal columns in \
one-to-one\\ncorrespondence with the flipped spins positions.\\n\""}]}, {
