            "Damon J. Binder, Shai M. Chester, Max Jerdee, and Silviu S. \
Pufu", "title" -> 
            "The 3d $\\mathcal{N}=6$ Bootstrap: From Higher Spins to Strings \
to\n  Membranes", "comments" -> 
            "61 pages plus appendices, 9 figures, v3 accepted to JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2021)083", 
            "report-no" -> "PUPT-2622, LCTP-20-26", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the space of 3d ${\\cal N} = 6$ SCFTs by combining \
numerical\nbootstrap techniques with exact results derived using \
supersymmetric\nlocalization. First we derive the superconformal block \
decomposition of the\nfour-point function of the stress tensor multiplet \
superconformal primary. We\nthen use supersymmetric localization results for \
the ${\\cal N} = 6$\n$U(N)_k\\times U(N+M)_{-k}$ Chern-Simons-matter theories \
to determine two\nprotected OPE coefficients for many values of $N,M,k$. \
These two exact inputs\nare combined with the numerical bootstrap to compute \
precise rigorous islands\nfor a wide range of $N,k$ at $M=0$, so that we can \
non-perturbatively\ninterpolate between SCFTs with M-theory duals at small \
$k$ and string theory\nduals at large $k$. We also present evidence that the \
localization results for\nthe $U(1)_{2M}\\times U(1+M)_{-2M}$ theory, which \
has a vector-like large-$M$\nlimit dual to higher spin theory, saturates the \
bootstrap bounds for certain\nprotected CFT data. The extremal functional \
allows us to then conjecturally\nreconstruct low-lying CFT data for this \
theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
