            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011.06533\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Urs Schreiber\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hisham Sati, Urs Schreiber\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The character map in equivariant twistorial Cohomotopy \
implies the\\n  Green-Schwarz mechanism with heterotic M5-branes\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"67 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.AT math.DG math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The celebrated Green-Schwarz mechanism in heterotic \
string theory has been\\nsuggested to secretly underly a higher gauge \
theoretic phenomenon, embodying a\\nhigher Bianchi identity for a \
higher-degree analog of a curvature form of a\\nhigher gauge field. Here we \
prove that the non-perturbative Horava-Witten\\nGreen-Schwarz mechanism for \
heterotic line bundles in heterotic M-theory with\\nM5-branes parallel to \
MO9-planes on $A_1$-singularities is accurately encoded\\nin the higher gauge \
theory for higher gauge group of the equivariant homotopy\\ntype of the \
Z/2-equivariant A-infinity-loop group of twistor space.\\n  In this \
formulation, the flux forms of the heterotic gauge field, the B-field\\non \
the M5-brane, and of the C-field in the M-theory bulk are all unified \
into\\nthe character image of a single cocycle in equivariant twistorial \
Cohomotopy\\ntheory; and that cocycle enforces the quantization condition on \
all fluxes: the\\nintegrality of the gauge flux, the half-shifted integrality \
of the C-field flux\\nand the integrality of the dual C-field flux (i.e., of \
the Page charge in the\\nbulk and of the Hopf-WZ term on the M5-brane). This \
result is in line with the\\nHypothesis H that M-brane charges are quantized \
in J-twisted Cohomotopy theory.\\n  The mathematical essence of our proof is, \
first, the construction of the\\nequivariant twisted non-abelian character \
map via an equivariant twisted\\nnon-abelian de Rham theorem, which we prove; \
and, second, the computation of\\nthe equivariant relative minimal model of \
the Z/2-equivariant\\nSp(1)-parametrized twistor fibration. We lay out the \
relevant background in\\nequivariant rational homotopy theory and explain how \
this brings about the\\nsubtle flux quantization relations in heterotic \
M-theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 12 Nov 2020 17:47:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
