            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  The celebrated Green-Schwarz mechanism in heterotic string \
theory has been\nsuggested to secretly underly a higher gauge theoretic \
phenomenon, embodying a\nhigher Bianchi identity for a higher-degree analog \
of a curvature form of a\nhigher gauge field. Here we prove that the \
non-perturbative Horava-Witten\nGreen-Schwarz mechanism for heterotic line \
bundles in heterotic M-theory with\nM5-branes parallel to MO9-planes on \
$A_1$-singularities is accurately encoded\nin the higher gauge theory for \
higher gauge group of the equivariant homotopy\ntype of the Z/2-equivariant \
A-infinity-loop group of twistor space.\n  In this formulation, the flux \
forms of the heterotic gauge field, the B-field\non the M5-brane, and of the \
C-field in the M-theory bulk are all unified into\nthe character image of a \
single cocycle in equivariant twistorial Cohomotopy\ntheory; and that cocycle \
enforces the quantization condition on all fluxes: the\nintegrality of the \
gauge flux, the half-shifted integrality of the C-field flux\nand the \
integrality of the dual C-field flux (i.e., of the Page charge in the\nbulk \
and of the Hopf-WZ term on the M5-brane). This result is in line with the\n\
Hypothesis H that M-brane charges are quantized in J-twisted Cohomotopy \
theory.\n  The mathematical essence of our proof is, first, the construction \
of the\nequivariant twisted non-abelian character map via an equivariant \
twisted\nnon-abelian de Rham theorem, which we prove; and, second, the \
computation of\nthe equivariant relative minimal model of the Z/2-equivariant\
\nSp(1)-parametrized twistor fibration. We lay out the relevant background in\
\nequivariant rational homotopy theory and explain how this brings about the\n\
subtle flux quantization relations in heterotic M-theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 12 Nov 2020 17:47:10 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2020-11-13", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Sati", "Hisham", ""}, {
              "Schreiber", "Urs", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
