 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study quantum aspects of the target space of the \
non-linear sigma model\\nwhich is a low-energy effective theory of the gauged \
linear sigma model (GLSM).\\nAs such, we especially compute the exact sphere \
partition function of GLSM for\\nKK$5$-branes whose background geometry is a \
Taub-NUT space, using the\\nsupersymmetric localization technique on the \
Coulomb branch.\\n  From the sphere partition function, we distill the \
world-sheet instanton\\neffects. In particular, we show that concerning the \
single-centered Taub-NUT\\nspace, the instanton contributions exist only if \
the asymptotic radius of the\\n$S^1$ fiber in the Taub-NUT space is \
zero.\\n\""}]}, {
