                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We ask the question of classical integrability for \
certain (classes of)\\nsupergravity vacua that contain an AdS$_3$ factor \
arising in massive IIA and\\nIIB theories and realizing various and different \
amounts of supersymmetry. Our\\napproach is based on a well-established \
method of analytic non-integrability\\nfor Hamiltonian systems. To detect a \
non-integrable sector we consider a\\nnon-trivially wrapped string soliton \
and study its fluctuations. We answer in\\nthe negative for each and every \
one of the supergravity solutions. That is, of\\ncourse, modulo very specific \
limits where the metrics reduce to the AdS$_3\\n\\\\times$ S$^3 \\\\times \
\\\\tilde{S}^3 \\\\times$ S$^1$ and AdS$_3 \\\\times$ S$^3 \\\\times$\\nT$^4$ \
solutions which are known to be integrable.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
