 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the correlator of two concentric circular \
Wilson loops with equal\\nradii for arbitrary spatial and internal separation \
at strong coupling within a\\ndefect version of $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM. \
Compared to the standard Gross-Ooguri\\nphase transition between connected \
and disconnected minimal surfaces, a more\\ncomplicated pattern of \
saddle-points contributes to the two-circles correlator\\ndue to the defect's \
presence. We analyze the transitions between different\\nkinds of minimal \
surfaces and their dependence on the setting's \
numerous\\nparameters.\\n\""}]}, {
