               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Skenderis Kostas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"George Katsianis, Ioannis Papadimitriou, Kostas \
Skenderis, Marika\\n  Taylor\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Supersymmetry anomaly in the superconformal Wess-Zumino \
model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"37 pages + 45 pages appendices v2: minor improvements and \
amendments;\\n  v3: minor additions, version to appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. High Energ. Phys. 2021, 209 (2021)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2021)209\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"KIAS-P20067\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a comprehensive analysis of supersymmetry \
anomalies in the free\\nand massless Wess-Zumino (WZ) model in perturbation \
theory. At the classical\\nlevel the model possesses ${\\\\mathcal N}=1$ \
superconformal symmetry, which is\\npartially broken by quantum anomalies. \
The form of the anomalies and the part\\nof the symmetry they break depend on \
the multiplet of conserved currents used.\\nIt was previously shown that the \
R-symmetry anomaly of the conformal current\\nmultiplet induces an anomaly in \
Q-supersymmetry, which appears first in 4-point\\nfunctions. Here we confirm \
this result by an explicit 1-loop computation using\\na supersymmetric \
Pauli-Villars regulator.\\n  The conformal current multiplet does not exist \
in the regulated theory\\nbecause the regulator breaks conformal invariance, \
R-symmetry and\\nS-supersymmetry explicitly. The minimal massive multiplet is \
the Ferrara-Zumino\\n(FZ) one and the supersymmetry preserved by the \
regulator is a specific field\\ndependent combination of Q- and S- \
supersymmetry of the conformal multiplet.\\nWhile this supersymmetry is non \
anomalous, conformal invariance, R-symmetry and\\nthe original Q- and \
S-supersymmetries are explicitly broken by finite contact\\nterms, both in \
the regulated and renormalized theories.\\n  A conformal current multiplet \
does exist for the renormalized theory and may\\nbe obtained from the FZ \
multiplet by a set of finite local counterterms that\\neliminate the explicit \
symmetry breaking, thus restoring superconformal\\ninvariance up to \
anomalies. However, this necessarily renders both Q- and\\nS-supersymmetries \
anomalous, as is manifest starting at 4-point functions of\\nconformal \
multiplet currents. The paper contains a detailed discussion of a\\nnumber of \
issues and subtleties related to Ward identities that may be useful\\nin a \
wider context.\\n\""}]}, {
