                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The psu(2,2|4) integrable super spin chain underlying \
the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence has integrable boundary states which describe \
set-ups where k\\nD3-branes get dissolved in a probe D5-brane. Overlaps \
between Bethe eigenstates\\nand these boundary states encode the one-point \
functions of conformal operators\\nand are expressed in terms of the \
superdeterminant of the Gaudin matrix that in\\nturn depends on the Dynkin \
diagram of the symmetry algebra. The different\\npossible Dynkin diagrams of \
super Lie algebras are related via fermionic\\ndualities and we determine how \
overlap formulae transform under these\\ndualities. As an application we show \
how to consistently move between overlap\\nformulae obtained for k=1 from \
different Dynkin diagrams.\\n\""}]}, {
