        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{13.618676268777977`, -9.027506494488264}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2012.04664\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wei Gu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wei Gu, Jirui Guo, Yaoxiong Wen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonabelian mirrors and Gromov-Witten invariants\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"71 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.AG\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose Picard-Fuchs equations for periods of \
nonabelian mirrors in this\\npaper. The number of parameters in our \
Picard-Fuchs equations is the rank of\\nthe gauge group of the nonabelian \
GLSM, which is eventually reduced to the\\nactual number of K\\\\\\\"{a}hler \
parameters. These Picard-Fuchs equations are\\nconcise and novel. We justify \
our proposal by reproducing existing mathematical\\nresults, namely \
Picard-Fuchs equations of Grassmannians and Calabi-Yau\\nmanifolds as \
complete intersections in Grassmannians. Furthermore, our approach\\ncan be \
applied to other nonabelian GLSMs, so we compute Picard-Fuchs equations\\nof \
some other Fano-spaces, which were not calculated in the literature \
before.\\nFinally, the cohomology-valued generating functions of mirrors can \
be read off\\nfrom our Picard-Fuchs equations. Using these generating \
functions, we compute\\nGromov-Witten invariants of various Calabi-Yau \
manifolds, including complete\\nintersection Calabi-Yau manifolds in \
Grassmannians and non-complete\\nintersection Calabi-Yau examples such as \
Pfaffian Calabi-Yau threefold and\\nGulliksen-Neg{\\\\aa}rd Calabi-Yau \
threefold, and find agreement with existing\\nresults in the literature. The \
generating functions we propose for non-complete\\nintersection Calabi-Yau \
manifolds are genuinely new.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
