                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study possible geometries and R-symmetry breaking \
patterns that lead to\\nglobally BPS surface operators in the six dimensional \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=(2,0)$\\ntheory. We find four main classes of solutions in \
different subspaces of\\n$\\\\mathbb{R}^6$ and a multitude of subclasses and \
specific examples. We prove\\nthat these constructions lead to supersymmety \
preserving observables and count\\nthe number of preserved supercharges. We \
discuss the underlying geometry,\\ncalculate their anomalies and present \
analogous structures for the holographic\\ndual M2-branes in $AdS_7\\\\times \
S^4$. We also comment on the dimensional\\nreduction of these observables to \
line and surface operators in 4d and 5d\\ntheories. This rich spectrum of \
operators are proposed as the simplest and most\\nnatural observables of this \
mysterious theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
