 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct the one-dimensional topological sector of \
$\\\\mathcal N = 6$\\nABJ(M) theory and study its relation with the \
mass-deformed partition function\\non $S^3$. Supersymmetric localization \
provides an exact representation of this\\npartition function as a matrix \
integral, which interpolates between weak and\\nstrong coupling regimes. It \
has been proposed that correlation functions of\\ndimension-one topological \
operators should be computed through suitable\\nderivatives with respect to \
the masses, but a precise proof is still lacking.\\nWe present non-trivial \
evidence for this relation by computing the two-point\\nfunction at twoloop, \
successfully matching the matrix model expansion at weak\\ncoupling and \
finite ranks. As a by-product we obtain the two-loop explicit\\nexpression \
for the central charge $c_T$ of ABJ(M) theory. Three- and \
four-point\\nfunctions up to one-loop confirm the relation as well. Our \
result points\\ntowards the possibility to localize the one-dimensional \
topological sector of\\nABJ(M) and may also be useful in the bootstrap \
program for 3d SCFTs.\\n\""}]}, {
