               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The aim of this memoir for \\\"Habilitation \\\\`a \
Diriger des Recherches\\\" is to\\npresent quantum geometric and algebraic \
aspects of supersymmetric gauge theory,\\nwhich emerge from non-perturbative \
nature of the vacuum structure induced by\\ninstantons. We start with a brief \
summary of the equivariant localization of\\nthe instanton moduli space, and \
show how to obtain the instanton partition\\nfunction and its generalization \
to quiver gauge theory and supergroup gauge\\ntheory in three ways: the \
equivariant index formula, the contour integral\\nformula, and the \
combinatorial formula. We then explore the geometric\\ndescription of \
$\\\\mathcal{N} = 2$ gauge theory based on Seiberg-Witten geometry\\ntogether \
with its string/M-theory perspective. Through its relation to\\nintegrable \
systems, we show how to quantize such a geometric structure via \
the\\n$\\\\Omega$-deformation of gauge theory. We also discuss the underlying \
quantum\\nalgebraic structure arising from the supersymmetric vacua. We \
introduce the\\nnotion of quiver W-algebra constructed through double \
quantization of\\nSeiberg-Witten geometry, and show its specific features: \
affine quiver\\nW-algebras, fractional quiver W-algebras, and their elliptic \
deformations.\\n\""}]}, {
