            "  We consider a family of $\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal field \
theories in four\ndimensions, defined as $\\mathbb{Z}_q$ orbifolds of \
$\\mathcal{N}=4$ Super\nYang-Mills theory. We compute the chiral/anti-chiral \
correlation functions at a\nperturbative level, using both the matrix model \
approach arising from\nsupersymmetric localisation on the four-sphere and \
explicit field theory\ncalculations on the flat space using the \
$\\mathcal{N}=1$ superspace formalism.\nWe implement a highly efficient \
algorithm to produce a large number of results\nfor finite values of $N$, \
exploiting the symmetries of the quiver to reduce the\ncomplexity of the \
mixing between the operators. Finally the interplay with the\nfield theory \
calculations allows to isolate special observables which deviate\nfrom \
$\\mathcal{N}=4$ only at high orders in perturbation theory.\n", 
