               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Roberto Ruiz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The $\\\\mathrm{SL}(2,\\\\mathbb{R})$ \
Wess-Zumino-Novikov-Witten spin-chain\\n  $\\\\sigma$-model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages. v2: Minor corrections and improvements. v3: \
Minor\\n  corrections and improvements. Manuscript corresponds to the \
published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys. Rev. D 103, 106024 (2021)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.103.106024\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The $\\\\textrm{SL}(2,\\\\mathbb{R})$ \
Wess-Zumino-Novikov-Witten model realises\\nbosonic-string theory in \
$\\\\textrm{AdS}_{3}$ with pure\\nNeveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz flux. We \
construct an effective action in the\\nsemi-classical limit of the model, \
which corresponds to a\\n$\\\\textrm{SL}(2,\\\\mathbb{R})$ spin-chain \
$\\\\sigma$-model. We adopt two\\ncomplementary points of view. Firstly, we \
consider the classical action. We\\nidentify fast and slow target-space \
coordinates. We impose a gauge-fixing\\ncondition to the former. By expanding \
the gauge-fixed action in an effective\\ncoupling, we obtain the effective \
action for the slow coordinates. Secondly, we\\nconsider the spin chain of \
the model. We postulate a set of coherent states to\\nexpress a transition \
amplitude in the spin chain as a path integral. We observe\\nthat the \
temporal interval is discretised in terms of the step length of the\\nspatial \
interval. This relationship implies that the Landau-Lifshitz limit of\\nthe \
spin chain involves both intervals. The limit yields a semi-classical \
path\\nintegral over coherent states, wherein we identify the effective \
action again.\\n\""}]}, {
