            "The $\\mathrm{SL}(2,\\mathbb{R})$ Wess-Zumino-Novikov-Witten \
spin-chain\n  $\\sigma$-model", "comments" -> 
            "18 pages. v2: Minor corrections and improvements. v3: Minor\n  \
corrections and improvements. Manuscript corresponds to the published \
version", "journal-ref" -> "Phys. Rev. D 103, 106024 (2021)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.103.106024", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The $\\textrm{SL}(2,\\mathbb{R})$ Wess-Zumino-Novikov-Witten \
model realises\nbosonic-string theory in $\\textrm{AdS}_{3}$ with pure\n\
Neveu-Schwarz-Neveu-Schwarz flux. We construct an effective action in the\n\
semi-classical limit of the model, which corresponds to a\n\
$\\textrm{SL}(2,\\mathbb{R})$ spin-chain $\\sigma$-model. We adopt two\n\
complementary points of view. Firstly, we consider the classical action. We\n\
identify fast and slow target-space coordinates. We impose a gauge-fixing\n\
condition to the former. By expanding the gauge-fixed action in an effective\n\
coupling, we obtain the effective action for the slow coordinates. Secondly, \
we\nconsider the spin chain of the model. We postulate a set of coherent \
states to\nexpress a transition amplitude in the spin chain as a path \
integral. We observe\nthat the temporal interval is discretised in terms of \
the step length of the\nspatial interval. This relationship implies that the \
Landau-Lifshitz limit of\nthe spin chain involves both intervals. The limit \
yields a semi-classical path\nintegral over coherent states, wherein we \
identify the effective action again.\n", 
