                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The ground state energy of integrable asymptotically \
free theories can be\\nconjecturally computed by using the Bethe ansatz, once \
the theory has been\\ncoupled to an external potential through a conserved \
charge. This leads to a\\nprecise prediction for the perturbative expansion \
of the energy. We provide a\\nnon-trivial test of this prediction in the \
non-linear sigma model and its\\nsupersymmetric extension, by calculating \
analytically the associated Feynman\\ndiagrams at next-to-leading order in \
the $1/N$ expansion, and at all loops. By\\ninvestigating the large order \
behaviour of the diagrams, we locate the position\\nof the renormalons of the \
theory and we obtain an analytic expression for the\\nlarge $N$ trans-series \
associated to each. As a spin-off of our calculation, we\\nprovide a direct \
derivation of the beta function of these theories, at\\nnext-to-leading order \
in the $1/N$ expansion.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
