theories can be\nconjecturally computed by using the Bethe ansatz, once the \
theory has been\ncoupled to an external potential through a conserved charge. \
This leads to a\nprecise prediction for the perturbative expansion of the \
energy. We provide a\nnon-trivial test of this prediction in the non-linear \
sigma model and its\nsupersymmetric extension, by calculating analytically \
