Takeuchi, Siyi\\n  Zhou\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spiky strings in de Sitter space\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"31 pages, 16 figures: version published in JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2021)047\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"UT-Komaba/21-1, KOBE-COSMO-21-04\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study semiclassical spiky strings in de Sitter space \
and the corresponding\\nRegge trajectories, generalizing the analysis in \
anti-de Sitter space. In\\nparticular we demonstrate that each Regge \
trajectory has a maximum spin due to\\nde Sitter acceleration, similarly to \
the folded string studied earlier. While\\nthis property is useful for the \
spectrum to satisfy the Higuchi bound, it makes\\na nontrivial question how \
to maintain mildness of high-energy string scattering\\nwhich we are familiar \
with in flat space and anti-de Sitter space. Our analysis\\nimplies that in \
order to have infinitely many higher spin states, one needs to\\nconsider \
infinitely many Regge trajectories with an increasing folding \
number.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 19 Feb 2021 05:16:44 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
