          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2102.09746", "submitter" -> "Kanji Nishii", "authors" -> 
            "Mitsuhiro Kato, Kanji Nishii, Toshifumi Noumi, Toshiaki \
Takeuchi, Siyi\n  Zhou", "title" -> "Spiky strings in de Sitter space", 
            "comments" -> "31 pages, 16 figures: version published in JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2021)047", 
            "report-no" -> "UT-Komaba/21-1, KOBE-COSMO-21-04", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study semiclassical spiky strings in de Sitter space and \
the corresponding\nRegge trajectories, generalizing the analysis in anti-de \
Sitter space. In\nparticular we demonstrate that each Regge trajectory has a \
maximum spin due to\nde Sitter acceleration, similarly to the folded string \
studied earlier. While\nthis property is useful for the spectrum to satisfy \
the Higuchi bound, it makes\na nontrivial question how to maintain mildness \
of high-energy string scattering\nwhich we are familiar with in flat space \
and anti-de Sitter space. Our analysis\nimplies that in order to have \
infinitely many higher spin states, one needs to\nconsider infinitely many \
Regge trajectories with an increasing folding number.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 19 Feb 2021 05:16:44 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 13 Sep 2022 15:35:45 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
