 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We describe the on-going effort to formulate the \
baryon-quark continuity in\\nterms of a topology change in the equation of \
state (EoS) of dense baryonic\\nmatter in analogy to -- and inspired by -- \
the mapping of the characteristics\\nof Chern-Simon topological field theory \
to Kohn-Sham density functional theory\\nin the fractional quantized Hall \
effect (FQHE). This is done by translating the\\ndensity-dependent \
characteristics of the skyrmion-half-skyrmion transition\\nformulated in the \
presence of hidden local symmetry and (hidden) scale symmetry\\nto the \
density-dependent parameters of a renormalization-group approach \
to\\nFermi-liquid fixed point theory. Predictions made in finite nuclei and \
infinite\\ncompact-star matter are presented.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
