 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This review summarizes recent advances in our \
understanding of anomalous\\ntransport in spin chains, viewed through the \
lens of integrability. Numerical\\nadvances, based on tensor-network methods, \
have shown that transport in many\\ncanonical integrable spin chains -- most \
famously the Heisenberg model -- is\\nanomalous. Concurrently, the framework \
of generalized hydrodynamics has been\\nextended to explain some of the \
mechanisms underlying anomalous transport. We\\npresent what is currently \
understood about these mechanisms, and discuss how\\nthey resemble (and \
differ from) the mechanisms for anomalous transport in other\\ncontexts. We \
also briefly review potential transport anomalies in systems \
where\\nintegrability is an emergent or approximate property. We survey \
instances of\\nanomalous transport and dynamics that remain to be understood.\
\\n\""}]}, {
