         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2103.01976", "submitter" -> "Vir Bulchandani", "authors" -> 
            "Vir B. Bulchandani, Sarang Gopalakrishnan, Enej Ilievski", 
            "title" -> "Superdiffusion in spin chains", "comments" -> 
            "v2: published version. Review article, 73 pages, 8 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> "J. Stat. Mech. (2021) 084001", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/ac12c7", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.quant-gas cond-mat.str-el quant-ph", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This review summarizes recent advances in our understanding of \
anomalous\ntransport in spin chains, viewed through the lens of \
integrability. Numerical\nadvances, based on tensor-network methods, have \
shown that transport in many\ncanonical integrable spin chains -- most \
famously the Heisenberg model -- is\nanomalous. Concurrently, the framework \
of generalized hydrodynamics has been\nextended to explain some of the \
mechanisms underlying anomalous transport. We\npresent what is currently \
understood about these mechanisms, and discuss how\nthey resemble (and differ \
from) the mechanisms for anomalous transport in other\ncontexts. We also \
briefly review potential transport anomalies in systems where\nintegrability \
is an emergent or approximate property. We survey instances of\nanomalous \
transport and dynamics that remain to be understood.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
