            "Separation of Variables in AdS/CFT: Functional Approach for the \
Fishnet\n  CFT", "comments" -> 
            "53 pages + appendices, 5 figures. v2: references added, small \
changes\n  to the text. Accepted for publication in JHEP", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP06(2021)131", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The major simplification in a number of quantum integrable \
systems is the\nexistence of special coordinates in which the eigenstates \
take a factorised\nform. Despite many years of studies, the basis realising \
the separation of\nvariables (SoV) remains unknown in N=4 SYM and similar \
models, even though it\nis widely believed they are integrable. In this paper \
we initiate the SoV\napproach for observables with nontrivial coupling \
dependence in a close cousin\nof N=4 SYM - the fishnet 4D CFT. We develop the \
functional SoV formalism in\nthis theory, which allows us to compute \
non-perturbatively some nontrivial\nobservables in a form suitable for \
numerical evaluation. We present some\napplications of these methods. In \
particular, we discuss the possible SoV\nstructure of the one-point \
correlators in presence of a defect, and write down\na SoV-type expression \
for diagonal OPE coefficients involving an arbitrary\nstate and the \
Lagrangian density operator. We believe that many of the findings\nof this \
paper can be applied in the N=4 SYM case, as we speculate in the last\npart \
of the article.\n", 
