          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2103.15840", "submitter" -> "Yunfeng Jiang", "authors" -> 
            "Peihe Yang, Yunfeng Jiang, Shota Komatsu, Jun-Bao Wu", "title" -> 
            "Three-Point Functions in ABJM and Bethe Ansatz", "comments" -> 
            "Typos corrected, report number added, published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP01(2022)002", 
            "report-no" -> 
            "CERN-TH-2021-042, USTC-ICTS/PCFT-21-14, CJQS-2022-001", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We develop an integrability-based framework to compute \
structure constants of\ntwo sub-determinant operators and a single-trace \
non-BPS operator in ABJM\ntheory in the planar limit. In this first paper, we \
study them at weak coupling\nusing a relation to an integrable spin chain. We \
first develop a nested Bethe\nansatz for an alternating SU(4) spin chain that \
describes single-trace\noperators made out of scalar fields. We then apply it \
to the computation of the\nstructure constants and show that they are given \
by overlaps between a Bethe\neigenstate and a matrix product state. We \
conjecture that the determinant\noperator corresponds to an integrable matrix \
product state and present a\nclosed-form expression for the overlap, which \
resembles the so-called Gaudin\ndeterminant. We also provide evidence for the \
integrability of general\nsub-determinant operators. The techniques developed \
in this paper can be\napplied to other quantities in ABJM theory including \
three-point functions of\nsingle-trace operators.\n", 
