            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2021.115429", "report-no" -> "DESY 21-043", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute the non-planar contribution to the universal \
anomalous dimension\nof twist-two operators in N=4 supersymmetric Yang-Mills \
theory at four loops\nthrough Lorentz spin eighteen. Exploiting the results \
of this and our previous\ncalculations along with recent analytic results for \
the cusp anomalous\ndimension and some expected analytic properties, we \
reconstruct a general\nexpression valid for arbitrary Lorentz spin. We study \
various properties of\nthis general result, such as its large-spin limit, its \
small-x limit, and\nothers. In particular, we present a prediction for the \
non-planar contribution\nto the anomalous dimension of the single-magnon \
operator in the beta-deformed\nversion of the theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 30 Mar 2021 15:20:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2021-06-30", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kniehl", "B. A.", ""}, {
              "Velizhanin", "V. N.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{15.179148036866616`, -6.21026232095504}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2103.16580\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yunfeng Jiang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Peihe Yang, Yunfeng Jiang, Shota Komatsu, Jun-Bao \
Wu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"D-branes and Orbit Average\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"References added, typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SciPost Phys. 12, 055 (2022)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.21468/SciPostPhys.12.2.055\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"CERN-TH-2021-043, USTC-ICTS/PCFT-21-15\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study correlation functions of D-branes and a \
supergravity mode in AdS,\\nwhich are dual to structure constants of two \
sub-determinant operators with\\nlarge charge and a BPS single-trace \
operator. Our approach is inspired by the\\nlarge charge expansion of CFT and \
resolves puzzles and confusions in the\\nliterature on the holographic \
computation of correlation functions of heavy\\noperators. In particular, we \
point out two important effects which are often\\nmissed in the literature; \
the first one is an average over classical\\nconfigurations of the heavy \
state, which physically amounts to projecting the\\nstate to an eigenstate of \
quantum numbers. The second one is the contribution\\nfrom wave functions of \
the heavy state. To demonstrate the power of the method,\\nwe first analyze \
the three-point functions in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills\\nand \
reproduce the results in field theory from holography, including the \
cases\\nfor which the previous holographic computation gives incorrect \
answers. We then\\napply it to ABJM theory and make solid predictions at \
strong coupling. Finally\\nwe comment on possible applications to states dual \
to black holes and\\nfuzzballs.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
