            "SciPost Phys. 12, 055 (2022)", "doi" -> 
            "10.21468/SciPostPhys.12.2.055", "report-no" -> 
            "CERN-TH-2021-043, USTC-ICTS/PCFT-21-15", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study correlation functions of D-branes and a supergravity \
mode in AdS,\nwhich are dual to structure constants of two sub-determinant \
operators with\nlarge charge and a BPS single-trace operator. Our approach is \
inspired by the\nlarge charge expansion of CFT and resolves puzzles and \
confusions in the\nliterature on the holographic computation of correlation \
functions of heavy\noperators. In particular, we point out two important \
effects which are often\nmissed in the literature; the first one is an \
average over classical\nconfigurations of the heavy state, which physically \
amounts to projecting the\nstate to an eigenstate of quantum numbers. The \
second one is the contribution\nfrom wave functions of the heavy state. To \
demonstrate the power of the method,\nwe first analyze the three-point \
functions in $\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills\nand reproduce the results in \
field theory from holography, including the cases\nfor which the previous \
holographic computation gives incorrect answers. We then\napply it to ABJM \
theory and make solid predictions at strong coupling. Finally\nwe comment on \
possible applications to states dual to black holes and\nfuzzballs.\n", 
