               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Intersecting defects in gauge theory, quantum spin \
chains, and\\n  Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov equations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"85 pages; v2. published version; v3. journal reference \
number\\n  corrected; v4. references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP10(2021)120\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2021)120\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.AG math.MP math.QA math.RT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose an interesting BPS/CFT correspondence \
playground: the correlation\\nfunction of two intersecting half-BPS surface \
defects in four-dimensional\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ supersymmetric $SU(N)$ gauge \
theory with $2N$ fundamental\\nhypermultiplets. We show it satisfies a \
difference equation, the fractional\\nquantum T-Q relation. Its Fourier \
transform is the $5$-point conformal block of\\nthe \
$\\\\widehat{\\\\mathfrak{sl}}_N$ current algebra with one of the \
vertex\\noperators corresponding to the $N$-dimensional \
$\\\\mathfrak{sl}_N$\\nrepresentation, which we demonstrate with the help of \
the\\nKnizhnik-Zamolodchikov equation. We also identify the correlator with a \
state\\nof the $XXX_{\\\\mathfrak{sl}_2}$ spin chain of $N$ Heisenberg-Weyl \
modules over\\n$Y(\\\\mathfrak{sl}_2)$. We discuss the associated quantum Lax \
operators, and\\nconnections to isomonodromic deformations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
