 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the expectation value $\\\\langle \\\\cal W \
\\\\rangle$ of the circular\\nBPS Wilson loop in ${\\\\cal N}=2$ \
superconformal $SU(N)$ gauge theory containing\\na vector multiplet coupled \
to two hypermultiplets in rank-2 symmetric and\\nantisymmetric \
representations. This model admits a regular large $N$ expansion,\\nis \
planar-equivalent to ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM theory and is expected to be dual to \
a\\ncertain orbifold/orientifold projection of AdS$_5\\\\times S^5$ \
superstring\\ntheory. On the string theory side $\\\\langle\\\\cal W \
\\\\rangle $ is represented by\\nthe path integral expanded near the same \
AdS$_2$ minimal surface as in the\\nmaximally supersymmetric case. Following \
the string theory argument in\\narXiv:2007.08512, we suggest that as in the \
${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM case and in the\\n${\\\\cal N}=2$ $SU(N) \\\\times SU(N)$ \
superconformal quiver theory discussed in\\narXiv:2102.07696, the coefficient \
of the leading non-planar $1/N^2$ correction\\nin $\\\\langle\\\\cal W \
\\\\rangle $ should have the universal $\\\\lambda^{3/2}$ scaling\\nat large \
't Hooft coupling. We confirm this prediction by starting with \
the\\nlocalization matrix model representation for $\\\\langle\\\\cal W \
\\\\rangle $. We\\ncomplement the analytic derivation of the \
$\\\\lambda^{3/2}$ scaling by a\\nnumerical high-precision resummation and \
extrapolation of the weak-coupling\\nexpansion using conformal mapping \
improved Pad\\\\'e analysis.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
