               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Intersecting Defects and Supergroup Gauge Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v1: 50 pages; v2: 51 pages, added more references, minor \
comments and\\n  report n; v3: published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/ac2716\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DESY 21-060\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.QA\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider 5d supersymmetric gauge theories with \
unitary groups in the\\n$\\\\Omega$-background and study codim-2/4 BPS \
defects supported on orthogonal\\nplanes intersecting at the origin along a \
circle. The intersecting defects\\narise upon implementing the most generic \
Higgsing (geometric transition) to the\\nparent higher dimensional theory, \
and they are described by pairs of 3d\\nsupersymmetric gauge theories with \
unitary groups interacting through 1d matter\\nat the intersection. We \
explore the relations between instanton and generalized\\nvortex calculus, \
pointing out a duality between intersecting defects subject to\\nthe \
$\\\\Omega$-background and a deformation of supergroup gauge theories, \
the\\nexact supergroup point being achieved in the self-dual or unrefined \
limit.\\nEmbedding our setup into refined topological strings and in the \
simplest case\\nwhen the parent 5d theory is Abelian, we are able to identify \
the supergroup\\ntheory dual to the intersecting defects as the supergroup \
version of refined\\nChern-Simons theory via open/closed duality. We also \
discuss the BPS/CFT side\\nof the correspondence, finding an interesting \
large rank duality with\\nsuper-instanton counting.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
