            "v1: 50 pages; v2: 51 pages, added more references, minor \
comments and\n  report n; v3: published version", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8121/ac2716", "report-no" -> "DESY 21-060",
             "categories" -> "hep-th math.QA", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider 5d supersymmetric gauge theories with unitary \
groups in the\n$\\Omega$-background and study codim-2/4 BPS defects supported \
on orthogonal\nplanes intersecting at the origin along a circle. The \
intersecting defects\narise upon implementing the most generic Higgsing \
(geometric transition) to the\nparent higher dimensional theory, and they are \
described by pairs of 3d\nsupersymmetric gauge theories with unitary groups \
interacting through 1d matter\nat the intersection. We explore the relations \
between instanton and generalized\nvortex calculus, pointing out a duality \
between intersecting defects subject to\nthe $\\Omega$-background and a \
deformation of supergroup gauge theories, the\nexact supergroup point being \
achieved in the self-dual or unrefined limit.\nEmbedding our setup into \
refined topological strings and in the simplest case\nwhen the parent 5d \
theory is Abelian, we are able to identify the supergroup\ntheory dual to the \
intersecting defects as the supergroup version of refined\nChern-Simons \
theory via open/closed duality. We also discuss the BPS/CFT side\nof the \
correspondence, finding an interesting large rank duality with\n\
super-instanton counting.\n", 
