five-manifolds\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"29 pages; LaTex errors on pages 26 and 27 fixed in v2. v3 \
final\\n  version to appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 07 (2021) 209\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2021)209\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"EMPG-21-06\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.DG math.RT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate the relevant Spencer cohomology of the \
minimal Poincar\\\\'e\\nsuperalgebra in 5 spacetime dimensions and use it to \
define Killing spinors via\\na connection on the spinor bundle of a \
5-dimensional lorentzian spin manifold.\\nWe give a definition of bosonic \
backgrounds in terms of this data. By imposing\\nconstraints on the curvature \
of the spinor connection, we recover the field\\nequations of minimal \
(ungauged) 5-dimensional supergravity, but also find a set\\nof field \
equations for an $\\\\mathfrak{sp}(1)$-valued one-form which we \
interpret\\nas the bosonic data of a class of rigid supersymmetric theories \
on curved\\nbackgrounds. We define the Killing superalgebra of bosonic \
backgrounds and show\\nthat their existence is implied by the field \
equations. The maximally\\nsupersymmetric backgrounds are characterised and \
their Killing superalgebras\\nare explicitly described as filtered \
deformations of the Poincar\\\\'e\\nsuperalgebra.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
