         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2105.05775", "submitter" -> 
            "Jos\\'e M. Figueroa-O'Farrill", "authors" -> 
            "Andrew Beckett and Jos\\'e Figueroa-O'Farrill", "title" -> 
            "Killing superalgebras for lorentzian five-manifolds", "comments" -> 
            "29 pages; LaTex errors on pages 26 and 27 fixed in v2. v3 final\n\
  version to appear in JHEP", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 07 (2021) 209", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP07(2021)209", "report-no" -> "EMPG-21-06", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math.DG math.RT", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate the relevant Spencer cohomology of the minimal \
Poincar\\'e\nsuperalgebra in 5 spacetime dimensions and use it to define \
Killing spinors via\na connection on the spinor bundle of a 5-dimensional \
lorentzian spin manifold.\nWe give a definition of bosonic backgrounds in \
terms of this data. By imposing\nconstraints on the curvature of the spinor \
connection, we recover the field\nequations of minimal (ungauged) \
5-dimensional supergravity, but also find a set\nof field equations for an \
$\\mathfrak{sp}(1)$-valued one-form which we interpret\nas the bosonic data \
of a class of rigid supersymmetric theories on curved\nbackgrounds. We define \
the Killing superalgebra of bosonic backgrounds and show\nthat their \
existence is implied by the field equations. The maximally\nsupersymmetric \
backgrounds are characterised and their Killing superalgebras\nare explicitly \
described as filtered deformations of the Poincar\\'e\nsuperalgebra.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
