               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mathieu Massicotte, Giancarlo Soavi, Alessandro Principi, \
Klaas-Jan\\n  Tielrooij\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hot carriers in graphene -- fundamentals and applications\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nanoscale 13 (2021) 8376\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1039/d0nr09166a\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cond-mat.mes-hall\""}]}
              , {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Hot charge carriers in graphene exhibit fascinating \
physical phenomena, whose\\nunderstanding has improved greatly over the past \
decade. They have distinctly\\ndifferent physical properties compared to, for \
example, hot carriers in\\nconventional metals. This is predominantly the \
result of graphene's linear\\nenergy-momentum dispersion, its phonon \
properties, its all-interface character,\\nand the tunability of its carrier \
density down to very small values, and from\\nelectron- to hole-doping. Since \
a few years, we have witnessed an increasing\\ninterest in technological \
applications enabled by hot carriers in graphene. Of\\nparticular interest \
are optical and optoelectronic applications, where hot\\ncarriers are used to \
detect (photodetection), convert (nonlinear photonics), or\\nemit \
(luminescence) light. Graphene-enabled systems in these application \
areas\\ncould find widespread use and have a disruptive impact, for example \
in the\\nfield of data communication, high-frequency electronics, and \
industrial quality\\ncontrol. The aim of this review is to provide an \
overview of the most relevant\\nphysics and working principles that are \
relevant for applications exploiting\\nhot carriers in graphene.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 18 May 2021 08:24:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2021-05-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
