 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute holographic complexity for the \
non-supersymmetric Janus\\ndeformation of AdS$_5$ according to the volume \
conjecture. The result is\\ncharacterized by a power-law ultraviolet \
divergence. When a ball-shaped region\\nlocated around the interface is \
considered, a sub-leading logarithmic divergent\\nterm and a finite part \
appear in the corresponding subregion volume complexity.\\nUsing two \
different prescriptions to regularize the divergences, we find that\\nthe \
coefficient of the logarithmic term is universal.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
