               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the planar limit of 2- and 3-point functions \
of single-trace chiral\\nprimary operators of ${\\\\cal N}=2$ SQCD on $S^4$, \
to all orders in the 't Hooft\\ncoupling. In order to do so, we first obtain \
a combinatorial expression for the\\nplanar free energy of a hermitian matrix \
model with an infinite number of\\narbitrary single and double trace terms in \
the potential; this solution might\\nhave applications in many other \
contexts. We then use these results to evaluate\\nthe analogous planar \
correlation functions on ${\\\\mathbb R}^4$. Specifically, we\\ncompute all \
the terms with a single value of the $\\\\zeta$ function for a few\\nplanar \
2- and 3-point functions, and conjecture general formulas for these\\nterms \
for all 2- and 3-point functions on ${\\\\mathbb R}^4$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
