            "  We investigate interactions between branes of various \
dimensions, both\ncharged and uncharged, in three non-supersymmetric string \
models. These include\nthe $USp(32)$ and $U(32)$ orientifold projections of \
the type IIB and type $0$B\nstrings, as well as the $SO(16) \\times SO(16)$ \
projection of the exceptional\nheterotic string. The resulting \
ten-dimensional spectra are free of tachyons,\nand the combinations of branes \
that they contain give rise to rich and varied\ndynamics. We compute static \
potentials for parallel stacks of branes in three\ncomplementary regimes: the \
probe regime, in which one of the two stacks is\nparametrically heavier than \
the other, the string-amplitude regime, in which\nboth stacks are light, and \
the holographic regime. Whenever comparisons are\npossible, we find \
qualitative agreement despite the absence of supersymmetry.\nFor charged \
branes, our analysis reveals that the Weak Gravity Conjecture is\nsatisfied \
in a novel way via a renormalization of the effective\ncharge-to-tension \
ratio.\n", "versions" -> {{
