            "id" -> "2106.08116", "submitter" -> "Konstantin Zarembo", 
             "authors" -> 
             "Charlotte Kristjansen, Dennis M\\\"uller and Konstantin \
Zarembo", "title" -> 
             "Duality Relations for Overlaps of Integrable Boundary States in \
AdS/dCFT", "comments" -> "28 pages, 3 figures; v2: minor changes", 
             "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP09(2021)004", 
             "report-no" -> "NORDITA 2021-042", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
             "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  The encoding of all possible sets of Bethe equations for a \
spin chain with\nSU(N|M) symmetry into a QQ-system calls for an expression of \
spin chain\noverlaps entirely in terms of Q-functions. We take a significant \
step towards\nderiving such a universal formula in the case of overlaps \
between Bethe\neigenstates and integrable boundary states, of relevance for \
AdS/dCFT, by\ndetermining the transformation properties of the overlaps under \
fermionic as\nwell as bosonic dualities which allows us to move between any \
two descriptions\nof the spin chain encoded in the QQ-system. An important \
part of our analysis\ninvolves introducing a suitable regularization for \
singular Bethe root\nconfigurations.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Tue, 15 Jun 2021 13:21:32 GMT"}, {
