                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review the correspondence between integrable sigma \
models with complex\\nhomogeneous target spaces and chiral bosonic (and \
possibly mixed\\nbosonic/fermionic) Gross-Neveu models. Mathematically, the \
latter are models\\nwith quiver variety phase spaces, which reduce to the \
more conventional sigma\\nmodels in special cases. We discuss the geometry of \
the models, as well as\\ntheir trigonometric and elliptic deformations, Ricci \
flow and the inclusion of\\nfermions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
