                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analytically study the Fermi-gas formulation of \
sphere correlation\\nfunctions of the Coulomb branch operators for 3d \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ ADHM theory\\nwith a gauge group $U(N)$, an adjoint \
hypermultiplet and $l$ hypermultiplets\\nwhich can describe a stack of $N$ \
M2-branes at $A_{l-1}$ singularities. We find\\nthat the leading coefficients \
of the perturbative grand canonical correlation\\nfunctions are invariant \
under a hidden triality symmetry conjectured from the\\ntwisted M-theory. The \
triality symmetry also helps us to fix the\\nnext-to-leading corrections \
analytically.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
