            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2107.12398\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kiril Hristov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Kiril Hristov, Valentin Reys\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Factorization of log-corrections in AdS$_4$/CFT$_3$ from \
supergravity\\n  localization\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages; v2 minor corrections, references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP12(2021)031\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.DG\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We use the Atiyah-Singer index theorem to derive the \
general form of the\\none-loop corrections to observables in asymptotically \
anti-de Sitter (AdS$_4$)\\nsupersymmetric backgrounds of abelian gauged \
supergravity. Using the method of\\nsupergravity localization combined with \
the factorization of the supergravity\\naction on fixed points (NUTs) and \
fixed two-manifolds (Bolts) we show that an\\nanalogous factorization takes \
place for the one-loop determinants of\\nsupergravity fields. This allows us \
to propose a general fixed-point formula\\nfor the logarithmic corrections to \
a large class of supersymmetric partition\\nfunctions in the large $N$ \
expansion of a given 3d dual theory. The corrections\\nare uniquely fixed by \
some simple topological data pertaining to a particular\\nbackground in the \
form of its regularized Euler characteristic $\\\\chi$, together\\nwith a \
single dynamical coefficient that counts the underlying degrees of\\nfreedom \
of the theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 26 Jul 2021 18:00:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 4 Aug 2021 12:07:02 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
