               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Sigma model in $AdS_3\\\\times S^3$ background \
supported by both NS-NS and R-R\\nfluxes is one of the most distinguished \
integrable models. We study a class of\\nclassical string solutions for \
$N$-spike strings moving in $AdS_3 \\\\times S^1$\\nwith angular momentum $J$ \
in $S^1 \\\\subset S^5$ in the presence of mixed flux.\\nWe observe that the \
addition of angular momentum $J$ or winding number $m$\\nresults in the \
spikes getting rounded off and not end in cusp. The presence of\\nflux shows \
no alteration to the rounding-off nature of the spikes. We also\\nconsider \
the large $N$-limit of $N$-spike string in $AdS_3 \\\\times S^1$ in \
the\\npresence of flux and show that the so-called Energy-Spin dispersion \
relation is\\nanalogous to the solution we get for the periodic-spike in \
$AdS_3-pp-$wave\\n$\\\\times S^1$ background with flux.\\n\""}]}, {
