Sberveglieri and Marco\\n  Serone\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Resurgence and $1/N$ Expansion in Integrable Field \
Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"59 pages, 5 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2021)166\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th hep-lat hep-ph math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In theories with renormalons the perturbative series is \
factorially divergent\\neven after restricting to a given order in $1/N$, \
making the $1/N$ expansion a\\nnatural testing ground for the theory of \
resurgence. We study in detail the\\ninterplay between resurgent properties \
and the $1/N$ expansion in various\\nintegrable field theories with \
renormalons. We focus on the free energy in the\\npresence of a chemical \
potential coupled to a conserved charge, which can be\\ncomputed exactly with \
the thermodynamic Bethe ansatz (TBA). In some examples,\\nlike the first \
$1/N$ correction to the free energy in the non-linear sigma\\nmodel, the \
terms in the $1/N$ expansion can be fully decoded in terms of a\\nresurgent \
trans-series in the coupling constant. In the principal chiral field\\nwe \
find a new, explicit solution for the large $N$ free energy which can \
be\\nwritten as the median resummation of a trans-series with infinitely \
many,\\nanalytically computable IR renormalon corrections. However, in other \
examples,\\nlike the Gross-Neveu model, each term in the $1/N$ expansion \
includes\\nnon-perturbative corrections which can not be predicted by a \
resurgent analysis\\nof the corresponding perturbative series. We also study \
the properties of the\\nseries in $1/N$. In the Gross-Neveu model, where this \
is convergent, we\\nanalytically continue the series beyond its radius of \
convergence and show how\\nthe continuation matches with known dualities with \
sine-Gordon theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 5 Aug 2021 14:35:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
