            "  We present the Standard Model Effective Field Theories (SMEFT) \
from purely\non-shell arguments. Starting from a few basic assumptions such \
as Poincar\\'e\ninvariance and locality, we classify all the renormalisable \
and\nnon-renormalisable interactions at the lowest order in the couplings. \
From\nthese building blocks, we review how locality and unitarity enforce Lie \
algebra\nstructures to appear in the S-matrix elements together with \
relations among\ncouplings (and hypercharges). Furthermore, we give a fully \
on-shell algorithm\nto compute any higher-point tree-level amplitude (or form \
factor) in generic\nEFTs, bypassing BCFW-like recursion relations which are \
known to be problematic\nwhen non-renormalisable interactions are involved. \
