S^3\\times\n  S^3\\times S^1$ describing BPS line operators", "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, 1 figure; v3: typos corrected and clarifications \
added.\n  Version to appear in J.Phys.A", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1751-8121/ac354d", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study supersymmetric open strings in type IIB $AdS_3 \
\\times S^3 \\times S^3\n\\times S^1$ with mixed R-R and NS-NS fields. We \
focus on strings ending along a\nstraight line at the boundary of $AdS_3$, \
which can be interpreted as line\noperators in a dual CFT$_2$. We study both \
classical configurations and\nquadratic fluctuations around them. We find \
that strings sitting at a fixed\npoint in $S^3 \\times S^3 \\times S^1$, i.e. \
satisfying Dirichlet boundary\nconditions, are 1/2 BPS. We also show that \
strings sitting at different points\nof certain submanifolds of $S^3 \\times \
S^3 \\times S^1$ can still share some\nfraction of the supersymmetry. This \
allows to define supersymmetric smeared\nconfigurations by the superposition \
of them, which range from 1/2 BPS to 1/8\nBPS. In addition to the smeared \
configurations, there are as well 1/4 BPS and\n1/8 BPS strings satisfying \
Neumann boundary conditions. All these\nsupersymmetric strings are shown to \
be connected by a network of interpolating\nBPS boundary conditions. Our \
study reveals the existence of a rich moduli of\nsupersymmetric open string \
configurations, for which the appearance of massless\nfermionic fields in the \
spectrum of quadratic fluctuations is crucial.\n", 
