            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2109.00559\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alberto Lerda\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M. Billo, M. Frau, F. Galvagno, A. Lerda, A. Pini\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Strong-coupling results for $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
superconformal quivers and\\n  holography\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"45 pages, 9 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2021)161\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal quiver \
gauge theories in four\\ndimensions and evaluate the chiral/anti-chiral \
correlators of single-trace\\noperators. We show that it is convenient to \
form particular twisted and\\nuntwisted combinations of these operators \
suggested by the dual holographic\\ndescription of the theory. The various \
twisted sectors are orthogonal and the\\ncorrelators in each sector have \
always the same structure, as we show at the\\nlowest orders in perturbation \
theory with Feynman diagrams. Using localization\\nwe then map the \
computation to a matrix model. In this way we are able to\\nobtain formal \
expressions for the twisted correlators in the planar limit that\\nare valid \
for all values of the 't Hooft coupling $\\\\lambda$, and find that \
they\\nare proportional to $1/\\\\lambda$ at strong coupling. We successfully \
test the\\ncorrectness of our extrapolation against a direct numerical \
evaluation of the\\nmatrix model and argue that the $1/\\\\lambda$ behavior \
qualitatively agrees with\\nthe holographic description.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 1 Sep 2021 18:05:02 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
