            "  We consider $\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal quiver gauge \
theories in four\ndimensions and evaluate the chiral/anti-chiral correlators \
of single-trace\noperators. We show that it is convenient to form particular \
twisted and\nuntwisted combinations of these operators suggested by the dual \
holographic\ndescription of the theory. The various twisted sectors are \
orthogonal and the\ncorrelators in each sector have always the same \
structure, as we show at the\nlowest orders in perturbation theory with \
Feynman diagrams. Using localization\nwe then map the computation to a matrix \
model. In this way we are able to\nobtain formal expressions for the twisted \
correlators in the planar limit that\nare valid for all values of the 't \
Hooft coupling $\\lambda$, and find that they\nare proportional to \
$1/\\lambda$ at strong coupling. We successfully test the\ncorrectness of our \
extrapolation against a direct numerical evaluation of the\nmatrix model and \
argue that the $1/\\lambda$ behavior qualitatively agrees with\nthe \
holographic description.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
