           "id" -> "2109.06164", "submitter" -> "Dmytro Volin", "authors" -> 
            "Simon Ekhammar, Dmytro Volin", "title" -> 
            "Monodromy Bootstrap for SU(2|2) Quantum Spectral Curves: From \
Hubbard\n  model to AdS3/CFT2", "comments" -> 
            "53 pages; substantial revision", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP03(2022)192", "report-no" -> 
            "UUITP-44/21, NORDITA 2021-090", "categories" -> 
            "math-ph hep-th math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We propose a procedure to derive quantum spectral curves of \
AdS/CFT type by\nrequiring that a specially designed analytic continuation \
around the branch\npoint results in an automorphism of the underlying \
algebraic structure. In this\nway we derive four new curves. Two are based on \
SU(2|2) symmetry, and we show\nthat one of them, under the assumption of \
square root branch points, describes\nHubbard model. Two more are based on \
SU(2|2) x SU(2|2). In the special subcase\nof zero central charge, they both \
reduce to the unique nontrivial curve which\nfurthermore has analytic \
properties compatible with PSU(1,1|2) x PSU(1,1|2)\nreal form. A natural \
conjecture follows that this is the quantum spectral curve\nof AdS/CFT \
integrable system with AdS3 x S3 x T4 background supported by\nRR-flux. We \
support the conjecture by verifying its consistency with the\nmassive sector \
of asymptotic Bethe equations in the large volume regime. For\nthis spectral \
curve, it is compulsory that branch points are not of the square\nroot type \
which qualitatively distinguishes it from the previously known cases.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 13 Sep 2021 17:58:44 GMT"}, {
