            "  We develop a systematic approach to compute physical \
observables of\nintegrable spin chains with finite length. Our method is \
based on Bethe ansatz\nsolution of the integrable spin chain and \
computational algebraic geometry. The\nfinal results are analytic and no \
longer depend on Bethe roots. The computation\nis purely algebraic and does \
not rely on further assumptions or numerics. This\nmethod can be applied to \
compute a broad family of physical quantities in\nintegrable quantum spin \
chains. We demonstrate the power of the method by\ncomputing two important \
quantities in quench dynamics: the diagonal entropy and\nthe Loschmidt echo \
and obtain new analytic results.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 22 Sep 2021 08:02:55 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2021-09-23", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Jiang", "Yunfeng", ""}, {
              "Wen", "Rui", ""}, {"Zhang", "Yang", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
