 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the calculation of one-loop corrections to \
the partition functions\\nof a string ending on a circular or straight line \
in type IIB string theory on\\n$AdS_3\\\\times S^3 \\\\times T^4$ supported \
by a mixture of 3-form fluxes depending\\non a parameter $q$ (with $q=0$ \
being R-R and $q=1$ pure NS-NS cases).\\nCorrecting earlier results in the \
literature, we find that the partition\\nfunction depends on $q$ only through \
rescaled tension $T= T_0/(1-q^2)$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
