                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider gauge/gravity correspondence between \
maximally supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills theory in ($p+1$) dimensions and \
superstring theory on the\\nnear-horizon limit of the D$p$-brane solution. \
The string-frame metric is\\nAdS$_{p+1}\\\\times S^{8-p}$ times a Weyl \
factor, and there is no conformal\\nsymmetry except for $p=3$. In a previous \
paper by one of the present authors,\\nthe free-field result of gauge theory \
has been reproduced from string theory\\nfor a particular operator which has \
angular momentum along $S^{8-p}$. In this\\npaper, we extend this result to \
operators which have angular momenta along\\nAdS$_{p+2}$. Our approach is \
based on a Euclidean formulation proposed by\\nDobashi, Shimada and Yoneya \
and on the \\\"string bit\\\" picture. We first show that\\nthe spinning \
string solution in Lorentzian AdS, found by Gubser, Klebanov and\\nPolyakov, \
can be recast in a form which connects two points on the boundary \
of\\nEuclidean AdS. Transition amplitudes of such strings can be interpreted \
as\\ngauge theory correlators. We study the case of zero gauge coupling by \
ignoring\\ninteractions among string bits (massless particles in \
ten-dimensional spacetime\\nwhich constitute a string), and show that the \
free-field results of gauge\\ntheory are reproduced.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
