            "title" -> 
            "Rotating particles in AdS: Holography at weak gauge coupling and \
without\n  conformal symmetry", "comments" -> 
            "38 pages; v2: Corrected typos; v3: Corrected a misleading \
statement\n  about fluctuations around the geodesic at the end of Sec. 4, and \
presented\n  explicit calculations in Appendix A. Conclusion of the paper is \
unchanged", "journal-ref" -> "Prog Theor Exp Phys (2022)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1093/ptep/ptac041", "report-no" -> "RUP-21-18, WUCG-21-11", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider gauge/gravity correspondence between maximally \
supersymmetric\nYang-Mills theory in ($p+1$) dimensions and superstring \
theory on the\nnear-horizon limit of the D$p$-brane solution. The \
string-frame metric is\nAdS$_{p+1}\\times S^{8-p}$ times a Weyl factor, and \
there is no conformal\nsymmetry except for $p=3$. In a previous paper by one \
of the present authors,\nthe free-field result of gauge theory has been \
reproduced from string theory\nfor a particular operator which has angular \
momentum along $S^{8-p}$. In this\npaper, we extend this result to operators \
which have angular momenta along\nAdS$_{p+2}$. Our approach is based on a \
Euclidean formulation proposed by\nDobashi, Shimada and Yoneya and on the \
\"string bit\" picture. We first show that\nthe spinning string solution in \
Lorentzian AdS, found by Gubser, Klebanov and\nPolyakov, can be recast in a \
form which connects two points on the boundary of\nEuclidean AdS. Transition \
amplitudes of such strings can be interpreted as\ngauge theory correlators. \
We study the case of zero gauge coupling by ignoring\ninteractions among \
string bits (massless particles in ten-dimensional spacetime\nwhich \
constitute a string), and show that the free-field results of gauge\ntheory \
are reproduced.\n", 
