            "  In this pedagogical review we introduce systematic approaches \
to deforming\nintegrable 2-dimensional sigma models. We use the integrable \
principal chiral\nmodel and the conformal Wess-Zumino-Witten model as our \
starting points and\nexplore their Yang-Baxter and current-current \
deformations. There is an\nintricate web of relations between these models \
based on underlying algebraic\nstructures and worldsheet dualities, which is \
highlighted throughout. We finish\nwith a discussion of the generalisation to \
other symmetric integrable models,\nincluding some original results related \
to Z T cosets and their deformations,\nand the application to string theory. \
This review is based on notes written for\nlectures delivered at the school \
\"Integrability, Dualities and Deformations\",\nwhich ran from 23 to 27 \
August 2021 in Santiago de Compostela and virtually.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
