         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2109.14699", "submitter" -> "Richard Szabo", "authors" -> 
            "Lotte Hollands, Philipp R\\\"uter, Richard J. Szabo", "title" -> 
            "A geometric recipe for twisted superpotentials", "comments" -> 
            "102 pages, 42 figures; v2: references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP12(2021)164", "report-no" -> 
            "EMPG-20-02", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.AG math.DG math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We give a pedagogical introduction to spectral networks and \
abelianization,\nas well as their relevance to $\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
supersymmetric field theories in\nfour dimensions. Motivated by a conjecture \
of Nekrasov-Rosly-Shatashvili, we\ndetail a geometric recipe for computing \
the effective twisted superpotential\nfor $\\mathcal{N}=2$ field theories of \
class $\\mathcal{S}$ as a generating\nfunction of the brane of opers, with \
respect to the spectral coordinates found\nfrom abelianization. We present \
two new examples, the simplest Argyres-Douglas\ntheory and the pure $SU(2)$ \
gauge theory, while we conjecture the\n$\\epsilon$-expansion of the effective \
twisted superpotential for the $E_6$\nMinahan-Nemeschansky theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 29 Sep 2021 20:07:09 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 25 Oct 2021 19:43:53 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2022-01-05", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Hollands", "Lotte", ""}, {
              "R\[UDoubleDot]ter", "Philipp", ""}, {
              "Szabo", "Richard J.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
