               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matteo Beccaria\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Beccaria, Simone Giombi, Arkady A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Higher order RG flow on the Wilson line in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25 pages, several TikZ figures. v2: minor \
corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2022)056\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-AT-2021-04\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Extending earlier work, we find the two-loop term in \
the beta-function for\\nthe scalar coupling $\\\\zeta$ in a generalized \
Wilson loop operator of the\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM theory, working in the \
planar weak-coupling expansion. The\\nbeta-function for $\\\\zeta$ has fixed \
points at $\\\\zeta=\\\\pm 1$ and $\\\\zeta=0$,\\ncorresponding respectively \
to the supersymmetric Wilson-Maldacena loop and to\\nthe standard Wilson loop \
without scalar coupling. As a consequence of our\\nresult for the \
beta-function, we obtain a prediction for the two-loop term in\\nthe \
anomalous dimension of the scalar field inserted on the standard \
Wilson\\nloop. We also find a subset of higher-loop contributions (with \
highest powers\\nof $\\\\zeta$ at each order in `t Hooft coupling) coming \
from the scalar ladder\\ngraphs determining the corresponding terms in the \
five-loop beta-function. We\\ndiscuss the related structure of the circular \
Wilson loop expectation value\\ncommenting, in particular, on consistency \
with a 1d defect version of the\\nF-theorem. We also compute (to two loops in \
the planar ladder approximation)\\nthe two-point correlators of scalars \
inserted on the Wilson line.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
