             "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Extending earlier work, we find the two-loop term in the \
beta-function for\nthe scalar coupling $\\zeta$ in a generalized Wilson loop \
operator of the\n$\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM theory, working in the planar \
weak-coupling expansion. The\nbeta-function for $\\zeta$ has fixed points at \
$\\zeta=\\pm 1$ and $\\zeta=0$,\ncorresponding respectively to the \
supersymmetric Wilson-Maldacena loop and to\nthe standard Wilson loop without \
scalar coupling. As a consequence of our\nresult for the beta-function, we \
obtain a prediction for the two-loop term in\nthe anomalous dimension of the \
scalar field inserted on the standard Wilson\nloop. We also find a subset of \
higher-loop contributions (with highest powers\nof $\\zeta$ at each order in \
`t Hooft coupling) coming from the scalar ladder\ngraphs determining the \
corresponding terms in the five-loop beta-function. We\ndiscuss the related \
structure of the circular Wilson loop expectation value\ncommenting, in \
particular, on consistency with a 1d defect version of the\nF-theorem. We \
also compute (to two loops in the planar ladder approximation)\nthe two-point \
correlators of scalars inserted on the Wilson line.\n", 
