                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a real time holographic framework to study \
thermalization\\nprocesses of a family of QFT excited states. The \
construction builds on\\nSkenderis-van Rees's holographic duals to QFT \
Schwinger-Keldysh complex-time\\nordered paths. Thermalization is explored \
choosing a set of observables $F_n$\\nwhich essentially isolate the excited \
state contribution. Focusing on theories\\ndefined on compact manifolds and \
with excited states defined in terms of\\nEuclidean path integrals, we \
identify boundary conditions that allow to avoid\\nany number of modes in the \
initial field state. In the large conformal\\ndimensions regime, we give \
precise prescriptions on how to compute the\\nobservables in terms of bulk \
geodesics.\\n\""}]}, {
