                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the integrable two-site states of the quantum \
integrable models\\nsolvable by the nested algebraic Bethe ansatz and \
possessing\\n$\\\\mathfrak{gl}(N)$-invariant R-matrix. We investigate the \
overlaps between the\\nintegrable two-site states and the wave-functions. To \
find exact derivations\\nfor the factorized overlap formulas for the nested \
integrable systems is a\\nlongstanding unsolved problem. In this paper we \
give a derivation for a large\\nclass of the integrable states of the \
$\\\\mathfrak{gl}(N)$ symmetric spin chain.\\nThe first part of the \
derivation is to calculate recurrence relations for the\\noff-shell overlap \
that uniquely fix it. Using these recursions we prove that\\nthe normalized \
overlaps of the multi-particle states have factorized forms\\nwhich contain \
the products of the one-particle overlaps and the ratio of the\\nGaudin-like \
determinants. We also show that the previously proposed overlap\\nformulas \
agree with our general formula.\\n\""}]}, {
