             "comments" -> "79 pages, accepted version (Nucl.Phys.B)", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2022.115909",
             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the integrable two-site states of the quantum \
integrable models\nsolvable by the nested algebraic Bethe ansatz and \
possessing\n$\\mathfrak{gl}(N)$-invariant R-matrix. We investigate the \
overlaps between the\nintegrable two-site states and the wave-functions. To \
find exact derivations\nfor the factorized overlap formulas for the nested \
integrable systems is a\nlongstanding unsolved problem. In this paper we give \
a derivation for a large\nclass of the integrable states of the \
$\\mathfrak{gl}(N)$ symmetric spin chain.\nThe first part of the derivation \
is to calculate recurrence relations for the\noff-shell overlap that uniquely \
fix it. Using these recursions we prove that\nthe normalized overlaps of the \
multi-particle states have factorized forms\nwhich contain the products of \
the one-particle overlaps and the ratio of the\nGaudin-like determinants. We \
also show that the previously proposed overlap\nformulas agree with our \
general formula.\n", 
