 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the large charge sector of the defect CFT \
defined by the half-BPS\\nWilson loop in planar $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory.\\nSpecifically, we consider correlation \
functions of two large charge insertions\\nand several light insertions in \
the double-scaling limit where the 't Hooft\\ncoupling $\\\\lambda$ and the \
large charge $J$ are sent to infinity, with the\\nratio \
$J/\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}$ held fixed. They are holographically dual to \
the\\nexpectation values of light vertex operators on a classical string \
solution\\nwith large angular momentum, which we evaluate in the leading \
large $J$ limit.\\nWe also compute the two-point function of large charge \
insertions by evaluating\\nthe on-shell string action, supplemented by the \
boundary terms that generalize\\nthe one introduced by Drukker, Gross and \
Ooguri for the Wilson loop without\\ninsertions. For a special class of \
correlation functions, we reproduce the\\nstring results from field theory by \
using supersymmetric localization. The\\nresults are given by correlation \
functions in an \\\"emergent\\\" matrix model whose\\nmatrix size is \
proportional to $J$ and whose spectral curve coincides with that\\nof the \
classical string. Similar matrix models appeared in the study of\\nextremal \
correlators in rank-1 $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal field theories,\\nbut \
our results hold also for non-extremal cases.\\n\""}]}, {
