               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Tanay Kibe\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Tanay Kibe, Prabha Mandayam and Ayan Mukhopadhyay\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic spacetime, black holes and quantum error \
correcting codes: A\\n  review\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"92 pages; version to appear in a special EPJC volume \
\\\"New Frontiers\\n  in Holographic Duality\\\"\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Eur. Phys. J. C 82, 463 (2022)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1140/epjc/s10052-022-10382-1\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc quant-ph\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This article reviews the progress in our understanding \
of the reconstruction\\nof the bulk spacetime in the holographic \
correspondence from the dual field\\ntheory including an account of how these \
developments have led to the\\nreproduction of the Page curve of the Hawking \
radiation from black holes. We\\nreview quantum error correction and relevant \
recovery maps with toy examples\\nbased on tensor networks, and discuss how \
it provides the desired framework for\\nbulk reconstruction in which apparent \
inconsistencies with properties of the\\noperator algebra in the dual field \
theory are naturally resolved. The\\nimportance of understanding the modular \
flow in the dual field theory has been\\nemphasized. We discuss how the \
state-dependence of reconstruction of black hole\\nmicrostates can be \
formulated in the framework of quantum error correction with\\ninputs from \
extremal surfaces along with a quantification of the complexity of\\nencoding \
of bulk operators. Finally, we motivate and discuss a class of\\ntractable \
microstate models of black holes which can illuminate how the black\\nhole \
complementarity principle can emerge operationally without \
encountering\\ninformation paradoxes, and provide new insights into \
generation of desirable\\nfeatures of encoding into the Hawking radiation.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
