            "Holographic spacetime, black holes and quantum error correcting \
codes: A\n  review", "comments" -> 
            "92 pages; version to appear in a special EPJC volume \"New \
Frontiers\n  in Holographic Duality\"", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Eur. Phys. J. C 82, 463 (2022)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1140/epjc/s10052-022-10382-1", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc quant-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This article reviews the progress in our understanding of the \
reconstruction\nof the bulk spacetime in the holographic correspondence from \
the dual field\ntheory including an account of how these developments have \
led to the\nreproduction of the Page curve of the Hawking radiation from \
black holes. We\nreview quantum error correction and relevant recovery maps \
with toy examples\nbased on tensor networks, and discuss how it provides the \
desired framework for\nbulk reconstruction in which apparent inconsistencies \
with properties of the\noperator algebra in the dual field theory are \
naturally resolved. The\nimportance of understanding the modular flow in the \
dual field theory has been\nemphasized. We discuss how the state-dependence \
of reconstruction of black hole\nmicrostates can be formulated in the \
framework of quantum error correction with\ninputs from extremal surfaces \
along with a quantification of the complexity of\nencoding of bulk operators. \
Finally, we motivate and discuss a class of\ntractable microstate models of \
black holes which can illuminate how the black\nhole complementarity \
principle can emerge operationally without encountering\ninformation \
paradoxes, and provide new insights into generation of desirable\nfeatures of \
encoding into the Hawking radiation.\n", 
