 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give a precise definition of BPS vortex loops in 3D \
non-abelian gauge\\ntheories with ${\\\\cal N}=2$ SUSY by the path integral \
over fields with a\\nprescribed singular behavior. We compute the expectation \
value of a BPS vortex\\nloop on an ellipsoid. Using the result we revisit the \
known equivalence between\\nWilson and vortex loops in pure Chern-Simons \
theory. Naive computations of\\nexpectation values in ${\\\\cal N}=2$ theory \
leads to an unwanted shift of\\nparameters in the rule of correspondence. We \
resolve the problem by relating\\nthe shift to the global anomaly of \
${\\\\cal N}=2$ SUSY quantum mechanics. For\\ntheories with $U(N)$ gauge \
group we also develop an alternative description of\\nvortex loops in terms \
of 1D ${\\\\cal N}=2$ SUSY quantum mechanics on their\\nworldline. For vortex \
loops in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ theories, our construction\\nreproduces some of the \
quiver GLSMs of Assel and Gomis.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
