               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Shai M. Chester, Ross Dempsey, and Silviu S. Pufu\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bootstrapping $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super-Yang-Mills on the \
conformal manifold\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"31 pages plus appendices, 13 figures, v3 expanded \
discussion of\\n  integration region\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUPT-2627\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We combine supersymmetric localization results with \
numerical bootstrap\\ntechniques to compute upper bounds on the low-lying CFT \
data of ${\\\\cal N} = 4$\\nsuper-Yang-Mills theory as a function of the \
complexified gauge coupling\\n$\\\\tau$. In particular, from the stress \
tensor multiplet four-point function, we\\nextract the scaling dimension of \
the lowest-lying unprotected scalar operator\\nand its OPE coefficient. While \
our method can be applied in principle to any\\ngauge group $G$, we focus on \
$G = SU(2)$ and $SU(3)$ for simplicity. At weak\\ncoupling, the upper bounds \
we find are very close to the corresponding\\nfour-loop results. We also give \
preliminary evidence that these upper bounds\\nbecome small islands under \
reasonable assumptions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
