         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2111.07989", "submitter" -> "Shai Chester", "authors" -> 
            "Shai M. Chester, Ross Dempsey, and Silviu S. Pufu", "title" -> 
            "Bootstrapping $\\mathcal{N}=4$ super-Yang-Mills on the conformal \
manifold", "comments" -> 
            "31 pages plus appendices, 13 figures, v3 expanded discussion of\n\
  integration region", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "PUPT-2627", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We combine supersymmetric localization results with numerical \
bootstrap\ntechniques to compute upper bounds on the low-lying CFT data of ${\
\\cal N} = 4$\nsuper-Yang-Mills theory as a function of the complexified \
gauge coupling\n$\\tau$. In particular, from the stress tensor multiplet \
four-point function, we\nextract the scaling dimension of the lowest-lying \
unprotected scalar operator\nand its OPE coefficient. While our method can be \
applied in principle to any\ngauge group $G$, we focus on $G = SU(2)$ and \
$SU(3)$ for simplicity. At weak\ncoupling, the upper bounds we find are very \
close to the corresponding\nfour-loop results. We also give preliminary \
evidence that these upper bounds\nbecome small islands under reasonable \
assumptions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 15 Nov 2021 18:50:45 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 19 Nov 2021 15:06:26 GMT"}, {
