                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Sacchi and Orr Sela and Gabi Zafrir\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the 3d compactifications of 5d SCFTs associated with \
SU(N+1) gauge\\n  theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"87 pages, 24 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 05 (2022) 053\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2022)053\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the $3d$ $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ theories resulting \
from the\\ncompactification of a family of $5d$ SCFTs on a torus with flux in \
the global\\nsymmetry. The family of $5d$ SCFTs used in the analysis is the \
one that UV\\ncompletes the $5d$ $SU(N+1)$ gauge theories with Chern--Simons \
level $k$ and\\n$N_f$ fundamental hypermultiplets, generalizing the previous \
investigation of\\nthe torus compactifications of the rank 1 Seiberg \
$E_{N_f+1}$ SCFT (which is\\nthe $N=1$ member of the family). This \
construction systematically yields\\nthree-dimensional theories presenting \
highly non-trivial non-perturbative\\nphenomena such as infra-red dualities \
and enhanced symmetries, which we check\\nusing various methods.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
