               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Simone Noja\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Simone Noja\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the Geometry of Forms on Supermanifolds\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"60 pages, matches the published version. Thanks to the \
anonymous\\n  referee for useful comments and remarks\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Differential Geometry and its Applications, vol. 88 \
(2023) 101999\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/j.difgeo.2023.101999\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"math.AG math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper provides a rigorous account on the geometry \
of forms on\\nsupermanifolds, with a focus on its algebraic-geometric \
aspects. First, we\\nintroduce the de Rham complex of differential forms and \
we compute its\\ncohomology. We then discuss three intrinsic definitions of \
the Berezinian sheaf\\nof a supermanifold - as a quotient sheaf, via \
cohomology of the super Koszul\\ncomplex or via cohomology of the total de \
Rham complex. Further, we study the\\nproperties of the Berezinian sheaf, \
showing in particular that it defines a\\nright $\\\\mathcal{D}$-module. Then \
we introduce integral forms and their complex\\nand we compute their \
cohomology, by providing a suitable Poincar\\\\'e lemma. We\\nshow that the \
complex of differential forms and integral forms are\\nquasi-isomorphic and \
their cohomology computes the de Rham cohomology of the\\nreduced space of \
the supermanifold. The notion of Berezin integral is then\\nintroduced and \
put to the good use to prove the superanalog of Stokes' theorem\\nand Poincar\
\\\\'e duality, which relates differential and integral forms \
on\\nsupermanifolds. Finally, a different point of view is discussed by \
introducing\\nthe total tangent supermanifold and (integrable) pseudoforms in \
a new way. In\\nthis context, it is shown that a particular class of \
integrable pseudoforms\\nhaving a distributional dependence supported at a \
point on the fibers are\\nisomorphic to integral forms. Within the general \
overview several new proofs of\\nresults are scattered.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 24 Nov 2021 23:21:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 18 Apr 2023 16:27:28 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2023-04-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Noja\"", ",", "\"Simone\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
