            "Simone Noja", "title" -> 
            "On the Geometry of Forms on Supermanifolds", "comments" -> 
            "60 pages, matches the published version. Thanks to the anonymous\
\n  referee for useful comments and remarks", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Differential Geometry and its Applications, vol. 88 (2023) \
101999", "doi" -> "10.1016/j.difgeo.2023.101999", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "math.AG math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This paper provides a rigorous account on the geometry of \
forms on\nsupermanifolds, with a focus on its algebraic-geometric aspects. \
First, we\nintroduce the de Rham complex of differential forms and we compute \
its\ncohomology. We then discuss three intrinsic definitions of the \
Berezinian sheaf\nof a supermanifold - as a quotient sheaf, via cohomology of \
the super Koszul\ncomplex or via cohomology of the total de Rham complex. \
Further, we study the\nproperties of the Berezinian sheaf, showing in \
particular that it defines a\nright $\\mathcal{D}$-module. Then we introduce \
integral forms and their complex\nand we compute their cohomology, by \
providing a suitable Poincar\\'e lemma. We\nshow that the complex of \
differential forms and integral forms are\nquasi-isomorphic and their \
cohomology computes the de Rham cohomology of the\nreduced space of the \
supermanifold. The notion of Berezin integral is then\nintroduced and put to \
the good use to prove the superanalog of Stokes' theorem\nand Poincar\\'e \
duality, which relates differential and integral forms on\nsupermanifolds. \
Finally, a different point of view is discussed by introducing\nthe total \
tangent supermanifold and (integrable) pseudoforms in a new way. In\nthis \
context, it is shown that a particular class of integrable pseudoforms\n\
having a distributional dependence supported at a point on the fibers are\n\
isomorphic to integral forms. Within the general overview several new proofs \
of\nresults are scattered.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 24 Nov 2021 23:21:12 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 18 Apr 2023 16:27:28 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-04-19", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Noja", "Simone", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
