               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Francesco Galvagno\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Emitted Radiation in Superconformal Field Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, 4 figures, Review article to be published in \
EPJ Plus\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The computation of the emitted radiation by an \
accelerated external particle\\ncan be addressed in a gauge theory with the \
insertion of a Wilson loop. With\\nthe addition of conformal symmetry this \
problem is consistently formalized in\\nterms of correlation functions in \
presence of the Wilson loop, which are\\nconstrained by defect CFT \
techniques. In theories with extended supersymmetry\\nwe can also resort to \
supersymmetric localization on a four-sphere. By using\\nthis set of tools, \
we review the close relation between the Bremsstrahlung\\nfunction and the \
stress energy tensor one-point coefficient in abelian theories\\nand in \
superconformal field theories. After presenting the state of the art \
for\\ngeneric CFTs, we mainly focus on the supersymmetric cases. We discuss \
the\\ndifferences between the maximally supersymmetric $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
case and\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCFTs, and finally we review the general and \
exact result for\\nthe emitted radiation in terms of a first order derivative \
of the Wilson loop\\nexpectation value on a squashed sphere.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 7 Dec 2021 17:26:05 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
