           "id" -> "2112.03841", "submitter" -> "Francesco Galvagno", 
            "authors" -> "Francesco Galvagno", "title" -> 
            "Emitted Radiation in Superconformal Field Theories", "comments" -> 
            "28 pages, 4 figures, Review article to be published in EPJ Plus",
             "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The computation of the emitted radiation by an accelerated \
external particle\ncan be addressed in a gauge theory with the insertion of a \
Wilson loop. With\nthe addition of conformal symmetry this problem is \
consistently formalized in\nterms of correlation functions in presence of the \
Wilson loop, which are\nconstrained by defect CFT techniques. In theories \
with extended supersymmetry\nwe can also resort to supersymmetric \
localization on a four-sphere. By using\nthis set of tools, we review the \
close relation between the Bremsstrahlung\nfunction and the stress energy \
tensor one-point coefficient in abelian theories\nand in superconformal field \
theories. After presenting the state of the art for\ngeneric CFTs, we mainly \
focus on the supersymmetric cases. We discuss the\ndifferences between the \
maximally supersymmetric $\\mathcal{N}=4$ case and\n$\\mathcal{N}=2$ SCFTs, \
and finally we review the general and exact result for\nthe emitted radiation \
in terms of a first order derivative of the Wilson loop\nexpectation value on \
a squashed sphere.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 7 Dec 2021 17:26:05 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2021-12-08", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Galvagno", "Francesco", ""}}}], 
