 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider superstrings on the pure-Ramond-Ramond \
$AdS_3\\\\times S^3\\\\times\\nT^4$ background. Using the recently-proposed \
dressing factors for the\\nworldsheet S matrix, we formulate the string \
hypothesis for the mirror\\nBethe-Yang equations, and use it to derive the \
canonical mirror thermodynamic\\nBethe ansatz (TBA) equations of the model. \
For the first time, these equations\\naccount for all massive and massless \
modes of the model, and do not resort to\\nany limit or special kinematics. \
We also discuss the simplified mirror TBA\\nequations and the Y-system of the \
model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
