                 "\"Index of the Transversally Elliptic Complex in \
Pestunization\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages + appendices; version to be published in \
J.Phys.A\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/ac7921\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this note we present a formula for the equivariant \
index of the\\ncohomological complex obtained from localization of \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SYM on\\nsimply-connected compact four-manifolds with a \
$T^2$-action. Knowledge of said\\nindex is essential to compute the \
perturbative part of the partition function\\nfor the theory. In the \
topologically twisted case, the complex is elliptic and\\nits index can be \
computed in a standard way using the Atiyah-Bott localization\\nformula. \
Recently, a framework for more general types of twisting, \
so-called\\ncohomological twisting, was introduced for which the complex \
turns out to be\\nonly transversally elliptic. While the index of such a \
complex has been\\ncomputed for some cases where the manifold can be lifted \
to a Sasakian\\n$S^1$-fibration in five dimensions, a general \
four-dimensional treatment was\\nstill lacking. We provide a formal, purely \
four-dimensional treatment of the\\ncohomological complex, showing that the \
Laplacian part can be globally split\\noff while the remaining part can be \
trivialized uniquely in the\\ngroup-direction. This ultimately produces a \
simple formula for the index\\napplicable for any compact simply-connected \
four-manifold. Finally, the index\\nformula is applied to examples on $S^4$, \
$\\\\mathbb{CP}^2$ and $\\\\mathbb{F}^1$.\\nFor the latter, we use the result \
to compute the perturbative partition\\nfunction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
