         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2112.10658", "submitter" -> "Roman Mauch", "authors" -> 
            "Roman Mauch and Lorenzo Ruggeri", "title" -> 
            "Index of the Transversally Elliptic Complex in Pestunization", 
            "comments" -> 
            "26 pages + appendices; version to be published in J.Phys.A", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1088/1751-8121/ac7921", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  In this note we present a formula for the equivariant index of \
the\ncohomological complex obtained from localization of $\\mathcal{N}=2$ SYM \
on\nsimply-connected compact four-manifolds with a $T^2$-action. Knowledge of \
said\nindex is essential to compute the perturbative part of the partition \
function\nfor the theory. In the topologically twisted case, the complex is \
elliptic and\nits index can be computed in a standard way using the \
Atiyah-Bott localization\nformula. Recently, a framework for more general \
types of twisting, so-called\ncohomological twisting, was introduced for \
which the complex turns out to be\nonly transversally elliptic. While the \
index of such a complex has been\ncomputed for some cases where the manifold \
can be lifted to a Sasakian\n$S^1$-fibration in five dimensions, a general \
four-dimensional treatment was\nstill lacking. We provide a formal, purely \
four-dimensional treatment of the\ncohomological complex, showing that the \
Laplacian part can be globally split\noff while the remaining part can be \
trivialized uniquely in the\ngroup-direction. This ultimately produces a \
simple formula for the index\napplicable for any compact simply-connected \
four-manifold. Finally, the index\nformula is applied to examples on $S^4$, $\
\\mathbb{CP}^2$ and $\\mathbb{F}^1$.\nFor the latter, we use the result to \
compute the perturbative partition\nfunction.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 20 Dec 2021 16:34:22 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 1 Mar 2022 16:50:15 GMT"}, {
