               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2112.12025\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sibylle Driezen\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riccardo Borsato, Sibylle Driezen and J. Luis \
Miramontes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Homogeneous Yang-Baxter deformations as undeformed yet \
twisted models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30+10 pages; v2 published version. Small clarifications \
in {\\\\S}3.3.1\\n  added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2022)053\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The homogeneous Yang-Baxter deformation is part of a \
larger web of integrable\\ndeformations and dualities that recently have been \
studied with motivations in\\nintegrable $\\\\sigma$-models, \
solution-generating techniques in supergravity and\\nDouble Field Theory, and \
possible generalisations of the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence. The \
$\\\\sigma$-models obtained by the homogeneous Yang-Baxter\\ndeformation with \
periodic boundary conditions on the worldsheet are on-shell\\nequivalent to \
undeformed models, yet with twisted boundary conditions. While\\nthis has \
been known for some time, the expression provided so far for the \
twist\\nfeatures non-localities (in terms of the degrees of freedom of the \
deformed\\nmodel) that prevent practical calculations, and in particular the \
construction\\nof the classical spectral curve. We solve this problem by \
rewriting the\\nequation defining the twist in terms of the degrees of \
freedom of the\\nundeformed yet twisted model, and we show that we are able \
to solve it in full\\ngenerality. Remarkably, this solution is a local \
expression. We discuss the\\nconsequences of the twist at the level of the \
monodromy matrix and of the\\nclassical spectral curve, analysing in \
particular the concrete examples of\\nabelian, almost abelian and Jordanian \
deformations of the Yang-Baxter class.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 22 Dec 2021 16:50:18 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 Jun 2022 13:09:23 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2022-06-24\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
