               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sanefumi Moriyama\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Tomohiro Furukawa, Kazunobu Matsumura, Sanefumi Moriyama, \
Tomoki\\n  Nakanishi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Duality Cascades and Affine Weyl Groups\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"51 pages, 12 eps figures; v3: published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2022)132\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NITEP 127, OCU-PHYS 554\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Brane configurations in a circle allow subsequent \
applications of the\\nHanany-Witten transitions, which are known as duality \
cascades. By studying the\\nprocess of duality cascades corresponding to \
quantum curves with symmetries of\\nWeyl groups, we find a hidden structure \
of affine Weyl groups. Namely, the\\nfundamental domain of duality cascades \
consisting of all the final destinations\\nis characterized by the affine \
Weyl chamber and the duality cascades are\\nrealized as translations of the \
affine Weyl group, where the overall rank in\\nthe brane configuration \
associates to the grading operator of the affine\\nalgebra. The structure of \
the affine Weyl group guarantees the finiteness of\\nthe processes and the \
uniqueness of the endpoint of the duality cascades. In\\naddition to the \
original duality cascades, we can generalize to the cases \
with\\nFayet-Iliopoulos parameters. There we can utilize the Weyl group to \
analyze the\\nfundamental domain similarly and find that the fundamental \
domain continues to\\nbe the affine Weyl chamber. We further interpret the \
Weyl group we impose as a\\n\\\"half\\\" of the Hanany-Witten \
transition.\\n\""}]}, {
