            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Brane configurations in a circle allow subsequent applications \
of the\nHanany-Witten transitions, which are known as duality cascades. By \
studying the\nprocess of duality cascades corresponding to quantum curves \
with symmetries of\nWeyl groups, we find a hidden structure of affine Weyl \
groups. Namely, the\nfundamental domain of duality cascades consisting of all \
the final destinations\nis characterized by the affine Weyl chamber and the \
duality cascades are\nrealized as translations of the affine Weyl group, \
where the overall rank in\nthe brane configuration associates to the grading \
operator of the affine\nalgebra. The structure of the affine Weyl group \
guarantees the finiteness of\nthe processes and the uniqueness of the \
endpoint of the duality cascades. In\naddition to the original duality \
cascades, we can generalize to the cases with\nFayet-Iliopoulos parameters. \
There we can utilize the Weyl group to analyze the\nfundamental domain \
similarly and find that the fundamental domain continues to\nbe the affine \
Weyl chamber. We further interpret the Weyl group we impose as a\n\"half\" of \
the Hanany-Witten transition.\n", 
