               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sibylle Driezen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Modave Lectures on Classical Integrability in $2d$ Field \
Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"50 pages, 5 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  These lecture notes are based on a blackboard course \
given at the XVII Modave\\nSummer School in Mathematical Physics held from 13 \
-- 17 September 2021 in\\nBrussels (Belgium), and aimed at Ph.D. students in \
High Energy Theoretical\\nPhysics. We start with introducing classical \
integrability in\\nfinite-dimensional systems to set the stage for our main \
purpose: introducing\\ntwo-dimensional classical field theories which are \
integrable. We focus on\\ntheir zero-curvature formulation through the \
so-called Lax connection, which\\nensures the existence of an infinite tower \
of conserved charges. We then move\\non to their Poisson bracket structure, \
known as the Sklyanin or Maillet\\nstructure, which ensures complete \
classical integrability. All the concepts\\nthat we encounter will be \
illustrated with the integrable Principal Chiral\\nModel, which is the \
canonical sigma-model that appears (or its generalisations)\\non the \
worldsheet of many string backgrounds. Along the way we briefly comment\\non \
the properties of integrability at the quantum level.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
