 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Superconformal field theory with $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
supersymmetry in four\\ndimensional spacetime provides a prime playground to \
study strongly coupled\\nphenomena in quantum field theory. Its rigid \
structure ensures valuable\\nanalytic control over non-perturbative effects, \
yet the theory is still\\nflexible enough to incorporate a large landscape of \
quantum systems. Here we\\naim to offer a guidebook to fundamental features \
of the 4d $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$\\nsuperconformal field theories and basic tools \
to construct them in\\nstring/M-/F-theory. The content is based on a series \
of lectures at the Quantum\\nField Theories and Geometry \
School\\n(https://sites.google.com/view/qftandgeometrysummerschool/home) in \
July 2020.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
