 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  According to lattice simulations and other theoretical \
approaches, the scalar\\nglueball is the lightest state in the Yang-Mills \
sector of QCD. Since within\\nthis sector the scalar glueball is stable, the \
scattering between two glueballs\\nis a well-defined process. Moreover, a \
glueball-glueball bound state, called\\nglueballonium, might exist if the \
attraction turns out to be large enough. In\\nthis work, we concentrate on \
the formation of the glueballonium in the context\\nof the dilaton potential. \
In particular, we investigate the parameter values\\nfor which such a \
glueballonium emerges.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
