            "  Integrable models of statistical mechanics play a prominent \
role in modern\nmathematical physics, especially in conformal field theory, \
knot theory,\ncombinatorics, topology, etc. In this brief review, we discuss \
a program of\nconstructing integrable lattice spin models with the nearest \
neighbor\ninteraction using methods inspired by the supersymmetric gauge \
theory\ncomputations, called gauge/YBE correspondence. After a brief \
introduction to\nthe topic, we review some recent examples of this \
correspondence and the role\nof special functions and symmetries. Finally, we \
discuss future directions of\nresearch.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 2 Jan 2022 12:53:35 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2022-01-04", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Gahramanov", "Ilmar", ""}}}],
