          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2201.10554", "submitter" -> "Dimitrios Katsinis", 
            "authors" -> "Dimitrios Katsinis", "title" -> 
            "Novel aspects of integrability for NLSMs in symmetric spaces", 
            "comments" -> 
            "38 pages, v2: added section on the conserved charges generated \
by the\n  monodromy matrix, matches published version", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rev.D 105 (2022) 12, 126008", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.105.126008", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We obtained the formal solution of the auxiliary system of Non \
Linear Sigma\nModels, whose target space is a rank 1 symmetric space based on \
the indefinite\northogonal group O(p,q), corresponding to an arbitrary \
solution of the NLSM.\nThis class includes Anti-de Sitter, de Sitter and \
Hyperbolic spaces, which are\nof interest in view of the AdS/CFT \
correspondence. The formal solution is\nrelated to the Pohlmeyer reduction of \
the NLSM, constituting another link\nbetween the NLSM and the reduced theory. \
Besides deriving the solution, we also\nreview the Pohlmeyer reduction of \
such models. Finally, we comment on the\nimplications for the monodromy \
matrix and its eigenvalues.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 25 Jan 2022 18:58:50 GMT"}, {
