            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2201.12223\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pietro Longhi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sibasish Banerjee, Pietro Longhi, Mauricio Romo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A-branes, foliations and localization\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"51 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s00023-022-01231-8\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.AG math.SG\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper studies a notion of enumerative invariants \
for stable $A$-branes,\\nand discusses its relation to invariants defined by \
spectral and exponential\\nnetworks. A natural definition of stable \
$A$-branes and their counts is\\nprovided by the string theoretic origin of \
the topological $A$-model. This is\\nthe Witten index of the supersymmetric \
quantum mechanics of a single $D3$ brane\\nsupported on a special Lagrangian \
in a Calabi-Yau threefold. Geometrically,\\nthis is closely related to the \
Euler characteristic of the $A$-brane moduli\\nspace. Using the natural torus \
action on this moduli space, we reduce the\\ncomputation of its Euler \
characteristic to a count of fixed points via\\nequivariant localization. \
Studying the $A$-branes that correspond to fixed\\npoints, we make contact \
with definitions of spectral and exponential networks.\\nWe find agreement \
between the counts defined via the Witten index, and the BPS\\ninvariants \
defined by networks. By extension, our definition also matches \
with\\nDonaldson-Thomas invariants of $B$-branes related by homological \
mirror\\nsymmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 28 Jan 2022 16:25:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
