            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th math.AG math.SG", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  This paper studies a notion of enumerative invariants for \
stable $A$-branes,\nand discusses its relation to invariants defined by \
spectral and exponential\nnetworks. A natural definition of stable $A$-branes \
and their counts is\nprovided by the string theoretic origin of the \
topological $A$-model. This is\nthe Witten index of the supersymmetric \
quantum mechanics of a single $D3$ brane\nsupported on a special Lagrangian \
in a Calabi-Yau threefold. Geometrically,\nthis is closely related to the \
Euler characteristic of the $A$-brane moduli\nspace. Using the natural torus \
action on this moduli space, we reduce the\ncomputation of its Euler \
characteristic to a count of fixed points via\nequivariant localization. \
Studying the $A$-branes that correspond to fixed\npoints, we make contact \
with definitions of spectral and exponential networks.\nWe find agreement \
between the counts defined via the Witten index, and the BPS\ninvariants \
defined by networks. By extension, our definition also matches with\n\
Donaldson-Thomas invariants of $B$-branes related by homological mirror\n\
symmetry.\n", 
