            "  Integrable sl(N) spin chains, which we consider in this paper, \
are not only\nthe prototypical example of quantum integrable systems but also \
systems with a\nwide range of applications. For these models we use the \
Functional Separation\nof Variables (FSoV) technique with a new tool called \
Character Projection to\ncompute all matrix elements of a complete set of \
operators, which we call\nprincipal operators, in the basis diagonalising the \
tower of conserved charges\nas determinants in Q-functions. Building up on \
these results we then derive\nsimilar determinant forms for the form-factors \
of combinations of multiple\nprincipal operators between arbitrary \
factorizable states, which include, in\nparticular, off-shell Bethe vectors \
and Bethe vectors with arbitrary twists. We\nprove that the set of principal \
operators generates the complete spin chain\nYangian. Furthermore, we derive \
the representation of these operators in the\nSoV bases allowing one to \
compute correlation functions with an arbitrary\nnumber of principal \
operators. Finally, we show that the available combinations\nof multiple \
insertions includes Sklyanin`s SoV B operator. As a result, we are\nable to \
derive the B operator for sl(N) spin chains using a minimal set of\n\
ingredients, namely the FSoV method and the structure of the SoV basis.\n", 
