 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  ABJM theory in the presence of a half-BPS domain wall \
is dual to the D2-D4\\nprobe brane system with nonzero worldvolume flux. The \
ABJM domain wall was\\nrecently shown to be integrable to lowest order in \
perturbation theory and bond\\ndimension. In the present paper we show that \
the string theory dual of this\\nsystem is integrable, namely that the string \
boundary conditions on the probe\\nD4-brane preserve the integrability of the \
Green-Schwarz sigma model. Our\\nresult suggests that the ABJM domain wall is \
integrable to all loop orders and\\nfor any value of the bond \
dimension.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
