 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the 3-point functions of single-trace scalar \
operators in a\\nfour-dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SYM theory with gauge \
group $\\\\mathrm{SU}(N)$\\nand matter in the symmetric plus anti-symmetric \
representation, which has a\\nvanishing $\\\\beta$-function. By mapping this \
computation to the matrix model\\narising from localization on a 4-sphere we \
are able to resum the perturbative\\nexpansion in the large-$N$ 't Hooft \
limit and derive the behavior of the\\ncorrelators at strong coupling. \
Finally, by combining our results on the\\n3-point functions with those on \
the 2-point functions that have been recently\\nfound, we obtain the \
normalized 3-point coefficients of this conformal field\\ntheory at strong \
coupling and find that they depend in a simple way on the\\nconformal \
dimensions of the single-trace operators.\\n\""}]}, {
