         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2202.10501", "submitter" -> "Maxim Zabzine", "authors" -> 
            "Victor Alekseev, Guido Festuccia, Victor Mishnyakov, Nicolai \
Terziev\n  and Maxim Zabzine", "title" -> 
            "Localizing non-linear ${\\cal N}=(2,2)$ sigma model on $S^2$", 
            "comments" -> "51 pages, refs added", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> "10.1140/epjc/s10052-022-10610-8", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a systematic study of ${\\cal N}=(2,2)$ \
supersymmetric non-linear\nsigma models on $S^2$ with the target being a \
K\\\"ahler manifold. We discuss\ntheir reformulation in terms of \
cohomological field theory. In the\ncohomological formulation we use a novel \
version of 2D self-duality which\ninvolves a $U(1)$ action on $S^2$. In \
addition to the generic model we discuss\nthe theory with target space \
equivariance corresponding to a supersymmetric\nsigma model coupled to a \
non-dynamical supersymmetric background gauge\nmultiplet. We discuss the \
localization locus and perform a one-loop calculation\naround the constant \
maps. We argue that the theory can be reduced to some\nexotic model over the \
moduli space of holomorphic disks.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 21 Feb 2022 19:18:00 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 3 Mar 2022 15:13:49 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
