               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider quantum aspects of a class of generalized \
Gross-Neveu models,\\nwhich in special cases reduce to sigma models. We show \
that, in the case of\\ngauged models, an admissible gauge is $A_\\\\mu=0$, \
which is a direct analogue of\\nthe conformal gauge in string models. Chiral \
anomalies are a gauge counterpart\\nof the Weyl anomaly, and are required to \
vanish. Topological effects on the\\nworldsheet lead to an integration over \
moduli spaces of connections on a\\nRiemann surface. This is an initial step \
in studying the effects of worldsheet\\ngeometry and topology in integrable \
sigma models.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
