               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mannque Rho\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mannque Rho\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mapping topology of skyrmions and fractional quantum Hall \
droplets to\\n  nuclear EFT for ultra-dense baryonic matter\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A few typo corrections in published version. arXiv admin \
note:\\n  substantial text overlap with arXiv:2103.01860\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Symmetry 2022, 14, 994\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.3390/sym14050994\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"nucl-th astro-ph.SR hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We describe the mapping at high density of topological \
structure of baryonic\\nmatter to a nuclear effective field theory that \
implements hidden symmetries\\nemergent from strong nuclear correlations. The \
theory so constructed is found\\nto be consistent with no conflicts with the \
presently available observations in\\nboth normal nuclear matter and \
compact-star matter. The hidden symmetries\\ninvolved are \\\"local flavor \
symmetry\\\" of the vector mesons identified to be\\n(Seiberg-)dual to the \
gluons of QCD and hidden \\\"quantum scale symmetry\\\" with an\\nIR fixed \
point with a \\\"genuine dilaton (GD)\\\" characterized by \
non-vanishing\\npion and dilaton decay constants. Both the skyrmion topology \
for $N_f \\\\geq 2$\\nbaryons and the fractional quantum Hall (FQH) droplet \
topology for $N_f=1$\\nbaryons are unified in the \\\"homogeneous/hidden\\\" \
Wess-Zumino term in the hidden\\nlocal symmetry (HLS) Lagrangian. The \
possible indispensable role of the FQH\\ndroplets in going beyond the density \
regime of compact stars approaching\\nscale-chiral restoration is explored by \
moving toward the limit where both the\\ndilaton and the pion go massless.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
