         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2203.09556", "submitter" -> "Michelangelo Preti", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Andrea Cavagli\\`a, Nikolay Gromov, Julius Julius, Michelangelo \
Preti", "title" -> 
            "Bootstrability in Defect CFT: Integrated Correlators and Sharper \
Bounds", "comments" -> 
            "Appendix F added showing how another integral relation can be \
used to\n  derive the bps part of the correlator from integrability alone. \
Ancillary\n  file added with numerical and analytical conformal data. Other \
minor\n  corrections", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP05(2022)164", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We continue to develop Bootstrability -- a method merging \
Integrability and\nConformal Bootstrap to extract CFT data in integrable \
conformal gauge theories\nsuch as $\\mathcal{N}$=4 SYM. In this paper, we \
consider the 1D defect CFT\ndefined on a $\\frac{1}{2}$-BPS Wilson line in \
the theory, whose\nnon-perturbative spectrum is governed by the Quantum \
Spectral Curve (QSC). In\naddition, we use that the deformed setup of a \
cusped Wilson line is also\ncontrolled by the QSC. In terms of the defect \
CFT, this translates into two\nnontrivial relations connecting integrated \
4-point correlators to cusp spectral\ndata, such as the Bremsstrahlung and \
Curvature functions -- known analytically\nfrom the QSC. Combining these new \
constraints and the spectrum of the $10$\nlowest-lying states with the \
Numerical Conformal Bootstrap, we obtain very\nsharp rigorous numerical \
bounds for the structure constant of the first\nnon-protected state, giving \
this observable with seven digits precision for the\n't Hooft coupling in the \
intermediate coupling region\n$\\frac{\\sqrt{\\lambda}}{4\\pi}\\sim 1$, with \
the error decreasing quickly at large\n't Hooft coupling. Furthermore, for \
the same structure constant we obtain a\n$4$-loop analytic result at weak \
coupling. We also present results for excited\nstates.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 17 Mar 2022 18:38:29 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
