            "  We study the partition functions of multiple replicas (copies) \
of D-brane\nconfigurations in the type IIB (IKKT) matrix model. We consider \
the quenched\nregime, where small fluctuations of the matrices are \
superimposed onto the slow\n(quenched) dynamics of the background, so the \
partition function is an ensemble\naverage over the background. Interacting \
D-branes always factorize in a simple\nway. On the other hand, the \
non-interacting BPS configurations may or may not\nfactorize depending on the \
number of replicas, and their factorization\nmechanism is more involved as \
the corresponding saddle-point solutions\n(half-wormholes) break the replica \
symmetry. We argue that the simple\nfactorization mechanism of interacting \
branes is actually more interesting as\nit carries the specific signatures of \
quantum gravity, which are absent from\ndisordered field theories like the \
SYK model.\n", 
