                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We define a new dilaton Weyl multiplet of \
${\\\\mathcal{N}}=2$ conformal\\nsupergravity in four dimensions. This is \
constructed by reinterpreting the\\nequations of motion of an on-shell \
hypermultiplet as constraints that render\\nsome of the fields of the \
standard Weyl multiplet composite. The independent\\nbosonic components \
include four scalar fields and a triplet of gauge two-forms.\\nThe resulting, \
so-called, hyper-dilaton Weyl multiplet defines a $24+24$\\noff-shell \
representation of the local ${\\\\mathcal{N}}=2$ superconformal algebra.\\nBy \
coupling the hyper-dilaton Weyl multiplet to an off-shell vector \
multiplet\\ncompensator, we obtain one of the two minimal $32+32$ off-shell \
multiplets of\\n${\\\\mathcal{N}}=2$ Poincar\\\\'e supergravity constructed \
by M\\\\\\\"uller in 1986.\\nOn-shell, this contains the minimal \
${\\\\mathcal{N}}=2$ Poincar\\\\'e supergravity\\nmultiplet together with a \
hypermultiplet where one of its physical scalars\\nplays the role of a \
dilaton, while its three other scalars are dualised to a\\ntriplet of real \
gauge two-forms. Interestingly, a $BF$-coupling induces a\\nscalar potential \
for the dilaton without a standard gauging.\\n\""}]}, {
