                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct for the first time Drukker-Trancanelli \
(DT) type fermionic\\nBogomol\\\\`nyi-Prasad-Sommerfield (BPS) Wilson loops \
in four-dimensional\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal $SU(N)\\\\times \
SU(N)$ quiver theory and\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang-Mills theory. The \
connections of these fermionic BPS\\nWilson loops have a supermatrix \
structure. We construct timelike BPS Wilson\\nlines in Minkowski spacetime \
and circular BPS Wilson loops in Euclidean space.\\nThese Wilson loops \
involve dimensionful parameters. For generic values of\\nparameters, they \
preserve one real (complex) supercharge in Lorentzian\\n(Euclidean) \
signature. Supersymmetry enhancement for Wilson loops happens when\\nthe \
parameters satisfy certain constraints. The nature of such loops is \
quite\\ndifferent from the Wilson loop operators involving fermions \
constructed\\npreviously in the literature on four-dimensional gauge \
theories. We hope that\\nfurther investigations of such new Wilson loops will \
explore deep structures in\\nboth the gauge theories and gauge/gravity \
dualities.\\n\""}]}, {
