               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2205.01459\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Francois Gieres\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Francois Gieres\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Improvement of a conserved current density versus adding \
a total\\n  derivative to a Lagrangian density\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"44 pages, 1 figure, Dedicated to the memory of Krzysztof \
Gawedzki;\\n  Published version with a new section on currents associated to \
conformal\\n  invariance and a new appendix on the procedure of Gell-Mann and \
Levy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Fortschr. Phys. 70 (2022) 7-8, 2200078\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1002/prop.202200078\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  For classical relativistic field theory in Minkowski \
space-time, the addition\\nof a superpotential term to a conserved current \
density is trivial in the sense\\nthat it does not modify the local \
conservation law nor change the conserved\\ncharge, though it may allow us to \
obtain a current density with some improved\\nproperties. The addition of a \
total derivative term to a Lagrangian density is\\nalso trivial in the sense \
that it does not modify the equations of motion of\\nthe theory. These facts \
suggest that both operations are related and possibly\\nequivalent to each \
other for any global symmetry of an action functional. We\\naddress this \
question following the study of two quite different (and well\\nknown) \
instances: the Callan-Coleman-Jackiw improvement of the \
canonical\\nenergy-momentum tensor for scalar and vector fields (providing an \
on-shell\\ntraceless energy-momentum tensor) and the construction of a \
current density\\nsatisfying a zero curvature condition for two-dimensional \
sigma models on\\ndeformed spaces (notably the squashed three-sphere and \
warped AdS spaces).\\nThese instances correspond to fairly different \
implementations of the general\\nresults. An appendix addresses the precise \
relationship between the approaches\\nto local conservation laws based on \
active and passive symmetry\\ntransformations, respectively.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
