          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2205.09775\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Davide Bonomi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lorenzo Bianchi, Davide Bonomi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Conformal dispersion relations for defects and boundaries\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"36 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SciPost Phys. 15, 055 (2023)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.21468/SciPostPhys.15.2.055\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive a dispersion relation for two-point \
correlation functions in defect\\nconformal field theories. The correlator is \
expressed as an integral over a\\n(single) discontinuity that is controlled \
by the bulk channel operator product\\nexpansion (OPE). This very simple \
relation is particularly useful in\\nperturbative settings where the \
discontinuity is determined by a subset of bulk\\noperators. In particular, \
we apply it to holographic correlators of two chiral\\nprimary operators in $\
\\\\mathcal{N}= 4$ Super Yang-Mills theory in the presence\\nof a \
supersymmetric Wilson line. With a very simple computation, we are able \
to\\nreproduce and extend existing results. We also propose a second \
relation, which\\nreconstructs the correlator from a double discontinuity, \
and is controlled by\\nthe defect channel OPE. Finally, for the case of \
codimension-one defects\\n(boundaries and interfaces) we derive a dispersion \
relation which receives\\ncontributions from both OPE channels and we apply \
it to the boundary correlator\\nin the $O(N)$ critical model. We reproduce \
the order $\\\\epsilon^2$ result in the\\n$\\\\epsilon$-expansion using as \
input a finite number of boundary CFT data.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
