              "Bonomi", "Davide", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{1.019662645620004, -3.8667213803092046`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2205.12166\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Johannes Branahl\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Johannes Branahl and Alexander Hock\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Complete solution of the LSZ Model via Topological \
Recursion\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"63 pages, 6 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Communications in Mathematical Phyiscs (2023)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s00220-023-04702-z\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We prove that the Langmann-Szabo-Zarembo (LSZ) model \
with quartic potential,\\na toy model for a quantum field theory on \
noncommutative spaces grasped as a\\ncomplex matrix model, obeys topological \
recursion of Chekhov, Eynard and\\nOrantin. By introducing two families of \
correlation functions, one\\ncorresponding to the meromorphic differentials $\
\\\\omega_{g,n}$ of topological\\nrecursion, we obtain Dyson-Schwinger \
equations that eventually lead to the\\nabstract loop equations being, \
together with their pole structure, the\\nnecessary condition for topological \
recursion. This strategy to show the exact\\nsolvability of the LSZ model \
establishes another approach towards the\\nexceptional property of \
integrability in some quantum field theories. We\\ncompare differences in the \
loop equations for the LSZ model (with complex\\nfields) and the \
Grosse-Wulkenhaar model (with hermitian fieldss) and their\\nconsequences for \
the resulting particular type of topological recursion that\\ngoverns the \
models.\\n\""}]}, {
