         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2205.12166", "submitter" -> "Johannes Branahl", "authors" -> 
            "Johannes Branahl and Alexander Hock", "title" -> 
            "Complete solution of the LSZ Model via Topological Recursion", 
            "comments" -> "63 pages, 6 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Communications in Mathematical Phyiscs (2023)", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/s00220-023-04702-z", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We prove that the Langmann-Szabo-Zarembo (LSZ) model with \
quartic potential,\na toy model for a quantum field theory on noncommutative \
spaces grasped as a\ncomplex matrix model, obeys topological recursion of \
Chekhov, Eynard and\nOrantin. By introducing two families of correlation \
functions, one\ncorresponding to the meromorphic differentials \
$\\omega_{g,n}$ of topological\nrecursion, we obtain Dyson-Schwinger \
equations that eventually lead to the\nabstract loop equations being, \
together with their pole structure, the\nnecessary condition for topological \
recursion. This strategy to show the exact\nsolvability of the LSZ model \
establishes another approach towards the\nexceptional property of \
integrability in some quantum field theories. We\ncompare differences in the \
loop equations for the LSZ model (with complex\nfields) and the \
Grosse-Wulkenhaar model (with hermitian fieldss) and their\nconsequences for \
the resulting particular type of topological recursion that\ngoverns the \
models.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 24 May 2022 15:56:18 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-04-24", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Branahl", "Johannes", ""}, {
              "Hock", "Alexander", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
