                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive exact relations between certain integrals of \
the conserved flavor\\ncurrent four point function in 4d $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
conformal field theories\\n(CFTs) and derivatives of the mass deformed sphere \
free energy, which can be\\ncomputed exactly for gauge theories using \
supersymmetric localization. For\\nconformal gauge theories with flavor \
groups of rank greater than one, there are\\nat least two such integrated \
constraints, which can then be combined with the\\nnumerical conformal \
bootstrap to bound CFT data as a function of the\\ncomplexified gauge \
coupling $\\\\tau$. We apply this strategy to the case of\\n$SU(2)$ conformal \
SQCD with flavor group $SO(8)$, where we compute bounds on\\nunprotected \
scaling dimensions as a function of $\\\\tau$ that match the free\\ntheory \
limit, and exhibit the expected mixing between the action of \
the\\n$SL(2,\\\\mathbb{Z})$ duality group and $SO(8)$ triality.\\n\""}]}, {
