                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We report a perturbative calculation of the expectation \
value of the infinite\\nstraight line Maldacena-Wilson loop in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills theory to order $g^6$. Thus, \
we extend the previous perturbative\\nresult by one order. The vacuum \
expectation value is reformulated in terms of a\\nnon-linear and non-local \
transformation, the Nicolai map, mapping the full\\nfunctional measure of the \
interacting theory to that of a free bosonic theory.\\nThe results are \
twofold. The perturbative cancellations of the different\\ncontributions to \
the Maldacena-Wilson loop are by no means trivial and seem to\\nresemble \
those of the circular Maldacena-Wilson loop at order $g^4$.\\nFurthermore, we \
argue that our approach to computing quantum correlation\\nfunctions is \
competitive with more standard diagrammatic techniques.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
