            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the quench dynamics of the one-dimensional Hubbard \
model through the\nQuench Action formalism. We introduce a class of \
integrable initial states --\nexpressed as product states over two sites -- \
for which we can provide an exact\ncharacterisation of the late-time regime. \
This is achieved by finding a\nclosed-form expression for the overlaps \
between our states and the Bethe ansatz\neigenstates, which we check \
explicitly in the limits of low densities and\ninfinite repulsion. Our \
solution gives access to the stationary values attained\nby local observables \
(we show the explicit example of the density of doubly\noccupied sites) and \
the asymptotic entanglement dynamics directly in the\nthermodynamic limit. \
Interestingly, we find that for intermediate interaction\nstrength R\\'enyi \
entropies display a double-slope structure.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
