            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2206.09705\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Bo Sundborg\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nadia Flodgren and Bo Sundborg\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"One-loop fixed points of adjoint multi-scalar gauge \
theory in four\\n  dimensions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The preprint is withrawn because of its erroneous \
conclusion on real\\n  fixed points. The determination of coefficients in \
equation 6.1 was mistaken,\\n  not to the algebraic approach, and correct \
results will be published in a\\n  different context\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We determine complete one-loop beta functions of the \
multi-scalar four-point\\ncouplings in four-dimensional $SU(N)$ gauge \
theories with $M$ adjoint scalar\\nmultiplets. For adjoints scalars, the sign \
of the one loop gauge coupling beta\\nfunction depends solely on $M$, \
vanishing and changing sign precisely at\\n$M=22$. For the multi-scalar \
potential at fixed gauge coupling we find several\\nfixed points with \
different stability properties at large $N$. The analysis\\ncrucially \
involves the full set of four $SU(N)$ and $O(M)$ invariant single\\ntrace and \
double trace couplings. Taking the gauge coupling into account, there\\nare \
asymptotically free RG flows for $M<22$ and non-trivial fixed points \
for\\n$M=22$ at one loop, while $M>22$ appears to ruin the UV properties of \
the\\ntheory. Surprisingly, uniquely between $M=22$ and $M=21$ the number of \
fixed\\nflows drops from eight to four in the large $N$ limit. There seems to \
be\\nsomething very special about $M=22$. More speculatively, the $M=22$ \
one-loop\\nconformal fixed point theory with $M$ adjoint scalars in $d=4$ \
suggests the\\npossibility of an isolated non-supersymmetric, purely bosonic \
AdS$_{4+1}\\n\\\\times$S$^{22-1}$/CFT$_4$ correspondence.\\n  Our example \
suggests that extending the potential to the complete set of\\nterms allowed \
by symmetries may lead to real fixed points also in\\nnon-supersymmetric \
theories descending from $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
super-Yang-Mills\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 20 Jun 2022 10:53:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 27 Nov 2022 09:41:07 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
