 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive renormalised finite functional flow equations \
for quantum field\\ntheories in real and imaginary time that incorporate \
scale transformations of\\nthe renormalisation conditions, hence implementing \
a flowing renormalisation.\\nThe flows are manifestly finite in general \
non-perturbative truncation schemes\\nalso for regularisation schemes that do \
not implement an infrared suppression\\nof the loops in the flow. \
Specifically, this formulation includes finite\\nfunctional flows for the \
effective action with a spectral Callan-Symanzik\\ncutoff, and therefore \
gives access to Lorentz invariant spectral flows. The\\nfunctional setup is \
fully non-perturbative and allows for the spectral\\ntreatment of general \
theories. In particular, this includes theories that do\\nnot admit a \
perturbative renormalisation such as asymptotically safe theories.\\nFinally, \
the application of the Lorentz invariant spectral \
functional\\nrenormalisation group is briefly discussed for theories ranging \
from real\\nscalar and Yukawa theories to gauge theories and quantum gravity.\
\\n\""}]}, {
