               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable supersymmetric deformations of $\\\\rm AdS_3 \
\\\\times S^3 \\\\times\\n  T^4$\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"34 pages, minor corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2022)018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct a family of type IIB string backgrounds \
that are deformations of\\n$\\\\rm AdS_3 \\\\times S^3 \\\\times T^4$ with a \
\\\"squashed\\\" $\\\\rm AdS_3 \\\\times S^3$\\nmetric supported by a \
combination of NSNS and RR fluxes. They have global $\\\\rm\\nSU(1,1) \
\\\\times SU(2)$ symmetry, regular curvature, constant dilaton and\\npreserve \
8 supercharges. Upon compactification to 4 dimensions they reduce \
to\\n$\\\\mathcal N=2$ supersymmetric $\\\\rm AdS_2 \\\\times S^2$ solutions \
with electric\\nand magnetic Maxwell fluxes. These type IIB supergravity \
solutions can be found\\nfrom the undeformed $\\\\rm AdS_3 \\\\times S^3 \
\\\\times T^4$ background by a\\ncombination of T-dualities and S-duality. In \
contrast to T-duality, S-duality\\ntransformations of a type IIB supergravity \
background do not generally preserve\\nthe classical integrability of the \
corresponding Green-Schwarz superstring\\nsigma model. Nevertheless, we show \
that integrability is preserved in the\\npresent case. Indeed, we find that \
these backgrounds can be obtained, up to\\nT-dualities, from an integrable \
inhomogeneous Yang-Baxter deformation (with\\nunimodular Drinfel'd-Jimbo \
R-matrix) of the original $\\\\rm AdS_3 \\\\times S^3$\\nsupercoset model.\\n\
\""}]}, {
