 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In a four-dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal \
quiver theory with gauge\\ngroup \
$\\\\mathrm{SU}(N)\\\\times\\\\mathrm{SU}(N)$ and bi-fundamental matter, \
we\\nanalytically obtain the exact strong-coupling behavior of the normalized\
\\n3-point correlators of single-trace scalar operators in the large-$N$ \
limit\\nusing localization techniques. We then obtain the same \
strong-coupling behavior\\nfrom the holographic dual using the AdS/CFT \
correspondence at the supergravity\\nlevel. This agreement confirms the \
validity of the analytic strong-coupling\\nresults and of the holographic \
correspondence in a non-maximally supersymmetric\\nset-up in four dimensions.\
\\n\""}]}, {
