               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Luis F. Alday and Shai M. Chester\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Pure anti-de Sitter supergravity and the conformal \
bootstrap\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"6 pages plus appendices, 8 figures, v2 typos corrected \
and submitted\\n  for publication\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1103/PhysRevLett.129.211601\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider graviton scattering in maximal supergravity \
on Anti-de Sitter\\nspace (AdS) in $d+1$ dimensions for $d=3,4,\\\\text{and \
$6$}$ with no extra\\ncompact spacetime factor. Holography suggests that this \
theory is dual to an\\nexotic maximally supersymmetric conformal field theory \
(CFT) in $d$ dimensions\\nwhose only light single trace operator is the \
stress tensor. This contrasts\\nwith more standard cases like Type IIB string \
theory on $AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ dual\\nto $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ Super-Yang-Mills, \
where the CFT has light single trace\\noperators for each Kaluza-Klein mode \
on $S^5$. We compute the 1-loop correction\\nto the pure AdS$_{d+1}$ theory \
in a small Planck length expansion, which is\\ndual to the large central \
charge expansion in the CFT. We find that this\\ncorrection saturates the \
most general non-perturbative conformal bootstrap\\nbounds on this correlator \
in the large central charge regime for $d=3,4,6$,\\nwhile the 1-loop \
correction to CFTs with string/M-theory duals all lie inside\\nthe allowed \
region.\\n\""}]}, {
