            "6 pages plus appendices, 8 figures, v2 typos corrected and \
submitted\n  for publication", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevLett.129.211601", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider graviton scattering in maximal supergravity on \
Anti-de Sitter\nspace (AdS) in $d+1$ dimensions for $d=3,4,\\text{and $6$}$ \
with no extra\ncompact spacetime factor. Holography suggests that this theory \
is dual to an\nexotic maximally supersymmetric conformal field theory (CFT) \
in $d$ dimensions\nwhose only light single trace operator is the stress \
tensor. This contrasts\nwith more standard cases like Type IIB string theory \
on $AdS_5\\times S^5$ dual\nto $\\mathcal{N}=4$ Super-Yang-Mills, where the \
CFT has light single trace\noperators for each Kaluza-Klein mode on $S^5$. We \
compute the 1-loop correction\nto the pure AdS$_{d+1}$ theory in a small \
Planck length expansion, which is\ndual to the large central charge expansion \
in the CFT. We find that this\ncorrection saturates the most general \
non-perturbative conformal bootstrap\nbounds on this correlator in the large \
central charge regime for $d=3,4,6$,\nwhile the 1-loop correction to CFTs \
with string/M-theory duals all lie inside\nthe allowed region.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 11 Jul 2022 18:00:00 GMT"}, {
