          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2207.06092\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Dimitrios Zoakos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"George Georgiou, Georgios Itsios and Dimitrios \
Zoakos\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marginally deformed Schr\\\\\\\"{o}dinger/dipole CFT \
correspondence\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1+36 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct and thoroughly study a new integrable \
example of the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence with Schr\\\\\\\"{o}dinger symmetry. \
On the gravity side, the\\nsupergravity solution depends on two parameters \
and is obtained by marginally\\ndeforming the internal space of the \
Schr\\\\\\\"{o}dinger background through a series\\nof TsT transformations. \
On the field theory side, we identify the dual field\\ntheory which also \
depends on two parameters. We find a point-like string\\nsolution and derive \
its dispersion relation. A non-trivial test of the\\ncorrespondence is \
provided by using the Landau-Lifshitz coherent state approach\\nto reproduce \
the leading, in the deformation parameters, terms of that\\nrelation. Then, \
we calculate the Wilson loop, describing the quark/anti-quark\\npotential at \
strong coupling. It exhibits confining behaviour when the\\nseparation length \
is much less than the Schr\\\\\\\"{o}dinger parameter. When the\\nseparation \
length is much greater than the Schr\\\\\\\"{o}dinger parameter \
the\\nbehaviour is that of a conformal theory. Subsequently, we take the \
Penrose\\nlimit along a certain null geodesic of the constructed background \
and calculate\\nthe bosonic spectrum. Based on that spectrum, we make an \
educated guess for the\\nexact, in the 't Hooft coupling, dispersion relation \
of the magnon excitations\\nin the original doubly deformed background. This \
provides us with an exact\\nprediction for the dimensions of the dual field \
theory operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 13 Jul 2022 10:05:03 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2022-07-14\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
