            "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct and thoroughly study a new integrable example of \
the AdS/CFT\ncorrespondence with Schr\\\"{o}dinger symmetry. On the gravity \
side, the\nsupergravity solution depends on two parameters and is obtained by \
marginally\ndeforming the internal space of the Schr\\\"{o}dinger background \
through a series\nof TsT transformations. On the field theory side, we \
identify the dual field\ntheory which also depends on two parameters. We find \
a point-like string\nsolution and derive its dispersion relation. A \
non-trivial test of the\ncorrespondence is provided by using the \
Landau-Lifshitz coherent state approach\nto reproduce the leading, in the \
deformation parameters, terms of that\nrelation. Then, we calculate the \
Wilson loop, describing the quark/anti-quark\npotential at strong coupling. \
It exhibits confining behaviour when the\nseparation length is much less than \
the Schr\\\"{o}dinger parameter. When the\nseparation length is much greater \
than the Schr\\\"{o}dinger parameter the\nbehaviour is that of a conformal \
theory. Subsequently, we take the Penrose\nlimit along a certain null \
geodesic of the constructed background and calculate\nthe bosonic spectrum. \
Based on that spectrum, we make an educated guess for the\nexact, in the 't \
Hooft coupling, dispersion relation of the magnon excitations\nin the \
original doubly deformed background. This provides us with an exact\n\
prediction for the dimensions of the dual field theory operators.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 13 Jul 2022 10:05:03 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2022-07-14", 
