                 "\"M. Beccaria, G.P. Korchemsky and A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Strong coupling expansion in $\\\\mathbf{\\\\mathcal \
N=2}$ superconformal\\n  theories and the Bessel kernel\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"65 pages. v2: misprints and eq.(4.20) corrected, note \
added; v3:\\n  minor clarifications\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP09(2022)226\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"IPhT--T22/040, Imperial-TP-AT-2022-04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider strong 't Hooft coupling expansion in \
special four-dimensional\\n$\\\\mathcal N=2$ superconformal models that are \
planar-equivalent to $\\\\mathcal\\nN=4$ super Yang-Mills theory. Various \
observables in these models that admit\\nlocalization matrix model \
representation can be expressed at large $N$ in terms\\nof a Fredholm \
determinant of a Bessel operator. The latter previously appeared\\nin the \
study of level spacing distributions in matrix models and, more\\nrecently, \
in four-point correlation functions of infinitely heavy half-BPS\\noperators \
in planar $\\\\mathcal N=4$ SYM. We use this relation and a \
suitably\\ngeneralized Szego-Akhiezer-Kac formula to derive the strong 't \
Hooft coupling\\nexpansion of the leading corrections to free energy, \
half-BPS circular Wilson\\nloop, and certain correlators of chiral primaries \
operators in the $\\\\mathcal\\nN=2$ models. This substantially generalizes \
partial results in the literature\\nand represents a challenge for dual \
string theory calculations in AdS/CFT\\ncontext. We also demonstrate that the \
resulting strong-coupling expansions\\nsuffer from Borel singularities and \
require adding non-perturbative,\\nexponentially suppressed corrections. As a \
byproduct of our analysis, we\\ndetermine the non-perturbative correction to \
the above mentioned four-point\\ncorrelator in planar $\\\\mathcal N=4$ \
SYM.\\n\""}]}, {
