         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2207.11475", "submitter" -> "Arkady Tseytlin", "authors" -> 
            "M. Beccaria, G.P. Korchemsky and A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Strong coupling expansion in $\\mathbf{\\mathcal N=2}$ \
superconformal\n  theories and the Bessel kernel", "comments" -> 
            "65 pages. v2: misprints and eq.(4.20) corrected, note added; v3:\
\n  minor clarifications", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP09(2022)226", "report-no" -> 
            "IPhT--T22/040, Imperial-TP-AT-2022-04", "categories" -> "hep-th",
             "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider strong 't Hooft coupling expansion in special \
four-dimensional\n$\\mathcal N=2$ superconformal models that are \
planar-equivalent to $\\mathcal\nN=4$ super Yang-Mills theory. Various \
observables in these models that admit\nlocalization matrix model \
representation can be expressed at large $N$ in terms\nof a Fredholm \
determinant of a Bessel operator. The latter previously appeared\nin the \
study of level spacing distributions in matrix models and, more\nrecently, in \
four-point correlation functions of infinitely heavy half-BPS\noperators in \
planar $\\mathcal N=4$ SYM. We use this relation and a suitably\ngeneralized \
Szego-Akhiezer-Kac formula to derive the strong 't Hooft coupling\nexpansion \
of the leading corrections to free energy, half-BPS circular Wilson\nloop, \
and certain correlators of chiral primaries operators in the $\\mathcal\nN=2$ \
models. This substantially generalizes partial results in the literature\nand \
represents a challenge for dual string theory calculations in AdS/CFT\n\
context. We also demonstrate that the resulting strong-coupling expansions\n\
suffer from Borel singularities and require adding non-perturbative,\n\
exponentially suppressed corrections. As a byproduct of our analysis, we\n\
determine the non-perturbative correction to the above mentioned four-point\n\
correlator in planar $\\mathcal N=4$ SYM.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 23 Jul 2022 09:33:50 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
