                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider integrable boundary states in the XXX \
spin-1/2 spin chain. We\\nbegin by briefly reviewing the algebraic Bethe \
Ansatz as well as integrable\\nboundary states in spin chains. Then a \
recently discovered class of integrable\\nstates known as crosscap states is \
described and expanded. In these states each\\nspin is entangled with its \
antipodal spin. We present a novel proof of the\\nintegrability of both a \
crosscap state that is known in the literature and one\\nthat has not \
previously been studied. We then use the machinery of the\\nalgebraic Bethe \
Ansatz to derive the overlaps between the crosscap states and\\noff-shell \
Bethe states.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
