           "id" -> "2207.12354", "submitter" -> "Christopher Ekman", 
            "authors" -> "Christopher Ekman", "title" -> 
            "Crosscap states in the XXX spin-1/2 spin chain", "comments" -> 
            "17 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP",
             "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider integrable boundary states in the XXX spin-1/2 \
spin chain. We\nbegin by briefly reviewing the algebraic Bethe Ansatz as well \
as integrable\nboundary states in spin chains. Then a recently discovered \
class of integrable\nstates known as crosscap states is described and \
expanded. In these states each\nspin is entangled with its antipodal spin. We \
present a novel proof of the\nintegrability of both a crosscap state that is \
known in the literature and one\nthat has not previously been studied. We \
then use the machinery of the\nalgebraic Bethe Ansatz to derive the overlaps \
between the crosscap states and\noff-shell Bethe states.\n", 
