               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Leonardo Santilli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"David P\\\\'erez-Garc\\\\'ia, Leonardo Santilli and \
Miguel Tierz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Dynamical quantum phase transitions from random matrix \
theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2: 60 pages, 18 figures, published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum 8, 1271 (2024)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.22331/q-2024-02-29-1271\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"quant-ph cond-mat.quant-gas cond-mat.stat-mech \
cond-mat.str-el\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We uncover a novel dynamical quantum phase transition, \
using random matrix\\ntheory and its associated notion of planar limit. We \
study it for the isotropic\\nXY Heisenberg spin chain. For this, we probe its \
real-time dynamics through the\\nLoschmidt echo. This leads to the study of a \
random matrix ensemble with a\\ncomplex weight, whose analysis requires novel \
technical considerations, that we\\ndevelop. We obtain three main results: 1) \
There is a third order phase\\ntransition at a rescaled critical time, that \
we determine. 2) The third order\\nphase transition persists away from the \
thermodynamic limit. 3) For times below\\nthe critical value, the difference \
between the thermodynamic limit and a finite\\nchain decreases exponentially \
with the system size. All these results depend in\\na rich manner on the \
parity of the number of flipped spins of the quantum state\\nconforming the \
fidelity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 2 Aug 2022 18:00:03 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
