         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2208.01659", "submitter" -> "Leonardo Santilli", 
            "authors" -> 
            "David P\\'erez-Garc\\'ia, Leonardo Santilli and Miguel Tierz", 
            "title" -> 
            "Dynamical quantum phase transitions from random matrix theory", 
            "comments" -> "v2: 60 pages, 18 figures, published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Quantum 8, 1271 (2024)", "doi" -> 
            "10.22331/q-2024-02-29-1271", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "quant-ph cond-mat.quant-gas cond-mat.stat-mech cond-mat.str-el", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We uncover a novel dynamical quantum phase transition, using \
random matrix\ntheory and its associated notion of planar limit. We study it \
for the isotropic\nXY Heisenberg spin chain. For this, we probe its real-time \
dynamics through the\nLoschmidt echo. This leads to the study of a random \
matrix ensemble with a\ncomplex weight, whose analysis requires novel \
technical considerations, that we\ndevelop. We obtain three main results: 1) \
There is a third order phase\ntransition at a rescaled critical time, that we \
determine. 2) The third order\nphase transition persists away from the \
thermodynamic limit. 3) For times below\nthe critical value, the difference \
between the thermodynamic limit and a finite\nchain decreases exponentially \
with the system size. All these results depend in\na rich manner on the \
parity of the number of flipped spins of the quantum state\nconforming the \
fidelity.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 2 Aug 2022 18:00:03 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 27 Feb 2024 01:35:52 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-03-04", 
