               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages + appendices, 7 figures. v2: minor \
clarifications; published\\n  version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2023.116250\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DESY-22-132\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Nearly all 6D superconformal field theories (SCFTs) \
have a partial tensor\\nbranch description in terms of a generalized quiver \
gauge theory consisting of\\na long one-dimensional spine of quiver nodes \
with links given by conformal\\nmatter; a strongly coupled generalization of \
a bifundamental hypermultiplet.\\nFor theories obtained from M5-branes \
probing an ADE singularity, this was\\nrecently leveraged to extract a \
protected large R-charge subsector of\\noperators, with operator mixing \
controlled at leading order in an inverse large\\nR-charge expansion by an \
integrable spin $s$ Heisenberg spin chain, where $s$\\nis determined by the $\
\\\\mathfrak{su}(2)_{R}$ R-symmetry representation of the\\nconformal matter \
operator. In this work, we show that this same structure\\nextends to the \
full superconformal algebra $\\\\mathfrak{osp}(6,2|1)$. In\\nparticular, we \
determine the corresponding Bethe ansatz equations which govern\\nthis \
super-spin chain, as well as distinguished subsectors which close \
under\\noperator mixing. Similar considerations extend to 6D little string \
theories\\n(LSTs) and 4D $\\\\mathcal{N} = 2$ SCFTs with the same generalized \
quiver\\nstructures.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
