            "Super-Spin Chains for 6D SCFTs", "comments" -> 
            "35 pages + appendices, 7 figures. v2: minor clarifications; \
published\n  version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2023.116250", "report-no" -> "DESY-22-132", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Nearly all 6D superconformal field theories (SCFTs) have a \
partial tensor\nbranch description in terms of a generalized quiver gauge \
theory consisting of\na long one-dimensional spine of quiver nodes with links \
given by conformal\nmatter; a strongly coupled generalization of a \
bifundamental hypermultiplet.\nFor theories obtained from M5-branes probing \
an ADE singularity, this was\nrecently leveraged to extract a protected large \
R-charge subsector of\noperators, with operator mixing controlled at leading \
order in an inverse large\nR-charge expansion by an integrable spin $s$ \
Heisenberg spin chain, where $s$\nis determined by the \
$\\mathfrak{su}(2)_{R}$ R-symmetry representation of the\nconformal matter \
operator. In this work, we show that this same structure\nextends to the full \
superconformal algebra $\\mathfrak{osp}(6,2|1)$. In\nparticular, we determine \
the corresponding Bethe ansatz equations which govern\nthis super-spin chain, \
as well as distinguished subsectors which close under\noperator mixing. \
Similar considerations extend to 6D little string theories\n(LSTs) and 4D \
$\\mathcal{N} = 2$ SCFTs with the same generalized quiver\nstructures.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 3 Aug 2022 18:00:13 GMT"}, {
