            "  We extend the fixed-charge semiclassical method by computing \
anomalous\ndimensions of fixed-charge scalar operators in models with Yukawa \
interactions.\nIn particular, we discuss the Nambu-Jona-Lasinio-Yukawa theory \
as well as an\nasymptotically safe gauge-Yukawa model in four dimensions. In \
the weakly\ncoupled regime, we cross-check our results to the respective \
maximum known\norders of perturbation theory in these models and predict \
higher order terms\nfor future comparisons with other computational methods. \
In the strongly\ncoupled regime, we match our results to the predictions of \
the large-charge\neffective field theory which can be compared to future \
Monte Carlo and lattice\nstudies.\n", 
