                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore a novel class of Yang-Baxter deformed \
AdS$_{4}$ $\\\\times$ CP$^{3}$\\nbackgrounds [Jour. High Ener. Phys. \
\\\\textbf{01} (2021) 056] which exhibit a\\nnon-chaotic dynamics for \
(super)strings propagating over it. We explicitly use\\nthe \
\\\\textit{Kovacic's algorithm} in order to establish non-chaotic dynamics of\
\\nstring $ \\\\sigma $ models over these deformed backgrounds. This analysis \
is\\ncomplemented with numerical techniques whereby we probe the classical \
phase\\nspace of these (semi)classical strings and calculate various chaos \
indicators,\\nsuch as, the Poincar\\\\'{e} sections and the Lyapunov \
exponents. We find\\ncompatibility between the two approaches. Nevertheless, \
our analysis does not\\nensure integrability; rather, it excludes the \
possibility of non-integrability\\nfor the given string embeddings.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
