            "title" -> 
            "Non-chaotic dynamics for Yang-Baxter deformed \
$\\text{AdS}_{4}\\times\n  \\text{CP}^{3}$ superstrings", "comments" -> 
            "v3, improved presentation, Accepted for publication in EPJC", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We explore a novel class of Yang-Baxter deformed AdS$_{4}$ \
$\\times$ CP$^{3}$\nbackgrounds [Jour. High Ener. Phys. \\textbf{01} (2021) \
056] which exhibit a\nnon-chaotic dynamics for (super)strings propagating \
over it. We explicitly use\nthe \\textit{Kovacic's algorithm} in order to \
establish non-chaotic dynamics of\nstring $ \\sigma $ models over these \
deformed backgrounds. This analysis is\ncomplemented with numerical \
techniques whereby we probe the classical phase\nspace of these \
(semi)classical strings and calculate various chaos indicators,\nsuch as, the \
Poincar\\'{e} sections and the Lyapunov exponents. We find\ncompatibility \
between the two approaches. Nevertheless, our analysis does not\nensure \
integrability; rather, it excludes the possibility of non-integrability\nfor \
the given string embeddings.\n", 
