            "  The generating functional $\\mathcal{W}[J_{\\mathcal O}]$ of \
Euclidean\ncorrelators of twist-$2$ operators in SU($N$) Yang-Mills theory \
admits the 't\nHooft large-$N$ expansion: $\\mathcal{W}[J_{\\mathcal\n\
O}]=\\mathcal{W}_{sphere}\\,\\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O}]+\\mathcal{W}_{torus}\n\
\\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O}]+ \\cdots$. Nonperturbatively, \
$\\mathcal{W}_{sphere}\n\\,\\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O}]$ is a sum of tree \
diagrams involving glueball\npropagators and vertices, while \
$\\mathcal{W}_{torus} \\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O}]$ is\na sum of glueball \
one-loop diagrams. Moreover, it has been predicted that\n$\\mathcal{W}_{torus \
} \\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O}]$ should admit the structure of the\nlogarithm of \
a functional determinant summing glueball one-loop diagrams. We\nwork out in \
a closed form the ultraviolet (UV) asymptotics of\n$\\mathcal{W}_{sphere} \\,\
\\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O},\\lambda] \\sim \\mathcal{W}_{asym\n\\, sphere} \\,\
\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O},\\lambda]$ and $\\mathcal{W}_{torus}\n\
\\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O},\\lambda] \\sim \\mathcal{W}_{asym \\, torus}\n\
\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O},\\lambda]$ in the coordinate \
representation as all\nthe coordinates of the correlators are uniformly \
rescaled by a factor $\\lambda\n\\rightarrow 0$. Remarkably, we verify the \
above prediction that\n$\\mathcal{W}_{asym \\, torus} \
\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O},\\lambda]$ -- being\nasymptotic in the UV \
to $\\mathcal{W}_{torus} \\,\\,\\,[J_{\\mathcal O}, \\lambda]$\n-- admits the \
structure of the logarithm of a functional determinant as well.\nHence, the \
computation above sets strong UV asymptotic constraints on the\n\
nonperturbative solution of large-$N$ YM theory and it may be a pivotal guide\
\nfor the search of such a solution.\n", 
