 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider generalized Scherk-Schwarz reductions of \
E$_9$ exceptional field\\ntheory to D=2 space-time dimensions and in \
particular construct the resulting\\nscalar potential of all gauged \
supergravities that can be obtained in this way.\\nThis provides the first \
general expression for a multitude of theories with an\\ninteresting \
structure of vacua, covering potentially many new AdS$_2$ cases. As\\nan \
application, we prove the consistency of the truncation \
of\\neleven-dimensional supergravity on $S^8\\\\times S^1$ to SO(9) gauged \
maximal\\nsupergravity. Fluctuations around its supersymmetric \
SO(9)-invariant vacuum\\ndescribe holographically the dynamics of interacting \
D0-branes.\\n\""}]}, {
