 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  By extending the recent analysis of arXiv:2203.12203 \
for ${\\\\mathcal{N}}=2$\\nconformal supergravity in four dimensions, we \
define new hyper-dilaton Weyl\\nmultiplets for five-dimensional \
${\\\\mathcal{N}}=1$, and six-dimensional\\n${\\\\mathcal{N}}=(1,0)$ \
conformal supergravities. These are constructed by\\ncoupling the five- and \
six-dimensional standard Weyl multiplets to on-shell\\nhypermultiplets and \
reinterpreting the systems as new multiplets of conformal\\nsupergravity. In \
the five-dimensional case, we also construct a new\\nhyper-dilaton \
Poincar\\\\'e supergravity by coupling to an off-shell vector\\nmultiplet \
compensator. As in four dimensions, a $BF$-coupling induces a\\nnon-trivial \
scalar potential for the five-dimensional dilaton that admits\\nAdS$_5$ \
vacua.\\n\""}]}, {
