Pandit, Kamal L.\\n  Panigrahi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Neumann-Rosochatius system for rotating strings in $AdS_3 \
\\\\times\\n  S^3\\\\times S^3\\\\times S^1$ with flux\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"24 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP12(2022)059\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Strings on $AdS_3 \\\\times S^3\\\\times S^3\\\\times \
S^1$ with mixed flux exhibit\\nexact integrability. We wish to construct an \
integrable Neumann-Rosochatius\\n(NR) model of strings starting with the type \
IIB supergravity action in $AdS_3\\n\\\\times S^3\\\\times S^3\\\\times S^1$ \
with pure NSNS flux. We observe that the forms\\nof the Lagrangian and the \
Uhlenbeck integrals of motion of the considered\\nsystem are NR-like with \
some suitable deformations which eventually appear due\\nto the presence of \
flux. We utilize the integrable framework of the deformed NR\\nmodel to \
analyze rigidly rotating spiky strings moving only in $S^3\\\\times \
S^1$.\\nWe further present some mathematical speculations on the rounding-off \
nature of\\nthe spike in the presence of non-zero angular momentum $J$ in \
$S^1$.\\n\""}]}, {
