                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the 5d AGT correspondence of supergroup \
gauge theories with A-type\\nsupergroups. We introduce two intertwiners \
called positive and negative\\nintertwiners to compute the instanton \
partition function. The positive\\nintertwiner is the ordinary \
Awata-Feigin-Shiraishi intertwiner while the\\nnegative intertwiner is an \
intertwiner obtained by using central charges with\\nnegative levels. We show \
that composition of them gives the basic Nekrasov\\nfactors appearing in \
supergroup partition functions. We explicitly derive the\\ninstanton \
partition functions of supergroup gauge theories with A and D-type\\nquiver \
structures. Using the intertwiners, we briefly study the Gaiotto \
state,\\n$qq$-characters and the relation with quiver W-algebra. Furthermore, \
we show\\nthat the negative intertwiner corresponds to the anti-refined \
topological\\nvertex recently defined by Kimura and Sugimoto. We also discuss \
how superquiver\\ntheories should appear in our formalism if they exist. The \
existence of the AGT\\ncorrespondence of the theories we study in this paper \
implies that there is a\\nbroader 2d/4d (5d/$q$-algebra) correspondence, or \
more generally the BPS/CFT\\ncorrespondence, where new non-unitary theories \
play important roles.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
