                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study rigidly rotating and pulsating strings in the \
background of a 1+1\\ndimensional intersection of two orthogonal stacks of \
fivebranes in type IIB\\nstring theory by using the Neumann-Rosochatius (NR) \
model. Starting with the\\nPolyakov action of the probe fundamental string we \
show that a generalised\\nansatz reduce the system into the one dimensional \
NR model in the presence of\\nflux. The integrable construction of the model \
is exploited to analyze the\\nrotating and oscillating string solution. We \
render the large $J$ BMN-type\\nexpansion for the energy of rotating string \
states while the same for the\\noscillating string has been derived in long \
string and small angular momenta\\nlimit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
