            "  We study rigidly rotating and pulsating strings in the \
background of a 1+1\ndimensional intersection of two orthogonal stacks of \
fivebranes in type IIB\nstring theory by using the Neumann-Rosochatius (NR) \
model. Starting with the\nPolyakov action of the probe fundamental string we \
show that a generalised\nansatz reduce the system into the one dimensional NR \
model in the presence of\nflux. The integrable construction of the model is \
