               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2209.14274\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Christian Ferko\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riccardo Borsato, Christian Ferko, Alessandro \
Sfondrini\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the Classical Integrability of Root-$T \
\\\\overline{T}$ Flows\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"34 pages; LaTeX; references added; comment added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.107.086011\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Root-$T \\\\overline{T}$ flow was recently \
introduced as a universal and\\nclassically marginal deformation of any \
two-dimensional translation-invariant\\nfield theory. The flow commutes with \
the (irrelevant) $T \\\\overline{T}$ flow and\\nit can be integrated \
explicitly for a large class of actions, leading to\\nnon-analytic \
Lagrangians reminiscent of the four-dimensional Modified-Maxwell\\ntheory \
(ModMax). It is not a priori obvious whether the Root-$T \
\\\\overline{T}$\\nflow preserves integrability, like it is the case for the \
$T \\\\overline{T}$\\nflow. In this paper we demonstrate that this is the \
case for a large class of\\nclassical models by explicitly constructing a \
deformed Lax connection. We\\ndiscuss the principal chiral model and the \
non-linear sigma models on symmetric\\nand semi-symmetric spaces, without or \
with Wess-Zumino term. We also construct\\nLax connections for the \
two-parameter families of theories deformed by both\\nRoot-$T \
\\\\overline{T}$ and $T \\\\overline{T}$ for all of these models.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
