         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2209.14274", "submitter" -> "Christian Ferko", "authors" -> 
            "Riccardo Borsato, Christian Ferko, Alessandro Sfondrini", 
            "title" -> 
            "On the Classical Integrability of Root-$T \\overline{T}$ Flows", 
            "comments" -> "34 pages; LaTeX; references added; comment added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.107.086011", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The Root-$T \\overline{T}$ flow was recently introduced as a \
universal and\nclassically marginal deformation of any two-dimensional \
translation-invariant\nfield theory. The flow commutes with the (irrelevant) \
$T \\overline{T}$ flow and\nit can be integrated explicitly for a large class \
of actions, leading to\nnon-analytic Lagrangians reminiscent of the \
four-dimensional Modified-Maxwell\ntheory (ModMax). It is not a priori \
obvious whether the Root-$T \\overline{T}$\nflow preserves integrability, \
like it is the case for the $T \\overline{T}$\nflow. In this paper we \
demonstrate that this is the case for a large class of\nclassical models by \
explicitly constructing a deformed Lax connection. We\ndiscuss the principal \
chiral model and the non-linear sigma models on symmetric\nand semi-symmetric \
spaces, without or with Wess-Zumino term. We also construct\nLax connections \
for the two-parameter families of theories deformed by both\nRoot-$T \
\\overline{T}$ and $T \\overline{T}$ for all of these models.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 28 Sep 2022 17:39:19 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 4 Oct 2022 23:02:00 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 13 Oct 2022 16:01:46 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v4", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 15 Dec 2022 19:29:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-05-10", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Borsato", "Riccardo", ""}, {
              "Ferko", "Christian", ""}, {"Sfondrini", "Alessandro", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
