            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2210.09318\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Junho Hong\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nikolay Bobev, Junho Hong, Valentin Reys\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Large $N$ Partition Functions of the ABJM Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v1: 56 pages, 4 figures; v2: corrected typos in equations \
(2.5) and\\n  (4.69), updated references; v3: added footnote 11, minor \
revisions in\\n  Subsection 4.4; v4: minor typos corrected\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP02(2023)020\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"  We study the large $N$ limit of some supersymmetric \
partition functions of\\nthe $\\\\mathrm{U}(N)_{k}\\\\times \
\\\\mathrm{U}(N)_{-k}$ ABJM theory computed by\\nsupersymmetric localization. \
We conjecture an explicit expression, valid to all\\norders in the large $N$ \
limit, for the partition function on the\\n$\\\\mathrm{U}(1)\\\\times \
\\\\mathrm{U}(1)$ invariant squashed sphere in the presence\\nof real masses \
in terms of an Airy function. Several non-trivial tests of this\\nconjecture \
are presented. In addition, we derive an explicit compact expression\\nfor \
the topologically twisted index of the ABJM theory valid at fixed $k$ \
to\\nall orders in the $1/N$ expansion. We use these results to derive \
the\\ntopologically twisted index and the sphere partition function in the 't \
Hooft\\nlimit which correspond to genus $\\\\tt g$ type IIA string theory \
free energies to\\nall orders in the $\\\\alpha'$ expansion. We discuss the \
implications of our\\nresults for holography and the physics of AdS$_4$ black \
holes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
