          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2210.09318", "submitter" -> "Junho Hong", "authors" -> 
            "Nikolay Bobev, Junho Hong, Valentin Reys", "title" -> 
            "Large $N$ Partition Functions of the ABJM Theory", "comments" -> 
            "v1: 56 pages, 4 figures; v2: corrected typos in equations (2.5) \
and\n  (4.69), updated references; v3: added footnote 11, minor revisions in\n\
  Subsection 4.4; v4: minor typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP02(2023)020", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the large $N$ limit of some supersymmetric partition \
functions of\nthe $\\mathrm{U}(N)_{k}\\times \\mathrm{U}(N)_{-k}$ ABJM theory \
computed by\nsupersymmetric localization. We conjecture an explicit \
expression, valid to all\norders in the large $N$ limit, for the partition \
function on the\n$\\mathrm{U}(1)\\times \\mathrm{U}(1)$ invariant squashed \
sphere in the presence\nof real masses in terms of an Airy function. Several \
non-trivial tests of this\nconjecture are presented. In addition, we derive \
an explicit compact expression\nfor the topologically twisted index of the \
ABJM theory valid at fixed $k$ to\nall orders in the $1/N$ expansion. We use \
these results to derive the\ntopologically twisted index and the sphere \
partition function in the 't Hooft\nlimit which correspond to genus $\\tt g$ \
type IIA string theory free energies to\nall orders in the $\\alpha'$ \
expansion. We discuss the implications of our\nresults for holography and the \
physics of AdS$_4$ black holes.\n", 
