superconformal\n  gauge theory from localization", "comments" -> 
            "41 pages. v2: minor correction; v3: eqs.(2.41) and (2.43) \
corrected", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP01(2023)037", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We apply the localization technique to compute the free energy \
on four-sphere\nand the circular BPS Wilson loop in the four-dimensional \
$\\cal N$=2\nsuperconformal $Sp(2N)$ gauge theory containing vector multiplet \
coupled to\nfour hypermultiplets in fundamental representation and one \
hypermultiplet in\nrank-2 antisymmetric representation. This theory is unique \
among similar $\\cal\nN$=2 superconformal models that are planar-equivalent \
to $\\cal N$=4 SYM in that\nthe corresponding localization matrix model has \
the interaction potential\ncontaining single-trace terms only. We exploit \
this property to show that, to\nany order in large $N$ expansion and an \
arbitrary 't Hooft coupling $\\lambda$,\nthe free energy and the Wilson loop \
satisfy Toda lattice equations. Solving\nthese equations at strong coupling, \
we find remarkably simple expressions for\nthese observables which include \
all corrections in $1/N$ and\n$1/\\sqrt{\\lambda}$. We also compute the \
leading exponentially suppressed ${\\cal\nO}(e^{-\\sqrt{\\lambda}})$ \
corrections and consider a generalization to the case\nwhen the fundamental \
hypermultiplets have a non-zero mass. The string theory\ndual of this $\\cal \
N$=2 gauge theory should be a particular orientifold of\nAdS$_5 \\times S^5$ \
type IIB string and we discuss the string theory\ninterpretation of the \
obtained strong-coupling results.\n", 
