         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2211.03203", "submitter" -> "Julius Julius", "authors" -> 
            "Andrea Cavagli\\`a and Nikolay Gromov and Julius Julius and\n  \
Michelangelo Preti", "title" -> 
            "Integrated correlators from integrability: Maldacena-Wilson line \
in\n  $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM", "comments" -> 
            "45 pages, 6 figures, ancillary Mathematica notebook; 1 figure \
added\n  and minor changes in Appendix C", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP04(2023)026", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a systematic method for the derivation of a \
relation which\nconnects the correlation function of operators on the \
straight Maldacena-Wilson\nline with the integrability data for the cusp \
anomalous dimension. As we show,\nthe derivation requires very careful \
treatment of the UV divergences. Our\nmethod opens a way to derive infinitely \
many constraints on integrals of\nmulti-point correlation functions, relating \
them with the integrability data\nfor the generalised cusp anomalous \
dimension governed by the Quantum Spectral\nCurve. Such constraints have been \
shown recently to be very powerful in\ncombination with the numerical \
conformal bootstrap, leading to very narrow\nnon-perturbative bounds on \
conformal data beyond the spectrum.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 6 Nov 2022 19:05:44 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 28 Dec 2022 13:50:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
