                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrability treatment of AdS/CFT orbifolds\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"54 pages, 6 figures; v4: further calculations added, \
published\\n  version v3: comments and references added, some reformulations \
for clarity,\\n  v2: minor comment and references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1751-8121/ace947\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We elaborate on the treatment of orbifolds of type IIB \
string theory on\\n$AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ and their dual gauge theories with \
integrability techniques.\\nThe implementation of orbifolds via twisted \
spin-chains, thermodynamic Bethe\\nAnsatz equations with chemical potentials \
and $Y$- and $T$-systems with\\nmodified asymptotics is confronted with \
twisted boundary conditions of the\\nstring sigma-model. This allows us to \
consistently twist the quantum spectral\\ncurve, which is believed to bridge \
the two sides of the AdS/CFT duality. We\\ndiscuss Abelian orbifolds of \
$PSU(2,2|4)$ and treat the special cases of\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
supersymmetric $\\\\mathbb{Z}_2$-orbifolds and type 0B string\\ntheory on \
$AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ as primary examples. This opens a pathway to probe\\nthe \
validity of the duality and to study the long-standing question of \
tachyon\\nstabilisation in non-supersymmetric AdS/CFT. We comment on the \
current\\nunderstanding of this issue and point out the next steps in this \
challenge.\\n\""}]}, {
