            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We elaborate on the treatment of orbifolds of type IIB string \
theory on\n$AdS_5\\times S^5$ and their dual gauge theories with \
integrability techniques.\nThe implementation of orbifolds via twisted \
spin-chains, thermodynamic Bethe\nAnsatz equations with chemical potentials \
and $Y$- and $T$-systems with\nmodified asymptotics is confronted with \
twisted boundary conditions of the\nstring sigma-model. This allows us to \
consistently twist the quantum spectral\ncurve, which is believed to bridge \
the two sides of the AdS/CFT duality. We\ndiscuss Abelian orbifolds of \
$PSU(2,2|4)$ and treat the special cases of\n$\\mathcal{N}=2$ supersymmetric \
$\\mathbb{Z}_2$-orbifolds and type 0B string\ntheory on $AdS_5\\times S^5$ as \
primary examples. This opens a pathway to probe\nthe validity of the duality \
and to study the long-standing question of tachyon\nstabilisation in \
non-supersymmetric AdS/CFT. We comment on the current\nunderstanding of this \
issue and point out the next steps in this challenge.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
