               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2211.04479\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrea Fontanella\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Andrea Fontanella, Juan Miguel Nieto Garc\\\\'ia and Olof \
Ohlsson Sax\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-relativistic string monodromies\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"20 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2023)165\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NORDITA 2022-079\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Spectral curve methods proved to be powerful techniques \
in the context of\\nrelativistic integrable string theories, since they allow \
to derive the\\nsemiclassical spectrum from the minimal knowledge of a Lax \
pair and a classical\\nstring solution. In this paper we initiate the study \
of the spectral curve for\\nnon-relativistic strings in AdS$_5\\\\times S^5$. \
First we show that for string\\nsolutions whose Lax connection is independent \
of $\\\\sigma$, the eigenvalues of\\nthe monodromy matrix do not have any \
spectral parameter dependence. We remark\\nthat this particular behaviour \
also appears for relativistic strings in flat\\nspace. Second, for some \
simple non-relativistic string solutions where the path\\nordered exponential \
of the Lax connection can be computed, we show that the\\nmonodromy matrix is \
either diagonalisable with quasi-momenta independent of the\\nspectral \
parameter, or non-diagonalisable. For the latter case, we propose a\\nnotion \
of generalised quasi-momenta, based on maximal abelian subalgebras,\\nwhich \
retain a dependence on the spectral parameter.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 8 Nov 2022 19:00:01 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
