            "authors" -> 
            "Andrea Fontanella, Juan Miguel Nieto Garc\\'ia and Olof Ohlsson \
Sax", "title" -> "Non-relativistic string monodromies", "comments" -> 
            "20 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP01(2023)165", "report-no" -> "NORDITA 2022-079", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Spectral curve methods proved to be powerful techniques in the \
context of\nrelativistic integrable string theories, since they allow to \
derive the\nsemiclassical spectrum from the minimal knowledge of a Lax pair \
and a classical\nstring solution. In this paper we initiate the study of the \
spectral curve for\nnon-relativistic strings in AdS$_5\\times S^5$. First we \
show that for string\nsolutions whose Lax connection is independent of \
$\\sigma$, the eigenvalues of\nthe monodromy matrix do not have any spectral \
parameter dependence. We remark\nthat this particular behaviour also appears \
for relativistic strings in flat\nspace. Second, for some simple \
non-relativistic string solutions where the path\nordered exponential of the \
Lax connection can be computed, we show that the\nmonodromy matrix is either \
diagonalisable with quasi-momenta independent of the\nspectral parameter, or \
non-diagonalisable. For the latter case, we propose a\nnotion of generalised \
quasi-momenta, based on maximal abelian subalgebras,\nwhich retain a \
dependence on the spectral parameter.\n", 
