                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the 3-point functions of gauge-invariant \
scalar operators in four\\ndimensional $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal \
quiver theories using supersymmetric\\nlocalization in the planar limit of a \
large number of colors. By exploiting a\\nweb of nontrivial relations, we \
show that the 3-point functions can be\\nexpressed in terms of the 2-point \
functions through exact Ward-like identities\\nthat are valid for all values \
of the coupling constant. In this way, using\\nrecent results about the \
2-point functions, we are able to obtain the\\nasymptotic strong-coupling \
expansion of the 3-point functions and of the\\ncorresponding structure \
constants in the planar limit. Our results extend to\\nsub-leading orders \
what has been recently found at leading order, where a\\nprecise match with \
calculations within the AdS/CFT correspondence at the\\nsupergravity level is \
possible. Therefore, our findings can be interpreted also\\nas a prediction \
for the sub-leading string corrections to these \
holographic\\ncalculations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
