            "  We study the 3-point functions of gauge-invariant scalar \
operators in four\ndimensional $\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal quiver \
theories using supersymmetric\nlocalization in the planar limit of a large \
number of colors. By exploiting a\nweb of nontrivial relations, we show that \
the 3-point functions can be\nexpressed in terms of the 2-point functions \
through exact Ward-like identities\nthat are valid for all values of the \
coupling constant. In this way, using\nrecent results about the 2-point \
