               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matrix Models and Holography: Mass Deformations of Long \
Quiver Theories\\n  in 5d and 3d\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"46 pages plus appendices. Various figures. Some \
improvements and\\n  references added. SciPost Physics version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SciPost Phys. 15, 086 (2023)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.21468/SciPostPhys.15.3.086\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We enlarge the dictionary between matrix models for \
long linear quivers\\npreserving eight supercharges in $d=5$ and $d=3$ and \
type IIB supergravity\\nbackgrounds with AdS$_{d+1}$ factors. We introduce \
mass deformations of the\\nfield theory that break the quiver into a \
collection of interacting linear\\nquivers, which are decoupled at the end of \
the RG flow. We find and solve a\\nLaplace problem in supergravity which \
realises these deformations\\nholographically. The free energy and \
expectation values of antisymmetric Wilson\\nloops are calculated on both \
sides of the proposed duality, finding agreement.\\nOur matching procedure \
sheds light on the F-theorem in five dimensions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
