               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Partition functions on squashed seven-spheres and \
holography\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"46 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP03(2023)178\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Our paper presents two main results. First, we study \
the renormalized free\\nenergies of Euclidean Einstein gravity in \
asymptotically AdS$_8$ and various\\nfield theories on a squashed seven \
sphere. In the gravity theory, we\\ndemonstrate the absence of the \
Hawking-Page transition, while in the field\\ntheory, we focus on the O($N$) \
vector model and the massless free fermion\\nmodel. The conformal symmetry \
governs the universal behaviors of the free\\nenergies for small and large \
squashings, which we confirm numerically and\\nanalytically. Second, we \
evaluate the second-order derivative of CFT free\\nenergy with respect to the \
squashing parameter, finding universal results that\\nhold for generic \
conformal field theories. We examine two different squashings,\\none with an \
SU(2) bundle, which is the primary focus of our paper, and another\\nwith a \
U(1) bundle, where our results align with the conjectured formula from\\nthe \
gravity side in the literature.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
