           "id" -> "2211.13516", "submitter" -> "Xuao Zhang", "authors" -> 
            "Xuao Zhang", "title" -> 
            "Partition functions on squashed seven-spheres and holography", 
            "comments" -> "46 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP03(2023)178", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Our paper presents two main results. First, we study the \
renormalized free\nenergies of Euclidean Einstein gravity in asymptotically \
AdS$_8$ and various\nfield theories on a squashed seven sphere. In the \
gravity theory, we\ndemonstrate the absence of the Hawking-Page transition, \
while in the field\ntheory, we focus on the O($N$) vector model and the \
massless free fermion\nmodel. The conformal symmetry governs the universal \
behaviors of the free\nenergies for small and large squashings, which we \
confirm numerically and\nanalytically. Second, we evaluate the second-order \
derivative of CFT free\nenergy with respect to the squashing parameter, \
finding universal results that\nhold for generic conformal field theories. We \
examine two different squashings,\none with an SU(2) bundle, which is the \
primary focus of our paper, and another\nwith a U(1) bundle, where our \
results align with the conjectured formula from\nthe gravity side in the \
literature.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
