         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2212.01359", "submitter" -> "Finn Bjarne Kohl", "authors" -> 
            "Finn Bjarne Kohl and Raimar Wulkenhaar", "title" -> 
            "Intersection theory of the complex quartic Kontsevich model", 
            "comments" -> "22 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "math-ph math.MP", 
            "license" -> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We expand correlation functions of the Langmann-Szabo-Zarembo \
(LSZ) model in\nterms of intersection numbers on the moduli space of complex \
curves. This\nprovides an explicit, physically motivated example for the \
expansion of\ncorrelation functions generated by Chekhov-Eynard-Orantin \
topological\nrecursion. To this end, we unify notation as well as different \
conventions\npresent in the literature and use a set of moduli of the \
spectral curve adapted\nto the physically motivated model. The presentation \
focuses on an illustrative,\nstep-by-step comprehension of the work.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 2 Dec 2022 18:38:53 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2022-12-05", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kohl", "Finn Bjarne", ""}, {
              "Wulkenhaar", "Raimar", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
