            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2212.03886\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Nadav Drukker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nadav Drukker and Ziwen Kong\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1/3 BPS loops and defect CFTs in ABJM theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"38 pages, half of them appendices; V2: minor changes, \
version to\\n  appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2023)137\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We address a longstanding question of whether ABJM \
theory has Wilson loop\\noperators preserving eight supercharges (so 1/3 \
BPS). We present such Wilson\\nloops made of a large supermatrix combining \
two 1/2 BPS Wilson loops. We study\\nthe spectrum of operator insertions into \
them including the displacement\\noperator and several others and study their \
correlation functions. Another\\nnatural construction arising in this context \
are Wilson loops with alternating\\nsuperconnections. This amounts to \
including \\\"defect changing operators\\\" along\\nthe loop, similar to a \
discrete cusp. This insertion is topological and\\npreserves two \
supercharges. We study the multiplet of this operator and how it\\ncan be \
used to introduce further operators. We also construct the defect\\nconformal \
manifold arising from marginal defect operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
