            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2212.08625\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fiona Seibold\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ben Hoare, Nat Levine, Fiona K. Seibold\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bi-$\\\\eta$ and bi-$\\\\lambda$ deformations of \
$\\\\mathbb{Z}_4$ permutation\\n  supercosets\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages, published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2023)024\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-FS-2022-03\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Integrable string sigma models on AdS$_3$ backgrounds \
with 16 supersymmetries\\nhave the distinguishing feature that their \
superisometry group is a direct\\nproduct. As a result the deformation theory \
of these models is particularly\\nrich since the two supergroups in the \
product can be deformed independently. We\\nconstruct bi-$\\\\eta$ and bi-$\\\
\\lambda$ deformations of two classes of\\n$\\\\mathbb{Z}_4$ permutation \
supercoset sigma models, which describe sectors of\\nthe Green-Schwarz and \
pure-spinor string worldsheet theories on type II AdS$_3$\\nbackgrounds with \
pure R-R flux. We discuss an important limit of these models\\nwhen one \
supergroup is undeformed. The associated deformed supergravity\\nbackground \
should preserve 8 supersymmetries and is expected to have better\\nproperties \
than the full bi-deformation. As a step towards investigating the\\nquantum \
properties of these models, we study the two-loop RG flow of the\\nbosonic \
truncation of the bi-$\\\\lambda$ deformation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
