permutation\n  supercosets", "comments" -> "35 pages, published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP04(2023)024", 
            "report-no" -> "Imperial-TP-FS-2022-03", "categories" -> "hep-th",
             "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Integrable string sigma models on AdS$_3$ backgrounds with 16 \
supersymmetries\nhave the distinguishing feature that their superisometry \
group is a direct\nproduct. As a result the deformation theory of these \
models is particularly\nrich since the two supergroups in the product can be \
deformed independently. We\nconstruct bi-$\\eta$ and bi-$\\lambda$ \
deformations of two classes of\n$\\mathbb{Z}_4$ permutation supercoset sigma \
models, which describe sectors of\nthe Green-Schwarz and pure-spinor string \
worldsheet theories on type II AdS$_3$\nbackgrounds with pure R-R flux. We \
discuss an important limit of these models\nwhen one supergroup is \
undeformed. The associated deformed supergravity\nbackground should preserve \
8 supersymmetries and is expected to have better\nproperties than the full \
bi-deformation. As a step towards investigating the\nquantum properties of \
these models, we study the two-loop RG flow of the\nbosonic truncation of the \
bi-$\\lambda$ deformation.\n", 
