            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2212.09732\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Enrico Olivucci\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Vladimir Kazakov and Enrico Olivucci\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Loom for General Fishnet CFTs\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"35 pages, 21 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP06(2023)041\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a broad class of $d$-dimensional conformal \
field theories of\\n$SU(N)$ adjoint scalar fields generalising the 4$d$ \
Fishnet CFT (FCFT)\\ndiscovered by \\\\\\\"O. G\\\\\\\"urdogan and one of the \
authors as a special limit of\\n$\\\\gamma$-deformed $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM \
theory. In the planar $N\\\\to\\\\infty $ limit\\nthe FCFTs are dominated by \
the ``fishnet\\\" planar Feynman graphs. These graphs\\nare explicitly \
integrable, as was shown long ago by A. Zamolodchikov. The\\nZamolodchikov's \
construction, based on the dual Baxter lattice (straight lines\\non the plane \
intersecting at arbitrary slopes) and the star-triangle\\nidentities, can \
serve as a ``loom\\\" for ``weaving\\\" the Feynman graphs of these\\nFCFTs, \
with certain types of propagators, at any $d$. The Baxter lattice with\\n$M$ \
different slopes and any number of lines parallel to those, generates \
an\\nFCFT consisting of $M(M-1)$ fields and a certain number of chiral \
vertices of\\ndifferent valences with distinguished couplings. These \
non-unitary, logarithmic\\nCFTs enjoy certain reality properties for their \
spectrum due to a symmetry\\nsimilar to the PT-invariance of non-hermitian \
hamiltonians proposed by C.\\nBender. We discuss in more detail the theories \
generated by a loom with\\n$M=2,3,4$, and the generalisation of the loom \
FCFTs for spinning fields in\\n4$d$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 19 Dec 2022 18:53:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2023-06-28\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kazakov\"", ",", "\"Vladimir\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Olivucci\"", ",", "\"Enrico\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
