            "  We propose a broad class of $d$-dimensional conformal field \
theories of\n$SU(N)$ adjoint scalar fields generalising the 4$d$ Fishnet CFT \
(FCFT)\ndiscovered by \\\"O. G\\\"urdogan and one of the authors as a special \
limit of\n$\\gamma$-deformed $\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM theory. In the planar \
$N\\to\\infty $ limit\nthe FCFTs are dominated by the ``fishnet\" planar \
Feynman graphs. These graphs\nare explicitly integrable, as was shown long \
ago by A. Zamolodchikov. The\nZamolodchikov's construction, based on the dual \
Baxter lattice (straight lines\non the plane intersecting at arbitrary \
slopes) and the star-triangle\nidentities, can serve as a ``loom\" for \
``weaving\" the Feynman graphs of these\nFCFTs, with certain types of \
propagators, at any $d$. The Baxter lattice with\n$M$ different slopes and \
any number of lines parallel to those, generates an\nFCFT consisting of \
$M(M-1)$ fields and a certain number of chiral vertices of\ndifferent \
valences with distinguished couplings. These non-unitary, logarithmic\nCFTs \
enjoy certain reality properties for their spectrum due to a symmetry\n\
similar to the PT-invariance of non-hermitian hamiltonians proposed by C.\n\
Bender. We discuss in more detail the theories generated by a loom with\n\
$M=2,3,4$, and the generalisation of the loom FCFTs for spinning fields in\n\
4$d$.\n", "versions" -> {{
