 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider four dimensional $U(N)$ $\\\\mathcal N=4$ \
SYM theory interacting\\nwith a 3d $\\\\mathcal N=4$ theory living on a \
codimension-one interface and\\nholographically dual to the D3-D5 system \
without flux. Localization captures\\nseveral observables in this dCFT, \
including its free energy, related to the\\ndefect expectation value, and \
single trace $\\\\frac{1}{2}$-BPS composite scalars.\\nThese quantities may \
be computed in a hermitian one-matrix model with\\nnon-polynomial \
single-trace potential. We exploit the integrable Volterra\\nhierarchy \
underlying the matrix model and systematically study its $1/N$\\nexpansion at \
any value of the 't Hooft coupling. In particular, the strong\\ncoupling \
regime is determined -- up to non-perturbative exponentially\\nsuppressed \
corrections -- by differential relations that constrain higher order\\nterms \
in the $1/N$ expansion. The analysis is extended to the model with\\n$SU(N)$ \
gauge symmetry by resorting to the more general Toda lattice \
equations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 23 Dec 2022 15:56:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
