           "id" -> "2212.12415", "submitter" -> "Matteo Beccaria", "authors" -> 
            "Matteo Beccaria, Alejandro Cabo-Bizet", "title" -> 
            "$1/N$ expansion of the D3-D5 defect CFT", "comments" -> 
            "39 pages. v2: extended bibliography", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider four dimensional $U(N)$ $\\mathcal N=4$ SYM theory \
interacting\nwith a 3d $\\mathcal N=4$ theory living on a codimension-one \
interface and\nholographically dual to the D3-D5 system without flux. \
Localization captures\nseveral observables in this dCFT, including its free \
energy, related to the\ndefect expectation value, and single trace \
$\\frac{1}{2}$-BPS composite scalars.\nThese quantities may be computed in a \
hermitian one-matrix model with\nnon-polynomial single-trace potential. We \
exploit the integrable Volterra\nhierarchy underlying the matrix model and \
systematically study its $1/N$\nexpansion at any value of the 't Hooft \
coupling. In particular, the strong\ncoupling regime is determined -- up to \
non-perturbative exponentially\nsuppressed corrections -- by differential \
relations that constrain higher order\nterms in the $1/N$ expansion. The \
analysis is extended to the model with\n$SU(N)$ gauge symmetry by resorting \
to the more general Toda lattice equations.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
