               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ismail Zahed\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Yizhuang Liu, Maciej A. Nowak and Ismail Zahed\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Nambu-Goto string in QCD: Dipole interactions, \
scattering and\\n  entanglement\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"version published in PRD\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph hep-lat nucl-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit some aspects of the stringy approach to \
dipole-dipole\\ninteractions, scattering and entanglement in QCD, using the \
Nambu-Goto (NG)\\nstring, without recourse to holography. We first show that \
the potential\\nbetween two static dipoles exchanging closed NG strings is \
attractive at all\\nseparations. Underlining the exchange there is an \
emergent entropy, that is\\ndominated by the tachyon at large separation, and \
vanishes at short separation,\\na measure of the confinement-deconfinement \
transition. The same tachyon is\\ndominant in the scattering amplitude, as a \
correlator of two Wilson loops for\\ntwo fixed dipole-like hadrons separated \
at large rapidity gap, where the\\ncontribution of the worldsheet fermions is \
included. While the tachyon causes\\nthe mean string bit density to grow \
exponentially with the rapidity, the total\\nscattering cross section still \
satisfies the Froissart bound by quantum\\nshadowing. The stringy scattering \
exchange also carries an entanglement\\nentropy, that saturates when the \
bound is reached. For hadrons with varying\\ndipole sizes, the tachyon \
exchange takes place in hyperbolic space in the\\nconformal limit. The result \
for the full S-matrix is reminiscent of the one\\nfrom Mueller$^\\\\prime$s \
evolved dipole wavefunction, for the total dipole-dipole\\ncross section in \
perturbative QCD.\\n\""}]}, {
