         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2301.06154", "submitter" -> "Ismail Zahed", "authors" -> 
            "Yizhuang Liu, Maciej A. Nowak and Ismail Zahed", "title" -> 
            "The Nambu-Goto string in QCD: Dipole interactions, scattering \
and\n  entanglement", "comments" -> "version published in PRD", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-ph hep-lat nucl-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We revisit some aspects of the stringy approach to \
dipole-dipole\ninteractions, scattering and entanglement in QCD, using the \
Nambu-Goto (NG)\nstring, without recourse to holography. We first show that \
the potential\nbetween two static dipoles exchanging closed NG strings is \
attractive at all\nseparations. Underlining the exchange there is an emergent \
entropy, that is\ndominated by the tachyon at large separation, and vanishes \
at short separation,\na measure of the confinement-deconfinement transition. \
The same tachyon is\ndominant in the scattering amplitude, as a correlator of \
two Wilson loops for\ntwo fixed dipole-like hadrons separated at large \
rapidity gap, where the\ncontribution of the worldsheet fermions is included. \
While the tachyon causes\nthe mean string bit density to grow exponentially \
with the rapidity, the total\nscattering cross section still satisfies the \
Froissart bound by quantum\nshadowing. The stringy scattering exchange also \
carries an entanglement\nentropy, that saturates when the bound is reached. \
For hadrons with varying\ndipole sizes, the tachyon exchange takes place in \
hyperbolic space in the\nconformal limit. The result for the full S-matrix is \
reminiscent of the one\nfrom Mueller$^\\prime$s evolved dipole wavefunction, \
for the total dipole-dipole\ncross section in perturbative QCD.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 15 Jan 2023 18:33:35 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 5 Dec 2023 18:01:55 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-12-06", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Liu", "Yizhuang", ""}, {
              "Nowak", "Maciej A.", ""}, {"Zahed", "Ismail", ""}}}], 
