               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2302.10370\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imtak Jeon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Alfredo Gonz\\\\'alez Lezcano, Imtak Jeon, Augniva \
Ray\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Supersymmetric localization: ${\\\\cal N}=(2,2)$ theories \
on S$^2$ and\\n  AdS$_2$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"63 pages + appendices, v2: references added, v3: typos \
corrected,\\n  matches with published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP07(2023)056\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Application of the supersymmetric localization method \
to theories on anti-de\\nSitter spacetime has received recent interest, yet \
still remains as a\\nchallenging problem. In this paper, we focus on (global) \
Euclidean AdS$_2$, on\\nwhich we consider an Abelian ${\\\\cal N}=(2,2)$ \
theory and implement localization\\ncomputation to obtain the exact partition \
function. For comparison, we also\\nrevisit the theory on S$^2$ and perform a \
parallel computation. We refine the\\nnotion of equivariant supersymmetry and \
use appropriate functional integration\\nmeasure. For AdS$_2$ we choose a \
supersymmetric boundary condition which is\\ncompatible with the principle of \
variation. To evaluate the 1-loop determinant\\nabout the localization \
saddle, we use index theory and fixed point formula,\\nwhere we pay attention \
to the effect of zero modes and their superpartners. The\\nexistence of \
fermionic superpartner of 1-form boundary zero modes is proven.\\nObtaining \
the 1-loop determinant requires expansion of the index that presents\\nan \
ambiguity, which we resolve using boundary condition. The \
resulting\\npartition function reveals an overall dependence on the size of \
the background\\nmanifold, AdS$_2$ as well as S$^2$, as a sum of two types of \
contributions: a\\nlocal one from local conformal anomaly through the index \
computation and a\\nglobal one coming from zero modes. This overall size \
dependence is confirmed by\\nthe perturbative 1-loop evaluation using heat \
kernel method.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
