            "  Application of the supersymmetric localization method to \
theories on anti-de\nSitter spacetime has received recent interest, yet still \
remains as a\nchallenging problem. In this paper, we focus on (global) \
Euclidean AdS$_2$, on\nwhich we consider an Abelian ${\\cal N}=(2,2)$ theory \
and implement localization\ncomputation to obtain the exact partition \
function. For comparison, we also\nrevisit the theory on S$^2$ and perform a \
parallel computation. We refine the\nnotion of equivariant supersymmetry and \
use appropriate functional integration\nmeasure. For AdS$_2$ we choose a \
supersymmetric boundary condition which is\ncompatible with the principle of \
variation. To evaluate the 1-loop determinant\nabout the localization saddle, \
we use index theory and fixed point formula,\nwhere we pay attention to the \
effect of zero modes and their superpartners. The\nexistence of fermionic \
superpartner of 1-form boundary zero modes is proven.\nObtaining the 1-loop \
determinant requires expansion of the index that presents\nan ambiguity, \
which we resolve using boundary condition. The resulting\npartition function \
reveals an overall dependence on the size of the background\nmanifold, \
AdS$_2$ as well as S$^2$, as a sum of two types of contributions: a\nlocal \
one from local conformal anomaly through the index computation and a\nglobal \
one coming from zero modes. This overall size dependence is confirmed by\nthe \
perturbative 1-loop evaluation using heat kernel method.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
