            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In planar maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills, we can compute \
three-point\nfunctions at weak coupling using the so-called hexagonalization \
formalism. The\nmain objects in this framework are called hexagons. We are \
interested in two\nsectors of the theory, spanned by operators built entirely \
from scalar fields,\nand by spinning operators, respectively. By reviewing \
the analytic properties\nof these building blocks, we find new \
representations for them at weak coupling\nwhere the two sectors are on equal \
footing. We compute the classical limit of\nthe hexagons and of correlation \
functions in both sectors for some choices of\npolarizations and our results \
match previous predictions in the literature.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 23 Feb 2023 17:56:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-02-24", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Fabri", "Matheus", ""}, {
              "Lefundes", "Gabriel", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
