 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study, in the context of the three-dimensional \
${\\\\cal N}=6$\\nChern-Simons-matter (ABJM) theory, the infrared-finite \
functions that result\\nfrom performing $L-1$ loop integrations over the \
$L$-loop integrand of the\\nlogarithm of the four-particle scattering \
amplitude. Our starting point are the\\nintegrands obtained from the recently \
proposed all-loop projected amplituhedron\\nfor the ABJM theory. Organizing \
them in terms of negative geometries ensures\\nthat no divergences occur upon \
integration if at least one loop variable is\\nleft unintegrated. We \
explicitly perform the integrations up to $L=3$, finding\\nboth parity-even \
and -odd terms. Moreover, we discuss a prescription to compute\\nthe cusp \
anomalous dimension $\\\\Gamma_{\\\\rm cusp}$ of ABJM in terms of \
the\\nintegrated negative geometries, and we use it to reproduce the \
first\\nnon-trivial order of $\\\\Gamma_{\\\\rm cusp}$. Finally, we show that \
the leading\\nsingularities that characterize the integrated results are \
conformally\\ninvariant.\\n\""}]}, {
