               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2303.06769\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kallol Sen\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kallol Sen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exploring $2d$ localization with a step dependent \
coin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"19 pages, 8 figures, Data Availability added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"quant-ph cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We generalize the coin operator of \
\\\\cite{Zahed_2023}, to include a step\\ndependent feature which induces \
localization in $2d$. This is evident from the\\nprobability distributions \
which can be further used to categorize the localized\\nwalks. Localization \
is also evident from the entropic measures. We compute and\\ncompare three \
distinct measures (a) Shannon Entropy in the position and coin\\nspace, (b) \
Entanglement entropy between position and spin space, and (c)\\nQuantum \
Relative Entropy which is a POVM of density operators of the step\\ndependent \
and step independent coins. Shannon Entropy and Entanglement Entropy\\nare \
periodic and bounded functions of the time steps. The zeros of Shannon \
and\\nEntanglement entropies signify a complete localization of the \
wave-function.\\nThe Quantum Relative Entropy and Quantum Information \
Variance exhibit a similar\\nperiodic feature with a zero minima where the \
step dependent and step\\nindependent walks coincide. Finally, we compute the \
numerical localization\\nlength (inverse of the Lyapunov Exponent) for the \
step dependent coin as a\\nfunction of energy and compare with an approximate \
perturbative computation,\\nwhere we put the step dependent coin as a \
perturbation in the background of a\\nstep independent coin. In both the \
instances, we find that the localization\\nlength peaks at approximately the \
same positions in the momentum space.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 12 Mar 2023 22:27:30 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 26 Oct 2023 05:44:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2023-10-27\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Sen\"", ",", "\"Kallol\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
