         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2303.06769", "submitter" -> "Kallol Sen", "authors" -> 
            "Kallol Sen", "title" -> 
            "Exploring $2d$ localization with a step dependent coin", 
            "comments" -> "19 pages, 8 figures, Data Availability added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> 
            "quant-ph cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We generalize the coin operator of \\cite{Zahed_2023}, to \
include a step\ndependent feature which induces localization in $2d$. This is \
evident from the\nprobability distributions which can be further used to \
categorize the localized\nwalks. Localization is also evident from the \
entropic measures. We compute and\ncompare three distinct measures (a) \
Shannon Entropy in the position and coin\nspace, (b) Entanglement entropy \
between position and spin space, and (c)\nQuantum Relative Entropy which is a \
POVM of density operators of the step\ndependent and step independent coins. \
Shannon Entropy and Entanglement Entropy\nare periodic and bounded functions \
of the time steps. The zeros of Shannon and\nEntanglement entropies signify a \
complete localization of the wave-function.\nThe Quantum Relative Entropy and \
Quantum Information Variance exhibit a similar\nperiodic feature with a zero \
minima where the step dependent and step\nindependent walks coincide. \
Finally, we compute the numerical localization\nlength (inverse of the \
Lyapunov Exponent) for the step dependent coin as a\nfunction of energy and \
compare with an approximate perturbative computation,\nwhere we put the step \
dependent coin as a perturbation in the background of a\nstep independent \
coin. In both the instances, we find that the localization\nlength peaks at \
approximately the same positions in the momentum space.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
