 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the correlation function between one \
single-trace scalar operator\\nand a circular Wilson loop in the $4d$ \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ superconformal field\\ntheory with gauge group $SU(N)$ and \
matter transforming in the symmetric and\\nanti-symmetric representations. By \
exploiting supersymmetric localization, we\\nresum the perturbative expansion \
of this correlator in the large-$N$ 't Hooft\\nlimit. Furthermore, using both \
analytical and numerical techniques, we provide\\na prediction for the \
leading term of its strong coupling expansion and we\\ncompare this \
prediction to numerical Pad\\\\'e resummations of the \
perturbative\\nseries.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
