               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hong-Zhe Zhang, Wan-Zhe Feng, Jun-Bao Wu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Holographic Operator Product Expansion of Loop Operators \
in\\n  $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ $SO(N)$ Super Yang-Mills Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2, 22 pages, no figures, comparing with results in the \
case of gauge\\n  group SU(N) added, other minor reversion performed; v1, 20 \
pages, no figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Chin.Phys.C 47 (2023) 8, 083101\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1674-1137/acd364\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper, we compute the correlation functions of \
Wilson(-'t~Hooft)\\nloops with chiral primary operators in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills theory with $SO(N)$ gauge symmetry, which has a \
holographic dual\\ndescription of Type IIB superstring theory on \
the\\n$AdS_{5}\\\\times\\\\mathbf{RP}^{5}$ background. Specifically, we \
compute the\\ncoefficients of the chiral primary operators in the operator \
product expansion\\nof Wilson loops in the fundamental representation, \
Wilson-'t Hooft loops in the\\nsymmetric representation, Wilson loops in the \
anti-fundamental representation\\nand the spinor representation. We also \
