multi-scalar\n  gauge theory", "comments" -> "22 pages, 3 figures", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP04(2023)129", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the one loop renormalisation of 4d $SU(N)$ Yang-Mills \
theory with\n$M$ adjoint representation scalar multiplets related by $O(M)$ \
symmetry.\nGeneral $M$ are of field theoretic interest, and the 4d one loop \
beta function\nof the gauge coupling $g^2$ vanishes for the case $M=22$, \
which is intriguing\nfor string theory. This case is related to D3 branes of \
critical bosonic string\ntheory in $D=22+4=26$. An RG fixed point could have \
provided a definition for a\npurely bosonic AdS/CFT, but we show that scalar \
self-couplings $\\lambda$ ruin\none-loop conformal invariance in the large \
$N$ limit. There are real fixed\nflows (fixed points of $\\lambda/g^2$) only \
for $M\\ge 406$, rendering one-loop\nfixed points of the gauge coupling and \
scalar couplings incompatible.\n  We develop and check an algebraic approach \
to the one-loop renormalisation\ngroup which we find to be characterised by a \
non-associative algebra of\nmarginal couplings. In the large $N$ limit, the \
resulting RG flows typically\nsuffer from strong coupling in both the \
ultraviolet and the infrared. Only for\n$M\\ge 406$ fine-tuned solutions \
exist which are weakly coupled in the infrared.\n", 
