 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct infinite-dimensional R-matrices that \
generalise the relativistic\\nscattering of massless modes with the same \
chirality on $\\\\mathrm{AdS}_2$ near\\nthe Berestein-Maldacena-Nastase \
vacuum. We show that the infrared limit of the\\nR-matrices reproduces \
finite-dimensional scattering of massless modes on\\n$\\\\mathrm{AdS}_2$, \
from which the R-matrices borrow modified braiding unitary.\\nWe also prove \
that the R-matrices enjoy an infinite-dimensional symmetry\\nsuperalgebra \
that embeds that of $\\\\mathrm{AdS}_2$. Finally, we verify that \
the\\nR-matrices are also invariant under crossing symmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
