               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2303.16305\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Gregory Korchemsky\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M. Beccaria, G.P. Korchemsky, A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-planar corrections in orbifold/orientifold \
$\\\\mathcal N=2$\\n  superconformal theories from localization\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"54 pages. v2: minor clarifications\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2023)165\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"IPhT-T23/015, Imperial-TP-AT-2023-01\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study non-planar corrections in two special \
$\\\\mathcal N=2$ superconformal\\n$SU(N)$ gauge theories that are \
planar-equivalent to $\\\\mathcal N=4$ SYM theory:\\ntwo-nodes quiver model \
with equal couplings and $\\\\mathcal N=2$ vector multiplet\\ncoupled to two \
hypermultiplets in rank-2 symmetric and antisymmetric\\nrepresentations. We \
focus on two observables in these theories that admit\\nrepresentation in \
terms of localization matrix model: free energy on 4-sphere\\nand the \
expectation value of half-BPS circular Wilson loop. We extend the\\nmethods \
developed in arXiv:2207.11475 to derive a systematical expansion \
of\\nnon-planar corrections to these observables at strong 't Hooft \
coupling\\nconstant $\\\\lambda$. We show that the leading non planar \
corrections are given\\nby a power series in $\\\\lambda^{3/2}/N^2$ with \
rational coefficients. Sending\\n$N$ and the coupling constant $\\\\lambda$ \
to infinity with $\\\\lambda^{3/2}/N^2$\\nkept fixed corresponds to the \
familiar double scaling limit in matrix models.\\nWe find that in this limit \
the observables in the two models are related in a\\nremarkably simple way: \
the free energies differ by the factor of $2$, whereas\\nthe Wilson loop \
expectation values coincide. Surprisingly, these relations hold\\nonly at \
strong coupling, they are not valid in the weak coupling regime. We\\nalso \
discuss a dual string theory interpretation of the leading corrections \
to\\nthe free energy in the double scaling limit suggesting their relation to\
\\ncurvature corrections in type IIB string effective action.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
