$\\mathcal N=4$ SYM theory:\ntwo-nodes quiver model with equal couplings and \
$\\mathcal N=2$ vector multiplet\ncoupled to two hypermultiplets in rank-2 \
symmetric and antisymmetric\nrepresentations. We focus on two observables in \
these theories that admit\nrepresentation in terms of localization matrix \
model: free energy on 4-sphere\nand the expectation value of half-BPS \
circular Wilson loop. We extend the\nmethods developed in arXiv:2207.11475 to \
derive a systematical expansion of\nnon-planar corrections to these \
observables at strong 't Hooft coupling\nconstant $\\lambda$. We show that \
the leading non planar corrections are given\nby a power series in \
$\\lambda^{3/2}/N^2$ with rational coefficients. Sending\n$N$ and the \
coupling constant $\\lambda$ to infinity with $\\lambda^{3/2}/N^2$\nkept \
fixed corresponds to the familiar double scaling limit in matrix models.\nWe \
find that in this limit the observables in the two models are related in a\n\
remarkably simple way: the free energies differ by the factor of $2$, whereas\
\nthe Wilson loop expectation values coincide. Surprisingly, these relations \
hold\nonly at strong coupling, they are not valid in the weak coupling \
regime. We\nalso discuss a dual string theory interpretation of the leading \
corrections to\nthe free energy in the double scaling limit suggesting their \
relation to\ncurvature corrections in type IIB string effective action.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 28 Mar 2023 20:57:06 GMT"}, {
