Leopoldo A. Pando\\n  Zayas, Guillermo A. Silva\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Beyond AdS$_2$/dCFT$_1$: Insertions in Two Wilson \
Loops\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP10(2023)127\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP10(2023)127\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"LCTP-23-02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider two-point correlators of local operator \
insertions in a system of\\ntwo Wilson-Maldacena loops in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory on\\nboth sides of the AdS/CFT \
correspondence. On the holographic side the\\ncorrelator of two \
Wilson-Maldacena loops is given by a classical string\\nworld-sheet which in \
one phase connects two asymptotically AdS$_2$ regions and\\nin the other \
phase is given by two disconnected AdS$_2$ caps; this\\nconfiguration breaks \
supersymmetry as well as conformal invariance. We present\\na complete \
systematic account of the string world-sheet fluctuations, including\\nthe \
fermionic sector, and study the behavior of the holographic \
two-point\\ncorrelators. On the field theory side we compute certain \
two-point correlators\\nof local operator insertions by resumming sets of \
ladder diagrams. Our results\\ndemonstrate the efficacy of previously \
developed methods in tackling this\\nnon-conformal, non-susy \
regime.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
