Pando\n  Zayas, Guillermo A. Silva", "title" -> 
            "Beyond AdS$_2$/dCFT$_1$: Insertions in Two Wilson Loops", 
            "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> "JHEP10(2023)127", "doi" -> 
            "10.1007/JHEP10(2023)127", "report-no" -> "LCTP-23-02", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider two-point correlators of local operator insertions \
in a system of\ntwo Wilson-Maldacena loops in ${\\cal N}=4$ supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory on\nboth sides of the AdS/CFT correspondence. On the \
holographic side the\ncorrelator of two Wilson-Maldacena loops is given by a \
classical string\nworld-sheet which in one phase connects two asymptotically \
AdS$_2$ regions and\nin the other phase is given by two disconnected AdS$_2$ \
caps; this\nconfiguration breaks supersymmetry as well as conformal \
invariance. We present\na complete systematic account of the string \
world-sheet fluctuations, including\nthe fermionic sector, and study the \
behavior of the holographic two-point\ncorrelators. On the field theory side \
we compute certain two-point correlators\nof local operator insertions by \
resumming sets of ladder diagrams. Our results\ndemonstrate the efficacy of \
previously developed methods in tackling this\nnon-conformal, non-susy \
regime.\n", 
