            "  Using results on topological line defects of 4D Chern-Simons \
theory and the\nalgebra/cycle homology correspondence in complex surfaces \
$\\mathcal{S}$ with\nADE singularities, we study the graded properties of the \
$sl(m|n)$ chain and\nits embedding in string theory. Because of the \
$\\mathbb{Z}_{2}$-grading of $\nsl(m|n)$, we show that the $\\left( \
m+n\\right) !/m!n!$ varieties of superspin\nchains with underlying super \
geometries have different cycle homologies. We\ninvestigate the algebraic and \
homological features of these integrable quantum\nchains and give a link \
between graded 2-cycles and genus-g Rieman surfaces\n$\\Sigma _{g}$. \
Moreover, using homology language, we yield the brane\nrealisation of the \
$sl(m|n)$ chain in type IIA string and its uplift to\nM-theory. Other \
\\textrm{aspects} like graded complex surfaces with $sl(m|n)$\nsingularity as \
well as super magnons are also described.\n", 
