                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Previous studies have shown that a gauge-invariant \
correlation function of\\ntwo chromoelectric fields connected by a straight \
timelike adjoint Wilson line\\nencodes crucial information about quark-gluon \
plasma (QGP) that determines the\\ndynamics of small-sized quarkonium in the \
medium. Motivated by the successes of\\nholographic calculations to describe \
strongly coupled QGP, we calculate the\\nanalog gauge-invariant correlation \
function in strongly coupled $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills \
theory at finite temperature by using the AdS/CFT\\ncorrespondence. Our \
results indicate that the transition processes between\\nbound and unbound \
quarkonium states are suppressed in strongly coupled plasmas,\\nand moreover, \
the leading contributions to these transition processes vanish in\\nboth the \
quantum Brownian motion and quantum optical limits of open quantum\\nsystem \
approaches to quarkonia.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
