strongly\n  coupled $\\mathcal{N}=4$ Yang-Mills plasma from AdS/CFT", 
            "comments" -> "82 pages, 11 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP06(2023)007", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP06(2023)007", 
            "report-no" -> "MIT-CTP/5545; IQuS@UW-21-049", "categories" -> 
            "hep-ph hep-th nucl-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Previous studies have shown that a gauge-invariant correlation \
function of\ntwo chromoelectric fields connected by a straight timelike \
adjoint Wilson line\nencodes crucial information about quark-gluon plasma \
(QGP) that determines the\ndynamics of small-sized quarkonium in the medium. \
Motivated by the successes of\nholographic calculations to describe strongly \
coupled QGP, we calculate the\nanalog gauge-invariant correlation function in \
strongly coupled $\\mathcal{N}=4$\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory at finite \
temperature by using the AdS/CFT\ncorrespondence. Our results indicate that \
the transition processes between\nbound and unbound quarkonium states are \
suppressed in strongly coupled plasmas,\nand moreover, the leading \
contributions to these transition processes vanish in\nboth the quantum \
Brownian motion and quantum optical limits of open quantum\nsystem approaches \
to quarkonia.\n", 
