               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2304.10509\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Samuel Laliberte\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Samuel Laliberte and Suddhasattwa Brahma\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"IKKT thermodynamics and early universe cosmology\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Matrix theory is a proposed non-perturbative definition \
of superstring theory\\nin which space is emergent. Recently, it was shown \
that space-time can emerge\\nwith a scale-invariant spectrum of cosmological \
perturbations which is sourced\\nby thermal fluctuations of the BFSS model at \
finite temperature. Inspired by\\nthese results, we begin a study of the IKKT \
model at finite temperature. We\\nfind that in this model, which is closely \
related to the BFSS model at finite\\ntemperature, thermal fluctuations can \
also source a scale-invariant spectrum of\\nscalar and tensor \
fluctuations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
