Jesse van\\n  Muiden\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantized Strings and Instantons in Holography\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"38 pages. v2: Minor corrections. v3: Corrections to the \
fermion\\n  partition function, appendix added. v4: Minor corrections\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study worldsheet instantons in holographic type IIA \
backgrounds directly\\nin string theory. The first background is a \
dimensional reduction of\\nAdS$_7\\\\times S^4$ and is dual to the maximally \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory\\non $S^5$. The second background is \
AdS$_4\\\\times \\\\mathbf{C}P^3$ dual to ABJM in\\nthe type IIA limit. We \
compute the one-loop partition function of the\\nfundamental string in these \
backgrounds and show that the result is in exact\\nagreement with field \
theory predictions. We argue that for higher rank\\ninstantons, the string \
partition function takes a product form of the single\\ninstanton partition \
function times the contribution of two orbifolds on the\\nworldsheet. We \
determine the orbifold factor to be $n^{-3/2}$ where $n$ is the\\ninstanton \
rank. With this result, we reproduce the series of \
non-perturbative\\ncorrections in $\\\\alpha'$ to the planar $S^5$ free \
energy. When studying the\\nworldsheet instanton partition function on \
$\\\\mathbf{C}P^3$, we encounter twelve\\nfermionic and twelve bosonic zero \
modes. By deforming the ABJM theory, the\\nzero-modes are lifted and \
consequently the tower of worldsheet instantons can\\nbe evaluated and \
matched to known results in the QFT. As a by-product, we\\ndetermine a series \
of higher rank instanton corrections to the free energy of\\nthe \
mass-deformed and orbifolded ABJ(M) theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
