                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We introduce and study several classes of quantum spin \
models with multi-body\\ninteractions that exhibit quantum many-body scars. \
The models are constructed\\nby two different methods: one exploiting \
boundary states in integrable spin\\nchains and the other based on a variant \
of existing methods such as restricted\\nspectrum generating algebras. The \
first method allows us to construct\\ndeformations of the Majumdar-Ghosh and \
Affleck-Kennedy-Lieb-Tasaki models --\\nprototypes of frustration-free \
systems. With the second method, we construct a\\nlarge class of spin-$1$ \
models involving scalar spin chirality in both one and\\ntwo dimensions. \
Interestingly, in some cases, the models so constructed have\\ntowers of scar \
states of different character. For each example, we show that\\nthe scar \
states behave differently from thermal states by comparing their\\nspectral \
and dynamical properties with those of other states. We also show that\\na \
superposition of the scar states constructed by the second method \
exhibits\\nperfectly periodic revivals in the dynamics.\\n\""}]}, {
