               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider gluons scattering in Type IIB string theory \
on AdS$_5\\\\times\\nS^5/\\\\mathbb{Z}_2$ in the presence of D7 branes, which \
is dual to the flavor\\nmultiplet correlator in a certain 4d \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ $USp(2N)$ gauge theory\\nwith $SO(8)$ flavor symmetry and \
complexified coupling $\\\\tau$. We compute this\\nholographic correlator in \
the large $N$ and finite $\\\\tau$ expansion using\\nconstraints from \
derivatives of the mass deformed sphere free energy, which we\\ncompute to \
all orders in $1/N$ and finite $\\\\tau$ using supersymmetric\\nlocalization. \
In particular, we fix the $F^4$ higher derivative correction to\\ngluon \
scattering on AdS at finite string coupling $\\\\tau_s=\\\\tau$ in terms \
of\\nJacobi theta functions, which feature the expected relations between the\
\\n$SL(2,\\\\mathbb{Z})$ duality and the $SO(8)$ triality of the CFT, and \
match it to\\nthe known flat space term. We also use the flat space limit to \
compute $D^2F^4$\\ncorrections of the correlator at finite $\\\\tau$ in terms \
of a non-holomorphic\\nEisenstein series. At weak string coupling, we find \
that the AdS correlator\\ntakes a form which is remarkably similar to that of \
the flat space Veneziano\\namplitude.\\n\""}]}, {
