            "  We consider gluons scattering in Type IIB string theory on \
AdS$_5\\times\nS^5/\\mathbb{Z}_2$ in the presence of D7 branes, which is dual \
to the flavor\nmultiplet correlator in a certain 4d $\\mathcal{N}=2$ \
$USp(2N)$ gauge theory\nwith $SO(8)$ flavor symmetry and complexified \
coupling $\\tau$. We compute this\nholographic correlator in the large $N$ \
and finite $\\tau$ expansion using\nconstraints from derivatives of the mass \
deformed sphere free energy, which we\ncompute to all orders in $1/N$ and \
finite $\\tau$ using supersymmetric\nlocalization. In particular, we fix the \
$F^4$ higher derivative correction to\ngluon scattering on AdS at finite \
string coupling $\\tau_s=\\tau$ in terms of\nJacobi theta functions, which \
feature the expected relations between the\n$SL(2,\\mathbb{Z})$ duality and \
the $SO(8)$ triality of the CFT, and match it to\nthe known flat space term. \
