            "id" -> "2305.03649", "submitter" -> "Konstantin Zarembo", 
             "authors" -> "Charlotte Kristjansen, Konstantin Zarembo", 
             "title" -> "'t Hooft loops and integrability", "comments" -> 
             "47 pages, 4 figures; v2: references added, discussion of sl(2)\n\
  overlaps extended; v3: misprints corrected", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We consider the defect CFT defined by a 't Hooft line \
embedded in N=4 super\nYang-Mills theory. By explicitly quantizing around the \
given background we\nexactly reproduce a prediction from S-duality for the \
correlators between the\n't Hooft line and chiral primaries in the bulk and \
pave the way for higher loop\nanalyses for non-protected operators. \
Furthermore, we demonstrate at the\nleading perturbative order that \
correlators between the 't Hooft line and\nnon-protected bulk operators can \
be efficiently computed using integrability.\nAs a byproduct we find new \
integrable overlaps in sl(2) spin chains in\ndifferent representations.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Fri, 5 May 2023 16:10:40 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
                "Sun, 14 May 2023 19:33:45 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
                "Sat, 26 Aug 2023 18:28:33 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2023-08-29", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kristjansen", "Charlotte", ""}, {
               "Zarembo", "Konstantin", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
