                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Motivated by understanding the scattering of gravitons \
and their\\nsuperpartners from extended $(p, q)$-strings in type IIB string \
theory via\\nAdS/CFT, we study an integrated two-point function of stress \
tensor multiplet\\noperators in the presence of a half-BPS line defect in \
${\\\\cal N} = 4$ $SU(N)$\\nsuper-Yang-Mills theory. We determine this \
integrated correlator at the five\\nlowest non-trivial orders in \
$1/\\\\sqrt{N}$ at fixed Yang-Mills coupling and\\n$\\\\theta$ angle. Our \
calculations are performed explicitly when the line defect\\nis a Wilson \
line, in which case we find a finite number of perturbative\\ncontributions \
at each order in $1/\\\\sqrt{N}$, as well as instanton\\ncontributions. Using \
$SL(2, \\\\mathbb{Z})$ transformations, our results can also\\nbe applied to \
Wilson-'t Hooft line defects dual to extended $(p, q)$-strings in\\nthe bulk. \
We analyze features of these integrated correlators in the weak\\ncoupling \
expansion by comparing with open-closed amplitudes of type IIB \
string\\ntheory on $\\\\text{AdS}_5\\\\times \\\\text{S}^5$, as well as in \
its flat space limit.\\nWe predict new higher-derivative interaction vertices \
on the D1-brane and, more\\ngenerally, on $(p,q)$-strings.\\n\""}]}, {
