           "id" -> "2305.15470", "submitter" -> "Tim Meier", "authors" -> 
            "Tim Meier, Stijn J. van Tongeren", "title" -> 
            "Gauge theory on twist-noncommutative spaces", "comments" -> 
            "62 pages, 11 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> "HU-EP-23/11-RTG", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We construct actions for four dimensional noncommutative \
Yang-Mills theory\nwith star-gauge symmetry, with non-constant \
noncommutativity, to all orders in\nthe noncommutativity. Our construction \
covers all noncommutative spaces\ncorresponding to Drinfel'd twists based on \
the Poincar\\'e algebra, including\nnonabelian ones, whose $r$ matrices are \
unimodular. This includes particular\nLie-algebraic and quadratic \
noncommutative structures. We prove a planar\nequivalence theorem for all \
such noncommutative field theories, and discuss how\nour actions realize \
twisted Poincar\\'e symmetry, as well as twisted conformal\nand twisted \
supersymmetry, when applicable. Finally, we consider noncommutative\nversions \
of maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory, conjectured to be\nAdS/CFT \
dual to certain integrable deformations of the AdS$_5\\times$S$^5$\n\
superstring.\n", 
