            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2305.16046\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Miao He\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Miao He, Yunfeng Jiang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable Crosscap States: From Spin Chains to 1D Bose \
Gas\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"38 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP08(2023)079\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2023)079\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The notion of a crosscap state, a special conformal \
boundary state first\\ndefined in 2d CFT, was recently generalized to 2d \
massive integrable quantum\\nfield theories and integrable spin chains. It \
has been shown that the crosscap\\nstates preserve integrability. In this \
work, we first generalize this notion to\\nthe Lieb-Liniger model, which is a \
prototype of integrable non-relativistic\\nmany-body systems. We then show \
that the defined crosscap state preserves\\nintegrability. We derive the \
exact overlap formula of the crosscap state and\\nthe on-shell Bethe states. \
As a byproduct, we prove the conjectured overlap\\nformula for integrable \
spin chains rigorously by coordinate Bethe ansatz. It\\nturns out that the \
overlap formula for both models take the same form as a\\nratio of \
Gaudin-like determinants with a trivial prefactor. Finally we study\\nquench \
dynamics of the crosscap state, which turns out to be surprisingly\\nsimple. \
The stationary density distribution is simply a constant. We also\\nderive \
the analytic formula for dynamical correlation functions in \
the\\nTonks-Girardeau limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 25 May 2023 13:23:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-01-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"He\"", ",", "\"Miao\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Jiang\"", ",", "\"Yunfeng\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
