            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2305.16046", "submitter" -> "Miao He", "authors" -> 
            "Miao He, Yunfeng Jiang", "title" -> 
            "Integrable Crosscap States: From Spin Chains to 1D Bose Gas", 
            "comments" -> "38 pages", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP08(2023)079", 
            "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2023)079", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The notion of a crosscap state, a special conformal boundary \
state first\ndefined in 2d CFT, was recently generalized to 2d massive \
integrable quantum\nfield theories and integrable spin chains. It has been \
shown that the crosscap\nstates preserve integrability. In this work, we \
first generalize this notion to\nthe Lieb-Liniger model, which is a prototype \
of integrable non-relativistic\nmany-body systems. We then show that the \
defined crosscap state preserves\nintegrability. We derive the exact overlap \
formula of the crosscap state and\nthe on-shell Bethe states. As a byproduct, \
we prove the conjectured overlap\nformula for integrable spin chains \
rigorously by coordinate Bethe ansatz. It\nturns out that the overlap formula \
for both models take the same form as a\nratio of Gaudin-like determinants \
with a trivial prefactor. Finally we study\nquench dynamics of the crosscap \
state, which turns out to be surprisingly\nsimple. The stationary density \
distribution is simply a constant. We also\nderive the analytic formula for \
dynamical correlation functions in the\nTonks-Girardeau limit.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 25 May 2023 13:23:41 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-01-19", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"He", "Miao", ""}, {
              "Jiang", "Yunfeng", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
