superstring sigma\nmodel with fermions and bosons subject to twisted boundary \
conditions to find\nthe ground state energy in the semi-classical \
approximation where effective\nstring tension $h$ and the light-cone momentum \
$L$ are sent to infinity in such\na way that ${\\cal J}\\equiv L/h$ is kept \
fixed. We then analyse the ground state\nenergy of the model by means of the \
mirror TBA equations for the $AdS_{3}\\times\nS^{3}\\times T^{4}$ superstring \
in the pure RR background. The calculation is\nperformed for small twist \
$\\mu$ with $L$ and $h$ fixed, for large $L$ with\n$\\mu$ and $h$ fixed, and \
for small $h$ with $\\mu$ and $L$ fixed. In these\nlimits the contribution of \
the gapless worldsheet modes coming from the $T^4$\nbosons and fermions can \
be computed exactly, and is shown to be proportional to\n$hL/(4L^2-1)$. \
Comparison with the semi-classical result shows that the TBA\nequations \
