               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ramon Miravitllas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marcos Marino, Ramon Miravitllas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Large N instantons from topological strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"31 pages, added comments about the Fermi gas\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SciPost Phys. 16, 155 (2024)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.21468/SciPostPhys.16.6.155\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The $1/N$ expansion of matrix models is asymptotic, and \
it requires\\nnon-perturbative corrections due to large $N$ instantons. \
Explicit expressions\\nfor large $N$ instanton amplitudes are known in the \
case of Hermitian matrix\\nmodels with one cut, but not in the multi-cut \
case. We show that the recent\\nexact results on topological string instanton \
amplitudes provide the\\nnon-perturbative contributions of large $N$ \
instantons in generic multi-cut,\\nHermitian matrix models. We present a \
detailed test in the case of the cubic\\nmatrix model by considering the \
asymptotics of its $1/N$ expansion, which we\\nobtain at relatively high \
genus for a generic two-cut background. These results\\ncan be extended to \
certain non-conventional matrix models which admit a\\ntopological string \
theory description. As an application, we determine the\\nlarge $N$ instanton \
corrections for the free energy of ABJM theory on the\\nthree-sphere, which \
correspond to D-brane instanton corrections in superstring\\ntheory. We also \
illustrate the applications of topological string instantons in\\na more \
mathematical setting by considering orbifold Gromov-Witten invariants.\\nBy \
focusing on the example of $\\\\mathbb{C}^3/\\\\mathbb{Z}_3$, we show that \
they\\ngrow doubly-factorially with the genus and we obtain and test explicit\
\\nasymptotic formulae for them.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
