           "id" -> "2306.01104", "submitter" -> "Ramon Miravitllas", 
            "authors" -> "Marcos Marino, Ramon Miravitllas", "title" -> 
            "Large N instantons from topological strings", "comments" -> 
            "31 pages, added comments about the Fermi gas", "journal-ref" -> 
            "SciPost Phys. 16, 155 (2024)", "doi" -> 
            "10.21468/SciPostPhys.16.6.155", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The $1/N$ expansion of matrix models is asymptotic, and it \
requires\nnon-perturbative corrections due to large $N$ instantons. Explicit \
expressions\nfor large $N$ instanton amplitudes are known in the case of \
Hermitian matrix\nmodels with one cut, but not in the multi-cut case. We show \
that the recent\nexact results on topological string instanton amplitudes \
provide the\nnon-perturbative contributions of large $N$ instantons in \
generic multi-cut,\nHermitian matrix models. We present a detailed test in \
the case of the cubic\nmatrix model by considering the asymptotics of its \
$1/N$ expansion, which we\nobtain at relatively high genus for a generic \
two-cut background. These results\ncan be extended to certain \
non-conventional matrix models which admit a\ntopological string theory \
description. As an application, we determine the\nlarge $N$ instanton \
corrections for the free energy of ABJM theory on the\nthree-sphere, which \
correspond to D-brane instanton corrections in superstring\ntheory. We also \
illustrate the applications of topological string instantons in\na more \
mathematical setting by considering orbifold Gromov-Witten invariants.\nBy \
focusing on the example of $\\mathbb{C}^3/\\mathbb{Z}_3$, we show that they\n\
grow doubly-factorially with the genus and we obtain and test explicit\n\
asymptotic formulae for them.\n", 
