               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Beccaria, Arkady A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Comments on ABJM free energy on $S^{3}$ at large $N$ and \
perturbative\\n  expansions in M-theory and string theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"24 pages. v3: comments added in Appendix B\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2023.116286\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-AT-2023-03\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compare large $N$ expansion of the localization \
result for the free energy\\n$F$ in the 3d $\\\\mathcal{N}=6$ superconformal \
$U(N)_k \\\\times U(N)_{-k}$\\nChern-Simons-matter theory to its AdS/CFT \
counterpart, i.e. to the perturbative\\nexpansion of M-theory partition \
function on AdS$_{4}\\\\times\\nS^{7}/\\\\mathbb{Z}_{k}$ and to the weak \
string coupling expansion of type IIA\\neffective action on AdS$_{4}\\\\times \
{\\\\rm CP}^3$. We show that the general form\\nof the perturbative \
expansions of $F$ on the two sides of the AdS/CFT duality\\nis indeed the \
same. Moreover, the transcendentality properties of the\\ncoefficients in the \
large $N$, large $k$ expansion of $F$ match those in the\\ncorresponding \
M-theory or string theory expansions. To shed light on the\\nstructure of the \
1-loop M-theory partition function on \
AdS$_{4}\\\\times\\nS^{7}/\\\\mathbb{Z}_{k}$ we use the expression for the \
1-loop 4-graviton\\nscattering amplitude in the 11d supergravity. We also use \
the known information\\nabout the transcendental coefficients of the leading \
curvature invariants in\\nthe low-energy effective action of type II string \
theory. Matching of the\\nremaining rational factors in the coefficients \
requires a precise information\\nabout currently unknown RR field strength \
terms in the corresponding\\nsuperinvariants.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
