            "Imperial-TP-AT-2023-03", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We compare large $N$ expansion of the localization result for \
the free energy\n$F$ in the 3d $\\mathcal{N}=6$ superconformal $U(N)_k \
\\times U(N)_{-k}$\nChern-Simons-matter theory to its AdS/CFT counterpart, \
i.e. to the perturbative\nexpansion of M-theory partition function on \
AdS$_{4}\\times\nS^{7}/\\mathbb{Z}_{k}$ and to the weak string coupling \
expansion of type IIA\neffective action on AdS$_{4}\\times {\\rm CP}^3$. We \
show that the general form\nof the perturbative expansions of $F$ on the two \
sides of the AdS/CFT duality\nis indeed the same. Moreover, the \
transcendentality properties of the\ncoefficients in the large $N$, large $k$ \
expansion of $F$ match those in the\ncorresponding M-theory or string theory \
expansions. To shed light on the\nstructure of the 1-loop M-theory partition \
function on AdS$_{4}\\times\nS^{7}/\\mathbb{Z}_{k}$ we use the expression for \
the 1-loop 4-graviton\nscattering amplitude in the 11d supergravity. We also \
use the known information\nabout the transcendental coefficients of the \
leading curvature invariants in\nthe low-energy effective action of type II \
string theory. Matching of the\nremaining rational factors in the \
coefficients requires a precise information\nabout currently unknown RR field \
strength terms in the corresponding\nsuperinvariants.\n", 
