                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that supersymmetric supergravity solutions with \
an R-symmetry Killing\\nvector are equipped with a set of equivariantly \
closed forms. Various physical\\nobservables may be expressed as integrals of \
these forms, and then evaluated\\nusing the Berline-Vergne-Atiyah-Bott fixed \
point theorem. We illustrate with a\\nvariety of holographic examples, \
including on-shell actions, black hole\\nentropies, central charges, and \
scaling dimensions of operators. The resulting\\nexpressions depend only on \
topological data and the R-symmetry vector, and\\nhence may be evaluated \
without solving the supergravity equations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
