 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Building on the recent discovery of the first candidate \
black hole operator\\nin $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ super-Yang-Mills, we explore the \
near-supersymmetric aspects\\nof the theory that capture lightly excited, \
highly stringy black holes. We\\nextend the superspace formalism describing \
the classically supersymmetric\\n(1/16-BPS) sector of $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
super-Yang-Mills and compute a large\\nnumber of one-loop anomalous \
dimensions. Despite being in the highly stringy\\nregime, we find hints of a \
gap in the spectrum, similar to that found by a\\ngravitational path \
integral. We also determine the actual expression of the\\nfirst candidate \
black hole operator at weak gauge coupling, going beyond the\\ncohomological \
construction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
