               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2306.06966\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Michele Caselle\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Alberto Baffigo and Michele Caselle\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ising string beyond Nambu-Goto\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"27 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Physical Review D 109, 034520 (2024)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.109.034520\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-lat cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A major result of the Effective String Theory (EST) \
description of\\nconfinement is the so called \\\"low energy \
universality,\\\" which states that the\\nfirst few terms of the large \
distance expansion of any EST are universal and\\ncoincide with those of the \
Nambu-Goto action. Going beyond this approximation\\nis one of the most \
interesting open problems in the EST. In the higher order\\nterms beyond \
Nambu-Goto several important pieces of physical information are\\nencoded, \
which could improve our understanding of the physical mechanisms\\nbehind \
confinement and of the physical degrees of freedoms which originate \
the\\nEST. In this paper we evaluate numerically the first two of these \
corrections\\nin the case of the three dimensional gauge Ising model. The \
first of them turns\\nout to be negative: $\\\\gamma_3=-0.00048(4)$, similar \
(but not equal) to the one\\nrecently measured in the $SU(2)$ Yang Mills \
theory in three dimensions and\\ncompatible with the bootstrap bound \
$\\\\gamma_3 \\\\geq -\\\\frac{1}{768}$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 12 Jun 2023 08:53:09 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-03-05\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
