               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ronald Reid-Edwards\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"N. M. McStay and R. A. Reid-Edwards\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Symmetries and Covering Maps for the Minimal Tension \
String on\\n  $\\\\mathbf{AdS_3\\\\times S^3\\\\times T^4}$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"63 pages, 8 figures. Published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 04 (2024) 048\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP04(2024)048\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This paper considers a recently-proposed string theory \
on $AdS_3\\\\times\\nS^3\\\\times T^4$ with one unit of NS-NS flux ($k=1$). \
We discuss interpretations\\nof the target space, including connections to \
twistor geometry and a more\\nconventional spacetime interpretation via the \
Wakimoto representation. We\\npropose an alternative perspective on the role \
of the Wakimoto formalism in the\\n$k=1$ string, for which no large radius \
limit is required by the inclusion of\\nextra operator insertions in the path \
integral. This provides an exact Wakimoto\\ndescription of the worldsheet \
CFT. We also discuss an additional local\\nworldsheet symmetry, $Q(z)$, that \
emerges when $k=1$ and show that this\\nsymmetry plays an important role in \
the localisation of the path integral to a\\nsum over covering maps. We \
demonstrate the emergence of a rigid worldsheet\\ntranslation symmetry in the \
radial direction of the $AdS_3$, for which again\\nthe presence of $Q(z)$ is \
crucial. We conjecture that this radial symmetry\\nplays a key role in \
understanding, in the case of the $k=1$ string, the\\nencoding of the bulk \
physics on the two-dimensional boundary.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
