               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2307.06841\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shubham Kumar Sinha\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Shiroman Prakash and Shubham Kumar Sinha\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Emergent Supersymmetry at Large $N$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"80 pages, 19 figures. v2: fixed typos and added \
references; v3:\\n  accepted for publication in JHEP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP01(2024)025\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th cond-mat.str-el\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We search for infrared fixed points of Gross-Neveu \
Yukawa models with matrix\\ndegrees of freedom in $d=4-\\\\varepsilon$. We \
consider three models -- a model\\nwith $SU(N)$ symmetry in which the scalar \
and fermionic fields both transform\\nin the adjoint representation, a model \
with $SO(N)$ symmetry in which the\\nscalar and fermion fields both transform \
as real symmetric-traceless matrices,\\nand a model with $SO(N)$ symmetry in \
which the scalar field transforms as a\\nreal symmetric-traceless matrix, \
while the fermion transforms in the adjoint\\nrepresentation. These models \
differ at finite $N$, but their large-$N$ limits\\nare perturbatively \
equivalent. The first two models contain a supersymmetric\\nfixed point for \
all $N$, which is attractive to all classically-marginal\\ndeformations for \
$N$ sufficiently large. The third model possesses a stable\\nfixed point \
that, although non-supersymmetric, gives rise to many correlation\\nfunctions \
that are identical to those of a supersymmetric fixed point when $N$\\nis \
sufficiently large. We also find several non-supersymmetric fixed points \
at\\nfinite and large-$N$. Planar diagrams dominate the large-$N$ limit of \
these\\nfixed points, which suggests the possibility of a stringy holographic \
dual\\ndescription.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 13 Jul 2023 16:05:40 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 8 Sep 2023 07:48:31 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 21 Dec 2023 06:32:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-01-15\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Prakash\"", ",", "\"Shiroman\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Sinha\"", ",", "\"Shubham Kumar\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
