 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We introduce the topologically twisted index for \
four-dimensional $\\\\mathcal\\nN=1$ gauge theories quantized on ${\\\\rm \
AdS}_2 \\\\times S^1$. We compute the index\\nby applying supersymmetric \
localization to partition functions of vector and\\nchiral multiplets on ${\\\
\\rm AdS}_2 \\\\times T^2$, with and without a boundary: in\\nboth instances \
we classify normalizability and boundary conditions for gauge,\\nmatter and \
ghost fields. The index is twisted as the dynamical fields are\\ncoupled to a \
R-symmetry background 1-form with non-trivial exterior derivative\\nand \
proportional to the spin connection. After regularization the index \
is\\nwritten in terms of elliptic gamma functions, reminiscent of \
four-dimensional\\nholomorphic blocks, and crucially depends on the R-charge.\
\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
