                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study integrability and non-integrability for \
marginal deformations of 4d\\n$\\\\mathcal N =2$ SCFTs. We estimate various \
chaos indicators for the bulk theory\\nwhich clearly shows the onset of a \
chaotic string dynamics in the limit of\\nlarge deformations. On the other \
hand, for small values of the deformation\\nparameter, the resulting dynamics \
exhibits a non-chaotic motion and therefore\\npresumably an underlying \
integrable structure. Our analysis reveals that the\\n$\\\\gamma$-deformation \
in the type-IIA theory could be interpreted as an\\ninterpolation between a \
class of integrable $\\\\mathcal N =2$ SCFTs and a class\\nof non-integrable \
$\\\\mathcal N =1$ SCFTs at strong coupling. We also generalise\\nour results \
in the presence of the flavor branes.\\n\""}]}, {
