Gangopadhyay\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mixed state entanglement measures for the dipole deformed \
supersymmetric\\n  Yang-Mills theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"23 pages Latex,7 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Annals of Physics 460(2024)169565\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Two different entanglement measures for mixed states, \
namely, the\\nentanglement of purification and entanglement negativity has \
been\\nholographically computed for the dipole deformed supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills\\n(SYM) theory by considering its gravity dual. The dipole \
deformation induces\\nnon-locality in the SYM theory which is characterized \
by a length-scale\\n$a=\\\\lambda^{\\\\frac{1}{2}}\\\\tilde{L}$. Considering \
a strip like subsystem of\\nlength $\\\\frac{l}{a}$ (in dimensionless form), \
we first analytically calculate\\nthe holographic entanglement entropy for \
and compare the obtained results with\\nthat of obtained numerically.~The \
analytical calculations have been carried out\\nby considering $au_t \\\\leq \
1$,~$1\\\\leq au_t < au_b$ and $au_t\\\\sim au_b$, where\\n$au_b$ is the UV \
cut-off. The choice of these regions enable us to identify the\\nexpansion \
parameters needed to carry out binomial expansions. The \
entanglement\\nmeasures expectedly displays a smooth behaviour with respect \
to the subsystem\\nsize as the geometry has a smooth transition between the \
mentioned regions.\\nUsing these results, the holographic mutual information \
is then computed for\\ntwo disjoint subsystems $A$ and $B$. Based upon the \
$E_{P}=E_{W}$ duality, the\\nentanglement of purification ($E_{P}$) is then \
computed and the effects of\\ndipole deformation in this context have been \
studied. Finally, we proceed to\\ncompute entanglement negativity for this \
theory and compare the obtained result\\nwith that of the standard SYM theory \
in order to get a better understanding\\nabout the effects of the \
non-locality.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
