            "Anirban Roy Chowdhury, Ashis Saha, Sunandan Gangopadhyay", 
            "title" -> 
            "Mixed state entanglement measures for the dipole deformed \
supersymmetric\n  Yang-Mills theory", "comments" -> 
            "23 pages Latex,7 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Annals of Physics 460(2024)169565", "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Two different entanglement measures for mixed states, namely, \
the\nentanglement of purification and entanglement negativity has been\n\
holographically computed for the dipole deformed supersymmetric Yang-Mills\n\
(SYM) theory by considering its gravity dual. The dipole deformation induces\n\
non-locality in the SYM theory which is characterized by a length-scale\n\
$a=\\lambda^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\tilde{L}$. Considering a strip like subsystem of\n\
length $\\frac{l}{a}$ (in dimensionless form), we first analytically \
calculate\nthe holographic entanglement entropy for and compare the obtained \
results with\nthat of obtained numerically.~The analytical calculations have \
been carried out\nby considering $au_t \\leq 1$,~$1\\leq au_t < au_b$ and \
$au_t\\sim au_b$, where\n$au_b$ is the UV cut-off. The choice of these \
regions enable us to identify the\nexpansion parameters needed to carry out \
binomial expansions. The entanglement\nmeasures expectedly displays a smooth \
behaviour with respect to the subsystem\nsize as the geometry has a smooth \
transition between the mentioned regions.\nUsing these results, the \
holographic mutual information is then computed for\ntwo disjoint subsystems \
$A$ and $B$. Based upon the $E_{P}=E_{W}$ duality, the\nentanglement of \
purification ($E_{P}$) is then computed and the effects of\ndipole \
deformation in this context have been studied. Finally, we proceed to\n\
compute entanglement negativity for this theory and compare the obtained \
result\nwith that of the standard SYM theory in order to get a better \
understanding\nabout the effects of the non-locality.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
