               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matteo Beccaria\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Beccaria, Simone Giombi, Arkady A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Instanton contributions to the ABJM free energy from \
quantum M2 branes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"27 pages. v2: comments added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PUPT-2645, Imperial-TP-AT-2023-04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a quantum M2 brane computation of the \
instanton prefactor in the\\nleading non-perturbative contribution to the \
ABJM 3-sphere free energy at large\\n$N$ and fixed level $k$. Using \
supersymmetric localization, such instanton\\ncontribution was found earlier \
to take the form $F^{\\\\rm inst}(N,k) = -\\n({\\\\sin^{2} \
\\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{k}} )^{-1} \\\\, \\\\exp (-2\\\\pi \\\\sqrt\\\\frac{2N}{k}) \
+ \\\\cdots$ .\\nThe exponent comes from the action of an M2 brane instanton \
wrapped on\\n$S^3/{\\\\mathbb Z}_k$, which represents the M-theory uplift of \
the\\n$\\\\mathbb{C}P^1$ instanton in type IIA string theory on AdS$_4 \
\\\\times\\n\\\\mathbb{C}P^3$. The IIA string computation of the leading \
large $k$ term in the\\ninstanton prefactor was recently performed in \
arXiv:2304.12340. Here we find\\nthat the exact value of the prefactor \
$({\\\\sin^{2} \\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{k}})^{-1} $ is\\nreproduced by the 1-loop \
term in the M2 brane partition function expanded near\\nthe \
$S^3/\\\\mathbb{Z}_k$ instanton configuration. As in the Wilson loop \
example\\nin arXiv:2303.15207, the quantum M2 brane computation is well \
defined and\\nproduces a finite result in exact agreement with \
localization.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
