          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2307.14112", "submitter" -> "Matteo Beccaria", "authors" -> 
            "Matteo Beccaria, Simone Giombi, Arkady A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Instanton contributions to the ABJM free energy from quantum M2 \
branes", "comments" -> "27 pages. v2: comments added", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> "PUPT-2645, Imperial-TP-AT-2023-04",
             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a quantum M2 brane computation of the instanton \
prefactor in the\nleading non-perturbative contribution to the ABJM 3-sphere \
free energy at large\n$N$ and fixed level $k$. Using supersymmetric \
localization, such instanton\ncontribution was found earlier to take the form \
$F^{\\rm inst}(N,k) = -\n({\\sin^{2} \\frac{2\\pi}{k}} )^{-1} \\, \\exp \
(-2\\pi \\sqrt\\frac{2N}{k}) + \\cdots$ .\nThe exponent comes from the action \
of an M2 brane instanton wrapped on\n$S^3/{\\mathbb Z}_k$, which represents \
the M-theory uplift of the\n$\\mathbb{C}P^1$ instanton in type IIA string \
theory on AdS$_4 \\times\n\\mathbb{C}P^3$. The IIA string computation of the \
leading large $k$ term in the\ninstanton prefactor was recently performed in \
arXiv:2304.12340. Here we find\nthat the exact value of the prefactor \
$({\\sin^{2} \\frac{2\\pi}{k}})^{-1} $ is\nreproduced by the 1-loop term in \
the M2 brane partition function expanded near\nthe $S^3/\\mathbb{Z}_k$ \
instanton configuration. As in the Wilson loop example\nin arXiv:2303.15207, \
the quantum M2 brane computation is well defined and\nproduces a finite \
result in exact agreement with localization.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 26 Jul 2023 11:15:28 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 24 Sep 2023 13:23:52 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-09-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Beccaria", "Matteo", ""}, {
              "Giombi", "Simone", ""}, {"Tseytlin", "Arkady A.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{12.244385337249515`, -6.0754816244166}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2308.03848\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alessandro Pini\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Alessandro Pini, Paolo Vallarino\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wilson loop correlators at strong coupling in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ quiver\\n  gauge theories\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 11 (2023) 003\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP11(2023)003\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider 4-dimensional $\\\\mathcal{N} = 2$ \
superconformal quiver theories\\nwith $SU(N)^M$ gauge group and \
bi-fundamental matter and we evaluate\\ncorrelation functions of $n$ \
coincident Wilson loops in the planar limit of the\\ntheory. Exploiting \
specific untwisted/twisted combinations of these operators\\nand using \
supersymmetric localization, we are able to resum the whole\\nperturbative \
expansion and find exact expressions for these correlators that\\nare valid \
for all values of the 't Hooft coupling. Moreover, we analytically\\nderive \
the leading strong coupling behaviour of the correlators, showing that\\nthey \
obey a remarkable simple rule. Our analysis is complemented by \
numerical\\nchecks based on a Pad\\\\'e resummation of the perturbative \
series.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
