                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We use holography in conjunction with recent results \
from supersymmetric\\nlocalization to compute certain thermal observables for \
3d $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$\\nholographic SCFTs arising on the worldvolume of $N$ \
M2-branes. We obtain\\nresults for the thermal free energy density on $S^1 \\\
\\times \\\\mathbb{R}^2$, the\\nCasimir energy on $T^{2} \\\\times \
\\\\mathbb{R}$, and the three leading coefficients\\nin the large temperature \
limit of the free energy on $S^1\\\\times S^2$ valid to\\nsubleading order in \
the large $N$ limit. As a byproduct of our holographic\\nanalysis we also \
present a conjecture for the structure of the large\\ntemperature expansion \
of the thermal free energy of general 3d CFTs on\\n$S^1\\\\times \
S^2$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
