               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2310.08545\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Go Noshita\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Taro Kimura and Go Noshita\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gauge origami and quiver W-algebras\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"149+36 pages, v2: fixed typos and added references, \
published version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2024)208\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP math.QA math.RT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore the quantum algebraic formalism of the gauge \
origami system in\\n$\\\\mathbb{C}^{4}$, where D2/D4/D6/D8-branes are \
present. We demonstrate that the\\ncontour integral formulas have free field \
interpretations, leading to the\\noperator formalism of $qq$-characters \
associated with each D-brane. The\\n$qq$-characters of D2 and D4-branes \
correspond to screening charges and\\ngenerators of the affine quiver \
W-algebra, respectively. On the other hand, the\\n$qq$-characters of D6 and \
D8-branes represent novel types of $qq$-characters,\\nwhere monomial terms \
are characterized by plane partitions and solid\\npartitions. The composition \
of these $qq$-characters yields the instanton\\npartition functions of the \
gauge origami system, eventually establishing the\\nBPS/CFT \
correspondence.\\n  Additionally, we demonstrate that the fusion of \
$qq$-characters of D-branes\\nin lower dimensions results in \
higher-dimensional D-brane $qq$-characters. We\\nalso investigate quadratic \
relations among these $qq$-characters. Furthermore,\\nwe explore the \
relationship with the representations, $q$-characters, and the\\nBethe ansatz \
equations of the quantum toroidal $\\\\mathfrak{gl}_{1}$. This\\nconnection \
provides insights into the Bethe/Gauge correspondence of the gauge\\norigami \
system from both gauge-theoretic and quantum-algebraic perspectives.\\n  We \
finally present conjectures regarding generalizations to general \
toric\\nCalabi-Yau four-folds. These generalizations imply the existence of \
an\\nextensive class of $qq$-characters, which we call BPS $qq$-characters. \
These\\nBPS $qq$-characters offer a new systematic approach to derive a \
broader range\\nof BPS/CFT correspondence and Bethe/Gauge \
correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 12 Oct 2023 17:39:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 May 2024 12:13:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-05-24\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kimura\"", ",", "\"Taro\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
