           "id" -> "2310.08545", "submitter" -> "Go Noshita", "authors" -> 
            "Taro Kimura and Go Noshita", "title" -> 
            "Gauge origami and quiver W-algebras", "comments" -> 
            "149+36 pages, v2: fixed typos and added references, published \
version", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP05(2024)208", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP math.QA math.RT", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We explore the quantum algebraic formalism of the gauge \
origami system in\n$\\mathbb{C}^{4}$, where D2/D4/D6/D8-branes are present. \
We demonstrate that the\ncontour integral formulas have free field \
interpretations, leading to the\noperator formalism of $qq$-characters \
associated with each D-brane. The\n$qq$-characters of D2 and D4-branes \
correspond to screening charges and\ngenerators of the affine quiver \
W-algebra, respectively. On the other hand, the\n$qq$-characters of D6 and \
D8-branes represent novel types of $qq$-characters,\nwhere monomial terms are \
characterized by plane partitions and solid\npartitions. The composition of \
these $qq$-characters yields the instanton\npartition functions of the gauge \
origami system, eventually establishing the\nBPS/CFT correspondence.\n  \
Additionally, we demonstrate that the fusion of $qq$-characters of D-branes\n\
in lower dimensions results in higher-dimensional D-brane $qq$-characters. We\
\nalso investigate quadratic relations among these $qq$-characters. \
Furthermore,\nwe explore the relationship with the representations, \
$q$-characters, and the\nBethe ansatz equations of the quantum toroidal \
$\\mathfrak{gl}_{1}$. This\nconnection provides insights into the Bethe/Gauge \
correspondence of the gauge\norigami system from both gauge-theoretic and \
quantum-algebraic perspectives.\n  We finally present conjectures regarding \
generalizations to general toric\nCalabi-Yau four-folds. These \
generalizations imply the existence of an\nextensive class of \
$qq$-characters, which we call BPS $qq$-characters. These\nBPS \
$qq$-characters offer a new systematic approach to derive a broader range\nof \
BPS/CFT correspondence and Bethe/Gauge correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 12 Oct 2023 17:39:55 GMT"}, {
