               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrability and non-integrability for holographic dual \
of Matrix model\\n  and non-Abelian T-dual of AdS$_5\\\\times$S$^5$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+23 pages; 15 Figs; Major revision; v3; Accepted to \
Nucl. Phys. B\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl. Phys. B 1004 (2024) 116570\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2024.116570\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we study integrability and \
non-integrability for type-IIA\\nsupergravity background dual to deformed \
plane wave matrix model. From the bulk\\nperspective, we estimate various \
chaos indicators that clearly shows chaotic\\nstring dynamics in the limit of \
small value of the parameter $L$ present in the\\ntheory. On the other hand, \
the string dynamics exhibits a non-chaotic motion\\nfor the large value of \
the parameter $L$ and therefore presumably an underlying\\nintegrable \
structure. Our findings reveals that the parameter $L$ in the\\ntype-IIA \
background acts as an interpolation between a non-integrable theory to\\nan \
integrable theory in dual SCFTs.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
