            "  In this paper we study integrability and non-integrability for \
type-IIA\nsupergravity background dual to deformed plane wave matrix model. \
From the bulk\nperspective, we estimate various chaos indicators that clearly \
shows chaotic\nstring dynamics in the limit of small value of the parameter \
$L$ present in the\ntheory. On the other hand, the string dynamics exhibits a \
non-chaotic motion\nfor the large value of the parameter $L$ and therefore \
presumably an underlying\nintegrable structure. Our findings reveals that the \
parameter $L$ in the\ntype-IIA background acts as an interpolation between a \
non-integrable theory to\nan integrable theory in dual SCFTs.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
