            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2310.12322\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shai Chester\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Luis F. Alday, Shai M. Chester, Daniele Dorigoni, Michael \
B. Green,\\n  and Congkao Wen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Relations between integrated correlators in \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$\\n  Supersymmetric Yang--Mills Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages plus appendices, 8 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"QMUL-PH-23-20\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Integrated correlation functions in $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
supersymmetric\\nYang--Mills theory with gauge group $SU(N)$ can be expressed \
in terms of the\\nlocalised $S^4$ partition function, $Z_N$, deformed by a \
mass $m$. Two such\\ncases are $\\\\mathcal{C}_N=(\\\\text{Im} \\\\tau)^2 \
\\\\partial_\\\\tau\\\\partial_{\\\\bar\\\\tau}\\n\\\\partial_m^2\\\\log \
Z_N\\\\vert_{m=0}$ and \
$\\\\mathcal{H}_N=\\\\partial_m^4\\\\log\\nZ_N\\\\vert_{m=0}$, which are \
modular invariant functions of the complex coupling\\n$\\\\tau$. While \
$\\\\mathcal{C}_N$ was recently written in terms of a\\ntwo-dimensional \
lattice sum for any $N$ and $\\\\tau$, $\\\\mathcal{H}_N$ has only\\nbeen \
evaluated up to order $1/N^3$ in a large-$N$ expansion in terms of \
modular\\ninvariant functions with no known lattice sum realisation. Here we \
develop\\nmethods for evaluating $\\\\mathcal{H}_N$ to any desired order in \
$1/N$ and finite\\n$\\\\tau$. We use this new data to constrain higher loop \
corrections to the stress\\ntensor correlator, and give evidence for several \
intriguing relations between\\n$\\\\mathcal{H}_N$ and $\\\\mathcal{C}_N$ to \
all orders in $1/N$. We also give\\nevidence that the coefficients of the \
$1/N$ expansion of $\\\\mathcal{H}_N$ can be\\nwritten as lattice sums to all \
orders. Lastly, these large $N$ and finite\\n$\\\\tau$ results are used to \
accurately estimate the integrated correlators at\\nfinite $N$ and finite $\\\
\\tau$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 18 Oct 2023 20:45:03 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
