         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2310.12322", "submitter" -> "Shai Chester", "authors" -> 
            "Luis F. Alday, Shai M. Chester, Daniele Dorigoni, Michael B. \
Green,\n  and Congkao Wen", "title" -> 
            "Relations between integrated correlators in $\\mathcal{N}=4$\n  \
Supersymmetric Yang--Mills Theory", "comments" -> 
            "30 pages plus appendices, 8 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> "QMUL-PH-23-20", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  Integrated correlation functions in $\\mathcal{N}=4$ \
supersymmetric\nYang--Mills theory with gauge group $SU(N)$ can be expressed \
in terms of the\nlocalised $S^4$ partition function, $Z_N$, deformed by a \
mass $m$. Two such\ncases are $\\mathcal{C}_N=(\\text{Im} \\tau)^2 \\partial_\
\\tau\\partial_{\\bar\\tau}\n\\partial_m^2\\log Z_N\\vert_{m=0}$ and \
$\\mathcal{H}_N=\\partial_m^4\\log\nZ_N\\vert_{m=0}$, which are modular \
invariant functions of the complex coupling\n$\\tau$. While $\\mathcal{C}_N$ \
was recently written in terms of a\ntwo-dimensional lattice sum for any $N$ \
and $\\tau$, $\\mathcal{H}_N$ has only\nbeen evaluated up to order $1/N^3$ in \
a large-$N$ expansion in terms of modular\ninvariant functions with no known \
lattice sum realisation. Here we develop\nmethods for evaluating \
$\\mathcal{H}_N$ to any desired order in $1/N$ and finite\n$\\tau$. We use \
this new data to constrain higher loop corrections to the stress\ntensor \
correlator, and give evidence for several intriguing relations between\n\
$\\mathcal{H}_N$ and $\\mathcal{C}_N$ to all orders in $1/N$. We also give\n\
evidence that the coefficients of the $1/N$ expansion of $\\mathcal{H}_N$ can \
be\nwritten as lattice sums to all orders. Lastly, these large $N$ and finite\
\n$\\tau$ results are used to accurately estimate the integrated correlators \
at\nfinite $N$ and finite $\\tau$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 18 Oct 2023 20:45:03 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2023-10-20", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Alday", "Luis F.", ""}, {
