                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Quiver theories constitute an important class of \
supersymmetric gauge\\ntheories with well-defined holographic duals. \
Motivated by holographic duality,\\nwe use localisation on $S^d$ to study \
long linear quivers at large-N. The\\nlarge-N solution shows a remarkable \
degree of universality across dimensions,\\nincluding $d = 4$ where quivers \
are genuinely superconformal. In that case we\\nupgrade the solution of long \
quivers to quivers of any length.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
