 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We combine supersymmetric localization with the \
numerical conformal bootstrap\\nto bound the scaling dimension and OPE \
coefficient of the lowest-dimension\\noperator in $\\\\mathcal{N} = 4$ \
$\\\\text{SU}(N)$ super-Yang-Mills theory for a wide\\nrange of $N$ and \
Yang-Mills couplings $g_\\\\text{YM}$. We find that our bounds\\nare \
approximately saturated by weak coupling results at small \
$g_\\\\text{YM}$.\\nFurthermore, at large $N$ our bounds interpolate between \
integrability results\\nfor the Konishi operator at small $g_\\\\text{YM}$ \
and strong-coupling results,\\nincluding the first few stringy corrections, \
for the lowest-dimension\\ndouble-trace operator at large $g_\\\\text{YM}$. \
In particular, our scaling\\ndimension bounds describe the level splitting \
between the single- and\\ndouble-trace operators at intermediate coupling.\\n\
\""}]}, {
