               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ben Hoare, Ana L. Retore and Fiona K. Seibold\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Elliptic deformations of the $\\\\mathsf{AdS}_3 \\\\times \
\\\\mathsf{S}^3 \\\\times\\n  \\\\mathsf{T}^4$ string\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages; v2 minor comments added, matches published \
version\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial-TP-FS-2023-02\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  With the aim of investigating the existence of an \
integrable elliptic\\ndeformation of strings on $\\\\mathsf{AdS}_3 \\\\times \
\\\\mathsf{S}^3 \\\\times\\n\\\\mathsf{T}^4$, we compute the tree-level \
worldsheet S-matrix of the\\nelliptically-deformed bosonic sigma model on $\\\
\\mathsf{AdS}_3 \\\\times\\n\\\\mathsf{S}^3$ in uniform light-cone gauge. The \
resulting tree-level S-matrix is\\ncompatible with the integrability of the \
model and has interesting features,\\nincluding a hidden $\\\\mathsf{U}(1)$ \
symmetry not manifest in the Lagrangian. We\\nfind that it cannot be embedded \
in the known exact integrable R-matrices\\ndescribing deformations of the \
undeformed $\\\\mathsf{AdS}_3 \\\\times \\\\mathsf{S}^3\\n\\\\times \
\\\\mathsf{T}^4$ light-cone gauge S-matrix including fermions. \
Therefore,\\nwe construct embeddings of the deformed 6-d metric in type II \
supergravity with\\nconstant dilaton and homogeneous fluxes. The simplicity \
of these solutions\\nsuggests they are promising candidates to lead to an \
integrable string sigma\\nmodel including fermions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 21 Dec 2023 17:01:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 10 Apr 2024 07:43:51 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-04-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Hoare\"", ",", "\"Ben\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Retore\"", ",", "\"Ana L.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Seibold\"", ",", "\"Fiona K.\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
