         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2312.14031", "submitter" -> "Ben Hoare", "authors" -> 
            "Ben Hoare, Ana L. Retore and Fiona K. Seibold", "title" -> 
            "Elliptic deformations of the $\\mathsf{AdS}_3 \\times \
\\mathsf{S}^3 \\times\n  \\mathsf{T}^4$ string", "comments" -> 
            "28 pages; v2 minor comments added, matches published version", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-FS-2023-02", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  With the aim of investigating the existence of an integrable \
elliptic\ndeformation of strings on $\\mathsf{AdS}_3 \\times \\mathsf{S}^3 \
\\times\n\\mathsf{T}^4$, we compute the tree-level worldsheet S-matrix of the\
\nelliptically-deformed bosonic sigma model on $\\mathsf{AdS}_3 \\times\n\
\\mathsf{S}^3$ in uniform light-cone gauge. The resulting tree-level S-matrix \
is\ncompatible with the integrability of the model and has interesting \
features,\nincluding a hidden $\\mathsf{U}(1)$ symmetry not manifest in the \
Lagrangian. We\nfind that it cannot be embedded in the known exact integrable \
R-matrices\ndescribing deformations of the undeformed $\\mathsf{AdS}_3 \
\\times \\mathsf{S}^3\n\\times \\mathsf{T}^4$ light-cone gauge S-matrix \
including fermions. Therefore,\nwe construct embeddings of the deformed 6-d \
metric in type II supergravity with\nconstant dilaton and homogeneous fluxes. \
The simplicity of these solutions\nsuggests they are promising candidates to \
lead to an integrable string sigma\nmodel including fermions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
