               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-perturbative de Sitter Jackiw-Teitelboim \
gravity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35+10 pages, 4 figures; v2: references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  With non-perturbative de Sitter gravity and holography \
in mind, we deduce the\\ngenus expansion of de Sitter Jackiw-Teitelboim (dS \
JT) gravity. We find that\\nthis simple model of quantum cosmology has an \
effective string coupling which\\nis pure imaginary. This imaginary coupling \
gives rise to alternating signs in\\nthe genus expansion of the dS JT \
S-matrix, which as a result appears to be\\nBorel-Le Roy resummable. We \
explain how dS JT gravity is dual to a formal\\nmatrix integral with, in a \
sense, a negative number of degrees of freedom.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
