         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2401.01925", "submitter" -> "Jordan Cotler", "authors" -> 
            "Jordan Cotler, Kristan Jensen", "title" -> 
            "Non-perturbative de Sitter Jackiw-Teitelboim gravity", 
            "comments" -> "35+10 pages, 4 figures; v2: references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  With non-perturbative de Sitter gravity and holography in \
mind, we deduce the\ngenus expansion of de Sitter Jackiw-Teitelboim (dS JT) \
gravity. We find that\nthis simple model of quantum cosmology has an \
effective string coupling which\nis pure imaginary. This imaginary coupling \
gives rise to alternating signs in\nthe genus expansion of the dS JT \
S-matrix, which as a result appears to be\nBorel-Le Roy resummable. We \
explain how dS JT gravity is dual to a formal\nmatrix integral with, in a \
sense, a negative number of degrees of freedom.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 3 Jan 2024 19:00:00 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 26 Jan 2024 02:08:41 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-01-29", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Cotler", "Jordan", ""}, {
              "Jensen", "Kristan", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
