            "  We study the counting problem of BPS D-branes wrapping \
holomorphic cycles of\na general toric Calabi-Yau manifold. We evaluate the \
Jeffrey-Kirwan residues\nfor the flavoured Witten index for the \
supersymmetric quiver quantum mechanics\non the worldvolume of the D-branes, \
and find that BPS degeneracies are\ndescribed by a statistical mechanical \
model of crystal melting. For Calabi-Yau\nthreefolds, we reproduce the \
crystal melting models long known in the\nliterature. For Calabi-Yau \
fourfolds, however, we find that the crystal does\nnot contain the full \
information for the BPS degeneracy and we need to\nexplicitly evaluate \
non-trivial weights assigned to the crystal configurations.\nOur discussions \
treat Calabi-Yau threefolds and fourfolds on equal footing, and\ninclude \
discussions on elliptic and rational generalizations of the BPS states\n\
counting, connections to the mathematical definition of generalized\n\
Donaldson-Thomas invariants, examples of wall crossings, and of trialities in\
\nquiver gauge theories.\n", 
