 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  These lecture notes, adapted from the habilitation \
thesis of the author,\\nsurvey in a first part various exact results obtained \
in the past few decades\\nabout KPZ fluctuations in one dimension, with a \
special focus on finite volume\\neffects describing the relaxation to its \
stationary state of a finite system\\nstarting from a given initial \
condition. The second part is more specifically\\ndevoted to an approach \
allowing to express in a simple way the statistics of\\nthe current in the \
totally asymmetric simple exclusion process in terms of a\\ncontour integral \
on a compact Riemann surface, whose infinite genus limit leads\\nto KPZ \
fluctuations in finite volume.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
