, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We review a class of integrable, supersymmetric defect \
conformal field\\ntheories which have holographic duals in the form of probe \
brane models. Our\\nmain examples are defect versions of N=4 SYM and ABJM \
theory, both involving a\\ndomain wall with Nahm pole boundary conditions, \
and the case of a 't Hooft line\\nembedded in N=4 SYM. The field theory \
defect respectively the probe D-brane can\\nbe described as an integrable \
boundary state of the integrable system\\nunderlying the AdS/CFT \
correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
