               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Lagares\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mart\\\\'in Lagares, Shun-Qing Zhang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Higher-loop integrated negative geometries in ABJM\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"26 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"MPP-2024-37\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the three-dimensional ${\\\\cal N}=6$ Chern-Simons \
matter (ABJM) theory, the\\nintegrand for the logarithm of the scattering \
amplitude admits a decomposition\\nin terms of negative geometries, which \
implies that all the infrared\\ndivergences concentrate in the last loop \
integration. We compute the\\ninfrared-finite functions that arise from \
performing a three-loop integration\\nover the four-loop integrand for the \
logarithm of the four-point amplitude, for\\nwhich we use the method of \
differential equations. Our results provide a direct\\ncomputation of the \
four-loop cusp anomalous dimension of the theory, in\\nagreement with the \
current all-loop integrability-based proposal. We find an\\napparent \
simplicity in the leading singularities of the integrated results,\\nprovided \
one works in the frame in which the unintegrated loop variable goes \
to\\ninfinity. Finally, our results suggest an alternating sign pattern for \
the\\nintegrated negative geometries in the Euclidean region.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 27 Feb 2024 11:44:11 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-02-28\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
