           "id" -> "2402.17432", "submitter" -> "Martin Lagares", "authors" -> 
            "Mart\\'in Lagares, Shun-Qing Zhang", "title" -> 
            "Higher-loop integrated negative geometries in ABJM", "comments" -> 
            "26 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "MPP-2024-37", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In the three-dimensional ${\\cal N}=6$ Chern-Simons matter \
(ABJM) theory, the\nintegrand for the logarithm of the scattering amplitude \
admits a decomposition\nin terms of negative geometries, which implies that \
all the infrared\ndivergences concentrate in the last loop integration. We \
compute the\ninfrared-finite functions that arise from performing a \
three-loop integration\nover the four-loop integrand for the logarithm of the \
four-point amplitude, for\nwhich we use the method of differential equations. \
Our results provide a direct\ncomputation of the four-loop cusp anomalous \
dimension of the theory, in\nagreement with the current all-loop \
integrability-based proposal. We find an\napparent simplicity in the leading \
singularities of the integrated results,\nprovided one works in the frame in \
which the unintegrated loop variable goes to\ninfinity. Finally, our results \
suggest an alternating sign pattern for the\nintegrated negative geometries \
in the Euclidean region.\n", 
