           "id" -> "2403.14062", "submitter" -> "Baiyang Zhang", "authors" -> 
            "Jarah Evslin, Kehinde Ogundipe, Baiyang Zhang, Hengyuan Guo", 
            "title" -> "A (2+1)-Dimensional Domain Wall at One-Loop", 
            "comments" -> "21 pages, 1figure", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the domain wall in the (2+1)-dimensional $\\phi^4$ \
double well\nmodel, created by extending the $\\phi^4$ kink in an additional \
infinite\ndirection. Classically, the tension is $m^3/3\\lambda$ where \
$\\lambda$ is the\ncoupling and $m$ is the meson mass. At order \
$O(\\lambda^0)$ all ultraviolet\ndivergences can be removed by normal \
ordering, less trivial divergences arrive\nonly at the next order. This \
allows us to easily quantize the domain wall,\nworking at order \
$O(\\lambda^0)$. We calculate the leading quantum correction to\nits tension \
as a two-dimensional integral over a function which is determined\n\
analytically. This integral is performed numerically, resulting in\n\
$-0.0866m^2$. This correction has previously been computed twice in the\n\
literature, and the results of these two computations disagreed. Our result\n\
agrees with and so confirms that of Jaimunga, Semenoff and Zarembo. We also\n\
find, at this order, the excitation spectrum and a general expression for the\
\none-loop tensions of domain walls in other scalar models.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
