               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pietro Ferrero\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Connor Behan and Shai M. Chester and Pietro \
Ferrero\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Towards Bootstrapping F-theory\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"51 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider type IIB string theory with $N$ D3 branes \
and various\\nconfigurations of sevenbranes, such that the string coupling \
$g_s$ is fixed to\\na constant finite value. These are the simplest \
realizations of F-theory, and\\nare holographically dual to rank $N$ \
Argyres-Douglas conformal field theories\\n(CFTs) with $SU(2)$ and $SU(3)$ \
flavor groups, and Minahan-Nemeschansky CFTs\\nwith $E_6, E_7$ and $E_8$ \
flavor groups. We use the Seiberg-Witten curves of\\nthese theories to \
compute the mass deformed sphere free energy $F(m)$ at large\\n$N$ in terms \
of novel matrix models with non-polynomial potentials. We show how\\n$F(m)$ \
can be used along with the analytic bootstrap to fix the large \
$N$\\nexpansion of flavor multiplet correlators in these CFTs, which are dual \
to\\nscattering of gluons on $AdS_5\\\\times S^3$, and in the flat space \
limit\\ndetermine the effective theory of sevenbranes in F-theory. As a first \
step in\\nthis program, we use the matrix models to compute the $\\\\log N$ \
term in $F(m)$\\nand thereby fix the logarithmic threshold in the \
$AdS_5\\\\times S^3$ holographic\\ncorrelator, which matches the flat space \
prediction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 25 Mar 2024 18:00:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-03-27\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Behan\"", ",", "\"Connor\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Chester\"", ",", "\"Shai M.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Ferrero\"", ",", "\"Pietro\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2403.17049", "submitter" -> "Pietro Ferrero", "authors" -> 
            "Connor Behan and Shai M. Chester and Pietro Ferrero", "title" -> 
            "Towards Bootstrapping F-theory", "comments" -> "51 pages", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider type IIB string theory with $N$ D3 branes and \
various\nconfigurations of sevenbranes, such that the string coupling $g_s$ \
is fixed to\na constant finite value. These are the simplest realizations of \
F-theory, and\nare holographically dual to rank $N$ Argyres-Douglas conformal \
field theories\n(CFTs) with $SU(2)$ and $SU(3)$ flavor groups, and \
Minahan-Nemeschansky CFTs\nwith $E_6, E_7$ and $E_8$ flavor groups. We use \
the Seiberg-Witten curves of\nthese theories to compute the mass deformed \
sphere free energy $F(m)$ at large\n$N$ in terms of novel matrix models with \
non-polynomial potentials. We show how\n$F(m)$ can be used along with the \
analytic bootstrap to fix the large $N$\nexpansion of flavor multiplet \
correlators in these CFTs, which are dual to\nscattering of gluons on \
$AdS_5\\times S^3$, and in the flat space limit\ndetermine the effective \
theory of sevenbranes in F-theory. As a first step in\nthis program, we use \
the matrix models to compute the $\\log N$ term in $F(m)$\nand thereby fix \
the logarithmic threshold in the $AdS_5\\times S^3$ holographic\ncorrelator, \
which matches the flat space prediction.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
