           "id" -> "2403.19228", "submitter" -> "Naotaka Kubo", "authors" -> 
            "Naotaka Kubo", "title" -> 
            "Duality between $U\\times U$ and $O\\times USp$ theories from\n  \
$A_{3}=D_{3}$", "comments" -> "49 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            
            "  We study the duality between the ABJ(M) theory at Chern-Simons \
level $k=4$\nand the orientifold ABJ theory at Chern-Simons level $k=1$ by \
using the $S^{3}$\npartition function. The partition function can be computed \
using the\nsupersymmetric localization in terms of a matrix model, and we \
derive an ideal\nFermi gas system by applying the Fermi gas formalism to the \
matrix model. By\nusing this formalism, we show that the matrix model can be \
embedded in the\npartition function of $\\hat{A}_{3}$ or $\\hat{D}_{3}$ \
quiver theories, and the\nequality of these quiver theories, which comes from \
$\\hat{A}_{3}=\\hat{D}_{3}$,\nleads to exact relations of the matrix models. \
These exact relations can be\nused to check the identification of the flavor \
symmetries. The perfect\nagreement between the matrix models also implies \
that no decoupled sector is\nneeded.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 28 Mar 2024 08:43:14 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 3 Apr 2024 07:23:52 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
