          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2403.19538\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Victor Mishnyakov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"V. Mishnyakov, I. Myakutin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Superintegrability of the monomial Uglov matrix \
model\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"42 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we propose a resolution to the problem of \
$\\\\beta$-deforming the\\nnon-Gaussian monomial matrix models. The naive \
guess of substituting Schur\\npolynomials with Jack polynomials does not work \
in that case, therefore, we are\\nforced to look for another basis for \
superintegrability. We find that the\\nrelevant symmetric functions are given \
by Uglov polynomials, and that the\\nintegration measure should also be \
deformed. The measure appears to be related\\nto the Uglov limit as well, \
when the quantum parameters $(q,t)$ go to a root of\\nunity. The degree of \
the root must be equal to the degree of the potential. One\\ncannot derive \
these results directly, for example, by studying Virasoro\\nconstraints. \
Instead, we use the recently developed techniques of $W$-operators\\nto \
arrive at the root of unity limit. From the perspective of matrix \
models\\nthis new example demonstrates that even with a rather nontrivial \
integration\\nmeasure one can find a superintegrability basis by studying the \
hidden symmetry\\nof the moduli space of deformations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 28 Mar 2024 16:12:45 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
