, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The two-dimensional Gross-Neveu model is anticipated \
to undergo a crystalline\\nphase transition at high baryon charge densities. \
This conclusion is drawn from\\nthe mean-field approximation, which closely \
resembles models of Peierls\\ninstability. We demonstrate that this \
transition indeed occurs when both the\\nrank of the symmetry group and the \
dimension of the particle representation\\ncontributing to the baryon density \
are large (the large-N limit). We derive\\nthis result through the exact \
solution of the model, developing the large-N\\nlimit of the Bethe Ansatz. \
Our analytical construction of the large-N solution\\nof the Bethe Ansatz \
equations aligns perfectly with the periodic (finite-gap)\\nsolution of the \
Korteweg-de Vries (KdV) of the mean-field analysis.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
