               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Saulo De Mesquita Diles\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Saulo Diles\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the spectrum of open strings in the Hard-Wall model of \
AdS/QCD: the\\n  role of $S^5$\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"6 pages; 2 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th hep-lat math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the problem of a classical open string \
representing a meson in the\\nhard-wall geometry and consider the $S^5$ \
compact space. The existence of a\\nconfining region due to the hard cut-off \
leads to a discrete set of string\\nconfigurations parameterized by the \
number of complete turnarounds $S^5$ great\\ncircles. On the one hand, for a \
given angular momentum, there is a discrete set\\nof possible separations, \
and the confined quarks on the boundary are restrict\\nto a lattice. On the \
other hand, for a given separation in the confining\\nregion, there is a \
discrete set of permitted values for the angular momentum.\\nThe \
$q\\\\bar{q}$ potential is linear for large separations, and the \
string\\ntension is very sensitive to the angular momentum.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
