               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Roman Mauch and Lorenzo Ruggeri\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Super Yang-Mills on Branched Covers and Weighted \
Projective Spaces\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"22 pages; 9 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this work we conjecture the Coulomb branch partition \
function, including\\nflux and instanton contributions, for the \
$\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ vector multiplet on\\nweighted projective space \
$\\\\mathbb{CP}^2_{\\\\boldsymbol{N}}$ for equivariant\\nDonaldson-Witten and \
``Pestun-like'' theories. More precisely, we claim that\\nthis partition \
function agrees with the one computed on a certain branched\\ncover of \
$\\\\mathbb{CP}^2$ upon matching conical deficit angles with\\ncorresponding \
branch indices. Our conjecture is substantiated by checking that\\nsimilar \
partition functions on spindles agree with their equivalent on \
certain\\nbranched covers of $\\\\mathbb{CP}^1$. We compute the one-loop \
determinant on the\\nbranched cover of $\\\\mathbb{CP}^2$ for all flux \
sectors via dimensional\\nreduction from the $\\\\mathcal{N}=1$ vector \
multiplet on a branched five-sphere\\nalong a free $S^1$-action. This work \
paves the way for obtaining partition\\nfunctions on more generic symplectic \
toric orbifolds.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
