            "Roman Mauch and Lorenzo Ruggeri", "title" -> 
            "Super Yang-Mills on Branched Covers and Weighted Projective \
Spaces", "comments" -> "22 pages; 9 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this work we conjecture the Coulomb branch partition \
function, including\nflux and instanton contributions, for the \
$\\mathcal{N}=2$ vector multiplet on\nweighted projective space \
$\\mathbb{CP}^2_{\\boldsymbol{N}}$ for equivariant\nDonaldson-Witten and \
``Pestun-like'' theories. More precisely, we claim that\nthis partition \
function agrees with the one computed on a certain branched\ncover of \
$\\mathbb{CP}^2$ upon matching conical deficit angles with\ncorresponding \
branch indices. Our conjecture is substantiated by checking that\nsimilar \
partition functions on spindles agree with their equivalent on certain\n\
branched covers of $\\mathbb{CP}^1$. We compute the one-loop determinant on \
the\nbranched cover of $\\mathbb{CP}^2$ for all flux sectors via dimensional\n\
reduction from the $\\mathcal{N}=1$ vector multiplet on a branched \
five-sphere\nalong a free $S^1$-action. This work paves the way for obtaining \
partition\nfunctions on more generic symplectic toric orbifolds.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 17 Apr 2024 17:50:31 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-04-18", 
