           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2404.12446\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Emil Albrychiewicz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Emil Albrychiewicz, Andr\\\\'es Franco Valiente, Ori J. \
Ganor, Chao Ju\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ground States of Class S Theory on ADE Singularities and \
dual\\n  Chern-Simons theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"41 pages, 2 figures, v2 updated section 3 and appendix \
B\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In radial quantization, the ground states of a gauge \
theory on ADE\\nsingularities $\\\\mathbb{R}^4/\\\\Gamma$ are characterized \
by flat connections that\\nare maps from $\\\\Gamma$ to the gauge group. We \
study Class $\\\\mathcal{S}$ theory\\nof type \
$\\\\mathfrak{a}_1=\\\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ on a Riemann surface of genus \
$g>1$,\\nwithout punctures. The fundamental building block of Class \
$\\\\mathcal{S}$ theory\\nis the trifundamental Trinion theory - a low energy \
limit of two M5 branes\\ncompactified on the three-punctured Riemann sphere. \
We show, through the\\nsuperconformal index, that the supersymmetric Casimir \
energy of the\\ntrifundamental theory imposes a constraint on the set of \
allowed flat\\nconnections, which agrees with the prediction of a duality \
relating the ground\\nstate Hilbert space of Class $\\\\mathcal{S}$ on ADE \
singularities to the Hilbert\\nspace of a certain dual Chern-Simons theory \
whose gauge group is given by the\\nMcKay correspondence. The conjecture is \
shown to hold for\\n$\\\\Gamma=\\\\mathbb{Z}_k$, agreeing with the previous \
results of Benini et al. and\\nAlday et al. A non-abelian generalization of \
this duality is analyzed by\\nconsidering the example of the dicyclic group $\
\\\\Gamma=\\\\text{Dic}_2$,\\ncorresponding to Chern-Simons gauge group \
SO$(8)$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
