         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2404.12446", "submitter" -> "Emil Albrychiewicz", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Emil Albrychiewicz, Andr\\'es Franco Valiente, Ori J. Ganor, \
Chao Ju", "title" -> 
            "Ground States of Class S Theory on ADE Singularities and dual\n  \
Chern-Simons theory", "comments" -> 
            "41 pages, 2 figures, v2 updated section 3 and appendix B", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In radial quantization, the ground states of a gauge theory on \
ADE\nsingularities $\\mathbb{R}^4/\\Gamma$ are characterized by flat \
connections that\nare maps from $\\Gamma$ to the gauge group. We study Class \
$\\mathcal{S}$ theory\nof type $\\mathfrak{a}_1=\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ on a \
Riemann surface of genus $g>1$,\nwithout punctures. The fundamental building \
block of Class $\\mathcal{S}$ theory\nis the trifundamental Trinion theory - \
a low energy limit of two M5 branes\ncompactified on the three-punctured \
Riemann sphere. We show, through the\nsuperconformal index, that the \
supersymmetric Casimir energy of the\ntrifundamental theory imposes a \
constraint on the set of allowed flat\nconnections, which agrees with the \
prediction of a duality relating the ground\nstate Hilbert space of Class \
$\\mathcal{S}$ on ADE singularities to the Hilbert\nspace of a certain dual \
Chern-Simons theory whose gauge group is given by the\nMcKay correspondence. \
The conjecture is shown to hold for\n$\\Gamma=\\mathbb{Z}_k$, agreeing with \
the previous results of Benini et al. and\nAlday et al. A non-abelian \
generalization of this duality is analyzed by\nconsidering the example of the \
dicyclic group $\\Gamma=\\text{Dic}_2$,\ncorresponding to Chern-Simons gauge \
group SO$(8)$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
