               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we present three new families of smooth \
Type II string theory\\nbackgrounds. These are dual to \
supersymmetry-preserving deformations of 4d\\nSCFTs. The deformations include \
a VEV for a global current and a `twisted\\ncompactification' on a circle. We \
study various holographic aspects of the dual\\nQFTs, focusing on Wilson \
loops and Entanglement Entropy. Additionally, we\\npresent a monotonic \
quantity calculating the density of degrees of freedom in\\nterms of the \
energy, which interpolates between the IR 3d gapped theory and the\\n4d SCFT \
result. Other probes related to global aspects of the QFTs are \
briefly\\ndiscussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
