               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2405.17562\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Nathan Benjamin\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nathan Benjamin, Jaeha Lee, Sridip Pal, David \
Simmons-Duffin, Yixin Xu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Angular fractals in thermal QFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages + appendices, 7 figures; v2: references \
added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CALT-TH 2024-021\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that thermal effective field theory controls \
the long-distance\\nexpansion of the partition function of a $d$-dimensional \
QFT, with an insertion\\nof any finite-order spatial isometry. Consequently, \
the thermal partition\\nfunction on a sphere displays a fractal-like \
structure as a function of angular\\ntwist, reminiscent of the behavior of a \
modular form near the real line. As an\\nexample application, we find that \
for CFTs, the effective free energy of\\neven-spin minus odd-spin operators \
at high temperature is smaller than the\\nusual free energy by a factor of \
$1/2^d$. Near certain rational angles, the\\npartition function receives \
subleading contributions from \\\"Kaluza-Klein vortex\\ndefects\\\" in the \
thermal EFT, which we classify. We illustrate our results with\\nexamples in \
free and holographic theories, and also discuss nonperturbative\\ncorrections \
from worldline instantons.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
