             "  We study correlation functions on the Coulomb branch of \
planar $\\mathcal{N} =\n4$ super-Yang- Mills theory (SYM), and their \
relationship with integrability,\nthe operator product expansion (OPE), the \
sum rule, the large charge expansion,\nand holography. First, we compute \
one-point functions of arbitrary scalar\noperators at weak coupling and \
derive a compact spin-chain representation. We\nnext study the two-point \
functions of chiral primaries at one loop and find\nthat the radius of \
convergence of OPE in position space is infinite. We\nestimate the asymptotic \
growth of the OPE data based on this finding. Finally,\nwe propose a concrete \
nonperturbative formula that connects the correlation\nfunctions on the \
Coulomb branch with the correlation functions with large\ncharge insertions \
at the conformal point and provide a holographic\ninterpretation based on a \
large D3-brane in AdS. The formula extends the known\nconnection between the \
large charge sector and the Coulomb branch for rank-1\ntheories to the large \
$N$ limit.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Wed, 29 May 2024 12:34:59 GMT"}, {
