            "Sibylle Driezen and Niranjan Kamath", "title" -> 
            "Regularising Spectral Curves for Homogeneous Yang-Baxter \
strings", "comments" -> "8 pages", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this Letter, we study the semi-classical spectrum of \
integrable worldsheet\n$\\sigma$-models using the Spectral Curve. We consider \
a Homogeneous Yang-Baxter\ndeformation of the $AdS_5\\times S^5$ superstring, \
understood as the composition\nof a Jordanian with a \"non-diagonal\" TsT \
deformation. We derive its type IIB\nsupergravity solution, whose isometry \
algebra features zero supercharges and a\nnon-relativistic conformal algebra \
in $0+1$ dimensions. While the Spectral\nCurves of non-diagonal TsT models \
are ill-defined, we demonstrate that the\ncomposition with a Jordanian model \
regularises this issue. From the regularised\nCurve, we derive the one-loop \
shift of the classical energy and the\nsemi-classical spectrum of excitations \
of a point-like string. In the TsT\nlimit, the one-loop shift vanishes \
despite the loss of supersymmetry. Our\nresults suggest that it may be \
possible to use standard Bethe Ansatze on spin\nchain pictures of deformed \
$N=4$ Super-Yang-Mills theory dual to non-diagonal\nTsT models.\n", 
