               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Regularization effects in the Nambu-Jona-Lasinio model: \
Strong scheme\\n  dependence of inhomogeneous phases and persistence of the \
moat regime\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"16 pages, 11 figures, 12 pages appendix & \
references\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph hep-lat\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This work investigates the phase structure of the \
non-renormalizable\\n(3+1)-dimensional Nambu-Jona-Lasinio (NJL) model with \
particular focus on\\ninhomogeneous phases (IPs), where the chiral condensate \
is non-uniform in\\nspace, and the closely related moat regimes, where \
mesonic dispersion relations\\nfavor non-vanishing momenta. We use the \
mean-field approximation and consider\\nfive different regularization schemes \
including three lattice discretizations.\\nThe results within the different \
regularization schemes are systematically\\nanalyzed in order to study the \
dependence of the IP on the choice of\\nregulatization scheme and regulator \
value. The IP exhibits a drastic dependence\\non the chosen regularization \
scheme rendering any physical interpretation of\\nresults on inhomogeneous \
phases in this model doubtful. In contrast, we find\\nonly a mild scheme \
dependence of the moat regime suggesting that its existence\\nis a \
consequence of the action of the NJL model and its symmetries and, \
thus,\\nthat it might also exist in QCD.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
