             "title" -> 
            "A correspondence between the quantum K theory and quantum \
cohomology of\n  Grassmannians", "comments" -> "36 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> "MPIM-Bonn-2024", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We utilize physics arguments, and the nonabelian/abelian \
correspondence, to\nrelate the Givental and Lee's quantum K theory ring of \
Grassmannians to a\ntwisted variant of the quantum cohomology ring. \
Furthermore, the quantum K\npairing is related to correlators arising from \
supersymmetric localization. We\nstate some mathematical conjectures, which \
we illustrate in several examples.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 19 Jun 2024 18:00:02 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-07-17", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Gu", "Wei", ""}, {"Guo", "Jirui", ""}, {
              "Mihalcea", "Leonardo", ""}, {"Wen", "Yaoxiong", ""}, {
              "Yan", "Xiaohan", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{14.88681142037108, -2.7643332373531777`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2406.13741\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Adolfo Holguin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Marius de Leeuw, Adolfo Holguin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable Conformal Defects in N=4 SYM\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we classify integrable conformal defects \
in N=4 SYM theory for\\nwhich the scalar fields pick up a non-trivial vacuum \
expectation value. Defects\\nof this form correspond to Dirichlet boundary \
conditions that have a pole at\\nthe defect. These set-ups typically appear \
on the field theory side of probe\\nbrane set-ups in the AdS/CFT \
correspondence. We show that such defects, for any\\ncodimension, are related \
to fuzzy spheres. We discuss the properties of the\\ndifferent possible fuzzy \
spheres that can appear and present the corresponding\\nMatrix Product \
States. We furthermore set-up the quantum field theoretic\\nframework by \
computing the mass matrix and finding the propagators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
