            "  In this paper we classify integrable conformal defects in N=4 \
SYM theory for\nwhich the scalar fields pick up a non-trivial vacuum \
expectation value. Defects\nof this form correspond to Dirichlet boundary \
conditions that have a pole at\nthe defect. These set-ups typically appear on \
the field theory side of probe\nbrane set-ups in the AdS/CFT correspondence. \
We show that such defects, for any\ncodimension, are related to fuzzy \
spheres. We discuss the properties of the\ndifferent possible fuzzy spheres \
that can appear and present the corresponding\nMatrix Product States. We \
furthermore set-up the quantum field theoretic\nframework by computing the \
mass matrix and finding the propagators.\n", 
