Nikita Tselousov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Algorithms for representations of quiver Yangian algebras\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"41 pages, 9 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 08 (2024) 209\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP08(2024)209\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP math.QA math.RT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this note, we aim to review algorithms for \
constructing crystal\\nrepresentations of quiver Yangians in detail. Quiver \
Yangians are believed to\\ndescribe an action of the BPS algebra on BPS \
states in systems of D-branes\\nwrapping toric Calabi-Yau three-folds. \
Crystal modules of these algebras\\noriginate from molten crystal models for \
Donaldson-Thomas invariants of\\nrespective three-folds. Despite the fact \
that this subject was originally at\\nthe crossroads of algebraic geometry \
with effective supersymmetric field\\ntheories, equivariant toric action \
simplifies applied calculations drastically.\\nSo the sole pre-requisite for \
this algorithm's implementation is linear\\nalgebra. It can be easily taught \
to a machine with the help of any symbolic\\ncalculation system. Moreover, \
these algorithms may be generalized to toroidal\\nand elliptic algebras and \
exploited in various numerical experiments with those\\nalgebras. We \
illustrate the work of the algorithms in applications to simple\\ncases of \
$\\\\mathsf{Y}(\\\\mathfrak{sl}_2)$,\\n$\\\\mathsf{Y}(\\\\widehat{\\\\\
mathfrak{gl}}_{1})$ \
and\\n$\\\\mathsf{Y}(\\\\widehat{\\\\mathfrak{gl}}_{1|1})$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
