         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2406.20074", "submitter" -> "Alexey Gavshin", "authors" -> 
            "Dmitry Galakhov, Alexei Gavshin, Alexei Morozov, and Nikita \
Tselousov", "title" -> 
            "Algorithms for representations of quiver Yangian algebras", 
            "comments" -> "41 pages, 9 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 08 (2024) 209", "doi" -> "10.1007/JHEP08(2024)209", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP math.QA math.RT", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this note, we aim to review algorithms for constructing \
crystal\nrepresentations of quiver Yangians in detail. Quiver Yangians are \
believed to\ndescribe an action of the BPS algebra on BPS states in systems \
of D-branes\nwrapping toric Calabi-Yau three-folds. Crystal modules of these \
algebras\noriginate from molten crystal models for Donaldson-Thomas \
invariants of\nrespective three-folds. Despite the fact that this subject was \
originally at\nthe crossroads of algebraic geometry with effective \
supersymmetric field\ntheories, equivariant toric action simplifies applied \
calculations drastically.\nSo the sole pre-requisite for this algorithm's \
implementation is linear\nalgebra. It can be easily taught to a machine with \
the help of any symbolic\ncalculation system. Moreover, these algorithms may \
be generalized to toroidal\nand elliptic algebras and exploited in various \
numerical experiments with those\nalgebras. We illustrate the work of the \
algorithms in applications to simple\ncases of \
$\\mathsf{Y}(\\mathfrak{sl}_2)$,\n\
$\\mathsf{Y}(\\widehat{\\mathfrak{gl}}_{1})$ and\n\
$\\mathsf{Y}(\\widehat{\\mathfrak{gl}}_{1|1})$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 28 Jun 2024 17:34:10 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-09-02", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Galakhov", "Dmitry", ""}, {
              "Gavshin", "Alexei", ""}, {"Morozov", "Alexei", ""}, {
              "Tselousov", "Nikita", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
