          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2407.03509\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alberto Lerda\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M. Billo, M. Frau, A. Lerda, A. Pini, P. Vallarino\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrated correlators in a $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ SYM theory \
with fundamental\\n  flavors: a matrix-model perspective\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"31 pages\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-EP-24/21\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The D theory is a $\\\\mathcal{N}=2$ conformal SYM \
theory in four dimensions\\nwith gauge group SU($N$), four matter \
hypermultiplets in the fundamental and\\ntwo in the anti-symmetric \
representation, and a flavor symmetry that contains a\\nU(4) factor. Its \
holographic dual is obtained via a combination of orbifold and\\norientifold \
projections from Type II B string theory on $\\\\mathrm{AdS}_5 \
\\\\times\\nS^5$ and possesses a sector of open strings attached to D7 branes \
with U(4)\\nChan-Paton factors. The AdS Veneziano amplitude of the U(4) \
gluons is dual to\\nfour-point correlators of moment-map operators of the \
U(4) flavor symmetry in\\nthe D theory. An integrated version of these \
correlators is captured by a\\ndeformation of the D theory in which the \
fundamental hypermultiplets acquire a\\nmass. The partition function of this \
massive theory can be evaluated with\\nmatrix-model techniques using \
localization. In this paper we analyze the matrix\\nmodel of the \
mass-deformed D theory arising from localization using the\\nso-called ``full \
Lie algebra'' approach in a $1/N$ expansion. In particular, we\\nstudy the \
partition function and its mass derivatives up to $O(1/N^2)$\\ncorrections \
obtaining exact expressions that are valid for all values of the 't\\nHooft \
coupling. We also analyze their behavior at strong coupling where \
our\\nresults produce useful constraints on the dual open string \
scattering\\namplitudes in AdS.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 3 Jul 2024 21:13:06 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-07-08\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Billo\"", ",", "\"M.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Frau\"", ",", "\"M.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Lerda\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Pini\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Vallarino\"", ",", "\"P.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
