         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "2407.03509", "submitter" -> "Alberto Lerda", "authors" -> 
            "M. Billo, M. Frau, A. Lerda, A. Pini, P. Vallarino", "title" -> 
            "Integrated correlators in a $\\mathcal{N}=2$ SYM theory with \
fundamental\n  flavors: a matrix-model perspective", "comments" -> "31 pages",
             "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "HU-EP-24/21", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The D theory is a $\\mathcal{N}=2$ conformal SYM theory in \
four dimensions\nwith gauge group SU($N$), four matter hypermultiplets in the \
fundamental and\ntwo in the anti-symmetric representation, and a flavor \
symmetry that contains a\nU(4) factor. Its holographic dual is obtained via a \
combination of orbifold and\norientifold projections from Type II B string \
theory on $\\mathrm{AdS}_5 \\times\nS^5$ and possesses a sector of open \
strings attached to D7 branes with U(4)\nChan-Paton factors. The AdS \
Veneziano amplitude of the U(4) gluons is dual to\nfour-point correlators of \
moment-map operators of the U(4) flavor symmetry in\nthe D theory. An \
integrated version of these correlators is captured by a\ndeformation of the \
D theory in which the fundamental hypermultiplets acquire a\nmass. The \
partition function of this massive theory can be evaluated with\nmatrix-model \
techniques using localization. In this paper we analyze the matrix\nmodel of \
the mass-deformed D theory arising from localization using the\nso-called \
``full Lie algebra'' approach in a $1/N$ expansion. In particular, we\nstudy \
the partition function and its mass derivatives up to $O(1/N^2)$\ncorrections \
obtaining exact expressions that are valid for all values of the 't\nHooft \
coupling. We also analyze their behavior at strong coupling where our\n\
results produce useful constraints on the dual open string scattering\n\
amplitudes in AdS.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 3 Jul 2024 21:13:06 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2024-07-08", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Billo", "M.", ""}, {"Frau", "M.", ""}, {
              "Lerda", "A.", ""}, {"Pini", "A.", ""}, {
              "Vallarino", "P.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
