               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Peihe Yang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jun-Bao Wu and Peihe Yang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Three-point Functions in \
Aharony--Bergman--Jafferis--Maldacena Theory\\n  and Integrable Boundary \
States\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10+5 pages, no figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the correlators of three single-trace \
operators in\\nAharony-Bergman-Jafferis-Maldacena (ABJM) theory from the \
perspective of\\nintegrable boundary states. Specifically, we focus on \
scenarios where two\\noperators being $1/3$-BPS and the entire correlation \
function is considered\\nwithin the twisted-translated frame. The correlator \
can be expressed as the\\noverlap between a boundary state and a Bethe state. \
It is found that the\\nboundary state formed by the two $1/3$-BPS operators \
is integrable only when\\nthe number of Wick contractions between the non-BPS \
operator and one of the\\n$1/3$-BPS operators is 0 or 1. We compute the \
overlaps for the integrable cases\\nutilizing the symmetries preserved by the \
correlators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
