            "Simone Giombi, Stefan A. Kurlyand and Arkady A. Tseytlin", 
            "title" -> 
            "Non-planar corrections in ABJM theory from quantum M2 branes", 
            "comments" -> 
            "37 pages. v2: changes in footnote 24 and appendix D, references \
added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AT-2024-03", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  The quantization of semiclassical strings in AdS spacetimes \
yields\npredictions for the strong-coupling behaviour of the scaling \
dimensions of the\ncorresponding operators in the planar limit of the dual \
gauge theory. Finding\nnon-planar corrections requires computing string loops \
(corresponding to torus\nand higher genus surfaces), which is a challenging \
task. It turns out that in\nthe case of the $U_k(N) \\times U_{-k}(N)$ ABJM \
theory there is an alternative\napproach: one may semiclassically quantize M2 \
branes in AdS$_{4}\\times\nS^7/\\mathbb{Z}_{k}$ which are wrapped around the \
11d circle of radius $1/k=\n\\lambda/N$. Such M2 branes are the M-theory \
generalization of the strings in\nAdS$_4\\times $CP$^3$. In this work, we \
show that by expanding in large M2 brane\ntension $ T_2 \\sim \\sqrt{kN} $ \
for fixed $k$, followed by an expansion in large\n$k$, we can predict the \
large $\\lambda$ asymptotics of the non-planar\ncorrections to the dimensions \
of the dual ABJM operators. As a specific\nexample, we consider the M2 brane \
configuration that generalizes the long\nfolded string with large spin in \
AdS$_4$, and compute the 1-loop correction to\nits energy. This calculation \
allows us to determine non-planar corrections to\nthe universal scaling \
function or cusp anomalous dimension. We extend our\nanalysis to the \
semiclassical M2 branes that generalize the \"short\" and \"long\"\ncircular \
strings with two equal angular momenta in CP$^3$. The \"short\" M2 brane\n\
corresponds to a dual operator whose dimension at strong coupling scales as\n\
$\\Delta \\sim \\lambda^{1/4} + \\dots$, and we derive the leading non-planar\
\ncorrection to it.\n", 
