                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  4d $\\\\mathcal N=4$ SYM admits half-BPS boundaries, \
defects and interfaces as\\nwell as compactifications to 3d $\\\\mathcal \
N\\\\,{=}\\\\,4$ SCFTs, realized as\\nintersections of D3, D5 and NS5 branes. \
We explore operators with large\\nR-charge. We identify Penrose limits in the \
holographic duals with geometry\\n$\\\\rm AdS_4\\\\times S^2\\\\times \
S^2\\\\times\\\\Sigma$, which describe, for each theory, a\\nspectrum of \
`seed' operators which each give rise to a BMN-like sector\\ndescribed by a \
pp-wave. We relate the number of BMN-like sectors to the flavor\\nsymmetry of \
the CFT. For a sample of theories including the Janus interface,\\nD3/D5 \
BCFTs and BCFTs with 3d SCFTs on the boundary, we determine the spectra\\nof \
nearby operators and discuss the field theory realization of the \
seed\\noperators. We further identify families of Penrose limits which give \
rise to\\nmore general pp-wave sectors.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
