           "id" -> "2408.12651", "submitter" -> "Christoph Uhlemann", 
            "authors" -> "Andrea Chaney, Christoph F. Uhlemann", "title" -> 
            "BMN-like sectors in 4d $\\mathcal N=4$ SYM with boundaries and \
interfaces", "comments" -> "35 pages, 13 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  4d $\\mathcal N=4$ SYM admits half-BPS boundaries, defects and \
interfaces as\nwell as compactifications to 3d $\\mathcal N\\,{=}\\,4$ SCFTs, \
realized as\nintersections of D3, D5 and NS5 branes. We explore operators \
with large\nR-charge. We identify Penrose limits in the holographic duals \
with geometry\n$\\rm AdS_4\\times S^2\\times S^2\\times\\Sigma$, which \
describe, for each theory, a\nspectrum of `seed' operators which each give \
rise to a BMN-like sector\ndescribed by a pp-wave. We relate the number of \
BMN-like sectors to the flavor\nsymmetry of the CFT. For a sample of theories \
including the Janus interface,\nD3/D5 BCFTs and BCFTs with 3d SCFTs on the \
boundary, we determine the spectra\nof nearby operators and discuss the field \
theory realization of the seed\noperators. We further identify families of \
Penrose limits which give rise to\nmore general pp-wave sectors.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
