            "Pinaki Dutta, Kamal L. Panigrahi and Balbeer Singh", "title" -> 
            "Chaos Bound and its violation in Black p-brane", "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, 26 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  In this work, we have extensively investigated the dynamics of \
circular\ngeodesic (chargeless massive particle) followed by the \
investigation of the\npulsating classical string in the p-brane background. \
This study is a\ncontinuation of our previous work (arXiv:2307.12350v3), in \
which we numerically\nidentified the presence of chaos for a classical string \
hovering near generic\np-branes ($p < 7$). Here, for a particle probe, we \
have found evidence of chaos\nin the vicinity of the horizon. Furthermore, we \
observed a violation of the\nwell-known MSS bound in specific extremal \
p-branes; however, no such violation\nis seen in the non-extremal cases. \
Similar observations were made for the\nclassical string, where the violation \
of the bound is significant near the\nhorizon. Thus, our semi-analytical \
arguments demonstrate that chaotic dynamics\nin black p-branes exhibit the \
(generalized) universal bound with notable\nviolations, regardless of whether \
a particle or classical string is used as a\nprobe.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 26 Aug 2024 07:28:47 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 7 Sep 2024 18:15:01 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
