 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Integrable $su(2\\\\vert2)_{c}$ symmetric models have \
integrable boundaries with\\n$osp(2\\\\vert2)$ symmetries, which can be \
embedded into $su(2\\\\vert2)_{c}$ in two\\ndifferent ways. We dualize the \
previously obtained asymptotic overlap formulas\\nfor one of the embeddings \
to describe the other embedding and apply the results\\nto describe the \
asymptotic expectation values of local operators in the\\npresence of a 't \
Hooft line in N=4 SYM. A peculiar feature of the setting is\\nthat in certain \
gradings only descendant states have non-vanishing overlaps\\nwith the \
boundary state and the overlap formula is not factorized for the \
Bethe\\nroots.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
