                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We suggest a dynamical mechanism which explains why in \
the supersymmetric\\nIKKT matrix model the $SO(9)$ symmetry of the Lagrangian \
is spontaneously\\nbroken to $SO(3) \\\\times SO(6)$, allowing only three \
large classical spatial\\ndimensions to emerge. The argument relies on the \
identification of D1-strings\\nas stable excitations of the matrices about \
the cosmological background, and\\nthe absence of forces between parallel \
D1-string excitations. A spatial\\ndimension can only become large if the \
D1-strings winding that direction can\\nannihilate. In the absence of forces, \
this requires the string world sheets to\\nintersect, a process which is \
highly suppressed if more than three dimensions\\nof space are large. \
Implications for a recently proposed matrix cosmology\\nscenario are \
discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 30 Aug 2024 20:55:19 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
