        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{0.4179794634103158, -13.364701228926032`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2409.03058\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jacky Wan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Jacky C. Wan, Trevor B. Arp, Nathaniel M. Gabor\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Dirac excited state quenching in graphene\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cond-mat.mes-hall\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Hot, dense phases of Dirac fermions - predicted to \
resemble relativistic\\nplasma - are uniquely accessible through \
photoexcitation of pristine, charge\\nneutral graphene. We demonstrate a \
sensitive temperature probe of the\\nphotoexcited Dirac state, called \
interlayer optoelectronic thermometry, which\\nmeasures out-of-plane \
transport of hot carriers in high-mobility, neutral\\ngraphene encapsulated \
within graphene-hBN-graphene heterostructures. At a\\ncritical intermediate \
sample temperature T = 50 K, the electronic temperature\\nTe is quenched, \
exhibiting an intrinsic cooling rate that exceeds 10^14\\nKelvin/s within the \
first picosecond after photoexcitation. Quenching is\\nfurther enhanced by \
applying in-plane voltages within the stack-engineered\\nheterostructure. \
Extreme sensitivity of Te to sample temperature and applied\\nvoltages \
reveals anomalously efficient hot-carrier quenching, which we identify\\nas \
an essential feature of the strongly interacting hot Dirac excited \
state.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 4 Sep 2024 20:14:33 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
