           "id" -> "2409.09463", "submitter" -> "Vitaly Velizhanin", 
            "authors" -> "B.A. Kniehl, V.N. Velizhanin", "title" -> 
            "Nonplanar Four-Loop Anomalous Dimensions of Twist-Two Operators \
in N=4\n  Super Yang-Mills Theory: Higher Moment, General Result, and Cusp \
Anomalous\n  Dimension", "comments" -> "6 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the nonplanar universal anomalous dimension of \
twist-two\noperators at four loops in N=4 supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory \
and push its\ndirect diagrammatic calculation through Lorentz spin j=20, one \
unit beyond the\nstate of the art, so as to confirm the correctness of the \
general, all-j result\nconjectured previously by us [1] imposing certain \
constraints on its analytic\nform. Thanks to our new result, such constraints \
can be eliminated altogether.\nBy the same token, this allows us to \
re-derive, in a completely independent\nway, the nonplanar four-loop cusp \
anomalous dimension by taking the large-j\nlimit of the general result.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
