            "  We construct integrable generalised models in a systematic way \
exploring\ndifferent representations of the gl(N) algebra. The models are \
then interpreted\nin the context of atomic and molecular physics, most of \
them related to\ndifferent types of Bose-Einstein condensates. The spectrum \
of the models is\ngiven through the analytical Bethe ansatz method. We \
further extend these\nresults to the case of the superalgebra gl(M|N), \
providing in this way models\nwhich also include fermions.\n", 
