             "xx pages, Latex, no macros needed", "journal-ref" -> 
             "Nucl.Phys. B482 (1996) 660-674", "doi" -> 
             "10.1016/S0550-3213(96)00526-3", "report-no" -> 
             "NBI-HE-96-20, ITEP-TH-15/96, SMI-96-3", "categories" -> 
             "cond-mat hep-lat hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  We solve a supersymmetric matrix model with a general \
potential. While matrix\nmodels usually describe surfaces, supersymmetry \
enforces a cancellation of\nbosonic and fermionic loops and only diagrams \
corresponding to so-called\nbranched polymers survive. The eigenvalue \
distribution of the random matrices\nnear the critical point is of a new \
kind.\n", "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Fri, 7 Jun 1996 09:17:36 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2009-10-28", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ambjorn", "J.", ""}, {
               "Makeenko", "Y.", ""}, {"Zarembo", "K.", ""}}}], 
           "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
