                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Color--Flavor Transformation of induced QCD\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"24 pages, 6 figures, to appear in Int. J. Mod. Phys. \
A\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Int.J.Mod.Phys. A20 (2005) 4965-4994\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1142/S0217751X05025401\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"ICTP Preprint, IC/2002/124, Trieste, 2002\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-lat\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Zirnbauer's color-flavor transformation is applied \
to the $U(N_c)$\\nlattice gauge model, in which the gauge theory is induced \
by a heavy chiral\\nscalar field sitting on lattice sites. The flavor degrees \
of freedom can\\nencompass several `generations' of the auxiliary field, and \
for each\\ngeneration, remaining indices are associated with the elementary \
plaquettes\\ntouching the lattice site. The effective, color-flavor \
transformed theory is\\nexpressed in terms of gauge singlet matrix fields \
carried by lattice links. The\\neffective action is analyzed for a hypercubic \
lattice in arbitrary dimension.\\nWe investigate the corresponding d=2 and \
d=3 dual lattices. The saddle points\\nequations of the model in the \
large-$N_c$ limit are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 30 Jun 2005 09:48:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Shnir\"", ",", "\"Yasha\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
