                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Zarembo\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"K. Zarembo\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Dispersion Laws for Goldstone Bosons in a Color \
Superconductor\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"17 pages, 2 figures; v2: important clarifications and \
discussion of\\n  weak decays in a color superconductor are added\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Rev.D62:054003,2000\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.62.054003\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ITEP-TH-9/00\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The effective action for Goldstone bosons in the \
color-flavor locking phase\\nof dense QCD is analyzed. Interaction terms and \
higher derivatives in the\\neffective action appear to be controlled by \
different scales. At energies of\\norder of the superconducting gap, the \
derivative expansion breaks down, while\\ninteractions still remain \
suppressed. The effective action valid at energies\\nand momenta comparable \
to the gap is derived. Dispersion laws following from\\nthis action are such \
that the energy of Goldstone bosons is always smaller than\\nthe gap in the \
quasiparticle spectrum, and Goldstone bosons always propagate\\nwithout \
damping.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
