                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Thermal pion fluctuations, in principle, can \
completely disorder the phase of\\nthe quark condensate and thus restore \
chiral symmetry. If this happens before\\nthe quark condensate melts, \
strongly-interacting matter will be in the\\npseudogap state just above the \
chiral phase transition. The quark condensate\\ndoes not vanish locally and \
quarks acquire constituent masses in the pseudogap\\nphase, despite chiral \
symmetry is restored.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
