            "10.1016/S0375-9474(01)01272-6", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-ph nucl-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the effect of SU(3) flavor breaking on high density \
quark matter. We\ndiscuss, in particular, the effect a non-zero electron \
chemical potential and a\nfinite strange quark mass. We argue that these \
perturbations trigger pion or\nkaon condensation. The critical chemical \
potential behaves as $\\mu_e\\sim\\sqrt{m\nm_s} \\Delta/p_F$ and the critical \
strange quark mass as $m_s \\sim m^{1/3}\n\\Delta^{2/3}$, where $m$ is the \
light quark mass, $\\Delta$ is the gap, and\n$p_F$ is the Fermi momentum. We \
note that parametrically, both the critical\n$\\mu_e$ and $m_s^2/(2p_F)$ are \
much smaller than the gap.\n", 
