            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph/0108175\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Igor Shovkovy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"V. P. Gusynin and I. A. Shovkovy\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Collective modes of color-flavor locked phase of dense \
QCD at finite\\n  temperature\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, 8 figures. REVTeX. Two references added and \
minor\\n  modifications introduced (see p. 5 and pp. 13,14). To appear in \
Nucl. Phys. A\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. A700 (2002) 577-617\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0375-9474(01)01317-3\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NUC-MINN-01-10-T\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-ph cond-mat hep-th nucl-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A detailed analysis of collective modes that couple to \
either vector or axial\\ncolor currents in color-flavor locked phase of color \
superconducting dense\\nquark matter at finite temperature is presented. \
Among the realm of collective\\nmodes, including the plasmons and the \
Nambu-Goldstone bosons, we also reveal\\nthe gapless Carlson-Goldman modes, \
resembling the scalar Nambu-Golstone bosons.\\nThese latter exist only in a \
close vicinity of the critical line. Their\\npresence does not eliminate the \
Meissner effect, proving that the system\\nremains in the color broken phase. \
The finite temperature properties of the\\nplasmons and the Nambu-Goldstone \
bosons are also studied. In addition to the\\nordinary plasmon, we also \
reveal a \\\"light\\\" plasmon which has a narrow width and\\nwhose mass is \
of the order of the superconducting gap.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
