         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-ph/0108175", "submitter" -> "Igor Shovkovy", 
            "authors" -> "V. P. Gusynin and I. A. Shovkovy", "title" -> 
            "Collective modes of color-flavor locked phase of dense QCD at \
finite\n  temperature", "comments" -> 
            
            "28 pages, 8 figures. REVTeX. Two references added and minor\n  \
modifications introduced (see p. 5 and pp. 13,14). To appear in Nucl. Phys. \
A", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys. A700 (2002) 577-617", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0375-9474(01)01317-3", "report-no" -> 
            "NUC-MINN-01-10-T", "categories" -> 
            "hep-ph cond-mat hep-th nucl-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  A detailed analysis of collective modes that couple to either \
vector or axial\ncolor currents in color-flavor locked phase of color \
superconducting dense\nquark matter at finite temperature is presented. Among \
the realm of collective\nmodes, including the plasmons and the \
Nambu-Goldstone bosons, we also reveal\nthe gapless Carlson-Goldman modes, \
resembling the scalar Nambu-Golstone bosons.\nThese latter exist only in a \
close vicinity of the critical line. Their\npresence does not eliminate the \
Meissner effect, proving that the system\nremains in the color broken phase. \
The finite temperature properties of the\nplasmons and the Nambu-Goldstone \
bosons are also studied. In addition to the\nordinary plasmon, we also reveal \
a \"light\" plasmon which has a narrow width and\nwhose mass is of the order \
of the superconducting gap.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 22 Aug 2001 14:25:39 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 3 Oct 2001 07:48:35 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-07", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Gusynin", "V. P.", ""}, {
              "Shovkovy", "I. A.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{8.657249755190314, -12.436039006756271`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph/0109173\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Michael McNeil Forbes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Michael McNeil Forbes and Ariel R. Zhitnitsky\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Global Strings in High Density QCD\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX JHEP-format (26 pages) Option in source for REVTeX4 \
format\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev. D65 (2002) 085009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.65.085009\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"MIT-CTP-3190\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-ph astro-ph hep-th nucl-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that several types of global strings occur in \
colour superconducting\\nquark matter due to the spontaneous violation of \
relevant U(1) symmetries.\\nThese include the baryon U(1)_B, and approximate \
axial U(1)_A symmetries as\\nwell as an approximate U(1)_S arising from kaon \
condensation. We discuss some\\ngeneral properties of these strings and their \
interactions. In particular, we\\ndemonstrate that the U(1)_A strings behave \
as superconducting strings. We draw\\nsome parallels between these strings \
and global cosmological strings and\\ndiscuss some possible implications of \
these strings to the physics in neutron\\nstar cores.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
