            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph/0202037\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Giuseppe Nardulli\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Giuseppe Nardulli\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Effective Description of QCD at Very High \
Densities\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"85 pages, 11 figures, v3: minor grammatical changes, some \
misprints\\n  corrected, Fig, 4.1 replaced. This version will appear in \
Rivista del Nuovo\\n  Cimento\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Riv.Nuovo Cim.25N3:1-80,2002\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"BARI-TH 431/02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We describe the effective lagrangian approach to the \
color superconductivity.\\nThe effective description that arises if one \
considers only the leading terms\\nin the expansion for very high densities \
is particularly simple. It is based on\\na lagrangian whose effective fermion \
fields are velocity-dependent; moreover\\nstrong interactions do not change \
quark velocity and the effective lagrangian\\ndoes not contain spin matrices. \
All these features render the effective theory\\nsimilar to the Heavy Quark \
Effective Theory, which is the limit of Quantum\\nChromoDynamics for infinite \
quark masses. For this reason one can refer to the\\neffective lagrangian at \
high density as the High Density Effective Theory\\n(HDET). In some cases \
HDET results in analytical, though approximate, relations\\nthat are \
particularly simple to handle. After a pedagogical introduction,\\nseveral \
topics are considered. They include the treatment of \
the\\nColor-Flavor-Locking and the 2SC model, with evaluation of the gap \
parameters\\nby the Nambu-Gorkov equations, approximate dispersion laws for \
the gluons and\\ncalculations of the Nambu-Goldstone Bosons properties. We \
also discuss the\\neffective lagrangian for the crystalline color \
superconductive (LOFF) phase and\\nwe give a description of the phonon field \
related to the breaking of the\\nrotational and translational invariance. \
Finally a few astrophysical\\napplications of color superconductivity are \
discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 5 Feb 2002 12:33:25 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 15 May 2002 09:48:47 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 21 Jun 2002 17:42:44 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-07-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Nardulli\"", ",", "\"Giuseppe\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                    "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> Left, 
             ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
