         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-ph/0202037", "submitter" -> "Giuseppe Nardulli", 
            "authors" -> "Giuseppe Nardulli", "title" -> 
            "Effective Description of QCD at Very High Densities", "comments" -> 
            "85 pages, 11 figures, v3: minor grammatical changes, some \
misprints\n  corrected, Fig, 4.1 replaced. This version will appear in \
Rivista del Nuovo\n  Cimento", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Riv.Nuovo Cim.25N3:1-80,2002", "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> 
            "BARI-TH 431/02", "categories" -> "hep-ph", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We describe the effective lagrangian approach to the color \
superconductivity.\nThe effective description that arises if one considers \
only the leading terms\nin the expansion for very high densities is \
particularly simple. It is based on\na lagrangian whose effective fermion \
fields are velocity-dependent; moreover\nstrong interactions do not change \
quark velocity and the effective lagrangian\ndoes not contain spin matrices. \
All these features render the effective theory\nsimilar to the Heavy Quark \
Effective Theory, which is the limit of Quantum\nChromoDynamics for infinite \
quark masses. For this reason one can refer to the\neffective lagrangian at \
high density as the High Density Effective Theory\n(HDET). In some cases HDET \
results in analytical, though approximate, relations\nthat are particularly \
simple to handle. After a pedagogical introduction,\nseveral topics are \
considered. They include the treatment of the\nColor-Flavor-Locking and the \
2SC model, with evaluation of the gap parameters\nby the Nambu-Gorkov \
equations, approximate dispersion laws for the gluons and\ncalculations of \
the Nambu-Goldstone Bosons properties. We also discuss the\neffective \
lagrangian for the crystalline color superconductive (LOFF) phase and\nwe \
give a description of the phonon field related to the breaking of the\n\
rotational and translational invariance. Finally a few astrophysical\n\
applications of color superconductivity are discussed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 5 Feb 2002 12:33:25 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 15 May 2002 09:48:47 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 21 Jun 2002 17:42:44 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-07-19", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Nardulli", "Giuseppe", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{2.30374610363968, -10.513564458671251`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph/0307111\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Hee-Jung Lee\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hee-Jung Lee, Byung-Yoon Park, Mannque Rho, Vicente Vento\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Pion Velocity in Dense Skyrmion Matter\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"11 pages, 4 figures; added references, changed \
content\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.A741:161-178,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysa.2004.06.010\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph nucl-th\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We have developed a field theory formalism to calculate \
$in$-$medium$\\nproperties of hadrons within a unified approach that exploits \
a single\\nLagrangian to describe simultaneously both matter background and \
meson\\nfluctuations. In this paper we discuss the consequences on physical \
observables\\nof a possible phase transition of hadronic matter taking place \
in the chiral\\nlimit. We pay special attention to the pion velocity \
$v_\\\\pi$, which controls,\\nthrough a dispersion relation, the pion \
propagation in the hadronic medium. The\\n$v_\\\\pi$ is defined in terms of \
parameters related to the matrix element in\\nmatter of the axial-vector \
current, namely, the in-medium pion decay constants,\\n$f_t$ and $f_s$. Both \
of the pion decay constants change dramatically with\\ndensity and even \
vanish in the chiral limit when chiral symmetry is restored,\\nbut the pion \
velocity does not go to zero, decreasing at most 10% over the\\nwhole density \
range studied. A possible pseudogap structure is indicated.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 8 Jul 2003 11:38:37 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 10 Jul 2003 16:09:34 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 11 May 2004 14:08:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Lee\"", ",", "\"Hee-Jung\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Park\"", ",", "\"Byung-Yoon\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Rho\"", ",", "\"Mannque\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
