         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-ph/0307111", "submitter" -> "Hee-Jung Lee", "authors" -> 
            "Hee-Jung Lee, Byung-Yoon Park, Mannque Rho, Vicente Vento", 
            "title" -> "The Pion Velocity in Dense Skyrmion Matter", 
            "comments" -> 
            "11 pages, 4 figures; added references, changed content", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.A741:161-178,2004", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysa.2004.06.010", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-ph nucl-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We have developed a field theory formalism to calculate \
$in$-$medium$\nproperties of hadrons within a unified approach that exploits \
a single\nLagrangian to describe simultaneously both matter background and \
meson\nfluctuations. In this paper we discuss the consequences on physical \
observables\nof a possible phase transition of hadronic matter taking place \
in the chiral\nlimit. We pay special attention to the pion velocity $v_\\pi$, \
which controls,\nthrough a dispersion relation, the pion propagation in the \
hadronic medium. The\n$v_\\pi$ is defined in terms of parameters related to \
the matrix element in\nmatter of the axial-vector current, namely, the \
in-medium pion decay constants,\n$f_t$ and $f_s$. Both of the pion decay \
constants change dramatically with\ndensity and even vanish in the chiral \
limit when chiral symmetry is restored,\nbut the pion velocity does not go to \
zero, decreasing at most 10% over the\nwhole density range studied. A \
possible pseudogap structure is indicated.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
