               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Andrei Kryjevski (INT, Washington) and Thomas Schaefer \
(North Carolina\\n  State and Riken-BNL)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"An Effective Theory for Baryons in the CFL Phase\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"12 pages, 2 figures; corrected Fig. 2; clarified \
eq.(23)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett. B606 (2005) 52-58\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2004.11.081\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"INT-PUB 04-18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the effective field theory for fermions in the \
color-flavor locked\\n(CFL) phase of high density QCD. The effective theory \
contains a flavor nonet\\nof baryons interacting with a nonet of pseudoscalar \
Goldstone bosons as well as\\na singlet scalar Goldstone boson. The theory is \
similar to chiral perturbation\\ntheory in the one-baryon sector. We explain \
how to incorporate quark mass terms\\nand study the spectrum as a function of \
the strange quark mass. Without meson\\ncondensation gapless baryon modes \
appears if the strange quark mass exceeds a\\ncritical value \
m_s^2/(2p_F)=Delta, where p_F is the Fermi momentum and Delta is\\nthe gap in \
the chiral limit. We show that kaon condensation leads to a\\nrearrangement \
of the baryon spectrum and shifts the critical strange quark mass\\nfor the \
appearance of a gapless mode to higher values.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
