               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph/0411346\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrea Beraudo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"W.M. Alberico, A. Beraudo and A. Molinari\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Meson correlation functions in a QCD plasma\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"35 pages, 15 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. A750 (2005) 359-390\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysa.2004.12.070\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The temporal pseudoscalar meson correlation function in \
a QCD plasma is\\ninvestigated in a range of temperatures exceeding $T_c$ and \
yet of experimental\\ninterest. Only the flavour-singlet channel is \
considered and the imaginary time\\nformalism is employed for the finite \
temperature calculations. The behaviour of\\nthe meson spectral function and \
of the temporal correlator is first studied in\\nthe HTL approximation, where \
one replaces the free thermal quark propagators\\nwith the HTL resummed ones. \
This procedure satisfactory describes the soft\\nfermionic modes, but its \
application to the propagation of hard quarks is not\\nreliable. An improved \
version of the so-called NLA scheme, which allows a\\nbetter treatment of the \
hard fermionic modes, is then proposed. The impact of\\nthe improved NLA on \
the pseudoscalar temporal correlator is investigated.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
