          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-ph/0512054", "submitter" -> "Cristina Manuel", 
            "authors" -> "Cristina Manuel", "title" -> 
            "Low energy properties of color-flavor locked superconductors", 
            "comments" -> 
            "13 pages, 1 figure; talk given at the 29th Johns Hopkins \
Workshop on\n  current problems in particle theory; August 2005, Budapest", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss some low energy properties of color-flavor locked \
(CFL)\nsuperconductors. First, we study how an external magnetic field \
affects their\nGoldstone physics in the chiral limit, stressing that there is \
a long-range\ncomponent of the field that penetrates the superconductor. We \
note that the\nmost remarkable effect of the applied field is giving a mass \
to the charged\npions and kaons. By estimating this effect, we see that for \
values $e B \\sim 2\nf_\\pi \\Delta$, where $\\Delta$ is the quark gap, and \
$f_\\pi$ the pion decay\nconstant, the charged Goldstone bosons become so \
heavy, that they turn out to\nbe unstable. The symmetry breaking pattern is \
then changed, agreeing with that\nof the magnetic color-flavor locked (MCFL) \
phase, recently proposed in\nhep-ph/0503162. Finally, we discuss the physics \
of the superfluid phonon of the\nCFL phase, compare it with that of the \
phonon of a Bose-Einstein condensate,\nand discuss transport phenomena at low \
temperature. Astrophysical implications\nof all the above low energy \
properties are also commented.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 5 Dec 2005 17:24:33 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2007-05-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Manuel", "Cristina", ""}}}], 
