                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.Lett. 97 (2006) 122301\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevLett.97.122301\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the effects of an external magnetic \
field in the gluon\\ndynamics of a color superconductor with three massless \
quark flavors. In the\\nframework of gluon mean-field theory at asymptotic \
densities, we show that the\\nlong-range component $\\\\widetilde{H}$ of the \
external magnetic field that\\npenetrates the CFL phase produces an \
instability when its strength becomes\\nlarger than the Meissner mass of the \
charged gluons. As a consequence, the\\nmagnetic field causes the formation \
of a vortex state characterized by the\\ncondensation of charged gluons and \
the creation of magnetic flux tubes. Inside\\nthe flux tubes the magnetic \
field is stronger than the applied one. This\\nantiscreening effect is \
connected to the anomalous magnetic moment of the gluon\\nfield. We suggest \
how this same mechanism could serve to remove the\\nchromomagnetic \
instabilities existing in gapless color superconductivity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
