               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a Nambu-Jona-Lasinio (NJL) type model with \
two-flavor quark matter\\nin $\\\\beta$-equilibrium. It turns out that the \
system develops instabilities in\\nthe dispersion relations of the diquark \
fields, i.e., the velocity squared\\n$v^2$ becomes negative in a certain \
region of the electron chemical potential.\\nThe critical point is the same \
as that of the chromomagnetic instability. The\\nresults imply the existence \
of spatially inhomogeneous diquark condensates in\\nthe genuine vacuum. We \
also discuss gauge equivalent classes between the\\ninhomogeneous diquark \
condensates and gluon condensates.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
