            "Strongly Coupled Quark-Gluon Plasma: The Status Report", 
            "comments" -> 
            "It is brief review of the field, in 14 pages, written for \
proceedings\n  of Continuous Advances in QCD, April 2006. As the progress is \
very rapid, it\n  includes several new papers which appeared between April \
and August. The\n  version 2 has more references and few statements get \
clarified better", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1142/9789812708267_0001", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  RHIC data have shown robust collective flows, strong jet and \
charm quenching,\nand charm flow.\n  Recently ``conical flows'' from damped \
jets were seen. Non-Abelian classical\nstrongly coupled plasmas were \
introduced and studied via molecular dynamics,\nwith first results for its \
transport (diffusion and viscosity) reported.\n  Quantum-mechanical studies \
reveal the survival for $T>T_c$ of the lowest\nbinary states, including \
colored ones, and also of some manybody ones such as\nbaryons. ``Polymeric \
chains'' $\\bar q.g.g... q$ are also bound in some range of\n$T$, perhaps the \
progenitors of the QCD strings.\n  AdS/CFT applications advanced to a \
completely new level of detail: they now\ninclude studies of thermal heavy \
quark motion, jet quenching and even conical\nflow. Confinement is however \
still beyond simply strong coupling: its de-facto\ninclusion the so called \
AdS/QCD approach is so far added as a model, while true\nunderstanding may \
probably only come from further insights into the monopole\ndynamics.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 16 Aug 2006 14:31:55 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 23 Aug 2006 16:55:08 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2017-08-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Shuryak", "E. V.", ""}}}], 
