            "  We discuss a two dimensional SU(N) Yang-Mills theory coupled \
to massive\nadjoint fermions for different worlds classified by the integer \
k=0,1,...N-1.\nWe study the fermion condensate for these unconnected worlds \
as a function of\nthe parameter k. We show that the condensate as well as the \
spectrum of the\ntheory do depend on this vacuum parameter k. Technically, \
the value of the\nfermion condensate is related to the value of the gluon \
condensate via the\nOperator Product Expansion. We use this to find the \
leading dependence (in the\nlimit of a heavy quark) of the fermion condensate \
on the nontrivial vacuum\nangle k. We also determine the gluon condensate of \
the theory using low-energy\ntheorems.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
