                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We demonstrate that, due to the finite thickness of \
domain walls, and the\\nconsequent ambiguity in defining their locations, the \
effective string\\ndescription obtained by integrating out bulk degrees of \
freedom contains\\nambiguities in the coefficients of the various geometric \
terms. The only term\\nwith unambiguous coefficient is the zeroth order \
Nambu-Goto term. We argue that\\nfermionic ghost fields which implement \
gauge-fixing act to balance these\\nambiguities. The renormalized string \
tension, obtained after integrating out\\nboth bulk and world-sheet degrees \
of freedom, can be defined in a scheme\\nindependent manner; and we compute \
the explicit finite expressions, to\\none-loop, for the case of compact \
quantum electrodynamics and phi-4 theory.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 4 Nov 1998 02:06:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-10-31\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Jaimungal\"", ",", "\"S.\"", ",", "\"\"", ",", 
                    "\"British Columbia U.\""}], "}"}], ",", 
