Freedom\n  in D-brane Matrix Models", "comments" -> 
            "15 pages, LaTeX, no figures, arguments on the action and \
symmetry are\n  improved", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Lett. B481 (2000) 97-106", 
            "doi" -> "10.1016/S0370-2693(00)00418-4", "report-no" -> 
            "KEK Preprint 99-160", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  It is known that when there are several D-branes, their \
space-time\ncoordinates in general become noncommutative. From the point of \
view of\nnoncommutative geometry, it reflects noncommutativity of the world \
volume of\nthe D-branes. On the other hand, as we showed in the previous \
work, in the\npresence of the constant antisymmetric tensor field the \
momentum operators of\nthe D-branes have noncommutative structure. In the \
present paper, we\ninvestigate a relation between these noncommutativities \
and the description of\nD-branes in terms of the noncommutative Yang-Mills \
theory recently proposed by\nSeiberg and Witten. It is shown that the \
noncommutativity of the Yang-Mills\ntheory, which implies that of the world \
volume coordinates, originates from\nboth noncommutativities of the \
transverse coordinates and momenta from the\nviewpoint of the \
lower-dimensional D-branes. Moreover, we show that this\nnoncommutativity is \
transformed by coordinate transformations on the world\nvolume and thereby \
can be chosen in an arbitrary fixed value. We also make a\nbrief comment on a \
relation between this fact and a hidden symmetry of the IIB\nmatrix models.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
