        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{12.910314782480604`, -3.2324976746542333`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0003032\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jacob Sonnenschein\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jacob Sonnenschein (TAU)\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"What does the string/gauge correspondence teach us about \
Wilson loops?\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lectures presented at Santiago de Compostela-99, 47 \
pages, 13 figs\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In these lectures we describe the attempt to extract \
the expectation values\\nof Wilson loops from the string/gauge \
correspondence. We start with the\\noriginal calculation in $AdS_5$. It is \
then extended to the non-conformal\\nbackground of $D_p$ in the near horizon \
limit. We discuss the computation at\\nfinite temperature. Supergravity \
models that admit confinement in 3d and 4d are\\ndescribed. A theorem that \
determines the classical values of loops associated\\nwith a generalized \
background is derived.In particular we determine sufficient\\nconditions for \
confining behavior. We then apply the theorem to various string\\nmodels \
including type 0 ones. We describe an attempt to go beyond the \
classical\\nstring picture by incorporating quadratic quantum fluctuations. \
In particular\\nwe address the BPS configuration of a single quark, the \
supersymmetric\\ndeterminant of $AdS_5\\\\times S^$ and a setup that \
corresponds to a confining\\ngauge theory. We determine the form of the \
Wilson loop for actions that include\\nnon trivial $B_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}$ field. \
The issue of an exact determination of the\\nvalue of the stringy Wilson loop \
is discussed. We end with a brief review of\\nthe baryons from the \
string/gauge correspondence Lectures presented in the\\n``Advanced School on \
Supersymmetry in the theories of fields, strings and\\nbranes'' Santiago de \
Compostela-99.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 4 Mar 2000 16:11:15 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2007-05-23\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Sonnenschein\"", ",", "\"Jacob\"", ",", "\"\"", ",", 
                    "\"TAU\""}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, 
