            "authors" -> "Jacob Sonnenschein (TAU)", "title" -> 
            "What does the string/gauge correspondence teach us about Wilson \
loops?", "comments" -> 
            "Lectures presented at Santiago de Compostela-99, 47 pages, 13 \
figs", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In these lectures we describe the attempt to extract the \
expectation values\nof Wilson loops from the string/gauge correspondence. We \
start with the\noriginal calculation in $AdS_5$. It is then extended to the \
non-conformal\nbackground of $D_p$ in the near horizon limit. We discuss the \
computation at\nfinite temperature. Supergravity models that admit \
confinement in 3d and 4d are\ndescribed. A theorem that determines the \
classical values of loops associated\nwith a generalized background is \
derived.In particular we determine sufficient\nconditions for confining \
behavior. We then apply the theorem to various string\nmodels including type \
0 ones. We describe an attempt to go beyond the classical\nstring picture by \
incorporating quadratic quantum fluctuations. In particular\nwe address the \
BPS configuration of a single quark, the supersymmetric\ndeterminant of \
$AdS_5\\times S^$ and a setup that corresponds to a confining\ngauge theory. \
We determine the form of the Wilson loop for actions that include\nnon \
trivial $B_{\\mu\\nu}$ field. The issue of an exact determination of the\n\
value of the stringy Wilson loop is discussed. We end with a brief review of\n\
the baryons from the string/gauge correspondence Lectures presented in the\n\
``Advanced School on Supersymmetry in the theories of fields, strings and\n\
branes'' Santiago de Compostela-99.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 4 Mar 2000 16:11:15 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2007-05-23", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Sonnenschein", "Jacob", "", "TAU"}}}], 
