            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0003208\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wolfgang Bietenholz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Ambjorn, K. N. Anagnostopoulos, W. Bietenholz, T. \
Hotta and J.\\n  Nishimura\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Large N Dynamics of Dimensionally Reduced 4D SU(N) Super \
Yang-Mills\\n  Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"35 pages, 17 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0007 (2000) 013\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2000/07/013\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"NBI-HE-00-14, NORDITA-2000/8-HE, UT-KOMABA 99-19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-lat\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We perform Monte Carlo simulations of a supersymmetric \
matrix model, which is\\nobtained by dimensional reduction of 4D SU(N) super \
Yang-Mills theory. The\\nmodel can be considered as a four-dimensional \
counterpart of the IIB matrix\\nmodel. We extract the space-time structure \
represented by the eigenvalues of\\nbosonic matrices. In particular we \
compare the large N behavior of the\\nspace-time extent with the result \
obtained from a low energy effective theory.\\nWe measure various Wilson loop \
correlators which represent string amplitudes\\nand we observe a nontrivial \
universal scaling in N. We also observe that the\\nEguchi-Kawai equivalence \
to ordinary gauge theory does hold at least within a\\nfinite range of scale. \
Comparison with the results for the bosonic case\\nclarifies the role of \
supersymmetry in the large N dynamics. It does affect the\\nmulti-point \
correlators qualitatively, but the Eguchi-Kawai equivalence is\\nobserved \
even in the bosonic case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 Mar 2000 16:30:47 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
