            "  We perform Monte Carlo simulations of a supersymmetric matrix \
model, which is\nobtained by dimensional reduction of 4D SU(N) super \
Yang-Mills theory. The\nmodel can be considered as a four-dimensional \
counterpart of the IIB matrix\nmodel. We extract the space-time structure \
represented by the eigenvalues of\nbosonic matrices. In particular we compare \
the large N behavior of the\nspace-time extent with the result obtained from \
a low energy effective theory.\nWe measure various Wilson loop correlators \
which represent string amplitudes\nand we observe a nontrivial universal \
scaling in N. We also observe that the\nEguchi-Kawai equivalence to ordinary \
gauge theory does hold at least within a\nfinite range of scale. Comparison \
with the results for the bosonic case\nclarifies the role of supersymmetry in \
the large N dynamics. It does affect the\nmulti-point correlators \
qualitatively, but the Eguchi-Kawai equivalence is\nobserved even in the \
bosonic case.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
