         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0003235", "submitter" -> "Fuchs Ehud", "authors" -> 
            "Ehud Fuchs", "title" -> 
            "The U(1)s in the Finite N Limit of Orbifold Field Theories", 
            "comments" -> "2+35 pages, 2 figures, LaTex", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0010 (2000) 028", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2000/10/028", 
            "report-no" -> "TAUP-2624-2000", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study theories generated by orbifolding the {\\cal N}=4 \
super conformal\nU(N) Yang Mills theory with finite N, focusing on the \
r\\^ole of the remnant\nU(1) gauge symmetries of the orbifold process. It is \
well known that the one\nloop beta functions of the non abelian SU(N) gauge \
couplings vanish in these\ntheories. It is also known that in the large N \
limit the beta functions vanish\nto all order in perturbation theory. We show \
that the beta functions of the non\nabelian SU(N) gauge couplings vanish to \
two and three loop order even for\nfinite N. This is the result of taking the \
abelian U(1) of U(N)=SU(N)xU(1) into\naccount. However, the abelian U(1) \
gauge couplings have a non vanishing beta\nfunction. Hence, those theories \
are not conformal for finite N. We analyze the\nrenormalization group flow of \
the orbifold theories, discuss the suppression of\nthe cosmological constant \
and tackle the hierarchy problem in the non\nsupersymmetric models.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 26 Mar 2000 17:37:50 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 31 Jul 2000 12:29:42 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
