               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0005128\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Lori D. Paniak\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"L.D. Paniak (Princeton) and R.J. Szabo (NBI)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fermionic Quantum Gravity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"59 pages LaTeX, 1 eps figure. Uses epsf. References \
and\\n  acknowledgments added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B593 (2001) 671-725\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00631-3\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUPT-1931, NBI-HE-00-23\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the statistical mechanics of random surfaces \
generated by NxN\\none-matrix integrals over anti-commuting variables. These \
Grassmann-valued\\nmatrix models are shown to be equivalent to NxN unitary \
versions of generalized\\nPenner matrix models. We explicitly solve for the \
combinatorics of 't Hooft\\ndiagrams of the matrix integral and develop an \
orthogonal polynomial\\nformulation of the statistical theory. An examination \
of the large N and double\\nscaling limits of the theory shows that the genus \
expansion is a Borel summable\\nalternating series which otherwise coincides \
with two-dimensional quantum\\ngravity in the continuum limit. We demonstrate \
that the partition functions of\\nthese matrix models belong to the \
relativistic Toda chain integrable hierarchy.\\nThe corresponding string \
equations and Virasoro constraints are derived and\\nused to analyse the \
generalized KdV flow structure of the continuum limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
