            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0005147\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jun Nishimura\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Ambjorn, K.N. Anagnostopoulos, W. Bietenholz, T. Hotta \
and J.\\n  Nishimura\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Monte Carlo Studies of the IIB Matrix Model at Large \
N\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages, LaTeX, 7 eps figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0007 (2000) 011\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2000/07/011\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"NBI-HE-00-24, NORDITA-2000/50-HE\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-lat\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The low-energy effective theory of the IIB matrix model \
developed by H. Aoki\\net al. is written down explicitly in terms of bosonic \
variables only. The\\neffective theory is then studied by Monte Carlo \
simulations in order to\\ninvestigate the possibility of a spontaneous \
breakdown of Lorentz invariance.\\nThe imaginary part of the effective \
action, which causes the so-called sign\\nproblem in the simulation, is \
dropped by hand. The extent of the eigenvalue\\ndistribution of the bosonic \
matrices shows a power-law large N behavior,\\nconsistent with a simple \
branched-polymer prediction. We observe, however, that\\nthe eigenvalue \
distribution becomes more and more isotropic in the\\nten-dimensional \
space-time as we increase N. This suggests that if the\\nspontaneous \
breakdown of Lorentz invariance really occurs in the IIB matrix\\nmodel, a \
crucial role must be played by the imaginary part of the \
effective\\naction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 16 May 2000 16:26:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-10-31\""}]}, {
