             "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  A previous calculation of the phase transition in the Wilson \
loop correlator\nin the zero temperature AdS/CFT correspondence is extended \
to the case where\nthe loops are concentric circles of unequal radii. This \
phase transition occurs\ndue to the instability of the classical string \
stretched between the loops. We\ncompute the string action and its expansion \
in the distance h between the loops\nfor small h. We also find that the \
connected minimal surface is subleading or\ndoes not even exist when h=0 and \
the radii are considerably different. This\nfeature has no analogue in flat \
space.\n", "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Tue, 26 Sep 2000 20:20:04 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2007-05-23", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Olesen", "P.", ""}, {
               "Zarembo", "K.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
