               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Dp-D(p+4) in Noncommutative Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"16 pages. v2 eq.(3.28) and typos corrected, ref. added v3 \
extended to\\n  25 pages including various examples and explanations v4 \
misleading comments\\n  on the instanton position are corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0103:033,2001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2001/03/033\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"KEK-TH 720\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  An anti-self-dual instanton solution in Yang-Mills \
theory on noncommutative\\n${\\\\R}^4$ with an anti-self-dual noncommutative \
parameter is constructed. The\\nsolution is constructed by the ADHM \
construction and it can be treated in the\\nframework of the IIB matrix \
model. In the IIB matrix model, this solution is\\ninterpreted as a system of \
a Dp-brane and D(p+4)-branes, with the Dp-brane\\ndissolved in the \
worldvolume of the D(p+4)-branes. The solution has a parameter\\nthat \
characterises the size of the instanton. The zero of this \
parameter\\ncorresponds to the singularity of the moduli space. At this \
point, the solution\\nis continuously connected to another solution which can \
be interpreted as a\\nsystem of a Dp-brane and D(p+4)-branes, with the \
Dp-brane separated from the\\nD(p+4)-branes. It is shown that even when the \
parameter of the solution comes\\nto the singularity of the moduli space, the \
gauge field itself is non-singular.\\nA class of multi-instanton solutions is \
also constructed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
