          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0011038\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ysuke Kimura\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Y. Kimura, Y. Kitazawa\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Supercurrent Interactions in Noncommutative Yang-Mills \
and IIB Matrix\\n  Model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"16 pages, LaTex, minor changes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B598 (2001) 73-86\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00785-9\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"KEK-TH-723, TIT/HEP-458\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It is known that noncommutative Yang-Mills is \
equivalent to IIB matrix model\\nwith a noncommutative background, which is \
interpreted as a twisted reduced\\nmodel. In noncommutative Yang-Mills, long \
range interactions can be seen in\\nnonplanar diagrams after integrating high \
momentum modes. These interactions\\ncan be understood as block-block \
interactions in the matrix model. Using this\\nrelation, we consider long \
range interactions in noncommutative Yang-Mills\\nassociated with fermionic \
backgrounds. Exchanges of gravitinos, which couple to\\na supersymmetry \
current, are examined.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
