            "Y. Kimura, Y. Kitazawa", "title" -> 
            "Supercurrent Interactions in Noncommutative Yang-Mills and IIB \
Matrix\n  Model", "comments" -> "16 pages, LaTex, minor changes", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys. B598 (2001) 73-86", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00785-9", "report-no" -> 
            "KEK-TH-723, TIT/HEP-458", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  It is known that noncommutative Yang-Mills is equivalent to \
IIB matrix model\nwith a noncommutative background, which is interpreted as a \
twisted reduced\nmodel. In noncommutative Yang-Mills, long range interactions \
can be seen in\nnonplanar diagrams after integrating high momentum modes. \
These interactions\ncan be understood as block-block interactions in the \
matrix model. Using this\nrelation, we consider long range interactions in \
noncommutative Yang-Mills\nassociated with fermionic backgrounds. Exchanges \
of gravitinos, which couple to\na supersymmetry current, are examined.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
