          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0101232\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Francesco Bigazzi\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"F. Bigazzi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"RG Flows Towards IR Isolated Fixed Points: Some Type 0 \
Samples\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"19 pages, LateX; version revised for publication in \
JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0106:068,2001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2001/06/068\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"FT-01-06\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We perform here a critical analysis of some \
non-supersymmetric gravity\\nsolutions in Type 0B string theory. We first \
consider the most general\\nconfiguration of parallel N electric and M \
magnetic D3-branes. The field theory\\nliving on their worldvolume is \
non-supersymmetric and non-conformal (if N is\\ndifferent from M) and has \
gauge group SU(N)XSU(M). We study the IR regime of\\nthe conjectured dual \
gravity background. A fine tuned solution exists with an\\nasymptotically \
vanishing tachyon and a running dilaton, which could correspond\\nto a flow \
towards an IR isolated fixed point at strong coupling. This opens \
the\\nquestion upon the possibility of extending AdS/CFT techniques to flows \
towards\\nIR isolated fixed points. We then use D3-branes as probes of this \
and other\\nType 0 backgrounds available in literature which cover the M=0 \
(or N=0) case.\\nWe shaw that for the fine tuned IR conformal solutions the \
stacks of parallel\\nbranes are plagued by instabilities, due to the \
repulsive force between branes\\nof the same type. Curiously, for a \
particular solution which could be dual to a\\nconfining gauge theory, the \
stack should instead be stable.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 31 Jan 2001 22:05:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 5 Feb 2001 12:17:34 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 23 Jul 2001 10:19:59 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2014-11-18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Bigazzi\"", ",", "\"F.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
