         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0101232", "submitter" -> "Francesco Bigazzi", 
            "authors" -> "F. Bigazzi", "title" -> 
            "RG Flows Towards IR Isolated Fixed Points: Some Type 0 Samples", 
            "comments" -> 
            "19 pages, LateX; version revised for publication in JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0106:068,2001", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2001/06/068", "report-no" -> "FT-01-06", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            
            "  We perform here a critical analysis of some non-supersymmetric \
gravity\nsolutions in Type 0B string theory. We first consider the most \
general\nconfiguration of parallel N electric and M magnetic D3-branes. The \
field theory\nliving on their worldvolume is non-supersymmetric and \
non-conformal (if N is\ndifferent from M) and has gauge group SU(N)XSU(M). We \
study the IR regime of\nthe conjectured dual gravity background. A fine tuned \
solution exists with an\nasymptotically vanishing tachyon and a running \
dilaton, which could correspond\nto a flow towards an IR isolated fixed point \
at strong coupling. This opens the\nquestion upon the possibility of \
extending AdS/CFT techniques to flows towards\nIR isolated fixed points. We \
then use D3-branes as probes of this and other\nType 0 backgrounds available \
in literature which cover the M=0 (or N=0) case.\nWe shaw that for the fine \
tuned IR conformal solutions the stacks of parallel\nbranes are plagued by \
instabilities, due to the repulsive force between branes\nof the same type. \
Curiously, for a particular solution which could be dual to a\nconfining \
gauge theory, the stack should instead be stable.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 31 Jan 2001 22:05:41 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 5 Feb 2001 12:17:34 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 23 Jul 2001 10:19:59 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-11-18", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Bigazzi", "F.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{12.52235203825817, -3.6069475960629767`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0101235\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DaeKil Park\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Hungsoo Kim, D. K. Park, S. Tamaryan, H.J.W. \
M\\\\\\\"uller-Kirsten\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gross-Ooguri Phase Transition at Zero and Finite \
Temperature: Two\\n  Circular Wilson Loop Case\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"13pages, 6 postscript figures, published version in \
JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0103:003,2001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2001/03/003\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In the context of $AdS/CFT$ correspondence the two \
Wilson loop correlator is\\nexamined at both zero and finite temperatures. On \
the basis of an entirely\\nanalytical approach we have found for Nambu-Goto \
strings the functional\\nrelation $d S_c^{(Reg)} / dL = 2 \\\\pi k$ between \
Euclidean action $S_c$ and loop\\nseparation $L$ with integration constant \
$k$, which corresponds to the\\nanalogous formula for point-particles. The \
physical implications of this\\nrelation are explored in particular for the \
Gross-Ooguri phase transition at\\nfinite temperature.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 31 Jan 2001 23:27:57 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 2 Mar 2001 16:52:37 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
