             "abstract" -> 
             "  We study the spectrum of massive excitations in \
three-dimensional models\nbelonging to the Ising universality class. By \
solving the Bethe-Salpeter\nequation for 3D $\\phi^4$ theory in the broken \
symmetry phase we show that\nrecently found non-perturbative states can be \
interpreted as bound states of\nthe fundamental excitation. We show that \
duality predicts an exact\ncorrespondence between the spectra of the Ising \
model in the broken symmetry\nphase and of the Z(2) gauge theory in the \
confining phase. The interpretation\nof the glueball states of the gauge \
theory as bound states of the dual spin\nsystem allows us to explain the \
qualitative features of the glueball spectrum,\nin particular, its peculiar \
angular momentum dependence.\n", 
