         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0105039", "submitter" -> "DaeKil Park", "authors" -> 
            "D. K. Park", "title" -> 
            "Hidden functional relation in Large-N Quark-Monopole system at \
finite\n  temperature", "comments" -> 
            "22 pages, 3 figures, v1 one more reference added v2 version to \
appear\n  in NPB", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys. B618 (2001) 157-170", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0550-3213(01)00484-9", "report-no" -> "MCTP-01-19", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The quark-monopole potential is computed at finite temperature \
in the context\nof $AdS/CFT$ correspondence. It is found that the potential \
is invariant under\n$g \\to 1/g$ and $U_T \\to U_T / g$. As in the \
quark-quark case there exists a\nmaximum separation between quark and \
monopole, and $L$-dependence of the\npotential exhibits a bifurcation \
behavior. We find a functional relation\n$dE_{QM}^{Reg} / dL = \
[(1/E_{(1,0)}^{Reg}(U_0))^2 +\n(1/E_{(0,1)}^{Reg}(U_0))^2]^{-1/2}$ which is \
responsible for the bifurcation.\nThe remarkable property of this relation is \
that it makes a relation between\nphysical quantities defined at the $AdS$ \
boundary through a quantity defined at\nthe bulk. The physical implication of \
this relation for the existence of the\nextra dimension is speculated.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 3 May 2001 19:12:18 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 18 Jun 2001 19:55:22 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 26 Sep 2001 15:58:27 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-07", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Park", "D. K.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
