                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"NSF-ITP-01-46, SLAC-PUB-8843, WIS/10/01-MAY-DPP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose that a novel deformation of string \
perturbation theory, involving\\nnon-local interactions between strings, is \
required to describe the gravity\\nduals of field theories deformed by \
multiple-trace operators. The new\\nperturbative expansion involves a new \
parameter, which is neither the string\\ncoupling nor the coefficient of a \
vertex operator on the worldsheet. We explore\\nsome of the properties of \
this deformation, focusing on a special case where\\nthe deformation in the \
field theory is exactly marginal.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
