             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0106015\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Zarembo\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Gordon W. Semenoff, K. Zarembo\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"More exact predictions of SUSYM for string theory\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"14 pages, 3 figures; v2: misprints corrected\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Nucl.Phys. B616 (2001) 34-46\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(01)00455-2\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ITEP-TH-28/01\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We compute the coefficients of an infinite family of \
chiral primary operators\\nin the local operator expansion of a circular \
Wilson loop in N=4 supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills theory. The computation sums \
all planar rainbow Feynman graphs. We\\nargue that radiative corrections from \
planar graphs with internal vertices\\ncancel in leading orders and we \
conjecture that they cancel to all orders in\\nperturbation theory. The \
coefficients are non-trivial functions of the 'tHooft\\ncoupling and their \
strong coupling limits are in exact agreement with those\\npreviously \
computed using the AdS/CFT correspondence. They predict the\\nsubleading \
orders in strong coupling and could in principle be compared with\\nstring \
theory calculations.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
