             "  We compute the coefficients of an infinite family of chiral \
primary operators\nin the local operator expansion of a circular Wilson loop \
in N=4 supersymmetric\nYang-Mills theory. The computation sums all planar \
rainbow Feynman graphs. We\nargue that radiative corrections from planar \
graphs with internal vertices\ncancel in leading orders and we conjecture \
that they cancel to all orders in\nperturbation theory. The coefficients are \
non-trivial functions of the 'tHooft\ncoupling and their strong coupling \
limits are in exact agreement with those\npreviously computed using the \
AdS/CFT correspondence. They predict the\nsubleading orders in strong \
coupling and could in principle be compared with\nstring theory calculations.\
\n", "versions" -> {{
