          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0106178\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Robert C. Myers\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Robert C. Myers\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonabelian D-branes and Noncommutative Geometry\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, Latex, ref. added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Math.Phys.42:2781-2797,2001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1142/S0217751X01004037\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the nonabelian world-volume action which \
governs the dynamics of N\\ncoincident Dp-branes. In this theory, the branes' \
transverse displacements are\\ndescribed by matrix-valued scalar fields, and \
so this is a natural physical\\nframework for the appearance of \
noncommutative geometry. One example is the\\ndielectric effect by which \
Dp-branes may be polarized into a noncommutative\\ngeometry by external \
fields. Another example is the appearance of\\nnoncommutative geometries in \
the description of intersecting D-branes of\\ndiffering dimensions, such as \
D-strings ending on a D3- or D5-brane. We also\\ndescribe the related physics \
of giant gravitons.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
