         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0106178", "submitter" -> "Robert C. Myers", 
            "authors" -> "Robert C. Myers", "title" -> 
            "Nonabelian D-branes and Noncommutative Geometry", "comments" -> 
            "21 pages, Latex, ref. added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J.Math.Phys.42:2781-2797,2001", "doi" -> 
            "10.1142/S0217751X01004037", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss the nonabelian world-volume action which governs \
the dynamics of N\ncoincident Dp-branes. In this theory, the branes' \
transverse displacements are\ndescribed by matrix-valued scalar fields, and \
so this is a natural physical\nframework for the appearance of noncommutative \
geometry. One example is the\ndielectric effect by which Dp-branes may be \
polarized into a noncommutative\ngeometry by external fields. Another example \
is the appearance of\nnoncommutative geometries in the description of \
intersecting D-branes of\ndiffering dimensions, such as D-strings ending on a \
D3- or D5-brane. We also\ndescribe the related physics of giant gravitons.\n",
             "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 19 Jun 2001 23:21:59 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 27 Jun 2001 21:25:00 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
