        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{5.324741261335987, -1.6415029100592493`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0107251\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A. Konechny, A. Schwarz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Introduction to M(atrix) theory and noncommutative \
geometry, Part II\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"34 pages, Latex\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rept. 360 (2002) 353-465\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0370-1573(01)00096-5\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This review paper is a continuation of hep-th/0012145 \
and it deals primarily\\nwith noncommutative ${\\\\mathbb R}^{d}$ spaces. We \
start with a discussion of\\nvarious algebras of smooth functions on \
noncommutative ${\\\\mathbb R}^{d}$ that\\nhave different asymptotic behavior \
at infinity. We pay particular attention to\\nthe differences arising when \
working with nonunital algebras and the unitized\\nones obtained by adjoining \
the unit element. After introducing main objects of\\nnoncommutative geometry \
over those algebras such as inner products, modules,\\nconnections, etc., we \
continue with a study of soliton and instanton solutions\\nin field theories \
defined on these spaces. The discussion of solitons includes\\nthe basic \
facts regarding the exact soliton solutions in the Yang-Mills-Higgs\\nsystems \
as well as an elementary discussion of approximate solitons in \
scalar\\ntheories in the $\\\\theta \\\\to \\\\infty$ limit. We concentrate \
on the module\\nstructure and topological numbers characterizing the \
solitons. The section on\\ninstantons contains a thorough description of \
noncommutative ADHM construction,\\na discussion of gauge triviality \
conditions at infinity and the structure of a\\nmodule underlying the ADHM \
instanton solution. Although some familiarity with\\ngeneral ideas of \
noncommutative geometry reviewed in the first part is expected\\nfrom the \
reader, this part is largely independent from the first one.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
