            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0108075\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Eva Silverstein\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A. Adams, J. Polchinski, and E. Silverstein\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Don't Panic! Closed String Tachyons in ALE \
Spacetimes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"48 pages, harvmac big; 13 figures. v2: added references; \
comment on\\n  gravity regime added to section 5.2. v3: added \
references\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0110:029,2001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2001/10/029\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"NSF-ITP-01-75, SLAC-PUB-8955\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider closed string tachyons localized at the \
fixed points of\\nnoncompact nonsupersymmetric orbifolds. We argue that \
tachyon condensation\\ndrives these orbifolds to flat space or supersymmetric \
ALE spaces. The decay\\nproceeds via an expanding shell of dilaton gradients \
and curvature which\\ninterpolates between two regions of distinct angular \
geometry. The string\\ncoupling remains weak throughout. For small tachyon \
VEVs, evidence comes from\\nquiver theories on D-branes probes, in which \
deformations by twisted couplings\\nsmoothly connect non-supersymmetric \
orbifolds to supersymmetric orbifolds of\\nreduced order. For large tachyon \
VEVs, evidence comes from worldsheet RG flow\\nand spacetime gravity. For $\\\
\\IC^2/\\\\IZ_n$, we exhibit infinite sequences of\\ntransitions producing \
SUSY ALE spaces via twisted closed string condensation\\nfrom \
non-supersymmetric ALE spaces. In a $T$-dual description this provides \
a\\nmechanism for creating NS5-branes via {\\\\it closed} string tachyon \
condensation\\nsimilar to the creation of D-branes via {\\\\it open} string \
tachyon condensation.\\nWe also apply our results to recent duality \
conjectures involving fluxbranes\\nand the type 0 string.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
