         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0108140", "submitter" -> "Arkady Tseytlin", 
            "authors" -> "A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Magnetic backgrounds and tachyonic instabilities in closed \
string theory", "comments" -> 
            "12 pages, latex. Contribution to the proceedings of the 10-th \
Tohwa\n  International Symposium on String Theory, Fukuoka, Japan, July 3-7, \
2001; v2:\n  references added", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
            "10.1063/1.1454381", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss some aspects of closed superstrings in Melvin-type \
magnetic\nbackgrounds. A 2-parameter family of such NS-NS backgrounds are \
exactly\nsolvable as weakly coupled string models with the spectrum \
containing tachyonic\nmodes. Magnetic field allows one to interpolate between \
free superstring\ntheories with periodic and antiperiodic boundary conditions \
for the space-time\nfermions around some compact direction, and, in \
particular, between type 0 and\ntype II string theories. Using ``9-11'' flip, \
this interpolation can be\nextended to M-theory and may be used to study the \
issue of tachyon in type 0\nstring theory. We review, following \
hep-th/0104238, related duality proposals,\nand, in particular, consider a \
description of type 0 theory in terms of\nM-theory in a curved magnetic flux \
background in which the type 0 tachyon\nappears to correspond to a state in \
$d=11$ supergravity fluctuation spectrum.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 20 Aug 2001 09:26:58 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 29 Aug 2001 07:30:25 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-07", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Tseytlin", "A. A.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
