               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1002/1521-3978(200203)50:3/4<221::AID-PROP221>3.0.CO;2-\
P\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This review is devoted to strings and branes. Firstly, \
perturbative string\\ntheory is introduced. The appearance of various types \
of branes is discussed.\\nThese include orbifold fixed planes, D-branes and \
orientifold planes. The\\nconnection to BPS vacua of supergravity is \
presented afterwards. As\\napplications, we outline the role of branes in \
string dualities, field theory\\ndualities, the AdS/CFT correspondence and \
scenarios where the string scale is\\nat a TeV. Some issues of warped \
compactifications are also addressed. These\\ncomprise corrections to \
gravitational interactions as well as the cosmological\\nconstant problem.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
