                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"  We consider Schwinger type processes involving the \
creation of the charge and\\nmonopole pairs in the external fields and \
propose interpretation of these\\nprocesses via corresponding brane \
configurations in Type IIB string theory. We\\nsuggest simple description of \
some new interesting nonperturbative processes\\nlike monopole/dyon \
transitions in the electric field and W-boson decay in the\\nmagnetic field \
using the brane language. Nonperturbative pair production in the\\nstrong \
coupling regime using the AdS/CFT correspondence is studied. The\\ntreatment \
of the similar processes in the noncommutative theories \
when\\nnoncommutativity is traded for the background fields is presented and \
the\\npossible role of the critical magnetic field which is S-dual to the \
critical\\nelectric field is discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
