            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0201018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Euro Spallucci\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"S. Ansoldi, C. Castro, E.I. Guendelman, \
E.Spallucci\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nambu-Goto Strings from SU(N) Born-Infeld model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"11pages, no figures, LateX2e; added discussion\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Class.Quant.Grav.19:L135-3570,2002\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/0264-9381/19/14/103\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The spectrum of quenched Yang-Mills theory in the \
large-N limit displays\\nstrings and higher dimensional extended objects. The \
effective dynamics of\\nstring-like excitations is encoded into area \
preserving Schild action. In this\\nletter, we bridge the gap between SU(N) \
gauge models and fully\\nreparametrization invariant Nambu-Goto string models \
by introducing an extra\\nmatrix degree of freedom in the Yang-Mills action. \
In the large-N limit this\\nmatrix variable becomes the world-sheet auxiliary \
field allowing a smooth\\ntransition between the Schild and Nambu-Goto \
strings. The new improved matrix\\nmodel we propose here can be extended to \
p-branes provided we enlarge the\\ndimensionality of the target spacetime.\\n\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
