               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0202148\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mahbub Majumdar\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mahbub Majumdar, Anne-Christine Davis\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Cosmological Creation of D-branes and \
anti-D-branes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages, 5 eps figures; v2 more references added; v3 \
section 4\\n  slightly improved\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0203 (2002) 056\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2002/03/056\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DAMTP 2002-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We argue that the early universe may be described by an \
initial state of\\nspace-filling branes and anti-branes. At high temperature \
this system is\\nstable. At low temperature tachyons appear and lead to a \
phase transition,\\ndynamics, and the creation of D-branes. These branes are \
cosmologically\\nproduced in a generic fashion by the Kibble mechanism. From \
an entropic point\\nof view, the formation of lower dimensional branes is \
preferred and $D3$\\nbrane-worlds are exponentially more likely to form than \
higher dimensional\\nbranes. Virtually any brane configuration can be created \
from such phase\\ntransitions by adjusting the tachyon profile. A lower bound \
on the number\\ndefects produced is: one D-brane per Hubble volume.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
