           "id" -> "hep-th/0204182", "submitter" -> "Carlos Castro", 
            "authors" -> "Carlos Castro", "title" -> 
            "On Wilson Loops and Confinement without Supersymmetry from \
Composite\n  Antisymmeric Tensor Field theories", "comments" -> 
            "8 pages, plain Tex", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  A novel approach that does not rely on supersymmetry, nor in \
the AdS/CFT\ncorrespondence, to evaluate the Wilson loops asociated with a \
gauge theory of\narea-preserving diffeomorphisms in terms of pure string \
degrees of freedoms is\npresented. It is based on the \
Guendelman-Nissimov-Pacheva formulation of\ncomposite antisymmetric tensor \
field theories of volume-preserving\ndiffeomorphisms. Such theories admit \
p-brane solutions. The quantum effects are\ndiscussed and we evaluate exactly \
the vev of the Wilson loops, in the large N\nlimit of quenched-reduced SU(N) \
QCD, in terms of a path integral involving pure\nstring degrees of freedom. \
It is consistent with the recent results based on\nthe AdS/CFT correspondence \
and dual QCD models (dual Higgs model with dual\nDirac strings). More general \
Loop wave equations in C-spaces (Clifford\nmanifolds) are proposed in terms \
of holographic variables that contain the\ndynamics of an aggregate of closed \
branes (p-loops) of various\ndimensionalities.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 22 Apr 2002 15:28:43 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2007-05-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Castro", "Carlos", ""}}}], 
