                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  I construct 1/16, 1/8 and 1/4 BPS Wilson loops in N=4 \
supersymmetric\\nYang-Mills theory and argue that expectation values of 1/4 \
BPS loops do not\\nreceive quantum corrections. At strong coupling, \
non-renormalization of\\nsupersymmetric Wilson loops implies subtle \
cancellations in the partition\\nfunction of the AdS string with special \
boundary conditions. The cancellations\\nare shown to occur in the \
semiclassical approximation.\\n\""}]}, {
