               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A. Bassetto and F. Vian\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wilson line correlators in two-dimensional noncommutative \
Yang-Mills\\n  theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, 1 figure, typeset in JHEP style; some formulas \
corrected in\\n  Sect.3, one reference added, results unchanged\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0210 (2002) 004\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2002/10/004\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DFPD 02/TH 19\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the correlator of two parallel Wilson lines in \
two-dimensional\\nnoncommutative Yang-Mills theory, following two different \
approaches. We first\\nconsider a perturbative expansion in the large-N limit \
and resum all planar\\ndiagrams. The second approach is non-perturbative: we \
exploit the Morita\\nequivalence, mapping the two open lines on the \
noncommutative torus (which\\neventually gets decompacted) in two closed \
Wilson loops winding around the dual\\ncommutative torus. Planarity allows us \
to single out a suitable region of the\\nvariables involved, where a \
saddle-point approximation of the general Morita\\nexpression for the \
correlator can be performed. In this region the correlator\\nnicely compares \
with the perturbative result, exhibiting an exponential\\nincrease with \
respect to the momentum p.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
