            "A note on twist two operators in N=4 SYM and Wilson loops in \
Minkowski\n  signature", "comments" -> 
            "16 pages, 4 figures, LaTeX. v2: References added. Some \
corrections", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0212:024,2002", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2002/12/024", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently the anomalous dimension of twist two operators in N=4 \
SYM theory was\ncomputed by Gubser, Klebanov and Polyakov in the limit of \
large 't Hooft\ncoupling using semi-classical rotating strings in AdS_5. Here \
we reproduce\ntheir results for large angular momentum by using the cusp \
anomaly of Wilson\nloops in Minkowski signature also computed within the \
AdS/CFT correspondence.\nIn this case the anomalous dimension is related to \
an Euclidean worldsheet\nwhose properties are completely determined by the \
symmetries of the problem.\nThis gives support to the proposed identification \
of rotating strings and twist\ntwo operators.\n", 
