               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0210157\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Douglas J. Smith\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Douglas J. Smith\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Intersecting brane solutions in string and \
M-theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"85 pages. Prepared as a Topical Review for Classical and \
Quantum\\n  Gravity. v2 Added references. v3 Added a short discussion of \
entropy of\\n  non-SUSY (but extremal or classically BPS) black holes to \
section 4.2.2. Also\\n  added/updated references\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Class.Quant.Grav.20:R233,2003\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/0264-9381/20/9/203\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"DTP/02/67\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review various aspects of configurations of \
intersecting branes, including\\nthe conditions for preservation of \
supersymmetry. In particular, we discuss the\\nprojection conditions on the \
Killing spinors for given brane configurations and\\nthe relation to \
calibrations. This highlights the close connection between\\nintersecting \
branes and branes wrapping supersymmetric cycles as well as\\nspecial \
holonomy manifolds. We also explain how these conditions can be used \
to\\nfind supergravity solutions without directly solving the Einstein \
equations.\\nThe description of intersecting branes is considered both in \
terms of the brane\\nworldvolume theories and as supergravity solutions. \
There are well-known simple\\nprocedures (harmonic function rules) for \
writing down the supergravity\\nsolutions for supersymmetric configurations \
of orthogonally intersecting\\nbranes. However, such solutions involve \
smeared or delocalised branes. We\\ndescribe several methods of constructing \
solutions with less smearing,\\nincluding some fully localised solutions. \
Some applications of these\\nsupergravity solutions are also considered - in \
particular the study of black\\nholes and gauge theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
