                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0212208\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Joseph A. Minahan\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"J. A. Minahan and K. Zarembo (Uppsala)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"The Bethe-Ansatz for N=4 Super Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"35 pages, 3 figures, LaTeX; v2 references added, typos \
corrected,\\n  \\\\Lambda fixed; v3 expanded discussion of higher loops in \
conclusion, matches\\n  published version\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0303 (2003) 013\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2003/03/013\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"UUITP-17/02, ITEP-TH-73/02\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We derive the one loop mixing matrix for anomalous \
dimensions in N=4 Super\\nYang-Mills. We show that this matrix can be \
identified with the Hamiltonian of\\nan integrable SO(6) spin chain with \
vector sites. We then use the Bethe ansatz\\nto find a recipe for computing \
anomalous dimensions for a wide range of\\noperators. We give exact results \
for BMN operators with two impurities and\\nresults up to and including first \
order 1/J corrections for BMN operators with\\nmany impurities. We then use a \
result of Reshetikhin's to find the exact\\none-loop anomalous dimension for \
an SO(6) singlet in the limit of large bare\\ndimension. We also show that \
this last anomalous dimension is proportional to\\nthe square root of the \
string level in the weak coupling limit.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
