           "id" -> "hep-th/0212235", "submitter" -> "David Tong", "authors" -> 
            "David Tong", "title" -> 
            "Comments on Condensates in Non-Supersymmetric Orbifold Field \
Theories", "comments" -> 
            "10 Pages. Added clarifying comments, computational steps and a \
nice\n  pretty picture", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0303 (2003) 022", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2003/03/022", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Non-supersymmetric orbifolds of N=1 super Yang-Mills theories \
are conjectured\nto inherit properties from their supersymmetric parent. We \
examine this\nconjecture by compactifying the Z_2 orbifold theories on a \
spatial circle of\nradius R. We point out that when the orbifold theory lies \
in the weakly coupled\nvacuum of its parent, fractional instantons do give \
rise to the conjectured\ncondensate of bi-fundamental fermions. \
Unfortunately, we show that quantum\neffects render this vacuum unstable \
through the generation of twisted\noperators. In the true vacuum state, no \
fermion condensate forms. Thus, in\ncontrast to super Yang-Mills, the \
compactified orbifold theory undergoes a\nchiral phase transition as R is \
varied.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 19 Dec 2002 12:50:45 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 25 Mar 2003 16:24:04 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-07", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Tong", "David", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
