            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0301099\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Adi Armoni\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Adi Armoni, Esperanza Lopez, Angel M. Uranga\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Closed Strings Tachyons and Non-Commutative Instabilities\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"27 pages, Latex. v2: Comment about anomalies and refs. \
added. Version\\n  published in JHEP. v3: minor changes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0302:020,2003\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2003/02/020\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"CERN-TH/2002-386, IFT UAM-CSIC/02-58, FT-UAM-02/33\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We observe a relation between closed strings tachyons \
and one-loop\\ninstabilities in non-supersymmetric non-commutative gauge \
theories. In\\nparticular we analyze the spectra of type IIB string theory on \
C^3/Z_N orbifold\\nsingularities and the non-commutative field theory that \
lives on D3 branes\\nlocated at the singularity. We find a surprising \
correspondence between the\\nexistence or not of one-loop low-momentum \
instabilities in the non-commutative\\nfield theory and the existence or not \
of tachyons in the closed string twisted\\nsectors. Moreover, the relevant \
piece of the non-commutative field theory\\neffective action is suggestive of \
an exchange of closed string modes. This\\nsuggests that non-commutative \
field theories retain some information about the\\ndynamics of the underlying \
string configuration. Finally, we also comment on a\\npossible relation \
between closed string tachyon condensation and field theory\\ntachyon \
condensation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
