            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We observe a relation between closed strings tachyons and \
one-loop\ninstabilities in non-supersymmetric non-commutative gauge theories. \
In\nparticular we analyze the spectra of type IIB string theory on C^3/Z_N \
orbifold\nsingularities and the non-commutative field theory that lives on D3 \
branes\nlocated at the singularity. We find a surprising correspondence \
between the\nexistence or not of one-loop low-momentum instabilities in the \
non-commutative\nfield theory and the existence or not of tachyons in the \
closed string twisted\nsectors. Moreover, the relevant piece of the \
non-commutative field theory\neffective action is suggestive of an exchange \
of closed string modes. This\nsuggests that non-commutative field theories \
retain some information about the\ndynamics of the underlying string \
configuration. Finally, we also comment on a\npossible relation between \
closed string tachyon condensation and field theory\ntachyon condensation.\n",
