               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0303072\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Robert C. Myers\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Robert C. Myers\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonabelian Phenomena on D-branes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lecture at Leuven workshop on ``The quantum structure of \
spacetime\\n  and the geometrical nature of fundamental interactions'' \
(September 13-19,\\n  2002); ref.'s added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Class.Quant.Grav. 20 (2003) S347-S372\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/0264-9381/20/12/302\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A remarkable feature of D-branes is the appearance of a \
nonabelian gauge\\ntheory in the description of several (nearly) coincident \
branes. This\\nnonabelian structure plays an important role in realizing \
various geometric\\neffects with D-branes. In particular, the branes' \
transverse displacements are\\ndescribed by matrix-valued scalar fields and \
so noncommutative geometry\\nnaturally appears in this framework. I review \
the action governing this\\nnonabelian theory, as well as various related \
physical phenomena such as the\\ndielectric effect, giant gravitons and fuzzy \
funnels.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 8 Mar 2003 13:53:16 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
