Background Magnetic\\n  Fields\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"9 Pages AMSTeX; Typos corrected\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Lett. B569 (2003) 95-101\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2003.07.020\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"HWM-03-6, EMPG-03-06, UUITP-02/03\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We obtain the exact non-perturbative solution of a \
scalar field theory\\ndefined on a space with noncommuting position and \
momentum coordinates. The\\nmodel describes non-locally interacting charged \
particles in a background\\nmagnetic field. It is an exactly solvable quantum \
field theory which has\\nnon-trivial interactions only when it is defined \
with a finite ultraviolet\\ncutoff. We propose that small perturbations of \
this theory can produce solvable\\nmodels with renormalizable \
interactions.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
