           "id" -> "hep-th/0303141", "submitter" -> "Wang Xiao-jun", 
            "authors" -> "Xiao-Jun Wang and Sen Hu", "title" -> 
            "Confinement of N=1 Super Yang-Mills from Supergravity", 
            "comments" -> "use revtex4.cls, 8 pages, 4 eps figs", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate circular Wilson loop expectation value of pure ${\
\\cal N}=1$\nsuper Yang-Mills from the Klebanov-Strassker-Tseytlin solution \
of supergravity\nand the proposed gauge/gravity duality. The calculation is \
performed\nnumerically via searching world-sheet minimal surface. It is shown \
that Wilson\nloop exhibits area law for large radius which implies that \
${\\cal N}=1$ super\nYang-Mills is confined at large distance or low energy \
scale. Meanwhile, Wilson\nloop exhibits logarithmic behavior for small radius \
and it indicates\nasymptotical freedom of ${\\cal N}=1$ super Yang-Mills at \
short distance or high\nenergy scale.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
