         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0304062", "submitter" -> "Gautam Mandal", 
            "authors" -> "Avinash Dhar, Gautam Mandal and Spenta R. Wadia", 
            "title" -> 
            "String bits in small radius AdS and weakly coupled N=4 Super \
Yang-Mills\n  Theory: I", "comments" -> 
            "35 pages; (v2)problems in taking the continuum limit \
highlighted, the\n  section on AdS/CFT matching rewritten in the light of \
these problems, typos\n  corrected and references added; the main conclusion \
about finiteness of the\n  small radius expansion unchanged", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> "TIFR/TH/03-09", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study light-cone gauge quantization of IIB strings in AdS_5 \
\\times S^5 for\nsmall radius in Poincare coordinates. A picture of strings \
made up of\nnoninteracting bits emerges in the zero radius limit. In this \
limit, each bit\nbehaves like a superparticle moving in the AdS_5 \\times S^5 \
background,\ncarrying appropriate representations of the super conformal \
group PSU(2,2|4).\nThe standard Hamiltonian operator which causes evolution \
in the light-cone time\nhas continuous eigenvalues and provides a basis of \
states which is not suitable\nfor comparing with the dual super Yang-Mills \
theory. However, there exist\noperators in the light-cone gauge which have \
discrete spectra and can be used\nto label the states. We obtain the spectrum \
of single bit states and construct\nmulti-bit states in this basis. There are \
difficulties in the construction of\nstring states from the multi-bit states, \
which we discuss. A non-zero value of\nthe radius introduces interactions \
between the bits and the spectrum of\nmulti-bit states gets modified. We \
compute the leading perturbative corrections\nat small radius for a few \
simple cases. Potential divergences in the\nperturbative corrections, arising \
from strings near the boundary, cancel. This\nencourages us to believe that \
our perturbative treatment could provide a\nframework for a rigorous and \
detailed testing of the AdS/CFT conjecture, once\nthe difficulties in the \
construction of string states are resolved.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 7 Apr 2003 15:00:35 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 7 Oct 2003 07:21:16 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2007-05-23", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Dhar", "Avinash", ""}, {
              "Mandal", "Gautam", ""}, {"Wadia", "Spenta R.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
