          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0304139\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arkady Tseytlin\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On semiclassical approximation and spinning string vertex \
operators in\\n  AdS_5 x S^5\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages, harvmac; v2: references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B664:247-275,2003\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(03)00456-5\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Following earlier work by Polyakov and Gubser, Klebanov \
and Polyakov, we\\nattempt to clarify the structure of vertex operators \
representing string states\\nwhich have large (``semiclassical'') values of \
AdS energy (equal to 4-d\\ndimension \\\\Delta) and angular momentum J in S^5 \
or spin S in AdS_5. We comment\\non the meaning of semiclassical limit in the \
context of \\\\alpha' perturbative\\nexpansion for the 2-d anomalous \
dimensions of the corresponding vertex\\noperators. We consider in detail the \
leading-order 1-loop renormalization of\\nthese operators in AdS_5 x S^5 \
sigma model (ignoring fermionic contributions).\\nWe find new examples of \
operators for which, as in the case considered in\\nhep-th/0110196, the \
1-loop anomalous dimension can be made small by tuning\\nquantum numbers. We \
also comment on a possibility of deriving the semiclassical\\nrelation \
between \\\\Delta and J or S from the marginality condition for the\\nvertex \
operators, using a stationary phase approximation in the path \
integral\\nexpression for their 2-point correlator on a complex \
plane.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 16 Apr 2003 15:08:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 26 Apr 2003 18:32:51 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-09-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Tseytlin\"", ",", "\"A. A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
