           "id" -> "hep-th/0304139", "submitter" -> "Arkady Tseytlin", 
            "authors" -> "A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "On semiclassical approximation and spinning string vertex \
operators in\n  AdS_5 x S^5", "comments" -> 
            "35 pages, harvmac; v2: references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B664:247-275,2003", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0550-3213(03)00456-5", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Following earlier work by Polyakov and Gubser, Klebanov and \
Polyakov, we\nattempt to clarify the structure of vertex operators \
representing string states\nwhich have large (``semiclassical'') values of \
AdS energy (equal to 4-d\ndimension \\Delta) and angular momentum J in S^5 or \
spin S in AdS_5. We comment\non the meaning of semiclassical limit in the \
context of \\alpha' perturbative\nexpansion for the 2-d anomalous dimensions \
of the corresponding vertex\noperators. We consider in detail the \
leading-order 1-loop renormalization of\nthese operators in AdS_5 x S^5 sigma \
model (ignoring fermionic contributions).\nWe find new examples of operators \
for which, as in the case considered in\nhep-th/0110196, the 1-loop anomalous \
dimension can be made small by tuning\nquantum numbers. We also comment on a \
possibility of deriving the semiclassical\nrelation between \\Delta and J or \
S from the marginality condition for the\nvertex operators, using a \
stationary phase approximation in the path integral\nexpression for their \
2-point correlator on a complex plane.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 16 Apr 2003 15:08:10 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 26 Apr 2003 18:32:51 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
