             "abstract" -> 
            "  Attempts to solve Yang-Mills theory must eventually face the \
problem of\nanalyzing the theory at intermediate values of the coupling \
constant. In this\nregime neither perturbation theory nor the gravity dual \
are adequate, and one\nmust consider the full string theory in the \
appropriate background. We suggest\nthat in some nontrivial cases the world \
sheet theory may be exactly solvable.\nFor the Green-Schwarz superstring on \
AdS_5 x S^5 we find an infinite set of\nnonlocal classically conserved \
charges, of the type that exist in integrable\nfield theories.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
