        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{13.01037617646076, -5.467173322935705}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0305196\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Mikhailov\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Mikhailov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonlinear waves in AdS/CFT correspondence\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"15 pages, Latex, 9 Postscript figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NSF-KITP-03-38\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math.DG\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate in the strong coupling and large N limit \
the energy emitted by\\nan accelerated external charge in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ \
SU(N) Yang-Mills theory, using\\nthe AdS/CFT correspondence. We find that the \
energy is a local functional of\\nthe trajectory of the charge. It coincides \
up to an overall factor with the\\nLienard formula of the classical \
electrodynamics. In the AdS description the\\nradiated energy is carried by a \
nonlinear wave on the string worldsheet for\\nwhich we find an exact \
solution.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
