         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0305196", "submitter" -> "Andrei Mikhailov", 
            "authors" -> "Andrei Mikhailov", "title" -> 
            "Nonlinear waves in AdS/CFT correspondence", "comments" -> 
            "15 pages, Latex, 9 Postscript figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, 
            "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> "NSF-KITP-03-38", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math.DG", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate in the strong coupling and large N limit the \
energy emitted by\nan accelerated external charge in ${\\cal N}=4$ SU(N) \
Yang-Mills theory, using\nthe AdS/CFT correspondence. We find that the energy \
is a local functional of\nthe trajectory of the charge. It coincides up to an \
overall factor with the\nLienard formula of the classical electrodynamics. In \
the AdS description the\nradiated energy is carried by a nonlinear wave on \
the string worldsheet for\nwhich we find an exact solution.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 22 May 2003 02:17:06 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2007-05-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Mikhailov", "Andrei", ""}}}],
           "Tooltip"]& ], 
