               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0306118\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Philip C. Argyres\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Philip C. Argyres, Adel M. Awad, Gregory A. Braun, and F. \
Paul\\n  Esposito (U. Cincinnati)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Higher-Derivative Terms in N=2 Supersymmetric Effective \
Actions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages. Added references and simplified final form of \
WZ term\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0307:060,2003\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2003/07/060\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UCTP-106-03\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show how to systematically construct \
higher-derivative terms in effective\\nactions in harmonic superspace despite \
the infinite redundancy in their\\ndescription due to the infinite number of \
auxiliary fields. Making an\\nassumption about the absence of certain \
superspace Chern-Simons-like terms\\ninvolving vector multiplets, we write \
all 3- and 4-derivative terms on Higgs,\\nCoulomb, and mixed branches. Among \
these terms are several with only\\nholomorphic dependence on fields, and at \
least one satisfies a\\nnon-renormalization theorem. These holomorphic terms \
include a novel\\n3-derivative term on mixed branches given as an integral \
over 3/4 of\\nsuperspace. As an illustration of our method, we search for \
Wess-Zumino terms\\nin the low energy effective action of N=2 supersymmetric \
QCD. We show that such\\nterms occur only on mixed branches. We also present \
an argument showing that\\nthe combination of space-time locality with \
supersymmetry implies locality in\\nthe anticommuting superspace coordinates \
of for unconstrained superfields.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
