            "authors" -> 
            "Philip C. Argyres, Adel M. Awad, Gregory A. Braun, and F. Paul\n \
 Esposito (U. Cincinnati)", "title" -> 
            "Higher-Derivative Terms in N=2 Supersymmetric Effective Actions",
             "comments" -> 
            "30 pages. Added references and simplified final form of WZ term",
             "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0307:060,2003", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2003/07/060", "report-no" -> "UCTP-106-03", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We show how to systematically construct higher-derivative \
terms in effective\nactions in harmonic superspace despite the infinite \
redundancy in their\ndescription due to the infinite number of auxiliary \
fields. Making an\nassumption about the absence of certain superspace \
Chern-Simons-like terms\ninvolving vector multiplets, we write all 3- and \
4-derivative terms on Higgs,\nCoulomb, and mixed branches. Among these terms \
are several with only\nholomorphic dependence on fields, and at least one \
satisfies a\nnon-renormalization theorem. These holomorphic terms include a \
novel\n3-derivative term on mixed branches given as an integral over 3/4 of\n\
superspace. As an illustration of our method, we search for Wess-Zumino terms\
\nin the low energy effective action of N=2 supersymmetric QCD. We show that \
such\nterms occur only on mixed branches. We also present an argument showing \
that\nthe combination of space-time locality with supersymmetry implies \
locality in\nthe anticommuting superspace coordinates of for unconstrained \
superfields.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 12 Jun 2003 20:32:01 GMT"}, {
