         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0306143", "submitter" -> "Sergey Frolov", 
            "authors" -> "S. Frolov, A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Rotating string solutions: AdS/CFT duality in non-supersymmetric \
sectors", "comments" -> "11 pages, harvmac. v2: refs added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Lett.B570:96-104,2003", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physletb.2003.07.022", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We find the minimal energy solution describing a folded closed \
string located\nat the center of AdS_5 and rotating simultaneously in two \
planes in S^5 with\ntwo arbitrary SO(6) angular momenta J_1 and J_2. In the \
case when J_1=J_2=J' we\nobserve the precise agreement between the leading \
coefficient in the large J'\nexpansion of the energy of this solution and the \
minimal eigen-value of the\n1-loop anomalous dimension matrix of the \
corresponding [J',0,J'] SYM operators\nobtained by Beisert, Minahan, \
Staudacher and Zarembo in hep-th/0306139. We find\nalso perfect agreement \
between string and SYM results in cases of states with\nunequal spins J_1 and \
J_2 dual to [J_2,J_1-J_2,J_2] operators. This represents\na remarkable \
quantitative test of the AdS/CFT duality in a non-supersymmetric\n(and \
non-near-BPS) sector.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 16 Jun 2003 19:37:44 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 24 Jun 2003 15:48:49 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-09-17", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Frolov", "S.", ""}, {
              "Tseytlin", "A. A.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
