           "id" -> "hep-th/0307042", "submitter" -> "Niklas Beisert", 
            "authors" -> "Niklas Beisert, Matthias Staudacher", "title" -> 
            "The N=4 SYM Integrable Super Spin Chain", "comments" -> 
            "25 pages, v2: discussion of developments in QCD improved, \
references\n  added, minor corrections, v3: published version", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B670:439-463,2003", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2003.08.015", "report-no" -> "AEI-2003-057", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat hep-ph", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently it was established that the one-loop planar \
dilatation generator of\nN=4 Super Yang-Mills theory may be identified, in \
some restricted cases, with\nthe Hamiltonians of various integrable quantum \
spin chains. In particular\nMinahan and Zarembo established that the \
restriction to scalar operators leads\nto an integrable vector so(6) chain, \
while recent work in QCD suggested\nrestricting to twist operators, \
containing mostly covariant derivatives, yields\ncertain integrable \
Heisenberg XXX chains with non-compact spin symmetry sl(2).\nHere we unify \
and generalize these insights and argue that the complete\none-loop planar \
dilatation generator of N=4 is described by an integrable\nsu(2,2|4) super \
spin chain. We also write down various forms of the associated\nBethe ansatz \
equations, whose solutions are in one-to-one correspondence with\nthe set of \
all one-loop planar anomalous dimensions in the N=4 gauge theory. We\nfinally \
speculate on the non-perturbative extension of these integrable\nstructures, \
which appears to involve non-local deformations of the conserved\ncharges.\n",
             "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 3 Jul 2003 19:58:22 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 25 Jul 2003 21:52:46 GMT"}, {
