to derive two-loop\nanomalous dimensions of gauge invariant operators from \
this knowledge: the\nvalue for the second anomalous correction to the \
dimension is essentially the\nsquare of the two-fermion admixture. The method \
effectively increases the loop\norder by one. For low J we find agreement to \
all orders in N with results\nobtained upon diagonalisation of the N=4 \
dilation operator.\n  We give a formula for the generalised Konishi anomaly \
and display its role in\nthe mixing. For J=2 we resolve the mixing up to \
