                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spinning strings in AdS_5 x S^5 and integrable \
systems\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex, 49 pages, 3 figures, v2: the new section about \
agreement with\\n  super YM theory in the case of the general circular \
two-spin solution is\\n  added, v3: misprints are corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B671:3-50,2003\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2003.08.036\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2003-059\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that solitonic solutions of the classical \
string action on the AdS_5\\nx S^5 background that carry charges (spins) of \
the Cartan subalgebra of the\\nglobal symmetry group can be classified in \
terms of periodic solutions of the\\nNeumann integrable system. We derive \
equations which determine the energy of\\nthese solitons as a function of \
spins. In the limit of large spins J, the first\\nsubleading 1/J coefficient \
in the expansion of the string energy is expected to\\nbe non-renormalised to \
all orders in the inverse string tension expansion and\\nthus can be directly \
compared to the 1-loop anomalous dimensions of the\\ncorresponding composite \
operators in N=4 super YM theory. We obtain a closed\\nsystem of equations \
that determines this subleading coefficient and, therefore,\\nthe 1-loop \
anomalous dimensions of the dual SYM operators. We expect that \
an\\nequivalent system of equations should follow from the thermodynamic \
limit of\\nthe algebraic Bethe ansatz for the SO(6) spin chain derived from \
SYM theory. We\\nalso identify a particular string solution whose classical \
energy exactly\\nreproduces the one-loop anomalous dimension of a certain set \
of SYM operators\\nwith two independent R charges J_1, J_2.\\n\""}]}, {
