               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Christoph Sieg\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Harald Dorn, Mario Salizzoni and Christoph Sieg (Humboldt \
University\\n  of Berlin)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the propagator of a scalar field in AdS x S and in its \
plane wave\\n  limit\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages, LaTeX, 1 figure; extended final version, \
section added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0502:047,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/02/047\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HU-Berlin-EP-03/41\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the scalar propagator on generic AdS x S \
backgrounds. For the\\nconformally flat situations and masses corresponding \
to Weyl invariant actions,\\nthe propagator is powerlike in the sum of the \
chordal distances with respect to\\nAdS(d+1) and S(d'+1). In these cases we \
analyze its source structure. In all\\nother cases the propagator depends on \
both chordal distances separately. There\\nan explicit formula is found for \
certain special mass values. For pure AdS we\\nshow how the well known \
propagators in the Weyl invariant case can be expressed\\nas linear \
combinations of simple powers of the chordal distance. For AdS(5) x\\nS(5) we \
relate our propagator to the expression in the plane wave limit and\\nfind a \
geometric interpretation of the variables occurring in the known\\nexplicit \
construction on the plane wave. As a byproduct of comparing \
different\\ntechniques, including the KK mode summation, a theorem for \
summing certain\\nproducts of Legendre and Gegenbauer functions is \
derived.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
