            "HU-Berlin-EP-03/41", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null,
             "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss the scalar propagator on generic AdS x S \
backgrounds. For the\nconformally flat situations and masses corresponding to \
Weyl invariant actions,\nthe propagator is powerlike in the sum of the \
chordal distances with respect to\nAdS(d+1) and S(d'+1). In these cases we \
analyze its source structure. In all\nother cases the propagator depends on \
both chordal distances separately. There\nan explicit formula is found for \
certain special mass values. For pure AdS we\nshow how the well known \
propagators in the Weyl invariant case can be expressed\nas linear \
combinations of simple powers of the chordal distance. For AdS(5) x\nS(5) we \
relate our propagator to the expression in the plane wave limit and\nfind a \
geometric interpretation of the variables occurring in the known\nexplicit \
construction on the plane wave. As a byproduct of comparing different\n\
techniques, including the KK mode summation, a theorem for summing certain\n\
products of Legendre and Gegenbauer functions is derived.\n", 
