                  "\"Exact Solution of Quantum Field Theory on Noncommutative \
Phase Spaces\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"70 pages AMSTeX\""}]}, {
               
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0401 (2004) 017\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/01/017\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"HWM-03-9, EMPG-03-12, ITEP-TH-38/03, UUITP-14/03\""}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We present the exact solution of a scalar field theory \
defined with\\nnoncommuting position and momentum variables. The model \
describes charged\\nparticles in a uniform magnetic field and with an \
interaction defined by the\\nGroenewold-Moyal star-product. Explicit results \
are presented for all Green's\\nfunctions in arbitrary even spacetime \
dimensionality. Various scaling limits of\\nthe field theory are analysed \
non-perturbatively and the renormalizability of\\neach limit examined. A \
supersymmetric extension of the field theory is also\\nconstructed in which \
the supersymmetry transformations are parametrized by\\ndifferential \
operators in an infinite-dimensional noncommutative algebra.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 6 Aug 2003 15:40:16 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-10\""}]}, {
