            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0308182\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gorsky Alexander Sergeevich\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A.Gorsky\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spin Chains and Gauge/String Duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"20 pages,reference added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Theor.Math.Phys. 142 (2005) 153-165; Teor.Mat.Fiz. 142 \
(2005)\\n  179-196\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The stringy picture behind the integrable spin chains \
governing the evolution\\nequations in Yang-Mills theory is discussed. It is \
shown that one-loop\\ndilatation operator in N=4 theory can be expressed in \
terms of two-point\\nfunctions on 2d worldsheet. Using the relation between \
Neumann integrable\\nsystem and the spin chains it is argued that the \
transition to the finite gauge\\ntheory coupling implies the discretization \
of the worldsheet. We conjecture\\nthat string bit model for the discretized \
worldsheet corresponds to the\\nrepresentation of the integrable spin chains \
in terms of the separated\\nvariables.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
