            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0309118\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Bogdan Kulik\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Z. Guralnik and B. Kulik\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Properties of Chiral Wilson Loops\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"15 pages, two pictures, some references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0401 (2004) 065\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/01/065\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a class of Wilson Loops in N =4, D=4 \
Yang-Mills theory belonging to\\nthe chiral ring of a N=2, d=1 subalgebra. We \
show that the expectation value of\\nthese loops is independent of their \
shape. Using properties of the chiral ring,\\nwe also show that the \
expectation value is identically 1. We find the same\\nresult for chiral \
loops in maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory in three,\\nfive and six \
dimensions. In seven dimensions, a generalized Konishi anomaly\\ngives an \
equation for chiral loops which closely resembles the loop equations\\nof the \
three dimensional Chern-Simons theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
