            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study a class of Wilson Loops in N =4, D=4 Yang-Mills \
theory belonging to\nthe chiral ring of a N=2, d=1 subalgebra. We show that \
the expectation value of\nthese loops is independent of their shape. Using \
properties of the chiral ring,\nwe also show that the expectation value is \
identically 1. We find the same\nresult for chiral loops in maximally \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory in three,\nfive and six dimensions. In seven \
dimensions, a generalized Konishi anomaly\ngives an equation for chiral loops \
which closely resembles the loop equations\nof the three dimensional \
Chern-Simons theory.\n", 
