            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0309161\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Schvellinger\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Schvellinger\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spinning and rotating strings for N=1 SYM theory and \
brane constructions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages. Dedicated to the memory of Ian I. Kogan. \
References added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0402 (2004) 066\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/02/066\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"OUTP-03-24-P\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We obtain spinning and rotating closed string solutions \
in AdS_5 \\\\times\\nT^{1,1} background, and show how these solutions can be \
mapped onto rotating\\nclosed strings embedded in configurations of \
intersecting branes in type IIA\\nstring theory. Then, we discuss spinning \
closed string solutions in the UV\\nlimit of the Klebanov-Tseytlin \
background, and also properties of classical\\nsolutions in the related \
intersecting brane constructions in the UV limit. We\\ncomment on extensions \
of this analysis to the deformed conifold background, and\\nin the \
corresponding intersecting brane construction, as well as its relation\\nto \
the deep IR limit of the Klebanov-Strassler solution. We briefly discuss \
on\\nthe relation between type IIA brane constructions and their related \
M-theory\\ndescriptions, and how solitonic solutions are related in both \
descriptions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
