            "Spinning and rotating strings for N=1 SYM theory and brane \
constructions", "comments" -> 
            "35 pages. Dedicated to the memory of Ian I. Kogan. References \
added", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0402 (2004) 066", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/02/066", "report-no" -> "OUTP-03-24-P", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We obtain spinning and rotating closed string solutions in \
AdS_5 \\times\nT^{1,1} background, and show how these solutions can be mapped \
onto rotating\nclosed strings embedded in configurations of intersecting \
branes in type IIA\nstring theory. Then, we discuss spinning closed string \
solutions in the UV\nlimit of the Klebanov-Tseytlin background, and also \
properties of classical\nsolutions in the related intersecting brane \
constructions in the UV limit. We\ncomment on extensions of this analysis to \
the deformed conifold background, and\nin the corresponding intersecting \
brane construction, as well as its relation\nto the deep IR limit of the \
Klebanov-Strassler solution. We briefly discuss on\nthe relation between type \
IIA brane constructions and their related M-theory\ndescriptions, and how \
solitonic solutions are related in both descriptions.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 16 Sep 2003 10:13:48 GMT"}, {
