           "id" -> "hep-th/0310031", "submitter" -> "Edward Shuryak", 
            "authors" -> "Edward V. Shuryak and Ismail Zahed", "title" -> 
            "Spin-Spin and Spin-Orbit Interactions in Strongly Coupled Gauge \
Theories", "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Lett. B608 (2005) 258-264", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physletb.2004.12.077", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We evaluate the spin-orbit and spin-spin interaction between \
two fermions in\nstrongly coupled gauge theories in their Coulomb phase. We \
use the\nquasi-instantaneous character of Coulomb's law at strong coupling to \
resum a\nclass of ladder diagrams. For ${\\cal N}=4$ SYM we derive both weak \
and strong\ncoupling limits of the the spin-orbit and spin-spin interactions, \
and find that\nin the latter case these interactions are subleading \
corrections and do not\nseriously affect the deeply bound Coulomb states with \
large angular momentum,\npointed out in our previous paper. The results are \
important for understanding\nof the regime of intermediate coupling, which is \
the case for QCD somewhat\nabove the chiral transition temperature.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 3 Oct 2003 16:15:30 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-10", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Shuryak", "Edward V.", ""}, {
              "Zahed", "Ismail", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
