                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Joseph A. Minahan\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"J. Engquist, J. A. Minahan, K. Zarembo\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Yang-Mills Duals for Semiclassical Strings\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"26 Pages, LaTeX; v2 Typos corrected, reference \
updated\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0311:063,2003\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2003/11/063\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"UUITP-19-03, CTP-MIT-3425, ITEP-TH-53/03\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We consider a semiclassical multiwrapped circular \
string pulsating on S_5,\\nwhose center of mass has angular momentum J on an \
S_3 subspace. Using the\\nAdS/CFT correspondence we argue that the one-loop \
anomalous dimension of the\\ndual operator is a simple rational function of \
J/L, where J is the R-charge and\\nL is the bare dimension of the operator. \
We then reproduce this result directly\\nfrom a super Yang-Mills computation, \
where we make use of the integrability of\\nthe one-loop system to set up an \
integral equation that we solve. We then\\nverify the results of Frolov and \
Tseytlin for circular rotating strings with\\nR-charge assignment (J',J',J). \
In this case we solve for an integral equation\\nfound in the O(-1) matrix \
model when J'< J and the O(+1) matrix model if J'> J.\\nThe latter region \
starts at J'=L/2 and continues down, but an apparent critical\\npoint is \
reached at J'=4J. We argue that the critical point is just an artifact\\nof \
the Bethe ansatz and that the conserved charges of the underlying \
integrable\\nmodel are analytic for all J' and that the results from the \
O(-1) model\\ncontinue onto the results of the O(+1) model.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
