            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0310193\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Stefano Kovacs\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Stefano Kovacs\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On instanton contributions to anomalous dimensions in N=4 \
supersymmetric\\n  Yang-Mills theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX, 71 pages, no figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B684 (2004) 3-74\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.02.014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2003-081\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Instanton contributions to the anomalous dimensions of \
gauge-invariant\\ncomposite operators in the N=4 supersymmetric SU(N) \
Yang-Mills theory are\\nstudied in the one-instanton sector. Independent sets \
of scalar operators of\\nbare dimension 2, 3, 4 and 5 are constructed in all \
the allowed representations\\nof the SU(4) R-symmetry group and their \
two-point functions are computed in the\\nsemiclassical approximation. \
Analysing the moduli space integrals the sectors\\nin which the scaling \
dimensions receive non-perturbative contributions are\\nidentified. The \
requirement that the integrations over the fermionic collective\\ncoordinates \
which arise in the instanton background are saturated leads \
to\\nnon-renormalisation properties for a large class of \
operators.\\nInstanton-induced corrections to the scaling dimensions are \
found only for\\ndimension 4 SU(4) singlets and for dimension 5 operators in \
the representation\\n[0,1,0] of SU(4). In many cases the non-renormalisation \
results are argued to\\nbe specific to operators of small dimension, but for \
some special sectors it is\\nshown that they are valid for arbitrary \
dimension. Comments are also made on\\nthe implications of the results on the \
form of the instanton contributions to\\nthe dilation operator of the theory \
and on the possibility of realising its\\naction on the instanton moduli \
space.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 20 Oct 2003 19:11:13 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
