         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0310232", "submitter" -> "Thomas Klose", "authors" -> 
            "Thomas Klose and Jan Plefka", "title" -> 
            "On the Integrability of large N Plane-Wave Matrix Theory", 
            "comments" -> "20 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys. B679 (2004) 127-142", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2003.11.043", "report-no" -> "AEI-2003-086", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We show the three-loop integrability of large N plane-wave \
matrix theory in a\nsubsector of states comprised of two complex light scalar \
fields. This is done\nby diagonalizing the theory's Hamiltonian in \
perturbation theory and taking the\nlarge N limit. At one-loop level the \
result is known to be equal to the\nHeisenberg spin-1/2 chain, which is a \
well-known integrable system. Here,\nintegrability implies the existence of \
hidden conserved charges and results in\na degeneracy of parity pairs in the \
spectrum. In order to confirm integrability\nat higher loops, we show that \
this degeneracy is not lifted and that\n(corrected) conserved charges exist. \
Plane-wave matrix theory is intricately\nconnected to N=4 Super Yang-Mills, \
as it arises as a consistent reduction of\nthe gauge theory on a \
three-sphere. We find that after appropriately\nrenormalizing the mass \
parameter of the plane-wave matrix theory the effective\nHamiltonian is \
identical to the dilatation operator of N=4 Super Yang-Mills\ntheory in the \
considered subsector. Our results therefore represent a strong\nsupport for \
the conjectured three-loop integrability of planar N=4 SYM and are\nin \
disagreement with a recent dual string theory finding. Finally, we study the\n\
stability of the large N integrability against nonsupersymmetric deformations\
\nof the model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 24 Oct 2003 19:01:02 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 27 Oct 2003 15:45:59 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 13 Nov 2003 15:36:46 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-04-05", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Klose", "Thomas", ""}, {
              "Plefka", "Jan", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.369203074672253`, -2.4987069150347265`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0310252\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Niklas Beisert\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Niklas Beisert\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The su(2|3) Dynamic Spin Chain\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"34 pages, 5 figures, v2: additional coefficient at three \
loops\\n  explained, discussion of integrability enhanced, figures \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B682:487-520,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2003.12.032\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI 2003-087\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The complete one-loop, planar dilatation operator of \
the N=4 superconformal\\ngauge theory was recently derived and shown to be \
integrable. Here, we present\\nfurther compelling evidence for a \
generalisation of this integrable structure\\nto higher orders of the \
coupling constant. For that we consider the su(2|3)\\nsubsector and \
investigate the restrictions imposed on the spin chain\\nHamiltonian by the \
symmetry algebra. This allows us to uniquely fix the energy\\nshifts up to \
the three-loop level and thus prove the correctness of a\\nconjecture in \
hep-th/0303060. A novel aspect of this spin chain model is that\\nthe \
higher-loop Hamiltonian, as for N=4 SYM in general, does not preserve \
the\\nnumber of spin sites. Yet this dynamic spin chain appears to be \
integrable.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 28 Oct 2003 20:34:38 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 9 Dec 2003 13:44:01 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-03-23\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Beisert\"", ",", "\"Niklas\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
