           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0310286\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ehud Schreiber\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"K. Furuuchi, E. Schreiber, G. W. Semenoff\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Five-Brane Thermodynamics from the Matrix Model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+34 pages, JHEP style. v2: typos, refs corrected\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A certain sector of the matrix model for M-theory on a \
plane wave background\\nhas recently been shown to produce the transverse \
five-brane. We consider this\\ntheory at finite temperature. We find that, at \
a critical temperature it has a\\nGross-Witten phase transition which \
corresponds to deconfinement of the matrix\\nmodel gauge theory. We interpret \
the phase transition as the Hagedorn\\ntransition of M-theory and of type II \
string theory in the five-brane\\nbackground. We also show that there is no \
Hagedorn behaviour in the transverse\\nmembrane background case.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
