String Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"latex, 35 pages, based on lectures delivered at the IPM \
Workshop on\\n  String Theory, Bandar-e-Anzali, Iran, in October 2003, v5: \
few corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"TIFR/TH/03-21\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This is a review of some beautiful matrix models \
related to the moduli space\\nof Riemann surfaces as well as to noncritical \
c=1 string theory at self-dual\\nradius. These include the Penner model and \
the W-infinity model, which have\\ndifferent origins but are equivalent to \
each other. In the final section, which\\nis new material, it is shown that \
these models are also equivalent to a\\nLiouville matrix model. We speculate \
that this might be interpreted in terms of\\nN D-instantons of the c=1 \
string.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
