            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0311004\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arutyunov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"G. Arutyunov, J. Russo, A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spinning strings in AdS_5 x S^5: new integrable system \
relations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex, 33 pages; v2: few minor misprints corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D69:086009,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.69.086009\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2003-091\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A general class of rotating closed string solutions in \
AdS_5 x S^5 is shown\\nto be described by a Neumann-Rosochatius \
one-dimensional integrable system. The\\nlatter represents an oscillator on a \
sphere or a hyperboloid with an additional\\n``centrifugal'' potential. We \
expect that the reduction of the AdS_5 x S^5\\nsigma model to the \
Neumann-Rosochatius system should have further\\ngeneralizations and should \
be useful for uncovering new relations between\\nintegrable structures on the \
two sides of the AdS/CFT duality. We find, in\\nparticular, new circular \
rotating string solutions with two AdS_5 and three S^5\\nspins. As in other \
recently discussed examples, the leading large-spin\\ncorrection to the \
classical energy turns out to be proportional to the square\\nof the string \
tension or the 't Hooft coupling \\\\lambda, suggesting that it can\\nbe \
matched onto the one-loop anomalous dimensions of the corresponding \
``long''\\noperators on the SYM side of the AdS/CFT duality.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 2 Nov 2003 18:14:57 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 23 Nov 2004 18:18:20 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-09-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Arutyunov\"", ",", "\"G.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Russo\"", ",", "\"J.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Tseytlin\"", ",", "\"A. A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
