            "Latex, 33 pages; v2: few minor misprints corrected", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D69:086009,2004", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.69.086009", "report-no" -> "AEI-2003-091", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  A general class of rotating closed string solutions in AdS_5 x \
S^5 is shown\nto be described by a Neumann-Rosochatius one-dimensional \
integrable system. The\nlatter represents an oscillator on a sphere or a \
hyperboloid with an additional\n``centrifugal'' potential. We expect that the \
reduction of the AdS_5 x S^5\nsigma model to the Neumann-Rosochatius system \
should have further\ngeneralizations and should be useful for uncovering new \
relations between\nintegrable structures on the two sides of the AdS/CFT \
duality. We find, in\nparticular, new circular rotating string solutions with \
two AdS_5 and three S^5\nspins. As in other recently discussed examples, the \
leading large-spin\ncorrection to the classical energy turns out to be \
proportional to the square\nof the string tension or the 't Hooft coupling \
\\lambda, suggesting that it can\nbe matched onto the one-loop anomalous \
dimensions of the corresponding ``long''\noperators on the SYM side of the \
AdS/CFT duality.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 2 Nov 2003 18:14:57 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 23 Nov 2004 18:18:20 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
