         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0311019", "submitter" -> "Andrei Mikhailov", 
            "authors" -> "Andrei Mikhailov", "title" -> "Speeding Strings", 
            "comments" -> "v3: added a reference to the earlier work", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0312 (2003) 058", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2003/12/058", "report-no" -> 
            "NSF-KITP-03-95, ITEP-TH-55/03", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  There is a class of single trace operators in ${\\cal N}=4$ \
Yang-Mills theory\nwhich are related by the AdS/CFT correspondence to \
classical string solutions.\nInteresting examples of such solutions \
corresponding to periodic trajectories\nof the Neumann system were studied \
recently. In our paper we study a\ngeneralization of these solutions. We \
consider strings moving with large\nvelocities. We show that the worldsheet \
of the fast moving string can be\nconsidered as a perturbation of the \
degenerate worldsheet, with the small\nparameter being the relativistic \
factor $\\sqrt{1-v^2}$. The series expansion in\nthis relativistic factor \
should correspond to the perturbative expansion in the\ndual Yang-Mills \
theory. The operators minimizing the anomalous dimension in the\nsector with \
given charges correspond to periodic trajectories in the mechanical\nsystem \
which is closely related to the product of two Neumann systems.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 4 Nov 2003 01:39:38 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
