               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0311041\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Luca Griguolo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Luca Griguolo, Domenico Seminara\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Classical Solutions of the TEK Model and Noncommutative \
Instantons in\\n  Two Dimensions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"41 pages, JHEP3. Minor corrections, references \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0403 (2004) 068\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/03/068\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UPRF-20003-09\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The twisted Eguchi-Kawai (TEK) model provides a \
non-perturbative definition\\nof noncommutative Yang-Mills theory: the \
continuum limit is approached at large\\n$N$ by performing suitable double \
scaling limits, in which non-planar\\ncontributions are no longer suppressed. \
We consider here the two-dimensional\\ncase, trying to recover within this \
framework the exact results recently\\nobtained by means of Morita \
equivalence. We present a rather explicit\\nconstruction of classical gauge \
theories on noncommutative toroidal lattice for\\ngeneral topological \
charges. After discussing the limiting procedures to\\nrecover the theory on \
the noncommutative torus and on the noncommutative plane,\\nwe focus our \
attention on the classical solutions of the related TEK models. We\\nsolve \
the equations of motion and we find the configurations having finite\\naction \
in the relevant double scaling limits. They can be explicitly described\\nin \
terms of twist-eaters and they exactly correspond to the instanton \
solutions\\nthat are seen to dominate the partition function on the \
noncommutative torus.\\nFluxons on the noncommutative plane are recovered as \
well. We also discuss how\\nthe highly non-trivial structure of the exact \
partition function can emerge\\nfrom a direct matrix model computation. The \
quantum consistency of the TEK\\nformulation is eventually checked by \
computing Wilson loops in a particular\\nlimit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 5 Nov 2003 20:30:50 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 19 Nov 2003 17:15:45 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-10\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
