Instantons in\n  Two Dimensions", "comments" -> 
            "41 pages, JHEP3. Minor corrections, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0403 (2004) 068", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/03/068", "report-no" -> "UPRF-20003-09", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The twisted Eguchi-Kawai (TEK) model provides a \
non-perturbative definition\nof noncommutative Yang-Mills theory: the \
continuum limit is approached at large\n$N$ by performing suitable double \
scaling limits, in which non-planar\ncontributions are no longer suppressed. \
We consider here the two-dimensional\ncase, trying to recover within this \
framework the exact results recently\nobtained by means of Morita \
equivalence. We present a rather explicit\nconstruction of classical gauge \
theories on noncommutative toroidal lattice for\ngeneral topological charges. \
After discussing the limiting procedures to\nrecover the theory on the \
noncommutative torus and on the noncommutative plane,\nwe focus our attention \
on the classical solutions of the related TEK models. We\nsolve the equations \
of motion and we find the configurations having finite\naction in the \
relevant double scaling limits. They can be explicitly described\nin terms of \
twist-eaters and they exactly correspond to the instanton solutions\nthat are \
seen to dominate the partition function on the noncommutative torus.\nFluxons \
on the noncommutative plane are recovered as well. We also discuss how\nthe \
highly non-trivial structure of the exact partition function can emerge\nfrom \
a direct matrix model computation. The quantum consistency of the TEK\n\
formulation is eventually checked by computing Wilson loops in a particular\n\
limit.\n", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
