          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0311065\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Valentin V. Khoze\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Valentin V. Khoze\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"From Branes to Branes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages, 12 figures, references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B682 (2004) 217\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.01.030\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CERN-TH/2003-273\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We use the `branes within branes' approach to study the \
appearance of stable\\n$ (p-2)-branes and unstable (p-1)-branes in type II \
string theory from\\np-brane--p-antibrane pairs.Our goal is to describe the \
emergence of these lower\\ndimensional branes from brane-antibrane pairs in \
string theory using a\\ntractable gauge theory language. This is achieved by \
suspending the original\\np-brane--p-antibrane pair between two (p+2)-branes, \
and describing its dynamics\\nin terms of the worldvolume gauge theory on the \
spectator (p+2)-branes.\\nInstantons, monopoles, sphalerons and their \
higher-dimensional generalizations\\nin this worldvolume gauge theory \
correspond to stable (BPS) and unstable\\n(non-BPS) branes in string theory. \
Collisions of stable branes with\\ncorresponding antibranes and production of \
lower-dimensional branes in string\\ntheory are described in a \
straightforward way in gauge theory. Tachyonic modes\\non the \
p-brane--p-antibrane worldvolume do not appear in our analysis since \
we\\nwork on the worldvolume of the spectator (p+2)-branes. Our results on \
brane\\ndescent relations are in agreement with Sen's tachyon condensation \
approach.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
