               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spinning strings and AdS/CFT duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"57 pages, latex. To appear in Ian Kogan Memorial Volume, \
``From\\n  Fields to Strings: Circumnavigating Theoretical Physics'', M. \
Shifman, A.\\n  Vainshtein, and J. Wheater, eds. (World Scientific, 2004); \
v2: table of\\n  contents and references added; v3: minor misprints corrected\
\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review a special class of semiclassical string \
states in AdS_5 x S^5 which\\nhave a regular expansion of their energy in \
integer powers of the ratio of the\\nsquare of string tension (`t Hooft \
coupling) and the square of large angular\\nmomentum in S^5. They allow one \
to quantitatively check the AdS/CFT duality in\\nnon-supersymmetric sector of \
states and also help to uncover the role of\\nintegrable structures on the \
two sides of the string theory -- gauge theory\\nduality.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
