            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We find new explicit solutions describing closed strings \
spinning with equal\nangular momentum in two independent planes in AdS(5). \
These are 2N-folded\nstrings in the radial direction and also winding M times \
around an angular\ndirection. Thus in spacetime they consist of 2N segments. \
Solutions fulfilling\nthe closed string periodicity conditions exist provided \
N/M>2, i.e. the strings\nmust be folded at least six times in the radial \
coordinate. The strings are\nspinning, or actually orbiting, similarly to \
solutions found previously in\nblack hole spacetimes, but unlike the one-spin \
solutions in AdS which spin\naround their center. For long strings we recover \
the logaritmic scaling\nrelation between energy and spin known from the \
one-spin case, but different\nfrom other known two-spin cases.\n", 
