               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0312191\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ali Kaya\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"S. Arapoglu, N.S. Deger, A. Kaya, E. Sezgin and P. \
Sundell\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Multi-Spin Giants\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages, v3: Supersymmetry of the two-spin solution \
corrected from\\n  1/4 to 1/2. Sections 2.6 and 3.6 improved. A reference and \
comments added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev. D69 (2004) 106006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.69.106006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We examine spherical p-branes in AdS_m x S^n, that wrap \
an S^p in either\\nAdS_m (p=m-2) or S^n (p=n-2). We first construct a \
two-spin giant solution\\nexpanding in S^n and has spins both in AdS_m and \
S^n. For\\n(m,n)={(5,5),(4,7),(7,4)}, it is 1/2 supersymmetric, and it \
reduces to the\\nsingle-spin giant graviton when the AdS spin vanishes. We \
study some of its\\nbasic properties such as instantons, non-commutativity, \
zero-modes, and the\\nperturbative spectrum. All vibration modes have real \
and positive frequencies\\ndetermined uniquely by the spacetime curvature, \
and evenly spaced. We next\\nconsider the (0+1)-dimensional sigma-models \
obtained by keeping generally\\ntime-dependent transverse coordinates, \
describing warped product of a\\nbreathing-mode and a point-particle on S^n \
or AdS_m x S^1. The BPS bounds show\\nthat the only spherical supersymmetric \
solutions are the single and the\\ntwo-spin giants. Moreover, we integrate \
the sigma-model and separate the\\ncanonical variables. We quantize exactly \
the point-particle part of the motion,\\nwhich in local coordinates gives \
Poschl-Teller type potentials, and calculate\\nits contribution to the \
anomalous dimension.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
