        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.78253374824605, -2.2959944149813616`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0312218\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Radu Roiban\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Radu Roiban\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On spin chains and field theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages, Latex; v2. typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0409:023,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/09/023\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We point out that the existence of global symmetries in \
a field theory is not\\nan essential ingredient in its relation with an \
integrable model. We describe\\nan obvious construction which, given an \
integrable spin chain, yields a field\\ntheory whose 1-loop scale \
transformations are generated by the spin chain\\nHamiltonian. We also \
identify a necessary condition for a given field theory to\\nbe related to an \
integrable spin chain.\\n  As an example, we describe an anisotropic and \
parity-breaking generalization\\nof the XXZ Heisenberg spin chain and its \
associated field theory. The system\\nhas no nonabelian global symmetries and \
generally does not admit a\\nsupersymmetric extension without the \
introduction of more propagating bosonic\\nfields. For the case of a 2-state \
chain we find the spectrum and the\\neigenstates. For certain values of its \
coupling constants the field theory\\nassociated to this general type of \
chain is the bosonic sector of the\\nLeigh-Strassler deformation of N=4 SYM \
theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 17 Dec 2003 23:23:06 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 6 May 2004 16:32:11 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Roiban\"", ",", "\"Radu\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
