           "id" -> "hep-th/0312218", "submitter" -> "Radu Roiban", "authors" -> 
            "Radu Roiban", "title" -> "On spin chains and field theories", 
            "comments" -> "22 pages, Latex; v2. typos corrected", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0409:023,2004", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/09/023", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We point out that the existence of global symmetries in a \
field theory is not\nan essential ingredient in its relation with an \
integrable model. We describe\nan obvious construction which, given an \
integrable spin chain, yields a field\ntheory whose 1-loop scale \
transformations are generated by the spin chain\nHamiltonian. We also \
identify a necessary condition for a given field theory to\nbe related to an \
integrable spin chain.\n  As an example, we describe an anisotropic and \
parity-breaking generalization\nof the XXZ Heisenberg spin chain and its \
associated field theory. The system\nhas no nonabelian global symmetries and \
generally does not admit a\nsupersymmetric extension without the introduction \
of more propagating bosonic\nfields. For the case of a 2-state chain we find \
the spectrum and the\neigenstates. For certain values of its coupling \
constants the field theory\nassociated to this general type of chain is the \
bosonic sector of the\nLeigh-Strassler deformation of N=4 SYM theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 17 Dec 2003 23:23:06 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 6 May 2004 16:32:11 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
