           "id" -> "hep-th/0401057", "submitter" -> "Didina Serban", 
            "authors" -> "D. Serban and M. Staudacher", "title" -> 
            "Planar N=4 gauge theory and the Inozemtsev long range spin \
chain", "comments" -> 
            "31 pages, no figure; v1: one reference added, minor changes; v2:\
\n  slightly extended discussion of rapidity, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0406 (2004) 001", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/06/001", "report-no" -> 
            "AEI-2004-001, SPhT-T04/002", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate whether the (planar, two complex scalar) \
dilatation operator\nof N=4 gauge theory can be, perturbatively and, perhaps, \
non-perturbatively,\ndescribed by an integrable long range spin chain with \
elliptic exchange\ninteraction. Such a chain was introduced some time ago by \
Inozemtsev. In the\nlimit of sufficiently ``long'' operators a Bethe ansatz \
exists, which we apply\nat the perturbative two- and three-loop level. \
Spectacular agreement is found\nwith spinning string predictions of Frolov \
and Tseytlin for the two-loop\nenergies of certain large charge operators. \
However, we then go on to show that\nthe agreement between perturbative gauge \
theory and semi-classical string\ntheory begins to break down, in a subtle \
fashion, at the three-loop level. This\ncorroborates a recently found \
disagreement between three-loop gauge theory and\nnear plane-wave string \
theory results, and quantitatively explains a previously\nobtained puzzling \
deviation between the string proposal and a numerical\nextrapolation of \
finite size three-loop anomalous dimensions. At four loops and\nbeyond, we \
find that the Inozemtsev chain exhibits a generic breakdown of\nperturbative \
BMN scaling. However, our proposal is not necessarily limited to\n\
perturbation theory, and one would hope that the string theory results can be\
\nrecovered from the Inozemtsev chain at strong 't Hooft coupling.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 9 Jan 2004 20:30:04 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
