                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We construct an approximation to field theories on the \
noncommutative torus\\nbased on soliton projections and partial isometries \
which together form a\\nmatrix algebra of functions on the sum of two \
circles. The matrix quantum\\nmechanics is applied to the perturbative \
dynamics of scalar field theory, to\\ntachyon dynamics in string field \
theory, and to the Hamiltonian dynamics of\\nnoncommutative gauge theory in \
two dimensions. We also describe the adiabatic\\ndynamics of solitons on the \
noncommutative torus and compare various classes of\\nnoncommutative solitons \
on the torus and the plane.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
