               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Duality between IIB String Theory on PP-wave and N=4 \
SYM: a Status\\n  Report\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages, 5 figures; Contribution to the proceedings of \
the\\n  Copenhagen RTN workshop, 15-20 September 2003; v3, few comments \
added,\\n  misprints corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Class.Quant.Grav. 21 (2004) S1265-2196\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/0264-9381/21/10/001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The aim of this report is to give an overview of the \
duality between type IIB\\nstring theory on the maximally supersymmetric \
PP-wave and the BMN sector of N=4\\nSuper Yang-Mills theory. The general \
features of the string and the field\\ntheory descriptions are reviewed, but \
the main focus of this report is on the\\ncomparison between the two sides of \
the duality. In particular, it is first\\nexplained how free IIB strings \
emerge on the gauge theory side and then the\\ngeneralizations of this \
relation to the full interacting theory are considered.\\nAn ``historical'' \
approach is taken and the various proposals presented in the\\nliterature are \
described.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
