               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Marshakov\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A.Marshakov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Strings, Integrable Systems, Geometry and Statistical \
Models\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"7 pages, LaTeX, Contribution to the proceedings of the \
conference\\n  \\\"Lie theory and its applications in physics\\\", June 2003, \
Varna, Bulgaria;\\n  misprints corrected, acknowledgments added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"FIAN/TD-03/04, ITEP/TH-06/04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The role of integrable systems in string theory is \
discussed. We remind old\\nexamples of the correspondence between stringy \
partition functions or effective\\nactions and integrable equations, based on \
effective application of the matrix\\nmodel technique. Then we turn to a new \
example, coming from the Nekrasov\\ndeformation of the Seiberg-Witten \
prepotential. In the last case the deformed\\ntheory is described by a \
different statistical model, which becomes equivalent\\nto a partition \
function of a topological string. The full partition function of\\nstring \
theory arises therefore always as a certain \\\"quantization\\\" of \
its\\nquasiclassical geometry.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
