            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The role of integrable systems in string theory is discussed. \
We remind old\nexamples of the correspondence between stringy partition \
functions or effective\nactions and integrable equations, based on effective \
application of the matrix\nmodel technique. Then we turn to a new example, \
coming from the Nekrasov\ndeformation of the Seiberg-Witten prepotential. In \
the last case the deformed\ntheory is described by a different statistical \
model, which becomes equivalent\nto a partition function of a topological \
string. The full partition function of\nstring theory arises therefore always \
as a certain \"quantization\" of its\nquasiclassical geometry.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
