           "id" -> "hep-th/0402007", "submitter" -> "Amir Esmaeil Mosaffa", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Mohsen Alishahiha, Amir E. Mosaffa and Hossein Yavartanoo", 
            "title" -> 
            "Multi-spin string solutions in AdS Black Hole and confining \
backgrounds", "comments" -> "26 pages, LaTeX, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys. B686 (2004) 53-74", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.03.015", "report-no" -> 
            "IPM/P-2004/001", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study semi-classical multi-spin strings in the \
non-supersymmetric\nbackgrounds of $AdS$ Black Hole and Witten's confining \
model. We consider\nconstant radius strings with rotations along the \
isometries of the backgrounds.\nIn the $AdS$ Black Hole, solutions exist only \
if there is a non-zero spin in\nthe Black Hole part. In contrast with the \
$AdS$ background, we find solutions\nwhich although have no rotation in the \
$S^5$ part, have a regular $\\lambda$\nexpansion in the expression for large \
energy. In the near-extremal $D_3$ and\n$D_4$ backgrounds, we find that \
strings have to be located on the confining\nwall. We also discuss the \
stability of solutions by considering the fluctuation\nLagrangians.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 1 Feb 2004 13:59:59 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 23 Feb 2004 09:56:41 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-04-05", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Alishahiha", "Mohsen", ""}, {
              "Mosaffa", "Amir E.", ""}, {"Yavartanoo", "Hossein", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.94922741877493, -2.191814977970262}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0402033\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Charlotte Kristjansen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"C. Kristjansen (NORDITA)\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Three-spin Strings on AdS_5 x S^5 from N=4 SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"13 pages, v2: refs. added, minor textual changes, v3: \
more refs.\\n  added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett. B586 (2004) 106-116\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2004.02.037\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NORDITA-2004-3\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Using the integrable spin chain picture we study the \
one-loop anomalous\\ndimension of certain single trace scalar operators of \
N=4 SYM expected to\\ncorrespond to semi-classical string states on AdS_5 x \
S^5 with three large\\nangular momenta (J_1,J_2,J_3) on S^5. In particular, \
we investigate the\\nanalyticity structure encoded in the Bethe equations for \
various distributions\\nof Bethe roots. In a certain region of the parameter \
space our operators reduce\\nto the gauge theory duals of the folded string \
with two large angular momenta\\nand in another region to the duals of the \
circular string with angular momentum\\nassignment (J,J',J'), J>J'. In \
between we locate a critical line. We propose\\nthat the operators above the \
critical line are the gauge theory duals of the\\ncircular elliptic string \
with three different spins and support this by a\\nperturbative \
calculation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
