               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0402044\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yusuke Kimura\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yusuke Kimura\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nonabelian gauge field and dual description of fuzzy \
sphere\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"28 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0404 (2004) 058\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/04/058\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"KEK-TH-938\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In matrix models, higher dimensional D-branes are \
obtained by imposing a\\nnoncommutative relation to coordinates of lower \
dimensional D-branes. On the\\nother hand, a dual description of this \
noncommutative space is provided by\\nhigher dimensional D-branes with gauge \
fields. Fuzzy spheres can appear as a\\nconfiguration of lower dimensional \
D-branes in a constant R-R field strength\\nbackground. In this paper, we \
consider a dual description of higher dimensional\\nfuzzy spheres by \
introducing nonabelian gauge fields on higher dimensional\\nspherical \
D-branes. By using the Born-Infeld action, we show that a fuzzy\\n$2k$-sphere \
and spherical D$2k$-branes with a nonabelian gauge field whose\\nChern \
character is nontrivial are the same objects when $n$ is large. We\\ndiscuss \
a relationship between the noncommutative geometry and nonabelian \
gauge\\nfields. Nonabelian gauge fields are represented by noncommutative \
matrices\\nincluding the coordinate dependence. A similarity to the quantum \
Hall system is\\nalso studied.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
