            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0402067\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Mikhailov\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Mikhailov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Slow evolution of nearly-degenerate extremal \
surfaces\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v4: added a reference to the earlier work\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Geom.Phys. 54 (2005) 228-250\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.geomphys.2004.09.007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CALT-68-2477, MPG-10/04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It was conjectured recently that the string worldsheet \
theory for the fast\\nmoving string in AdS times a sphere becomes effectively \
first order in the time\\nderivative and describes the continuous limit of an \
integrable spin chain. In\\nthis paper we will try to make this statement \
more precise. We interpret the\\nfirst order theory as describing the long \
term evolution of the tensionless\\nstring perturbed by a small tension. The \
long term evolution is a Hamiltonian\\nflow on the moduli space of periodic \
trajectories. It should correspond to the\\nrenormgroup flow on the field \
theory side.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
