               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0402093\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Raimar Wulkenhaar\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Harald Grosse (Vienna), Raimar Wulkenhaar \
(Leipzig)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The \\\\beta-function in duality-covariant noncommutative \
\\\\phi^4-theory\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"11 pages, LaTeX\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Eur.Phys.J. C35 (2004) 277-282\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1140/epjc/s2004-01853-x\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the one-loop \\\\beta-functions describing \
the renormalisation of the\\ncoupling constant \\\\lambda and the frequency \
parameter \\\\Omega for the real\\nfour-dimensional duality-covariant \
noncommutative \\\\phi^4-model, which is\\nrenormalisable to all orders. The \
contribution from the one-loop four-point\\nfunction is reduced by the \
one-loop wavefunction renormalisation, but the\\n\\\\beta_\\\\lambda-function \
remains non-negative. Both \\\\beta_\\\\lambda and\\n\\\\beta_\\\\Omega \
vanish at the one-loop level for the duality-invariant model\\ncharacterised \
by \\\\Omega=1. Moreover, \\\\beta_\\\\Omega also vanishes in the \
limit\\n\\\\Omega \\\\to 0, which defines the standard noncommutative \
\\\\phi^4-quantum field\\ntheory. Thus, the limit \\\\Omega \\\\to 0 exists \
at least at the one-loop level.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
