            "  We compute the one-loop \\beta-functions describing the \
renormalisation of the\ncoupling constant \\lambda and the frequency \
parameter \\Omega for the real\nfour-dimensional duality-covariant \
noncommutative \\phi^4-model, which is\nrenormalisable to all orders. The \
contribution from the one-loop four-point\nfunction is reduced by the \
one-loop wavefunction renormalisation, but the\n\\beta_\\lambda-function \
remains non-negative. Both \\beta_\\lambda and\n\\beta_\\Omega vanish at the \
one-loop level for the duality-invariant model\ncharacterised by \\Omega=1. \
Moreover, \\beta_\\Omega also vanishes in the limit\n\\Omega \\to 0, which \
defines the standard noncommutative \\phi^4-quantum field\ntheory. Thus, the \
limit \\Omega \\to 0 exists at least at the one-loop level.\n", 
