               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0402207\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Marshakov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"V.A.Kazakov, A.Marshakov, J.A.Minahan, K.Zarembo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Classical/quantum integrability in AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"49 pages, 5 figures, LaTeX; v2: complete proof of the \
two-loop\\n  equivalence between the sigma model and the gauge theory is \
added. References\\n  added; v4,v5,v6: misprints corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0405 (2004) 024\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/05/024\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LPTENS-04/09, FIAN/TD-04/04, MPG/ITEP-11/04, \
IHES/P/04/05,\\n  UUITP-05/04, CTP-MIT-3472\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the AdS/CFT duality from the perspective of \
integrable systems and\\nestablish a direct relationship between the \
dimension of single trace local\\noperators composed of two types of scalar \
fields in N=4 super Yang-Mills and\\nthe energy of their dual semiclassical \
string states in AdS(5) X S(5). The\\nanomalous dimensions can be computed \
using a set of Bethe equations, which for\\n``long'' operators reduces to a \
Riemann-Hilbert problem. We develop a unified\\napproach to the long \
wavelength Bethe equations, the classical ferromagnet and\\nthe classical \
string solutions in the SU(2) sector and present a general\\nsolution, \
governed by complex curves endowed with meromorphic differentials\\nwith \
integer periods. Using this solution we compute the anomalous dimensions\\nof \
these long operators up to two loops and demonstrate that they agree \
with\\nstring-theory predictions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
