            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0403121\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Radoslav Rashkov\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"H. Dimov, R.C. Rashkov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A note on spin chain/string duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v.2 One reference added, typos corrected, 21 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Int.J.Mod.Phys. A20 (2005) 4337\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1142/S0217751X05020975\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently a significant progress in matching the \
anomalous dimensions of\\ncertain class of operators in N=4 SYM theory and \
rotating strings was made. The\\ncorrespondence was established mainly using \
Bethe ansatz technique applied to\\nthe spin s Heisenberg model. In a recent \
paper Kruczenski (hep-th/0311203)\\nsuggested to solve the Heisenberg model \
by using of sigme model approach. In\\nthis paper we generalize the solutions \
obtained by Kruczenski and comment on\\nthe dual string theory. It turns out \
that our solutions are related to the so\\ncalled Neumann-Rosochatius \
integrable system. We comment on the spin chain\\nsolutions and on the \
string/gauge theory correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
