            "authors" -> "H. Dimov, R.C. Rashkov", "title" -> 
            "A note on spin chain/string duality", "comments" -> 
            "v.2 One reference added, typos corrected, 21 pages", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Int.J.Mod.Phys. A20 (2005) 4337", "doi" -> 
            "10.1142/S0217751X05020975", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently a significant progress in matching the anomalous \
dimensions of\ncertain class of operators in N=4 SYM theory and rotating \
strings was made. The\ncorrespondence was established mainly using Bethe \
ansatz technique applied to\nthe spin s Heisenberg model. In a recent paper \
Kruczenski (hep-th/0311203)\nsuggested to solve the Heisenberg model by using \
of sigme model approach. In\nthis paper we generalize the solutions obtained \
by Kruczenski and comment on\nthe dual string theory. It turns out that our \
solutions are related to the so\ncalled Neumann-Rosochatius integrable \
system. We comment on the spin chain\nsolutions and on the string/gauge \
theory correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 11 Mar 2004 07:47:11 GMT"}, {
