               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study multi-charged rotating string states on Type \
IIB regular backgrounds\\ndual to confining SU(N) gauge theories with (softly \
broken) {\\\\cal N}=1\\nsupersymmetry, in the infra red regime. After \
exhibiting the classical\\nenergy/charge relations for the folded and \
circular two-charge strings, we\\ncompute in the latter case the one loop \
sigma-model quantum correction. The\\nclassical relation has an expansion in \
positive powers of the analogous of the\\nBMN effective coupling, while the \
quantum corrections are non perturbative in\\nnature and are not subleading \
in the limit of infinite charge. We comment about\\nthe dual field theory \
multi-charged hadrons and the implications of our\\ncomputation for the AdS/{\
\\\\cal N}=4 duality.\\n\""}]}, {
