Sochichiu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spin bit models from non-planar N=4 SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages, 2 figures, some typos corrected in eqs. (2.6), \
(2.8),\\n  (2.11), (2.14)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B699 (2004) 151-173\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.07.025\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study spin models underlying the non-planar dynamics \
of ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM\\ngauge theory. In particular, we derive the non-local \
spin chain Hamiltonian\\ngenerating dilatations in the gauge theory at \
leading order in $g_{\\\\rm YM}^2 N$\\nbut exact in ${1\\\\over N}$.\\n  \
States in the spin chain are characterized by a spin-configuration and \
a\\nlinking variable describing how sites in the chain are connected. Joining \
and\\nsplitting of string/traces are mimicked by a twist operator acting on \
the\\nlinking variable. The results are applied to a systematic study of \
non-planar\\nanomalous dimensions and operator mixing in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ SYM. \
Intriguingly, we\\nidentify a sequence of SYM operators for which corrections \
to the one-loop\\nanomalous dimensions stop at the first ${1\\\\over N}$ \
non-planar order.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
