            "  We study spin models underlying the non-planar dynamics of \
${\\cal N}=4$ SYM\ngauge theory. In particular, we derive the non-local spin \
chain Hamiltonian\ngenerating dilatations in the gauge theory at leading \
order in $g_{\\rm YM}^2 N$\nbut exact in ${1\\over N}$.\n  States in the spin \
chain are characterized by a spin-configuration and a\nlinking variable \
describing how sites in the chain are connected. Joining and\nsplitting of \
string/traces are mimicked by a twist operator acting on the\nlinking \
variable. The results are applied to a systematic study of non-planar\n\
anomalous dimensions and operator mixing in ${\\cal N}=4$ SYM. Intriguingly, \
we\nidentify a sequence of SYM operators for which corrections to the \
one-loop\nanomalous dimensions stop at the first ${1\\over N}$ non-planar \
order.\n", "versions" -> {{
