               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0404133\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Bogdan Stefanski jr.\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"B. Stefanski, Jr. and A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Large spin limits of AdS/CFT and generalized \
Landau-Lifshitz equations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages, LaTeX. v3 minor comments and one reference \
added. v4 an\\n  equivalent form of the action in sect. 5.1 added, misprints \
corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0405:042,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/05/042\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider AdS_5 x S^5 string states with several \
large angular momenta\\nalong AdS_5 and S^5 directions which are dual to \
single-trace Super-Yang-Mills\\n(SYM) operators built out of chiral \
combinations of scalars and covariant\\nderivatives. In particular, we focus \
on the SU(3) sector (with three spins in\\nS^5) and the SL(2) sector (with \
one spin in AdS_5 and one in S^5), generalizing\\nrecent work hep-th/0311203 \
and hep-th/0403120 on the SU(2) sector with two\\nspins in S^5. We show that, \
in the large spin limit and at the leading order in\\nthe effective coupling \
expansion, the string sigma model equations of motion\\nreduce to matrix \
Landau-Lifshitz equations. We then demonstrate that the\\ncoherent-state \
expectation value of the one-loop SYM dilatation operator\\nrestricted to the \
corresponding sector of single trace operators is also\\neffectively \
described by the same equations. This implies a universal leading\\norder \
equivalence between string energies and SYM anomalous dimensions, as \
well\\nas a matching of integrable structures. We also discuss the more \
general 5-spin\\nsector and comment on SO(6) states dual to non-chiral scalar \
operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
