               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Supersymmetric null-surfaces\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v4: added a reference to the earlier work; corrected the \
formula for\\n  the stabilizer of the BMN vacuum; added the discussion of the \
complex\\n  structure of the odd coordinates in Section 3.2\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0409:068,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/09/068\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CALT-68-2494\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Single trace operators with the large R-charge in \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills\\ntheory correspond to the null-surfaces in \
$AdS_5\\\\times S^5$. We argue that the\\nmoduli space of the null-surfaces \
is the space of contours in the\\nsuper-Grassmanian parametrizing the complex \
$(2|2)$-dimensional subspaces of\\nthe complex $(4|4)$-dimensional space. The \
odd coordinates on this\\nsuper-Grassmanian correspond to the fermionic \
degrees of freedom of the\\nsuperstring.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
