           "id" -> "hep-th/0404173", "submitter" -> "Andrei Mikhailov", 
            "authors" -> "Andrei Mikhailov", "title" -> 
            "Supersymmetric null-surfaces", "comments" -> 
            "v4: added a reference to the earlier work; corrected the formula \
for\n  the stabilizer of the BMN vacuum; added the discussion of the complex\n\
  structure of the odd coordinates in Section 3.2", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP0409:068,2004", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/09/068", 
            "report-no" -> "CALT-68-2494", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Single trace operators with the large R-charge in \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills\ntheory correspond to the null-surfaces in \
$AdS_5\\times S^5$. We argue that the\nmoduli space of the null-surfaces is \
the space of contours in the\nsuper-Grassmanian parametrizing the complex \
$(2|2)$-dimensional subspaces of\nthe complex $(4|4)$-dimensional space. The \
odd coordinates on this\nsuper-Grassmanian correspond to the fermionic \
degrees of freedom of the\nsuperstring.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 22 Apr 2004 18:17:50 GMT"}, {
