               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0404215\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Anton V. Ryzhov\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A.V. Ryzhov and A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Towards the exact dilatation operator of N=4 super \
Yang-Mills theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"20 pages, latex, no figures; v2: the expression in the \
case of the\\n  Konishi descendant simplified, additional explanations and \
references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B698:132-148,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.07.037\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"BRX TH-540\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the structure of the dilatation operator \
D of planar N=4 SYM\\nin the sector of single trace operators built out of \
two chiral combinations of\\nthe 6 scalars. Previous results at low orders in \
`t Hooft coupling \\\\lambda\\nsuggest that D has the form of an SU(2) spin \
chain Hamiltonian with long range\\nmultiple spin interactions. Instead of \
the usual perturbative expansion in\\npowers of \\\\lambda, we split D into \
parts D^(n) according to the number n of\\nindependent pairwise interactions \
between spins at different sites. We\\ndetermine the coefficients of \
spin-spin interaction terms in D^(1) by imposing\\nthe condition of \
regularity of a BMN-type scaling limit. For long spin chains,\\nthese \
coefficients turn out to be expressible in terms of \
hypergeometric\\nfunctions of \\\\lambda, which have regular expansions at \
both small and large\\nvalues of \\\\lambda. This suggest that anomalous \
dimensions of ``long'' operators\\nin the two-scalar sector should \
generically scale as square root of \\\\lambda at\\nlarge coupling, i.e. in \
the same way as energies of semiclassical states in\\ndual AdS5 x S5 string \
theory. We speculate that D^(1) may be a Hamiltonian of a\\nnew integrable \
spin chain.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
