            "Towards the exact dilatation operator of N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory", "comments" -> 
            "20 pages, latex, no figures; v2: the expression in the case of \
the\n  Konishi descendant simplified, additional explanations and references \
added", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B698:132-148,2004", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.07.037", "report-no" -> "BRX TH-540", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate the structure of the dilatation operator D of \
planar N=4 SYM\nin the sector of single trace operators built out of two \
chiral combinations of\nthe 6 scalars. Previous results at low orders in `t \
Hooft coupling \\lambda\nsuggest that D has the form of an SU(2) spin chain \
Hamiltonian with long range\nmultiple spin interactions. Instead of the usual \
perturbative expansion in\npowers of \\lambda, we split D into parts D^(n) \
according to the number n of\nindependent pairwise interactions between spins \
at different sites. We\ndetermine the coefficients of spin-spin interaction \
terms in D^(1) by imposing\nthe condition of regularity of a BMN-type scaling \
limit. For long spin chains,\nthese coefficients turn out to be expressible \
in terms of hypergeometric\nfunctions of \\lambda, which have regular \
expansions at both small and large\nvalues of \\lambda. This suggest that \
anomalous dimensions of ``long'' operators\nin the two-scalar sector should \
generically scale as square root of \\lambda at\nlarge coupling, i.e. in the \
same way as energies of semiclassical states in\ndual AdS5 x S5 string \
theory. We speculate that D^(1) may be a Hamiltonian of a\nnew integrable \
spin chain.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 27 Apr 2004 19:56:31 GMT"}, {
