               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0405001\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matthias Staudacher\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"N. Beisert, V. Dippel and M. Staudacher\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A Novel Long Range Spin Chain and Planar N=4 Super \
Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"48 pages, 1 figure. v2, further results added: discussion \
of the\\n  relationship to an inhomogeneous spin chain, normalization in sec \
3 unified,\\n  v3: minor mistakes corrected, published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0407:075,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/07/075\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI 2004-036\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We probe the long-range spin chain approach to planar \
N=4 gauge theory at\\nhigh loop order. A recently employed hyperbolic spin \
chain invented by\\nInozemtsev is suitable for the SU(2) subsector of the \
state space up to three\\nloops, but ceases to exhibit the conjectured \
thermodynamic scaling properties\\nat higher orders. We indicate how this may \
be bypassed while nevertheless\\npreserving integrability, and suggest the \
corresponding all-loop asymptotic\\nBethe ansatz. We also propose the local \
part of the all-loop gauge transfer\\nmatrix, leading to conjectures for the \
asymptotically exact formulae for all\\nlocal commuting charges. The ansatz \
is finally shown to be related to a\\nstandard inhomogeneous spin chain. A \
comparison of our ansatz to semi-classical\\nstring theory uncovers a \
detailed, non-perturbative agreement between the\\ncorresponding expressions \
for the infinite tower of local charge densities.\\nHowever, the respective \
Bethe equations differ slightly, and we end by refining\\nand elaborating a \
previously proposed possible explanation for this\\ndisagreement.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 3 May 2004 19:43:49 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 19 Jul 2004 11:41:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 3 Sep 2004 15:31:26 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-03-23\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
