           "id" -> "hep-th/0405001", "submitter" -> "Matthias Staudacher", 
            "authors" -> "N. Beisert, V. Dippel and M. Staudacher", "title" -> 
            "A Novel Long Range Spin Chain and Planar N=4 Super Yang-Mills", 
            "comments" -> 
            "48 pages, 1 figure. v2, further results added: discussion of the\
\n  relationship to an inhomogeneous spin chain, normalization in sec 3 \
unified,\n  v3: minor mistakes corrected, published version", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0407:075,2004", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/07/075", 
            "report-no" -> "AEI 2004-036", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We probe the long-range spin chain approach to planar N=4 \
gauge theory at\nhigh loop order. A recently employed hyperbolic spin chain \
invented by\nInozemtsev is suitable for the SU(2) subsector of the state \
space up to three\nloops, but ceases to exhibit the conjectured thermodynamic \
scaling properties\nat higher orders. We indicate how this may be bypassed \
while nevertheless\npreserving integrability, and suggest the corresponding \
all-loop asymptotic\nBethe ansatz. We also propose the local part of the \
all-loop gauge transfer\nmatrix, leading to conjectures for the \
asymptotically exact formulae for all\nlocal commuting charges. The ansatz is \
finally shown to be related to a\nstandard inhomogeneous spin chain. A \
comparison of our ansatz to semi-classical\nstring theory uncovers a \
detailed, non-perturbative agreement between the\ncorresponding expressions \
for the infinite tower of local charge densities.\nHowever, the respective \
Bethe equations differ slightly, and we end by refining\nand elaborating a \
previously proposed possible explanation for this\ndisagreement.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 3 May 2004 19:43:49 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 19 Jul 2004 11:41:27 GMT"}, {
