           "id" -> "hep-th/0405243", "submitter" -> "Joseph A. Minahan", 
            "authors" -> "Joseph A.Minahan", "title" -> 
            "Higher Loops Beyond the SU(2) Sector", "comments" -> 
            "LaTex, 26 pages, 1 figure;v2 misprints corrected; v3 misprints\n \
 corrected, ref. added", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0410:053,2004", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/10/053", "report-no" -> 
            "UUITP-16-04, CTP-MIT-3496", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the case of coherent gauge invariant operators in \
the SU(3) and\nSO(4) sectors. We argue that in many cases, these sectors can \
be closed in the\nthermodynamic limit, even at higher loops. We then use a \
modification of the\nBethe equations which is a natural generalization of a \
proposal put forward by\nSerban and Staudacher to make gauge theory \
predictions for the anomalous\ndimensions for a certain class of operators in \
each sector. We show that the\npredictions are consistent with semiclassical \
string predictions at two loops\nbut in general fail to agree at three loops. \
Interestingly, in both cases there\nis one point in the configuration space \
where the gauge theory and string\ntheory predictions agree. In the SU(3) \
case it corresponds to a circular string\nwith R-charge assignment (J,J,J).\n\
", "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 26 May 2004 17:55:06 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 30 Jun 2004 15:26:59 GMT"}, {
