         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0405288", "submitter" -> "Gordon Semenoff", 
            "authors" -> "Gordon W. Semenoff and Donovan Young", "title" -> 
            "Wavy Wilson Line and AdS/CFT", "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> 
            "Int.J.Mod.Phys. A20 (2005) 2833-2846", "doi" -> 
            "10.1142/S0217751X0502077X", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Wilson loops which are small deviations from straight, \
infinite lines, called\nwavy lines, are considered in the context of the \
AdS/CFT correspondence. A\nsingle wavy line and the connected correlation \
function of a straight and wavy\nline are considered. It is argued that, to \
leading order in ``waviness'', the\nfunctional form of the loop is universal \
and the coefficient, which is a\nfunction of the 't Hooft coupling, is found \
in weak coupling perturbation\ntheory and the strong coupling limit using the \
AdS/CFT correspondence.\nSupersymmetric arguments are used to simplify the \
computation and to show that\nthe straight line obeys the Migdal-Makeenko \
loop equation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 31 May 2004 19:38:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-10", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Semenoff", "Gordon W.", ""}, {
              "Young", "Donovan", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
