            "abstract" -> 
            "  In the context of the Penrose/BMN limit of the AdS/CFT \
correspondence, we\nconsider four-impurity BMN operators in Yang-Mills \
theory, and demonstrate\nexplicitly their correspondence to four-oscillator \
states in string theory.\nUsing the dilatation operator on the gauge-theory \
side of the correspondence,\nwe calculate matrix elements between \
four-impurity states. Since conformal\ndimensions of gauge-theory operators \
correspond to light-cone energies of\nstring states, these matrix elements \
may be compared with the string-theory\nlight-cone Hamiltonian matrix \
elements calculated in the plane-wave background\nusing the string field \
theory vertex. We find that the two calculations agree,\nextending the cases \
of two- and three-impurity operators considered in the\nliterature using BMN \
gauge-theory quantum mechanics. The results are also in\nagreement with \
calculations in the literature based on perturbative\ngauge-theory methods.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
