            "  We calculate quantum averages of Wilson loops (holonomies) in \
gauge theories\non the Euclidean noncommutative plane, using a path-integral \
representation of\nthe star-product. We show how the perturbative expansion \
emerges from a concise\ngeneral formula and demonstrate its anomalous \
behavior at large parameter of\nnoncommutativity for the simplest nonplanar \
diagram of genus 1. We discuss\nvarious UV/IR regularizations of the \
two-dimensional noncommutative gauge\ntheory in the axial gauge and, using \
the noncommutative loop equation,\nconstruct a consistent regularization.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
