        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.88114279831903, -2.275529334615139}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0406189\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Kruczenski\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M. Kruczenski, A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Semiclassical relativistic strings in S^5 and long \
coherent operators in\\n  N=4 SYM theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX, 50 pages, 1 figure. v2: References added, minor \
corrections.\\n  54 pages. v3: Few changes. One paragraph added at the end of \
section 3. 55\\n  pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0409:038,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/09/038\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the low energy effective action \
corresponding to the 1-loop,\\nplanar, dilatation operator in the scalar \
sector of N=4 SU(N) SYM theory. For a\\ngeneral class of non-holomorphic \
``long'' operators, of bare dimension L>>1, it\\nis a sigma model action with \
8-dimensional target space and agrees with a limit\\nof the phase-space \
string sigma model action describing generic fast-moving\\nstrings in the S^5 \
part of AdS_5 x S^5. The limit of the string action is taken\\nin a way that \
allows for a systematic expansion to higher orders in the\\neffective \
coupling $\\\\lambda/L^2$. This extends previous work on rigid \
rotating\\nstrings in S^5 (dual to operators in the SU(3) sector of the \
dilatation\\noperator) to the case when string oscillations or pulsations in \
S^5 are\\nallowed. We establish a map between the profile of the leading \
order string\\nsolution and the structure of the corresponding coherent, \
``locally BPS'', SYM\\nscalar operator. As an application, we explicitly \
determine the form of the\\nnon-holomorphic operators dual to the pulsating \
strings. Using action--angle\\nvariables, we also directly compute the energy \
of pulsating solutions,\\nsimplifying previous treatments.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 22 Jun 2004 19:42:02 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 29 Jun 2004 18:46:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 4 Aug 2004 22:07:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-09-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
