           "id" -> "hep-th/0406189", "submitter" -> "Martin Kruczenski", 
            "authors" -> "M. Kruczenski, A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Semiclassical relativistic strings in S^5 and long coherent \
operators in\n  N=4 SYM theory", "comments" -> 
            "LaTeX, 50 pages, 1 figure. v2: References added, minor \
corrections.\n  54 pages. v3: Few changes. One paragraph added at the end of \
section 3. 55\n  pages", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0409:038,2004", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/09/038", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the low energy effective action corresponding to \
the 1-loop,\nplanar, dilatation operator in the scalar sector of N=4 SU(N) \
SYM theory. For a\ngeneral class of non-holomorphic ``long'' operators, of \
bare dimension L>>1, it\nis a sigma model action with 8-dimensional target \
space and agrees with a limit\nof the phase-space string sigma model action \
describing generic fast-moving\nstrings in the S^5 part of AdS_5 x S^5. The \
limit of the string action is taken\nin a way that allows for a systematic \
expansion to higher orders in the\neffective coupling $\\lambda/L^2$. This \
extends previous work on rigid rotating\nstrings in S^5 (dual to operators in \
the SU(3) sector of the dilatation\noperator) to the case when string \
oscillations or pulsations in S^5 are\nallowed. We establish a map between \
the profile of the leading order string\nsolution and the structure of the \
corresponding coherent, ``locally BPS'', SYM\nscalar operator. As an \
application, we explicitly determine the form of the\nnon-holomorphic \
operators dual to the pulsating strings. Using action--angle\nvariables, we \
also directly compute the energy of pulsating solutions,\nsimplifying \
previous treatments.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 22 Jun 2004 19:42:02 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 29 Jun 2004 18:46:55 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 4 Aug 2004 22:07:00 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-09-17", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kruczenski", "M.", ""}, {
              "Tseytlin", "A.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.709584305401204`, -2.7008591729838027`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0406256\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matthias Staudacher\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gleb Arutyunov, Sergey Frolov, Matthias Staudacher\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bethe Ansatz for Quantum Strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages, LaTeX, JHEP3.cls;v2: minor changes, typos \
fixed; v3:\\n  explicit, general formula for confluent mode numbers \
obtained\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0410 (2004) 016\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/10/016\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2004-046\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose Bethe equations for the diagonalization of \
the Hamiltonian of\\nquantum strings on AdS_5 x S^5 at large string tension \
and restricted to\\ncertain large charge states from a closed su(2) \
subsector. The ansatz differs\\nfrom the recently proposed all-loop gauge \
theory asymptotic Bethe ansatz by\\nadditional factorized scattering terms \
for the local excitations. We also show\\nthat our ansatz quantitatively \
reproduces everything that is currently known\\nabout the string spectrum of \
these states. Firstly, by construction, we recover\\nthe integral Bethe \
equations describing semiclassical spinning strings.\\nSecondly, we explain \
how to derive the 1/J energy corrections of arbitrary\\nM-impurity BMN \
states, provide explicit, general formulae for both distinct and\\nconfluent \
mode numbers, and compare to asymptotic gauge theory. In the special\\ncases \
M=2,3 we reproduce the results of direct quantization of Callan et \
al.\\nLastly, at large string tension and relatively small charge we recover \
the\\nfamous 2 (n^2 lambda)^(1/4) asymptotics of massive string modes at \
level n.\\nRemarkably, this behavior is entirely determined by the novel \
scattering terms.\\nThis is qualitatively consistent with the conjecture that \
these terms occur due\\nto wrapping effects in gauge theory. Our finding does \
not in itself cure the\\ndisagreements between gauge and string theory, but \
leads us to speculate about\\nthe structure of an interpolating Bethe ansatz \
for the AdS/CFT system at finite\\ncoupling and charge.\\n\""}]}, {
