           "id" -> "hep-th/0406256", "submitter" -> "Matthias Staudacher", 
            "authors" -> "Gleb Arutyunov, Sergey Frolov, Matthias Staudacher",
             "title" -> "Bethe Ansatz for Quantum Strings", "comments" -> 
            "22 pages, LaTeX, JHEP3.cls;v2: minor changes, typos fixed; v3:\n \
 explicit, general formula for confluent mode numbers obtained", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0410 (2004) 016", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/10/016", "report-no" -> "AEI-2004-046", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We propose Bethe equations for the diagonalization of the \
Hamiltonian of\nquantum strings on AdS_5 x S^5 at large string tension and \
restricted to\ncertain large charge states from a closed su(2) subsector. The \
ansatz differs\nfrom the recently proposed all-loop gauge theory asymptotic \
Bethe ansatz by\nadditional factorized scattering terms for the local \
excitations. We also show\nthat our ansatz quantitatively reproduces \
everything that is currently known\nabout the string spectrum of these \
states. Firstly, by construction, we recover\nthe integral Bethe equations \
describing semiclassical spinning strings.\nSecondly, we explain how to \
derive the 1/J energy corrections of arbitrary\nM-impurity BMN states, \
provide explicit, general formulae for both distinct and\nconfluent mode \
numbers, and compare to asymptotic gauge theory. In the special\ncases M=2,3 \
we reproduce the results of direct quantization of Callan et al.\nLastly, at \
large string tension and relatively small charge we recover the\nfamous 2 \
(n^2 lambda)^(1/4) asymptotics of massive string modes at level n.\n\
Remarkably, this behavior is entirely determined by the novel scattering \
terms.\nThis is qualitatively consistent with the conjecture that these terms \
occur due\nto wrapping effects in gauge theory. Our finding does not in \
itself cure the\ndisagreements between gauge and string theory, but leads us \
to speculate about\nthe structure of an interpolating Bethe ansatz for the \
AdS/CFT system at finite\ncoupling and charge.\n", 
