            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0406266\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jorge Russo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.M. Pons, J.G. Russo, P. Talavera\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Semiclassical string spectrum in a string model dual to \
large N QCD\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"20 pages, harvmac. References added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B700 (2004) 71-88\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.08.039\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore the string spectrum in the Witten QCD model \
by considering\\nclassical string configurations, thereby obtaining energy \
formulas for quantum\\nstates with large excitation quantum numbers \
representing glueballs and\\nKaluza-Klein states. In units of the string \
tension, the energies of all states\\nincrease as the 't Hooft coupling \
$\\\\lambda $ is decreased, except the energies\\nof glueballs corresponding \
to strings lying on the horizon, which remain\\nconstant. We argue that some \
string solutions can be extrapolated to the small\\n$\\\\lambda $ regime. We \
also find the classical mechanics description of\\nsupergravity glueballs in \
terms of point-like string configurations oscillating\\nin the radial \
direction, and reproduce the glueball energy formula previously\\nobtained by \
solving the equation for the dilaton fluctuation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
