               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Eva Silverstein\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Counter-intuition and Scalar Masses\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"11 pages, harvmac big\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"SLAC-PUB-10569, SU-ITP-04/30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The Bousso-Polchinski mechanism for discretely \
fine-tuning the cosmological\\nconstant favors a large bare negative \
cosmological constant. I argue (using\\ngeneralizations of results of \
Klebanov and Tseytlin) that a similar mechanism\\nfor fine-tuning the scalar \
masses to small values favors a large bare negative\\n(i.e. tachyonic) scalar \
mass. I comment briefly on the related issue of the\\nrole of low energy \
supersymmetry in string theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
