                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"S.A. Frolov, I.Y. Park and A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On one-loop correction to energy of spinning strings in \
S^5\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"21 pages, 8 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D71:026006,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.71.026006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We revisit the computation (hep-th/0306130) of 1-loop \
AdS_5 x S^5 superstring\\nsigma model correction to energy of a closed \
circular string rotating in S^5.\\nThe string is spinning around its center \
of mass with two equal angular momenta\\nJ_2=J_3 and its center of mass \
angular momentum is J_1. We revise the argument\\nin hep-th/0306130 that the \
1-loop correction is suppressed by 1/J factor (J=\\nJ_1 + 2 J_2 is the total \
SO(6) spin) relative to the classical term in the\\nenergy and use numerical \
methods to compute the leading 1-loop coefficient. The\\ncorresponding gauge \
theory result is known (hep-th/0405055) only in the J_1=0\\nlimit when the \
string solution becomes unstable and thus the 1-loop shift of\\nthe energy \
formally contains an imaginary part. While the comparison with gauge\\ntheory \
may not be well-defined in this case, our numerical string theory value\\nof \
the 1-loop coefficient seems to disagree with the gauge theory one. \
A\\nplausible explanation should be (as in hep-th/0405001) in the different \
order\\nof limits taken on the gauge theory and the string theory sides of \
the AdS/CFT\\nduality.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
