               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Notes on fast moving strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2: added Section 4.4; v3: added references, expanded \
review section,\\n  small corrections in Section 4, added Section 4.6; v4: \
added conclusion\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Commun.Math.Phys. 264 (2006) 683-703\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s00220-005-1487-2\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CALT-68-2518\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review the recent work on the mechanics of fast \
moving strings in anti-de\\nSitter space times a sphere and discuss the role \
of conserved charges. An\\ninteresting relation between the local conserved \
charges of rigid solutions was\\nfound in the earlier work. We propose a \
generalization of this relation for\\narbitrary solutions, not necessarily \
rigid. We conjecture that an infinite\\ncombination of local conserved \
charges is an action variable generating\\nperiodic trajectories in the \
classical string phase space. It corresponds to\\nthe length of the operator \
on the field theory side.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
