            "journal-ref" -> "Fortsch.Phys.53:852-860,2005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1002/prop.200410207", "report-no" -> "AEI 2004-070", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We review and compare the integrable structures in N=4 gauge \
theory and\nstring theory on AdS5xS5. Recently, Bethe ansaetze for gauge \
theory/weak\ncoupling and string theory/strong coupling were proposed to \
describe scaling\ndimensions in the su(2) subsector. Here we investigate the \
Bethe equations for\nquantum string theory, naively extrapolated to weak \
coupling. Excitingly, we\nfind a spin chain Hamiltonian similar, but not \
equal, to the gauge theory\ndilatation operator.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 3 Sep 2004 20:34:37 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 14 Sep 2004 15:39:25 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-03-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Beisert", "Niklas", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.60965016236923, -2.2184685734907728`}, 0.],
