          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0409115", "submitter" -> "David Berenstein", 
            "authors" -> "David Berenstein", "title" -> 
            "A matrix model for a quantum hall droplet with manifest \
particle-hole\n  symmetry", "comments" -> 
            "25 pages, uses JHEP format, young.sty (included). v2: Updated\n  \
references, typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev. D71 (2005) 085001", 
            "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.71.085001", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th cond-mat.mes-hall", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We find that a gauged matrix model of rectangular fermionic \
matrices (a\nmatrix version of the fermion harmonic oscillator) realizes a \
quantum hall\ndroplet with manifest particle-hole symmetry. The droplet \
consists of free\nfermions on the topology of a sphere. It is also possible \
to deform the\nHamiltonian by double trace operators, and we argue that this \
device can\nproduce two body potentials which might lead the system to \
realize a fractional\nquantum hall state on the sphere. We also argue that a \
single gauged fermionic\nquantum mechanics of hermitian matrices realizes a \
droplet with an edge that\nhas $c=1/2$ CFT on it.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 10 Sep 2004 19:02:28 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 23 Sep 2004 18:07:40 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-10", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Berenstein", "David", ""}}}],
           "Tooltip"]& ], 
