            "authors" -> "Shijong Ryang", "title" -> 
            "Circular and Folded Multi-Spin Strings in Spin Chain Sigma \
Models", "comments" -> "16 pages, LaTeX, no figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP0410:059,2004", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2004/10/059", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  From the SU(2) spin chain sigma model at the one-loop and \
two-loop orders we\nrecover the classical circular string solution with two \
S^5 spins (J_1, J_2) in\nthe AdS_5 x S^5 string theory. In the SL(2) sector \
of the one-loop spin chain\nsigma model we explicitly construct a solution \
which corresponds to the folded\nstring solution with one AdS_5 spin S and \
one S^5 spin J. In the one-loop\ngeneral sigma model we demonstrate that \
there exists a solution which\nreproduces the energy of the circular \
constant-radii string solution with three\nspins (S_1, S_2, J).\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
