           "id" -> "hep-th/0409259", "submitter" -> "Toni Mateos", "authors" -> 
            "Toni Mateos", "title" -> 
            "D-branes, gauge/string duality and noncommutative theories", 
            "comments" -> 
            "PhD thesis, 281 pages, 41 figures. v2: added references", 
            "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In this thesis we elaborate on the three subjects of the \
title. We first show\nthat supertubes exist and still preserve some \
supersymmetry in a large variety\nof curved backgrounds. Within the AdS/CFT \
correspondence we study the\nsupersymmetry of rotating strings with 3 angular \
momenta, and we consider the\npossibility of adding matter in a stable but \
non-supersymmetric way. We\ncontribute to the extension of the duality to \
more realistic YM theories by\nconstructing the sugra dual of an N=2 pure SYM \
in 3d, given in terms of a\nCalabi-Yau four-fold in M-theory. We study the \
unitarity of noncommutative\nnonrelativistic field theories, we construct the \
sugra dual of noncommutative\npure SYM theories with N=1 in 4d and N=2 in 3d, \
and we study holographically\nproperties like UV/IR mixing, confinement, \
chiral symmetry breaking and moduli\nspaces.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 24 Sep 2004 17:26:19 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 13 Nov 2004 18:59:11 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2007-05-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Mateos", "Toni", ""}}}], 
