           "id" -> "hep-th/0409296", "submitter" -> "Arkady Tseytlin", 
            "authors" -> "A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Semiclassical strings and AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "34 pages. Contribution to Proceedings of Cargese Summer School, \
June\n  7-19, 2004, extended version of hep-th/0407218", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss AdS/CFT duality in the sector of ``semiclassical'' \
string states\nwith large quantum numbers. We review the coherent-state \
effective action\napproach, in which similar 2d sigma model actions appear \
from the AdS_5 x S^5\nstring action and from the integrable spin chain \
Hamiltonian representing the\nN=4 super Yang-Mills dilatation operator. We \
consider mostly the leading-order\nterms in the energies/anomalous dimensions \
which match but comment also on\nhigher-order corrections.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 29 Sep 2004 02:28:27 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2007-05-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Tseytlin", "A. A.", ""}}}], 
