               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Shirin Hadizadeh, Bojan Ramadanovic, Gordon W. Semenoff \
and Donovan\\n  Young\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Free Energy and Phase Transition of the Matrix Model on a \
Plane-Wave\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"24 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev. D71 (2005) 065016\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.71.065016\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It has recently been observed that the weakly coupled \
plane wave matrix model\\nhas a density of states which grows exponentially \
at high energy. This implies\\nthat the model has a phase transition. The \
transition appears to be of first\\norder. However, its exact nature is \
sensitive to interactions. In this paper,\\nwe analyze the effect of \
interactions by computing the relevant parts of the\\neffective potential for \
the Polyakov loop operator in the finite temperature\\nplane-wave matrix \
model to three loop order. We show that the phase transition\\nis indeed of \
first order. We also compute the correction to the Hagedorn\\ntemperature to \
order two loops.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
