               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0410080\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sukjin Yoon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sungho Hong (U. Pennsylvania and U. Washington), Sukjin \
Yoon (U.\\n  Washington), Matthew J. Strassler (U. Washington)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Adjoint Trapping: A New Phenomenon at Strong 't Hooft \
Coupling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Clarified transition with a better figure and improved \
presentation;\\n  added careful discussion of the small regime of validity of \
the\\n  Born-Oppenheimer computation and adjusted some remarks appropriately; \
also\\n  added two references\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0603 (2006) 012\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/03/012\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UW/PT 04-19, UPR-1094-T\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Adding matter of mass m, in the fundamental \
representation of SU(N), to N=4\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory, we study \
``generalized quarkonium''\\ncontaining a (s)quark, an anti(s)quark, and J \
massless (or very light) adjoint\\nparticles. At large 't Hooft coupling \
$\\\\lambda$ >> 1, the states of spin <= 1\\nare surprisingly light \
(Kruczenski et al., hep-th/0304032) and small\\n(hep-th/0312071) with a \
J-independent size of order $\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}/m$. This\\n``trapping'' of \
adjoint matter in a region small compared with its Compton\\nwavelength and \
compared to any confinement scale in the theory is an \
unfamiliar\\nphenomenon, as it does not occur at small $\\\\lambda$. We \
explore adjoint\\ntrapping further by considering the limit of large J. In \
particular, for J >>\\n$\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}$ >> 1, we expect the trapping \
phenomenon to become unstable.\\nUsing Wilson loop methods, we show that a \
sharp transition, in which the\\ngeneralized quarkonium states become unbound \
(for massless adjoints) occurs at\\n$J \\\\simeq 0.22 \\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}$. \
If the adjoint scalars of N=4 are massive and\\nthe theory is confining (as, \
for instance, in N=1* theories) then the\\ntransition becomes a cross-over, \
across which the size of the states changes\\nrapidly from \
~$\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}/m$ to something of order the confinement scale ~\\n$\\\
\\Lambda^{-1}$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 8 Oct 2004 18:47:13 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
