\n  Washington), Matthew J. Strassler (U. Washington)", "title" -> 
            "Adjoint Trapping: A New Phenomenon at Strong 't Hooft Coupling", 
            "comments" -> 
            "Clarified transition with a better figure and improved \
presentation;\n  added careful discussion of the small regime of validity of \
the\n  Born-Oppenheimer computation and adjusted some remarks appropriately; \
also\n  added two references", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0603 (2006) 012", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/03/012", "report-no" -> 
            "UW/PT 04-19, UPR-1094-T", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Adding matter of mass m, in the fundamental representation of \
SU(N), to N=4\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory, we study ``generalized \
quarkonium''\ncontaining a (s)quark, an anti(s)quark, and J massless (or very \
light) adjoint\nparticles. At large 't Hooft coupling $\\lambda$ >> 1, the \
states of spin <= 1\nare surprisingly light (Kruczenski et al., \
hep-th/0304032) and small\n(hep-th/0312071) with a J-independent size of \
order $\\sqrt{\\lambda}/m$. This\n``trapping'' of adjoint matter in a region \
small compared with its Compton\nwavelength and compared to any confinement \
scale in the theory is an unfamiliar\nphenomenon, as it does not occur at \
small $\\lambda$. We explore adjoint\ntrapping further by considering the \
limit of large J. In particular, for J >>\n$\\sqrt{\\lambda}$ >> 1, we expect \
the trapping phenomenon to become unstable.\nUsing Wilson loop methods, we \
show that a sharp transition, in which the\ngeneralized quarkonium states \
become unbound (for massless adjoints) occurs at\n$J \\simeq 0.22 \
\\sqrt{\\lambda}$. If the adjoint scalars of N=4 are massive and\nthe theory \
is confining (as, for instance, in N=1* theories) then the\ntransition \
becomes a cross-over, across which the size of the states changes\nrapidly \
from ~$\\sqrt{\\lambda}/m$ to something of order the confinement scale ~\n\
$\\Lambda^{-1}$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
