                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev. D71 (2005) 126006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.71.126006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"KEK-TH-990, UTHEP-499\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider defect composite operators in a defect \
superconformal field\\ntheory obtained by inserting an AdS_4 x S^2-brane in \
the AdS_5 x S^5\\nbackground. The one-loop dilatation operator for the scalar \
sector is\\nrepresented by an integrable open spin chain. We give a \
description to\\nconstruct coherent states for the open spin chain. Then, by \
evaluating the\\nexpectation value of the Hamiltonian with the coherent \
states in a long\\noperator limit, a Landau-Lifshitz type of sigma model \
action is obtained. This\\naction is also derived from the string action and \
hence we find a complete\\nagreement in both SYM and string sides. We see \
that an SO(3)_H pulsating string\\nsolution is included in the action and its \
energy completely agrees with the\\nresult calculated in a different method. \
In addition, we argue that our\\nprocedure would be applicable to other \
AdS-brane cases.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
