            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0410282\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ian J. Swanson\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ian Swanson\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Quantum string integrability and AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2: references and typos corrected; v3: minor corrections \
and\\n  comments, 23 pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B709:443-464,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.01.003\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CALT-68-2527\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recent explorations of the AdS/CFT correspondence have \
unveiled integrable\\nstructures underlying both planar N = 4 \
super-Yang-Mills theory and type IIB\\nstring theory on AdS_5 x S^5. \
Integrability in the gauge theory emerges from\\nthe fact that the dilatation \
generator can be identified with the Hamiltonian\\nof an integrable quantum \
spin chain, and the classical string theory has been\\nshown to contain \
infinite towers of hidden currents, a typical signature of\\nintegrability. \
Efforts to match the integrable structures of various classical\\nstring \
configurations to those of corresponding gauge theory quantum spin\\nchains \
have been largely successful. By studying a semiclassical expansion\\nabout a \
class of point-like solitonic solutions to the classical string\\nequations \
of motion on AdS_5 x S^5, we take a step toward demonstrating \
that\\nintegrability in the string theory survives quantum corrections beyond \
tree\\nlevel. Quantum fluctuations are chosen to align with background \
curvature\\ncorrections to the pp-wave limit of AdS_5 x S^5, and we present \
evidence for an\\ninfinite tower of local bosonic charges that are conserved \
by the quantum\\ntheory to quartic order in the expansion. We explicitly \
compute several higher\\ncharges based on a Lax representation of the \
worldsheet sigma model and provide\\na prescription for matching the \
eigenvalue spectra of these charges with\\ncorresponding quantities \
descending from the integrable structure of the gauge\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 28 Oct 2004 19:42:47 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
