           "id" -> "hep-th/0410282", "submitter" -> "Ian J. Swanson", 
            "authors" -> "Ian Swanson", "title" -> 
            "Quantum string integrability and AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "v2: references and typos corrected; v3: minor corrections and\n  \
comments, 23 pages", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B709:443-464,2005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.01.003", "report-no" -> "CALT-68-2527", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Recent explorations of the AdS/CFT correspondence have \
unveiled integrable\nstructures underlying both planar N = 4 super-Yang-Mills \
theory and type IIB\nstring theory on AdS_5 x S^5. Integrability in the gauge \
theory emerges from\nthe fact that the dilatation generator can be identified \
with the Hamiltonian\nof an integrable quantum spin chain, and the classical \
string theory has been\nshown to contain infinite towers of hidden currents, \
a typical signature of\nintegrability. Efforts to match the integrable \
structures of various classical\nstring configurations to those of \
corresponding gauge theory quantum spin\nchains have been largely successful. \
By studying a semiclassical expansion\nabout a class of point-like solitonic \
solutions to the classical string\nequations of motion on AdS_5 x S^5, we \
take a step toward demonstrating that\nintegrability in the string theory \
survives quantum corrections beyond tree\nlevel. Quantum fluctuations are \
chosen to align with background curvature\ncorrections to the pp-wave limit \
of AdS_5 x S^5, and we present evidence for an\ninfinite tower of local \
bosonic charges that are conserved by the quantum\ntheory to quartic order in \
the expansion. We explicitly compute several higher\ncharges based on a Lax \
representation of the worldsheet sigma model and provide\na prescription for \
matching the eigenvalue spectra of these charges with\ncorresponding \
quantities descending from the integrable structure of the gauge\ntheory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 28 Oct 2004 19:42:47 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 2 Nov 2004 00:46:02 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 17 Nov 2004 17:23:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Swanson", "Ian", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{13.091800989772423`, -3.20903899015328}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0411009\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Kuperstein Stanislav\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"S. Kuperstein, J. Sonnenschein\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-critical, near extremal AdS_6 background as a \
holographic laboratory\\n  of four dimensional YM theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"25 pages, JHEP style\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0411:026,2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2004/11/026\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"TAUP-2781-04\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study certain properties of the low energy regime of \
a theory which\\nresembles four dimensional YM theory in the framework of a \
non-critical\\nholographic gravity dual. We use for the latter the near \
extremal $AdS_6$\\nnon-critical SUGRA. We extract the glueball spectra that \
associates with the\\nfluctuations of the dilaton, one form and the graviton \
and compare the results\\nto those of the critical near extremal $D4$ model \
and lattice simulations. We\\nshow an area law behavior for the Wilson loop \
and screening for the 't Hooft\\nloop. The Luscher term is found to be \
$-{3/24}\\\\frac {\\\\pi}{L}$. We derive the\\nRegge trajectories of \
glueballs associated with the spinning folded \
string\\nconfigurations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
