               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0411089\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arutyunov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"G. Arutyunov and S. Frolov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable Hamiltonian for Classical Strings on AdS_5 x \
S^5\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages, LaTex; v2: a few comments added, misprints \
corrected,\\n  references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0502 (2005) 059\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/02/059\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2004-105\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find the Hamiltonian for physical excitations of the \
classical bosonic\\nstring propagating in the AdS_5 x S^5 space-time. The \
Hamiltonian is obtained\\nin a so-called uniform gauge which is related to \
the static gauge by a 2d\\nduality transformation. The Hamiltonian is of the \
Nambu type and depends on two\\nparameters: a single S^5 angular momentum J \
and the string tension \\\\lambda. In\\nthe general case both parameters can \
be finite. The space of string states\\nconsists of short and long strings. \
In the sector of short strings the large J\\nexpansion with \
\\\\lambda'=\\\\lambda/J^2 fixed recovers the plane-wave Hamiltonian\\nand \
higher-order corrections recently studied in the literature. In the \
strong\\ncoupling limit \\\\lambda\\\\to \\\\infty, J fixed, the energy of \
short strings scales\\nas \\\\sqrt[4]{\\\\lambda} while the energy of long \
strings scales as \\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}.\\nWe further show that the \
gauge-fixed Hamiltonian is integrable by constructing\\nthe corresponding Lax \
representation. We discuss some general properties of the\\nmonodromy matrix, \
and verify that the asymptotic behavior of the quasi-momentum\\nperfectly \
agrees with the one obtained earlier for some specific cases.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 8 Nov 2004 17:49:11 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 15 Nov 2004 16:09:58 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-10\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Arutyunov\"", ",", "\"G.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Frolov\"", ",", "\"S.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
