         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0411089", "submitter" -> "Arutyunov", "authors" -> 
            "G. Arutyunov and S. Frolov", "title" -> 
            "Integrable Hamiltonian for Classical Strings on AdS_5 x S^5", 
            "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, LaTex; v2: a few comments added, misprints corrected,\n\
  references added", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0502 (2005) 059", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2005/02/059", "report-no" -> "AEI-2004-105", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We find the Hamiltonian for physical excitations of the \
classical bosonic\nstring propagating in the AdS_5 x S^5 space-time. The \
Hamiltonian is obtained\nin a so-called uniform gauge which is related to the \
static gauge by a 2d\nduality transformation. The Hamiltonian is of the Nambu \
type and depends on two\nparameters: a single S^5 angular momentum J and the \
string tension \\lambda. In\nthe general case both parameters can be finite. \
The space of string states\nconsists of short and long strings. In the sector \
of short strings the large J\nexpansion with \\lambda'=\\lambda/J^2 fixed \
recovers the plane-wave Hamiltonian\nand higher-order corrections recently \
studied in the literature. In the strong\ncoupling limit \\lambda\\to \
\\infty, J fixed, the energy of short strings scales\nas \\sqrt[4]{\\lambda} \
while the energy of long strings scales as \\sqrt{\\lambda}.\nWe further show \
that the gauge-fixed Hamiltonian is integrable by constructing\nthe \
corresponding Lax representation. We discuss some general properties of the\n\
monodromy matrix, and verify that the asymptotic behavior of the \
quasi-momentum\nperfectly agrees with the one obtained earlier for some \
specific cases.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 8 Nov 2004 17:49:11 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 15 Nov 2004 16:09:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-10", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Arutyunov", "G.", ""}, {
              "Frolov", "S.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
