               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  AdS space is the universal covering of a hyperboloid. \
We consider the action\\nof the deck transformations on a classical string \
worldsheet in $AdS_5\\\\times\\nS^5$. We argue that these transformations are \
generated by an infinite linear\\ncombination of the local conserved charges. \
We conjecture that a similar\\nrelation holds for the corresponding operators \
on the field theory side. This\\nwould be a generalization of the recent \
field theory results showing that the\\none loop anomalous dimension is \
proportional to the Casimir operator in the\\nrepresentation of the Yangian \
algebra.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
