Fortsch.Phys.53:647-657,2005", "doi" -> "10.1002/prop.200410233", "report-no" -> 
             "UUITP-27/04, ITEP-TH-50/04", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
             "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  The Bethe ansatz can be used to compute anomalous dimensions \
in N=4 SYM\ntheory. The classical solutions of the sigma-model on AdS(5)xS(5) \
can also be\nparameterized by an integral equation of Bethe type. In this \
note the\nrelationship between the two Bethe ansaetze is reviewed following\n\
hep-th/0402207.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Mon, 22 Nov 2004 05:51:41 GMT"}, {
