analyse\nthe spectrum of the model and present some evidence in favour of \
Hagedorn and\nfractal behaviours. The decompactification limit of \
noncommutative torus\ninstantons is shown to map in a very precise way, at \
both the classical and\nquantum level, onto fluxon solutions on the \
noncommutative plane. The\nweak-coupling singularities of the usual \
Gross-Taylor string partition function\nfor QCD on the torus are studied in \
