                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"AEI 2004-088, ITEP-TH-51/04, NSF-KITP-04-116, PUTP-2139, \
UUITP-28/04\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We study the renormalization of gauge invariant \
operators in large Nc QCD. We\\ncompute the complete matrix of anomalous \
dimensions to leading order in the 't\\nHooft coupling and study its \
eigenvalues. Thinking of the mixing matrix as the\\nHamiltonian of a \
generalized spin chain we find a large integrable sector\\nconsisting of \
purely gluonic operators constructed with self-dual field\\nstrengths and an \
arbitrary number of derivatives. This sector contains the true\\nground state \
of the spin chain and all the gapless excitations above it. The\\nground \
state is essentially the anti-ferromagnetic ground state of a XXX1 \
spin\\nchain and the excitations carry either a chiral spin quantum number \
with\\nrelativistic dispersion relation or an anti-chiral one with \
non-relativistic\\ndispersion relation.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
