            "Wilson Line Correlators in N=4 Non-commutative Gauge Theory on \
S^2 x S^2", "comments" -> "33 pages, latex file,references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B715:665-694,2005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.02.022", "report-no" -> "KEK-TH-1002", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate the Wilson line correlators dual to \
supergravity multiplets in\nN=4 non-commutative gauge theory on S^2 x S^2. We \
find additional non-analytic\ncontributions to the correlators due to UV/IR \
mixing in comparison to ordinary\ngauge theory. Although they are no longer \
BPS off shell, their renormalization\neffects are finite as long as they \
carry finite momenta. We propose a\nrenormalization procedure to obtain local \
operators with no anomalous\ndimensions in perturbation theory. We reflect on \
our results from dual\nsupergravity point of view. We show that supergravity \
can account for both IR\nand UV/IR contributions.\n", 
