            "I.Y. Park, A. Tirziu and A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Spinning strings in AdS_5 x S^5: one-loop correction to energy \
in SL(2)\n  sector", "comments" -> 
            "31 pages, 1 figure, latex; v3: minor changes and corrections", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0503:013,2005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2005/03/013", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider a circular string with spin $S$ in $AdS_5$ wrapped \
around big\ncircle of $S^5$ and carrying also momentum $J$. The corresponding \
N=4 SYM\noperator belongs to the SL(2) sector, i.e. has tr$(D^S Z^J)+...$ \
structure. The\nleading large $J$ term in its 1-loop anomalous dimension can \
be computed using\nBethe ansatz for the SL(2) spin chain and was previously \
found to match the\nleading term in the classical string energy. The string \
solution is stable at\nlarge $J$, and the Lagrangian for string fluctuations \
has constant\ncoefficients, so that the 1-loop string correction to the \
energy $E_1$ is given\nsimply by the sum of characteristic frequencies. \
Curiously, we find that the\nleading term in the zero-mode part of $E_1$ is \
the same as a 1/J correction to\nthe one-loop anomalous dimension on the \
gauge theory (spin chain) side that was\nfound in hep-th/0410105. However, \
the contribution of non-zero string modes\ndoes not vanish. We also discuss \
the ``fast string'' expansion of the classical\nstring action which coincides \
with the coherent state action of the SL(2) spin\nchain at the first order in \
$\\l$, and extend this expansion to higher orders\nclarifying the role of the \
$S^5$ winding number.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
