               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0502054\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Richard Szabo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sam Halliday and Richard J. Szabo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Isometric Embeddings and Noncommutative Branes in \
Homogeneous\\n  Gravitational Waves\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"52 pages; v2: References added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Class.Quant.Grav. 22 (2005) 1945-1990\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/0264-9381/22/11/004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HWM-05-01, EMPG-05-01\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We characterize the worldvolume theories on symmetric \
D-branes in a\\nsix-dimensional Cahen-Wallach pp-wave supported by a constant \
Neveu-Schwarz\\nthree-form flux. We find a class of flat noncommutative \
euclidean D3-branes\\nanalogous to branes in a constant magnetic field, as \
well as curved\\nnoncommutative lorentzian D3-branes analogous to branes in \
an electric\\nbackground. In the former case the noncommutative field theory \
on the branes is\\nconstructed from first principles, related to dynamics of \
fuzzy spheres in the\\nworldvolumes, and used to analyse the flat space \
limits of the string theory.\\nThe worldvolume theories on all other \
symmetric branes in the background are\\nlocal field theories. The physical \
origins of all these theories are described\\nthrough the interplay between \
isometric embeddings of branes in the spacetime\\nand the Penrose-Gueven \
limit of AdS3 x S3 with Neveu-Schwarz three-form flux.\\nThe noncommutative \
field theory of a non-symmetric spacetime-filling D-brane is\\nalso \
constructed, giving a spatially varying but \
time-independent\\nnoncommutativity analogous to that of the Dolan-Nappi \
model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
