            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We characterize the worldvolume theories on symmetric D-branes \
in a\nsix-dimensional Cahen-Wallach pp-wave supported by a constant \
Neveu-Schwarz\nthree-form flux. We find a class of flat noncommutative \
euclidean D3-branes\nanalogous to branes in a constant magnetic field, as \
well as curved\nnoncommutative lorentzian D3-branes analogous to branes in an \
electric\nbackground. In the former case the noncommutative field theory on \
the branes is\nconstructed from first principles, related to dynamics of \
fuzzy spheres in the\nworldvolumes, and used to analyse the flat space limits \
of the string theory.\nThe worldvolume theories on all other symmetric branes \
in the background are\nlocal field theories. The physical origins of all \
these theories are described\nthrough the interplay between isometric \
embeddings of branes in the spacetime\nand the Penrose-Gueven limit of AdS3 x \
S3 with Neveu-Schwarz three-form flux.\nThe noncommutative field theory of a \
non-symmetric spacetime-filling D-brane is\nalso constructed, giving a \
spatially varying but time-independent\nnoncommutativity analogous to that of \
the Dolan-Nappi model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 4 Feb 2005 13:37:32 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 28 Feb 2005 11:12:06 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Halliday", "Sam", ""}, {
              "Szabo", "Richard J.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.422683960704827`, -5.149841803908789}, 0.],
