           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "hep-th/0502226", "submitter" -> "Niklas Beisert", 
             "authors" -> "N. Beisert, V.A. Kazakov, K. Sakai, K. Zarembo", 
             "title" -> 
             "The Algebraic Curve of Classical Superstrings on AdS_5xS^5", 
             "comments" -> 
             "56 pages, v2: first local charge derived, minor improvements,\n \
 references added, v3: minor corrections, reference added, to appear in\n  \
Commun. Math. Phys", "journal-ref" -> "Commun.Math.Phys.263:659-710,2006", 
             "doi" -> "10.1007/s00220-006-1529-4", "report-no" -> 
             "ITEP-TH-13/05, LPTENS-05/10, NSF-KITP-05-12, PUTP-2152, \
UUITP-03/05", "categories" -> "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  We investigate the monodromy of the Lax connection for \
classical IIB\nsuperstrings on AdS_5xS^5. For any solution of the equations \
of motion we\nderive a spectral curve of degree 4+4. The curve consists \
purely of conserved\nquantities, all gauge degrees of freedom have been \
eliminated in this form. The\nmost relevant quantities of the solution, such \
as its energy, can be expressed\nthrough certain holomorphic integrals on the \
curve. This allows for a\nclassification of finite gap solutions analogous to \
the general solution of\nstrings in flat space. The role of fermions in the \
context of the algebraic\ncurve is clarified. Finally, we derive a set of \
integral equations which\nreformulates the algebraic curve as a \
Riemann-Hilbert problem. They agree with\nthe planar, one-loop N=4 \
supersymmetric gauge theory proving the complete\nagreement of spectra in \
this approximation.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Fri, 25 Feb 2005 20:57:11 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
                "Fri, 25 Mar 2005 17:43:54 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
                "Mon, 3 Oct 2005 19:35:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2011-03-23", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Beisert", "N.", ""}, {
               "Kazakov", "V. A.", ""}, {"Sakai", "K.", ""}, {
               "Zarembo", "K.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ]}, 
        TagBox[
