            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We derive the coherent state representation of the integrable \
spin chain\nHamiltonian with non-compact supersymmetry group G=SU(1,1|1). By \
passing to the\ncontinuous limit, we find a spin chain sigma model describing \
a string moving\non the supercoset G/H, H being the stabilizer group. The \
action is written in a\nmanifestly G-invariant form in terms of the Cartan \
forms and the string\ncoordinates in the supercoset.\n  The spin chain sigma \
model is shown to agree with that following from the\nGreen-Schwarz action \
describing two-charged string spinning on AdS_5 x S^5.\n", 
