               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0503185\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Bogdan Stefanski jr.\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"B. Stefanski, Jr., A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Super spin chain coherent state actions and $AdS_5 \
\\\\times S^5$\\n  superstring\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"33 pages, LaTeX\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B718:83-112,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.04.026\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider a generalization of the leading-order \
matching of coherent state\\nactions for semiclassical states on the super \
Yang-Mills and the superstring\\nsides of the AdS/CFT duality to sectors with \
fermions. In particular, we\\ndiscuss the $SU(1|1)$ and $SU(2|3)$ sectors \
containing states with angular\\nmomentum $J$ in $S^5$ and spin in $AdS_5$. \
On the SYM side, we start with the\\ndilatation operator in the $SU(2|3)$ \
sector having super spin chain Hamiltonian\\ninterpretation and derive the \
corresponding coherent state action which is\\nquartic in fermions. This \
action has essentially the same ``Landau-Lifshitz''\\nform as the action in \
the bosonic SU(3) sector with the target space $CP^2$\\nreplaced by the \
projective superspace $CP^{2|2}$. We then attempt to relate it\\nto the \
corresponding truncation of the full $AdS_5 \\\\times S^5$ \
superstring\\naction written in a light-cone gauge where it has simple \
quartic fermionic\\nstructure. In particular, we find that part of the \
superstring action\\ndescribing $SU(1|1)$ sector reduces to an action of a \
massive two-dimensional\\nrelativistic fermion, with the expansion in the \
effective coupling\\n$\\\\lambda/J^2$ being equivalent to a non-relativistic \
expansion.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
