           "id" -> "hep-th/0503185", "submitter" -> "Bogdan Stefanski jr.", 
            "authors" -> "B. Stefanski, Jr., A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Super spin chain coherent state actions and $AdS_5 \\times S^5$\n\
  superstring", "comments" -> "33 pages, LaTeX", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B718:83-112,2005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.04.026", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider a generalization of the leading-order matching of \
coherent state\nactions for semiclassical states on the super Yang-Mills and \
the superstring\nsides of the AdS/CFT duality to sectors with fermions. In \
particular, we\ndiscuss the $SU(1|1)$ and $SU(2|3)$ sectors containing states \
with angular\nmomentum $J$ in $S^5$ and spin in $AdS_5$. On the SYM side, we \
start with the\ndilatation operator in the $SU(2|3)$ sector having super spin \
chain Hamiltonian\ninterpretation and derive the corresponding coherent state \
action which is\nquartic in fermions. This action has essentially the same \
``Landau-Lifshitz''\nform as the action in the bosonic SU(3) sector with the \
target space $CP^2$\nreplaced by the projective superspace $CP^{2|2}$. We \
then attempt to relate it\nto the corresponding truncation of the full $AdS_5 \
\\times S^5$ superstring\naction written in a light-cone gauge where it has \
simple quartic fermionic\nstructure. In particular, we find that part of the \
superstring action\ndescribing $SU(1|1)$ sector reduces to an action of a \
massive two-dimensional\nrelativistic fermion, with the expansion in the \
effective coupling\n$\\lambda/J^2$ being equivalent to a non-relativistic \
expansion.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 23 Mar 2005 21:49:55 GMT"}, {
