               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sergey Frolov Dr.\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sergey Frolov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lax Pair for Strings in Lunin-Maldacena Background\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, v2: a discussion of a 4+2 parameter solution \
added in\\n  section 5; new Appendix B with a 6+2 parameter deformation of \
AdS_5 x S^5;\\n  typos corrected, references added, v3: typos \
corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0505:069,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/05/069\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently Lunin and Maldacena used an SL(3,R) \
transformation of the AdS_5 x\\nS^5 background to generate a supergravity \
solution dual to a so-called\\nbeta-deformation of N = 4 super Yang-Mills \
theory. We use a\\nT-duality-shift-T-duality (TsT) transformation to obtain \
the beta-deformed\\nbackground for real beta, and show that solutions of \
string theory equations of\\nmotion in this background are in one-to-one \
correspondence with those in AdS_5\\nx S^5 with twisted boundary conditions \
imposed on the U(1) isometry fields. We\\nthen apply the TsT transformation \
to derive a local and periodic Lax pair for\\nthe bosonic part of string \
theory in the beta-deformed background. We also\\nperform a chain of three \
consecutive TsT transformations to generate a\\nthree-parameter deformation \
of AdS_5 x S^5. The three-parameter background is\\ndual to a \
nonsupersymmetric marginal deformation of N=4 SYM. Finally, we\\ncombine the \
TsT transformations with SL(2,R) ones to obtain a 6+2 parameter\\ndeformation \
of AdS_5 x S^5.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
