          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0503201", "submitter" -> "Sergey Frolov Dr.", 
            "authors" -> "Sergey Frolov", "title" -> 
            "Lax Pair for Strings in Lunin-Maldacena Background", "comments" -> 
            "28 pages, v2: a discussion of a 4+2 parameter solution added in\n\
  section 5; new Appendix B with a 6+2 parameter deformation of AdS_5 x S^5;\n\
  typos corrected, references added, v3: typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0505:069,2005", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2005/05/069", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently Lunin and Maldacena used an SL(3,R) transformation of \
the AdS_5 x\nS^5 background to generate a supergravity solution dual to a \
so-called\nbeta-deformation of N = 4 super Yang-Mills theory. We use a\n\
T-duality-shift-T-duality (TsT) transformation to obtain the beta-deformed\n\
background for real beta, and show that solutions of string theory equations \
of\nmotion in this background are in one-to-one correspondence with those in \
AdS_5\nx S^5 with twisted boundary conditions imposed on the U(1) isometry \
fields. We\nthen apply the TsT transformation to derive a local and periodic \
Lax pair for\nthe bosonic part of string theory in the beta-deformed \
background. We also\nperform a chain of three consecutive TsT transformations \
to generate a\nthree-parameter deformation of AdS_5 x S^5. The \
three-parameter background is\ndual to a nonsupersymmetric marginal \
deformation of N=4 SYM. Finally, we\ncombine the TsT transformations with \
SL(2,R) ones to obtain a 6+2 parameter\ndeformation of AdS_5 x S^5.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 25 Mar 2005 18:55:58 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 3 Apr 2005 19:06:39 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 25 May 2005 15:22:02 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Frolov", "Sergey", ""}}}], 
