               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It was conjectured that the classical bosonic string in \
AdS times a sphere\\nhas a special action variable which corresponds to the \
length of the operator\\non the field theory side. We discuss the analogous \
action variable in the\\nsine-Gordon model. We explain the relation between \
this action variable and the\\nBacklund transformations and show that the \
corresponding hidden symmetry acts\\non breathers by shifting their phase. It \
can be considered a nonlinear analogue\\nof splitting the solution of the \
free field equations into the positive- and\\nnegative-frequency \
part.\\n\""}]}, {
