            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0504039\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Akitsugu Miwa\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Akitsugu Miwa\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"BMN Operators from Wilson Loop\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"17 pages, v2: arguments on the correction terms expanded, \
references\\n  added, v3: minor corrections, to appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0506 (2005) 050\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/06/050\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"KUNS-1961\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that the BMN operators arise from the expansion \
of the Wilson loop in\\nfour-dimensional N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. The \
Wilson loop we consider is\\nobtained from ``dimensional reduction'' of \
ten-dimensional N=1 super Yang-Mills\\ntheory, and it contains six scalar \
fields as well as the gauge field. We expand\\nthe Wilson loop twice. First \
we expand it in powers of the fluctuations around\\na BPS loop configuration. \
Then we further expand each term in the result of the\\nfirst step in powers \
of the scalar field Z associated with the BPS\\nconfiguration. We find that \
each operator in this expansion with large number\\nof Z is the BMN operator. \
The number of fluctuations corresponds to the number\\nof impurities, and the \
phase factor of each BMN operator is supplied correctly.\\nWe have to impose \
the BPS condition on the loop for obtaining the complete form\\nof the BMN \
operators including the correction terms with \\\\bar Z. Our\\nobservation \
suggests the correspondence between the Wilson loop and the \
string\\nfield.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 5 Apr 2005 12:57:38 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
