           "id" -> "hep-th/0504039", "submitter" -> "Akitsugu Miwa", 
            "authors" -> "Akitsugu Miwa", "title" -> 
            "BMN Operators from Wilson Loop", "comments" -> 
            "17 pages, v2: arguments on the correction terms expanded, \
references\n  added, v3: minor corrections, to appear in JHEP", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0506 (2005) 050", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2005/06/050", 
            "report-no" -> "KUNS-1961", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We show that the BMN operators arise from the expansion of the \
Wilson loop in\nfour-dimensional N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. The Wilson loop \
we consider is\nobtained from ``dimensional reduction'' of ten-dimensional \
N=1 super Yang-Mills\ntheory, and it contains six scalar fields as well as \
the gauge field. We expand\nthe Wilson loop twice. First we expand it in \
powers of the fluctuations around\na BPS loop configuration. Then we further \
expand each term in the result of the\nfirst step in powers of the scalar \
field Z associated with the BPS\nconfiguration. We find that each operator in \
this expansion with large number\nof Z is the BMN operator. The number of \
fluctuations corresponds to the number\nof impurities, and the phase factor \
of each BMN operator is supplied correctly.\nWe have to impose the BPS \
condition on the loop for obtaining the complete form\nof the BMN operators \
including the correction terms with \\bar Z. Our\nobservation suggests the \
correspondence between the Wilson loop and the string\nfield.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
