               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0504144\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marija Zamaklar\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gleb Arutyunov and Marija Zamaklar\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Linking Backlund and Monodromy Charges for Strings on \
AdS_5 x S^5\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"25 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0507 (2005) 026\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/07/026\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"AEI-2005-003, SPIN-05/11, ITP-05/13\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find an explicit relation between the two known ways \
of generating an\\ninfinite set of local conserved charges for the string \
sigma model on AdS_5 x\\nS^5: the Backlund and monodromy approaches. We start \
by constructing the\\ntwo-parameter family of Backlund transformations for \
the string with an\\narbitrary world-sheet metric. We then show that only for \
a special value of one\\nof the parameters the solutions generated by this \
transformation are compatible\\nwith the Virasoro constraints. By solving the \
Backlund equations in a\\nnon-perturbative fashion, we finally show that the \
generating functional of the\\nBacklund conservation laws is equal to a \
certain sum of the quasi-momenta. The\\npositions of the quasi-momenta in the \
complex spectral plane are uniquely\\ndetermined by the real parameter of the \
Backlund transform.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 18 Apr 2005 19:05:01 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
