               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0504156\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Paul Heslop\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M. Bianchi, P.J. Heslop and F. Riccioni\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"More on La Grande Bouffe: towards higher spin symmetry \
breaking in AdS\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX file, JHEP3 class, 24 pages. Corrections to \
formulae in section\\n  5.1 and reference added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0508 (2005) 088\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/08/088\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"ROM2F-05/08, DAMTP-2005-40\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss higher spin gauge symmetry breaking in AdS \
space from a\\nholographic prespective. Indeed, the AdS/CFT correspondence \
implies that N=4\\nSYM theory at vanishing coupling constant is dual to a \
theory in AdS which\\nexhibits higher spin gauge symmetry enhancement. When \
the SYM coupling is\\nnon-zero, the current conservation condition becomes \
anomalous, and\\ncorrespondingly the local higher spin symmetry in the bulk \
gets spontaneously\\nbroken. In agreement with previous results and \
holographic expectations, we\\nfind that the Goldstone mode responsible for \
the symmetry breaking in AdS has a\\nnon-vanishing mass even in the limit in \
which the gauge symmetry is restored.\\nMoreover, we show that the mass of \
the Goldstone mode is exactly the one\\npredicted by the correspondence. \
Finally, we obtain the precise form of the\\nhigher spin supercurrents in the \
SYM side.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
