            "license" -> 
            "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", "abstract" -> 
            "  We show that there exists a certain limit in type I and type \
II superstring\ntheory in the presence of a suitable configuration of \
magnetic U(1) fields\nwhere all string excitations get an infinite mass, \
except for the neutral\nmassless sector and for the boson and fermion string \
states lying on the\nleading Regge trajectory. For a supersymmetric \
configuration of magnetic fields\nin internal directions, the resulting \
theory after the limit is a 3+1 Lorentz\ninvariant supersymmetric theory. \
Supersymmetry can be broken by introducing\nextra components of the magnetic \
field or else by finite temperature. In both\ncases we compute the one-loop \
partition function for the type I string model\nafter taking the limit, which \
turns out to be different from the Yang-Mills\nresult that arises by a direct \
$\\alpha'\\to 0$ limit. In the case of finite\ntemperature, no Hagedorn \
transition appears, in consistency with the reduction\nof the string \
spectrum. In type II superstring theory, the analogous limit is\nconstructed \
by starting with a configuration of Melvin twists in two or more\ncomplex \
planes. The resulting theory contains gravitation plus an infinite\nnumber of \
states of the leading Regge trajectory.\n", 
