               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Long-Range PSU(2,2|4) Bethe Ansaetze for Gauge Theory and \
Strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"67 pages, In Honor of Hans Bethe, v2: references added, \
typos fixed,\\n  sign conventions improved, v3: published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B727:1-62,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.06.038\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2005-092, PUTP-2159\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We generalize various existing higher-loop Bethe \
ansaetze for simple sectors\\nof the integrable long-range dynamic spin chain \
describing planar N=4 Super\\nYang-Mills Theory to the full psu(2,2|4) \
symmetry and, asymptotically, to\\narbitrary loop order. We perform a large \
number of tests of our conjectured\\nequations, such as internal consistency, \
comparison to direct three-loop\\ndiagonalization and expected thermodynamic \
behavior. In the special case of the\\nsu(1|2) subsector, corresponding to a \
long-range t-J model, we are able to\\nderive, up to three loops, the \
S-matrix and the associated nested Bethe ansatz\\nfrom the gauge theory \
dilatation operator. We conjecture novel all-order\\nS-matrices for the \
su(1|2) and su(1,1|2) subsectors, and show that they satisfy\\nthe \
Yang-Baxter equation. Throughout the paper, we muse about the idea \
that\\nquantum string theory on AdS_5xS^5 is also described by a psu(2,2|4) \
spin\\nchain. We propose asymptotic all-order Bethe equations for this \
putative\\n\\\"string chain\\\", which differ in a systematic fashion from \
the gauge theory\\nequations.\\n\""}]}, {
