               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0504203\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ian J. Swanson\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Tristan McLoughlin, Ian Swanson\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Open string integrability and AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2: minor clarifications, typos corrected, references \
added; v3:\\n  references added; LaTeX, 32 pages, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B723:132-162,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.06.014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CALT-68-2546\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a set of long-range Bethe ansatz equations \
for open quantum\\nstrings on AdS_5 x S^5 and demonstrate that they \
diagonalize bosonic su(2) and\\nsl(2) sectors of the theory in the \
near-pp-wave limit. Results are compared\\nwith energy spectra obtained by \
direct quantization of the open string theory,\\nand we find agreement in \
this limit to all orders in the 't Hooft coupling\\nlambda = g_YM^2 N_c. We \
also propose long-range Bethe ansaetze for su(2) and\\nsl(2) sectors of the \
dual N=2 defect conformal field theory. In accordance with\\nprevious \
investigations, we find exact agreement between string theory and\\ngauge \
theory at one- and two-loop order in lambda, but a general disagreement\\nat \
higher loops. It has been conjectured that the sudden mismatch at \
three-loop\\norder may be due to long-range interaction terms that are lost \
in the weak\\ncoupling expansion of the gauge theory dilatation operator. \
These terms are\\nthought to include interactions that wrap around \
gauge-traced operators, or\\naround the closed-string worldsheet. We comment \
on the role these interactions\\nplay in both open and closed sectors of \
string states and operators near the\\npp-wave/BMN limit of the AdS/CFT \
correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
