            "authors" -> "Tristan McLoughlin, Ian Swanson", "title" -> 
            "Open string integrability and AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "v2: minor clarifications, typos corrected, references added; v3:\
\n  references added; LaTeX, 32 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B723:132-162,2005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.06.014", "report-no" -> "CALT-68-2546", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We present a set of long-range Bethe ansatz equations for open \
quantum\nstrings on AdS_5 x S^5 and demonstrate that they diagonalize bosonic \
su(2) and\nsl(2) sectors of the theory in the near-pp-wave limit. Results are \
compared\nwith energy spectra obtained by direct quantization of the open \
string theory,\nand we find agreement in this limit to all orders in the 't \
Hooft coupling\nlambda = g_YM^2 N_c. We also propose long-range Bethe \
ansaetze for su(2) and\nsl(2) sectors of the dual N=2 defect conformal field \
theory. In accordance with\nprevious investigations, we find exact agreement \
between string theory and\ngauge theory at one- and two-loop order in lambda, \
but a general disagreement\nat higher loops. It has been conjectured that the \
sudden mismatch at three-loop\norder may be due to long-range interaction \
terms that are lost in the weak\ncoupling expansion of the gauge theory \
dilatation operator. These terms are\nthought to include interactions that \
wrap around gauge-traced operators, or\naround the closed-string worldsheet. \
We comment on the role these interactions\nplay in both open and closed \
sectors of string states and operators near the\npp-wave/BMN limit of the \
AdS/CFT correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
