references added,\\n  published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett. B624 (2005) 115-124\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2005.07.058\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"KEK-Th-1001, OU-HET-524, UTHEP-500\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We further study the correspondence between open \
semiclassical strings and\\nlong defect operators which is discussed in our \
previous work [hep-th/0410139].\\nWe give an interpretation of the \
spontaneous symmetry breaking of SO(6)->\\nSO(3)_H x SO(3)_V from the \
viewpoint of the Riemann surface by following the\\nargument of Minahan. Then \
we use the concrete form of the resolvent for a\\nsingle cut solution and \
compute the anomalous dimension of operators dual to an\\nopen pulsating \
string at three-loop level. In the string side we obtain the\\nenergy of the \
open pulsating string solution by semiclassical analysis. Both\\nresults \
agree at two-loop level but we find a three-loop discrepancy.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
