                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Swanson\"", ",", "\"Ian\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0505028", "submitter" -> "Ian J. Swanson", 
            "authors" -> "Ian Swanson", "title" -> 
            "Superstring holography and integrability in AdS_5 x S^5", 
            "comments" -> 
            "Ph.D. Thesis (revised and formatted), LaTeX, 190 pages; v2:\n  \
references added; v3: typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> "CALT-68-2542", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The AdS/CFT correspondence provides a rich testing ground for \
many important\ntopics in theoretical physics. The earliest and most striking \
example of the\ncorrespondence is the conjectured duality between the energy \
spectrum of type\nIIB superstring theory on AdS_5 x S^5 and the operator \
anomalous dimensions of\nN=4 supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory in four \
dimensions. While there is a\nsubstantial amount of evidence in support of \
this conjecture, direct tests have\nbeen elusive. The difficulty of \
quantizing superstring theory in a curved\nRamond-Ramond background is \
compounded by the problem of computing anomalous\ndimensions for non-BPS \
operators in the strongly coupled regime of the gauge\ntheory. The former \
problem can be circumvented to some extent by taking a\nPenrose limit of \
AdS_5 x S^5, reducing the background to that of a pp-wave\n(where the string \
theory is soluble). A corresponding limit of the gauge theory\nwas discovered \
by Berenstein, Maldacena and Nastase, who obtained successful\nagreement \
between a class of operator dimensions in this limit and\ncorresponding \
string energies in the Penrose limit. In this dissertation we\npresent a body \
of work based largely on the introduction of worldsheet\ninteraction \
corrections to the free pp-wave string theory by lifting the\nPenrose limit \
of AdS_5 x S^5. This provides a new class of rigorous tests of\nAdS/CFT that \
probe a truly quantum realm of the string theory. By studying the\n\
correspondence in greater detail, we stand to learn not only about how the\n\
duality is realized on a more microscopic level, but how Yang-Mills theories\n\
behave at strong coupling. The methods presented here will hopefully \
contribute\nto the realization of these important goals.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
