               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0505046\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Kruczenski\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Sergio Benvenuti and Martin Kruczenski\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Semiclassical strings in Sasaki-Einstein manifolds and \
long operators in\\n  N=1 gauge theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"44 pages, LaTeX, 9 figures. v2: References added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0610 (2006) 051\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/10/051\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the AdS/CFT relation between an infinite class \
of 5-d Ypq\\nSasaki-Einstein metrics and the corresponding quiver theories. \
The long BPS\\noperators of the field theories are matched to massless \
geodesics in the\\ngeometries, providing a test of AdS/CFT for these cases. \
Certain small\\nfluctuations (in the BMN sense) can also be successfully \
compared. We then go\\nfurther and find, using an appropriate limit, a \
reduced action, first order in\\ntime derivatives, which describes strings \
with large R-charge. In the field\\ntheory we consider holomorphic operators \
with large winding numbers around the\\nquiver and find, interestingly, that, \
after certain simplifying assumptions,\\nthey can be described effectively as \
strings moving in a particular metric.\\nAlthough not equal, the metric is \
similar to the one in the bulk. We find it\\nencouraging that a string \
picture emerges directly from the field theory and\\ndiscuss possible ways to \
improve the agreement.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
