            "Semiclassical strings in Sasaki-Einstein manifolds and long \
operators in\n  N=1 gauge theories", "comments" -> 
            "44 pages, LaTeX, 9 figures. v2: References added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0610 (2006) 051", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/10/051", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the AdS/CFT relation between an infinite class of 5-d \
Ypq\nSasaki-Einstein metrics and the corresponding quiver theories. The long \
BPS\noperators of the field theories are matched to massless geodesics in the\
\ngeometries, providing a test of AdS/CFT for these cases. Certain small\n\
fluctuations (in the BMN sense) can also be successfully compared. We then go\
\nfurther and find, using an appropriate limit, a reduced action, first order \
in\ntime derivatives, which describes strings with large R-charge. In the \
field\ntheory we consider holomorphic operators with large winding numbers \
around the\nquiver and find, interestingly, that, after certain simplifying \
assumptions,\nthey can be described effectively as strings moving in a \
particular metric.\nAlthough not equal, the metric is similar to the one in \
the bulk. We find it\nencouraging that a string picture emerges directly from \
the field theory and\ndiscuss possible ways to improve the agreement.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
