function of\n  composite operators", "comments" -> 
            "41 pages, LaTeX, 12 figures, minor changes, final version in \
NPB", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys. B723 (2005) 3-32", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.06.011", "report-no" -> 
            "MPP-2005-41, HU-EP-05/21", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We perform a systematic analysis of wrapping interactions for \
a general class\nof theories with color degrees of freedom, including N=4 \
SYM. Wrapping\ninteractions arise in the genus expansion of the 2-point \
function of composite\noperators as finite size effects that start to appear \
at a certain order in the\ncoupling constant at which the range of the \
interaction is equal to the length\nof the operators. We analyze in detail \
the relevant genus expansions, and\nintroduce a strategy to single out the \
wrapping contributions, based on adding\nspectator fields. We use a toy model \
to demonstrate our procedure, performing\nall computations explicitly. \
Although completely general, our treatment should\nbe particularly useful for \
applications to the recent problem of wrapping\ncontributions in some checks \
of the AdS/CFT correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
