               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0505075\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Laurence G. Yaffe\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Pavel Kovtun, Mithat Unsal and Laurence G. Yaffe\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Can large Nc equivalence between supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory and\\n  its orbifold projections be valid?\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, added discussion of anomaly matching in parent \
and\\n  daughter, and differences between N=4 and N=1 SYM cases\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev. D72 (2005) 105006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.72.105006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UW/PT 05-12\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Necessary and sufficient conditions for large Nc \
equivalence between parent\\nand daughter theories, for a wide class of \
orbifold projections of U(Nc) gauge\\ntheories, are just the natural \
requirements that the discrete symmetry used to\\ndefine the projection not \
be spontaneously broken in the parent theory, and the\\ndiscrete symmetry \
permuting equivalent gauge group factors not be spontaneously\\nbroken in the \
daughter theory. In this paper, we discuss the application of\\nthis result \
to Z_k projections of N=1 supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory in \
four\\ndimensions, as well as various multi-flavor generalizations. Z_k \
projections\\nwith k > 2 yielding chiral gauge theories violate the symmetry \
realization\\nconditions needed for large Nc equivalence, due to the \
spontaneous symmetry\\nbreaking of discrete chiral symmetry in the parent \
super-Yang-Mills theory. But\\nfor Z_2 projections, we show that previous \
assertions of large Nc\\ninequivalence, in infinite volume, between the \
parent and daughter theories\\nwere based on incorrect mappings of vacuum \
energies, theta angles, or connected\\ncorrelators between the two theories. \
With the correct identifications, there\\nis no sign of any inconsistency. A \
subtle but essential feature of the\\nconnection between parent and daughter \
theories involves multi-valuedness in\\nthe mapping of theta parameters from \
parent to daughter.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
