         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0505099", "submitter" -> "Radu Roiban", "authors" -> 
            "A. Dymarsky, I.R. Klebanov, R. Roiban", "title" -> 
            "Perturbative Search for Fixed Lines in Large N Gauge Theories", 
            "comments" -> 
            "31 pages, 4 figures, latex v2: Clarifications and reference \
added", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0508 (2005) 011", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2005/08/011", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The logarithmic running of marginal double-trace operators is \
a general\nfeature of 4-d field theories containing scalar fields in the \
adjoint or\nbifundamental representation. Such operators provide leading \
contributions in\nthe large N limit; therefore, the leading terms in their \
beta functions must\nvanish for a theory to be large N conformal. We \
calculate the one-loop beta\nfunctions in orbifolds of the N=4 SYM theory by \
a discrete subgroup Gamma of\nthe SU(4) R-symmetry, which are dual to string \
theory on AdS_5 x S^5/Gamma. We\npresent a general strategy for determining \
whether there is a fixed line\npassing through the origin of the coupling \
constant space. Then we study in\ndetail some classes of non-supersymmetric \
orbifold theories, and emphasize the\nimportance of decoupling the U(1) \
factors. Among our examples, which include\norbifolds acting freely on the \
S^5, we do not find any large N\nnon-supersymmetric theories with fixed lines \
passing through the origin.\nConnection of these results with closed string \
tachyon condensation in AdS_5 x\nS^5/Gamma is discussed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 11 May 2005 19:39:03 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 7 Jun 2005 13:24:35 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Dymarsky", "A.", ""}, {
              "Klebanov", "I. R.", ""}, {"Roiban", "R.", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
