            "  We consider circular strings rotating with equal spins \
S_1=S_2=S in two\northogonal planes in AdS_5 and suggest that they may be \
dual to \"long\" gauge\ntheory operators built out of self-dual components of \
gauge field strength. As\nwas found in hep-th/0404187, the one-loop anomalous \
dimensions of the such\ngauge-theory operators are described by an \
anti-ferromagnetic XXX_1 spin chain\nand scale linearly with length L>>1. We \
find that in the case of rigid rotating\nstring both the classical energy E_0 \
and the 1-loop string correction E_1\ndepend linearly on the spin S (within \
the stability region of the solution).\nThis supports the relation between \
the rigid rotating string and the\ngauge-theory operator corresponding to the \
maximal-spin (ferromagnetic) state\nof the XXX_1 spin chain. The energy of \
more general rotating and pulsating\nstrings also happens to scale linearly \
with both the spin and the oscillation\nnumber. Such solutions should be dual \
to other lower-spin states of the spin\nchain, with the anti-ferromagnetic \
ground state presumably corresponding to the\nstring pulsating in two planes \
with no rotation.\n", 
