               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Niklas Beisert\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"N. Beisert, R. Roiban\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Beauty and the Twist: The Bethe Ansatz for Twisted N=4 \
SYM\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"28 pages, v2: reference flip corrected, v3: some typos in\
\\n  (4.10,4.20,5.5) corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0508:039,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/08/039\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUTP-2162\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It was recently shown that the string theory duals of \
certain deformations of\\nthe N=4 gauge theory can be obtained by a \
combination of T-duality\\ntransformations and coordinate shifts. Here we \
work out the corresponding\\nprocedure of twisting the dual integrable spin \
chain and its Bethe ansatz. We\\nderive the Bethe equations for the complete \
twisted N=4 gauge theory at one and\\nhigher loops. These have a natural \
generalization which we identify as twists\\ninvolving the Cartan generators \
of the conformal algebra. The underlying model\\nappears to be a form of \
noncommutative deformation of N=4 SYM.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
