           "id" -> "hep-th/0507047", "submitter" -> "Machiko Hatsuda", 
            "authors" -> "Machiko Hatsuda", "title" -> 
            "Sugawara form for AdS superstring", "comments" -> 
            "16 pages, references added, version to appear in Nucl. Phys. B", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys. B730 (2005) 364-376", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.10.001", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We show that the stress-energy tensor for a superstring in the \
AdS5xS5\nbackground is written in a supersymmetric generalized \"Sugawara\" \
form. It is\nthe \"supertrace\" of the square of the right-invariant current \
which is the\nNoether current satisfying the flatness condition. The \
Wess-Zumino term is\ntaken into account through the supersymmetric gauge \
connection in the\nright-invariant currents, therefore the obtained \
stress-energy tensor is kappa\ninvariant. The integrability of the AdS \
superstring provides an infinite number\nof the conserved \"local\" currents \
which are supertraces of the n-th power of\nthe right-invariant current. For \
even n the \"local\" current reduces to terms\nproportional to the Virasoro \
constraint and the kappa symmetry constraint,\nwhile for odd n it reduces to \
a term proportional to the kappa symmetry\nconstraint .\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
