          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0507136\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jan Plefka\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jan Plefka\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spinning strings and integrable spin chains in the \
AdS/CFT\\n  correspondence\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 
                 "\"40 pages, invited contribution to Living Reviews in \
Relativity. v2:\\n  improvements in the text and references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LivingRev.Rel.8:9,2005\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.12942/lrr-2005-9\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2005-124\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this introductory review we discuss dynamical tests \
of the AdS_5 x S^5\\nstring/N=4 super Yang-Mills duality. After a brief \
introduction to AdS/CFT we\\nargue that semiclassical string energies yield \
information on the quantum\\nspectrum of the string in the limit of large \
angular momenta on the S^5. The\\nenergies of the folded and circular \
spinning string solutions rotating on a S^3\\nwithin the S^5 are derived, \
which yield all loop predictions for the dual gauge\\ntheory scaling \
dimensions. These follow from the eigenvalues of the dilatation\\noperator of \
N=4 super Yang-Mills in a minimal SU(2) subsector and we display\\nits \
reformulation in terms of a Heisenberg s=1/2 spin chain along with \
the\\ncoordinate Bethe ansatz for its explicit diagonalization. In order to \
make\\ncontact to the spinning string energies we then study the \
thermodynamic limit\\nof the one-loop gauge theory Bethe equations and \
demonstrate the matching with\\nthe folded and closed string result at this \
loop order. Finally the known gauge\\ntheory results at higher-loop orders \
are reviewed and the associated long-range\\nspin chain Bethe ansatz is \
introduced, leading to an asymptotic all-loop\\nconjecture for the gauge \
theory Bethe equations. This uncovers discrepancies at\\nthe three-loop order \
between gauge theory scaling dimensions and string theory\\nenergies and the \
implications of this are discussed. Along the way we comment\\non further \
developments and generalizations of the subject and point to the\\nrelevant \
literature.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 14 Jul 2005 12:47:55 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 5 Aug 2005 10:44:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
