         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0507136", "submitter" -> "Jan Plefka", "authors" -> 
            "Jan Plefka", "title" -> 
            "Spinning strings and integrable spin chains in the AdS/CFT\n  \
correspondence", "comments" -> 
            "40 pages, invited contribution to Living Reviews in Relativity. \
v2:\n  improvements in the text and references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "LivingRev.Rel.8:9,2005", "doi" -> "10.12942/lrr-2005-9", 
            "report-no" -> "AEI-2005-124", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In this introductory review we discuss dynamical tests of the \
AdS_5 x S^5\nstring/N=4 super Yang-Mills duality. After a brief introduction \
to AdS/CFT we\nargue that semiclassical string energies yield information on \
the quantum\nspectrum of the string in the limit of large angular momenta on \
the S^5. The\nenergies of the folded and circular spinning string solutions \
rotating on a S^3\nwithin the S^5 are derived, which yield all loop \
predictions for the dual gauge\ntheory scaling dimensions. These follow from \
the eigenvalues of the dilatation\noperator of N=4 super Yang-Mills in a \
minimal SU(2) subsector and we display\nits reformulation in terms of a \
Heisenberg s=1/2 spin chain along with the\ncoordinate Bethe ansatz for its \
explicit diagonalization. In order to make\ncontact to the spinning string \
energies we then study the thermodynamic limit\nof the one-loop gauge theory \
Bethe equations and demonstrate the matching with\nthe folded and closed \
string result at this loop order. Finally the known gauge\ntheory results at \
higher-loop orders are reviewed and the associated long-range\nspin chain \
Bethe ansatz is introduced, leading to an asymptotic all-loop\nconjecture for \
the gauge theory Bethe equations. This uncovers discrepancies at\nthe \
three-loop order between gauge theory scaling dimensions and string theory\n\
energies and the implications of this are discussed. Along the way we comment\
\non further developments and generalizations of the subject and point to the\
\nrelevant literature.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 14 Jul 2005 12:47:55 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 5 Aug 2005 10:44:27 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2015-06-26", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Plefka", "Jan", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
