               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0507261\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Mikhailov\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Mikhailov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Baecklund transformations, energy shift and the plane \
wave limit\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"30 pages LaTeX; v2,3,4: added explanations, discussion of \
canonicity\\n  (Section 2.2.5); v5: direct derivation of Eq. (64) (Section \
3.4); v6:\\n  corrected Section 2.2.2\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"CALT-68-2568, ITEP-TH-50/05\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss basic properties of the Baecklund \
transformations for the\\nclassical string in AdS space in the context of the \
null-surface perturbation\\ntheory. We explain the relation between the \
Baecklund transformations and the\\nenergy shift of the dual field theory \
state. We show that the Baecklund\\ntransformations can be represented as a \
finite-time evolution generated by a\\nspecial linear combination of the \
Pohlmeyer charges. This is a manifestation of\\nthe general property of \
Baecklund transformations known as spectrality. We also\\ndiscuss the plane \
wave limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
