            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/01/131", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We demonstrate that the one-loop anomalous dimension matrix in \
N = 2 SYM with\na single chiral hypermultiplet of fundamental matter, which \
is dual to AdS_5 X\nS^5 with a D7-brane filling AdS_5 and wrapped around an \
$^3 in the S^5, is an\nintegrable open spin chain Hamiltonian. We also use \
the doubling trick to\nrelate these open spin chains to closed spin chains in \
pure N = 4 SYM. By using\nthe AdS/CFT correspondence, we find a relation \
between the corresponding open\nand closed strings that differs from a simple \
doubling trick by terms that\nvanish in the semiclassical limit. We also \
demonstrate that in some cases the\nclosed string is simpler and easier to \
study than the corresponding open\nstring, and we speculate on the nature of \
corrections due to the presence of\nD-branes that this implies.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
