               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0508077\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Mark Van Raamsdonk\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ofer Aharony, Joseph Marsano, Shiraz Minwalla, Kyriakos \
Papadodimas,\\n  Mark Van Raamsdonk, and Toby Wiseman\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Phase Structure of Low Dimensional Large N Gauge \
Theories on Tori\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"harvmac, 67 pages, 21 figures. v2: minor corrections \
and\\n  clarifications\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0601:140,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/01/140\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we continue our study of the \
thermodynamics of large N gauge\\ntheories on compact spaces. We consider \
toroidal compactifications of pure\\nSU(N) Yang-Mills theories and of \
maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theories\\ndimensionally reduced to 0+1 \
or 1+1 dimensions, and generalizations of such\\ntheories where the adjoint \
fields are massive. We describe the phase structure\\nof these theories as a \
function of the gauge coupling, the geometry of the\\ncompact space and the \
mass parameters. In particular, we study the behavior of\\norder parameters \
associated with the holonomy of the gauge field around the\\ncycles of the \
torus. Our methods combine analytic analysis, numerical Monte\\nCarlo \
simulations, and (in the maximally supersymmetric case) information \
from\\nthe dual gravitational theories.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
