            "authors" -> 
            "Ofer Aharony, Joseph Marsano, Shiraz Minwalla, Kyriakos \
Papadodimas,\n  Mark Van Raamsdonk, and Toby Wiseman", "title" -> 
            "The Phase Structure of Low Dimensional Large N Gauge Theories on \
Tori", "comments" -> 
            "harvmac, 67 pages, 21 figures. v2: minor corrections and\n  \
clarifications", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0601:140,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/01/140", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we continue our study of the thermodynamics of \
large N gauge\ntheories on compact spaces. We consider toroidal \
compactifications of pure\nSU(N) Yang-Mills theories and of maximally \
supersymmetric Yang-Mills theories\ndimensionally reduced to 0+1 or 1+1 \
dimensions, and generalizations of such\ntheories where the adjoint fields \
are massive. We describe the phase structure\nof these theories as a function \
of the gauge coupling, the geometry of the\ncompact space and the mass \
parameters. In particular, we study the behavior of\norder parameters \
associated with the holonomy of the gauge field around the\ncycles of the \
torus. Our methods combine analytic analysis, numerical Monte\nCarlo \
simulations, and (in the maximally supersymmetric case) information from\nthe \
dual gravitational theories.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
