Gordon W.\\n  Semenoff and Donovan Young\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Divergence Cancellation and Loop Corrections in String \
Field Theory on a\\n  Plane Wave Background\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"27 pages; added references, acknowledgments, missing \
normalization in\\n  equations 2.3 - 2.8, also cleaned up notation, and added \
a few footnotes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0512 (2005) 017\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/12/017\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the one-loop energy shift E to certain \
two-impurity string\\nstates in light-cone string field theory on a plane \
wave background. We find\\nthat there exist logarithmic divergences in the \
sums over intermediate mode\\nnumbers which cancel between the cubic \
Hamiltonian and quartic ``contact\\nterm''. Analyzing the impurity \
non-conserving channel we find that the\\nnon-perturbative, order g_2^2 \
sqrt(lambda') contribution to E/mu predicted in\\nhep-th/0211220 is in fact \
an artifact of these logarithmic divergences and\\nvanishes with them, \
leaving an order g_2^2 lambda' contribution. Exploiting the\\nsupersymmetry \
algebra, we present a form for the energy shift which appears to\\nbe \
manifestly convergent and free of non-perturbative terms. We use this \
form\\nto argue that E/mu receives order g_2^2 lambda' contributions at every \
order in\\nintermediate state impurities.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
