            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0508140\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Luis Fernando Alday\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"L. F. Alday, G. Arutyunov, S. Frolov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"New Integrable System of 2dim Fermions from Strings on \
AdS_5 x S^5\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"35 pages;v2:typos corrected, references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0601:078,2006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/01/078\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider classical superstrings propagating on AdS_5 \
x S^5 space-time. We\\nconsistently truncate the superstring equations of \
motion to the so-called\\nsu(1|1) sector. By fixing the uniform gauge we show \
that physical excitations\\nin this sector are described by two complex \
fermionic degrees of freedom and we\\nobtain the corresponding Lagrangian. \
Remarkably, this Lagrangian can be cast in\\na two-dimensional \
Lorentz-invariant form. The kinetic part of the Lagrangian\\ninduces a \
non-trivial Poisson structure while the Hamiltonian is just the one\\nof the \
massive Dirac fermion. We find a change of variables which brings \
the\\nPoisson structure to the canonical form but makes the Hamiltonian \
nontrivial.\\nThe Hamiltonian is derived as an exact function of two \
parameters: the total\\nS^5 angular momentum J and string tension \\\\lambda; \
it is a polynomial in 1/J\\nand in \\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda'} where \\\\lambda'=\\\
\\frac{\\\\lambda}{J^2} is the effective BMN\\ncoupling. We identify the \
string states dual to the gauge theory operators from\\nthe closed su(1|1) \
sector of N=4 SYM and show that the corresponding near-plane\\nwave energy \
shift computed from our Hamiltonian perfectly agrees with that\\nrecently \
found in the literature. Finally we show that the Hamiltonian is\\nintegrable \
by explicitly constructing the corresponding Lax representation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 19 Aug 2005 13:47:13 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 27 Oct 2005 09:44:14 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
