           "id" -> "hep-th/0508140", "submitter" -> "Luis Fernando Alday", 
            "authors" -> "L. F. Alday, G. Arutyunov, S. Frolov", "title" -> 
            "New Integrable System of 2dim Fermions from Strings on AdS_5 x \
S^5", "comments" -> "35 pages;v2:typos corrected, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0601:078,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/01/078", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider classical superstrings propagating on AdS_5 x S^5 \
space-time. We\nconsistently truncate the superstring equations of motion to \
the so-called\nsu(1|1) sector. By fixing the uniform gauge we show that \
physical excitations\nin this sector are described by two complex fermionic \
degrees of freedom and we\nobtain the corresponding Lagrangian. Remarkably, \
this Lagrangian can be cast in\na two-dimensional Lorentz-invariant form. The \
kinetic part of the Lagrangian\ninduces a non-trivial Poisson structure while \
the Hamiltonian is just the one\nof the massive Dirac fermion. We find a \
change of variables which brings the\nPoisson structure to the canonical form \
but makes the Hamiltonian nontrivial.\nThe Hamiltonian is derived as an exact \
function of two parameters: the total\nS^5 angular momentum J and string \
tension \\lambda; it is a polynomial in 1/J\nand in \\sqrt{\\lambda'} where \
\\lambda'=\\frac{\\lambda}{J^2} is the effective BMN\ncoupling. We identify \
the string states dual to the gauge theory operators from\nthe closed su(1|1) \
sector of N=4 SYM and show that the corresponding near-plane\nwave energy \
shift computed from our Hamiltonian perfectly agrees with that\nrecently \
found in the literature. Finally we show that the Hamiltonian is\nintegrable \
by explicitly constructing the corresponding Lax representation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 19 Aug 2005 13:47:13 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 27 Oct 2005 09:44:14 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Alday", "L. F.", ""}, {
              "Arutyunov", "G.", ""}, {"Frolov", "S.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{13.1254368490512, -0.6712837708566521}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0508148\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Albion Lawrence\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Martin Kruczenski, Albion Lawrence\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Random walks and the Hagedorn transition\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"34 pages (7 of references), 5 figures. v2: Reference \
added, grant\\n  acknowledgement added, typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0607 (2006) 031\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/07/031\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"BRX-TH-556\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study details of the approach to the Hagedorn \
temperature in string theory\\nin various static spacetime backgrounds. We \
show that the partition function\\nfor a {\\\\it single} string at finite \
temperature is the torus amplitude\\nrestricted to unit winding around \
Euclidean time. We use the worldsheet path\\nintegral to derive the statement \
that the the sum over random walks of the\\nthermal scalar near the Hagedorn \
transition is precisely the image under a\\nmodular transformation of the sum \
over spatial configurations of a single\\nhighly excited string. We compute \
the radius of gyration of thermally excited\\nstrings in $AdS_D\\\\times \
S^n$. We show that the winding mode indicates an\\ninstability despite the \
AdS curvature at large radius, and that the negative\\nmass squared decreases \
with decreasing AdS radius, much like the type 0\\ntachyon. We add further \
arguments to statements by Barbon and Rabinovici, and\\nby Adams {\\\\it et. \
al.}, that the Euclidean AdS black hole can thought of as a\\ncondensate of \
the thermal scalar. We use this to provide circumstantial\\nevidence that the \
condensation of the thermal scalar decouples closed string\\nmodes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 22 Aug 2005 05:01:06 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 5 May 2006 19:32:17 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Kruczenski\"", ",", "\"Martin\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Lawrence\"", ",", "\"Albion\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
