            "authors" -> "Martin Kruczenski, Albion Lawrence", "title" -> 
            "Random walks and the Hagedorn transition", "comments" -> 
            "34 pages (7 of references), 5 figures. v2: Reference added, \
grant\n  acknowledgement added, typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0607 (2006) 031", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/07/031", 
            "report-no" -> "BRX-TH-556", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study details of the approach to the Hagedorn temperature \
in string theory\nin various static spacetime backgrounds. We show that the \
partition function\nfor a {\\it single} string at finite temperature is the \
torus amplitude\nrestricted to unit winding around Euclidean time. We use the \
worldsheet path\nintegral to derive the statement that the the sum over \
random walks of the\nthermal scalar near the Hagedorn transition is precisely \
the image under a\nmodular transformation of the sum over spatial \
configurations of a single\nhighly excited string. We compute the radius of \
gyration of thermally excited\nstrings in $AdS_D\\times S^n$. We show that \
the winding mode indicates an\ninstability despite the AdS curvature at large \
radius, and that the negative\nmass squared decreases with decreasing AdS \
radius, much like the type 0\ntachyon. We add further arguments to statements \
by Barbon and Rabinovici, and\nby Adams {\\it et. al.}, that the Euclidean \
AdS black hole can thought of as a\ncondensate of the thermal scalar. We use \
this to provide circumstantial\nevidence that the condensation of the thermal \
scalar decouples closed string\nmodes.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 22 Aug 2005 05:01:06 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 5 May 2006 19:32:17 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
