           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0508183\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"A. Melikyan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ashok Das, A. Melikyan, Matsuo Sato\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The algebra of flat currents for the string on AdS_5 x \
S^5 in the\\n  light-cone gauge\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"27 pages, references added, version published in \
JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0511:015,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/11/015\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We continue the program initiated in hep-th/0411200 and \
calculate the algebra\\nof the flat currents for the string on AdS_5 x S^5 \
background in the light-cone\\ngauge with kappa-symmetry fixed. We find that \
the algebra has a closed form and\\nthat the non-ultralocal terms come with a \
weight factor e^{\\\\phi} that depends\\non the radial AdS_5 coordinate. \
Based on results in two-dimensional sigma\\nmodels coupled to gravity via the \
dilaton field, this suggests that the algebra\\nof transition matrices in the \
present case is likely to be unambigous.\\n\""}]}, {
