         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0508183", "submitter" -> "A. Melikyan", "authors" -> 
            "Ashok Das, A. Melikyan, Matsuo Sato", "title" -> 
            "The algebra of flat currents for the string on AdS_5 x S^5 in \
the\n  light-cone gauge", "comments" -> 
            "27 pages, references added, version published in JHEP", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0511:015,2005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2005/11/015", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We continue the program initiated in hep-th/0411200 and \
calculate the algebra\nof the flat currents for the string on AdS_5 x S^5 \
background in the light-cone\ngauge with kappa-symmetry fixed. We find that \
the algebra has a closed form and\nthat the non-ultralocal terms come with a \
weight factor e^{\\phi} that depends\non the radial AdS_5 coordinate. Based \
on results in two-dimensional sigma\nmodels coupled to gravity via the \
dilaton field, this suggests that the algebra\nof transition matrices in the \
present case is likely to be unambigous.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 24 Aug 2005 17:54:17 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 21 Nov 2005 00:06:21 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
