            "Bethe Ansatz for a Quantum Supercoset Sigma Model", "comments" -> 
            "30 pages, 1 figure, v2: references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rev.D72:086002,2005", "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.72.086002",
             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null,
             "abstract" -> 
            "  We study an integrable conformal OSp(2m + 2|2m) supercoset \
model as an analog\nto the AdS_5 X S^5 superstring world-sheet theory. Using \
the known S-matrix for\nthis system, we obtain integral equations for states \
of large particle density\nin an SU(2) sector, which are exact in the sigma \
model coupling constant. As a\ncheck, we derive as a limit the general \
classical Bethe equation of Kazakov,\nMarshakov, Minahan, and Zarembo. There \
are two distinct quantum expansions\naround the well-studied classical limit, \
the lambda^{-1/2} effects and the 1/J\neffects. Our approach captures the \
first type, but not the second.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
