            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0509015\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"David Berenstein\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"David Berenstein, Diego H. Correa, Samuel E. \
Vazquez\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"All loop BMN state energies from matrices\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"19 pages, 2 figures. v2: typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0602 (2006) 048\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/02/048\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NSF-KITP-05-82\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a quantum corrected SO(6) invariant matrix \
quantum mechanics\\nobtained from the s-wave modes of the scalars of N = 4 \
SYM on S^3. For\\ncommuting matrices, this model is believed to describe the \
1/8 BPS states of\\nthe full SYM theory. In the large N limit the ground \
state corresponds to a\\ndistribution of eigenvalues on a S^5 which we \
identify with the sphere on the\\ndual geometry AdS_5x S^5. We then consider \
non-BPS excitations by studying\\nmatrix perturbations where the off-diagonal \
modes are treated perturbatively.\\nTo a first approximation, these modes can \
be described by a free theory of\\n\\\"string bits\\\" whose energies depend \
on the diagonal degrees of freedom. We then\\nconsider a state with two \
string bits and large angular momentum J on the\\nsphere. In the large J \
limit we use a simple saddle point approximation to show\\nthat the energy of \
these states coincides precisely with the BMN spectrum to\\nall orders in the \
't Hooft coupling. We also find some new problems with the\\nall loop Bethe \
Ansatz conjecture of the N=4 SYM planar spin chain model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
