           "id" -> "hep-th/0509015", "submitter" -> "David Berenstein", 
            "authors" -> 
            "David Berenstein, Diego H. Correa, Samuel E. Vazquez", "title" -> 
            "All loop BMN state energies from matrices", "comments" -> 
            "19 pages, 2 figures. v2: typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0602 (2006) 048", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/02/048", 
            "report-no" -> "NSF-KITP-05-82", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study a quantum corrected SO(6) invariant matrix quantum \
mechanics\nobtained from the s-wave modes of the scalars of N = 4 SYM on S^3. \
For\ncommuting matrices, this model is believed to describe the 1/8 BPS \
states of\nthe full SYM theory. In the large N limit the ground state \
corresponds to a\ndistribution of eigenvalues on a S^5 which we identify with \
the sphere on the\ndual geometry AdS_5x S^5. We then consider non-BPS \
excitations by studying\nmatrix perturbations where the off-diagonal modes \
are treated perturbatively.\nTo a first approximation, these modes can be \
described by a free theory of\n\"string bits\" whose energies depend on the \
diagonal degrees of freedom. We then\nconsider a state with two string bits \
and large angular momentum J on the\nsphere. In the large J limit we use a \
simple saddle point approximation to show\nthat the energy of these states \
coincides precisely with the BMN spectrum to\nall orders in the 't Hooft \
coupling. We also find some new problems with the\nall loop Bethe Ansatz \
conjecture of the N=4 SYM planar spin chain model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 1 Sep 2005 18:50:39 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 13 Oct 2005 23:29:42 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
