        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{5.589681776657196, -1.0746364378605424`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0509067\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jian-Huang She\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jian-Huang She\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A Matrix Model for Misner Universe and Closed String \
Tachyons\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"15 pages, no figures, harvmac; added discussion on \
space-time\\n  noncommutativity and consequences in cosmology; some \
conclusions better\\n  clarified, added comparison with McGreevy & \
Silverstein's work, added\\n  footnotes and references\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0601:002,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/01/002\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We use D-instantons to probe the geometry of Misner \
universe, and calculate\\nthe world volume field theory action, which is of \
the 1+0 dimensional form and\\nhighly non-local. Turning on closed string \
tachyons, we see from the deformed\\nmoduli space of the D-instantons that \
the spacelike singularity is removed and\\nthe region near the singularity \
becomes a fuzzy cone, where space and time do\\nnot commute. When realized \
cosmologically there can be controllable\\ntrans-planckian effects. And the \
infinite past is now causally connected with\\nthe infinite future, thus also \
providing a model for big crunch/big bang\\ntransition. In the spirit of IKKT \
matrix theory, we propose that the\\nD-instanton action here provides a \
holographic description for Misner universe\\nand time is generated \
dynamically. In addition we show that winding string\\nproduction from the \
vacua and instability of D-branes have simple uniform\\ninterpretations in \
this second quantized formalism.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 9 Sep 2005 16:23:32 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 9 Sep 2005 22:56:53 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 13 Sep 2005 08:18:37 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
