        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.892509992076757`, -3.57358206608742}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0509071\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alin Tirziu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.A. Minahan, A. Tirziu and A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1/J corrections to semiclassical AdS/CFT states from \
quantum\\n  Landau-Lifshitz model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"52 pages, references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B735:127-171,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.12.003\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  One way to relate semiclassical string states and dual \
gauge theory states is\\nto show the equivalence between their low-energy \
effective 2d actions. The\\ngauge theory effective action, which is \
represented by an effective\\nLandau-Lifshitz (LL) model, was previously \
found to match with the string\\ntheory world-sheet action up to the first \
two orders in the effective parameter\\n$\\\\tilde{\\\\lambda} ={\\\\lambda / \
J^2}$, where $\\\\lambda$ is the `t Hooft coupling\\nand $J$ is the total \
$R$-charge. Here we address the question if quantizing the\\neffective LL \
action reproduces the subleading 1/J corrections to the spin chain\\nenergies \
as well as the quantum corrections to the string energies. We\\ndemonstrate \
that this is indeed the case provided one chooses an \
appropriate\\nregularization of the effective LL theory. Expanding near the \
BPS vacuum, we\\nshow that the quantum LL action gives the same 1/J \
corrections to energies of\\nBMN states as found previously on the gauge \
theory and string theory sides. We\\nalso compute the subleading $1/J^2$ \
corrections and show that these too match\\nwith corrections computed from \
the Bethe ansatz. We also compare the results\\nfrom the LL action with a \
more direct computation from the spin chain. We\\nrepeat the same computation \
for the $\\\\beta$-deformed LL action and find that\\nthe quantum LL result \
is again equal to the 1/J correction computed from the\\n$\\\\beta$-deformed \
Bethe ansatz equations. We also quantize the LL action near\\nthe rotating \
circular and folded string solutions, generalizing the known\\ngauge/string \
results for 1/J corrections to the classical energies. We\\nemphasize the \
simplicity of this effective field theory approach as compared to\\nthe full \
quantum string computations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 9 Sep 2005 19:37:34 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
