                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"N. Beisert, A. A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On Quantum Corrections to Spinning Strings and Bethe \
Equations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"12 pages, v2, v3: minor corrections, footnotes and \
references added,\\n  v3: to appear in Phys. Lett. B\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett.B629:102-110,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2005.09.054\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PUTP-2175, NSF-KITP-05-73\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, it was demonstrated that one-loop energy \
shifts of spinning\\nsuperstrings on AdS5xS5 agree with certain Bethe \
equations for quantum strings\\nat small effective coupling. However, the \
string result required artificial\\nregularization by zeta-function. Here we \
show that this matching is indeed\\ncorrect up to fourth order in effective \
coupling; beyond, we find new\\ncontributions at odd powers. We show that \
these are reproduced by quantum\\ncorrections within the Bethe ansatz. They \
might also identify the \\\"three-loop\\ndiscrepancy\\\" between string and \
gauge theory as an order-of-limits effect.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
