ansatz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"20 pages; v2: refs and section on exponential corrections \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0510:044,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/10/044\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"AEI-2005-145, DESY-05-163, ZMP-HH/05-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze the effects of zeta-function regularization \
on the evaluation of\\nquantum corrections to spinning strings. Previously, \
this method was applied in\\nthe sl(2) subsector and yielded agreement to \
third order in perturbation theory\\nwith the quantum string Bethe ansatz. In \
this note we discuss related sums and\\ncompare zeta-function regularization \
against exact evaluation of the sums,\\nthereby showing that the \
zeta-function regularized expression misses out\\nperturbative as well as \
non-perturbative terms. In particular, this may imply\\ncorrections to the \
proposed quantum string Bethe equations. This also explains\\nthe previously \
observed discrepancy between the semi-classical string and the\\nquantum \
string Bethe ansatz in the regime of large winding number.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
