            "  We analyze the effects of zeta-function regularization on the \
evaluation of\nquantum corrections to spinning strings. Previously, this \
method was applied in\nthe sl(2) subsector and yielded agreement to third \
order in perturbation theory\nwith the quantum string Bethe ansatz. In this \
note we discuss related sums and\ncompare zeta-function regularization \
against exact evaluation of the sums,\nthereby showing that the zeta-function \
regularized expression misses out\nperturbative as well as non-perturbative \
terms. In particular, this may imply\ncorrections to the proposed quantum \
