            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0509132\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Radu Roiban\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A. Dymarsky, I.R. Klebanov and R. Roiban\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Perturbative Gauge Theory and Closed String \
Tachyons\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25 pages, Latex; V2: Clarifications and references \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0511:038,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/11/038\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We find an interesting connection between perturbative \
large N gauge theory\\nand closed superstrings. The gauge theory in question \
is found on N D3-branes\\nplaced at the tip of the cone R^6/Gamma. In our \
previous work we showed that,\\nwhen the orbifold group Gamma breaks all \
supersymmetry, then typically the\\ngauge theory is not conformal because of \
double-trace couplings whose one-loop\\nbeta functions do not possess real \
zeros. In this paper we observe a precise\\ncorrespondence between the \
instabilities caused by the flow of these\\ndouble-trace couplings and the \
presence of tachyons in the twisted sectors of\\ntype IIB theory on orbifolds \
R^{3,1}x R^6/Gamma. For each twisted sectors that\\ndoes not contain \
tachyons, we show that the corresponding double-trace coupling\\nflows to a \
fixed point and does not cause an instability. However, whenever a\\ntwisted \
sector is tachyonic, we find that the corresponding one-loop beta\\nfunction \
does not have a real zero, hence an instability is likely to exist in\\nthe \
gauge theory. We demonstrate explicitly the one-to-one \
correspondence\\nbetween the regions of stability/instability in the space of \
charges under\\nGamma that arise in the perturbative gauge theory and in the \
free string\\ntheory. Possible implications of this remarkably simple \
gauge/string\\ncorrespondence are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 16 Sep 2005 18:59:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 24 Oct 2005 13:29:22 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Dymarsky\"", ",", "\"A.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Klebanov\"", ",", "\"I. R.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Roiban\"", ",", "\"R.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
