            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0509178\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Kruczenski\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Kruczenski\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Renormalization group flow of reduced string \
actions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX.19 pages. No figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It has been argued that certain reduced actions play a \
role in AdS/CFT when\\ncomparing fast moving strings to long single trace \
operators in gauge theories.\\nSuch actions arise in two ways: as a limit of \
the string action and as a\\ndescription of long single trace field theory \
operators. They are\\nnon-relativistic sigma models with the target space \
usually being a Kahler\\nmanifold. They are non-renormalizable and need a \
cut-off in the wave-length. If\\nthe total spin (or charge) contained in a \
minimal wavelength is large compared\\nto one, the system behaves \
approximately classically and an expansion in loops\\nis meaningful.\\n  In \
this paper we apply the renormalization group procedure to such actions\\nand \
find, at one-loop, that the Kahler potential flows in the infrared to \
a\\nKahler-Einstein one.Therefore, in this context, the anomalous dimensions \
of\\nlong operators are determined by a fixed point. This suggests that \
certain\\nfeatures of the large N-limit might be independent of the detailed \
properties\\nof a gauge theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 22 Sep 2005 17:59:34 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2016-09-06\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Kruczenski\"", ",", "\"Martin\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                    "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> Left, 
             ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
