         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0509178", "submitter" -> "Martin Kruczenski", 
            "authors" -> "Martin Kruczenski", "title" -> 
            "Renormalization group flow of reduced string actions", 
            "comments" -> "LaTeX.19 pages. No figures", "journal-ref" -> Null,
             "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  It has been argued that certain reduced actions play a role in \
AdS/CFT when\ncomparing fast moving strings to long single trace operators in \
gauge theories.\nSuch actions arise in two ways: as a limit of the string \
action and as a\ndescription of long single trace field theory operators. \
They are\nnon-relativistic sigma models with the target space usually being a \
Kahler\nmanifold. They are non-renormalizable and need a cut-off in the \
wave-length. If\nthe total spin (or charge) contained in a minimal wavelength \
is large compared\nto one, the system behaves approximately classically and \
an expansion in loops\nis meaningful.\n  In this paper we apply the \
renormalization group procedure to such actions\nand find, at one-loop, that \
the Kahler potential flows in the infrared to a\nKahler-Einstein \
one.Therefore, in this context, the anomalous dimensions of\nlong operators \
are determined by a fixed point. This suggests that certain\nfeatures of the \
large N-limit might be independent of the detailed properties\nof a gauge \
theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 22 Sep 2005 17:59:34 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2016-09-06", 
