        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.27259299109207, -3.541351332540936}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0509195\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shijong Ryang\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shijong Ryang\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Rotating Strings with Two Unequal Spins in \
Lunin-Maldacena Background\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"13 pages, LaTeX, no figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0511:006,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/11/006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a string motion in the Lunin-Maldacena \
background, that is, the\\n\\\\beta-deformed AdS_5 \\\\times \\\\tilde{S}^5 \
background dual to a \\\\beta-deformation\\nof \\\\mathcal{N} = 4 super \
Yang-Mills theory. For real \\\\beta we construct a\\nrotating and wound \
string solution which has two unequal spins in \\\\tilde{S}^5.\\nThe string \
energy is expressed in terms of the spins, the winding numbers and\\nthe \
deformation parameter. In the expansion of \\\\lambda/J^2 with the total spin\
\\nJ and the string tension \\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda} we present ``one-loop\\\" \
and ``two-loop\\\"\\nenergy corrections. The ``one-loop\\\" one agrees with \
the one-loop anomalous\\ndimension of the corresponding gauge-theory scalar \
operators obtained in\\nhep-th/0503192 from the \\\\beta-deformed Bethe \
equation as well as the\\nanisotropic Landau-Lifshitz equation.\\n\""}]}, {
