            "authors" -> "Shijong Ryang", "title" -> 
            "Rotating Strings with Two Unequal Spins in Lunin-Maldacena \
Background", "comments" -> "13 pages, LaTeX, no figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP0511:006,2005", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2005/11/006", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study a string motion in the Lunin-Maldacena background, \
that is, the\n\\beta-deformed AdS_5 \\times \\tilde{S}^5 background dual to a \
\\beta-deformation\nof \\mathcal{N} = 4 super Yang-Mills theory. For real \
\\beta we construct a\nrotating and wound string solution which has two \
unequal spins in \\tilde{S}^5.\nThe string energy is expressed in terms of \
the spins, the winding numbers and\nthe deformation parameter. In the \
expansion of \\lambda/J^2 with the total spin\nJ and the string tension \
\\sqrt{\\lambda} we present ``one-loop\" and ``two-loop\"\nenergy \
corrections. The ``one-loop\" one agrees with the one-loop anomalous\n\
dimension of the corresponding gauge-theory scalar operators obtained in\n\
hep-th/0503192 from the \\beta-deformed Bethe equation as well as the\n\
anisotropic Landau-Lifshitz equation.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
