          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0510124\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Niklas Beisert\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"N. Beisert, T. Klose\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Long-Range GL(n) Integrable Spin Chains and Plane-Wave \
Matrix Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages, v2: reference added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Stat.Mech.0607:P07006,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1742-5468/2006/07/P07006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"AEI-2005-157, PUTP-2178, UUITP-19/05\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Quantum spin chains arise naturally from perturbative \
large-N field theories\\nand matrix models. The Hamiltonian of such a model \
is a long-range deformation\\nof nearest-neighbor type interactions. Here, we \
study the most general\\nlong-range integrable spin chain with spins \
transforming in the fundamental\\nrepresentation of gl(n). We derive the \
Hamiltonian and the corresponding\\nasymptotic Bethe ansatz at the leading \
four perturbative orders with several\\nfree parameters. Furthermore, we \
propose Bethe equations for all orders and\\nidentify the moduli of the \
integrable system. We finally apply our results to\\nplane-wave matrix theory \
and show that the Hamiltonian in a closed sector is\\nnot of this form and \
therefore not integrable beyond the first perturbative\\norder. This also \
implies that the complete model is not integrable.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 17 Oct 2005 15:45:34 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 27 Oct 2005 12:05:22 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-02-16\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
