            "authors" -> "N. Beisert, T. Klose", "title" -> 
            "Long-Range GL(n) Integrable Spin Chains and Plane-Wave Matrix \
Theory", "comments" -> "22 pages, v2: reference added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J.Stat.Mech.0607:P07006,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/2006/07/P07006", "report-no" -> 
            "AEI-2005-157, PUTP-2178, UUITP-19/05", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Quantum spin chains arise naturally from perturbative large-N \
field theories\nand matrix models. The Hamiltonian of such a model is a \
long-range deformation\nof nearest-neighbor type interactions. Here, we study \
the most general\nlong-range integrable spin chain with spins transforming in \
the fundamental\nrepresentation of gl(n). We derive the Hamiltonian and the \
corresponding\nasymptotic Bethe ansatz at the leading four perturbative \
orders with several\nfree parameters. Furthermore, we propose Bethe equations \
for all orders and\nidentify the moduli of the integrable system. We finally \
apply our results to\nplane-wave matrix theory and show that the Hamiltonian \
in a closed sector is\nnot of this form and therefore not integrable beyond \
the first perturbative\norder. This also implies that the complete model is \
not integrable.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 17 Oct 2005 15:45:34 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 27 Oct 2005 12:05:22 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
