        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.202954031400804`, -2.941983048197213}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0510136\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wung-Hong Huang\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wung-Hong Huang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Multi-spin String Solutions in Magnetic-flux Deformed \
$AdS_n \\\\times S^m$\\n  Spacetime\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex 15 pages, add a little comment in discussion\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0512:013,2005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2005/12/013\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We perform the dimensional reduction of the spacetime \
of a stack of N\\nD3-branes by the ``twist'' identification of a circle to \
obtain a new Melvin\\nbackground. In the near-horizon limit the background \
becomes the magnetic-flux\\ndeformed $AdS_5 \\\\times S^4$ or $AdS_4 \
\\\\times S^5$ spacetime. After analyzing\\nthe classical closed string \
solutions with several angular momenta in different\\ndirections of the \
deformed spacetimes we obtain two string solutions. The first\\nsolution \
describes a circular closed string located at a fixed value of\\ndeformed \
$AdS_5$ radius while rotating simultaneously in two planes in \
deformed\\n$AdS_5$ with equal spins $S$. The second solution describes a \
string rotating\\nin deformed $S^5$ with two equal angular momenta $J$ in the \
two rotation\\nplanes. We investigate the small fluctuations therein and show \
that the\\nmagnetic fluxes have inclination to improve the stability of these \
classical\\nstring solutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 17 Oct 2005 14:03:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
