               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Jan Ambjorn, Romuald A. Janik, Charlotte \
Kristjansen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wrapping interactions and a new source of corrections to \
the\\n  spin-chain/string duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, 1 figure; v3:references added; v4:journal \
version, minor\\n  corrections; v5: typo in acknowledgments fixed\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B736:288-301,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.12.007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Assuming that the world-sheet sigma-model in the \
AdS/CFT correspondence is an\\nintegrable {\\\\em quantum} field theory, we \
deduce that there might be new\\ncorrections to the spin-chain/string Bethe \
ansatz paradigm. These come from\\nvirtual particles propagating around the \
circumference of the cylinder and\\nrender Bethe ansatz quantization \
conditions only approximate. We determine the\\nnature of these corrections \
both at weak and at strong coupling in the near BMN\\nlimit, and find that \
the first corrections behave qualitatively as wrapping\\ninteractions at weak \
coupling.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
