            "authors" -> 
            "Jan Ambjorn, Romuald A. Janik, Charlotte Kristjansen", "title" -> 
            "Wrapping interactions and a new source of corrections to the\n  \
spin-chain/string duality", "comments" -> 
            "21 pages, 1 figure; v3:references added; v4:journal version, \
minor\n  corrections; v5: typo in acknowledgments fixed", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B736:288-301,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2005.12.007", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Assuming that the world-sheet sigma-model in the AdS/CFT \
correspondence is an\nintegrable {\\em quantum} field theory, we deduce that \
there might be new\ncorrections to the spin-chain/string Bethe ansatz \
paradigm. These come from\nvirtual particles propagating around the \
circumference of the cylinder and\nrender Bethe ansatz quantization \
conditions only approximate. We determine the\nnature of these corrections \
both at weak and at strong coupling in the near BMN\nlimit, and find that the \
first corrections behave qualitatively as wrapping\ninteractions at weak \
coupling.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 20 Oct 2005 08:27:49 GMT"}, {
