        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.26542701410118, -2.9133865261309495`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0510189\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mohammad M. Sheikh-Jabbari\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Darius Sadri, M. M. Sheikh-Jabbari\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable Spin Chains on the Conformal Moose\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"53 pages, 14 eps figures; Added references\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0603:024,2006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/03/024\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"IPM/P-2005/037, SU-ITP-05/30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider N=1, D=4 superconformal U(N)^{pq} \
Yang-Mills theories dual to\\nAdS_5xS^5/Z_pxZ_q orbifolds. We construct the \
dilatation operator of this\\nsuperconformal gauge theory at one-loop planar \
level. We demonstrate that a\\nspecific sector of this dilatation operator \
can be thought of as the transfer\\nmatrix for a two-dimensional statistical \
mechanical system, related to an\\nintegrable SU(3) anti-ferromagnetic spin \
chain system, which in turn is\\nequivalent to a 2+1-dimensional string \
theory where the spatial slices are\\ndiscretized on a triangular lattice. \
This is an extension of the SO(6) spin\\nchain picture of N=4 super \
Yang-Mills theory. We comment on the integrability\\nof this N=1 gauge theory \
and hence the corresponding three-dimensional\\nstatistical mechanical \
system, its connection to three-dimensional lattice\\ngauge theories, \
extensions to six-dimensional string theories, AdS/CFT type\\ndualities and \
finally their construction via orbifolds and brane-box models. In\\nthe \
process we discover a new class of almost-BPS BMN type operators with \
large\\nengineering dimensions but controllably small anomalous \
corrections.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sat, 22 Oct 2005 22:14:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 9 Nov 2005 07:15:54 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
