         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0510189", "submitter" -> 
            "Mohammad M. Sheikh-Jabbari", "authors" -> 
            "Darius Sadri, M. M. Sheikh-Jabbari", "title" -> 
            "Integrable Spin Chains on the Conformal Moose", "comments" -> 
            "53 pages, 14 eps figures; Added references", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0603:024,2006", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/03/024", 
            "report-no" -> "IPM/P-2005/037, SU-ITP-05/30", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider N=1, D=4 superconformal U(N)^{pq} Yang-Mills \
theories dual to\nAdS_5xS^5/Z_pxZ_q orbifolds. We construct the dilatation \
operator of this\nsuperconformal gauge theory at one-loop planar level. We \
demonstrate that a\nspecific sector of this dilatation operator can be \
thought of as the transfer\nmatrix for a two-dimensional statistical \
mechanical system, related to an\nintegrable SU(3) anti-ferromagnetic spin \
chain system, which in turn is\nequivalent to a 2+1-dimensional string theory \
where the spatial slices are\ndiscretized on a triangular lattice. This is an \
extension of the SO(6) spin\nchain picture of N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. We \
comment on the integrability\nof this N=1 gauge theory and hence the \
corresponding three-dimensional\nstatistical mechanical system, its \
connection to three-dimensional lattice\ngauge theories, extensions to \
six-dimensional string theories, AdS/CFT type\ndualities and finally their \
construction via orbifolds and brane-box models. In\nthe process we discover \
a new class of almost-BPS BMN type operators with large\nengineering \
dimensions but controllably small anomalous corrections.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 22 Oct 2005 22:14:41 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 9 Nov 2005 07:15:54 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
