            "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP nlin.SI", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We find explicit expressions for two first finite size \
corrections to the\ndistribution of Bethe roots, the asymptotics of energy \
and high conserved\ncharges in the sl(2) quantum Heisenberg spin chain of \
length J in the\nthermodynamical limit J->\\infty for low energies E\\sim \
1/J. This limit was\nrecently studied in the context of integrability in \
perturbative N=4\nsuper-Yang-Mills theory. We applied the double scaling \
technique to Baxter\nequation, similarly to the one used for large random \
matrices near the edge of\nthe eigenvalue distribution. The positions of \
Bethe roots are described near\nthe edge by zeros of Airy function. Our \
method can be generalized to any order\nin 1/J. It should also work for other \
quantum integrable models.\n", 
