            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0510208\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arutyunov Gleb E\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gleb Arutyunov and Sergey Frolov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Uniform Light-Cone Gauge for Strings in AdS_5 x S^5: \
Solving su(1|1)\\n  Sector\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages, Latex, v2: comparison to the strong coupling \
expansion of\\n  the quantum string Bethe ansatz is added, discussion of the \
winding sector is\\n  extended, references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0601:055,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/01/055\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"ITP-UU-05/47, SPIN-05/32, AEI-2005-160\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We introduce a uniform light-cone gauge for strings \
propagating in AdS\\nspace-time. We use the gauge to analyze strings from the \
su(1|1) sector, and\\nshow that the reduced model is described by a quadratic \
action for two complex\\nfermions. Thus, the uniform light-cone gauge allows \
us to solve the model\\nexactly. We analyze the near BMN spectrum of states \
from the su(1|1) sector and\\nshow that it correctly reproduces the 1/J \
corrections. We also compute the\\nspectrum in the strong coupling limit, and \
derive the famous \\\\lambda^{1/4}\\nasymptotics. We then show that the same \
string spectrum can be also derived by\\nsolving Bethe ansatz type equations, \
and discuss their relation to the quantum\\nstring Bethe ansatz for the \
su(1|1) sector.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 24 Oct 2005 16:16:59 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
