            "CALT-68-2581, ITEP-TH-69/05", "categories" -> "hep-th nlin.SI", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  It is well known that the classical string on a two-sphere is \
more or less\nequivalent to the sine-Gordon model. We consider the nonabelian \
dual of the\nclassical string on a two-sphere. We show that there is a \
projection map from\nthe phase space of this model to the phase space of the \
sine-Gordon model. The\ncorresponding Poisson structure of the sine-Gordon \
model is nonlocal with one\nintegration.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 7 Nov 2005 00:07:46 GMT"}, {
