         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0511139", "submitter" -> "Keisuke Okamura", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Keisuke Okamura, Yastoshi Takayama and Kentaroh Yoshida", 
            "title" -> "Open Spinning Strings and AdS/dCFT Duality", 
            "comments" -> 
            "1+50 pages, 7 figures, JHEP style, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0601:112,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/01/112", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider open spinning string solutions on an AdS_4 x \
S^2-brane (D5-brane)\nin the bulk AdS_5 x S^5 background. By taking account \
of the breaking of\nSO(6)_R to SO(3)_H x SO(3)_V due to the presence of the \
AdS-brane, the open\nrotating string ansatz is discussed. We construct the \
elliptic folded/circular\nopen string solutions in the SU(2) and the SL(2) \
sectors, so that they satisfy\nthe appropriate boundary conditions. On the \
other hand, in the SU(2) sector of\nthe gauge theory, we compute the matrix \
of anomalous dimension of the defect\noperator, which turns out to be the \
Hamiltonian of an open integrable spin\nchain. Then we consider the \
coordinate Bethe ansatz with arbitrary number of\nimpurities, and compare the \
boundary condition of the Bethe wavefunction with\nthat of the corresponding \
open string solution. We also discuss the Bethe\nansatz for the open SL(2) \
spin chain with several supports from the string\ntheory side. Then, in both \
SU(2) and SL(2) sectors, we analyze the Bethe\nequations in the thermodynamic \
limit and formulate the `doubling trick' on the\nRiemann surface associated \
with the gauge theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 14 Nov 2005 13:33:25 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 25 Nov 2005 11:24:44 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", 
