            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/03/051", "report-no" -> "DAMTP-2005-103", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We obtain the solutions and explicitly calculate the energy \
for a class of\ntwo-spin semiclassical string states in the Lunin-Maldacena \
background. These\nconfigurations are \\beta-deformed versions of the folded \
string solutions in\nAdS_{5}\\times S^{5} background. They correspond to \
certain single trace\noperators in the \\mathcal{N}=1 superconformal \\beta \
deformation of\n\\mathcal{N}=4 Yang-Mills. We calculate the one loop \
anomalous dimension for the\ndual single trace operator from the associated \
twisted spin chain with a\ngeneral two-cut distribution of Bethe roots. Our \
results show a striking match\nbetween the two calculations. We demonstrate \
the natural identification of\nparameters on the two sides of the analysis, \
and explain the significance of\nthe Virasoro constraint associated with the \
winding motion of semiclassical\nstrings from the perspective of the spin \
chain solution.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
