               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0511205\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sanjay Siwach\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Rabin Banerjee, Choonkyu Lee and Sanjay Siwach\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Deformed conformal and super-Poincar\\\\'e symmetries in \
the\\n  non-(anti)commutative spaces\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+19 pages, a typos in the title corrected, to appear in \
EPJC\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Eur.Phys.J.C48:305-313,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1140/epjc/s10052-006-0005-9\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"SNUTP/05-017\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Generators of the super-Poincar\\\\'e algebra in the \
non-(anti)commutative\\nsuperspace are represented using appropriate \
higher-derivative operators\\ndefined in this quantum superspace. Also \
discussed are the analogous\\nrepresentations of the conformal and \
superconformal symmetry generators in the\\ndeformed spaces. This \
construction is obtained by generalizing the recent work\\nof Wess et al on \
the Poincar\\\\'e generators in the $\\\\theta$-deformed Minkowski\\nspace, \
or by using the substitution rules we derived on the basis of \
the\\nphase-space structures of non-(anti)commutative-space variables. Even \
with the\\nnonzero deformation parameters the algebras remain unchanged \
although the\\ncomultiplication rules are deformed. The transformation of the \
fields under\\ndeformed symmetry is also discussed. Our construction can be \
used for\\nsystematic developments of field theories in the deformed \
spaces.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
