         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0511216", "submitter" -> "Radoslav Rashkov", 
            "authors" -> "N.P. Bobev, H. Dimov and R.C. Rashkov", "title" -> 
            "Semiclassical Strings, Dipole Deformations of N=1 SYM and \
Decoupling of\n  KK Modes", "comments" -> 
            "31 pages, references added, new solutions in Section 7 \
presented, an\n  appendix added, to appear in JHEP", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP0602:064,2006", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/02/064", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we investigate the recently found \
$\\gamma$-deformed\nMaldacena-Nunez background by studying the behavior of \
different semiclassical\nstring configurations. This background is \
conjectured to be dual to dipole\ndeformations of $\\N=1$ SYM. We compare our \
results to those in the pure\nMaldacena-Nunez background and show that the \
energies of our string\nconfigurations are higher than in the undeformed \
background. Thinking in the\nlines of (hep-th/0505100) we argue that this is \
an evidence for better\ndecoupling of the Kaluza-Klein modes from the pure \
SYM theory excitations.\nMoreover we are able to find a limit of the \
background in which the string\nenergy is independent of $\\gamma$, these \
strings are interpreted as\ncorresponding to pure gauge theory effects.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 22 Nov 2005 07:29:55 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 25 Nov 2005 13:42:06 GMT"}, {
