          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0512117\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wung-Hong Huang\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wung-Hong Huang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Semiclassical Strings in Electric and Magnetic Fields \
Deformed $AdS_5\\n  \\\\times S^5$ Spacetimes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex 18 pages, correct sec. 3.2\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D73:026007,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.73.026007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We first apply the transformation of mixing azimuthal \
and internal coordinate\\nor mixing time and internal coordinate to the 11D \
M-theory with a stack N\\nM2-branes to find the spacetime of a stack of N \
D2-branes with magnetic or\\nelectric flux in 10 D IIA string theory, after \
the Kaluza-Klein reduction. We\\nthen perform the T duality to the spacetime \
to find the background of a stack\\nof N D3-branes with magnetic or electric \
flux. In the near-horizon limit the\\nbackground becomes the magnetic or \
electric field deformed $AdS_5 \\\\times S^5$.\\nWe adopt an ansatz to find \
the classical string solution which is rotating in\\nthe deformed $S^5$ with \
three angular momenta in the three rotation planes. The\\nrelations between \
the classical string energy and its angular momenta are found\\nand results \
show that the external magnetic and electric fluxes will increase\\nthe \
string energy. Therefore, from the AdS/CFT point of view, the \
corrections\\nof the anomalous dimensions of operators in the dual SYM theory \
will be\\npositive. We also investigate the small fluctuations in these \
solutions and\\ndiscuss the effects of magnetic and electric fields on the \
stability of these\\nclassical rotating string solutions. Finally, we find \
the possible solutions of\\nstring pulsating on the deformed spacetimes and \
show that the corrections to\\nthe anomalous dimensions of operators in the \
dual SYM theory are non-negative.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 12 Dec 2005 14:48:29 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
