         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0512117", "submitter" -> "Wung-Hong Huang", 
            "authors" -> "Wung-Hong Huang", "title" -> 
            "Semiclassical Strings in Electric and Magnetic Fields Deformed \
$AdS_5\n  \\times S^5$ Spacetimes", "comments" -> 
            "Latex 18 pages, correct sec. 3.2", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rev.D73:026007,2006", "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.73.026007",
             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null,
             "abstract" -> 
            "  We first apply the transformation of mixing azimuthal and \
internal coordinate\nor mixing time and internal coordinate to the 11D \
M-theory with a stack N\nM2-branes to find the spacetime of a stack of N \
D2-branes with magnetic or\nelectric flux in 10 D IIA string theory, after \
the Kaluza-Klein reduction. We\nthen perform the T duality to the spacetime \
to find the background of a stack\nof N D3-branes with magnetic or electric \
flux. In the near-horizon limit the\nbackground becomes the magnetic or \
electric field deformed $AdS_5 \\times S^5$.\nWe adopt an ansatz to find the \
classical string solution which is rotating in\nthe deformed $S^5$ with three \
angular momenta in the three rotation planes. The\nrelations between the \
classical string energy and its angular momenta are found\nand results show \
that the external magnetic and electric fluxes will increase\nthe string \
energy. Therefore, from the AdS/CFT point of view, the corrections\nof the \
anomalous dimensions of operators in the dual SYM theory will be\npositive. \
We also investigate the small fluctuations in these solutions and\ndiscuss \
the effects of magnetic and electric fields on the stability of these\n\
classical rotating string solutions. Finally, we find the possible solutions \
of\nstring pulsating on the deformed spacetimes and show that the corrections \
to\nthe anomalous dimensions of operators in the dual SYM theory are \
non-negative.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 12 Dec 2005 14:48:29 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 18 Dec 2005 02:23:40 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 6 Jan 2006 12:57:58 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Huang", "Wung-Hong", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{0.571126772105476, -4.785077819761768}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0512203\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Harold Steinacker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"H. Grosse, H. Steinacker\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Renormalization of the noncommutative phi^3 model through \
the Kontsevich\\n  model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"30 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B746:202-226,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.04.007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UWThPh-2005-30\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We point out that the noncommutative selfdual phi^3 \
model can be mapped to\\nthe Kontsevich model, for a suitable choice of the \
eigenvalues in the latter.\\nThis allows to apply known results for the \
Kontsevich model to the quantization\\nof the field theory, in particular the \
KdV flows and Virasoro constraints. The\\n2-dimensional case is worked out \
explicitly. We obtain nonperturbative\\nexpressions for the genus expansion \
of the free energy and some n-point\\nfunctions. The full renormalization for \
finite coupling is found, which is\\ndetermined by the genus 0 sector only. \
All contributions in a genus expansion\\nof any n-point function are finite \
after renormalization. A critical coupling\\nis determined beyond which the \
model is unstable. The model is free of UV/IR\\ndiseases.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 16 Dec 2005 15:03:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Grosse\"", ",", "\"H.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Steinacker\"", ",", "\"H.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
