            "Renormalization of the noncommutative phi^3 model through the \
Kontsevich\n  model", "comments" -> "30 pages, 3 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B746:202-226,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.04.007", "report-no" -> 
            "UWThPh-2005-30", "categories" -> "hep-th math-ph math.MP", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We point out that the noncommutative selfdual phi^3 model can \
be mapped to\nthe Kontsevich model, for a suitable choice of the eigenvalues \
in the latter.\nThis allows to apply known results for the Kontsevich model \
to the quantization\nof the field theory, in particular the KdV flows and \
Virasoro constraints. The\n2-dimensional case is worked out explicitly. We \
obtain nonperturbative\nexpressions for the genus expansion of the free \
energy and some n-point\nfunctions. The full renormalization for finite \
coupling is found, which is\ndetermined by the genus 0 sector only. All \
contributions in a genus expansion\nof any n-point function are finite after \
renormalization. A critical coupling\nis determined beyond which the model is \
unstable. The model is free of UV/IR\ndiseases.\n", 
