            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0512253\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arutyunov Gleb E\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"L. F. Alday, G. Arutyunov, S. Frolov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Green-Schwarz Strings in TsT-transformed \
backgrounds\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages, latex, v2: typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0606:018,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/06/018\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"ITP-UU-05/58, SPIN-05/41, AEI-2005-186\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider classical strings propagating in a \
background generated by a\\nsequence of TsT transformations. We describe a \
general procedure to derive the\\nGreen-Schwarz action for strings. We show \
that the U(1) isometry variables of\\nthe TsT-transformed background are \
related to the isometry variables of the\\ninitial background in a universal \
way independent of the details of the\\nbackground. This allows us to prove \
that strings in the TsT-transformed\\nbackground are described by the \
Green-Schwarz action for strings in the initial\\nbackground subject to \
twisted boundary conditions. Our construction implies\\nthat a TsT \
transformation preserves integrability properties of the string\\nsigma \
model. We discuss in detail type IIB strings propagating in \
the\\n\\\\g_i-deformed AdS_5 x S^5 space-time, find the twisted boundary \
conditions for\\nbosons and fermions, and use them to write down an explicit \
expression for the\\nmonodromy matrix. We also discuss string zero modes \
whose dynamics is governed\\nby a fermionicgeneralization of the integrable \
Neumann model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 20 Dec 2005 18:00:21 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 15 Mar 2006 16:13:33 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Alday\"", ",", "\"L. F.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Arutyunov\"", ",", "\"G.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Frolov\"", ",", "\"S.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
