               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jian-Huang She\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Winding String Condensation and Noncommutative \
Deformation of Spacelike\\n  Singularity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"16 pages, no figures, harvmac; references added; added a \
section of\\n  discussion on disk and cylinder amplitudes\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D74:046005,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.74.046005\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In a previous paper (hep-th/0509067) using matrix \
model, we showed that\\nclosed string tachyons can resolve spacelike \
singularity in one particular\\nclass of Misner space (with anti-periodic \
boundary conditions for fermions\\naround the spatial circle). In this note, \
we show that for Misner space without\\nclosed string tachyons, there also \
exists a mechanism to resolve the\\nsingularity in the context of the matrix \
model, namely cosmological winding\\nstring production. We show that here \
space and time also become noncommutative\\ndue to these winding strings. \
Employing optical theorem, we study the bulk\\nboundary coupling by \
calculating the four-open-string cylinder amplitudes.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
