               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss a slow-moving limit of a rigid circular \
equal-spin solution on R x\\nS^3. We suggest that the solution with the \
winding number equal to the total\\nspin approximates the quantum string \
state dual to the maximal-dimension\\n``antiferromagnetic'' state of the \
SU(2) spin chain on the gauge theory side.\\nAn expansion of the string \
action near this solution leads to a weakly coupled\\nsystem of a sine-Gordon \
model and a free field. We show that a similar\\neffective Hamiltonian \
appears in a certain continuum limit from the half-filled\\nHubbard model \
that was recently suggested to describe the all-order dilatation\\noperator \
of the dual gauge theory in the SU(2) sector. We also discuss some\\nother \
slow-string solutions with one spin component in AdS_5 and one in \
S^5.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
