          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0601112\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Belitsky\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A.V. Belitsky, A.S. Gorsky, G.P. Korchemsky\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Logarithmic scaling in gauge/string correspondence\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"37 pages, 4 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B748:24-59,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.04.030\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study anomalous dimensions of (super)conformal \
Wilson operators at weak\\nand strong coupling making use of the \
integrability symmetry on both sides of\\nthe gauge/string correspondence and \
elucidate the origin of their\\nsingle-logarithmic behavior for long \
operators/strings in the limit of large\\nLorentz spin. On the gauge theory \
side, we apply the method of the Baxter\\nQ-operator to identify different \
scaling regimes in the anomalous dimensions in\\nintegrable sectors of \
(supersymmetric) Yang-Mills theory to one-loop order and\\ndetermine the \
values of the Lorentz spin at which the logarithmic scaling sets\\nin. We \
demonstrate that the conventional semiclassical approach based on \
the\\nanalysis of the distribution of Bethe roots breaks down in this domain. \
We work\\nout an asymptotic expression for the anomalous dimensions which is \
valid\\nthroughout the entire region of variation of the Lorentz spin. On the \
string\\ntheory side, the logarithmic scaling occurs when two most distant \
points of the\\nfolded spinning string approach the boundary of the AdS \
space. In terms of the\\nspectral curve for the classical string sigma model, \
the same configuration is\\ndescribed by an elliptic curve with two branching \
points approaching values\\ndetermined by the square root of the 't Hooft \
coupling constant. As a result,\\nthe anomalous dimensions cease to obey the \
BMN scaling and scale\\nlogarithmically with the Lorentz spin.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
