          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0601112", "submitter" -> "Andrei Belitsky", 
            "authors" -> "A.V. Belitsky, A.S. Gorsky, G.P. Korchemsky", 
            "title" -> "Logarithmic scaling in gauge/string correspondence", 
            "comments" -> "37 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B748:24-59,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.04.030", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study anomalous dimensions of (super)conformal Wilson \
operators at weak\nand strong coupling making use of the integrability \
symmetry on both sides of\nthe gauge/string correspondence and elucidate the \
origin of their\nsingle-logarithmic behavior for long operators/strings in \
the limit of large\nLorentz spin. On the gauge theory side, we apply the \
method of the Baxter\nQ-operator to identify different scaling regimes in the \
anomalous dimensions in\nintegrable sectors of (supersymmetric) Yang-Mills \
theory to one-loop order and\ndetermine the values of the Lorentz spin at \
which the logarithmic scaling sets\nin. We demonstrate that the conventional \
semiclassical approach based on the\nanalysis of the distribution of Bethe \
roots breaks down in this domain. We work\nout an asymptotic expression for \
the anomalous dimensions which is valid\nthroughout the entire region of \
variation of the Lorentz spin. On the string\ntheory side, the logarithmic \
scaling occurs when two most distant points of the\nfolded spinning string \
approach the boundary of the AdS space. In terms of the\nspectral curve for \
the classical string sigma model, the same configuration is\ndescribed by an \
elliptic curve with two branching points approaching values\ndetermined by \
the square root of the 't Hooft coupling constant. As a result,\nthe \
anomalous dimensions cease to obey the BMN scaling and scale\nlogarithmically \
with the Lorentz spin.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 16 Jan 2006 22:10:17 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 1 Feb 2006 00:38:36 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
