           "id" -> "hep-th/0601139", "submitter" -> "Alin Tirziu", "authors" -> 
            "A. Tirziu", "title" -> 
            "Quantum Landau-Lifshitz model at four loops: 1/J and 1/J^2 \
corrections\n  to BMN energies", "comments" -> "22 pages, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D73:106001,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.73.106001", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In a previous paper (hep-th/0510080) the effective \
Landau-Lifshitz (LL)\nLagrangians in the SU(2) sector coming from string \
theory and gauge theory have\nbeen found to three loops in the effective \
expansion parameter\n$\\tilde\\lambda=\\lambda/J^2$. In this paper we \
continue this study and find the\neffective Landau-Lifshitz Lagrangians to \
four loops. We extend to four-loops\n$\\tilde\\lambda^4$ the computations of \
1/J and $1/J^2$ corrections to BMN\nenergies done in hep-th/0510080 to \
three-loops. We compare these corrections\nobtained from quantum \
``gauge-theory'' LL action with the corrections obtained\nfrom the \
conjectured Bethe ansatz for the long range spin chain representing\n\
perturbative {large $N$} $\\NN=4$ Super Yang-Mills in the SU(2) sector and \
find\nperfect matching to four loops $\\tilde\\lambda^4$. We compare also the \
1/J and\n$1/J^2$ corrections obtained from quantum ``string-theory'' LL \
action with\nthose obtained from the \"quantum string\" Bethe ansatz and \
again find perfect\nmatching to four-loops.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 19 Jan 2006 18:03:51 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 30 Jan 2006 16:43:42 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
