         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{19.32162771296427, -4.123475276321808}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0601194\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Benoit Vicedo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nick Dorey and Benoit Vicedo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the Dynamics of Finite-Gap Solutions in Classical \
String Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"64 Pages, 5 Figures; typos corrected and references added\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0607:014,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/07/014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the dynamics of finite-gap solutions in \
classical string theory on R\\nx S^3. Each solution is characterised by a \
spectral curve, \\\\Sigma, of genus g\\nand a divisor, \\\\gamma, of degree g \
on the curve. We present a complete\\nreconstruction of the general solution \
and identify the corresponding\\nmoduli-space, M^(2g)_R, as a real symplectic \
manifold of dimension 2g. The\\ndynamics of the general solution is shown to \
be equivalent to a specific\\nHamiltonian integrable system with phase-space \
M^(2g)_R. The resulting\\ndescription resembles the free motion of a rigid \
string on the Jacobian torus\\nJ(\\\\Sigma). Interestingly, the \
canonically-normalised action variables of the\\nintegrable system are \
identified with certain filling fractions which play an\\nimportant role in \
the context of the AdS/CFT correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
