           "id" -> "hep-th/0601194", "submitter" -> "Benoit Vicedo", 
            "authors" -> "Nick Dorey and Benoit Vicedo", "title" -> 
            "On the Dynamics of Finite-Gap Solutions in Classical String \
Theory", "comments" -> 
            "64 Pages, 5 Figures; typos corrected and references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0607:014,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/07/014", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the dynamics of finite-gap solutions in classical \
string theory on R\nx S^3. Each solution is characterised by a spectral \
curve, \\Sigma, of genus g\nand a divisor, \\gamma, of degree g on the curve. \
We present a complete\nreconstruction of the general solution and identify \
the corresponding\nmoduli-space, M^(2g)_R, as a real symplectic manifold of \
dimension 2g. The\ndynamics of the general solution is shown to be equivalent \
to a specific\nHamiltonian integrable system with phase-space M^(2g)_R. The \
resulting\ndescription resembles the free motion of a rigid string on the \
Jacobian torus\nJ(\\Sigma). Interestingly, the canonically-normalised action \
variables of the\nintegrable system are identified with certain filling \
fractions which play an\nimportant role in the context of the AdS/CFT \
correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 25 Jan 2006 17:33:37 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 8 May 2006 13:54:50 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Dorey", "Nick", ""}, {
              "Vicedo", "Benoit", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
