               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the coherent state representation of the \
integrable spin chain\\nHamiltonian with supersymmetry group $SU(1,1|2)$. By \
the use of a projected\\nHamiltonian onto bosonic states, we give explicitly \
the action of the\\nHamiltonian on $SU(2)\\\\times SL(2)$ coherent states. \
Passing to the continuous\\nlimit, we find that the corresponding bosonic \
sigma model is the sum of the\\nknown SU(2) and SL(2) ones, and thus it gives \
a string spinning fast on\\n$S^1_{\\\\phi_1}\\\\times \
S^1_{\\\\phi_1}\\\\times S^1_{\\\\phi_2}$ in $\\\\rm{AdS}_5 \\\\times\\nS^5$. \
The full sigma model on the supercoset $SU(1,1|2)/SU(1|1)^2$ is \
given.\\n\""}]}, {
