            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0602100\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yuri Makeenko\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Yuri Makeenko (ITEP), Poul Olesen (NBI), Gordon W. \
Semenoff (UBC)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Cusped SYM Wilson loop at two loops and beyond\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"32pp., Latex, 6 figures\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B748:170-199,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.05.002\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Report-no: ITEP-TH-03/06\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We calculate the anomalous dimension of the cusped \
Wilson loop in ${\\\\cal\\nN}=4$ supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory to order \
$\\\\lambda^2$\\n($\\\\lambda=g^2_{YM}N$). We show that the cancellation \
between the diagrams with\\nthe three-point vertex and the self-energy \
insertion to the propagator which\\noccurs for smooth Wilson loops is not \
complete for cusped loops, so that an\\nanomaly term remains. This term \
contributes to the cusp anomalous dimension.\\nThe result agrees with the \
anomalous dimensions of twist-two conformal\\noperators with large spin. We \
verify the loop equation for cusped loops to\\norder $\\\\lambda^2$, \
reproducing the cusp anomalous dimension this way. We also\\nexamine the \
issue of summing ladder diagrams to all orders. We find an exact\\nsolution \
of the Bethe-Salpeter equation, summing light-cone ladder diagrams,\\nand \
show that for certain values of parameters it reduces to a Bessel \
function.\\nWe find that the ladder diagrams cannot reproduce for large \
$\\\\lambda$ the\\n$\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}$-behavior of the cusp anomalous \
dimension expected from the\\nAdS/CFT correspondence.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 9 Feb 2006 22:47:24 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 12 Feb 2006 18:24:11 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Makeenko\"", ",", "\"Yuri\"", ",", "\"\"", ",", 
                    "\"ITEP\""}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Olesen\"", ",", "\"Poul\"", ",", "\"\"", ",", 
                    "\"NBI\""}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Semenoff\"", ",", "\"Gordon W.\"", ",", "\"\"", ",", 
                    "\"UBC\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, 
