         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0602100", "submitter" -> "Yuri Makeenko", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Yuri Makeenko (ITEP), Poul Olesen (NBI), Gordon W. Semenoff \
(UBC)", "title" -> "Cusped SYM Wilson loop at two loops and beyond", 
            "comments" -> "32pp., Latex, 6 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys.B748:170-199,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.05.002", "report-no" -> 
            "Report-no: ITEP-TH-03/06", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate the anomalous dimension of the cusped Wilson loop \
in ${\\cal\nN}=4$ supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory to order $\\lambda^2$\n\
($\\lambda=g^2_{YM}N$). We show that the cancellation between the diagrams \
with\nthe three-point vertex and the self-energy insertion to the propagator \
which\noccurs for smooth Wilson loops is not complete for cusped loops, so \
that an\nanomaly term remains. This term contributes to the cusp anomalous \
dimension.\nThe result agrees with the anomalous dimensions of twist-two \
conformal\noperators with large spin. We verify the loop equation for cusped \
loops to\norder $\\lambda^2$, reproducing the cusp anomalous dimension this \
way. We also\nexamine the issue of summing ladder diagrams to all orders. We \
find an exact\nsolution of the Bethe-Salpeter equation, summing light-cone \
ladder diagrams,\nand show that for certain values of parameters it reduces \
to a Bessel function.\nWe find that the ladder diagrams cannot reproduce for \
large $\\lambda$ the\n$\\sqrt{\\lambda}$-behavior of the cusp anomalous \
dimension expected from the\nAdS/CFT correspondence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 9 Feb 2006 22:47:24 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 12 Feb 2006 18:24:11 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
