            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0602214\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sakura Schafer-Nameki\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Sakura Schafer-Nameki\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Exact expressions for quantum corrections to spinning \
strings\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"12 pages, 1 figure\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett.B639:571-578,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2006.03.033\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"DESY-06-018, ZMP-HH/06-02\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The one-loop worldsheet quantum corrections to the \
energy of spinning strings\\non R x S^3 within AdS_5 x S^5 are reexamined. \
The explicit expansion in the\\neffective 't Hooft coupling \\\\lambda'= \
\\\\lambda/J^2 is rigorously derived. The\\nexpansion contains both analytic \
and non-analytic terms in \\\\lambda', as well as\\nexponential corrections. \
Furthermore, we pin down the origin of the terms that\\nare not captured by \
the quantum string Bethe ansatz, which only produces\\nanalytic terms in \
\\\\lambda'. It is shown that the analytic terms arise from\\nstring \
fluctuations within the S^3, whereas the non-analytic and \
exponential\\nterms, which are not captured by the Bethe ansatz, originate \
from the\\nfluctuations in all directions within the supersymmetric sigma \
model on AdS_5 x\\nS^5. We also comment on the case of spinning string in \
AdS_3 x S^1.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 21 Feb 2006 18:35:27 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Schafer-Nameki\"", ",", "\"Sakura\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
