            "authors" -> "Sakura Schafer-Nameki", "title" -> 
            "Exact expressions for quantum corrections to spinning strings", 
            "comments" -> "12 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Lett.B639:571-578,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physletb.2006.03.033", "report-no" -> 
            "DESY-06-018, ZMP-HH/06-02", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The one-loop worldsheet quantum corrections to the energy of \
spinning strings\non R x S^3 within AdS_5 x S^5 are reexamined. The explicit \
expansion in the\neffective 't Hooft coupling \\lambda'= \\lambda/J^2 is \
rigorously derived. The\nexpansion contains both analytic and non-analytic \
terms in \\lambda', as well as\nexponential corrections. Furthermore, we pin \
down the origin of the terms that\nare not captured by the quantum string \
Bethe ansatz, which only produces\nanalytic terms in \\lambda'. It is shown \
that the analytic terms arise from\nstring fluctuations within the S^3, \
whereas the non-analytic and exponential\nterms, which are not captured by \
the Bethe ansatz, originate from the\nfluctuations in all directions within \
the supersymmetric sigma model on AdS_5 x\nS^5. We also comment on the case \
of spinning string in AdS_3 x S^1.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Tue, 21 Feb 2006 18:35:27 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Schafer-Nameki", "Sakura", ""}}}], 
