        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{12.234858654973959`, -3.4798643771412188`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0602255\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Igor Klebanov\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"I. R. Klebanov, J. Maldacena and C. B. Thorn\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Dynamics of Flux Tubes in Large N Gauge Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages, 4 figures; v2: clarifications in section 5, 1 \
reference\\n  added; v3: the final version (minor changes, 1 more reference \
added)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0604:024,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/04/024\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PUPT-2193, UFIFT-HEP-06-5\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The gluonic field created by a static quark anti-quark \
pair is described via\\nthe AdS/CFT correspondence by a string connecting the \
pair which is located on\\nthe boundary of AdS. Thus the gluonic field in a \
strongly coupled large N CFT\\nhas a stringy spectrum of excitations. We \
trace the stability of these\\nexcitations to a combination of large N \
suppressions and energy conservation.\\nComparison of the physics of the \
N=infinity flux tube in the {\\\\cal N}=4 SYM\\ntheory at weak and strong \
coupling shows that the excitations are present only\\nabove a certain \
critical coupling. The density of states of a highly excited\\nstring with a \
fold reaching towards the horizon of AdS is in exact agreement at\\nstrong \
coupling with that of the near-threshold states found in a ladder\\ndiagram \
model of the weak-strong coupling transition. We also study large\\ndistance \
correlations of local operators with a Wilson loop, and show that the\\nfall \
off at weak coupling and N=infinity (i.e. strictly planar diagrams)\\nmatches \
the strong coupling predictions given by the AdS/CFT correspondence,\\nrather \
than those of a weakly coupled U(1) gauge theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 24 Feb 2006 20:30:10 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 23 Mar 2006 21:19:08 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
