            "The AdS_5xS^5 superstring worldsheet S-matrix and crossing \
symmetry", "comments" -> 
            "27 pages, no figures; v2: sign typo fixed in (24), everything \
else\n  unchanged", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D73:086006,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.73.086006", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP math.QA", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  An S-matrix satisying the Yang-Baxter equation with symmetries \
relevant to\nthe AdS_5xS^5 superstring has recently been determined up to an \
unknown scalar\nfactor. Such scalar factors are typically fixed using \
crossing relations,\nhowever due to the lack of conventional relativistic \
invariance, in this case\nits determination remained an open problem.\n  In \
this paper we propose an algebraic way to implement crossing relations for\n\
the AdS_5xS^5 superstring worldsheet S-matrix. We base our construction on a\n\
Hopf-algebraic formulation of crossing in terms of the antipode and introduce\
\ngeneralized rapidities living on the universal cover of the parameter space\
\nwhich is constructed through an auxillary, coupling constant dependent,\n\
elliptic curve. We determine the crossing transformation and write functional\
\nequations for the scalar factor of the S-matrix in the generalized rapidity\
\nplane.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
