            "  We study the quantum Bethe ansatz equations in the O(2n) \
sigma-model for\nhysical particles on a circle, with the interaction given by \
the\nZamolodchikovs' S-matrix, in view of its application to quantization of \
the\nstring on the S^{2n-1} x R_t space. For a finite number of particles, \
the\nsystem looks like an inhomogeneous integrable O(2n) spin chain. \
Similarly to\nOSp(2m+n|2m) conformal sigma-model considered by Mann and \
Polchinski, we\nreproduce in the limit of large density of particles the \
finite gap\nKazakov-Marshakov-Minahan-Zarembo solution for the classical \
string and its\ngeneralization to the S^5 x R_t sector of the \
Green-Schwarz-Metsaev-Tseytlin\nsuperstring. We also reproduce some quantum \
effects: the BMN limit and the\nquantum homogeneous spin chain similar to the \
one describing the bosonic sector\nof the one-loop N=4 super Yang-Mills \
theory. We discuss the prospects of\ngeneralization of these Bethe equations \
to the full superstring sigma-model.\n", 
