            "authors" -> "Machiko Hatsuda and Shun'ya Mizoguchi", "title" -> 
            "Nonlocal charges of T-dual strings", "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, 1 figure", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0607:029,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/07/029", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We obtain sets of infinite number of conserved nonlocal \
charges of strings in\na flat space and pp-wave backgrounds, and compare them \
before and after\nT-duality transformation. In the flat background the set of \
nonlocal charges is\nthe same before and after the T-duality transformation \
with interchanging odd\nand even-order charges. In the IIB pp-wave background \
an infinite number of\nnonlocal charges are independent, contrast to that in \
a flat background only\nthe zero-th and first order charges are independent. \
In the IIA pp-wave\nbackground, which is the T-dualized compactified IIB \
pp-wave background, the\nzero-th order charges are included as a part of the \
set of nonlocal charges in\nthe IIB background. To make this correspondence \
complete a variable conjugate\nto the winding number is introduced as a \
Lagrange multiplier in the IIB action\na la Buscher's transformation.\n", 
