Yang-Mills\n  theory", "comments" -> "23 pages, Latex", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0605:033,2006", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/05/033", 
            "report-no" -> "ITP-UU-06-09, SPIN-06-07, Imperial-TP-AT-6-1", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider the highest-energy state in the su(1|1) sector of \
N=4 super\nYang-Mills theory containing operators of the form tr(Z^{L-M} \
\\psi^M) where Z\nis a complex scalar and \\psi is a component of gaugino. We \
show that this state\ncorresponds to the operator tr(\\psi^L) and can be \
viewed as an analogue of the\nantiferromagnetic state in the su(2) sector. We \
find perturbative expansions of\nthe energy of this state in both weak and \
strong 't Hooft coupling regimes\nusing asymptotic gauge theory Bethe ansatz \
equations. We also discuss a\npossible analog of this state in the \
conjectured string Bethe ansatz equations.\n", 
