            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0603157\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Burkhard Eden\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"B.Eden and M.Staudacher\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrability and Transcendentality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"45 pages LaTeX, 3 postscript figures. v2: Chapter on BMN \
scaling and\\n  transcendentality added. v3: version accepted for publication \
in JSTAT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Stat.Mech.0611:P11014,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1742-5468/2006/11/P11014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2005-165\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the two-loop Bethe ansatz for the sl(2) twist \
operator sector of\\nN=4 gauge theory directly from the field theory. We then \
analyze a recently\\nproposed perturbative asymptotic all-loop Bethe ansatz \
in the limit of large\\nspacetime spin at large but finite twist, and find a \
novel all-loop scaling\\nfunction. This function obeys the Kotikov-Lipatov \
transcendentality principle\\nand does not depend on the twist. Under the \
assumption that one may extrapolate\\nback to leading twist, our result \
yields an all-loop prediction for the\\nlarge-spin anomalous dimensions of \
twist-two operators. The latter also appears\\nas an undetermined function in \
a recent conjecture of Bern, Dixon and Smirnov\\nfor the all-loop structure \
of the maximally helicity violating (MHV) n-point\\ngluon amplitudes of N=4 \
gauge theory. This potentially establishes a direct\\nlink between the \
worldsheet and the spacetime S-matrix approach. A further\\nassumption for \
the validity of our prediction is that perturbative \
BMN\\n(Berenstein-Maldacena-Nastase) scaling does not break down at four \
loops, or\\nbeyond. We also discuss how the result gets modified if BMN \
scaling does break\\ndown. Finally, we show that our result qualitatively \
agrees at strong coupling\\nwith a prediction of string theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 20 Mar 2006 20:43:00 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 22 May 2006 17:44:13 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 14 Nov 2006 20:51:57 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2011-02-16\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Eden\"", ",", "\"B.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Staudacher\"", ",", "\"M.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
