           "id" -> "hep-th/0603157", "submitter" -> "Burkhard Eden", 
            "authors" -> "B.Eden and M.Staudacher", "title" -> 
            "Integrability and Transcendentality", "comments" -> 
            "45 pages LaTeX, 3 postscript figures. v2: Chapter on BMN scaling \
and\n  transcendentality added. v3: version accepted for publication in \
JSTAT", "journal-ref" -> "J.Stat.Mech.0611:P11014,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/2006/11/P11014", "report-no" -> "AEI-2005-165",
             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We derive the two-loop Bethe ansatz for the sl(2) twist \
operator sector of\nN=4 gauge theory directly from the field theory. We then \
analyze a recently\nproposed perturbative asymptotic all-loop Bethe ansatz in \
the limit of large\nspacetime spin at large but finite twist, and find a \
novel all-loop scaling\nfunction. This function obeys the Kotikov-Lipatov \
transcendentality principle\nand does not depend on the twist. Under the \
assumption that one may extrapolate\nback to leading twist, our result yields \
an all-loop prediction for the\nlarge-spin anomalous dimensions of twist-two \
operators. The latter also appears\nas an undetermined function in a recent \
conjecture of Bern, Dixon and Smirnov\nfor the all-loop structure of the \
maximally helicity violating (MHV) n-point\ngluon amplitudes of N=4 gauge \
theory. This potentially establishes a direct\nlink between the worldsheet \
and the spacetime S-matrix approach. A further\nassumption for the validity \
of our prediction is that perturbative BMN\n(Berenstein-Maldacena-Nastase) \
scaling does not break down at four loops, or\nbeyond. We also discuss how \
the result gets modified if BMN scaling does break\ndown. Finally, we show \
that our result qualitatively agrees at strong coupling\nwith a prediction of \
string theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 20 Mar 2006 20:43:00 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 22 May 2006 17:44:13 GMT"}, {
