            "authors" -> "G. Arutyunov and S. Frolov", "title" -> 
            "On AdS_5 x S^5 String S-matrix", "comments" -> 
            "10 pages, version2: misprints are corrected", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Lett.B639:378-382,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physletb.2006.06.064", "report-no" -> 
            "AEI-2006-022, ITP-UU-06-15, SPIN-06-13", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently two interesting conjectures about the string S-matrix \
on AdS_5 x S^5\nhave been made. First, assuming the existence of a Hopf \
algebra symmetry Janik\nderived a functional equation for the dressing factor \
of the quantum string\nBethe ansatz. Second, Hernandez and Lopez proposed an \
explicit form of\n1/\\sqrt\\lambda correction to the dressing factor. In this \
note we show that in\nthe strong coupling expansion Janik's equation is \
solved by the dressing factor\nup to the order of its validity. This \
observation provides a strong evidence in\nfavor of a conjectured Hopf \
algebra symmetry for strings in AdS_5 x S^5 as well\nas the perturbative \
string S-matrix.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 6 Apr 2006 13:49:41 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 9 Jun 2006 14:01:53 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
