            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0604058\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Steven Gubser\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"A. Dymarsky, S. Gubser, Z. Guralnik, and J. \
Maldacena\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Calibrated Surfaces and Supersymmetric Wilson \
Loops\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"28 pages, 2 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0609:057,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/09/057\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"PUPT-2194, Brown HET-1467, ITEP-TH-12-06\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the dual gravity description of supersymmetric \
Wilson loops whose\\nexpectation value is unity. They are described by \
calibrated surfaces that end\\non the boundary of anti de-Sitter space and \
are pseudo-holomorphic with respect\\nto an almost complex structure on an \
eight-dimensional slice of AdS_5 x S^5.\\nThe regularized area of these \
surfaces vanishes, in agreement with field theory\\nnon-renormalization \
theorems for the corresponding operators.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
