           "id" -> "hep-th/0604058", "submitter" -> "Steven Gubser", 
            "authors" -> 
            "A. Dymarsky, S. Gubser, Z. Guralnik, and J. Maldacena", "title" -> 
            "Calibrated Surfaces and Supersymmetric Wilson Loops", "comments" -> 
            "28 pages, 2 figures", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0609:057,2006", 
            "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/09/057", "report-no" -> 
            "PUPT-2194, Brown HET-1467, ITEP-TH-12-06", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the dual gravity description of supersymmetric Wilson \
loops whose\nexpectation value is unity. They are described by calibrated \
surfaces that end\non the boundary of anti de-Sitter space and are \
pseudo-holomorphic with respect\nto an almost complex structure on an \
eight-dimensional slice of AdS_5 x S^5.\nThe regularized area of these \
surfaces vanishes, in agreement with field theory\nnon-renormalization \
theorems for the corresponding operators.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 7 Apr 2006 22:17:04 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
