               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Higher Loop Bethe Ansatz for Open Spin-Chains in \
AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+24 pages, 1 figure, typos corrected, references added, \
discussions\\n  on the integrability for giant gravitons modified, version to \
appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0609:081,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/09/081\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We propose a perturbative asymptotic Bethe ansatz \
(PABA) for open spin-chain\\nsystems whose Hamiltonians are given by matrices \
of anomalous dimension for\\ncomposite operators, and apply it to two types \
of composite operators related\\nto two different brane configurations. One \
is an AdS_4 \\\\times S^2-brane in the\\nbulk AdS_5 \\\\times S^5 which gives \
rise to a defect conformal field theory\\n(dCFT) in the dual field theory, \
and the other is a giant graviton system with\\nan open string excitation. In \
both cases, excitations on open strings attaching\\nto D-branes (a D5-brane \
for the dCFT case, and a spherical D3-brane for the\\ngiant graviton case) \
can be represented by magnon states in the spin-chains\\nwith appropriate \
boundary conditions, in which informations of the D-branes are\\nencoded. We \
concentrate on single-magnon problems, and explain how to \
calculate\\nboundary S-matrices via the PABA technique. We also discuss the \
energy spectrum\\nin the BMN limit.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
