        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.243083442458904`, -2.2298870415844085`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0604108\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Michael McGuigan\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Michael McGuigan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Cosmological Constant Seesaw in String/M-Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"25 pages, 0 figures\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this paper we extend the Cosmological Constant \
Seesaw treatment of\\nhep-th/0602112 to String/M-Theory where the \
cosmological constant is finite. We\\ndiscuss how transitions between \
different $\\\\lambda$, one of Planckian vacuum\\nenergy, can give rise to a \
large $M_{Pl}^4$ denominator in the Cosmological\\nConstant Seesaw relation \
discussed by Banks, Motl and Carroll. We apply these\\nideas to 2d/3d \
String/M-Theory and show how the existence of a large N dual\\nfermionic \
theory makes the demonstration of a transition between \
different\\n$\\\\lambda$ relatively straight forward. We also consider 2d/3d \
Heterotic\\nString/M-Theory cosmology, a theory for which the large N dual is \
unknown. The\\nminisuperspace associated to these models is 26/27 dimensional \
for the SO(24)\\ntheory and 10/11 dimensional for the $SO(8) \\\\times E_8$ \
theory and consists of\\nthe $T$ fields as well as the dilaton and metric. 2d \
Heterotic String Quantum\\nCosmology is similar to critical string dynamics \
except for the inclusion of\\nthe 2d gauge fields. These 2d gauge fields have \
an important effect on the\\nvacuum energy and on transitions between \
different $\\\\lambda$ through the\\neffects of Wilson lines. Finally we \
discuss the extension to existing higher\\ndimensional string cosmologies \
possessing large N duals.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 14 Apr 2006 22:44:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2007-05-23\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"McGuigan\"", ",", "\"Michael\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
