           "id" -> "hep-th/0604108", "submitter" -> "Michael McGuigan", 
            "authors" -> "Michael McGuigan", "title" -> 
            "Cosmological Constant Seesaw in String/M-Theory", "comments" -> 
            "25 pages, 0 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  In this paper we extend the Cosmological Constant Seesaw \
treatment of\nhep-th/0602112 to String/M-Theory where the cosmological \
constant is finite. We\ndiscuss how transitions between different $\\lambda$, \
one of Planckian vacuum\nenergy, can give rise to a large $M_{Pl}^4$ \
denominator in the Cosmological\nConstant Seesaw relation discussed by Banks, \
Motl and Carroll. We apply these\nideas to 2d/3d String/M-Theory and show how \
the existence of a large N dual\nfermionic theory makes the demonstration of \
a transition between different\n$\\lambda$ relatively straight forward. We \
also consider 2d/3d Heterotic\nString/M-Theory cosmology, a theory for which \
the large N dual is unknown. The\nminisuperspace associated to these models \
is 26/27 dimensional for the SO(24)\ntheory and 10/11 dimensional for the \
$SO(8) \\times E_8$ theory and consists of\nthe $T$ fields as well as the \
dilaton and metric. 2d Heterotic String Quantum\nCosmology is similar to \
critical string dynamics except for the inclusion of\nthe 2d gauge fields. \
These 2d gauge fields have an important effect on the\nvacuum energy and on \
transitions between different $\\lambda$ through the\neffects of Wilson \
lines. Finally we discuss the extension to existing higher\ndimensional \
string cosmologies possessing large N duals.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 14 Apr 2006 22:44:12 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2007-05-23", "authors_parsed" -> {{"McGuigan", "Michael", ""}}}],
