          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0604124\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Nadav Drukker\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nadav Drukker and Shoichi Kawamoto\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Small deformations of supersymmetric Wilson loops and \
open spin-chains\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages, amstex, 4 figures. V2: Corrected eqn (2.14) and \
some\\n  equations in section 5. Version to appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0607:024,2006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/07/024\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study insertions of composite operators into Wilson \
loops in N=4\\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory in four dimensions. The loops \
follow a\\ncircular or straight path and the composite insertions transform \
in the adjoint\\nrepresentation of the gauge group. This provides a gauge \
invariant way to\\ndefine the correlator of non-singlet operators. Since the \
basic loop preserves\\nan SL(2,R) subgroup of the conformal group, we can \
assign a conformal dimension\\nto those insertions and calculate the \
corrections to the classical dimension in\\nperturbation theory. The \
calculation turns out to be very similar to that of\\nsingle-trace local \
operators and may also be expressed in terms of a\\nspin-chain. In this case \
the spin-chain is open and at one-loop order has\\nNeumann boundary \
conditions on the type of scalar insertions that we consider.\\nThis system \
is integrable and we write the Bethe ansatz describing it. We\\ncompare the \
spectrum in the limit of large angular momentum both in the dilute\\ngas \
approximation and the thermodynamic limit to the relevant string \
solution\\nin the BMN limit and in the full AdS_5 x S^5 metric and find \
agreement.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 18 Apr 2006 20:00:28 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 13 Jul 2006 14:42:14 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Drukker\"", ",", "\"Nadav\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kawamoto\"", ",", "\"Shoichi\"", ",", "\"\""}],
