            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study insertions of composite operators into Wilson loops \
in N=4\nsupersymmetric Yang-Mills theory in four dimensions. The loops follow \
a\ncircular or straight path and the composite insertions transform in the \
adjoint\nrepresentation of the gauge group. This provides a gauge invariant \
way to\ndefine the correlator of non-singlet operators. Since the basic loop \
preserves\nan SL(2,R) subgroup of the conformal group, we can assign a \
conformal dimension\nto those insertions and calculate the corrections to the \
classical dimension in\nperturbation theory. The calculation turns out to be \
very similar to that of\nsingle-trace local operators and may also be \
expressed in terms of a\nspin-chain. In this case the spin-chain is open and \
at one-loop order has\nNeumann boundary conditions on the type of scalar \
insertions that we consider.\nThis system is integrable and we write the \
Bethe ansatz describing it. We\ncompare the spectrum in the limit of large \
angular momentum both in the dilute\ngas approximation and the thermodynamic \
limit to the relevant string solution\nin the BMN limit and in the full AdS_5 \
x S^5 metric and find agreement.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
