         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0604151", "submitter" -> "Edward Witten", 
            "authors" -> "Anton Kapustin and Edward Witten", "title" -> 
            "Electric-Magnetic Duality And The Geometric Langlands Program", 
            "comments" -> "225 pp; further clarifications", "journal-ref" -> 
            Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The geometric Langlands program can be described in a natural \
way by\ncompactifying on a Riemann surface C a twisted version of N=4 super \
Yang-Mills\ntheory in four dimensions. The key ingredients are \
electric-magnetic duality of\ngauge theory, mirror symmetry of sigma-models, \
branes, Wilson and 't Hooft\noperators, and topological field theory. \
Seemingly esoteric notions of the\ngeometric Langlands program, such as Hecke \
eigensheaves and D-modules, arise\nnaturally from the physics.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 21 Apr 2006 19:17:43 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 15 Dec 2006 20:16:49 GMT"}, {
