               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Nick Dorey\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Nick Dorey\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Magnon Bound States and the AdS/CFT Correspondence\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX File, 14 Pages. Minor improvements and corrected \
references\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A39:13119-13128,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/0305-4470/39/41/S18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the spectrum of asymptotic states in the \
spin-chain description of\\nplanar N=4 SUSY Yang-Mills. In addition to \
elementary magnons, the asymptotic\\nspectrum includes an infinite tower of \
multi-magnon bound states with exact\\ndispersion relation, Delta-J_{1} = \
sqrt{Q^{2}+(lambda/pi^2)sin^2(p/2)}, where\\nthe positive integer Q is the \
number of constituent magnons. These states\\naccount precisely for the known \
poles in the exact S-matrix. Like the\\nelementary magnon, they transform in \
small representations of supersymmetry and\\nare present for all values of \
the 't Hooft coupling. At strong coupling we\\nidentify the dual states in \
semiclassical string theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
