               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0605018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ian J. Swanson\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Tristan McLoughlin and Ian Swanson\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrable twists in AdS/CFT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"v2: references and clarifications added, 46 pages\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0608:084,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/08/084\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  A class of marginal deformations of four-dimensional \
N=4 super Yang-Mills\\ntheory has been found to correspond to a set of \
smooth, multiparameter\\ndeformations of the S^5 target subspace in the \
holographic dual on AdS_5 x S^5.\\nWe present here an analogous set of \
deformations that act on global toroidal\\nisometries in the AdS_5 subspace. \
Remarkably, certain sectors of the string\\ntheory remain classically \
integrable in this larger class of so-called\\ngamma-deformed AdS_5 x S^5 \
backgrounds. Relying on studies of deformed\\nsu(2)_gamma models, we \
formulate a local sl(2)_gamma Lax representation that\\nadmits a classical, \
thermodynamic Bethe equation (based on the Riemann-Hilbert\\ninterpretation \
of Bethe's ansatz) encoding the spectrum in the deformed AdS_5\\ngeometry. \
This result is extended to a set of discretized, asymptotic Bethe\\nequations \
for the twisted string theory. Near-pp-wave energy spectra \
within\\nsl(2)_gamma and su(2)_gamma sectors provide a useful and stringent \
test of such\\nequations, demonstrating the reliability of this technology in \
a wider class of\\nstring backgrounds. In addition, we study a twisted \
Hubbard model that yields\\ncertain predictions of the dual beta-deformed \
gauge theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
