           "id" -> "hep-th/0605018", "submitter" -> "Ian J. Swanson", 
            "authors" -> "Tristan McLoughlin and Ian Swanson", "title" -> 
            "Integrable twists in AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "v2: references and clarifications added, 46 pages", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0608:084,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/08/084", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  A class of marginal deformations of four-dimensional N=4 super \
Yang-Mills\ntheory has been found to correspond to a set of smooth, \
multiparameter\ndeformations of the S^5 target subspace in the holographic \
dual on AdS_5 x S^5.\nWe present here an analogous set of deformations that \
act on global toroidal\nisometries in the AdS_5 subspace. Remarkably, certain \
sectors of the string\ntheory remain classically integrable in this larger \
class of so-called\ngamma-deformed AdS_5 x S^5 backgrounds. Relying on \
studies of deformed\nsu(2)_gamma models, we formulate a local sl(2)_gamma Lax \
representation that\nadmits a classical, thermodynamic Bethe equation (based \
on the Riemann-Hilbert\ninterpretation of Bethe's ansatz) encoding the \
spectrum in the deformed AdS_5\ngeometry. This result is extended to a set of \
discretized, asymptotic Bethe\nequations for the twisted string theory. \
Near-pp-wave energy spectra within\nsl(2)_gamma and su(2)_gamma sectors \
provide a useful and stringent test of such\nequations, demonstrating the \
reliability of this technology in a wider class of\nstring backgrounds. In \
addition, we study a twisted Hubbard model that yields\ncertain predictions \
of the dual beta-deformed gauge theory.\n", 
