               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Nelia Mann\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The SU(2) Long Range Bethe Ansatz and Continuous \
Integrable Systems\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"16 pages, v2: references added\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explore the relationship between the SU(2) sector of \
a general integrable\\nfield theory and the all-loop guess for the anomalous \
dimensions of SU(2)\\noperators in N=4 super Yang-Mills theory. We \
demonstrate that the SU(2)\\nstructure of a nested Bethe ansatz alone \
reproduces much of the all-loop guess\\nwithout depending on the details of \
the particular field theory. We speculate\\non the implications of this for \
strings in AdS_5 X S^5 being described by the\\nmulti-particle states of an \
integrable worldsheet theory, and relate the\\ntechniques here to the known \
relationship between the Hubbard model and the\\nall-loop guess.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
