            "authors" -> "Gleb Arutyunov, Sergey Frolov and Marija Zamaklar", 
            "title" -> "Finite-size Effects from Giant Magnons", "comments" -> 
            "42 pages, many figures, movies are available at\n  \
http://www.aei.mpg.de/~peekas/magnons/ ; v2: Additional comments included and\
\n  references added", "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B778:1-35,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.12.026", "report-no" -> 
            "AEI-2006-049, ITP-UU-06-28, SPIN-06-24", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  In order to analyze finite-size effects for the gauge-fixed \
string sigma\nmodel on AdS_5 x S^5, we construct one-soliton solutions \
carrying finite\nangular momentum J. In the infinite J limit the solutions \
reduce to the\nrecently constructed one-magnon configuration of Hofman and \
Maldacena. The\nsolutions do not satisfy the level-matching condition and \
hence exhibit a\ndependence on the gauge choice, which however disappears as \
the size J is taken\nto infinity. Interestingly, the solutions do not \
conserve all the global\ncharges of the psu(2,2|4) algebra of the sigma \
model, implying that the\nsymmetry algebra of the gauge-fixed string sigma \
model is different from\npsu(2,2|4) for finite J, once one gives up the \
level-matching condition. The\nmagnon dispersion relation exhibits \
exponential corrections with respect to the\ninfinite J solution. We also \
find a generalisation of our one-magnon\nconfiguration to a solution carrying \
two charges on the sphere. We comment on\nthe possible implications of our \
findings for the existence of the Bethe ansatz\ndescribing the spectrum of \
strings carrying finite charges.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 14 Jun 2006 16:48:06 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 17 Sep 2006 13:29:03 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Arutyunov", "Gleb", ""}, {
              "Frolov", "Sergey", ""}, {"Zamaklar", "Marija", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.19081520998283, -3.7022239759554614`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0606138\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matteo Beccaria\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Beccaria, Carmine Ortix\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Strong coupling anomalous dimensions of ${\\\\cal N} = 4$ \
super Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"38 pages, 16 eps figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0609:016,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/09/016\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the strong coupling behaviour of fixed length \
single trace operators\\nin the scalar SU(2) sector of ${\\\\cal N} = 4$ SYM. \
We assume the recently\\nproposed connection with a twisted half-filled \
Hubbard model. By explicit\\ndirect diagonalization of operators with length \
$L=4, 6, 8$ we study the full\\n{\\\\em perturbative multiplet} of those \
lattice states which have a clear\\ncorrespondence with gauge theory \
composite operators. For this multiplet, we\\nfollow the weak-strong coupling \
flow to free fermion states and identify in\\nparticular the precise \
asymptotic fermion configuration. Next, we analyze the\\nLieb-Wu equations of \
the twisted Hubbard model. For the antiferromagnetic state\\nwe derive its \
strong coupling expansion working at $L$ up to 32. We also study\\nthe \
lightest state in the perturbative multiplet. This state is non \
trivial\\nsince involves complex solutions of the Lieb-Wu equations. It is \
particularly\\ninteresting for $AdS_5\\\\times S^5$ duality since it is dual \
to the folded string\\nsemiclassical solution in the thermodynamical limit. \
We are able to perform the\\nfull analysis and compute the next-to-next-to \
leading terms in the strong\\ncoupling expansion for the non trivial lengths \
L=12 and L=20. A general formula\\nis proposed for the NLO expansion for any \
$L=4(2k+1)$, $k\\\\in\\\\mathbb{N}$.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 15 Jun 2006 15:05:34 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Beccaria\"", ",", "\"Matteo\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Ortix\"", ",", "\"Carmine\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0606138", "submitter" -> "Matteo Beccaria", 
            "authors" -> "Matteo Beccaria, Carmine Ortix", "title" -> 
            "Strong coupling anomalous dimensions of ${\\cal N} = 4$ super \
Yang-Mills", "comments" -> "38 pages, 16 eps figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP0609:016,2006", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/09/016", 
            "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the strong coupling behaviour of fixed length single \
trace operators\nin the scalar SU(2) sector of ${\\cal N} = 4$ SYM. We assume \
the recently\nproposed connection with a twisted half-filled Hubbard model. \
By explicit\ndirect diagonalization of operators with length $L=4, 6, 8$ we \
study the full\n{\\em perturbative multiplet} of those lattice states which \
have a clear\ncorrespondence with gauge theory composite operators. For this \
multiplet, we\nfollow the weak-strong coupling flow to free fermion states \
and identify in\nparticular the precise asymptotic fermion configuration. \
Next, we analyze the\nLieb-Wu equations of the twisted Hubbard model. For the \
antiferromagnetic state\nwe derive its strong coupling expansion working at \
$L$ up to 32. We also study\nthe lightest state in the perturbative \
multiplet. This state is non trivial\nsince involves complex solutions of the \
Lieb-Wu equations. It is particularly\ninteresting for $AdS_5\\times S^5$ \
duality since it is dual to the folded string\nsemiclassical solution in the \
thermodynamical limit. We are able to perform the\nfull analysis and compute \
the next-to-next-to leading terms in the strong\ncoupling expansion for the \
non trivial lengths L=12 and L=20. A general formula\nis proposed for the NLO \
expansion for any $L=4(2k+1)$, $k\\in\\mathbb{N}$.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 15 Jun 2006 15:05:34 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Beccaria", "Matteo", ""}, {
              "Ortix", "Carmine", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.241792896713637`, -3.251667214321814}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0606145\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alin Tirziu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.A. Minahan, A. Tirziu and A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Infinite spin limit of semiclassical string states\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"38 pages, 3 figures; v2: comments on derivation of bound \
states of\\n  magnons from discrete Bethe equations added in section 4 and \
appendix C,\\n  references added, Imperial-TP-AT-6-4, HUTP-06/A0024\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0608:049,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/08/049\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Motivated by recent works of Hofman and Maldacena and \
Dorey we consider a\\nspecial infinite spin limit of semiclassical spinning \
string states in AdS5 x\\nS5. We discuss examples of known folded and \
circular 2-spin string solutions\\nand demonstrate explicitly that the 1-loop \
superstring correction to the\\nclassical expression for the energy vanishes \
in the limit when one of the spins\\nis much larger that the other. We also \
give a general discussion of this limit\\nat the level of integral equations \
describing finite gap solutions of the\\nstring sigma model and argue that \
the corresponding asymptotic form of the\\nstring and gauge Bethe equations \
is the same.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 15 Jun 2006 18:49:26 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
