               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0607044\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Martin Kruczenski\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M. Kruczenski, J. Russo and A.A. Tseytlin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Spiky strings and giant magnons on S5\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"33 pages, LaTeX, 2 figures. v2: minor corrections, v3: \
minor\\n  corrections, figures enlarged\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0610:002,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/10/002\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Recently, classical solutions for strings moving in \
AdS5 x S5 have played an\\nimportant role in understanding the AdS/CFT \
correspondence. A large set of them\\nwere shown to follow from an ansatz \
that reduces the solution of the string\\nequations of motion to the study of \
a well-known integrable 1-d system known as\\nthe Neumann-Rosochatius (NR) \
system. However, other simple solutions such as\\nspiky strings or giant \
magnons in S5 were not included in the NR ansatz. We\\nshow that, when \
considered in the conformal gauge, these solutions can be also\\naccomodated \
by a version of the NR-system. This allows us to describe in detail\\na giant \
magnon solution with two additional angular momenta and show that it\\ncan be \
interpreted as a superposition of two magnons moving with the same\\nspeed. \
In addition, we consider the spin chain side and describe the\\ncorresponding \
state as that of two bound states in the infinite SU(3) spin\\nchain. We \
construct the Bethe ansatz wave function for such bound state.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 6 Jul 2006 19:40:22 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 7 Jul 2006 19:25:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v3\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 14 Jul 2006 21:35:01 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
