          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0607044", "submitter" -> "Martin Kruczenski", 
            "authors" -> "M. Kruczenski, J. Russo and A.A. Tseytlin", "title" -> 
            "Spiky strings and giant magnons on S5", "comments" -> 
            "33 pages, LaTeX, 2 figures. v2: minor corrections, v3: minor\n  \
corrections, figures enlarged", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0610:002,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/10/002", "report-no" -> Null, 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently, classical solutions for strings moving in AdS5 x S5 \
have played an\nimportant role in understanding the AdS/CFT correspondence. A \
large set of them\nwere shown to follow from an ansatz that reduces the \
solution of the string\nequations of motion to the study of a well-known \
integrable 1-d system known as\nthe Neumann-Rosochatius (NR) system. However, \
other simple solutions such as\nspiky strings or giant magnons in S5 were not \
included in the NR ansatz. We\nshow that, when considered in the conformal \
gauge, these solutions can be also\naccomodated by a version of the \
NR-system. This allows us to describe in detail\na giant magnon solution with \
two additional angular momenta and show that it\ncan be interpreted as a \
superposition of two magnons moving with the same\nspeed. In addition, we \
consider the spin chain side and describe the\ncorresponding state as that of \
two bound states in the infinite SU(3) spin\nchain. We construct the Bethe \
ansatz wave function for such bound state.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 6 Jul 2006 19:40:22 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 7 Jul 2006 19:25:12 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 14 Jul 2006 21:35:01 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kruczenski", "M.", ""}, {
              "Russo", "J.", ""}, {"Tseytlin", "A. A.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.561497525678117`, -3.926148954844007}, 0.],
