sector", "comments" -> 
            "11 pages, 1 figure; (v2) a reference added; (v3) comments added,\
\n  typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Lett.B645:293-298,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.physletb.2006.12.035", "report-no" -> "UTHEP-522", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the scaling law of the energy spectrum of classical \
strings on AdS_5\nx S^5, in particular, in the SL(2) sector for large S (AdS \
spin) and fixed J\n(S^1 \\subset S^5 spin). For any finite gap solution, we \
identify the limit in\nwhich the energy exhibits the logarithmic scaling in \
S, characteristic to the\nanomalous dimension of low-twist gauge theory \
operators. Our result therefore\nshows that the log S scaling, first observed \
by Gubser, Klebanov and Polyakov\nfor the folded string, is universal also on \
the string side, suggesting another\ninteresting window to explore the \
AdS/CFT correspondence as in the\nBMN/Frolov-Tseytlin limit.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
