           "id" -> "hep-th/0607235", "submitter" -> "Harold Steinacker", 
            "authors" -> "Harald Grosse, Harold Steinacker", "title" -> 
            
            "Exact renormalization of a noncommutative \\phi^3 model in 6 \
dimensions", "comments" -> 
            "32 pages, 3 figures. V2: discussion added, minor stylistic \
changes", "journal-ref" -> "Adv.Theor.Math.Phys.12:605,2008", "doi" -> Null, 
            "report-no" -> "UWThPh-2006-16", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th math-ph math.MP", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  The noncommutative selfdual \\phi^3 model in 6 dimensions is \
quantized and\nessentially solved, by mapping it to the Kontsevich model. The \
model is shown\nto be renormalizable and asymptotically free, and solvable \
genus by genus. It\nrequires both wavefunction and coupling constant \
renormalization. The exact\n(all-order) renormalization of the bare \
parameters is determined explicitly,\nwhich turns out to depend on the genus \
0 sector only. The running coupling\nconstant is also computed exactly, which \
decreases more rapidly than predicted\nby the one-loop beta function. A phase \
transition to an unstable phase is\nfound.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 28 Jul 2006 11:03:36 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 5 Jul 2007 16:36:43 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
