        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.555222866727444`, -2.8948570463820245`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0607236\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matteo Beccaria\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Matteo Beccaria, Luigi Del Debbio\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Bethe Ansatz solutions for highest states in ${\\\\cal \
N}=4$ SYM and\\n  AdS/CFT duality\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"42 pages, JHEP style LaTeX\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0609:025,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2006/09/025\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the operators with highest anomalous \
dimension $\\\\Delta$ in the\\ncompact rank-one sectors \
$\\\\mathfrak{su}(1|1)$ and $\\\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ of ${\\\\cal\\nN}=4$ super \
Yang-Mills. We study the flow of $\\\\Delta$ from weak to strong 't\\nHooft \
coupling $\\\\lambda$ by solving (i) the all-loop gauge Bethe Ansatz, \
(ii)\\nthe quantum string Bethe Ansatz. The two calculations are carefully \
compared in\\nthe strong coupling limit and exhibit different exponents \
$\\\\nu$ in the leading\\norder expansion $\\\\Delta\\\\sim \
\\\\lambda^{\\\\nu}$. We find $\\\\nu = 1/2$ and $\\\\nu = 1/4$\\nfor the \
gauge or string solution. This strong coupling discrepancy is \
not\\nunexpected, and it provides an explicit example where the gauge Bethe \
Ansatz\\nsolution cannot be trusted at large $\\\\lambda$. Instead, the \
string solution\\nperfectly reproduces the Gubser-Klebanov-Polyakov law \
$\\\\Delta = 2\\\\sqrt{n}\\n\\\\lambda^{1/4}$. In particular, we provide an \
analytic expression for the\\ninteger level $n$ as a function of the U(1) \
charge in both sectors.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 28 Jul 2006 11:11:21 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2010-02-03\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Beccaria\"", ",", "\"Matteo\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Del Debbio\"", ",", "\"Luigi\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
