               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The planar dilatation operator of N=4 supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills is the\\nhamiltonian of an integrable spin chain whose length is \
allowed to fluctuate.\\nWe will identify the dynamics of length fluctuations \
of planar N=4 Yang-Mills\\nwith the existence of an abelian Hopf algebra Z \
symmetry with non-trivial\\nco-multiplication and antipode. The intertwiner \
conditions for this Hopf\\nalgebra will restrict the allowed magnon irreps to \
those leading to the magnon\\ndispersion relation. We will discuss magnon \
kinematics and crossing symmetry on\\nthe spectrum of Z. We also consider \
general features of the underlying Hopf\\nalgebra with Z as central Hopf \
subalgebra, and discuss the giant magnon\\nsemiclassical regime.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
