            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0608156\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ofer Aharony\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ofer Aharony, Joseph Marsano and Mark Van \
Raamsdonk\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Two loop partition function for large N pure Yang-Mills \
theory on a\\n  small three-sphere\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages, 4 figures, harvmac\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D74:105012,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.74.105012\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"WIS/10/06-AUG-DPP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give a direct path-integral calculation of the \
partition function for pure\\n3+1 dimensional U(N) Yang-Mills theory at large \
N on a small three-sphere, up\\nto two-loop order in perturbation theory. \
From this, we calculate the one-loop\\nshift in the Hagedorn/deconfinement \
temperature for the theory at small volume,\\nfinding that it increases (in \
units of the inverse sphere radius) as we go to\\nlarger coupling (larger \
volume). Our results also allow us to read off the sum\\nof one-loop \
anomalous dimensions for all operators with a given engineering\\ndimension \
in planar Yang-Mills theory on R^4. As checks on our calculation, \
we\\nreproduce both the Hagedorn shift and some of the anomalous dimension \
sums by\\nindependent methods using the results of hep-th/0412029 and \
hep-th/0408178. The\\nsuccess of our calculation provides a significant check \
of methods used in\\nhep-th/0502149 to establish a first order deconfinement \
transition for pure\\nYang-Mills theory on a small three-sphere.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
