               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Lectures On AdS-CFT At Weak 't Hooft Coupling At Finite \
Temperature\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Based on lectures delivered at IPM String School and \
Workshop April\\n  2006, Strings 2006 Shanghai Workshop and Hangzhou Workshop \
June, ICTS-USTC\\n  March 2006 and Chulalongkorn University April 2006. 50 \
pages, 18 figures; v2\\n  minor corrections\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]},\
 {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This is an introductory lecture note aiming at \
providing an overview of the\\nAdS-CFT correspondence at weak 't Hooft \
coupling at finite temperature. The\\nfirst aim of this note is to describe \
the equivalence of three interesting\\nthermodynamical phenomena in \
theoretical physics, namely, Hawking-Page\\ntransition to black hole \
geometry, deconfinement transition in gauge theories,\\nand vortex \
condensation on string worldsheets. The Hawking-Page transition and\\nthe \
deconfinement transition in weakly coupled gauge theories are \
briefly\\nreviewed. Emphasis is on the study of 't Hooft-Feynman diagrams in \
the large\\n$N$ gauge theories, which are supposed to describe closed string \
worldsheets\\nand probe the above equivalence. Nature of the 't Hooft-Feynman \
diagrams at\\nfinite temperature is analyzed, both in the Euclidean signature \
(the imaginary\\ntime formalism) and in the Lorentzian signature (the real \
time formalism). The\\nsecond aim of this note is to give an introduction to \
the real time formalism\\napplied to AdS-CFT.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
