               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0608212\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Denis Dalmazi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"D. Dalmazi and Elias L. Mendonca\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Static potential in scalar QED$_3$ with non-minimal \
coupling\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"13 pages, 3 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Phys.A39:11091-11099,2006\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/0305-4470/39/35/010\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Here we compute the static potential in scalar $QED_3$ \
at leading order in\\n$1/N_f$. We show that the addition of a non-minimal \
coupling of Pauli-type\\n($\\\\eps \
j^{\\\\mu}\\\\partial^{\\\\nu}A^{\\\\alpha}$), although it breaks parity, it \
does\\nnot change the analytic structure of the photon propagator and \
consequently the\\nstatic potential remains logarithmic (confining) at large \
distances. The\\nnon-minimal coupling modifies the potential, however, at \
small charge\\nseparations giving rise to a repulsive force of short range \
between opposite\\nsign charges, which is relevant for the existence of bound \
states. This effect\\nis in agreement with a previous calculation based on M$\
\\\\ddot{o}$ller\\nscattering, but differently from such calculation we show \
here that the\\nrepulsion appears independently of the presence of a tree \
level Chern-Simons\\nterm which rather affects the large distance behavior of \
the potential turning\\nit into constant.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 30 Aug 2006 01:30:38 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-11\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Dalmazi\"", ",", "\"D.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Mendonca\"", ",", "\"Elias L.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
