         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0608212", "submitter" -> "Denis Dalmazi", 
            "authors" -> "D. Dalmazi and Elias L. Mendonca", "title" -> 
            "Static potential in scalar QED$_3$ with non-minimal coupling", 
            "comments" -> "13 pages, 3 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J.Phys.A39:11091-11099,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/0305-4470/39/35/010", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Here we compute the static potential in scalar $QED_3$ at \
leading order in\n$1/N_f$. We show that the addition of a non-minimal \
coupling of Pauli-type\n($\\eps j^{\\mu}\\partial^{\\nu}A^{\\alpha}$), \
although it breaks parity, it does\nnot change the analytic structure of the \
photon propagator and consequently the\nstatic potential remains logarithmic \
(confining) at large distances. The\nnon-minimal coupling modifies the \
potential, however, at small charge\nseparations giving rise to a repulsive \
force of short range between opposite\nsign charges, which is relevant for \
the existence of bound states. This effect\nis in agreement with a previous \
calculation based on M$\\ddot{o}$ller\nscattering, but differently from such \
calculation we show here that the\nrepulsion appears independently of the \
presence of a tree level Chern-Simons\nterm which rather affects the large \
distance behavior of the potential turning\nit into constant.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 30 Aug 2006 01:30:38 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-11-11", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Dalmazi", "D.", ""}, {
              "Mendonca", "Elias L.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
