          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0609007", "submitter" -> "Tamiaki Yoneya", 
            "authors" -> "Akitsugu Miwa and Tamiaki Yoneya", "title" -> 
            "Holography of Wilson-Loop Expectation Values with Local Operator\
\n  Insertions", "comments" -> 
            "16 pages, 5 figures, version to be published in JHEP, no change \
from\n  the previous version, only extraneous figure file is removed", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP0612:060,2006", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2006/12/060", "report-no" -> "UT-Komaba 06-8", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study the expectation values of Wilson-loop operators with \
the\ninsertionsof local operators Z^J and Zbar^J with large R-charge J from \
the bulk\nviewpoint of AdS/CFT correspondence. Classical solutions of strings \
attached to\nsuch deformed Wilson loops at the conformal boundary are \
constructed and are\napplied to the computation of Wilson-loop expectation \
values. We argue that in\norder to have such solutions for general insertions \
at finite positions in the\nbase spacetime of the gauge theory, it is crucial \
to interpret the holographic\ncorrespondence in the semi-classical picture as \
a tunneling phenomenon, as has\nbeen previously established for holographic \
computations of correlators of BMN\noperators. This also requires to use the \
Euclideanized AdS background and\nEuclidean super Yang-Mills theory.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 1 Sep 2006 14:25:34 GMT"}, {
