Sine-Gordon Solitons\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"1+26 pages, 6 figures. v2: minor corrections. v3: minor \
corrections,\\n  references added, published version. v4: minor \
corrections\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D75:046001,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.75.046001\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UT-06-18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study a family of classical string solutions with \
large spins on R x S^3\\nsubspace of AdS_5 x S^5 background, which are \
related to Complex sine-Gordon\\nsolitons via Pohlmeyer's reduction. The \
equations of motion for the classical\\nstrings are cast into Lame equations \
and Complex sine-Gordon equations. We\\nsolve them under periodic boundary \
conditions, and obtain analytic profiles for\\nthe closed strings. They \
interpolate two kinds of known rigid configurations\\nwith two spins: on one \
hand, they reduce to folded or circular\\nspinning/rotating strings in the \
limit where a soliton velocity goes to zero,\\nwhile on the other hand, the \
dyonic giant magnons are reproduced in the limit\\nwhere the period of a \
kink-array goes to infinity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
