            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0609153\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Vladimir Mangazeev\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Vladimir V. Bazhanov and Vladimir V. Mangazeev\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Analytic theory of the eight-vertex model\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"58 pages, 12 figures, minor corrections\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B775:225-282,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.12.021\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We observe that the exactly solved eight-vertex \
solid-on-solid model contains\\nan hitherto unnoticed arbitrary field \
parameter, similar to the horizontal\\nfield in the six-vertex model. The \
parameter is required to describe a\\ncontinuous spectrum of the unrestricted \
solid-on-solid model, which has an\\ninfinite-dimensional space of states \
even for a finite lattice. The\\nintroduction of the continuous field \
parameter allows us to completely review\\nthe theory of functional relations \
in the eight-vertex/SOS-model from a uniform\\nanalytic point of view. We \
also present a number of analytic and numerical\\ntechniques for the analysis \
of the Bethe Ansatz equations. It turns out that\\ndifferent solutions of \
these equations can be obtained from each other by\\nanalytic continuation. \
In particular, for small lattices we explicitly\\ndemonstrate that the \
largest and smallest eigenvalues of the transfer matrix of\\nthe eight-vertex \
model are just different branches of the same multivalued\\nfunction of the \
field parameter.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
