            "  We observe that the exactly solved eight-vertex solid-on-solid \
model contains\nan hitherto unnoticed arbitrary field parameter, similar to \
the horizontal\nfield in the six-vertex model. The parameter is required to \
describe a\ncontinuous spectrum of the unrestricted solid-on-solid model, \
which has an\ninfinite-dimensional space of states even for a finite lattice. \
The\nintroduction of the continuous field parameter allows us to completely \
review\nthe theory of functional relations in the eight-vertex/SOS-model from \
a uniform\nanalytic point of view. We also present a number of analytic and \
numerical\ntechniques for the analysis of the Bethe Ansatz equations. It \
turns out that\ndifferent solutions of these equations can be obtained from \
each other by\nanalytic continuation. In particular, for small lattices we \
explicitly\ndemonstrate that the largest and smallest eigenvalues of the \
transfer matrix of\nthe eight-vertex model are just different branches of the \
same multivalued\nfunction of the field parameter.\n", 
