        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{17.427375478258764`, -1.6154912152638126`}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0610014\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Abhishek Agarwal\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Abhishek Agarwal\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Mass-Gaps and Spin Chains for (Super) Membranes\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"36 Pages\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Int.J.Mod.Phys.A22:3563-3603,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1142/S0217751X07037007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present a method for computing the non-perturbative \
mass-gap in the theory\\nof Bosonic membranes in flat background spacetimes \
with or without background\\nfluxes. The computation of mass-gaps is carried \
out using a matrix\\nregularization of the membrane Hamiltonians. The mass \
gap is shown to be\\nnaturally organized as an expansion in a 'hidden' \
parameter, which turns out to\\nbe $\\\\frac{1}{d}$: d being the related to \
the dimensionality of the background\\nspace. We then proceed to develop a \
large $N$ perturbation theory for the\\nmembrane/matrix-model Hamiltonians \
around the quantum/mass corrected effective\\npotential. The same parameter \
that controls the perturbation theory for the\\nmass gap is also shown to \
control the Hamiltonian perturbation theory around\\nthe effective potential. \
The large $N$ perturbation theory is then translated\\ninto the language of \
quantum spin chains and the one loop spectra of various\\nBosonic matrix \
models are computed by applying the Bethe ansatz to the one-loop\\neffective \
Hamiltonians for membranes in flat space times. Apart from membranes\\nin \
flat spacetimes, the recently proposed matrix models (hep-th/0607005) \
for\\nnon-critical membranes in plane wave type spacetimes are also analyzed \
within\\nthe paradigm of quantum spin chains and the Bosonic sectors of all \
the models\\nproposed in (hep-th/0607005) are diagonalized at the one-loop \
level.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 1 Oct 2006 02:18:41 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Agarwal\"", ",", "\"Abhishek\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
