               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0610027\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shinji Hirano\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Shinji Hirano\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Fat Magnon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"18 pages, 5 figures; v2 references added; v3 a reference \
added; v4\\n  added a reference and discussions on the physical CFT operator. \
The version\\n  to appear in JHEP\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0704:010,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/04/010\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider a D-brane type state which shares the \
characteristic of the\\nrecently found giant magnon of Hofman and Maldacena. \
More specifically we find\\na bound state of giant graviton (D3-brane) and \
giant magnon (F-string), which\\nhas exactly the same anomalous dimension as \
that of the giant magnon. It is\\ndescribed by the D3-brane with electric \
flux which is topologically a $S^3$\\nelongated by the electric flux. The \
angular momentum and energy are infinite,\\nbut split sensibly into two parts \
-- the infinite part precisely the same as\\nthat of the giant magnon and the \
finite part which can be identified as the\\ncontribution from the giant \
graviton. We discuss that the corresponding dual\\ngauge theory operator is \
not a simple chain type but rather admixture of the\\n(sub-)determinant and \
chain types.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
