         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{8.610645097078619, -5.848677854142034}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0610257\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pallab Basu\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Pallab Basu, Bobby Ezhuthachan, Spenta R. Wadia\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Plasma balls/kinks as solitons of large $N$ confining \
gauge theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"26+1 pages, 10 figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0701:003,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/01/003\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"TIFR/TH/06-35\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss finite regions of the deconfining phase of a \
confining gauge\\ntheory (plasma balls/kinks) as solitons of the large $N$, \
long wavelength,\\neffective Lagrangian of the thermal gauge theory expressed \
in terms of suitable\\norder parameters. We consider a class of confining \
gauge theories whose\\neffective Lagrangian turns out to be a generic 1 dim. \
unitary matrix model. The\\ndynamics of this matrix model can be studied by \
an exact mapping to a\\nnon-relativistic many fermion problem on a circle. We \
present an approximate\\nsolution to the equations of motion which \
corresponds to the motion (in\\nEuclidean time) of the Fermi surface \
interpolating between the phase where the\\nfermions are uniformly \
distributed on the circle (confinement phase) and the\\nphase where the \
fermion distribution has a gap on the circle (deconfinement\\nphase). We \
later self-consistently verify that the approximation is a good one.\\nWe \
discuss some properties and implications of the solution including \
the\\nsurface tension which turns out to be positive. As a by product of \
our\\ninvestigation we point out the problem of obtaining time dependent \
solutions in\\nthe collective field theory formalism due to generic shock \
formation.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 24 Oct 2006 19:22:02 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2010-02-03\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Basu\"", ",", "\"Pallab\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Ezhuthachan\"", ",", "\"Bobby\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                     ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Wadia\"", ",", "\"Spenta R.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
