               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The AdS_5 x S^5 superstrings in the generalized \
light-cone gauge\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages; v2: references added, typos corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Prog.Theor.Phys.117:957-972,2007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1143/PTP.117.957\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"OCU-PHYS 257\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The kappa-symmetry-fixed Green-Schwarz action in the \
AdS_5 x S^5 background\\nis treated canonically in a version of the \
light-cone gauge. After reviewing\\nthe generalized light-cone gauge for a \
bosonic sigma model, we present the\\nHamiltonian dynamics of the \
Green-Schwarz action by using the transverse\\ndegrees of freedom. The \
remaining fermionic constraints are all second class,\\nwhich we treat by the \
Dirac bracket. Upon quantization, all of the transverse\\ncoordinates are \
inevitably non-commutative.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
