               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study one-loop low-energy effective action in the \
hypermultiplet sector\\nfor ${\\\\cal N}=2$ superconformal models. Any such a \
model contains ${\\\\cal N}=2$\\nvector multiplet and some number of \
hypermultiplets. Gauge group $G$ is assumed\\nto be broken down to \
$\\\\tilde{G}\\\\times K$ where $K$ is an Abelian subgroup and a\\nbackground \
vector multiplet belongs to the Cartan subalgebra corresponding to\\n$K$. We \
find a general expression for the low-energy effective action in a form\\nof \
a proper-time integral. The leading space-time dependent contributions \
to\\nthe effective action are derived and their bosonic component structure \
is\\nanalyzed. The component action contains the terms with three and \
four\\nspace-time derivatives of component fields and has the Chern-Simons \
form.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
