hypermultiplet sector\nfor ${\\cal N}=2$ superconformal models. Any such a \
model contains ${\\cal N}=2$\nvector multiplet and some number of \
hypermultiplets. Gauge group $G$ is assumed\nto be broken down to $\\tilde{G}\
\\times K$ where $K$ is an Abelian subgroup and a\nbackground vector \
multiplet belongs to the Cartan subalgebra corresponding to\n$K$. We find a \
general expression for the low-energy effective action in a form\nof a \
proper-time integral. The leading space-time dependent contributions to\nthe \
