Konstantin Zarembo\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Worldsheet Scattering in AdS_5 x S^5\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"51 pages, v2: references added, v3: sign in (2.12), \
(6.19) and (6.21)\\n  corrected; v4: discussion of classical YBE is \
considerably modified\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0703:094,2007\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/03/094\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"ITEP-TH-61/06, UUITP-15/06\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We calculate the S-matrix in the gauge-fixed \
sigma-model on AdS_5 x S^5 to\\nthe leading order in perturbation theory, and \
analyze how supersymmetry is\\nrealized on the scattering states. A mild \
nonlocality of the supercharges\\nimplies that their action on multi-particle \
states does not follow the Leibniz\\nrule, which is replaced by a nontrivial \
coproduct. The plane wave symmetry\\nalgebra is thus naturally enhanced to a \
Hopf algebra. The scattering matrix\\nelements obey the classical Yang-Baxter \
equation modified by the existence of\\nthe coproduct. This structure mirrors \
that of the large 't Hooft coupling\\nexpansion of the S-matrix for the spin \
chain in the dual super-Yang-Mills\\ntheory.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
