             "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  We calculate the S-matrix in the gauge-fixed sigma-model on \
AdS_5 x S^5 to\nthe leading order in perturbation theory, and analyze how \
supersymmetry is\nrealized on the scattering states. A mild nonlocality of \
the supercharges\nimplies that their action on multi-particle states does not \
follow the Leibniz\nrule, which is replaced by a nontrivial coproduct. The \
plane wave symmetry\nalgebra is thus naturally enhanced to a Hopf algebra. \
The scattering matrix\nelements obey the classical Yang-Baxter equation \
modified by the existence of\nthe coproduct. This structure mirrors that of \
the large 't Hooft coupling\nexpansion of the S-matrix for the spin chain in \
the dual super-Yang-Mills\ntheory.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
