            "Logarithmic corrections to higher twist scaling at strong \
coupling from\n  AdS/CFT", "comments" -> 
            "17 pages; 1 figure; v3: minor rephrasing; misprints corrected", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Nucl.Phys.B766:232-245,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.12.013", "report-no" -> 
            "Imperial-TP-AT-6-6, TCDMATH 06-17", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute 1-loop correction E_1 to the energy of folded \
string in AdS_5 x\nS^5 (carrying spin S in AdS_5 and momentum J in S^5) using \
``long string''\napproximation in which S >> J >> 1. According to AdS/CFT E_1 \
should represent\nthe first subleading correction to strong coupling \
expansion of anomalous\ndimension of higher twist SL(2) sector operators of \
the form Tr D^S Z^J. We\nshow that E_1 smoothly interpolates between the ln S \
regime (previously found\nin the J=0 case) and the \\lambda/J^2 ln^3 (S/J) \
regime (which is the leading\ncorrection to the thermodynamic limit on the \
spin chain side). This supports\nthe universality of the ln S scaling. As in \
previous work, we also find\n``non-analytic'' corrections related to \
non-trivial 1-loop phase in the\ncorresponding Bethe ansatz S-matrix.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
