            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0612018\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wung-Hong Huang\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Wung-Hong Huang\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"AdS/CFT Approach to Melvin Field Deformed Wilson \
Loop\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Latex 18 pages, construct new supergravity solution and \
perform new\\n  calculations\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"High Energy Physics Research Advances, 2008, pp. \
135-150\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We first apply the transformation of mixing azimuthal \
and internal coordinate\\nto the 11D M-theory with a stack N M2-branes to \
find the spacetime of a stack\\nof N D2-branes with Melvin one-form in 10D \
IIA string theory, after the\\nKaluza-Klein reduction. Next, we apply the \
Melvin twist to the spacetime and\\nperform the T duality to obtain the \
background of a stack of N D3-branes. In\\nthe near-horizon limit the \
background becomes the Melvin field deformed $AdS_5\\n\\\\times S^5$ with \
NS-NS B field. In the AdS/CFT correspondence it describes a\\nnon-commutative \
gauge theory with non-constant non-commutativity in the Melvin\\nfield \
deformed spacetime. We study the Wilson loop therein by investigating \
the\\nclassical Nambu-Goto action of the corresponding string configuration \
and find\\nthat, contrast to that in the undeformed spacetime, the string \
could be\\nlocalized near the boundary. Our result shows that while the \
geometry could\\nonly modify the Coulomb type potential in IR there presents \
a minimum distance\\nbetween the quarks. We argue that the mechanism behind \
producing a minimum\\ndistance is coming from geometry of the Melvin field \
deformed background and is\\nnot coming from the space \
non-commutativity.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
