         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0612018", "submitter" -> "Wung-Hong Huang", 
            "authors" -> "Wung-Hong Huang", "title" -> 
            "AdS/CFT Approach to Melvin Field Deformed Wilson Loop", 
            "comments" -> 
            "Latex 18 pages, construct new supergravity solution and perform \
new\n  calculations", "journal-ref" -> 
            "High Energy Physics Research Advances, 2008, pp. 135-150", "doi" -> 
            Null, "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We first apply the transformation of mixing azimuthal and \
internal coordinate\nto the 11D M-theory with a stack N M2-branes to find the \
spacetime of a stack\nof N D2-branes with Melvin one-form in 10D IIA string \
theory, after the\nKaluza-Klein reduction. Next, we apply the Melvin twist to \
the spacetime and\nperform the T duality to obtain the background of a stack \
of N D3-branes. In\nthe near-horizon limit the background becomes the Melvin \
field deformed $AdS_5\n\\times S^5$ with NS-NS B field. In the AdS/CFT \
correspondence it describes a\nnon-commutative gauge theory with non-constant \
non-commutativity in the Melvin\nfield deformed spacetime. We study the \
Wilson loop therein by investigating the\nclassical Nambu-Goto action of the \
corresponding string configuration and find\nthat, contrast to that in the \
undeformed spacetime, the string could be\nlocalized near the boundary. Our \
result shows that while the geometry could\nonly modify the Coulomb type \
potential in IR there presents a minimum distance\nbetween the quarks. We \
argue that the mechanism behind producing a minimum\ndistance is coming from \
geometry of the Melvin field deformed background and is\nnot coming from the \
space non-commutativity.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 4 Dec 2006 13:11:05 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 11 Dec 2006 12:47:02 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 28 Jan 2007 14:05:52 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v4", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 17 Mar 2007 11:24:43 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2012-05-04", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Huang", "Wung-Hong", ""}}}], 
          "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{18.791392787181568`, -3.226711973169632}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0612032\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Emiliano Imeroni\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Emiliano Imeroni, Asad Naqvi\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Giants and loops in beta-deformed theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages; typos corrected, published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0703:034,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/03/034\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"SWAT/06/482\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study extended objects in the gravity dual of the \
N=1 beta-deformation of\\nN=4 Super Yang-Mills theory. We identify probe \
brane configurations\\ncorresponding to giant gravitons and Wilson loops. In \
particular we identify a\\nnew class of objects, given by D5-branes wrapped \
on a two-torus with a\\nworld-volume gauge field strength turned on along the \
torus. These appear when\\nthe deformation parameter assumes a rational value \
and the gauge theory\\nspectrum has additional branches of vacua. We give an \
interpretation of the new\\nD5-brane dual giant gravitons in terms of \
rotating vacuum expectation values in\\nthese additional branches.\\n\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
