         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0612032", "submitter" -> "Emiliano Imeroni", 
            "authors" -> "Emiliano Imeroni, Asad Naqvi", "title" -> 
            "Giants and loops in beta-deformed theories", "comments" -> 
            "26 pages; typos corrected, published version", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0703:034,2007", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/03/034", 
            "report-no" -> "SWAT/06/482", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study extended objects in the gravity dual of the N=1 \
beta-deformation of\nN=4 Super Yang-Mills theory. We identify probe brane \
configurations\ncorresponding to giant gravitons and Wilson loops. In \
particular we identify a\nnew class of objects, given by D5-branes wrapped on \
a two-torus with a\nworld-volume gauge field strength turned on along the \
torus. These appear when\nthe deformation parameter assumes a rational value \
and the gauge theory\nspectrum has additional branches of vacua. We give an \
interpretation of the new\nD5-brane dual giant gravitons in terms of rotating \
vacuum expectation values in\nthese additional branches.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 4 Dec 2006 22:56:46 GMT"}, {
