           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0612099\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Stephen G. Naculich\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Howard J. Schnitzer\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Confinement/Deconfinement Transition of Large N Gauge \
Theories in\\n  Perturbation Theory with N_f Fundamentals: N_f/N \
Finite\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"17 pages; v2: references added; v3 minor changes\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"BRX-TH-579\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In hep-th/0402219 we considered large N zero-coupling \
d-dimensional U(N)\\ngauge theories, with N_f matter fields in the \
fundamental representation on a\\ncompact spatial manifold S^{d-1}x time, \
with N_f/N finite. This class of\\ntheories undergo a 3rd order deconfinement \
transition. As a consequence it was\\nproposed that the dual string theory \
has a 3rd order phase-transition to a\\nblack hole at high temperature. In \
this paper we argue that the same\\nconclusions are valid for such theories \
at any finite order in perturbation\\ntheory in the 't Hooft coupling lambda \
and N_f/N. It is conjectured that this\\ncontinues to hold at strong coupling \
and finite value of N_f/N < (1/lambda),\\nwhich suggests that the \
supergravity approximation to the dual string theory\\nhas a 3rd order \
thermal phase transition to a large black hole.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
