            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Recently it has been proposed that Wilson loops in \
high-dimensional\nrepresentations in N=4 supersymmetric Yang-Mills theory (or \
multiply wrapped\nloops) are described by D-branes in AdS_5 x S^5, rather \
than by fundamental\nstrings. Thus far explicit D3-brane solutions have been \
only found in the case\nof the half-BPS circle or line. Here we present \
D3-brane solutions describing\nsome 1/4 BPS loops. In one case, where the \
loop is conjectured to be given by a\nGaussian matrix model, the action of \
the brane correctly reproduces the\nexpectation value of the Wilson loop \
including all 1/N corrections at large\n\\lambda. As in the corresponding \
string solution, here too we find two\nclassical solutions, one stable and \
one not. The unstable one contributes\nexponentially small corrections that \
agree with the matrix model calculation.\n", 
