               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Arutyunov Gleb E\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Gleb Arutyunov, Sergey Frolov, Marija Zamaklar\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Zamolodchikov-Faddeev Algebra for AdS_5 x S^5 \
Superstring\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"40 pages, v2: derivation of symmetries from the S-matrix \
and the Hopf\\n  algebra interpretation added, typos corrected, references \
added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0704:002,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/04/002\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"AEI-2006-099, ITP-UU-06-58, SPIN-06-48, TCDMATH \
06-18\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th nlin.SI\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss the Zamolodchikov-Faddeev algebra for the \
superstring sigma-model\\non AdS_5 x S^5. We find the canonical su(2|2)^2 \
invariant S-matrix satisfying\\nthe standard Yang-Baxter and crossing \
symmetry equations. Its near-plane-wave\\nexpansion matches exactly the \
leading order term recently obtained by the\\ndirect perturbative \
computation. We also show that the S-matrix obtained by\\nBeisert in the \
gauge theory framework does not satisfy the standard Yang-Baxter\\nequation, \
and, as a consequence, the corresponding ZF algebra is twisted. \
The\\nS-matrices in gauge and string theories however are physically \
equivalent and\\nrelated by a non-local transformation of the basis states \
which is explicitly\\nconstructed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
