            "authors" -> "Gleb Arutyunov, Sergey Frolov, Marija Zamaklar", 
            "title" -> 
            "The Zamolodchikov-Faddeev Algebra for AdS_5 x S^5 Superstring", 
            "comments" -> 
            "40 pages, v2: derivation of symmetries from the S-matrix and the \
Hopf\n  algebra interpretation added, typos corrected, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0704:002,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/04/002", "report-no" -> 
            "AEI-2006-099, ITP-UU-06-58, SPIN-06-48, TCDMATH 06-18", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th nlin.SI", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We discuss the Zamolodchikov-Faddeev algebra for the \
superstring sigma-model\non AdS_5 x S^5. We find the canonical su(2|2)^2 \
invariant S-matrix satisfying\nthe standard Yang-Baxter and crossing symmetry \
equations. Its near-plane-wave\nexpansion matches exactly the leading order \
term recently obtained by the\ndirect perturbative computation. We also show \
that the S-matrix obtained by\nBeisert in the gauge theory framework does not \
satisfy the standard Yang-Baxter\nequation, and, as a consequence, the \
corresponding ZF algebra is twisted. The\nS-matrices in gauge and string \
theories however are physically equivalent and\nrelated by a non-local \
transformation of the basis states which is explicitly\nconstructed.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
