            "  The correspondence between ordinary differential equations and \
Bethe ansatz\nequations for integrable lattice models in their continuum \
limits is\ngeneralised to vertex models related to classical simple Lie \
algebras. New\nfamilies of pseudo-differential equations are proposed, and a \
link between\nspecific generalised eigenvalue problems for these equations \
and the Bethe\nansatz is deduced. The pseudo-differential operators resemble \
in form the\nMiura-transformed Lax operators studied in work on generalised \
KdV equations,\nclassical W-algebras and, more recently, in the context of \
the geometric\nLanglands correspondence. Negative-dimension and \
boundary-condition dualities\nare also observed.\n", 
