               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0701005\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Joseph A. Minahan\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"J. A. Minahan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Zero modes for the giant magnon\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"14 pages; v2 references added; v3 minor changes, \
references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0702:048,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/02/048\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UUITP-17/06\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We explicitly construct the eight fermion zero mode \
solutions for the\\nHofman-Maldacena giant magnon. The solutions are \
naturally gauge fixed under\\nthe \\\\kappa-symmetry. Substituting the \
solutions back into the Lagrangian leads\\nto a simple expression that can be \
quantized directly. We also show how to\\nconstruct the SU(2|2)\\\\times \
SU(2|2) superalgebra from these zero modes. For\\ncompleteness we also find \
the four bosonic zero mode solutions.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
