            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0701281\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alessandro Torrielli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Alessandro Torrielli\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Classical r-matrix of the su(2|2) SYM spin-chain\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"14 pages, LaTeX, no figures; corrections made, further \
analysis of\\n  the residue and references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D75:105020,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.75.105020\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"MIT-CTP 3809\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  In this note we straightforwardly derive and make use \
of the quantum R-matrix\\nfor the su(2|2) SYM spin-chain in the manifest \
su(1|2)-invariant formulation,\\nwhich solves the standard quantum \
Yang-Baxter equation, in order to obtain the\\ncorrespondent (undressed) \
classical r-matrix from the first order expansion in\\nthe ``deformation'' \
parameter 2 \\\\pi / \\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}, and check that this last\\nsolves \
the standard classical Yang-Baxter equation. We analyze its \
bialgebra\\nstructure, its dependence on the spectral parameters and its pole \
structure. We\\nnotice that it still preserves an su(1|2) subalgebra, thereby \
admitting an\\nexpression in terms of a combination of projectors, which \
spans only a subspace\\nof su(1|2) \\\\otimes su(1|2). We study the residue \
at its simple pole at the\\norigin, and comment on the applicability of the \
classical Belavin-Drinfeld type\\nof analysis.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
