               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0702083\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Ido Adam\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Ido Adam, Amit Dekel, Luca Mazzucato, Yaron Oz\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Integrability of Type II Superstrings on Ramond-Ramond \
Backgrounds in\\n  Various Dimensions\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTeX2e, 56 pages, 1 figure, JHEP style; v2: references \
added, typos\\n  fixed in some equations; v3: typos fixed to match the \
published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0706:085,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/06/085\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"TAUP-2849/07\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider type II superstrings on AdS backgrounds \
with Ramond-Ramond flux\\nin various dimensions. We realize the backgrounds \
as supercosets and analyze\\nexplicitly two classes of models: non-critical \
superstrings on AdS_{2d} and\\ncritical superstrings on AdS_p\\\\times \
S^p\\\\times CY. We work both in the\\nGreen--Schwarz and in the pure spinor \
formalisms. We construct a one-parameter\\nfamily of flat currents (a Lax \
connection) leading to an infinite number of\\nconserved non-local charges, \
which imply the classical integrability of both\\nsigma-models. In the pure \
spinor formulation, we use the BRST symmetry to prove\\nthe quantum \
integrability of the sigma-model. We discuss how \
classical\\n\\\\kappa-symmetry implies one-loop conformal invariance. We \
consider the addition\\nof space-filling D-branes to the pure spinor \
formalism.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
