Backgrounds in\n  Various Dimensions", "comments" -> 
            "LaTeX2e, 56 pages, 1 figure, JHEP style; v2: references added, \
typos\n  fixed in some equations; v3: typos fixed to match the published \
version", "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0706:085,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/06/085", "report-no" -> "TAUP-2849/07", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider type II superstrings on AdS backgrounds with \
Ramond-Ramond flux\nin various dimensions. We realize the backgrounds as \
supercosets and analyze\nexplicitly two classes of models: non-critical \
superstrings on AdS_{2d} and\ncritical superstrings on AdS_p\\times \
S^p\\times CY. We work both in the\nGreen--Schwarz and in the pure spinor \
formalisms. We construct a one-parameter\nfamily of flat currents (a Lax \
connection) leading to an infinite number of\nconserved non-local charges, \
which imply the classical integrability of both\nsigma-models. In the pure \
spinor formulation, we use the BRST symmetry to prove\nthe quantum \
integrability of the sigma-model. We discuss how classical\n\\kappa-symmetry \
implies one-loop conformal invariance. We consider the addition\nof \
space-filling D-branes to the pure spinor formalism.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 11 Feb 2007 21:30:38 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 12 May 2007 08:34:41 GMT"}, {
