            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0702151\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Matthias Staudacher\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Adam Rej, Matthias Staudacher and Stefan Zieme\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Nesting and Dressing\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"38 pages, 2 figures. v2: References and appendix \
discussing the\\n  emulation of the dressing phase added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Stat.Mech.0708:P08006,2007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1742-5468/2007/08/P08006\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2007-008\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We compute the anomalous dimensions of field strength \
operators Tr F^L in N=4\\nSYM from an asymptotic nested Bethe ansatz to \
all-loop order. Starting from the\\nexact solution of the one-loop problem at \
arbitrary L, we derive a single\\neffective integral equation for the \
thermodynamic limit of these dimensions. We\\nalso include the recently \
proposed phase factor for the S-matrix of the planar\\nAdS/CFT system. The \
terms in the effective equation corresponding to,\\nrespectively, the nesting \
and the dressing are structurally very similar. This\\nhints at the physical \
origin of the dressing phase, which we conjecture to\\narise from the hidden \
presence of infinitely many auxiliary Bethe roots\\ndescribing a non-trivial \
\\\"filled\\\" structure of the theory's BPS vacuum. We\\nfinally show that \
the mechanism for creating effective nesting/dressing kernels\\nis quite \
generic by also deriving the integral equation for the all-loop\\ndimension \
of a certain one-loop so(6) singlet state.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
