          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/0702151", "submitter" -> "Matthias Staudacher", 
            "authors" -> "Adam Rej, Matthias Staudacher and Stefan Zieme", 
            "title" -> "Nesting and Dressing", "comments" -> 
            "38 pages, 2 figures. v2: References and appendix discussing the\n\
  emulation of the dressing phase added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "J.Stat.Mech.0708:P08006,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/2007/08/P08006", "report-no" -> "AEI-2007-008",
             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We compute the anomalous dimensions of field strength \
operators Tr F^L in N=4\nSYM from an asymptotic nested Bethe ansatz to \
all-loop order. Starting from the\nexact solution of the one-loop problem at \
arbitrary L, we derive a single\neffective integral equation for the \
thermodynamic limit of these dimensions. We\nalso include the recently \
proposed phase factor for the S-matrix of the planar\nAdS/CFT system. The \
terms in the effective equation corresponding to,\nrespectively, the nesting \
and the dressing are structurally very similar. This\nhints at the physical \
origin of the dressing phase, which we conjecture to\narise from the hidden \
presence of infinitely many auxiliary Bethe roots\ndescribing a non-trivial \
\"filled\" structure of the theory's BPS vacuum. We\nfinally show that the \
mechanism for creating effective nesting/dressing kernels\nis quite generic \
by also deriving the integral equation for the all-loop\ndimension of a \
certain one-loop so(6) singlet state.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 19 Feb 2007 20:17:56 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 26 Mar 2007 17:21:53 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
