            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study how geometrical and topological aspects of certain \
1/2 BPS type IIB\nsupergravity solutions are captured by the N=4 Super \
Yang-Mills gauge theory in\nthe AdS/CFT context. The type IIB solutions are \
completely characterized by\narbitrary droplets in a plane and we consider, \
in particular, concentric\ndroplets. We probe the dual 1/2 BPS operators of \
the gauge theory with single\ntraces and extract their one-loop anomalous \
dimensions. The action of the\none-loop dilatation operator can be \
reformulated as the Hamiltonian of a\nbosonic lattice. The operators defining \
the Hamiltonian encode the topology of\nthe droplet. The axial symmetry of \
the droplets turns out to be essential for\nobtaining the spectrum of the \
Hamiltonians. In appropriate BMN limits, the\nnear-BPS spectrum reproduces \
the spectrum of near-BPS string excitations\npropagating along each \
individual edge of the droplet of the dual geometric\nbackground. We also \
study semiclassical regimes for the Hamiltonians. We show\nthat for droplets \
having disconnected constituents, the Hamiltonian admits\ndifferent \
complimentary semiclassical descriptions, each one replicating the\n\
semiclassical description for closed strings extending in each of the\n\
constituents.\n", 
