                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider an external gauge potential minimally \
coupled to a renormalisable\\nscalar theory on 4-dimensional Moyal space and \
compute in position space the\\none-loop Yang-Mills-type effective theory \
generated from the integration over\\nthe scalar field. We find that the \
gauge invariant effective action involves,\\nbeyond the expected \
noncommutative version of the pure Yang-Mills action,\\nadditional terms that \
may be interpreted as the gauge theory counterpart of the\\nharmonic \
oscillator term, which for the noncommutative $\\\\phi^4$-theory on \
Moyal\\nspace ensures renormalisability. The expression of a possible \
candidate for a\\nrenormalisable action for a gauge theory defined on Moyal \
space is conjectured\\nand discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
