               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0703086\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marcio Jose Martins\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"M.J. Martins and C.S. Melo\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Bethe ansatz approach for factorizable centrally \
extended S-matrices\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"22 pages, published version\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.B785:246-262,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2007.05.021\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UFSCAR-TH-07-03\""}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We consider the Bethe ansatz solution of integrable \
models interacting\\nthrough factorized $S$-matrices based on the central \
extention of the\\n$\\\\bf{su}(2|2)$ symmetry. The respective \
$\\\\bf{su}(2|2)$ $R$-matrix is explicitly\\nrelated to that of the covering \
Hubbard model through a spectral parameter\\ndependent transformation. This \
mapping allows us to diagonalize inhomogeneous\\ntransfer matrices whose \
statistical weights are given in terms of\\n$\\\\bf{su}(2|2)$ $S$-matrices by \
the algebraic Bethe ansatz. As a consequence of\\nthat we derive the \
quantization condition on the circle for the asymptotic\\nmomenta of \
particles scattering by the $\\\\bf{su}(2|2) \\\\otimes \
\\\\bf{su}(2|2)$\\n$S$-matrix. The result for the quantization rule may be of \
relevance in the\\nstudy of the energy spectrum of the $AdS_5 \\\\times \
S^{5}$ string sigma model in\\nthe thermodynamic limit. \\\\\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
