            "  We consider the Bethe ansatz solution of integrable models \
interacting\nthrough factorized $S$-matrices based on the central extention \
of the\n$\\bf{su}(2|2)$ symmetry. The respective $\\bf{su}(2|2)$ $R$-matrix \
is explicitly\nrelated to that of the covering Hubbard model through a \
spectral parameter\ndependent transformation. This mapping allows us to \
diagonalize inhomogeneous\ntransfer matrices whose statistical weights are \
given in terms of\n$\\bf{su}(2|2)$ $S$-matrices by the algebraic Bethe \
ansatz. As a consequence of\nthat we derive the quantization condition on the \
circle for the asymptotic\nmomenta of particles scattering by the \
$\\bf{su}(2|2) \\otimes \\bf{su}(2|2)$\n$S$-matrix. The result for the \
quantization rule may be of relevance in the\nstudy of the energy spectrum of \
the $AdS_5 \\times S^{5}$ string sigma model in\nthe thermodynamic limit. \\\n\
", "versions" -> {{
