            "Nick Dorey, Diego M. Hofman and Juan Maldacena", "title" -> 
            "On the Singularities of the Magnon S-matrix", "comments" -> 
            "40 pages, 14 figures; typos corrected, references added", 
            "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D76:025011,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.76.025011", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
            "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate the analytic structure of the magnon S-matrix \
in the\nspin-chain description of planar ${\\cal N}=4$ SUSY \
Yang-Mills/$AdS_{5}\\times\nS^{5}$ strings. Semiclassical analysis suggests \
that the exact S-matrix must\nhave a large family of poles near the real axis \
in momentum space. In this\narticle we show that these are double poles \
corresponding to the exchange of\npairs of BPS magnons. Their locations in \
the complex plane are uniquely fixed\nby the known dispersion relation for \
the BPS particles. The locations precisely\nagree with the recent conjecture \
for the $S$ matrix by Beisert, Hernandez,\nLopez, Eden and Staudacher \
(hep-th/0609044 and hep-th/0610251). These poles do\nnot signal the presence \
of new bound states. In fact, a certain non-BPS\nlocalized classical \
solution, which was thought to give rise to new bound\nstates, can actually \
decay into a pair of BPS magnons.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
