               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0703123\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Dubin\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Jan Ambjorn, Andrei Dubin, Yuri Makeenko\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wilson Loops in 2D Noncommutative Euclidean Gauge Theory: \
2. 1/\\\\theta\\n  Expansion\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LaTex, 50pp., 9 PostScript figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP0710:079,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2007/10/079\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"ITEP-TH-02/07\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We analyze the $1/\\\\theta$ and 1/N expansions of the \
Wilson loop averages\\n$<W(C)>_{U_\\\\theta (N)}$ in the two-dimensional \
noncommutative $U_\\\\theta (N)$\\ngauge theory with the parameter of \
noncommutativity $\\\\theta$. For a generic\\nrectangular contour $C$, a \
concise integral representation is derived\\n(non-perturbatively both in the \
coupling constant $g^{2}$ and in $\\\\theta$) for\\nthe next-to-leading term \
of the $1/\\\\theta$ expansion. In turn, in the limit\\nwhen ${\\\\theta}$ is \
much larger than the area $A(C)$ of the surface bounded by\\n$C$, the large $\
\\\\theta$ asymptote of this representation is argued to yield \
the\\nnext-to-leading term of the $1/\\\\theta$ series. For both of the \
expansions, the\\nnext-to-leading contribution exhibits only a power-like \
decay for areas\\n$A(C)>>\\\\sigma^{-1}$ (but $A(C)<<{\\\\theta}$) much \
larger than the inverse of the\\nstring tension $\\\\sigma$ defining the \
range of the exponential decay of the\\nleading term. Consequently, for large \
$\\\\theta$, it hinders a direct stringy\\ninterpretation of the subleading \
terms of the 1/N expansion in the spirit of\\nGross-Taylor proposal for the $\
\\\\theta=0$ commutative D=2 gauge theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 13 Mar 2007 14:02:17 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
