            "Matteo Beccaria, Gian Fabrizio De Angelis, Valentina Forini", 
            "title" -> 
            "The scaling function at strong coupling from the quantum string \
Bethe\n  equations", "comments" -> "25 pages, 5 eps figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 0704:066,2007", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/04/066", 
            "report-no" -> "HU-EP-07/06", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study at strong coupling the scaling function describing \
the large spin\nanomalous dimension of twist two operators in ${\\cal N}=4$ \
super Yang-Mills\ntheory. In the spirit of AdS/CFT duality, it is possible to \
extract it from the\nstring Bethe Ansatz equations in the $\\mathfrak{sl}(2)$ \
sector of the $\\ads$\nsuperstring. To this aim, we present a detailed \
analysis of the Bethe equations\nby numerical and analytical methods. We \
recover several short string\nsemiclassical results as a check. In the more \
difficult case of the long string\nlimit providing the scaling function, we \
analyze the strong coupling version of\nthe Eden-Staudacher equation, \
including the Arutyunov-Frolov-Staudacher phase.\nWe prove that it admits a \
unique solution, at least in perturbation theory,\nleading to the correct \
prediction consistent with semiclassical string\ncalculations.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 14 Mar 2007 16:23:56 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-10-27", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Beccaria", "Matteo", ""}, {
              "De Angelis", "Gian Fabrizio", ""}, {
              "Forini", "Valentina", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
