                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"On the origin of the dressing phase in N=4 Super \
Yang-Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"8 pages, no figures; (v2) comments and references added; \
(v3) changes\\n  in presentation and title\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett.B661:216-219,2008\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1016/j.physletb.2008.02.015\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UTHEP-540\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"hep-th cond-mat.stat-mech\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We derive the phase factor proposed by Beisert, Eden \
and Staudacher for the\\nS-matrix of planar N=4 Super Yang-Mills, from the \
all-loop Bethe ansatz\\nequations without the dressing factor. We identify a \
configuration of the Bethe\\nroots, from which the closed integral formula of \
the phase factor is reproduced\\nin the thermodynamic limit. This suggests \
that our configuration describes the\\n``physical vacuum'' in the sense that \
the dressing phase is nothing but the\\neffective phase for the scattering of \
fundamental excitations above this\\nvacuum, providing an interesting clue to \
the physical origin of the dressing\\nphase.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
