            "Testing the nested light-cone Bethe equations of the AdS_5 x S^5\
\n  superstring", "comments" -> 
            "34 pages, 1 figure, 12 tables, JHEP style. v2: clarifications \
and\n  references added. v3: reference added, version to be published", 
            "journal-ref" -> "JHEP 0705:021,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1126-6708/2007/05/021", "report-no" -> "HU-EP-07/07", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We perform a detailed test of the quantum integrability of the \
AdS_5 x S^5\nsuperstring in uniform light-cone gauge in its near plane-wave \
limit. For this\nwe establish the form of the general nested light-cone Bethe \
equations for the\nquantum string from the long range psu(2,2|4) Bethe \
equations of Beisert and\nStaudacher. Moreover the scheme for translating \
excited string states into\nBethe root excitations is given. We then confront \
the direct perturbative\ndiagonalization of the light-cone string Hamiltonian \
in the near plane-wave\nlimit with the energy spectrum obtained from the \
general nested light-cone\nBethe equations in various higher rank sectors. \
The analysis is performed both\nanalytically and numerically up to the level \
of six impurity states and\nsubsectors of maximal rank four. We find perfect \
agreement in all cases lending\nstrong support to the quantum integrability \
of the AdS_5 x S^5 superstring.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
