        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{6.408343895033552, -5.831819146633287}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9403024\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J. Ambjorn, Yu. Makeenko and C.F. Kristjansen\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Generalized Penner models to all genera\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"27 pages, PostScript\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev. D50 (1994) 5193-5203\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.50.5193\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"NBI-HE-94-14\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We give a complete description of the genus expansion \
of the one-cut solution\\nto the generalized Penner model. The solution is \
presented in a form which\\nallows us in a very straightforward manner to \
localize critical points and to\\ninvestigate the scaling behaviour of the \
model in the vicinity of these points.\\nWe carry out an analysis of the \
critical behaviour to all genera addressing all\\ntypes of multi-critical \
points. In certain regions of the coupling constant\\nspace the model must be \
defined via analytical continuation. We show in detail\\nhow this works for \
the Penner model. Using analytical continuation it is\\npossible to reach the \
fermionic 1-matrix model. We show that the critical\\npoints of the fermionic \
1-matrix model can be indexed by an integer, $m$, as it\\nwas the case for \
the ordinary hermitian 1-matrix model. Furthermore the \
$m$'th\\nmulti-critical fermionic model has to all genera the same value \
of\\n$\\\\gamma_{str}$ as the $m$'th multi-critical hermitian model. However, \
the\\ncoefficients of the topological expansion need not be the same in the \
two\\ncases. We show explicitly how it is possible with a fermionic matrix \
model to\\nreach a $m=2$ multi-critical point for which the topological \
expansion has\\nalternating signs, but otherwise coincides with the usual \
Painlev\\\\'{e}\\nexpansion.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 4 Mar 1994 09:24:09 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
              
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-10-28\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Ambjorn\"", ",", "\"J.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Makeenko\"", ",", "\"Yu.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Kristjansen\"", ",", "\"C. F.\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
             Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
