            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/9403024", "submitter" -> Null, "authors" -> 
            "J. Ambjorn, Yu. Makeenko and C.F. Kristjansen", "title" -> 
            "Generalized Penner models to all genera", "comments" -> 
            "27 pages, PostScript", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rev. D50 (1994) 5193-5203", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.50.5193", "report-no" -> "NBI-HE-94-14", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We give a complete description of the genus expansion of the \
one-cut solution\nto the generalized Penner model. The solution is presented \
in a form which\nallows us in a very straightforward manner to localize \
critical points and to\ninvestigate the scaling behaviour of the model in the \
vicinity of these points.\nWe carry out an analysis of the critical behaviour \
to all genera addressing all\ntypes of multi-critical points. In certain \
regions of the coupling constant\nspace the model must be defined via \
analytical continuation. We show in detail\nhow this works for the Penner \
model. Using analytical continuation it is\npossible to reach the fermionic \
1-matrix model. We show that the critical\npoints of the fermionic 1-matrix \
model can be indexed by an integer, $m$, as it\nwas the case for the ordinary \
hermitian 1-matrix model. Furthermore the $m$'th\nmulti-critical fermionic \
model has to all genera the same value of\n$\\gamma_{str}$ as the $m$'th \
multi-critical hermitian model. However, the\ncoefficients of the topological \
expansion need not be the same in the two\ncases. We show explicitly how it \
is possible with a fermionic matrix model to\nreach a $m=2$ multi-critical \
point for which the topological expansion has\nalternating signs, but \
otherwise coincides with the usual Painlev\\'{e}\nexpansion.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 4 Mar 1994 09:24:09 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-10-28", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ambjorn", "J.", ""}, {
