calculation\nof the interaction between operator-like solutions identified \
with D-brane\nconfigurations of type IIB superstring (in particular, for \
parallel moving and\nrotated static p-branes). Comparing to the superstring \
calculations, we show\nthat the matrix model reproduces the superstring \
results only at large\ndistances or small velocities, corresponding to \
keeping only the lowest mass\nclosed string modes. We propose a modification \
of the IKKT matrix model\nintroducing an integration over an additional \
Hermitian matrix required to have\npositive definite eigenvalues, which is \
similar to the square root of the\nmetric in the continuum Schild formulation \
of IIB superstrings. We show that\nfor this new matrix action the Nambu-Goto \
version of the Green-Schwarz action\nis reproduced even at quantum level.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Wed, 5 Mar 1997 20:45:30 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
                "Fri, 14 Mar 1997 14:56:35 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v3", "created" -> 
                "Fri, 4 Apr 1997 16:48:32 GMT"}, {
               "version" -> "v4", "created" -> 
                "Tue, 20 May 1997 08:48:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
