               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We show that a recently proposed Yang-Mills matrix \
model with an auxiliary\\nfield, which is a candidate for a non-perturbative \
description of type IIB\\nsuperstrings, captures the Euler characteristic of \
moduli space of Riemann\\nsurfaces. This happens at the saddle point for the \
Yang-Mills field. It turns\\nout that the large-n limit in this matrix model \
corresponds to a double scaling\\nlimit in the Penner model.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
