             "10.1142/S0217732397002417", "report-no" -> "ITEP-TH-18/97", 
             "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  We calculate an effective action and measure induced by the \
integration over\nthe auxiliary field in the matrix model recently proposed \
to describe IIB\nsuperstrings. It is shown that the measure of integration \
over the auxiliary\nmatrix is uniquely determined by locality and \
reparametrization invariance of\nthe resulting effective action. The \
large--$N$ limit of the induced measure for\nstring coordinates is discussed \
in detail. It is found to be ultralocal and,\nthus, possibly is irrelevant in \
the continuum limit. The model of the GKM type\nis considered in relation to \
the effective action problem.\n", 
