            "authors" -> "Shinji Hirano and Mitsuhiro Kato", "title" -> 
            "Topological Matrix Model", "comments" -> 
            
            "18 pages, LaTeX, no figures, minor corrections and \
modifications,\n  references added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Prog.Theor.Phys.98:1371-1384,1997", "doi" -> 
            "10.1143/PTP.98.1371", "report-no" -> 
            "OU-HET 274, UT-Komaba/97-11", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  Starting from the primal principle based on the noncommutative \
nature of\n(9+1)-dimensional spacetime, we construct a topologically twisted \
version of\nthe supersymmetric reduced model with a certain modification. Our \
formulation\nautomatically provides extra 1+1 dimensions, thereby the \
dimensions of\nspacetime are promoted to 10+2. With a suitable gauge choice, \
we can reduce the\nmodel with (10+2)-dimensional spacetime to the one with \
(9+1)-dimensions and\nthus we regard this gauge as the light-cone gauge. It \
is suggested that the\nmodel so obtained would describe the light-cone \
F-theory. From this viewpoint\nwe argue the relation of the reduced model to \
the matrix model of M-theory and\nthe SL(2,Z) symmetry of type IIB string \
theory. We also discuss the general\ncovariance of the matrix model in a \
broken phase, and make some comments on the\nbackground independence.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 7 Aug 1997 13:16:21 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Sat, 16 Aug 1997 08:05:27 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2014-11-18", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Hirano", "Shinji", ""}, {
              "Kato", "Mitsuhiro", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{8.57781069314273, -5.961156517034217}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9708115\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Simon Dalley\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"S. Dalley\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Adjoint QCD2 and the Non-Abelian Schwinger \
Mechanism\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10 pages LaTeX, uses boxedeps.tex. Figures clarified \
now\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Lett. B418 (1998) 160-166\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0370-2693(97)01474-3\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"CERN-TH/198\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  Massless Majorana fermions in the adjoint \
representation of SU(N_c) are\\nexpected to screen gauge interactions in 1+1 \
dimensions, analogous to a similar\\nHiggs phenomena known for \
1+1-dimensional U(1) gauge theory with massless\\nfundamental fermions \
(Schwinger model). Using the light-cone formalism and\\nlarge-N_c limit, a \
non-abelian analogue of the Schwinger boson is shown to be\\nresponsible for \
the screening between heavy test charges. This adjoint boson\\ndoes not exist \
simply as a physical state, but boundstates are built entirely\\nfrom this \
particle.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 21 Aug 1997 17:00:23 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 3 Oct 1997 11:22:44 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-10-30\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Dalley\"", ",", "\"S.\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}],
                    "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> Left, 
             ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
