                 "\"Interactions Between Branes and Matrix Theories\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"12 pages, latex. Contribution to Proceedings of \
STRINGS'97 (misprints\\n  corrected)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys.Proc.Suppl.68:99-110,1998\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0920-5632(98)00144-3\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Imperial/TP/96-97/66\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We review some tests of the 0-brane and instanton \
matrix models based on\\ncomparing long-distance interaction potentials \
between branes and their bound\\nstates (with 1/2,1/4 or 1/8 of \
supersymmetry) in supergravity and in super\\nYang-Mills descriptions. We \
first consider the supergravity-SYM correspondence\\nat the level of the \
leading term in the interaction potential, and then\\ndescribe some recent \
results concerning the subleading term and their\\nimplications for the \
structure of the 2-loop F^6 term in the SYM effective\\naction.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
