         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "hep-th/9802085", "submitter" -> "Hajime Aoki", "authors" -> 
            "H. Aoki, S. Iso, H. Kawai, Y. Kitazawa, T. Tada", "title" -> 
            "Space-Time Structures from IIB Matrix Model", "comments" -> 
            "39 pages, Latex, uses epsf and axodraw", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Prog.Theor.Phys. 99 (1998) 713-746", "doi" -> 
            "10.1143/PTP.99.713", "report-no" -> "KEK-TH-559, TIT/HEP-382", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We derive a long distance effective action for space-time \
coordinates from a\nIIB matrix model. It provides us an effective tool to \
study the structures of\nspace-time. We prove the finiteness of the theory \
for finite $N$ to all orders\nof the perturbation theory. Space-time is shown \
to be inseparable and its\ndimensionality is dynamically determined. The IIB \
matrix model contains a\nmechanism to ensure the vanishing cosmological \
constant which does not rely on\nthe manifest supersymmetry. We discuss \
possible mechanisms to obtain realistic\ndimensionality and gauge groups from \
the IIB matrix model.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 12 Feb 1998 12:21:47 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2009-10-31", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Aoki", "H.", ""}, {"Iso", "S.", ""}, {
              "Kawai", "H.", ""}, {"Kitazawa", "Y.", ""}, {
              "Tada", "T.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
