          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9809039\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Boris Pioline\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"N.A. Obers (CERN, Nordita) and B. Pioline (Ecole \
Polytechnique)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"U-duality and M-Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"132 pages, 37 tables, Latex2e; v3: minor corrections, \
text\\n  reformatted, update of refs, note added about boundaries of M-theory \
moduli\\n  space, final version to appear in Phys. Rept\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rept.318:113-225,1999\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0370-1573(99)00004-6\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"CERN-TH/98-282, CPHT-S639-0898\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  This work is intended as a pedagogical introduction to \
M-theory and to its\\nmaximally supersymmetric toroidal compactifications, in \
the frameworks of 11D\\nsupergravity, type II string theory and M(atrix) \
theory. U-duality is used as\\nthe main tool and guideline in uncovering the \
spectrum of BPS states. We review\\nthe 11D supergravity algebra and \
elementary 1/2-BPS solutions, discuss\\nT-duality in the perturbative and \
non-perturbative sectors from an algebraic\\npoint of view, and apply the \
same tools to the analysis of U-duality at the\\nlevel of the effective \
action and the BPS spectrum, with a particular emphasis\\non Weyl and Borel \
generators. We derive the U-duality multiplets of BPS\\nparticles and \
strings, U-duality invariant mass formulae for 1/2- and 1/4-BPS\\nstates for \
general toroidal compactifications on skew tori with gauge\\nbackgrounds, and \
U-duality multiplets of constraints for states to preserve a\\ngiven fraction \
of supersymmetry. A number of mysterious states are encountered\\nin D<=3, \
whose existence is implied by T-duality and 11D Lorentz invariance. We\\nthen \
move to the M(atrix) theory point of view, give an introduction to\\nDiscrete \
Light Cone Quantization (DLCQ) in general and DLCQ of M-theory \
in\\nparticular. We discuss the realization of U-duality as electric-magnetic\
\\ndualities of the Matrix gauge theory, display the Matrix gauge theory \
BPS\\nspectrum in detail, and discuss the conjectured extended U-duality \
group in\\nthis scheme.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 7 Sep 1998 17:10:48 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
