            "N.A. Obers (CERN, Nordita) and B. Pioline (Ecole Polytechnique)",
             "title" -> "U-duality and M-Theory", "comments" -> 
            "132 pages, 37 tables, Latex2e; v3: minor corrections, text\n  \
reformatted, update of refs, note added about boundaries of M-theory moduli\n \
 space, final version to appear in Phys. Rept", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rept.318:113-225,1999", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0370-1573(99)00004-6", "report-no" -> 
            "CERN-TH/98-282, CPHT-S639-0898", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  This work is intended as a pedagogical introduction to \
M-theory and to its\nmaximally supersymmetric toroidal compactifications, in \
the frameworks of 11D\nsupergravity, type II string theory and M(atrix) \
theory. U-duality is used as\nthe main tool and guideline in uncovering the \
spectrum of BPS states. We review\nthe 11D supergravity algebra and \
elementary 1/2-BPS solutions, discuss\nT-duality in the perturbative and \
non-perturbative sectors from an algebraic\npoint of view, and apply the same \
tools to the analysis of U-duality at the\nlevel of the effective action and \
the BPS spectrum, with a particular emphasis\non Weyl and Borel generators. \
We derive the U-duality multiplets of BPS\nparticles and strings, U-duality \
invariant mass formulae for 1/2- and 1/4-BPS\nstates for general toroidal \
compactifications on skew tori with gauge\nbackgrounds, and U-duality \
multiplets of constraints for states to preserve a\ngiven fraction of \
supersymmetry. A number of mysterious states are encountered\nin D<=3, whose \
existence is implied by T-duality and 11D Lorentz invariance. We\nthen move \
to the M(atrix) theory point of view, give an introduction to\nDiscrete Light \
Cone Quantization (DLCQ) in general and DLCQ of M-theory in\nparticular. We \
discuss the realization of U-duality as electric-magnetic\ndualities of the \
Matrix gauge theory, display the Matrix gauge theory BPS\nspectrum in detail, \
and discuss the conjectured extended U-duality group in\nthis scheme.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
