                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We show that the logarithmically rising static \
potential between\\nopposite-charged sources in two dimensions is screened by \
dynamical fields even\\nif the probe charges are fractional, in units of the \
charge of the dynamical\\nfields. The effect is due to quantum mechanics: the \
wave functions of the\\nscreening charges are superpositions of two bumps \
localized both near the\\nopposite- and the same-charge sources, so that each \
of them gets exactly\\nscreened.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
