                 "\"Mitsuhiro Kato and Tsunehide Kuroki\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"World Volume Noncommutativity versus Target Space \
Noncommutativity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"17 pages, LaTex, no figures\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 9903:012,1999\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/1999/03/012\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"UT-Komaba/99-3\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  It is known that the noncommutativity of D-brane \
coordinate is responsible\\nfor describing the higher-dimensional D-branes in \
terms of more fundamental\\nones such as D-particles or D-instantons, while \
considering a noncommutative\\ntorus as a target space is conjectured to be \
equivalent to introducing the\\nbackground antisymmetric tensor field in \
matrix models. In the present paper we\\nclarify the dual nature of both \
descriptions. Namely the noncommutativity of\\nconjugate momenta of the \
D-brane coordinates realizes the target space\\nstructure, whereas \
noncommutativity of the coordinates themselves realizes\\nworld volume \
structure. We explicitly construct a boundary state for the\\nDirichlet \
boundary condition where the string boundary is adhered to the\\nD-brane on \
the noncommutative torus. There are non-trivial relations between\\nthe \
parameters appeared in the algebra of the coordinates and that of \
the\\nmomenta.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Sun, 31 Jan 1999 09:18:22 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2010-02-03\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kato\"", ",", "\"Mitsuhiro\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kuroki\"", ",", "\"Tsunehide\"", ",", "\"\""}],
                     "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
