            "authors" -> "Mitsuhiro Kato and Tsunehide Kuroki", "title" -> 
            "World Volume Noncommutativity versus Target Space \
Noncommutativity", "comments" -> "17 pages, LaTex, no figures", "journal-ref" -> 
            "JHEP 9903:012,1999", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/1999/03/012", 
            "report-no" -> "UT-Komaba/99-3", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
            "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  It is known that the noncommutativity of D-brane coordinate is \
responsible\nfor describing the higher-dimensional D-branes in terms of more \
fundamental\nones such as D-particles or D-instantons, while considering a \
noncommutative\ntorus as a target space is conjectured to be equivalent to \
introducing the\nbackground antisymmetric tensor field in matrix models. In \
the present paper we\nclarify the dual nature of both descriptions. Namely \
the noncommutativity of\nconjugate momenta of the D-brane coordinates \
realizes the target space\nstructure, whereas noncommutativity of the \
coordinates themselves realizes\nworld volume structure. We explicitly \
construct a boundary state for the\nDirichlet boundary condition where the \
string boundary is adhered to the\nD-brane on the noncommutative torus. There \
are non-trivial relations between\nthe parameters appeared in the algebra of \
the coordinates and that of the\nmomenta.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Sun, 31 Jan 1999 09:18:22 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2010-02-03", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kato", "Mitsuhiro", ""}, {
              "Kuroki", "Tsunehide", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
