               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Joseph A. Minahan\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Joseph A. Minahan (IAS)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Asymptotic Freedom and Confinement from Type 0 String \
Theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25 pages; harvmac (b); v2 ref. added, typos corrected;v3 \
minor change\\n  to sec. 3, more sol'ns considered in sec.4, revised WKB \
analysis in 5.3\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 9904:007,1999\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/1999/04/007\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"IASSNS-HEP-99/14\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We argue that there are generic solutions to the type 0 \
gravity equations of\\nmotion that are confining in the infrared and have log \
scaling in the\\nultraviolet. The background curvature generically diverges \
in the IR.\\nNevertheless, there exist solutions where higher order string \
corrections\\nappear to be exponentially suppressed in the IR with respect to \
the leading\\ntype 0 gravity terms. For these solutions the tachyon flows to \
a fixed value.\\n  We show that the generic solutions lead to a long range \
linear quark\\npotential, magnetic screening and a discrete glueball \
spectrum. We also\\nestimate some WKB glueball mass ratios and compare them \
to ratios found using\\nfinite temperature models and lattice \
computations.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
