           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9902095\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"A.A. Tseytlin and K. Zarembo\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Effective potential in non-supersymmetric SU(N) x SU(N) \
gauge theory and\\n  interactions of type 0 D3-branes\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"14 pages, latex, v2: minor corrections, v3: a comment \
and references\\n  added at the end of section 5\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Lett.B457:77-86,1999\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1016/S0370-2693(99)00471-2\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"ITEP-TH-4/99, Imperial/TP/98-99/41\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We study some aspects of short-distance interaction \
between parallel\\nD3-branes in type 0 string theory as described by the \
corresponding\\nworld-volume gauge theory. We compute the one-loop effective \
potential in the\\nnon-supersymmetric SU(N) x SU(N) gauge theory (which is a \
Z_2 projection of the\\nU(2N) n=4 SYM theory) representing dyonic branes \
composed of N electric and N\\nmagnetic D3-branes. The branes of the same \
type repel at short distances, but\\nan electric and a magnetic brane \
attract, and the forces between self-dual\\nbranes cancel. The self-dual \
configuration (with the positions of the electric\\nand the magnetic branes, \
i.e. the diagonal entries of the adjoint scalar\\nfields, being the same) is \
stable against separation of one electric or one\\nmagnetic brane, but is \
unstable against certain modes of separation of several\\nsame-type branes. \
This instability should be suppressed in the large N limit,\\ni.e. should be \
irrelevant for the large N CFT interpretation of the gauge\\ntheory suggested \
in hep-th/9901101.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 12 Feb 1999 22:54:19 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 22 Feb 1999 16:12:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
