               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9903128\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Miguel S. Costa\""}]}, {
              
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Miguel S. Costa (Princeton University)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Intersecting D-branes and black holes in type 0 string \
theory\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"17 pages, latex; incorrect statement about potential \
between D-branes\\n  removed and minor corrections, version to appear in JHEP\
\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 9904:016,1999\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1088/1126-6708/1999/04/016\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"PUPT-1842\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study intersecting D-branes in type 0 string \
theories and show that the\\nD$p_{\\\\pm}$-brane bound states obey similar \
intersecting rules as the\\nD$p$-branes of the type II theories. The \
D$5_{\\\\pm}$-D$1_{\\\\pm}$ brane system is\\nstudied in detail. We show that \
the corresponding near-horizon geometry is the\\n$AdS_3\\\\times S^3\\\\times \
T^4$ space and that there is no tachyon instability in\\nthis background. The \
Bekenstein-Hawking entropy is calculated. The worldvolume\\ntheory on the \
D$5_{\\\\pm}$-D$1_{\\\\pm}$ system is also studied. This theory\\ncontains \
both bosons and fermions and it is seen to arise as a projection of\\nthe \
supersymmetric gauge theory related to the D5-D1 system of the type \
IIB\\ntheory. The Bekenstein-Hawking entropy formula is reproduced exactly \
using the\\ndual conformal field theory.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
