               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9906057\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Csaba Csaki\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Csaba Csaki (Berkeley), Witold Skiba (San Diego), John \
Terning\\n  (Berkeley)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Beta Functions of Orbifold Theories and the Hierarchy \
Problem\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"21 pages, LaTeX, 6 figures. Minor clarifications, \
references added\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Phys.Rev.D61:025019,2000\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.61.025019\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"LBNL-4342, UCB-PTH-99/27, UCSD-PTH-99/07\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th hep-ph\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We examine a class of gauge theories obtained by \
projecting out certain\\nfields from an N=4 supersymmetric SU(N) gauge \
theory. These theories are\\nnon-supersymmetric and in the large N limit are \
known to be conformal. Recently\\nit was proposed that the hierarchy problem \
could be solved by embedding the\\nstandard model in a theory of this kind \
with finite N. In order to check this\\nclaim one must find the conformal \
points of the theory. To do this we calculate\\nthe one-loop beta functions \
for the Yukawa and quartic scalar couplings. We\\nfind that with the beta \
functions set to zero the one-loop quadratic\\ndivergences are not canceled \
at sub-leading order in N; thus the hierarchy\\nbetween the weak scale and \
the Planck scale is not stabilized unless N is of\\nthe order 10^28 or \
larger. We also find that at sub-leading orders in N\\nrenormalization \
induces new interactions, which were not present in the\\noriginal \
Lagrangian.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 8 Jun 1999 01:10:07 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 15 Jun 1999 23:09:42 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                   "}"}]}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-09-17\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
