 (Berkeley)", "title" -> 
            "Beta Functions of Orbifold Theories and the Hierarchy Problem", 
            "comments" -> 
            "21 pages, LaTeX, 6 figures. Minor clarifications, references \
added", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D61:025019,2000", "doi" -> 
            "10.1103/PhysRevD.61.025019", "report-no" -> 
            "LBNL-4342, UCB-PTH-99/27, UCSD-PTH-99/07", "categories" -> 
            "hep-th hep-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We examine a class of gauge theories obtained by projecting \
out certain\nfields from an N=4 supersymmetric SU(N) gauge theory. These \
theories are\nnon-supersymmetric and in the large N limit are known to be \
conformal. Recently\nit was proposed that the hierarchy problem could be \
solved by embedding the\nstandard model in a theory of this kind with finite \
N. In order to check this\nclaim one must find the conformal points of the \
theory. To do this we calculate\nthe one-loop beta functions for the Yukawa \
and quartic scalar couplings. We\nfind that with the beta functions set to \
zero the one-loop quadratic\ndivergences are not canceled at sub-leading \
order in N; thus the hierarchy\nbetween the weak scale and the Planck scale \
is not stabilized unless N is of\nthe order 10^28 or larger. We also find \
that at sub-leading orders in N\nrenormalization induces new interactions, \
which were not present in the\noriginal Lagrangian.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
