            "10 pages, harvmac; v2: 1 minor clarification, 1 reference added",
             "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Lett. B466 (1999) 166-170", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0370-2693(99)01084-9", "report-no" -> "PUPT-1874", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We consider duality between type 0B string theory on \
$AdS_5\\times S^5$ and\nthe planar CFT on $N$ electric D3-branes coincident \
with $N$ magnetic\nD3-branes. It has been argued that this theory is stable \
up to a critical value\nof the `t Hooft coupling but is unstable beyond that \
point. We suggest that\nfrom the gauge theory point of view the development \
of instability is\nassociated with singularity in the dimension of the \
operator corresponding to\nthe tachyon field via the AdS/CFT map. Such \
singularities are common in large\n$N$ theories because summation over planar \
graphs typically has a finite radius\nof convergence. Hence we expect \
transitions between stability and instability\nfor string theories in AdS \
backgrounds that are dual to certain large $N$ gauge\ntheories: if there are \
tachyons for large AdS radius then they may be\nstabilized by reducing the \
radius below a critical value of order the string\nscale.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Mon, 28 Jun 1999 19:57:11 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 9 Jul 1999 20:52:56 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
