Tada", "title" -> "Noncommutative Yang-Mills in IIB Matrix Model", "comments" -> 
            "21pages, LaTeX, no figures, typos corrected", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys. B565 (2000) 176-192", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00633-1", "report-no" -> 
            "KEK-TH-637, KUNS-1595", "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> 
            Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We show that twisted reduced models can be interpreted as \
noncommutative\nYang-Mills theory. Based upon this correspondence, we obtain \
noncommutative\nYang-Mills theory with D-brane backgrounds in IIB matrix \
model. We propose that\nIIB matrix model with D-brane backgrounds serve as a \
concrete definition of\nnoncommutative Yang-Mills. We investigate D-instanton \
solutions as local\nexcitations on D3-branes. When instantons overlap, their \
interaction can be\nwell described in gauge theory and AdS/CFT \
correspondence. We show that IIB\nmatrix model gives us the consistent \
potential with IIB supergravity when they\nare well separated.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
