            "title" -> 
            "An Orbifold of Type 0B Strings and Non-supersymmetric Gauge \
Theories", "comments" -> 
            "15 pages, harvmac; v2: very minor corrections; v3: a comment \
about\n  pure glue theory added", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Nucl.Phys. B591 (2000) 26-38", "doi" -> 
            "10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00547-2", "report-no" -> 
            "PUPT-1891, ITEP-TH-48/99, NSF-ITP-99-27, YCTP-P24-99", 
            "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We study a ${{\\IZ}}_2$ orbifold of Type 0B string theory by \
reflection of six\nof the coordinates (this theory may also be thought of as \
a ${{\\IZ}}_4$\norbifold of Type IIB string theory by a rotation by $\\pi$ in \
three independent\nplanes). We show that the only massless mode localized on \
the fixed fourplane\n$\\IR^{3,1}$ is a U(1) gauge field. After introducing \
D3-branes parallel to the\nfixed fourplane we find non-supersymmetric \
non-abelian gauge theories on their\nworldvolume. One of our results is that \
the theory on equal numbers of electric\nand magnetic D3-branes placed at the \
fourplane is the ${{\\IZ}}_4$ orbifold of\n${\\cal N}=4$ supersymmetric \
Yang-Mills theory by the center of its R-symmetry\ngroup.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 15 Sep 1999 19:35:09 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Fri, 17 Sep 1999 21:03:24 GMT"}, {
