        TagBox[
         TooltipBox[DiskBox[{5.220670686100194, -2.329355085211626}, 0.],
          TagBox[
           TagBox[
            GridBox[{{
               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9910004\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Satoshi Iso\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nobuyuki Ishibashi, Satoshi Iso, Hikaru Kawai and \
Yoshihisa Kitazawa\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Wilson Loops in Noncommutative Yang Mills\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"25 pages, no figures, references added and typos \
corrected\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B573 (2000) 573-593\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00708-7\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We study the correlation functions of the Wilson loops \
in noncommutative\\nYang-Mills theory based upon its equivalence to twisted \
reduced models. We\\npoint out that there is a crossover at the \
noncommutativity scale. At large\\nmomentum scale, the Wilson loops in \
noncommmutative Yang-Mills represent\\nextended objects. They coincide with \
those in ordinary Yang-Mills theory in low\\nenergy limit. The correlation \
functions on D-branes in IIB matrix model exhibit\\nthe identical crossover \
behavior. It is observed to be consistent with the\\nsupergravity description \
with running string coupling. We also explain that the\\nresults of Seiberg \
and Witten can be simply understood in our formalism.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
