Zarembo\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Static Potential in N=4 Supersymmetric Yang-Mills Theory\
\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"8 pages, four figures using feynmf\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Rev. D61 (2000) 105006\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.61.105006\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We compute the leading order perturbative correction \
to the static potential\\nin ${\\\\cal N}=4$ supersymmetric Yang-Mills \
theory. We show that the perturbative\\nexpansion contains infrared \
logarithms which, when resummed, become logarithms\\nof the coupling \
constant. The resulting correction goes in the right direction\\nto match the \
strong coupling behavior obtained from the AdS/CFT correspondence.\\nWe find \
that the strong coupling extrapolation of the sum of ladder diagrams\\ngoes \
as $\\\\sqrt{g^2N}$, as in the supergravity approach.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
