Super\n  Yang-Mills Effective Actions", "comments" -> 
             "14 pages, 1 figure; a clarification and two important \
references\n  added; v4: comments on higher-derivative terms and on anomaly \
inflow on\n  D8-branes are added", "journal-ref" -> 
             "Phys.Lett.B474:95-102,2000", "doi" -> 
             "10.1016/S0370-2693(99)01499-9", "report-no" -> 
             "ITEP-TH-69/99, OHSTPY-HEP-T-99-028", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
             "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  There is a close relation between classical supergravity and \
quantum SYM\ndescriptions of interactions between separated branes. In the \
case of D3\nbranes, the equivalence of leading-order potentials is due to\n\
non-renormalization of the F^4 term in N=4 SYM theory. Here we point out the\n\
existence of another special non-renormalized term in quantum SYM effective\n\
action. This term reproduces the interaction potential between electric \
charge\nof a D3-brane probe and magnetic charge of a D3-brane source, \
represented by\nthe Chern-Simons part of the D-brane action. This unique \
Wess-Zumino term\ndepends on all six scalar fields and originates from a \
phase of the euclidean\nfermion determinant in SYM theory. It is manifestly \
scale invariant (i.e. is\nthe same for large and small separations between \
branes) and can not receive\nhigher loop corrections in gauge theory. \
Maximally supersymmetric SYM theories\nin D=p+1>4 contain mixed WZ terms \
which depend on both scalar and gauge field\nbackgrounds, and which reproduce \
the corresponding CS terms in the supergravity\ninteraction potentials \
between separated Dp-branes for p>3. Purely scalar WZ\nterms appear in other \
cases, e.g., in N=2 gauge theories in various dimensions\ndescribing magnetic \
interactions between Dp and D(6-p) branes.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Tue, 30 Nov 1999 05:06:21 GMT"}, {
