               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/9912257\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Carlo Angelantonj\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Carlo Angelantonj (ENS) and Adi Armoni (Ecole \
Polytechnique)\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Non-Tachyonic Type 0B Orientifolds, Non-Supersymmetric \
Gauge Theories\\n  and Cosmological RG Flow\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"26 pages. Minor changes. Refs added. To appear in Nucl. \
Phys. B\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Nucl.Phys. B578 (2000) 239-258\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00136-X\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"CPHT-S757.1299, LPTENS 99/55\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We discuss gauge theories on D3 branes embedded in \
special non-tachyonic\\norientifolds of the 0B string theory. In general, \
they correspond to\\nnon-supersymmetric SU(N) gauge theories with scalars in \
the adjoint\\nrepresentation and spinors in the (anti-)symmetric \
representation. We study\\nthese theories via the AdS/CFT correspondence and \
present evidence of their\\nrelation to N=4 SYM in the planar limit. We also \
discuss finite N properties,\\nfocusing in particular on the renormalization \
group flow. Up to two loops, the\\nlogarithmic running of the gauge coupling \
is described by the dilaton tadpole\\nand the cosmological constant that \
naturally emerge on the string theory side.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
