Doikou\n  (LAPTH), Luc Frappat (LAPTH), Eric Ragoucy (LAPTH)", "title" -> 
            "Analytical Bethe Ansatz for closed and open gl(n)-spin chains in \
any\n  representation", "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> 
            "J.Stat.Mech.0502:P02007,2005", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/2005/02/P02007", "report-no" -> 
            "LAPTH-1069/04", "categories" -> 
            "math-ph cond-mat.str-el math.MP math.QA", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We present an \"algebraic treatment\" of the analytical Bethe \
Ansatz. For this\npurpose, we introduce abstract monodromy and transfer \
matrices which provide an\nalgebraic framework for the analytical Bethe \
Ansatz. It allows us to deal with\na generic gl(n)-spin chain possessing on \
each site an arbitrary\ngl(n)-representation. For open spin chains, we use \
the classification of the\nreflection matrices to treat all the diagonal \
boundary cases. As a result, we\nobtain the Bethe equations in their full \
generality for closed and open spin\nchains. The classifications of finite \
dimensional irreducible representations\nfor the Yangian (closed spin chains) \
and for the reflection algebras (open spin\nchains) are directly linked to \
the calculation of the transfer matrix\neigenvalues. As examples, we recover \
the usual closed and open spin chains, we\ntreat the alternating spin chains \
and the closed spin chain with impurity.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Thu, 4 Nov 2004 20:04:50 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2011-02-16", 
