               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We present an ``algebraic treatment'' of the analytical \
Bethe ansatz for open\\nspin chains with soliton non preserving (SNP) \
boundary conditions. For this\\npurpose, we introduce abstract monodromy and \
transfer matrices which provide an\\nalgebraic framework for the analytical \
Bethe ansatz. It allows us to deal with\\na generic gl(N) open SNP spin chain \
possessing on each site an arbitrary\\nrepresentation. As a result, we obtain \
the Bethe equations in their full\\ngenerality. The classification of finite \
dimensional irreducible\\nrepresentations for the twisted Yangians are \
directly linked to the calculation\\nof the transfer matrix \
eigenvalues.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
