               RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"nlin/0610017\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Niklas Beisert\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Niklas Beisert\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"The Analytic Bethe Ansatz for a Chain with Centrally \
Extended su(2|2)\\n  Symmetry\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"66 pages, v2: minor changes, references added, to appear \
in JSTAT\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"J.Stat.Mech.0701:P01017,2007\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"10.1088/1742-5468/2007/01/P01017\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"AEI-2006-074, PUTP-2211\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"nlin.SI cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  We investigate the integrable structure of spin chain \
models with centrally\\nextended su(2|2) and psu(2,2|4) symmetry. These \
chains have their origin in the\\nplanar AdS/CFT correspondence, but they \
also contain the one-dimensional\\nHubbard model as a special case. We begin \
with an overview of the\\nrepresentation theory of centrally extended \
su(2|2). These results are applied\\nin the construction and investigation of \
an interesting S-matrix with su(2|2)\\nsymmetry. In particular, they enable a \
remarkably simple proof of the\\nYang-Baxter relation. We also show the \
equivalence of the S-matrix to Shastry's\\nR-matrix and thus uncover a hidden \
supersymmetry in the integrable structure of\\nthe Hubbard model. We then \
construct eigenvalues of the corresponding transfer\\nmatrix in order to \
formulate an analytic Bethe ansatz. Finally, the form of\\ntransfer matrix \
eigenvalues for models with psu(2,2|4) symmetry is sketched.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
