            "The Analytic Bethe Ansatz for a Chain with Centrally Extended \
su(2|2)\n  Symmetry", "comments" -> 
            "66 pages, v2: minor changes, references added, to appear in \
JSTAT", "journal-ref" -> "J.Stat.Mech.0701:P01017,2007", "doi" -> 
            "10.1088/1742-5468/2007/01/P01017", "report-no" -> 
            "AEI-2006-074, PUTP-2211", "categories" -> 
            "nlin.SI cond-mat.stat-mech hep-th", "license" -> Null, 
            "abstract" -> 
            "  We investigate the integrable structure of spin chain models \
with centrally\nextended su(2|2) and psu(2,2|4) symmetry. These chains have \
their origin in the\nplanar AdS/CFT correspondence, but they also contain the \
one-dimensional\nHubbard model as a special case. We begin with an overview \
of the\nrepresentation theory of centrally extended su(2|2). These results \
are applied\nin the construction and investigation of an interesting S-matrix \
with su(2|2)\nsymmetry. In particular, they enable a remarkably simple proof \
of the\nYang-Baxter relation. We also show the equivalence of the S-matrix to \
Shastry's\nR-matrix and thus uncover a hidden supersymmetry in the integrable \
structure of\nthe Hubbard model. We then construct eigenvalues of the \
corresponding transfer\nmatrix in order to formulate an analytic Bethe \
ansatz. Finally, the form of\ntransfer matrix eigenvalues for models with \
psu(2,2|4) symmetry is sketched.\n", 
