                "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Two lectures on color superconductivity\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"56 pages, 9 figures. Minor corrections and references \
added. Lectures\\n  delivered at the IARD 2004 conference, Saas Fee, \
Switzerland, June 12 - 19,\\n  2004, and at the Helmholtz International \
Summer School and Workshop on Hot\\n  points in Astrophysics and Cosmology, \
JINR, Dubna, Russia, August 2 - 13,\\n  2004\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"Found.Phys. 35 (2005) 1309-1358\""}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/s10701-005-6440-x\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"nucl-th astro-ph cond-mat.supr-con hep-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
               
               RowBox[{
                "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 "\"  The first lecture provides an introduction to the \
physics of color\\nsuperconductivity in cold dense quark matter. The main \
color superconducting\\nphases are briefly described and their properties are \
listed. The second\\nlecture covers recent developments in studies of color \
superconducting phases\\nin neutral and beta-equilibrated matter. The \
properties of gapless color\\nsuperconducting phases are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
               RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{
