           Function[BoxForm`e$, 
            TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
         Annotation[#, 
          
          TableForm[{
           "id" -> "nucl-th/0701067", "submitter" -> "Mark G. Alford", 
            "authors" -> 
            "Mark G. Alford (Washington U., St. Louis), Matt Braby \
(Washington U.,\n  St. Louis), Sanjay Reddy (LANL), Thomas Schaefer (NCSU)", 
            "title" -> 
            "Bulk viscosity due to kaons in color-flavor-locked quark matter",
             "comments" -> 
            "23 pages, LaTeX; corrected typos and a numerical error in the \
last 3\n  figures. Conclusions unchanged", "journal-ref" -> 
            "Phys.Rev.C75:055209,2007", "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevC.75.055209",
             "report-no" -> "LA-UR-07-0429", "categories" -> 
            "nucl-th astro-ph hep-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
            "  We calculate the bulk viscosity of color-superconducting quark \
matter in the\ncolor-flavor-locked (CFL) phase. We assume that the lightest \
bosons are the\nsuperfluid mode H and the kaons K0 and K+, and that there is \
no kaon\ncondensate. We calculate the rate of strangeness-equilibrating \
processes that\nconvert kaons into superfluid modes, and the resultant bulk \
viscosity. We find\nthat for oscillations with a timescale of milliseconds, \
at temperatures T << 1\nMeV, the CFL bulk viscosity is much less than that of \
unpaired quark matter,\nbut at higher temperatures the bulk viscosity of CFL \
matter can become larger.\n", 
            "versions" -> {{
              "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 24 Jan 2007 16:54:46 GMT"}, {
              "version" -> "v2", "created" -> 
               "Wed, 5 Sep 2007 19:49:04 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
            "2008-11-26", 
            "authors_parsed" -> {{
              "Alford", "Mark G.", "", "Washington U., St. Louis"}, {
              "Braby", "Matt", "", "Washington U.,\n  St. Louis"}, {
              "Reddy", "Sanjay", "", "LANL"}, {
              "Schaefer", "Thomas", "", "NCSU"}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
